b5b30e616afd-873b-7d80-8a0de17e74d4	2026-11-18 09:36:53	2026-11-18 09:36:53	0	<p><strong>PR opened:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/projects4me/gaia/pull/276">gaia#276</a> (commit b497b828, based on c4746edc).</p><p>Decisions:</p><ul><li>No generic bypass. Internal code that needs a system field (Ares search columns) uses the model directly.</li><li>CSV export needs no change: its headers come from the ACL-filtered data.</li><li>Review fixes in the ship run: Acl::isSystemField now fails closed (denies) if the metadata cannot be read, and delegates to metaManager; only a literal <code>'system' =&gt; true</code> sets the flag (shared <code>Manager::isSystemFieldMeta</code>, also used by AclMapCatalog).</li></ul><p>Follow-ups (not done here):</p><ul><li>Relationship wildcard selects (<code>rel.*</code>) still fetch system columns from the DB; they are stripped only by applyACLOnFields before serialization. Worth expanding wildcards without system fields once the embedding column lands (defense in depth, and avoids fetching large vectors).</li><li>The Acl clause path reports <code>alias.field</code> while WhereFieldValidator reports the field as typed; both are 400 unknown field.</li><li>Proposed dev-tools issue: <code>gaia-dev check action</code> stops on the host (needs nikic/php-parser); it should run in the container or be wrapped by <code>ai gaia-dev</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><pre>api backend: 220 passed, 0 failed, 22 skipped\napi acl: 248 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped\napi client: 396 passed, 6 failed, 6 skipped\n  FAIL settings-patch-secure-value-is-masked  (known)\n  FAIL settings-get-secure-value-is-masked  (known)\n  FAIL settings-list-secure-value-is-masked  (known)\n  FAIL settings-patch-empty-secure-keeps-value  (known)\n  FAIL settings-test-before-password  (known)\n  FAIL settings-test-password-unchanged  (known)\nphpunit tests/libraries/security: OK (261 tests, 769 assertions)\nphpunit tests/libraries/utils: OK (233 tests, 711 assertions)\nphpunit tests/libraries/authorization: OK (49 tests, 128 assertions)\nphpunit tests/models: Tests: 113, Assertions: 294, Failures: 6.\n  FAIL Gaia\\Tests\\Models\\Behaviors\\ShortCodeBehaviorTest::testGenerateShortCodeFromSingleWordIfNoShortCodeExists  (known)\n  FAIL Gaia\\Tests\\Models\\Behaviors\\ShortCodeBehaviorTest::testGenerateShortCodeFromSingleWordIfOneShortCodeExists  (known)\n  FAIL Gaia\\Tests\\Models\\Behaviors\\ShortCodeBehaviorTest::testGenerateShortCodeFromSingleWordIfMultipleShortCodeExists  (known)\n  FAIL Gaia\\Tests\\Models\\Behaviors\\ShortCodeBehaviorTest::testGenerateShortCodeFromMultipleWordsIfNoShortCodeExists  (known)\n  FAIL Gaia\\Tests\\Models\\Behaviors\\ShortCodeBehaviorTest::testGenerateShortCodeFromMultipleWordsIfOneShortCodeExists  (known)\n  FAIL Gaia\\Tests\\Models\\Behaviors\\ShortCodeBehaviorTest::testGenerateShortCodeFromMultipleWordsIfMultipleShortCodeExists  (known)\ntests/services: not in this checkout, skipped\nphpunit tests/tools: OK (180 tests, 1000 assertions)\nRESULT: PASS</pre><p>Size: 8 hand-written file(s), estimated 9</p><p>Cost so far: 51.2k output tokens, 96 turns, peak context 104.6k, cache reads 4967.0k (5 sessions).</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	conversationrooms	2ddd1f466afc-9bce-b62c-7f88fa361e29	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	\N
07bdb25667fd-73ae-c1ff-99b2a7be9f28	2025-04-14 14:09:11	2025-04-14 14:09:11	0	<p>For that feature we have to align the position of the button actions of the JQuery query builder using two options, 1 using css and other using DOM manipulation.</p>\n<p><strong>Using CSS:</strong><br>\nAs the number of rules is going to increase, the add rule/group buttons will be positioned under the list. So this will not work.</p>\n<p><strong>Using JS:</strong><br>\n- After trying to change the element parent using ember rendering events, the JQuery is unable to find the actual parent of the element and fails to add a rule/group by showing the error.</p>\n<p>Moreover, we also cannot handle nested button rendering right now.. The UI can break at any time because of the above issues.</p>\n<p>So closing this issue right now and going with the default UI is good from my side. Please let me know your thoughts on this.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	conversationrooms	072ba95367fd-73ae-c1ff-6d2d397a500e	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N
