7f2037f36afd-68e3-838a-ebc5d9a8bf64	2026-11-18 10:10:07	2026-11-18 10:10:07	0	<p><strong>PR opened:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/projects4me/gaia/pull/277">gaia#277</a> (commit 4e6d6e95, based on d4498171).</p><p>Review fixes in this session (design and correctness reviewers):</p><ul><li>Search indexes are matched by name ({table}_{field}) and by access method and operator class. An index of another kind is dropped and rebuilt, and the check no longer skips a column that already has another index.</li><li>Vector columns: a column of the right type without a signature is adopted. A filled column with a different definition throws MigrationDriver instead of losing its embeddings.</li><li>createExtensions skips extensions that are already installed and treats a failing CREATE EXTENSION (no privilege) as skipped. syncSearchSchema checks the needed extensions before any DDL.</li><li>Tsvector sources are limited to text types (varchar, char, text, mediumtext, longtext), because ::text casts of dates and numbers are not immutable.</li><li>MySQL createExtensions ignores the list, so it raises no false warnings.</li></ul><p>Decisions: extensions are declared in config and skipped when unavailable, so the current postgres:16-alpine containers keep migrating. A definition change is detected by the sha1 signature in the column comment, not by parsing generation_expression.</p><p>Reviewer findings not taken: moving the extension list out of the driver into AdapterConfig, and a shared handler interface for the search hooks. Both refactor the existing driver/handler shape and can be follow-ups.</p><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><pre>api backend: 220 passed, 0 failed, 22 skipped\napi acl: 248 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped\napi client: 396 passed, 6 failed, 6 skipped\n  FAIL settings-patch-secure-value-is-masked  (known)\n  FAIL settings-get-secure-value-is-masked  (known)\n  FAIL settings-list-secure-value-is-masked  (known)\n  FAIL settings-patch-empty-secure-keeps-value  (kno