219efab86afd-af76-ac82-dae9c2f8483a	2026-11-18 12:12:17	2026-11-18 12:12:17	0	<p><strong>PR opened:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/projects4me/gaia/pull/278">gaia#278</a> (commit fa4e43eb, based on f1b8849f).</p><p><b>Decisions</b></p><ul><li>The columns are added in one place (SearchBlock::apply), which both metadata read paths call. They are not written into model files.</li><li>Type uniqueness is checked in SearchableRegistry and at the start of migrate, not per model.</li><li>fts and fuzzy take text fields only. semantic and exact take any declared non-system field. display.title is required and display.snippet is optional.</li><li>A fuzzy field that already has another index (for example unique) is rejected, because search indexes are keyed by field. Supporting unique plus trigram needs a second index key; that is a follow-up if needed.</li></ul><p><b>Review follow-ups (not done here)</b></p><ul><li>The search behaviour issue must make sure an ORM save of a searchable model does not overwrite searchSemanticHash, searchEmbedding or searchEmbeddingHash with stale or null values. This could be a skip list for those system columns or an explicit write path.</li><li>Design review suggested splitting SearchBlock into a validator and a column expander, moving TEXT_SOURCE_TYPES out of PostgresSearchDdl, injecting SEARCH_EMBED_MAX_CHARS instead of reading the env in SemanticText, sharing model discovery between Driver and SearchableRegistry::fromMetadata, and naming the migrate check assertUniqueTypes(). I left these for the reviewer to decide.</li><li>Possible dev-tools issue: `ai test gaia` runs a fixed list of phpunit folders, so tests in a new folder are silently skipped.</li><li>Possible decision record: Gaia owns the canonical semantic text and its hash.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><pre>api backend: 220 passed, 0 failed, 22 skipped\napi acl: 248 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped\napi client: 396 passed, 6 failed, 6 skipped\n  FAIL settings-patch-secure-v