030e43256afa-fa11-9afe-fd7646d9c1e5	2026-11-16 10:29:23	2026-11-16 10:29:23	0	<p><strong>Agent Odysseus needs your input</strong></p><p><strong>#4537 not shipped yet. Nothing is committed; the work is still uncommitted on branch <code>claude-issue-4537</code>.</strong></p>\n\n<h4>Why it stopped</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Full suite:</strong> backend 222/0. acl 252 passed, 1 failed. client 401 passed, 9 failed. PHPUnit has only the known ShortCode failures.\n<ul>\n<li>4 of the failures are new: <code>acl-members-docassist-ask-allowed</code>, <code>client-docassist-ask-returns-html</code>, <code>client-docassist-complete-returns-completion</code> and <code>client-docassist-review-returns-findings</code>.</li>\n<li>All 4 answer 502 because the running gaia-test container has no <code>LLM_STUB=true</code>, so Gaia calls the unreachable <code>ares:8000</code>.</li>\n<li>With the stub forced on, all 14 docassist cases passed.</li>\n<li><code>ai ship</code> needs a clean full run, so I can't ship as things stand.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong>Design review, blocker:</strong> the stub lives in production code. That covers <code>core/services/StubLLM.php</code>, the <code>ares.stubLlm</code> / <code>LLM_STUB</code> config, the switch in <code>ServiceFactory::create('llm')</code> and the <code>STUB_FAIL</code> marker. Production behaviour then depends on a test flag (rule: testing must not change what is under test). The correctness review adds that a deploy with <code>LLM_STUB=true</code> would quietly return fake AI answers with 200s.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>Question: how should the api-tester stub Ares?</h4>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>A fake Ares HTTP server (recommended).</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Add a small stub server under <code>tools/api-tester</code> that serves fixed <code>/docs/ask|complete|review</code> answers and fails on <code>STUB_FAIL</code>.</li>\n<li>Point <code>llmServiceUrl</code> at it in the test containers, and remove StubLLM, the flag and the factory switch from Gaia.</li>\n<li>Production code stays free of test code.</li>\n<li>It needs a dev-tools change: the testenv / compose override has to start the stub and set the URL for gaia-test and the slot containers. That would be a separate dev-tools issue, and this PR would depend on it.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong>Keep the in-process stub, but guard it.</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore <code>LLM_STUB</code> unless <code>debug</code> is on, and log loudly when it is active.</li>\n<li>It still needs a dev-tools issue so that <code>testenv.py</code> <code>GaiaTestContainer.env()</code> and the p4m compose override set <code>LLM_STUB=true</code>.</li>\n<li>It's the smaller change, but test code stays in production.</li>\n</ul></li>\n</ol>\n\n<h4>Other review findings I'll fix in the same rework, unless you say otherwise</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Authorization:</strong> <code>isModelActionAllowed('Doc','update')</code> is a role-level check. A members-scope user, or one whose doc is locked, passes it for any doc in the project.\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: authorize doc.update against the actual Doc, the way DocController does, and move that check into the controller.</li>\n<li>Add an api case for a member of project A posting project B's doc.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong>Input types:</strong> <code>docId</code> and <code>projectId</code> aren't type-checked, so an array value reaches <code>(string)</code> casts. They should get a 422.</li>\n<li><strong>Final save:</strong> a failed save after Ares answers comes back as a 422. It should be a 5xx.</li>\n<li><strong>Layering:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Pass the user id into <code>DocAssistant::assist()</code> instead of reading <code>global $currentUser</code>.</li>\n<li>Count the rate limit through the Docassist model instead of raw SQL.</li>\n<li>Merge the duplicated per-kind switches into a single place for each kind.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong>Tests:</strong> add PHPUnit tests for <code>LLM::postDocs</code> using a Guzzle MockHandler, and a DB-level rate-limit window test.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>One more finding I plan to leave as is: the reviewer suggested using the standard create flow instead of overriding <code>postAction</code>. I'll keep the override for the reason recorded in D-006: RestController builds the create response from the stored row, so it can't return the completion, which is never stored.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Proposed dev-tools issue (needed for either option):</strong> make the test containers reach a stubbed Ares, either through the fake server URL or through <code>LLM_STUB=true</code> in <code>testenv.py</code> and the compose override. Separately, <code>dev-tools/ai/lib/tests.py</code> <code>PHPUNIT_FOLDERS</code> leaves out <code>tests/libraries/docs</code>, as well as the existing conversations, workflows and query folders; it should run <code>tests/libraries</code> as a whole.</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	conversationrooms	447a14b76afa-8715-b3ee-74f36b3c3804	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	\N
