71b144096afa-af75-0d65-8dd9423bc84b	2026-11-16 00:04:01	2026-11-16 00:04:01	0	<p><strong>PR opened:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/projects4me/gaia/pull/271">gaia#271</a> (commit eb75f7ca, based on b3bea3ab).</p><p><b>Decisions</b></p><ul><li>Phalcon 4.1.2 makes Request::getMethod(), getURI() and getHeader() final and they read $_SERVER, so a request subclass that never reads superglobals is not possible. The runner overlays the superglobals during the call and restores them; SubRequest overrides only the body methods. Implementing RequestInterface by hand (about 50 methods, and Phalcon internals type-hint the concrete class) was turned down.</li><li><b>Security:</b> Phalcon's dispatcher keeps each controller as a shared DI instance and only calls initialize() (where RestController authorizes) on a new one. Without eviction a second sub-request to the same controller would skip authentication and ACL (confirmed on 4.1.2). The runner evicts the controller before each dispatch and puts any outer instance back afterwards.</li><li>The classes live in core/mvc/http (namespace Gaia\\Core\\MVC\\Http), on the presentation side, not core/libs, per the design review. OAuthRequestFactory depends on the OAuthRequestSource interface, not on SubRequest.</li></ul><p><b>Design review items not taken (follow-ups if wanted)</b></p><ul><li>One shared exception-to-response mapper for public/index.php and the runner: it means changing the entry point's error handling, so it is outside this issue. The runner's mapping mirrors index.php's non-debug output.</li><li>Splitting SubRequestScope into separate superglobal and DI-swap pieces: kept as one class whose single job is to save and restore the outer request state.</li></ul><p><b>Possible dev-tools issue:</b> ai test runs only fixed phpunit folders (libraries/security, utils, authorization, models, tools), so tests/api, tests/foundation and new tests/libraries/&lt;dir&gt; never run. That is why the test sits under tests/libraries/u