a882fec16ace-ac13-b866-e2e09b4a1ec1	2026-10-13 17:55:52	2026-10-13 17:55:52	0	<p><strong>Paused: depends on #3958.</strong> Findings from the investigation:</p><ul>\n<li>The ACL catalog is not a hand-written list. <code>AclMapCatalog::buildModuleActions()</code> derives resources from the REST routes in <code>core/config/routes.php</code> plus each controller's <code>$aclMap</code>. A <code>setting</code> resource only exists once a <code>setting</code> route and controller exist.</li>\n<li><code>RestController::authorize()</code> (private) calls <code>Acl::authorizeAction()</code> with the model alias, which reads the model's metadata (<code>getModelGroups()</code> &rarr; <code>getModelMeta()</code>). A controller without <code>app/metadata/model/Setting.php</code> fails on every request, so the model from #3958 must come first.</li>\n<li>Gaia's actions are <code>get/create/update/delete</code>, not <code>read</code>: the resources will be <code>setting.get</code> and <code>setting.update</code>.</li>\n<li>Once #3958 adds the route and controller (aclMap limited to get/update), <code>setting.get</code>/<code>setting.update</code> appear in the catalog and the Roles screen automatically. What remains for this issue: guard writes to system issue statuses/types (<code>system = 1</code>) with <code>setting.update</code> (no beforeUpdate/beforeDelete events exist, so the guard goes in IssuestatusController/IssuetypeController), plus acl catalog tests.</li>\n<li>Permissive mode allows <code>setting.*</code> for every role until denied: logged as #3968.</li></ul>\n<p>Branch <code>claude-issue-3957</code> had no commits and was removed; it will be recreated when work resumes.</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	conversationrooms	97036e316ace-f427-02fa-e5456929fe13	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	\N
