d0b221b16acf-ef96-084b-47169bb3928f	2026-10-14 21:19:12	2026-10-14 21:19:12	0	<p><strong>Implemented on <code>claude-issue-3959</code> (uncommitted, awaiting approval).</strong></p><ul>\n<li><strong>Resolution:</strong> <code>Gaia\\Libraries\\Utils\\SmtpSettings</code>. Each value comes from the <code>email</code> settings group if set, otherwise from <code>core/config/smtp.php</code>. Today that config means host smtp.gmail.com, port 587, STARTTLS, SMTP_USERNAME/SMTP_PASSWORD, sender name "Projects4me" and sender address = username. Blank counts as unset. The secure password is decrypted; if it can't be decrypted, the config value is used and a warning is logged. Settings are read on every send, so there is no restart.</li>\n<li><strong>Encryption setting:</strong> <code>tls</code> (STARTTLS, default), <code>ssl</code> or <code>none</code>; anything else falls back to tls.</li>\n<li><strong>One mailer factory:</strong> <code>Gaia\\Events\\Notification\\Mailer</code>, used by both <code>resetPassword()</code> and <code>emailPassword()</code>. The duplicated setup is gone.</li>\n<li><strong>Behaviour notes:</strong> removed <code>SMTPDebug = DEBUG_SERVER</code>, which echoed the SMTP conversation (including the AUTH exchange) into the HTTP response. A failed send is now logged instead of silently ignored; it still doesn't fail the user's request. The old <code>catch (Exception)</code> pointed at a non-existent class; it now catches <code>\\Exception</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Endpoint:</strong> <code>POST /api/v1/setting/testemail</code> with <code>{"recipient": "..."}</code> (JSON:API <code>data.attributes.recipient</code> also accepted). It requires setting.update (aclMap <code>testemail</code> → update). Responses: 200 when the server accepts the message, 422 for a bad recipient, 502 with the SMTP error otherwise. The timeout is 15s.</li>\n<li><strong>Routing:</strong> REST modules can now declare <code>'actions' =&gt; ['testemail' =&gt; ['POST']]</code>. App routes turned out to be broken (logged as #3973), so I didn't use them.</li>\n<li><strong>Tests:</strong> PHPUnit <code>SmtpSettingsTest</code> (9 cases: config fallback, settings win, blanks, sender default, encryption mapping, PHPMailer setup). api-tester: 8 client cases (recipient validation; host pointed at 127.0.0.1:1 so the SMTP failure is reported as 502; JSON:API body; restore) and 1 acl case (403 without setting.update). backend 120/120, acl 82/82, client 117/118 (known membership failure, #3970); PHPUnit security 58/58, utils 25/25.</li>\n<li><strong>Deviation from the issue:</strong> no stubbed mailer. The test containers have real Gmail credentials and no SMTP sink, so the API tests cover the failure path (unreachable host) and PHPUnit covers the configuration. A real successful send was not exercised.</li></ul>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	conversationrooms	cf5b1cd36acf-ef96-084b-f9d61a0930c2	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	\N
