7d9cb8566ad3-856e-f0f7-8fdb9562f497	2026-10-17 22:23:57	2026-10-17 22:23:57	0	<p><strong>Observation from Hammad (2026-10-18)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Live updates do work in general: when Agent Odysseus <em>created</em> an issue, the board said it had changed and offered a reload, and Hammad keeps receiving notifications.</li>\n<li>Only the <strong>status changes made by Talos/Odysseus</strong> are missing: <code>new</code> → <code>in_progress</code>, <code>in_progress</code> → <code>feedback</code> / <code>pending</code>. They produce no notification and the card doesn't move lane.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Likely root cause (investigated, not fixed):</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Talos and <code>dev-tools/ai</code> change status through the gaia MCP client, which PATCHes <strong>only <code>statusId</code></strong> (<code>dev-tools/gaia-mcp/server.py</code>, <code>_resolve_fields</code>). Prometheus sends both <code>status</code> and <code>statusId</code> (<code>board.js</code> ~445-447).</li>\n<li>The <code>status</code> name is then filled in by a Postgres trigger, <code>update_issue_status</code> (<code>BEFORE UPDATE ON issues</code>: <code>IF NEW."statusId" &lt;&gt; OLD."statusId" THEN NEW.status := (select name from issue_statuses where id = NEW."statusId")</code>). The stored row ends up correct, e.g. #3967 shows <code>pending</code>.</li>\n<li>But the trigger runs inside the database, <em>after</em> PHP has built the model audit. So for these updates the audit holds <code>statusId</code> and not <code>status</code>:\n<ul>\n<li><code>IssueNotification</code> only notifies when <code>audit['status']</code> changed (<code>IssueNotification.php:116</code>), so <strong>no notification</strong>.</li>\n<li><code>IssueLiveEventsComponent::publishStatusChanged</code> builds <code>changes</code> from the audit, so <code>issue.status.changed</code> carries <code>statusId</code> but no <code>status</code>. The board's <code>handleIssueStatusChanged</code> copies only what's in <code>changes</code>, and lanes group by <code>status</code>, so <strong>the card stays in its old lane</strong>.</li>\n</ul></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Fix options:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Gaia (proper fix, any client):</strong> resolve <code>status</code> from <code>statusId</code> in the model layer before save, so the audit, notifications and live events always carry both. The trigger then becomes redundant. That's a Gaia change, so it may need its own A Gaia issue.</li>\n<li><strong>Client workaround:</strong> make the gaia MCP client send <code>status</code> (the name) along with <code>statusId</code>, like Prometheus does. This is quick, but every other API client would hit the same gap.</li>\n<li><strong>Board (defensive):</strong> when an envelope has only <code>statusId</code>, look up the status name from the store before moving the card.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Recommendation: option 1, with option 3 as a guard. Option 2 only if notifications are needed before the Gaia change lands.</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	conversationrooms	7c1b45906ad3-856e-f0f7-33271f4ab0e9	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	\N
