8ab197f36ad6-9dbb-2554-482d3a060ca3	2026-10-19 17:55:22	2026-10-19 17:55:22	0	<p><strong>Goal:</strong> Let admins check their email settings by sending a test email, without saving the settings and without adding a new route or controller.</p>\n<p><strong>Approach:</strong> Reuse the existing save endpoint and add a <code data-backticks="1">test</code> flag. When the flag is set, the endpoint sends a test email using the submitted settings and doesn’t save anything.</p>\n<h4>Prometheus (frontend)</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Add a <strong>Test Settings</strong> button next to <strong>Save</strong> on the Email Settings page.</li>\n<li>Clicking it opens a modal that asks for a recipient email address. Check that the address is valid before allowing submit.</li>\n<li>On submit, send the current form values (saved or not) to the existing save endpoint, plus <code data-backticks="1">test: true</code> and the recipient address.</li>\n<li>Translate the status code that comes back and show the right success or error message in the modal.</li>\n</ol>\n<h4>Gaia (backend) (Create an issue for it)</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Change the email settings save function:\n<ul>\n<li><strong>No <code data-backticks="1">test</code> flag:</strong> works exactly as it does today.</li>\n<li><strong><code data-backticks="1">test: true</code>:</strong> use the submitted settings to send a test email to the given address. <strong>Don’t save the settings.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Return the result as a status or error code, for example <code data-backticks="1">TEST_EMAIL_SENT</code>, <code data-backticks="1">SMTP_AUTH_FAILED</code>, <code data-backticks="1">SMTP_CONNECTION_FAILED</code>, <code data-backticks="1">INVALID_RECIPIENT</code> or <code data-backticks="1">UNKNOWN_ERROR</code>. Return codes only, not display text; Prometheus handles the translation.</li>\n</ol>\n<h4>Acceptance criteria</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Test Settings never changes the stored settings.</li>\n<li>Save behaves the same as before.</li>\n<l