c4350c126ad6-cd3f-1ae6-f7c75228d8cf	2026-10-19 18:51:48	2026-10-19 18:51:48	0	<p><b>Done:</b> <code>PATCH /api/v1/setting</code> with <code>"test": true</code> sends a test email with the submitted email settings to <code>recipient</code> and saves nothing. Without the flag the save works exactly as before.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>SettingController::patchCollectionAction</b> is overridden: with no test flag it calls the parent. With the flag, <code>testEmailSettings()</code> runs the save's per-record checks (<code>authorizeRecordUpdate</code>, lookup by bound id) and accepts only rows in the <code>email</code> group. It never calls save(), opens no transaction and fires no rest:afterUpdate. It returns <code>{"testResult": CODE}</code> with 200, 422 or 502.</li>\n<li><b>SmtpSettings::loadWith / overlay</b>: values are taken from the submission first, then the saved setting, then the config. As on Save, a blank plain value clears the setting so the config applies, and a blank (or ciphertext) secure value keeps the saved password. Ciphertext sent by a client is never decrypted.</li>\n<li><b>TestEmailSender</b> (new): checks the recipient before connecting (INVALID_RECIPIENT), sends with <code>new Mailer(10, $smtp)</code> and maps failures to a code. Only UNKNOWN_ERROR logs the real PHPMailer error (it never includes the password).</li>\n<li><b>MailerErrorMapper</b> (new): maps PHPMailer messages to codes, matched against PHPMailer's own translations. authenticate → SMTP_AUTH_FAILED; connect_host / smtp_connect_failed → SMTP_CONNECTION_FAILED; anything else → UNKNOWN_ERROR.</li>\n<li><b>Mailer</b> now runs PHPMailer with exceptions on, caught inside send(), so callers still get bool + getError(). With exceptions off, PHPMailer reports every connect, TLS and auth failure as the same "SMTP connect() failed." text, so auth and connection failures could not be told apart. <code>SMTPDebug = 0</code> is now set explicitly.</li>\n<li><b>RestController</b>: <code>authorizeRecordUpdate</code> is now protected, and the inverted collection check on line 776 is fixed (<code>!isset || !is_array</code>). A save with no collection now returns 400 instead of "Data saved successfully".</li>\n<li><b>api-tester</b>: new <code>jsonEqual</code> assertion for top-level body keys (documented in the README). New client cases: INVALID_RECIPIENT (bad and missing recipient), SMTP_CONNECTION_FAILED (127.0.0.1:1), missing collection, unknown record, host and password rows unchanged (value and dateModified), save without the flag, save with no collection → 400. New acl case: test without setting.update → 403. In mail.json: TEST_EMAIL_SENT to Mailpit using only submitted values, after the suite has blanked the settings, and the saved row is unchanged afterwards.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Tests (this branch):</b> PHPUnit utils 51/51 and security 60/60. api-tester backend 120 passed / 12 skipped, acl 84 passed, client 125 passed / 6 skipped, mail 20 passed. The local stack's gaia-dev and gaia-test mount <code>D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Projects4Me/gaia</code>, not the Pr4M checkout. So I ran the suites in a throwaway container from the gaia-test image that mounted this branch (same env, pr4m_test, backend network) and removed the container afterwards.</p>\n<p><b>Not covered:</b> SMTP_AUTH_FAILED has no api-tester case because Mailpit runs with MP_SMTP_AUTH_ACCEPT_ANY. It is covered by PHPUnit: the mapper is tested against PHPMailer's real "authenticate" message, and the sender maps it.</p>\n<p><b>Design review notes, left as follow-ups:</b> (1) <code>SmtpSettings::overlay</code> restates the blank/secure rules of settingBehavior. A shared rule would stop the two from drifting apart. (2) Matching on message text depends on PHPMailer's default language. PHPMailer exceptions carry no specific class or code to use instead. (3) An empty collection with <code>test: true</code> tests the saved values plus the config, which seems useful, so I allowed it.</p>\n<p><b>Side effect for notifications:</b> with exceptions on, an invalid sender address (e.g. the gaia-test config username <code>api-tester</code>) now fails at setFrom with "Invalid address" instead of failing later at connect. It still fails open and is logged.</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	conversationrooms	c20c09936ad6-cd3f-1ae6-7ff791102f6a	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	\N
