pends on <code>issues.status</code>. So the column can't be widened just by editing the metadata.</p>\n<p>Options:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>(Recommended)</b> Validate issue status <code>name</code> to at most 12 characters on create and update, returning 422, in this PR. Then file a follow-up issue to widen <code>issues.status</code>: teach the Postgres migration sync to alter column length and handle the dependent view. This turns an obscure database error into a clear validation message, matches what the column can hold today, and keeps the migration-tool change out of this PR.</li>\n<li>Widen <code>issues.status</code> to 255 in this PR. That means extending <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> to alter column types and dealing with <code>user_latest_issues</code>. It's a bigger change to the migration tool.</li>\n<li>Ship the trigger as it is and file a follow-up. Until then, renaming an in-use status to more than 12 characters fails with a server error.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Reply with 1, 2 or 3 and I'll finish and ship.</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	conversationrooms	a37893056ad8-b698-0c8e-590b00d38a54	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	\N
