>\n  </ul></li>\n<li><code>IssueStatusLabels</code> stores the Translation rows at <code>views.app.issue.lists.status.&lt;value&gt;</code>:\n  <ul>\n  <li>it creates or updates rows, and restores a soft-deleted row because (locale, path) is unique;</li>\n  <li>deleting a status removes its labels only when no other live status uses the same value;</li>\n  <li>after the transaction it clears the written locales' cache files again, because the behavior's clear runs before the commit.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n<li><code>TransactionScope</code> handles begin, commit and rollback. <code>IssuestatusController</code> runs create, update and delete inside it, the same pattern <code>RoleController</code> uses. <code>IssuestatusComponent</code> saves and deletes the labels on afterCreate, afterUpdate and afterDelete; a failed label write throws and rolls the status back.</li>\n<li>Renames are rejected with 422 on PATCH and on the collection PATCH. The collection PATCH also rejects <code>translations</code>, since labels are saved one status at a time. Every status read returns <code>translations</code>.</li>\n<li>api-tester:\n  <ul>\n  <li>new <code>jsonPathEqual</code> and <code>jsonPathAbsent</code> assertions, so cases can check nested values in a response;</li>\n  <li>19 new client cases;</li>\n  <li>the existing rename cases now expect 422;</li>\n  <li>existing status creates now send labels;</li>\n  <li>the generator skips <code>name</code> for issuestatus PATCH cases, and <code>backend.json</code> was regenerated;</li>\n  <li>the ACL create-denied case sends labels so it still gets its 403.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n<li>Unit tests: <code>IssueStatusRulesTest</code>, and <code>TransactionScopeTest</code>, which includes the case where a failed label write rolls the status back.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Decision on <code>rename_issue_status</code>:</b> keep the trigger. Renames are now rejected, so it never fires. Removing it from the metadata wouldn't drop it from existing databases anyway, because <code>migrateTriggers</code> only creates triggers. Dropping it would need a separate migration, which isn't worth doing.</p>\n<p><b>Shared labels:</b> labels are keyed by the status value. A system status and its project copies, or the same custom value in two projects, therefore share one label per locale. Saving a label for any of them changes it for all of them. This is documented in <code>IssueStatusLabels</code> and the controller docblock.</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	conversationrooms	030613686adb-807d-fa92-7edfe01974e1	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	\N
