4fa998816ade-46a0-1142-fa412f828dea	2026-10-25 18:11:27	2026-10-25 18:11:27	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(85, 85, 85);" data-tomark-pass=""><strong>Cross-idea and cross-project reference.</strong>&nbsp;We cannot restrict the creation of issue cross-project, but we will have to manage how we created them and what we say in them. There are going to be cases where a complex project is being managed using multiple repos or multiple projects all within Projects4Me. Just like in our case where we have separate project for the frontend and a separate project for the backend. In such cases if a user is in the front-end project and the Agent Nestor has access to other projects (linked to each other, which we are assuming are being linked in the workspace/runtime, we will ask project layer or linking in prometheus and gaia later) then it should be able to determine if the implementation of the front end needs a new API so we cannot limit the cross-project awareness or issue creation. I understand that so far I have only mentioned the permissions of the Agent Nestor. What about the permission of the user. I don't think that we should stop the user from seeing if their idea resulted in the creation of an issue in a project that they were not a part of, but I understand that if we should them a link that they do not have access to then it can needlessly take them to a page showing permission denied, this can easily be handled by not show those issue references as links if the other does not have accesso the said project or issue.&nbsp;Also regarding creation of the issue cross-project. If the user was in the project for the front-end the Agent should of course create and issue for the front-end project as per normal, but if they need an API then it while creating an issue for the back-end project it must explicitly mention this is a request by another project and must be evaluated for implementation as a request.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(85, 85, 85);" data-tomark-pass="">I imagine that this will most probably have little impact for Gaia and has more to do with Dev-tools project, so I have created issues to handle this in 'A Dev Tools project', you just handle Gaia changes assuming that Agent Nestor and Prometheus are already doing their part.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Concurrent Plan versions</strong><br>\nGo for transactions, they are better</p>\n	1	1	conversationrooms	8b1885a16adc-c5ba-f6ec-f3e74294b2dc	Hammad Hassan	Hammad Hassan	\N
