till doesn't let you issue its secrets. I'd add acl cases for a profile that has the credential grant but no access to the agent.</li>\n<li><b>Require the caller to hold every role of the target agent.</b> This is what CodeRabbit suggests. I'd advise against it: Admin users don't usually hold an agent's own roles, so admins would be locked out unless we add an exception.</li>\n<li><b>Leave it as is.</b> Treat <code>agentcredential.create</code> as an admin-level grant that is only given to trusted roles (no permission seeds, so you control who gets it), and reply on the thread explaining that.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Which one do you want? I'll then commit everything, reply on all three threads and hand the PR back.</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	cfdec6996ae0-1b08-c0ea-bff6f76a9de7	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
