ba8d81316ae2-e00a-ad40-ccefa28b1241	2026-10-28 16:15:54	2026-10-28 16:15:54	0	<p><strong>Agent Achilles is blocked</strong></p><p><b>Blocked: Docker Desktop is not running</b>, so I can't run tests. Every <code>ai test gaia --changed</code> suite failed with "Docker daemon is not running", and the context pack couldn't reach the Docker API either. PHP isn't installed on the host, so the gaia-dev drift checks (<code>graph export --check</code>, <code>docs generate --check</code>, <code>check api-cases</code>) can't run either.</p>\n<p><b>To unblock:</b> start Docker Desktop and the local stack (<code>dev-tools/installer/p4m status</code>), then reassign the issue. The next run will migrate the local test DB, which adds the new columns, then run the tests, regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> and go to ship.</p>\n<p><b>Done so far</b> (uncommitted in the <code>claude-issue-4182</code> worktree), following your call that the expiry slides:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Oauthrefreshtoken</code> metadata gets two new columns: <code>rememberMe</code> (int, default 0) and <code>sessionExpires</code> (datetime). The migration only adds columns.</li>\n<li>New <code>core/libs/authorization/SessionExpiry.php</code> holds the window rule (<code>expiresAt(rememberMe)</code>, <code>isOpen()</code>). It also checks that the timeout is a number, which <code>TokenController</code> used to do.</li>\n<li>The OAuth storage (<code>core/libs/oauth2.0/storage/pdo.php</code>) overrides <code>setRefreshToken</code>, so each refresh token is written with its session window in the same INSERT.</li>\n<li><code>OAuthServer</code>: a password sign-in opens a window based on <code>remember_me</code>. A refresh checks the presented token's own <code>sessionExpires</code>, then opens a fresh window that keeps the token's Remember Me flag. That makes the expiry slide. Refresh tokens issued before this change fall back to <code>users.sessionExpires</code>.</li>\n<li><code>TokenController</code> no longer writes <code>users.sessionExpires</code>. The column stays, to be removed in a later change.</li>\n<li>Revoking a user still ends all of their sessions: their tokens are deleted and the inactive-account check still applies to refreshes.</li>\n<li>Tests:\n<ul>\n<li><code>TokenControllerTest</code> adds:\n<ul>\n<li>a Remember Me session that survives a later sign-in without Remember Me, then stops once its own window ends;</li>\n<li>the sliding window;</li>\n<li>the 1-day and 14-day windows;</li>\n<li>the fallback for older tokens.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li>New <code>tests/libraries/authorization/SessionExpiryTest.php</code>.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li>Recorded the decision as D-061 in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Left out: the optional grace window for a just-rotated token. That belongs with the aprom multi-tab refresh work.</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	18b878e66ae2-440d-ad45-2976c9f8f805	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
