2f34ba396ae2-ca37-925f-9d0f34c01e5e	2026-10-28 19:08:31	2026-10-28 19:08:31	0	<p><strong>PR opened:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/projects4me/gaia/pull/226">gaia#226</a> (commit 85f0ff8, based on c832ba2).</p><p><b>Decisions</b></p><ul><li>Refresh is a flag on the normal PATCH (the CRUD-only rule, following the #190 <code>test</code> flag), not a custom route or a refresh-run resource. If the refresh fails, the other fields in the same PATCH are already saved.</li><li>Only MCP servers over HTTP can be refreshed. stdio servers, built-ins and OpenAPI servers are entered with POST /tool.</li><li>Design review: endpoints are now limited to http/https URLs. The server lookup moved from the controller into ToolServerRefresher. A failure while recording refreshError no longer hides the original error. PUT is already 405 and collection DELETE is a no-op, so post, patch, patchCollection and delete cover every grant write (the same as agentcredential).</li><li>Known risk: refresh calls a URL set by an admin. Private hosts are allowed because local Ares and MCP servers are private. Restricting them is a follow-up.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><pre>api backend: 164 passed, 0 failed, 14 skipped\napi acl: 148 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped\napi client: 256 passed, 0 failed, 6 skipped\nphpunit tests/libraries/security: OK (104 tests, 260 assertions)\nphpunit tests/libraries/utils: OK (119 tests, 291 assertions)\nphpunit tests/tools: OK (178 tests, 899 assertions)\nRESULT: PASS</pre><p>Cost so far: 88.3k output tokens, 117 turns, peak context 176.1k, cache reads 11066.6k (2 sessions).</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	2d5a0ba56ae2-ca37-925f-18a5267fdd5b	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
8e383cf96ae3-72c1-c477-aedf4e5e28d2	2026-10-29 08:40:46	2026-10-29 08:40:46	0	<p><strong>Agent Achilles is blocked</strong></p><p><strong>Blocked: the local Postgres is down, so I could not run the tests for the gaia#226 review round.</strong></p>\n<p><code>ai test gaia --changed</code> failed before any test ran. Every slot reported <code>postgres is not running - `p4m up postgres` first</code>. No PHP is installed on the host, so I could not run even the unit test outside the containers.</p>\n<p><strong>What is done.</strong> These changes are in the run checkout on <code>claude-issue-4031</code>. Nothing is committed or pushed.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>core/libs/tools/McpToolLister.php</code>:\n  <ul>\n  <li>The refresh now stops with an error when the server sends the same <code>nextCursor</code> twice (CodeRabbit 4405016083).</li>\n  <li>Error messages no longer include the raw transport error or the server's JSON-RPC error text. Both go to <code>$logger</code> instead; the response and <code>refreshError</code> only get a generic message such as "The tool server could not be reached." This is the error-leak half of the SSRF finding (4405016099).</li>\n  <li>The <code>PROTOCOL_VERSION</code> docblock now explains the date format.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n<li><code>tests/libraries/tools/McpToolListerTest.php</code>: a new test for the repeated cursor, and the expected messages updated to the generic text.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Answers I will post on the threads:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>"why a date? should be v1, v2"</em> (4410196799): The MCP spec names its revisions by release date (<code>2025-06-18</code>, see modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/versioning). Servers compare that exact string in <code>initialize</code> and in the <code>MCP-Protocol-Version</code> header. If we sent <code>v1</code>, servers would refuse it or answer with a revision we don't support. So the value has to stay a date. I made the docblock say so.</li>\n<li><em>SSRF destination check</em> (4405016099): Internal MCP servers, such as Ares and other Docker hostnames, are the main use case, so a blanket block on private and loopback addresses would break them. Only users with <code>toolserver</code> update permission can change the endpoint. I suggest a follow-up issue for a configurable host allowlist and will propose it before creating it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>To unblock:</strong> start Postgres with <code>p4m up postgres</code> (or <code>p4m up</code>) and assign the issue back. The next run will run the tests, commit, push, reply to the three threads and hand the issue back to you.</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	2d5a0ba56ae2-ca37-925f-18a5267fdd5b	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
