bfc6a0556ae3-3e0f-c477-2283f7958cc5	2026-10-29 08:50:07	2026-10-29 08:50:07	0	<p><strong>Agent Achilles needs your input</strong></p><p><strong>Question on the protocol version (gaia#226, thread 4410196799).</strong></p>\n<p>You asked for <code>2026-10-29</code>. That is today's date, but the MCP spec has no revision with that name.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The value we send must be a published revision. The published revisions are <code>2024-11-05</code>, <code>2025-03-26</code>, <code>2025-06-18</code>, <code>2025-11-25</code> and <code>2026-07-28</code>; the current one is <code>2026-07-28</code> (modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/versioning).</li>\n<li>The spec says a server SHOULD answer <code>400 Bad Request</code> when the <code>MCP-Protocol-Version</code> header holds a version it doesn't support. So with <code>2026-10-29</code>, every refresh would likely fail.</li>\n<li><code>2026-07-28</code> is a breaking revision. It removes the <code>initialize</code>/<code>notifications/initialized</code> handshake and the <code>Mcp-Session-Id</code> header, and makes the protocol stateless: each request carries its version and capabilities. That is not a constant bump. It means a second transport path in <code>McpToolLister</code>, and most servers in the field still speak the 2025 revisions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Options:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Recommended: keep the handshake and move to <code>2025-11-25</code></strong>, the newest revision that still uses <code>initialize</code>. Gaia would also send the version the server agrees to in the initialize result on later requests, so older servers keep working. This is a small change and fits this PR.</li>\n<li>Support <code>2026-07-28</code> as well: try the stateless revision first and fall back to the handshake for older servers. This is the right long-term move, but it is a transport rewrite. I suggest a follow-up issue in Claude-v1, which I would propose before creating it.</li>\n<li>Set the literal <code>2026-10-29</code> as asked. I advise against it, because conforming servers would reject it.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Status of the other two threads.</strong> Both fixes are made and pass <code>ai test gaia --changed</code> (api 84 passed; phpunit security, utils and tools OK). Nothing is committed yet; I will commit, push and reply to all three threads in one go after your answer.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Repeated <code>nextCursor</code> is now rejected (4405016083).</li>\n<li>Refresh errors are generic, and the raw transport and JSON-RPC errors go to the server log (4405016099). The SSRF destination allowlist would be a proposed follow-up.</li>\n</ul>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	2d5a0ba56ae2-ca37-925f-18a5267fdd5b	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
