907f92426ae3-d76c-0745-3332a10d8f97	2026-10-29 22:07:12	2026-10-29 22:07:12	0	<p><strong>PR opened:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/projects4me/gaia/pull/231">gaia#231</a> (commit 45def24, based on ec0e174).</p><p><b>Assumptions / decisions</b></p><ol>\n<li>Graph validation is split by when each rule can hold. Each node and edge save checks its own part (kind, config, port, single trigger, no loop). The whole-graph rules (exactly one trigger, every port connected or ended, every node reached) are checked when a workflow becomes Active, because a draft is incomplete while it is built with separate REST calls. Turned down: saving the whole graph in one nested PATCH, which isn't standard CRUD.</li>\n<li>An Active workflow's graph is read-only: creating, changing or deleting a node or edge returns 422 until the workflow is set to Draft or Disabled. Moving or renaming a node is still allowed.</li>\n<li>version starts at 0 and counts activations (each Draft/Disabled &rarr; Active). Clients cannot write it; a new workflow cannot be created as Active.</li>\n<li>"Explicitly ended" means an edge to an <code>end</code> action node.</li>\n<li>An empty scope means every project. Scope is stored as JSON text, not a join table.</li>\n<li>ACL: workflow.* resources only, no project grouping. No permission seed SQL is shipped.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><b>Design review follow-ups (not blocking, not done here)</b></p><ul>\n<li>Deleting a workflow removes its references but leaves its nodes and edges live. A cascade needs a decision, because node deletes are blocked while a workflow is Active.</li>\n<li>Workflow::save and Workflownode::save repeat the "join the caller's transaction or open one" block; it could move to a shared helper.</li>\n<li>LiveRecords hard-codes which models use a smallint <code>deleted</code>.</li>\n<li>Concurrency: the single-trigger and one-edge-per-port checks read before they write; activation re-checks the whole graph. Locking the workflow row is a possible follow-up.</li>\n<li>Possible dev-tools issue: <code>gaia-dev scaffold resource --acl</code> writes permission ids longer than 36 characters for long names (Workflowreference); <code>--parent</code> supports only Project.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Known failure outside this branch: tests/models/behaviors/ShortCodeBehaviorTest (6 failures, untouched, not in the full run).</p><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><pre>api backend: 197 passed, 0 failed, 15 skipped\napi acl: 158 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped\napi client: 284 passed, 0 failed, 6 skipped\nphpunit tests/libraries/security: OK (119 tests, 306 assertions)\nphpunit tests/libraries/utils: OK (119 tests, 291 assertions)\ntests/services: not in this checkout, skipped\nphpunit tests/tools: OK (178 tests, 944 assertions)\nRESULT: PASS</pre><p>Cost so far: 6.2k output tokens, 8 turns, peak context 40.7k, cache reads 255.6k (1 session).</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	8e63ab596ae3-d76c-0745-280ecb238f65	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
