3ea97ed76ae8-59cb-56d8-4b771212d94d	2026-11-02 09:56:14	2026-11-02 09:56:14	0	<p><strong>PR opened:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/projects4me/prometheus/pull/602">prometheus#602</a> (commit ad20d8aa, based on 8700a168).</p><p><b>Decisions:</b> draft + Apply as in the mockup (live edits rejected: rows would mutate shared node.config and the unsaved-change check could not track it); the draft is a deep copy; field help uses the info icon on FormFields::Label; new related-fields option renderer <code>relate-actor</code> for user pictures / agent avatars / expressions (selects stay FormFields::FieldRelate); catalog data loads through the routes and the service, components never call the store.</p><p><b>Design review:</b> moved the actor-path heuristic out of the component into <code>node-config.actorPaths</code> with a unit test; the catalog service now caches only the trigger catalog and reloads agents on each editor open. Not changed: users come from the app controller's usersList (same as the agent create page); updateNode clears the step's errors on Apply (they refresh on the next save) and drops edges from removed switch cases without a warning (possible follow-up).</p><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><pre>ember: pass 752, fail 0\nRESULT: PASS</pre><p>Size: 28 hand-written file(s). Why it is this large: One feature: the per-kind step form. Glimmer components are co-located .hbs+.js pairs (7 components = 14 files); the rest are the model, service, util, Mirage handler, translations and tests that the form needs to work and be tested. Splitting would ship a form with no settings or fields with no form.</p><p>Cost so far: 67.1k output tokens, 103 turns, peak context 137.6k, cache reads 7288.8k (3 sessions).</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	6d4188b86ae6-9a84-5224-2897aa5e3e62	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
d081f1d56ae8-59cb-56d8-4b67ff577e01	2026-11-02 09:58:40	2026-11-02 09:58:40	0	<p><strong>Agent Achilles needs your input</strong></p><p><b>Design for approval: list toolbar mass update and export (Agents and Workflows)</b></p>\n<p>The issue asks for the design to be approved in a comment before I build it. I have written no code yet.</p>\n\n<p><b>What already exists (the code differs from the issue text)</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The issue list (<code>app/templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs</code>) already has mass update and export buttons. Both open <code>bootstrap-modal</code> dialogs. The base <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code> has <code>showExportDialog</code>, <code>exportModules</code>, <code>prepareOptionsForExport</code> and <code>showMassUpdateDialog</code>. The issue's own <code>massUpdateIssue</code> saves each selected record through the standard PATCH. So there is already a pattern, but it is hard-wired to issues: the fields are fixed in the template and the strings say "issues".</li>\n<li>Gaia already exports CSV for <b>any</b> module through the standard list endpoint: <code>GET /api/v1/&lt;module&gt;?export=true&amp;ids=…</code>, or <code>selectAll=true&amp;query=…</code> (<code>RestController::updateParamsForExport</code> / <code>exportData</code>). It returns a <code>download_url</code>. No Gaia change is needed.</li>\n<li>Problems in the current base code: <code>exportModules</code> uses raw <code>fetch()</code>, which our rules forbid because it skips token refresh. It also always sends <code>projectId: this.trackedProject.id</code>, which doesn't apply to Agents and Workflows because they are admin lists outside any project.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><b>Proposed design</b> (keeps the issue list working; Agents and Workflows use the new pieces)</p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Field config (data/metadata):</b> each module declares which fields can be mass-updated, in <code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>, as <code>massUpdate: [{ field, label, type: 'enum'|'string'|'number', options }]</code>.\n  <ul><li>Agents: <code>accountStatus</code> (active/suspended…), <code>permissionMode</code>, <code>maxTurns</code>, <code>maxRunsPerIssue</code>.</li>\n  <li>Workflows: <code>status</code> (Draft/Active/…), <code>scope</code>.</li></ul>\n  Names, emails, prompts and sponsor are left out on purpose, because they are per-record.</li>\n<li><b><code>List::MassUpdateDialog</code></b> (Glimmer component, presentation only): a <code>bootstrap-modal</code> containing a <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> (relate-simple) to pick the field, then a value input chosen by type (<code>FieldRelate</code> for enums, <code>FieldText</code> for text and numbers). It shows "N selected". On Save it calls <code>@onSave(field, value)</code>. It never touches the store.</li>\n<li><b><code>List::ExportDialog</code></b> (Glimmer component, presentation only): a <code>bootstrap-modal</code> that says what will be exported ("N selected rows" or "all rows matching the current search"). On Export it calls <code>@onExport()</code>.</li>\n<li><b>Application logic in the base list controller</b> (generalised, not per module):\n  <ul><li><code>massUpdate(field, value)</code>: for each selected id, <code>peekRecord</code>, set the field and <code>save()</code> (standard PATCH, one record at a time). Messenger shows progress, then a result like "8 updated, 1 failed". Failed records are rolled back.</li>\n  <li><code>exportList()</code>: builds the options and calls the module's adapter (<code>adapterFor(module).ajax</code>) instead of raw <code>fetch</code>, then triggers the <code>download_url</code>. <code>projectId</code> is sent only when the list is project-scoped.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Toolbar:</b> on the Agents and Workflows lists, two buttons are added to the existing <code>list-controls</code> btn-group next to delete: <code>fa-pencil</code> (mass update, ACL <code>&lt;module&gt;.update</code>) and <code>fa-download</code> (export, ACL <code>&lt;module&gt;.read</code>). These are the same buttons and icons as the issue list.</li>\n<li>Tests: Mirage handlers for <code>export=true</code> on agent and workflow, plus Gherkin acceptance scenarios for "mass update the status of selected rows" and "export the selected rows / the current search".</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p><b>Decisions needed</b></p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Export with nothing selected and no search.</b> The issue says to "export the current search when none are selected". Gaia rejects <code>selectAll</code> with an empty query ("Search query is required for exporting all records"), and today's UI shows an error in that case.\n  <br>Options: (a) keep that rule: with no rows selected you need an active search, otherwise you see a message asking you to select rows or search; (b) send a match-all query so the whole list is exported.\n  <br><b>Recommended: (a).</b> It matches Gaia's rule and avoids unbounded exports.</li>\n<li><b>Scope of the refactor.</b> (a) Move the issue list onto the new dialogs and the generalised controller methods in this PR, so that only one pattern remains; or (b) leave the issue list as it is (apart from fixing the shared <code>exportModules</code> to go through the adapter) and log a follow-up to migrate it.\n  <br><b>Recommended: (b).</b> It keeps this PR to Agents and Workflows and limits the risk to the issue list.</li>\n<li><b>The mass-update field lists above</b>: confirm them, or tell me what to add or remove.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Reply with approval or changes and I'll build it on <code>claude-issue-4243</code>.</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	201682886ae8-59cb-56d8-210c05ebab86	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
