ts for a lock shared with other tabs (<code>navigator.locks.request</code> in <code>app/services/session.js</code>, <code>_withCrossTabLock</code>).</li>\n<li>If another tab holds that lock and never lets go, <code>save()</code> waits forever. No request, no error, no toast.</li>\n<li><code>isSaving</code> and the Save button's <code>disabled</code> then stay true, so every later click does nothing too.</li>\n<li>Mirage never reaches this code, because the test session has no <code>expires_at</code> or <code>refresh_token</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Checks, in the broken tab right after clicking Save:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Is the Save button disabled (<code>[data-workflow-save]</code> has <code>disabled</code>)?</li>\n<li>In the console: <code>owner = require('prometheus/app').default ? null : null</code>. If you use the Ember Inspector instead, check <code>controller:app.workflow.page</code> → <code>isSaving</code>, and <code>service:session</code> → <code>_inFlightRefresh</code>.</li>\n<li>Does it still happen with all other Prometheus tabs closed? Does saving another kind of step (Notify, Filter) work in the same tab?</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Options:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A (recommended):</strong> you run the checks above and reply. If it is the refresh hang, I'll open a separate issue for <code>session.js</code> (a timeout on the lock wait and on the token request). In this issue I'd then make a save that never finishes visible: a timeout toast through errorManager, and <code>isSaving</code> reset so Save can be clicked again. I'd also commit the three new scenarios.</li>\n<li><strong>B:</strong> I ship only the hardening without a confirmed cause: the save timeout toast, the new scenarios, and a test for the error display. That doesn't meet "start with a failing test".</li>\n<li><strong>C:</strong> you share the exact steps or the workflow id where it happens (Draft or Active, new or edited step, which settings were filled), and I reproduce from