51c47d666aee-03cb-55c5-1b93953036d9	2026-11-06 22:14:41	2026-11-06 22:14:41	0	<p><strong>PR opened:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/projects4me/prometheus/pull/628">prometheus#628</a> (commit 1bcf8073, based on 506ab976).</p><p>Decisions:</p><ul><li>A condition's operator is its registry key (the Gaia symbol, or IN / NOT IN). IN and NOT IN are written as <code>CONTAINS 'a','b'</code> and <code>!CONTAINS 'a','b'</code>; a single value is written with <code>:</code> or <code>!:</code>.</li><li>normalize keeps the root a group, so a single condition serializes as <code>((Issue.x : y))</code>, like existing app queries.</li><li>BETWEEN bounds are written unquoted: Clause.php explodes the value on ' AND ' and only trims the outer quotes, so quoting each bound would break the range.</li><li>Refused input is reported as {code, params, nodeId} and that condition is left out; the rest of the query is still returned. Refused: ( ) ' and uppercase NULL/EMPTY in any value (Clause.php matches these as substrings), ' AND ' inside a range bound, and fields that aren't a plain Module.field path (added after the design review, since Clause.php splits on spaces).</li><li>Nullary operators are written as <code>(Field NULL)</code>.</li><li>Fields take an optional translated label; only label and aliases are used in resolution. An ambiguous field prefix falls back to a text field.</li><li>Default operator: CONTAINS for text, : for other types.</li></ul><p>Follow-up: relax the refusals once the agaia Clause.php fixes land. Lint not run (no node_modules in the run worktree).</p><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><pre>ember: pass 866, fail 0\nRESULT: PASS</pre><p>Size: 11 hand-written file(s), estimated 10</p><p>Cost so far: 42.7k output tokens, 48 turns, peak context 80.6k, cache reads 2282.5k (2 sessions).</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	4ef163156aee-a7e9-ca02-76c25a6aa71d	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
