cc9517286aee-9f5b-6251-c79a77bd0b0e	2026-11-07 08:01:16	2026-11-07 08:01:16	0	<p><b>Cause confirmed.</b> A new integration test (<code>tests/integration/modifiers/render-markdown-test.js</code>) renders a body with <code>![shot.png](upload:42)</code> against Mirage, using the real <code>upload-preview</code> service and store, with no stub. On dev the modifier never settles and the test browser crashes ("Browser exited unexpectedly") during that test. <code>didReceiveArguments</code> ran the lookup synchronously inside the modifier's tracking frame. <code>store.query('upload', …)</code> read store state there, and when the query resolved it changed that state. The modifier re-ran, which minted a new token and called <code>setMarkdown</code> again, and the cycle repeated.</p>\n<p><b>Fix (app/modifiers/render-markdown.js):</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>didReceiveArguments</code> reads only the positional argument. It does nothing when the markdown equals the one already shown.</li>\n<li>The address lookup starts after <code>await Promise.resolve()</code>, outside the tracking frame.</li>\n<li>Resolved addresses are kept per upload id for the modifier's lifetime. A later run with the same image draws it straight from the kept address, with no new token. Lookups already in progress are shared, so an upload is never looked up twice at the same time.</li>\n<li>Unchanged behaviour: the name shows first, an unreadable upload stays as its name, a click opens the full size with a fresh token, only the current markdown is redrawn, and the maps are cleared on <code>willRemove</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Other screens:</b> the composer shows pasted images from the local file and does no lookup. The create page's first message renders through <code>Idea::MessageItem</code>, so it now uses the fixed modifier.</p>\n<p><b>Possible follow-up:</b> <code>idea/message-screen.js</code> also calls <code>previewUrl</code> from its constructor during render. It is not looping today, but it uses the same pattern.</p>\n<p><b>Tests:</b> the new modifier tests check that the image is requested once and drawn once, that re-running the same image doesn't request a new token, and that an unreadable upload stays as its name. The modifier tests and the idea component tests pass (49 of 49).</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	3f7313b66aee-8d2e-aab0-2126c765194f	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
