c023fbf36af0-c789-00cd-f1ed7d9488ff	2026-11-08 15:05:36	2026-11-08 15:05:36	0	<p><strong>Agent Achilles needs your input</strong></p><p><strong>Question before I build #4360: <code>limit + 1</code> conflicts with how Gaia turns <code>page</code> into an offset.</strong></p>\n<p>Gaia's list endpoints compute <code>offset = (page - 1) * limit</code> from the <code>limit</code> they receive (<code>gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php</code>, lines ~598 and ~658). If Prometheus sends <code>limit=21&amp;page=2</code>, the offset is 21, not 20. Row 21 (index 20) is never shown on any page, and page 3 skips two rows, and so on. The issue's acceptance case (<code>limit=21</code>, page 1 shows 20 and page 2 shows 21-25) only works if page 2 starts at row 21. With 25 ideas, page 2 would show 4 rows (22-25) instead of 5.</p>\n<p>Mirage can't expose this, because the issue asks it to honour <code>limit</code> as sent. A test against Mirage would pass while real Gaia drops rows.</p>\n<p><strong>Options</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Send an explicit offset.</strong> Prometheus sends <code>limit=21</code> plus an offset of <code>(page-1)*20</code>, if Gaia's list endpoints accept an <code>offset</code> param. I did not find one on the REST list path, only the computed offset. This needs a Gaia issue to accept <code>offset</code>, and the Mirage handler would honour it too.</li>\n<li><strong>Add a Gaia option.</strong> Gaia computes the offset from a separate page size, for example a <code>pageSize</code> param (offset = (page-1)*pageSize, rows = limit). Same cross-repo change, but it keeps the page/limit vocabulary.</li>\n<li><strong>Make Gaia peek ahead.</strong> The Gaia list endpoint fetches limit + 1 internally and reports <code>meta.hasNext</code>. Prometheus never changes its request. This moves the decision into Gaia, which contradicts the recorded decision that Prometheus asks for N + 1.</li>\n<li><strong>Keep limit + 1 as written</strong> and accept the skipped rows. I don't recommend it, because it silently hides data.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Recommendation:</strong> option 1 if Gaia can take an <code>offset</code> param (or option 2 if you prefer to keep page numbers). Open a Gaia issue for it, then I build the Prometheus side (helper, pagination, idea browser, decisions doc, Mirage, tests) against it. The decision doc should record the offset rule next to limit + 1.</p>\n<p>Everything else in the issue is clear, and I can proceed as scoped once you pick an option.</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	5d6283296af0-c789-00cd-52e84fd876b5	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
