7c6d5d406af0-e923-00cd-9be67e710a2d	2026-11-08 15:13:00	2026-11-08 15:13:00	0	<p><strong>Agent Achilles needs your input</strong></p><p><strong>How the Issue list and Project list page today (investigation only; I have changed nothing)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Both lists use the same mechanism.</strong> <code>routes/app/project/issue/index.js</code> and <code>routes/app/projects/index.js</code> query with <code>page</code> only and send no <code>limit</code>, so Gaia's default of 20 applies. Their templates (<code>templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs</code> and <code>templates/app/projects/index.hbs</code>) show <code>‹</code> and <code>›</code> buttons that read <code>model.meta.links.prev.href</code> and <code>model.meta.links.next.href</code>, and <code>get-page</code> extracts the page number from the link. The range text is <code>from-to / to</code>, computed from <code>(page-1)*20 + model.length</code>, so it shows no total. The total is never used.</p>\n<p><strong>Gaia already does the "one extra row" trick, server-side.</strong> In <code>gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php</code> (list handler, ~lines 650-680 and 1060-1120) it does:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>reads <code>limit</code> (default 20) and computes <code>offset = (page-1) * limit</code> from that original limit;</li>\n<li>then runs <code>$limit++</code> and queries for limit + 1 rows;</li>\n<li>if the extra row came back, it removes it from the response and leaves <code>endPage = false</code>;</li>\n<li>it adds <code>meta.links.next</code> only when <code>endPage</code> is false, and <code>meta.links.prev</code> only when <code>page &gt; 1</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>So the rule in the issue, "ask for N + 1; if N + 1 come back there is a next page", is already implemented in Gaia, and Gaia hides the extra row from the client. Gaia applies the offset to the original limit before the increment, so page boundaries stay exact.</p>\n<p><strong>Why the idea browser shows no pagination.</strong> It is the only list that ignores <code>meta.links.next</code>. It passes <code>@total</code> and tries to count loaded ideas, which never exceeds 20. The data to page is already in the response.</p>\n<p><strong>Consequence for this issue's plan.</strong> If Prometheus also sent <code>limit + 1</code> (21), Gaia would compute offset = (page-1)*21 and return 22 rows, trimmed to 21. That is the row-skipping problem I raised earlier, and Prometheus would also get one row too many. Prometheus shouldn't send <code>limit + 1</code> at all.</p>\n<p><strong>Proposed revised plan (no Gaia change needed), awaiting your go-ahead:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Idea browser keeps <code>limit=20</code>. The route/controller derives <code>hasNext</code> from <code>ideas.meta.links.next</code> (and <code>page &gt; 1</code> for prev). Drop the total fallback and the paging count queries.</li>\n<li><code>QuickList</code> and <code>QuickList::Pagination</code>: new <code>@hasNext</code>, optional <code>@total</code>, with the <code>1-20 / 20+</code> and <code>21-25 / 25</code> text and the button and hide rules from the issue. This part is unchanged.</li>\n<li>The helper becomes a tiny pure function, for example <code>hasNextPage(meta)</code> in <code>app/utils/quick-list/page-window.js</code>, with unit tests, in place of <code>requestLimit</code> and <code>pageWindow</code>.</li>\n<li>Mirage idea handler: slice at the sent limit (as today) and set <code>meta.links.next</code> when more rows exist, mirroring Gaia.</li>\n<li>Decision doc <code>docs/architecture/lists/decisions.md</code> records: no totals or count queries, Gaia fetches limit + 1 and exposes <code>meta.links.next</code>, use the helper. The "request limit + 1 from Prometheus" wording changes, because Gaia already does that.</li>\n<li>Acceptance test: with 25 ideas the request carries <code>limit=20</code> (not 21), page 1 shows <code>1-20 / 20+</code> with › enabled, page 2 shows <code>21-25 / 25</code> with › disabled.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I'll start only when you say go, and say so if you want the original <code>limit=21</code> plan instead.</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	5d6283296af0-c789-00cd-52e84fd876b5	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
