6f23cfc36af0-5657-eda5-e70fc8c1222e	2026-11-08 22:27:59	2026-11-08 22:27:59	0	<p><strong>PR opened:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/projects4me/gaia/pull/252">gaia#252</a> (commit dfc38df5, based on b5fad6df).</p><p><b>Decisions to review</b></p><ul><li>Read only: metadata may list any action, but only <code>get</code> is honoured. The write behaviours (createdUser, modifiedUser, audit) stamp a user, and a service has none. Opening writes needs a decision on whose name the write is stamped with (follow-up). The issue says "which actions", so this may need discussion.</li><li>All service denials are 401, as the issue asks, including field, clause and record-filter denials.</li><li>Authorization groups must also be opted in for services (e.g. Issue needs Project open to services). This keeps deny-by-default.</li><li>The record filter is a PHQL condition in metadata (<code>acl.service.filter</code>), like <code>assignment.condition</code>, rather than a PHP class hook. It is trusted metadata.</li><li>lastUsedAt is stamped on every service request (a bound UPDATE that bypasses audit).</li></ul><p><b>Behaviour with no current user</b>: currentUserBehavior (Permission, Project, User) sets an empty gaia.current_user_id; trackLastActivity is skipped; CSV export is refused; LiveEventEnvelope already sends no actor; createdUser/modifiedUser/audit are never reached because writes are closed; getAction 'me' on User can't be reached (User is not opted in).</p><p><b>Design-review findings left open (should-fix, not blocking)</b>: move the export refusal into ServiceAcl/authorize so it runs before the query; ServiceAcl relies on every Acl entry point going through the overridden hooks, so consider an ACL interface or a test that walks every public Acl method; isResourceAllowed maps module to model with ucfirst instead of the Acl module mapping; nits: fold the guard and recordUse into one domain method, an isServiceToken() helper, AND-combine aclWhere, use <code>?ServiceAccess