d77e66116af0-4df0-9303-d9a7ed510ec5	2026-11-08 22:33:59	2026-11-08 22:33:59	0	<p><strong>Agent Achilles: escalating to opus</strong></p><p>No code written. #4389 crosses a contract and needs a migration, and I'm not confident enough to settle the design on Sonnet.</p>\n<p><b>Open design points, from reading #4386 (<code>ServiceAccess</code>, <code>ServiceAcl</code>, <code>RestController::setServiceClient</code>) and <code>serviceClientBehavior</code>:</b></p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Writes are closed to services today.</b> <code>ServiceAccess::ACTIONS = ['get']</code>, and its doc comment says writes are excluded because a service request has no current user. The <code>createdUser</code>, <code>modifiedUser</code> and <code>audit</code> behaviors stamp a user. Opting PATCH in means adding <code>update</code> to <code>ACTIONS</code> and making those behaviors cope with a null user.</li>\n<li><b>"Own record only" can't be expressed yet.</b> <code>acl.service.filter</code> is a static PHQL string with no way to refer to the calling client. <code>ServiceAcl</code> would need a token-bound placeholder (for example the client's <code>clientId</code>).</li>\n<li><b>Grace period needs storage.</b> The old secret must stay valid for 10 minutes. The secret is hashed in the <code>oauth_clients</code> row, so this means new columns or a table (a migration). <code>ClientCredentialsGrant</code> or <code>OAuthServer</code> would then have to check the previous hash until it expires.</li>\n<li><b>Scopes and PATCH rules.</b> <code>serviceclient.rotate</code> must be added to every kind's defaults in <code>config/serviceclients.php</code>. Existing clients keep their stored scopes and would need a backfill. <code>ServiceclientController::PATCHABLE</code> currently allows only <code>id</code> and <code>status</code>. <code>rotateSecret</code> is a virtual field, and the response must show the new secret once.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><b>Recommendation:</b> rerun on Opus. Use a token-bound <code>{clientId}</code> placeholder in the service filter. Keep the rotation logic in a dedicated library, for example <code>ServiceClients::rotateSecret</code>, called from the behavior or controller. Store the previous secret hash and its expiry on the <code>oauth_clients</code> row. If Opus finds the migration or the ACL contract change too large, split this into two issues: (a) service write access for PATCH with an own-record filter, then (b) rotation and grace period.</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	7d3d1be76af0-4df0-9303-2e45fbe0ed8e	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
