9d3b5a086af1-601c-e3a5-74a09d4d1899	2026-11-09 00:23:57	2026-11-09 00:23:57	0	<p><strong>PR opened:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/projects4me/dev-tools/pull/131">dev-tools#131</a> (commit 7010f0b, based on a5d5770).</p><p><b>Gap on the Gaia side:</b> rotation uses PATCH /serviceclient/{id} with the Serviceclient record id, but the enrollment delivery returns only clientId and clientSecret, and a service's ACL cannot read /serviceclient. Talos reads an optional <code>serviceClientId</code> from the delivery; when missing it logs once and keeps its secret instead of rotating.</p><p><b>Proposed follow-up (not created; awaiting approval):</b> A Gaia issue, complexity simple: ServiceEnrollments::poll already sets <code>$enrollment-&gt;serviceclientId</code>; return it as the <code>serviceClientId</code> attribute on delivery next to clientId/clientSecret, with an api-tester case and a docs/architecture/rbac D-066 note.</p><p><b>Decisions:</b> enrollment on talos run runs in a background thread (nothing uses the token yet); client name "Talos on &lt;hostname&gt;", kind runtime; rotation 7 days after issuedAt, checked hourly; credential file stores gaiaUrl so another Gaia triggers re-enrollment; reused gaia-mcp's Gaia rather than a separate transport. If the credential file can't be restricted it is still kept (delivered once) with a warning.</p><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><pre>unittest talos: ran 832, OK; ai: ran 204, OK; installer: ran 91, OK; nestor: ran 5, OK; sim: ran 8, OK; gaia-mcp: ran 84, OK\nRESULT: PASS</pre><p>Size: 11 hand-written file(s), estimated 9</p><p>Cost so far: 52.4k output tokens, 56 turns, peak context 132.5k, cache reads 4309.5k (2 sessions).</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	9ee45c966af1-64a9-1bb8-539f949f076a	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
