0215ee336afa-e643-b3db-f5ec1a822f0c	2026-11-16 11:03:30	2026-11-16 11:03:30	0	<p><strong>Agent Odysseus is blocked</strong></p><p><strong>#4537 now uses option 1, a fake Ares HTTP server, and is ready apart from the test environment.</strong> Nothing is committed; the work is on branch <code>claude-issue-4537</code>.</p>\n\n<h4>What changed this run</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The test switch is gone from Gaia.</strong> I removed <code>StubLLM</code>, <code>ares.stubLlm</code>/<code>LLM_STUB</code> and the <code>ServiceFactory</code> switch.\n<ul>\n<li>The fake server is <code>tools/api-tester/fake-ares/</code> (<code>FakeAres.php</code> plus a <code>router.php</code> for <code>php -S</code>). It gives the same fixed answers as the stub did, and a 500 for a request containing <code>STUB_FAIL</code>.</li>\n<li><code>docker-compose.yaml</code> has a new <code>fake-ares</code> service (image <code>rananoman/gaia:env-dev</code>, <code>php -S 0.0.0.0:8000</code>). <code>gaia-test</code> and <code>gaia-test-hermes-down</code> get <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL: http://fake-ares:8000</code> and depend on it.</li>\n<li>On the host, the fake server answered <code>/docs/ask</code> and returned 500 for <code>STUB_FAIL</code>.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong>Review findings fixed:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>The doc.update check moved to <code>DocassistController</code>. It now checks <code>isModelActionAllowed('Doc','update')</code> plus <code>assertRecordIdInScope('Doc', docId)</code>, as a doc update would.</li>\n<li>Asking for AI help on a locked doc is now a 422 (D-005).</li>\n<li>A <code>docId</code> or <code>projectId</code> that isn't a string is a 422.</li>\n<li>Each kind is now a <code>DocAssistKind</code> strategy (Ask, Complete, Review) listed in <code>DocAssistKinds</code>, which the behaviour also uses.</li>\n<li>The rate-limit count goes through <code>Docassist::countRecent</code>.</li>\n<li>The user id is passed into <code>DocAssistant::assist()</code>.</li>\n<li>If the answer can't be saved, the request now gets a 500 and the row stays failed.</li>\n<li>Review findings that can't be encoded become a 502.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong>Tests:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>New <code>tests/libraries/docs/LLMDocsTest.php</code> uses a Guzzle MockHandler to check the paths, bodies and timeouts, and that every failure is a 502 without Ares' text.</li>\n<li>New <code>tests/tools/api-tester/FakeAresTest.php</code>.</li>\n<li><code>DocAssistantTest</code> is updated and covers the failed final save and the id types.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li>D-006, the backend skip reason and <code>docs/generated</code> are updated. The graph, docs and api-cases checks are clean.</li>\n<li>I pointed <code>acl-members-docassist-ask-allowed</code> at <code>{docId}</code>. <code>acl-members-doc-lock-by-owner-allowed</code> leaves <code>{membersDocId}</code> locked, and the new lock rule rightly refuses an ask on it.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>Test results (<code>ai test gaia --changed</code>)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>PHPUnit has only the 6 known ShortCode failures. The docs tests pass 13/13 and tests/tools passes 184/184.</li>\n<li>api: backend 13/0. The other docassist acl and client cases pass, including 502, 429, the failed row and input limits.</li>\n<li>Still failing with <strong>502</strong>: <code>acl-members-docassist-ask-allowed</code>, <code>client-docassist-ask-returns-html</code>, <code>client-docassist-complete-returns-completion</code> and <code>client-docassist-review-returns-findings</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>What blocks shipping</h4>\n<p>The shared test containers (gaia-test and the <code>p4m-test-gaia-slotN</code> containers that <code>ai test</code> uses) are created by dev-tools. They don't run <code>fake-ares</code> and have no <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL</code>, so Gaia calls the unreachable <code>ares:8000</code>. <code>ai ship</code> needs a clean full run, so I can't ship until that changes.</p>\n<p><strong>To unblock, a dev-tools issue (I'd suggest <code>complexity: simple</code>) should:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>In <code>dev-tools/installer/testenv.py</code> and the p4m compose override, start a <code>fake-ares</code> container from the checkout's <code>tools/api-tester/fake-ares</code> (<code>php -S 0.0.0.0:8000 router.php</code>) on the test network.</li>\n<li>Set <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL=http://fake-ares:8000</code> in <code>GaiaTestContainer.env()</code> for gaia-test, gaia-test-hermes-down and the slot containers.</li>\n<li>Also in that issue: <code>dev-tools/ai/lib/tests.py</code> <code>PHPUNIT_FOLDERS</code> should run <code>tests/libraries</code> as a whole. Right now <code>tests/libraries/docs</code> (and the conversations, workflows and query folders) never run in <code>ai test gaia</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Once that is merged and the runtime is updated, hand #4537 back to me and I'll run the full suite and ship. The alternative is to accept the 4 cases as known failures until then; tell me if you prefer that.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Follow-ups for the PR:</strong> two api cases still to add.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A member posting their own <code>projectId</code> with <code>{otherProjectDocId}</code> should get a 403 from the new per-doc scope check.</li>\n<li>An ask on <code>{lockedDocId}</code> should get a 422.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Adding them needs the gaia-dev CatalogAppender, which <code>ai gaia-dev</code> doesn't allow.</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	conversationrooms	447a14b76afa-8715-b3ee-74f36b3c3804	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	\N
