abc409516af7-113d-0f34-6db0f5f7cf80	2026-11-13 23:26:35	2026-11-13 23:26:35	0	<p><strong>Agent Achilles needs your input</strong></p><h4>Spike result: next Ember LTS</h4>\n<p><b>Bottom line:</b> the app runs on Ember 7.4 with one code change and one test fix. A full-suite trial passed 1486 of 1487 tests. The plan below needs your approval before I create anything.</p>\n\n<h4>Releases and target (npm, 14 Nov 2026)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><b>ember-source:</b> <code>lts</code> = 6.12.1, <code>latest</code> = 7.4.0 (released 26 Oct), 7.5 is in beta. Every fourth minor (x.4, x.8, x.12) becomes LTS about 6 weeks after release, when the next minor ships. So <b>7.4 should be tagged LTS in early December</b>, around when 6.12's bug-fix window closes (about 8 Dec).</li>\n<li><b>Target: Ember 7.4 LTS</b>, with ember-cli ~7.4. There is no newer 6.x LTS after 6.12.</li>\n<li><b>ember-data:</b> the npm <code>lts</code> tag still points at 5.3.13, which is stale. 5.3 only accepts <code>ember-source ^6</code>, so ember-data has to move to 5.8.2 or 5.9.1 (latest). 5.9 needs <code>qunit ^2.26</code>. Both gave the same result in the trial. <b>I recommend 5.9</b>: it is current, while 5.8's last patch was in April.</li>\n<li>ember-cli 7.4 needs Node 22.22 or later. Our images use <code>node:22-bookworm</code> (22.23.5), so that's fine. <code>engines</code> and the image's global <code>ember-cli@6.12.0</code> need bumping.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>Trial (throwaway container for dependency resolution and builds; suite through <code>ai test prometheus</code> on an uncommitted package.json; everything reverted and removed)</h4>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Ember 7.4 + ember-data 5.8.2, no code changes:</b> the build passed, but the test boot crashed with <code>Assertion Failed: &lt;Application#modules&gt; must be set when using the StrictResolver</code>.\n<ul><li><b>Cause:</b> Ember 7's <code>Engine</code> declares <code>Resolver = StrictResolver</code> as a class field. That shadows the <code>Resolver</code> we set on the prototype through <code>Application.extend({ Resolver })</code> in <code>app/app.js</code>.</li>\n<li><b>Fix:</b> the standard blueprint form <code>export default class App extends Application { modulePrefix = …; podModulePrefix = …; Resolver = Resolver; }</code>. It also works on 6.12.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Same trial with the native-class <code>app.js</code>:</b> 1486 pass, 1 fail, 3 todo. The same result with ember-data 5.9.1.\n<ul><li><b>The one failure:</b> <code>Integration | Component | issue/file-preview: it shows a pdf in an iframe</code>. Ember 7 now sanitizes <code>data:</code> URLs in an iframe <code>src</code> to <code>unsafe:data:…</code>.</li>\n<li>Only the test's stub adapter host is a <code>data:</code> URL. Production uses the API host, so this is a test-only fix: give the iframe case an http(s) or <code>about:</code> host.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Deprecations under ember-data 5.8/5.9:</b>\n<ul><li><code>warp-drive:deprecate-legacy-request-methods</code> fired about 416,000 times. Every <code>findRecord</code>, <code>query</code> and <code>findAll</code> raises it, and the test log grew to about 760 MB.</li>\n<li><code>warp-drive.deprecate-tracking-package</code> (1): <code>@ember-data/tracking</code> is deprecated.</li>\n<li><code>warp-drive.ember-inflector</code> (2, 5.9 only).</li>\n<li>No Ember 7 deprecations: 4512, 4546 and 4547 cleared them.</li></ul></li>\n</ol>\n\n<h4>Add-ons that pinned us before</h4>\n<p>All resolve against 7.4 with no peer warnings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>ember-cli-yadda 0.7.0 and yadda 2.2.0 (3.2.0 exists; the pin isn't needed for the move)</li>\n<li>ember-cli-mirage 3.0.4 (<code>ember-source &gt;=3.28</code>)</li>\n<li>ember-power-select 9.0.6 and ember-basic-dropdown 9.0.1</li>\n<li>ember-file-upload 10.1.0, ember-concurrency 5.3.0, ember-cli-deprecation-workflow 4.0.1</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I kept the <code>package.json</code> overrides from 4512 unchanged and didn't trial removing them, so they should stay.</p>\n\n<h4>Classic build or Embroider/Vite</h4>\n<p><b>Recommendation: stay on the classic build for the LTS move</b> and plan Embroider/Vite as a separate epic. Reasons:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>ember-cli 7.4 still builds the classic app, as the trial showed.</li>\n<li>The app depends on broccoli-era pieces that each need porting:\n<ul><li><code>app.import</code> of vendor scripts (AdminLTE, jQuery plugins, summernote, quill, pace)</li>\n<li>the custom <code>lib/bundled-translations</code> broccoli tree</li>\n<li>ember-cli-yadda's <code>.feature</code> compilation, which has no Vite equivalent we use today</li>\n<li>ember-cli-code-coverage, and loader.js-based test helpers</li></ul></li>\n<li>Mixing that with a deadline-driven LTS move adds risk without helping the move.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>Proposed issues, in order (nothing created yet)</h4>\n<ol>\n<li><b>[aprom, simple, on 6.12, do now] Ember 7 readiness: convert <code>app/app.js</code> to a native class and fix the file-preview iframe test host.</b> Both changes pass on 6.12 and remove the only two Ember 7 breakages.</li>\n<li><b>[aprom, complex, start once 7.4 is tagged LTS, early Dec] Upgrade to Ember 7.4 LTS and ember-data 5.9.</b>\n<ul><li>ember-source/ember-cli ~7.4, ember-data ~5.9.1, qunit ^2.26.</li>\n<li><code>engines.node &gt;= 22.22</code>; Dockerfile global <code>ember-cli@7.4</code>; check <code>.nvmrc</code>, CI and the dev/qa images.</li>\n<li>Route <code>deprecate-legacy-request-methods</code> through deprecation-workflow (silence and count it) so the test log stays small. Without this, CI logs are about 760 MB.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>[aprom, complex, after 2] Move data loading off the legacy store request methods</b> (<code>findRecord</code>/<code>query</code>/<code>findAll</code>/<code>save</code>) to <code>store.request</code> with builders. This is large and needs a design pass; it is needed before ember-data 6. It could split by module later.</li>\n<li><b>[aprom, simple, after 2] Drop <code>@ember-data/tracking</code></b> for WarpDrive's own reactivity, and replace <code>ember-inflector</code> use with WarpDrive's inflection utilities.</li>\n<li><b>[aprom, complex, later, not tied to the LTS] Spike: Embroider/Vite migration</b>: vendor imports, translations tree, yadda features, coverage.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p><b>Question:</b> approve this breakdown, including ember-data <b>5.9</b> (instead of 5.8) and staying on the <b>classic build</b>, so I can create the issues?</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	conversationrooms	a9b0b1e66af7-113d-0f34-cf930f4236c2	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N
