497bbe006ad9-bd7c-a941-061a47259e32	48d0b1d36ad9-bd7c-a941-71476aac218e	The current global search (search in the header) only works with API with OR for a fixed number of fields. It should work with the vectors in postgres enabled for multiple fields so that we have fast multi field fuzzy searching.	message	\N	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-10-21 18:41:13	f	\N
c4cb20f56ad9-89da-2a37-4175df66b921	48d0b1d36ad9-bd7c-a941-71476aac218e	This needs to be handled on the gaia side. the ability to vectorize a field should be in the model meta, and the database sync should enable the field as a vector.	message	\N	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-10-21 20:55:32	f	\N
428063156ad9-025d-c4b2-acc6ac1b0161	48d0b1d36ad9-bd7c-a941-71476aac218e	Agent Nestor is working on it.	system	\N	\N	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-22 09:37:06	f	\N
e4c994586ad9-025d-c4b2-0445d4594733	48d0b1d36ad9-bd7c-a941-71476aac218e	I'd move the header search from three `LIKE '%q%'` clauses joined with OR to Postgres full-text search. Fields would opt in through model metadata. The migration would build one GIN index per model from those fields, and a new query operator would match against that index and sort by relevance.\n\n## What exists today\n- **Prometheus** (`components/app-layouts/application-header.js:153`): sends `((Issue.issueNumber CONTAINS q) OR (Issue.subject CONTAINS q) OR (Issue.description CONTAINS q))`. Gaia turns that into three `LIKE '%q%'` scans, unindexed and unranked.\n- **Gaia query language** (`core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php:188`): has no full-text operator. Values are pasted straight into the query, not passed as bound parameters. The new operator must bind its input. The existing operators have the same flaw; I'd log that as a separate bug.\n- **Migration**: `core/libs/meta/migration.php` and `Postgres::syncExistingTable` only create btree indexes. The sync also **drops every column that isn't in the metadata**, which makes a generated `tsvector` column risky.\n- **Legacy `fts` flag**: it's already on dozens of fields, including ids, left over from the Elasticsearch era (`app/metadata/FTS.php`). It's far too broad to reuse, so I'd add a new key and leave `fts` alone.\n\n## Approach\n- **Metadata**: a field opts in with `'search' => ['weight' => 'A']`. Weights A to D set ranking priority.\n- **Migration**: builds one GIN **expression index** per model: `to_tsvector('simple', setweight(coalesce(subject,''),'A') || ...)`. There's no new column, so the column-drop problem and ORM side effects don't apply. The index is rebuilt when the set of fields changes.\n- **Query**: a new operator on a pseudo-field, `((Issue.search MATCHES 'logi bug'))`. Each word becomes a prefix term (`logi:*`), so partial words match. Without an explicit `sort`, results come back in relevance order. ACL scoping is unchanged because it's still the normal list query.\n- **Index usage**: Phalcon's query language (PHQL) can't express the `@@` operator. The likely route is a small inlinable SQL function created through the existing `functions` metadata, which the planner expands so the index still gets used. That needs checking, so the two framework issues are marked `complex`.\n\n## Questions (my recommendation in bold)\n1. By "vectors" you mean Postgres full-text (`tsvector` + GIN), not pgvector semantic embeddings? Embeddings would need Ares and are a much bigger feature. **Yes, full-text.**\n2. "Fuzzy" means prefix matching per word ("logi" finds "login"), without typo tolerance for now? Typo tolerance would need pg_trgm, which only the test database has today. **Yes, prefix only; trigram later.**\n3. Day one covers Issue subject and description only, since that's all the header searches. Projects, wiki and comments come later. **Yes.**\n\nAlso left out: the bound-parameter fix for the existing operators, removing the legacy `fts` flag, and a search results page beyond the 5-item dropdown.\n\nThe plan below assumes yes to all three.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search global search fulltext tsvector 2>&1 | head -40", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in gaia", "Reading gaia/app/metadata/FTS.php", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs", "Searching the code in gaia/tools/api-tester/harness/prepare-test-db.sh", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/prometheus/app && ls components/app-layouts/ | grep -i header; grep -n \\"search\\" -A3", "Searching for \\"search\\" in prometheus/app/components/app-layouts", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/application-header.js", "Searching the code in gaia/core", "Reading gaia/core/libs/meta/migration.php", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/models/query", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/models", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model/Issue.php", "Searching the code in gaia", "Updating the knowledge map"]	e406ab836ad9-025d-c4b2-2c17546bcc8c	0.740728	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-22 09:39:48	f	\N
4fcdee826ad9-95f2-5f53-b769bb7fe315	4f0ce6006ad9-95f2-5f53-2d0fd54845df	In the issue detail view, there is a section showing issue Hierarchy. Right now its showing the complete details which clutters the screen if in case an issue has 3-4 issues it become quite difficult to make sense out of the view. What I want is to have just the title cards displayed initially, if someone wants to view the details then they can expand and see the details.\n\nAlso the hierarchy is just one level, we can atleast show which issue is the parent of the current issue, if there is a parent, and then the children of the current issue at least. Visually it should be easy for the user to distinguish between the levels. Do create screen for the section. Add the issues to the milestone Claude-v1	message	\N	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-10-22 11:36:47	f	\N
