c5da36886ada-75e5-bcf0-e4f04e29361b	4f0ce6006ad9-95f2-5f53-2d0fd54845df	You're right: issue overview is the row pattern used for the Gantt task list (`app-ui/gantt-chart/task-row.hbs:37`), the project's latest issues (`templates/app/project/index.hbs:130`) and the issue list's first column. Each row is an `issue-overview` → `issue-block` → priority icon plus a `data-block` holding the subject, description and status badge. The current hierarchy box already uses this markup, but it always shows the description.\n\nIt's a repeated markup pattern rather than a component. So the plan now reuses it as is:\n- **Collapsed row:** the Gantt-list form (priority, `#number - subject`, status badge under it).\n- **Expanded row:** the latest-issues form, which adds the description between the subject and the badge.\n- **Chevron:** sits on the right, where the Gantt row has its eye button.\n\nTurning the pattern into one shared component used by all four places would be a separate refactor, so I've left it out.\n\n\n\n**What the screen shows:**\n- Collapsed rows look like Gantt task-list rows.\n- The expanded child (#4081) looks like a latest-issues row.\n- Parent and child rows have a plain left edge at different indents, while the current issue keeps its crimson bar. Two small new rules add the parent bar and the second indent step.\n\n**Still open:** whether an opened row should also show assignee and type. I still recommend not.\n\n\n\nI've revised the plan and screen above to use the issue overview rows. It's still one Prometheus issue in **Claude-v1**, with no Gaia change.\n\n- **Collapsed row:** looks like a Gantt task-list row (priority, `#number - subject`, status badge).\n- **Opened row:** looks like a row in the project's latest issues, with the description added.\n- **Levels:** parent, this issue and child issues each have a caption. Parent and child rows sit at different indents, and the current issue keeps its crimson bar.\n- **Other screens:** the shared issue-overview styles stay untouched, so the Gantt list, project overview and issue list look the same as before.\n\n**Decision for you:** should an opened row also show assignee and type? I recommend not for now.\n\nIssue overview is markup copied into four places, not a single component. Turning it into one shared component is a separate refactor, so I've left it out of this plan. Tell me if you want it as a follow-up issue.	message	["Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Listing prometheus/app/components/**/*overview*", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/gantt-chart/task-row.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/app/project/index.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/styles/modules/gantt.scss", "Updating the knowledge map"]	c50905076ada-75e5-bcf0-0607a26912f8	0.674127	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-22 13:04:05	f	[{"uploadId": "be5afc376ada-75e5-bcf0-6fe8ab58f0f6", "key": "issue-hierarchy", "title": "Issue detail: hierarchy using the issue overview rows", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}]
