fc0444a36ada-2ec4-1fa7-8fbeda72c15d	afa54b056ada-2ec4-1fa7-d7b41cc59b57	You want to change the assignee straight from a task board card, the same way you can in the issue detail view, without opening the quick view first.\n\n**What's there now**\n- The assignee dropdown exists only in `components/issue/issue-details` (the template around line 283; `availableAssignees` and `updateAssignee` in the JS around line 1199). It lists active project members other than the current assignee, saves the issue and shows a Messenger toast. aprom-3681 asked for this on the card, but it was deliberately built in the detail view.\n- The card in `components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs` (around line 125) shows only the assignee's avatar. The board already passes project members in as `@membersList`.\n- One risk: aprom-3700. Re-rendering a whole card after an assignee change used to break dragging. Clicking the avatar also mustn't start a drag or open the quick view.\n\n**My approach.** Take the dropdown and its save logic out of `issue-details` and make it a shared `Issue::AssigneeSelect` component. `issue-details` then uses it unchanged, and the card uses a compact version: the avatar opens the menu. This is one Prometheus issue with no Gaia change, since a PATCH to `assignee` already works and already publishes `issue.assignee.changed`.\n\n**Left out:** changing status, priority or estimate from the card, unassigning, and searching in the member list. aprom-3978 (the board doesn't update live when other users make changes) stays separate.\n\nI can mock up the card menu as a screen if you'd like to see it before approving.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching issues: task board assignee card --project aprom 2>&1 | head -40", "Reading issue 3681 2>&1 | head -40; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 3859 2>&1 | head -30", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs", "Searching the code