73c3c9276adb-bb24-3884-597cbb90db73	dc9f28086adb-14fc-3884-5d3000a5198e	I looked at the 4063 code (in review, PR #551). Here's what's behind the two problems:\n\n- **Collapsed groups.** `AppUi::Notifications::Group` is a toggle header with a caret, the newest notification's text, and update and unread counts. The notifications under it only show once you expand it. There's also a styling bug: expanded items sit in `ul.notification-group-items`, so the `.notifications-list > li > a` rules don't reach them. They lose their padding and flex layout and look different from the ungrouped items.\n- **Order.** `utils/notifications/group-by-issue.js` already does what you describe. It sorts each group by its newest notification and sorts inside the group newest first. So APROM-4063 should already sit at the "3 minutes ago" position. I think it looks wrong today because the header and its "updated X ago" line hide the order. If you've seen a group in the wrong place, tell me when it happened; it could be paging. The new issue keeps this rule and adds a test for it.\n\n**Proposed design.** Each group is a plain heading with the issue key, which links to the issue but doesn't mark anything read. Under it, every notification of that issue is always shown, newest first, using the same item as everywhere else. Then comes the next issue. Notifications that aren't about an issue (membership, milestone) stay as single items in the same time order. There's no caret, toggle or counts.\n\n\n\nThe mockup uses the real sidebar CSS. The heading's own style (`.notification-group-heading`: a light divider above it and a bold link-blue key, square edges) doesn't exist yet, so it shows with the default `h5` look. Avatars are placeholder icons because external images get stripped from mockups.\n\n**Two questions:**\n1. **An issue with a single notification:** should it still get a heading? I recommend **yes**, so every issue notification looks the same (APROM-4072 above). Today a one-item group shows as a plain item.\n2. **The heading:** should it show only the key? I recommend **yes**. The notification context has no issue subject. Showing one would need a Gaia change, so I left it out.\n\nThis is one Prometheus issue, built on top of 4063. It depends on aprom-4063 because that work isn't merged yet.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4063 2>&1 | head -80", "Listing prometheus/app/{components/app-ui/notifications/*,components/app-layouts/notifications-sidebar.*,utils/notifications/*,styles/components/notifications*}", "Listing prometheus/docs/ui/screens/*notif*", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/notifications/group.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/notifications-sidebar.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/utils/notifications/group-by-issue.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/notifications/notification.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Reading prometheus/app/styles/components/notifications-sidebar.scss", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/notifications-sidebar.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/docs/ui/design-system.md", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/notifications", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/notifications/modules/IssueNotification.php", "Updating the knowledge map"]	729b95e76adb-bb24-3884-828379070346	0.56392	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-23 17:59:15	f	[{"uploadId": "664eb6266adb-bb24-3884-1ae4db44bf6e", "key": "grouped-sidebar", "title": "Notifications sidebar: issue headings, all notifications visible", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}]
