5d52c3496adb-8ca9-66d5-4a18770c8f14	c3a4ac636adb-e65f-66d5-35fdd2e28d26	I've looked into all four. Two of them are simple fixes, one needs a bit of UI work, and the 404 needs an investigation.\n\n**1. "View the plan" does nothing.** `components/idea/message-item.hbs:34` links to `#ideaplan-<id>`, but nothing on the page has that id. The plan box also keeps the selected version to itself (`pickedVersion` in `plan-box.js`), so the page has no way to tell it which version to show. The fix: the link calls a page action, the plan box switches to that version's tab, and the page scrolls to the box.\n\n**2. Screens aren't visible in the plan.** The plan box only lists the screen keys as text (`plan-box.hbs:37`). I'd add a "Screens" row under the plan summary. It would show each screen the version lists once, as a thumbnail, reusing `Idea::MessageScreens`. It would show the latest version of each key, because that is the one Talos attaches on approval. Clicking a thumbnail opens the preview the conversation already has.\n\n**3. The screen attach 404.** Talos downloads the PNG with `GET /upload/{id}`, which Gaia serves in `UploadController::getAction`. The route exists, and uploads tied to an idea have an ACL scope through the idea (`Upload.php` ~l.171). So I can't tell from the code whether the 404 means the row is missing, the file is missing on disk, or the request is being routed or scoped wrongly. I tried to look up the upload row in Postgres, but I'm not allowed to run shell commands here. This goes in as a Gaia bug, starting with a test that fails. It's marked complex because the cause is unknown.\n\n**4. Status label off-center.** AdminLTE's own fix is to move the label into `<div class="box-tools pull-right">`, the same markup the conversation box uses (`conversation-box.hbs:24`). That uses the box-tools positioning instead of a bare float, so no new CSS is needed.\n\n**Split:** items 1, 2 and 4 all change the plan box, so they're one Prometheus issue, to avoid conflicts. The Gaia bug runs alongside it. One link between them: thumbnails load through `services/upload-preview.js`, which also reads `/upload/{id}`. If the bug turns out to be on Gaia's side, the thumbnails may be blank until it's fixed. The Prometheus issue doesn't need to wait for it, though.\n\nOne question: is a plan-level screen row OK, or do you want the thumbnails inside each planned issue's expanded detail? I recommend the plan-level row, because a screen used by two issues would otherwise show twice and is easy to miss when the issues are collapsed.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching the code in .", "Reading prometheus/translations/en-us.json", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/ideas/approval.py", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/message-item.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/plan-box.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/plan-box.js", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/app/project/idea/page.hbs", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/tracker.py", "Searching the code in .dev-tools-runtime/gaia-mcp/server.py", "Reading .dev-tools-runtime/gaia-mcp/server.py", "Reading .dev-tools-runtime/gaia-mcp/server.py", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/UploadController.php", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/services/upload-preview.js", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/UploadController.php", "Searching for \\"function assertUploadInScope\\" in gaia", "Searching for \\"function assertRecordIdInScope\\" in gaia/core/libs/security/Acl.php", "Searching for \\"upload\\" in gaia/core/config/routes.php", "Reading gaia/core/config/routes.php", "Running docker ps --format '{{.Names}}' 2>&1 | head -20", "Running docker exec postgres-dev sh -c 'for db in $(psql -U postgres -Atc \\"select datname from pg_database where not datistempla", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/ideas/client.py", "Listing prometheus/app/adapters/upload.js", "Sea