4f84b2b36adc-e07b-a0a9-a2493f199a28	f057b8796adc-e2c6-a0a9-8a64e255dbf5	Here's one Prometheus issue for the user side of your decision: users still see every issue their idea created, but an issue in a project they can't read shows as plain text, not as a link to a "permission denied" page.\n\n**What's there now**\n- Created issues are links in two places: `components/idea/created-issues-box.hbs:11` and `components/idea/plan-box.hbs:42`. The plan box gets its data from the `createdIssues` getter (`plan-box.js:141`). Both use the `ideaplanissue` query with `rels: 'issue'` (`controllers/app/project/idea/page.js:176`).\n- Prometheus already knows which projects the user is in. `services/current-user.js` loads the user with `include: 'projects'`, and `issue.projectId` is on the model. So the check needs no new API.\n\n**Approach**\n- The idea page controller works out which projects the user can read: the idea's own project plus `currentUser.user.projects`. It passes that list to both boxes.\n- A created issue in a readable project stays a link. Any other created issue shows its key and subject as muted text.\n- It also handles the case where Gaia returns no issue at all. Your Gaia fix may stop `rels=issue` from returning issues the user can't read. The row then shows the plan item's key and subject, with no link and no crash.\n- Gaia still decides who can read what. This only decides whether a link is shown.\n\n**Left out:** an "External request" label on plan items that target another project, and admin-wide read rules. Admins who aren't members of a project see plain text, which is safe. I can add the label to this issue if you want it.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search ideas plan issue link --project aprom 2>&1 | head -40;", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/idea", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/plan-box.js"