ada6beb56adc-b462-2863-29c936ec57fb	e5bbc5d16adc-d3fe-2863-120be2b9005e	Here's what I found. All four points are Prometheus-only, and none needs Gaia changes.\n\n**1. Message composer.** `Idea::Composer` is a plain 2-row `FieldTextArea`. The body column (`Ideamessage.body`, type `text`) has no size limit, so the limit is only in the UI. Issue comments use `AppUi::ToastUi` (wysiwyg with a toolbar, Ctrl+Enter to post), and we'll reuse it. One catch: the editor only outputs HTML (`getHtml()`). Idea messages are markdown, because the thread renders them with `render-markdown` and Nestor writes and reads markdown. I recommend a small opt-in `markdown` output on the editor modifier so messages stay markdown. I'd also put the same editor on the "Describe it" field of the create page. User @mentions and #issue links are left out.\n\n**2. "How it works".** It's the side box on the create page (`templates/app/project/idea/create.hbs`). Removing it is easy.\n\n**3. Approve modal.** I think I found the root cause. `bootstrap-modal.hbs` wires the confirm button straight to the `confirm` function passed in. That skips the component's own `confirm` action, which hides the modal when the function returns `true`. So `confirmApprove` returning `true` (the aprom-4103 fix) does nothing, and nothing shows that a save is running. Fix: `bootstrap-modal` accepts a Promise from `confirm`. While it's pending, both buttons are disabled and Confirm shows a spinner. On success the modal closes. On failure it stays open and the buttons come back. Existing modals that return `true` or `false` work as before. The plan box's Approve button stays disabled from the click until the save either succeeds (the plan is now `approved`, so the button goes away) or fails (it comes back). The status label also shows a spinner while the plan is `approved` or `creating`.\n\nSince `bootstrap-modal` is shared by 31 modals, that change gets its own `complex` issue. The plan box work then builds on it. Note that aprom-4105 (still new) also edits the plan box header, so expect a small merge overlap.\n\n**Questions:**\n1. **Which box has the negative space?** My guess: the Summary box (each stat is its own `h4`, so it's very tall) and the conversation box's padding around the thread. Or do you mean the create page, where removing "How it works" leaves the right column empty? In that case I'd make the form box full width. The plan below assumes both.\n2. **When should the modal close?** I recommend closing it as soon as the approval is saved, with the plan box's status label then showing creating → created live. Keeping it open until Talos finishes would leave it hanging whenever Talos isn't running.\n3. **Sending a message:** Ctrl+Enter plus the Send button, like issue comments? (Plain Enter now adds a new line, as it should in a rich editor.) I recommend yes.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Listing prometheus/app/{templates/app/project/idea,components/idea,controllers/app/project/idea}/**", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/app/project/idea/page.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/composer.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/composer.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/plan-box.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/conversation-box.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/translations/en-us.json", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/summary-box.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/plan-box.js", "Reading prometheus/translations/en-us.json", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/bootstrap-modal.js", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/app/project/idea/create.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/bootstrap-modal.js", "Searching for \\"approvePlan\\" in prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/idea/page.js", "Listing prometheus/app/{templates/components/bootstrap-modal.hbs,components/bootstrap-modal.hbs}", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/controllers/app/pro