41a3a9436ae0-a6b8-29af-3309609c6277	afa54b056ada-2ec4-1fa7-d7b41cc59b57	The cause isn't z-index or Sortable. The click on the avatar never reaches Bootstrap, so the menu can't open.\n\n**Why**\n- In `prometheus/app/components/issue/assignee-select.hbs:4` the wrapper `.dropdown` has `{{on "click" this.stopPropagation}}`. In compact mode it calls `event.stopPropagation()` (`assignee-select.js:40`).\n- Bootstrap 3 dropdowns open through a single listener on `document`, which handles every `[data-toggle="dropdown"]` click. Stopping the click inside the card means it never gets there. The issue detail view still works because it doesn't use compact mode, so nothing is stopped there.\n- Stopping the click wasn't needed anyway. The card itself has no click handler; the quick view only opens from the title link. Sortable already ignores the dropdown: `modifiers/initialize-sortable.js:582` has `filter: '[data-issue-assignee-dropdown]'` and `preventOnFilter: false`.\n- The tests probably passed because they triggered the menu items directly instead of opening the menu through the avatar.\n\n**Also worth fixing in the same issue**\n- **No visible cue:** compact mode is only the avatar, with no caret. That was my plan's call, and you're right that it gives no hint. I suggest adding a small `fa-caret-down` next to the avatar.\n- **Possible clipping:** the lanes' box body has `overflow-x: auto` (`styles/modules/board.scss:69`). That makes it scroll vertically as well, so the menu may get cut off on the last card of a lane. The fix should check that case and open the menu upward if it is clipped.\n\nSince aprom-4102 is closed, this is a new bug issue:	message	["Listing prometheus/app/components/issue/assignee-select.*", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Reading prometheus/app/components/issue/assignee-select.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/issue/assignee-select.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/app-ui", "Searching for \\"@members\\" in prometheu