fc2f84b26adc-7056-a2f4-f6e975c19aed	e5bbc5d16adc-d3fe-2863-120be2b9005e	Inline images are definitely useful. A circled screenshot says more than a paragraph. But choosing HTML over markdown doesn't decide whether they work. Markdown has images too (`![label](url)`). What matters is where the image is stored and whether I can actually see it.\n\n**Why I chose markdown:**\n- **I read every message as text.** Talos passes message bodies to me as text. Markdown is what I write and read natively. HTML from the editor works, but it adds noise and costs more tokens on every turn, because the whole thread is re-sent each time.\n- **One format per column.** My replies are markdown. If the engineer's messages were HTML, the same column would hold two formats. The viewer renders both today, but anything else that reads the thread would have to handle both.\n\n**Where images break today, whichever format we pick:**\n- **Pasted images get embedded in the message.** The editor (`modifiers/initialize-toastui.js`) has no image upload hook. A pasted screenshot becomes a base64 `data:` URI inside the body, and that applies to issue comments too. A single screenshot adds hundreds of KB to the message. That is slow to load and, for me, hundreds of thousands of tokens of unreadable text.\n- **I can't see an image that is only text in the body.** I can only see an image if Talos gives me the file, for example saved to disk so I can Read it as an image. Today Talos only handles images in the other direction: the screens I design, rendered to PNG.\n\n**What I recommend:** keep messages in markdown and make images a proper feature:\n1. **aprom:** when an image is pasted or dropped into the editor, upload it to Gaia as an `Upload` with `relatedTo` set to the idea. That ACL scoping already exists from the screens work. The message then gets a `![name](upload:<id>)` reference, and the thread renders it through the existing preview-token flow (`services/upload-preview.js`), the same way screen thumbnails load.\n2. **adt (Talos):** download the uploads a message references and give them to me as image files, so I actually see what you circled.\n3. **Prerequisite:** the open bug where downloading an upload returns 404 (from idea c3a4ac63). Talos needs that download to work.\n\nThat's a separate feature across Prometheus and dev-tools. It can build on the editor issue in this plan, and nothing in this plan blocks it. Storing HTML instead wouldn't get any closer to it.\n\n**Options:**\n- **A (recommended):** approve this plan as it is. I then plan inline images as a follow-up idea in the Ideas milestone, after the upload 404 fix.\n- **B:** I add the image issues to this plan now. It would become cross-repo, and the Talos part needs the 404 fix first.\n\nWhich do you want? The current plan is unchanged until you decide.	message	["Searching the code in prometheus/app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib/ideas/conversation.py", "Updating the knowledge map", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.159578	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-24 07:02:20	f	\N
