40ce68866adc-9a36-a2f4-43fd6965dde8	e5bbc5d16adc-d3fe-2863-120be2b9005e	I've added the image work to the plan. Both image issues depend on **agaia-4106**, the existing 404 bug where `GET /upload/{id}` fails for idea uploads. Each image issue also names agaia-4106 in its description as the issue it waits on.\n\n**How the image flow works:**\n- **The reference in the message is `![name](upload:<uploadId>)`.** The message stays markdown and contains no tokens or URLs that expire. Both issues use this format, so it's spelled out in each.\n- **aprom:** when an image is pasted or dropped into the composer, it's uploaded as an `Upload` related to the idea, using the same call issue attachments use. The editor gets an opt-in image hook, and the component that uses the editor does the upload, so the editor stays free of API calls. When the thread renders, it swaps each `upload:` reference for a preview address. This issue is `complex`: it's still open whether the editor's sanitizer keeps the `upload:` scheme, and the rendering has to wait for a fresh preview address before the image can show.\n- **adt (Talos):** when Talos builds my prompt, it downloads the images a message references into `dev-tools/talos/state/ideas/<idea>/images/` and replaces each reference with the file path. I already have read access there, so I see what you circled. My role instructions get one line telling me to open those images.\n- **No Gaia work** besides agaia-4106. The ACL path for uploads related to an idea already exists.\n- **Left out:** images in the create page's description (the idea doesn't exist yet when you write it, so there's nothing to attach the upload to), images in issue comments, and image previews or deleting images.\n\nAll six issues are in the **Ideas** milestone. It already exists in both A Prometheus and A Dev Tool.\n\n**One check on "parent issue association":** I've read it as "clearly tied to agaia-4106", which `dependsOn` and the description text now cover. If you meant