e9d182896adc-07a6-e36e-e02df6648d0b	93059cf66adc-07a6-e36e-fd991ee2f20e	I'll add a "mark as read" icon button to each issue group's heading in the notifications sidebar. Clicking it marks every notification in that group as read and doesn't leave the page.\n\n**What's already there:**\n- **Clicking a heading:** `components/app-ui/notifications/group.{hbs,js}` (from aprom-4104) runs `goToIssue`. That calls `_markGroupAsRead`, which marks each of the group's notifications read through `notifications.markAsRead`, then navigates. The new button can call `_markGroupAsRead` and skip the navigation.\n- **Server side:** Gaia needs no changes. Marking a single notification read already updates the unread count and the bell, and keeps other tabs in sync.\n- **Look:** the sidebar's "Mark all as read" button uses `fa-check-circle`. I'll use the same icon so the two read as the same action at different scopes.\n\n**Choices I made. Say if you want them different:**\n- **Placement:** an icon-only button on the right of the heading, with a "Mark as read" tooltip. The issue-key link stays on the left and still navigates.\n- **When it shows:** only when the group has at least one unread notification.\n- **Single-item groups:** they get the button too, because they also have a heading.\n- **Out of scope:** notifications that aren't grouped (e.g. membership). They only show one item each, so a per-item button is a separate idea.\n\nOne small issue in Prometheus. I didn't design a screen because the change is one icon. Say if you want one.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search notification group mark read 2>&1 | head -40", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/prometheus && cat app/components/app-ui/notifications/group.hbs app/components/app-", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/notifications/group.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/notifications/group.js", "Searching