0940f4926ade-bc23-4a93-b98af979ccc7	5b131d096adc-f42c-e36e-1693e76da846	I couldn't reproduce this because I can't run the app, but I found a concrete cause in the code. I'm fairly sure it's your bug, though it isn't new: it has been there since agaia-4064, and aprom-4118/4119 only made it more visible.\n\n## What's happening\n\naprom-4066 only marks notifications that are **loaded in the sidebar** and whose `relatedTo`/`relatedId` match the issue. That filter is in `_saveRelatedAsRead` in `prometheus/app/services/notifications.js` (~l.461).\n\nNotifications that arrive **live** through Hermes don't have those two fields:\n- Gaia's `NotificationLiveEvents.php:28` `NOTIFICATION_FIELDS` sends only `description`, `context`, `createdUser`, `createdUserName` and `dateCreated`.\n- agaia-4064 added the columns but never added them to this list.\n- `onNotificationCreated` (`notifications.js` ~l.644) pushes exactly what's in the event, so a live notification has `relatedTo` and `relatedId` undefined.\n\n**Result:** a notification that arrives while the page is open is never marked read when you view its issue, and the bell doesn't ring. After a page reload the same notification comes from REST with both fields, and it works again.\n\n**Why it looks like a regression:** aprom-4066 was most likely tested with notifications loaded at page load. Since aprom-4118 you test by clicking notifications on the board, and those are usually live ones. aprom-4118 has the same gap: a live notification has no `relatedTo`, so the click skips the quick view and uses the old link. aprom-4118 was asked to check this, but its PR comments don't mention it.\n\nThe aprom-4118/4119 changes don't touch any of 4066's code (`issue-details` trigger, service queue, recipient saves), so I don't think they broke it directly.\n\n**Quick check:** after a live notification arrives, reload the page and open the issue.\n- If it's marked read then, this is the cause.\n- If not, send me the exact steps and I'll look further.\n\nA related caveat: notifications created before agaia-4064 have NULL columns until agaia-4117 (the backfill, still `new`) runs. aprom-4066 skips them too.\n\n## Fix\n\nOne Gaia bug issue: add both fields to the live event. Prometheus already copies everything in the event onto the record, so it needs no change. Hermes passes `changes` through as they are, so it needs no change either.	message	["Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && for n in 4066 4117 4118 4119; do dev-tools/ai/ai kb show $n 2>&1 | head -4; dev-", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4118", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4066", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4117", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Reading prometheus/app/services/notifications.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/issue/issue-details.js", "Searching for \\"markNotificationsAsRead\\" in prometheus/app", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/notifications/notification.js", "Searching the code in gaia/app", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/NotificationLiveEvents.php", "Reading prometheus/app/services/notifications.js", "Searching the code in .", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching for \\"notification\\" in gaia/docs/architecture/live-updates/architecture.md", "Searching the code in gaia/tests/api/controllers/components/events/LiveEventsComponentsTest.php", "Updating the knowledge map"]	085992996ade-bc23-4a93-f01a27fcde9b	1.052892	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-25 17:31:53	f	\N
