984168f36ae0-6045-29af-0ed8514fede5	afa54b056ada-2ec4-1fa7-d7b41cc59b57	The analysis you pasted is right as far as the repo shows. It's a separate bug from the assignee menu, though, so I've added it as a second issue alongside the first.\n\n**What I confirmed in the code**\n- The board turns on `forceFallback`, so SortableJS does its own mouse-event dragging (`board.hbs:15`).\n- `getSortableOptions()` sets the options for the lanes the cards live in (`modifiers/initialize-sortable.js:571`). It sets no `fallbackTolerance`, `delay` or `delayOnTouchOnly`.\n- The `disableSortable` getter returns `this.args.named` (line 106). It's also passed to Sortable as `disableSortable`, which isn't a Sortable option; the real one is `disabled`. The board is its only caller and it passes `false`, so this does nothing today. It can be fixed in the same issue at no risk.\n- The milestone-tab Sortables (lines 484 and 547) only receive dropped cards and are never dragged from, so the tolerance only matters on the lanes.\n\n**Not confirmed:** the SortableJS internals the analysis relies on: the default tolerance of 0, the `if (fallbackTolerance && …)` check, and the swallowed click after a drag. `node_modules` isn't on the host and I couldn't open the package. It matches how SortableJS 1.14/1.15 behaves, and `package.json` pins `^1.14.0`.\n\n**How the two bugs interact:** none. The assignee avatar is in Sortable's `filter`, so a drag never starts there and the swallowed-click problem can't affect it. The two issues touch different files and can go in parallel.\n\n**About the test:** the "sometimes" comes from a 1px wobble during a fallback drag, which is hard to reproduce reliably in an acceptance test on Mirage. So I've asked for a unit test of the options plus a manual check in the running app.	message	["Reading prometheus/app/modifiers/initialize-sortable.js", "Reading prometheus/app/modifiers/initialize-sortable.js", "Running cd /d/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/prometheus && grep -