41a831636ae1-3497-9a2f-b552ce7b58a7	991f5df46ae1-2a68-9a2f-7cc8e5968877	I read the PR comments on the seven child issues of adt-4157 (4158–4164). Together they list about 30 follow-ups. None of them has an issue yet. I checked the main ones against `dev-tools` (the code merged to main):\n\n**Still open (confirmed in the code)**\n- `talos/lib/runner.py:238` `gaia_pack` runs `ai context` with `cwd=WORKSPACE` and no `P4M_WORKSPACE`. Gaia issues therefore get their context from the main checkout instead of the worktree.\n- `talos/lib/dispatcher.py:203` sets `P4M_TEST_SLOT` for every leased slot, whatever the repo.\n- Claude's memory is stored per working folder, so each `.runs/issue-N` run starts with an empty one. The agents lose the house memories, for example "never `p4m db migrate` from Pr4M" and "no permission seeds". This is the one I'd fix first.\n\n**Already covered or harmless, so no issue**\n- 4158 #2 ("p4m test uses the container mounts"): `ai/lib/tests.py` now passes `--src repo_dir(repo)`, which follows `P4M_WORKSPACE`, so tests run against the worktree. I've only added a regression test for it.\n- 4158 #1 (clean-up on close): `talos gc` already runs when `talos run` starts. The plan adds a second trigger when an issue reaches done.\n- Transcript stats work with per-issue cwds, because `runner.transcript` searches every `~/.claude/projects/*` folder.\n\n**Not issues, but you should know**\n- `.dev-tools-runtime` contains none of this work: there's no `P4M_TEST_SLOT` or `P4M_WORKSPACE` in it. Run `p4m runtime update` and restart `talos run`, or Talos keeps running serially.\n- 4160's limit matcher has never been checked against a real usage-limit result. Check the first one that turns up in `state/logs/`.\n\n**The plan:** 9 issues in A Dev Tool, milestone **Parallel Runtimes** (it already exists). Each description opens with "Part of adt-4157". The plan has no parent field, so you'll need to set the parent to 4157 by hand if you want them nested under it. To avoid merge conflicts, issues that edit the same file come one after another. Unrelated ones can be worked on at the same time.\n\nLeft out:\n- Delivering keys to remote Docker hosts goes into the container-hardening issue as a documented design only, not built.\n- Design-review naming nits that change no behaviour.\n\n\n\nI dropped one follow-up from the plan: 4162 #5, wrapping the browser checks in the `p4m-stack` skill with `ai devstack --`. That skill is in the Pr4M root repo. Should it go in A Dev Tool as a small pr4m issue, or will you change the skill yourself?	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Gaia: get issue 4157", "Searching issues: \\"parallel runtimes worktree test slot dispatcher\\" --project adt 2>&1 | head -60", "Gaia: get issue 4158", "Gaia: get issue 4159", "Gaia: get issue 4160", "Gaia: get issue 4161", "Gaia: get issue 4162", "Gaia: get issue 4163", "Gaia: get issue 4164", "Searching issues: \\"follow-ups talos workspace slot\\" --project adt --status new 2>&1 | head -30; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search \\"container runner ", "Searching the code in .dev-tools-runtime", "Searching the code in dev-tools", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/runner.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools/ai/lib/tests.py", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/dispatcher.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib/runner.py", "Updating the knowledge map"]	404fdf286ae1-3497-9a2f-bbf3a83bab0c	0.751671	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-28 07:24:49	f	\N
6817fe726ae1-2d79-4c27-23772c41d44c	991f5df46ae1-2a68-9a2f-7cc8e5968877	Nothing in the code blocks testing. I read all nine PR comments for adt-4167 to 4175. What's left over is refactors, performance and test gaps. But Talos as it runs today has none of this work yet, so there's some setup to do before you test.\n\n**Before testing (setup, not code):**\n1. **Update the runtime copy.** `.dev-tools-runtime` is still on the code from before adt-4158: it has no `workspace_gc.py`, `memory.py` or `filelock.py`. Run `p4m runtime update` and restart `talos run`. Until you do, Talos runs the old serial code.\n2. **Turn parallel runs on.** No `agent.json` sets `maxParallel` or `testSlots`, so the default of 1 keeps runs serial. Set `maxParallel` (for example 3) and `testSlots` on Odysseus.\n3. **Set up the test slots.** `p4m.env` has no `TEST_SLOTS`, so the code falls back to its built-in default. Set it to at least `testSlots`, then run `p4m test slots setup` to build the template database and the slot databases.\n4. **Container runs only:** rebuild the runner image (it's non-root now, from adt-4175), remove the old root-owned volumes, and set `dockerSocket: true` for agents whose tests need Docker. The image's Claude CLI must be new enough to know `autoMemoryDirectory` (adt-4168); older versions silently ignore it.\n5. **Clean-up:** delete the leftovers from adt-4168's probe by hand: `Pr4M/.runs/issue-0` and `~/.claude/projects/D--Claude-Workspace-Projects-Pr4M--runs-issue-0`.\n\n**Things to watch while testing:**\n- **Usage limits** (adt-4160): the matcher has never seen a real limit result. Check the first one in `state/logs/`.\n- **Slot templates** (adt-4172): if more seed keys are in use at once than templates are kept (3), a slot can fail with a `SlotError`. `p4m test slots setup` fixes it. That's unlikely with 2–3 slots.\n- **Load per status event** (adt-4174): gc does a Gaia read and Docker queries on every status event. Fine at our volume; just keep an eye on it.\n- **Stopping** (adt-4169): `stop()` only releases waits, and worker threads have no way to exit. Stopping Talos means ending the process, the same as today.\n\n**Not blocking, can wait:**\n- Splitting the Docker leftovers code out of `container.py`.\n- A per-agent gc collector.\n- Extracting `TemplateRegistry`.\n- A concurrency test for the dependency gate.\n- Two `workspaces.ensure` fetches per run.\n- The `filelock` module name could clash with the PyPI package.\n- `talos status` shows slot 0 for non-Gaia runs.\n- Env-only key delivery to remote Docker hosts.\n\nI'd test first, then file one batch that combines these with whatever the test turns up. Most of them are only worth doing if they actually cause trouble. When you have results, I'll plan the next set under adt-4157 in **Parallel Runtimes**.	message	["Gaia: get issue 4167", "Gaia: get issue 4168", "Gaia: get issue 4169", "Gaia: get issue 4170", "Gaia: get issue 4171", "Gaia: get issue 4172", "Gaia: get issue 4173", "Gaia: get issue 4174", "Gaia: get issue 4175", "Running grep -l \\"P4M_TEST_SLOT\\\\|autoMemoryDirectory\\\\|UsagePause\\" -r .dev-tools-runtime/talos/lib .dev-tools-runtime/installer 2>", "Listing {installer/filelock.py,talos/lib/workspace_gc.py,talos/lib/memory.py} in .dev-tools-runtime", "Listing .runs/* in .", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/agents", "Searching for \\"TEST_SLOTS\\" in dev-tools", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.784165	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-28 10:07:36	f	\N
