a9e52c696ae2-acfd-7f50-c2248f152ff6	e53706516ae2-baab-7f50-a57680d4b6c5	Right now the backlog and each milestone are separate tabs on the Task Board. The only way to plan is to drag one card at a time onto a tab header without seeing what's already in that sprint. I've drawn two ways to fix that, using the board's existing markup and AdminLTE boxes.\n\n**Option A: a Planning view (`planning-view`).** This is the one I recommend. A **Board | Planning** toggle sits next to Saved Searches on the board.\n- **Left:** the backlog as a list of issue rows (priority, number, subject, status, estimate), with checkboxes.\n- **Right:** a box for each open milestone, showing its dates, how many issues it has and their total estimate.\n- You drag issues between the backlog and sprints, or tick several and use **Move to ▾**.\n- The board itself stays as it is.\n\n**Option B: a backlog column beside the board (`board-backlog-panel`).** The active sprint's lanes stay on screen and the backlog sits in a narrow column on the right. You drag a card straight into a status lane. It's quicker for adding to the current sprint, but it only shows one sprint at a time. It also takes width from the lanes, and the quick-view panel already uses that space.\n\n\n\n\n\nSome things in the mockups need decisions:\n1. **A or B?** I recommend A.\n2. **Capacity.** Milestones have no capacity field today, so I've only shown the total estimate. A "31h / 40h" capacity bar would need a new field in Gaia. I'd start without it and keep this change Prometheus-only.\n3. **Backlog order.** Issues have no rank field, so the backlog is sorted by priority and then issue number. Ordering it by hand would also need a Gaia field. I'd leave that out for now too.\n\nOnce you've picked a direction I'll revise the screens and propose the plan.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search sprint planning backlog board milestone 2>&1 | he