752791b36ae2-fb26-79e3-4a2994d3452e	e53706516ae2-baab-7f50-a57680d4b6c5	Here's the plan:\n\n- **Planning view.** It's a second view of the Task Board at `?view=planning`. It reuses the milestones and backlog issues the board already loads, so there are no new API calls and no Gaia changes. You move issues by dragging them or with **Move to ▾**. Both save the issue's milestone the same way dropping a card on a tab does today.\n- **Capacity is calculated, not stored.** It's the team's velocity: the average estimated hours closed per working day over the last three completed sprints. That rate is multiplied by the working days (Mon–Fri) of the sprint being planned.\n  - Each sprint box shows "31h of 38h capacity" with a bar: amber above 90%, red above 100%.\n  - Until the project has completed a sprint, the box shows the estimate only.\n  - This takes one extra query for the last three completed sprints and their issues.\n- **No rank.** The backlog is sorted by priority, then by issue number.\n\n**Left out for now:**\n- Ordering the backlog by hand.\n- Capacity per assignee.\n- Planning on a narrow screen. The two columns stack, which works but isn't designed for.\n- Closing a sprint from the Planning view. **Mark as complete** stays on the Board view.\n\n\n\nThis is two Prometheus issues, one after the other: the capacity issue builds on the view's milestone boxes.	message	["Searching the code in .", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/board.js", "Reading prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/board.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes/app/project/board.js", "Reading prometheus/translations/en-us.json", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/models/issue.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/board.js", "Updating the knowledge map"]	747149a36ae2-fb26-79e3-15ac538f81b1	0.368724	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-28 15:02:13	f	[{"uploa