ca1c18a06ae2-5b7d-26f7-0d90e0d63cd1	90ec8e946ae2-5b7d-26f7-517aea1bffe5	The card subject has no wrap rules. In `prometheus/app/styles/modules/board.scss:281`, `.issue-card-subject a` sets only the font size (1.8rem), line height and `display: block`. The browser wraps only at spaces, so an unbroken token like `OAuthServer::addRefreshTokenGrant` runs past the card. This is a small CSS fix in one issue. Bug #3156 ("Taskboard Content overflow", done) was about the card body, not the subject, so this isn't a duplicate.\n\n**What I'd do:**\n1. **Break long words.** Add `overflow-wrap: anywhere` to the subject so a long token breaks mid-word at the card edge. Normal words still wrap at spaces.\n2. **Cap tall subjects.** A 10–15 word subject at 1.8rem takes about 4–6 lines on a narrow lane. I'd limit it to 3 lines with an ellipsis (`-webkit-line-clamp`, which works in all current browsers). A `title` attribute on the link shows the full subject on hover, and the quick view shows it too.\n\n**One question:** should the subject be cut to 3 lines, or always show in full?\n- **3 lines (my recommendation):** cards stay the same height, so lanes are easier to scan.\n- **In full:** say "no clamp" and I'll drop point 2. The word-break fix alone already stops the overflow.\n\nI left out a smaller font for long subjects and any change to the quick view or the issue page.	message	["Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/styles/modules/board.scss", "Reading prometheus/app/styles/modules/board.scss", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search board card subject overflow wrap --project aprom 2>&1 ", "Updating the knowledge map"]	c974dfe76ae2-5b7d-26f7-5fa01915a48d	0.703026	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb70