478733616ae5-4d5d-ae8f-4fb0f74175f2	d87ad5636ae5-1449-ae8f-5808a9dddbf1	## The fatal error\n\nThe bug is in Gaia, in `PreviewController.php`. Nothing in 4222 caused it. The controller was never wired up properly, so every `/preview/get/...` link fails: idea screens, images pasted into idea messages, and wiki images. The problems:\n\n- The `use Gaia\\MVC\\Models\\Downloadtoken;` line is missing. `DownloadController` has it, so `new Downloadtoken()` fails. That's your error.\n- Behind that are more bugs that would show up next:\n  - It reads the `readAll()` result without `['baseModel']`.\n  - It finds the file through a relation named after `relatedTo`. `Downloadtoken` only defines `issueUpload` and `wikiUpload`, so an idea upload would still fail.\n  - It pastes the token from the URL straight into the query instead of using bound parameters.\n  - It sends the response twice (`readfile` + `send()`).\n- It also returns any file type for display in the browser, from the API's own domain. An uploaded HTML file would run there as a page, which is a cross-site scripting risk. A preview endpoint should only serve images.\n\n## 1. Preview in a modal\n\nAgreed. Clicking a screen in the thread or the plan box opens it full size in a modal on the idea page, using the existing `bootstrap-modal` with only a Close button. No new tab.\n\n## 2. Downloading without authentication\n\nNo, I didn't assume that. Here is how it works today:\n\n1. Prometheus makes a normal authenticated request (`GET /upload?id=X&download=true`). Gaia checks the user can see that upload (`assertUploadInScope`), then creates a token.\n2. The token is a random GUID. It works **once** and expires after **10 minutes**.\n3. `/preview/get/<token>` itself has no auth header, because an `<img src>` can't send the Bearer token. The token takes its place. Once used, the link is dead, which is also why reopening an old link fails.\n\nSo only a user who passed the access check can get a link, and only for a short time. The remaining risk is that someone who copies an unused link could open it once within those 10 minutes.\n\nIf you'd rather have no URL-based access at all, the alternative is for Prometheus to fetch the image with the token-authenticated adapter and show it from a local in-memory URL. That's a larger change to how uploads are served, and it affects wiki and issue files too. I'd keep the token for now and make the endpoint safe with the fix below. Say if you want the stricter version planned.\n\n## Plan\n\nThere are two issues and they can go in parallel. The Prometheus one is built and tested against Mirage, so it doesn't need the Gaia fix to start, but you'll only see real images once the Gaia fix is in.\n\nLeft out:\n- Images pasted into messages still open in a new tab. They're handled by a different piece of code (`render-markdown.js`). Say if you want them in the modal too and I'll add an issue.\n- Smaller images for the plan box.\n- The stricter no-token option above.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Gaia: get idea", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/PreviewController.php", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4222 2>&1 | head -60", "Searching for \\"Downloadtoken\\" in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/core/config/routes.php", "Searching the code in gaia", "Listing gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/{Download,Upload,Preview}*.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app", "Searching the code in gaia/core", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/UploadController.php", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/DownloadController.php", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/prometheus/app && cat services/upload-preview.js components/idea/message-screen.js ", "Reading prometheus/app/services/upload-preview.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/message-screen.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/message-screen.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Reading prometheus/app/components/bootstrap-modal.js", "Listing prometheus/app/templates/components/bootstrap-modal.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/components/bootstrap-modal.hbs", "Updating the knowledge map", "Updating the knowledge map"]	46d842866ae5-4d5d-ae8f-beedf12089a3	0.738059	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-31 14:20:55	f	\N
