0b1996246ae6-01ee-104b-f696a2fbbdb8	34bdca956ae6-8157-e410-2af2948f16f3	I went through the 9 Prometheus issues in the Agents milestone (4036–4038, 4044, 4045, 4056–4059) and checked each against the Gaia code. The local `gaia` checkout is out of date, so I read the newest copy in `.runs/issue-4220`. Every Gaia issue they depend on is done (4027–4032, 4049–4053).\n\nThe UI is all still to build: Prometheus has no agent or workflow code yet. All nine issues were written on 2026-10-20 from the mockups, before the backend existed. They describe the screens well but leave out most of what the backend actually does. I wouldn't hand them to Agamemnon as they are.\n\n## Blockers (Agamemnon would stop or build the wrong thing)\n\n1. **No node-kind catalog from Gaia (4038, 4057).** The node kinds, their config fields and their output ports exist only in Gaia's `NodeKindCatalog.php`. `GET /workflowevent` lists triggers only. The palette and the properties panel would have to copy that list by hand and would drift from Gaia. I suggest a read-only `GET /workflownodekind` in Gaia, built like `WorkfloweventController`.\n2. **An Active workflow can't be edited (4038).** While a workflow is Active, Gaia refuses structural node and edge changes; only moving or renaming a node is allowed. Activating checks the whole graph and raises the version. The editor needs a flow for this (disable or draft, edit, re-activate) and must show the graph errors that come back.\n3. **There's no bulk graph save (4038).** "Save" means separate POST, PATCH and DELETE calls for each node and edge. Nodes have to exist before the edges that point at them, and a failure partway leaves half a graph saved. The issue doesn't mention any of this.\n4. **The graph library is undecided (4038).** The issue says a new library needs approval first, so Agamemnon would stop and ask. This needs deciding before it starts.\n\n## Missing details per issue\n\n- **4044 (agents module):**\n  - Creating an agent also needs `email` and `accountStatus`, because the agent is also a user.\n  - `maxRunsPerIssue` isn't mentioned.\n  - `modelConfig` must be a JSON object.\n  - `permissionMode` is free text in Gaia; the issue needs to name the allowed values.\n  - The Prometheus user model has no `type` field, so the AGENT badge has nothing to read.\n  - Comments and time logs carry only a user id and name, so the badge needs a lookup (members list) on those screens.\n  - The issue says "Admin › Agents", but the app now has a Settings menu with groups (Access, Projects, System). This should be a new group under Settings.\n- **4045 (credentials):**\n  - "Rotate" is just another `POST /agentcredential {agentId}`; Gaia revokes the old secret itself.\n  - The secret only ever comes back in that one 201 response.\n  - A user can't manage the credentials of the agent they are signed in as.\n  - It needs `agent.update` on top of the credential permission.\n- **4036 (tools and skills):**\n  - Refresh is `PATCH /toolserver/{id}` with `refresh: true`. A failure comes back as a 502, and the server's `refreshError` field holds the reason.\n  - Skills have file attachments and a version, which the issue doesn't mention.\n  - A grant is either a whole server or a single tool (`toolServerId` or `toolId`), plus `permissionRule`.\n- **4037 (identities):** The user record has no link to its identities, so they're read with a query on `userId`. Read access to the user's profile must also cover their identities.\n- **4056 (workflow list):**\n  - The trigger is a node, not a field on the workflow.\n  - The actors column comes from `references`.\n  - "Runs in 7 days" and "last run" have no aggregate in Gaia; they'd take one query per row.\n  - `scope` is a JSON list of project ids, and an Active workflow needs at least one.\n- **4057 (properties panel):**\n  - The run-agent node has more settings than the issue lists: session, model, maxTurns, claimTimeout and timeout.\n  - The issue doesn't give the config shape of each kind: filter `conditions`, switch `cases`, and expressions written as `{issue.assigneeId}`.\n- **4058 (runs and test run):**\n  - A test run is `POST /workflowrun` with `test: true`. It takes `entityId`, `changes` (for update triggers) and `actorPorts` (which way each simulated actor step goes). The issue mentions none of these.\n  - It has no live updates: Gaia sends no Hermes events for runs.\n  - It draws on the canvas, so it should wait for 4038.\n- **4059 (agent's workflows box):** Gaia only records a reference from a node setting that points directly at a user or agent (a Run agent node, for example). A filter never creates one, so "referenced in filter" can never appear.\n- **Ask a user:** nothing missing in the UI. The user answers by commenting on the record.\n\n## Order and size\n\nThe dependencies only list Gaia issues. The real order inside Prometheus:\n\n- 4045, 4037, 4036 and 4059 build on the agent page from 4044.\n- 4057 and 4058 build on the editor from 4038.\n\nAs written, the dispatcher would start all of them at once.\n\nThree issues are well over the 15-file budget:\n\n- **4044** is a whole module plus a badge on every place a user appears.\n- **4036** is three admin screens plus grants.\n- **4038** is the canvas, the palette and the save flow.\n\nEach should be split.\n\n## Decisions before I write the plan\n\n1. **Fixing the issues:** I can't edit existing issues. I'd write a plan of replacement issues that include these details, then you mark 4036, 4038, 4044 and 4056–4058 won't-fix. 4037, 4045 and 4059 are small enough to keep: you'd add the missing details to them yourself. **Recommended: yes.**\n2. **Graph library:** **Recommended: our own SVG layer** (nodes as boxes in HTML, edges as SVG paths). It adds no dependency, and pan, zoom and fit are small.\n3. **Node-kind catalog:** **Recommended: one new Gaia issue** for `GET /workflownodekind`, which 4038 and 4057 depend on. For the list, **recommended: drop "runs in 7 days" and keep "last run"** (one query for the visible rows).\n\nOnce you answer, I'll send the full plan.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Gaia: project options aprom", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search agent --project aprom 2>&1 | head -60; dev-tools/ai/ai", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search --help 2>&1 | head -30; for q in workflow \\"agent run\\" ", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search workflow --project aprom", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search \\"agaia-4026\\"", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search \\"agaia-4048\\"; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search agent --projec", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && for n in 4044 4045 4036 4037; do dev-tools/ai/ai kb show $n --project aprom 2>&1", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4044", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4045", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4036", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4037", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4038", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4056", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4057", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4058", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4059", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4026", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4031", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4053", "Listing gaia/app/metadata/model/{Agent,Tool,Skill,Useridentity,Workflow,Trigger,Credential,Oauth,User}*.php", "Listing gaia/app/api/