e2090d786ae8-203f-ed34-e9b349c440b6	48d0b1d36ad9-bd7c-a941-71476aac218e	I've refreshed the plan. I couldn't open the idea thread (the tool was denied), so if you meant changes you posted there, tell me what they are and I'll apply them.\n\n**Checked since last time:** no issue or code covers this yet. Nothing in `gaia` uses `tsvector`, `MATCHES` or a `search` metadata key, so the split stands.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Gaia issues now point to the docs.** Gaia's `docs/dev/bundles.md` §H ("Schema and migration infrastructure") lists which files to touch, in order. The issues name it, and test cases go in `client.json`.\n- **How to test the migration.** Run it only in a throwaway `gaia-gaia-test` container. Never run `p4m db migrate` from Pr4M: gaia-dev mounts the other checkout, and a stale migrate drops columns (adt-4150).\n- **The test database needs nothing new.** The `'simple'` full-text config and GIN indexes are built into Postgres, so `prepare-test-db.sh` stays as is. pg_trgm stays out of scope.\n- **Prometheus issue: guard after destroy.** The search task must check `isDestroying`/`isDestroyed` after the request returns, so a reply that comes back late doesn't touch a destroyed component.\n- **Empty search text.** Input that's empty after cleaning returns an error, not every row.\n\nMy assumptions from the first plan still apply, unless you say otherwise:\n- "Vectors" means Postgres full-text search, not pgvector embeddings.\n- "Fuzzy" means each word matches as a prefix, with no typo tolerance.\n- Only Issue subject and description are searchable on day one.	message	["Gaia: get idea", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search full text search vector 2>&1 | head -30; dev-tools/ai/", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/docs/dev/bundles.md"]	e12e8e076ae8-203f-ed34-3da54639dbe6	0.74971	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 07:46:42	f	\N
