84a936596ae8-8685-9cef-25e33e646303	395e4ef26ae8-8685-9cef-2a937ce05de0	You want every PR an agent opens to also get an `@coderabbitai full review` comment, so that CodeRabbit actually reviews it.\n\n**What I found**\n- Agents open PRs in one place only: `open_pr` in `dev-tools/ai/lib/workflow.py:166`. Both `ai pr` and `ai ship` call it. If the comment is posted from there, Talos runs and manual `/ship-issue` both get it, with no change to the agents' prompts.\n- `ai/config.json` already lists which repos use CodeRabbit (`codeRabbitRepos`: gaia, prometheus, hermes), and `coderabbit.enabled(repo)` checks that list. I'd post the comment only for those repos. Ares isn't in the list, so it gets nothing.\n- Nothing in dev-tools posts an `@coderabbitai` comment today. I couldn't search existing issues because shell access was denied this session, so please check that this isn't already filed.\n\n**Decisions I've made (say if you disagree)**\n- If posting the comment fails, the run prints a warning and carries on. The PR is already open by then, so a failed comment shouldn't stop the handoff.\n- When `ai ship` resumes and finds a PR it opened earlier, it won't post the comment again. That avoids duplicate comments.\n- The comment text goes in `config.json` (`codeRabbitTrigger`) so it can be changed without touching code.\n- If CodeRabbit's automatic review ever comes back on, these repos would get two reviews per PR. The `codeRabbitTrigger` setting is the switch to turn the comment off.\n\nThis is one small issue. The merged change only takes effect after `p4m runtime update` and a restart of `talos run`.	message	["Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching the code in dev-tools", "Searching the code in dev-tools/ai/lib/coderabbit.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools/ai/lib/ship.py", "Reading dev-tools/ai/lib/ship.py", "Reading dev-tools/ai/lib/coderabbit.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools", "Reading dev-tools/ai/lib/workflow.py", "Running c