badb2f536ae8-ebca-18a1-fe07276fcd85	3719f7d96ae4-aec9-1141-4c8f45c64770	This has already been built. **aprom-4198, "Show a pending comment while it is being posted"**, is marked done. It was shipped as prometheus#578 on 2026-10-30, and its code is in the current Prometheus checkout. It does what you describe:\n\n- **On Post:** only that comment box is cleared. The old global `clearContents` that wiped every open editor is gone.\n- **While saving:** the comment appears right away at the end of the list. It's dimmed, shows your avatar and name, and has an animated "Posting..." with dots (`conversation-ui/pending-comment.hbs`).\n- **Once saved:** the pending item is removed and the real comment shows.\n- **If the save fails:** the pending item stays, marked as not posted, with Retry and Discard buttons, so the text isn't lost. Your idea didn't mention this case.\n- **Where:** both conversation comments and issue comments (`conversation-ui/comment-composer`, used in `conversation-item.hbs` and `issue-details.hbs`).\n\nSo I'm not proposing a plan, because it would only duplicate 4198. Some possible reasons you still see the old behaviour:\n\n1. **Your environment is older than #578.** It may not be merged into `dev`, or not deployed where you tested. Check the PR's state first.\n2. **It's there but doesn't behave right**, for example it flickers, the dots are too subtle, or the order is wrong on a slow connection. Tell me what you see and I'll plan a focused bug issue against 4198.\n3. **You want something more**, like a different look or the pending state in other places (the issue description box, chat messages). Tell me which, and I'll plan that as a follow-up.\n\nWhich of these fits?	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching issues: comment posting pending optimistic --project aprom 2>&1 | head -40", "Reading issue 4198 2>&1 | head -80", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/conversation-ui", "Reading prometheus/app/components/conv