ca8706316ae8-69dc-04c3-a054e5d023d4	3719f7d96ae4-aec9-1141-4c8f45c64770	Yes. I followed the whole path this time, and in this checkout the feature is wired end to end on both screens:\n\n1. **Conversations.** `conversation.hbs:130/154` passes `saveComment` → `conversation-item.hbs:82` renders `ConversationUi::CommentComposer` with `@save={{@saveComment}}`.\n2. **Issue page.** `issue-details.hbs:217` renders the same composer with `@save={{this.saveComment}}`.\n3. **Clicking Post** calls `CommentComposer.post()` (`comment-composer.js:96`). It adds the comment to `pendingComments`, clears only this composer's editor, then queues the save.\n4. **Pending display.** `comment-composer.hbs:1-9` shows each pending comment above the input box, through `PendingComment`: dimmed, "Posting" with three animated dots (`conversation.scss:190-201`, `_animations.scss:29`).\n5. **The save handlers return the real promise:** `conversation.js:457` and `issue-details.js:729/740`. So the pending item stays until the server answers. Then it's removed, and the saved comment, already pushed into the list, takes its place.\n6. **On failure** the handlers clean up the unsaved record and rethrow. The composer marks the pending comment "not posted" with Retry and Discard.\n\nWhat I haven't done is run it in a browser. I can't check git either, so I can't tell whether this checkout matches `dev` or what's deployed where you tested.\n\nIf the feature isn't in your build, the cause is probably that prometheus#578 isn't merged or deployed there. If you are seeing it and it doesn't look or behave right, tell me what you see and I'll plan the fix.	message	["Reading prometheus/app/components/conversation/conversation-item.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/conversation-ui/comment-composer.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Reading prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/conversation.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/issue/issue-details.js"]	\N	0.303756	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-2298