090e52e06ae8-a01d-04c3-a354094578f4	ca4b85356ae8-4b25-04c3-5f32a380596a	Two copies of Talos were running at once. Each ran its own Nestor, and each one answered your message.\n\n**What the log shows** (`dev-tools/talos/state/talos.log`; I couldn't open the idea thread itself because the Gaia idea tool was denied):\n\n```\n17:10:13 [nestor] idea #3719f7d9… turn queued (event idea.message.created from user 7ea8b586…)\n17:10:13 [nestor] idea #3719f7d9… turn queued (event idea.message.created from user 7ea8b586…)\n17:10:48 [nestor] idea #3719f7d9…: replied ($0.30)\n17:10:48 [nestor] idea #3719f7d9…: replied ($0.28)\n```\n\nOne message was queued twice in the same second, and both replies landed at the same second. A single Nestor can't do that:\n\n- **It skips duplicates.** `IdeaWorker.submit` (`dev-tools/talos/lib/ideas/worker.py:39-50`) ignores a job for an idea that's already queued or running.\n- **It runs one turn at a time.** Two replies finishing together means two separate workers ran side by side.\n\nEarlier lines in the log show the second process:\n\n- From 16:16 on, every Nestor listener event appears twice: two "ping timeout" disconnects, two reconnects and two "listening to Hermes" lines (lines 1424–1441).\n- At 17:06:54 only one Talos logged `stopped`, and a new one started at 17:06:57. The older process kept running and stayed connected to Hermes. It was probably started by the 15:44 `talos run`.\n\nBoth processes got the `idea.message.created` event from Hermes. Each one's in-memory duplicate check only knows about its own queue, and neither had saved `answered_upto` yet when the other started. So both ran a full turn: the second reply cost an extra ~$0.28.\n\n**Fix now:** stop the extra Talos process (`ps aux | grep talos`, keep the newest, kill the other). Until then, every message on any idea will get two answers, and approvals could create issues twice.\n\n**Proper fix:** `talos run` doesn't stop you from starting a second copy. I searched the code and found no lock or pid file. Adding one would make a second `talos run` exit with "already running (pid N)". It should use a lock file under `LOCAL_DIR` that works on both Windows and Linux. That's one small `A Dev Tool` issue. Bash was blocked here, so I couldn't check the kb for an existing issue. If you want, I'll plan it as a short plan with that one issue.	message	["Gaia: get idea", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/dev-tools/talos && ls; ls state state/nestor 2>/dev/null | head -50", "Running grep -n \\"3719f7d96ae4\\" state/talos.log | tail -40; ls state/logs | tail; sqlite3 state/talos.db \\".tables\\" 2>&1", "Searching for \\"3719f7d96ae4\\" in dev-tools/talos/state/talos.log", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/talos.log", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/ideas/worker.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/talos.log", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/talos.log", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/talos.log", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/talos.log", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos"]	\N	0.296211	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 12:16:09	f	\N
16c274476ae8-a01d-04c3-3d190ede2afc	ca4b85356ae8-4b25-04c3-5f32a380596a	You got two answers because **two Talos processes were running, and each had its own Nestor.** Both got your message and both replied.\n\nI couldn't open the idea itself because the Gaia tool was denied, so this comes from `dev-tools/talos/state/talos.log`.\n\n**What the log shows**\n```\n17:10:13 [nestor] idea #3719f7d9… turn queued (event idea.message.created from user 7ea8b586…)\n17:10:13 [nestor] idea #3719f7d9… turn queued (event idea.message.created from user 7ea8b586…)\n17:10:48 [nestor] idea #3719f7d9…: replied ($0.30)\n17:10:48 [nestor] idea #3719f7d9…: replied ($0.28)\n```\n- One Talos process can't do this. `IdeaWorker.submit` (`dev-tools/talos/lib/ideas/worker.py:39`) skips a job that's already queued, and turns run one at a time. Two "queued" lines in the same second, then two replies in the same second, mean two separate processes.\n- The second process started at **15:39:19**: there's a `[talos] starting` line with no `stopped` before it, so the 15:32 instance was still running.\n- After that, every Nestor listener event shows up twice: the disconnects at 16:16, 16:34 and 17:04, and the two reconnects at 17:04:44 and 17:04:45.\n- The restart at 17:06 only replaced one of the two, so there were still two when you wrote at 17:10.\n- Each process keeps its own in-memory queue. Both read the stored `answered_upto` before either had answered, so both decided your message was unanswered.\n\n**What to do now**\n- Check for duplicates with `ps aux | grep "talos.py run"` (or `pgrep -af talos`) and stop the extra one.\n- This affects more than Nestor. Both processes also run Agamemnon, and at least one runs Odysseus, so issue work can be picked up twice too.\n\n**The real fix (dev-tools)**\n1. **Single-instance lock for `talos run`:** an OS file lock in `dev-tools/state` that works on Windows and POSIX. A second `talos run` would refuse to start and say which PID holds the lock. Right now there's no guard at all.\n2. **Atomic turn claim in Nestor:** claim `answered_upto` with a compare-and-set before launching Claude. A turn that loses the claim logs "nothing new to answer" and stops. This protects the conversation even if two processes somehow run again.\n\nIf you want, I can plan these as A Dev Tool issues. I'd make the lock `simple` and the turn claim `complex`. I couldn't search the existing issues (that command was denied too), so I'd check for duplicates first. I also tried to note this in my knowledge map, but the edit was denied, so it isn't recorded there yet.	message	["Gaia: get idea", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/dev-tools/talos; ls; ls state state/nestor 2>/dev/null | head -50", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/dev-tools/talos; grep -n \\"3719f7d96ae4\\" state/talos.log | tail -40; ls state/", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/dev-tools/talos; sed -n 1465,1480p state/talos.log; grep -rn \\"turn queued\\" --", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/talos.log", "Searching for \\"turn queued\\" in dev-tools/talos", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/ideas/policy.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/ideas/worker.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/talos.log", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/talos.log", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos", "Running /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/dev-tools/ai/ai kb search talos single instance two processes duplicate --projec", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.436348	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 12:16:22	f	\N
