4ea66b956ae8-042c-3709-6a7d3dfa1826	ca4b85356ae8-4b25-04c3-5f32a380596a	I'll plan this as one issue. It reuses the lock helper the other dev tools already use, `dev-tools/installer/filelock.py`. It works on both Windows and POSIX, the OS releases the lock if the holder dies, and it records the holder's PID.\n\n- **Change:** `cmd_run` (`dev-tools/talos/talos.py:36`) takes `filelock.held(STATE_DIR / "talos-run.lock", wait_seconds=0)` before anything else.\n  - Lock busy: it exits non-zero with a `TalosError` that names the running instance via `describe_holder`. That gives you the PID and command line so you can stop it.\n  - Lock free: it starts as today.\n- **Lock path:** `STATE_DIR` is built from `LOCAL_DIR`, so the runtime copy and the `dev-tools/` checkout use the same lock file. That stops the runtime copy and the checkout from running side by side.\n- **Dry runs:** `--dry-run` takes the lock too, because its dispatchers still listen and react.\n- **Restarts:** a quick stop-then-start (like your 17:06 restart) works, because a dead process no longer holds the lock.\n- **Left out:** the atomic Nestor turn claim, as agreed. Other long-running commands aren't changed either.\n\nI couldn't search the issues for duplicates, because `ai kb search` was denied. I also still couldn't save this to my knowledge map, because Edit was denied.	message	["Searching the code in dev-tools/talos", "Reading dev-tools/talos/talos.py", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/agamemnon/wiring.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools/installer", "Reading dev-tools/installer/filelock.py"]	4dcc90a56ae8-042c-3709-e9715bfa8eb1	0.166465	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 12:30:06	f	\N
