1397e5366ae8-a030-ab99-640951fee80a	ab9b79d46ae8-749b-ab99-c04ee42421fc	**The idea:** when someone has an issue open, status changes and new comments made by others appear without a reload.\n\n**What I found: only Prometheus needs to change.**\n- **Status:** Gaia already publishes `issue.status.changed` on every issue update (`IssueLiveEventsComponent`), and Hermes already allows that event.\n- **Comments:** on the issue page, comments are posted to the issue's conversation room (`issue-details.js` `_createComment` uses `relatedTo: 'conversationrooms'`). So Gaia already publishes `conversation.comment.created/updated/deleted` for them, with the room id in `meta.conversationId`. No new event names and no Gaia or Hermes work.\n- **The gap:** the issue page doesn't listen for these events yet. Prometheus decision D-011 says so on purpose: "issue detail is not live". This plan reverses that decision for the issue page, so the docs need updating too.\n- **Patterns to reuse:**\n  - `controllers/app/project/idea/page.js` only handles events for the open idea; the issue page can do the same for the open issue.\n  - `conversation.js` already has handlers for created, updated and deleted comments.\n- **Risk:** Talos and the MCP client change status by sending only `statusId`. In that case the event has no status name (this is why the board misses those changes, aprom-3978). The handler has to look the name up in the project's statuses, or this feature will miss changes made by agents.\n\n**Proposed approach:** one Prometheus issue. The issue page subscribes to these events while it is open, ignores events for other issues and other rooms, and updates the page in place.\n\n**Questions (my recommendation in brackets):**\n1. Should the assignee update live as well? Gaia already publishes `issue.assignee.changed`, so it's one more handler. (Not now: you asked for status and comments.)\n2. Should the activity list update live? (No. It's built when the page loads; leave it for later.)\n3. Should a new comment from someone else show a notice, or just appear? (Just appear.)\n\n**Left out:** assignee, dates, activity list, the issue list page, and the wiki.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching issues: realtime issue detail status comments socket 2>&1 | head -60", "Running ls */docs/architecture/live-updates/ 2>/dev/null; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 3978 2>&1 | head -60", "Running cat prometheus/docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md; grep -n \\"^#\\" prometheus/docs/architecture/live-updates/archi", "Running sed -n 55,92p prometheus/docs/architecture/live-updates/architecture.md; sed -n 24,128p gaia/docs/architecture/live-upda", "Running sed -n 79,96p gaia/docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md; cat gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/Conver", "Running grep -rn \\"idea\\\\.\\\\|EVENT_ALLOWLIST\\\\b\\" hermes/src --include=*.js | grep -v test | head; grep -n \\"const \\\\|ALL\\" gaia/app/api", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/prometheus && ls app/routes/app/project/issue* app/controllers/app/project/is", "Listing prometheus/app/{routes,controllers}/app/project/issue*/**", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/idea/page.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes/app/project/issue/page.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/issue/page.js", "Reading prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/issue/page.js", "Reading prometheus/app/routes/app/project/issue/page.js", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events", "Searching for \\"relatedTo\\" in prometheus/app/components/issue", "Reading prometheus/app/components/issue/issue-details.js", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/support/ProjectIdResolver.php", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/conversation.js", "Updating the knowledge map"]	12c193936ae8-a030-ab99-f6982c48715b	0.655994	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6f