aba68d546ae8-bf33-0ad0-91d816757fd5	34bdca956ae6-8157-e410-2af2948f16f3	Here are the issues for the four problems, one each, plus a Gaia request that bug 3 turned up. Your list starts at 2: if there was a point 1, send it and I'll add it.\n\n**What I found in the merged code:**\n\n- **2. Stuck on create:** this is a bug in the shared create controller.\n  - The base controller (`controllers/prometheus/create.js` ~l.222) neither waits on nor catches the step that runs after the agent is saved.\n  - For agents, that step saves the user's status, roles and project memberships. If any of those calls fails, the page never moves on and shows no error. The agent itself is already saved.\n  - Likely culprit: memberships are created with `deleted: '0'`, but Gaia's Membership has no `deleted` column.\n- **3. Detail page 404:** the body starting "PhalconExc…" is Gaia's `public/index.php` (~l.233). It catches Phalcon exceptions and prints them as plain text, not a JSON error.\n  - Prometheus can't parse that, so the real error is hidden.\n  - The page loads four things: the agent, roles, memberships and identities. Which one fails is still unknown, so the issue starts with finding it.\n  - The Gaia fix (always answer with a JSON error) is a separate request issue, so it can run in parallel.\n- **4. No profile picture:** the user page already has an upload-and-crop component. The agent pages don't use it, and the agent avatar always shows the robot, whatever the user's picture is.\n- **5. Projects select:** the multi-select component supports search, but the agent form never switches it on. The options aren't sorted, and why a click doesn't select is still unknown. It stays a multi-select. Roles get the same search and sorting.\n\n**Not in this plan:**\n- The Gaia node-kind catalog from my earlier review (the editor hard-codes the kinds today). Say if you still want it.\n- The list "runs in 7 days" column.\n\nThe issues will go in **Claude-v1** by default. The rest of the agent 