5c9863816ae8-7125-0ad0-05726b1aba09	f13058706ae8-bf33-0ad0-6d5a18240f8e	I read the issue detail code (`prometheus/app/components/issue/issue-details.{hbs,js}`). Two of your three points have clear causes. The attachment one needs a quick answer from you.\n\n**1. Opening attachments.** A preview already exists. Clicking the file name runs `previewFile`, which gets a one-time token and loads `/preview/get/<token>` into an iframe in a modal. That modal is only 35% wide (`.filePreviewModal` in `styles/modules/issue.scss`). Only the small name link opens it: the thumbnail and icon don't react to a click. And the iframe gets every file type, so a browser that can't show a type (docx, zip, …) downloads it instead. Gaia's `PreviewController` already serves files inline, so I don't think Gaia needs a change. This would be Prometheus-only.\n\n**2. Editing estimates.** I found the bug. In the edit-estimate modal the editor is wired as `@onContentChange={{@selectStatic this.editingLog 'description'}}`, without `fn` (`issue-details.hbs:420`). So it runs once while the modal renders instead of when the description changes. The edit-timelog modal next to it does it correctly. `editLog` also closes the modal and leaves the record half-changed when validation fails, and it has no error handling on save. Those get fixed in the same issue.\n\n**3. Long descriptions.** `.time-log .log-description` is set to one line with an ellipsis (`issue.scss` ~130), so anything longer is cut off. The fix: let the text wrap, cap the height and scroll inside it.\n\nTwo questions; my recommendation comes first in each:\n- **Attachments:** should clicking anywhere on the attachment (thumbnail, icon or name) open a wider modal? It would show images as images and PDFs, text and video in the viewer. Other types would show "No preview available for this file type" with a Download button. Leaving out: previews of Office documents (that needs a converter on the server).\n- **Descriptions:** wrap the text, cap the height at about 150px and scroll inside, the same in Estimates and Time logs?\n\nIf you say yes to both, here's the plan. The three issues are independent and can be worked in parallel.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching issues: attachment open preview --project aprom | head -40; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search estimate edit --project aprom | head -40", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/issue", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/issue/issue-details.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/issue/issue-details.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs", "Searching for \\"selectStatic\\" in prometheus/app", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/prometheus && grep -n '\\"est\\"\\\\|\\"spent\\"\\\\|\\"edited\\"\\\\|\\"preview\\"' translations/en-u", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/styles", "Searching the code in prometheus/translations/en-us.json", "Reading prometheus/app/components/issue/issue-details.js", "Searching the code in gaia/app", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/PreviewController.php", "Listing prometheus/app/components/idea/message-screen*", "Reading prometheus/app/components/idea/message-screen.hbs", "Updating the knowledge map"]	5bdbbd156ae8-7125-0ad0-2c3fb3fb0cea	0.640263	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 16:07:56	f	\N
