b6cc67f06ae8-1751-89d9-4cf7954c2648	48d0b1d36ad9-bd7c-a941-71476aac218e	Nothing new has changed the plan since the last version. Gaia still has no full-text code, and no new issue overlaps with this one. I also still can't read the idea thread, so I can't see any notes you posted there.\n\nThe open issues do include one that could share this work: **aprom-3776** ("Implement search functionality for issues in list section", status new). Once Gaia has the `Issue.search MATCHES` operator, that list search could use it instead of `CONTAINS`.\n\nI don't want to resend the same plan, so which of these did you have in mind?\n\n1. **Add aprom-3776 to the plan.** It would become a fifth, simple issue that uses `MATCHES` in the issue list search and depends on `issue-searchable`. I'd add it as a new Prometheus issue that points to aprom-3776, since I can't change an existing one.\n2. **Cover more models on day one**, such as Project name/description or Wiki. Each would be a small, simple Gaia issue that adds the metadata flag and api-tester cases.\n3. **Make search fuzzy beyond prefixes**, so typos still match. That adds pg_trgm: the extension in the migration plus a trigram fallback in the operator. It's a bigger, complex change.\n4. **Change the split**, for example merging the index and operator issues into one Gaia framework PR, or putting the issues in a different milestone.\n5. **Something else.** Tell me what to change and I'll send the full revised plan.	message	["Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search search --project agaia --status new 2>&1 | head -15; d", "Searching the code in gaia/core"]	\N	0.598533	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 18:55:50	f	\N
