6cf0a3036ae8-4e76-5f8b-b153be3473a3	22a9bd746ae8-4e76-5f8b-4f37d884cb93	Here's the idea as I understand it: today Talos's agents are defined in local `agent.json` files. You want them defined in Gaia (the Agent, Skill and Workflow modules that already exist), loaded live by Talos and signed in with their own agent credentials. You also want gaia-mcp to look up milestones so a completed milestone can be noticed and acted on.\n\n## What already exists\n- **Gaia is mostly ready.** It has Agent, Agentcredential (OAuth2 `client_credentials`, agaia-4028), Skill/Agentskill, Toolserver/Tool/Agenttool and the Workflow modules. The spec is served by a read-only `agentspec` resource (agaia-4043), not by `/agent/{id}/spec`. That resource returns the role prompt, models, limits, permission mode, tool grants and skill content in one document.\n- **adt-4041 (new, milestone "Agents") already covers your 3rd todo.** It switches gaia-mcp to `GAIA_CLIENT_ID`/`GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET` with `client_credentials`, and `p4m configure` asks for the secret. Today `Gaia.token()` in `gaia-mcp/server.py` uses the password grant. I'd reuse 4041 rather than plan a duplicate.\n- **adt-4047 (new) overlaps your 4th todo.** In it, Talos runs a workflow's "Run agent" steps (Hermes `workflow.agent.run.requested`) using the spec. It still waits on ah-4055.\n- **gaia-mcp has no milestone read tool.** Milestones only show up inside `project_options`, plus create/ensure. There are no tools for agents, skills or workflows either. Talos imports gaia-mcp's `Tools` in-process (`talos/lib/tracker.py`), so any lookup added there is available to Talos too.\n\n## Three questions that shape the plan\n1. **Milestone completion: who acts on it, and what happens?** I recommend that gaia-mcp gets `gaia_list_milestones`/`gaia_get_milestone`, returning status and open/done issue counts. Agamemnon would then check its `aga-` milestones on each sweep. When every issue is closed, it marks the milestone `completed` and comments or notifies you. Or do you only want the lookup for now?\n2. **What does "Talos executes a Gaia agent" mean on day one?** I recommend the smaller version: an `agent.json` gets a `gaiaAgentId`. Talos then takes the role prompt, model, turn limit, permission mode, skills and tool grants from `agentspec` at each run. Machine-local settings (repo paths, env file, worker pool) stay in `agent.json`, and runs are still triggered by issue assignment as today. Workflow-driven runs stay with adt-4047, after this.\n3. **adt-4041:** should it stay as the credentials issue, with you moving it to "aga-agentic system" and the new issues depending on it? I recommend yes. I can't move or edit issues myself.\n\nOnce you've answered, I'll send the plan. The likely shape is gaia-mcp milestone tools ∥ gaia-mcp agent/skill/workflow tools ∥ adt-4041, then Talos loading agents from Gaia (complex). If "aga-agentic system" doesn't exist in A Dev Tool yet, it will be created when the plan is approved.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M; ls dev-tools; ls dev-tools/gaia-mcp 2>/dev/null; ls .dev-tools-runtime/gaia-mcp; l", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search agent credential mcp 2>&1 | head -30; dev-tools/ai/ai kb", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M; ls .dev-tools-runtime/gaia-mcp .dev-tools-runtime/talos/lib .dev-tools-runtime/tal", "Listing .dev-tools-runtime/gaia-mcp/*", "Listing dev-tools/talos/{lib/*.py,agents/*/agent.json}", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search agentic agents runtime credentials --project adt 2>&1 | ", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4041 2>&1 | head -60; echo ======; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4043 2>&1 | head -40; echo =====; dev-tools/ai/ai kb searc", "Searching the code in .dev-tools-runtime/gaia-mcp/server.py", "