0e5748866ae9-639d-5b13-2e11d3ca3f27	b0c568b96ae9-5105-5b13-551a8315c38b	Here's how I read it: while the "Start an idea" form is open, the **New idea** button at the top of the idea browser turns grey and can't be clicked, because you're already creating one. When you open an existing idea or leave the form, it goes back to the normal blue button.\n\nThe two screens below show it:\n\n- **`create-open`**: the form is open and the New idea button is grey and disabled.\n- **`idea-open`**: an existing idea is open and the button looks like it does today.\n\n\n\n\n\n**How it would work:** the button is in `prometheus/app/templates/app/project/idea.hbs:9`. The idea controller would get the router service and an `isCreating` getter that is true while the route is `app.project.idea.create`. While it's true, the template shows a grey Bootstrap disabled button (`btn btn-default btn-sm disabled`, `aria-disabled="true"`) instead of the link, so you can't click it or reach it with Tab. This needs no backend change and fits in one small Prometheus issue.\n\n**Open question:** does "like disabled" mean grey, as in the screen? Or do you want it to stay blue but faded (`btn-primary disabled`)? I went with grey because you said not to use blue.	message	["Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/templates/app/project", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/app/project/idea.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/app/project/idea/create.hbs", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/prometheus; cat app/controllers/app/project/idea.js | sed -n 1,200p | grep -n", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/idea.js", "Reading prometheus/app/routes/app/project/idea/create.js", "Running /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/dev-tools/ai/ai kb search \\"new idea button\\" --project aprom", "Listing prometheus/docs/ui/screens