d082ceb06ae9-e9c5-bb3e-7185d320b520	a4ee4ed06ae9-e9c5-bb3e-1d547dcbeb34	I've confirmed how numbering works today and where the number is used to find an issue, so this is where things stand.\n\n**What you want:** each project counts its own issues from #1, so A Gaia and A Prometheus can both have #12. Today there is one global counter for every project.\n\n**How it works now**\n- Gaia uses one Postgres sequence for every project: `issues_issueNumber_seq` (`gaia/app/models/Issue.php:28`). `issueNumber` has to be unique across all issues (`gaia/app/metadata/model/Issue.php:224`).\n- Prometheus already looks issues up by project and number: `/app/:project/issue/:issue_number` queries `issueNumber AND projectId` (`routes/app/project/issue/page.js:99`). That part works with per-project numbers as it is.\n\n**Where the number alone finds an issue (these would break)**\n- **Gaia:** `Issue::findFirstByIssueNumber` in `IssuementionComponent.php:46` (the `#123` mentions in conversations) and in `IssueplanningController.php:59`.\n- **Prometheus:** `#123` links in the tag parser, notification links, `{{Issue@123}}` in activity text, and the gantt chart, board and calendar keyed by number (about 55 files use `issueNumber`; most only display it).\n- **Tooling outside the product:** the Gaia MCP tools (`gaia_get_issue issue_number`), `ai kb`, Talos, `ai start`, and branch names `claude-issue-NNNN`. All of them assume one number means one issue. Once numbers repeat across projects, each of these has to take a project too, for example `agaia-12`, a key like `AGAIA-12` (project short code plus number).\n\nSo creating the number is the small part: a counter per project, filled in when an issue is created. The real work is making every lookup carry the project.\n\n**Questions that shape the plan (my recommendation in bold)**\n1. **Existing issues: keep their numbers.** Each project's counter starts at its current highest number + 1, so links, branches and kb entries that already exist keep working. The alternative, renumbering every project from 1, breaks every old reference.\n2. **Show issues as `<SHORTCODE>-<n>` (e.g. `AGAIA-12`) and accept that form in mentions.** A bare `#12` would still mean "in the current project".\n3. **Scope: Gaia and Prometheus first, with the tooling (MCP, `ai`, Talos) as A Dev Tool issues in the same plan.** The tooling has to land before the first duplicate number appears, or agents will open the wrong issue. If you'd rather keep this idea to the product only, I'll leave the tooling out and flag it as a blocker for go-live.\n\nSay yes or adjust, and I'll come back with the plan.	message	["Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M; grep -n -i -E \\"issue ?number|issueNumber|short ?code|numbering\\" dev-tools/ta", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/app/models/Issue.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model/Issue.php", "Searching for \\"issueNumber\\" in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/IssuementionComponent.php", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/router.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes/app/project/issue/page.js", "Searching the code in gaia/app", "Searching the code in gaia/app"]	\N	0.159863	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-03 07:48:32	f	\N
