30707f546aea-40c3-be98-f3b31d76abfb	ba63ff326aea-3ad0-be98-b6a90d50524a	I found the cause. One request makes the database return so many rows that the API runs out of memory.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe issue **create** and **edit** screens in Prometheus (`routes/app/project/issue/create.js:37`, `edit.js:44`) load the project with `rels: members,milestones,issuetypes,issuestatuses`, `sort: members.name` and `limit: -1`.\n\nGaia joins every requested relationship into **one** SQL query (`Model::read` → `Relationship::prepareJoinsForQuery`). All four of those relationships are lists, so the query returns every combination of members × milestones × issue types × statuses as a separate row. For example, 20 members × 60 milestones × 10 types × 10 statuses is 120,000 rows for a single project. `RestController::prepareData` then converts and flattens each row, and the 128 MB memory limit runs out at line 1194. The limit doesn't help, because it applies to the joined rows, and here there is none.\n\nGaia has code to load list relationships in separate queries (`Model::executeQuery`), but it never runs. `passSplittingChecks` requires "≤ 3 relationships AND > 4 many-to-many relationships", which can never both be true. It is also turned off whenever there's a sort.\n\n`prometheus/CLAUDE.md` already says not to load list relationships through `rels` in the parent request. These two routes are old code that predates that rule.\n\n## Proposal\n\n1. **Prometheus fix (high):** load the project with only `members` (sorted by name, so one row per member) and fetch milestones, issue types and statuses with their own queries, in parallel. Keep the existing fallback to system statuses. This fixes the crash on its own.\n2. **Gaia framework fix (complex):** load each requested list relationship in its own query, keyed by the IDs of the records found, instead of joining them all. Replace the impossible check. This stops any client from crashing the API this way. It doesn't block 1.\n\n**Left out:** raising PHP's `memory_limit` (it only hides the problem) and a Gaia guard that rejects requests asking for several list relationships (it would break existing clients).\n\n**Question:** do you want both issues in this plan, or only the Prometheus fix with the Gaia change tracked for later? I recommend both: the Prometheus fix now and the Gaia one in parallel.\n\nI couldn't update my knowledge map; the edit was denied in this session, so these findings aren't saved for later conversations.	message	["Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M; grep -n -i \\"memory\\\\|RestController\\\\|limit\\\\|rels\\\\|query\\" dev-tools/talos/stat", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M; sed -n 1150,1215p gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php # raw", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search memory exhausted rels join 2>&1 | head -30; dev-to", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/gaia; grep -n -B2 -A8 \\"hasMany \\\\`rels\\\\`\\\\|Don't combine hasMany\\" docs/generate", "Searching the code in gaia/docs/generated/bundles/G.md", "Searching the code in gaia/docs/generated/models/Project.md", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/models", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/models/Query.php", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/models/Relationship.php", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/models/Model.php", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/models/Model.php", "Running sed -n 265,435p /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/gaia/core/mvc/models/Model.php # raw", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/gaia; grep -n \\"function passSplittingChecks\\" -A40 core/mvc/models/Model.php #", "Reading prometheus/app/routes/app/project/issue/create.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes/app/project/issue/edit.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Updating the knowledge map"]	2fa187f76aea-40c3-be98-52007f055b8d	0.628476	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-03 16:34:56	f	\N
