9b78acd46aea-58d1-813e-8769f12b2327	994b17496ae9-2420-fee8-e1f463ff8479	You aren't seeing the spinner because aprom-4267's change isn't in the app you're running yet. There may also be a second reason: the load may be too quick to notice.\n\n1. **The change isn't merged.** Odysseus opened [prometheus#617](https://github.com/projects4me/prometheus/pull/617) and moved aprom-4267 to `in_review`. The PR is waiting for you to review and merge it. The `prometheus` checkout in this workspace has none of it (`views.app.idea.progress.loading` doesn't appear anywhere), so if your app is built from this checkout, it's still the old code. To try it before merging, check out the PR branch (`claude-issue-4267`) and reload the app.\n2. **The load may be too quick to see.** Locally the plans request usually finishes in a few hundred milliseconds, so the spinner can show for less than a frame. To check it, open DevTools → Network, set throttling to **Slow 3G**, and reload the ideas page. Every open idea should show the grey "⟳ Loading" label until the plans response comes back.\n\nOn "right next to the title": the spinner doesn't sit beside the title. As in the screens, it takes the place of the status label on the **right** of each row (`label pull-right`, `data-idea-status`) and turns back into the status once loaded. If you want it beside the title instead, tell me and I'll plan that as a follow-up.\n\nI can't read the PR diff from here because shell access is denied. If neither of the checks above shows the spinner on the PR branch, tell me what you see and I'll plan a fix on top of aprom-4267.	message	["Searching the code in prometheus", "Gaia: get issue 4267", "Running gh pr diff 617 --repo projects4me/prometheus"]	\N	0.460815	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 07:24:11	f	\N
