af0c5b166aea-6fb0-813e-9c5b978d0d3b	994b17496ae9-2420-fee8-e1f463ff8479	I checked how the label is loaded, and part of your assumption doesn't hold. The idea model only has `status` = open or archived. The label in the browser (Brainstorming, Proposed, Created, …) comes from the **latest plan** (`ideaplan`). `routes/app/project/idea.js:66` queries plans separately, after the ideas have loaded. So the idea model resolving doesn't tell us the label yet. The skeleton has to run until the **plans query** resolves, which is the loading flag aprom-4267 already adds. Archived ideas get their label from the model, so they show "Archived" straight away.\n\nThe skeleton itself fits. Prometheus already has shimmer skeletons (`components/app-ui/skeleton/*`, `styles/components/skeleton.scss`, `.skeleton-line`). On each open idea, a short shimmering bar the size of a label replaces the spinner label, then turns into the real status.\n\n\n\n**What's in the plan:**\n- **Square edges:** `.skeleton-line` has a 0.4rem radius, which is legacy. The new scoped class `.idea-status-skeleton` in `idea.scss` sets it to label height, no margin and square edges, per the design system.\n- **Screen readers:** the bar is visually empty, so it carries a screen-reader-only "Loading" text.\n- **Shimmer:** the screen is a still image, so it can't show the shimmer. The app animates it.\n\n**How to ship it:**\n- **Recommended:** prometheus#617 isn't merged yet, so the cleanest route is to ask for this change on that PR. A review comment like "replace the spinner label with the skeleton bar described in …", handled with `/address-review`, keeps it to one PR and no new issue.\n- **Alternatively,** approve the follow-up below. It depends on aprom-4267, so #617 merges first.	message	["Searching the code in prometheus", "Reading prometheus/app/routes/app/project/idea.js", "Listing prometheus/app/{components/app-ui/skeleton/*,styles/**/*skeleton*}", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching the code