271e29556aec-a5ab-a4ea-dfebcaf283b7	c433e6f16aec-d3c1-a4ea-f400133f2b79	The "New" dropdown is at `application-header.hbs:30-39`. Each entry is a plain `LinkTo` with only a label. The icons can come straight from the nav menu metadata: Issue `fa-tasks`, Conversation `fa-comments`, Project `fa-briefcase`.\n\n**The shading needs your call.** The design system (`design-system.md` §1.4 and its checklist) forbids new shadows and gradients. The dropdown already has a legacy `box-shadow` that is too faint to show, and making it stronger would break that rule. So I've drawn two versions:\n\n- **A: icons only.** Same look as today, with a fixed-width icon before each name so the labels line up.\n- **B: icons plus depth from existing patterns (my recommendation).** The crimson 3px top border every `box-primary` has, and light separator lines between rows (AdminLTE's `box` + `nav-stacked`, as in the profile side boxes). This gives the menu edges and structure without new colours or shadows.\n\nThe real stylesheet draws both screens, so in B the separators and top border are AdminLTE's own styles. The real change would be a small rule in `header.scss`.\n\nOne detail for the build: the current `.create-module-btn i` style (extra left margin, 1.2rem) also hits icons inside the dropdown, because the menu sits inside the button. The fix has to limit that style to the caret.\n\nOnce you pick A or B (or ask for changes), I'll send the plan. It's one small `aprom` issue: template, `header.scss` and an integration test, about 3 files.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs", "Searching for \\"create-module\\" in prometheus/app/styles", "Searching for \\"icon:\\" in prometheus/app/utils/metadata/metadata.js", "Reading prometheus/app/styles/modules/header.scss", "Searching the co