9a46ccc86aeb-daa0-504d-d59d97795b26	393073e96aeb-daa0-504d-005f14c7084c	Your idea: replace the fixed green "Online" in the sidebar with a status that reflects what's actually happening.\n\n**What exists today**\n- The only status in the UI is the current user's own panel in the left sidebar (`prometheus/app/components/app-ui/nav-bar.hbs:10`, plus an old duplicate in `templates/components/nav-bar.hbs`). It's a hardcoded green dot with "Online", and it only ever shows **you**.\n- The right control sidebar has an "Online Users" list (`templates/components/application-controlbar.hbs`). Its component sets `users = []`, so the list is always empty.\n- Gaia already stores when each user was last seen. Every authenticated request updates `User.lastActivityAt` (`RestController::trackLastActivity`). User management and the agents list already show it ("5 minutes ago").\n- Hermes knows which users have a socket open, but its rules forbid it from keeping presence state: it is a relay with no storage, and only Gaia can publish events. True push-based presence would need a new Hermes decision record (ADR) plus a Gaia contract change, which makes it a cross-repo project.\n\n**The catch:** a status that only you see, on your own screen, is "Online" almost by definition. So "real time" has to mean one of these:\n\n1. **Your own connection state.** Online while Prometheus is connected to Hermes and the browser is online. "Away" when the tab has been hidden or idle for about 5 minutes. "Offline / reconnecting" when the connection drops. This is Prometheus-only and needs no contract change.\n2. **Other people's presence.** Fill the empty "Online Users" list: anyone active in the last ~5 minutes shows as online, idle up to 30 minutes as away. This uses `lastActivityAt`, refreshed every minute or so. It's Prometheus-only too (Gaia already has the data), but it's "near real time" (up to a minute's lag), not instant.\n3. **Instant push presence** for others through Hermes, with connect/disconnect events. This needs the Hermes ADR plus Gaia and Hermes work. I'd leave it out for now.\n\n**Questions (my recommendation in brackets):**\n1. Which meaning do you want? [Do 1 and 2, as two Prometheus issues; defer 3.]\n2. For 2, who counts? [Members of the selected project only, not every user in the system. Hide agents, or show them separately.]\n3. Do you want a status people set themselves (Busy / Do not disturb)? [No, not in this MVP.]\n\nThere's also something I'll log separately rather than fold in: `trackLastActivity` writes to the users table on every API request, and it builds its query by string concatenation. That's against Gaia's bound-parameter rule. The value comes from the token, so the risk is low, but it should be fixed in a small Gaia issue.\n\nOnce you confirm the scope, I'll send the plan.	message	["Running cat /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md; cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/P", "Searching for \\"Online\\" in prometheus/app", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search user online presence real time; ls hermes/src herm", "Searching issues: online users presence", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/nav-bar.hbs", "Reading hermes/CLAUDE.md", "Searching the code in gaia/docs/generated/models/User.md", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/components/application-controlbar.hbs", "Searching the code in hermes/docs/architecture/decisions.md", "Searching for \\"lastActivityAt\\" in gaia/app", "Searching the code in hermes/docs/architecture/decisions.md", "Reading hermes/docs/architecture/decisions.md", "Reading gaia/app/metadata/model/User.php", "Searching for \\"lastActivityAt\\" in .", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/application-controlbar.js", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php", "Reading prometheus/app/components/application-controlbar.js", "Searching for \\"lastActivityAt\\" in gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.ph