b5da5fb76aeb-63e3-c85a-f79c218c6e28	6327e0546aeb-63e3-c85a-4bc9562742d0	This is a big idea, and it overlaps with the **Collaborative Wiki** idea from yesterday (2026-11-03). Here's how I'd approach it.\n\n## What exists today\n- **Wiki** (Gaia model `Wiki`, Prometheus `routes/app/project/wiki.js`) is already a project-scoped tree of rich-text pages. Editing uses the Toast UI WYSIWYG editor and saves the whole document at once. There are no live events and no protection against stale writes, so the last save silently wins.\n- **Hermes can't carry live co-editing as it stands.** Its decision D-001 says it's a locked, stateless relay. Its decision D-002 says only Gaia can publish; browsers can't.\n- **Agents are already users.** There's a Gaia `Agent` model linked to `User`, and workflow runs already reach an agent through its own user scope (D-010). So an agent can be a real collaborator with a name, a cursor and an audit trail, not a hidden helper.\n- **Ares** only has `/planissue` today. There's no assist endpoint yet.\n\n## My take\n1. **Grow Wiki into Docs; don't build a second document module.** Two places for project documents would split search, permissions and links. The Wiki tree becomes the Docs tree. Google Docs extras (comments on a selection, suggestions, history) are added to the same model.\n2. **Real co-editing needs three new pieces.** Each is a real decision, so I'd start with a Research issue:\n   - **A shared-editing data model (Yjs).** Each person's changes merge automatically, without locking the document.\n   - **A new editor.** Toast UI can't do shared editing. I'd use Tiptap/ProseMirror, which has a mature Yjs binding.\n   - **A new stateful sync service.** It holds each open document in memory and relays edits and live cursors (a Hocuspocus-style Node service). It checks the user's token against Gaia (`user/me`) and project membership, and saves snapshots back to Gaia. Gaia stays the source of truth and the ACL authority, and Hermes keeps its rules.\n3. **Agents join as real participants.** An agent edits through the sync service as a server-side Yjs peer, using an MCP tool such as "edit doc section as agent X". Humans see its cursor and its text appearing live. Agents could edit through Gaia's REST API instead, but those edits would bypass the merging and overwrite whatever people typed at the same moment.\n4. **Agent edits land as suggestions by default.** People accept or reject them, like Google Docs' suggesting mode. This keeps a busy agent from rewriting a page under someone's cursor, and gives us a review trail.\n5. **Two ways to bring in an agent:**\n   - **Quick inline assist:** select text → "Rewrite / Summarize / Expand". This is a new Ares endpoint called through Gaia `LLM.php`, and it returns a suggestion.\n   - **Longer tasks:** @mention an agent in a doc comment, e.g. "@Odysseus draft the API section from aprom-4198". This reuses the workflow agent-run pattern (D-010). The agent works through MCP and edits live.\n\n## Rough phases\n| Phase | What | Repos |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | Research + decision record: editor, sync service placement/hosting, snapshot format, agent edit path, migrating existing Toast UI content | adt or ah |\n| 1 | Doc storage: Yjs snapshot + HTML/markdown copy for search and read view, plus revisions | agaia |\n| 2 | Sync service: auth via Gaia, rooms per doc, cursors, saves to Gaia | new service |\n| 3 | Tiptap editor in Docs with live cursors and avatars, replacing the Wiki edit page | aprom |\n| 4 | Agents as peers: MCP doc tools + suggestions mode | adt, aprom |\n| 5 | Inline assist through Ares | aa, agaia, aprom |\n| Later | Comments on a selection, version history UI, sharing outside the project, export to PDF/DOCX | — |\n\nPhases 1–3 alone are several weeks of work, and the sync service is a new deployable. That's why I'd start with the Research issue and not a dozen build issues.\n\n## Three questions that change the plan\n1. **Grow Wiki or add a separate "Docs" module?** I recommend growing Wiki, with a rename to "Docs" in the UI later if you like.\n2. **Should agent edits be suggestions people accept, or land directly?** I recommend suggestions by default, with an optional per-doc setting for direct edits later.\n3. **Can we add a new service and new dependencies (Yjs, Tiptap, Hocuspocus)?** House rules require approval for both, and there's no project for a new service yet. I recommend yes: the Research issue confirms the choice, and the service lives in a new repo. If you'd rather keep it to existing projects, I'd put it under A Hermes as a separate process with its own decision record.\n\nOnce you answer, I'll send the full plan: the Research issue first, then the Phase 1–3 build issues that depend on it. If it helps, I can also design the Docs editor screen (live cursors, agent avatars, suggestion sidebar).	message	["Running cat /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md 2>/dev/null | head -300", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search collaborative wiki editing realtime 2>&1 | head -4", "Gaia: list ideas aprom", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M; grep -n \\"D-00[1-9]\\" -A6 hermes/docs/*/decisions.md hermes/docs/**/decisions.", "Searching the code in hermes", "Listing ares/app/**/*.py in .", "Reading hermes/docs/architecture/decisions.md", "Searching the code in gaia/docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md", "Searching for \\"wiki\\" in dev-tools/gaia-mcp", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model/User.php", "Reading gaia/app/metadata/model/Wiki.php", "Searching for \\"'agent' =>\\" in gaia/app/metadata/model/User.php", "Searching for \\"wiki\\" in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/support/EventNames.php", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.389452	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 14:48:21	f	\N
