5a0ed3346aeb-f308-85f1-41bf1bc11ad2	599b10726aeb-f308-85f1-2dd28eca8a3d	Agamemnon should be able to start/restart docker engine if needed.\nAgamemnon should also be able to pause an issue if docker is overwhelmed due only to resume it when docker memory is free.\n\nI think in the last 50 issues, there were multiple that Agamemnon could have resumed but did not because its premise did not include anything related to docker.\n\nThis should happened with Agamemnon able to first understand the docker status i.e. started and its state, memory consumption and so on.	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-04 21:06:34	f	[]
