fa6b2d766aeb-f308-85f1-3d6face6cf67	599b10726aeb-f308-85f1-2dd28eca8a3d	Agamemnon should be able to see Docker's state (running or not, how much memory it is using), start or restart the engine when needed, and hold issues while Docker is short of memory, then give them back once it has room.\n\n## What exists today\n- **The premise allows almost nothing for Docker.** `docker_down` is only allowed to read, pause and notify (`talos/agents/agamemnon/premise.json`). The `pause` permission is granted, but no `aga` command uses it, so in practice Agamemnon can only report.\n- **The classifier only catches a stopped daemon** (`talos/lib/agamemnon/classifier.py`: "cannot connect to the docker daemon" and similar). Runs that died from running out of memory (exit 137, OOM kills, a killed ember build, the adt-4234 pattern) come out as `other` and go to you. That probably explains your "last 50 issues" observation. I can't read the run logs from here, so the plan asks for the patterns to be checked against real handbacks.\n- **Agamemnon is never given Docker's state.** The packet has a `docker` field, but `triage.py` fills it with `None`, and there is no command to read Docker.\n- **There are patterns to copy:** `UsagePause` (holding dispatch while a limit lasts) and `hold-until-tomorrow` plus `holds.release_due` (a hold released by the regular sweep). A Docker hold is the same thing with a condition instead of a time.\n\n## Proposed approach\n1. **Read Docker's state** in `talos/lib`: is the CLI there, is the daemon reachable, how much memory the VM has, how much each container uses, how many p4m test containers are running. From that, one verdict: `ok`, `pressured` or `down`.\n2. **Start and restart the engine** (Windows + Linux, behind `os.name`). This is the riskiest part: a restart also kills `gaia-dev`, Postgres and every other issue's test containers.\n3. **Hold dispatch** while Docker is down or short of memory, the same way `UsagePause` does. This is deterministic, with no AI involved, and it stops new runs piling onto a Docker that is already full.\n4. **New `aga` commands:** `docker` (read), `start-docker`, `restart-docker`, `hold-until-docker`. Held issues are given back one per sweep once memory is free, so they don't all start at once and run out of memory again.\n5. **A new `docker_pressure` incident type**, a wider `docker_down`, the premise and role updated, and the packet given Docker's state.\n\n## Questions (my recommendation in bold)\n1. **Who starts Docker?** **The dispatch hold starts the engine by itself when the daemon is down (cheap, no AI session). Restarts happen only in a triage session, and are refused while another issue has a run going, unless Docker is already unresponsive.**\n2. **Memory thresholds:** **hold above 85% of the Docker VM's memory, resume below 70%, both set in agent.json.**\n3. **Freeing memory** (stopping idle ember watch builds, cleaning up containers beyond what adt-4234 already removes): **left out of this plan.** I'd add it as a follow-up if holding issues turns out not to be enough.\n\n**Also left out:** remote Docker hosts and proactive alerts. Everything goes in **Claude-v1**. Earlier Agamemnon work used "aga-Parallel Runtime"; tell me if you want that milestone instead. The last two issues change protected Agamemnon paths, so their PRs fail the merge gate's `self` check and you'll need to merge them by hand.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/dev-tools; ls agamemnon; cat agamemnon/README.md | head -120; dev-tools/ai/ai kb se", "Searching issues: docker agamemnon", "Listing dev-tools/agamemnon/**/*", "Listing dev-tools/talos/agents/agamemnon/**/*", "Reading dev-tools/talos/agents/agamemnon/premise.json", "Reading dev-tools/talos/agents/agamemnon/role.md", "Reading issue 4228; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4232; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4234", "Listing dev-tools/talos/lib/{agamemnon,orchestrator}/*.py", "Searching for \\"docker\\" in dev-tools/talos/lib", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/agamemnon/classifier.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib/agamemnon/verbs.py", "Searching for \\"docker\\" in dev-tools/talos/lib/agamemnon/packet.py", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/agamemnon/verbs.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib/agamemnon/tool.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib/dispatcher.py", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/usage_pause.py", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/agamemnon/holds.py", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/agamemnon/tool.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools", "Searching issues: docker memory OOM pause --project adt; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search \\"docker desktop\\" restart", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos", "Reading dev-tools/agamemnon/README.md", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/agamemnon/triage.py", "Updating the knowledge map"]	f9978d376aeb-f308-85f1-013a3d7c8a09	0.926994	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 21:09:14	f	\N
