8743a0526aeb-4599-8fd2-2a0dc7e9dec6	599b10726aeb-f308-85f1-2dd28eca8a3d	Plan v2 is below. Everything is now in the existing **aga-agentic system** milestone.\n\n## What changed\n- **Local now, server later.** Engine control picks a default for the platform: Docker Desktop on Windows, `systemctl --user docker-desktop` on Linux. It also takes optional start and restart commands in agent.json, so a server can use something like `sudo -n systemctl restart docker` with a sudoers rule. Without a configured command, a rootful Docker install is refused, never prompted for. On a server, Talos may boot before Docker is ready, so the dispatch hold covers that: it just waits until Docker answers.\n- **85%** is now the threshold where dispatch holds. I kept 70% as the level where it resumes, so it doesn't flip on and off around 85%.\n- **"Stopping":** I took this to mean stopping an issue's p4m test containers to free memory (question 3 in v1). There's a new `docker-free` issue for it. When Docker is short of memory, it stops (doesn't remove) the test containers of issues that haven't changed in more than 72 hours, or that are in deferred or won't fix. It never touches an issue with a run going.\n  - Today's gc already removes test containers for done, closed and won't fix issues, but not for deferred or stale ones.\n  - I applied the same rule to Docker holds: a held issue goes to you after 72 hours, and the hold is dropped if the issue is moved to deferred or won't fix.\n  - If you meant only one of these, tell me.\n\nThe aga commands issue now also includes `stop-stale-containers`, so it is at 10 files.	message	["Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib/workspace_gc.py", "Gaia: list milestones adt", "Reading dev-tools/talos/lib/workspace_gc.py", "Updating the knowledge map"]	864be3b86aeb-4599-8fd2-6de56905ffbb	0.320385	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 21:20:07	f	\N
