b54f15126aeb-0633-6034-e02c28a2df3b	34bdca956ae6-8157-e410-2af2948f16f3	Well, its time to move onwards. When creating a workflow there are multiple issues. Some are visual, some are functional.\n\nIn the Run Agent step.\n\n1\\. In the Agent dropdown the agent profile image is not correctly picked up\\, its is showing a default state android avatar instead of the real image for the agent\\.\n2\\. In the same step in the dropdown the avatar is too big for the dropdown and is overflowing the boundaries of the dropdown item\\.\n3\\. Unable to save the step\n4\\. when an agent is selected ideally it should fill in the default values and allow edit for now\\, rather than keeping everything blank\\.\n5\\. In the step Run Agent\\, there is no way to gets its output\\, if we want to create an issue with the output\\, or make a decision based on the output\\, we cannot\\.\n6\\. In the workflow design section\\, scroll zoom ins and zoom out\\. This is quite frustrating since if we need to scroll down to see the actions list of the step settings\\, if the mouse is in the workflow editor section\\, which it normally is considering the size and position of the section\\, it just zooms in and out\\. I think zoom should only happen on Ctrl\\+Scroll or Alt\\+Scroll\\, what ever the industry standard is\\.	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-04 22:33:25	f	[]
