37760b196aeb-38b7-6034-ba3c06cc7eae	34bdca956ae6-8157-e410-2af2948f16f3	Here are six issues, one per problem, all in **aga-v1** like the last batch. One limit first: no local checkout has the workflow editor code (the agent checkouts were cleaned up and `prometheus` is out of date). So the issues name the pieces from aprom-4057's record and Gaia's rules, and each agent finds the exact files.\n\n**What I found:**\n\n1. **Agent picture in the dropdown:** aprom-4252 taught the agent avatar to show the user's picture, but the dropdown's option renderer (`related-fields/relate-actor`, from aprom-4057) still draws the plain robot.\n2. **Avatar too big:** the same renderer. It should use the small avatar size the user picker uses.\n3. **Can't save the step:** the cause isn't confirmed. Strong suspect: Gaia accepts every Run agent setting as a non-empty string, including max turns and the two timeouts. It rejects numbers and any key it doesn't know. If the panel sends `maxTurns: 80` as a number, the save fails, and the panel probably doesn't show Gaia's message.\n4. **Defaults when an agent is picked:** the agent's max turns, a new session, and Gaia's own defaults (15 minutes to claim, 240 to finish). I'd **leave the model empty** and show "Agent's default (simple: sonnet, complex: opus)". When the model is empty, Talos picks it by the issue's complexity. Filling it in would switch that off for this step. Say if you want it filled anyway.\n5. **Output:** Gaia already has it. When the agent reports, the next steps can read `{step.outcome}` (done, needs_input, blocked, failed, limit) and `{step.comment}` (Talos's summary of the run). The outcome ports already let you branch on the result. What's missing is the UI: the pickers only offer the trigger's fields, so nobody can find these. Two limits worth knowing:\n   - `step` holds only the latest actor step.\n   - The comment is free text, so you can test it with "contains" but can't read structured fields.\n\n   Structured output (e.g. a JSON object readable as `{step.output.title}`) would need Gaia and Talos changes. I've left it out until the simple version proves too thin.\n6. **Scroll zoom:** the standard in Figma, Miro and n8n is Ctrl+scroll (⌘+scroll on Mac) to zoom. Trackpad pinch arrives as Ctrl+scroll, so it keeps working. Plain scroll goes on scrolling the page. Panning by dragging the background stays.\n\nIssue 4 waits for issue 3, since both change the same Run agent form. The rest can run in parallel.	message	["Listing .runs/issue-*/prometheus/app/components/workflow/**/*.js in .", "Listing prometheus/app/components/workflow/**/*.js in .", "Listing **/prometheus/app/**/*workflow* in ..", "Listing **/app/models/workflownode.js in ../..", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4057", "Reading .runs/issue-4220/gaia/core/libs/workflows/NodeConfigRules.php", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4252 | head -5; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search \\"run agent out", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4220/gaia/core/libs/workflows/RunContext.php", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4220/gaia/core/libs/workflows/ExpressionResolver.php", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4220/gaia/core/libs/workflows/WaitingStepResumer.php", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4220/gaia/core/libs/workflows/ActorStepReports.php", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib/workflow_steps.py", "Updating the knowledge map"]	369dc1266aeb-38b7-6034-825abfb0ae13	2.308418	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 22:35:35	f	\N
