27ab52946aeb-2e52-6034-7f8ceb590a7a	34bdca956ae6-8157-e410-2af2948f16f3	Thanks. If no request goes out and nothing is logged, the problem is in Prometheus before anything reaches Gaia. So I rewrote issue 3 around the three likely client-side causes:\n\n- **Apply or Save does nothing.** The handler isn't wired up, or the button is disabled without any sign.\n- **The panel's own validation blocks the save silently.** It checks the draft, fails, and shows no message.\n- **The save skips the node.** The editor saves through a workflow-graph service, which only writes nodes it sees as changed. If Apply writes into the existing `config` object instead of replacing it, the node never counts as changed, so nothing is sent.\n\nMy bet is the third: the aprom-4057 notes mention exactly this tracking problem with `node.config`. Gaia's rules (every setting a string, no extra keys) stay in the issue, because the save will hit them once a request goes out.\n\nI've dropped the output issue (5). The other four issues are unchanged. Everything stays in aga-v1.	message	["Updating the knowledge map"]	26e988076aeb-2e52-6034-9b0b94fc76a9	0.226337	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 22:39:35	f	\N
