365ccb586aec-8a66-ed75-970ca795a095	ff0998196aec-c6f1-ed75-2f407967e79a	Here's what I found:\n\n- `gaia/docker/php/conf.d/custom.ini` sets `memory_limit = 512M`, but only `gaia/docker-compose.yaml` uses it. It bind-mounts the file into the containers, as `gaia.ini` on line 23 and as `zz-custom.ini` on lines 64 and 104.\n- Neither Dockerfile copies it in:\n  - `gaia/docker/dev/Dockerfile` builds the deployed image. It copies only `docker/dev/opcache.ini` (as `zz-opcache.ini`), so the deployed Gaia runs with the base image's default memory limit.\n  - `gaia/Dockerfile` is the local build. It works under compose because of the mount, but a plain `docker build` / `docker run` also misses the setting.\n\nThe fix is one small Gaia issue: copy `custom.ini` into `conf.d` in both Dockerfiles, using the same `zz-` naming as the opcache file so it loads last. I left the compose mounts and the base image in `docker-images/gaia` alone; neither needs to change.	message	["Searching for \\"memory_limit\\" in .", "Listing {gaia,docker-images}/**/{Dockerfile*,*.ini,docker-compose*.yml}", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M; cat gaia/Dockerfile; echo ----; cat gaia/docker/dev/Dockerfile; echo ----; c", "Reading gaia/Dockerfile", "Reading gaia/docker/dev/Dockerfile", "Searching the code in .", "Reading gaia/docker/php/conf.d/custom.ini", "Reading gaia/docker-compose.yaml", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Updating the knowledge map"]	35904f456aec-8a66-ed75-4fffff3c30a3	0.298939	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-05 07:24:38	f	\N
