0d097fc56aee-2243-248d-ce5e0272af59	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	Phase 1 is almost done, Gaia issues are left, but they are supplementary, 4300 is being shipped and reviewed  right now. Next phase: put the QueryBuilder on the Issue list only.\n\n\\- templates/app/project/issue/index\\.hbs: replace the readonly input and the jQuery \\`query\\-builder\\` panel with\n  \\<QueryBuilder> using the issue schema. Saved Searches loads into the bar and builder; Save Search, Clear,\n  paging and the ?query= param keep working.\n\\- controllers/app/project/issue/index\\.js: drop its \\`filters\\` array for the issue schema\\.\n\\- controllers/prometheus/list\\.js is shared with the Project list and the admin module lists\\, which stay on\n  jQuery QueryBuilder until a later phase. Add applyQuery(query) for the new component and keep their path\n  (searchByRules, openFilters, utils/query/builder.js) working. Remove nothing yet.\n\\- Gherkin acceptance tests on Mirage:\n  - type and run a query;\n  - accept a suggestion with the keyboard;\n  - edit in the builder and see the bar update;\n  - load a saved search;\n  - an error shown and the query not sent.\n\\- Gaia request: bind query values as parameters in gaia core/mvc/models/query/Clause\\.php\\. It concatenates\n  values into SQL today, so an apostrophe breaks the query and it looks injectable. Then a small Prometheus\n  issue that depends on it and lifts the apostrophe block in the bar.\n\nShow a screen of the Issue list with a query applied and the builder closed, then the plan.	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-07 01:51:09	f	[]
