bcbb04766aee-2243-248d-aa2114abbcaf	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	The screens and plan are below. I left out a new Gaia request for binding values because it already exists as agaia-4302 (after agaia-4301). The small Prometheus issue depends on 4302 instead. I also used `<EzSearch>` where your message says `<QueryBuilder>`, following the naming decision.\n\n**Findings that shape the plan**\n- **Clear and Save Search can't reuse the shared actions.** `clearSearch` (`list.js:328`) calls `queryBuilder.clear()`, which throws "First initialize the utility" when the jQuery plugin hasn't been set up. `showSaveSearchDialog` and the issue controller's `saveSearch` both call `searchByRules`, which reads the jQuery plugin. So the Issue list gets its own paths: `applyQuery`, and a save that takes the query from `@onSave`. The Project and admin lists keep the old actions untouched.\n- **The project filter must not be added twice.** The route already ANDs `(Issue.projectId : X)` onto `?query=` (`routes/app/project/issue/index.js:191-196`). The page therefore passes no `@baseQuery`; otherwise the project filter would be added twice.\n- **Saved searches have a different shape.** They store their query in `searchquery`, and the page keeps the active one in the `searchId` URL parameter (`toggleSearch`, `list.js:974`).\n- **Mirage doesn't filter issues by query.** The new acceptance steps check the `query` sent to `/issue`, and that nothing was sent when the query has an error, rather than the rows.\n\n**Question:** the local checkout doesn't have 4300's code yet, so I can't see whether `<EzSearch>` reports which saved search was picked. The page needs that to keep `?searchId=` working. I recommend adding `@activeSavedSearchId` and `@onSavedSearchChange(search|null)` to 4300 while it's in review. If you'd rather not, I'll add a small issue ahead of the integration.\n\n**Not in this phase:**\n- the Project and admin lists;\n- the board, Gantt and calendar;\n- removing jQuery QueryBuilder, `utils/query/builder.js`, the old parser and the `statusOptionsByName`-style getters, unless nothing else uses them;\n- lifting the bracket refusal (that needs agaia-4303).\n\n**Screens:** the Issue list with a query applied and the builder closed. The bar shows the formatted query with colours, and the list is filtered to 12 issues. A 390px mobile view of the same page is included.\n\n\n\n\n\n**Plan:** 2 issues in A Prometheus, milestone aga-v1.\n\n1. **ez-issue-list** puts `<EzSearch>` on the Issue list. It depends on aprom-4300 and includes the five Gherkin scenarios. It comes to about 10 files, so I didn't split the tests out.\n2. **ez-apostrophes** lifts the apostrophe refusal once agaia-4302 binds values. Apostrophes at the start or end of a value and inside IN lists stay refused, because Gaia trims `'` and splits lists on `','`. That last part waits for agaia-4303.	message	["Listing prometheus/app/{components/ez-search/**,utils/query/**,services/query-schema.js}", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/controllers/prometheus/list.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/issue/index.js", "Reading prometheus/app/controllers/prometheus/list.js", "Reading prometheus/app/controllers/prometheus/list.js", "Reading prometheus/app/controllers/prometheus/list.js", "Reading prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/issue/index.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes/app/project/issue/index.js", "Listing prometheus/tests/acceptance/**/*issue*", "Reading prometheus/tests/acceptance/issue/search-issue-from-list.feature", "Searching the code in prometheus/mirage", "Reading prometheus/mirage/route-handlers/issue.js", "Updating the knowledge map"]	bba3bad06aee-2243-248d-3cf90022a70a	1.865785	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 01:54:04	f	[{"uploadId": "a7a57c246aee-2243-248d-35700a1e42eb", "key": "issue-list-applied", "title": "Issue list with an ezSearch query applied, builder closed", "version": 1, "width": 1