0b89fae46aee-cdab-4f28-82879159cfc3	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	I've looked at your screenshot and planned one bug fix for it.\n\n**What the screenshot shows**\n- The toolbar takes three rows. Row 1 has Saved Searches on the left and Builder, Search and Clear on the right, with an empty gap between them.\n- The formatted query sits on its own row underneath.\n- A short stray underline sits on the right, probably the `.bar` of an input that has shrunk to almost no width.\n- There is empty space under all of it before the list controls.\n\nMy guess is that the bar's flex item collapses: the coloured query text is rendered outside the input's box, so it drops onto its own line and leaves the input's underline behind. No local checkout has the ez-search code (aprom-4300 and 4305 aren't in this checkout), so I can't confirm that. The issue therefore describes the expected result exactly and says what to check first.\n\n**Decision to confirm:** for long queries I propose that the bar stays one line. While it's not focused, the text is cut off with an ellipsis and the full query shows as a tooltip; while you're typing, the input scrolls sideways. Say if you'd rather the bar grow taller instead.\n\nOn mobile the toolbar still wraps to two rows (bar, then buttons) as planned, just without the extra gaps.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/ideas/c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e/images/6f77b1356aee-b066-4f28-b3da137ea19a.png", "Listing .runs/*/prometheus/app/components/ez-search/* in .", "Listing **/components/ez-search/search-bar.hbs in .", "Listing **/ez-search*.scss in ..", "Updating the knowledge map"]	0ab0d1526aee-cdab-4f28-cd42fb6a4e59	1.764021	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 07:15:23	f	\N
1e69eba06aee-8611-5ba1-f675cdd1ff35	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	I found the root cause, on the input field with data-field="ez-search-input" since it is a form-filed we are applying the form-field class to it and that is applying a margin of 3rem.\n\nFor this particular field, so we not need to do that.  There is another issue on mobile view. In the mobile view in the saved search dropdown is opening so that its out of the view. ![image.png](upload:f11f9f676aee-b0e7-5ba1-07178c2072ec) It seems to be aligned to the right of the dropdown, while it should have been aligned to the left of the dropdown	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-07 07:24:14	f	[]
