8949d8c56aee-4713-5ba1-51f7f557db87	d87ad5636ae5-1449-ae8f-5808a9dddbf1	The loop is almost certainly in the code that renders message text, `modifiers/render-markdown.js` from aprom-4114, not in Gaia. The network requests succeed; it's the screen that keeps asking again.\n\n## Likely cause\n\n`render-markdown` uses Ember's older modifier API, in which `didReceiveArguments` re-runs whenever anything it read changes. On each run it does this, part of it before its first `await`:\n\n1. Calls `showImages`, which calls `uploadPreview.previewUrl()`.\n2. That calls `store.query('upload', { id, download: true })`. The modifier now depends on store data the query reads.\n3. The query result comes back and changes that data, so the modifier runs again.\n4. Each run mints a new download token and calls `viewer.setMarkdown`, which redraws the whole message and reloads the image.\n\nThat matches what you see: every request succeeds, but the message keeps refreshing. There's also no check that the text is unchanged before starting again, and no cache of addresses already resolved. The single-use tokens make re-renders worse, because a redrawn `<img>` that reuses an old address gets a 404.\n\nScreens attached by Nestor aren't affected: they use the `Idea::MessageScreen` component, which loads once in its constructor.\n\nI'd still have the agent confirm the mechanism first, with a failing test, so the issue is marked complex. It's small: about three files.\n\nOn the Brainstorm ↔ Plan divider, I'm still waiting for your pick between **C** (drag with snapping) and **D** (step arrows).	message	["Listing */issue-42*/prometheus/app/modifiers/render-markdown.js in .", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search \\"idea image paste upload render markdown\\" --project ap", "Reading .runs/issue-4284/prometheus/app/modifiers/render-markdown.js", "Updating the knowledge map"]	884230936aee-4713-5ba1-61377f782fc1	1.229802	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent 