2d2915406aee-698e-6251-295768c5a631	599b10726aeb-f308-85f1-2dd28eca8a3d	A few upgrade to Agamemnon.\n1\\. There was an issue 4303 It was waiting on the completion of 4302 which is fine it was assigned to Achilles which was also good but even when there are additional slots available Agamemnon did not spot 4303 back in implementation even when 4302 got marked as done by a game\\.\n2\\. For the issue 4301\\, the CI job had failed\\. The reason for the failure was a timeout from GitHub side while retrieving an external resource\\. All I had to do was rerun the job and see I and everything resumed\\. I understand like Memnon shouldn't have to try rerunning the job even when they're failing but I think two to three attempts can be made just to verify if the issue was temporary or if there is a small conflict then it really needs to try and pick things up from there\\. If for any reason a job is failing there's no harm in Agamemnon creating a separate issue Working on it in order to help fix a bug coming in\\. So for example a while back the image preview test case was failing The steps were quite simple to resolve it\\. We had to create a separate issue that fixed the bug and then we had to rebase current issues workspace and resume the work\\. I think this is quite within Egmmnon's capabilities Let's analyze what happened here and how can we get AGM non to try and move things along for these small tasks and details	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-07 07:54:21	f	[]
