96a7d0926aee-b0cf-b49a-0546988c4a68	f1592e496aee-cb3c-b49a-239fcfcb2381	You want a daily CodeRabbit allowance of 25 reviews. Once it's used up, agent PRs stop going to CodeRabbit. The issue goes straight to you as **in_review**, and that applies to both the Odysseus side and Agamemnon.\n\n## Where CodeRabbit reviews get started today\n1. **New PR.** `ai ship` waits for CodeRabbit before handing off when the repo is CodeRabbit-enabled (`ai/lib/ship.py:197`). adt-4245 (in review) also posts `@coderabbitai full review` from `workflow.open_pr`.\n2. **Talos review loop.** A fix round pushes a commit, so CodeRabbit reviews again (`talos/lib/bot_review.py` `next_step`). Address-review runs in auto-merge milestones go back through the loop too (`Watcher.reenter`).\n3. **Agamemnon.** It updates PRs that have fallen behind their base on GitHub (`orchestrator/keeper.py` `_update`), and resolves conflicts that then go "through CodeRabbit again" (`_resolve`). Both push a new commit, which starts another review.\n\nNothing counts these reviews anywhere today.\n\n## Proposed approach\n- **One shared counter** in `dev-tools/ai/state/` with an `ai rabbit budget` command, used by every tool. The limit is a `codeRabbitDailyBudget` setting (25). Each place that starts a review checks the counter and records the review.\n- **When the limit is reached:**\n  - `ai ship` posts no trigger, doesn't wait, and hands the issue to you as in_review, with a comment saying why.\n  - The Talos loop runs no more fix rounds and doesn't re-enter; it hands the issue to you instead.\n  - Agamemnon doesn't update PRs that are behind. It doesn't fix conflicts and resend the PR either; you get the issue with a note.\n- Auto-merge is safe without changes: a PR that skipped CodeRabbit never comes back "clean", so it never reaches the merger.\n\n## Please confirm (my recommendation in brackets)\n1. **What counts as a review?** [Every review we start: the trigger on a new PR plus every push to a PR CodeRabbit already reviews. If only `full review` comments count on your plan, issues 3 and 4 shrink to almost nothing.]\n2. **What does "per day" mean?** [The last 24 hours, rolling. It can't overshoot, whatever window CodeRabbit uses.]\n3. **When the allowance frees up again, should anything waiting for review be re-sent?** [No. Once an issue is with you, it stays with you.]\n\n**Left out:** a dashboard or alert (`ai rabbit budget` and the hand-off comment cover it), counting your own pushes to PRs already handed to you, and re-sending later.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching the code in dev-tools", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search coderabbit --project adt 2>&1 | head -40", "Searching the code in dev-tools", "Searching the code in dev-tools", "Searching the code in dev-tools/ai/lib", "Reading dev-tools/ai/lib/ship.py", "Reading dev-tools/ai/lib/workflow.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4245 2>&1 | head -40; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search rate lim", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib/orchestrator/keeper.py", "Searching the code in .", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib/bot_review.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/dev-tools && grep -n \\"STATE_DIR\\\\s*=\\\\|LOCAL_DIR\\\\s*=\\" ai/lib/*.py | head; ls installe", "Searching the code in dev-tools/ai/lib", "Listing installer/filelock.py in dev-tools", "Updating the knowledge map"]	95a337c66aee-b0cf-b49a-ab98db7d11a2	0.950227	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 09:59:50	f	\N
