e0ab34696aee-ae49-cbf5-a2937ae766bf	f1592e496aee-cb3c-b49a-239fcfcb2381	adt-4245 (in review) also posts `@coderabbitai full review` from `workflow.open_pr`.\n\nthis is no longer relevant. Actually, this makes me think that since we are getting PR event per day, le me disabled auto\\_review on the PRs. I have the auto review enabled that cause Code Rabbit to pick up the review automatically. However, we can be more prudent.\n\nLets do the following\n1) Manually trigger the PR by posting `@coderabbitai full review always`\n2) For the first 10 pr events let CodeRabbit review every thing\n3) For 10-25 PR events lets only send larger PRs to CodeRabbit and send the simpler PRs to the human user.\n4) For anything beyond 25 PR events per day everything goes to Human and Agamemnon must be aware of this.\n\nWhat counts as a review.\n"What counts as a review? [Every PR evaluation: opening a PR, each push to a reviewed PR (pushes, not commits), each `@coderabbitai review`/`full review` comment, and branch updates, force-pushes, rebases and draft→ready changes. If `auto_incremental_review` is turned off, later pushes stop counting, and issues 3 and 4 shrink to almost nothing.]<span style="font-size: 1.4rem;">"\nper day is rolling 24 hours.</span>\n\nYes, we can easily push things waiting with auto review when we have the credit available.\n\nNo need for alert, I can ask for a mobile push notification later if I feel like it. (leave for now)	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-07 10:22:24	f	[]
