555273656aee-41e5-0b34-379e9e2db22f	f1592e496aee-cb3c-b49a-239fcfcb2381	I've revised the plan. Turning off `auto_review` makes this simpler: CodeRabbit only reviews when one of our tools posts the trigger, so the counter just counts those posts. You'll switch off `auto_review` and `auto_incremental_review` yourself in CodeRabbit; the plan assumes both are off.\n\n## Design\n- **One decision point.** A new `ai rabbit request` command takes the repo, the PR, its size and whether CodeRabbit already reviewed it. It checks the last 24 hours (rolling) and then either posts the trigger and records it, or answers `human` and records the PR as waiting.\n  - **Under 10 used:** every PR goes to CodeRabbit.\n  - **10 to 24 used:** only large PRs go to CodeRabbit (6 or more hand-written files, using the count `ai ship` already makes). Smaller PRs go to you.\n  - **25 or more used:** everything goes to you.\n  - **Follow-up reviews** of a PR CodeRabbit already reviewed carry on until the limit of 25, whatever the PR's size. Stopping halfway would waste the first review.\n- **Every push needs a new trigger.** Agamemnon only auto-merges when CodeRabbit has passed the PR's latest commit (`ai/lib/mergegate.py` `gate`). With auto review off, a new commit gets no review unless we ask for one. So:\n  - Talos asks for another review after each fix round.\n  - Agamemnon asks for one after updating a branch or fixing a conflict.\n\n  Each of these counts toward the 25, and when the answer is `human`, the issue comes to you as in_review.\n- **Catching up.** Agamemnon's sweep posts the trigger on PRs that went to you because of the limit, oldest first, once there is credit again. The issue stays with you; CodeRabbit's comments just arrive on the PR.\n- **adt-4245** can be closed. Posting the trigger moves into `ai rabbit request`; if 4245 gets merged anyway, it conflicts with this plan.\n\n## Worth a look\n- I'm not sure CodeRabbit understands `@coderabbitai full review always`, since `always` isn't a command I know. The trigger text is a setting, so test it once on a PR.\n- Branch updates cost a review each, so Agamemnon keeping PRs current can eat the allowance. A cheaper option is to let the merge check accept an earlier CodeRabbit pass when the only later commits are merges from the base branch. That needs care, so I left it out; say if you want it.\n- Reviews you trigger yourself on GitHub aren't counted.\n\n**Left out:** alerts and that merge-check shortcut.	message	["Searching the code in dev-tools/ai/lib/mergegate.py", "Searching the code in dev-tools/ai/lib/sizecheck.py", "Updating the knowledge map"]	542e0e276aee-41e5-0b34-cf4c4ab70fb7	0.334034	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 10:24:21	f	\N
