afbf66986aee-083f-0b34-a8de04d610b3	f1592e496aee-cb3c-b49a-239fcfcb2381	I've fixed the trigger text to `@coderabbitai full review`.\n\n**Marking the issue done when you merge:** yes. Today Agamemnon only sets an issue to done after a merge it did itself (`talos/lib/orchestrator/merging.py` `_finish`); issues that come to you stay in_review after you merge. I've added an issue for this (`merged-done`). Agamemnon's sweep looks at in_review issues assigned to you that have an agent PR (branch `claude-issue-N`, opened by Agent Odysseus). If that PR was merged by someone else, it sets the issue to done and comments "PR merged by Hammad Hassan". The comment wording differs from its own "merged automatically". It doesn't depend on the CodeRabbit work, so it can be built first.\n\n**Your GitHub activity vs Odysseus's:** only Agent Odysseus's trigger comments are counted and limited. Your own `@coderabbitai` comments, pushes and merges are never counted or blocked. A backlog PR you have already merged or closed is dropped without using a review.	message	["Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib/orchestrator/merging.py", "Updating the knowledge map"]	aeb148596aee-083f-0b34-b160c77d65e7	0.275367	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 10:34:23	f	\N
