836e2ee66aef-df8f-38f6-010bbf33b01e	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	No, lets do it the right way.  We should have implementation architecture documentation that explains that the when ever we want to build a list view extended from Module, that module needs to declare the search metadata. lets not hard code things we do not need to. I can imagine updating the entire architecture using metadata driven approach. However, that is a huge change. but what we can do is that if we have partial metadata based implementation we can double down and make sure that we make it a full metadata driven approach. especially when the impact is as little as in this case.\n\nMake sure that you documents this approach.\n\nRagarding YUI generated doc, leave it. We are going to build our md file base architecture and implementation documents so we can simple rely on that for now.	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-07 12:37:23	f	[]
