f248beb56aef-df8f-38f6-957548915ad7	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	Agreed. This version moves search fields out of code and into view metadata, and the architecture doc is written in the same PR as the code it describes.\n\n**Approach**\n- **One place for search fields.** Each module declares them under `views.<Module>.search` in `utils/metadata/metadata.js`. That replaces two things: the `filters` key that `module.js` reads but no module ever declared, and the hard-coded `utils/query/schemas/issue.js` and `project.js` from aprom-4295.\n- **The service builds the schema.** `query-schema.load(module, context)` turns the metadata into the schema with `createSchema`. Value lists (statuses, milestones, members and so on) are referenced by name, such as `{source: 'issueStatuses'}`, and the service keeps a small registry of loaders, one per name. Fields are declared in metadata; only a new kind of value list needs code.\n- **Search is opt-in.** A list view that extends Module gets ezSearch only if its module declares `search` metadata; without it there is no search box. The generic `app.module` list gets ezSearch from metadata instead of losing its search.\n- **No more filter arrays in controllers.** The Issue and Project controllers already lose theirs (in aprom-4305 and here).\n- **The doc** goes in `prometheus/docs/architecture/metadata-views/`, as `architecture.md` and `decisions.md`, following the existing `live-updates/` docs. It covers:\n  - what is metadata-driven today: navigation, dashboard widgets, the Project list fields and now search;\n  - the rule that a list view declares its search metadata;\n  - the field and value-source format;\n  - how to add a module or a value source;\n  - the principle you described: where something is partly metadata-driven and the change is small, make it fully metadata-driven.\n\n  Prometheus' `CLAUDE.md` gets a pointer to the doc.\n- **YUIDoc output in `docs/`** is not touched.\n\n**Order:** search-metadata first. The Project list and the generic module list then go in parallel. Removing the plugin comes last.\n\nThe generic list may have no module that actually reaches `app.module`. If so, its test uses the metadata of a module that does, or a test-only fixture, rather than inventing metadata for a real module.	message	["Listing prometheus/docs/{architecture,ui}/**/*.md", "Reading prometheus/app/utils/metadata/metadata.js", "Updating the knowledge map"]	f1347aa46aef-df8f-38f6-bb74f7085b77	0.399293	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 12:39:14	f	\N
