8c8743e26aef-ae10-a4c9-d728da263870	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	I went through your mockup. Its search controls cover all four of your points, so the screens below build Option A from them. It also has a few things that aren't search, which I'd keep out of this phase.\n\n**What I take from your mockup**\n- **Bar:** the bar on its own full-width row. The search icon at its right end is the Search button, so no separate button is needed in a narrow column.\n- **Controls row:** one row of small buttons under the bar. Saved searches is a `fa-bookmark` dropdown. Filter (`fa-sliders`) opens the builder and carries a crimson badge with the number of applied conditions.\n- **Applied filters as chips:** one chip per top-level condition (`Status: Open ×`), with **Clear** at the end of the chip row. That gives your points 1 and 3 without the long formatted query, which is unreadable in 300px. The bar still shows the exact query while you edit it.\n- **Saved search name (point 4):** when a saved search is applied, the Saved button turns crimson and shows its name (`fa-bookmark My open ideas ▾`). If you then change the query, the name stays, marked "edited", until you clear or pick another search. Today aprom-4304 drops the mark instead, so this would change that.\n- **Count:** the header shows how many ideas match (`Ideas 5 of 64`).\n\n**Not search, so not planned here (I'd keep them for the idea the screenshot seems to come from):**\n- the All | Mine 12 segments (Mine could later be a built-in saved search);\n- the Last updated sort;\n- tags or categories (they need a Gaia model);\n- "Search ideas and messages": searching message text means filtering on Idea's hasMany `messages`, which needs checking in Gaia first;\n- the richer rows with avatar, author, time and tags.\n\n**Screens** (rendered with today's CSS only, so they show layout and content, not the final look):\n- **idea-search-default:** nothing applied: empty bar, Saved and Filter buttons, the full list.\n- **idea-search-saved-applied:** "My open ideas" applied: name on the Saved button, Filter badge 2, two chips with Clear, 5 of 64 ideas.\n- **idea-search-saved-menu:** the Saved menu open, aligned to the button's left edge. It lists the saved searches with a check on the active one and ends with "Save current search…".\n- **idea-search-mobile:** the applied state at 390px.\n\n**Questions** (my recommendation first):\n1. **Build it into `<EzSearch>` for every list?** Chips and the saved search name go into `<EzSearch>` itself as a compact layout, so all lists get them. On the full-width lists the chips sit under the toolbar and the name shows on the Saved Searches button.\n2. **Removing a chip:** removing a chip takes that condition out and runs the search right away. A nested AND/OR group shows as one chip ("Any of: Type Bug, Story"), and its × removes the whole group.\n3. **Edited saved search:** keep the name with "edited" and let Save offer "Update My open ideas" or "Save as new". This replaces aprom-4304's drop-the-mark behaviour.\n\nOnce you answer, I'll write the plan.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/ideas/c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e/images/fc617db16aef-57d2-a4c9-676c91460625.png", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.428363	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 17:27:40	f	[{"uploadId": "60849f836aef-ae10-a4c9-8aa41cfad596", "key": "idea-search-default", "title": "Idea list: compact ezSearch, nothing applied", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}, {"uploadId": "6ebe30d36aef-ae10-a4c9-d0d1b727e47c", "key": "idea-search-saved-applied", "title": "Idea list: saved search 'My open ideas' applied, chips and count", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}, {"uploadId": "7d3284036aef-ae10-a4c9-10131a1f2794", "key": "idea-search-saved-menu", "title": "Idea list: Saved menu open (left-aligned), active search checked", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}, {"uploadId": "8b8b71336aef-ae10-a4c9-d3895c603dd6", "key": "idea-search-mobile", "title": "Idea list on mobile: saved search applied with chips", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}]
68c28d766aef-abad-a72a-af9c5317025f	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	This looks better. I am envisioning this as a ezSearchCompact. I would want to use this in multiple places, so lets make this something I can use in multiple places, including Threads, GanttCal, Taskboards, etc.\nIn the screenshots. I do not see any things to represent Search and Clear.The search input field should take full space for the limits 3-col that we have.Answers to questionsThe search input field should take full space for the limits 3-col that we have.Answers to questions\n1) As mentioned I would rather have EzSearchCompact, which should be a drop-in replacement for the EzSearch. i.e. depending on whether I want EzSearch or EzSearchCompact on any view all I should have to do is name the component I want to use.2) Removing a chip is limited space work well. 3) I will only be able to comment on edit once I see it. 2) Removing a chip is limited space work well. 3) I will only be able to comment on edit once I see it.\nAnother things is that I would want EzSearchCompact to be both linear or multi-row depending on the flag provided. default should be multi-row.\nWhy? Take a look at the Dashboard header, we show search there as well and I would love to have EzSearchCompact there as well, but due to limit space in the header we need to be quite efficient with the space in a linear (single row ) view.	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-07 17:44:08	f	[]
