082672966aef-41e1-a72a-7065bb5a4806	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	Here's round 3 of the screens, built on your answers.\n\n**How `<EzSearchCompact>` would work**\n- **Drop-in replacement:** it takes the same arguments as `<EzSearch>`, so switching a view between the two only means changing the component name. The one addition is `@linear` (default `false`, which means multi-row).\n- **Multi-row (default):**\n  - Row 1: the search input across the full width of the column, with **Search** (crimson, `fa-search`) and **Clear** (`fa-times`) attached to its right end.\n  - Row 2: the **Saved** button (it shows the active search's name) and **Filter**, which opens the builder in a modal and carries a badge with the number of applied conditions.\n  - Row 3: the chips, one per top-level condition, each removable.\n- **Linear (`@linear={{true}}`):** one row, all icons. From left to right: Saved (an icon, or the active search's name cut off with an ellipsis), the input filling the rest, then Filter with its badge, Search and Clear. There are no chips in this layout; the Filter badge shows how many conditions apply, and the modal shows them.\n- **Edited saved search** (you said you'd decide once you see it): after a change, the Saved button reads "My open ideas · edited". Its menu offers "Update 'My open ideas'", "Save as new search…" and "Revert to saved". Updating needs one new optional argument, `@onUpdateSavedSearch(search, query)`. Since the two components share their arguments, `<EzSearch>` would get it too.\n\n**Header search (for later):** the header box today is a type-ahead that lists matching issues and opens one when you pick it. The linear compact bar edits a query; it doesn't list results. Putting it in the header means deciding what Search does there, for example opening the Issue list with `?query=`. Its value lists also need a context outside a project. I'd make the header its own phase after this component.\n\n**Screens** (today's CSS only, so they show layout and content, not the final look):\n- **compact-multirow:** idea list, "My open ideas" applied: full-width bar with Search and Clear, the Saved name, Filter badge 2, and two chips.\n- **compact-edited:** the same after removing a chip and typing `search`: the button shows "edited" and the Saved menu is open with Update, Save as new and Revert.\n- **compact-linear-header:** the linear layout in the app header, empty and then with a saved search applied while typing (suggestions open).\n- **compact-mobile:** the multi-row layout at 390px.	message	["Searching the code in .runs/issue-4326/prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs", "Listing .runs/issue-4326/prometheus/app/**/application-header.hbs in .", "Listing prometheus/app/**/application-header.hbs in .", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.619875	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 17:46:48	f	[{"uploadId": "dd17fe366aef-abad-a72a-d726b2f2e878", "key": "compact-multirow", "title": "EzSearchCompact multi-row (default): idea list, saved search applied", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}, {"uploadId": "eb4a7b286aef-abad-a72a-1f6e71639185", "key": "compact-edited", "title": "EzSearchCompact: saved search edited, Saved menu with Update / Save as new / Revert", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}, {"uploadId": "f77eec766aef-abad-a72a-68054a50d304", "key": "compact-linear-header", "title": "EzSearchCompact linear (@linear=true) in the app header: empty, then saved search applied while typing", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 420}, {"uploadId": "0684c7746aef-41e1-a72a-78a69cef95a8", "key": "compact-mobile", "title": "EzSearchCompact multi-row on mobile: saved search applied", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}]
