beb59fc26aef-6ee9-711b-853af784fd1c	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	Here's a one-issue plan for it. In `ez-search-bar.scss` (~l.64) the suggestion menu is set to `z-index: 1000`, but the lane headers still show over it at 999 (`board.scss` ~l.84). So one of the menu's ancestors is probably creating a stacking context below them. Likely candidates are the board's `.milestone-filters` slot (absolutely positioned) or Bootstrap's input-group pieces, which set `position: relative` with small z-indexes.\n\nThe fix gives the menu, the Saved menu and the Filter menu a z-index above 999. It also gives the board's search slot its own stacking level above the lanes, so the menus sit on top whatever the ancestors do.\n\nI raised the menu rather than lowering the lane headers' 999. That 999 is a legacy workaround in the board, and changing it could break the sticky lane headers.\n\nThis issue waits for aprom-4339 (which restores the board's search slot) and aprom-4343 (which edits the same menu styles).	message	["Updating the knowledge map"]	be1240786aef-6ee9-711b-4a4cc54c0f40	3.042692	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 00:22:22	f	\N
