2bc66eb16aef-4618-07ee-ea15bc3fa122	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	This one is another mistake in my plan. aprom-4337's description told the agent to keep task rows and timeline rows aligned by giving the whole timeline side "the same top offset" as the search block. So the Days/Weeks tabs and the date header were pushed down by the full height of the search, leaving the empty band at the top right.\n\nThe fix treats the top of the chart as one header band across both sides:\n\n- **Top edge:** the Days/Weeks tabs start at the top, level with the top of the filter.\n- **Bottom edge:** the date header lines up with the left "Milestone / Start - End" header. That keeps task rows and timeline rows aligned below it.\n- **Leftover space:** any extra height (the search block is taller than the tabs) goes between the tabs and the date header on the right, not above the tabs. When the chips row is empty, the band is as short as the left side allows.\n\nNo local checkout has 4337's code, so the issue says what to find (the top offset 4337 added) rather than naming exact lines.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/ideas/c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e/images/c7b860b06aef-3957-07ee-1c855ff23f2d.png", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4344/prometheus/app/styles/modules/gantt.scss", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4344/prometheus/app/components/app-ui/gantt-chart.hbs", "Listing {.runs/*/prometheus,prometheus}/app/styles/modules/gantt.scss in .", "Updating the knowledge map"]	2af305b36aef-4618-07ee-667ce0a57d0a	0.504279	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 01:32:27	f	\N
