96843c956af0-b986-77e7-ce6c537fc37d	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	I found the cause of both bugs and went through the notes on all ten issues. Plan v3 below has the two fixes plus the review follow-ups, one issue each. I couldn't see the merged code: no local checkout has it. Paths below come from the agents' PR notes.\n\n**1. No pagination on the idea list.** Gaia's list responses have no total. `RestController::buildHAL` (l.1102) sets `meta.count` to the number of rows on the current page only. aprom-4356 noted this: with no total, the idea browser falls back to counting the ideas it loaded, so the total is never above 20. Pagination is built to hide when everything fits on one page (my spec), so it never shows. The Dev → UI page shows it because its fixture holds all 45 records. Gaia does tell us whether there's a next page: it fetches one extra row and only adds `meta.links.next` when there is one. Two fixes, which can run side by side:\n- **aprom:** pagination accepts a has-next flag when no total is known. It then shows `1-20` with › enabled when `links.next` exists.\n- **agaia:** an opt-in `meta.total`. Once it lands, the list shows `1-20 / 64` and the header count is right, with no further UI change.\n\n**2. Menu hover.** The selected option keeps its crimson text on top of the dropdown's crimson hover background, so you get crimson on crimson. It's the same kind of bug as aprom-4346 in the Saved menus. The fix: the selected option turns white on hover and focus, like the other options.\n\n**Follow-ups from the review notes**, one issue each:\n- When a creator isn't loaded, its group shows the raw user id instead of "Unknown".\n- Leaving the idea page resets the grouping but not the sort and order.\n- The test stand-in server (Mirage) ignores the two-field sort, so grouped order isn't actually tested.\n- The QuickList root holds both the selection and the collapsed-group state; the agent suggested giving each its own small class.\n- The idea browser's group definitions sit in the controller with no unit tests.\n\n**Two decisions I need from you** (I left them out of the plan):\n- **Search and archived ideas.** A search currently matches archived ideas too (aprom-4356 asked you to confirm). The browser also moves open ideas ahead of archived ones within each page, which no longer fits server paging (aprom-4359). [My recommendation: a search returns open ideas only unless "show archived" is on, and the order comes only from the server.]\n- **"Show archived" in the URL.** The toggle isn't in the URL, so a reload drops it. [My recommendation: put it in the URL, like the group choice.]\n\nI left out the unused `toolbar.none` translation key; it's too small for its own issue.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/ideas/c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282/images/cbe328d86af0-157f-77e7-cc17c78d85fc.png", "Listing .runs/*/prometheus/app/components/quick-list/toolbar.hbs in .", "Listing **/components/quick-list/toolbar.hbs in .", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && for n in 4350 4351 4352 4353 4354 4355 4356 4357 4358 4359; do dev-tools/ai/ai k", "Gaia: get issue 4359", "Gaia: get issue 4357", "Gaia: get issue 4356", "Gaia: get issue 4353", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php", "Gaia: get issue 4358", "Gaia: get issue 4350", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php", "Gaia: get issue 4351", "Gaia: get issue 4354", "Gaia: get issue 4352", "Gaia: get issue 4355", "Updating the knowledge map"]	95b677166af0-b986-77e7-189ea47a30d4	4.819588	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 14:52:06	f	\N
