c5000e416af0-06f4-8669-23556dab5d04	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	Here's how I understood your message, which came through a bit garbled: Enter runs the search too eagerly. While you type, pressing Enter starts a search, and on first load Enter runs a query even when the bar is empty. You'd rather searches only run on purpose.\n\nThat's the behaviour aprom-4297 specified: Enter with the suggestion menu closed formats the query and runs it.\n\n**Proposal** (one issue, in the shared search bar, so every ezSearch view gets it):\n- **Enter** accepts the highlighted suggestion when the menu is open. With the menu closed it only checks and formats the text into the exact query (and shows any error); it doesn't run anything.\n- **Ctrl+Enter** (**Cmd+Enter** on Mac) or the **Search** button runs the search. It's the usual "submit" shortcut, and Projects4Me already uses it to send in the idea composer, so it's consistent.\n- **Guard:** even with Ctrl+Enter or the button, nothing runs when the bar is empty and no search is applied, or when the query is unchanged since it was last applied. That covers the first-load case.\n- The menu's hint line changes to "Enter to accept, Ctrl+Enter to search, Esc to close".\n\nIf you'd rather run searches only from the button, with no shortcut, say so and I'll drop Ctrl+Enter from the issue.\n\nThe existing acceptance tests that run a query by pressing Enter (Issue, Project, Agents, Workflows, ideas, Gantt and Task Board) are updated in the same issue. That's mostly the shared step definitions, so it should stay within about 10 files.	message	["Updating the knowledge map", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4344/prometheus/app/components/ez-search/search-bar.js"]	c43d80336af0-06f4-8669-7eee42fb7ef0	3.268175	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 10:19:49	f	\N
