b24500446af0-e87c-60c0-30be2fe7c5b7	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	## Which parts should be yielded\n\nThe rule I'd follow: yield only the parts whose content changes from one module to another. QuickList keeps the frame, the state and the behaviour.\n\n| Yield | Why |\n|---|---|\n| `<:item as |record|>` with `<:primary>` and `<:secondary>` | Each module picks its own title, status, avatar, dates and tags. The row frame (checkbox, active bar, link) stays in QuickList. |\n| `<:actions>` in the header | New Idea, New Issue, or nothing at all. |\n| `<:search>` | A slot for `<EzSearchCompact>`. I'm dropping my `QuickList::Search` wrapper: it would only pass its arguments through. |\n| `<:selectionActions as |selected|>` | Bulk actions belong to the module (Archive, Move to, Assign…). QuickList keeps the count, the select-all box and clearing the selection. |\n| `<:group as |group|>` (optional) | Normally the heading shows the name and the count. A module can replace it, for example with avatars when grouping by creator. |\n| `<:empty>` (optional) | Default text with a "Clear the search" link; a module can replace it. |\n| **Not yielded** | The toolbar (group and sort come from `@groupOptions` and `@sortOptions`), pagination, loading and error. These should look the same in every list. |\n\n## Your answers\n1. **Grouping.** Gaia's `group` parameter is a SQL `GROUP BY` (`Clause::prepareGroupBy`), which merges rows, so it can't produce headed groups. QuickList asks Gaia to sort by the group field first, then groups the returned page in JS, so a group carries on across pages. I read your "it does so on the whole page" as "grouping works on the page Gaia returns". Tell me if you meant something else.\n2. **Counts.** Agreed: they're counted in JS from the loaded page.\n3. **Ideas only.** The plan covers the idea browser only.\n4. **Selection.** Ideas get no selection. QuickList still has it, and it shows up on a new dev page, Settings → Developer → UI → QuickList, which uses fixture data and dummy actions.\n\n## Plan\n1. The core component. This one is the contract, so I've marked it complex.\n2. Then pagination and group/sort, side by side.\n3. Then selection, then the dev page.\n4. The idea browser switches over once 1 and 2 are in. It also moves to server paging: today the browser loads every idea and filters open and archived in the browser.\n\nLeft out: Notifications, Gantt and the project overview; keyboard navigation; group totals across pages. All six issues go in **aga-Quick List**. This milestone is new and will be created on approval.	message	["Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4349/prometheus/app/utils/metadata/metadata.js", "Searching for \\"settingsItems\\" in .runs/issue-4349/prometheus/app", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/utils/metadata/metadata.js", "Reading prometheus/app/utils/metadata/metadata.js", "Searching for \\"settings\\" in prometheus/app/router.js", "Listing prometheus/app/templates/app/settings*.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/app/settings.hbs", "Updating the knowledge map"]	b1249ca66af0-e87c-60c0-cf097445dee8	1.010572	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 11:40:34	f	\N
