ef368e816af0-67ba-60c0-2e6d7403afb6	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	I've reshaped the plan into three waves. The critical path drops from four steps to three, and the first wave has 7 independent issues, so all 3 of your parallel slots stay busy.\n\n**How:** each piece (pagination, group heading, toolbar, selection bar) becomes a standalone component with its own tests, and none of them touch the root QuickList. One **assemble** issue then connects them into the root. The idea browser's server-side data change is split from its UI swap. It keeps loading all ideas until the UI issue switches to 20 per page, so nothing breaks in the meantime.\n\n| Wave | Issues (running in parallel) |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | core · pagination · group heading + helper · toolbar · selection bar · Settings developer section · idea data (server-side) |\n| 2 | assemble (connects all the pieces to the root) |\n| 3 | QuickList dev page · idea browser on QuickList |\n\nTo keep the parallel branches from conflicting, each piece puts its styles in its own SCSS partial, and only *assemble* imports them. Translation keys go under each part's own `components.quickList.<part>` section. Conflicts can still happen in `en-us.json`, but they'll be trivial.	message	["Updating the knowledge map"]	ee3554a06af0-67ba-60c0-a614c6ef3915	0.50412	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 11:45:51	f	\N
