398c9b766af0-9f8e-3bb7-7ed76e03b366	ded9f4396af0-2b69-3bb7-c36bdb48cfdf	The goal is to turn **Settings → UI** from a single QuickList demo page into a proper component library. Every entry would follow one template: a live demo, controls to change its settings and states, and docs on how to use it.\n\n## What's there today\nI read the newest checkout, `.runs/issue-4367`:\n- **Navigation:** `templates/app/settings/ui.hbs` is one box with tabs typed into the template. Right now there is one tab, and `routes/app/settings/ui/index.js` redirects to it. The ACL entries are `setting.read` (`services/acl.js` ~l.91).\n- **The QuickList demo:** `settings/ui/quick-list.{hbs,js}` runs on fixture data in memory (`utils/dev/quick-list-fixture.js`), with no calls to Gaia. It has buttons that force the normal, loading, empty and error states.\n- **Gaps:** there are no docs, no list of options and no usage snippet. Its search box is a plain `<input>`, not ezSearch.\n- **ezSearch can run on fixtures too.** All its inputs and callbacks are plain values: `@schema`, `@query`, `@savedSearches`, `@onApply`, `@onSave`, and so on. So it can be shown without Gaia.\n\n## 1) What every entry should have\n1. **Header:** the name, one line on what it's for, a status (stable or experimental), and **where it's used in the app**, so people can see real examples.\n2. **Live demo:** the full feature set on fixture data, never Gaia.\n3. **Controls:** switches for each option (for example selectable, group by, multi-row or single row) and buttons to force the loading, empty, error and disabled states.\n4. **Event log:** shows each callback as it fires and what it passed. For ezSearch, that includes the exact query string sent to Gaia, which is the most useful thing to see.\n5. **Usage snippet:** copy-ready code for the component.\n6. **Reference tables:** the options it takes (type, default, meaning), the slots it lets you fill with your own markup, and its callbacks.\n7. **Do / Don't:** a few lines, for example "don't wrap EzSearchCompact", or which modal and dropdown pitfalls we've already hit.\n\n**How it's built:** I recommend building this once and reusing it. That means one shared page layout for an entry and a registry that drives the tabs and a single page address per component (`ui/:component`). Adding a component would then take three things: a demo, a doc file and one line in the registry. With hand-made pages, every new entry needs its own route, ACL entries and template changes. The QuickList page would move onto the new layout as the first entry.\n\n## 2) Which components to document\n**First batch (I recommend these):**\n- **QuickList:** move the existing demo over and replace its plain search box with EzSearchCompact.\n- **ezSearch:** one entry with three variants: EzSearch, EzSearchCompact multi-row, and EzSearchCompact single-row (as in the header).\n- **Form fields (`FormFields::*`):** text, relate (single and multi), multi-select, date, checkbox, switch, upload, search and validation. The house rules say "always use the existing component", so the library should show them.\n- **`bootstrap-modal`:** async confirm, and rendering outside the parent with `in-element`. We've had bugs from both.\n- **`AppUi::Dropdown`:** alignment and hover colours. These caused the aprom-4309 and 4346 issues.\n\n**Later:** AppUi::Toolbar, AppUi::Table, Pagination, ToastUi with markdown rendering, InlineEditable, Loader and Skeleton, Timeline, AssigneeSelect, avatars with Agent::Badge, and status labels.\n\n**Left out:** Gantt and TaskBoard. They are page features, not reusable parts.\n\n## Questions\n1. **Where do the doc texts live?** The house rule puts every user-facing string in `en-us.json`. Several hundred lines of option descriptions there would be noise. **I recommend English-only doc files in JS for this developer page**, with only the page's own labels translated.\n2. **The first batch:** the five above, each as its own issue that depends only on the shared layout? **I recommend yes.**\n3. **Milestone:** a new **aga-Component Library** milestone, following the aga-Quick List pattern? **I recommend yes.**\n\nIf you'd like, I can also draw the entry page (demo and controls on the left, event log and reference tables below) before I write the plan.	message	["Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M; grep -n -i -A3 \\"component lib\\\\|styleguide\\\\|component-library\\\\|showcase\\" dev-tools/", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Listing .runs/*/prometheus/app/templates/app/settings/**/*.hbs in .", "Running echo", "Reading .runs/issue-4367/prometheus/app/templates/app/settings/ui/quick-list.hbs", "Reading .runs/issue-4367/prometheus/app/templates/app/settings/ui.hbs", "Listing app/{controllers,routes}/app/settings/ui* in .runs/issue-4367/prometheus", "Listing app/controllers/app/settings/**/*.js in .runs/issue-4367/prometheus", "Running ls D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/.runs/issue-4367/prometheus/app/components/ D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/.runs", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4367/prometheus/app", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4367/prometheus/docs/ui/design-system.md", "Reading .runs/issue-4367/prometheus/docs/ui/design-system.md", "Reading .runs/issue-4367/prometheus/app/controllers/app/settings/ui/quick-list.js", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4367/prometheus/app/components/ez-search/base.js", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.677443	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 15:41:45	f	\N
