a6ed57e26af0-cbed-bf1d-e4874bc7e4b2	ded9f4396af0-2b69-3bb7-c36bdb48cfdf	I've drawn the demo page and settled on a way to keep the docs out of the app bundle. The screen below is a rough guide for layout and content, not the final look.\n\n## Where the docs text lives (without making the app bigger)\n| Option | App size | Comment |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A. Markdown files in `prometheus/public/ui-docs/<component>.md`** (recommended) | **No change** | Copied into the build as static files and only downloaded when someone opens that entry. Shown with the markdown viewer we already have (toastui). Needs no build changes or new dependencies, because `broccoli-asset-rev` leaves `.md` files alone. They are reviewed in PRs like any code, readable on GitHub, and `design-system.md` can link to them. Agents read the same files. |\n| B. Lazy-loaded engine or route splitting (ember-engines / Embroider) | No change, and the demo code also leaves the bundle | Needs a new dependency and a build migration. Too big for now. |\n| C. Gaia wiki pages | No change | The content would live in the database, outside code review, and drift from the code. |\n| D. Docs as JS files in the app | **Grows** | This was my earlier proposal. Dropped. |\n\nThe demo components and their fixture data still go in the bundle, but they're small. Fixtures could move to `public/` as JSON too if you want. Excluding the whole library from production builds would be a later, separate step.\n\n## Navigation\nTabs are gone. **The library lives inside the Settings nav.** Clicking **Developer → Component Library** expands it into its own list:\n- a filter box at the top;\n- components grouped by category (Lists, Search, Forms, Overlays, Menus);\n- the active component marked with a crimson left border;\n- each item opens its own page address (`ui/:component`).\n\nIt reuses the existing nav box, so the entry gets the full content column. A registry drives the list, so adding a component only adds an entry to it. A variant count ("ezSearch · 3 variants") shows where one entry covers several forms.\n\n## The entry page\nFrom top to bottom:\n1. **Header box:** the name, a status label (Stable), what the component is for, and "Used in" links.\n2. **Demo (left), Controls and Event log (right):**\n   - Controls has the state buttons (Normal, Loading, Empty, Error) plus switches and selects for its options.\n   - The event log lists each callback as it fires, with what it passed.\n3. **Documentation box:** tabs for Usage, Arguments, Blocks and Do and Avoid, loaded from the component's `.md` file. The file name shows in the box header.\n\n\n\n**Two things to know about the mockup:**\n- The Documentation box header says `docs/ui/components/quick-list.md`. With option A the file would be `public/ui-docs/quick-list.md`.\n- In the real app, only the active tab's content shows. The mockup puts the Usage snippet and an Arguments table side by side to show both at once.\n\n**Still open:**\n- **Docs location:** OK with `public/ui-docs/*.md` (option A)?\n- **Navigation:** happy with the list nested in the Settings nav? The alternative is giving the library its own full-width page with a component index box on the left, and no Settings nav while you're in it.\n- **Copy-ready snippet:** the Usage snippet is written by hand in the `.md`. A snippet generated from the current control settings would be a later extra; I've left it out.\n\nOnce you confirm those three, I'll send the plan: the shared library framework first, then the five entries in parallel, all in **aga-Component Library**. That milestone doesn't exist yet; it will be created when the plan is approved.	message	["Reading .runs/issue-4367/prometheus/app/templates/app/settings.hbs", "Reading .runs/issue-4367/prometheus/app/utils/metadata/metadata.js", "Listing docs/ui/screens/* in .runs/issue-4367/prometheus", "Listing prometheus/docs/ui/screens/* in .", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4367/prometheus/app/styles", "Reading .runs/issue-4367/prometheus/app/components/quick-list/index.hbs", "Reading .runs/issue-4367/prometheus/app/components/quick-list/item.hbs", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"library-entry\\" title", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<\\"EOF\\" ```nestor-screen key=\\"library-entry\\" title", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<\\"EOF\\" ```nestor-screen key=\\"t\\" title=\\"t\\" size=\\"8", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<\\"EOF\\" ```nestor-screen key=\\"t\\" title=\\"t\\" size=\\"8", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<\\"EOF\\" ```nestor-screen key=\\"t\\" title=\\"t\\" size=\\"8", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<\\"EOF\\" ```nestor-screen key=\\"t\\" title=\\"t\\" size=\\"8", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<\\"EOF\\" ```nestor-screen key=\\"library-entry\\" title", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<\\"EOF\\" ```nestor-screen key=\\"t\\" title=\\"t\\" size=\\"8", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/styles/variables.scss", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<\\"EOF\\" ```nestor-screen key=\\"library-entry\\" title", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/library-entry.png", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4367/prometheus", "Updating the knowledge map", "Running echo"]	\N	1.108574	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 15:52:06	f	[{"uploadId": "a63a9bf46af0-cbed-bf1d-5a9f6277d4af", "key": "library-entry", "title": "Component Library: QuickList entry, library nested in the Settings nav", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 1150}]
