058a81196af0-f978-689a-8a3721b49f99	c31674596af0-6d25-f538-e6760785c02e	I've turned the decisions into a plan: 21 issues across Gaia, Hermes, dev-tools and Prometheus. Two choices I had to make while writing it need your yes (see the end).\n\n## The plan\n**Gaia: the base pieces**\n- **Service clients** (`g-service-clients`): a new kind of OAuth client, separate from apps and agents. A service gets a token with **no user** behind it. Gaia keeps only a hash of its secret.\n- **Service access** (`g-service-access`): when a request comes with a service token, Gaia allows only resources that opt in to service access and are on that service's scope list. Everything else gets a 401. This is a framework change in `RestController::authorize()`.\n- **Token scopes** (`g-token-scopes`): a token that carries scopes is held to them on top of the actor's ACL. Credentials, service clients, enrollments and ACL administration are always refused for such tokens.\n\n**Gaia: enrollment and delegation**\n- **Enrollment** (`g-enrollment`, `g-enrollment-tokens`): option A (the service shows a code and an admin approves it) and option B (single-use enrollment token).\n- **Secret rotation** (`g-secret-rotation`): a service replaces its own secret.\n- **Delegation** (`g-delegation`): `Agent.delegationScopes` (empty means no delegation) and a grant that gives a runtime a 1-hour token acting as the agent.\n- **Runtime reads** (`g-runtime-reads`): a runtime can list the agents it may run and read their specs and grants. Never credentials.\n- **Introspection** (`g-introspection`): returns actor type, client, scopes and project IDs. Hermes can call it with its service token.\n\n**Gaia + Hermes, merged together**\n- `user.access.changed` (`g-access-changed` + `h-access-changed`): Hermes clears a user's cached access and re-applies their subscriptions when access changes.\n- Run requests also go to a **runtimes** room (`g-runtimes-room` + `h-runtimes-room`).\n\n**Hermes**\n- Hardening of the shared-secret check (`h-hardening`, independent).\n- Enrollment and a service token (`h-service-identity`).\n- Socket authentication through introspection, with disconnect when the token expires (`h-socket-auth`).\n\n**dev-tools**\n- Talos enrolls (A or B) and keeps its secret in local state (`d-enroll`).\n- Talos finds the Gaia agents itself and runs them on delegated tokens (`d-discover`).\n- Talos takes run requests from the runtimes room (`d-runtimes-room`).\n\n**Prometheus**\n- Settings → Services: list and disable (`p-services`).\n- Pending enrollments with Approve/Deny, and enrollment tokens (`p-enrollments`).\n- A Delegation scopes field on the agent form (`p-delegation-scopes`).\n\n## Two choices to confirm\n1. **Gaia-declared agents run through Gaia workflows only.** The Gaia agent record has no repos or milestones, which `agent.json` gives Talos' own agents. So a discovered agent gets its work from `workflow.agent.run.requested`, the path adt-4047 built. `gaiaAgent` in `agent.json` is retired, and Hera becomes a workflow on the milestone-completed trigger (agaia-4271). Odysseus, Nestor and Agamemnon keep `agent.json` and their own credentials. **Yes?**\n2. **Hermes keeps its enrolled secret in a file on a mounted volume.** Its house rule says "no storage", so this needs an ADR. Without the file, a restarted Hermes would need a new enrollment token every time. **Yes?**\n\n## Left out\n- Ares inbound authentication (it has none today), for when Talos moves into Ares.\n- Key-pair credentials for services (needs a crypto library, so it waits for Ares).\n- Per-workflow-step scopes.\n- Restricting agents to particular runtimes.\n- Storing token hashes in Gaia's token table.\n- Moving Gaia → Hermes publishing off the shared secret (hardened only).\n- The ACL switch to restrictive (you'll set the config before production).\n\nNo milestone was asked for, so everything goes in **Claude-v1**.	message	["Searching the code in gaia/core/config/routes.php", "Listing gaia/docs/generated/bundles/*.md in .", "Reading gaia/docs/generated/bundles/README.md", "Searching the code in gaia/public/index.php", "Searching the code in gaia/public/index.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php", "Listing gaia/app/{metadata/model/Agent*.php,api/v1/controllers/Agent*.php,api/v1/controllers/Introspect*.php} in .", "Searching the code in gaia/core/config/routes.php", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib/agent_spec.py", "Searching for \\"gaiaAgent\\" in dev-tools/talos/lib/registry.py", "Searching issues: \\"Talos workflow run agent steps runtime\\" --project adt", "Updating the knowledge map"]	049cc0656af0-f978-689a-32cf2f8b8bec	0.821375	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 20:13:57	f	\N
fa921fe56af0-c4e7-7b74-89a4618271e1	c31674596af0-6d25-f538-e6760785c02e	Gaia-declared agents run through Gaia workflow only. Yes\nAs long as the token acquisition is automated, no issues in a new token on each restart	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-08 20:22:18	f	[]
