79c483826af1-661c-36e2-726bec235642	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	I hadn't looked at those before; I have now (local `prometheus` checkout). The Task Board and Gantt quick views already change state in place, but each page does it its own way.\n\n**Task Board** (`controllers/app/project/board.js`)\n- `selectIssue` (l.845) sets `@tracked selectedIssue` and `isLoadingIssueDetails`, then `loadIssueDetails` (l.911) runs a `store.query` and sets `selectedIssueDetails`.\n- The route stays put and the board doesn't redraw.\n- The open issue isn't in the URL, so a reload or back button loses it.\n- There's no newest-wins guard: click two cards quickly and the slower answer can show the wrong issue in the panel.\n\n**Gantt Cal** (`controllers/app/project/gantt.js`)\n- `openIssuePanel` (l.485) does the same thing with `panelIssue`/`selectedIssue`, written separately.\n\n**Both pages** still have `query: { refreshModel: true }` (routes: board.js l.26, gantt.js l.25), so a search there reloads the whole route, the same as on the idea browser.\n\nSo you're right. Each page handles the same concerns by hand: what lives in the URL, what to load, newest answer wins, loading and error, and resetting on exit. A small shared toolkit fixes that. It also covers most of the downsides I listed:\n\n| Piece | Job | Which downside it covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `AsyncResource` | One async value: `value`, `isLoading`, `error`, `retry()`; newest call wins | Stale answers; the board's fast-click bug |\n| `ListLoader` (built on `AsyncResource`) | A page of records: one extra row asked for, `items`, `hasNext`, seed with the first page | Route and loader drifting apart (one `buildRequest`) |\n| `UrlState` | Ties a set of query params to a typed state object: defaults, reset on exit or project switch, and a change callback for back/forward and links | URL and screen drifting apart; leftover controller state; saved searches |\n| Architecture doc | `docs/architecture/state/`: when to use the URL and when controller state; never refresh the route for list params | Every later page doing it the same way |\n\n**Proposed plan v6, replacing v5**\n1. Two framework issues in parallel: `AsyncResource` + `ListLoader`, and `UrlState`. Both are marked complex.\n2. Then the doc, side by side with the idea browser switching to the toolkit.\n\nThe Board and Gantt make the case for this, but I've left their switch-over out for now. That would be three issues:\n- the open issue in the URL;\n- the newest-wins detail load;\n- search without refreshing the route.\n\nDo you want them in this plan or as a next phase?	message	["Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes/app/project/board.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/board.js", "Reading prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/board.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Updating the knowledge map"]	78ebc3e56af1-661c-36e2-10b3e7592dff	0.592409	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 17:14:33	f	\N
