d76a33996af2-560a-5423-edd4f6bac8e0	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	Here's a first take on Roles with QuickList: the same layout as the idea browser, with the list on the left and the open role on the right.\n\n**What changes from today.** The Roles page (`templates/app/role.hbs`) is a grid of `Role::Card`s that squeezes into a narrow `col-lg-2` column when a role opens. With QuickList it's always list plus detail:\n- **List column.** QuickList in a `col-md-3`. Each row shows the role name with the access % as a label in the primary line, and "N members · Modified date" in the secondary line.\n- **Detail column.** The existing role page in a `col-md-9`. With no role open, it shows a short "Pick a role" box.\n- **Search.** EzSearch on the role name and description, through new `views.Role.search` metadata. This replaces today's name-only filter, which only searches the roles already loaded.\n- **New Role.** A header button that opens the same modal as today's "+" card.\n- **Group and sort.** Group by access tier (high, elevated, medium, low; worked out in the browser, so only for the loaded page). Sort by name or last modified.\n- **Paging.** 20 per page through the state toolkit (aprom-4425/4426).\n- **Fewer requests.** Today the page loads every role, every user–role link, and one permission request *per role*. With QuickList it only loads permissions and members for the roles on the current page.\n\nIn the screen, the access % uses issue-status labels as stand-ins. The real colours should follow the tier colours already in `role.scss`.\n\n**My assumptions, already written into the plan below. Say no to any you disagree with:**\n1. Always list plus detail; the big card grid goes away. [Yes, it matches Ideas and the narrow column already exists.]\n2. No selection or bulk delete for roles. Deleting a role is risky, so it stays one at a time on the role page. [None for now.]\n3. `Role::Card` and its styles are removed afterwards, and the role-cards architecture doc is rewritten. That's a separate small issue so the switch-over stays reviewable.\n\n**Order.** The switch-over waits for the state toolkit (aprom-4425 and 4426); the cleanup follows it.	message	["Listing prometheus/app/{templates,routes,controllers}/app/role*/** in .", "Listing prometheus/app/{templates,routes,controllers}/app/role*.* in .", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/app/role.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/routes/app/role.js", "Reading prometheus/app/controllers/app/role.js", "Listing prometheus/app/components/role/card.* in .", "Listing prometheus/docs/{architecture/role-cards/*,ui/screens/*role*} in .", "Reading prometheus/app/components/role/card.hbs", "Reading prometheus/docs/architecture/role-cards/architecture.md", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/templates/app/role/page.hbs", "Searching the code in gaia", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'ENDSCREEN' ```nestor-screen key=\\"roles-quick-li", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/roles-quick-list.png", "Updating the knowledge map"]	d6835e266af2-560a-5423-664af141f463	5.283053	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 19:19:51	f	[{"uploadId": "cb8a6be56af2-560a-5423-f27439e79718", "key": "roles-quick-list", "title": "Roles: QuickList beside the open role", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}]
