0f0357386af2-440d-d733-5bd0d43c8819	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	Each row now carries everything the card shows, and the first role opens by default. Updated screen and plan v8 below.\n\n**How the card's information fits into a row**\n\n| On the card | In the QuickList row |\n|---|---|\n| Initials icon, coloured by access tier | A square initials box on the left, in the tier colour from `role.scss` (square: the design system allows round shapes only for avatars) |\n| Name and `{percent}% ACCESS` pill | Name, then the granted % as a label in the tier colour |\n| Denied % (when there is any) | A red `N% denied` label next to the granted % |\n| Description | One line under the name, cut off with an ellipsis; "No description" in grey italic when empty |\n| Members (2 avatars + N) | `Project::MemberAvatars` with `@maxVisible={{2}}` at the bottom left of the row, or "No members" |\n| Modified date | At the bottom right of the same line |\n| Chevron and fading the other cards for the active role | Replaced by QuickList's crimson left bar on the active row |\n\n**One QuickList addition is needed.** The initials box sits in its own column on the left, with the text lines lined up beside it. QuickList's row has no slot for that yet, so I'm adding an optional `<:leading>` block to `QuickList::Item`. It's small, but it changes the QuickList contract, so it's its own issue. Issue lists can use it later for priority icons, and user lists for avatars. It runs alongside the state toolkit work (aprom-4425/4426).\n\n**Opening the first role by default**\n- When you land on Roles with no role open, the page replaces the URL with the first role in the list (`replaceWith`), so Back doesn't bounce you onto the list again.\n- The same happens after a search, a page change, or deleting the open role, as long as no role is open.\n- If you've opened a role yourself, changing the search or page doesn't move you away from it.\n- "Pick a role" shows only when no roles match.	message	["Ru