245960276af2-54cf-3ec9-6407f1c2c5ea	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	You're right, and the fault is in my issue text. aprom-4432 told the agent to keep the name and description as `FormFields::FieldText` and `FieldTextArea` with `@allowInlineEdit`. Those are form fields, so they show even when you're only reading:\n- each one carries the `.form-field` margin;\n- each stretches across the whole box, which pushes its pencil to the far right;\n- the description shows its placeholder and resize handle.\n\nThe facts also became big 18px headings spread out in thirds.\n\nPrometheus already has the right component for this: `AppUi::InlineEditable` (`components/app-ui/inline-editable.hbs`), which the user profile page uses (`templates/app/user/page.hbs`):\n- **Reading:** plain text with a small pencil right after it. Clicking the text or the pencil starts editing.\n- **Editing:** the form field shows only while you edit, with ✓ / ✕ next to it.\n- **Saving and validation:** `saveModelAttribute`, `validateInlineField` and `clearFieldMessage` come from the base create controller, which the role controller already extends.\n\n**The compact Role box** (screen below):\n- A 48px initials square, with the name as a bold heading beside it, its pencil right after it, and the created/modified caption underneath.\n- The description as a plain paragraph lined up under the name, with its pencil after the text. When there's no description, it shows a grey "Add a description" hint.\n- The facts on one tight row under a light separator: small grey label, bold value.\n\nThat last point departs from the design system's `<h4>` facts, which is what made the box so tall. Tell me if you'd rather keep the `<h4>` style and just tighten the spacing.\n\n**Order:** this changes `templates/app/role/page.hbs`, as aprom-4434 (moving Delete) does, so it follows that issue.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/ideas/c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282/images/aacf11b46af2-ed2c-3ec9-96161dd38e5b.png", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/styles/modules/form-fields.scss", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/app/user/page.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/inline-editable.hbs", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'ENDSCREEN' ```nestor-screen key=\\"role-record-in", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/role-record-inline.png", "Updating the knowledge map"]	23ae5e456af2-54cf-3ec9-7ae4278e1ac5	1.103773	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 21:41:56	f	[{"uploadId": "1b8877c06af2-54cf-3ec9-9b55ce786bb6", "key": "role-record-inline", "title": "Role box with AppUi::InlineEditable: display and editing", "version": 1, "width": 1100, "height": 620}]
e8abf7116af2-ca37-d7c4-580ac178f3e9	8ed0e1366af2-ca37-d7c4-675b9ea9985d	You're asking for one search box that finds issues, milestones and projects. It should match typos and partial words (fuzzy) and also find things by meaning (semantic), and the work should happen in Postgres, not Elasticsearch.\n\n## What already exists\n- **Header search** (`prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/application-header.js`, `loadSearchData`) only searches issues. It runs `CONTAINS` on number, subject and description and returns 5 rows. It's the natural place to start.\n- **Fuzzy matching is ready to use.** `pg_trgm` is already installed in the database (`gaia/db/Dump*.sql`, api-tester `prepare-test-db.sh:109`).\n- **Semantic search is not.** It has two gaps:\n  - Our Postgres image is plain `postgres:16-alpine` (`gaia/docker-compose.yaml:133`, and the same in CI). It has no **pgvector**, so the images have to change.\n  - Something has to turn text into vectors (embeddings), and nothing does that today. Ares only does Anthropic chat, and Anthropic has no embeddings API.\n- An earlier idea (2026-10-22) proposed a full-text `MATCHES` operator. No issues were created from it, so nothing conflicts.\n\n## Proposed approach\n1. **Gaia, fuzzy search:** a read-only `search` resource, following the precedent of `agentspec` and `workflowevent`, so it stays within "CRUD only". `GET /search?q=…&types=issue,milestone,project` returns ranked hits of the form `{type, id, title, snippet, projectShortcode}`.\n   - It combines full-text search with trigram similarity, using bound parameters and GIN indexes.\n   - Each model is queried through its normal ACL, so nobody sees a project they aren't a member of.\n2. **Semantic search:**\n   - pgvector goes into the Postgres images.\n   - A Gaia `searchembedding` table holds the vectors.\n   - Ares gets a new `POST /embed` endpoint and stays stateless.\n   - A Gaia batch task embeds new and changed records. If Ares is down, saves still succeed and search falls back to fuzzy only.\n   - Search then blends the fuzzy and semantic scores into one ranking.\n3. **Prometheus:** the header dropdown searches all three types and groups the results under Issues / Milestones / Projects.\n\nThis is bigger than it looks. The semantic half needs a database image change, a new Ares contract and a background job. I'd ship the fuzzy half first: it's useful on its own and has no new infrastructure.\n\n## Questions\n1. **Which embedding provider?** I recommend a **local Ollama container** running `nomic-embed-text`, called from Ares through a new embeddings adapter. No text leaves our servers, it has no per-call cost, and it needs no Python ML dependencies in Ares. The alternative is a hosted API such as Voyage or OpenAI, which is easier to run but sends issue text outside.\n2. **Should the plan be phased?** I recommend yes: fuzzy search in Gaia plus the header UI first, then the semantic issues in the same plan and milestone, built after them.\n3. **Is the header dropdown enough on day one?** I recommend yes: top 5 per type, grouped. I'd leave a full search results page with paging and filters for later.\n\nOnce you answer, I'll send the plan, and screens of the dropdown too if you'd like them.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search global search 2>&1 | head -40; dev-tools/ai/ai kb sear", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 3116 2>&1 | head -40; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 3506 2>&1 ", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search tsvector 2>&1 | head -15; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search fu", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search tsvector 2>&1 | head -15; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search fu", "Listing ares/app/**/*.py", "Searching the code in docker-images", "Searching the code in docker-images", "Searching the code in gaia", "Reading ares/app/adapters/base_ai_adapter.py", "Searching the code in .", "Searching the code in gaia/CLAUDE.md", "Reading gaia/CLAUDE.md", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.721239	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 22:27:52	f	\N
