e017cf336af2-bf67-cd6a-35a605183a09	8ed0e1366af2-ca37-d7c4-675b9ea9985d	Here's the plan: 10 issues in two phases.\n\n**Phase 1, fuzzy search (4 issues).** This ships a working global search with no new infrastructure.\n- **Gaia framework:** model metadata can declare trigram (`gin_trgm_ops`) indexes, and migrate makes sure the extensions they need exist.\n- **Gaia search core:** one search source per type (issue, milestone, project) and a coordinator that merges them. Every source applies the same project scope as the normal list endpoints, so search never bypasses the ACL.\n- **Gaia search API:** a read-only `search` resource built like `workflowevent`, so it stays within the CRUD-only rule.\n- **Prometheus:** the header dropdown searches all three types and groups the results.\n\n**Phase 2, semantic search (6 issues).**\n- **Database:** pgvector in the Postgres images, then a `vector` field type in Gaia's metadata.\n- **Ares:** a new `POST /embed` endpoint behind an embedding adapter, with Ollama as the first provider.\n- **p4m:** the local stack runs Ollama and pulls the model.\n- **Gaia:** a `Searchembedding` table filled by a cron task.\n- **Gaia:** search blends trigram and vector rankings, and falls back to fuzzy only when Ares or Ollama is down.\n\n**Keeping Ollama swappable.**\n- Ares picks the provider from env (`EMBEDDING_PROVIDER`).\n- Each embedding row records the model that produced it, and the column has no fixed dimension.\n- So changing provider means changing an env var and letting the task re-embed. No migration is needed.\n- The cost is an exact vector scan instead of an HNSW index. That's fine at our size, and the index can come later.\n\n**Changes from what I described before:**\n- I dropped the separate full-text (`tsvector`) layer. Trigram matching covers fuzzy search, and embeddings cover meaning, so it would add complexity for little gain.\n- I added the p4m issue for Ollama in the local stack.\n\n**Left out:**\n- a full results page and paging\n- searching comments, wikis or ideas\n- an HNSW vector index\n- highlighting why a result matched\n- selecting the milestone's tab on the board (milestone results open the project's board)\n- the production image in `docker-images`, which has no tracker project; someone needs to change it by hand\n\nThe Ares and p4m issues are written as requests to those projects. No milestone was asked for, so everything goes in Claude-v1. I can also show the grouped dropdown as a screen before you approve.	message	["Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/docker-compose.yaml", "Searching the code in gaia/core/services/LLM.php", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/WorkfloweventController.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/tasks/WorkflowTask.php", "Searching the code in .", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/libs/meta/migration.php", "Reading gaia/core/libs/meta/migration.php", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php", "Searching the code in dev-tools/installer", "Reading ares/docker-compose.yml", "Searching the code in ares/app/factories/ai_service_factory.py", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/router.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/app-layouts", "Searching for \\"searchedItem\\" in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Updating the knowledge map"]	dd4d1c826af2-bf67-cd6a-cb95854d457c	0.625651	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 22:40:32	f	\N
