89e265736af2-8040-cd6a-34e6f1511642	341481c56af2-8040-cd6a-5ea33d81936b	I've looked at the current Threads page. Here's how I'd move it to the same list + detail layout as Roles and Ideas.\n\n**What you're asking for:** Threads gets the Roles/Ideas layout. A `QuickList` of threads goes on the left (col-md-3) and the open thread goes on the right (col-md-9), with ezSearch, paging, sorting and grouping.\n\n**What's there today**\n- The page is one route, `app.project.conversation`. It shows an infinite-scroll feed of `Conversation::ConversationItem` cards in the middle. The opened thread (`?c_id=`) sits in a side column.\n- The controller is about 1,200 lines. It has hand-written filters (My Likes, Votes/Discussion, Linked/Unlinked) and date filters. The route reloads the whole page whenever the search changes (`refreshModel: true`), which is the same problem we fixed for Ideas in 4428.\n- The opened thread loads its comments and votes through `rels`. That breaks the rule against loading hasMany lists that way. The add-thread modal also uses a raw `<PowerSelect>` for the linked issue, where the design system requires a `FormFields` field.\n- Four places link to `?c_id=`, so those links have to keep working: the project overview, the issue list, the weekly-conversations widget and `tag-parser.js` (which builds the URL by hand).\n- Roles (aprom-4430) and Ideas (4428) already show how to do this: QuickList, the state toolkit (`ListLoader`/`UrlState`), `views.<Model>.search`, and the first row opening automatically.\n\n**Proposed shape**\n1. **List + routing:** add a child route `conversations/:conversation_id`. The first thread opens automatically, and the index page sends an old `?c_id=X` link on to `/conversations/X`. Searching and paging reload only the list. Each row shows the creator's avatar, the subject, a Vote/Discussion label, the linked issue badge if there is one, and the last-modified date. The `+` button opens the existing create modal.\n2. **Search:** move the hand-written filters into `views.Conversationroom.search` (subject, description, room type, linked issue, created and modified dates), shown in `<EzSearchCompact>` with saved searches.\n3. **Detail pane:** a new page for the open thread that loads its comments and votes with their own queries and keeps live updates.\n4. **Cleanup:** remove the old feed, the hand-written filters and the infinite-scroll code from the controller.\n\n**Questions (each with my recommendation, so "yes" works)**\n1. **Detail layout, Idea-like or Role-like?** I recommend **Idea-like**: the thread (subject, description, comments, reply box) in col-md-8, and side boxes in col-md-4 (linked issue, votes/poll results, details). Threads are conversations, so they read like an idea page. Role-like means everything stacked at full width.\n2. **"My Likes" filter:** it filters on who voted, which the search metadata can't express yet. I recommend **dropping it from v1** and adding it later as a saved search or a "Mine" toggle. Is that OK?\n3. **Counts in the rows:** showing comment and vote counts would mean loading every thread's comments and votes. I recommend **no counts in v1**; they'd need Gaia to return a count field (a later agaia issue). Is that OK?\n\n**Your screenshot:** it came through as inline data, not a file, so I couldn't open it. Is it the current Threads page or a mockup of what you want? If it's a mockup, could you attach it as a file?\n\nOnce you've answered, I'll render the screens (list + idea-like detail, empty state, mobile) before writing the plan.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching for \\"conversation\\" in prometheus/app/router.js", "Listing prometheus/app/{templates,routes,controllers}/app/project/conversation*/**", "Listing .runs/*/prometheus/app/components/quick-list/*.js", "Listing prometheus/app/**/conversation*", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M; ls .runs 2>/dev/null | tail