6b2109556af2-eedc-cd6a-a5875541f086	341481c56af2-8040-cd6a-5ea33d81936b	I've rendered two screens: the thread list with the first thread open, and the empty state. Both use milestone **aga-threads**. I couldn't look up the project's milestones, so if aga-threads doesn't exist in A Prometheus yet, it will be created when you approve the plan. These are a guide for layout and content only; the real QuickList and ezSearch components decide the final look.\n\n**Screen 1 (`threads-list`): list on the left, first thread open on the right**\n- **List (col-md-3):** "Threads 1-20 / 20+" with a New Thread button and the compact ezSearch bar.\n- **Grouping:** on by default, by the **milestone of the thread's linked issue**. Groups appear in sort order, and threads with no linked issue go last under "No milestone". As in Ideas, grouping only covers the page that was loaded.\n- **Sorting:** by last updated by default.\n- **Rows:** creator initials, subject, Vote or Discussion label, linked issue key, last-modified date. The open thread gets the crimson left bar.\n- **Detail (col-md-9), Idea-like:** the thread box (col-md-8) shows subject, likes and edit in the header, the description, comments with "Load older comments", and a reply box. Beside it (col-md-4) are a **Linked issue** box (status, key, subject, milestone) and a **Details** box (type, who started it, last updated, likes).\n\n**Screen 2 (`threads-empty`): nothing matches the search**\n- The applied filter shows as a chip, the list box says no thread matches with a Clear search button, and the right side says no thread is open.\n\n**Still open:**\n- **My earlier three questions.** The screens assume my recommendations: Idea-like detail, "My Likes" left out of v1, and no comment or vote counts in the rows.\n- **Vote threads.** Vote rooms currently show agree/disagree poll boxes, and the screen doesn't include them yet. I'd put them as a **Votes** box in the side column.\n- **Loading milestones for grouping.** I'd load t