300e08a86af2-deea-cd6a-1ba423bd435e	341481c56af2-8040-cd6a-5ea33d81936b	I've got your answers and written the plan.\n\n**Your artifact link:** I can't open it. I have no web access, and claude.ai artifacts need a login anyway. If it's a mockup, attach it as an image and I'll update the screens and the plan to match.\n\n**How I read your answers** (tell me if any are wrong):\n1. **Idea-like detail:** confirmed.\n2. **Keep "My Likes":** Gaia doesn't actually need a change for this. Today's filter already sends `(votes.createdUser : <me>)` and Gaia handles it. The work is in Prometheus: ezSearch gets a "Liked by" field. So the Gaia issue I've planned is the one for the counts.\n3. **Counts:** for now each row loads its counts with separate Gaia calls, as you said. Today's page does this only for comments (one query per thread); likes come in through `rels: 'votes'`, which breaks the house rule. Separately, there's a request to A Gaia for a read-only counts resource. `Userlatestproject` already counts this way (a database view with COUNT subqueries), so there's a precedent. Once it exists, a follow-up issue switches the rows to one query per page.\n\n**Defaults I've assumed:**\n- **Vote threads:** they get a **Votes** box in the side column, holding the existing agree/disagree poll.\n- **Grouping:** on by default, by the linked issue's milestone. The project's milestones are loaded once, and threads with no linked issue go in "No milestone", shown last.\n\n**Order of work:**\n- `threads-search` comes first, then `threads-list`.\n- After the list, `threads-row-counts` and `threads-detail` can run in parallel.\n- `threads-create-form` waits for the row-counts issue because both edit the same template.\n- The Gaia request runs in parallel with everything. `threads-counts-switch` comes after both it and the row-counts issue.\n- `threads-cleanup` runs last.\n\nAll issues go in milestone **aga-threads** (A Prometheus and A Gaia). I couldn't check whether it already exists; if it doesn't, it will be created when you approve.\n\n**Left out:**\n- Grouping across all pages: grouping covers only the loaded page, as in Ideas.\n- Reply threading (aprom-3750 is still open).\n- Moving Board and Gantt onto the state toolkit.	message	["Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model", "Listing gaia/app/metadata/model/{Conversationroom,Vote}.php", "Updating the knowledge map"]	2f09faf16af2-deea-cd6a-93defe2ddcd9	0.436596	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 22:50:24	f	\N
