a6235d176af2-ba30-232a-c28ed6b400d9	341481c56af2-8040-cd6a-5ea33d81936b	I've rendered the vote thread (`threads-vote`) and split vote threads out into their own issue in plan v2.\n\n**How votes work today** (from `ConversationItem`):\n- A vote is stored as a comment whose text is "I agree" or "I disagree". The thumbs add that comment.\n- Each person gets **one vote** and can't change it.\n- Vote threads have no reply box.\n- The tallies are counted in the browser over **all** of the thread's comments.\n\n**This affects the plan.** The thread page now loads comments 10 at a time, and counting only those 10 would give wrong tallies. So the vote panel needs its own query for all of the thread's vote comments. I've also asked Gaia to return `agreeCount` and `disagreeCount` alongside the other counts.\n\n**What the vote screen shows:**\n- The proposal, then the two existing agree/disagree boxes with counts, percentages and progress bars.\n- A "You haven't voted yet" hint. Once you've voted, the thumbs lock and the hint says "You voted: I agree".\n- The newest votes as a list of who voted what, with "Show all N votes".\n- On the side: a **Result** box ("Leaning: I agree (4 of 5)", "5 of 9 project members voted"), plus Linked issue and Details.\n- List rows for vote threads show the number of votes instead of comments.\n\nThe progress bars render empty in the preview because inline widths are stripped; the app sets the widths.\n\n**About the side boxes:** you said you like Linked issue and Details "on the left", but in the screens they sit on the **right** (col-md-4), as on the idea page. I've kept them on the right. If you want them on the left, say so and I'll swap them.\n\n**Other things a thread could do.** None of these are in the plan; pick any you want.\n\n| | What | Needs Gaia? |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | **Close a vote / record the decision**: the creator closes it, the result is fixed, and an "Outcome" line appears in the Result box | yes (status and closed date on the thread) |\n| B | **Create an issue from a thread**: a button in the Linked issue box that creates an issue already linked to the thread (for votes too, once decided) | no |\n| C | **Link an issue to vote threads**: today only discussions can be linked | no (just a UI rule) |\n| D | **Participants box**: who commented or voted, as avatars | no |\n| E | **Follow a thread**: get notified about new comments or votes | yes |\n| F | **Vote deadline**: the vote closes itself at a set date | yes |\n| G | **Change my vote** | maybe (update or delete the vote comment) |\n| H | **Activity**: created, edited, linked, closed | partly (activities exist) |\n\nMy recommendation: A, B and C give the most for the effort; A turns a vote into a recorded decision.	message	["Reading prometheus/app/components/conversation/conversation-item.hbs", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"threads-vote\\" title=", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/threads-vote.png", "Updating the knowledge map"]	a50aeb156af2-ba30-232a-3daac8cc6940	0.643028	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 23:00:54	f	[{"uploadId": "9e0f91326af2-ba30-232a-144c211ecade", "key": "threads-vote", "title": "Threads: vote thread open (not voted yet)", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}]
