89d239d76af2-c9f1-5ed1-7359a00ee456	341481c56af2-8040-cd6a-5ea33d81936b	I've redone all three screens from your mockup, kept the info column, and rewritten the plan as v3.\n\n**What changed in the screens:**\n- **Layout:** the list sits in col-md-3, the thread in col-md-6 and the info column in col-md-3. The 6 + 3 split is the same width as col-md-8 / col-md-4 inside the col-md-9 detail area.\n- **Header:** "New thread" moved to the page header, as in your mockup.\n- **Thread box, following your mockup:**\n  - a small uppercase type label (DISCUSSION / VOTE) above a 22px title;\n  - like and edit buttons on the right;\n  - the linked issue line with its status label, then "Started by … · date";\n  - the description, an "N COMMENTS" heading, comments with round initials avatars and highlighted mentions;\n  - the reply box with the user's avatar.\n- **Vote thread:** the agree/disagree boxes, a "you haven't voted" hint, and a list of who voted what (name, time, choice label). On the side: Result, Participants and Activity. There's no Linked issue box, since linking votes is left out.\n- **Discussion info column:** a Linked issue box with **Create issue from thread**, then Participants, then Activity.\n- **List:** consistent across all three screens, grouped by milestone. Per your point 1, no list screen is attached to any issue, so QuickList's own styling decides how the list looks.\n\n**Left out:**\n- From your mockup: the All/Discussions/Votes/Mine/Unread tabs (ezSearch and saved searches cover type and "Mine"; Unread would need read tracking in Gaia), "Any time", and Following.\n- From your decisions: linking issues to vote threads, vote deadlines, changing a vote.\n- The list uses QuickList's pager instead of "Load more".\n\n**Activity needs Gaia work.** Gaia records activities for issues (`IssueactivitiesComponent`, using the shared Activity model), but nothing records them for threads. So there's a second request to A Gaia. It records only a few kinds of change: thread started, subject or description edited, linked issue set or cleared. Comments and votes are left out because they already show in the thread.\n\n**Order of work:**\n- `threads-search` → `threads-list`.\n- After the list, `threads-row-counts` and `threads-detail` can run in parallel.\n- `threads-create-form` follows `threads-row-counts` because both edit the list template.\n- The detail-page issues run in a chain because they all edit the same page and info column: `threads-detail` → `threads-vote` → `threads-participants` → `threads-create-issue` → `threads-activity`. `threads-activity` also waits for the Gaia activities request.\n- Both Gaia requests can start at any time. `threads-counts-switch` comes after the Gaia counts request, the row counts and the vote issue.\n- `threads-cleanup` runs last.\n\nAll issues go in milestone **aga-threads**.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/ideas/341481c56af2-8040-cd6a-5ea33d81936b/images/threads-mockup.png", "Searching the code in gaia/app", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/ConversationroomController.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/IssueController.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/IssueactivitiesComponent.php", "Reading prometheus/app/styles/variables.scss", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"threads-list\\" title=", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/threads-list.png", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && mkdir -p .tmp/nestor 2>/dev/null; cat > .tmp/nestor/thr.css <<'EOF' .thr .thr-ql", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"threads-vote\\" title=", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/threads-vote.png", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"threads-empty\\" title", "Updating the knowled