015fb7096af3-c415-1996-a3bcd4e969db	00d17cb06af3-c415-1996-69951fb2ab5f	<span class="colour" style="color: rgb(191, 191, 191);">**Run the tests in parallel with `ember-exam`.** It splits the same test list across several browsers:</span>\n<br>\n```\nember build --environment=test --output-path=dist\nember exam --path dist --split=4 --parallel --load-balance\n```\n\n<span class="colour" style="color: rgb(191, 191, 191);">With four browsers, the 3 minutes of test time drops to about 1 minute, and the suite keeps working the same way as it grows. In CI you can go further: build once, pass `dist` to a matrix of jobs (`--split=N --partition=i`), and require all of them to pass.</span>\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\nInvestigate this, and will this work in Github as well are Talos?	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-10 16:10:41	f	[]
