704ff9a86af3-c415-1996-06fbd2707a7b	00d17cb06af3-c415-1996-69951fb2ab5f	Yes, it can work in both places, but it needs different changes in each. In both, the risk to plan for is not ember-exam itself: on GitHub it's an install bug that blocks it, and in Talos it's memory. Here is what I checked.\n\n## Where we are today\n\n- **ember-exam is not installed.** `tests/test-helper.js` uses ember-qunit's `start()`. `--load-balance` needs ember-exam's own `start` there instead (`ember-exam/test-support/start`). Our stack is ember-cli 4.1, ember-qunit 5.1 and testem 3.18, so we'd pin an ember-exam version that supports ember-qunit 5 (likely 7.x). That needs checking when the work is done.\n- **Talos and local runs already build once.** `p4m test ember` (`dev-tools/installer/testenv.py`) keeps `ember build --environment=test --watch` warm and runs `ember test --path /tmp/p4m-test-dist` (`test_command`, ~l.523). Moving to `ember exam --path … --split=N --parallel --load-balance` fits that directly.\n- **GitHub CI** (`prometheus/.github/workflows/ci.yml`) is one job, `Build-and-Test`, that runs `COVERAGE=true ember test`. That command builds and tests in one step, and the job uploads the coverage report.\n\n## Will it work on GitHub?\n\nYes, but first:\n\n1. **The CI cache key is a fixed `npm-cache`** and the repo has no `package-lock.json`. Once that cache exists, `npm install` is skipped, so adding ember-exam would never get installed in CI. The key has to depend on `package.json`. It's a latent bug today anyway.\n2. **Coverage.** Each parallel browser writes its own coverage. ember-cli-code-coverage needs `parallel: true` (there's no `config/coverage.js` yet) and an `ember coverage-merge` step, or the report covers only one part of the suite.\n3. **How much faster depends on the runner.** For public repos, `ubuntu-latest` has 4 vCPUs, so 4 browsers in one job is about right. Private repos get fewer cores, so gains are smaller.\n4. **One job or a matrix.** A matrix (build once, pass `dist` as an artifact, N jobs with `--partition`) scales further. But each job pays again for pulling the `rananoman/prometheus` image and restoring `node_modules`. The required-check names in branch protection also change. Agamemnon's merge gate (`ai/lib/mergegate.py` `check_ci`) is fine with it, because it checks every check run.\n\n## Will it work in Talos?\n\nYes, but memory is the catch. A Prometheus test container has a 4.5 GiB limit, and full runs of about 1,290 tests were already being killed for running out of memory (aprom-4450, adt-4370). Four Chromes add a lot of memory per container, and Talos runs several containers side by side. Also:\n\n- The number of browsers has to be a setting (e.g. `PROMETHEUS_TEST_SPLIT`) checked against the memory limit, probably 2 by default, not 4. It should be measured before we pick the number.\n- Only full runs should split. Filtered runs (`ai test --changed`, `--filter`) are small, so starting several browsers there costs more than it saves.\n- The output parser (`ai/lib/tests.py` `ember`, ~l.172) needs updating. ember-exam prefixes each result with the browser ("Browser Id 2 - …"), and the current regex would leave that in failing test names. The hang markers and the Chrome cleanup in `run_tests` should also be re-checked with several browsers.\n- `node_modules` is a Docker volume shared with `prometheus-dev`, so it has to get the new package too.\n\n## Proposed split\n\n1. **aprom:** add ember-exam and its `start` in the test helper.\n2. **aprom:** CI workflow: a cache key that depends on `package.json`, build once, `ember exam --parallel`, merged coverage. Depends on issue 1.\n3. **adt:** `p4m test ember` / `ai test` run full suites with ember-exam, with a configurable split, memory measured, and the parser fixed. Depends on issue 1, and can go side by side with issue 2.\n\nA matrix in CI, and test balancing that uses past timings, would come later and aren't included.\n\n## Questions\n\n1. **Scope:** both GitHub and Talos in this idea? *Recommended: yes, as the three issues above.*\n2. **GitHub shape:** one job with `--parallel` first, or the matrix now? *Recommended: one job. It's cheaper, needs no branch-protection change, and the matrix can come when the suite outgrows it.*\n3. **Coverage in CI:** keep it (merged) or drop it from the parallel run? *Recommended: keep it and merge it.*\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll send the plan.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/prometheus && cat package.json | head -120; ls; ls .github/workflows 2>/dev/null; c", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Listing {package.json,testem.js,ember-cli-build.js,.github/workflows/*,config/environment.js,tests/test-helper.js} in prometheus", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Listing * in prometheus", "Reading prometheus/.github/workflows/ci.yml", "Searching the code in prometheus/package.json", "Listing testem* in prometheus", "Reading prometheus/testem.js", "Searching the code in dev-tools/ai/lib/tests.py", "Listing config/coverage.js in prometheus", "Searching the code in dev-tools/installer", "Reading dev-tools/ai/lib/tests.py", "Reading dev-tools/installer/testenv.py", "Reading dev-tools/installer/testenv.py", "Listing {package-lock.json,yarn.lock,tests/test-helper.js,config/ember-cli-update.json} in prometheus", "Searching the code in dev-tools/ai/lib/mergegate.py", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search ember exam parallel tests; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search p", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4450 | head -60; echo ----; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4372", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search PROMETHEUS_TEST_MEMORY out of memory --project adt | g", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search prometheus test memory limit --project adt", "Sear