6c72a5d86af3-640b-1996-a28e7e79e3a5	00d17cb06af3-c415-1996-69951fb2ab5f	The deprecation fix is worth doing, but the code doesn't match the claim. That changes the plan.\n\n## What I found\n\n- **There is only one `assign` from `@ember/polyfills` in `app/`**, not about 10. It's in `app/authenticators/oauth2.js` (import on line 11, the call on line 106). Adapters use lodash's `_.assign`, and everything else already uses `Object.assign`.\n- **That one call can't cause the flood.** It runs in `authenticate()`, which is only used for a real login. Acceptance tests log in with ember-simple-auth's `authenticateSession` (`tests/acceptance/steps/app/sign-in-steps.js`), which skips it. Only the oauth2 unit test and the sign-in feature reach it.\n- So the ~18.7k stack traces most likely come from **our addons**: ember-simple-auth 4.2, ember-power-select 4, the ember-intl 6 beta, Mirage 2.2. Or they come from a different deprecation ID. `node_modules` is in the Docker volume, so I can't read it to confirm.\n- There's **no deprecation handling in tests today**: no handler and no ember-cli-deprecation-workflow. Ember's debug build writes every deprecation to `console.warn` with a stack trace, and testem captures each one.\n\n## What I suggest\n\n1. **Replace the one `assign`** in the oauth2 authenticator with `Object.assign`. It's tiny, but it removes our own use of the API.\n2. **Handle deprecations in `tests/test-helper.js`** with Ember's built-in `registerDeprecationHandler`. It's about 15 lines and needs no new dependency, which the house rules require us to get approval for. It hides the listed IDs, counts each deprecation by ID, and prints one summary line per ID when the run ends. That shows where the flood really comes from without the stack traces.\n   - ember-cli-deprecation-workflow does the same thing as a package. It fits better with the stack upgrade, where its "fix them one by one" workflow pays off.\n\nHiding deprecations only covers the tests. The real fix is upgrading the addons, which belongs with the stack upgrade. Neither issue needs the other, so they can go side by side.\n\n\n\nOne question: should the test helper hide **only `deprecate-assign`**, or **every deprecation ID that comes from an addon**? I recommend only `deprecate-assign` for now. The summary will show the other IDs and their counts, and we can add any to the list once we've seen them.	message	["Searching for \\"@ember/polyfills\\" in prometheus", "Searching the code in prometheus", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in prometheus/package.json", "Listing node_modules/ember-simple-auth/package.json in prometheus", "Searching for \\"@ember/polyfills\\" in .runs", "Listing */prometheus/node_modules/ember-simple-auth/package.json in .runs", "Listing */prometheus/app/authenticators/oauth2.js in .runs", "Reading prometheus/app/authenticators/oauth2.js", "Listing **/prometheus-ember*.log in dev-tools/ai/state", "Searching the code in prometheus/tests", "Searching the code in prometheus", "Searching the code in prometheus/tests/acceptance/steps/app/sign-in-steps.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/tests/acceptance", "Updating the knowledge map"]	6bc637a06af3-640b-1996-4d3c09c1b6c6	0.397799	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-10 16:21:00	f	\N
