751de9286af4-a328-1af5-a4a8b9af7309	e66181d96af4-7c69-1af5-a7b779ce5171	Here's how the paginated **Project Milestones** box would look on the project dashboard (side column, under Members).\n\n**How it works**\n- **What it reuses:** the existing `Pagination` component (`app/components/pagination.{hbs,js}`). The weekly activity/conversation widgets and `AppUi::Table` already use it, so the box gets the same ‹ › footer and no new markup or styles.\n- **What's on the page:** 5 milestones per page, with "1–5 / 14" in the middle of the footer. The footer only shows when there are more than 5 milestones.\n- **Paging happens in the browser, with no API change.** The route (`routes/app/project/index.js` ~88) already loads every milestone with `limit: -1`. The estimated-vs-spent chart filter and the per-milestone issue counts need that full list anyway, so paging on the server would mean extra queries for nothing. Paging just slices the list that's already sorted by start date, newest first.\n- **Edge cases:** adding a milestone through the existing "+" dialog updates the count and the › button, and editing one keeps you on the same page.\n\n**Left out (MVP):** server-side paging, page-size selector, filtering by status. The full milestone and issue load on this page is a separate performance issue and I'd keep it out of this one.\n\n**Open:** 5 per page is my pick, since the box is about one screen tall at that size. Say if you want a different number.\n\nI couldn't update my knowledge map this turn because the edit was denied. Nothing in the plan depends on it.\n\n\n\nThis all fits in one Prometheus issue:	message	["Running cat /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md | head -300", "Searching for \\"milestone\\" in prometheus/app/templates", "Searching for \\"milestone\\" in prometheus/app/templates/app/project/index.hbs", "Searching issues: milestone pagination --project aprom 2>&1 | head -40; ls prometheus/docs/ui/screens/", "Reading pr