0ee812276af4-eaef-53d2-dea75d8d5a54	a0d222596af4-fbea-53d2-9717e6de5108	Docs isn't a blank slate. **agaia-4488** is done: the `Doc` resource (title, `body text`, owner, `locked`, tags), plus ADR D-001, which says Docs is independent of Wiki and leaves the body format undecided. **aprom-4489–4492** (model, page, All Docs, create) exist but are deferred. That fits, since the body format is the first decision this architecture makes.\n\n## The core decision: a separate sync service, with Gaia as the system of record\n\nThe live part of the design can't run through today's pipeline:\n- **Gaia → Hermes:** Gaia is PHP request/response.\n- **Hermes is a locked relay** (D-001): no storage, no domain logic, and clients can only send `intents:set`.\n\nCursors, "is typing" and character-by-character co-editing need clients to send many small updates to each other, and something has to merge them. I recommend:\n\n| Piece | Choice | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Content model | **CRDT (Yjs)** | It merges concurrent edits without a central lock. It also gives offline editing (an IndexedDB copy in the browser that syncs on reconnect) and awareness (presence, cursors, selections, typing) for free. |\n| Editor | **ProseMirror via TipTap + y-prosemirror** in Prometheus | Toast UI is a markdown editor and can't do CRDT editing, suggestion marks or anchored comments. It's a new npm dependency, so it needs your approval. |\n| Live sync | **New Node service** (Hocuspocus-style), separate from Hermes | Hermes keeps its single job of relaying events. The sync service holds open docs in memory, and its sockets check per-doc access with Gaia. |\n| Persistence | **Gaia, through CRUD, with the service acting as a service client** | `Docstate` holds the Yjs binary state, saved a few seconds after editing goes quiet. Gaia also stores a derived `body` (HTML plus plain text) for search, AI and export. Gaia stays the only owner of the data. |\n| Project events | Unchanged: Gaia → Hermes (`doc.updated`, comment events, …) | The list, notifications and issue pages stay live the way they are today. |\n\nHow the rest of the design fits:\n- **Sharing** needs a new Gaia ACL concept: `Docaccess` (user or agent, with role viewer, commenter or editor), layered on top of the project scope, plus a `linkSharing` field on Doc. Today Gaia only knows project scope, so this is framework work and the riskiest piece.\n- **Suggestions and comment anchors** live inside the Yjs doc as marks carrying `authorId` and `actedForId`. Comment threads reuse Gaia's `Comment` (`relatedTo` already has ACL child paths), so mentions and notifications come for free.\n- **Agents** connect to the sync service as Yjs clients with delegated tokens (aga-Identity), and the service only lets them write in suggest mode. Each change then records both the agent and the person it acted for.\n- **History:** `Docversion` holds snapshots (autosaved and named). Compare shows a diff of two snapshots, and restore applies an old snapshot as a new edit.\n- **Locking** is enforced in two places: Gaia rejects writes to a locked doc, and the sync service opens it read-only.\n- **"Stop viewers downloading or copying"** can only be partly enforced. The server can refuse export and print for them, but blocking copy in the browser is just a deterrent. I'd say that in the UI rather than promise more.\n- **Search inside a doc** happens in the editor. **Search across docs** uses the derived plain text and should join the fuzzy-search work (aga-Fuzzies) rather than build a second index.\n- **Export:** for the MVP, PDF through print styles and the browser's own print. Word export is a later Gaia or Ares task.\n\n## Suggested phases\n1. **Foundations:** an ADR for the body format and sync architecture, Doc fields (`parentId`, `archived`, `linkSharing`, `milestoneId`), the 4488 ACL follow-ups, `Docstate`, the sync service, and the editor on the doc page. Then un-defer aprom-4489–4492.\n2. **Sharing:** `Docaccess`, the Share dialog, transfer ownership, lock.\n3. **Review:** anchored comments, suggestions, mentions and notifications.\n4. **History**, then **project links** (issues with live status, milestone, turning text into issues).\n5. **AI agents as suggesters**, then **export and search**.\n\nThat's roughly 35–45 issues across agaia, aprom, a new repo, aa and adt.\n\n## Three questions before I write phase 1\n1. **Where does the sync service live?** I can only plan in agaia, aprom, ah, aa and adt. *Recommended:* a new repo and project (a name in the Greek-myth style is your call), and you create the project first. The fallback is a separate process inside the Hermes repo, but that bends D-001.\n2. **Guests on day one?** Gaia has no guest user type, and adding one is an identity project of its own. *Recommended:* leave guests out. Share with project members and agents now, and add guests later.\n3. **Phase 1 scope:** *Recommended:* foundations only (phase 1 above), in the existing **aga-Docs-MVP** milestone, ending with a working shared editor that has presence and cursors. Sharing, comments and later phases come as follow-up plans.\n\nSay yes, or adjust, and I'll send the phase 1 plan with screens for the doc page.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Gaia: get idea", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Listing dev-tools/talos/state/ideas/a0d22259*/**", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search wiki lock --project agaia 2>&1 | head -30; dev-tools/a", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search \\"Docs:\\" 2>&1 | grep '^#' | head -40", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4488 2>&1 | head -60; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4489 2>&1 ", "Listing {gaia/docs/architecture/docs/*,gaia/app/metadata/model/Doc*.php,hermes/docs/**/*.md,hermes/src/**/*.js}", "Searching the code in hermes/docs/architecture/decisions.md", "Searching the code in hermes/CLAUDE.md", "Reading hermes/docs/architecture/decisions.md", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model/Comment.php", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search docs mvp milestone sync yjs 2>&1 | grep '^#' | head; d", "Searching the code in prometheus/package.json", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search wiki lock owner 2>&1 | grep '^#' | head -6", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.916165	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-11 14:17:50	f	\N
