40cd1e426af4-3b69-e9a2-ebbfe3194671	d98352c16af4-9ee0-e9a2-4dddf1b444ee	## Upgrading Gaia to PHP 8.5 and Phalcon 5\n\n**Where Gaia is now:** PHP 7.x (most likely 7.4 on Debian 10) and Phalcon 4. Both are past end of life. The repo files point to this, but I couldn't run commands in the container. `docker exec gaia-dev php -v` and `php --ri phalcon` would confirm it; the first issue records it.\n\n**Target:** PHP 8.5 needs Phalcon 5, because Phalcon 4 never supported PHP 8. I can't confirm that **Phalcon 5.23.0** exists: my information only goes to about 5.9/5.10. The first issue checks the release notes and pins the newest Phalcon 5 that supports PHP 8.5.\n\n### What will break\nSome failures stop Gaia from starting, so they're easy to see. Others change behaviour without any error, and those are the ones to plan for.\n\n| | What breaks | How we'll see it |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fails loudly | Phalcon 5 class renames: `Loader`, `Logger`, `Config`, `Text`, `Di` and the Session adapter. They're in about 12 files, mostly startup code. Also mismatched method signatures in about 20 model behaviours. | Gaia won't start or the class won't load. Any test catches it. |\n| Fails loudly | Old packages: the 6 `phalcon/incubator*` packages (no code uses them), `phalcon/devtools` (only needed for the Migration base class), `elasticsearch ~6` and `monolog ~1` (only used by `AdminTask`), and the `ext-psr` requirement | `composer install` fails |\n| **Silent, dangerous** | `docker/dev/start.sh` runs `migrate` every time Gaia starts, and migrate **drops columns that aren't in the metadata**. If Phalcon 5 reads Postgres columns differently, it could alter or drop columns on the deployed database. There's no dry run today. | Not visible today. Needs a `--dry-run` and a comparison of the schema each stack produces. |\n| Silent | Models declare no column properties, so all columns are dynamic properties, which PHP 8.2+ deprecates. Other PHP 8 changes: comparisons between strings and numbers, null passed to built-in functions, `Iterator` return types. | Deprecations nobody looks at. Needs a grouped deprecation log. |\n| Silent | Response shapes Prometheus reads can change: `"1"` vs `1`, null vs `""`, float precision | Responses can change and still pass the api-tester checks. Needs a comparison of the old and new stack's responses. |\n\n### Gaps in what we can test today\n- CI only runs 4 PHPUnit folders. `models/`, `foundation/`, `api/`, `libraries/workflows`, `query` and `authorization` never run there.\n- The CI and dev base image (`rananoman/gaia:env-dev`) has no Dockerfile in any repo, so we can't rebuild it or build a version-changed copy.\n- **Security:** `gaia/docker-compose.yaml` lines 7–8 contain a real Gmail app password. It should be rotated now, by hand. One issue below removes it from the file, but git history still has it.\n\n### Approach: run both stacks side by side\nRather than one big upgrade branch:\n1. Measure first: build the target image, run the full test suite in CI, and add the scan and reporting tools.\n2. Make the same code start on both the old and new stack.\n3. Add a non-blocking CI job on the new stack that lists everything that fails, in one summary.\n\nThe fixes and the final switch-over get planned from that list. That's the "how easy is it to see what fails" part: every PR shows the list going down.\n\n**Left out for now (planned after the first report):**\n- fixing the failures on the new stack;\n- the switch-over itself (default image, the xhgui `php7.4` image, CD, removing the compatibility layer);\n- upgrading PHPUnit to 10+ and php-parser to 5;\n- Phalcon 6.\n\n### Questions\n1. **Remove the old Elasticsearch search code in `AdminTask`?** I recommend yes. It's the only user of `elasticsearch ~6` and `monolog ~1`. The plan includes it as `drop-elasticsearch`.\n2. **Side-by-side stacks or one upgrade branch?** I recommend side by side. It adds one temporary compatibility class, but every failure shows up early and gets fixed in its own PR.\n3. **Keep the SMTP-secret issue in this plan?** I recommend yes, because it's in files we change anyway.	message	["Running cd /d/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M; grep -n -i -E \\"php|phalcon|docker|upgrade\\" dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md | h", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Listing {composer.json,Dockerfile*,docker-compose*.yml,phpunit*.xml*,codeception*.yml,.github/workflows/*} in gaia", "Listing **/Dockerfile* in docker-images", "Reading docker-images/gaia/Dockerfile", "Listing * in gaia", "Listing {composer.json,composer.lock,**/Dockerfile*,**/docker-compose*.y*ml,phpunit.xml*,**/phpunit.xml*,.github/workflows/*.yml} in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/CLAUDE.md", "Reading gaia/Dockerfile", "Reading gaia/docker/dev/Dockerfile", "Listing **/composer.{json,lock} in gaia", "Reading gaia/CLAUDE.md", "Reading gaia/composer.json", "Searching the code in .", "Reading gaia/docker-compose.yaml", "Listing {docker/**,.github/**,tests/*,tools/*} in gaia", "Listing docker/**/* in gaia", "Listing .github/**/* in gaia", "Listing tests/**/*.php in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/tests", "Reading gaia/tests/phpunit.xml", "Searching for \\".\\" in gaia/.github", "Reading gaia/.github/workflows/ci.yml", "Searching the code in gaia/.github/workflows/cd-ovh.yml", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/models/Model.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/tasks/MigrationTask.php", "Searching the code in gaia", "Reading gaia/core/tasks/MigrationTask.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/libs/meta/migration.php", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/app/models", "Searching the code in gaia/app/models", "Searching issues: php phalcon upgrade version 2>&1 | head -40", "Searching the code in .", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/docker/dev/start.sh", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching t