3fa2c4336af4-3f4c-45d1-902b63b20a0f	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	That's settled: the collab server goes in `hermes/collab/` for now. I changed only the `collab-server` issue to match; the other five issues are the same as before. The changes:\n\n- **Its own package.** `collab/` gets its own `package.json` (all the Yjs, Hocuspocus and Tiptap dependencies stay out of the relay), its own Dockerfile and its own docker-compose service.\n- **No imports from the relay's `src/`.** It gets its own small Gaia client instead of reusing `src/auth/gaia-session.js`, so moving it out later is just moving the folder.\n- **ADR D-016** records that it lives in the hermes repo for now. It moves to its own repo when it takes on agents or export, or when its releases start to clash with the relay's.\n- **Hermes CLAUDE.md update.** Its rule "Hermes stays a locked relay: no domain logic, no storage" will apply to `src/` only. A short section on `collab/` says what the collab server may do: hold docs in memory and save only through Gaia.\n- **Tests and Node 18.** The hermes test script will also run the collab tests, so `ai test hermes` covers them. The issue asks to check that the Hocuspocus version chosen supports Node 18, which Hermes runs on.\n\nThe milestone is still open: should these go in **Docs MVP** like 4488? Right now they would go to Claude-v1. Also remember to un-defer `aprom-4489` and `aprom-4490`, because the collab client issue depends on them.	message	["Updating the knowledge map", "Reading hermes/CLAUDE.md"]	3ea6aeb56af4-3f4c-45d1-b23e8faaed9c	0.221722	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-11 15:48:15	f	\N
cb810ea66af4-3f4c-45d1-2611cedcc927	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	The main idea is to sort data by how often it's written and who reads it. Small metadata goes in one place and heavy content in another, the live CRDT state is kept as one compact copy per doc, and short-lived state (cursors, typing) never touches the database. Gaia runs on PostgreSQL 16, so everything below uses Postgres features.\n\n## The tables\n\n| Table | What's in it | How often it's written | Read by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `doc` | title, projectId, parentId + position (nesting), ownerId, locked, status (active/archived), milestoneId, linkAccess, allowCopy | rarely (rename, move, lock) | lists, tree, every page |\n| **`doccontent`** (1:1 with doc) | `state` (Yjs, base64), `html`, `plainText`, `byteSize` | state every 2–10 s while editing; html/text when idle | collab server, export, search, agents |\n| `docversion` | docId, `state`, `html`, name (empty for automatic), kind auto/named | per editing session or on demand | history, compare, restore |\n| `doccomment` | docId, parentId (replies), anchor, quotedText, body, resolved, resolvedBy | per comment | comment sidebar, notifications |\n| `docshare` | docId, userId or guest email, role viewer/commenter/editor | rarely | access checks |\n| `docfollower` | docId, userId, starred, following | rarely | notifications, "Starred" filter |\n| `docissue` | docId, issueId | when a link is added | issue page, project page |\n| existing `tagged`, `upload` | tags, attachments, images (`relatedTo = 'doc'`) | | |\n\nNot stored anywhere: presence, cursors, "is typing" (collab server memory). Unsent offline edits stay in the browser (IndexedDB).\n\n## Why each choice\n\n**1. One merged snapshot per doc, not a log of every change.**\nThe collab server holds the merged doc in memory and saves the whole state every 2–10 s. Each doc is one row, and opening a doc is one read with nothing to replay or merge.\n- An append-only log of changes writes smaller rows. But it grows with every edit, needs a merge job, and makes opening slower over time.\n- The few seconds a snapshot can lose are covered by the browsers, which keep and resend unsent changes.\n- If very large or very busy docs show up later, we can add "snapshot + log since the snapshot" inside `doccontent` without changing the client contract.\n\n**2. base64 in `text`, not binary `bytea`.**\nGaia's metadata has `blob`, but the REST API speaks JSON, so binary would need encoding work in the framework. base64 is about 33% bigger. Postgres automatically compresses large values and stores them outside the main row (TOAST), which takes back part of that. A 10-page doc is roughly tens of KB of text, so the state should be on the order of 100 KB at most. Switching to `bytea` later is a contained migration if size ever matters.\n\n**3. Content in its own table, not on `doc`. This changes the plan.**\nGaia's `auditBehavior` (`core/mvc/models/behaviors/auditBehavior.php:42`) saves the **old and new value of every changed field**. With `Doc.body` autosaving every few seconds, each save would write two full HTML copies into the audit log. Keeping content out of `doc` also means:\n- list and tree queries never touch it;\n- renaming or locking a doc doesn't rewrite the content;\n- autosaves don't change `dateModified` or fire doc events;\n- the collab server needs write access only to `doccontent`.\n\nSo I'd **rename `Docstate` to `Doccontent`**, give it `state`, `html` and `plainText`, leave out audit, and **drop `Doc.body`**. Doc is new and holds only test rows, so dropping it is safe now and expensive later.\n\n**4. The HTML and plain-text copies are derived, at a slower pace.**\n`state` is the master copy. `html` (for export, previews and agents) and `plainText` (for search) are rebuilt by the collab server when editing goes idle (about 30 s) and on the last disconnect, not on every save.\n\n**5. Versions are full, independent copies.**\nEach `docversion` row holds a complete state and its HTML. We keep Yjs's cleanup of deleted content (garbage collection) **on**, which keeps the live state small. The other option, Yjs's built-in snapshots, needs that cleanup off forever, so every doc keeps every deleted character.\n- Restoring a version = applying its content to the live doc as a new change, so nobody's work is lost.\n- Comparing = diffing two HTML copies.\n- Automatic versions get thinned over time (for example, after 30 days keep one per day); named ones are kept.\n\n**6. Comments live in Gaia; suggestions live in the doc.**\n- **Comments** need notifications, mentions, resolving and listing, so they're rows. The anchor is a Yjs relative position plus a comment mark in the text, so the highlight moves with edits. The row keeps `quotedText` in case the anchored text is deleted.\n- **Suggestions** are edits that haven't been accepted yet, so they live inside the Yjs state as marks (author, `actedFor` for agents). Accept and reject are ordinary edits, and they save, sync, undo and get versioned like everything else. A table for suggestions would only duplicate that.\n\n**7. `projectId` on every Doc table.**\nGaia's access control groups by `projectId` on the row itself, so each child table carries a copy. The cost: moving a doc to another project updates its rows in all those tables, in **one transaction**. It's rare and the trade is worth it. The alternative, access rules inherited through the parent doc, is new framework work.\n\n**8. Search.**\nTo start, title plus a `plainText` filter. Real full-text search (a Postgres GIN `tsvector` index) needs index support in Gaia's declarative migrations. That's framework work for the search phase.\n\n## What this changes in the plan\n- `doc-state-api` becomes `Doccontent` (state, html, plainText, no audit) and drops `Doc.body`. D-002 is reworded to match.\n- `collab-server` writes only `Doccontent`: the state every 2–10 s, html and plainText when idle or on disconnect.\n- The deferred `aprom-4489` (data layer) and `aprom-4492` (Create Doc) mention `body`. Before they're picked up, they need a comment saying the doc model has no body and Create Doc makes an empty doc.\n\nDo you agree with the `Doccontent` change and dropping `Doc.body`? If so, I'll send the revised plan. I'll also put the other tables above in the decisions doc so the later phases build on them.	message	["Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model", "Searching the code in gaia/app/core/config", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia", "Reading gaia/core/libs/meta/manager.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/models/behaviors", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/models/behaviors/auditBehavior.php", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/models/behaviors/auditBehavior.php", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.434549	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-11 15:50:35	f	\N
