ec1ce4a26af5-c6ee-65e3-7deb6a1c54b6	e66181d96af4-7c69-1af5-a7b779ce5171	You're right. aprom-4493 only splits the box into pages in the browser. My plan said "no API change" and kept the `limit: -1` load, but I didn't spell out what that meant: the box got shorter, and the page loads exactly as much data as before. The only gain was visual, and I should have said so plainly.\n\n**Why making the milestones box fetch page by page wouldn't help much on its own**\n\nThe dashboard route (`routes/app/project/index.js` ~80) loads two things, and the milestones are the cheap one:\n\n- **Every issue of the project** (`limit: -1`, with the `estimated,spent` time logs attached to each). This is the real cost. It feeds the totals boxes, the issue-ratio chart, the estimated-vs-spent chart and the issue counts on each milestone.\n- **Every milestone.** These are a few small rows. The estimated-vs-spent chart's milestone dropdown also lists all of them.\n\nIf the box fetched 5 milestones at a time, all the issues would still load. The dropdown would still need every milestone name, so it would be a second milestone query on top. Each page would also lose its total: our paging helper (`utils/state/list-loader.js`) only asks Gaia whether there's a next page, so the footer would read "1 – 5", not "1 – 5 / 14".\n\n**Options**\n\n- **A. Make just the box fetch per page.** Gaia already supports this, so it would be one small Prometheus issue: load 5 at a time with `ListLoader`, and the footer drops the total. The page wouldn't get noticeably faster. I'd only do this if fetching per page matters to you for its own sake.\n- **B. Fix the dashboard's loading (my recommendation if the dashboard feels slow).** Stop loading every issue. Each widget would query only what it needs: totals and issue counts from small queries, the chart from the selected milestone's issues only, and the milestones box paged on the server as in A. That's a separate, bigger idea. It probably needs a Gaia issue for server-side counts, plus 2–3 Prometheus issues.\n\nWhich one are you after? If it's speed, I'll scope B as a new idea. If you just want the box to fetch per page, I'll send the one-issue plan for A.	message	["Reading prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/index.js", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/models/Milestone.php", "Reading issue 4493 2>&1 | head -60", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/utils/state", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/index.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Reading prometheus/app/utils/state/list-loader.js", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.764197	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-12 09:20:44	f	\N
