b74bdfe06af5-a32c-65e3-09f3d0bf652a	e66181d96af4-7c69-1af5-a7b779ce5171	Server-side paging works the same way as in the ideas browser. Each page is its own Gaia request with `limit: 5`, the footer arrows follow Gaia's `meta.links.next`, and the pager stays fixed in the box footer.\n\n**What changes**\n- **Box:** loads its milestones through `ListLoader` (`utils/state/list-loader.js`), the same helper as `controllers/app/project/idea.js`.\n- **Footer:** the box footer holds `QuickList::Pagination` unchanged (`components/quick-list/pagination`). It reads `1-5 / 5+` while there's a next page and `6-9 / 9` on the last one. It disables while a page loads.\n- **aprom-4493 code is replaced:** its in-browser slicing and inline pager in `controllers/app/project/index.js` (~244–372) go away.\n- **Chart dropdown:** the estimated-vs-spent chart still needs every milestone name. Its query becomes a light one (`fields: Milestone.id,Milestone.name,Milestone.dateCreated`, as `utils/state/thread-votes.js` does). The chart takes the selected milestone's issues from the already-loaded issues by `milestoneId`, not from `milestone.issues`.\n- **Issue counts per row:** still come from the issues the dashboard already loads. Each page's milestones get them attached, as `loadMilestones` does today.\n- **Adding a milestone:** reloads page 1.\n\n**Left out:** the dashboard still loads every issue. That's the heavier load, and it stays a separate idea if you want it.	message	["Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/quick-list", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/app/project/idea.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/idea.js", "Listing prometheus/app/components/quick-list*/**/*pag*", "Reading prometheus/app/components/quick-list/pagination.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/quick-list/pagination.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/styles", "Reading prometheus/app/styles/components/quick-list/_pagination.