b76c5bb76af7-b6c3-7359-3cfd0351e115	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	For now, the AI part of Docs has three features. All three go through **Gaia to Ares**; Prometheus never calls Ares directly. Here is how each works, plus the plan, which now covers the first slice and the AI work (13 issues).\n\n## How the three features work\n1. **Selection-based AI.** You select text and choose Improve wording, Shorten, Expand, Summarize, Find open questions, or type your own instruction.\n   - The result shows as a **preview** (the AI Assist box from the screens).\n   - **Insert as suggestion** puts it into the doc as tracked changes, labelled "AI Assist · Agent · for Rana Nouman".\n2. **Suggestions while writing (ghost text).** When you pause at the end of a paragraph, grey text continues your sentence. **Tab** accepts it, **Esc** or any typing dismisses it.\n   - It is off by default; each user turns it on with a toolbar toggle.\n   - It uses a fast model (Haiku 4.5) and is rate-limited.\n   - Text you accept with Tab counts as **your own writing**, not a suggestion. You chose each piece yourself, as with Gmail's Smart Compose; making it a suggestion would mean accepting everything twice.\n3. **AI reviewer.** **Review document** returns findings: unclear wording, open questions, inconsistencies, missing parts.\n   - Each finding quotes the exact text it's about. Clicking it selects that text, **Apply fix** adds a suggestion, and **Dismiss** removes it.\n   - The last review is saved, so the team can reopen it.\n\n## Decisions built into this plan (say if you disagree)\n- **`Doccontent` replaces `Docstate`, and `Doc.body` is dropped**, as I recommended in the storage discussion. I've applied it; tell me if you'd rather keep `body`.\n- **Every AI request is logged in a new Gaia `Docassist` resource.** It records who asked, when, what kind and the result. Ghost-text requests are logged without their text. That log is the `actedFor` record, the rate limit and the cost trail. It's a standard resource; the existing `IssueplanningController` custom action is not copied.\n- **Suggestions are built only for AI to start with.** The editor schema gets suggestion marks now. For you, they show the author and `actedFor`, can be accepted or rejected inline, and are listed in a Suggestions box. A **human Suggesting mode** (your own typing becoming suggestions) is harder and is left for later.\n- **Review findings point at an exact quote, not block ids.** That means no editor ids are needed yet. If the quoted text has been edited since the review, the finding says so.\n- **Credit for AI changes:** they are attributed to "AI Assist" (the source plus `actedFor`) without a new Agent account. Real agent accounts come with the agents-in-the-doc option later.\n\n## Left out for now\n- Agents joining the doc (Option 2), @mentioning agents.\n- Comments. Review findings stay a list; they become comments once comments exist.\n- Human Suggesting mode, streaming responses, catch-up and thread summaries.\n- Sharing, history, export, search.\n\n## Before these are picked up\n- `aprom-4489` (data layer) and `aprom-4492` (Create Doc) still mention `body`. Before they're un-deferred, they need a comment saying the doc model has no body and Create Doc makes an empty doc. I can't change issues myself.\n- Milestone: they would go to Claude-v1. Say **"Docs MVP"** if you want them with 4488.	message	["Reading ../../../.claude/projects/-home-rana-noman-web-hammad-hassan-Pr4M/memory/issue-descriptions-repo-scoped.md", "Running cat ares/CLAUDE.md | head -60; cat ares/app/routers/planissue.py | head -60; grep -n \\"function\\\\|curl\\\\|ARES\\" gaia/core/se", "Searching the code in gaia/app", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/IssueplanningController.php", "Searching issues: \\"issueplanning LLM Ares endpoint resource\\" 2>&1 | grep \\"^#\\" | head -6; grep -n \\"issueplanning\\" gaia/core/config/routes.php", "Updating the knowledge map"]	b64f8ee26af7-b6c3-7359-0cc1081595e7	1.634655	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-13 12:55:19	f	\N
