fa04fe486af7-b6c3-7359-62ce90cb8189	44c783b46af7-b6c3-7359-e3d9f0af5900	This is a small UI change: show the number of issues on each milestone tab of the task board, e.g. "Sprint Claude-v1 **12**".\n\n**What I found**\n- The tabs are in `prometheus/app/components/app-ui/task-board.hbs` (lines 3–12). Each tab already has its milestone, and the board loads `milestone.issues` for every milestone.\n- `controllers/app/project/board.js` already keeps `milestone.issues` up to date when an issue is created, moved or deleted, including when you drag a card onto another tab. So the count can just be `milestone.issues.length`, the same number the progress line "x/y issues" already shows. No Gaia change is needed.\n- I couldn't search the issue tracker for duplicates because the shell isn't available to me this session. Please check that nobody has already filed this.\n\n**Decisions I made (say if you want them different)**\n- The count shows the issues currently loaded on the board. When a board filter is on, it shows the filtered count, matching the lane counts. The other option, the true total, would need extra Gaia queries.\n- It's shown as an AdminLTE `label` (as the design system says) after the milestone name. It also gets a tooltip, e.g. "12 issues".\n- Left out: counts per status on the tab and open/closed splits. The milestone header already shows those.	message	["Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M; grep -n -i -A3 \\"milestone\\" dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md | head -60; d", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Listing prometheus/app/**/*milestone* in .", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching for \\"nav-tabs\\" in prometheus/app/components/app-ui/task-board.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching for \\"milest