f28143576af7-b1e2-90ec-552e0be3bb0c	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	I've changed the plan so there's no AI panel. AI shows up in three places inside the editor, and everything it writes goes through the Suggestions box for approval.\n\n1. **Ghost text, always on.** For anyone who can edit, grey text appears when they pause at the end of a paragraph for about half a second. **Tab** accepts it, and typing or Esc dismisses it. There's no toggle.\n   - The short pause is what keeps the cost reasonable; requests still have a rate limit with back-off.\n   - Text accepted with Tab is the writer's own, not a suggestion.\n2. **Ask AI on a selection.** Selecting text shows a small floating menu with **Ask AI**. The writer types a request ("make this clearer", "turn into a checklist") and presses Enter.\n   - The result goes **straight into the doc as a suggestion**, with no preview step. Nothing is final until someone accepts it.\n   - Because there's no preview, I dropped the preset actions (Improve, Shorten…): just the request field.\n3. **AI Reviewer button** in the toolbar. It reviews the whole doc. Concrete fixes arrive **as suggestions, each with its reason** ("Unclear: …"). Findings with no fix, such as open questions, appear as **notes** linked to their text.\n\nThe **Suggestions box** is the one place to approve or reject: Ask AI changes, reviewer fixes and notes. It's the general review box, not an AI tab, and will hold people's own suggestions too once Suggesting mode exists.\n\n**What changed in the plan**\n- Ares: `/docs/transform` becomes **`/docs/ask`** (the request text is required, no action list). Review findings get an optional `replacement`; without one they're notes.\n- The suggestion marks get a `reason` attribute. That's in both the editor and the collab-server schema.\n- Gaia `Docassist` kinds are now `ask | complete | review`. The completion rate limit goes up to 40 per minute because ghost text is always on.\n- Prometheus: `doc-ai-selection` becomes **`doc-ask-ai`** (floating menu). `doc-ai-complete` loses its toggle. `doc-ai-review` becomes the toolbar button plus suggestions and notes. The old assist-preview and assist-review screens are replaced by the two below.\n\n**Points for you to check**\n- **Everyone sees the reviewer's fixes.** They are suggestions in the shared doc, attributed "AI Reviewer · for <who clicked>". The notes are visible to anyone who opens the doc, and dismissing one hides it only for you.\n- **When a fix can't be placed it becomes a note.** That happens when the quoted text appears more than once or overlaps another fix, so a fix never lands in the wrong place.\n- **Still assumed:** `Doccontent` replacing `Doc.body`, and the Claude-v1 milestone (say "Docs MVP" if you want it).\n\n**The two screens**\n- **ask-ai:** a selected paragraph with the floating Ask AI menu open and a request typed. Grey ghost text is shown at the end of another paragraph only to illustrate it; in practice you'd see one or the other.\n- **ai-reviewer:** after clicking AI Reviewer. The toolbar button shows the review is done, two fixes are inline as suggestions, and the Suggestions box groups the review with Accept all, each fix with its reason, and one note.\n\nThe menu position, ghost-text grey and suggestion colours are approximations; the real styles go in `doc.scss` using existing colours.	message	["Updating the knowledge map"]	f19a1c176af7-b1e2-90ec-b4398bff2c3c	0.633063	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-13 13:17:38	f	[{"uploadId": "df0a8b576af7-b1e2-90ec-03fab79c25a5", "key": "ask-ai", "title": "Ask AI on a selection, and ghost text while writing", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}, {"uploadId": "ea1ac8e16af7-b1e2-90ec-500e09deb300", "key": "ai-reviewer", "title": "AI Reviewer: fixes as suggestions with reasons, plus notes", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 1000}]
8c9c1f466af7-a85f-40f4-4ee18a2af4a8	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	Let's talk about the technical architecture of this. Please share the design for how the backend will work, ensuring everything is real-time.	message	[]	\N	\N	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	Rana Nouman	2026-11-13 13:37:16	f	[]
