b092c3206af7-32e9-40f4-52b4c5124aef	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	The way we store docs is fine for search, but on its own it can't search well. Gaia has no full-text search today, so we'd add a Postgres full-text index on the text we already keep. We don't need a separate search engine.\n\n## What a keyword search would do today\nThe searchable text is already in place: `doc.title` and `doccontent.plainText`. The Yjs state is binary and can't be searched, which is why `plainText` exists. The problem is how Gaia queries text:\n- Its query language's `CONTAINS` becomes `LIKE '%keyword%'` (`gaia/core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php:275`).\n- Model metadata only supports `primary`, `unique` and plain `INDEX` indexes (e.g. `Issue.php:222`). There's nothing for full-text search anywhere in Gaia.\n\nSo a keyword search would:\n- **read every doc's whole text** in the user's projects on each query. A `%…%` match can't use an index, and each body has to be unpacked from Postgres' compressed side storage (TOAST);\n- be **case-sensitive** (Postgres `LIKE`) and literal: "saving" doesn't find "save", and two words must appear together in that exact order;\n- give **no ranking** (a title match counts the same as a passing mention) and **no snippets**.\n\nRoughly: a few hundred docs is fine. Around 1,000 docs of 30 KB means scanning about 30 MB per search, a few hundred ms. With tens of thousands of docs, every search takes seconds.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option | Good | Bad |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Postgres full-text search** (`tsvector` + GIN index) | Millisecond lookups, word stemming, AND/OR/"phrase" queries, ranking, title weighted above body, highlighted snippets (`ts_headline`). Same database, so **permission filtering stays in the same query** and nothing new to run. | No typo tolerance. Gaia's framework needs new support for it. |\n| **Trigram index** (`pg_trgm`) | Makes `%keyword%` fast, case-insensitive and typo-tolerant ("colab" finds "collab"). | Weak relevance ranking. Large index on long text. Best for **titles**. |\n| **External engine** (OpenSearch, Meilisearch, Typesense) | Best relevance, typo tolerance, facets. | A new service to run and keep in sync through events, so results lag behind edits. Permissions must be **copied into the engine**, which risks leaking docs the user can't see. Only worth it at very large scale or for one search across issues, docs and wiki. |\n| **Semantic search** (`pgvector` embeddings) | "Find docs about X" without exact words; fits the AI direction. | Needs embeddings from Ares and chunking. Fine as a later addition next to keyword search, not instead of it. |\n\n## My recommendation: keep the tables, add a search index in Postgres\n- **`doccontent.searchVector`** (`tsvector`): title with weight A plus `plainText` with weight B, with a **GIN index**. Gaia keeps it up to date whenever the collab server writes `plainText` (after 30 s idle or on the last disconnect) and whenever the doc title changes.\n- **Trigram index on `doc.title`**, for the All Docs filter and quick "jump to doc": typo-tolerant and instant.\n- The search query **joins the user's projects** (later also doc sharing), ranks with `ts_rank`, and builds snippets with `ts_headline` **only for the top 20** results, because snippets are the expensive part.\n- **Search inside one doc** (Ctrl+F style) stays in the browser, as an editor search plugin over the live doc. It's instant and needs no backend.\n- **How fresh results are:** a doc being edited shows up in search with its new text within about 30 s of a pause. Titles update immediately.\n- Word handling: Postgres' `english` setting, so "saving" finds "save". If docs are written in other languages too, the `simple` setting instead (no stemming, works for any language).\n\n## What this adds to the plan\n1. **A Gaia, framework (complex):** full-text and trigram support in Gaia.\n   - `tsvector` columns, GIN and trigram indexes, and the `pg_trgm` extension in the declarative migrations.\n   - A match operator in `Clause.php` with bound parameters.\n   - Sorting by rank and returning a snippet.\n\n   This is new framework capability, so it gets its own issue. Issue search can use it later too.\n2. **A Gaia (simple):** doc search: `searchVector` on `Doccontent` kept up to date, the trigram index on `doc.title`, and api-tester cases including permission scoping.\n3. **A Prometheus (simple):** search on the All Docs list: results with highlighted snippets, then filters. A separate small issue for search inside the doc.\n\n## Questions (my recommendation in bold)\n1. **English** word handling, or language-neutral (`simple`)?\n2. Search **one project at a time** to start, or across all of the user's projects from day one? Both use the same index; across projects only changes the scope and the UI.\n\nThe questions from last time are still open too: do you agree with the real-time architecture changes (Gaia doc events, the collab access endpoint, notes in the Y.Doc), and which milestone? Once you answer, I'll send the full revised plan with search included.	message	["Reading gaia/core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model/Issue.php", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.324339	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-13 13:50:40	f	\N
