562d27946af7-e1c1-cc28-d6b4e9b062ec	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	OK, search is out of scope for now. The All Docs list keeps the plain title filter from `aprom-4491`, and full-text search is a later improvement.\n\nHere's the full revised plan with the real-time design from last time. Compared with the previous plan:\n\n- **4 new issues:**\n  - **Gaia `doc-live-events`**: `doc.created/updated/deleted` through Hermes, plus a `CollabNotifier` that tells the collab server about a lock or delete.\n  - **Hermes `hermes-doc-events`**: the relay accepts those event names.\n  - **Hermes `collab-access`**: the internal endpoint that switches open editors to read-only or closes them, sends client messages, warns "not saved", and limits update size and rate.\n  - **Prometheus `doc-live-client`**: lists and the doc page react to those events and messages.\n- **Reviewer notes live in the Y.Doc** (a shared `notes` map anchored to the text). They're live for everyone, and resolving one is shared. Loading the "latest review" from Gaia is gone.\n- **`doc-presence` shows the AI busy flag** ("Rana Nouman is asking AI…"). Ask AI and the Reviewer set it.\n- **Two dependency pairs belong together:** `doc-live-events` with `hermes-doc-events`, and `doc-live-events` with `collab-access`. Each pair is an event or API contract, so both PRs should be merged together.\n\nMilestone: none set, so they go to **Claude-v1**. Say "Docs MVP" if you want them next to 4488. Remember that `aprom-4489` to `4492` need un-deferring, and 4489 and 4492 need a note that the doc model has no `body`.	message	["Updating the knowledge map"]	54dfde486af7-e1c1-cc28-88b3d893e724	0.504092	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-13 13:57:42	f	\N
