e91a8a626afa-b491-52a3-cd5cf0556f6c	5aa975066afa-b491-52a3-8ddda4f295d5	The idea: clients like the Task Board and Dashboard send one `POST` that holds several ordinary Gaia REST calls. Gaia runs each call with its own authentication and ACL checks, and returns one result per call. A failing call returns its own error and the others still succeed.\n\n## What I found in Gaia\n- **Dispatch:** `public/index.php:232` handles one request per process with `Phalcon\\Mvc\\Application`. Every CRUD route comes from metadata in `core/mvc/Router.php` `init`.\n- **Errors are the main blocker.** `index.php:234-264` catches each `Gaia\\Exception\\*` and calls `handle()`. That method builds the error response and **sends it straight away** (`core/exceptions/*.php`, 11 classes). In a bulk call, the first failing item would write its error to the client and end the whole batch. Building the error response has to be separated from sending it first.\n- **Request state is global.** `RestController` reads the body with `request->getJsonRawBody()` and the query with `request->getQuery()`. It sets the user in `$GLOBALS['currentUser']` during `authorize()`. Each sub-call therefore needs its own Request and Response objects in the DI container. That means new framework work.\n- **House rule:** Gaia allows only CRUD resources. So bulk becomes a resource, `POST /api/v1/bulk`, which "creates" a batch and is never stored. It is not a custom route.\n- Nothing like this exists in the tracker yet.\n\n## Proposed approach\n- **Request:** `{"requests": [{"id": "lanes", "method": "GET", "url": "/api/v1/issue?query=…"}, …]}`\n- **Response:** `{"responses": [{"id": "lanes", "status": 200, "body": {…}}, {"id": "x", "status": 403, "body": {"error": "…"}}]}`\n- **Status codes:** the outer call returns 200 if the batch was valid. It returns 400 if the batch itself is invalid, and then nothing runs.\n- **Execution:** items run in-process, one after another, in the order sent. That is where the time saving comes from: one round trip instead of N.\n\n**Security:**\n- The bulk call itself must be authenticated.\n- Every item goes through the normal `authorize()` and ACL checks with the caller's token. Bulk never grants more access than the separate calls would.\n- Only `/api/v1/<resource>` URLs are allowed. These are refused: nested bulk calls, OAuth, unauthenticated endpoints and streaming endpoints (`/preview`, `/download`, upload file streams).\n- There is a configurable maximum number of items, plus a body size limit.\n- `bulk` gets ACL metadata like any other resource. Per house rules there is no permission seed, so the reviewer grants `bulk.create` by hand.\n\n## Questions (my recommendation in bold)\n1. **Writes in a batch on day one?** **Yes. Writes run in the order sent, each one independent, and a failure rolls nothing back.** An "all or nothing" mode would come later.\n2. **Maximum items per batch?** **25 by default, configurable with `BULK_MAX_REQUESTS`.**\n3. **Should each item's response include its own timing (ms)?** **Yes. It's cheap and shows which part of a board load is slow.**\n\n## Left out (later ideas)\n- All-or-nothing transactions.\n- Items that use earlier items' results (`$ref`).\n- Running items in parallel.\n- The Prometheus client that would use bulk. The idea is limited to Gaia, but the board and dashboard only benefit once that client exists.\n\nThe plan below assumes my recommended answers. If you answer differently, I'll send a revised plan. All three issues are `complex` because each one either changes framework internals or sets a new contract.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching issues: bulk api batch requests 2>&1 | head -40; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search multiple requests single call 2>&1 | head -20", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Reading gaia/CLAUDE.md", "Running cd /d/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/gaia && wc -l public/index.php core/config/routes.php core/mvc/controllers/RestCont", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd /d/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/gaia && wc -l public/index.php core/config/routes.php; grep -n \\"Application\\\\|Micro\\\\", "Searching the code in gaia/public/index.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/config/routes.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/exceptions", "Reading gaia/public/index.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php", "Searching issues: transaction rollback partial failure --project agaia 2>&1 | grep '^#' | head; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search rate limit TooMany", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php", "Running cd /d/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/gaia && php tools/gaia-dev/bin/gaia-dev route /api/v1/issue 2>&1 | head -30", "Listing gaia/docs/architecture/*/decisions.md", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/Router.php", "Updating the knowledge map"]	e871c6e16afa-b491-52a3-c3a741a14dec	0.832146	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-15 23:06:17	f	\N
