d65870616afa-5047-dae4-e4cb0f0d3d9d	61698d956afa-5047-dae4-71e5f7daf8d5	Here's the idea as I understand it: when a new Prometheus build has been deployed, a tab still running the old build shows a yellow (warning) Messenger message asking the user to reload. It stays on screen until they close it.\n\n**What I found**\n- Nothing in the tracker covers this yet.\n- No build id exists today. `package.json` is at version `0.0.0`. QA and dev deploys run `ember build -prod` in `docker/<branch>/Dockerfile`, and Apache serves `dist/`.\n- Production builds already fingerprint their scripts, e.g. `assets/prometheus-<hash>.js`. So the app can fetch `index.html` with `cache: 'no-store'` and compare those script names with the ones it loaded. If they differ, there's a new build. That needs **no change to the build, Docker, Gaia or Hermes**.\n- Messenger already supports `type: 'warning'` (used in `list.js` and `create.js`). `services/live-reload-prompt.js` already shows a prompt that stays open; I'll follow its pattern but put this in a separate service, because that one handles reloading data on one screen.\n- One limit: `ember serve` (local dev) doesn't fingerprint, so the prompt only appears on QA and production builds.\n\n**Three decisions, with what I recommend (say "yes" to accept all three)**\n1. **A Reload button** in the message, next to the close ×. Recommended: yes, because it saves the user a step.\n2. **When to check:** every 5 minutes, and again whenever the tab becomes visible. Recommended: yes. It costs one small static request and touches no API.\n3. **After the user closes it:** don't show it again for that build, only if another build is deployed later. Recommended: yes, so it doesn't nag.\n\n**Left out:** forcing a reload, showing what changed in the new build, and using a service worker.\n\nIt's one Prometheus issue of about 7 files.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching issues: new build reload version 2>&1 | head -40; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search messenger toast 2>&1 | head -30", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Reading issue 3929 2>&1 | head -60; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search app version update reload page stale --project aprom 2>&1 | head -30", "Searching the code in prometheus", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Running cd /d/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/prometheus && ls; ls config public 2>&1; grep -n \\"version\\\\|fingerprint\\\\|APP\\" config", "Reading prometheus/app/services/live-reload-prompt.js", "Listing {Dockerfile*,docker/**,config/*.js,.github/workflows/*,public/*,ember-cli-build.js,nginx*} in prometheus", "Listing * in prometheus/config", "Listing **/{Dockerfile*,*.conf,ci.yml,*.yml,ember-cli-build.js} in prometheus", "Reading prometheus/.github/workflows/cd-ovh.yml", "Reading prometheus/docker/apache/prometheus.conf", "Reading prometheus/Dockerfile", "Searching the code in prometheus", "Searching the code in prometheus/config/environment.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/ember-cli-build.js", "Reading prometheus/docker/qa/Dockerfile", "Searching the code in prometheus/package.json", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Listing ci-cd/* in prometheus", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/styles", "Searching for \\".\\" in prometheus/ci-cd", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes", "Updating the knowledge map"]	d5a276686afa-5047-dae4-da5baa0942d2	0.779025	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-15 23:27:18	f	\N
6377dd526afa-54dd-5288-fa812dae8386	61698d956afa-5047-dae4-71e5f7daf8d5	Rather than a poll every 5 mins, I want to explore the possibility of having a signature which is compared whenever we send a request from the browser. Can this not be a header that the Prometheus server retuned in the header?	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-16 01:20:35	f	[]
