bf63c4046afa-54dd-5288-5dfce3974ffe	61698d956afa-5047-dae4-71e5f7daf8d5	A header signature works, but it can't come back on the requests the app already makes. Nearly all of those go to **Gaia** (`devapi`/`qaapi.projects4.me`, a different server). Gaia doesn't know which Prometheus build is deployed, and the two are deployed separately. The Prometheus server (Apache serving `dist/`) only answers the first page load and asset requests, and JavaScript can't read the headers of those.\n\n**Two ways to do it:**\n\n- **A. Gaia sends the header** (e.g. `X-Client-Build`), and the adapter compares it in `handleResponse` (`adapters/application.js:149`). The check comes free on every API call. But Prometheus's deploy would have to push its build id into Gaia's config on every release, which ties the two releases together. Not recommended.\n- **B. Prometheus's own server sends the header** (recommended):\n  - **Signature:** the CD workflow passes the commit sha as `BUILD_ID` into the Docker build. Apache sends it on every response as `X-Prometheus-Build`, and the build bakes the same value into the app as `ENV.APP.buildId`. The header and the running app's id come from one value.\n  - **When it's checked:** whenever the app makes a Gaia request (a hook in the adapter's `handleResponse`) or the tab becomes visible again. That triggers a `HEAD index.html`, a request with no body that only reads the header, at most once a minute. There's no timer, so an idle tab costs nothing.\n  - **The message:** same as before. A warning Messenger message with Reload and ×, it stays until closed, and it's shown once per build. If the header is missing, as in local `ember serve`, no message appears.\n\nWith B, the two issues touch different files, so they can go in parallel. The app side does nothing until the header exists.	message	["Reading prometheus/docker/dev/Dockerfile", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/adapters/application.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Updating the knowledge map"]	bebdb3e46afa-54dd-5288-e2cc68ad359a	0.780054	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 01:22:07	f	\N
a0b547d96afa-e792-fe2e-a398b46058f9	9fd531f66afa-e792-fe2e-e0480570c2cd	Now that Gaia is supporting Bulk API we need to start leveraging that Let's target task board for now Right now we are pulling in multiple milestones that are active in multiple API request. This is adding network latency so we to pull all the milestones in a single bulk API request	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-16 02:04:16	f	[]
