0fec2db46afa-23c6-fe2e-cc20144a3365	9fd531f66afa-e792-fe2e-e0480570c2cd	The idea is to have the Task Board load its lanes through Gaia's new `POST /api/v1/bulk` (agaia-4587, done) in one request, not one request per milestone.\n\n## How the board loads today\nIn `prometheus/app/routes/app/project/board.js` `model` (l.61–131) the board makes **3 + N requests**:\n1. Active milestones (l.73), backlog issues (l.89) and issue statuses (l.97). These run one after another, and none of them depends on the others.\n2. Then one `store.query('issue')` for each milestone (l.99–112), run in parallel.\n\nPrometheus has no bulk client yet. `utils/milestone-overview-api.js` `fetchMilestoneOverviewsBulk` has "bulk" in its name, but it only runs raw `fetch` calls in parallel.\n\n## What I propose\n- **A reusable bulk client in the data layer.** A `bulk` service takes a list of `{id, modelName, query}` items. It builds the same GET URLs that `store.query` would build and sends one `POST /bulk` through the application adapter's `ajax`, so token refresh and the 401 retry still apply. It normalizes each successful result with the model's serializer, pushes it into the store and returns the records or an error for each id. A batch larger than the server limit of 25 is split into several requests.\n- **The board uses the client in two rounds:**\n  - Round 1: milestones, backlog and statuses in one bulk call.\n  - Round 2: the issues of every milestone in one bulk call.\n\n  That is 2 requests instead of 3 + N, and the three requests that ran one after another today no longer wait on each other.\n\n## Things to know\n- **Permission.** The `bulk` call needs `bulk.create`, which has no seed, so you grant it to the roles yourself. Until a role has it, the board would break for those users. So the client **falls back to separate queries** when the whole bulk call fails (403 or a network error). If a single item fails, only that lane shows the error, as today.\n- **Gaia runs bulk items one at a time** (decision D-003). The browser no longer pays a round trip per milestone, but the server time adds up across items. With a handful of milestones the change is a clear gain. With very many large lanes the gain is smaller.\n- **A smaller option.** Round 2 could also be one issue query with `Issue.milestoneId CONTAINS id1,id2,…` (Gaia turns that into `IN`), grouped by milestone in the browser. It needs no new client. I kept the bulk route because you want a client that other screens can reuse, starting with the Dashboard and Gantt.\n- **Left out:** the Dashboard, the Gantt chart, milestone overviews and the board's reloads after live (Hermes) updates. Each can move to the client later.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search bulk api 2>&1 | head -40; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search ta", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4587 2>&1 | head -80", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes/app/project/board.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Reading prometheus/app/routes/app/project/board.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/utils/milestone-overview-api.js", "Reading prometheus/app/utils/milestone-overview-api.js", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search bulk prometheus --project aprom 2>&1 | grep '^#' | hea", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/adapters/application.js", "Listing prometheus/app/adapters/*.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/tests/acceptance", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/controllers/app/project/board.js", "Reading prometheus/app/adapters/application.js", "Updating the knowledge map"]	0f48bdd16afa-23c6-fe2e-3be5b114f3d3	0.769225	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 02:06:07	f	\N
