e4d422706afa-c6cf-7528-ae8874979043	9fd531f66afa-e792-fe2e-e0480570c2cd	I looked at every route and widget that makes more than one call. Bulk helps most where calls run **one after another** or where a page makes **more than about 6 calls at once**. Calls that already run in parallel gain less, because Gaia runs bulk items one at a time, so their server time adds up.\n\n## Where bulk helps (best first)\n| Screen | Today | With bulk |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Dashboard** (`routes/app/index.js` l.61–83) | Issue statuses, then each widget's query **one at a time** (`for … await`). Then Active Milestones makes N raw `fetch` calls for milestone overviews and passes the token itself. | 1 request for every widget, plus 1 for the overviews |\n| **Gantt** (`routes/app/project/gantt.js` l.90–124) | Same as the board: milestones, then one issue query per milestone | 2 requests |\n| **Agent page** (`routes/app/agent/page.js` l.30–54) | The agent, then 9 calls in parallel | 2 requests |\n| **Workflow list** (`routes/app/workflow/index.js` l.80–118) | Saved searches, nodes, runs, agents and projects, mostly one after another | 2–3 requests |\n| **Project overview** (`routes/app/project/index.js` l.97) | 5 calls in parallel | 1 request |\n\nSmaller gains that I left out: the issue page, create and list routes (project → statuses → issue chains of 2–3 calls), the user page (4 calls), the role page (3) and agent tools (4).\n\n## Dashboard: how widgets register their call\nYour idea already has a foothold. Each widget declares its first query in metadata: `views.Dashboard.widgets.<name>` = `{model, options}` (`utils/metadata/metadata.js` ~l.592). The route reads the user's widget list (`currentUser.user.dashboard.widgets`) and loads each widget's declared query.\n\n**I recommend that this metadata entry be the widget's registration:**\n- The route collects the entries of the widgets visible right now and sends them together with the statuses query in **one bulk call**. Each widget gets its own result as `@data`.\n- After the first load, widgets fetch directly, as they do today: paging, switching week, refresh.\n- On a customizable dashboard this follows the user's widget list. A widget added while the page is open loads itself. A widget that doesn't need a first load declares nothing.\n- If one widget's item fails, only that widget shows the error. Batches over 25 items are split by the service.\n\n**The alternative** is for widgets to register at runtime: each widget calls something like `bulk.schedule(...)` from its constructor, and the service sends everything scheduled in the same tick as one request. That works even for widgets with no metadata, but the batch depends on render timing and the route no longer knows when the page has finished loading. I'd only choose it if widgets later become plugins that don't have metadata entries. **Say if you prefer it.**\n\nActive Milestones' overviews depend on which milestones come back, so they can't go in the first batch. The widget sends them as a second bulk call. That needs the service to accept plain GET items that return JSON rather than store records, and it removes the widget's raw `fetch` calls (house rule).\n\n## Plan v2\nAll issues depend on aprom-4595. They are one issue per screen, so they can run in parallel; none of them change the same files.	message	["Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/prometheus/app && ls components/widgets/ && grep -rn \\"store.query\\\\|fetch(\\" componen", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes/app/project/gantt.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/components/widgets", "Reading prometheus/app/routes/app/project/gantt.js", "Listing prometheus/app/{routes,controllers,templates}/app/{dashboard,index}*", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes/app/index.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/templates/app/index.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/utils/metadata/metadata.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/widgets/active-milestones.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes/app", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes/app", "Updating the knowledge map"]	e3a3fbd46afa-c6cf-7528-996e85fe6d52	1.119311	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 09:46:12	f	\N
13b909036afa-bdaf-7528-c077fb0cc1d8	ded9f4396af0-2b69-3bb7-c36bdb48cfdf	I have a change request for the Avatar components. if there is not image or we are unable to load an image we need to use the User's initial. However, if the background for each default profile picture will be the same it will get a bit difficult to tell them apart, so we need to have a different background for each user. That being said if the background for a particular user is not the same all the time, it will get confusing. So using interesting background, which remains the same for each user but is generated at run time with the initials is the ask.	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-16 09:51:15	f	[]
1888cdd46afa-bdaf-7528-ffb87ee0d995	ded9f4396af0-2b69-3bb7-c36bdb48cfdf	Agent Nestor is working on it.	working	\N	\N	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 09:51:20	f	\N
a1c00f106afa-bdaf-7528-51e62a82ce9a	ded9f4396af0-2b69-3bb7-c36bdb48cfdf	I've planned this as a follow-up to aprom-4588 rather than changing it, since 4588 may already be in progress. When there's no image, or the image fails to load, the avatar shows the person's initials. The background is generated in the browser from the user's id, so each user always gets the same one.\n\nThe screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look.\n\n\n\n## How it works\n- **Initials:** the first letter of the first and last word of the name, so "Hammad Hassan" becomes HH. A one-word name gives one letter. At xs (20px) it's always one letter. With no name it falls back to a `fa-user` icon.\n- **Background:**\n  - A hash of the user id (or the name if there's no id) picks a base colour, a pattern shape and a second colour drawn at 50% opacity.\n  - Base colours are the 6 dark palette colours (crimson, plum, blue, red, amber, `#333`), so white text stays readable.\n  - The 5 shapes are half bottom, half left, two corner circles and a ring. Together that gives about 150 combinations instead of one grey placeholder.\n- **Why it stays stable:** nothing is stored. The same id always produces the same avatar, on every page and every visit. The colour and shape lists must keep their order, because reordering them changes every user's avatar. The issue says so in the docs.\n- **Design system:** it uses palette colours, flat shapes and only the round edge, with no gradients or shadows.\n- **Agents** keep the robot, as decided in 4588. Initials are only for people, which keeps agents easy to tell apart.\n\n## One problem to decide\nUsers created in Prometheus usually won't get initials, because their default picture is saved as a real image:\n- `models/user.js:56` sets `profilePicture` to the `default.png` image (as base64) by default, so new users get the placeholder stored as their picture.\n- Gaia's `UserimageController` only returns a 404 when the picture is empty. So it serves the placeholder, the image loads fine, and initials never show.\n\nTo fix it for everyone I'd add two small issues:\n- **aprom:** the user model stops defaulting `profilePicture`.\n- **agaia:** a one-off cleanup task that clears stored pictures equal to the placeholder.\n\nShould I add them? Until they're done, only users with no picture at all, or a broken one, get initials.	message	["Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/UserimageController.php", "Searching for \\"defaultProfilePicture\\" in prometheus/app", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<\\"EOF\\" ```nestor-screen key=\\"avatar-initials\\" tit", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/avatar-initials.png", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<\\"EOF\\" ```nestor-screen key=\\"avatar-initials\\" tit", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/avatar-initials.png", "Updating the knowledge map"]	a11397646afa-bdaf-7528-8696074fd152	2.476109	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 09:53:37	f	[{"uploadId": "9c8b62606afa-bdaf-7528-b020c70d6efb", "key": "avatar-initials", "title": "Avatar initials: stable two-tone background per user", "version": 1, "width": 1100, "height": 420}]
