db3c5b736afa-5122-b3db-0f6e95171544	dcdfbac46afa-a4f4-35fc-b54d188e59a0	Yes. The comment editor in place is the same **Toast UI editor** (`AppUi::ToastUi`) the modal uses today, with the same toolbar, `@` user mentions, `#` issue links and `:` emojis. `InlineEditable` doesn't supply its own field. It shows whatever goes in its edit slot, and the plan puts `AppUi::ToastUi` there with the same arguments the modal passes.\n\nI checked that it will work in place:\n- **Your text stays put while typing.** The Toast UI modifier (`modifiers/initialize-toastui.js`, `modify` at line 83) builds the editor once and ignores argument changes after that. Passing the draft as `@initialValue` won't reset the text or the cursor on each keystroke, and every change still reaches the draft through `onContentChange`.\n- **One thing to avoid:** `inline-editable.scss` hides every `label` inside a `.form-field` in the edit slot. Toast UI's link and image popups contain labels. So the editor must not be wrapped in a `.form-field` the way the modal wraps it. I've added that to the comment issue.\n- **Not new, but worth checking:** the modifier never destroys the editor or its mention menu when it's removed. Opening and closing the editor over and over could leave mention menus behind. The modal has the same problem today. I've asked the comment issue to check for it and log a separate issue if it shows up, rather than fix it there.\n\nOnly the comment issue changed. Updated plan:	message	["Searching the code in prometheus/app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/toast-ui.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js"]	da81b0156afa-5122-b3db-7c577473353c	0.20773	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 11:11:23	f	\N
62aea1576afa-46e4-b3db-7f631b1199a1	1ab1aae46afa-46e4-b3db-a3ebef9820fc	You want users to choose which widgets show on their home dashboard and how they're laid out, instead of everyone getting the same fixed set.\n\n**What already exists**\n- **Gaia** already stores a dashboard per user: the `Dashboard` model (`name`, `userId`, `widgets` as a comma-separated list). Every new user gets one with 5 widgets from `DashboardComponent::DEFAULT_WIDGETS`. But there is no `dashboard` endpoint at all. Prometheus can only read it through the `User.dashboard` relationship, so users can't save changes today.\n- **Prometheus** already respects that list:\n  - `routes/app/index.js` `_getValidWidgets` reads the list and drops unknown names.\n  - `metadata.js` `views.Dashboard.widgets` is the registry of the 5 widgets.\n  - `components/widgets.hbs` fills the left column with the first 3 widgets and the right column with the next 3, so 6 at most.\n- **Related issues:** aprom-4598 (in progress) is rewriting the first load in `routes/app/index.js`, and its description already expects "customizable dashboards". The UI work should wait for it. aprom-3659 (layout) is still in review.\n\nSo most of the plumbing exists. Two pieces are missing:\n\n1. **Saving the dashboard (Gaia).** We need a `dashboard` resource where a user can read and update only their own row. Gaia has no "own record" access rule today; the RBAC decisions list it as out of scope. That makes it framework work: a metadata-declared owner field (e.g. `userId`) that limits list, get and update to the signed-in user. I'd give that its own issue (complex), then a simple issue for the Dashboard resource on top of it.\n2. **A Customize mode (Prometheus).** A "Customize" button on the dashboard opens a panel where the user turns widgets on or off, reorders them and picks the column for each. Save writes the change through the new resource; Reset goes back to the defaults.\n\n**Questions (my recommendation in bold)**\n1. **Scope for day one:** only **show/hide, order and column for the existing 5 widgets**? Drag-and-drop resizing, settings per widget (e.g. page size, default filter) and new widget types would come later.\n2. **Storage:** keep `widgets` as a **list of names, with column placement saved as a short JSON** (`[{"name":"recentIssues","column":1}, ...]`), with old comma lists still read as before? Or skip column choice and keep alternating columns, which avoids any format change?\n3. **One dashboard per user** (no named or multiple dashboards, no admin-set team defaults)?\n\nIf you say yes to all three, I'll send the plan: Gaia owner-scope ACL, then the Gaia Dashboard resource, then the Prometheus customize mode (after aprom-4598). I can also draw the Customize panel as a screen first if you'd like to see it.	message	["Running cat /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md 2>/dev/null | head -300; cd /home/rana.n", "Reading issue 4598 2>&1 | head -50; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 3659 2>&1 | head -20; cat gaia/docs/generated/models/Dashboard.md | head -40", "Running sed -n 40,80p gaia/docs/generated/models/Dashboard.md; grep -rn -i \\"dashboard\\" gaia/app/api/v1/controllers --include=*.p", "Searching the code in gaia/app", "Listing prometheus/app/components/widgets/*", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/routes/app/index.js", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/DashboardComponent.php", "Reading gaia/app/metadata/model/Dashboard.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/UserController.php", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/templates/app/index.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/utils/metadata/metadata.js", "Searching for \\"dashboard\\" in gaia/app/metadata/model/User.php", "Listing prometheus/app/components/widgets.*", "Reading prometheus/app/templates/app/index.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/utils/metadata/metadata.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/widgets.hbs", "Searching issues: --kind doc acl own record