2dced8a36afa-1926-b3db-100e9806a9da	1ab1aae46afa-46e4-b3db-a3ebef9820fc	So the idea grows to two parts: let users customize their dashboard, and add new widgets that answer "what should I focus on first?". That's a good fit. Each widget is one entry in `views.Dashboard.widgets` plus a component. The route already fills in tokens like `ME`, `NOW` and `TODAY_END` in widget queries, so new widgets can run on data Gaia already has.\n\n**Widgets I'd add, all built from existing data**\n\n| Widget | What it shows | Built from |\n|---|---|---|\n| **My Focus** | My open issues, ranked: overdue, then due within 3 days, then blocker/critical/high, then the rest. Each row shows why it's there ("Overdue 2d", "Due tomorrow", "Blocker"). | `Issue` assignee = me, status not done (`Issuestatus.done`), `endDate`, `priority` |\n| **Milestones at risk** | Active milestones that are overdue or end within 7 days, with how many of their issues are still open | `Milestone` endDate/status + the existing `overview` (agaia-3875) |\n| **Mentions for me** | Recent comments where someone @mentioned me, linking to the issue or conversation | `Mention` userId = me, with the `comment` rel |\n| **Stalled work** | My in-progress issues with no activity for 5+ days | `Issue.lastActivityDate` |\n\nI'd leave out of the first version:\n- **AI daily brief** ("here's what changed and what to tackle"): it needs a new Ares endpoint behind Gaia. It's worth doing, but as its own idea.\n- **Over budget** (time spent above the estimate): it would need the time-log hasMany rels in the widget query, which the Prometheus rules forbid. It needs a server-side aggregate first.\n- Team-level widgets (workload per member) and settings per widget.\n\nWith these, the dashboard has 9 widgets, which breaks today's fixed 3+3 layout. That's one more reason customize mode (show, hide, order, column) has to ship with them.\n\n**Questions (my recommendation in bold)**\n1. **All four widgets for day one**, or would you add or drop one?\n2. **Defaults:** existing users keep their current dashboard, and new users get **My Focus first, then Recent Issues, Active Milestones, Milestones at risk, Mentions**. Customize mode is where people add the rest. OK?\n3. My earlier questions still stand. Is the recommendation OK: **show/hide, order and column** saved as JSON in `Dashboard.widgets` (old comma lists still read), **one dashboard per user**, and **Gaia owner-scope ACL** as the first issue?\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll draw the dashboard with My Focus and the Customize panel as screens, then send the plan.	message	["Running sed -n 1,40p gaia/docs/generated/models/Issue.md; sed -n 1,20p gaia/docs/generated/models/Milestone.md; ls gaia/docs/gen", "Running sed -n 6,20p gaia/docs/generated/models/Issuestatus.md; sed -n 6,22p gaia/docs/generated/models/Mention.md; dev-tools/ai", "Reading prometheus/app/routes/app/index.js", "Searching for \\"overview\\" in prometheus/app/models/milestone.js", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.177985	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 11:17:01	f	\N
3022e0276afa-1926-b3db-a8ee56af5916	de3303a86afa-5122-b3db-e6498ef24096	I found about 35 places that show a user's picture. Only `Project::MemberAvatars` already uses `AppUi::Avatar`. Everything else is a raw `/userimage/get` `<img>`, `Agent::UserAvatar` or `Agent::Avatar`, each sized by its own CSS. Here is each place at the size it renders today and the standard size I'd move it to (xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96):\n\n| Where | Today | Proposed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Assignee select menu options; relate-user / relate-actor in form selects | 20 / 25 | **xs** |\n| Comments (comment-frame: issue + thread comments, idea messages), composer, weekly-conversations widget, watcher modal | 30 | **s** |\n| Header navbar user image | 25 | **s** |\n| Board card assignee (compact AssigneeSelect), role list rows (MemberAvatars) | 24 | **s** |\n| Notifications, issue list, gantt bar, user management, close-members, controlbar, projects list stack, thread participants, project-overview conversations | 40 | **m** |\n| Agent list | 36 | **m** |\n| Role "view all" modal | 36 | **m** |\n| Issue time logs | 50 | **m** |\n| Sidebar user panel | 45 | **m** |\n| Header user menu, agent page picture | 90 / 96 | **l** |\n| Project manager, issue assignee (`.project-manager img {width:100%}`) | fluid, ~100–130 | **l** |\n| **Members grids**: project overview, issue Members box, role page | ~70–80 | **?** |\n\n**Questions** (each with my recommendation):\n1. **Members grids (~70–80px).** The scale has no size there. l (96) overflows the cells and m (40) halves them. → I recommend one new size, **`ml` 64px** (close to AdminLTE's `img-md` 60px), added to the component first. Rename it if you prefer.\n2. **24–25px spots.** → **xs inside menus and select fields** (so rows don't grow), **s everywhere else**. The header grows to 30px, which still fits the 50px navbar.\n3. **Milestone.** You didn't name one, so the plan defaults to Claude-v1. The earlier avatar work (4588, 4604) was in **aga-Cleanup**. Say if you want these issues there too.\n\n**How the issues are cut.** One issue per area. Each page issue changes its own markup. If an old CSS rule still reaches the avatar's inner image (for example the compact assignee's `img.img-circle` 24px or the time log's `.user-img img` 50px), that issue removes or rescopes the rule. Legacy classes still used elsewhere stay until a final cleanup issue, which also removes `Agent::UserAvatar` and adds an "every user picture is AppUi::Avatar" rule to the design system.\n\nSome issues share stylesheets (`issue.scss`, `project.scss`, `role.scss`, `agent.scss`), so those are chained. The rest run in parallel.\n\n**Left out:**\n- The profile-picture editor (a 140px crop preview of an unsaved upload, not a display avatar).\n- Skeleton placeholders.\n- Switching other places to `UserChip`: it's only used where the avatar and name already sit inline.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search avatar --project aprom 2>&1 | head -40", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4569 2>&1 | head -60; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4578 2>&1 ", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4588 2>&1 | head -50; dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4604 2>&1 ", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/prometheus && cat app/components/app-ui/avatar.hbs; sed -n 1,200p app/components/ap", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/avatar.hbs", "Listing prometheus/app/components/{app-ui/avatar*,app-ui/user-chip*,agent/*avatar*,agent/badge*}", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/avatar.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/user-chip.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/agent/user-avatar.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in pro