c39052a96afb-dac1-e111-70c208df5794	de3303a86afa-5122-b3db-e6498ef24096	This overlap comes from my spec for aprom-4610, not from the component. I gave the assignee a fixed `l` (96px) in a `col-xs-3 col-md-2` column. Those column widths are set by the window size, but the board quick view is a narrow panel even on a wide screen. So the column there is only about 40–60px wide, and the 96px avatar spills into the description next to it. The old `<img>` didn't overlap because it was `width: 100%` and shrank with the column. The project overview manager (aprom-4612) has the same setup and would overlap on small screens.\n\n**I recommend doing both, as three issues:**\n\n1. **The container fix (your option 1) is the actual bug fix.** The avatar column sizes itself from its content, and the description takes the rest and wraps beside it. That stops the overlap at any width. It's small and can ship right away.\n2. **Auto-resize (your option 2) becomes a feature of the component**, so it isn't hand-written per page. It adds an optional `@minSize` argument: the avatar steps down from `@size` towards `@minSize` (l → ml → m, at most two steps) when its container is too narrow, and steps back up when there's room. It reuses the existing `observe-width` modifier, so only avatars that set `@minSize` measure anything.\n3. **Use it** for the issue assignee and the project overview manager (`@size="l" @minSize="m"`), with their column capped at 25% of the row.\n\nOption 2 alone wouldn't be enough. The avatar can only measure the space it's given, and the current column has no size of its own to measure. So the container fix comes first either way, and resizing then makes the result look right in narrow panels.\n\nAll three issues go in **aga-Cleanup**. The third one waits for aprom-4612 (project overview), because it changes the manager's markup.	message	["Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb show 4610 2>&1 | head -40", "Reading prometheus/app/components