394f44706afb-da5e-948b-5a87ad2714b3	de3303a86afa-5122-b3db-e6498ef24096	I think this is the assignee avatar on the board card (the compact assignee select). If you meant the board's quick view, tell me. I haven't seen the broken view myself; this comes from reading the code.\n\n**Cause.** For a person, `AppUi::Avatar` renders `<img class="img-circle">` (`components/app-ui/avatar.hbs:17`). `img-circle` is a global AdminLTE class, and the board styles it on cards with `.board .board-issue-item .img-circle` (`styles/modules/board.scss:230`). That rule sets a 3rem size, a `#ddd` border and `object-fit` on the avatar's own image. It is more specific than the component's `.app-ui-avatar > img`, so it wins. An agent renders `span.agent-avatar`, not an `img.img-circle`, so agents escape the rule. That is why only humans break. The issue page has no such rule, so it looks right there.\n\nTwo more page rules can reach the same image:\n- `.board-issue-item p > img` (10rem `!important`) on the board.\n- `.users-list .dropdown .dropdown-menu li img` (`issue.scss:540`, 20px plus a right margin) in the assignee menu in issue details. The margin pushes the image off its circle.\n\n**Fix.** The component stops relying on a global class:\n- The image gets its own class, `app-ui-avatar-image`, and loses `img-circle`.\n- The component's stylesheet resets everything a page rule might set on it (size, max size, margin, border, padding).\n- The board and assignee-menu rules that leak into it are deleted.\n\nPages can't out-rank an `!important` rule, so deleting the leaking rules is part of the fix, not just a tidy-up. This is one bug issue in **aga-Cleanup**.	message	["Searching for \\"img\\" in prometheus/app/styles", "Reading prometheus/app/components/issue/assignee-select.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/styles/modules/board.scss", "Reading prometheus/app/styles/modules/issue.scss", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/styles/modules/board.scss", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/com