6172fae76afb-1ee8-c328-487915d1a14d	1cecd6c76afb-1ee8-c328-6f16c99cd135	Here's how I read it: today an issue can only point to one parent (`Issue.parentId`). You want typed links between issues (blocks, blocked by, relates to, split into, parent/child) that are stored properly and protected against cycles.\n\n## What exists today\n- **Gaia:** parent/child is just the `parentId` column on `Issue`, with the relations `parentissue` and `childissues` (`gaia/app/metadata/model/Issue.php:191`, `:290`, `:319`). **Nothing checks for cycles yet.** You can set A → B → A, or make an issue its own parent.\n- **Prometheus:** about 26 files use `parentId`: Gantt, the board, issue create/edit, AI planning (`issue-planning.js`), `modeltotree.js` and the hierarchy box on the issue page.\n- Nothing in the tracker covers issue links yet, so there's nothing to duplicate.\n\n## Proposed approach\n- **A new CRUD resource `Issuelink`** with `sourceIssueId`, `targetIssueId` and `type` (`blocks`, `relates`, `splits`). Each link is stored once in one direction and read from both sides:\n  - "A blocks B" shows on B as "blocked by A". So items 1 and 2 are the same row.\n  - "A splits into B, C" shows on B and C as "split from A".\n  - `relates` is symmetric, so A–B and B–A count as the same link.\n- **Cycle rules, checked in a domain service (not in the controller), all returning 422:**\n  - **For every link type:** an issue can't link to itself, and the same pair can't be linked twice with the same type.\n  - **`blocks`:** no cycles anywhere in the chain (A blocks B blocks C blocks A is a deadlock).\n  - **`splits`:** no cycles either, and an issue can be split from only one source.\n  - **Parent/child:** the same check applied to `parentId`, so an issue can't become a descendant of itself.\n- **Prometheus:** a "Links" box on the issue page, grouped by type, with an add form (type plus issue picker) and a remove action.\n\n## Three questions (my recommendation in bold)\n1. **Parent/child: should it stay on `parentId` and just get the cycle guard?** Moving it into `Issuelink` would mean rewriting those ~26 Prometheus files plus Gantt and the board, for no new capability. I'd also show parent/child in the Links box, but read it from the existing fields.\n2. **Can links cross projects?** **Yes.** Our own work does this all the time (a Prometheus issue blocked by a Gaia one). The rule would be: you can see a link only if you can read both issues, and you can create one if you can update the source issue and read the target.\n3. **Should "blocked" be enforced (for example, refusing to start or close an issue while a blocker is still open)?** **No, not for the MVP.** Links would be information only, and enforcement could be a later idea.\n\n**Left out of the MVP:**\n- Links on the board and Gantt.\n- Live events for links.\n- Searching by link in ezSearch.\n- Moving Talos' "Depends on" lines over to real links.\n\nOnce you confirm or change these three answers, I'll send the plan. It will likely be four issues: one for the cycle-guard service, then the `Issuelink` resource and the `parentId` guard in parallel, then the Prometheus Links box.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search issue dependency blocks blocked related 2>&1 | head -6", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model/Issue.php", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && ls gaia/app/metadata/model/ | tr '\\\\n' ' '; echo; grep -rln \\"parentId\\" gaia/app/a", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search blocked by issue link --project agaia 2>&1 | head -30", "Searching for \\"parentId\\" in gaia", "Listing app/metadata/model/*.php in gaia", "Listing gaia/app/metadata/model/*.php", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/CLAUDE.md", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Reading gaia/CLAUDE.md", "Reading gaia/app/metadata/model/Tagged.php", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.621533	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 21:02:25	f	\N
6f1e54a36afb-b5db-dcfe-539ab0950f88	1cecd6c76afb-1ee8-c328-6f16c99cd135	We can keep the parent/child with the parentId for now, just to keep the system going on. After we the IssueLink built up then we can migrate away from it.\nWe need to think about this seriously as then we will need to store the projectId information in the issue link. we would need to visually show an issue that does not belong to the current project and how the project memebership ACL will work here, we need to figure out.\nBlocked does not need to be enforced right now. I would like to enforce things like block using workflow.\nThe scope of this idea is to handle just the back end system. All front end related changes will be done later.	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-16 21:11:11	f	[]
