aab5d4366afc-8e2e-d8ff-9038f7d93bd8	368036d36afc-ae59-6053-37801a47463a	I've made three screens for the new header and navbar: desktop with the sidebar open, desktop with it collapsed, and phone. No plan yet; I'll write it once you've reviewed the screens and answered the questions below.\n\n**How each of your points is handled**\n1. **Project selector:** it moves out of the sidebar into the header, as a crimson button right after the hamburger. On desktop it shows the project name and short code ("A Prometheus APROM"); on a phone, just the code. It opens a searchable project list with the current project ticked and an "All projects" link. Because it's in the header, the current project stays visible when the sidebar is collapsed or closed.\n2. **User picture and live status:** the user block at the top of the sidebar goes. The online status becomes a green dot on the avatar that's already in the header.\n3. **Grouping:** the sidebar has three groups:\n   - **Workspace:** Dashboard, Projects.\n   - **Project APROM:** Issues, Task Board, Gantt Cal, Threads, Ideas.\n   - **Admin:** unchanged.\n\n   When the sidebar is collapsed to icons, the group titles are hidden, so thin dividers separate the groups.\n4. **Phone:** the navigation slides over a dimmed page. Tapping a menu item or the dimmed page closes it.\n\nOn phones, the header search shrinks to a search icon and "New" to a crimson **+** button.\n\n**What I found in the code**\n- The menu items already say whether they belong to a project (a `projectRelated` flag in `utils/metadata/metadata.js`), so the grouping can come from that flag. Nothing needs hard-coding.\n- The project-change logic already exists in `nav-bar.js` (`projectChanged` and `getTransitionUrl`), so the header switcher can reuse it.\n- `modifiers/initialize-sidebar.js` only remembers whether the sidebar is collapsed. Nothing closes the open sidebar after you navigate, which is why it stays open on phones.\n- The "Online" status is fixed text. There's no real presence data behind it yet.\n\n**Questions** (my recommendation in brackets):\n1. For point 4, I took "the Dashboard sticks around" to mean the sidebar stays open on a phone after you pick a page. Is that right? *(Yes, so it closes on navigation, on screens narrower than 768px only.)*\n2. On the Dashboard with no project selected, what should the Project group show? *(The group title plus one muted line, "Select a project to see its issues, board and threads". The switcher shows "Select a project".)*\n3. Should the green dot reflect real presence (online, away, offline from Hermes), or stay a fixed "online" for now? *(Fixed for now; real presence would be a separate idea that needs Gaia and Hermes work.)*\n\nIf you agree with the shape, I'll propose about four Prometheus issues: the header project switcher; the online dot on the header avatar plus removing the sidebar user block; the grouped sidebar from metadata; and auto-closing the sidebar on phones. They can mostly be done in parallel.\n\nThe PNGs only guide the layout and content; the design system and the real components decide the final look. Phones are drawn as 390px frames because the screen renderer won't go narrower than 800px.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Listing prometheus/app/{components/app-ui/nav*,components/app-ui/navbar*,components/app-layouts/*,templates/app.hbs,templates/application.hbs,styles/modules/header.scss,styles/modules/nav*,styles/components/nav*}", "Listing prometheus/docs/ui/**/*", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/application-sidebar.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/nav-bar.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/navbar-items.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/utils/metadata/metadata.js", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/nav-bar.js", "Reading prometheus/app/ut