bc7316916afc-8e2e-d8ff-06218d4d78b4	1cecd6c76afb-1ee8-c328-6f16c99cd135	I've parked this, and no issues were created. I noted where we stopped in my knowledge map, so we can pick it up again from there:\n\n- **Your decisions so far:**\n  - Parent/child stays on `parentId` for now; links take it over later.\n  - Blocking isn't enforced here; workflows will do that later.\n  - This idea covers the Gaia backend only.\n  - Linking issues across projects needs project linking first.\n- **Still open:** the three questions on project linking: what a link grants, what members of the other project see of a linked issue, and who requests and accepts it.\n- **Superseded:** the three-issue plan (ACL capability, cycle-check service, `Issuelink` resource) will be redone once project linking is settled.\n\nOn the agent question, there's a likely overlap. As far as I know, agents get their projects the same way users do, through `Membership` rows when the agent is created. If agents end up working across a group of projects, that grouping may well be the same thing as project linking. When we resume, it's worth checking whether one "project group" or "project link" concept can serve both agents and cross-project issues before we design each separately.	message	["Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.059894	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 09:22:04	f	\N
e92934796afc-64d2-0c6d-15e8ca20ecab	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	1\\. nomic\\-embed\\-text model will run inside Ares\\, not in the Ollama container\\. This should be run by Ares\\.\n2. **Saving a record never calls Ares:** What for my call on that.\n3\\. Yes UI will be implemented later on\\.\n\nFurthermore, no need to add a new table. Embeddings and other columns related to the search will be added inside the module itself e.g. let's add this inside issues for now.\n\n2nd, there is no need to get user input on what type of search is needed.	message	[]	\N	\N	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	Rana Nouman	2026-11-17 14:34:17	f	[]
6812cc256afc-9c53-0c6d-ee37b1db39f9	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	I've revised the plan to your answers.\n\n**The model now runs inside Ares.** I propose `fastembed`: it runs nomic-embed-text-v1.5 on ONNX Runtime on the CPU, with no PyTorch. That keeps the Ares image hundreds of MB smaller than `sentence-transformers` would. The model weights are downloaded when the image is built, so the first request doesn't wait for a download. Inference runs in a thread pool so it doesn't block Ares's async routes. It is a new Ares dependency, which the house rules say needs approval. I'm counting your answer as that approval; tell me if you'd rather use `sentence-transformers`.\n\n**Ollama and the separate table are gone.** Search columns now live on the module. Issue gets four:\n- `searchVector`: a generated full-text column with a GIN index, so FTS never goes stale\n- `searchEmbedding`: `vector(768)` with an HNSW index\n- `searchEmbeddingHash`\n- `searchEmbeddedAt`\n\nThe framework adds these four columns itself to any model with a `search` block, so a new module only needs the block.\n\nOne problem comes with this. Gaia has no way to mark a field as managed by the system. Without that, these columns would show up in REST responses, could be written by clients, and the audit log would copy all 768 numbers on every change. So the framework work now includes that marker. Writing the embedding is also a direct `UPDATE`, so it doesn't touch `dateModified`, the audit log or live events.\n\n**The `modes` parameter is gone.** Every search runs exact, FTS, fuzzy and semantic. The request is just `GET /api/v1/search?types=issue&q=…`.\n\n**Embedding on save — your call.** I read your point 2 as "wait for my call". Both options share most of the work:\n- When subject or description changes, the save clears `searchEmbeddedAt`, in the same write. That marks the record stale.\n- `search embed` fills in stale records.\n- `search reindex` runs every 24 hours.\n\nWhat's left to decide is when a stale record gets its embedding:\n- **(a) Worker every minute** (my recommendation, and what the plan has now). Saves stay fast and never fail because of Ares. Semantic results lag by up to a minute.\n- **(b) Inline:** embed right after the save commits, and leave the record stale if Ares fails. Results are fresh immediately, but every Issue save waits about 100–300 ms of CPU work in Ares.\n\nIf you pick (b), only `index-sync` changes, and the scheduler then only runs the daily reindex.	message	["Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/models/behaviors", "Updating the knowledge map"]	670a60566afc-9c53-0c6d-5fad5d8c6e20	0.424112	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 14:36:24	f	\N
