095c8ef06afc-5e99-d022-71f8d3802f9f	368036d36afc-ae59-6053-37801a47463a	I've reworked the screens with your feedback and added a first plan, since your answers settle the shape.\n\n**What changed in the screens**\n- **Profile:** the header avatar shows a profile picture (drawn as a head-and-shoulders placeholder, because the renderer can't embed images) with the green dot. The profile menu now has an **Online · Visible to your team** row above Profile / Sign out. The status stays fixed, as you decided.\n- **Navigation:** with no project selected, the Project group is still shown but its items are greyed out and don't work. The group title says **Select a project**, and so does the switcher button.\n- **Header:**\n  - On desktop, the search is centred in the header.\n  - On phones, the search has its own full-width row under the switcher, **+**, bell and avatar.\n  - The switcher's project name and short code now sit on the same line.\n- **Sidebar cut off after Admin:** that was a fault in my mockup, not in the design. The renderer adds 20px of padding around the page, which broke the fixed sidebar. The mockups now work around it, and the sidebar runs the full height.\n- On phones the menu closes after you pick a page. The dimmed backdrop shown in round 1 still applies; this round's phone screen shows the no-project menu.\n\n**One thing to check:** on phones the header is now three rows deep (the existing logo row, the action row and the search row), about 142px. If that's too tall, the logo row could be hidden on phones. That would be a small addition to the search-layout issue.\n\n**Plan:** five Prometheus issues.\n1. The header project switcher comes first, because it also removes the selector from the sidebar.\n2. The sidebar grouping and the search layout come next. They can be done in parallel.\n3. The profile status comes after both, because it edits the same header and sidebar files they do.\n4. Closing the menu after navigation on phones touches none of those files, so it can be done at any time.\n\nI left out real presence (online / away / offline) and hiding the logo row on phones. Each issue says the screens are a guide to layout and content only.	message	["Listing prometheus/public/img/**/*.{png,jpg}", "Reading prometheus/public/img/default.png", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/prometheus/public/img && ls -l default.png pm.png newpf.jpg", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"nav-desktop\\" title=\\"", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/nav-desktop.png", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"nav-no-project\\" titl", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"nav-no-project\\" titl", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/nav-no-project.png", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"nav-mobile\\" title=\\"P", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"nav-mobile\\" title=\\"P", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"nav-mobile\\" title=\\"P", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && cat > .tmp/nav-mobile-a.txt <<'EOF' <div class=\\"phone-off\\">x</div> <li class=\\"he", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"nav-mobile\\" title=\\"P", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/nav-mobile.png", "Running cd D:/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"nav-desktop-collapse", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/nav-desktop-collapsed.png", "Listing prometheus/tests/**/*{nav-bar,navbar,application-header,sidebar}*", "Updating 