4babc5036afc-9973-ac6f-53470828d8e9	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	I've planned a module-agnostic search for Gaia: a request asks for a module type and a query, and Gaia returns matches from that module using full-text (FTS), fuzzy, semantic and exact matching, with that module's own ACL applied.\n\n## What exists now\n- **No real full-text search.** The query language's `CONTAINS` is a plain `LIKE '%x%'`. `config/fts.php` is an unused Elasticsearch stub. The per-field `'fts' => true` flags in metadata do nothing.\n- **Migrations can't do what this needs.** They only create primary, unique and plain indexes. They can't enable Postgres extensions or create `vector` columns, GIN indexes or HNSW indexes. So the framework work comes first and gets its own issue.\n- **Postgres has no pgvector.** It runs `postgres:16-alpine`, so the image has to change to `pgvector/pgvector:pg16`.\n- **Ares can be extended without new packages.** It only has `/planissue`. Gaia already calls Ares through `core/services/LLM.php`, so the embeddings client copies that pattern.\n- **Nothing runs scheduled jobs yet.** `php cli.php workflow schedule` is written to run from cron, but no container runs cron. The 24-hour scheduler needs container work.\n\n## How it fits together\n- **Search endpoint:** `GET /api/v1/search?types=issue&q=…&modes=fts,fuzzy,semantic`.\n  - The `SearchController` itself has no ACL, as you asked.\n  - Each requested type needs `<module>.get`. A type the caller lacks is a 403, the same way Gaia already rejects query criteria the caller isn't allowed to use.\n  - The project-membership filter is applied inside the candidate SQL, before ranking and the result limit. Filtering afterwards would drop results from a page.\n  - A field the user can't read is never matched and never shown.\n  - This is not a standard CRUD resource, which Gaia's house rules normally require. I've kept it because you asked for it, and the endpoint issue writes down why.\n- **FTS and fuzzy** run directly on the module's table, using indexes generated from the `search` metadata. They never go stale.\n- **Embeddings** live in one shared `searchembedding` table: one row per record, 768 dimensions, with an HNSW index for fast similarity search.\n- **Event-driven updates:** a behaviour is attached automatically to every model with a `search` block, so a module becomes searchable through metadata alone.\n  - When a record is saved, it gets a "pending" row (only if its text changed). When it's deleted, its row goes.\n  - A worker turns pending rows into embeddings every minute.\n  - A daily `reindex` catches anything that was missed.\n- **Ranking:** Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) combines the results of each search mode. Exact matches (e.g. `issueNumber`) are pinned first.\n- **If Ares is down,** search still returns the FTS and fuzzy results, with `meta.semantic = "unavailable"`.\n\n## I assumed these — say yes or correct me\n1. **nomic-embed-text runs in an Ollama container**, and Ares calls it over HTTP. That keeps PyTorch out of the Ares image.\n2. **Saving a record never calls Ares.** Saves only mark the record pending and the worker embeds it. Calling Ares during the save would slow every save and could fail it.\n3. **Day one is Issue only, with no Prometheus search UI.** Docs and others become searchable by adding a `search` block. The UI is a later idea.\n\n**Left out:** chunking long text (each record gets one embedding of its first N characters), a search UI, highlighting inside semantic matches, a production deploy, and turning on the existing `workflow schedule` cron (the scheduler issue asks you about it).\n\nThe Ares and Dev Tool issues are written as requests to those teams. There are 11 issues; the longest chain is framework → queue → worker → scheduler.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching issues: semantic search embeddings 2>&1 | head -40; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search pgvector 2>&1 | head -20; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search ", "Running grep -n \\"^##\\\\|^###\\" gaia/CLAUDE.md | head -50; ls gaia/app/api/v1/controllers | head -80; ls ares ares/app 2>/dev/null; ", "Running sed -n 1,80p gaia/CLAUDE.md; cat ares/CLAUDE.md | head -80; cat ares/docker-compose.yml ares/requirements.txt", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/gaia && grep -rn \\"'fts'\\" app/metadata core | head -15; grep -rln \\"fts\\" core |", "Searching for \\"'fts'\\" in gaia", "Listing gaia/{core/*,core/libs/*,core/services/*,cli/*,app/tasks/*,app/cli/*} in .", "Reading gaia/config/fts.php", "Searching the code in gaia", "Reading gaia/core/services/LLM.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/tasks", "Searching the code in gaia/docker-compose.yaml", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php", "Reading gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php", "Searching issues: list record scope query acl filter project members 2>&1 | head -25; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search custom controller non-CRUD r", "Reading gaia/docs/architecture/rbac/implementation-plan.md", "Searching the code in gaia/docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md", "Reading gaia/app/metadata/model/Doc.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/MilestoneoverviewController.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core", "Searching the code in .", "Searching the code in .", "Updating the knowledge map"]	4abddbf96afc-9973-ac6f-c808aa5ef21d	1.218207	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 13:48:59	f	\N
4487f9206afc-a7a6-0c6d-0c3eaa9a824d	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	There is a flag that take cares of whether the field is system field or not, so that it isn't shared as part of the end response. Further more, Ares will wait for an event to occur from Hermes. When an event happens e.g. Issue.created, Ares will check the dirty state of the model and if embeddings will be required, it will create that and store it through the Gaia channel. So that is how the embeddings should be created/updated.	message	[]	\N	\N	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	Rana Nouman	2026-11-17 14:44:20	f	[]
