2a32f3306afc-aa6f-0c6d-3708e8ced854	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	I've revised the plan: Ares now creates and updates the embeddings by reacting to Hermes events. Making that work needs changes in Gaia, Hermes and Ares that don't exist yet.\n\n**I couldn't find the system-field flag you mentioned.** It isn't in the local Gaia checkout. The nearest is `'acl' => false`, but that only keeps a field out of the field-ACL list; the field is still returned. The issues say "use the existing system-field flag". **What's it called?** I'll name it in the issues; it may be on a branch that isn't checked out here.\n\n## Gaps found\n1. **No event fires when an issue's text changes.** Issue events today are `created`, `status.changed`, `assignee.changed`, `dates.changed` and `dependency.*`. Editing the subject or description publishes nothing. These events also come from controller components, so only REST writes publish them.\n2. **Ares can't listen to Hermes today.** Hermes only accepts user tokens, and a subscription has to name a project the user is a member of. Ares would have to join every project, plus each new one, within a limit of 100 subscriptions per socket.\n3. **Ares can't write to Gaia today.** It has no service login yet; it only uses the `X-Ares-Secret` header. Service logins can only read: writes are closed until someone decides whose name a service write is recorded under.\n\n## What I propose\n- **One generic event, `search.document.changed`.**\n  - Gaia publishes it from the search behaviour, so every write path is covered, not just REST. It fires when a record is created or one of its semantic fields changes.\n  - The event carries `type`, `resource`, `recordId`, the ordered `semanticFields` and `maxChars`. So Ares keeps no copy of the metadata, and adding a module needs no Ares change.\n  - It goes to a service-only room, `projectId = "service:ares"`. This copies Hermes's existing `user:<id>` pattern (D-009): one subscription, no project memberships.\n- **Ares listens and decides.**\n  - It reads the record through Gaia, builds the text and hashes it.\n  - If the hash matches `searchEmbeddingHash`, it only updates `searchEmbeddedAt`. Otherwise it embeds the text and PATCHes the embedding, hash and timestamp.\n- **Writes are narrowly scoped.** A new `ares` service kind may only update the three search columns. The write bypasses audit, modified-by fields and live events, so it can't loop back into another event. That settles the open "whose name is on a service write" question for this case, and the issue writes it down as a decision.\n- **The 24-hour scheduler stays in Gaia.** Hermes keeps no history, so events sent while Ares is down are lost. A daily `search reindex` re-publishes the event for every record whose embedding is missing or older than its last change.\n- **Ares keeps `POST /embeddings`,** because Gaia still has to embed the user's search query at search time.\n\nThat's 15 issues across 4 projects. **New dependencies that need approval:** `fastembed` and `python-socketio` in Ares.	message	["Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model", "Running cut -d: -f2- /home/rana.noman/.claude/projects/-home-rana-noman-web-hammad-hassan-Pr4M/3fd2fbc0-7dac-4ffc-abd2-a8cea69a4", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/core", "Reading gaia/core/libs/meta/manager.php", "Searching issues: field excluded from response serializer hidden system field 2>&1 | head -24", "Running ls dev-tools/talos/lib/events; head -60 dev-tools/talos/lib/events/*.py | grep -n -i \\"hermes\\\\|socket\\\\|token\\\\|room\\\\|subsc", "Searching the code in hermes/docs/architecture/decisions.md", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/lib/hermes.py", "Running grep -n \\"issue\\\\.\\" hermes/src/contract/names.js; grep -n \\"changes\\\\|changed\\\\|ISSUE_\\" gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/component", "Reading gaia/docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/IssueLiveEventsComponent.php", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching for \\"service\\" in hermes/docs/architecture/decisions.md", "Searching the code in hermes/src", "Updating the knowledge map"]	2922d9656afc-aa6f-0c6d-c355d92eec03	1.022679	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 14:48:10	f	\N
46a691746afc-2d64-3ed5-8b4da9eb4a3f	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	Right now there are multiple events that are being thrown for Hermes to capture. We need to list the events that are currently being thrown.\n\nThese events are already being used by Workflows, they will be used be used by other services e.g. Ares, Integration, Talos, etc.  However, it is also quite important that we do not throw everything, that will overwhelm the system and is not required.\n\nIdeally we should be able to create a registry that records all the events we want to throw so that if we need to add or remove any event we can do so in the registry, the registry should not be in the database as it will be required in almost all the API calls.	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-17 14:52:54	f	[]
