9c55ae916afc-2d64-3ed5-f08e5d602213	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	So you want one place that decides which events Gaia emits and who can use them. Adding or dropping an event should mean editing that place, it should be a file rather than a database table, and the system shouldn't publish everything.\n\n## What's thrown today\n\nGaia has **two separate event lists**, and they don't overlap much.\n\n**1. Live events sent to Hermes:** 23 names in `gaia/.../components/events/support/EventNames.php`. Thirteen hand-written `*LiveEvents*` components publish them, and `HermesPublisher` refuses any name not on the list.\n\n| Area | Events |\n|---|---|\n| Issue | `issue.created`, `issue.status.changed`, `issue.assignee.changed`, `issue.dates.changed`, `issue.dependency.created`, `issue.dependency.deleted` |\n| Milestone | `milestone.created`, `milestone.completed` |\n| Conversation | `conversation.created`, `conversation.comment.created/updated/deleted`, `conversation.vote.added/removed` |\n| Idea | `idea.created`, `idea.updated`, `idea.message.created`, `idea.plan.created`, `idea.plan.status.changed`, `idea.planissue.created` |\n| User-scoped | `notification.created`, `workflow.agent.run.requested`, `user.access.changed` |\n\nHermes keeps its own copy in `hermes/src/contract/names.js`, and the local copy has **already drifted**: it's missing `user.access.changed`. Either that's a real gap or my Hermes checkout is out of date. Either way, keeping two hand-maintained lists in sync is fragile.\n\n**2. Workflow triggers:** `core/libs/workflows/TriggerEventCatalog.php`. These are raised inside Gaia by `WorkflowTriggersComponent` and listed through `GET /workflowevent`. They are **not sent through Hermes**: workflows never listen to Hermes. There are 9 triggers:\n- 4 have the same names as live events: `issue.created`, `issue.assignee.changed`, `issue.status.changed`, `milestone.completed`.\n- 5 exist only here: `issue.modified`, `comment.added`, `wiki.created`, `wiki.modified`, `time.logged`.\n\nThe trigger catalog is already close to what you're describing. Each entry is declared as data: the model, whether it fires on create or update, which fields it watches, and a "changed to" condition.\n\n## Proposed direction\n\nOne registry file in Gaia, for example `app/metadata/events.php`: a plain PHP array that opcache keeps in memory, so reading it on every request costs almost nothing and there's no database lookup. Each entry would hold:\n- the name and a description;\n- the scope (project or user);\n- the source: model, create or update, watched fields, and the "changed to" condition;\n- the **channels**: `hermes` (sent to Hermes, which Prometheus, Talos and later Ares and integrations listen to) and/or `workflow` (in-Gaia trigger);\n- an `enabled` flag.\n\n`EventNames` and `TriggerEventCatalog` would read from the registry instead of keeping their own lists. "Don't throw everything" then comes down to two controls: an event goes to Hermes only if `hermes` is among its channels, and a disabled event is dropped before anything is sent. Hermes keeps its allowlist, and a check against a list exported from the registry catches drift like the one above.\n\n## Questions that change the plan\n\n1. **How far should the registry go on day one?** I recommend that it decides *which* events exist, their channels and whether they're on, while the 13 components keep building their own payloads. Several of them need custom data or project lookups, so a fully generic "add one entry and Gaia publishes it" publisher is a bigger job for later.\n2. **Should the workflow trigger catalog move into the same registry?** I recommend yes: one list, with channels per event. The alternative is a registry for Hermes events only.\n3. **How should Hermes stay in step?** I recommend Hermes keeps its own allowlist, Gaia exports the registry as JSON (alongside its other generated docs), and a test or CI check fails when the two differ. The alternative is Hermes accepting any well-formed name, which goes against its rule that the contract is closed.\n\nIf you say yes to all three, the plan would be about three issues:\n- a Gaia registry plus `EventNames` reading from it;\n- `TriggerEventCatalog` moved onto the registry;\n- the Hermes drift check, which also fixes the `user.access.changed` gap if it's real.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching issues: event registry hermes events 2>&1 | head -60", "Searching the code in dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Running cd /d/Claude/Workspace/Projects/Pr4M/gaia && ls app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/ app/api/v1/controllers/compone", "Listing app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/**/*.php in gaia", "Listing src/contract/* in hermes", "Listing **/EventNames.php in .", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/support/EventNames.php", "Listing gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/*.php", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching for \\"EventNames::\\" in gaia/app", "Listing gaia/core/libs/workflows/*Catalog*.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/libs/workflows/TriggerEventCatalog.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/WorkflowTriggersComponent.php", "Reading gaia/core/libs/workflows/TriggerEventCatalog.php", "Listing hermes/src/contract/*", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/WorkfloweventController.php", "Reading hermes/src/contract/names.js", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.810066	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 14:54:20	f	\N
