fa8d5c986afc-e6e8-3ed5-94ef6288306e	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	I've added the system-field flag as its own issue, `system-fields`. It's general framework work, so it comes first, and `search-metadata` now uses it instead of building it. The new flag is `'system' => true` on a field. A field marked with it:\n- is never in a response: not in its own record, in included relationships, `fields=` or CSV export\n- is silently dropped from user request bodies, so users can't write it\n- isn't listed in the field-ACL catalog, and users can't use it in `query` clauses or sorting\n- is skipped by `auditBehavior`\n\nThe only way to read or write a system field is an explicit opt-in path. The first one is the Ares search-column update in `service-search-access`.\n\nThat makes 16 issues; nothing else changed from the last version.\n\n**Your message ends at "I have some points:" and the points didn't come through.** Send them and I'll fold them in.	message	["Updating the knowledge map"]	f97422e06afc-e6e8-3ed5-bac671370e1b	0.419479	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 15:04:26	f	\N
