2d83eb256afc-07a6-74f5-ce6e8e06ca0f	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	Noted on all three. Here is what Gaia doesn't emit today, and which events I think are worth adding.\n\n## What's not covered\n\nBesides live events and workflow triggers, Gaia has a third "something happened" path: **notifications**. Its handlers live in `components/notifications/modules/`, one each for issues, memberships, comments, time logs and milestones. The registry won't absorb them, since they write notification rows for people rather than events, but they show what the product already treats as important.\n\nThese resources have **no event at all**: users and agents, roles (`Userrole`), projects, uploads, mentions, workflow runs, and every delete except dependencies and comments. Doc events are already planned in agaia-4531.\n\n## Candidates\n\nI'd add an event only when a consumer is named. Each entry in the registry should say who it's for, which is how we keep the bus quiet.\n\n| Event | Fired by | Who uses it | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `user.mentioned` | `Mention` create | Talos (respond when an agent like Odysseus is @-mentioned), Prometheus live badge, workflows | **Yes, first.** Sent only to the mentioned user. |\n| Role changes | `Userrole` create/delete | Hermes and Prometheus need to re-check access | **Yes, but not as a new name.** Extend `user.access.changed`: it already covers account status and memberships, and a role change is the same "your access changed" signal. |\n| `user.created` | `User`/`Agent` create | Integrations (provisioning), workflows (onboarding) | **Yes.** Event says whether it's a person or an agent. |\n| `workflow.run.finished` | `Workflowrun` reaches done or failed | Prometheus run view, Talos/Agamemnon monitoring | **Yes.** Today a run's end is invisible outside Gaia. |\n| `issue.deleted` | Issue soft delete | Prometheus lists and board, Ares (when it indexes issues), integrations | Yes |\n| `project.created` / `project.updated` | Project | Integrations, Talos (repo or project setup) | Later, unless you have a consumer now |\n| `upload.created`, `milestone.updated` (dates), project-wide membership events | — | No consumer yet | Leave out |\n| Logins, tokens, failed sign-ins | — | — | **Not on the bus.** These belong in an audit log, not events. |\n\nTwo cleanups the registry makes easy:\n- **One name for one thing.** The workflow trigger `comment.added` and the live event `conversation.comment.created` both fire on comment create. The registry should hold one entry with both channels, not two names.\n- **Workflow-only events stay workflow-only.** `issue.modified`, `wiki.*` and `time.logged` stay off Hermes: they're the noisy ones.\n\n## How it would split\n1. Build the registry with **today's events only**: the three issues from before.\n2. Then **one issue pair per new event family**, a Gaia issue plus a Hermes issue for the allowlist and its decision record (Hermes requires one per new event). Each pair depends on the registry, and the pairs can go in parallel.\n\n**Which new events go in the first wave?** I recommend: `user.mentioned`, role changes folded into `user.access.changed`, `user.created`, and `workflow.run.finished`, with `issue.deleted` and project events left for later. Say yes or adjust the list, and I'll send the plan.	message	["Listing gaia/app/metadata/model/*.php", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/core", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components", "Searching issues: mention event 2>&1 | grep '^#' | head -12; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search integration webhook events 2>&1 | grep '^#' | head -1", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/IssuementionComponent.php", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/NotificationComponent.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/notifications", "Listing gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/**/Notification*/**/*.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/notifications/modules", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model/Mention.php", "Listing gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/{Mention,Role,Userrole,Project,Upload,Doc,Agent}Controller.php", "Updating the knowledge map"]	\N	0.402502	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 15:09:33	f	\N
3eaa32126afc-07a6-74f5-f6ffc918980a	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	Points are:\n\n* What if a slow write can overwrite a newer embedding? If event1 Patch comes after event2? Then there would be old embedding stored in the backend. Suggestion is that ares PATCH should send the hash of the text it embedded, <span style="font-size: 1.4rem;">and Gaia stores the vector only if that matches the hash of the record’s </span>*current*<span style="font-size: 1.4rem;"> semantic text. Otherwise 409, and Ares drops it.</span>\n* Event should be search.semantic.changed, not the other one.	message	[]	\N	\N	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	Rana Nouman	2026-11-17 15:09:50	f	[]
