44a8d9546afc-f0b3-74f5-8a70bcb51cb2	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	Here's the plan. Three findings shaped it:\n\n- **User mentions aren't recorded anywhere.** The editor writes `<a class="badge" href="/app/user/<id>">@Name</a>` into the comment HTML. Only *issue* mentions reach Gaia, through `meta.mentionedIssues`, and nothing writes rows to the existing `Mention` table. So `user.mentioned` needs Gaia to find the mentions itself, by reading the saved comment. I recommend that over having Prometheus send a list: Gaia then catches mentions from any client, including Talos and agents.\n- **`user.created` has no audience in Hermes today.** Hermes delivers to a project's members or to one user (`user:<id>`), and a new user belongs to neither. It needs a new **`system` scope**. I propose that Gaia's `GET /user/me` says whether the caller may receive system events, through a new ACL resource that the reviewer grants by hand (agents like Talos, admins), and that Hermes checks this flag when a client subscribes. It's the one real design choice in this plan, so it's marked complex. Tell me if you'd rather restrict it some other way.\n- **A run finishing** is recorded in one place, `RunJournal::finish`. Every run has a `projectId`, so `workflow.run.finished` can be project-scoped like the other events. Role changes reuse the membership pattern and need no Hermes change.\n\n**How the issues fit together**\n- The registry comes first.\n- Then three in parallel: the gaia-dev tooling and JSON export, the trigger catalog moved onto the registry, and the Gaia side of each new event.\n- Each Hermes issue comes after the Gaia issue it pairs with, because the drift check compares against Gaia's `dev` branch.\n\n**Left out:**\n- Merging `comment.added` into `conversation.comment.created`: existing workflows store the trigger name in their trigger nodes, so this needs a data migration. It's a follow-up.\n- Mentions in idea messages.\n- Notifications for mentions.\n- Anything in Talos or Prometheus that *reacts* to the new events.\n- `issue.deleted` and project events.	message	["Listing {gaia,hermes}/.github/workflows/*.yml", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/tools/gaia-dev/src", "Searching the code in hermes/.github/workflows/ci.yml", "Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/UserAccessLiveEventsComponent.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers", "Searching the code in gaia/core/libs/workflows", "Reading gaia/core/libs/workflows/RunJournal.php", "Searching for \\"const\\" in gaia/core/libs/workflows/RunStatus.php", "Searching for \\"mention\\" in prometheus/app", "Searching the code in .", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/helpers/translate-comment.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js", "Reading prometheus/app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js", "Searching the code in hermes/src", "Listing hermes/src/**/*.js", "Reading hermes/src/intents/evaluate.js", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model/Workflowrun.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/MembershipLiveEventsComponent.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/libs/workflows", "Listing gaia/app/metadata/*", "Listing gaia/core/config/*.php", "Searching the code in hermes/src/auth/gaia-session.js", "Updating the knowledge map"]	43b953236afc-f0b3-74f5-95cb48aa6d7f	0.973536	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 15:22:44	f	\N
c04859c66afc-b1c2-311d-d53b0c459a32	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	I am fine with Gaia determining if a user was mentioned, we just need to make sure that we are handling both create and update on all comments and descriptions, this is going to be the difficult part. As a user may be mentioned in a issue description or in a comment.\nLets drop user.created. It is beneficial in some place but is not that important for now.\nI would want to handle Mentions in both ideas and well as notifications for mentions in this Idea.\nNo need to handle Talos or Prometheus, but what ever we can do to handle Gaia changes related to these events we should.	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-17 15:29:04	f	[]
