6540de536afc-02d0-311d-af5265f83f80	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	Plan v2 is below. `user.created` and the system scope are gone. Mentions are now built as a small framework plus the resources that use it, and mention notifications are in.\n\n**Covering every create and update.** If mention detection lived in the controllers, it would miss writes that don't go through them: a bulk update, or a workflow "Set field" action changing an issue description. So it goes into a **model behavior**, like `ideaScreensBehavior`, which runs on every save whatever the path.\n- Each model declares which fields can contain mentions: `Issue.description`, `Comment.comment`, `Conversationroom.description` (thread starters), `Idea.description` and `Ideamessage.body` (markdown links).\n- On create and on any update of those fields, Gaia reads the saved text for links to `/app/user/<id>` and records one `Mention` row per record and user.\n- Rows are **only ever added**: re-saving or editing a record never notifies anyone twice, and removing a mention doesn't delete its row.\n- Gaia only records mentions of project members, and never a mention of yourself.\n\n**Side effects come from creating a `Mention` row.** The notification and the `user.mentioned` event both start there, the same way notification recipients publish `notification.created` today (`Systemnotificationrecipient` → `NotificationLiveEvents`). Someone mentioned in a comment on an issue they watch gets the mention notification, **not** a second "commented" one.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **Ideas:** Prometheus' idea composer has no @-picker today. Gaia will still find mentions there (for example a markdown link Nestor writes, or one pasted in), but people can't type one until Prometheus adds the picker. That's a follow-up outside this plan.\n- **Prometheus follow-up:** the notification item may not know how to link to an idea or a thread yet.\n- **Possible leak:** `MentionController` says its endpoints aren't action-ACL managed, so anyone may be able to read who mentioned whom. I left it out of this plan, but it's worth its own bug once you've checked it.\n\n**Left out:**\n- Mentions in wiki pages and docs.\n- Emails for mentions.\n- Merging `comment.added` with `conversation.comment.created`.\n- `user.created`.\n- Anything in Talos or Prometheus.	message	["Reading gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/notifications/modules/CommentNotification.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model/Systemnotification.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/notifications", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model", "Searching the code in gaia/app/metadata/model/Ideamessage.php", "Searching the code in gaia/core/mvc/models/behaviors/ideaScreensBehavior.php", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components", "Searching the code in gaia/core", "Searching the code in gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/NotificationLiveEvents.php", "Searching for \\"NotificationLiveEvents\\" in gaia/app", "Updating the knowledge map"]	643ad1006afc-02d0-311d-1687c7c44e28	0.709408	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 15:31:49	f	\N
