debfb9086afd-3eec-75db-de47ee09f3b6	6c7240d86afd-3eec-75db-a5acaf1064a6	I found what causes it. The nested route's own request is fine. The blank screen comes from the parent route `app.project`, which every project page sits under.\n\n## Why the screen is blank\n\nEmber resolves the hooks of a parent route before any child route's `model()` runs. In `routes/app/project.js`, those parent hooks are slow, and nothing is drawn while they run:\n\n1. **Three requests in a row before any child request.**\n   - `beforeModel` awaits `store.query('project', …)` with members, issue statuses and issue types.\n   - If the project has no statuses, it also awaits `store.query('issuestatus', …)`.\n   - `afterModel` then loads **all issues of the project** (`limit: -1`).\n   \n   Only after all of these finish does the nested route's request start. That gap is what you see in the network tab.\n2. **There is no loading template for that wait.** Ember looks for `app/project-loading.hbs`, then `app/loading.hbs`, then `loading.hbs`, and none of them exist. The header and sidebar are already drawn, so `content-wrapper` stays empty. `app/project/loading.hbs` and the `*-loading.hbs` files only cover the *children's* hooks. (`app/settings-loading.hbs` is the precedent for doing this at the right level.)\n3. **The child skeletons are hidden as well.** `templates/app/project.hbs` only renders `{{outlet}}` inside `{{#if this.projectId}}`. `setupController` sets `projectId` inside the `.then()` of a **second** project query (`fields: Project.id,Project.name`), even though `beforeModel` already loaded that project. So a child's loading skeleton can't show until this extra request returns.\n\nWhen you move between pages of the same project, the parent hooks don't run again, so the skeletons work. The blank happens on a fresh load or reload of any project URL, and after the `loading-assets` redirect. Switching to another project doesn't go blank: the old page just stays up until the new one is ready.\n\n## Proposed fix (Prometheus only, 2 issues)\n\n- **Show something right away:** add `app/project-loading.hbs`, and set `projectId`, `projectName` and `model` straight away from the project `beforeModel` already loaded. That drops the extra query, so the child skeletons appear immediately.\n- **Stop waiting for every issue:** start the all-issues query without waiting for it, and fill in the controller's `issues` when it returns. Its only users are the `issuesList` getter in `controllers/app/project.js` and the places that read it (`issue-details`, `projectrelated`), and that getter updates when `issues` changes. The child route's request then starts right after the project query. One risk: the issue picker in issue details is empty for a moment on a cold load. The issue asks for a check of that.\n\nNot included: replacing the all-issues preload with a search-as-you-type picker (worth doing, but a bigger change), and the store migration in aprom-4552. Both issues change `routes/app/project.js`, so the second one waits for the first.	message	["Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/map.md", "Searching issues: blank screen loading nested route --project aprom 2>&1 | head -40", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/prometheus/app && ls templates | head -50; find . -name \\"*loading*\\" | head -3", "Running sed -n 1,140p router.js; ls routes routes/app routes/app/project; wc -l routes/app.js routes/application.js routes/app/p", "Running cat routes/app.js | sed -n 1,281p", "Running sed -n 1,157p routes/app/project.js | grep -v '^\\\\s*\\\\*' ; cat templates/app/project/loading.hbs templates/app/project/iss", "Running cat templates/app.hbs | head -40; echo ---; ls templates/*loading* templates/app/*loading* 2>&1; echo ---; grep -n \\"befo", "Running cat templates/app/project.hbs | head -20; echo ---; cat templates/app/settings-loading.hbs templates/app/index-loading.h", "Running sed -n 45,70p controllers/app/project.js; grep -rn \\"issueList\\\\|projectController\\\\.\\\\(issues\\\\|get('issues')\\\\)\\" --include=*", "Searching the code in prometheus/app", "Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M && dev-tools/ai/ai kb search project route skeleton loading issues limit befo", "Updating the knowledge map"]	de01bff36afd-3eec-75db-2de637cf275a	0.674248	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 09:50:22	f	\N
e0b970b76afd-5fb4-75db-a2e164b7214a	6c7240d86afd-3eec-75db-a5acaf1064a6	It's not only the nested routes, even it's caused in the starting of the application before the translations are being requested.	message	[]	\N	\N	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	Rana Nouman	2026-11-18 09:58:56	f	[]
