3c3c70b16afd-5c6b-838a-a8084316c98e	6c7240d86afd-3eec-75db-a5acaf1064a6	You're right. The app start has blank gaps of its own, before the translations request and before any route draws anything. On a cold load there are four in a row:\n\n## The blank stretches on a cold load\n\n1. **While the JS bundles load (no request yet).** The `<body>` in `app/index.html` contains nothing but the two `<script>` tags. Until `vendor.js` and `prometheus.js` have downloaded and run, the page is empty. The CSS loads in `<head>`, so it is ready, but there is no markup for it to style.\n2. **Session restore, still before translations.** `routes/application.js` `beforeModel` first awaits `session.setup()`. That calls `_restore()`, which can refresh the token and wait on the cross-tab refresh lock if the token has expired. Only then does it await `translations.load()` (the locales request plus the default locale's translations). That is the gap you saw before the translations request.\n3. **Translations.** While `translations.load()` runs, nothing has rendered yet. There is no top-level loading template either: no `application-loading.hbs` or `loading.hbs`.\n4. **`app.loading-assets`.** This step loads the current user and then users, roles, projects and settings. Its template is a hardcoded `<h1>Loading Assets...</h1>` inside the empty app shell, so it looks nearly blank.\n\nAfter that, the project route gap from my last reply follows (the project query and the all-issues preload).\n\n## Fix for the start\n\nEmber's `application-loading` template would cover steps 2 and 3, but not step 1, because Ember isn't running yet. One mechanism covers steps 1 to 3:\n\n- Put a **static boot loader** in `index.html`. It needs no text, since translations aren't loaded yet.\n- Remove it once the application route has finished, which is when the first real screen (sign-in or the app) appears.\n- Replace the `Loading Assets...` heading with the existing page skeleton so step 4 isn't blank either.\n\nThis touches different files from the project-route issues, so it can be done at the same time as them.\n\nThe other two issues stay the same as before. One thing that didn't happen: saving these findings to my knowledge map was denied this turn, so a later conversation won't remember them.	message	["Running cd /home/rana.noman/web/hammad-hassan/Pr4M/prometheus/app && grep -v '^\\\\s*\\\\*\\\\|^\\\\s*/\\\\*\\\\*' routes/application.js; echo ---", "Running sed -n '/<body/,/<\\\\/body>/p' index.html; echo ----; grep -n \\"async setup\\\\|setup()\\" -A25 services/session.js | head -45; ", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/index.html", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/services", "Reading prometheus/app/services/translations.js", "Reading prometheus/app/services/session.js", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/services/session.js", "Listing prometheus/app/templates/*loading*.hbs in .", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/skeleton/page-loading.hbs", "Reading prometheus/app/index.html", "Updating the knowledge map"]	3b7763776afd-5c6b-838a-ee875da766e5	0.378976	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 10:00:28	f	\N
