e6299e386afd-68e3-838a-3511a16b06cf	6c7240d86afd-3eec-75db-a5acaf1064a6	Each step has a different constraint, so here are the options for each and the one I'd pick. I've drawn my picks.\n\n## Step 1: before the JS has loaded (bundle download, session restore, translations)\n\nOnly static HTML from `index.html` is possible here: no Ember components, no translations, no user data. The CSS is already loaded, though.\n\n| Option | What it looks like | Trade-off |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A. Splash (recommended)** | Grey `#ecf0f5` page with the logo and a crimson spinner in the middle, and a thin progress bar under it | Works for signed-in and signed-out users, and stays the same as the app changes |\n| B. Static shell skeleton | Header, sidebar and content drawn as grey skeleton blocks, so the app seems to "fill in" | Wrong for signed-out users, who get sign-in, not the shell. The header and sidebar markup would also have to be copied into `index.html` |\n| C. Progress bar only | A thin crimson bar at the top of an otherwise empty page | Cheapest, but it still looks blank |\n\n## Step 2: `app.loading-assets` (current user, users, roles, projects, settings)\n\nToday the app shell renders here with no data: no projects in the sidebar, no user name, and `Loading Assets...` as the content.\n\n| Option | Trade-off |\n|---|---|\n| **A. Keep the step 1 splash until loading-assets is done (recommended)** | One loader from first paint to a working page. No half-empty shell |\n| B. Shell plus `AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader` | Feels faster, but the sidebar and header have no data, so it looks broken |\n| C. Shell plus the inline `AppUi::Loader` spinner | Same problem as B, and less informative |\n\nWith A, the splash is removed when sign-in renders (signed out) or when loading-assets finishes (signed in). That is a change from the plan I sent, which removed it earlier and gave loading-assets its own skeleton.\n\n## Step 3: `app.project` (project query and issue preload)\n\nHere the shell and its data are ready, so the design system's rule applies: a `-loading.hbs` file with `AppUi::Skeleton`.\n\n| Option | Trade-off |\n|---|---|\n| **A. `PageLoading @showHeader` (recommended)** | A title and breadcrumb skeleton, plus a list box and a side box. It matches the child skeletons, so the switch to the page's own skeleton is barely visible |\n| B. Inline `AppUi::Loader` spinner in the content area | Simpler, but it goes against the skeleton rule and jumps visually when the child skeleton appears |\n| C. Choose a skeleton for the target page (board, issue, list) from `transition.to` | Most accurate, but it's extra logic, and it matters less once the issue preload stops blocking |\n\n## The screens\n\n- **boot-splash:** steps 1 and 2. In the real `index.html`, the box would hold `img/app/logo-256.png` above the spinner. The preview can't load images, so it shows only the spinner. The spinner and bar use `$primaryColor` (#B3244F) on `#ecf0f5`.\n- **project-loading:** step 3. This is the existing `PageLoading` skeleton inside the app shell with the project already selected. It needs no new CSS.\n\nStill open:\n- **Step 2:** should the splash stay through loading-assets (A) or hand over to a skeleton shell (B)? If you agree with A, I'll update the boot issue and attach these screens to the issues.\n- **Step 1:** do you want the progress bar under the spinner? It can't show real progress, so it would just loop.	message	["Searching the code in prometheus/docs/ui/design-system.md", "Listing prometheus/app/components/app-ui/skeleton/*", "Reading prometheus/docs/ui/design-system.md", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/skeleton/page-loading-body.hbs", "Listing prometheus/app/components/app-ui/loader*", "Reading prometheus/app/components/app-ui/loader.hbs", "Listing prometheus/app/templates/components/app-layouts/application-{header,sidebar}.hbs", "Listing prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/*.hbs", "Searching for \\"logo\\" in prometheus/app/components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/styles", "Reading prometheus/app/styles/components/loader.scss", "Running dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"boot-splash\\" title=\\"Boot splash (steps 1-2)\\" size=\\"1440x900\\"", "Searching the code in prometheus/app/styles/variables.scss", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/project-loading.png", "Running dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"boot-splash\\" title=\\"Boot splash (steps 1-2)\\" size=\\"1440x900\\"", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/boot-splash.png"]	\N	0.437806	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 10:11:50	f	[{"uploadId": "dab81ac26afd-68e3-838a-ffbc290f4b26", "key": "boot-splash", "title": "Boot splash (steps 1-2)", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}, {"uploadId": "e5768e986afd-68e3-838a-9a9b40052a6b", "key": "project-loading", "title": "Project route loading (step 3)", "version": 1, "width": 1440, "height": 900}]
