ffc701566afd-a500-49c2-026dcb4651e8	6c7240d86afd-3eec-75db-a5acaf1064a6	The header in the static boot skeleton is now skeleton too, using the same existing classes:\n\n- the logo slot has a `skeleton-line` instead of the logo image;\n- the search box (`global-search`) is a skeleton bar;\n- the three items on the right (New, notifications, user) are `skeleton-line--xs` placeholders inside the real `navbar-custom-menu` markup.\n\nThere's still no text and no new CSS. Everything visible during the boot is now a skeleton.\n\nOne decision for you. The static skeleton is removed when the application route finishes. After that, during `app.loading-assets` (signed-in users only), the real header renders: logo, search, New and the bell, with only the user name missing. The content area shows `PageLoading`. I think that's right, because the header controls are real by then. If you want the header to stay skeleton until loading-assets finishes, it would need a skeleton variant of `ApplicationHeader` driven by `dataLoaded`. That's one more component change. Say so and I'll add it.	message	["Searching the code in prometheus/app/styles/components/skeleton.scss", "Reading prometheus/app/styles/components/skeleton.scss", "Running sed -n '/^```nestor-screen key=\\"boot-splash\\"/,/^```$/p' /dev/null; cat > /tmp/nestor-header.txt <<'EOF' <header class=\\"m", "Running dev-tools/ai/ai screen render <<'EOF' ```nestor-screen key=\\"boot-splash\\" title=\\"Boot skeleton (index.html, before Ember)", "Reading dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/boot-splash.png"]	feb63c356afd-a500-49c2-500b7d7c7b2c	0.415073	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 10:29:19	f	[{"uploadId": "fb5232746afd-a500-49c2-f72cc2953283", "key": "boot-splash", "title": "Boot skeleton (index.html, before Ember)", "version": 3, "width": 1440, "height": 900}]
