bce082456afd-a884-838a-10bccfaf9010	d98352c16af4-9ee0-e9a2-4dddf1b444ee	## Plan v1 checked against a real PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5 run\n\nI ran Gaia `dev` (d4498171) on **PHP 8.5.12 + Phalcon 5.23.0** in throwaway containers to check the plan's steps:\n- built a PHP 8.5 + Phalcon 5.23 image;\n- ran `composer install` with the dual-stack constraints from `dual-stack-boot`;\n- booted the CLI and API on a copy of the local DB, with a small shim that maps the Phalcon 4 class names Gaia uses to Phalcon 5;\n- ran the same migration on both stacks and diffed the schemas;\n- sent the same 33 API requests to both stacks and diffed the responses.\n\n**The side-by-side approach works.** Several steps need to change for plan v2.\n\n### Confirmed\n- **Current stack:** PHP 7.4.21, Phalcon 4.1.2, Debian 10 (`rananoman/gaia:env-dev`).\n- **Target exists:** Phalcon **5.23.0** (released 2026-10-15, needs PHP ≥ 8.1) builds on PHP 8.5.12. So do imagick, xdebug 3.5.3, xhprof 2.3.10 and pdo_pgsql.\n- **The same code runs on both stacks.** With the shim, Gaia booted, migrated and served the API on 8.5. 29 of 33 requests returned identical responses.\n- **Migration gives an identical schema on both stacks:** all 920 columns (type, length, nullability, default) and every index match. On Postgres, existing tables go through Gaia's own `syncExistingTable`, which compares column *names* (plus varchar length). A type that Phalcon 5 reads differently can't cause a drop.\n- **Repo claims are correct:**\n  - CI runs only 4 PHPUnit folders.\n  - `phpunit.xml` still uses `whitelist`/`syntaxCheck`.\n  - There's no `composer.lock`.\n  - The SMTP password is in compose.\n  - Elasticsearch is only used in `AdminTask`.\n  - No code uses the incubator packages.\n\n### Changes needed for plan v2\n1. **The renames reach far beyond startup code.** v1 says "about 12 files" and that nothing outside startup branches on the version. Files using classes that Phalcon 5 removed:\n\n   | Class | Files |\n   |---|---|\n   | `Phalcon\\Di` | 49 |\n   | `Phalcon\\Exception` | 16 |\n   | `Phalcon\\Config` | 10 |\n   | `Phalcon\\Text` | 8 (v1 names 4) |\n   | `Phalcon\\Logger` | 5 |\n   | `Phalcon\\Loader` | 3 |\n\n   `autoload.php` is the first file to fail and isn't in the `dual-stack-boot` file list. What worked: a single shim file loaded only on Phalcon 5. It defines the old names, using `class_alias` for Di, DiInterface, Config and Logger, and small subclasses for Loader (`registerNamespaces` → `setNamespaces`) and Text. That needed no edits in the 80+ files. `dual-stack-boot` should use this approach instead of a factory class wired into each startup file.\n2. **`Phalcon\\Exception` is missing from v1, and it's the most dangerous change.** Phalcon 5's own exceptions (`Mvc\\Dispatcher\\Exception`, `Mvc\\Model\\Exception`) no longer extend it. So the `catch (\\Phalcon\\Exception)` in `public/index.php` stops catching them, and on the new stack:\n   - an unknown route returns **HTTP 200 with a PHP fatal-error HTML page** instead of a JSON 404;\n   - a PHQL error does the same instead of a 500.\n\n   Fix, which works on both stacks: add a final `catch (\\Throwable)` in `public/index.php`, and check the other 15 files that catch `Phalcon\\Exception`. This belongs in `php8-safe-code`.\n3. **PHPUnit can't start on PHP 8.** `tests/TestHelper.php` requires `tests/UnitTestCase.php`, which doesn't compile on PHP 8 ("Cannot use parent when current class scope has no parent"). Nothing extends that class, so delete it and the require instead of editing it as `dual-stack-boot` says. This is a `php8-safe-code` item.\n4. **`POST /bulk` returns an empty `200` on the new stack**, with `Content-Length: 0` and nothing logged; the old stack returns the responses. The likely cause is the nested `Application::handle()` in `core/mvc/http/SubRequestRunner.php`. Bulk is newer than v1. It's exactly the kind of silent break `response-diff` should catch, so keep that issue at high priority.\n5. **`phalcon/migrations` constraint:**\n   - `^2.2 || ^3.0` installs on PHP 8.5 only because composer falls back to 2021 versions: `nette/php-generator` 3.5.4 and `nette/utils` 3.1.6. Their metadata has no PHP upper bound, but they were never tested on 8.5. Newer 3.x versions cap PHP at < 8.3/8.4.\n   - The supported option on 8.5 is v4 (PHP ≥ 8.2), a rewrite released 2026-11-09. It removes the static `$connection` Gaia uses and `setup()` takes its own `Utils\\Config`.\n   - On Postgres, Gaia only uses `morphTable` to **create** new tables.\n\n   Recommendation: drop `phalcon/migrations` (and `phalcon/devtools`) entirely and create tables with the DB adapter's `createTable()`, which both Phalcon 4 and 5 have. That removes the riskiest dependency and makes `migration.php` the same on both stacks.\n6. **More version-neutral fixes for `php8-safe-code`** (from `php -l` on 8.5 across 715 files):\n   - 63 parameters that are implicitly nullable (deprecated in 8.4; an explicit `?Type` also works on 7.4);\n   - 8 warnings "Private methods cannot be final" (mostly in `RestController.php`);\n   - dynamic properties outside models, such as `DialectFactory::$dialect`.\n\n   Over HTTP no deprecations reached the PHP log, because Gaia's own error handling hides them. That confirms the `deprecation-log` issue is needed.\n7. **Fold in the answers from this thread:**\n   - **SMTP:** remove the environment-variable setup in favour of the Settings page, as discussed, not `.env`.\n   - **Elasticsearch:** removal confirmed.\n   - **Branching:** the `upgradephp8512` choice (or everything on `dev`).\n8. **Smaller corrections:**\n   - `env-image`: `docker-images/gaia/Dockerfile` does exist, but it's a stale MySQL-era recipe (`mileschou/phalcon:7.4`, PHPUnit 5.7). Replace it or mark it obsolete.\n   - `drop-elasticsearch` doesn't need to wait for `compat-scan`.\n   - `migrate-dry-run` can drop to medium priority. A before/after schema snapshot diff covers the main risk; it's what found the identical schemas above.\n\n### Not covered\n- PHPUnit on 8.5 (blocked by item 3).\n- The api-tester catalog.\n- Write endpoints.\n- The data was the local DB copy, not production.	message	\N	\N	\N	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	Agent Achilles	2026-11-18 10:15:24	t	\N
