febb34c76afd-cdc7-49c2-100bc0eb4f66	d98352c16af4-9ee0-e9a2-4dddf1b444ee	## Plan v2: PHP 8.5.12 and Phalcon 5.23.0\n\nYour test run settles the open questions, and I've rebuilt the plan around what it found:\n- **Alias shim instead of a compatibility class.** One file, loaded only on Phalcon 5, keeps the old class names working. None of the 80+ files that use them need editing for the dual-stack phase.\n- **New: the `\\Throwable` catch-all.** It's the most dangerous break, so it's its own issue, `php8-errors`.\n- **Removing `UnitTestCase.php`** goes into `dual-stack-boot`.\n- **Known break: `POST /bulk`** returns an empty 200 on the new stack. It gets its own bug issue.\n- **`phalcon/migrations` is dropped.** Gaia creates tables through the database adapter's `createTable()`. That goes in one issue with `--dry-run` and the schema snapshot, so they don't edit the same files in parallel. Priority is high, because 8.5 can't install the package safely.\n- **The PHP 8.4/8.5 deprecation fixes** (63 parameters that are implicitly nullable, 8 `private final`, dynamic properties) are split into `core/` and the rest, to stay within 15 files each.\n- **`compat-scan` is gone.** Your run already produced its findings, and `deprecation-log` gets a `lint-next` script that runs `php -l` over every file on the new image.\n- **Elasticsearch:** removed; it no longer waits on anything.\n- **SMTP:** now removes the environment-variable setup completely. Settings is the only source; with nothing configured, Gaia sends no mail and logs it. **Before that issue deploys, the deployed environment's SMTP must already be saved in Settings**, or mail stops.\n\n**Branching:** the plan puts everything on `dev`. Your run showed the shim doesn't touch the current stack, so there's nothing to isolate, and agents can only branch from `dev` today. If you still want `upgradephp8512`, say so and I'll add the A Dev Tool issue for a per-issue base branch and point `dual-stack-boot`, `next-stack-ci` and `bulk-next` at it.\n\n**Not in this plan:**\n- fixing whatever else `next-stack-ci` reports;\n- the switch-over and removing the shim;\n- replacing `Phalcon\\Text`;\n- PHPUnit 10 and php-parser 5;\n- `docker-images/gaia/Dockerfile`: it belongs to a repo I can't plan in, so delete it or mark it obsolete there.\n\nThe issues go in **Claude-v1**.	message	["Searching the code in gaia", "Listing **/{autoload.php,SubRequestRunner.php,UnitTestCase.php,DialectFactory.php} in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia", "Searching the code in gaia/core/libs/utils/SmtpSettings.php", "Updating the knowledge map"]	fdad78e56afd-cdc7-49c2-2c6f2a925171	1.358946	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 10:20:46	t	\N
f2f0e6866afd-fac5-42c4-a48b519579f8	d98352c16af4-9ee0-e9a2-4dddf1b444ee	I had the plan checked against a real run: Gaia \\`dev\\` on \\*\\*PHP 8.5.12 + Phalcon 5.23.0\\*\\* in throwaway containers. It covered composer with the dual-stack constraints, booting the CLI and API on a copy of the local DB, the same migration on both stacks, and the same 33 API requests on both stacks. Side by side works. Please update the plan with the following.\n\n\\*\\*Confirmed\\*\\*\n\\- Current stack: PHP 7\\.4\\.21\\, Phalcon 4\\.1\\.2\\, Debian 10\\.\n\\- Phalcon 5\\.23\\.0 exists \\(2026\\-10\\-15\\) and builds on PHP 8\\.5\\. So do imagick\\, xdebug 3\\.5\\.3\\, xhprof 2\\.3\\.10 and pdo\\_pgsql\\.\n\\- With a small shim that maps the Phalcon 4 class names to Phalcon 5\\, Gaia booted\\, migrated and served the API on 8\\.5\\. 29 of 33 requests returned identical responses\\.\n\\- Migration gives an identical schema on both stacks: all 920 columns and every index\\. Existing tables are synced by column name\\, so a type that Phalcon 5 reads differently can't drop a column\\.\n\n\\*\\*Changes\\*\\*\n1\\. \\*\\*Renames go far beyond startup code:\\*\\* \\`Phalcon\\Di\\` in 49 files\\, \\`Phalcon\\Exception\\` 16\\, \\`Phalcon\\Config\\` 10\\, \\`Phalcon\\Text\\` 8\\, \\`Phalcon\\Logger\\` 5\\, \\`Phalcon\\Loader\\` 3\\. \\`autoload\\.php\\` fails first and isn't in the \\`dual\\-stack\\-boot\\` list\\. Use one shim file\\, loaded only on Phalcon 5\\, that defines the old names \\(\\`class\\_alias\\` for Di\\, DiInterface\\, Config and Logger; small subclasses for Loader and Text\\)\\, instead of a factory class wired into each startup file\\.\n2\\. \\*\\*\\`Phalcon\\Exception\\` is the most dangerous break\\.\\*\\* Phalcon 5's own exceptions no longer extend it\\, so the catch in \\`public/index\\.php\\` misses them\\. An unknown route returns HTTP 200 with a PHP fatal\\-error page instead of a JSON 404\\, and a query error does the same instead of a 500\\. Add a final \\`catch \\(\\Throwable\\)\\` and check the other 15 files\\. It works on both stacks\\.\n3\\. \\*\\*PHPUnit can't start on PHP 8\\.\\*\\* \\`tests/TestHelper\\.php\\` requires \\`tests/UnitTestCase\\.php\\`\\, which doesn't compile \\("Cannot use parent"\\)\\. Nothing extends it\\, so delete it\\.\n4\\. \\*\\*\\`POST /bulk\\` returns an empty 200 on the new stack\\*\\*\\, with nothing logged\\. The likely cause is the nested \\`Application::handle\\(\\)\\` in \\`SubRequestRunner\\`\\. Give it its own issue\\, and keep \\`response\\-diff\\`\\, since this is exactly what it should catch\\.\n5\\. \\*\\*\\`phalcon/migrations\\`:\\*\\* on 8\\.5\\, v3 only installs through 2021 \\`nette\\` versions never tested on 8\\.5\\, and v4 is a fresh rewrite with a different API\\. Gaia only uses \\`morphTable\\` to create new tables\\, so drop the package \\(and \\`phalcon/devtools\\`\\) and use the adapter's \\`createTable\\(\\)\\`\\, which Phalcon 4 and 5 both have\\.\n6\\. \\*\\*More fixes that work on both stacks:\\*\\* 63 parameters that are implicitly nullable\\, 8 "private methods cannot be final" warnings\\, and dynamic properties outside models \\(e\\.g\\. \\`DialectFactory::$dialect\\`\\)\\. Gaia hides deprecations at runtime\\, so keep \\`deprecation\\-log\\`\\.\n7\\. \\*\\*My earlier answers:\\*\\* remove Elasticsearch now; it doesn't need to wait for \\`compat\\-scan\\`\\. SMTP: remove the environment\\-variable setup entirely\\, so Settings is the only source\\.\n8\\. \\*\\*Branching:\\*\\* \\[everything on \\`dev\\` / the \\`upgradephp8512\\` branch plus the A Dev Tool issue for a per\\-issue base branch\\]\\.\n9\\. \\*\\*Smaller corrections:\\*\\* \\`docker\\-images/gaia/Dockerfile\\` exists but is a stale MySQL\\-era recipe; mark it obsolete\\. \\`migrate\\-dry\\-run\\` can drop to medium priority\\, because a before/after schema snapshot covers the main risk\\.\n\n\\*\\*Not covered by the run:\\*\\* PHPUnit on 8.5 (blocked by item 3), the api-tester catalog, write endpoints, and production data.	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-18 10:46:11	f	[]
