f166afa66afd-9969-0c24-cd08a8df026c	7281afa46afd-7a77-8aba-64fa90d6419b	Understood: `none` isn't part of the backend contract, so there's no Gaia change and the whole fix is on the client side. The client learns the API as it is and stops sending options Gaia doesn't support.\n\nThe rules the client has to follow:\n- **`rels` must be a list of real relationship names.** Gaia rejects `none` or a misspelled name, and the whole request fails. That's what happens to the archived count today: the error is caught at `controllers/app/project/idea.js:416` and the count just disappears.\n- **Leaving `rels` out loads every relationship, hasMany included.** For Idea that means messages, plans and plan issues. So every call must name its relations, and only hasOne/belongsTo ones. hasMany children get their own query (this rule is already in `CLAUDE.md`).\n- **There's no way to ask for zero relationships.** A call that needs none asks for its cheapest hasOne. For the archived count that's `createdBy`, the same relation the idea list already loads.\n\nThe plan is now one Prometheus issue. It adds a builder that encodes these rules and a contract doc, and moves the idea browser to it. The other ~27 callers move in later issues, because some still pass hasMany `rels` on purpose and need their own changes.	message	["Updating the knowledge map"]	f0c6ce096afd-9969-0c24-dd934c43d79f	0.550695	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 14:15:13	f	\N
b722d6d26afd-3a92-67b1-99d0d65c10ec	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	Since the implementation started there were other changes with global semantic search we need to up update Gaia registry\n\n**Recommendation: option 1.**<span class="colour" style="color: rgb(85, 85, 85);"> The registry is meant to be the source of truth, and its gaps (doc.\\*, search.semantic.changed) look like omissions. Hermes still shouldn't allow events it doesn't have a handler or room routing for, so the two Gaia-only names need an owner's decision. Please also confirm whether gaia is publicly readable (otherwise the CI fetch needs a read-only token secret).</span>	message	[]	\N	\N	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-18 18:51:35	f	[]
d003b2b46afd-3a92-67b1-f5d826488f29	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	Agent Nestor is working on it.	working	\N	\N	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 18:52:00	f	\N
4d81ad046afd-d3df-b689-1bf140811d8d	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	I agree with Achilles' option 1, with one change: Gaia's registry has to be able to describe **every scope Hermes knows, and events that aren't raised yet**. Otherwise it can't list these names correctly.\n\n## What drifted\n\n| Name | Hermes | Gaia today | Gaia work that will raise it |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `doc.created/updated/deleted` | Allowed (ah-4530) | Not raised | agaia-4531 (pending) |\n| `search.semantic.changed` | Allowed, scope **`service:ares`** (ah-4657) | Not raised | agaia-4658 (new) |\n| `workflow.agent.run.requested` | User scope **and** the **`runtimes`** scope | Registry says `user` only | Already published to both by `AgentRunLiveEvents` |\n| `user.mentioned`, `workflow.run.finished` | Not allowed yet | In the registry, on the Hermes channel | ah-4650 and ah-4652 add them |\n\nGaia's registry only knows the scopes `project` and `user`, and only one scope per event. If we added the doc and search names as normal entries, the check from agaia-4641 would fail, because no component publishes them yet. If we added them disabled, the publisher would silently drop them later, when 4531 and 4658 start publishing.\n\n## Fix\nOne Gaia issue:\n- `scope` becomes a list of **`scopes`** covering `project`, `user`, `runtimes` and `service` (with a `serviceKind`).\n- A new **`planned: true`** marker means "Hermes may already allow this; Gaia doesn't raise it yet."\n- The gaia-dev check fails as soon as code publishes a planned event. That forces agaia-4531 and agaia-4658 to remove the marker, so nothing gets dropped silently.\n\n**Drift rule for ah-4643** (replaces the "must be equal" rule in the issue):\n1. Every name Gaia actually sends to Hermes (enabled, not planned, on the Hermes channel) must be in `EVENT_ALLOWLIST`.\n2. Every `EVENT_ALLOWLIST` name must be in the registry on the Hermes channel. Planned names are fine.\n3. The scope sets must match: user ⇔ `USER_SCOPED_EVENTS`, runtimes ⇔ `RUNTIME_SCOPED_EVENTS`, `service:<kind>` ⇔ `SERVICE_SCOPED_EVENTS`.\n\nThe rule allows Hermes to accept a name before Gaia publishes it, which is how doc events were shipped. It never allows the reverse: Gaia sending a name Hermes would reject.\n\n**Order.** `user.mentioned` and `workflow.run.finished` must be in Hermes before the check can pass on `dev`. Today ah-4650 and ah-4652 depend on ah-4643, which is backwards. I can't change issues, so please:\n- remove ah-4643 from the dependencies of ah-4650 and ah-4652;\n- make ah-4643 depend on ah-4650, ah-4652 and the new Gaia issue below.\n\n**Is the gaia repo public?** I can't tell from here: I have no git or GitHub access. You'll need to confirm it, or the CI fetch needs a read-only token secret.\n\n**Reply for Achilles on ah-4643** (paste it yourself):\n> Option 1, adapted. Gaia gets one issue that adds multiple scopes (`project`, `user`, `runtimes`, `service:<kind>`) and `planned` entries to the registry, and lists doc.* and search.semantic.changed as planned. Use this drift rule instead of equality: (1) Gaia's enabled, non-planned hermes names ⊆ `EVENT_ALLOWLIST`; (2) `EVENT_ALLOWLIST` ⊆ the registry's hermes names (planned included); (3) the scope sets match: user ⇔ `USER_SCOPED_EVENTS`, runtimes ⇔ `RUNTIME_SCOPED_EVENTS`, service:<kind> ⇔ `SERVICE_SCOPED_EVENTS`. Unit-test each rule. This issue now waits for ah-4650 and ah-4652 (they add user.mentioned and workflow.run.finished) and the Gaia issue. Gaia repo visibility: <confirm>.\n\nYou'll also want a one-line note on agaia-4531 and agaia-4658: "remove `planned` from the registry entry when you publish it". The check will catch it anyway, but the note saves them a failed CI run.	message	["Reading issue 4643 2>&1 | tail -60", "Gaia: get issue 4643", "Searching the code in .", "Listing .runs/*/gaia/app/metadata/events.php", "Listing .runs/*/hermes/src/contract/names.js", "Reading .runs/issue-4643/hermes/src/contract/names.js", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4649/gaia/app/metadata/events.php", "Reading .runs/issue-4643/hermes/src/contract/names.js", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4649/gaia", "Searching the code in .runs", "Searching issues: search.semantic.changed 2>&1 | grep '^#' | head -8; dev-tools/ai/ai kb search doc.created doc.updated live events 2>&1 | g", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4649/gaia/app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/AgentRunLiveEvents.php", "Reading .runs/issue-4649/gaia/app/metadata/events.php", "Searching the code in .runs/issue-4649/gaia/tools/gaia-dev/src", "Listing .runs/issue-4649/gaia/core/libs/events/*.php", "Updating the knowledge map"]	4c7859a26afd-d3df-b689-ab9cc2457a5a	2.001294	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 18:54:05	f	\N
