fd583b336ae5-ef52-7dee-a1b870ebc2f6	6471d1b46ae5-10d2-613b-e3f2313332d0	5	{"summary": "Four Prometheus issues in aga-v1. screens-parse fixes the root cause of invisible idea screens: Ideamessage screens and steps arrive from Gaia as JSON text and are never parsed, so neither the thread nor the plan box finds them. screen-preview (after screens-parse) shows each screen as its full image through the download token, because GET /upload/{id} only returns fileThumbnail as a boolean. plan-review adds a review mode that gives the plan the wide column, and browser-collapse lets the ideas list collapse; both are independent.", "issues": [{"key": "screens-parse", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea messages: parse the screens and steps JSON from Gaia so screens show in the thread and plan box", "description": "<p>Agent Nestor's screens never appear on the idea page. The plan box shows only a static <code>fa-picture-o</code> icon and the screen key (the \\"missing\\" branch in <code>components/idea/plan-box.hbs</code> ~l.29), and the conversation shows nothing. Engineers can't see a mockup before its issues are created.</p><p>Cause: Gaia stores <code>Ideamessage.screens</code> and <code>Ideamessage.steps</code> as JSON <strong>text</strong> (<code>gaia/core/mvc/models/behaviors/ideaScreensBehavior.php</code> encodes arrays; fields are <code>type text</code>) and returns them as strings. <code>models/ideamessage.js</code> declares <code>@attr screens</code> and <code>@attr steps</code> with no transform, so they stay strings. <code>components/idea/message-screens.js</code>, <code>plan-box.js</code> <code>screens</code> and <code>message-item.js</code> <code>steps</code> all require <code>Array.isArray</code> and get nothing. The Mirage factory (<code>mirage/factories/ideamessage.js</code>) returns arrays, which hid it.</p><ul><li>Start with a failing test: make the Mirage <code>ideamessage</code> factory (and any fixtures) return <code>screens</code>/<code>steps</code> as JSON strings, as Gaia does.</li><li>Declare both as <code>@attr('json')</code> (existing <code>transforms/json.js</code>). If the transform's lack of a <code>serialize</code> breaks saving a user message, add a <code>serialize</code> that sends arrays as JSON text (Gaia's behaviour accepts both). Make sure null, empty string and invalid JSON give an empty list, not an error.</li><li>No component changes beyond what the parsed arrays need. <code>Idea::MessageScreens</code> then renders each screen and the plan box finds it by key and version, so title and version show and the click opens it (existing <code>open</code>).</li><li>Tests: a unit test for the model/transform (string, array, null, invalid). The acceptance case in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/</code> shows a Nestor message with a screen as a clickable entry in the thread and in the plan box, and its steps listed.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on an idea whose Nestor messages carry screens, each screen appears as a clickable entry with its title and version, in the message and in the plan box, and Nestor's steps show again. This works with the real Gaia response, not just Mirage.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the thumbnail image itself (separate issue), Gaia changes.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "screen-preview", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea screens: show the full image instead of the boolean fileThumbnail", "description": "<p>Once the screens of idea messages are parsed (previous issue), <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code> (<code>components/idea/message-screen.{hbs,js}</code>, used in the thread and the plan box) still can't show an image. It takes the <code>img src</code> from <code>services/upload-preview.js</code> <code>thumbnail()</code>, which reads <code>upload.fileThumbnail</code> from <code>findRecord('upload', id)</code>. For <code>GET /upload/{id}</code> Gaia returns that field as the stored <strong>boolean</strong>. Only the POST response and Gaia's <code>FilethumbComponent</code> (for files <code>included</code> with a parent such as an issue) swap in base64 data. The image is broken, and even a real thumbnail would be a 198x132 crop, too small for a mockup.</p><ul><li>Show each screen as its full image, scaled to the available width, using <code>uploadPreview.previewUrl(uploadId)</code> (download token + <code>/preview/get/&lt;token&gt;</code>). <code>modifiers/render-markdown.js</code> already shows pasted images this way. Show the title and version (<code>views.app.idea.conversation.screenVersion</code>) under it, and the <code>fa-picture-o</code> placeholder while it loads or if it fails.</li><li>Keep the click that opens the full-size image in a new tab (existing <code>open</code>).</li><li>Remove the <code>thumbnail()</code> use, and the method if nothing else calls it. Don't treat <code>fileThumbnail</code> as an address in this component.</li><li>Sizes in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code>: in a message the screen spans the message width (<code>.idea-message-screen</code> is a fixed 160px today). In the plan box screen row (<code>plan-box.hbs</code> ~l.23) keep a compact size that fits the side column.</li><li>Guard the async load after destroy (check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after the await).</li><li>Tests: integration test for <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code>. With a Mirage upload whose <code>fileThumbnail</code> is <code>true</code>, it renders an <code>img</code> with the preview address. A failed token shows the placeholder.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the idea page every screen in Nestor's messages and in the plan box shows its image as soon as the page loads, before any plan is approved. A click opens it full size.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> an in-app lightbox, Gaia thumbnail changes, issue Files box thumbnails.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["screens-parse"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "plan-review", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea page: plan review mode with the plan in the wide column", "description": "<p>The idea page (<code>templates/app/project/idea/page.hbs</code>) puts the conversation in <code>col-md-8</code> and the Plan, Created Issues and Summary boxes in <code>col-md-4</code>. The page itself sits in the <code>col-md-9</code> beside the ideas browser. That suits chatting, but reviewing a plan with several issues in about a quarter of the screen is hard. Engineers need to switch to a layout that favours the plan.</p><ul><li>Add a box-tool button to the Plan box header (<code>components/idea/plan-box.hbs</code>, <code>btn btn-box-tool</code>, <code>fa-expand</code> / <code>fa-compress</code>, title from <code>translations/en-us.json</code>) that toggles review mode through an action passed from the page.</li><li>Review mode: the side column (Plan, Created Issues, Summary) becomes <code>col-md-8</code> and the conversation <code>col-md-4</code>, with the plan column first, so the plan is on the left. The composer stays usable. Normal mode is today's layout.</li><li>State: query param <code>view=plan</code> on the page route (<code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>), so the mode survives reload and can be linked. Opening another idea keeps the mode. Leaving the ideas route resets it.</li><li>The plan's screen row and issue rows use the extra width (screens larger than in the side column). No new colours or components: reuse the plan box markup and classes in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code>.</li><li>Tests: acceptance cases in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-plan.feature</code>: the button switches the columns, a reload with <code>?view=plan</code> opens in review mode, toggling back restores the layout.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> from any idea with a plan, one click gives the plan the wide column and the conversation the narrow one. Another click goes back. Approve and version tabs work in both modes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> collapsing the ideas browser (separate issue), resizable columns.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "browser-collapse", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: collapse the ideas browser so the idea page uses the full width", "description": "<p>The ideas browser takes <code>col-md-3</code> of the ideas layout (<code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>), so an open idea (conversation and plan) only gets <code>col-md-9</code>. Engineers working in one idea want the full width for the conversation and the plan.</p><ul><li>Add a collapse button to the browser box header (<code>box-tools</code>, <code>btn btn-box-tool</code>, <code>fa-angle-double-left</code>, title in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>) next to the \\"New\\" button.</li><li>Collapsed: the browser column is hidden and the outlet column becomes <code>col-md-12</code>. A small box-tool button (<code>fa-angle-double-right</code>) at the left of the outlet expands it again.</li><li>State: a tracked flag on <code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>, kept in <code>localStorage</code> so the choice survives reloads. Default expanded.</li><li>The New Idea page (create route) and the idea page both follow the flag.</li><li>Styles, if any, scoped under <code>.idea-wrapper</code> in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code>. Square edges, existing colours.</li><li>Tests: acceptance cases in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-browser.feature</code>: collapse hides the list and widens the content, expand restores it, the state survives a reload.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> one click hides the ideas list and the idea page spans the content area. One click brings it back. The choice is remembered.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> plan review mode (separate issue), mobile layout changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-31 09:38:05	2026-10-31 09:38:05	f
59a5fa556afa-4645-5654-e98278cee66b	de3303a86afa-5122-b3db-e6498ef24096	2	{"summary": "Adopt AppUi::Avatar everywhere a user's picture is shown (~35 call sites), each mapped from its current rendered size to the standard scale (xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96) plus a new ml 64px size for the member grids, which have no fitting size today. One issue per area; issues that share a stylesheet are chained (issue.scss: issue details -> assignee avatars; project.scss: issue details -> project overview -> member stacks -> role page; agent.scss: relate fields -> agent pages). A final cleanup removes Agent::UserAvatar and the dead avatar CSS and records the rule in the design system. All in milestone aga-Cleanup.", "issues": [{"key": "avatar-ml", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::Avatar: add size ml (64px) for member grids", "description": "<p>We are moving every user picture in the app to <code>AppUi::Avatar</code>. The member grids (project overview Members, issue Members box, role page Members) render avatars at about 70-80px today, between m (40px) and l (96px), so the scale needs one more size.</p><ul><li><code>components/app-ui/avatar.js</code>: add <code>ml</code> to <code>SIZES</code> (order xs, s, m, ml, l). Unknown values still fall back to m.</li><li><code>styles/components/app-ui-avatar.scss</code>: <code>.app-ui-avatar-ml</code> 64px x 64px; agent icon font size and initials text scaled between m and l; the robot marker shows (as from s up).</li><li>Update the header comment of the scss and the component YUIDoc.</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>: add the ml column and size option.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-avatar.md</code> and its manifest json: list ml 64px and when to use it (stacked member grids with the name below).</li><li>Integration test: ml renders 64px, with initials and with the agent marker.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>@size=\\"ml\\"</code> renders a 64px avatar for a person, a person without an image and an agent; the existing sizes are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing any page that uses the avatar.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-shell", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar in the header, user menu, sidebar user panel and control bar", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in). Today the app shell renders raw <code>/userimage/get</code> images sized by AdminLTE.</p><ul><li><code>components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs:56</code> navbar <code>img.user-image</code> (25px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code>; keep it beside the name, vertically centred in the 50px navbar.</li><li>Same file l.64 user menu <code>li.user-header img.img-circle</code> (90px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"l\\"</code>, centred as today.</li><li><code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.hbs:5</code> sidebar <code>.user-panel .image img</code> (45px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>.</li><li><code>components/application-controlbar.hbs:16</code> <code>img.contacts-list-img</code> (40px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>.</li><li>Pass <code>this.currentUser.user</code> (or the listed user) as <code>@user</code>.</li><li>If an AdminLTE rule (<code>.navbar .user-image</code>, <code>.user-header &gt; img</code>, <code>.user-panel &gt; .image &gt; img</code>, <code>.contacts-list-img</code>) no longer matches, re-add the float/margin it gave by scoping a rule in the layout's own module scss, not by restyling the avatar.</li><li>Update the tests that select these images (use <code>data-test-avatar</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the 4 spots show AppUi::Avatar at the sizes above; the header, menu and sidebar layouts look as before apart from the size change; a user without an image shows initials.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> deleting legacy CSS used elsewhere (cleanup issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-comments", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar in comments, the comment composer and the weekly conversations widget", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in).</p><ul><li><code>components/conversation-ui/comment-frame.hbs:3</code> <code>Agent::UserAvatar @class=\\"img-circle img-sm\\"</code> (30px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code> with <code>(hash id=@userId name=@userName)</code>. This frame is shared by issue comments, thread comments and idea messages; check all three.</li><li><code>components/conversation-ui/comment-composer.hbs:12</code> current user image (30px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code>.</li><li><code>components/widgets/weekly-conversations.hbs:~60</code> <code>img.img-circle.img-sm</code> (30px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code> with <code>(hash id=comment.createdUser name=...)</code>.</li><li>AdminLTE floats <code>.box-comment img</code> and offsets the comment text by 40px; keep the avatar floated left with the text beside it (scope a rule in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code> if needed). Its 30px <code>!important</code> rule matches s.</li><li>Update tests that select the old images (use <code>data-test-avatar</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> comments, the composer and the widget show 30px AppUi avatars with the same layout as before; agents show the agent look; a missing image shows initials.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> removing <code>Agent::UserAvatar</code> (cleanup issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-notifications", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar in notifications", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in).</p><ul><li><code>components/app-ui/notifications/notification.hbs:5</code> <code>img.img-circle.img-xs.user-image</code>, rendered 40px by <code>styles/components/notifications-sidebar.scss:100</code> -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code> with <code>(hash id=@notification.createdUser name=@notification.createdUserName)</code>.</li><li>Keep the wrapper <code>span.user-image[data-notification-user-image]</code>: <code>notification.js</code> (~l.236-260) decides that a click on the avatar opens the user, partly by checking for an <code>IMG</code> with class <code>user-image</code>. Make that check rely on the wrapper's data attribute only, so initials (no img) behave the same.</li><li>Rescope the 4rem sidebar rule so it no longer resizes the avatar's inner img.</li><li>Update the notification integration and acceptance tests (avatar click still opens the user).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> notifications show 40px AppUi avatars; clicking the avatar (image or initials) opens the user, clicking elsewhere opens the item as before.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-issue-details", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar in issue details (assignee, members, time logs, watchers)", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, ml 64, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in). Issue details (<code>components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code>) is shared by the issue page, the list and board quick views and the gantt panel.</p><ul><li>l.129 assignee in <code>.project-manager</code> (img stretched to the col-md-2 width, about 100-130px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"l\\"</code>, centred above the name.</li><li>l.275-293 Members box <code>users-list</code> (assigned to, owned by, modified by, reported by; fluid, about 70-80px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"ml\\"</code>, centred in its cell with the name and label below.</li><li>l.376 and l.490 time logs (<code>.time-log .user-img img</code> 50px, <code>styles/modules/issue.scss:99</code>) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>; drop the <code>user-img</code> wrapper class there (keep the tooltip) and remove the issue.scss <code>.user-img img</code> rule if nothing else uses it.</li><li>l.710 add-watcher modal <code>img.img-circle.img-sm</code> (30px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code>.</li><li>Replace every <code>Agent::UserAvatar</code> here; pass <code>(hash id=... name=... type=...)</code> where only fields are at hand.</li><li>Make sure <code>.project-manager img { width: 100% }</code> (<code>styles/modules/project.scss:11</code>, also used by the project overview) doesn't stretch the avatar's inner img: scope it to the old markup or move it under a class only the old markup has. Don't delete it (the project overview still uses it until its own issue).</li><li>Update tests that select the old images.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the issue page and quick views, the avatars show at the sizes above with the layout as before; agents show the agent look; missing images show initials.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-ml"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-assignee", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar for issue assignees (assignee select, issue list, gantt bar)", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in).</p><ul><li><code>components/issue/assignee-select.hbs:8</code> compact trigger on board cards (24px from <code>styles/modules/issue.scss:693</code> <code>img.img-circle</code>) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code>; remove that rule. Keep the caret and the dropdown toggle behaviour (aprom-4155: don't stop click propagation).</li><li>Same file l.28 menu options (<code>.assignee-select-option-avatar</code> 20px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"xs\\"</code>, still left of the name with the same gap.</li><li><code>templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs:108</code> issue list assignee (<code>img.img-circle.user-img</code>, 40px from the global <code>.user-img</code> in profile.scss) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>, title = the name. Don't delete <code>.user-img</code> (still used elsewhere).</li><li><code>components/app-ui/gantt-chart/gantt-bar.hbs:47</code> (40px, <code>styles/modules/gantt.scss:466</code> <code>!important</code>) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>; keep the tooltip (initialize-tooltip on the wrapper) and the position right of the bar; remove the img size rule.</li><li>Check the board card with Sortable: the avatar must still open the menu, not start a drag (the sortable filter is <code>[data-issue-assignee-dropdown]</code>).</li><li>Update tests that select these images.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> board cards, the issue list, the gantt bars and the assignee menu show AppUi avatars at the sizes above; the assignee menu still opens and changes the assignee.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-issue-details"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-project-overview", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar on the project overview (manager, conversations, members)", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, ml 64, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in). Page: <code>templates/app/project/index.hbs</code>.</p><ul><li>l.30 manager in <code>.project-manager</code> (img stretched to the col-md-2 width) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"l\\"</code>, centred above the name. <code>.project-manager img { width: 100% }</code> (<code>styles/modules/project.scss:11</code>) must no longer hit the avatar; remove it if issue details no longer needs it.</li><li>l.92 latest conversations <code>.user-block img.img-circle</code> (40px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code> with <code>(hash id=conversation.createdBy ...)</code>; keep the subject and description offset beside it.</li><li>l.273 Members box grid (<code>users-list</code>, about 70-80px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"ml\\"</code>, keeping the inactive/invited status badge on the avatar (<code>.member-avatar-wrap</code>, <code>.member-account-status</code>) and the delete button.</li><li>Update tests that select these images.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the three boxes show AppUi avatars at the sizes above with the layout as before; the member status badges still sit on the avatar.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-ml", "avatar-issue-details"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-member-stack", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project::MemberAvatars: pass a size to AppUi::Avatar instead of resizing it with CSS", "description": "<p><code>components/project/member-avatars.hbs</code> already renders <code>AppUi::Avatar</code>, but its size is forced by CSS on the wrapper: <code>.member-avatars .member-avatar</code> 4rem (<code>styles/modules/project.scss:318</code>) and 2.4rem in role rows (<code>styles/modules/role.scss:70</code>). Use the component's sizes instead.</p><ul><li>Add <code>@size</code> to MemberAvatars (default m), passed to each <code>AppUi::Avatar</code>; the overflow badge (<code>.member-avatars-overflow</code>) takes the same diameter.</li><li>Callers: projects list (<code>templates/app/projects/index.hbs:111</code>, 40px) -&gt; m; role rows (<code>templates/app/role.hbs:79</code>, 24px) -&gt; s; thread participants (<code>components/conversation/participants-box.hbs:7</code>) -&gt; m.</li><li>Remove the width/height overrides from project.scss and role.scss; keep the overlap margin and hover.</li><li>YUIDoc for <code>@size</code>; integration test per size.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the stacks render at 40px (projects, participants) and 30px (role rows) through <code>@size</code>, with no CSS size override left.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-project-overview"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-role-page", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar on the role page (members and view-all modal)", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, ml 64, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in). Page: <code>templates/app/role/page.hbs</code>.</p><ul><li>l.145 Members grid (<code>.member-avatar-wrap img</code> 7rem, <code>styles/modules/role.scss:188</code>) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"ml\\"</code>, name below; remove the img size rule.</li><li>l.229 view-all modal (<code>.role-members-view-all__avatar</code> 3.6rem, role.scss:227) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>, beside the name; keep the class on the wrapper for layout (flex-shrink) but drop its size.</li><li>Pass <code>userrole.user</code> (or <code>(hash id=... name=...)</code>).</li><li>Update tests that select these images.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> role members and the modal list show AppUi avatars at 64px and 40px with the layout as before.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-ml", "avatar-member-stack"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-users", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar in user management and the profile's close members", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in).</p><ul><li><code>templates/app/user/management.hbs:97</code> <code>img.user-img</code> (40px, global <code>.user-img</code> in profile.scss:456) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>; keep the 1rem gap before the name (<code>styles/modules/user-management.scss:48</code>, move it to the wrapper).</li><li><code>components/user-profile/close-members.hbs:4</code> <code>img.user-img</code> (40px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>.</li><li>alt/title = the user's name (today the alt is the literal user-img).</li><li>Don't delete <code>.user-img</code> (cleanup issue).</li><li>Update tests that select these images.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> both lists show 40px AppUi avatars, layout as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the profile picture editor (<code>components/user/edit/profile-picture.hbs</code>), which previews an unsaved upload.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-relate-fields", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar in the user and actor relate fields", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in). The relate renderers show people as a 25px raw image and agents through <code>Agent::Avatar</code>; <code>relate-user</code> passes no user, so an agent's picture never shows.</p><ul><li><code>components/related-fields/relate-user.hbs</code>: one <code>AppUi::Avatar @size=\\"xs\\"</code> for people and agents, with <code>(hash id=@data.value name=@data.label)</code> (add <code>type</code> when <code>@data.isAgent</code>); keep the sponsor text.</li><li><code>components/related-fields/relate-actor.hbs</code>: same for <code>kind</code> user and agent (<code>@data.user</code> for agents); the expression icon stays.</li><li>Remove <code>.user-relate-icon</code> (<code>styles/modules/form-fields.scss:226</code>) if unused afterwards, and the <code>.relate-user.relate-agent .agent-avatar</code> size rule (<code>styles/modules/agent.scss:97</code>), which would override the avatar size; keep the sponsor line-height aligned.</li><li>Check select rows in issue create (assignee), the workflow properties panel (actor) and agent sponsor pickers: same row height, no overflow (aprom-4283).</li><li>Update tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> people and agents show 20px AppUi avatars in these selects (agents with their picture when they have one); rows don't grow.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-agents", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar on the agent list and agent page", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px). It renders <code>Agent::Avatar</code> for agents itself, plus the robot marker when the agent has a picture.</p><ul><li><code>templates/app/agent/index.hbs:49</code> <code>Agent::Avatar @user=agent.user</code> (36px) -&gt; <code>AppUi::Avatar @user=agent.user @size=\\"m\\"</code>; keep the 10px gap to the name (<code>.agents-list .agent-cell</code> in agent.scss, move it to the wrapper).</li><li><code>templates/app/agent/page.hbs:54</code> and <code>:58</code> <code>Agent::Avatar @large</code> (96px), inside <code>User::Edit::ProfilePicture</code> and its fallback -&gt; <code>@size=\\"l\\"</code>; the upload click and crop flow keep working.</li><li>Remove agent.scss page rules that only sized these avatars, if unused afterwards. Keep <code>Agent::Avatar</code> itself (AppUi::Avatar uses it).</li><li>Update the agent list and page tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the agent list shows 40px and the agent page 96px avatars with the agent look; uploading a picture still works and shows it.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-relate-fields"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-cleanup", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Remove Agent::UserAvatar and the dead avatar CSS; record AppUi::Avatar as the only user picture", "description": "<p>After every user picture has moved to <code>AppUi::Avatar</code>, remove what is left of the old ways.</p><ul><li>Delete <code>components/agent/user-avatar.{hbs,js}</code> and its tests (no callers left; check with a search).</li><li>Search <code>app/</code> for <code>/userimage/get</code> outside <code>components/app-ui/avatar.js</code> and the profile picture editor; any left is a missed call site: move it (pick the size closest to its current rendered size) or list it in a comment.</li><li>Remove CSS rules that no longer match anything: e.g. <code>.user-img</code> (profile.scss:456), <code>.user-relate-icon</code>, <code>.assignee-select-option-avatar</code>, <code>.users-list .agent-avatar</code>, <code>.box-comment &gt; .agent-avatar</code>, <code>.project-manager img</code>, gantt <code>.users-list &gt; li &gt; img</code>. Check each with a search of the templates first.</li><li><code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>: add the rule that every user picture is <code>AppUi::Avatar</code> with a standard size (xs, s, m, ml, l and when to use each), and add it to the checklist.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> no <code>Agent::UserAvatar</code>, no raw user images outside the two allowed places, no dead avatar CSS; full test suite and lint pass.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-shell", "avatar-comments", "avatar-notifications", "avatar-assignee", "avatar-role-page", "avatar-users", "avatar-agents"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 11:22:01	2026-11-16 11:29:22	f
f1347aa46aef-df8f-38f6-bb74f7085b77	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	8	{"summary": "ezSearch phase 3, metadata-driven: search fields come from view metadata (views.<Module>.search) instead of hard-coded schema files or controller filter arrays, and the approach is documented as Prometheus architecture. First the framework: metadata format, query-schema service building schemas from it with a named value-source registry, Issue and Project moved into metadata, and the architecture doc. Then, in parallel, the Project list moves to <EzSearch>, and the generic admin module list (app.module) gets <EzSearch> from its module's search metadata in place of the jQuery panel. Last, jQuery QueryBuilder, the old utils, the old search code and the plugin's styles are removed. YUIDoc output in docs/ is left alone.", "issues": [{"key": "search-metadata", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: search fields from view metadata, documented as the list-view architecture", "description": "<p>Prometheus is partly metadata-driven: <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> <code>views</code> drives navigation, dashboard widgets and the Project list fields, and its comment states the goal of building all views from metadata. Search is not: ezSearch's fields are hard-coded in <code>app/utils/query/schemas/issue.js</code> and <code>project.js</code> (aprom-4295), and the generic admin list (<code>controllers/app/module.js</code> <code>setupQuery</code>) reads a <code>views.&lt;Module&gt;.filters</code> key that no module declares. Engineer's decision: where something is already partly metadata-driven and the change is small, make it fully metadata-driven. A list view gets search by declaring search metadata, and nothing is hard-coded per page. This issue builds that capability and documents it; the pages move in later issues.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Metadata format, in <code>views.&lt;Module&gt;.search</code> of <code>metadata.js</code>: <code>{ module: 'Issue', textField: 'Issue.subject', fields: { 'Issue.priority': { label: 'views.app.issue.fields.priority', type: 'enum', aliases: ['priority','prio'], values: { source: 'translation', key: 'views.app.issue.lists.priority' } }, ... } }</code>.<ul><li>Types are those of the operator registry (<code>app/utils/query/operators.js</code>): text, number, enum, user, date.</li><li><code>values</code> names a source plus its parameters; it is never a literal list built in code.</li><li>Field order in the metadata is the order shown in the builder and suggestions.</li></ul></li><li>Move the Issue and Project fields from <code>app/utils/query/schemas/issue.js</code> and <code>project.js</code> into <code>views.Issue.search</code> and <code>views.Project.search</code> unchanged (ids, aliases, labels, types, text fields), then delete both schema files.</li><li><code>MD.getViewMeta</code>: remove the <code>filters</code> branch (~l.478-486, which mutates labels in place). Search labels stay translation keys and are translated where they are shown.</li><li><code>app/services/query-schema.js</code>:<ul><li><code>load(module, context)</code> reads <code>getViewMeta(module, 'search')</code>, resolves each field's value source and returns <code>createSchema(...)</code> as today. It returns <code>null</code> when the module declares no search, and callers then render no search.</li><li>A value-source registry keyed by name, each entry loading values through the store with the context (e.g. <code>projectId</code>): <code>translation</code> (static, from a translation key), <code>issueStatuses</code>, <code>milestones</code>, <code>issueTypes</code>, <code>members</code> (project members with avatars) and <code>users</code>.</li><li>An unknown source name throws a clear error in development and tests. Caching per module and context stays.</li><li>The public API stays as 4295 shipped it, so the Issue list (aprom-4305) keeps working without changes.</li></ul></li><li>Documentation (new): <code>prometheus/docs/architecture/metadata-views/architecture.md</code> and <code>decisions.md</code>, in the style of <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/</code>:<ul><li>What is metadata-driven today (navigation, dashboard widgets, list fields, search) and where it lives.</li><li>The rule: a list view that extends Module (generic <code>app.module</code>, or a module list on <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>) gets search only by declaring <code>views.&lt;Module&gt;.search</code>; controllers don't define filters.</li><li>The search metadata format with a full example.</li><li>How to add search to a module, and how to add a value source (the only part that needs code).</li><li>The principle: when a feature is partly metadata-driven and the change is small, finish it as metadata rather than adding hard-coded code; a full metadata-driven architecture is the direction, taken step by step.</li></ul>Add a one-line pointer to this doc in <code>prometheus/CLAUDE.md</code> under Architecture.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests:<ul><li><code>query-schema</code> builds the Issue and Project schemas from metadata with the same resolution results as before (aliases, labels, prefixes, values from Mirage).</li><li>It returns <code>null</code> for a module without search metadata.</li><li>It throws on an unknown value source.</li><li>Each registered source loads its values.</li></ul></li><li>The parser, completer and EzSearch tests and the Issue list acceptance tests pass unchanged.</li><li>No search field definitions remain in code outside <code>metadata.js</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> moving other views (forms, details) to metadata, loading metadata from the server, the Project and generic lists' UI (separate issues), YUIDoc output in <code>docs/</code>.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ez-project-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project list: replace jQuery QueryBuilder with ezSearch", "description": "<p>ezSearch replaced jQuery QueryBuilder on the Issue list (aprom-4305). The Project list is one of the two remaining jQuery users. Follow aprom-4305's pattern, with the Project search fields from <code>views.Project.search</code> metadata, loaded through <code>services/query-schema.js</code> (see <code>docs/architecture/metadata-views/architecture.md</code>), and the saved-search arguments of <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> (aprom-4304).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>templates/app/projects/index.hbs</code> ~l.17-75: replace the Saved Searches dropdown, the readonly <code>FieldText</code>, Search, Clear and the <code>.list-view-filters</code> block (<code>{{query-builder module=\\"project\\"}}</code> and its Save Search button) with <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code>, wired as on the Issue list: <code>@schema</code>, <code>@query</code>, <code>@savedSearches</code>, <code>@activeSavedSearchId</code>, <code>@onSavedSearchChange</code>, <code>@onApply</code>, <code>@onSave</code> and <code>@aclContext=\\"project.read\\"</code>. No <code>@baseQuery</code>. Keep the save dialog in the page.</li><li><code>routes/app/projects/index.js</code>: load the schema with <code>query-schema</code> <code>load('Project')</code> next to the saved searches (~l.178) and set <code>controller.querySchema</code>.</li><li><code>controllers/app/projects/index.js</code>:<ul><li>Remove the <code>metadata.filters</code> array (l.29-56).</li><li>Add <code>ezSavedSearches</code> (query from <code>searchquery</code>) and <code>selectSavedSearch(search|null)</code>.</li><li>Add a save path that saves the query from <code>@onSave</code> without <code>searchByRules</code>.</li><li>Clear goes through <code>applyQuery('')</code> (<code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>, added by 4305).</li></ul></li><li>Check that <code>views.Project.search</code> covers today's filters (<code>Project.name</code>, <code>Project.shortCode</code>, <code>Project.status</code> with <code>views.app.project.lists.status</code>, <code>manager.name</code> as a user field) and fix the metadata, not code, if not.</li><li><code>mirage/route-handlers/project.js</code>: record the last <code>query</code> param in the scenario context, as 4305 did for issues.</li><li>Tests:<ul><li>Update <code>tests/acceptance/project/search-project-from-list.feature</code> and its steps.</li><li>New <code>tests/acceptance/project/ez-search-project-list.feature</code> + steps:<ol><li>Type and run a query: the formatted query shows and is sent.</li><li>Accept a field suggestion with the keyboard.</li><li>Edit in the builder and see the bar update.</li><li>Load a saved search: the bar shows it and <code>searchId</code> is in the URL.</li><li>An error is shown and nothing is sent.</li></ol></li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios pass.</li><li>The existing project list tests (render, mass update, select and navigate) pass.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px next to the Issue list.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> removing the plugin (separate issue), the generic admin list.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-metadata", "aprom-4304", "aprom-4305"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "module-list-search", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Generic module list: ezSearch from the module's search metadata", "description": "<p>The generic admin list (route <code>app.module</code>, path <code>/app/:module</code>, <code>controllers/app/module.js</code> + <code>templates/app/module.hbs</code>) has a jQuery QueryBuilder panel (<code>#builder</code>) that reads <code>views.&lt;Module&gt;.filters</code>. No module declares that key, so the panel can't work today. Under the metadata-driven list-view architecture (<code>docs/architecture/metadata-views/architecture.md</code>, from the search-metadata issue), a list view gets search by declaring <code>views.&lt;Module&gt;.search</code>. This list should do exactly that: show <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> when the module declares search metadata, and no search when it doesn't. No per-module code.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>templates/app/module.hbs</code> ~l.19-50: replace the <code>text-field</code> search (<code>populateQuery</code>/<code>openFilters</code>/<code>filter</code>), the <code>toggleFilters</code> button and the <code>.list-view-filters</code> row with <code>#builder</code> with <code>&lt;EzSearch @schema={{this.querySchema}} @query={{this.query}} @onApply={{this.applyQuery}} /&gt;</code>, rendered only when <code>querySchema</code> is set. Generic lists have no saved searches and no Save Search for now.</li><li><code>routes/app/module.js</code> <code>setupController</code>: load <code>query-schema</code> <code>load(this.module)</code> and set <code>controller.querySchema</code> (null when the module has no search metadata). Check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after the await if it is done in the controller.</li><li><code>controllers/app/module.js</code>:<ul><li>Add <code>applyQuery(query)</code>: set <code>queryString</code>, reset <code>page</code>, then <code>navigate</code>.</li><li>Remove <code>searchByRules</code>, <code>setupQuery</code>, <code>openFilters</code>, <code>toggleFilters</code>, <code>populateQuery</code> and the imports of the old <code>utils/query/parser</code> and <code>utils/query/builder</code>.</li><li><code>?query=</code> keeps working through <code>navigate</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Acceptance test (<code>tests/acceptance/module/</code> + steps) for a module list that resolves to <code>app.module</code>:<ul><li>With search metadata: the bar shows, a typed query is applied and sent, and an error sends nothing.</li><li>Without search metadata: no search is rendered and the list still pages.</li></ul>If no real module reaches <code>app.module</code> with Mirage, use a test-only metadata fixture and say so in the PR. Don't add search metadata to real modules just for the test.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The tests above pass.</li><li>No references to <code>utils/query/builder</code>, <code>utils/query/parser</code>, <code>#builder</code> or a <code>filters</code> view key remain in the module list.</li><li>The other lists are unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> declaring search metadata for more modules, saved searches on generic lists, removing the plugin (separate issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-metadata"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "remove-jquery-qb", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Remove jQuery QueryBuilder and the old query utils", "description": "<p>ezSearch now serves the Issue list (aprom-4305), the Project list and the generic module list, all driven by search metadata. Nothing uses jQuery QueryBuilder any more, so remove it with its helpers, the old search code and its styles.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>package.json</code>: remove <code>jQuery-QueryBuilder</code> (l.107) and <code>jquery-extendext</code> (l.105), and update the lockfile. <code>ember-cli-build.js</code>: remove both <code>app.import</code> lines (l.45-46). Keep <code>jquery</code> itself.</li><li>Delete <code>app/utils/query/builder.js</code>, the old <code>app/utils/query/parser.js</code> (not ezSearch's <code>parse.js</code>), <code>app/utils/metadata/querybuilder-operators.js</code> and <code>app/components/query-builder.js</code> (and its template if there is one).</li><li><code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>:<ul><li>Remove the imports of the old builder and parser.</li><li>Remove <code>searchByRules</code>, <code>openFilters</code>, the <code>_searchRulesHandler</code> property (~l.147-152) and the global <code>keydown</code> listener it adds.</li><li>Remove <code>queryBuilder.clear()</code> from <code>clearSearch</code>, or drop <code>clearSearch</code> if no template uses it.</li><li>Remove the <code>send('searchByRules')</code> in <code>showSaveSearchDialog</code>, or drop that action if unused.</li></ul>Keep <code>applyQuery</code>, <code>applySearch</code>, <code>toggleSearch</code> and <code>isSearchActive</code> if the lists still use them.</li><li>Styles: remove the \\"jQuery query Builder custom styles\\" block in <code>app/styles/modules/document.scss</code> (~l.456-466) and the <code>.query-builder</code> rules in <code>app/styles/modules/module.scss</code> (~l.11-46). Remove <code>.dropToggle</code> (<code>document.scss</code> ~l.360) only if nothing uses it any more. Keep the <code>.search</code> block (<code>document.scss</code> ~l.329): the ezSearch toolbar uses it.</li><li>Search the app for any remaining reference (<code>queryBuilder</code>, <code>query-builder</code>, <code>getRules</code>, <code>metadata.filters</code>, <code>.list-view-filters</code>) and remove it.</li><li>Update <code>docs/architecture/metadata-views/architecture.md</code> if it still mentions the old plugin. The generated YUIDoc in <code>docs/</code> is left as is.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The app builds without the two packages.</li><li>No source references to the plugin or the deleted files remain.</li><li>The full test suite passes, including the Issue, Project and generic list ezSearch acceptance tests.</li><li>Issue list, Project list and a generic module list checked in the browser: no console errors.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> board, Gantt and calendar search (later phase), regenerating YUIDoc.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ez-project-list", "module-list-search"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 12:39:13	2026-11-07 12:48:39	f
f3acd5f76ae5-7860-7dee-53f92575e2d5	6471d1b46ae5-10d2-613b-e3f2313332d0	6	{"summary": "Four Prometheus issues in aga-v1 for the idea page. screens-parse fixes the root cause of invisible idea screens: Ideamessage screens and steps arrive from Gaia as JSON text and are never parsed, so neither the thread nor the plan box finds them. screen-preview (after screens-parse) shows each screen as its full image through the download token, because GET /upload/{id} only returns fileThumbnail as a boolean. plan-review adds a review mode that gives the plan the wide column, and browser-collapse lets the ideas list collapse; both are independent.", "issues": [{"key": "screens-parse", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea messages: parse the screens and steps JSON from Gaia so screens show in the thread and plan box", "description": "<p>Agent Nestor's screens never appear on the idea page. The plan box shows only a static <code>fa-picture-o</code> icon and the screen key (the \\"missing\\" branch in <code>components/idea/plan-box.hbs</code> ~l.29), and the conversation shows nothing. Engineers can't see a mockup while planning; they only see it once the issues are created (attachments on created issues work).</p><p>Cause: Gaia stores <code>Ideamessage.screens</code> and <code>Ideamessage.steps</code> as JSON <strong>text</strong> (<code>gaia/core/mvc/models/behaviors/ideaScreensBehavior.php</code> encodes arrays; fields are <code>type text</code>) and returns them as strings. <code>models/ideamessage.js</code> declares <code>@attr screens</code> and <code>@attr steps</code> with no transform, so they stay strings. <code>components/idea/message-screens.js</code>, <code>plan-box.js</code> <code>screens</code> and <code>message-item.js</code> <code>steps</code> all require <code>Array.isArray</code> and get nothing. The Mirage factory (<code>mirage/factories/ideamessage.js</code>) returns arrays, which hid it.</p><ul><li>Start with a failing test: make the Mirage <code>ideamessage</code> factory (and any fixtures) return <code>screens</code>/<code>steps</code> as JSON strings, as Gaia does.</li><li>Declare both as <code>@attr('json')</code> (existing <code>transforms/json.js</code>). If the transform's lack of a <code>serialize</code> breaks saving a user message, add a <code>serialize</code> that sends arrays as JSON text (Gaia's behaviour accepts both). Make sure null, empty string and invalid JSON give an empty list, not an error.</li><li>No component changes beyond what the parsed arrays need. <code>Idea::MessageScreens</code> then renders each screen and the plan box finds it by key and version, so title and version show and the click opens it (existing <code>open</code>).</li><li>Tests: a unit test for the model/transform (string, array, null, invalid). The acceptance case in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/</code> shows a Nestor message with a screen as a clickable entry in the thread and in the plan box, and its steps listed.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on an idea whose Nestor messages carry screens, each screen appears as a clickable entry with its title and version, in the message and in the plan box, and Nestor's steps show again. This works with the real Gaia response, not just Mirage.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the thumbnail image itself (separate issue), Gaia changes, attachments on created issues (they work).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "screen-preview", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea screens: show the full image instead of the boolean fileThumbnail", "description": "<p>Once the screens of idea messages are parsed (previous issue), <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code> (<code>components/idea/message-screen.{hbs,js}</code>, used in the thread and the plan box) still can't show an image. It takes the <code>img src</code> from <code>services/upload-preview.js</code> <code>thumbnail()</code>, which reads <code>upload.fileThumbnail</code> from <code>findRecord('upload', id)</code>. For <code>GET /upload/{id}</code> Gaia returns that field as the stored <strong>boolean</strong>. Only the POST response and Gaia's <code>FilethumbComponent</code> (for files <code>included</code> with a parent such as an issue) swap in base64 data. The image is broken, and even a real thumbnail would be a 198x132 crop, too small for a mockup.</p><ul><li>Show each screen as its full image, scaled to the available width, using <code>uploadPreview.previewUrl(uploadId)</code> (download token + <code>/preview/get/&lt;token&gt;</code>). <code>modifiers/render-markdown.js</code> already shows pasted images this way. Show the title and version (<code>views.app.idea.conversation.screenVersion</code>) under it, and the <code>fa-picture-o</code> placeholder while it loads or if it fails.</li><li>Keep the click that opens the full-size image in a new tab (existing <code>open</code>).</li><li>Remove the <code>thumbnail()</code> use, and the method if nothing else calls it. Don't treat <code>fileThumbnail</code> as an address in this component.</li><li>Sizes in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code>: in a message the screen spans the message width (<code>.idea-message-screen</code> is a fixed 160px today). In the plan box screen row (<code>plan-box.hbs</code> ~l.23) keep a compact size that fits the side column.</li><li>Guard the async load after destroy (check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after the await).</li><li>Tests: integration test for <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code>. With a Mirage upload whose <code>fileThumbnail</code> is <code>true</code>, it renders an <code>img</code> with the preview address. A failed token shows the placeholder.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the idea page every screen in Nestor's messages and in the plan box shows its image as soon as the page loads, before any plan is approved. A click opens it full size.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> an in-app lightbox, Gaia thumbnail changes, issue Files box thumbnails.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["screens-parse"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "plan-review", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea page: plan review mode with the plan in the wide column", "description": "<p>The idea page (<code>templates/app/project/idea/page.hbs</code>) puts the conversation in <code>col-md-8</code> and the Plan, Created Issues and Summary boxes in <code>col-md-4</code>. The page itself sits in the <code>col-md-9</code> beside the ideas browser. That suits chatting, but reviewing a plan with several issues in about a quarter of the screen is hard. Engineers need to switch to a layout that favours the plan.</p><ul><li>Add a box-tool button to the Plan box header (<code>components/idea/plan-box.hbs</code>, <code>btn btn-box-tool</code>, <code>fa-expand</code> / <code>fa-compress</code>, title from <code>translations/en-us.json</code>) that toggles review mode through an action passed from the page.</li><li>Review mode: the side column (Plan, Created Issues, Summary) becomes <code>col-md-8</code> and the conversation <code>col-md-4</code>, with the plan column first, so the plan is on the left. The composer stays usable. Normal mode is today's layout.</li><li>State: query param <code>view=plan</code> on the page route (<code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>), so the mode survives reload and can be linked. Opening another idea keeps the mode. Leaving the ideas route resets it.</li><li>The plan's screen row and issue rows use the extra width (screens larger than in the side column). No new colours or components: reuse the plan box markup and classes in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code>.</li><li>Tests: acceptance cases in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-plan.feature</code>: the button switches the columns, a reload with <code>?view=plan</code> opens in review mode, toggling back restores the layout.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> from any idea with a plan, one click gives the plan the wide column and the conversation the narrow one. Another click goes back. Approve and version tabs work in both modes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> collapsing the ideas browser (separate issue), resizable columns.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "browser-collapse", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: collapse the ideas browser so the idea page uses the full width", "description": "<p>The ideas browser takes <code>col-md-3</code> of the ideas layout (<code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>), so an open idea (conversation and plan) only gets <code>col-md-9</code>. Engineers working in one idea want the full width for the conversation and the plan.</p><ul><li>Add a collapse button to the browser box header (<code>box-tools</code>, <code>btn btn-box-tool</code>, <code>fa-angle-double-left</code>, title in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>) next to the \\"New\\" button.</li><li>Collapsed: the browser column is hidden and the outlet column becomes <code>col-md-12</code>. A small box-tool button (<code>fa-angle-double-right</code>) at the left of the outlet expands it again.</li><li>State: a tracked flag on <code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>, kept in <code>localStorage</code> so the choice survives reloads. Default expanded.</li><li>The New Idea page (create route) and the idea page both follow the flag.</li><li>Styles, if any, scoped under <code>.idea-wrapper</code> in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code>. Square edges, existing colours.</li><li>Tests: acceptance cases in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-browser.feature</code>: collapse hides the list and widens the content, expand restores it, the state survives a reload.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> one click hides the ideas list and the idea page spans the content area. One click brings it back. The choice is remembered.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> plan review mode (separate issue), mobile layout changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-31 09:42:11	2026-10-31 09:48:34	f
085992996ade-bc23-4a93-f01a27fcde9b	5b131d096adc-f42c-e36e-1693e76da846	3	{"summary": "Live notification.created events leave out relatedTo/relatedId, so a notification that arrives while the page is open can't be matched by its entity. Two features break for such notifications: aprom-4066 (viewing an issue marks its notifications read) and aprom-4118/4119 (a click opens the issue in the current screen's quick view). One Gaia fix adds both fields to the event; Prometheus and Hermes need no change.", "issues": [{"key": "live-notif-related", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Live events: include relatedTo and relatedId on notification.created", "description": "<p>agaia-4064 added <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code> to <code>system_notifications</code>, and Prometheus now relies on them. Viewing an issue marks its notifications read (aprom-4066), and clicking a notification opens its issue in the current screen's quick view (aprom-4118, aprom-4119). The live <code>notification.created</code> event doesn't send these two fields, so a notification that arrives through Hermes while the page is open has neither. It is then never marked read when its issue is viewed, and its click skips the quick view. After a page reload the REST load includes them and both features work, which is how the bug was spotted.</p><ul><li>Add <code>relatedTo</code> and <code>relatedId</code> to <code>NOTIFICATION_FIELDS</code> in <code>app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/NotificationLiveEvents.php</code> (they are copied into <code>changes</code> when set, like the other fields).</li><li>Extend <code>tests/api/controllers/components/events/LiveEventsComponentsTest.php</code> (<code>testNotificationLiveEventsPicksAllowlistedFields</code> or a new case): the posted <code>changes</code> contain both fields when the notification has them and leave them out when they are NULL. Write it first and watch it fail.</li><li>Update the notification row in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/architecture.md</code> if it lists the payload fields.</li></ul><p><strong>Contract:</strong> two extra keys in the existing <code>changes</code> of <code>notification.created</code>. The event name is unchanged, so Hermes needs no change. Prometheus <code>services/notifications.js</code> <code>onNotificationCreated</code> already pushes every key of <code>changes</code> onto the <code>systemnotification</code> record, whose model has both attributes.</p><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A <code>notification.created</code> envelope for an issue, comment or time-log notification carries <code>relatedTo: issue</code> and the issue id in <code>changes</code>. Milestone and membership notifications carry their own values.</li><li>Manual check in the running app: with an issue's notification arriving live (no reload), opening that issue marks it read and rings the bell, and clicking it on the task board opens the board's quick view.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> backfilling old rows (agaia-4117), and any other notification field.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-25 17:31:52	2026-10-25 17:34:32	f
14669e826aec-f3eb-ed75-eade1a60f368	ff0998196aec-c6f1-ed75-2f407967e79a	2	{"summary": "One Gaia issue: bake docker/php/conf.d/custom.ini (memory_limit = 512M) into the deployed image (docker/dev/Dockerfile) and the local image (Dockerfile). Today it only reaches containers through docker-compose bind mounts, so the deployed Gaia runs with PHP's default memory limit.", "issues": [{"key": "php-ini-in-images", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docker: copy custom.ini (memory_limit 512M) into the Gaia images", "description": "<p><code>docker/php/conf.d/custom.ini</code> sets <code>memory_limit = 512M</code>, but only the bind mounts in <code>docker-compose.yaml</code> apply it. Neither Dockerfile copies it, so the deployed image built from <code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code> runs with the base image's default memory limit.</p><ul><li><code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code>: add <code>COPY ./docker/php/conf.d/custom.ini /usr/local/etc/php/conf.d/zz-custom.ini</code> next to the existing <code>zz-opcache.ini</code> copy.</li><li><code>Dockerfile</code> (local build): add the same <code>COPY</code> so the image is correct without compose too. The existing compose mounts stay as they are.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An image built from <code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code> reports <code>memory_limit =&gt; 512M</code> from <code>docker run --rm &lt;image&gt; php -i | grep memory_limit</code>, with no volumes mounted.</li><li>The same holds for an image built from <code>Dockerfile</code>.</li><li>The local compose stack still starts and reports 512M.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing the base image in <code>docker-images/gaia</code>, other ini settings and the compose mounts.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-05 07:28:20	2026-11-05 07:29:47	f
97653d476ae0-6045-29af-a02b312dc90b	afa54b056ada-2ec4-1fa7-d7b41cc59b57	3	{"summary": "Two independent Prometheus bug fixes on the task board, which can go in parallel. (1) The compact Issue::AssigneeSelect on cards (aprom-4102) never opens because it stops the click before Bootstrap's document-level dropdown handler sees it. Remove that, add a caret, and make sure the menu isn't clipped. (2) The quick view sometimes doesn't open on click because Sortable's fallback drag starts after a 1px move and then swallows the click. Set fallbackTolerance (plus a touch delay) in the lane Sortable options, and fix the dead disableSortable option on the way.", "issues": [{"key": "card-assignee-menu-fix", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task board: card assignee dropdown never opens (click stopped before Bootstrap sees it)", "description": "<p>aprom-4102 added the shared <code>Issue::AssigneeSelect</code> component and uses it in compact form on task board cards (<code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code> ~l.126). On the board, clicking a card's assignee avatar does nothing: no menu opens and nothing shows that the avatar is clickable. The issue detail view, which uses the non-compact form, works.</p><p><strong>Cause</strong>: the wrapper <code>.dropdown</code> in <code>components/issue/assignee-select.hbs</code> has <code>{{on \\"click\\" this.stopPropagation}}</code>. When <code>@compact</code> is set, <code>stopPropagation</code> (<code>assignee-select.js</code> ~l.40) stops the event. Bootstrap 3 opens dropdowns from one delegated <code>click.bs.dropdown.data-api</code> listener on <code>document</code>, so the click from <code>[data-toggle=\\"dropdown\\"]</code> never gets there. Stopping the click isn't needed: the card has no click handler (the quick view opens only from the title <code>LinkTo</code>), and Sortable already ignores the dropdown (<code>modifiers/initialize-sortable.js</code> ~l.582, <code>filter: '[data-issue-assignee-dropdown]'</code>, <code>preventOnFilter: false</code>).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Start with a test that fails: an acceptance scenario on the board (Mirage) that clicks the avatar trigger on a card (<code>[data-issue-assignee-toggle]</code>), checks that the dropdown gets the <code>open</code> class and that its menu is visible, then picks a member and checks the new avatar.</li><li>In <code>assignee-select.hbs</code>, remove the <code>click</code> handler from the wrapper. Keep the <code>mousedown</code> one only if a test shows it's needed to stop a drag; otherwise remove it and the <code>stopPropagation</code> action.</li><li>Compact trigger: add a small <code>fa fa-caret-down</code> after the avatar so it reads as a dropdown, the same way the detail view does. Size and space it in the <code>&amp;.assignee-select-compact</code> block in <code>styles/modules/issue.scss</code> (~l.639) so the card footer layout stays unchanged.</li><li>Check in the running app that the menu is fully visible on the last card of a lane. The lane body (<code>.milestone.box-body</code>, <code>styles/modules/board.scss</code> ~l.69) has <code>overflow-x: auto</code>, which also clips vertically. If the menu is cut off, open it upward on cards (Bootstrap's <code>dropup</code> on the compact wrapper). Don't change the lane's overflow or z-index.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>On the task board, clicking a card's assignee avatar (or caret) opens the member menu. Choosing a member saves the issue and updates the avatar, with the existing toasts.</li><li>Clicking the avatar doesn't open the quick view. Dragging the card by its body still works, before and after a reassignment.</li><li>The menu is fully visible for the first and last card of a lane.</li><li>The issue detail view's assignee dropdown is unchanged. Existing tests and lint pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: other quick edits on the card; the drag tolerance (separate issue); live updates from other users (aprom-3978).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}, {"key": "board-drag-tolerance", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task board: clicking a card title sometimes doesn't open the quick view (drag starts on a 1px move)", "description": "<p>On the task board, clicking a card's subject sometimes doesn't open the quick view. A perfectly still click works; a click where the mouse or trackpad moves by a pixel doesn't.</p><p><strong>Cause</strong>: the board passes <code>@forceFallback={{true}}</code> (<code>templates/app/project/board.hbs</code> l.15), so SortableJS does its own mouse-event dragging instead of native HTML5 drag. The lane options in <code>modifiers/initialize-sortable.js</code> <code>getSortableOptions()</code> (~l.571, used by <code>_attachSortableToLanes</code>) set no <code>fallbackTolerance</code>, and Sortable's default is <code>0</code>. Its tolerance check (<code>if (fallbackTolerance &amp;&amp; …)</code>) is then skipped, so any <code>mousemove</code> after <code>mousedown</code> starts a drag. After a fallback drag, Sortable sets <code>ignoreNextClick</code> and swallows the next <code>click</code> in a document capture listener. The <code>{{on \\"click\\" (fn @selectIssue issue)}}</code> on the title <code>LinkTo</code> (<code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code> ~l.62) then never runs. Sortable's default <code>ignore: 'a, img'</code> applies only to native drag, so it doesn't help here. Confirm this against the installed SortableJS version (<code>package.json</code>: <code>^1.14.0</code>) before changing anything.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In <code>getSortableOptions()</code>, add <code>fallbackTolerance: 5</code> and, for touch, <code>delay: 150</code> with <code>delayOnTouchOnly: true</code>. Put the values in named constants with a YUIDoc comment explaining why. Don't add the title link to <code>filter</code>: the subject is most of the card and must still start a drag.</li><li>Fix the <code>disableSortable</code> getter (~l.106), which returns <code>this.args.named</code> instead of <code>this.args.named.disableSortable</code>. Pass it to Sortable as <code>disabled</code> (the real option name) instead of <code>disableSortable</code>, in <code>getSortableOptions()</code> and in the two milestone-tab instances (~l.484, ~l.547). The board is the only caller and passes <code>false</code>, so behaviour stays the same.</li><li>Leave the milestone-tab instances' other options alone: they only receive dropped cards.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit test (modifier) asserting that the lane options include <code>fallbackTolerance</code> &gt; 0, <code>delayOnTouchOnly: true</code> and <code>disabled: false</code> when the board passes <code>@disableSortable={{false}}</code>.</li><li>Manual check in the running app: clicking a card subject with a slight mouse movement opens the quick view every time; dragging a card between lanes and onto a milestone tab still works; the parent-issue link on a card still opens its quick view.</li><li>Existing board tests (<code>tests/unit/controllers/app/project/board*.js</code>, <code>tests/acceptance/taskboard/</code>, <code>tests/acceptance/live/board-live-updates.feature</code>) and lint pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: switching off <code>forceFallback</code>, the assignee dropdown on cards (separate issue) and other Sortable refactoring.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-27 16:13:11	2026-10-27 16:16:39	f
28d1c2c96ae0-008b-29af-23b229a048f1	5b131d096adc-f42c-e36e-1693e76da846	4	{"summary": "Fix the idea page's Created Issues box, which shows 'undefined-undefined' as grey text instead of linked issue refs. It reads the async ideaplanissue.issue belongsTo proxy with plain property access. The fix moves reading a link's created issue into one helper shared with the plan box, tests the box with real store records, and checks the version grouping against real data.", "issues": [{"key": "created-issues-proxy", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea page: Created Issues box shows 'undefined-undefined' instead of the issue refs", "description": "<p>The Created Issues box on the idea page lists every created issue as grey text <code>undefined-undefined</code>, with no link and no subject. <code>describe</code> in <code>app/components/idea/created-issues-box.js</code> reads <code>link.issue.projectShortcode</code>, <code>issueNumber</code>, <code>subject</code> and <code>projectId</code> as plain properties. <code>issue</code> on <code>app/models/ideaplanissue.js</code> is an async <code>belongsTo</code>, so <code>link.issue</code> is a promise proxy: those reads return <code>undefined</code>, <code>readable</code> is false, and because the proxy is always truthy the 'no loaded issue' fallback never runs. The plan box reads the same data through <code>get(link, 'issue.…')</code> (<code>plan-box.js</code> <code>createdIssues</code> ~l.192) and works.</p><ul><li>Add one small helper (for example in <code>app/utils/idea-plan-body.js</code>, next to <code>isProjectReadable</code>) that returns the created issue of an ideaplanissue: <code>link.belongsTo('issue').value()</code>, which gives the loaded record or <code>null</code> without triggering a fetch, plus a fallback for plain objects if the tests need one.</li><li>Use it in <code>created-issues-box.js</code> <code>describe</code>. With a record: label <code>&lt;shortcode&gt;-&lt;number&gt;</code>, the subject, and a link when <code>isProjectReadable</code> allows it. Without a record (Gaia left the issue out, for example because it isn't readable): the existing fallback, the plan item's key and subject as plain text.</li><li>Use the same helper in <code>plan-box.js</code> <code>createdIssues</code> instead of <code>get(link, 'issue.…')</code>, so both boxes read the issue the same way and a missing issue never triggers a <code>findRecord</code>.</li><li><strong>Check the version grouping:</strong> the engineer saw issues created from plans v2 and v3 listed under 'Plan v1' and 'Plan v3'. <code>groups</code> uses the plan whose id equals <code>link.ideaplanId</code>. On a real idea with several plan versions, check that the headings match the versions the issues were created from. If the box is wrong, fix it here. If the stored <code>ideaplanId</code>s are wrong (Talos records them), file an adt issue and mention it in the PR.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>On an idea with created issues, the box lists <code>aprom-4118</code>-style refs as links with their subjects, grouped under the plan version each was created from.</li><li>An issue that isn't loaded shows the plan item's key and subject as plain text, with no 'undefined'.</li><li>The integration tests in <code>tests/integration/components/idea/created-issues-box-test.js</code> (and the plan-box test if it uses plain objects) build real store records (<code>ideaplanissue</code> with a pushed <code>issue</code>, plus one without). The new test fails before the fix.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing what Gaia includes in <code>rels: 'issue'</code>, and any other change to the box's layout.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-27 16:19:52	2026-10-27 16:23:00	f
734325646af3-41f4-8178-59d90f28731c	00d17cb06af3-c415-1996-69951fb2ab5f	2	{"summary": "Stop the deprecation flood in the Prometheus test runs without new dependencies. One issue removes the app's only use of the deprecated assign from @ember/polyfills (the oauth2 authenticator). The other adds a deprecation handler to the test helper that hides only ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign for now, counts every deprecation by ID and prints one summary at the end of the run. The output stops carrying thousands of stack traces, the summary shows which IDs remain, and those IDs are handled one by one later. The two issues are independent. Upgrading the addons that raise the deprecations is left to the separate stack upgrade.", "issues": [{"key": "oauth2-object-assign", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "OAuth2 authenticator: use Object.assign instead of the deprecated assign from @ember/polyfills", "description": "<p><code>assign</code> from <code>@ember/polyfills</code> is deprecated in Ember 4 (ID <code>ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign</code>). The only use in <code>app/</code> is the OAuth2 authenticator. Removing it is part of cutting the deprecation noise in the test runs.</p><ul><li><code>app/authenticators/oauth2.js</code>: remove the <code>import { assign } from '@ember/polyfills'</code> (line 11) and replace <code>response = assign(response, { 'expires_at': expiresAt })</code> in <code>authenticate()</code> (~line 106) with <code>Object.assign</code>. The behaviour stays the same: the response object gets <code>expires_at</code>.</li><li>Extend <code>tests/unit/authenticators/oauth2-test.js</code> to check that <code>authenticate()</code> resolves with <code>expires_at</code> when the server returns <code>expires_in</code>, if that case isn't covered yet.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>grep -r \\"@ember/polyfills\\" app tests mirage</code> finds nothing; the oauth2 unit test and the sign-in acceptance feature pass; the full suite passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> deprecations raised by addons (handled in the test helper issue and the later stack upgrade); lodash <code>_.assign</code> in <code>adapters/application.js</code> (not deprecated).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "test-deprecation-handler", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Tests: hide the deprecate-assign deprecation and print one count per deprecation ID at the end of the run", "description": "<p>A full Prometheus test run writes about 18.7k deprecation stack traces: Ember's debug build sends each deprecation to <code>console.warn</code> with a stack, and testem captures all of them. That bloats the run log that <code>ai test</code>, Talos and CI read, and hides real failures. Most of them come from addons, not from <code>app/</code> code (the app's only <code>assign</code> from <code>@ember/polyfills</code> is in the oauth2 authenticator, which acceptance tests skip by logging in with <code>authenticateSession</code>). Fixing the addons belongs to a later stack upgrade. This issue hides one deprecation ID in tests and reports the rest, so the remaining IDs can be handled one by one later.</p><ul><li>In <code>tests/test-helper.js</code>, register a handler with <code>registerDeprecationHandler</code> from <code>@ember/debug</code>, before <code>start()</code>. Use no new dependency (not ember-cli-deprecation-workflow).</li><li>Keep the list of hidden deprecation IDs in a small test-support module (e.g. <code>tests/helpers/deprecations.js</code>). It holds only <code>ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign</code> for now; more IDs get added later, one at a time. For a hidden ID, count it and don't call <code>next</code>, so nothing is logged.</li><li>Count every deprecation by ID, hidden or not. Other IDs still go to <code>next</code>, so they log as before.</li><li>On <code>QUnit.done</code>, print one <code>console.log</code> line per ID with its count (e.g. <code>DEPRECATIONS ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign: 18734</code>), and print nothing when there were none.</li><li>Before the change, run the full suite and record in the PR the number of deprecation lines per ID and the log size. Record them again after the change.</li><li>Unit test for the counting and hiding logic in the helper module.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the full suite passes with the same number of tests; the run log has no stack traces for <code>ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign</code>; other deprecation IDs still log as before; the end-of-run summary lists the counts per ID; the PR shows the before and after numbers.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> hiding any deprecation ID other than <code>ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign</code>; upgrading the addons that raise the deprecations; making deprecations fail tests; hiding deprecations outside tests (dev and production builds are unchanged); ember-exam / parallel test runs.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-10 16:29:39	2026-11-10 16:33:53	f
3fe345456af4-3b69-e9a2-62d04c94ccfd	d98352c16af4-9ee0-e9a2-4dddf1b444ee	1	{"summary": "Prepares Gaia's move from PHP 7.x / Phalcon 4 to PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5 and makes failures easy to see. First, six issues that can run in parallel: a Dockerfile in the repo for the current and target images (env-image), the full PHPUnit suite in CI (ci-full-suite), a static compatibility scan with a sorted findings list (compat-scan), a migrate --dry-run with schema snapshots (migrate-dry-run), saving api-tester responses and comparing two runs (response-diff), and removing the committed SMTP password (smtp-secret). Then a deprecation report (after ci-full-suite), fixes that still run on PHP 7.4 (after compat-scan), and removing the old Elasticsearch code. dual-stack-boot makes the same code start on Phalcon 4 and 5, and next-stack-ci adds a non-blocking CI job on the target stack that reports PHPUnit, schema, api-tester, deprecation and response differences in one summary. Fixing what that job reports and switching the default stack are planned from its first report.", "issues": [{"key": "env-image", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Runtime image: Dockerfile in the repo for the current and the target PHP/Phalcon stack", "description": "<p>Gaia, its CI and the test containers build on <code>rananoman/gaia:env-dev</code>, but no repo contains the recipe for that image, so we can't rebuild it or build a copy with other versions. This issue puts the recipe in the repo, with the PHP and Phalcon versions as build arguments, as the first step of the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5 upgrade.</p><ul><li>Inspect the current image (<code>php -v</code>, <code>php --ri phalcon</code>, <code>php -m</code>, <code>/etc/os-release</code>, the conf.d ini files) and record the exact versions and extensions in <code>docker/env/README.md</code>.</li><li><code>docker/env/Dockerfile</code> with build args <code>PHP_VERSION</code> and <code>PHALCON_VERSION</code>. It installs what Gaia needs today: pdo_pgsql, imagick, zip, mbstring, curl, xml, psr (only for Phalcon 4), xdebug, xhprof, composer, Apache with mod_rewrite.</li><li>Two documented targets: <strong>current</strong> rebuilds today's image (same PHP 7.x and Phalcon 4.x), and <strong>next</strong> uses PHP 8.5.x with a Phalcon 5 release that supports it. The engineer suggested Phalcon 5.23.0: check the Phalcon release notes / PECL that it exists and supports PHP 8.5, otherwise take the newest 5.x that does, and record the choice and why in the README. Check that xdebug, xhprof and imagick build on 8.5; if one doesn't, note it.</li><li>A small build script (<code>docker/env/build.sh</code>) that tags <code>gaia-env:current</code> and <code>gaia-env:next</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> both images build. With <code>gaia/Dockerfile</code> pointed at <code>gaia-env:current</code> locally, PHPUnit and the api-tester give the same results as with env-dev. In <code>gaia-env:next</code>, <code>php -m</code> lists phalcon and the versions match the README.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> switching the Dockerfiles, compose or CI to these images, and publishing to a registry (the reviewer publishes the tags).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ci-full-suite", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "CI: run the whole PHPUnit suite and modernise phpunit.xml", "description": "<p>CI runs only <code>tests/libraries/security</code>, <code>utils</code>, <code>libraries/tools</code> and <code>tests/tools</code>. The tests in <code>models/</code>, <code>foundation/</code>, <code>api/</code>, <code>libraries/workflows</code>, <code>libraries/query</code> and <code>libraries/authorization</code> never run in CI. Before the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5 upgrade we need the whole suite green on today's stack, so that a failure on the new stack means something.</p><ul><li><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code>: run the whole suite (<code>tests/phpunit.xml</code>), excluding <code>tests/tools/gaia-dev/fixtures</code>. Write a JUnit report and upload it as an artifact.</li><li>Move <code>tests/phpunit.xml</code> to the PHPUnit 9.6 schema: <code>whitelist</code> becomes <code>coverage</code>, and <code>syntaxCheck</code> and other removed attributes go.</li><li>Fix tests that fail because of the test itself. A failure that reveals a product bug: create a new issue for it, put the test in a <code>quarantine</code> group with that issue number, and exclude the group in CI.</li><li>Add the image name to the vendor cache key (today it is <code>hashFiles('composer.json')</code> only), so a different PHP version never reuses another version's vendor folder.</li><li>Each test file must still pass when run alone.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> CI runs every test folder and is green on the current image. Quarantined tests are listed in the PR with their issue numbers.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> upgrading PHPUnit past 9.6, and fixing the product bugs found.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "compat-scan", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Static PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5 compatibility scan and sorted findings list", "description": "<p>For the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5 upgrade we need a list of what has to change before running anything on the new stack. Add the tools and do a one-time sort of the results. This issue makes no code fixes.</p><ul><li>Dev dependencies: <code>phpcompatibility/php-compatibility</code> (with <code>squizlabs/php_codesniffer</code>) and <code>rector/rector</code>.</li><li><code>phpcs-compat.xml</code>: testVersion 7.4 to 8.5 over <code>app</code>, <code>core</code>, <code>public</code>, <code>cli.php</code>, <code>tools</code> and <code>tests</code>, excluding vendor and <code>tests/tools/gaia-dev/fixtures</code>. If the PHPCompatibility release doesn't know 8.4/8.5 yet, say so in the doc and list the 8.4/8.5 deprecations to check by hand.</li><li><code>rector.php</code>, dry run only: the PHP 8.x sets plus a <code>RenameClassRector</code> map for the Phalcon 5 renames this codebase uses. Known so far: <code>Phalcon\\\\Loader</code>, <code>Phalcon\\\\Logger</code>, <code>Phalcon\\\\Config</code>, <code>Phalcon\\\\Text</code>, <code>Phalcon\\\\Di</code>/<code>DI</code>, <code>Phalcon\\\\Session\\\\Adapter\\\\Files</code>.</li><li>composer scripts <code>compat:php</code> and <code>compat:phalcon</code>.</li><li><code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>: findings grouped (class renames, method signatures against Phalcon 5 interfaces, removed or changed functions, dynamic properties on models, null passed to built-in functions, Iterator/ArrayAccess return types, package versions), with file counts. Mark each item <strong>version-neutral</strong> (can be fixed now and still runs on PHP 7.4 / Phalcon 4) or <strong>new stack only</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> both composer scripts run in the current container and the doc reflects their output.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing anything, and adding the scan to CI.</p>", "type": "Research", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "migrate-dry-run", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migrations: --dry-run that prints the planned DDL, plus a schema snapshot script", "description": "<p><code>docker/dev/start.sh</code> runs <code>php cli.php migration migrate</code> every time Gaia starts, and <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> <code>syncExistingTable</code> drops columns that aren't in the metadata. If Phalcon 5 reads Postgres columns or types differently from Phalcon 4, the first start on the new stack could alter or drop columns. We need to see what migrate would do before it does it.</p><ul><li><code>php cli.php migration migrate --dry-run</code> (<code>core/tasks/MigrationTask.php</code>) prints every CREATE, ALTER, DROP, index and function statement that <code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> and the Postgres driver (<code>syncExistingTable</code>, <code>syncIndexes</code>, <code>syncMultiColumnIndex</code>, <code>migrateFunctions</code>) would run, one per line with its table, and runs none of them. Exit code 0 when nothing is planned, a separate non-zero code when changes are planned, and the usual failure code on errors.</li><li>Put the switch between running and collecting statements in the migration driver, not in the task.</li><li><code>tools/upgrade/schema-snapshot.sh</code>: <code>pg_dump --schema-only</code> of a given database, with owners, comments and ordering noise removed, so two snapshots can be diffed.</li><li>PHPUnit tests for the dry run with a fake database adapter: planned statements are collected and nothing is executed.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a freshly migrated local database, <code>--dry-run</code> plans nothing. After removing a field from a model's metadata, it lists the DROP without running it. Two snapshots of the same database diff clean.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing what migrate does, and changing <code>start.sh</code>.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "response-diff", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "api-tester: save response bodies and compare two runs", "description": "<p>The silent risk in the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5 upgrade is responses that still pass the api-tester checks but have changed shape: <code>1</code> vs <code>\\\\u00221\\\\u0022</code>, null vs empty string, float precision, missing keys, different error text. Prometheus reads these responses. We need to compare the same catalog run on two stacks.</p><ul><li><code>tools/api-tester</code>: an opt-in flag (<code>--record-bodies</code>) that writes each case's status and JSON body into the report.</li><li><code>tools/api-tester/bin/compare-reports.php a.json b.json</code>: matches cases by id and reports differences in status, keys, value types and values. It ignores runtime ids/GUIDs, timestamps and tokens through a documented ignore list, prints a grouped summary (per endpoint, per kind of difference), and exits non-zero when there are differences.</li><li>The comparer's logic sits in its own class with unit tests; the bin script only parses arguments and prints.</li><li>Document the flag and the tool in the api-tester README.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two recorded runs of the same stack compare clean (no flaky differences), and a deliberately changed value type in one report is reported.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> wiring it into CI (next-stack-ci does that).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "smtp-secret", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Remove the committed SMTP password from docker-compose.yaml", "description": "<p><code>docker-compose.yaml</code> (gaia service, the <code>SMTP_USERNAME</code>/<code>SMTP_PASSWORD</code> lines) contains a real Gmail account and app password. House rules forbid secrets in compose files.</p><ul><li>Read both values from the environment (<code>${SMTP_USERNAME:-}</code>, <code>${SMTP_PASSWORD:-}</code>), supplied by a git-ignored <code>.env</code>.</li><li>Add <code>.env.example</code> with empty placeholders and make sure <code>.env</code> is git-ignored.</li><li>Say in the PR that the password is still in git history and must be rotated by its owner. Rotating it is a manual step outside this PR.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> no credentials in tracked files; gaia-dev still sends mail when <code>.env</code> is filled in.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> rewriting git history.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "deprecation-log", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Collect PHP deprecations and warnings from test runs into a grouped report", "description": "<p>PHP 8.x reports many upgrade problems only as E_DEPRECATED or E_WARNING (dynamic properties on models, null passed to built-in functions, return types). Today nobody sees them. We need them collected and grouped so the new-stack CI job can report them.</p><ul><li>A <code>docker/php/conf.d/diagnostics.ini</code> mounted only on the <code>gaia-test</code> services in <code>docker-compose.yaml</code>: <code>error_reporting=E_ALL</code>, <code>log_errors=On</code>, <code>display_errors=Off</code>, log to <code>logs/php-diagnostics.log</code>.</li><li>PHPUnit runs write deprecations and warnings to the same kind of log without failing the tests (PHPUnit 9's error handler otherwise swallows or converts them). Pick the mechanism, for example through <code>tests/phpunit.xml</code> or <code>tests/TestHelper.php</code>.</li><li><code>tools/upgrade/deprecations-report.php &lt;log&gt;...</code>: groups entries by message pattern and <code>file:line</code>, separates Gaia code from vendor, counts them, and prints markdown suitable for a CI job summary. Unit-test the grouping.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> running PHPUnit and the api-tester against gaia-test produces a log, and the report groups it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing the deprecations, and the CI wiring (next-stack-ci).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ci-full-suite"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "drop-elasticsearch", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Remove the legacy Elasticsearch indexing and its dependencies", "description": "<p><code>elasticsearch/elasticsearch ~6.0</code> and <code>monolog/monolog ~1.0</code> are used only by the legacy search indexing in <code>core/tasks/AdminTask.php</code> (from the Elasticsearch era; Gaia now searches through Postgres). Both are old majors that block the PHP 8.5 upgrade.</p><ul><li>Remove the Elasticsearch/Monolog commands and code from <code>AdminTask</code>, and any config used only by them.</li><li>Remove both packages from <code>composer.json</code>.</li><li>Leave the <code>fts</code> flags in model metadata and <code>app/metadata/FTS.php</code> alone unless they reference the removed code.</li><li>Update the gaia-dev graph and generated docs if they change.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>composer install</code> and CI are green, and no reference to <code>Elasticsearch\\\\</code> or <code>Monolog\\\\</code> remains outside vendor.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> new search features.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["compat-scan"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "php8-safe-code", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Version-neutral PHP 8 / Phalcon 5 fixes that still run on PHP 7.4 / Phalcon 4", "description": "<p>Fix the items that <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code> (from the compatibility scan) marks <strong>version-neutral</strong>, on today's stack, so the later switch is smaller.</p><ul><li><code>#[\\\\AllowDynamicProperties]</code> on the Gaia base model <code>core/mvc/models/Model.php</code>. Model columns are dynamic properties, and the attribute is inherited by every model; on PHP 7.4 the line is read as a comment.</li><li><code>#[\\\\ReturnTypeWillChange]</code> on the Iterator methods of <code>core/mvc/models/ResultStream.php</code>.</li><li>Replace <code>Phalcon\\\\Text</code>, which Phalcon 5 removed, in <code>FileattachmentComponent</code>, <code>TimeloggedComponent</code>, <code>ProjectActivitiesComponent</code> and <code>IssueactivitiesComponent</code> with plain PHP.</li><li>Fix further version-neutral items from the doc within the file budget, and tick them off in the doc. List what's left in the PR so it can become a follow-up issue.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> CI is green on the current image, and the scan reports fewer findings than before (numbers in the PR).</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> anything that only works on Phalcon 5 or PHP 8.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["compat-scan"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "dual-stack-boot", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Boot Gaia on both Phalcon 4 / PHP 7.4 and Phalcon 5 / PHP 8.5", "description": "<p>So that every PR shows what fails on the new stack, the same code must start on the current image and on <code>gaia-env:next</code> until the switch-over. The differences are almost all in startup code.</p><ul><li>One small class (e.g. <code>core/libs/compat/PhalconCompat.php</code>) that builds the Loader, Logger with its stream adapter, Config, Di and session adapter for the installed Phalcon major (<code>Phalcon\\\\Autoload\\\\Loader</code> with <code>setNamespaces</code> vs <code>Phalcon\\\\Loader</code>, <code>Phalcon\\\\Logger\\\\Logger</code>, <code>Phalcon\\\\Config\\\\Config</code>, <code>Phalcon\\\\Di\\\\Di</code>). Use it in <code>cli.php</code>, <code>public/index.php</code>, <code>app/config/loader.php</code>, <code>app/config/services.php</code>, <code>core/libs/config.php</code>, <code>core/libs/authorization/OAuthServer.php</code>, <code>tests/TestHelper.php</code> and <code>tests/UnitTestCase.php</code>. Nothing else branches on the version.</li><li><code>composer.json</code>: <code>php</code> becomes <code>^7.4 || ^8.5</code>. Drop the <code>ext-psr</code> requirement and the six unused <code>phalcon/incubator*</code> packages. Replace <code>phalcon/devtools</code> with <code>phalcon/migrations</code> (base of <code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code>), using a version range that resolves on both stacks. Move <code>bshaffer/oauth2-server-php</code> to a PHP 8-compatible 1.x. There is no lock file, so composer resolves per image.</li><li>Fix method-signature mismatches against Phalcon 5 interfaces (behaviours, the Migration subclass, controllers) in a form both versions accept.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the current image, CI is green as before. On <code>gaia-env:next</code>, Gaia starts, a login token request and one list read succeed, PHPUnit runs to completion (failures allowed), and <code>migration migrate --dry-run</code> runs. Other failures on next are listed in the PR, not fixed.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing all failures on the new stack, making next the default, and removing the compatibility class.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["env-image", "php8-safe-code", "drop-elasticsearch"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "The startup files and composer.json must change together for Gaia to start on either stack; splitting them leaves an app that can't start on one of them.", "screens": []}, {"key": "next-stack-ci", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "CI: non-blocking new-stack job that reports what fails", "description": "<p>The CI side of the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5 upgrade: on every PR, run the same checks on <code>gaia-env:next</code> and publish one summary of what differs from the current stack, so the remaining work is visible and shrinks PR by PR.</p><ul><li>A <code>next-stack</code> job in <code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code> on the published next image, with <code>continue-on-error: true</code> and a vendor cache keyed per image. It loads the baseline dump, runs <code>migrate --dry-run</code> then <code>migrate</code>, takes a schema snapshot, prepares <code>pr4m_test</code>, runs the full PHPUnit suite (JUnit), and runs the api-tester backend and acl modes with <code>--record-bodies</code>, collecting the PHP diagnostics log.</li><li>The current-stack job also records api-tester bodies and a schema snapshot, and uploads both as artifacts.</li><li>A compare step diffs the two schema snapshots and the two api-tester reports (<code>compare-reports.php</code>), runs <code>deprecations-report.php</code>, and writes one markdown summary to <code>$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY</code>: PHPUnit failures, migrate dry-run statements, schema diff, api-tester failures, response differences and deprecations, each with a count and its artifact.</li><li>The current-stack job stays the only blocking check.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a PR shows the new-stack summary; the summary is reproducible locally with the documented commands (add them to <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>).</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing what it reports, and making the job blocking.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["env-image", "ci-full-suite", "deprecation-log", "migrate-dry-run", "response-diff", "dual-stack-boot"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-11 15:09:51	2026-11-11 15:09:51	f
404fdf286ae1-3497-9a2f-bbf3a83bab0c	991f5df46ae1-2a68-9a2f-7cc8e5968877	1	{"summary": "Follow-ups from the PR comments of adt-4157's children (4158-4164), in milestone Parallel Runtimes. Workspace hardening (gaia_pack in the worktree, clear error for a branch already checked out, one base-branch table) comes first; shared auto-memory for per-issue runs builds on it, and so does the gc follow-up. In parallel: a thread-safe usage-limit pause refactor in the dispatcher, followed by the DependencyGate extraction and slot leasing only for Gaia runs; test-slot templates per seed key; one shared file-lock module; the p4m-stack skill using the dev-stack lock; and container runner hardening.", "issues": [{"key": "ws-hardening", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos workspaces: gaia_pack in the worktree, clear error for a checked-out branch, one base-branch table", "description": "<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups 4, 5 and 6 from the PR comment on adt-4158 (dev-tools#40). With per-issue workspaces (<code>talos/lib/workspaces.py</code>, <code>.runs/issue-N</code>), some code still assumes the main checkout.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/runner.py</code> <code>gaia_pack</code> (~l.238) runs <code>ai context</code> with <code>cwd=WORKSPACE</code> and no <code>P4M_WORKSPACE</code>, so the Gaia pack is built from the main checkout. Build it from the issue's workspace: pass the workspace folder and <code>workspaces.env(folder)</code>. If the workspace doesn't exist yet when the pack is built, reorder the calls so it is created first.</li><li>If <code>claude-issue-N</code> is checked out in the main checkout, git refuses the worktree and the run fails with git's raw message. Detect this case before creating the worktree. Hand the issue back with a clear comment (which folder holds the branch and how to free it) instead of a generic failure, and don't count it as an iteration.</li><li><code>workspaces.py</code> has its own base-branch table next to <code>ai/lib/common.py</code> <code>base_branch</code>. Use the <code>ai</code> one only.</li><li>Move the rule that pr4m (workspace root) issues get no worktree from the dispatcher into <code>workspaces.py</code>.</li><li>When an existing <code>claude-issue-N</code> branch is reused, log whether it is behind <code>origin/&lt;base&gt;</code>. Don't rebase it.</li><li>Add a regression test that <code>ai test</code> run with <code>P4M_WORKSPACE</code> passes the worktree as <code>--src</code> (<code>ai/lib/tests.py</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: a Gaia run's pack comes from the worktree; the checked-out-branch case gives a readable hand-back; there is one base-branch source; unit tests cover each case and pass on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: auto-memory (separate issue), gc.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Parallel Runtimes", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}, {"key": "ws-memory", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos workspaces: per-issue runs share the workspace's Claude auto-memory", "description": "<p>Part of adt-4157, follow-up 3 on adt-4158. Claude Code keys its per-project data, including auto-memory (<code>~/.claude/projects/&lt;cwd-slug&gt;/memory/MEMORY.md</code>), by the working folder. Talos runs Claude in <code>&lt;workspace&gt;/.runs/issue-N</code>, so every run starts with an empty memory. Agents lose the team's memories (for example: never <code>p4m db migrate</code> from Pr4M, no permission seeds, guard async after destroy) and write new ones into folders nobody reads again.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Find out how Claude Code resolves the memory folder: a setting, an environment variable, or the slug of the cwd. Pick the least fragile way for a run in <code>.runs/issue-N</code> to read and write the workspace's memory: a setting if one exists, otherwise a junction (Windows) or symlink (Linux) from the run's slug folder to the workspace's <code>memory</code> folder, created by <code>workspaces.py</code> along with the workspace.</li><li>Writes from parallel runs go to the same folder. Document how concurrent writes to <code>MEMORY.md</code> behave, and accept the risk or guard against it.</li><li>The container runner (<code>talos/lib/container.py</code>) mounts <code>~/.claude</code>. Make sure container runs get the same memory, or document why they don't.</li><li><code>talos gc</code> removes the link together with the workspace, never the shared memory itself.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: a run in <code>.runs/issue-N</code> loads the workspace's MEMORY.md (check it in a real session); a memory saved in a run shows up in the workspace's memory folder; unit tests cover link creation and removal on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: changes to what goes into memory.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ws-hardening"], "milestone": "Parallel Runtimes", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}, {"key": "pause-refactor", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos dispatcher: thread-safe usage-limit pause in its own class, priority read when a job is taken", "description": "<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups from adt-4160 (dev-tools#42) and adt-4162 #3 and #6 (dev-tools#44). The worker pool now runs several threads per agent. The usage-limit state (<code>_limit_streak</code>, <code>_paused_until</code> in <code>talos/lib/dispatcher.py</code>) is shared between those threads without a lock.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Extract a <code>UsagePause</code> class (own module under <code>talos/lib/</code>) that owns the streak, the pause deadline and the backoff, behind a lock.</li><li>Make the pause wait interruptible (<code>threading.Event.wait</code>), so stop and shutdown don't hang until the reset time.</li><li>Put a limited issue back at the front of the queue, not the back.</li><li>Return a named constant instead of the string <code>'limited'</code> from <code>handle</code>, and have <code>policy.read_outcome</code> return it, so the dispatcher no longer checks limits separately.</li><li>Move the tracker call out of <code>enqueue</code>: read the issue's priority when a worker takes the job, so priority changes made while the issue waits are respected.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests with several workers hitting a limit at once give one pause and one comment; stop interrupts a pause; a limited issue runs first after the reset; the queue order uses the priority at pop time. Behaviour with <code>maxParallel: 1</code> is unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: spend-based concurrency throttling.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Parallel Runtimes", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}, {"key": "dep-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: DependencyGate class, unreadable vs unmet dependencies, release off the Hermes thread", "description": "<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups 1-5 from the PR comment on adt-4161 (dev-tools#43).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Extract a <code>DependencyGate</code> class from <code>talos/lib/dispatcher.py</code> that owns the held set and the comment-once memory. Move <code>parse_dependencies</code> so that <code>policy</code> doesn't need to import the tracker.</li><li>Tell an unreadable dependency (Gaia error) apart from one that isn't done. Add a status-only lookup. If the status can't be read, retry later without posting the waiting comment.</li><li><code>release_held</code> runs on the Hermes listener thread and re-reads every held issue on each status event. Re-check only the held issues that depend on the changed issue, and do it on a worker, not the listener thread.</li><li>Read the done statuses from config, defaulting to <code>done</code>/<code>closed</code>, instead of a hard-coded constant.</li><li>Log when a held issue leaves the held set because it is no longer actionable.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests cover a Gaia error (no comment), targeted release, config statuses and the log line; the existing gating tests still pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: storing the held set in <code>talos.db</code> across restarts.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["pause-refactor"], "milestone": "Parallel Runtimes", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}, {"key": "slot-lease", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: lease test slots only for Gaia runs, none when maxParallel is 1, validate testSlots at load", "description": "<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups 1 and 2 from the PR comment on adt-4162 (dev-tools#44). Only Gaia suites use <code>pr4m_test</code> and slots (adt-4159), but the dispatcher leases a slot for every run, and with <code>maxParallel: 1</code> it still sets <code>P4M_TEST_SLOT=1</code> (<code>talos/lib/dispatcher.py</code> ~l.203). As a result, Prometheus, Hermes and dev-tools runs wait for a slot they never use.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Lease a slot only when the issue's repo is <code>gaia</code>. Other repos pass the caps without a slot.</li><li>With <code>maxParallel: 1</code>, lease no slot and set no <code>P4M_TEST_SLOT</code>, so <code>ai test</code> behaves as before adt-4159.</li><li>When <code>agent.json</code> is loaded (<code>talos/lib/registry.py</code>), check that <code>testSlots</code> is no larger than <code>TEST_SLOTS</code> in p4m.env (<code>installer/testslots.py</code> <code>slot_count</code>). Fail with a clear message if it is.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests show that a Prometheus run gets no slot, a Gaia run does, <code>maxParallel: 1</code> sets no slot, and a bad <code>testSlots</code> fails at load.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: changes to slot management in p4m.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["pause-refactor"], "milestone": "Parallel Runtimes", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}, {"key": "slot-template", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "p4m test slots: one template database per seed key, Slots.prepare and a separate psql gateway", "description": "<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups from adt-4159 (dev-tools#41). There is one template database, and it is rebuilt whenever the checkout under test has a different key (schema fingerprint + seed files). Baseline reruns in a slot use a different checkout, so two branches with different seeds keep rebuilding the template in turn.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Keep a template per key (e.g. <code>pr4m_test_tpl_&lt;short key&gt;</code>), keep at most a configurable number of them (default 3), and drop the least recently used. Clone a slot from the template that matches its checkout.</li><li>Move the orchestration (slot lock, template ensure, clone, container sync) into <code>Slots.prepare(slot, src, lock)</code> in <code>installer/testslots.py</code>.</li><li>Split the psql calls into their own gateway class (single responsibility).</li><li>Keep the lock order: slot lock, then template lock.</li><li><code>p4m test slots status</code> lists the templates with their keys.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: running a branch and its baseline one after another doesn't rebuild a template the second time; unit tests (fake docker/psql, as in <code>test_testslots.py</code>) cover per-key selection, eviction and lock order.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: slots for suites other than Gaia.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Parallel Runtimes", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}, {"key": "filelock", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "dev-tools: one cross-platform file-lock module (merge talos filelock and installer dblock)", "description": "<p>Part of adt-4157, follow-up 4 on adt-4162. adt-4162 added an OS file lock (msvcrt/fcntl) for <code>ai/state/timers.json</code> and the dev-stack lock. <code>installer/dblock</code> already does the same job for <code>pr4m_test</code> and the slots, so there are now two lock implementations.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Keep one module that every tool can import (pick the location that fits the runtime copy rules in <code>dev-tools/CLAUDE.md</code>). Move the callers of both onto it: timers, dev-stack, slot and template locks.</li><li>Keep the orphan-proof behaviour from adt-4143: a lock held by a dead process is released by the OS, with no stale-file takeover.</li><li>Add <code>Windows</code> and POSIX branches next to each other; tests use temp dirs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: one lock implementation remains; the existing tests for <code>ai</code>, <code>installer</code> and <code>talos</code> pass; a new test covers two processes contending for the lock.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: new locks.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["slot-template"], "milestone": "Parallel Runtimes", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}, {"key": "gc-followups", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "talos gc: move into lib with tests, run when an issue is done, remove container volumes", "description": "<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups from adt-4163 (dev-tools#45), adt-4164 (container volumes) and adt-4158 #1 (remove the workspace on close or merge).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Move the <code>gc_workspaces</code> orchestration from <code>talos.py</code> into <code>talos/lib/workspace_gc.py</code>, so the status lookup can be unit-tested. Move <code>pr_merged</code> out of the policy module.</li><li>Add tests for <code>pr_merged</code> (fake <code>gh</code>), the Gaia status lookup (including an error, which keeps the workspace) and the hook at <code>talos run</code> start.</li><li>Also collect one workspace when Talos sees its issue become done/closed/wont_fix (reconcile or a Hermes status event), not only at startup. Never touch a run in flight.</li><li>Remove the per-issue Claude volumes and leftover containers of finished issues created by the container runner (<code>talos/lib/container.py</code>), with the same rules.</li><li>Make <code>talos run --dry-run</code> report what gc would remove instead of skipping it.</li><li>Leave the shared memory link from the auto-memory issue alone, apart from removing the link itself.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests cover status resolution, the PR lookup, the done trigger and volume removal; <code>talos gc --dry-run</code> lists workspaces and volumes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: gc on remote Docker hosts.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ws-memory"], "milestone": "Parallel Runtimes", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}, {"key": "container-hardening", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos container runner: non-root image user, opt-in docker socket, design for keys on remote hosts", "description": "<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups from adt-4164 (dev-tools#47). The runner image runs as root, and the container always gets the docker socket, which gives root on the Docker host. Key files and the bind-mounted home must exist at the same path on a remote <code>dockerHost</code>.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Run the image as a non-root user, with a matching uid/gid for the bind-mounted <code>~/.claude</code> on Linux. Check that Windows Docker Desktop still works.</li><li>Mount the docker socket only when <code>agent.json</code> asks for it (e.g. <code>dockerSocket: true</code>). Without it, tests that need Docker fail with a clear message.</li><li>Key delivery to remote Docker hosts: write the options (docker secrets, env-only, a per-run volume fed by <code>docker cp</code>) and a recommendation into the Talos README. Don't build it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: a container run works end to end as non-root on the local Docker host, with and without the socket option; unit tests cover the docker arguments; the README covers the security notes and the remote-key options.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: implementing key delivery to remote hosts.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Parallel Runtimes", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-28 07:24:48	2026-10-28 07:28:57	f
747149a36ae2-fb26-79e3-15ac538f81b1	e53706516ae2-baab-7f50-a57680d4b6c5	1	{"summary": "Sprint planning on the Task Board, Prometheus only, with no Gaia changes. The first issue adds a Planning view next to the existing Board view (?view=planning): the backlog on the left, a box for each open milestone on the right, moving issues by drag or by a multi-select 'Move to', and estimate totals. The second issue adds calculated capacity to each sprint box, based on velocity from the last three completed sprints. There is no capacity field and no backlog rank field.", "issues": [{"key": "planning-view", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task Board: Planning view with backlog and milestone boxes side by side", "description": "<p>Sprint planning is hard today: the backlog and each milestone are separate tabs on the Task Board. The only way to plan is to drag one card at a time onto a tab header without seeing the sprint's contents. This issue adds a second view of the board where the backlog and every open milestone are visible together. It is Prometheus only, with no Gaia changes; see the attached <code>planning-view</code> screen.</p><ul><li><strong>Toggle:</strong> add a <code>view</code> query param (<code>board</code> default, <code>planning</code>) to <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code> / <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code>. Show <strong>Board | Planning</strong> as Bootstrap <code>nav nav-tabs</code> above the board, with the existing Saved Searches dropdown and search input on the right. Search and saved searches filter both views.</li><li><strong>Data:</strong> reuse what the route already loads (open milestones with status in_progress|planned, the backlog issues, and each issue's <code>estimated</code>/<code>spent</code> timelogs). Add no new requests.</li><li><strong>New component</strong> <code>AppUi::TaskBoard::Planning</code> (co-located in <code>app/components/app-ui/task-board/</code>). Layout: <code>.row</code> &gt; <code>col-md-5</code> + <code>col-md-7</code>.<ul><li>Left: a <code>box box-primary</code> \\"Backlog\\". The header shows the issue count and total estimated hours. Below it, a <code>table table-hover</code> of rows: checkbox, <code>AppUi::PriorityIcon</code>, linked number - subject, status label underneath, estimate on the right. Sort by priority (blocker → low), then issue number. Show the first 20 rows, with a \\"Show N more\\" link in the box footer.</li><li>Right: a <code>box box-info</code> per open milestone, in the board's order. Sprints and in_progress milestones come first and are expanded; other types are <code>box-default</code> and collapsed. Each header shows the milestone type, name, dates, a status label, the issue count and the total estimate. Rows match the backlog's, plus the assignee and without the checkbox. An empty milestone shows a drop hint row.</li><li>A <strong>New Sprint</strong> button under the boxes opens the existing create-milestone modal from <code>task-board.hbs</code>, preset to type sprint. Extract the modal if needed; don't duplicate it.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Moving issues:</strong><ul><li>Drag rows between the backlog and any milestone box, and between milestone boxes, with SortableJS (shared group). Reuse <code>modifiers/initialize-sortable.js</code> where it fits; otherwise add a small modifier for list rows. On drop, save only <code>milestoneId</code> (null for the backlog) through the controller's existing <code>updateIssue</code> path, so the board view, saving overlay and Hermes updates stay consistent.</li><li>Multi-select: ticking backlog rows enables <strong>Move N to ▾</strong> (a Bootstrap dropdown listing the open milestones), which saves each selected issue's milestone.</li><li>Totals update straight away. A failed save moves the row back and shows the error through the notifications service.</li></ul></li><li>Clicking an issue subject opens the existing quick view (<code>selectIssue</code>), as on the board.</li><li>All strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>. Styles are scoped under <code>.board-planning</code> in <code>app/styles/modules/board.scss</code>, with square edges and no new colours.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li><code>?view=planning</code> shows the backlog and all open milestones together; the Board tab returns to the current board unchanged.</li><li>Dragging or Move to changes the issue's milestone in Gaia, and the issue appears in the right lane when you switch back to Board.</li><li>Counts and estimate totals are correct after every move; search filters both columns.</li><li>Mirage handlers plus an integration test for the component and an acceptance test for the toggle and Move to.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> capacity (separate issue), ordering the backlog by hand (there is no rank field), closing a milestone from this view, and a mobile layout.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "screens": ["planning-view"]}, {"key": "sprint-capacity", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task Board Planning view: calculated sprint capacity from past velocity", "description": "<p>When planning a sprint, the Planning view (previous issue) shows each milestone's estimate total but not whether the team can deliver it. We don't want a capacity field in Gaia, so capacity is calculated from past velocity. See the attached <code>planning-view</code> screen: \\"31h of 38h capacity\\", the bar, and the info line in the box footer.</p><ul><li><strong>Calculation</strong> in a pure util <code>app/utils/board/sprint-capacity.js</code> (unit tested):<ul><li>Take the project's last 3 milestones with <code>milestoneType</code> sprint and <code>status</code> completed (status set by mark-as-complete, <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> ~l.990), latest <code>endDate</code> first.</li><li>For each one: velocity = the sum of estimated hours of its closed issues (statuses done, complete, closed, as in <code>getCompletedIssuesCount</code>, but excluding deferred), divided by its working days (Mon-Fri between startDate and endDate, inclusive).</li><li>Rate = the average velocity of those sprints. A milestone's capacity = rate × its working days, rounded to whole hours.</li><li>No completed sprint (or none with dates): no capacity. The box shows the estimate only.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Data:</strong> in <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code>, query the 3 completed sprints (sort by <code>Milestone.endDate</code> DESC, limit 3). Then query their issues separately with <code>rels: 'estimated'</code> only (no hasMany rels on the milestone request, per CLAUDE.md). Load these only when the Planning view is opened, not for the plain board.</li><li><strong>UI</strong> in each milestone box header of <code>AppUi::TaskBoard::Planning</code>:<ul><li>\\"<strong>Xh</strong> of Yh capacity\\" and a <code>progress progress-xs</code> bar under the header: success up to 90%, warning from 90 to 100%, danger with <code>fa-exclamation-triangle</code> above 100%.</li><li>A <code>box-footer</code> line with <code>fa-info-circle</code> explains the figure (\\"3.8h per working day (average of the last 3 completed sprints) × 10 working days\\").</li><li>Update straight away when issues are moved.</li></ul></li><li>Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; no new colours.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests cover the util: working days across weekends, sprints without dates skipped, no history means no capacity, deferred issues excluded.</li><li>The capacity figure and bar colour change as issues move in and out of a sprint.</li><li>The plain Board view makes no extra requests.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a stored capacity field, capacity per assignee, holidays and per-member availability.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["planning-view"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "screens": ["planning-view"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-28 15:02:12	2026-10-28 15:02:12	f
b64f8ee26af7-b6c3-7359-0cc1081595e7	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	4	{"summary": "Collaborative Docs, first slice plus the first AI features. Gaia stores each doc's Yjs state and its derived HTML and plain text in a new Doccontent resource (Doc.body is dropped), and enforces doc.update and the lock on writes. A Hocuspocus collab server in hermes/collab syncs the docs and saves them to Gaia. Prometheus gets a Tiptap editor whose schema includes suggestion marks, real-time co-editing with offline recovery, and presence. For AI, Ares gets /docs/transform, /docs/complete and /docs/review; Gaia exposes them through a standard Docassist resource that checks access, rate-limits and logs who asked. Prometheus adds AI-made suggestions (accept/reject), then selection-based AI, ghost-text completion and an AI reviewer on top of a shared doc-ai data layer.", "issues": [{"key": "doc-content-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Doccontent resource (Yjs state, HTML and plain text) and drop Doc.body", "description": "<p>Docs become real-time co-edited documents. A doc's content is a Yjs CRDT state kept live by a collab server and saved to Gaia. The content gets its own resource so that the frequent autosaves don't rewrite the doc metadata, aren't copied into the audit log (<code>auditBehavior</code> stores old and new values of every changed field) and never travel with list queries.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Doccontent</code> (table <code>doccontent</code>), following <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code> (exemplar gaia#264, the Doc resource): <code>docId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>projectId</code> varchar(36) required (the doc's project, for the ACL group), <code>state</code> text nullable (base64-encoded Yjs update), <code>html</code> text nullable, <code>plainText</code> text nullable, <code>byteSize</code> int, plus the standard id, dates, createdUser, modifiedUser and deleted fields. Behaviours: createdUser, modifiedUser, dateCreated, dateModified, softDelete. <strong>No auditBehavior.</strong></li><li>Relationships: <code>doc</code> hasOne Doc (docId); inverse <code>content</code> hasOne Doccontent on <code>Doc</code>.</li><li>Validation: one Doccontent per doc (a second create for the same <code>docId</code> fails validation); <code>docId</code> must be a doc in the same <code>projectId</code>.</li><li>Remove the <code>body</code> field from <code>Doc</code> metadata and its api-tester cases. Existing doc rows are test data only, so their body is dropped.</li><li>ACL metadata <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via projectId, permissions <code>doccontent.get/create/update/delete</code>. No permission seed SQL.</li><li>Model, empty controller, <code>core/config/models.php</code>, <code>core/config/routes.php</code>, <code>routes.v1.json</code>, backend api placeholders and regenerated outputs as in B.md. api-tester harness/seed rows plus acl.json (member with and without doccontent.*, non-member) and client.json cases (create, get by docId, update, duplicate docId rejected).</li><li><code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>: D-002 (the Yjs state in Doccontent is the master copy; <code>html</code> and <code>plainText</code> are derived copies for export, search and AI, written by the collab server and never edited directly; base64 in text because the REST API is JSON), D-003 (content is written with the connected user's own token, so Gaia ACL and modifiedUser stay authoritative; no service account), D-004 (one merged snapshot row per doc, no update log).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a project member with doccontent.* can create, read and update one content row per doc; non-members are denied; Doc has no body field; the regenerated docs and graph have no drift.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> version history, lock enforcement (separate issue), sharing, full-text indexes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "A standard new-resource bundle per B.md (metadata, model, controller, config, routes, api-tester cases) plus removing Doc.body and the decisions doc; splitting it would leave a half resource that breaks dev.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-write-guard", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: require doc.update for Doc/Doccontent writes and reject writes on locked docs", "description": "<p>The collab server and the UI rely on Gaia to refuse writes a user isn't allowed to make. The review of agaia-4488 (gaia#264) found that a project member with only <code>doc.get</code>/<code>doc.create</code> got 200 on <code>PATCH /api/v1/doc/{id}</code>, and that <code>Doc.locked</code> is stored but not enforced.</p><ul><li>Find why update was authorized without <code>doc.update</code> (check how RestController/ACL authorizes PATCH for project-group resources, and whether other resources are affected) and fix it at the root. If the cause is in shared ACL code, fix it there and add denial cases for one other resource too.</li><li>Enforce <code>locked</code>: while a doc is locked, updates to its <code>Doccontent</code> are rejected (403 or a validation error, following the layering in the Design section). Only the doc's owner (<code>ownerId</code>) or a user with the project admin role may change <code>locked</code>, like the wiki lock today.</li><li>api-tester acl.json cases: Doc update and delete denied without doc.update/doc.delete; Doccontent update denied without doccontent.update; Doccontent update rejected on a locked doc; lock/unlock by the owner allowed, by another editor denied.</li><li>Record the lock rule as a decision in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the new denial cases pass and the existing Doc cases still pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-doc sharing roles, ownerId validation against project members.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-content-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "collab-server", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Docs collab server: self-contained collab/ package (Hocuspocus) with Gaia auth and Doccontent persistence", "description": "<p>Projects4Me Docs need Google-Docs-style co-editing. Each doc is a Yjs CRDT document that must be held in memory, synced between browsers and saved to Gaia. The relay can't do this (D-001 locked stateless relay, D-002 browsers never publish), so a collab server is added to this repo as a <strong>self-contained package in <code>collab/</code></strong>: its own process, port and container, sharing no code or dependencies with the relay, so it can later move to its own repo by moving the folder.</p><ul><li><strong>Isolation:</strong> its own <code>collab/package.json</code> (dependencies <code>@hocuspocus/server</code>, <code>yjs</code>, <code>@tiptap/html</code> and the Tiptap extensions below, approved for this module; pick versions that run on Node 18, Hermes' runtime), its own entrypoint <code>collab/server.js</code>, its own Dockerfile and docker-compose service. No imports from the relay's <code>src/</code> and no changes to relay code: its own small Gaia client module, modelled on <code>src/auth/gaia-session.js</code>.</li><li><strong>ADR D-016</strong> in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>: the collab server lives in <code>collab/</code> as a separate process; it holds Yjs documents and awareness in memory only and persists only through Gaia; the relay rules D-001 to D-015 are unchanged. It moves to its own repo when it takes on agents or export, or when its releases start to clash with the relay's.</li><li><code>CLAUDE.md</code>: scope the rule \\"Hermes stays a locked relay: no domain logic, no storage\\" to the relay (<code>src/</code>), and add a short <code>collab/</code> section (what it may do, its own package.json, no imports across the two).</li><li>Root test script also runs <code>collab/</code> tests, so the existing hermes test command covers both.</li><li>Document name contract: <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>. The client sends the user's Gaia OAuth access token as the Hocuspocus token. Never log tokens or document content.</li><li>onAuthenticate: call Gaia <code>GET /api/v1/user/me</code> with the token. Reject without <code>doc.get</code> in <code>aclPermissions</code>, then <code>GET /api/v1/doc/&lt;id&gt;</code> with the same token (reject on 403/404). The connection is read-only when the user lacks <code>doc.update</code> or the doc is <code>locked</code>.</li><li>onLoadDocument: load the Doccontent for the doc (<code>GET /api/v1/doccontent</code> filtered by docId) and apply the base64 <code>state</code>; start empty if there is none.</li><li>onStoreDocument (debounce about 2 s, max 10 s): encode the state and create or PATCH the Doccontent <code>state</code> and <code>byteSize</code>. After about 30 s without changes and on the last disconnect, also write <code>html</code> (generated from the Yjs fragment) and <code>plainText</code>. Use the token of a connected user who has write access.</li><li><strong>Schema</strong> in <code>collab/schema.js</code>, matching the Prometheus editor: StarterKit, Underline, Link, Table/TableRow/TableHeader/TableCell, TaskList/TaskItem, and two marks <code>suggestionInsert</code> / <code>suggestionDelete</code> (attrs <code>id</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>authorId</code>, <code>actedFor</code>, <code>requestId</code>, <code>createdAt</code>; rendered as <code>&lt;ins data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;del data-suggestion-id&gt;</code>). Document it in <code>collab/README.md</code> with the env config (<code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>COLLAB_PORT</code>) and how to run it.</li><li>Unit tests with a stubbed Gaia: rejected token, missing doc.get, read-only for no doc.update and for locked, load applies stored state, store creates then updates the content, html/plainText written on idle and on last disconnect.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two clients editing <code>doc:&lt;id&gt;</code> converge; after a restart the content reloads from Gaia; unauthorized users can't connect; read-only users can't change the document; the relay's tests and image are unchanged apart from the test script.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> agents as server-side peers, version snapshots, comments, scaling beyond one instance.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-content-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "A new self-contained service package: entrypoint, auth, Gaia client/persistence and schema modules, its package.json, Dockerfile and compose service, README, ADR, CLAUDE.md, root test script and two test files. Auth and persistence can't ship apart, because the server is unusable without both.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-editor", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Tiptap editor component with toolbar, tables, checklists, outline and suggestion marks", "description": "<p>The Docs module needs a structured rich-text editor that can co-edit through Yjs. Toast UI can't, so Docs uses Tiptap (open-source packages only). This issue builds the editor as a standalone component. Real-time wiring and suggestion behaviour come in later issues.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>@tiptap/core</code>, <code>@tiptap/starter-kit</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-underline</code>, <code>-link</code>, <code>-table</code>, <code>-table-row</code>, <code>-table-header</code>, <code>-table-cell</code>, <code>-task-list</code>, <code>-task-item</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>utils/docs/schema.js</code>: the single list of extensions, plus two marks <code>suggestionInsert</code> and <code>suggestionDelete</code> (attrs <code>id</code>, <code>source</code> (<code>ai</code>), <code>authorId</code>, <code>actedFor</code>, <code>requestId</code>, <code>createdAt</code>; rendered as <code>&lt;ins data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;del data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> with a <code>doc-suggestion</code> class). The collab server builds the stored HTML from the same list (<code>hermes/collab/schema.js</code>), so a change here needs the same change there.</li><li><code>Docs::Editor</code> (<code>components/docs/editor.{js,hbs}</code>): mounts Tiptap on an element. Args <code>@content</code> (initial HTML), <code>@editable</code>, <code>@extensions</code> (extra extensions added to the schema list), <code>@onReady(editor)</code>. Destroys the editor on teardown. No persistence.</li><li><code>Docs::Toolbar</code>: bold, italic, underline, strike, H1 to H3, bullet and ordered list, checklist, blockquote, code block, link, insert table and add/remove rows and columns. Buttons are <code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code> with Font Awesome 4 icons, <code>aria-pressed</code> for active marks, and the toolbar is hidden when not editable. It yields a slot for extra buttons (used later by AI).</li><li><code>Docs::Outline</code>: a <code>col-md-4</code> side box listing the document's headings; clicking or pressing Enter scrolls to the heading.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code> (square edges, colours from <code>variables.scss</code> only), including the suggestion marks (inserted text underlined, deleted text struck through, in existing colours). Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Integration tests: renders the content, a toolbar action applies a mark, read-only hides the toolbar and blocks typing, the outline lists headings and scrolls, suggestion marks render with their attributes.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the component renders and edits formatted content, tables and checklists, renders suggestion marks, and follows <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> saving, real-time collaboration, accepting/rejecting suggestions, images and attachments, comments.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Editor, toolbar and outline components (js+hbs each), the schema module, styles, translations and tests. The toolbar and outline are small and only make sense with the editor they drive.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-collab-client", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: real-time co-editing on the doc page with autosave status and offline recovery", "description": "<p>Connects the Docs editor to the collab server (<code>hermes/collab</code>), so several people edit one doc live and changes save themselves with no Save button.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>yjs</code>, <code>@hocuspocus/provider</code>, <code>y-indexeddb</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>config/environment.js</code>: <code>ENV.docs.collabUrl</code> (no secrets).</li><li><code>services/doc-collab.js</code>: <code>open(docId)</code> creates a Y.Doc, an <code>IndexeddbPersistence</code> for offline recovery and a <code>HocuspocusProvider</code> (name <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>, token = the session's current access token, refreshed through <code>services/session.js</code> before a reconnect). Exposes tracked <code>status</code> (connecting, saving, saved, offline) and <code>readOnly</code> (from the server). <code>close()</code> destroys both. One responsibility: the connection; no UI.</li><li>Doc page from aprom-4490 (<code>app.project.doc.page</code>): renders <code>Docs::Editor</code> with the Collaboration extension bound to the Y.Doc. Editable only when <code>acl</code> allows doc.update, the doc isn't locked and the server didn't mark the connection read-only. Opens on route enter and closes on exit. A new doc starts empty.</li><li><code>Docs::SaveStatus</code> in the record box header: \\"Saving…\\", \\"All changes saved\\", \\"Offline – changes are kept on this device\\".</li><li>Tests: the service with a stubbed provider (status transitions, readOnly, close on exit) and an acceptance test of the page in read-only and editable modes with the service stubbed (Mirage has no websocket).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two browsers on the same doc see each other's edits live; reloading keeps the content; edits made offline sync after reconnecting; a locked doc, or a user without doc.update, gets a read-only editor.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence and cursors (next issue), version history.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-editor", "collab-server", "aprom-4489", "aprom-4490"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-presence", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: who's in the doc, live cursors and selections, and 'is typing'", "description": "<p>Collaborators should see who else is in a doc and where they are working, like Google Docs. This uses the collab server's awareness channel from <code>services/doc-collab.js</code>; nothing is stored.</p><ul><li>Dependency: <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration-cursor</code> (approved for this module).</li><li>Awareness state: <code>{ user: { id, name, color }, typing: boolean }</code>. Pick the colour deterministically from the user id out of a fixed palette of existing <code>variables.scss</code> colours; no new colours.</li><li>Live cursors and selections in the editor, each with a name label in the user's colour (styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>).</li><li>A \\"who's in the doc\\" avatar stack in the record box header, reusing the existing avatar markup (<code>components/project/member-avatars.hbs</code> pattern, <code>userimage/get</code>). One entry per user even with several tabs, with a tooltip of the name.</li><li>\\"<em>Name</em> is typing…\\": set <code>typing</code> on local input and clear it after about 2 s of no input; show it under the avatars.</li><li>Tests: the avatar stack de-duplicates users and hides the current user; the typing flag clears after the timeout; the colour is stable for an id.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with two users in a doc each sees the other's avatar, cursor, selection and typing indicator, and these disappear when the other leaves.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence on the All Docs list, follow-a-user mode.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-docs", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Docs AI endpoints: /docs/transform, /docs/complete and /docs/review", "description": "<p>Projects4Me Docs get AI help: rewrite a selection, complete the sentence being written, and review a whole document. Gaia (<code>core/services/LLM.php</code>) stays the only caller; it sends the text and returns the result to the editor.</p><ul><li>New router <code>routers/docs.py</code> (prefix <code>/docs</code>) with Pydantic request/response models, one service per use case in <code>services/</code>, prompts kept out of the router. Register it in <code>main.py</code>.</li><li><code>POST /docs/transform</code>: request <code>{action: improve|shorten|expand|summarize|questions|custom, instruction?: str (max 500, required for custom), selectionHtml: str (max 8000), context: {title, headingPath: [str], before: str (max 2000), after: str (max 500)}}</code>. Response <code>{html: str}</code>, using only the tags p, h1-h3, ul, ol, li, strong, em, u, s, a, blockquote, code, pre. <code>questions</code> returns a bullet list of open questions.</li><li><code>POST /docs/complete</code>: request <code>{title, headingPath, before (max 2000), after (max 500)}</code>. Response <code>{text: str}</code>: plain text continuing the sentence, at most about 200 characters, possibly empty. Uses a fast model from env (<code>ARES_DOCS_COMPLETE_MODEL</code>, default <code>claude-haiku-4-5-20251001</code>) with a low max-token limit.</li><li><code>POST /docs/review</code>: request <code>{title, text (max 60000, plain text with headings on their own lines)}</code>. Response <code>{findings: [{quote: str, category: unclear|open_question|inconsistency|missing|wording, message: str, replacement?: str}]}</code>, at most 20. Every <code>quote</code> must be an exact substring of <code>text</code>: the service drops findings whose quote isn't found.</li><li>Model names and token limits come from env; extend the adapter so a service can pick its model.</li><li>Document text is untrusted input: prompts tell the model to treat it as content, never as instructions.</li><li>Errors: invalid input gives 422; a provider failure gives a clear error status and message, never empty or fake output.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter (no live calls): each endpoint's request validation and response shape, review drops non-matching quotes, complete truncates long output.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the three endpoints return the documented shapes with the fake adapter; no prompt or provider logic in the router.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming, agent loops, storing anything.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Three endpoints that share one router, one set of request/response models and one adapter change; each service and its test is small.", "screens": []}, {"key": "docassist-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Docassist resource for AI help (transform, complete, review) via Ares", "description": "<p>The Docs editor asks for AI help (rewrite a selection, complete a sentence, review the document). Gaia owns access and must record who asked, so each request is a <code>Docassist</code> record created through standard CRUD. The create calls Ares and returns the result in the response.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Docassist</code> (table <code>docassist</code>) per <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code>: <code>docId</code>, <code>projectId</code> (varchar(36), required), <code>kind</code> (transform|complete|review), <code>action</code> (improve|shorten|expand|summarize|questions|custom, transform only), <code>instruction</code> varchar(500) nullable, <code>status</code> (done|failed), <code>result</code> text nullable (transform: HTML; review: JSON findings; complete: not stored), <code>inputChars</code> and <code>outputChars</code> int, standard fields and behaviours (no audit). The person who asked is <code>createdUser</code> (the <code>actedFor</code> of the resulting suggestions).</li><li>Request-only inputs, never stored: <code>selectionHtml</code>, <code>context</code> {title, headingPath, before, after}, <code>text</code> (review). Decide how the framework accepts non-persisted create inputs (e.g. a component on create) and record it in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>.</li><li>On create: check the doc exists in <code>projectId</code> and the caller has <code>doc.update</code> on it; enforce input limits (selection 8000, before 2000, after 500, text 60000 chars); rate-limit per user (complete 30/min, transform and review 10/min, counted from the user's recent Docassist rows) with 429; call Ares through <code>core/services/LLM.php</code> (new methods for <code>/docs/transform</code>, <code>/docs/complete</code>, <code>/docs/review</code>); save the row with <code>status</code> and return the result in the response (<code>result</code> for transform and review; a transient <code>completion</code> field for complete).</li><li>A failed Ares call saves <code>status = failed</code> and returns an error status with a message, never an empty success.</li><li>ACL metadata <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via projectId; permissions <code>docassist.create/get</code> (get is used to reopen the latest review). No permission seed SQL.</li><li>api-tester with a stubbed LLM service in the test environment (no live Ares): acl cases (member with and without docassist.create, without doc.update, non-member) and client cases (each kind returns its shape, input over the limit is rejected, rate limit returns 429, Ares failure gives an error and a failed row, completion text is not stored).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the three kinds work end to end with the stub; only users who can edit the doc can ask; every request leaves a row with who, when, kind and status.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming, cost accounting in money, agents.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ares-docs", "doc-content-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 14, "sizeReason": "A new-resource bundle per B.md plus the LLM service methods, the request-only input handling, the rate limit and a test stub for the LLM service; the AI call and the resource that carries it can't ship apart.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-suggestions", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: apply, accept and reject suggestions (AI-made) with a Suggestions box", "description": "<p>Changes made by AI in a doc never land directly: they arrive as suggestions that people accept or reject, each showing who it was made for. The editor schema already has the <code>suggestionInsert</code>/<code>suggestionDelete</code> marks; this issue adds the behaviour. Suggesting mode for people's own typing is not part of this issue.</p><ul><li><code>utils/docs/suggestions.js</code>: <code>proposeReplacement(editor, from, to, html, attrs)</code> marks the old range with <code>suggestionDelete</code> and inserts the new content with <code>suggestionInsert</code>, both with the same <code>id</code>; <code>proposeInsertion</code>; <code>accept(id)</code> (removes inserted marks, deletes text marked deleted); <code>reject(id)</code> (deletes inserted text, removes deleted marks); <code>acceptAll</code>/<code>rejectAll(requestId)</code>; <code>list(editor)</code> groups pending suggestions by <code>requestId</code>. All as single editor transactions, so they sync and undo like normal edits.</li><li><code>Docs::SuggestionsBox</code>: a <code>box-info</code> side box (as in the screens) listing pending suggestions grouped by request, with Accept/Reject per suggestion and Accept all/Reject all per request. The author line uses <code>Agent::Badge</code> with the \\"for {name}\\" sponsor text (as <code>components/agent/user-tag.hbs</code> does) and the name \\"AI Assist\\" for <code>source: ai</code>. Clicking an entry scrolls to and selects it.</li><li>Clicking a suggestion in the text shows a small popover with Accept/Reject (Bootstrap popover markup, keyboard reachable).</li><li>Buttons only for users who can edit; others see the suggestions read-only.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>, strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the helpers (replacement then accept and reject give the expected document; acceptAll per request) and an integration test of the box (grouping, sponsor text, read-only hides buttons).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a suggestion added through the helper shows inline and in the box; accept and reject change the document as expected for everyone in the doc.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> Suggesting mode for people's typing, comments on suggestions, notifications.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-ai-data", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: docassist model, adapter, Mirage and a doc-ai service", "description": "<p>The Docs AI features (selection actions, ghost-text completion, reviewer) all call Gaia's <code>Docassist</code> resource. This issue adds the shared data layer so each feature only builds its UI.</p><ul><li>Ember Data <code>docassist</code> model (docId, projectId, kind, action, instruction, status, result, inputChars, outputChars, createdUser, dateCreated, plus the request-only <code>selectionHtml</code>, <code>context</code>, <code>text</code>), adapter and serializer following the existing ones; request-only attributes are sent on create and never read back.</li><li><code>services/doc-ai.js</code>: <code>transform(doc, action, selectionHtml, context, instruction)</code>, <code>complete(doc, context)</code>, <code>review(doc, text)</code>, <code>latestReview(doc)</code>. Latest request wins per kind (a new call makes an older pending result be ignored); errors are thrown with Gaia's message, and 429 becomes a \\"too many requests, try again shortly\\" error.</li><li>Mirage: a <code>docassist</code> factory and a POST handler that returns canned results per kind (and a 429 scenario).</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the service (latest wins, error mapping, review result parsed from JSON).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the service returns parsed results from Mirage for each kind and surfaces errors.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["docassist-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-ai-selection", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: selection-based AI Assist box with preview and insert as suggestion", "description": "<p>A writer selects text and asks AI to improve, shorten, expand or summarize it, list open questions, or follow their own instruction. The result is previewed first and only enters the doc as a suggestion.</p><ul><li>An \\"AI Assist\\" button (<code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code>, <code>fa-magic</code>) in the editor toolbar slot opens the <code>Docs::AiAssistBox</code> side box (<code>box-info</code>, as in the screens). Shown only to users who can edit.</li><li>The box shows the action buttons (Improve wording, Shorten, Expand, Summarize, Open questions) and a custom instruction field (<code>FormFields::FieldText</code>), the current selection (\\"Selection: 1 paragraph in <em>Heading</em>\\") and an empty state when nothing is selected.</li><li>On an action: send the selection as HTML plus context (doc title, heading path, up to 2000 characters before and 500 after) through <code>services/doc-ai.js</code>; show <code>AppUi::Loader</code> while waiting, then a preview rendered through the editor schema (never raw HTML). Buttons: Insert as suggestion (<code>btn-primary</code>), Try again, Discard. Errors show in the box with a retry.</li><li>Insert as suggestion uses <code>proposeReplacement</code> from <code>utils/docs/suggestions.js</code> with <code>source: ai</code>, <code>actedFor</code> = current user, <code>requestId</code> = the Docassist id. If the selected text changed while waiting, insert at the original range only if it still matches; otherwise show \\"The text changed, try again\\".</li><li>One pending request at a time; the button is disabled while busy.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>, styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>.</li><li>Integration test with Mirage: select, choose Improve wording, preview shown, insert creates a suggestion with the right attrs; error path; empty-selection state.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the flow matches the assist-preview and assist-review screens; nothing changes in the doc until the user inserts.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming, AI on images or tables as a whole.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-ai-data", "doc-suggestions"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["assist-preview", "assist-review"]}, {"key": "doc-ai-complete", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: ghost-text AI completion while writing (Tab to accept)", "description": "<p>While writing, AI can suggest how the sentence continues, shown as grey text after the cursor. Accepting it is the writer's own choice, so accepted text is a normal edit, not a suggestion.</p><ul><li>A toolbar toggle \\"AI suggestions\\" (<code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code>, <code>aria-pressed</code>), off by default, remembered per user in local storage. Only for users who can edit.</li><li>A Tiptap extension <code>utils/docs/ghost-text.js</code>: after about 800 ms without typing, with the cursor at the end of a non-empty text block and no selection, ask <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>complete()</code> with the title, heading path, up to 2000 characters before and 500 after. Show the result as a widget decoration (local only, not synced, not saved).</li><li>Tab inserts the text at the cursor; Esc, any typing, moving the cursor or losing focus dismisses it. Any newer request makes older responses be ignored. Ignore while composing (IME) and while the doc is read-only.</li><li>On 429 or errors, show nothing and back off for 30 s; no toasts.</li><li>Ghost text style in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code> (muted colour from <code>variables.scss</code>); strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the extension (debounce, shown only at block end, Tab inserts, typing dismisses, stale response ignored) and an integration test of the toggle.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the toggle on, pausing at the end of a paragraph shows a completion that Tab inserts; nothing is requested with the toggle off.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> multi-line or multi-paragraph completions, completions in the middle of text.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-ai-data", "doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-ai-review", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: AI reviewer box with findings, jump to text and apply fix as suggestion", "description": "<p>Before sharing a doc for review, a writer can ask AI to review it: unclear wording, open questions, inconsistencies and missing parts. Findings point at exact text and fixes arrive as suggestions.</p><ul><li>\\"Review document\\" in <code>Docs::AiAssistBox</code> sends the doc's plain text (headings on their own lines) through <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>review()</code>.</li><li><code>Docs::ReviewBox</code> (<code>box-info</code> side box): one entry per finding with its category as a <code>label</code> (existing classes), the message and the quoted text; a header line \\"Reviewed by <em>Name</em>, <em>time ago</em>\\". On page load it shows the latest review of the doc (<code>latestReview</code>), if any.</li><li>Clicking a finding finds its <code>quote</code> in the current document and selects and scrolls to it; if it's no longer there, the finding shows \\"Text changed since the review\\".</li><li>\\"Apply fix\\" (when the finding has a <code>replacement</code>) uses <code>proposeReplacement</code> with <code>source: ai</code>, <code>actedFor</code> = current user and <code>requestId</code> = the review's Docassist id. \\"Dismiss\\" hides the finding for this user (local only).</li><li>Loader while reviewing, errors with retry, button disabled while busy. Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>, styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>.</li><li>Integration tests with Mirage: findings render, click selects the quote, missing quote shows the changed state, apply fix creates a suggestion, latest review loads on open.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a review lists findings that jump to their text, and fixes appear as suggestions attributed to the user who asked.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> turning findings into comments, scheduled or automatic reviews.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-ai-selection"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-13 12:55:18	2026-11-13 12:55:18	f
d9cfa4b76ae2-fb26-79e3-77de4efc24cf	e53706516ae2-baab-7f50-a57680d4b6c5	2	{"summary": "Sprint planning on the Task Board, Prometheus only, with no Gaia changes. The first issue adds a Planning view next to the existing Board view (?view=planning): the backlog on the left, a box for each open milestone on the right, moving issues by drag or by a multi-select 'Move to', and estimate totals. The second issue adds calculated capacity to each sprint box, based on velocity from the last three completed sprints. There is no capacity field and no backlog rank field. Both issues go in the new milestone 'Board planning'.", "issues": [{"key": "planning-view", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task Board: Planning view with backlog and milestone boxes side by side", "description": "<p>Sprint planning is hard today: the backlog and each milestone are separate tabs on the Task Board. The only way to plan is to drag one card at a time onto a tab header without seeing the sprint's contents. This issue adds a second view of the board where the backlog and every open milestone are visible together. It is Prometheus only, with no Gaia changes; see the attached <code>planning-view</code> screen.</p><ul><li><strong>Toggle:</strong> add a <code>view</code> query param (<code>board</code> default, <code>planning</code>) to <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code> / <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code>. Show <strong>Board | Planning</strong> as Bootstrap <code>nav nav-tabs</code> above the board, with the existing Saved Searches dropdown and search input on the right. Search and saved searches filter both views.</li><li><strong>Data:</strong> reuse what the route already loads (open milestones with status in_progress|planned, the backlog issues, and each issue's <code>estimated</code>/<code>spent</code> timelogs). Add no new requests.</li><li><strong>New component</strong> <code>AppUi::TaskBoard::Planning</code> (co-located in <code>app/components/app-ui/task-board/</code>). Layout: <code>.row</code> &gt; <code>col-md-5</code> + <code>col-md-7</code>.<ul><li>Left: a <code>box box-primary</code> \\"Backlog\\". The header shows the issue count and total estimated hours. Below it, a <code>table table-hover</code> of rows: checkbox, <code>AppUi::PriorityIcon</code>, linked number - subject, status label underneath, estimate on the right. Sort by priority (blocker → low), then issue number. Show the first 20 rows, with a \\"Show N more\\" link in the box footer.</li><li>Right: a <code>box box-info</code> per open milestone, in the board's order. Sprints and in_progress milestones come first and are expanded; other types are <code>box-default</code> and collapsed. Each header shows the milestone type, name, dates, a status label, the issue count and the total estimate. Rows match the backlog's, plus the assignee and without the checkbox. An empty milestone shows a drop hint row.</li><li>A <strong>New Sprint</strong> button under the boxes opens the existing create-milestone modal from <code>task-board.hbs</code>, preset to type sprint. Extract the modal if needed; don't duplicate it.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Moving issues:</strong><ul><li>Drag rows between the backlog and any milestone box, and between milestone boxes, with SortableJS (shared group). Reuse <code>modifiers/initialize-sortable.js</code> where it fits; otherwise add a small modifier for list rows. On drop, save only <code>milestoneId</code> (null for the backlog) through the controller's existing <code>updateIssue</code> path, so the board view, saving overlay and Hermes updates stay consistent.</li><li>Multi-select: ticking backlog rows enables <strong>Move N to ▾</strong> (a Bootstrap dropdown listing the open milestones), which saves each selected issue's milestone.</li><li>Totals update straight away. A failed save moves the row back and shows the error through the notifications service.</li></ul></li><li>Clicking an issue subject opens the existing quick view (<code>selectIssue</code>), as on the board.</li><li>All strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>. Styles are scoped under <code>.board-planning</code> in <code>app/styles/modules/board.scss</code>, with square edges and no new colours.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li><code>?view=planning</code> shows the backlog and all open milestones together; the Board tab returns to the current board unchanged.</li><li>Dragging or Move to changes the issue's milestone in Gaia, and the issue appears in the right lane when you switch back to Board.</li><li>Counts and estimate totals are correct after every move; search filters both columns.</li><li>Mirage handlers plus an integration test for the component and an acceptance test for the toggle and Move to.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> capacity (separate issue), ordering the backlog by hand (there is no rank field), closing a milestone from this view, and a mobile layout.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Board planning", "newMilestone": true, "screens": ["planning-view"]}, {"key": "sprint-capacity", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task Board Planning view: calculated sprint capacity from past velocity", "description": "<p>When planning a sprint, the Planning view (previous issue) shows each milestone's estimate total but not whether the team can deliver it. We don't want a capacity field in Gaia, so capacity is calculated from past velocity. See the attached <code>planning-view</code> screen: \\"31h of 38h capacity\\", the bar, and the info line in the box footer.</p><ul><li><strong>Calculation</strong> in a pure util <code>app/utils/board/sprint-capacity.js</code> (unit tested):<ul><li>Take the project's last 3 milestones with <code>milestoneType</code> sprint and <code>status</code> completed (status set by mark-as-complete, <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> ~l.990), latest <code>endDate</code> first.</li><li>For each one: velocity = the sum of estimated hours of its closed issues (statuses done, complete, closed, as in <code>getCompletedIssuesCount</code>, but excluding deferred), divided by its working days (Mon-Fri between startDate and endDate, inclusive).</li><li>Rate = the average velocity of those sprints. A milestone's capacity = rate × its working days, rounded to whole hours.</li><li>No completed sprint (or none with dates): no capacity. The box shows the estimate only.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Data:</strong> in <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code>, query the 3 completed sprints (sort by <code>Milestone.endDate</code> DESC, limit 3). Then query their issues separately with <code>rels: 'estimated'</code> only (no hasMany rels on the milestone request, per CLAUDE.md). Load these only when the Planning view is opened, not for the plain board.</li><li><strong>UI</strong> in each milestone box header of <code>AppUi::TaskBoard::Planning</code>:<ul><li>\\"<strong>Xh</strong> of Yh capacity\\" and a <code>progress progress-xs</code> bar under the header: success up to 90%, warning from 90 to 100%, danger with <code>fa-exclamation-triangle</code> above 100%.</li><li>A <code>box-footer</code> line with <code>fa-info-circle</code> explains the figure (\\"3.8h per working day (average of the last 3 completed sprints) × 10 working days\\").</li><li>Update straight away when issues are moved.</li></ul></li><li>Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; no new colours.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests cover the util: working days across weekends, sprints without dates skipped, no history means no capacity, deferred issues excluded.</li><li>The capacity figure and bar colour change as issues move in and out of a sprint.</li><li>The plain Board view makes no extra requests.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a stored capacity field, capacity per assignee, holidays and per-member availability.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["planning-view"], "milestone": "Board planning", "newMilestone": true, "screens": ["planning-view"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-28 15:03:53	2026-10-28 15:05:09	f
934503d76ae5-3f15-613b-2c37f851a001	6471d1b46ae5-10d2-613b-e3f2313332d0	2	{"summary": "Two independent Prometheus issues in aga-v1. ideas-entry tidies the Ideas entry points: a direct nav link with no New Idea submenu, the New Idea page opening by default instead of the empty Brainstorm box, and the create page's title field lined up with the description. idea-status makes the ideas list show each idea's progress from the status of its latest plan (Brainstorming when there is no plan, Archived when archived), shares the plan status colours with the plan box and keeps the list live on plan events.", "issues": [{"key": "ideas-entry", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: direct nav link, New Idea page by default, title field aligned with the description", "description": "<p>The Ideas screens have three small problems. The nav menu has a List / New Idea submenu, which Task Board and Gantt don't. The ideas route opens an empty 'Brainstorm an Idea' box that is always replaced by the create page or an idea. The create page's title field sits at a different margin from the description.</p><ul><li><strong>Nav:</strong> in <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> remove the <code>actions</code> block from <code>views.Navigation.items.Idea</code>, so Ideas renders as a direct link to <code>app.project.idea</code> like <code>Board</code> and <code>Gantt</code>. Keep its icon, order and <code>aclContext</code>. Remove translation keys that are no longer used (<code>views.nav.menu.idea.list</code>/<code>create</code>) if nothing else uses them.</li><li><strong>Default page:</strong> <code>routes/app/project/idea/index.js</code> redirects (<code>replaceWith</code>) to <code>app.project.idea.create</code> when the user has <code>idea.create</code> (use the <code>acl</code> service). Users without it keep the current hint box in <code>templates/app/project/idea/index.hbs</code>. The browser's selection is still cleared. The \\"New\\" button in the ideas browser box (<code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>) stays.</li><li><strong>Cancel:</strong> <code>controllers/app/project/idea/create.js</code> <code>cancel</code> currently goes to <code>app.project.idea.index</code>, which would now reopen the create page. Instead it resets the form (title, description, validation messages) and clears the editor (pubSub <code>clearContents</code>, as the composer does).</li><li><strong>Alignment:</strong> in <code>templates/app/project/idea/create.hbs</code> remove the extra <code>&lt;div class=\\"form-field\\"&gt;</code> around <code>FormFields::FieldText</code>, which renders its own <code>form-field</code>. The title then has the same margin as the description (the description is laid out correctly; leave it alone).</li><li>Tests: update <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-browser.feature</code> / <code>idea-create.feature</code> and their steps: opening Ideas shows the create page, the nav has no New Idea entry, and Cancel clears the form.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> clicking Ideas in the nav opens the New Idea page directly, with the ideas list beside it. The nav item has no submenu. Title and description labels and inputs line up. Cancel leaves an empty form. Opening an existing idea still works.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the status shown in the ideas list (separate issue) and any Gaia change.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "idea-status", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas list: show each idea's progress from the status of its latest plan", "description": "<p>The ideas browser (<code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>, ~l.21) labels every idea with <code>Idea.status</code>, which is only <code>open</code> or <code>archived</code>, so every listed idea reads \\"Open\\". The engineer wants the list to show where each idea is: the status of its latest plan.</p><ul><li><strong>Status shown:</strong> <code>archived</code> idea: \\"Archived\\" (<code>deferred</code> label, as today). Open idea with no plan: \\"Brainstorming\\" (<code>new</code> label). Otherwise the status of the idea's plan with the highest <code>version</code>: proposed \\"Plan proposed\\", approved \\"Approved\\", creating \\"Creating issues\\", created \\"Issues created\\", failed \\"Failed\\". Add these under a new key such as <code>views.app.idea.progress.*</code> in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>. An unknown status falls back to the plan status translation <code>views.app.idea.plan.status.*</code>.</li><li><strong>Label colours:</strong> move <code>STATUS_LABELS</code> (plan status to label class) out of <code>components/idea/plan-box.js</code> into a shared util (e.g. <code>app/utils/idea/plan-status.js</code>), used by the plan box and the list, so both always use the same colours. The plan box keeps behaving as now.</li><li><strong>Data:</strong> in <code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code>, next to <code>loadIdeas</code>, load the plans of the listed ideas in one <code>store.query('ideaplan', …)</code> (Ideaplan has <code>ideaId</code>, no <code>projectId</code>: filter by the loaded idea ids, or through the <code>idea</code> rel's projectId if Gaia's query supports it). Load only plans, no hasMany rels. The layout controller (<code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>) holds the latest plan status per idea id and exposes it to the template, e.g. a getter on the listed rows or a small helper. Keep the template free of the logic.</li><li><strong>Live:</strong> the controller registers only <code>idea.created</code>/<code>idea.updated</code> today. Also handle <code>idea.plan.created</code> and <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code> (already in the Hermes contract; the idea page uses them) by reloading the plans, so the label changes while a plan is proposed or its issues are created. Keep the existing <code>reloadSequence</code> guard so a stale reload can't overwrite a newer one.</li><li><strong>Tests:</strong> Mirage <code>ideaplan</code> handler supports the query. Acceptance cases in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-browser.feature</code>: idea without plan = Brainstorming; latest version wins (v1 created, v2 proposed = Plan proposed); archived idea = Archived. Integration test for the util.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> each idea in the browser shows Brainstorming, its latest plan's status or Archived, coloured like the plan box's status label, and updates live when a plan is proposed or its status changes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Open/Archived label in the conversation box header, any Gaia change (no new Idea field) and filtering or sorting the list by status.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-30 22:05:07	2026-10-30 22:05:07	f
c974dfe76ae2-5b7d-26f7-5fa01915a48d	90ec8e946ae2-5b7d-26f7-517aea1bffe5	1	{"summary": "One Prometheus CSS fix for the task board card subject. Long unbroken words, such as a class::method name, wrap inside the card instead of overflowing it. Long subjects are cut to 3 lines with an ellipsis, and the full subject shows as a tooltip on hover.", "issues": [{"key": "card-subject-wrap", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task board: wrap long words in the card subject and cut it to 3 lines", "description": "<p>On the task board, a card subject with a word longer than the card is wide (for example <code>OAuthServer::addRefreshTokenGrant</code>) runs past the right edge of the card, because <code>.issue-card-subject a</code> has no wrap rules. A subject of 10 to 15 words also makes the card very tall.</p><ul><li>In <code>app/styles/modules/board.scss</code>, under <code>.issue-card-subject a</code> (around line 281), add <code>overflow-wrap: anywhere</code> (with <code>word-break: break-word</code> as a fallback) so long tokens break inside the card. Words of normal length still wrap at spaces.</li><li>In the same rule, cut the subject to 3 lines with an ellipsis: <code>display: -webkit-box; -webkit-box-orient: vertical; -webkit-line-clamp: 3; overflow: hidden;</code>. Keep the font size and line height as they are.</li><li>In <code>app/components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code> (subject <code>LinkTo</code>, around line 62), add <code>title={{issue.subject}}</code> so the full subject shows on hover. The plain-text <code>title</code> attribute is enough; don't render the subject as HTML.</li><li>Check that clicking the subject still opens the quick view and that dragging cards still works.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A subject with a single 40+ character token stays inside the card in every lane, at the narrowest lane width.</li><li>A 15-word subject shows at most 3 lines and ends with an ellipsis. Hovering over it shows the full subject.</li><li>Short subjects look the same as before.</li><li>An integration test for the task board renders a card with a long unbroken subject, checks that the subject link has the <code>title</code> attribute, and checks that the subject does not overflow the card (<code>scrollWidth &lt;= clientWidth</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing the font size, and the subject on the quick view or the issue page.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-28 18:02:49	2026-10-28 18:03:50	f
e44e9ea16ae5-10d2-613b-5f03d1afa9d4	6471d1b46ae5-10d2-613b-e3f2313332d0	1	{"summary": "One Prometheus issue tidies the Ideas entry points: Ideas becomes a direct nav link (no New Idea submenu), the create page's title field lines up with the description, and the ideas route opens the New Idea page by default instead of the empty Brainstorm box. The list status (item 3) will be added as a second issue once its meaning is settled.", "issues": [{"key": "ideas-entry", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: direct nav link, New Idea page by default, title field aligned with the description", "description": "<p>The Ideas screens have three small problems. The nav menu has a List / New Idea submenu, which Task Board and Gantt don't. The ideas route opens an empty 'Brainstorm an Idea' box that is always replaced by the create page or an idea. The create page's title field sits at a different margin from the description.</p><ul><li><strong>Nav:</strong> in <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> remove the <code>actions</code> block from <code>views.Navigation.items.Idea</code>, so Ideas renders as a direct link to <code>app.project.idea</code> like <code>Board</code> and <code>Gantt</code>. Keep its icon, order and <code>aclContext</code>. Remove translation keys that are no longer used (<code>views.nav.menu.idea.list</code>/<code>create</code>) if nothing else uses them.</li><li><strong>Default page:</strong> <code>routes/app/project/idea/index.js</code> redirects (<code>replaceWith</code>) to <code>app.project.idea.create</code> when the user has <code>idea.create</code> (use the <code>acl</code> service). Users without it keep the current hint box in <code>templates/app/project/idea/index.hbs</code>. The browser's selection is still cleared. The \\"New\\" button in the ideas browser box (<code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>) stays.</li><li><strong>Cancel:</strong> <code>controllers/app/project/idea/create.js</code> <code>cancel</code> currently goes to <code>app.project.idea.index</code>, which would now reopen the create page. Instead it resets the form (title, description, validation messages) and clears the editor (pubSub <code>clearContents</code>, as the composer does).</li><li><strong>Alignment:</strong> in <code>templates/app/project/idea/create.hbs</code> remove the extra <code>&lt;div class=\\"form-field\\"&gt;</code> around <code>FormFields::FieldText</code>, which renders its own <code>form-field</code>. The title then has the same margin as the description (the description is laid out correctly; leave it alone).</li><li>Tests: update <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-browser.feature</code> / <code>idea-create.feature</code> and their steps: opening Ideas shows the create page, the nav has no New Idea entry, and Cancel clears the form.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> clicking Ideas in the nav opens the New Idea page directly, with the ideas list beside it. The nav item has no submenu. Title and description labels and inputs line up. Cancel leaves an empty form. Opening an existing idea still works.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the status shown in the ideas list (separate issue) and any Gaia change.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-30 22:02:12	2026-10-30 22:02:12	f
f1823e636ae5-3f15-1173-de26a5aadfc4	6471d1b46ae5-10d2-613b-e3f2313332d0	3	{"summary": "Five Prometheus issues in aga-v1, one per reported item: nav-link (Ideas as a direct nav link), create-align (title field aligned with the description), default-create (the New Idea page opens by default, Cancel clears the form), idea-status (the ideas list shows the status of each idea's latest plan) and idea-status-live (that status updates live on plan events, after idea-status). Only idea-status-live has to wait; the other four can be worked on at the same time.", "issues": [{"key": "nav-link", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Nav: Ideas as a direct link, no New Idea submenu", "description": "<p>The Ideas nav item opens a List / New Idea submenu, while Task Board and Gantt are direct links. Ideas should be a direct link too. Starting an idea stays possible from the \\"New\\" button in the ideas browser box.</p><ul><li>In <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> remove the <code>actions</code> block from <code>views.Navigation.items.Idea</code>, so <code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.hbs</code>/<code>navbar-items.hbs</code> render it as a direct link to <code>app.project.idea</code>, like <code>Board</code> and <code>Gantt</code>. Keep its icon, order and <code>aclContext</code>.</li><li>Remove the translation keys this leaves unused (<code>views.nav.menu.idea.list</code>, <code>views.nav.menu.idea.create</code>) from <code>translations/en-us.json</code> if nothing else uses them.</li><li>Test: an acceptance step (e.g. in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-browser.feature</code>) checks that clicking Ideas in the nav opens the ideas route and that there is no New Idea entry.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the Ideas nav item has no submenu and opens the ideas page in one click. It is still hidden without <code>idea.read</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> what the ideas route shows first (separate issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "create-align", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "New idea page: title field aligned with \\"Describe it\\"", "description": "<p>On the New Idea page the title field and the \\"Describe it\\" description field have different margins. The description is laid out correctly.</p><ul><li>In <code>templates/app/project/idea/create.hbs</code> the title's <code>FormFields::FieldText</code> is wrapped in an extra <code>&lt;div class=\\"form-field\\"&gt;</code>. The component already renders its own <code>div.form-field</code> (<code>components/form-fields/field-text.hbs</code>), so the title gets the spacing twice. Remove the wrapper so the title sits directly in the <code>form-group</code>, as in <code>templates/app/project/issue/create.hbs</code>.</li><li>Leave the description field and its <code>idea.scss</code> rule (<code>.idea-create .form-field &gt; #editor</code>) alone unless the change shows they need adjusting.</li><li>Check it in the running app next to the issue create page.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the title and description labels and inputs start at the same left edge with the same spacing. Title validation messages still show.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other create page changes.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "default-create", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: open the New Idea page by default instead of the empty Brainstorm box", "description": "<p>Opening Ideas shows an empty \\"Brainstorm an Idea\\" box (<code>templates/app/project/idea/index.hbs</code>), which the user always replaces with the New Idea page or an existing idea. Ideas should open on the New Idea page instead.</p><ul><li><code>routes/app/project/idea/index.js</code>: when the user has <code>idea.create</code> (use the <code>acl</code> service), redirect with <code>replaceWith('app.project.idea.create')</code>. Users without it keep the current hint box. The browser's selection (<code>selectedIdeaId = null</code>) is still cleared.</li><li><code>controllers/app/project/idea/create.js</code> <code>cancel</code> (~l.129) goes to <code>app.project.idea.index</code>, which would now reopen the create page. Make it reset the form instead (title, description, validation messages) and clear the editor (pubSub <code>clearContents</code>, as the composer does).</li><li>Tests: update <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-create.feature</code> / <code>idea-browser.feature</code> and their steps: opening Ideas shows the New Idea form, a user without <code>idea.create</code> sees the hint, Cancel leaves an empty form.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Ideas opens on the New Idea form, with the ideas list beside it. Opening an existing idea still works. Cancel empties the form and stays on the page.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the nav item and the field alignment (separate issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "idea-status", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas list: show each idea's progress from the status of its latest plan", "description": "<p>The ideas browser (<code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>, ~l.21) labels every idea with <code>Idea.status</code>, which is only <code>open</code> or <code>archived</code>, so every listed idea reads \\"Open\\". The engineer wants the list to show where each idea is: the status of its latest plan.</p><ul><li><strong>Status shown:</strong> <code>archived</code> idea: \\"Archived\\" (<code>deferred</code> label, as today). Open idea with no plan: \\"Brainstorming\\" (<code>new</code> label). Otherwise the status of the idea's plan with the highest <code>version</code>: proposed \\"Plan proposed\\", approved \\"Approved\\", creating \\"Creating issues\\", created \\"Issues created\\", failed \\"Failed\\". Add these under a new key such as <code>views.app.idea.progress.*</code> in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>. An unknown status falls back to <code>views.app.idea.plan.status.*</code>.</li><li><strong>Label colours:</strong> move <code>STATUS_LABELS</code> (plan status to label class) out of <code>components/idea/plan-box.js</code> into a shared util (e.g. <code>app/utils/idea/plan-status.js</code>), used by the plan box and the list, so both always use the same colours. The plan box keeps behaving as now.</li><li><strong>Data:</strong> in <code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code>, after <code>loadIdeas</code>, load the plans of the listed ideas in one <code>store.query('ideaplan', …)</code> (Ideaplan has <code>ideaId</code>, no <code>projectId</code>: filter by the loaded idea ids, or through the <code>idea</code> rel's projectId if Gaia's query supports it). No hasMany rels. The layout controller (<code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>) holds the latest plan status per idea id and gives the template the status and class per row. Keep the logic out of the template.</li><li><strong>Tests:</strong> the Mirage <code>ideaplan</code> handler supports the query. Acceptance cases in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-browser.feature</code>: idea without plan = Brainstorming; latest version wins (v1 created, v2 proposed = Plan proposed); archived idea = Archived. Unit test for the util.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> each idea in the browser shows Brainstorming, its latest plan's status or Archived, coloured like the plan box's status label, after loading or reloading the page.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> live updates on plan events (separate issue), the Open/Archived label in the conversation box header, any Gaia change, filtering or sorting by status.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "idea-status-live", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas list: update the plan status live on plan events", "description": "<p>After the ideas list shows each idea's latest plan status, it must stay current while Nestor proposes a plan or Talos creates the issues, without a page reload.</p><ul><li><code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> <code>registerHermesIntents</code> handles only <code>idea.created</code> and <code>idea.updated</code>. Also handle <code>idea.plan.created</code> and <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code> (already in the Hermes contract; the idea page controller uses them) by reloading the plans the list uses (the plan loader added by the list status issue, passed in by <code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code> like <code>loadIdeas</code>).</li><li>Keep the <code>reloadSequence</code> guard so a slower, earlier reload can't overwrite a newer one, and nothing runs after the route is left.</li><li>Tests: acceptance or integration case where a pushed <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code> (created) changes the row's label from Plan proposed to Issues created.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the ideas page open, a new plan version or a plan status change updates that idea's label within the usual live-update delay.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> Gaia or Hermes changes (none needed).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["idea-status"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-30 22:06:41	2026-10-30 22:08:17	f
ab3684f86af3-60d4-8333-4e91d0c10436	341481c56af2-8040-cd6a-5ea33d81936b	6	{"summary": "One bug fix: the Threads template opens its own section.content inside the one the project layout already provides, so the content section is nested twice (and padded twice). Remove the inner wrapper after the header/New-button fixes that touch the same template.", "issues": [{"key": "thr-nested-content", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: section.content is nested twice", "description": "<p>The project layout <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> already wraps every project page in <code>&lt;section class=\\"content\\"&gt;{{outlet}}&lt;/section&gt;</code>. <code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code> opens another <code>&lt;section class=\\"content\\"&gt;</code> around the Threads row, so the DOM has <code>section.content &gt; section.content &gt; div.row.conversation-wrapper</code> and AdminLTE's <code>.content</code> padding applies twice. No other <code>app/project/*</code> template does this (Task Board, Gantt start directly with their content).</p><ul><li>Remove the inner <code>&lt;section class=\\"content\\"&gt;</code> wrapper from <code>conversation.hbs</code>; the template starts with the <code>.row.conversation-wrapper</code> (keep any modal/in-element markup that lived inside the section).</li><li>Check <code>conversation-loading.hbs</code> and the Threads child templates (<code>conversation/index.hbs</code>, <code>conversation/page.hbs</code>) for the same wrapper; check any styles that targeted the nested section.</li><li>Leave <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the Threads page has exactly one <code>section.content</code> (acceptance test asserts the count) and the list starts at the same left/top offset as the Task Board. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other pages.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4455"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-10 17:08:59	2026-11-10 17:08:59	f
f5220da96af4-3b69-e9a2-525823ee6a6a	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	1	{"summary": "Phase 1 of Docs builds the real-time co-editing backbone. The architecture decisions are recorded first (Gaia Docs ADRs). Gaia gets the Doc content fields: the Yjs state, the HTML and full-text copies, and field-level ACL so only the collab service account writes them. Separately, a new Hocuspocus collab server in the hermes repo authenticates each connection against Gaia and makes non-editors read-only. A second collab issue saves documents to Gaia and seeds legacy ones from their HTML, which needs the Gaia fields. Prometheus then replaces the Doc body editor with Tiptap bound to Yjs, with offline recovery, and finally adds presence, live cursors and typing indicators through Yjs awareness. Comments, suggestions, sharing, organisation, history, project links, AI and search/export are later phases.", "issues": [{"key": "docs-adr", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: record the collaboration architecture decisions (content format, collab service, write model)", "description": "<p>Docs becomes a Google-Docs-style collaborative editor. Before building it, the architecture must be agreed and recorded so every later Docs issue follows it. Add the decisions to <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code> (D-001 already exists).</p><ul><li><strong>D-002 Content format:</strong> the content is a Yjs CRDT document. Gaia stores its latest state base64-encoded in <code>Doc.content</code>, with two copies made from it: <code>body</code> (HTML) and <code>bodyText</code> (plain text, full-text indexed). Everything outside the editor (search, export, AI, link boxes) reads only <code>body</code>/<code>bodyText</code>.</li><li><strong>D-003 Collab service:</strong> a separate Hocuspocus process (in the hermes repo, not the Hermes relay) holds live documents. It authenticates each connection with the user's token against Gaia and saves documents through a dedicated service account. Only that account may write <code>content</code>, <code>body</code> and <code>bodyText</code>.</li><li><strong>D-004 Write model:</strong> only users with edit rights write to the CRDT. Comments, replies and suggestions are Gaia records anchored by encoded Yjs relative positions plus the quoted text. Accepting a suggestion is an edit an editor makes in the editor.</li><li><strong>D-005 Agents:</strong> agents never connect to the CRDT with write access. They only create comments and suggestions, which record the user they acted for (<code>actedForUserId</code>).</li><li><strong>D-006 Locked:</strong> a locked doc gets read-only connections for everyone, and Gaia rejects new suggestions on it.</li><li><strong>D-007 Schema contract:</strong> the editor's extension list is shared by Prometheus and the collab server. Adding a node or mark type is a contract change in both repos.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the decisions are in the file in the existing table format, and the decisions test passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> code changes. Sharing roles, versions and links get their own decisions in their issues.</p>", "type": "Research", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 1, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-content-fields", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Doc: Yjs content, HTML and full-text fields writable only by the collab service", "description": "<p>The collab service saves each doc's live state to Gaia, along with HTML and plain-text copies used for search and display (see D-002/D-003 in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>). Extend the existing <code>Doc</code> resource (<code>app/metadata/model/Doc.php</code>) to hold them, and stop browsers from overwriting them.</p><ul><li>Add <code>content</code> (text, null, the base64 Yjs state) and <code>bodyText</code> (text, null, <code>'fts' =&gt; true</code>). Keep <code>body</code> as the HTML copy. Turn on <code>fts</code> for the model.</li><li>Add field-level ACL (<code>doc.content.update</code>, <code>doc.body.update</code>, <code>doc.bodyText.update</code>) so only a role given to the collab service account can write these fields. Normal users can still read <code>body</code>/<code>bodyText</code>. <code>content</code> is readable only by the service role, because browsers get it from the collab server.</li><li>Existing rows: <code>content</code> stays null. The collab service seeds it from <code>body</code> the first time the doc is opened. No data migration.</li><li>Regenerate the gaia-dev graph and <code>docs/generated</code>.</li><li>Add api-tester cases: the service role can PATCH the fields, a project member cannot (403), and a search on <code>bodyText</code> finds a doc.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases above pass, and the full suite and lint pass. The PR says which role the reviewer must grant to the service account (no permission seeds).</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> versions, sharing roles, the collab server itself.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["docs-adr"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "collab-server", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Collab: Hocuspocus server for Docs with Gaia authentication and read-only connections", "description": "<p>Docs needs live co-editing through Yjs, which takes a stateful server. The Hermes relay must stay a stateless relay (D-001), so add a <strong>separate process</strong> in this repo under <code>collab/</code> with its own entry point, Docker service and decision record.</p><ul><li>Add the dependencies <code>@hocuspocus/server</code> and <code>yjs</code> (approved for Docs).</li><li><code>onAuthenticate</code>: read the user's token from the connection, then load the doc as that user through Gaia (<code>GET /docs/{id}</code>). The Gaia session lookup and caching follow D-011/D-012 (reuse that code). If Gaia refuses, refuse the connection. The connection is read-only when the doc is <code>locked</code> or the user lacks <code>doc.update</code>.</li><li>Document name = Doc id, validated as a GUID.</li><li>For now, documents are kept in memory only. Saving to Gaia is a separate issue.</li><li>Add a decision record to <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>: collab is separate from the relay and holds state per document. Bind the port from config, and add the compose service.</li><li>In-process Node tests with a stubbed Gaia (as in D-015): refused token, read-only when locked, two clients see each other's updates.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two browser clients with valid tokens share updates live; a locked doc or a user without update rights cannot change it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> saving to Gaia, per-doc sharing roles, comments.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["docs-adr"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "collab-store", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Collab: load and save Docs content through Gaia with the collab service account", "description": "<p>The collab server (<code>collab/</code>) holds documents in memory only. Make it load and save them through Gaia, so content survives restarts and Gaia keeps the HTML and full-text copies for search and display.</p><ul><li>Add <code>@hocuspocus/transformer</code> and the Tiptap extensions that make up the Docs editor schema (StarterKit, Table, TaskList/TaskItem, Image, Link). This list is a contract with Prometheus' Docs editor and must stay identical.</li><li>Load: read <code>Doc.content</code> (base64 Yjs) as the service account. When it is null and <code>body</code> has HTML, seed the Y document from that HTML through the shared schema.</li><li>Save: debounced (a few seconds of quiet) and when the last client leaves, PATCH <code>content</code>, <code>body</code> (HTML) and <code>bodyText</code> as the service account. The credentials come from env only.</li><li>A failed save is logged and retried on the next change. It never drops the in-memory document.</li><li>Tests with a stubbed Gaia: load from content, seed from legacy body, save after debounce, failed save retried.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> edit a doc, restart the server, reopen it, and the content is unchanged. A search on the doc's text in Gaia finds it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> version snapshots, editor UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["collab-server", "doc-content-fields"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-editor", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Tiptap collaborative editor bound to the collab server, with offline recovery", "description": "<p>Docs moves from whole-document saves to live co-editing. Replace body editing on the Doc page with a Tiptap editor bound to a Yjs document that syncs through the collab server. This is for Docs only; Toast UI stays in use everywhere else.</p><ul><li>Add the dependencies <code>@tiptap/core</code> with the extensions StarterKit, Table, TaskList/TaskItem, Image (by URL for now), Link and Collaboration, plus <code>yjs</code>, <code>@hocuspocus/provider</code> and <code>y-indexeddb</code>.</li><li>The extension list is a contract with the collab server's schema and must stay identical.</li><li>New component <code>Docs::Editor</code>:<ul><li>Opens a <code>HocuspocusProvider</code> for the doc id, passing the session token. The collab URL comes from <code>config/environment.js</code>.</li><li>Keeps a <code>y-indexeddb</code> copy, so edits made offline merge on reconnect.</li><li>Has a formatting toolbar in the design system's style and an outline built from the headings.</li><li>Is read-only (the Viewing mode) when the server says so.</li></ul></li><li>Show the save state in the box header: Saved, Saving, Offline (changes kept on this device).</li><li>No save button and no PATCH of <code>body</code> from the UI.</li><li>Add integration tests for the component with a stubbed provider: read-only mode, status label, toolbar commands.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two browsers editing the same doc see each other's changes; going offline, editing and reconnecting keeps the edits; a locked doc opens read-only. Follow <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> Suggesting mode, comments, uploaded images, presence/cursors.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["collab-server"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-presence", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: who's here avatars, live cursors and selections, and typing indicator", "description": "<p>People co-editing a doc need to see each other. Use Yjs awareness on the existing <code>Docs::Editor</code> connection. It is not saved and doesn't touch Gaia or Hermes.</p><ul><li>Add the Tiptap CollaborationCursor extension. It publishes the user's name, avatar URL (<code>userimage/get</code>) and a colour picked from existing <code>variables.scss</code> colours by user id.</li><li>Show live cursors and selections with name labels.</li><li>Add an avatar stack in the doc box header of everyone connected, with a tooltip of their name. Your own avatar comes first.</li><li>Add an \\"is typing\\" indicator: an awareness field set while the user types and cleared after about 3 seconds idle, shown as a line under the header.</li><li>Add integration tests with a stubbed awareness: avatars rendered, typing line shown and hidden.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with two browsers, each sees the other's avatar, cursor and selection live; the typing line appears and disappears. Square edges, colours from the design system only.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> online status outside Docs, presence on the All Docs list.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-editor"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-11 15:12:53	2026-11-11 15:12:53	f
46d842866ae5-4d5d-ae8f-beedf12089a3	d87ad5636ae5-1449-ae8f-5808a9dddbf1	1	{"summary": "Fix Gaia's token preview endpoint (/preview/get/<token>), which crashes for every upload and also has an injection and inline-HTML risk. In parallel, open idea screens in a modal on the idea page instead of a new tab. With both done, a screen shows inline and opens full size in place.", "issues": [{"key": "preview-fix", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Preview: fix /preview/get/<token> (missing Downloadtoken import, upload lookup, bound token, images only)", "description": "<p>Every <code>GET /preview/get/&lt;token&gt;</code> fails with <code>Class 'Gaia\\\\MVC\\\\REST\\\\Controllers\\\\Downloadtoken' not found</code> (<code>app/api/v1/controllers/PreviewController.php:45</code>). Prometheus uses this endpoint to show idea screens, images pasted into idea messages and wiki images, so none of them load. The token is created by the authenticated, ACL-checked <code>GET /upload?id=X&amp;download=true</code> (<code>UploadController::listAction</code>). It is single-use and lasts 10 minutes. That design stays: an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> can't send a Bearer token.</p><ul><li>Add <code>use Gaia\\\\MVC\\\\Models\\\\Downloadtoken;</code>, as in <code>DownloadController</code>.</li><li>Look the token up with a bound parameter. Never put the URL value into the query or <code>find()</code> string.</li><li>Read the <code>readAll()</code> result as <code>DownloadController</code> does (<code>['baseModel']</code>), or use a single bound <code>findFirst</code>.</li><li>Load the upload by the token's <code>uploadId</code>, not through the <code>&lt;relatedTo&gt;Upload</code> relation. <code>Downloadtoken</code> metadata only has <code>issueUpload</code> and <code>wikiUpload</code>, so idea uploads would still fail.</li><li>Serve images only: when <code>fileMime</code> isn't <code>image/*</code>, return the same not-found response as an invalid token. Send <code>Content-Disposition: inline</code> and <code>X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</code>.</li><li>Return the content with <code>setContent</code> and return the response once, as <code>DownloadController</code> does. Drop the <code>readfile</code> + <code>send()</code> double send.</li><li>Keep the token single-use: delete it after a successful response or when it has expired.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong> (start with a failing one): a valid token for an idea upload returns 200 with the image bytes and mime. The same token a second time returns not found. Expired, unknown and non-image tokens return not found. A token containing quotes or query syntax is treated as not found.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the idea page, screens and pasted images load. Wiki images load again.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing token-based access with authenticated blob fetching, and <code>DownloadController</code>'s own unbound queries (log a separate issue).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "screen-modal", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea screens: open the full-size screen in a modal instead of a new tab", "description": "<p>Clicking a screen on the idea page (thread and plan box, both <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code> in <code>components/idea/message-screen.{hbs,js}</code>) opens <code>/preview/get/&lt;token&gt;</code> in a new tab. The engineer wants the preview in a modal on the same page.</p><ul><li>Replace the <code>open</code> action's <code>window.open</code> with a tracked <code>previewOpen</code>. Render the existing <code>bootstrap-modal</code> only while it is set, with the <code>close</code> callback clearing it (pattern: <code>components/idea/conversation-box.hbs</code> ~l.48). Use <code>@removeConfirmBtn={{true}}</code> so only Close shows.</li><li>The modal title is a new translation (e.g. <code>views.app.idea.screen.preview</code>), because <code>bootstrap-modal</code> passes its title through <code>t</code>. The body shows the screen title and version (<code>views.app.idea.conversation.screenVersion</code>), then the image at full width.</li><li>Get a fresh address with <code>uploadPreview.previewUrl(uploadId)</code> each time the modal opens (tokens are single-use, and the inline image already used its own). Show a spinner while it loads, and the <code>fa-picture-o</code> placeholder plus a translated message if it fails. Check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after the await.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code>, scoped by a <code>@containerClass</code> (e.g. <code>idea-screen-modal</code>): a wide dialog (about 90% of the viewport), the image <code>max-width: 100%</code>, the body scrolls for tall screens. Square edges, design-system colours only.</li><li>Tests: an integration test for <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code> with Mirage: a click opens the modal with the image at the preview address, no new tab opens, Close removes the modal, and a failed token shows the placeholder.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the idea page, clicking any screen in a message or in the plan box shows it full size in a modal over the page. Closing it returns to the same place.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> images pasted into messages (<code>modifiers/render-markdown.js</code>, still a new tab), zoom/next/previous, and smaller images for the plan box.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-31 14:20:54	2026-10-31 14:24:21	f
eaa08e266ae6-5efb-935c-ff17a1a6f9db	d87ad5636ae5-1449-ae8f-5808a9dddbf1	2	{"summary": "Fix the idea thread's screen preview modal, which shows the image at thumbnail size, by rendering it outside the conversation thread. The plan box already works. The ideas list collapse and the Brainstorm/Plan switch follow in a later plan, once the screens are approved.", "issues": [{"key": "thread-screen-modal", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea thread: the screen preview modal shows a thumbnail-size image instead of the full screen", "description": "<p>Since aprom-4237, clicking a screen opens <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code>'s preview modal. In the plan box the modal shows the full-size screen. In the conversation thread (Brainstorm) it only shows a thumbnail-size image. Both places use the same component, so the cause is most likely the modal's position on the page, not the image it loads.</p><p><strong>Likely cause (confirm first):</strong> in the thread, the modal is rendered inside the message's <code>.box-comment</code> (<code>ConversationUi::CommentFrame</code> via <code>components/idea/message-item.hbs</code>). <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code> (~l.180 and ~l.232) forces every <code>img</code> in a <code>.box-comment</code> to <code>width: 100% !important; height: 100% !important</code>. <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code> also makes <code>.idea-message-screen</code> 160px wide in the conversation. The plan box isn't inside a comment, so none of this applies there. Check this in the browser before changing anything. If the cause is different, say so in the issue.</p><ul><li>Start with an integration test that fails today: a <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code> rendered inside a <code>.box-comment</code> (as <code>Idea::MessageItem</code> renders it) opens a modal whose image isn't inside the comment or the screen link.</li><li>Render the preview modal outside the thread, e.g. with <code>{{#in-element}}</code> to a target outside the conversation box (Bootstrap modals usually sit at the end of <code>body</code>). Don't add more <code>!important</code> overrides to win against <code>conversation.scss</code>. Don't change <code>conversation.scss</code> either: issue comments rely on it.</li><li>The modal image uses its own class (not <code>idea-message-screen-image</code>), so the inline screen sizes don't apply. Keep the behaviour from aprom-4237: a fresh <code>uploadPreview.previewUrl</code> per opening, spinner, placeholder on failure, Close only, the destroy guards.</li><li>Check the plan box (normal and review mode) still opens the same way.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> clicking a screen in a Nestor message in the thread opens the modal with the full-size screen, the same as from the plan box. Closing it leaves the thread where it was. The ember suite passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> images pasted into messages (<code>render-markdown.js</code>), the inline thumbnail sizes in the thread, and the layout changes for the ideas list and the plan (separate issues).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-31 16:48:42	2026-10-31 16:48:42	f
0b92c2976ae6-76ba-935c-9627b89b6041	d87ad5636ae5-1449-ae8f-5808a9dddbf1	3	{"summary": "Two Prometheus issues for the ideas page, in parallel. First, render the screen preview modal outside the conversation thread, so AdminLTE's 30px comment-image rule no longer shrinks it. Second, replace the ideas list's text collapse buttons with the board's gutter handle. The Brainstorm/Plan divider follows once option C or D is chosen.", "issues": [{"key": "thread-screen-modal", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea thread: the screen preview modal shows a 30px image because it renders inside the comment", "description": "<p>Since aprom-4237, clicking a screen opens <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code>'s preview modal. From the plan box it shows the full-size screen. From the conversation thread (Brainstorm) it shows a tiny image. The cause is confirmed in the browser: in the thread the modal is rendered inside the message's <code>.box-comment</code> (<code>ConversationUi::CommentFrame</code> via <code>components/idea/message-item.hbs</code>). AdminLTE's rule <code>.box-comments .box-comment img, .img-sm, .user-block.user-block-sm img</code> (30px, <code>!important</code>) then applies to the modal image. Prometheus' <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code> (~l.180, ~l.232) adds more <code>!important</code> image rules for comments.</p><ul><li>Start with an integration test that fails today: <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code> rendered inside a <code>.box-comments .box-comment</code> opens a modal whose image is not a descendant of the comment.</li><li>Render the preview modal outside the thread, e.g. <code>{{#in-element}}</code> to a target outside the conversation box (Bootstrap modals usually sit at the end of <code>body</code>). Don't fight the AdminLTE rule with more <code>!important</code> overrides, and don't change <code>conversation.scss</code>: issue comments rely on it.</li><li>Give the modal image its own class (not <code>idea-message-screen-image</code>), so the inline screen sizes don't apply.</li><li>Keep the aprom-4237 behaviour: a fresh <code>uploadPreview.previewUrl</code> per opening, spinner, placeholder on failure, Close only, the isDestroying/isDestroyed guards. The plan box (normal and wide) opens the same way.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> clicking a screen in a Nestor message in the thread opens the modal with the full-size screen, as from the plan box. Closing it leaves the thread where it was. The ember suite passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> images pasted into messages (<code>render-markdown.js</code>), the inline thumbnail sizes, and the ideas page layout.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "list-collapse-handle", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: collapse the ideas list with the board's gutter handle instead of text buttons", "description": "<p>aprom-4224 added a collapse button with a long text label (\\"Hide the ideas list\\") to the ideas browser header, and a separate \\"Show\\" button above the content when collapsed. The engineer wants the small handle that the task board and issue list use between their panels: <code>button.board-panel-divider &gt; span.divider-handle &gt; i.fa-angle-left|right</code> (<code>templates/app/project/board.hbs</code> ~l.45, <code>templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs</code> ~l.231, styles <code>styles/modules/issue.scss</code> ~l.566-608). The attached screen <code>ideas-dividers</code> shows it in the gap between the ideas list and the idea page. That screen also shows a second handle between the conversation and the plan: ignore it, it is a separate issue.</p><ul><li>In <code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>, remove the browser header's collapse button (<code>data-collapse-browser</code>) and the <code>.idea-browser-expand</code> block with its button (<code>data-expand-browser</code>), including the <code>idea-browser-toggle-label</code> spans.</li><li>Put one <code>board-panel-divider</code> button at the top of the outlet column (col-md-9 or col-md-12). It sits in the gutter because Bootstrap columns are <code>position: relative</code>. It shows <code>fa-angle-left</code> when the list is visible and <code>fa-angle-right</code> when it's hidden. Its title comes from the existing <code>views.app.idea.browser.collapse</code>/<code>expand</code> translations, reworded if needed. It calls the existing <code>toggleBrowser</code>. Keep the <code>data-collapse-browser</code>/<code>data-expand-browser</code> attributes on it for the tests.</li><li>Keep the state as is: <code>browserCollapsed</code> on <code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>, saved in localStorage.</li><li>Positioning in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code> under <code>.idea-wrapper</code> (the board's offsets are scoped to <code>.issue-details-container</code>): centred in the gutter when the list shows, flush with the left edge of the content when hidden. Remove the styles of the deleted buttons. Reuse the handle's look as it is.</li><li>Below the md breakpoint the columns stack: always show the list there and hide the handle, so a saved collapsed state can't hide the list on a phone.</li><li>Tests: update <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-browser.feature</code> (and steps): the handle hides the list and widens the content, clicking it again restores it, and the state survives a reload.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the ideas list has no text collapse buttons. A small crimson handle in the gap hides and shows the list, as on the task board. The idea page and New Idea page both follow it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Brainstorm/Plan divider between conversation and plan (separate issue), and squaring the handle's legacy rounded corners.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ideas-dividers"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-10-31 16:57:47	2026-10-31 16:59:12	f
e12e8e076ae8-203f-ed34-3da54639dbe6	48d0b1d36ad9-bd7c-a941-71476aac218e	2	{"summary": "Postgres full-text search driven by model metadata. Gaia framework first: a field-level `search` metadata key that makes the migration build a GIN tsvector expression index per model (agaia, complex), then a MATCHES query operator on the `Model.search` pseudo-field that uses that index with prefix matching and relevance ordering (agaia, complex). Issue's subject and description are then marked searchable (agaia, simple), and the Prometheus header search switches to the new operator (aprom, simple). The chain is sequential because each step needs the previous one.", "issues": [{"key": "search-index", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Metadata: `search` field flag and GIN full-text index in the migration", "description": "<p>Global search runs unindexed <code>LIKE '%q%'</code> scans OR-ed across fields. We want Postgres full-text search, declared in model metadata and created by the database sync. This issue adds the metadata key and the index; the query operator is a separate issue. Schema-machinery change: follow <code>docs/dev/bundles.md</code> §H.</p><ul><li>New optional field key in <code>app/metadata/model/&lt;Model&gt;.php</code>: <code>'search' =&gt; ['weight' =&gt; 'A'|'B'|'C'|'D']</code> (weight defaults to D). Do <strong>not</strong> reuse the legacy <code>fts</code> key (Elasticsearch era, set on far too many fields); leave it untouched.</li><li>One class (e.g. <code>Gaia\\\\Libs\\\\Search\\\\SearchVector</code> under <code>core/libs</code>) that reads a model's metadata and returns its searchable fields and the vector SQL expression, e.g. <code>setweight(to_tsvector('simple', coalesce(\\"subject\\", '')), 'A') || setweight(to_tsvector('simple', coalesce(\\"description\\", '')), 'B')</code>; cast non-text fields to text. The query operator issue reuses this class, so the index and the query use exactly the same expression.</li><li>Migration: for a model with searchable fields, create a GIN expression index <code>{table}_search</code> with <code>CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ... USING GIN (&lt;expression&gt;)</code>, both for new tables (<code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> <code>migrateTable</code>) and existing ones (<code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> next to <code>syncIndexes</code>). When the searchable field set or weights change, drop and recreate the index (compare against <code>pg_indexes.indexdef</code> or a hash in the index name). When no fields are searchable any more, drop it.</li><li>Use an expression index, not a stored tsvector column: <code>syncExistingTable</code> drops columns missing from metadata and the ORM would expose the column.</li><li>Dictionary <code>'simple'</code> (no stemming: works for code, ids and any language). Built into Postgres, so <code>prepare-test-db.sh</code> needs no new extension.</li><li>Test the migration only in a throwaway <code>gaia-gaia-test</code> container mounting this checkout (recipe in <code>dev-tools/CLAUDE.md</code>); never <code>p4m db migrate</code> from Pr4M, as gaia-dev mounts another checkout and a stale migrate drops columns.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a model with <code>search</code> fields gets the GIN index on a fresh and on an existing database; re-running migrate is a no-op; changing a weight recreates the index; unit tests for the expression builder; existing tables and indexes unaffected.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the query operator, marking real models searchable, pg_trgm/typo tolerance, removing the <code>fts</code> key.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-operator", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Query language: MATCHES operator for full-text search with relevance order", "description": "<p>Lets API clients search all searchable fields of a model at once with the GIN index from the metadata <code>search</code> key, instead of OR-ing <code>CONTAINS</code> clauses.</p><ul><li>New operator in <code>core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php</code> <code>prepareWhere</code> on the pseudo-field <code>&lt;Model&gt;.search</code>: <code>((Issue.search MATCHES 'logi bug'))</code>. Reject it with a clear error for models without searchable fields or on any other field.</li><li>Build the tsquery from user input: split on whitespace, drop tsquery special characters, each word becomes a prefix term joined with AND (<code>logi:* &amp; bug:*</code>), via <code>to_tsquery('simple', :param)</code>. Input that is empty after cleaning is a validation error, not a match-all. The value <strong>must be a bound parameter</strong>, never concatenated (the existing operators concatenate; don't copy that).</li><li>Match with the exact vector expression from the <code>SearchVector</code> class of the index issue so the planner uses the <code>{table}_search</code> index. PHQL can't express <code>@@</code>: decide between an inlinable <code>LANGUAGE sql IMMUTABLE</code> wrapper function created through the metadata <code>functions</code> / <code>migrateFunctions</code> mechanism and another route, and verify with <code>EXPLAIN</code> that the GIN index is used.</li><li>Ordering: when a MATCHES clause is present and the request has no <code>sort</code>, order by <code>ts_rank(vector, query)</code> descending; an explicit <code>sort</code> wins.</li><li>Works together with other clauses (<code>AND</code>/<code>OR</code>), <code>rels</code>, paging and the existing ACL/project scoping, which must still apply.</li><li>Document the operator in the <code>Clause.php</code> docblock list.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for tsquery building (special characters, empty input, quotes); EXPLAIN on a seeded table shows a bitmap index scan on the GIN index; results ordered by rank; injection attempts are inert.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> typo tolerance, highlighting/snippets, fixing the concatenation in the existing operators.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-index"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "issue-searchable", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Issues: make subject and description full-text searchable", "description": "<p>Apply the new metadata <code>search</code> key to Issue so the header global search can use <code>Issue.search MATCHES</code>.</p><ul><li><code>app/metadata/model/Issue.php</code>: <code>subject</code> gets <code>'search' =&gt; ['weight' =&gt; 'A']</code>, <code>description</code> gets <code>'search' =&gt; ['weight' =&gt; 'B']</code>. Leave the legacy <code>fts</code> keys alone.</li><li>Migrate in a throwaway <code>gaia-gaia-test</code> container (not <code>p4m db migrate</code> from Pr4M); the <code>issues_search</code> GIN index is created.</li><li><code>tools/api-tester</code> <code>client.json</code> cases: <code>GET /issue?query=((Issue.search MATCHES 'word'))</code> finds by subject word, by description word and by word prefix; subject hits rank above description-only hits; a user only gets issues from projects they can access (ACL case).</li></ul><p><strong>Contract:</strong> new query capability Prometheus will use (<code>Issue.search MATCHES</code>); no change to the resource shape.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other models (projects, wiki, comments).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-operator"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "header-search", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Header global search: use full-text MATCHES query", "description": "<p>The header search ORs three <code>CONTAINS</code> clauses (unindexed LIKE scans, no ranking). Gaia now supports <code>((Issue.search MATCHES 'q'))</code> over subject and description, with prefix matching and relevance order.</p><ul><li><code>app/components/app-layouts/application-header.js</code> <code>loadSearchData</code>: query <code>((Issue.search MATCHES 'q'))</code>; when the input is a whole number, OR it with <code>(Issue.issueNumber : q)</code> so issue numbers still work. Escape apostrophes in the input as the Gaia query language requires (<code>\\\\'</code>). Skip the request for blank input.</li><li>Don't send <code>sort</code>, so Gaia returns results by relevance. Keep the limit of 5, <code>rels</code>, the 500 ms debounce and result formatting as they are.</li><li>In the <code>search</code> task, check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after the request resolves before touching component state.</li><li>Update the Mirage handler for <code>GET /issue</code> to understand the MATCHES clause (simple substring match on subject/description is enough) and adjust the acceptance test of the global search.</li></ul><p><strong>Contract:</strong> depends on Gaia's new <code>Issue.search MATCHES</code> query operator; no resource change.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> typing part of a word finds issues by subject or description; typing an issue number finds that issue; the acceptance test passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> searching other modules, a full results page, highlighting.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 07:46:41	2026-11-02 07:46:41	f
623782116ae8-162c-ab99-6b44aab5fad8	ab9b79d46ae8-749b-ab99-c04ee42421fc	3	{"summary": "Make the issue detail page live for status, assignee and comments, with a Messenger toast when another user changes the status or assignee or adds or edits a comment. Gaia already publishes issue.status.changed, issue.assignee.changed and conversation.comment.created/updated/deleted for the issue's conversation room, and Hermes allows all of them, so this is one Prometheus issue: the issue page registers Hermes intents on enter, disposes them on exit, ignores events for other issues and rooms, and updates the page in place. The live activity list is left out for now.", "issues": [{"key": "issue-detail-live", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue detail: live status, assignee and comments with Messenger toasts", "description": "<p>While a user has an issue's detail page open, status, assignee and comment changes made by other users (or agents) only appear after a reload. Gaia and Hermes already publish everything needed, so only the issue page needs to subscribe. Follow the existing screen pattern (<code>docs/architecture/live-updates/</code>). The closest example is <code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>, which only handles events for the open idea.</p><p><strong>Events (no contract change):</strong></p><ul><li><code>issue.status.changed</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the issue id. <code>changes</code> may carry <code>status</code>, <code>statusId</code> or both. Changes made through the gaia MCP client send only <code>statusId</code>.</li><li><code>issue.assignee.changed</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the issue id. <code>changes</code> carries the new assignee id (check <code>IssueLiveEventsComponent</code> for the field name).</li><li><code>conversation.comment.created</code> / <code>updated</code> / <code>deleted</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the comment id. <code>meta.conversationId</code> (also <code>changes.relatedId</code>) is the room id. Issue comments are posted to the issue's room (<code>issue-details.js</code> <code>_createComment</code>, relatedId <code>issue.conversationRoomId</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Changes:</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/controllers/app/project/issue/page.js</code>: inject <code>hermes</code> and <code>currentUser</code>. Add <code>registerHermesIntents(projectId)</code> / <code>unregisterHermesIntents()</code> with a disposer, as in <code>idea/page.js</code>. Event names are literals at the register site (D-005).</li><li>Status handler: apply only when <code>resource.id</code> is the open issue. Set <code>statusId</code> and <code>status</code>. When only <code>statusId</code> is sent, take the name from <code>issueStatuses</code>. Don't save the record.</li><li>Assignee handler: same issue check. Set <code>assignedTo</code> from the store, using <code>findRecord('user', id)</code> when the user isn't loaded. A null id clears the assignee.</li><li>Comment handlers: apply only when the room id equals <code>issue.conversationRoomId</code>.<ul><li>Created: <code>store.findRecord('comment', id)</code>, then add it to <code>issue.comments</code> once (guard by id).</li><li>Updated: reload that comment if it is listed.</li><li>Deleted: remove it from the list and unload it.</li></ul>Use the handlers in <code>controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code> (~line 1139) as reference.</li><li>Toasts: when <code>envelope.actorId</code> is set and is not the current user, post <code>new Messenger().post({message, type: 'info', showCloseButton: true})</code>, the pattern already used in <code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code>:<ul><li>\\"&lt;user&gt; changed the status to &lt;status&gt;\\"</li><li>\\"&lt;user&gt; assigned this issue to &lt;user&gt;\\"</li><li>\\"&lt;user&gt; commented\\" / \\"&lt;user&gt; edited a comment\\"</li></ul>No toast for deletes. Take the actor's name from the store (or <code>createdUserName</code> on comments). Put every string in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>After every <code>await</code> in a handler, check that the controller isn't destroyed and that the same issue is still open. Catch failures: log them, leave the page unchanged, and show no toast.</li><li><code>app/routes/app/project/issue/page.js</code>: register in <code>setupController</code> with the tracked project id. Unregister on exit (<code>resetController</code>) and when moving to another issue.</li><li>Docs: in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/architecture.md</code>, add the issue page row to the \\"Which screens register which events\\" table and remove issue detail from the \\"not live\\" line. In <code>decisions.md</code>, change D-011 so the issue page is no longer silent (its activity list stays silent), and add a decision: the issue page shows a Messenger toast for changes made by other actors, never for its own.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong> (Mirage + Fake Hermes, D-012):</p><ul><li>QUnit tests for the controller handlers:<ul><li>status and assignee are applied for the open issue and ignored for another issue;</li><li>a <code>statusId</code>-only change resolves the name;</li><li>a comment is added once and ignored for another room; update and delete are applied;</li><li>a toast appears only when the actor is someone else;</li><li>a failed <code>findRecord</code> leaves the page unchanged.</li></ul></li><li>One Yadda acceptance scenario: open an issue, inject status, assignee and comment envelopes from another user, and see the changes and the toasts. Steps used only by this feature go in a per-feature steps file, not in <code>steps.js</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong></p><ul><li>With an issue open, a status (including a <code>statusId</code>-only change), assignee or comment change made elsewhere shows without a reload, with no duplicates.</li><li>Changes by another user show a Messenger toast; the user's own changes don't.</li><li>Events for other issues or rooms change nothing. Leaving the page removes its intents.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the live activity list, dates and other issue fields, the issue list page, and any change to Gaia or Hermes.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 13:38:42	2026-11-02 13:38:42	f
83ce93666ae8-8685-9cef-432b5207bd20	395e4ef26ae8-8685-9cef-2a937ce05de0	1	{"summary": "One dev-tools change: after Agent Odysseus opens a PR (workflow.open_pr, used by both `ai pr` and `ai ship`), it posts an `@coderabbitai full review` comment on PRs in the repos listed in codeRabbitRepos, so CodeRabbit reviews every agent PR.", "issues": [{"key": "rabbit-trigger", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "ai: comment \\"@coderabbitai full review\\" on every new agent PR in CodeRabbit repos", "description": "<p>CodeRabbit doesn't review agent PRs on its own; it needs a <code>@coderabbitai full review</code> comment on the PR. Without that comment the bot-review loop (<code>ai/lib/coderabbit.py</code>, <code>talos/lib/bot_review.py</code>) waits for a review that never starts. Agents should post the comment themselves every time they open a PR.</p><ul><li>Add <code>\\"codeRabbitTrigger\\": \\"@coderabbitai full review\\"</code> to <code>dev-tools/ai/config.json</code>. An empty value or a missing key turns the trigger off.</li><li>In <code>dev-tools/ai/lib/workflow.py</code> <code>open_pr</code>: after <code>gh pr create</code> succeeds, if <code>coderabbit.enabled(repo)</code> and the trigger is set, post the trigger as a PR comment as Agent Odysseus (<code>ody(repo, \\"gh\\", \\"pr\\", \\"comment\\", url, \\"--repo\\", REPOS[repo], \\"--body\\", trigger)</code>). Print <code>say(\\"CodeRabbit: requested full review\\")</code>. Watch for an import cycle (<code>coderabbit</code> imports <code>review</code>); import it inside the function if needed.</li><li>If the comment fails, print a warning and keep going. The PR is already open, so the handoff must still finish.</li><li>Both <code>ai pr</code> (<code>cmd_pr</code>) and <code>ai ship</code> (<code>ship.py</code> <code>cmd_ship</code>) go through <code>open_pr</code>, so both get the comment. When <code>ai ship</code> resumes and finds a PR it opened earlier (<code>existing_pr</code>), it doesn't post the comment again.</li><li>Unit tests in <code>dev-tools/ai/tests/</code> with <code>ody</code> mocked: the comment is posted for an enabled repo; it isn't posted for a disabled repo (e.g. ares) or when the trigger is empty; a failed comment still returns the PR URL.</li><li>Document the behaviour and the <code>codeRabbitTrigger</code> key in <code>dev-tools/ai/README.md</code>, where CodeRabbit is described.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a PR opened with <code>ai ship</code> or <code>ai pr</code> in gaia, prometheus or hermes has exactly one <code>@coderabbitai full review</code> comment from Agent Odysseus, and CodeRabbit starts a review. A PR in ares has no comment. <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> posting the trigger again after later pushes (CodeRabbit's incremental reviews handle those); changes to the bot-review polling.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 08:32:03	2026-11-02 08:34:07	f
09c8c9116ae8-20b5-ab99-e626ce692687	a43af2e76ae8-162c-ab99-d45c339909fd	1	{"summary": "Make the 'Agent Nestor is working on it' line a temporary, animated indicator. Talos posts the working notice with its own message kind 'working' instead of 'system', so it can be told apart from real notices. Prometheus shows a working message (and the old 'system' version of the line, for existing threads) as an animated typing indicator, and hides it as soon as a later message exists. The two issues are independent and can go in parallel.", "issues": [{"key": "talos-working-kind", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos ideas: post the working notice with message kind 'working'", "description": "<p>When Talos starts a turn on a Gaia idea it posts \\"&lt;Agent&gt; is working on it.\\" as an idea message of kind <code>system</code>. Other real notices also use <code>system</code> (e.g. from <code>lib/ideas/approval.py</code>), so the UI can't tell this temporary status apart from them. Prometheus wants to show it as an animated indicator and hide it once the reply arrives, which needs a dedicated kind.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/ideas/client.py</code> <code>set_state</code>: post the notice with role/kind <code>working</code> instead of <code>system</code> (the body stays \\"&lt;display name&gt; is working on it.\\"). Update the module docstring that describes the kinds.</li><li>Check that nothing in <code>lib/ideas/</code> (<code>policy.py</code>, <code>conversation.py</code>) treats the new kind as a user or agent message: turns start only on <code>kind: message</code>, and history replays only the <code>user</code>/<code>agent</code> roles.</li><li><code>talos/tests/test_gaia_ideas.py</code>: update the expectations that assert <code>(\\"system\\", \\"Agent Nestor is working on it.\\")</code> and add a test that a <code>working</code> message neither starts a turn nor shows up in the replayed history.</li><li><code>talos/README.md</code> (Idea client section): say that the turn starts with a <code>kind: working</code> notice.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a new turn on a Gaia idea posts one message with kind <code>working</code>; replies, errors and approval notices keep their current kinds; <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the sim client, live progress events, any Gaia change (<code>Ideamessage.kind</code> is free text).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "idea-working-indicator", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: animated 'working on it' indicator that disappears when the reply arrives", "description": "<p>On the idea page the agent's \\"Agent Nestor is working on it.\\" line stays in the thread forever as an info notice, which clutters the conversation. It should look like a live typing indicator while the agent works and go away once its reply (or any later message) arrives. Talos will post this notice with message kind <code>working</code>. Existing threads have it as kind <code>system</code>.</p><ul><li><code>components/idea/message-item.{js,hbs}</code>: add an <code>isWorking</code> state for kind <code>working</code>, and for legacy kind <code>system</code> messages whose body ends with <code>is working on it.</code>. Render it as a compact row with the author's avatar/name (<code>createdUserName</code>), the translated text \\"{name} is working on it\\" and three animated dots, instead of the info notice. Give it <code>aria-busy=\\"true\\"</code> / <code>role=\\"status\\"</code>.</li><li><code>components/idea/conversation-box.js</code>: leave working messages out of <code>orderedMessages</code> unless they are the last message in the thread, so a superseded indicator disappears and only the newest one shows while the agent is working. This updates live because the page already reloads messages on <code>idea.message.created</code>.</li><li>Dots: reuse the <code>comment-posting-dot</code> keyframes from <code>styles/_animations.scss</code> (as used by <code>.comment-posting-dots</code> in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code>). Scope any new class under the idea module's styles. Square edges, existing colours only, per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</li><li>Translation in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: integration tests for <code>Idea::MessageItem</code> (working and legacy-system render the indicator; other system notices and errors render as before) and <code>Idea::ConversationBox</code> (a working message followed by a reply is hidden; a working message that is last is shown). Add a Mirage fixture with a <code>working</code> message if the acceptance tests need one.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> while the agent works, the thread ends with an animated \\"Agent Nestor is working on it\\" row. When the reply arrives (live or after refresh), the row is gone. Old threads no longer show the stale lines. Other system notices and errors look unchanged. Lint and tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming progress text or steps, a timeout for an agent that stopped mid-turn, any Gaia or Hermes change.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 13:41:29	2026-11-02 13:41:29	f
4dcc90a56ae8-042c-3709-e9715bfa8eb1	ca4b85356ae8-4b25-04c3-5f32a380596a	1	{"summary": "Stop two Talos processes from running at once. Duplicate processes made every idea message get two Nestor replies and could make Odysseus/Agamemnon pick up the same work twice. `talos run` takes an exclusive OS file lock in the shared state folder, using the existing installer/filelock.py helper, and a second instance refuses to start and names the one already running. One dev-tools issue; the atomic Nestor turn claim is left for later.", "issues": [{"key": "talos-run-lock", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: allow only one `talos run` per workspace (single-instance lock)", "description": "<p>Nothing stops a second <code>talos run</code> from starting while one is already running. On 2026-11-02 two instances ran side by side from 15:39 (talos.log has a <code>[talos] starting</code> with no <code>stopped</code> before it). Every agent then worked each event twice: Nestor posted two answers to one idea message, and both instances ran Agamemnon and the Hermes listeners. Each instance only removes duplicates from its own in-memory queue (<code>lib/ideas/worker.py</code> <code>IdeaWorker._pending</code>), so the guard has to cover the whole process.</p><ul><li>In <code>talos/talos.py</code> <code>cmd_run</code>, take an exclusive lock before any other work (before <code>db.import_legacy()</code> and the workspace gc) and hold it until the command returns. Use <code>installer/filelock.py</code> <code>held(path, wait_seconds=0)</code>, the lock every dev tool already uses (msvcrt on Windows, fcntl elsewhere; the OS drops it when the holder dies; it writes the holder's PID).</li><li>Lock file: <code>STATE_DIR / \\"talos-run.lock\\"</code> (from <code>lib/config.py</code>). <code>STATE_DIR</code> comes from <code>LOCAL_DIR</code>, so the runtime copy (<code>.dev-tools-runtime</code>) and the <code>dev-tools/</code> checkout share it.</li><li>If the lock is held, catch <code>filelock.LockTimeout</code> and fail with a <code>TalosError</code> such as <code>Talos is already running (pid N (command line)); stop it first</code>, using <code>filelock.describe_holder</code>. Exit non-zero and don't write a <code>[talos] starting</code> line.</li><li><code>--dry-run</code> takes the lock as well: its dispatchers and listeners still react to events.</li><li>Other subcommands (<code>runs</code>, <code>pause</code>, status, etc.) don't take the lock.</li><li>README: one line in the run section saying only one <code>talos run</code> per workspace is allowed and what the error means.</li><li>Tests (OS-independent, temp dir with STATE_DIR patched): a second <code>cmd_run</code> while the lock is held raises <code>TalosError</code> naming the holder's PID; after the holder releases the lock, <code>cmd_run</code> takes it again. Stub out agent loading and the sleep loop so the test doesn't start listeners.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with <code>talos run</code> running, a second <code>talos run</code> (from either the runtime copy or the checkout) exits at once with the running instance's PID and command line; after the first is stopped or killed, <code>talos run</code> starts normally; this works on Linux and Windows; <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> an atomic Nestor turn claim (claiming <code>answered_upto</code> before a turn) and locks for other long-running tools.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 12:30:05	2026-11-02 12:38:19	f
12c193936ae8-a030-ab99-f6982c48715b	ab9b79d46ae8-749b-ab99-c04ee42421fc	1	{"summary": "Make the issue detail page live for status and comments. Gaia and Hermes already publish everything needed (issue.status.changed, and conversation.comment.created/updated/deleted for the issue's conversation room), so this is a single Prometheus issue: the issue page registers Hermes intents on enter and disposes them on exit. Handlers ignore events for other issues and other rooms and update the page in place. The live-updates docs change to record that the issue page is now live.", "issues": [{"key": "issue-detail-live", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue detail: live status and comment updates via Hermes", "description": "<p>While a user has an issue's detail page open, status changes and comments made by other users (or agents) only appear after a reload. Gaia already publishes the events needed, and Hermes already allows them, so only the issue page needs to subscribe. The page follows the existing screen pattern (<code>docs/architecture/live-updates/</code>), with the idea page (<code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>) as the closest example: it only handles events for the entity that is open.</p><p><strong>Events (no contract change):</strong></p><ul><li><code>issue.status.changed</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the issue id. <code>changes</code> may carry <code>status</code>, <code>statusId</code> or both. Status changes made through the gaia MCP client send only <code>statusId</code>.</li><li><code>conversation.comment.created</code> / <code>updated</code> / <code>deleted</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the comment id. <code>meta.conversationId</code> (also <code>changes.relatedId</code>) is the room id. Issue comments are posted to the issue's room (<code>issue-details.js</code> <code>_createComment</code>, relatedId <code>issue.conversationRoomId</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Changes:</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/controllers/app/project/issue/page.js</code>: inject <code>hermes</code>. Add <code>registerHermesIntents(projectId)</code> / <code>unregisterHermesIntents()</code> with a disposer, as in <code>idea/page.js</code>. Event names are literals at the register site (D-005).</li><li>Status handler: apply only when <code>resource.id</code> equals the open issue's id. Update the issue's <code>statusId</code> and <code>status</code>. When only <code>statusId</code> is sent, take the name from <code>issueStatuses</code>. Don't re-save the record.</li><li>Comment handlers: apply only when the room id equals <code>issue.conversationRoomId</code>.<ul><li>Created: load the comment with <code>store.findRecord('comment', id)</code> and add it to <code>issue.comments</code> with no duplicate (this tab's own echo is already dropped by <code>noteLocalWrite</code>; still guard by id).</li><li>Updated: reload that comment if it is in the list.</li><li>Deleted: remove it from the list and unload it.</li></ul>Use the handlers in <code>controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code> (~line 1139) as reference, but don't share code with them.</li><li>After every <code>await</code> in a handler, check that the controller isn't destroyed and that the same issue is still open, since the user may have moved to another issue. Catch failures: log them, don't break the page.</li><li><code>app/routes/app/project/issue/page.js</code>: register in <code>setupController</code> with the tracked project id. Unregister in <code>resetController</code> / on exit, and when moving to another issue.</li><li>Docs: in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/architecture.md</code>, add the issue page row to the \\"Which screens register which events\\" table and remove issue detail from the \\"not live\\" line. In <code>decisions.md</code>, change D-011 so the issue page is no longer listed as silent (issue list, wiki and activity stay silent), and update the open question.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong> (Mirage + Fake Hermes, D-012):</p><ul><li>QUnit tests for the controller handlers:<ul><li>status applied for the open issue and ignored for another issue;</li><li>a <code>statusId</code>-only change resolves the status name;</li><li>a comment is added once and ignored for another room;</li><li>update and delete are applied;</li><li>a failed <code>findRecord</code> leaves the page as it was.</li></ul></li><li>One Yadda acceptance scenario: open an issue, inject a status change and a comment envelope, see both on the page. Steps used only by this feature go in a per-feature steps file, not in <code>steps.js</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong></p><ul><li>With an issue open, a status change made elsewhere (including a <code>statusId</code>-only change) shows the new status without a reload.</li><li>A comment added, edited or deleted elsewhere appears, changes or disappears without a reload, with no duplicates.</li><li>Events for other issues or rooms change nothing. Leaving the page removes its intents.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> assignee, dates and other issue fields; the activity list; the issue list page; a notice or toast for new comments; changes to Gaia or Hermes.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 13:33:06	2026-11-02 13:33:06	f
032f5db06ae8-162c-ab99-78db5d55cf44	ab9b79d46ae8-749b-ab99-c04ee42421fc	2	{"summary": "Make the issue detail page live: status, assignee, comments and the activity list, with a Messenger toast when another user changes the status or assignee or adds or edits a comment. Status, assignee and comment events already exist, so aprom 'issue-detail-live' can start now. Activity needs a new event: Gaia publishes issue.activity.created from an Activity model hook (covering status, time log, attachment and mention activities), and Hermes adds the name to its allowlist. Those two ship together. aprom 'issue-detail-activity-live' then adds the activity handler to the issue page once all three are done.", "issues": [{"key": "activity-event", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Live events: publish issue.activity.created when an issue activity row is saved", "description": "<p>The issue detail page in Prometheus is becoming live, and its activity list needs an event when a new activity row is added to an issue. Activity rows are created by several request components: <code>IssueactivitiesComponent</code> (issue created, status changed), <code>TimeloggedComponent</code>, <code>FileattachmentComponent</code> and <code>IssuementionComponent</code>. All of them create <code>Activity</code> with <code>relatedTo = 'issue'</code>. None of them publishes a live event today. Publishing from the model covers every source in one place, the same way <code>Systemnotificationrecipient::afterCreate</code> uses <code>NotificationLiveEvents</code> (decision D-004).</p><p><strong>Changes:</strong></p><ul><li><code>support/EventNames.php</code>: add <code>ISSUE_ACTIVITY_CREATED = 'issue.activity.created'</code> to the constants and to <code>ALL</code>.</li><li>New <code>app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/IssueActivityLiveEvents.php</code>, modelled on <code>NotificationLiveEvents</code>. Method <code>publishCreated($activity)</code> publishes only when <code>relatedTo</code> is <code>issue</code> or <code>issues</code> and the row has an id and a <code>relatedId</code>. The envelope:<ul><li><code>projectId</code>: from <code>ProjectIdResolver</code> (relatedTo issue).</li><li><code>resource</code>: <code>{type: 'activity', id}</code>.</li><li><code>actorId</code>: the row's <code>createdUser</code>.</li><li><code>changes</code>: <code>type</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>relatedActivity</code>, <code>relatedActivityId</code>, <code>relatedActivityModule</code>, <code>createdUser</code>, <code>createdUserName</code>, <code>dateCreated</code>.</li><li><code>meta</code>: <code>{issueId: relatedId}</code>.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/models/Activity.php</code>: add <code>afterCreate()</code> that calls <code>publishCreated</code> inside try/catch and logs failures. It must fail open: a Hermes error never fails the write that created the activity (D-002).</li><li>Docs: in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/architecture.md</code>, add the Activity row to the \\"Model hook\\" table and remove \\"activity rows are not live-synced\\". In <code>decisions.md</code>, add a decision: issue activity rows publish <code>issue.activity.created</code> from the model hook; project activities (<code>relatedTo 'project'</code>) do not.</li><li>Tests: <code>tests/api/controllers/components/events/LiveEventsComponentsTest.php</code> (or a new test next to it):<ul><li>publishes for an issue activity, with the expected envelope fields;</li><li>skips project activities and rows without a <code>relatedId</code>;</li><li>a publisher exception is swallowed.</li></ul>Add a live api-tester case in <code>tools/api-tester/apis/live.json</code>: a status PATCH also produces <code>issue.activity.created</code>.</li><li>Regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> and the graph as CI requires.</li></ul><p><strong>Contract:</strong> new event name <code>issue.activity.created</code>. Hermes must add the same name to <code>src/contract/names.js</code> (linked Hermes issue). Merge the two PRs together.</p><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong></p><ul><li>Changing an issue's status, logging time, attaching a file or mentioning an issue each publishes one <code>issue.activity.created</code> for that issue's project.</li><li>Project-level activities publish nothing.</li><li>A Hermes outage doesn't fail any of those writes.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> update or delete events for activities, project activities, and changes to how activities are created.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "activity-allowlist", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Contract: allow issue.activity.created", "description": "<p>Gaia will publish a new domain event, <code>issue.activity.created</code>, when an activity row is added to an issue, so that the Prometheus issue page can update its activity list live. Hermes rejects names that are not on its allowlist, so the name has to be added there.</p><ul><li><code>src/contract/names.js</code>: add <code>'issue.activity.created'</code> to <code>EVENT_ALLOWLIST</code>. It is project-scoped, so it does not go in <code>USER_SCOPED_EVENTS</code>.</li><li>Extend the contract test that checks the allowlist (or add one): an <code>intents:set</code> with this name is accepted, and a <code>/publish</code> envelope with it is delivered to the <code>(projectId, issue.activity.created)</code> room.</li><li>While there: if <code>names.js</code> is behind Gaia's <code>EventNames::ALL</code> (for example the <code>idea.*</code> names), report it in the PR. Don't fix it here.</li></ul><p><strong>Envelope</strong> (from Gaia): <code>resource {type: 'activity', id}</code>, <code>meta.issueId</code>, <code>changes</code> with the activity fields. Ships together with the matching Gaia PR.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Hermes accepts intents for <code>issue.activity.created</code> and relays it. Existing names are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any other contract change.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "issue-detail-live", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue detail: live status, assignee and comments with Messenger toasts", "description": "<p>While a user has an issue's detail page open, status, assignee and comment changes made by other users (or agents) only appear after a reload. Gaia and Hermes already publish everything needed, so only the issue page needs to subscribe. Follow the existing screen pattern (<code>docs/architecture/live-updates/</code>). The closest example is <code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>, which only handles events for the open idea.</p><p><strong>Events (no contract change):</strong></p><ul><li><code>issue.status.changed</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the issue id. <code>changes</code> may carry <code>status</code>, <code>statusId</code> or both. Changes made through the gaia MCP client send only <code>statusId</code>.</li><li><code>issue.assignee.changed</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the issue id. <code>changes</code> carries the new assignee id (check <code>IssueLiveEventsComponent</code> for the field name).</li><li><code>conversation.comment.created</code> / <code>updated</code> / <code>deleted</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the comment id. <code>meta.conversationId</code> (also <code>changes.relatedId</code>) is the room id. Issue comments are posted to the issue's room (<code>issue-details.js</code> <code>_createComment</code>, relatedId <code>issue.conversationRoomId</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Changes:</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/controllers/app/project/issue/page.js</code>: inject <code>hermes</code> and <code>currentUser</code>. Add <code>registerHermesIntents(projectId)</code> / <code>unregisterHermesIntents()</code> with a disposer, as in <code>idea/page.js</code>. Event names are literals at the register site (D-005).</li><li>Status handler: apply only when <code>resource.id</code> is the open issue. Set <code>statusId</code> and <code>status</code>. When only <code>statusId</code> is sent, take the name from <code>issueStatuses</code>. Don't save the record.</li><li>Assignee handler: same issue check. Set <code>assignedTo</code> from the store, using <code>findRecord('user', id)</code> when the user isn't loaded. A null id clears the assignee.</li><li>Comment handlers: apply only when the room id equals <code>issue.conversationRoomId</code>.<ul><li>Created: <code>store.findRecord('comment', id)</code>, then add it to <code>issue.comments</code> once (guard by id).</li><li>Updated: reload that comment if it is listed.</li><li>Deleted: remove it from the list and unload it.</li></ul>Use the handlers in <code>controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code> (~line 1139) as reference.</li><li>Toasts: when <code>envelope.actorId</code> is set and is not the current user, post <code>new Messenger().post({message, type: 'info', showCloseButton: true})</code>, the pattern already used in <code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code>:<ul><li>\\"&lt;user&gt; changed the status to &lt;status&gt;\\"</li><li>\\"&lt;user&gt; assigned this issue to &lt;user&gt;\\"</li><li>\\"&lt;user&gt; commented\\" / \\"&lt;user&gt; edited a comment\\"</li></ul>No toast for deletes. Take the actor's name from the store (or <code>createdUserName</code> on comments). Put every string in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>After every <code>await</code> in a handler, check that the controller isn't destroyed and that the same issue is still open. Catch failures: log them, leave the page unchanged, and show no toast.</li><li><code>app/routes/app/project/issue/page.js</code>: register in <code>setupController</code> with the tracked project id. Unregister on exit (<code>resetController</code>) and when moving to another issue.</li><li>Docs: in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/architecture.md</code>, add the issue page row to the \\"Which screens register which events\\" table and remove issue detail from the \\"not live\\" line. In <code>decisions.md</code>, change D-011 so the issue page is no longer silent, and add a decision: the issue page shows a Messenger toast for changes made by other actors, never for its own.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong> (Mirage + Fake Hermes, D-012):</p><ul><li>QUnit tests for the controller handlers:<ul><li>status and assignee are applied for the open issue and ignored for another issue;</li><li>a <code>statusId</code>-only change resolves the name;</li><li>a comment is added once and ignored for another room; update and delete are applied;</li><li>a toast appears only when the actor is someone else;</li><li>a failed <code>findRecord</code> leaves the page unchanged.</li></ul></li><li>One Yadda acceptance scenario: open an issue, inject status, assignee and comment envelopes from another user, and see the changes and the toasts. Steps used only by this feature go in a per-feature steps file, not in <code>steps.js</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong></p><ul><li>With an issue open, a status (including a <code>statusId</code>-only change), assignee or comment change made elsewhere shows without a reload, with no duplicates.</li><li>Changes by another user show a Messenger toast; the user's own changes don't.</li><li>Events for other issues or rooms change nothing. Leaving the page removes its intents.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the activity list (separate issue), dates and other issue fields, the issue list page, and any change to Gaia or Hermes.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "issue-detail-activity-live", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue detail: live activity list via issue.activity.created", "description": "<p>The issue detail page builds its activity list once, when the page loads (<code>routes/app/project/issue/page.js</code> <code>setupActivities</code>, which groups activities by date into <code>controller.activities</code>). Gaia now publishes <code>issue.activity.created</code> when an activity row is added to an issue: status change, time log, attachment or mention. This issue adds the event to the issue page's live handlers, so new activities appear without a reload.</p><p><strong>Event:</strong> <code>issue.activity.created</code>.</p><ul><li><code>resource</code>: <code>{type: 'activity', id}</code>.</li><li><code>meta.issueId</code>: the issue the activity belongs to.</li><li><code>actorId</code>: the user who created it.</li><li><code>changes</code>: <code>type</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>relatedActivity*</code>, <code>createdUser</code>, <code>createdUserName</code>, <code>dateCreated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes:</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/controllers/app/project/issue/page.js</code>: add <code>'issue.activity.created'</code> to the map registered by <code>registerHermesIntents</code>. The handler applies only when <code>meta.issueId</code> is the open issue. It loads the activity with <code>store.findRecord('activity', id)</code> and adds it, once (guard by id), to the right date group in <code>activities</code>, creating the group when it is new. The grouping must then match what <code>setupActivities</code> builds on load, so move that grouping into one helper used by both the route and the handler.</li><li>Apply the event even when it comes from the current user. This tab doesn't add its own activity rows locally, and the adapter's echo suppression keys on the issue, not the activity. No toast: the status, assignee and comment toasts already cover these changes.</li><li>After the <code>await</code>, check that the controller isn't destroyed and that the same issue is still open. On failure, log it and leave the list unchanged.</li><li>Docs: add <code>issue.activity.created</code> to the issue page row in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/architecture.md</code>. In <code>decisions.md</code>, remove activity from the D-011 silent list for the issue page.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests:</strong></p><ul><li>QUnit:<ul><li>an activity for the open issue is added to the right date group, once;</li><li>an activity for another issue is ignored;</li><li>a failed load leaves the list unchanged;</li><li>the shared grouping helper gives the same groups as before.</li></ul></li><li>Acceptance: extend the issue page live feature with an injected activity envelope that appears in the activity list. Add a Mirage handler for <code>activity</code> if there isn't one.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> with an issue open, an activity added elsewhere (status change, time log, attachment, mention) appears in the activity list without a reload, in the right date group, with no duplicates.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> toasts for activities, project activity pages, and activity edits or deletes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["activity-event", "activity-allowlist", "issue-detail-live"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 13:37:07	2026-11-02 13:37:07	f
d675fdb06ae8-fb0c-741d-d063325c5188	a43af2e76ae8-162c-ab99-d45c339909fd	3	{"summary": "Make the 'Agent Nestor is working on it' line a temporary, animated indicator. Talos posts the working notice with its own message kind 'working' instead of 'system', so it can be told apart from real notices. Prometheus shows a working message (and the old 'system' version of the line, for existing threads) as an animated typing indicator, and hides it as soon as a later message exists. The two issues are independent and can go in parallel. Both go in milestone aga-v2.", "issues": [{"key": "talos-working-kind", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos ideas: post the working notice with message kind 'working'", "description": "<p>When Talos starts a turn on a Gaia idea it posts \\"&lt;Agent&gt; is working on it.\\" as an idea message of kind <code>system</code>. Other real notices also use <code>system</code> (e.g. from <code>lib/ideas/approval.py</code>), so the UI can't tell this temporary status apart from them. The idea page needs a dedicated kind to show it as an animated indicator and hide it once the reply arrives.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/ideas/client.py</code> <code>set_state</code>: post the notice with role/kind <code>working</code> instead of <code>system</code> (the body stays \\"&lt;display name&gt; is working on it.\\"). Update the module docstring that describes the kinds.</li><li>Check that nothing in <code>lib/ideas/</code> (<code>policy.py</code>, <code>conversation.py</code>) treats the new kind as a user or agent message: turns start only on <code>kind: message</code>, and history replays only the <code>user</code>/<code>agent</code> roles.</li><li><code>talos/tests/test_gaia_ideas.py</code>: update the expectations that assert <code>(\\"system\\", \\"Agent Nestor is working on it.\\")</code> and add a test that a <code>working</code> message neither starts a turn nor shows up in the replayed history.</li><li><code>talos/README.md</code> (Idea client section): say that the turn starts with a <code>kind: working</code> notice.</li></ul><p><strong>Contract:</strong> idea messages gain the kind <code>working</code>, which the Prometheus idea page renders as a transient indicator. Gaia needs no change (<code>Ideamessage.kind</code> is free text).</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a new turn on a Gaia idea posts one message with kind <code>working</code>; replies, errors and approval notices keep their current kinds; <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the sim client, live progress events.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "idea-working-indicator", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: animated 'working on it' indicator that disappears when the reply arrives", "description": "<p>On the idea page the agent's \\"Agent Nestor is working on it.\\" line stays in the thread forever as an info notice, which clutters the conversation. It should look like a live typing indicator while the agent works and go away once its reply (or any later message) arrives. The agent posts this notice as an idea message of kind <code>working</code>; existing threads have it as kind <code>system</code>.</p><ul><li><code>components/idea/message-item.{js,hbs}</code>: add an <code>isWorking</code> state for kind <code>working</code>, and for legacy kind <code>system</code> messages whose body ends with <code>is working on it.</code>. Render it in the comment layout (<code>ConversationUi::CommentFrame</code>, so the author's avatar and name show, no date) with the translated text \\"{name} is working on it\\" in muted text, followed by three animated dots, instead of the info notice. Give it <code>role=\\"status\\"</code> and <code>aria-busy=\\"true\\"</code>. See the attached screens.</li><li><code>components/idea/conversation-box.js</code>: leave working messages out of <code>orderedMessages</code> unless they are the last message in the thread, so a superseded indicator disappears and only the newest one shows while the agent works. This updates live because the page already reloads messages on <code>idea.message.created</code>.</li><li>Dots: reuse the <code>comment-posting-dot</code> keyframes from <code>styles/_animations.scss</code> (as used by <code>.comment-posting-dots</code> in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code>). Put the new classes in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code> under <code>.idea-page</code>. Square edges, existing colours only, per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</li><li>Translation in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: integration tests for <code>Idea::MessageItem</code> (working and legacy-system render the indicator; other system notices and errors render as before) and <code>Idea::ConversationBox</code> (a working message followed by a reply is hidden; a working message that is last is shown). Add a Mirage fixture with a <code>working</code> message if the acceptance tests need one.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> while the agent works, the thread ends with an animated \\"Agent Nestor is working on it\\" row. When the reply arrives (live or after refresh), the row is gone. Old threads no longer show the stale lines. Other system notices and errors look unchanged. Lint and tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming progress text or steps, a timeout for an agent that stopped mid-turn, any Gaia or Hermes change.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["idea-working", "idea-replied"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 19:13:26	2026-11-02 19:14:08	f
a5e568126ae8-20b5-32a1-368f5dfbef0b	a43af2e76ae8-162c-ab99-d45c339909fd	2	{"summary": "Make the 'Agent Nestor is working on it' line a temporary, animated indicator. Talos posts the working notice with its own message kind 'working' instead of 'system', so it can be told apart from real notices. Prometheus shows a working message (and the old 'system' version of the line, for existing threads) as an animated typing indicator, and hides it as soon as a later message exists. The two issues are independent and can go in parallel.", "issues": [{"key": "talos-working-kind", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos ideas: post the working notice with message kind 'working'", "description": "<p>When Talos starts a turn on a Gaia idea it posts \\"&lt;Agent&gt; is working on it.\\" as an idea message of kind <code>system</code>. Other real notices also use <code>system</code> (e.g. from <code>lib/ideas/approval.py</code>), so the UI can't tell this temporary status apart from them. The idea page needs a dedicated kind to show it as an animated indicator and hide it once the reply arrives.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/ideas/client.py</code> <code>set_state</code>: post the notice with role/kind <code>working</code> instead of <code>system</code> (the body stays \\"&lt;display name&gt; is working on it.\\"). Update the module docstring that describes the kinds.</li><li>Check that nothing in <code>lib/ideas/</code> (<code>policy.py</code>, <code>conversation.py</code>) treats the new kind as a user or agent message: turns start only on <code>kind: message</code>, and history replays only the <code>user</code>/<code>agent</code> roles.</li><li><code>talos/tests/test_gaia_ideas.py</code>: update the expectations that assert <code>(\\"system\\", \\"Agent Nestor is working on it.\\")</code> and add a test that a <code>working</code> message neither starts a turn nor shows up in the replayed history.</li><li><code>talos/README.md</code> (Idea client section): say that the turn starts with a <code>kind: working</code> notice.</li></ul><p><strong>Contract:</strong> idea messages gain the kind <code>working</code>, which the Prometheus idea page renders as a transient indicator. Gaia needs no change (<code>Ideamessage.kind</code> is free text).</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a new turn on a Gaia idea posts one message with kind <code>working</code>; replies, errors and approval notices keep their current kinds; <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the sim client, live progress events.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "idea-working-indicator", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: animated 'working on it' indicator that disappears when the reply arrives", "description": "<p>On the idea page the agent's \\"Agent Nestor is working on it.\\" line stays in the thread forever as an info notice, which clutters the conversation. It should look like a live typing indicator while the agent works and go away once its reply (or any later message) arrives. The agent posts this notice as an idea message of kind <code>working</code>; existing threads have it as kind <code>system</code>.</p><ul><li><code>components/idea/message-item.{js,hbs}</code>: add an <code>isWorking</code> state for kind <code>working</code>, and for legacy kind <code>system</code> messages whose body ends with <code>is working on it.</code>. Render it in the comment layout (<code>ConversationUi::CommentFrame</code>, so the author's avatar and name show, no date) with the translated text \\"{name} is working on it\\" in muted text, followed by three animated dots, instead of the info notice. Give it <code>role=\\"status\\"</code> and <code>aria-busy=\\"true\\"</code>. See the attached screens.</li><li><code>components/idea/conversation-box.js</code>: leave working messages out of <code>orderedMessages</code> unless they are the last message in the thread, so a superseded indicator disappears and only the newest one shows while the agent works. This updates live because the page already reloads messages on <code>idea.message.created</code>.</li><li>Dots: reuse the <code>comment-posting-dot</code> keyframes from <code>styles/_animations.scss</code> (as used by <code>.comment-posting-dots</code> in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code>). Put the new classes in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code> under <code>.idea-page</code>. Square edges, existing colours only, per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</li><li>Translation in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: integration tests for <code>Idea::MessageItem</code> (working and legacy-system render the indicator; other system notices and errors render as before) and <code>Idea::ConversationBox</code> (a working message followed by a reply is hidden; a working message that is last is shown). Add a Mirage fixture with a <code>working</code> message if the acceptance tests need one.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> while the agent works, the thread ends with an animated \\"Agent Nestor is working on it\\" row. When the reply arrives (live or after refresh), the row is gone. Old threads no longer show the stale lines. Other system notices and errors look unchanged. Lint and tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming progress text or steps, a timeout for an agent that stopped mid-turn, any Gaia or Hermes change.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["idea-working", "idea-replied"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 13:44:05	2026-11-02 13:44:05	f
3672fc106ae8-20b5-ab99-c02c482f6828	ab9b79d46ae8-749b-ab99-c04ee42421fc	4	{"summary": "Make the issue detail page live for status, assignee and comments, with a Messenger toast when another user changes the status or assignee or adds or edits a comment. Gaia already publishes issue.status.changed, issue.assignee.changed and conversation.comment.created/updated/deleted for the issue's conversation room, and Hermes allows all of them, so this is one Prometheus issue: the issue page registers Hermes intents on enter, disposes them on exit, ignores events for other issues and rooms, and updates the page in place. The live activity list is left out for now. The issue goes in the new milestone ag-v2.", "issues": [{"key": "issue-detail-live", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue detail: live status, assignee and comments with Messenger toasts", "description": "<p>While a user has an issue's detail page open, status, assignee and comment changes made by other users (or agents) only appear after a reload. Gaia and Hermes already publish everything needed, so only the issue page needs to subscribe. Follow the existing screen pattern (<code>docs/architecture/live-updates/</code>). The closest example is <code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>, which only handles events for the open idea.</p><p><strong>Events (no contract change):</strong></p><ul><li><code>issue.status.changed</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the issue id. <code>changes</code> may carry <code>status</code>, <code>statusId</code> or both. Changes made through the gaia MCP client send only <code>statusId</code>.</li><li><code>issue.assignee.changed</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the issue id. <code>changes</code> carries the new assignee id (check <code>IssueLiveEventsComponent</code> for the field name).</li><li><code>conversation.comment.created</code> / <code>updated</code> / <code>deleted</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the comment id. <code>meta.conversationId</code> (also <code>changes.relatedId</code>) is the room id. Issue comments are posted to the issue's room (<code>issue-details.js</code> <code>_createComment</code>, relatedId <code>issue.conversationRoomId</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Changes:</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/controllers/app/project/issue/page.js</code>: inject <code>hermes</code> and <code>currentUser</code>. Add <code>registerHermesIntents(projectId)</code> / <code>unregisterHermesIntents()</code> with a disposer, as in <code>idea/page.js</code>. Event names are literals at the register site (D-005).</li><li>Status handler: apply only when <code>resource.id</code> is the open issue. Set <code>statusId</code> and <code>status</code>. When only <code>statusId</code> is sent, take the name from <code>issueStatuses</code>. Don't save the record.</li><li>Assignee handler: same issue check. Set <code>assignedTo</code> from the store, using <code>findRecord('user', id)</code> when the user isn't loaded. A null id clears the assignee.</li><li>Comment handlers: apply only when the room id equals <code>issue.conversationRoomId</code>.<ul><li>Created: <code>store.findRecord('comment', id)</code>, then add it to <code>issue.comments</code> once (guard by id).</li><li>Updated: reload that comment if it is listed.</li><li>Deleted: remove it from the list and unload it.</li></ul>Use the handlers in <code>controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code> (~line 1139) as reference.</li><li>Toasts: when <code>envelope.actorId</code> is set and is not the current user, post <code>new Messenger().post({message, type: 'info', showCloseButton: true})</code>, the pattern already used in <code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code>:<ul><li>\\"&lt;user&gt; changed the status to &lt;status&gt;\\"</li><li>\\"&lt;user&gt; assigned this issue to &lt;user&gt;\\"</li><li>\\"&lt;user&gt; commented\\" / \\"&lt;user&gt; edited a comment\\"</li></ul>No toast for deletes. Take the actor's name from the store (or <code>createdUserName</code> on comments). Put every string in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>After every <code>await</code> in a handler, check that the controller isn't destroyed and that the same issue is still open. Catch failures: log them, leave the page unchanged, and show no toast.</li><li><code>app/routes/app/project/issue/page.js</code>: register in <code>setupController</code> with the tracked project id. Unregister on exit (<code>resetController</code>) and when moving to another issue.</li><li>Docs: in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/architecture.md</code>, add the issue page row to the \\"Which screens register which events\\" table and remove issue detail from the \\"not live\\" line. In <code>decisions.md</code>, change D-011 so the issue page is no longer silent (its activity list stays silent), and add a decision: the issue page shows a Messenger toast for changes made by other actors, never for its own.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong> (Mirage + Fake Hermes, D-012):</p><ul><li>QUnit tests for the controller handlers:<ul><li>status and assignee are applied for the open issue and ignored for another issue;</li><li>a <code>statusId</code>-only change resolves the name;</li><li>a comment is added once and ignored for another room; update and delete are applied;</li><li>a toast appears only when the actor is someone else;</li><li>a failed <code>findRecord</code> leaves the page unchanged.</li></ul></li><li>One Yadda acceptance scenario: open an issue, inject status, assignee and comment envelopes from another user, and see the changes and the toasts. Steps used only by this feature go in a per-feature steps file, not in <code>steps.js</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong></p><ul><li>With an issue open, a status (including a <code>statusId</code>-only change), assignee or comment change made elsewhere shows without a reload, with no duplicates.</li><li>Changes by another user show a Messenger toast; the user's own changes don't.</li><li>Events for other issues or rooms change nothing. Leaving the page removes its intents.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the live activity list, dates and other issue fields, the issue list page, and any change to Gaia or Hermes.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "ag-v2", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 13:42:14	2026-11-02 13:44:25	f
5bdbbd156ae8-7125-0ad0-2c3fb3fb0cea	f13058706ae8-bf33-0ad0-6d5a18240f8e	1	{"summary": "Three independent Prometheus issues on the issue detail page (components/issue/issue-details). (1) Clicking an attachment opens it in a wider preview modal: images inline, PDF/text/video in the viewer, a 'no preview' message with Download for other types. (2) Fix editing an estimate: the description editor is wired without fn, and editLog closes the modal and keeps changes on failure. (3) Long time log and estimate descriptions wrap and scroll inside a capped height instead of being cut to one line. No Gaia changes: PreviewController already serves files inline.", "issues": [{"key": "attachment-preview", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue detail: open an attachment in a preview modal by clicking it, without downloading", "description": "<p>On the issue detail page, users have to download an attachment to see it. Only the small file name opens the existing preview, which is a 35% wide iframe modal. And types the browser can't render get downloaded. Clicking an attachment should open it for viewing.</p><p><strong>Today</strong>: <code>app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> (Files box ~302-360) shows each file with a thumbnail or <code>AppUi::AttachmentIcon</code>, a name link calling <code>previewFile</code> and a download button calling <code>downloadFile</code>. <code>previewFile</code> in <code>issue-details.js</code> (~488) queries <code>upload</code> with <code>download: true</code> for a one-time token and sets the iframe <code>#file_preview</code> src to <code>&lt;upload adapter host&gt;/preview/get/&lt;token&gt;</code> through jQuery. Gaia's PreviewController serves the file with its mime type and no attachment disposition. The token is deleted after one use.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Make the whole attachment (thumbnail or icon, and name) a keyboard-reachable control that opens the preview. Keep the separate download and delete buttons.</li><li>Move the preview modal out of <code>issue-details</code> into its own component (e.g. <code>Issue::FilePreview</code>). It gets the file and builds the preview URL through the store (no raw fetch, no jQuery) and picks the view from <code>fileMime</code>: <code>image/*</code> as an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> scaled to fit; <code>application/pdf</code>, <code>text/*</code>, <code>video/*</code>, <code>audio/*</code> in the iframe/media element; any other type shows a 'No preview available for this file type' message with a Download button that reuses the existing download flow. Don't request a preview token for types that can't be previewed.</li><li>Make the modal wide enough to read in (e.g. Bootstrap <code>modal-lg</code> or most of the viewport), replacing the 35% width rule in <code>styles/modules/issue.scss</code> (<code>.filePreviewModal</code>). Square edges, design-system modal look.</li><li>Show a loading state while the token is fetched, and an error message if the request fails. Ignore a stale response if another file was opened meanwhile.</li><li>All new strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Clicking an image attachment's thumbnail or name opens the image in the modal; nothing is downloaded.</li><li>A PDF opens in the modal's viewer.</li><li>A .docx/.zip shows the no-preview message with a working Download button.</li><li>The modal can be opened and closed by keyboard; focus returns to the attachment on close.</li><li>Integration test for the preview component (image, PDF and unsupported mime cases) and an acceptance scenario with Mirage for opening an attachment from the issue page.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: previews of Office documents, any Gaia change, and changes to upload or delete.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "estimate-edit-fix", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue detail: editing an estimate doesn't work (description handler wired without fn)", "description": "<p>On the issue detail page, editing an existing estimate (pencil icon in the Estimates box) doesn't work. Editing a time log works.</p><p><strong>Cause</strong>: in <code>app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> the edit-estimate modal (~401-433) passes <code>@onContentChange={{@selectStatic this.editingLog 'description'}}</code> to <code>AppUi::ToastUi</code>, without <code>fn</code>. So <code>selectStatic</code> runs once during render instead of being passed as the change handler. The edit-timelog modal (~549) correctly uses <code>{{fn @selectStatic this.editingLog 'description'}}</code>. The ToastUi there also has a stray <code>@label</code> argument that the time log one doesn't have.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Wire the edit-estimate description with <code>fn</code>, matching the edit-timelog modal.</li><li>In <code>editLog</code> (<code>issue-details.js</code> ~655): when validation fails, keep the modal open with the error instead of closing it. Add a catch on <code>log.save()</code> that shows the error and calls <code>rollbackAttributes()</code>. When the modal is closed without saving, roll back the unsaved changes so the list doesn't show values that were never saved. Ignore a second Save while one is pending.</li><li>Check the estimate save end to end against Gaia (PATCH of the timelog with <code>context: est</code>) and fix anything else that stops it from saving.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Start with an acceptance test (Mirage) that edits an estimate's time and description and asserts the saved values and the 'Time estimated has been updated' message. It fails before the fix.</li><li>Editing an estimate's days/hours/minutes and description saves and shows the new values.</li><li>Cancelling the edit leaves the estimate unchanged; a failed save shows an error and restores the old values.</li><li>Editing a time log still works.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: redesigning the estimate or time log modals.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "log-description-scroll", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue detail: wrap long estimate and time log descriptions and scroll inside a capped height", "description": "<p>In the Estimates and Time logs boxes on the issue detail page, a description is cut to one line with an ellipsis. Anything longer can't be read.</p><p><strong>Today</strong>: <code>app/styles/modules/issue.scss</code> (~130) styles <code>.time-log .log-description</code> with <code>white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis</code>. The markup is in <code>app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> (<code>span.log-description</code> in both boxes, rendering the HTML description).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Let the description wrap (including long words and URLs) and cap its height (about 150px) with <code>overflow-y: auto</code>, so a long description scrolls inside its row. Short descriptions look as they do today, without an empty scroll area.</li><li>Keep the rich-text content (lists, code, images) within the row width.</li><li>Same rule for Estimates and Time logs. Style in <code>issue.scss</code> only, colours from <code>variables.scss</code>, no inline styles.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A multi-paragraph description is fully readable by scrolling inside its row; the box layout doesn't break.</li><li>A one-line description shows as before.</li><li>Checked in the running app next to the current issue page.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: an expand/collapse toggle, and changes to the description editor.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 16:07:55	2026-11-02 16:07:55	f
9f8e1d676ae8-7125-0ad0-7f64e9da3750	f13058706ae8-bf33-0ad0-6d5a18240f8e	2	{"summary": "Three independent Prometheus issues on the issue detail page (components/issue/issue-details), all in milestone aga-v2. (1) Clicking an attachment opens it in a wider preview modal: images inline, PDF/text/video in the viewer, a 'no preview' message with Download for other types. (2) Fix editing an estimate: the description editor is wired without fn, and editLog closes the modal and keeps changes on failure. (3) Long time log and estimate descriptions wrap and scroll inside a capped height instead of being cut to one line. No Gaia changes: PreviewController already serves files inline.", "issues": [{"key": "attachment-preview", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue detail: open an attachment in a preview modal by clicking it, without downloading", "description": "<p>On the issue detail page, users have to download an attachment to see it. Only the small file name opens the existing preview, which is a 35% wide iframe modal. And types the browser can't render get downloaded. Clicking an attachment should open it for viewing.</p><p><strong>Today</strong>: <code>app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> (Files box ~302-360) shows each file with a thumbnail or <code>AppUi::AttachmentIcon</code>, a name link calling <code>previewFile</code> and a download button calling <code>downloadFile</code>. <code>previewFile</code> in <code>issue-details.js</code> (~488) queries <code>upload</code> with <code>download: true</code> for a one-time token and sets the iframe <code>#file_preview</code> src to <code>&lt;upload adapter host&gt;/preview/get/&lt;token&gt;</code> through jQuery. Gaia's PreviewController serves the file with its mime type and no attachment disposition. The token is deleted after one use.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Make the whole attachment (thumbnail or icon, and name) a keyboard-reachable control that opens the preview. Keep the separate download and delete buttons.</li><li>Move the preview modal out of <code>issue-details</code> into its own component (e.g. <code>Issue::FilePreview</code>). It gets the file and builds the preview URL through the store (no raw fetch, no jQuery) and picks the view from <code>fileMime</code>: <code>image/*</code> as an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> scaled to fit; <code>application/pdf</code>, <code>text/*</code>, <code>video/*</code>, <code>audio/*</code> in the iframe/media element; any other type shows a 'No preview available for this file type' message with a Download button that reuses the existing download flow. Don't request a preview token for types that can't be previewed.</li><li>Make the modal wide enough to read in (e.g. Bootstrap <code>modal-lg</code> or most of the viewport), replacing the 35% width rule in <code>styles/modules/issue.scss</code> (<code>.filePreviewModal</code>). Square edges, design-system modal look.</li><li>Show a loading state while the token is fetched, and an error message if the request fails. Ignore a stale response if another file was opened meanwhile.</li><li>All new strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Clicking an image attachment's thumbnail or name opens the image in the modal; nothing is downloaded.</li><li>A PDF opens in the modal's viewer.</li><li>A .docx/.zip shows the no-preview message with a working Download button.</li><li>The modal can be opened and closed by keyboard; focus returns to the attachment on close.</li><li>Integration test for the preview component (image, PDF and unsupported mime cases) and an acceptance scenario with Mirage for opening an attachment from the issue page.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: previews of Office documents, any Gaia change, and changes to upload or delete.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "estimate-edit-fix", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue detail: editing an estimate doesn't work (description handler wired without fn)", "description": "<p>On the issue detail page, editing an existing estimate (pencil icon in the Estimates box) doesn't work. Editing a time log works.</p><p><strong>Cause</strong>: in <code>app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> the edit-estimate modal (~401-433) passes <code>@onContentChange={{@selectStatic this.editingLog 'description'}}</code> to <code>AppUi::ToastUi</code>, without <code>fn</code>. So <code>selectStatic</code> runs once during render instead of being passed as the change handler. The edit-timelog modal (~549) correctly uses <code>{{fn @selectStatic this.editingLog 'description'}}</code>. The ToastUi there also has a stray <code>@label</code> argument that the time log one doesn't have.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Wire the edit-estimate description with <code>fn</code>, matching the edit-timelog modal.</li><li>In <code>editLog</code> (<code>issue-details.js</code> ~655): when validation fails, keep the modal open with the error instead of closing it. Add a catch on <code>log.save()</code> that shows the error and calls <code>rollbackAttributes()</code>. When the modal is closed without saving, roll back the unsaved changes so the list doesn't show values that were never saved. Ignore a second Save while one is pending.</li><li>Check the estimate save end to end against Gaia (PATCH of the timelog with <code>context: est</code>) and fix anything else that stops it from saving.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Start with an acceptance test (Mirage) that edits an estimate's time and description and asserts the saved values and the 'Time estimated has been updated' message. It fails before the fix.</li><li>Editing an estimate's days/hours/minutes and description saves and shows the new values.</li><li>Cancelling the edit leaves the estimate unchanged; a failed save shows an error and restores the old values.</li><li>Editing a time log still works.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: redesigning the estimate or time log modals.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "log-description-scroll", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue detail: wrap long estimate and time log descriptions and scroll inside a capped height", "description": "<p>In the Estimates and Time logs boxes on the issue detail page, a description is cut to one line with an ellipsis. Anything longer can't be read.</p><p><strong>Today</strong>: <code>app/styles/modules/issue.scss</code> (~130) styles <code>.time-log .log-description</code> with <code>white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis</code>. The markup is in <code>app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> (<code>span.log-description</code> in both boxes, rendering the HTML description).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Let the description wrap (including long words and URLs) and cap its height (about 150px) with <code>overflow-y: auto</code>, so a long description scrolls inside its row. Short descriptions look as they do today, without an empty scroll area.</li><li>Keep the rich-text content (lists, code, images) within the row width.</li><li>Same rule for Estimates and Time logs. Style in <code>issue.scss</code> only, colours from <code>variables.scss</code>, no inline styles.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A multi-paragraph description is fully readable by scrolling inside its row; the box layout doesn't break.</li><li>A one-line description shows as before.</li><li>Checked in the running app next to the current issue page.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: an expand/collapse toggle, and changes to the description editor.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 16:09:03	2026-11-02 16:09:03	f
