ep the separate download and delete buttons.</li><li>Move the preview modal out of <code>issue-details</code> into its own component (e.g. <code>Issue::FilePreview</code>). It gets the file and builds the preview URL through the store (no raw fetch, no jQuery) and picks the view from <code>fileMime</code>: <code>image/*</code> as an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> scaled to fit; <code>application/pdf</code>, <code>text/*</code>, <code>video/*</code>, <code>audio/*</code> in the iframe/media element; any other type shows a 'No preview available for this file type' message with a Download button that reuses the existing download flow. Don't request a preview token for types that can't be previewed.</li><li>Make the modal wide enough to read in (e.g. Bootstrap <code>modal-lg</code> or most of the viewport), replacing the 35% width rule in <code>styles/modules/issue.scss</code> (<code>.filePreviewModal</code>). Square edges, design-system modal look.</li><li>Show a loading state while the token is fetched, and an error message if the request fails. Ignore a stale response if another file was opened meanwhile.</li><li>All new strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Clicking an image attachment's thumbnail or name opens the image in the modal; nothing is downloaded.</li><li>A PDF opens in the modal's viewer.</li><li>A .docx/.zip shows the no-preview message with a working Download button.</li><li>The modal can be opened and closed by keyboard; focus returns to the attachment on close.</li><li>Integration test for the preview component (image, PDF and unsupported mime cases) and an acceptance scenario with Mirage for opening an attachment from the issue page.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: previews of Office documents, any Gaia change, and changes to upload or delete.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, 