ws the new values.</li><li>Cancelling the edit leaves the estimate unchanged; a failed save shows an error and restores the old values.</li><li>Editing a time log still works.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: redesigning the estimate or time log modals.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "log-description-scroll", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue detail: wrap long estimate and time log descriptions and scroll inside a capped height", "description": "<p>In the Estimates and Time logs boxes on the issue detail page, a description is cut to one line with an ellipsis. Anything longer can't be read.</p><p><strong>Today</strong>: <code>app/styles/modules/issue.scss</code> (~130) styles <code>.time-log .log-description</code> with <code>white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis</code>. The markup is in <code>app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> (<code>span.log-description</code> in both boxes, rendering the HTML description).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Let the description wrap (including long words and URLs) and cap its height (about 150px) with <code>overflow-y: auto</code>, so a long description scrolls inside its row. Short descriptions look as they do today, without an empty scroll area.</li><li>Keep the rich-text content (lists, code, images) within the row width.</li><li>Same rule for Estimates and Time logs. Style in <code>issue.scss</code> only, colours from <code>variables.scss</code>, no inline styles.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A multi-paragraph description is fully readable by scrolling inside its row; the box layout doesn't break.</li><li>A one-line description shows as before.</li><li>Checked in the running app next to the current issue page.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: an expand/collapse toggle, and changes to the description editor.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 19:10:03	2026-11-02 19:14:42	f
ab0ab6456ae8-bf33-0ad0-cb7064628d9e	34bdca956ae6-8157-e410-2af2948f16f3	1	{"summary": "Four Prometheus fixes on the agent pages, one per reported problem, plus one request to A Gaia. Save-stuck and page-404 are bugs whose root cause still needs to be found, so they are complex. The profile picture reuses the existing user component. The projects multi-select gets search, sorting and working selection. The Gaia request turns plain-text Phalcon exceptions into JSON:API errors, so failures like the agent page 404 show their real message. It runs in parallel and the Prometheus fixes don't wait for it.", "issues": [{"key": "agent-save-stuck", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Agent create: page stays on the form after a successful save, with no message", "description": "<p>Saving a new agent stores it in Gaia, but the page stays on the create form: no success message and no move to the agent page. The agent pages are from aprom-4044.</p><p><strong>What the code shows</strong></p><ul><li>The base <code>controllers/prometheus/create.js</code> <code>_save</code> (~l.222) calls <code>afterSave(data).then(...)</code> without returning it and without a <code>catch</code>. When <code>afterSave</code> rejects, <code>navigateToSuccess</code> and <code>showSuccess</code> never run, the error is swallowed, and the save promise never settles.</li><li>The agent's <code>afterSave</code> (<code>controllers/app/agent/create.js</code> ~l.232) saves the agent user's <code>accountStatus</code>, then creates and deletes <code>userrole</code> and <code>membership</code> records. Any one of these failing leaves the page stuck.</li><li>Likely culprit: <code>syncMembers</code> creates memberships with <code>deleted: '0'</code>, but Gaia's Membership has no <code>deleted</code> field (no soft delete, see <code>gaia/docs/generated/models/Membership.md</code>). Also check whether <code>agent.user</code> and <code>agent.userId</code> are set on the POST response.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Reproduce it in the running app and in a failing test first. Find the call that fails and fix it.</li><li>In <code>_save</code>, return the <code>afterSave</code> chain and handle its failure: show the error through <code>errorManager</code> and settle the promise. The record is already saved, so still go to the success route and tell the user which follow-up step failed. Check the other create controllers that override <code>afterSave</code> still behave.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Creating an agent with roles, projects and Active set shows the success message and opens the agent page with them saved.</li><li>If a follow-up save fails, the user sees an error and the page doesn't hang.</li><li>Tests cover both cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> moving the role, project and status sync into a service (a design-review follow-up from aprom-4044).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "agent-page-404", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Agent detail page fails with 404 and a non-JSON 'PhalconException' response", "description": "<p>Opening an agent's detail page (<code>app.agent.page</code>) fails. The console shows <code>Error while processing route: app.agent.page Unexpected token 'P', \\"PhalconExc\\"... is not valid JSON</code> and a 404. Gaia's <code>public/index.php</code> (~l.233) catches <code>\\\\Phalcon\\\\Exception</code> and prints <code>PhalconException: &lt;message&gt;</code> as plain text, so one of the page's requests hits a Phalcon error. The JSON error fix in Gaia is a separate request issue.</p><p><strong>What the page loads</strong> (<code>routes/app/agent/page.js</code>)</p><ul><li><code>agent</code> with <code>query (Agent.id : id)</code> and <code>rels user,sponsor</code>, then <code>userrole</code> (rels role), <code>membership</code> (rels project) and <code>useridentity</code> by <code>userId</code>.</li><li>The page's boxes load their own data too: Credentials (aprom-4045), Tools and Skills (4036), Workflows (4059), Activities (4242) and Identities (4037).</li><li>When a query fails, the route's <code>catch</code> calls <code>errorManager.handleError</code> and returns <code>undefined</code>, and <code>setupController</code> then destructures it.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Find the failing request: run each one against the local Gaia and read the Phalcon message. Fix the Prometheus request: the query, rels or field names it uses.</li><li>If the cause is in Gaia, not in the request, stop and report the failing request and its Phalcon message in a comment, so a Gaia issue can be filed.</li><li>Make the route handle a failed load cleanly: an error message or the not-found page, never a crash in <code>setupController</code>.</li><li>Check the edit route (<code>routes/app/agent/edit.js</code>), which uses the same agent query.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The detail page opens for an agent with and without a sponsor, roles, projects and identities.</li><li>A failed load shows an error instead of a broken page.</li><li>An acceptance test covers opening the page.</li></ul>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gaia-phalcon-json", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Return Phalcon exceptions as JSON:API errors instead of plain text", "description": "<p>A Prometheus needs every Gaia error to come back as JSON. Today a <code>\\\\Phalcon\\\\Exception</code> that reaches <code>public/index.php</code> (~l.233) is printed as plain text, <code>PhalconException: &lt;message&gt;</code>, keeping whatever status was set. Ember Data can't parse that, so the user sees <code>Unexpected token 'P'... is not valid JSON</code> instead of the real error. This hid the cause of the agent detail page 404 in Prometheus.</p><p><strong>Proposed change</strong> (please accept, adapt or decline)</p><ul><li>Handle <code>\\\\Phalcon\\\\Exception</code> like the <code>\\\\Gaia\\\\Exception\\\\*</code> classes: a JSON:API <code>errors</code> document with the Content-Type the other errors use.</li><li>Status: 404 for dispatcher not-found errors, 500 for the rest.</li><li>Keep the raw Phalcon message (it can name tables, columns or PHQL) out of the response unless debug is on. Log it on the server.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A request that raises a Phalcon exception gets a JSON:API error body with a 404 or 500 status.</li><li>A test covers both statuses.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing the exceptions themselves.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "agent-profile-picture", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Agents: upload a profile picture, and show it instead of the robot avatar", "description": "<p>An agent is a user (users.type = Agent), so it has the user's <code>profilePicture</code>, but the agent pages give no way to set it. <code>Agent::Avatar</code> takes no user and always draws the robot, so a picture wouldn't show either.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>On the agent detail page header (<code>templates/app/agent/page.hbs</code> ~l.40), reuse <code>User::Edit::ProfilePicture</code> (<code>components/user/edit/profile-picture.hbs</code>) and <code>User::ProfilePictureCropper</code> with the user page's flow: <code>controllers/app/user/page.js</code> <code>uploadImage</code> (~l.307, type and size checks from <code>ENV.app.upload.profilePicture</code>) and <code>applyCrop</code> (~l.349: set the cropped base64 on <code>profilePicture</code>, save the user, roll back on error). Apply it to the agent's user (<code>agent.user</code>). Don't copy the code: move the shared part into a helper or service if both controllers need it.</li><li>Gate the edit control on <code>user.update</code>.</li><li><code>Agent::Avatar</code>: take the user and show its picture when there is one, the robot otherwise. Keep the AGENT badge next to it. Update the callers that have a user at hand: agent list rows, the detail header, and the aprom-4244 badge places.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>On an agent's page, a user with <code>user.update</code> can upload and crop a picture, and it shows after a reload.</li><li>Agents without a picture still show the robot.</li><li>Integration tests cover both avatar cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a picture field on the create form.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "agent-projects-select", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Agent create/edit: projects multi-select doesn't select, search or sort", "description": "<p>In the agent form's Access box (<code>templates/app/agent/create.hbs</code> ~l.173, shared by create and edit), the Projects list opens, but clicking a project doesn't select it, you can't search it, and the list isn't sorted. It stays a multi-select.</p><p><strong>What the code shows</strong></p><ul><li><code>FormFields::FieldRelateMulti</code> (<code>components/form-fields/field-relate-multi.hbs</code>) passes <code>@searchEnabled</code> on to <code>PowerSelectMultiple</code>, but the agent form doesn't set it. <code>@searchField=\\"label\\"</code> is set.</li><li>The options come unsorted from <code>routes/app/agent/create.js</code> <code>loadOptions</code> (<code>store.query('project', {limit: -1})</code>, mapped to <code>{label, value}</code>).</li><li>Why a click doesn't select is unknown: <code>selectProjects</code> sets the tracked <code>selectedProjects</code>. Check the <code>AccessControl</code> wrapper (<code>@aclContext=\\"membership.create\\"</code>), the <code>related-fields/relate-simple</code> option template, and whether the options array is rebuilt on each render. The Roles select next to it uses the same setup: check it too.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Fix the selection.</li><li>Turn on search for Projects and Roles.</li><li>Sort both lists by name: in the query if Gaia's sort fits, else when mapping.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Several projects and roles can be picked and removed.</li><li>Typing filters the list, and options are in alphabetical order.</li><li>The picks are saved and shown again on edit.</li><li>An integration or acceptance test covers picking and searching.</li></ul>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 16:04:59	2026-11-02 16:20:33	f
91c032376aef-1001-619b-4f2a65ecc31a	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	9	{"summary": "Unblock the jQuery QueryBuilder removal (aprom-4326): the Agents and Workflows lists still use it. First, the ezSearch saved-search handling that the Issue and Project lists each copied (ezSavedSearches, selectSavedSearch, showEzSaveSearchDialog, saveEzSearch) moves into the shared list controller. Then the Agents and Workflows lists move to <EzSearch>, in parallel, with their fields declared as views.Agent.search and views.Workflow.search metadata (the metadata-views architecture from aprom-4323) instead of controller filter arrays. aprom-4326 is held until both are merged.", "issues": [{"key": "list-saved-search-base", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: move saved-search handling into the shared list controller", "description": "<p>The Issue list (aprom-4305) and the Project list (aprom-4324) each define the same ezSearch saved-search code in their controllers: <code>ezSavedSearches</code>, <code>selectSavedSearch</code>, <code>showEzSaveSearchDialog</code> and <code>saveEzSearch</code> (<code>controllers/app/project/issue/index.js</code> ~l.36-110, <code>controllers/app/projects/index.js</code> ~l.41-100). The Agents and Workflows lists are moving to ezSearch next and would copy it again. Move it into <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code> (which already has <code>applyQuery</code>, ~l.328) so every list gets it from the base class.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>:<ul><li><code>ezSavedSearches</code> (getter over <code>savedsearches</code>, query from <code>searchquery</code>).</li><li><code>selectSavedSearch(search|null)</code> (sets or clears <code>searchId</code>/<code>activeSearch</code>).</li><li><code>showEzSaveSearchDialog(query)</code> and <code>saveEzSearch()</code>, taking the values that differ per list from one overridable method, e.g. <code>savedSearchContext()</code> returning <code>{relatedTo, projectId?}</code>, and the translation keys for its messages from the list's module.</li><li>Keep the behaviour and messages exactly as they are on the Issue and Project lists today.</li></ul></li><li>Issue and Project controllers: delete their copies and override only <code>savedSearchContext()</code> (<code>issue</code> + <code>projectId</code>; <code>project</code>).</li><li>Unit tests for the base actions, with a fake store.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The Issue and Project list ezSearch acceptance tests (load, select, deselect, save a search) pass unchanged.</li><li>No copy of these four members remains in a page controller.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Agents and Workflows lists (separate issues), removing the old jQuery actions (aprom-4326).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4305", "aprom-4324"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ez-agent-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Agents list: replace jQuery QueryBuilder with ezSearch", "description": "<p>The Agents list is one of the two remaining jQuery QueryBuilder users that block its removal (aprom-4326). Move it to <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> the metadata-driven way (<code>docs/architecture/metadata-views/architecture.md</code>): its search fields are declared in view metadata, not in the controller, and the saved-search handling comes from <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code> (base-class issue this one depends on).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>: add <code>views.Agent.search</code> in the format of <code>views.Project.search</code>, covering today's filters in <code>controllers/app/agent/index.js</code> ~l.22-41:<ul><li>module <code>Agent</code>, text field <code>Agent.name</code>;</li><li><code>Agent.name</code> and <code>Agent.purpose</code> as text (labels <code>views.app.agent.list.name</code> / <code>.purpose</code>);</li><li><code>sponsor.name</code> as a user field with source <code>users</code> (label <code>views.app.agent.list.sponsor</code>);</li><li>aliases name, purpose, sponsor.</li></ul></li><li><code>templates/app/agent/index.hbs</code> ~l.15-50: replace the Saved Searches dropdown, the readonly <code>FieldText</code> (<code>openFilters</code>), Search (<code>searchByRules</code>), Clear (<code>clearSearch</code>) and <code>{{query-builder module=\\"agent\\"}}</code> with <code>&lt;EzSearch @schema @query @savedSearches={{this.ezSavedSearches}} @activeSavedSearchId={{this.searchId}} @onSavedSearchChange={{this.selectSavedSearch}} @onApply={{this.applyQuery}} @aclContext=\\"agent.read\\" /&gt;</code>. No <code>@onSave</code>: the list has no Save Search today.</li><li><code>routes/app/agent/index.js</code>: load <code>query-schema</code> <code>load('Agent')</code> next to the saved searches (~l.62) and set <code>controller.querySchema</code>.</li><li><code>controllers/app/agent/index.js</code>: remove <code>metadata.filters</code> and override <code>savedSearchContext()</code> (<code>relatedTo: 'agent'</code>, or whatever the route's saved-search query uses).</li><li>Mirage: record the last <code>query</code> param of the agent list request, as aprom-4305 did for issues.</li><li>Tests: update <code>tests/acceptance/agents/agents-list.feature</code> and its steps, and add scenarios:<ol><li>Type and run a query (e.g. <code>sponsor in hammad</code>): the formatted query shows and is sent.</li><li>Accept a suggestion with the keyboard.</li><li>Load a saved search: the bar shows it and <code>searchId</code> is in the URL.</li><li>An error is shown and nothing is sent.</li></ol></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios pass.</li><li>The other agent tests (catalog, create, detail, activation and mass actions) pass.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a Save Search button on this list, the Workflows list, removing the plugin (aprom-4326).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["list-saved-search-base"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ez-workflow-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflows list: replace jQuery QueryBuilder with ezSearch", "description": "<p>The Workflows list is one of the two remaining jQuery QueryBuilder users that block its removal (aprom-4326). Move it to <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> the metadata-driven way (<code>docs/architecture/metadata-views/architecture.md</code>): its search fields are declared in view metadata, not in the controller, and the saved-search handling comes from <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code> (base-class issue this one depends on).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>: add <code>views.Workflow.search</code> in the format of <code>views.Project.search</code>, covering today's filters in <code>controllers/app/workflow/index.js</code> ~l.23-49:<ul><li>module <code>Workflow</code>, text field <code>Workflow.name</code>;</li><li><code>Workflow.name</code> and <code>Workflow.description</code> as text (labels <code>views.app.workflow.list.name</code> / <code>.description</code>);</li><li><code>Workflow.status</code> as an enum with source <code>translation</code>, key <code>views.app.workflow.status</code> (stored values Draft, Active, Disabled; label <code>views.app.workflow.fields.status</code>);</li><li>aliases name, description, status.</li></ul>If the <code>translation</code> source can't express stored values that equal the translation keys, fix the source in <code>services/query-schema.js</code> rather than hard-coding values.</li><li><code>templates/app/workflow/index.hbs</code> ~l.15-55: replace the Saved Searches dropdown, the readonly <code>FieldText</code> (<code>openFilters</code>), Search (<code>searchByRules</code>), Clear (<code>clearSearch</code>) and <code>{{query-builder module=\\"workflow\\"}}</code> with <code>&lt;EzSearch @schema @query @savedSearches={{this.ezSavedSearches}} @activeSavedSearchId={{this.searchId}} @onSavedSearchChange={{this.selectSavedSearch}} @onApply={{this.applyQuery}} @aclContext=\\"workflow.read\\" /&gt;</code>. No <code>@onSave</code>: the list has no Save Search today.</li><li><code>routes/app/workflow/index.js</code>: load <code>query-schema</code> <code>load('Workflow')</code> next to the saved searches (~l.67) and set <code>controller.querySchema</code>.</li><li><code>controllers/app/workflow/index.js</code>: remove <code>metadata.filters</code> and override <code>savedSearchContext()</code> (<code>relatedTo: 'workflow'</code>, or whatever the route's saved-search query uses).</li><li>Mirage: record the last <code>query</code> param of the workflow list request, as aprom-4305 did for issues.</li><li>Tests: update <code>tests/acceptance/workflows/workflows-list.feature</code> and its steps, and add scenarios:<ol><li>Type <code>status:act</code>, press Enter: <code>(Workflow.status : Active)</code> shows and is sent.</li><li>Accept a suggestion with the keyboard.</li><li>Load a saved search: the bar shows it and <code>searchId</code> is in the URL.</li><li>An error (<code>status:zzz</code>) is shown and nothing is sent.</li></ol></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios pass.</li><li>The other workflow tests (editor, runs) pass.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a Save Search button on this list, the Agents list, removing the plugin (aprom-4326).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["list-saved-search-base"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 14:45:37	2026-11-07 14:47:20	f
e0360f006af3-89a1-8333-a4ceed1234ac	341481c56af2-8040-cd6a-5ea33d81936b	7	{"summary": "Two issues: the Threads template stops nesting a second section.content inside the project layout's (after aprom-4455, same template). In parallel, the design system doc gets the rules this review uncovered: project pages never render their own header, breadcrumb or section.content. It also gains a List + detail (QuickList) page pattern (create button in the QuickList header, pagination in its footer, wrapping toolbar, info column), label and status rules, the composer, and matching checklist items.", "issues": [{"key": "thr-nested-content", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: section.content is nested twice", "description": "<p>The project layout <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> already wraps every project page in <code>&lt;section class=\\"content\\"&gt;{{outlet}}&lt;/section&gt;</code>. <code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code> opens another <code>&lt;section class=\\"content\\"&gt;</code> around the Threads row, so the DOM has <code>section.content &gt; section.content &gt; div.row.conversation-wrapper</code> and AdminLTE's <code>.content</code> padding applies twice. No other <code>app/project/*</code> template does this (Task Board, Gantt start directly with their content).</p><ul><li>Remove the inner <code>&lt;section class=\\"content\\"&gt;</code> wrapper from <code>conversation.hbs</code>; the template starts with the <code>.row.conversation-wrapper</code> (keep any modal/in-element markup that lived inside the section).</li><li>Check <code>conversation-loading.hbs</code> and the Threads child templates (<code>conversation/index.hbs</code>, <code>conversation/page.hbs</code>) for the same wrapper; check any styles that targeted the nested section.</li><li>Leave <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the Threads page has exactly one <code>section.content</code> (acceptance test asserts the count) and the list starts at the same left/top offset as the Task Board. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other pages.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4455"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ds-doc-list-detail", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Design system doc: shell rules for project pages and the List + detail (QuickList) pattern", "description": "<p>The Threads review (aprom-4454..4460 and the nested section.content bug) found mistakes that <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code> doesn't prevent. Section 2 lists the content header and <code>section.content</code> as shell parts but never says pages must not render them, section 3 has no pattern for the QuickList list + detail layout used by Roles, Ideas and Threads, and nothing covers the label/status details. Agents read this doc before every UI change, so write the rules down. Docs only, no code.</p><ul><li><strong>Section 2 (App shell):</strong> add that pages under <code>app.project</code> start directly with their <code>.row</code>: they never render their own <code>section.content-header</code>, page title row, <code>&lt;BreadCrumb/&gt;</code> or <code>section.content</code>, because <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> renders the project-name link, the single breadcrumb and the content section. Project pages have no page title (like Task Board and Gantt Cal); breadcrumb labels come from <code>services/breadcrumb.js</code>.</li><li><strong>Section 3 (Page patterns), new \\"List + detail page (QuickList)\\":</strong> <code>.row</code> with <code>.col-md-3</code> <code>QuickList</code> in a <code>box box-primary</code> + <code>.col-md-9</code> outlet; the detail is a <code>.col-md-8</code> record box + <code>.col-md-4</code> info column of small boxes; the first row opens by default (index route <code>replaceWith</code>), empty state only when nothing matches. QuickList box order: header = title + create button in <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> (<code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code>, ACL), then <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> with <code>EzSearchCompact</code>, then the group/sort toolbar (wraps when narrow, never overflows), then the rows (group headings when grouped), then <strong>pagination in the box footer</strong> (range <code>1-20 / 20+</code> + ‹ ›, limit+1, never in the header). State via <code>utils/state/</code> (UrlState + ListLoader), list reloads in place. Examples: Roles, Ideas, Threads.</li><li><strong>Section 8 (Buttons, labels, icons, avatars):</strong> no small uppercase type/eyebrow label above a box title (the title is <code>h3.box-title</code>); issue statuses always render with the <code>status-label</code> + <code>status-style</code> helpers and the status class (as in <code>components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code>), never the raw value; information shown in a side box (e.g. a linked issue) is not repeated in the record header.</li><li><strong>Section 9 (Other building blocks):</strong> add \\"Reply / comment box\\" = <code>ConversationUi::CommentComposer</code> (toast-ui WYSIWYG with its toolbar, mentions and issue links); never a plain textarea. Record boxes are plain <code>box box-*</code> with no extra shadow or border.</li><li><strong>Section 12 (Checklist):</strong> add items: no own content-header/breadcrumb/section.content in project pages; List + detail pages follow the QuickList order (create in header, pagination in footer); statuses via <code>status-label</code>; comment input is the CommentComposer.</li><li>If <code>public/ui-docs/quick-list.md</code> (component library) says anything that contradicts the pagination/actions placement, align it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the doc sections above are updated, consistent with the code of Roles/Ideas/Threads; markdown renders cleanly. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> code changes; new reference screenshots.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-10 17:14:08	2026-11-10 18:30:37	f
9e441ca36ae8-0772-4071-926af978bd02	22a9bd746ae8-4e76-5f8b-4f37d884cb93	1	{"summary": "Bring the first Gaia-defined agent to life: Agent Hera writes a retrospective issue when a milestone completes. gaia-mcp gains milestone read tools and agent lookup (parallel). Talos learns to take an agent's role prompt, model and limits from Gaia's agentspec, and gets a new agent kind that runs on Hermes events (parallel). Hera, the first such agent, listens for milestone.completed and creates 'Retrospective {{Milestone Name}}'. Agents sign in with their own client credentials via the existing adt-4041, which the engineer moves into this milestone.", "issues": [{"key": "ms-tools", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "gaia-mcp: milestone read tools and a milestone filter on gaia_list_issues", "description": "<p>Agents need to look up milestones and read every issue in one. Today gaia-mcp shows milestones only inside <code>gaia_project_options</code> (name, id, endDate) and can only filter issues by project, status, assignee and subject. The first user is Agent Hera, who writes a retrospective once a milestone completes.</p><ul><li><code>gaia_list_milestones</code> (project, optional status, e.g. <code>completed</code>): name, id, status, milestoneType, start and end dates.</li><li><code>gaia_get_milestone</code> (project + name, or id): the fields above plus its description and issue counts per status.</li><li><code>gaia_list_issues</code>: new optional <code>milestone</code> argument (name or id, resolved within the project) and a <code>page</code> argument, so a milestone with more than 100 issues can be read fully. Values go through the existing sanitising and lookups; never paste raw input into the query.</li><li>Code: <code>gaia-mcp/server.py</code> (<code>Gaia.find</code>, the tools class, the <code>TOOLS</code> table) plus README; unit tests in the gaia-mcp tests with a stubbed Gaia.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the new tools appear in <code>tools/list</code>; listing completed milestones of a project works; <code>gaia_list_issues</code> with a milestone returns only that milestone's issues and pages through all of them. Tests pass on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing milestones (existing <code>gaia_create_milestone</code> stays as is).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "agent-tools", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "gaia-mcp: look up agents and their spec", "description": "<p>Talos is starting to run agents defined in Gaia (Agent module, agaia-4027) instead of in local <code>agent.json</code> files. It needs to find an agent and read its spec. Gaia serves the spec as the read-only resource <code>GET /api/v1/agentspec/{agentId}</code> (agaia-4043; needs <code>agentspec.get</code>). The spec holds the role prompt, model config, limits, permission mode, tool grants and skills.</p><ul><li><code>gaia_list_agents</code>: the agents visible to the caller (id, name, email, purpose, account status).</li><li><code>gaia_get_agent_spec</code> (agent name, email or id): resolves the agent, then returns the agentspec document as is.</li><li>A plain method on the Gaia client (e.g. <code>Gaia.agent_spec(name_or_id)</code>) that both the tool and Talos (which imports gaia-mcp in-process, see <code>talos/lib/tracker.py</code>) can call.</li><li>Clear errors: unknown agent, several matches, or 403 when the caller lacks <code>agentspec.get</code> (say which permission is missing).</li><li>Code: <code>gaia-mcp/server.py</code>, README, unit tests with a stubbed Gaia.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> both tools listed and tested; the spec of an agent can be fetched by name.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> workflow and skill lookup tools; editing agents.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "talos-gaia-spec", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: take an agent's role prompt, model and limits from its Gaia agentspec", "description": "<p>Agents are now defined in Gaia (Agent + agentspec, agaia-4027/4043), but Talos still reads every agent's role prompt, model and limits from <code>talos/agents/&lt;name&gt;/agent.json</code>. This issue lets an agent.json point at a Gaia agent and take those settings from its spec, so the definition lives in Gaia and is edited there.</p><ul><li>agent.json gains optional <code>gaiaAgent</code> (agent name or id). When set, <code>rolePrompt</code> and <code>model</code> are no longer required in <code>registry.py</code> <code>load_agent</code> (~l.130).</li><li>New module (e.g. <code>talos/lib/agent_spec.py</code>, single responsibility: spec to Talos settings) that maps the spec onto the <code>Agent</code> dataclass: role prompt, model (from modelConfig), maxTurns, permission mode. Validate the permission mode against Claude Code's modes and refuse unknown values instead of passing them through.</li><li>The spec is fetched with the agent's own credentials (its <code>gaiaEnv</code>) via gaia-mcp's <code>Gaia.agent_spec</code>. It is fetched when Talos starts and again before each run, so edits in Gaia take effect without a restart. If Gaia is unreachable, the run uses the last good spec and logs it; with no spec at all the agent is not started, with a clear error.</li><li>Machine-local settings stay in agent.json: gaiaEnv, projects, allowedTools/deniedTools, runner, parallelism. The spec's tool grants and skills are ignored for now (logged once).</li><li>README section; unit tests for the mapping, the fallback and the loader with and without <code>gaiaAgent</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> an agent with <code>gaiaAgent</code> runs with the role prompt and model set in Gaia; changing the role prompt in Gaia changes the next run; existing agents (Odysseus, Nestor, Agamemnon) load unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> skills, mapping tool grants to Claude Code tools, moving existing agents to Gaia.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["agent-tools", "adt-4041"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "talos-event-kind", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: new agent kind 'events' that runs an agent once per Hermes event", "description": "<p>Talos agents run today on assigned issues (kind <code>issues</code>), ideas (<code>ideas</code>) or as an orchestrator. A retrospective agent must instead run when something happens in Gaia, starting with <code>milestone.completed</code>. Gaia already publishes that event via <code>MilestoneLiveEventsComponent</code>, project-scoped, and Hermes already allows it.</p><ul><li><code>registry.py</code>: add <code>events</code> to <code>KINDS</code>. Such an agent needs <code>name</code>, <code>gaiaEnv</code>, <code>projects</code> and <code>triggers</code>, a map of event name to <code>{prompt}</code>. It needs no <code>actions</code>, <code>acceptAssignmentsFrom</code> or <code>handoffTo</code>.</li><li>Subscribe to the trigger events in the agent's projects through the existing Hermes listener (<code>lib/hermes.py</code> <code>intents(project_ids, events)</code>), as the agent's own Gaia user.</li><li>On an event: render the trigger prompt with the event's fields (<code>{{projectName}}</code>, <code>{{projectShortcode}}</code>, <code>{{resourceId}}</code> and the event's changes, e.g. <code>{{name}}</code>) and run Claude once with the agent's role prompt and limits, using the runner, workspace and usage-pause machinery the other kinds use. No issue is claimed.</li><li>Run each (agent, event name, resource id) at most once: record it in the Talos db, so a re-sent or duplicate event (several projects, reconnects) doesn't run twice. Failures are logged and kept for <code>talos status</code>; there is no hand-off target.</li><li>README section; unit tests for loading, prompt rendering and dedupe (no Hermes or Claude needed).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> an events agent with a <code>milestone.completed</code> trigger runs once when a milestone in one of its projects is marked completed, and not again for the same milestone.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> replaying events missed while Talos was down; events other than those named in triggers; workflow-dispatched runs (adt-4047).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hera", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agent Hera: write a retrospective issue when a milestone completes", "description": "<p>Hera is the first agent defined in Gaia and run by Talos. When a milestone completes, she reads all of its issues and creates a retrospective issue named <strong>Retrospective {{Milestone Name}}</strong> in the milestone's project. Her role prompt, model and limits live in her Gaia Agent record; Talos takes them from her agentspec.</p><ul><li><code>talos/agents/hera/agent.json</code>: kind <code>events</code>, <code>gaiaAgent</code> \\"Agent Hera\\", <code>gaiaEnv</code> <code>gaia-mcp/hera.env</code> (her client id and secret, adt-4041), the projects she covers, and allowedTools limited to the gaia MCP tools she needs: <code>gaia_get_milestone</code>, <code>gaia_list_issues</code>, <code>gaia_get_issue</code>, <code>gaia_create_issue</code>. No file editing and no git.</li><li>Trigger <code>milestone.completed</code> with a prompt naming the milestone and project.</li><li>The role prompt, shipped as <code>talos/agents/hera/role.md</code> for the engineer to paste into Hera's Gaia record. Hera:<ul><li>first checks that no issue \\"Retrospective &lt;name&gt;\\" exists in the project, so she never writes a second one;</li><li>reads every issue of the milestone (paging), including comments and time;</li><li>creates one Task in the milestone's project, assigned to her sponsor, with an HTML description covering: what shipped (issue refs grouped by type); estimate vs logged time; issues reopened, handed back, blocked or needing input, and why; review rounds; what went well; what went badly; proposed follow-ups.</li></ul></li><li>README: setting Hera up. Create the Agent in Gaia, issue a credential, grant <code>agentspec.get</code>, <code>milestone.get</code>, <code>issue.get</code>/<code>issue.create</code> and <code>comment.get</code>, add project memberships, write <code>hera.env</code>.</li><li>A test that hera/agent.json loads with the events kind.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> marking a test milestone completed produces exactly one \\"Retrospective &lt;name&gt;\\" issue covering all of the milestone's issues; completing it again (or a duplicate event) creates none.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> catching up on milestones that completed while Talos was down, skills, other retrospective triggers.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ms-tools", "talos-gaia-spec", "talos-event-kind", "adt-4041"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-02 20:59:10	2026-11-02 21:03:33	f
e195edd76ae9-467f-90e3-62433add6e32	34bdca956ae6-8157-e410-2af2948f16f3	2	{"summary": "Gaia adds a 'Milestone completed' workflow trigger. That needs a small catalog addition: an update trigger can require a field to change to a value. Talos learns to run a Run agent step that isn't about an issue, with no repo workspace, branch or PR, just the step's prompt, the record and the agent's tools. Prometheus then shows the trigger in the editor and lets a test run pick a milestone. Gaia and Talos run in parallel; Prometheus follows Gaia. With these, the engineer sets up a Retrospective agent and a workflow in the UI that creates a retrospective issue when a milestone is completed.", "issues": [{"key": "trigger-milestone-completed", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Workflows: 'Milestone completed' trigger (update triggers that match a field changing to a value)", "description": "<p>A Prometheus needs a workflow that starts when a milestone is completed, so an agent can write a retrospective and create an issue from it. The trigger catalog (<code>core/libs/workflows/TriggerEventCatalog.php</code>) has issue, comment, wiki and time-log events only. Its update events match the fields that changed, never the value they changed to. Milestone writes aren't wired to workflows at all.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Catalog: let an update event name a transition, e.g. <code>'to' =&gt; ['status' =&gt; 'completed']</code>. The event is raised only when the field changes to that value from another value. <code>raisedBy</code> then needs the audit's old and new values, not only the changed field names. Update <code>WorkflowTriggersComponent::raise</code> and <code>changed</code> to pass them. Keep the current behaviour for events without <code>to</code>.</li><li>Add <code>EventNames::MILESTONE_COMPLETED</code> (<code>milestone.completed</code>, already a live event) as a trigger: model <code>Milestone</code>, on update, field <code>status</code>, to <code>completed</code>, label 'Milestone completed'. Use the same rule as <code>MilestoneLiveEventsComponent</code> (~l.77): new status completed, old status not completed.</li><li>Add <code>Events\\\\WorkflowTriggers</code> to <code>MilestoneController</code> <code>$uses</code>.</li><li>Check that the payload, the describer (<code>TriggerEventDescriber</code>: fields and types for filters and expressions such as <code>{milestone.name}</code>), <code>ProjectIdResolver</code> (knows milestone), <code>SetFieldAction</code>'s model check and the test run (<code>TestRunPayload</code>, <code>WorkflowrunController</code> with <code>entityType</code> Milestone) all work for a milestone.</li><li><code>GET /workflowevent</code> lists the new trigger.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Completing a milestone (PATCH status to <code>completed</code>) starts the Active workflows with this trigger in the milestone's project. A Run agent step's actor step has <code>entityType</code> Milestone and the milestone's id.</li><li>Other milestone edits don't start them, and neither does saving an already completed milestone.</li><li>A test run against a milestone works.</li><li>Unit tests cover the catalog's transition matching. Regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other milestone triggers (created, started).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "talos-record-runs", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: run 'Run agent' workflow steps that aren't about an issue (no repo workspace)", "description": "<p>A workflow can now ask an agent to work on a record that isn't an issue: first case, a Retrospective agent started by 'Milestone completed', which reads the milestone and creates an issue. Gaia's Run agent step works with any record (<code>entityType</code>/<code>entityId</code> on the actor step), but Talos refuses it: <code>talos/lib/workflow_steps.py</code> <code>_subject</code> (~l.197) says 'Talos runs agents on issues only'. <code>dispatcher.run_step</code> (~l.274) and <code>_start</code> assume an issue and its repo: workspace, branch, Gaia pack, ship flow and CodeRabbit loop.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In <code>workflow_steps.py</code>, issue steps run exactly as today. Any other <code>entityType</code> becomes a record run.</li><li>A record run: Claude with the step's prompt, the agent's spec (role prompt, model, tool grants, permission mode, turn cap) and a short context block (record type, id and project; for a milestone, its name and dates through gaia-mcp <code>get_milestone</code>).</li><li>Its cwd is a scratch folder under the per-machine state (from <code>LOCAL_DIR</code>), not a repo checkout. No branch, no commit, no PR, no ship session, no CodeRabbit loop, no test slot.</li><li>Sessions are keyed by record (type + id), so <code>session: resume</code> works per record.</li><li>Report the outcome with the existing five (done, needs_input, blocked, failed, limit), and handle usage limits as issue steps do.</li><li>Keep the step logic in <code>lib/</code> functions that can be unit tested. Update the Talos README.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A Run agent step on a milestone is claimed, runs in a scratch folder without touching any repo, and reports done or a hand-off.</li><li>Issue steps behave exactly as before.</li><li>Unit tests cover the issue/record split, the record context and the outcome reporting.</li><li>Works on Windows and Linux.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> record runs that change code.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "editor-milestone-trigger", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: show the 'Milestone completed' trigger and test-run a milestone", "description": "<p>Gaia adds a 'Milestone completed' workflow trigger (listed by <code>GET /workflowevent</code>) so a workflow can start an agent when a milestone is completed. The editor from aprom-4038 and 4057 keeps its own <code>catalog.js</code> copy of Gaia's node kinds and triggers (noted on aprom-4038), and its test run may only pick issues.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Check where the palette and the trigger form get their triggers. If they're hard-coded, add <code>milestone.completed</code> (label 'Milestone completed', module Milestone). Better: take the triggers from the cached <code>workflowevent</code> catalog so later triggers need no UI change.</li><li>The properties panel's field and expression pickers offer the milestone's fields (from the trigger catalog's payload paths).</li><li>Test run: when the trigger's module is Milestone, the record picker lists the scope's milestones (<code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code>, searchable), and the run posts <code>entityType</code> Milestone with the milestone's id.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A workflow with the Milestone completed trigger and a Run agent step can be built, saved, activated and test-run against a milestone.</li><li>Mirage handlers and an integration or acceptance test cover the trigger and the milestone picker.</li></ul>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["trigger-milestone-completed"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-03 06:10:41	2026-11-03 06:10:41	f
12ef67196af4-6cc7-77af-393c270651bb	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	2	{"summary": "First slice of the collaborative Docs module: real-time co-editing with presence. Gaia gets a Docstate resource that holds each doc's Yjs CRDT state (the master copy of the content; Doc.body becomes the derived HTML copy), plus a fix so Doc/Docstate writes need doc.update and are refused on locked docs. A Hocuspocus collab server, run as a separate process in the hermes repo, signs users in through Gaia and saves the state with the connected user's token. In Prometheus, a Tiptap editor component (formatting, tables, checklists, outline) comes first. The collab client then connects it to the server with autosave status and offline recovery, and the presence issue adds avatars, live cursors and 'is typing'. The Prometheus issues build on the deferred aprom-4489 (data layer) and aprom-4490 (doc page).", "issues": [{"key": "doc-state-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Docstate resource for the doc's Yjs state, and the Docs storage decisions", "description": "<p>Docs get real-time co-editing. Each document's content becomes a Yjs CRDT state, kept live by a collab server (A Hermes) and saved to Gaia, so it survives server restarts. <code>Doc.body</code> stays as the readable HTML snapshot used for search, export and agents.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Docstate</code> (table <code>docstate</code>), following <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code> (exemplar gaia#264, the Doc resource): <code>docId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>projectId</code> varchar(36) required (the doc's project, for the ACL group), <code>state</code> text nullable (base64-encoded Yjs update), <code>byteSize</code> int, plus the standard id, dates, createdUser, modifiedUser and deleted fields. Behaviours: createdUser, modifiedUser, dateCreated, dateModified, softDelete. No auditBehavior, because it would copy the blob on every save.</li><li>Relationships: <code>doc</code> hasOne Doc (docId); add the inverse <code>docstate</code> hasOne on <code>Doc</code>.</li><li>Validation: one Docstate per doc (a second create for the same <code>docId</code> fails validation); <code>docId</code> must be a doc in the same <code>projectId</code>.</li><li>ACL metadata <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via projectId, permissions <code>docstate.get/create/update/delete</code>. No permission seed SQL.</li><li>Model, empty controller, <code>core/config/models.php</code>, <code>core/config/routes.php</code>, <code>routes.v1.json</code>, backend api placeholders and regenerated outputs as in B.md. api-tester harness/seed rows plus acl.json (member with and without docstate.*, non-member) and client.json cases (create, get by docId, update, duplicate docId rejected).</li><li><code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>: add D-002 (the Yjs state in Docstate is the master copy of a doc's content; <code>Doc.body</code> is a derived HTML snapshot written by the collab server and not edited directly) and D-003 (the collab server writes Docstate and Doc.body with the connected user's own token, so Gaia ACL and modifiedUser stay authoritative; there is no service account).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a project member with docstate.* can create, read and update one state row per doc; non-members are denied; the regenerated docs and graph have no drift; the decisions are recorded.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> version history, locked enforcement (separate issue), sharing.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 12, "sizeReason": "A standard new-resource bundle per B.md (metadata, model, controller, config, routes, api-tester cases) plus the decisions doc; splitting it would leave a half resource that breaks dev.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-write-guard", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: require doc.update for Doc/Docstate writes and reject writes on locked docs", "description": "<p>The collab server and the UI rely on Gaia to refuse writes a user isn't allowed to make. The review of agaia-4488 (gaia#264) found that a project member with only <code>doc.get</code>/<code>doc.create</code> got 200 on <code>PATCH /api/v1/doc/{id}</code>, and that <code>Doc.locked</code> is stored but not enforced.</p><ul><li>Find why update was authorized without <code>doc.update</code> (check how RestController/ACL authorizes PATCH for project-group resources, and whether other resources are affected) and fix it at the root. If the cause is in shared ACL code, fix it there and add denial cases for one other resource too.</li><li>Enforce <code>locked</code>: while a doc is locked, updates to its <code>body</code> and to its <code>Docstate</code> are rejected (403 or a validation error, following the layering in the Design section). Only the doc's owner (<code>ownerId</code>) or a user with the project admin role may change <code>locked</code>, like the wiki lock today.</li><li>api-tester acl.json cases: update and delete denied without doc.update/doc.delete; Docstate update denied without docstate.update; body and Docstate update rejected on a locked doc; lock/unlock by owner allowed, by another editor denied.</li><li>Record the lock rule as a decision in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the new denial cases pass and the existing Doc cases still pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-doc sharing roles, ownerId validation against project members.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-state-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "collab-server", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Docs collab server: Hocuspocus process with Gaia auth and Docstate persistence", "description": "<p>Projects4Me Docs need Google-Docs-style co-editing. Each doc is a Yjs CRDT document that must be held in memory, synced between browsers and saved. Hermes' relay can't do this (D-001 locked stateless relay, D-002 browsers never publish), so this adds a <strong>separate</strong> collab server process to this repo, with its own entrypoint, port and Docker service. It shares no runtime with the relay and changes no relay code.</p><ul><li>ADR in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>: the collab server is a separate process; it holds Yjs documents and awareness only, persists through Gaia, and the relay rules D-001 to D-009 are unchanged.</li><li>New dependencies: <code>@hocuspocus/server</code>, <code>yjs</code>, <code>@tiptap/html</code> and the Tiptap extensions listed below (approved for this module).</li><li>Document name contract: <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>. The client sends the user's Gaia OAuth access token as the Hocuspocus token.</li><li>onAuthenticate: call Gaia <code>GET /api/v1/user/me</code> with the token (reuse the request helper in <code>src/auth/gaia-session.js</code>). Reject without <code>doc.get</code> in <code>aclPermissions</code>, then <code>GET /api/v1/doc/&lt;id&gt;</code> with the same token (reject on 403/404). The connection is read-only when the user lacks <code>doc.update</code> or the doc is <code>locked</code>.</li><li>onLoadDocument: load the Docstate for the doc (<code>GET /api/v1/docstate</code> filtered by docId) and apply the base64 state; start empty if there is none.</li><li>onStoreDocument (debounce about 2 s, max 10 s, and on last disconnect): encode the state, create or PATCH the Docstate, and PATCH <code>Doc.body</code> with the HTML generated from the Yjs fragment. Use the token of a connected user who has write access.</li><li><strong>Schema contract with Prometheus:</strong> the HTML is generated with the same Tiptap extension list as the Prometheus editor: StarterKit, Underline, Link, Table/TableRow/TableHeader/TableCell, TaskList/TaskItem. Keep it in one module (e.g. <code>collab/schema.js</code>) and document it in the README.</li><li>Config by env (<code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>COLLAB_PORT</code>), a docker-compose service, README section.</li><li>Unit tests with a stubbed Gaia: rejected token, missing doc.get, read-only for no doc.update and for locked, load applies stored state, store creates then updates the Docstate and writes the HTML body.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two clients editing <code>doc:&lt;id&gt;</code> converge; after a restart the content reloads from Gaia; unauthorized users can't connect; read-only users can't change the document.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> agents as server-side peers, version snapshots, comments.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-state-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 12, "sizeReason": "A new service process: entrypoint, auth, persistence and schema modules, Docker/compose wiring, README, ADR and their tests. Auth and persistence can't ship apart, because the server is unusable without both.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-editor", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Tiptap editor component with toolbar, tables, checklists and outline", "description": "<p>The Docs module needs a structured rich-text editor that can later co-edit through Yjs. Toast UI can't, so Docs uses Tiptap (open-source packages only). This issue builds the editor as a standalone component. Real-time wiring comes in a later issue.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>@tiptap/core</code>, <code>@tiptap/starter-kit</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-underline</code>, <code>-link</code>, <code>-table</code>, <code>-table-row</code>, <code>-table-header</code>, <code>-table-cell</code>, <code>-task-list</code>, <code>-task-item</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>utils/docs/schema.js</code>: the single list of extensions. <strong>This is a contract with the Hermes collab server</strong>, which makes the HTML snapshot from the same list, so changing it needs a matching Hermes change.</li><li><code>Docs::Editor</code> (<code>components/docs/editor.{js,hbs}</code>): mounts Tiptap on an element. Args <code>@content</code> (initial HTML), <code>@editable</code>, <code>@extensions</code> (extra extensions added to the schema list, used later for collaboration), <code>@onReady(editor)</code>. Destroys the editor on teardown. No persistence.</li><li><code>Docs::Toolbar</code>: bold, italic, underline, strike, H1 to H3, bullet and ordered list, checklist, blockquote, code block, link, insert table and add/remove rows and columns. Buttons are <code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code> with Font Awesome 4 icons, <code>aria-pressed</code> for active marks, and the toolbar is hidden when not editable.</li><li><code>Docs::Outline</code>: a <code>col-md-4</code> side box listing the document's headings; clicking or pressing Enter scrolls to the heading.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code> (square edges, colours from <code>variables.scss</code> only). Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Integration tests: renders the content, a toolbar action applies a mark, read-only hides the toolbar and blocks typing, the outline lists headings and scrolls.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the component renders and edits formatted content, tables and checklists, and follows <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> saving, real-time collaboration, images and attachments, comments, suggestions.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Editor, toolbar and outline components (js+hbs each), the schema module, styles, translations and tests. The toolbar and outline are small and only make sense with the editor they drive.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-collab-client", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: real-time co-editing on the doc page with autosave status and offline recovery", "description": "<p>Connects the Docs editor to the Hermes collab server, so several people edit one doc live and changes save themselves with no Save button.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>yjs</code>, <code>@hocuspocus/provider</code>, <code>y-indexeddb</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>config/environment.js</code>: <code>ENV.docs.collabUrl</code> (no secrets).</li><li><code>services/doc-collab.js</code>: <code>open(docId)</code> creates a Y.Doc, an <code>IndexeddbPersistence</code> for offline recovery and a <code>HocuspocusProvider</code> (name <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>, token = the session's current access token, refreshed through <code>services/session.js</code> before a reconnect). Exposes tracked <code>status</code> (connecting, saving, saved, offline) and <code>readOnly</code> (from the server). <code>close()</code> destroys both. One responsibility: the connection; no UI.</li><li>Doc page from aprom-4490 (<code>app.project.doc.page</code>): renders <code>Docs::Editor</code> with the Collaboration extension bound to the Y.Doc. Editable only when <code>acl</code> allows doc.update, the doc isn't locked and the server didn't mark the connection read-only. Opens on route enter and closes on exit.</li><li>First open of an existing doc: if the Y.Doc is still empty after the first sync and <code>doc.body</code> has content, load it into the editor once.</li><li><code>Docs::SaveStatus</code> in the record box header: \\"Saving…\\", \\"All changes saved\\", \\"Offline – changes are kept on this device\\".</li><li>Tests: the service with a stubbed provider (status transitions, readOnly, close on exit) and an acceptance test of the page in read-only and editable modes with the service stubbed (Mirage has no websocket).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two browsers on the same doc see each other's edits live; reloading keeps the content; edits made offline sync after reconnecting; a locked doc, or a user without doc.update, gets a read-only editor.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence and cursors (next issue), version history.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-editor", "collab-server", "aprom-4489", "aprom-4490"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-presence", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: who's in the doc, live cursors and selections, and 'is typing'", "description": "<p>Collaborators should see who else is in a doc and where they are working, like Google Docs. This uses the collab server's awareness channel from <code>services/doc-collab.js</code>; nothing is stored and Hermes isn't involved.</p><ul><li>Dependency: <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration-cursor</code> (approved for this module).</li><li>Awareness state contract: <code>{ user: { id, name, color }, typing: boolean }</code>. Pick the colour deterministically from the user id out of a fixed palette of existing <code>variables.scss</code> colours; no new colours.</li><li>Live cursors and selections in the editor, each with a name label in the user's colour (styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>).</li><li>A \\"who's in the doc\\" avatar stack in the record box header, reusing the existing avatar markup (<code>components/project/member-avatars.hbs</code> pattern, <code>userimage/get</code>). One entry per user even with several tabs, with a tooltip of the name.</li><li>\\"<em>Name</em> is typing…\\": set <code>typing</code> on local input and clear it after about 2 s of no input; show it under the avatars.</li><li>Tests: the avatar stack de-duplicates users and hides the current user; the typing flag clears after the timeout; the colour is stable for an id.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with two users in a doc each sees the other's avatar, cursor, selection and typing indicator, and these disappear when the other leaves.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence on the All Docs list, follow-a-user mode.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-11 15:13:22	2026-11-11 15:13:22	f
c27283d96afb-dac1-e111-9a0ac3a34aba	de3303a86afa-5122-b3db-e6498ef24096	3	{"summary": "Fix the assignee avatar overlapping the description in narrow issue views (board quick view), caused by aprom-4610 putting a fixed 96px avatar in a viewport-sized Bootstrap column. First the container fix in issue details (flex row, avatar column sized by its content, description wraps beside it). In parallel, AppUi::Avatar gets an optional @minSize: it steps down through the standard sizes (at most l -> ml -> m) to fit the width its parent gives it. Then the issue assignee and the project overview manager use @size l with @minSize m in a column capped at 25% of the row.", "issues": [{"key": "assignee-row-fix", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue details: assignee avatar overlaps the description in narrow views", "description": "<p>Since aprom-4610 the assignee in issue details is a fixed 96px <code>AppUi::Avatar @size=\\"l\\"</code> inside <code>div.col-xs-3.col-md-2 &gt; .project-manager</code> (<code>components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code>, first row of the details box, next to <code>.col-xs-9.col-md-10.issue-description</code>). Bootstrap sizes those columns from the window width, but issue details also renders inside narrow panels (board and issue list quick views, gantt panel). There the column is about 40-60px wide and the avatar overlaps the description text. The old image was <code>width: 100%</code> and shrank with the column.</p><ul><li>Make that first row a flex row (scoped class in <code>styles/modules/issue.scss</code>): the assignee column <code>flex: 0 0 auto</code> with the gutter as padding, the description column <code>flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0</code>, so it wraps beside the avatar. Drop the <code>col-*</code> fractions from these two columns. Long words or URLs in the description wrap instead of overflowing.</li><li>The assignee name and the 'assigned to' label stay centred under the avatar, wrapping within the column's width (no wider than the avatar plus padding).</li><li>Keep <code>data-field</code> attributes, the user tag and links as they are.</li><li>Add a test (integration or acceptance) that renders issue details in a narrow container (e.g. 320px) and asserts the description column starts to the right of the avatar column (no overlap).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> in the board quick view at any window width, and on the issue page, the description never overlaps the assignee avatar; on a wide issue page the layout looks as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> resizing the avatar (separate issues); the project overview manager.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-min-size", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::Avatar: optional @minSize to step down to the space available", "description": "<p>Large avatars (l 96px) sit in columns whose width depends on where the view is rendered (full page vs narrow quick-view panels). Instead of each page choosing a fixed size, the avatar should step down through the standard sizes when its container is too narrow.</p><ul><li>New optional arg <code>@minSize</code> on <code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code> (same values and alias as <code>@size</code>). Without it, nothing changes and nothing is measured.</li><li>With it, the avatar observes the content width of its parent element (reuse <code>modifiers/observe-width.js</code>) and renders the largest standard size from <code>@size</code> down to <code>@minSize</code> (order xs, s, m, ml, l) whose width fits. If none fits, it renders <code>@minSize</code>. The rendered size is what <code>data-size</code> and the size class show.</li><li>No oscillation: decide only from the parent's width, never from the avatar's own; cover a parent whose width depends on its content in a test.</li><li>An invalid <code>@minSize</code> or one larger than <code>@size</code> is ignored (fixed <code>@size</code>).</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>: a resizable/width-controlled container showing l stepping to ml and m. Docs <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-avatar.md</code> + manifest: the new arg and when to use it (large avatars in containers of varying width).</li><li>Integration tests: fits at l, steps to ml, steps to m, stays at minSize when nothing fits, no observing without <code>@minSize</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @size=\\"l\\" @minSize=\\"m\\"&gt;</code> renders 96, 64 or 40px depending on its parent's width and updates when the parent resizes; existing usages are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> using it on pages (next issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-fit-assignee-manager", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue assignee and project manager avatars shrink to fit narrow columns (@minSize)", "description": "<p>The issue details assignee and the project overview manager show a 96px avatar (<code>@size=\\"l\\"</code>). In narrow views (board quick view, small windows) there is no room for it. Use the avatar's new <code>@minSize</code> so it steps down to ml (64px) or m (40px) when the column is narrow.</p><ul><li><code>components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> assignee (the flex row from the assignee row fix): <code>@size=\\"l\\" @minSize=\\"m\\"</code>; cap the assignee column at 25% of the row (<code>max-width</code> in <code>styles/modules/issue.scss</code>).</li><li><code>templates/app/project/index.hbs</code> manager in <code>.project-manager</code> (after aprom-4612): same row pattern as issue details (flex row, manager column auto width capped at 25%, the project details wrap beside it) and <code>@size=\\"l\\" @minSize=\\"m\\"</code>.</li><li>Name and label under the avatar keep wrapping within the column.</li><li>Tests: in a narrow container (e.g. 320px row) the avatar renders m or ml (check <code>data-size</code>), at full page width l; no overlap.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> in the board quick view the assignee avatar is smaller instead of cramped; on the full issue page and project overview it is 96px; nothing overlaps at any width.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["assignee-row-fix", "avatar-min-size", "aprom-4612"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 17:39:14	2026-11-16 19:16:35	f
b4d0edf56aef-41e1-a72a-c33e000f52b6	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	10	{"summary": "EzSearchCompact: a drop-in alternative to <EzSearch> for narrow places (idea list now; Threads, Gantt Cal, Task Board and the header later), multi-row by default or linear for one-row spaces. First the shared state of <EzSearch> moves into a base class both components extend. Then the saved-search name and edited state (Update / Save as new / Revert, new optional @onUpdateSavedSearch, store calls moved to a saved-search service) for both components, and in parallel the applied-filter chips component. Then <EzSearchCompact> itself (multi-row and linear layouts, Search and Clear on the bar, Saved and Filter buttons, chips, builder in a modal), and finally the idea list uses it with views.Idea.search metadata.", "issues": [{"key": "ez-search-base", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: move EzSearch's state into a shared base class", "description": "<p>A compact variant, <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code>, is coming. It must be a drop-in replacement for <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code>: same arguments, same behaviour, only the layout differs, so a view switches by changing the component name. To guarantee that, the state and actions of <code>app/components/ez-search/index.js</code> (aprom-4300, extended by aprom-4304) move into a base class that both components extend. This issue only moves code; nothing visible changes.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New <code>app/components/ez-search/base.js</code> (Glimmer component class, no template), holding:<ul><li>the tracked tree, parsing <code>@query</code> and its errors;</li><li>the saved-search selection (<code>@savedSearches</code>, <code>@activeSavedSearchId</code>, <code>@onSavedSearchChange</code>);</li><li>apply (<code>@onApply</code> with <code>@baseQuery</code> composed), Clear, Save (<code>@onSave</code>), <code>@aclContext</code>;</li><li>the builder open/closed state.</li></ul>Document the full argument list in its YUIDoc; it is the shared contract of both components.</li><li><code>app/components/ez-search/index.js</code> extends the base and keeps only what is specific to its toolbar layout.</li><li>Add a unit or integration test for the base's state transitions (parse, apply, clear, select and deselect a saved search) so both components are covered.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>All existing EzSearch tests and the Issue, Project, Agents and Workflows list acceptance tests pass unchanged.</li><li><code>index.js</code> contains no logic that a compact layout would also need.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> new behaviour, the compact component.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4304"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ez-saved-name-edited", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: show the active saved search's name and an edited state with Update, Save as new and Revert", "description": "<p>When a saved search is applied, people should see which one it is, and changing it should not silently drop it. Today (aprom-4304) the mark is dropped as soon as an edited query is applied. New behaviour, agreed with the engineer from screen <code>compact-edited</code>:</p><ul><li>the Saved Searches button shows the active search's name;</li><li>after the query changes it shows \\"&lt;name&gt; · edited\\";</li><li>its menu offers Update \\"&lt;name&gt;\\", Save as new search… and Revert to saved.</li></ul><p>This goes in the shared base (<code>app/components/ez-search/base.js</code>, previous issue) so <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> gets it now and <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> gets it with no extra work. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Base:<ul><li>Track whether the current tree differs from the active saved search's query (compare the serialized forms).</li><li>Keep the active search while edited.</li><li>Revert loads the saved query. Picking another search or Clear ends the edited state.</li><li>New optional <code>@onUpdateSavedSearch(search, query)</code>: Update calls it, and Save as new calls <code>@onSave(query)</code> as today.</li><li>The menu entries only show when the related callback is given.</li></ul>Update the base's YUIDoc argument list.</li><li><code>app/components/ez-search/index.hbs</code>: the Saved Searches button shows the active name (truncated with an ellipsis and a <code>title</code> tooltip) and \\"edited\\". The menu gets the three entries above the list, with the active search checked.</li><li>New <code>app/services/saved-search.js</code>: the store calls for saved searches (load by <code>relatedTo</code> and optional <code>projectId</code> for the current user, create, update <code>searchquery</code>). <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code> (aprom-4327) delegates to it, so controllers that don't extend the list controller (the idea browser, next issues) can reuse it. Add <code>updateEzSavedSearch(search, query)</code> to <code>list.js</code>.</li><li>Issue and Project list templates pass <code>@onUpdateSavedSearch={{this.updateEzSavedSearch}}</code>. Agents and Workflows keep no save.</li><li>Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.savedSearch.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Integration tests for the name, the edited marker, Update, Save as new, Revert, and leaving the edited state via another search or Clear.</li><li>A unit test for the service.</li><li>An acceptance scenario on the Issue list: apply a saved search, change it, Update, reload, and see the updated query.</li><li>Existing tests pass. Where an aprom-4304 test expected the mark to drop, update it to the new behaviour.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> renaming or deleting saved searches, the compact component.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ez-search-base", "aprom-4327"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["compact-edited"]}, {"key": "ez-chips", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: applied-filter chips component", "description": "<p>In narrow places the formatted query is too long to read, so <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> shows the applied conditions as removable chips (screen <code>compact-multirow</code>: \\"Status: Open ×\\", \\"Created by: Hammad Hassan ×\\"). This issue builds the chips as their own component over the query tree; the compact component uses it next. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search/applied-filters.{js,hbs}</code>: <code>&lt;EzSearch::AppliedFilters @tree @schema @onChange /&gt;</code>.<ul><li>One chip per complete top-level condition of the root group: the field label from the schema, the operator in words for anything other than equals (e.g. \\"Title contains: search\\", \\"Start between: 2026-05-01 and 2026-08-31\\"), and the display value (enum and user labels from the schema values, IN values joined with commas).</li><li>A nested group is one chip: \\"Any of: …\\" for OR, \\"All of: …\\" for AND, built from its conditions.</li><li>Removing a chip calls <code>@onChange</code> with the tree without that condition or group, using the <code>app/utils/query/ast.js</code> helpers. The caller applies it.</li><li>Incomplete conditions get no chip.</li></ul></li><li>Markup: <code>btn btn-default btn-xs</code> chips with the value in <code>strong</code> and an <code>fa-times</code>, wrapping onto more lines. Long values are truncated with an ellipsis and a <code>title</code> tooltip. Render as text, never <code>htmlSafe</code>.</li><li>Styles go in <code>app/styles/components/ez-search-chips.scss</code> (imported in <code>app.scss</code>, scoped). Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.chips.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>Chips render for equals, contains, IN, BETWEEN and a nested OR group.</li><li>Removing each chip emits the expected tree.</li><li>Incomplete rows are ignored.</li><li>Labels come from the schema.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> editing a chip in place, using chips on <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code>.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["compact-multirow"]}, {"key": "ez-search-compact", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "EzSearchCompact: drop-in compact ezSearch, multi-row or linear", "description": "<p>Narrow places (the idea list now; Threads, Gantt Cal, Task Board and the app header later) need ezSearch without the full toolbar. <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> is a drop-in replacement for <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code>: it extends the same base (<code>app/components/ez-search/base.js</code>) and takes exactly the same arguments, so a view switches by changing the component name. Its only extra argument is <code>@linear</code>. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search-compact/index.{js,hbs}</code> (Glimmer, extends the base; no logic of its own beyond layout).</li><li><strong>Multi-row</strong> (default, screens <code>compact-multirow</code>, <code>compact-edited</code>, <code>compact-mobile</code>):<ul><li>Row 1: <code>EzSearch::SearchBar</code> across the full width, with <strong>Search</strong> (<code>btn-primary</code>, <code>fa-search</code>) and <strong>Clear</strong> (<code>btn-default</code>, <code>fa-times</code>) attached at its right end (Bootstrap <code>input-group input-group-sm</code> look). The suggestion menu and errors show under the bar.</li><li>Row 2: <strong>Saved</strong>: <code>fa-bookmark-o</code> \\"Saved\\" when none is active; <code>btn-primary</code> with <code>fa-bookmark</code> and the name (plus \\"· edited\\") when one is. The menu opens left-aligned with the edited entries and the list, plus \\"Save current search…\\" when <code>@onSave</code> is given. Then <strong>Filter</strong> (<code>fa-sliders</code>) with a <code>label label-primary</code> badge counting the complete conditions.</li><li>Row 3: <code>EzSearch::AppliedFilters</code>; removing a chip applies immediately.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Linear</strong> (<code>@linear={{true}}</code>, screen <code>compact-linear-header</code>): one row with the Saved icon button (the active name, truncated, when one is active), the bar filling the rest, Filter with its badge, Search and Clear as icon buttons. No chips. Icon-only buttons get translated <code>title</code> tooltips.</li><li>Filter opens the builder in a <code>bootstrap-modal</code> (screen <code>idea-search-a-builder</code>): the formatted query, <code>EzSearch::Panel</code>, and footer buttons Clear (left), Cancel and Search. Search applies and closes; Cancel discards the panel's changes.</li><li>The bar needs no form-field margin (as aprom-4308 did for EzSearch). If <code>EzSearch::SearchBar</code> can't sit inside an input group as it is, add a layout option to it rather than duplicating it.</li><li><code>app/styles/components/ez-search-compact.scss</code> (imported, scoped under <code>.ez-search-compact</code>): square edges, existing tokens. It fills its container's width at any size, down to 390px.</li><li>Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearchCompact.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>The same argument set as <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code>: render both with identical arguments and check apply, clear, saved-search select/edit/update and save produce the same callbacks.</li><li>Multi-row: the rows, the badge count, chip removal applying, and Search/Clear.</li><li>Linear: a single row (bar, Filter, Search and Clear share one top) and no chips.</li><li>The modal applies on Search and discards on Cancel.</li><li>Checked in a browser in a <code>col-md-3</code> column at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> using it on any page (next issues and later phases), the header integration.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ez-search-base", "ez-saved-name-edited", "ez-chips"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["compact-multirow", "compact-edited", "compact-linear-header", "compact-mobile", "idea-search-a-builder"]}, {"key": "ez-idea-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea list: search with EzSearchCompact", "description": "<p>The idea list (the <code>col-md-3</code> browser in <code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>) has no search. Add <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> (multi-row) under its box header, driven by search metadata as the list-view architecture requires (<code>docs/architecture/metadata-views/architecture.md</code>). <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>: add <code>views.Idea.search</code>:<ul><li>module <code>Idea</code>, text field <code>Idea.title</code>;</li><li><code>Idea.title</code> and <code>Idea.description</code> as text;</li><li><code>Idea.status</code> as an enum (open, archived; source <code>translation</code> on <code>views.app.idea.status</code>; add <code>open</code> if missing);</li><li><code>createdBy.name</code> as a user field (source <code>members</code>);</li><li><code>Idea.dateCreated</code> and <code>Idea.dateModified</code> as dates;</li><li>aliases title, description, status, creator/author, created, updated.</li></ul>The plan progress label is computed client-side and can't be searched in Gaia; leave it out.</li><li><code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code> (~l.47 loads all ideas with <code>(Idea.projectId : X)</code>, <code>limit -1</code>):<ul><li>Load the schema with <code>query-schema</code> <code>load('Idea', {projectId})</code> and the project's saved searches through <code>services/saved-search.js</code> (<code>relatedTo: 'idea'</code>, <code>projectId</code>).</li><li>With a query, load <code>((Idea.projectId : X) AND (&lt;query&gt;))</code>. Keep the unfiltered count for the header.</li></ul></li><li><code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>:<ul><li>Add <code>query</code> and <code>searchId</code> to <code>queryParams</code> (next to <code>view</code>) and to <code>linkQuery</code>, so the search stays when another idea is opened.</li><li>Apply, saved-search select, save and update use the saved-search service. Don't copy the list controller's code.</li><li><code>reloadIdeas</code> (Hermes reloads) keeps the active query.</li><li>While a search is active, matching archived ideas are listed after the open ones with their Archived label and the \\"Show archived\\" footer is hidden; without a search the list behaves as today.</li></ul></li><li><code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>: the header shows \\"Ideas &lt;count&gt;\\" or \\"Ideas &lt;n&gt; of &lt;total&gt;\\" while searching, and <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> sits in a <code>box-body</code> above the list. Keep the save dialog in the page, as on the Issue list.</li><li>Mirage: the idea handler records the last <code>query</code> param.</li><li>Acceptance (<code>tests/acceptance/idea/</code> + steps):<ol><li>Type and run a query: the list is requested with it and the count shows \\"n of total\\".</li><li>Remove a chip: it re-runs.</li><li>Apply a saved search: its name shows. Change it: \\"edited\\" shows. Update it.</li><li>Open another idea: the search stays.</li><li>An error shows and nothing is sent.</li></ol></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios pass.</li><li>The existing idea tests (create, page, plan review, live updates, collapse) pass.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> searching message text, Mine, sorting, tags/categories, richer rows, plan progress as a search field.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ez-search-compact"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["compact-multirow", "compact-edited", "compact-mobile"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 17:49:40	2026-11-07 17:52:22	f
88ab90d36ae9-639d-5b13-139ddeee5a6d	b0c568b96ae9-5105-5b13-551a8315c38b	2	{"summary": "One Prometheus issue in milestone aga-v2: while the Start an idea form (route app.project.idea.create) is open, the idea browser's New idea button is shown as a grey, non-clickable disabled button; on any other idea route it stays the normal blue link.", "issues": [{"key": "new-idea-disabled", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: show the New idea button disabled while the Start an idea form is open", "description": "<p>The <strong>New idea</strong> button in the idea browser stays an active blue button while the user is already on the <em>Start an idea</em> form, so it looks as if it does something. While the form is open, it should look disabled and not be clickable.</p><ul><li><code>app/controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>: inject the <code>router</code> service and add an <code>isCreating</code> getter (YUIDoc) that is true when <code>router.currentRouteName === 'app.project.idea.create'</code>.</li><li><code>app/templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code> (box-tools, inside the existing <code>AccessControl @aclContext=\\"idea.create\\"</code>): when <code>isCreating</code> is true, render <code>&lt;span class=\\"btn btn-default btn-sm disabled\\" aria-disabled=\\"true\\" data-new-idea&gt;</code> with the same icon and label instead of the <code>LinkTo</code>. Otherwise keep the current <code>LinkTo</code> with <code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code>. Use only Bootstrap classes and add no new styles.</li><li>Acceptance test (Gherkin, ember-cli-yadda on Mirage): on the create page the <code>[data-new-idea]</code> button has the <code>disabled</code> class and is not a link. After you open an existing idea or cancel the form, it is the blue link again. Put any feature-only steps in a per-feature steps file, not <code>steps.js</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>On <code>app.project.idea.create</code>, the New idea button is grey (<code>btn-default disabled</code>), cannot be clicked or reached with Tab, and has <code>aria-disabled=\\"true\\"</code>.</li><li>On the ideas index and on an idea page, the button looks and works as it does today.</li><li>The button still shows only for users with the <code>idea.create</code> permission.</li><li>Tests and lint pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any other change to the idea browser or the create form.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["create-open", "idea-open"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-03 07:43:04	2026-11-03 07:44:27	f
8e43eb136af4-7c69-00ad-499bb6f782f5	5a1482d46af4-0fdf-00ad-c45029d7a40d	2	{"summary": "Docs module foundation, built from scratch beside the existing Wiki (Wiki is left as is). Gaia gets a standard project-scoped Doc REST resource (title, body, projectId, ownerId, locked, tags via the shared Tag/Tagged tables) plus a decision record. Prometheus then gets the doc model/adapter/serializer with Mirage support, the doc page (app.project.doc.page), and, in parallel, the All Docs list (app.project.doc.index) and Create Doc form (app.project.doc.create), each with its sidebar entry, ACL route mapping, loading skeleton, empty state, translations and acceptance tests.", "issues": [{"key": "doc-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Doc resource (title, body, owner, locked, tags) as standard project-scoped CRUD", "description": "<p>Projects get a Docs module where teams create, list and open documents. This adds the backing <code>Doc</code> resource as plain REST CRUD, following the new-resource guide <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code> (exemplar gaia#193, Idea).</p><ul><li><code>app/metadata/model/Doc.php</code>, table <code>doc</code>: <code>title</code> varchar(255) required, <code>body</code> text (nullable), <code>projectId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>ownerId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>locked</code> bool default false, plus the standard <code>id</code>, <code>dateCreated</code>, <code>dateModified</code>, <code>createdUser</code>, <code>modifiedUser</code>, <code>deleted</code>. Behaviours: <code>createdUserBehavior</code>, <code>modifiedUserBehavior</code>, <code>dateCreatedBehavior</code>, <code>dateModifiedBehavior</code>, <code>softDeleteBehavior</code>, <code>auditBehavior</code>.</li><li>Relationships: <code>project</code> belongsTo Project, <code>owner</code> hasOne User (via <code>ownerId</code>), <code>createdBy</code>/<code>modifiedBy</code> hasOne User, <code>tag</code> hasManyToMany Tag via Tagged (<code>relatedTo = 'doc'</code>), <code>tagged</code> hasMany Tagged. Add the inverse <code>doc</code> relationship on <code>Tagged</code> and <code>docs</code> on <code>Project</code>, the same way Issue is wired.</li><li>ACL metadata: <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via <code>projectId</code>, so only project members with the <code>doc.*</code> permissions can read/create/update/delete.</li><li>Empty <code>app/models/Doc.php</code> and <code>DocController</code> (RestController subclass), the <code>'Doc'</code> line in <code>core/config/models.php</code>, the <code>doc</code> route in <code>core/config/routes.php</code>, <code>routes.v1.json</code>, the placeholders in <code>generate-backend-apis.php</code> and a regenerated <code>backend.json</code>.</li><li>api-tester: harness table and seed rows, fixture ids, <code>acl.json</code> cases (member with and without <code>doc.*</code>, non-member) and <code>client.json</code> cases (create, list by project, get with <code>owner</code> and <code>tag</code> rels, delete).</li><li>New <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>, D-001: Docs is a new, independent module built from scratch; the existing Wiki is kept unchanged beside it, shares no code or tables with Docs (beyond the generic Tag/Tagged tagging), and no migration or retirement of Wiki is planned.</li><li>No permission seed SQL (the reviewer grants <code>doc.*</code> by hand). Regenerate the gaia-dev graph and <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a project member with <code>doc.create</code> can POST a doc and list it with <code>((Doc.projectId : X))</code>; a user without <code>doc.read</code> or outside the project gets 403/empty; tags attach through Tagged; the full test suite and CI drift checks pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> live events, enforcing <code>locked</code>, owner-change rules, body format/versioning, any change to Wiki.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "A new resource has a fixed set of touchpoints (metadata, parent relationships, model, controller, models/routes config, api-tester catalog and acl/client cases) that must ship together, or dev is left with a resource that has no ACL cases; the decision doc is one small file.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-data", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: doc model, adapter, serializer and Mirage support", "description": "<p>Data layer for the new Docs module, used by the doc page, All Docs and Create Doc screens. It reads the Gaia <code>doc</code> resource. Docs is a new module built from scratch; don't reuse or change the Wiki code.</p><ul><li><code>app/models/doc.js</code> (native class, YUIDoc): <code>title</code>, <code>body</code>, <code>projectId</code>, <code>ownerId</code>, <code>locked</code> (boolean), <code>dateCreated</code>, <code>dateModified</code>, <code>createdUser</code>, <code>modifiedUser</code>; relationships <code>project</code>, <code>owner</code> (user), <code>tag</code> (hasMany tag, async). Follow the <code>idea</code> model for naming and date handling.</li><li><code>app/adapters/doc.js</code> and <code>app/serializers/doc.js</code> extending the application adapter/serializer with no custom endpoints (singular path <code>/api/v1/doc</code>).</li><li>Mirage: <code>mirage/factories/doc.js</code> (realistic titles, an owner, some tags) and handlers in <code>mirage/config.js</code> for list with the Gaia <code>query</code> filter on projectId, get by id, create and delete, written like the <code>idea</code> handlers. Tagged rows with <code>relatedTo: 'doc'</code> must work in Mirage.</li><li>Unit tests for the model and serializer.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>store.query('doc', { query: '((Doc.projectId : X))', rels: 'owner,tag' })</code>, <code>findRecord</code>, <code>createRecord().save()</code> and <code>destroyRecord</code> work against Mirage; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> routes and UI (separate issues), live updates.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-api"], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-page", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: doc page route (app.project.doc.page) with detail layout, skeleton and empty state", "description": "<p>Opening a doc in a project. This is the page the All Docs rows link to and Create Doc lands on after saving. Editing the body comes later; this page is read-only.</p><ul><li><code>app/router.js</code>: add <code>this.route('doc', function(){ this.route('page', {path: '/:doc_id'}); })</code> under <code>project</code> (the index and create routes are added by their own issues).</li><li><code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code>: <code>{ name: 'app.project.doc.page', map: 'doc.read' }</code>.</li><li>Route <code>routes/app/project/doc/page.js</code> (native class, extends <code>routes/app.js</code>): loads the doc with <code>rels</code> for <code>owner</code> and <code>tag</code> only (no unbounded hasMany); a missing or forbidden doc shows the existing not-found/error handling.</li><li>Template <code>templates/app/project/doc/page.hbs</code> on the design-system detail pattern: <code>col-md-8</code> <code>box box-primary</code> with the title (lock icon <code>fa fa-lock</code> when <code>locked</code>) and the body as escaped text (no <code>htmlSafe</code>/triple-stash); when the body is empty, the design-system §4 empty state (\\"This doc has no content yet\\"). <code>col-md-4</code> side box with owner, tags (<code>label</code>s), created and last edited.</li><li><code>templates/app/project/doc/page-loading.hbs</code> skeleton matching the layout (design-system §4).</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Acceptance <code>.feature</code> (with steps in a per-feature steps file, not <code>steps.js</code>): opens a doc and sees title, owner, tags; empty body shows the empty state; a user without <code>doc.read</code> is redirected away.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the scenarios above pass on Mirage; page matches an existing detail screen side by side; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> editing, delete button, comments, presence, live updates.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-data"], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: All Docs list page (app.project.doc.index) and Docs sidebar item", "description": "<p>The project's list of docs, reached from a new \\"Docs\\" item in the sidebar.</p><ul><li><code>app/router.js</code>: add <code>this.route('index', {path: '/'})</code> to the <code>doc</code> route. <code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code>: <code>app.project.doc.index</code> → <code>doc.read</code>.</li><li>Sidebar: in <code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> <code>views.Navigation.items</code> add <code>Doc</code> (icon <code>file-text-o</code>, route <code>app.project.doc</code>, <code>anchorRoute: 'doc'</code>, <code>projectRelated: true</code>, <code>aclContext: 'doc.read'</code>) with <code>actions.section1.list</code> \\"All Docs\\" like the Issue item. The \\"Create Doc\\" child is added by the Create Doc issue; if it is already there, keep it.</li><li>Route <code>routes/app/project/doc/index.js</code> and controller <code>controllers/app/project/doc/index.js</code> extending <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>, modelled on <code>controllers/app/agent/index.js</code>: query <code>((Doc.projectId : X))</code> with rels <code>owner,tag</code>, sort by last edited desc, pagination, search by title.</li><li>Template <code>templates/app/project/doc/index.hbs</code>: list page pattern, one full-width <code>box box-primary</code> with search toolbar, table (title linking to <code>app.project.doc.page</code> with a lock icon when locked, owner, last edited, tags) and pagination; row delete through the base list's delete with <code>aclContext=\\"doc.delete\\"</code>; a \\"New doc\\" button (<code>aclContext=\\"doc.create\\"</code>) to <code>app.project.doc.create</code> if that route exists, otherwise the Create Doc issue adds it.</li><li><code>templates/app/project/doc/index-loading.hbs</code> skeleton and an empty state (\\"No docs yet\\") per design-system §4.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; acceptance <code>.feature</code> with a per-feature steps file: list shows seeded docs with owner/tags, search filters, empty state, delete removes a row, no <code>doc.read</code> → route blocked and sidebar item hidden.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> scenarios pass on Mirage; screen matches an existing list page side by side; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> saved searches beyond what <code>list.js</code> gives for free, export, mass update, live updates.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-page"], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-create", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Create Doc form (app.project.doc.create) and sidebar entry", "description": "<p>Lets a project member with <code>doc.create</code> start a new doc. The body is written later in the editor, so the form asks only for title and tags.</p><ul><li><code>app/router.js</code>: add <code>this.route('create')</code> to the <code>doc</code> route. <code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code>: <code>app.project.doc.create</code> → <code>doc.create</code>.</li><li>Sidebar: add <code>actions.section1.create</code> \\"Create Doc\\" (route <code>app.project.doc.create</code>, <code>aclContext: 'doc.create'</code>) to the Docs item in <code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>; if the Docs item isn't there yet, add it (icon <code>file-text-o</code>, route <code>app.project.doc</code>, <code>aclContext: 'doc.read'</code>). If All Docs has shipped, add its \\"New doc\\" button (<code>aclContext=\\"doc.create\\"</code>) to the list's box-tools.</li><li>Route/controller <code>app/project/doc/create</code> (native classes) and <code>templates/app/project/doc/create.hbs</code> on the create/edit pattern: <code>col-md-8</code> form box with <code>FormFields::FieldText</code> title (required, validation message) and <code>FormFields::FieldRelateMulti</code> for tags (existing project tags), <code>col-md-4</code> side box with owner (current user) and project; Save/Cancel below the boxes.</li><li>Save: creates the doc with <code>projectId</code> and <code>ownerId</code> = current user, then the Tagged rows (<code>relatedTo: 'doc'</code>), then transitions to <code>app.project.doc.page</code>. Ignore a second submit while saving and disable Save; on failure show the error and roll back. Cancel returns to <code>app.project.doc.index</code> (or the project dashboard if that route doesn't exist yet).</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; acceptance <code>.feature</code> with a per-feature steps file: create with title and tags lands on the doc page; empty title shows validation; failed save shows an error; no <code>doc.create</code> → route blocked and sidebar child hidden.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> scenarios pass on Mirage; a created doc appears in All Docs; screen matches an existing create form side by side; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> body editing, creating new tags inline, templates, edit route.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-page"], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-11 09:55:26	2026-11-11 09:55:26	f
3ea6aeb56af4-3f4c-45d1-b23e8faaed9c	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	3	{"summary": "First slice of the collaborative Docs module: real-time co-editing with presence. Gaia gets a Docstate resource that holds each doc's Yjs CRDT state (the master copy of the content; Doc.body becomes the derived HTML copy), plus a fix so Doc/Docstate writes need doc.update and are refused on locked docs. A Hocuspocus collab server lives in the hermes repo as a self-contained collab/ package with its own dependencies and container, and can move to its own repo later. It signs users in through Gaia and saves the state with the connected user's token. In Prometheus, a Tiptap editor component (formatting, tables, checklists, outline) comes first. The collab client then connects it to the server with autosave status and offline recovery, and the presence issue adds avatars, live cursors and 'is typing'. The Prometheus issues build on the deferred aprom-4489 (data layer) and aprom-4490 (doc page).", "issues": [{"key": "doc-state-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Docstate resource for the doc's Yjs state, and the Docs storage decisions", "description": "<p>Docs get real-time co-editing. Each document's content becomes a Yjs CRDT state, kept live by a collab server (A Hermes) and saved to Gaia, so it survives server restarts. <code>Doc.body</code> stays as the readable HTML snapshot used for search, export and agents.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Docstate</code> (table <code>docstate</code>), following <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code> (exemplar gaia#264, the Doc resource): <code>docId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>projectId</code> varchar(36) required (the doc's project, for the ACL group), <code>state</code> text nullable (base64-encoded Yjs update), <code>byteSize</code> int, plus the standard id, dates, createdUser, modifiedUser and deleted fields. Behaviours: createdUser, modifiedUser, dateCreated, dateModified, softDelete. No auditBehavior, because it would copy the blob on every save.</li><li>Relationships: <code>doc</code> hasOne Doc (docId); add the inverse <code>docstate</code> hasOne on <code>Doc</code>.</li><li>Validation: one Docstate per doc (a second create for the same <code>docId</code> fails validation); <code>docId</code> must be a doc in the same <code>projectId</code>.</li><li>ACL metadata <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via projectId, permissions <code>docstate.get/create/update/delete</code>. No permission seed SQL.</li><li>Model, empty controller, <code>core/config/models.php</code>, <code>core/config/routes.php</code>, <code>routes.v1.json</code>, backend api placeholders and regenerated outputs as in B.md. api-tester harness/seed rows plus acl.json (member with and without docstate.*, non-member) and client.json cases (create, get by docId, update, duplicate docId rejected).</li><li><code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>: add D-002 (the Yjs state in Docstate is the master copy of a doc's content; <code>Doc.body</code> is a derived HTML snapshot written by the collab server and not edited directly) and D-003 (the collab server writes Docstate and Doc.body with the connected user's own token, so Gaia ACL and modifiedUser stay authoritative; there is no service account).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a project member with docstate.* can create, read and update one state row per doc; non-members are denied; the regenerated docs and graph have no drift; the decisions are recorded.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> version history, locked enforcement (separate issue), sharing.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 12, "sizeReason": "A standard new-resource bundle per B.md (metadata, model, controller, config, routes, api-tester cases) plus the decisions doc; splitting it would leave a half resource that breaks dev.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-write-guard", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: require doc.update for Doc/Docstate writes and reject writes on locked docs", "description": "<p>The collab server and the UI rely on Gaia to refuse writes a user isn't allowed to make. The review of agaia-4488 (gaia#264) found that a project member with only <code>doc.get</code>/<code>doc.create</code> got 200 on <code>PATCH /api/v1/doc/{id}</code>, and that <code>Doc.locked</code> is stored but not enforced.</p><ul><li>Find why update was authorized without <code>doc.update</code> (check how RestController/ACL authorizes PATCH for project-group resources, and whether other resources are affected) and fix it at the root. If the cause is in shared ACL code, fix it there and add denial cases for one other resource too.</li><li>Enforce <code>locked</code>: while a doc is locked, updates to its <code>body</code> and to its <code>Docstate</code> are rejected (403 or a validation error, following the layering in the Design section). Only the doc's owner (<code>ownerId</code>) or a user with the project admin role may change <code>locked</code>, like the wiki lock today.</li><li>api-tester acl.json cases: update and delete denied without doc.update/doc.delete; Docstate update denied without docstate.update; body and Docstate update rejected on a locked doc; lock/unlock by owner allowed, by another editor denied.</li><li>Record the lock rule as a decision in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the new denial cases pass and the existing Doc cases still pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-doc sharing roles, ownerId validation against project members.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-state-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "collab-server", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Docs collab server: self-contained collab/ package (Hocuspocus) with Gaia auth and Docstate persistence", "description": "<p>Projects4Me Docs need Google-Docs-style co-editing. Each doc is a Yjs CRDT document that must be held in memory, synced between browsers and saved to Gaia. The relay can't do this (D-001 locked stateless relay, D-002 browsers never publish). So a collab server is added to this repo as a <strong>self-contained package in <code>collab/</code></strong>: its own process, port and container, sharing no code or dependencies with the relay, so it can later move to its own repo by moving the folder.</p><ul><li><strong>Isolation:</strong> its own <code>collab/package.json</code> (dependencies <code>@hocuspocus/server</code>, <code>yjs</code>, <code>@tiptap/html</code> and the Tiptap extensions below, approved for this module; pick versions that run on Node 18, Hermes' runtime), its own entrypoint <code>collab/server.js</code>, its own Dockerfile and docker-compose service. No imports from the relay's <code>src/</code> and no changes to relay code: its own small Gaia client module, modelled on <code>src/auth/gaia-session.js</code>.</li><li><strong>ADR D-016</strong> in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>: the collab server lives in <code>collab/</code> as a separate process; it holds Yjs documents and awareness in memory only and persists only through Gaia; the relay rules D-001 to D-015 are unchanged. It moves to its own repo when it takes on agents or export, or when its releases start to clash with the relay's.</li><li><code>CLAUDE.md</code>: scope the rule \\"Hermes stays a locked relay: no domain logic, no storage\\" to the relay (<code>src/</code>), and add a short <code>collab/</code> section (what it may do, its own package.json, no imports across the two).</li><li>Root test script also runs <code>collab/</code> tests, so the existing hermes test command covers both.</li><li>Document name contract: <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>. The client sends the user's Gaia OAuth access token as the Hocuspocus token. Never log tokens or document content.</li><li>onAuthenticate: call Gaia <code>GET /api/v1/user/me</code> with the token. Reject without <code>doc.get</code> in <code>aclPermissions</code>, then <code>GET /api/v1/doc/&lt;id&gt;</code> with the same token (reject on 403/404). The connection is read-only when the user lacks <code>doc.update</code> or the doc is <code>locked</code>.</li><li>onLoadDocument: load the Docstate for the doc (<code>GET /api/v1/docstate</code> filtered by docId) and apply the base64 state; start empty if there is none.</li><li>onStoreDocument (debounce about 2 s, max 10 s, and on last disconnect): encode the state, create or PATCH the Docstate, and PATCH <code>Doc.body</code> with the HTML generated from the Yjs fragment. Use the token of a connected user who has write access.</li><li><strong>Schema contract with Prometheus:</strong> the HTML is generated with the same Tiptap extension list as the Prometheus editor: StarterKit, Underline, Link, Table/TableRow/TableHeader/TableCell, TaskList/TaskItem. Keep it in <code>collab/schema.js</code> and document it in <code>collab/README.md</code>, together with the env config (<code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>COLLAB_PORT</code>) and how to run it.</li><li>Unit tests with a stubbed Gaia: rejected token, missing doc.get, read-only for no doc.update and for locked, load applies stored state, store creates then updates the Docstate and writes the HTML body.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two clients editing <code>doc:&lt;id&gt;</code> converge; after a restart the content reloads from Gaia; unauthorized users can't connect; read-only users can't change the document; the relay's tests and image are unchanged apart from the test script.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> agents as server-side peers, version snapshots, comments, scaling beyond one instance.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-state-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "A new self-contained service package: entrypoint, auth, Gaia client/persistence and schema modules, its package.json, Dockerfile and compose service, README, ADR, CLAUDE.md, root test script and two test files. Auth and persistence can't ship apart, because the server is unusable without both.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-editor", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Tiptap editor component with toolbar, tables, checklists and outline", "description": "<p>The Docs module needs a structured rich-text editor that can later co-edit through Yjs. Toast UI can't, so Docs uses Tiptap (open-source packages only). This issue builds the editor as a standalone component. Real-time wiring comes in a later issue.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>@tiptap/core</code>, <code>@tiptap/starter-kit</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-underline</code>, <code>-link</code>, <code>-table</code>, <code>-table-row</code>, <code>-table-header</code>, <code>-table-cell</code>, <code>-task-list</code>, <code>-task-item</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>utils/docs/schema.js</code>: the single list of extensions. <strong>This is a contract with the Hermes collab server</strong> (<code>hermes/collab/schema.js</code>), which makes the HTML snapshot from the same list, so changing it needs a matching Hermes change.</li><li><code>Docs::Editor</code> (<code>components/docs/editor.{js,hbs}</code>): mounts Tiptap on an element. Args <code>@content</code> (initial HTML), <code>@editable</code>, <code>@extensions</code> (extra extensions added to the schema list, used later for collaboration), <code>@onReady(editor)</code>. Destroys the editor on teardown. No persistence.</li><li><code>Docs::Toolbar</code>: bold, italic, underline, strike, H1 to H3, bullet and ordered list, checklist, blockquote, code block, link, insert table and add/remove rows and columns. Buttons are <code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code> with Font Awesome 4 icons, <code>aria-pressed</code> for active marks, and the toolbar is hidden when not editable.</li><li><code>Docs::Outline</code>: a <code>col-md-4</code> side box listing the document's headings; clicking or pressing Enter scrolls to the heading.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code> (square edges, colours from <code>variables.scss</code> only). Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Integration tests: renders the content, a toolbar action applies a mark, read-only hides the toolbar and blocks typing, the outline lists headings and scrolls.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the component renders and edits formatted content, tables and checklists, and follows <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> saving, real-time collaboration, images and attachments, comments, suggestions.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Editor, toolbar and outline components (js+hbs each), the schema module, styles, translations and tests. The toolbar and outline are small and only make sense with the editor they drive.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-collab-client", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: real-time co-editing on the doc page with autosave status and offline recovery", "description": "<p>Connects the Docs editor to the collab server (<code>hermes/collab</code>), so several people edit one doc live and changes save themselves with no Save button.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>yjs</code>, <code>@hocuspocus/provider</code>, <code>y-indexeddb</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>config/environment.js</code>: <code>ENV.docs.collabUrl</code> (no secrets).</li><li><code>services/doc-collab.js</code>: <code>open(docId)</code> creates a Y.Doc, an <code>IndexeddbPersistence</code> for offline recovery and a <code>HocuspocusProvider</code> (name <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>, token = the session's current access token, refreshed through <code>services/session.js</code> before a reconnect). Exposes tracked <code>status</code> (connecting, saving, saved, offline) and <code>readOnly</code> (from the server). <code>close()</code> destroys both. One responsibility: the connection; no UI.</li><li>Doc page from aprom-4490 (<code>app.project.doc.page</code>): renders <code>Docs::Editor</code> with the Collaboration extension bound to the Y.Doc. Editable only when <code>acl</code> allows doc.update, the doc isn't locked and the server didn't mark the connection read-only. Opens on route enter and closes on exit.</li><li>First open of an existing doc: if the Y.Doc is still empty after the first sync and <code>doc.body</code> has content, load it into the editor once.</li><li><code>Docs::SaveStatus</code> in the record box header: \\"Saving…\\", \\"All changes saved\\", \\"Offline – changes are kept on this device\\".</li><li>Tests: the service with a stubbed provider (status transitions, readOnly, close on exit) and an acceptance test of the page in read-only and editable modes with the service stubbed (Mirage has no websocket).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two browsers on the same doc see each other's edits live; reloading keeps the content; edits made offline sync after reconnecting; a locked doc, or a user without doc.update, gets a read-only editor.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence and cursors (next issue), version history.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-editor", "collab-server", "aprom-4489", "aprom-4490"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-presence", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: who's in the doc, live cursors and selections, and 'is typing'", "description": "<p>Collaborators should see who else is in a doc and where they are working, like Google Docs. This uses the collab server's awareness channel from <code>services/doc-collab.js</code>; nothing is stored and the Hermes relay isn't involved.</p><ul><li>Dependency: <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration-cursor</code> (approved for this module).</li><li>Awareness state contract: <code>{ user: { id, name, color }, typing: boolean }</code>. Pick the colour deterministically from the user id out of a fixed palette of existing <code>variables.scss</code> colours; no new colours.</li><li>Live cursors and selections in the editor, each with a name label in the user's colour (styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>).</li><li>A \\"who's in the doc\\" avatar stack in the record box header, reusing the existing avatar markup (<code>components/project/member-avatars.hbs</code> pattern, <code>userimage/get</code>). One entry per user even with several tabs, with a tooltip of the name.</li><li>\\"<em>Name</em> is typing…\\": set <code>typing</code> on local input and clear it after about 2 s of no input; show it under the avatars.</li><li>Tests: the avatar stack de-duplicates users and hides the current user; the typing flag clears after the timeout; the colour is stable for an id.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with two users in a doc each sees the other's avatar, cursor, selection and typing indicator, and these disappear when the other leaves.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence on the All Docs list, follow-a-user mode.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-11 15:48:14	2026-11-11 15:48:14	f
388f11926afb-da5e-948b-bc6855ac3e7f	de3303a86afa-5122-b3db-e6498ef24096	4	{"summary": "Bug: on the task board the person avatar (AppUi::Avatar's img) is restyled by page CSS aimed at the global img-circle class and bare img selectors, while agents (span.agent-avatar) are not affected. AppUi::Avatar's image gets its own class instead of img-circle and resets the properties pages tend to set; the board and assignee-menu rules that reach into it are removed.", "issues": [{"key": "avatar-img-isolation", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::Avatar: person image picks up page CSS on the task board (img-circle rules)", "description": "<p>On the task board, the assignee avatar of a <strong>person</strong> on an issue card looks wrong, while agents look right and the same avatar is fine in issue details. Cause: for a person, <code>components/app-ui/avatar.hbs</code> (~l.17) renders <code>&lt;img class=\\"img-circle\\"&gt;</code>. Pages style that global AdminLTE class and bare <code>img</code> tags, and those rules are more specific than the component's <code>.app-ui-avatar &gt; img</code>. Agents render <code>span.agent-avatar</code>, so they escape.</p><p>Rules that reach the avatar's image today:</p><ul><li><code>styles/modules/board.scss:230</code> <code>.board .board-issue-item .img-circle</code> (3rem, 0.1rem #ddd border, object-fit). The card avatar is the compact <code>Issue::AssigneeSelect</code> in <code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs:126</code> (AppUi::Avatar @size s since aprom-4611).</li><li><code>styles/modules/board.scss:225</code> <code>.board-issue-item p &gt; img</code> (10rem !important).</li><li><code>styles/modules/issue.scss:540</code> <code>.users-list .dropdown .dropdown-menu li img</code> (20px, margin-right 0.5rem): the assignee menu options in issue details (xs avatars), where the margin pushes the image off its circle.</li></ul><p>Changes:</p><ul><li><code>avatar.hbs</code>: the person image uses a component class <code>app-ui-avatar-image</code> instead of <code>img-circle</code>.</li><li><code>styles/components/app-ui-avatar.scss</code>: style the image through <code>.app-ui-avatar .app-ui-avatar-image</code>: width and height 100%, <code>max-width: none</code>, margin 0, padding 0, border 0, round (50%), object-fit cover, display block.</li><li>Delete the board <code>.img-circle</code> rule if nothing else on the card uses <code>img-circle</code> (check the card markup), and the <code>p &gt; img</code> rule if it no longer has a target (check whether description images on cards need it; if they do, scope it to them). Remove the <code>img</code> sizing/margin in the issue.scss <code>.dropdown-menu li img</code> rule; the option avatar's own gap stays on its wrapper (<code>.assignee-select-option-avatar</code>).</li><li>Search the other stylesheets for rules on <code>.img-circle</code> or bare <code>img</code> inside containers that now render AppUi::Avatar (users-list, box-comment, user-block, gantt) and confirm they don't change the avatar's image; list any you leave in the PR.</li><li>Tests: an integration test that renders a person avatar inside a container carrying a hostile rule (e.g. a test-only class setting width, margin and border on <code>img</code> and <code>.img-circle</code>) is not realistic with scoped CSS, so instead assert the image has <code>app-ui-avatar-image</code> and no <code>img-circle</code>; an acceptance or integration check on the board card that the person avatar's computed width equals the agent's for the same size and it has no border.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-avatar.md</code>: note that pages must not style the avatar's inner elements; size comes only from <code>@size</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the task board, person and agent avatars on cards render at the same size (s, 30px) with no extra border; the assignee menus in issue details and on cards show xs avatars centred in their circle; issue details, comments and other pages look unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the wider dead-CSS cleanup (aprom-4618).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 19:57:44	2026-11-16 20:02:57	f
0d9343f06ae9-639d-5b13-3b09a37201ab	b0c568b96ae9-5105-5b13-551a8315c38b	1	{"summary": "One Prometheus issue: while the Start an idea form (route app.project.idea.create) is open, the idea browser's New idea button is shown as a grey, non-clickable disabled button; on any other idea route it stays the normal blue link.", "issues": [{"key": "new-idea-disabled", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: show the New idea button disabled while the Start an idea form is open", "description": "<p>The <strong>New idea</strong> button in the idea browser stays an active blue button while the user is already on the <em>Start an idea</em> form, so it looks as if it does something. While the form is open, it should look disabled and not be clickable.</p><ul><li><code>app/controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>: inject the <code>router</code> service and add an <code>isCreating</code> getter (YUIDoc) that is true when <code>router.currentRouteName === 'app.project.idea.create'</code>.</li><li><code>app/templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code> (box-tools, inside the existing <code>AccessControl @aclContext=\\"idea.create\\"</code>): when <code>isCreating</code> is true, render <code>&lt;span class=\\"btn btn-default btn-sm disabled\\" aria-disabled=\\"true\\" data-new-idea&gt;</code> with the same icon and label instead of the <code>LinkTo</code>. Otherwise keep the current <code>LinkTo</code> with <code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code>. Use only Bootstrap classes and add no new styles.</li><li>Acceptance test (Gherkin, ember-cli-yadda on Mirage): on the create page the <code>[data-new-idea]</code> button has the <code>disabled</code> class and is not a link. After you open an existing idea or cancel the form, it is the blue link again. Put any feature-only steps in a per-feature steps file, not <code>steps.js</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>On <code>app.project.idea.create</code>, the New idea button is grey (<code>btn-default disabled</code>), cannot be clicked or reached with Tab, and has <code>aria-disabled=\\"true\\"</code>.</li><li>On the ideas index and on an idea page, the button looks and works as it does today.</li><li>The button still shows only for users with the <code>idea.create</code> permission.</li><li>Tests and lint pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any other change to the idea browser or the create form.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["create-open", "idea-open"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-03 07:41:01	2026-11-03 07:43:42	f
d34909876ae9-2420-fee8-e80072636b80	994b17496ae9-2420-fee8-e1f463ff8479	1	{"summary": "A single Prometheus fix. The idea browser shows a spinner 'Loading' label on open ideas until their plan statuses have loaded, instead of falling back to 'Brainstorming'.", "issues": [{"key": "idea-status-loading", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea browser: show a loading label until plan statuses have loaded", "description": "<p>Every open idea in the idea browser shows <strong>Brainstorming</strong> while its status loads, then switches to its real status (Proposed, Created, ...). The cause: <code>progressByIdea</code> in <code>app/controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> treats a missing entry in <code>planStatuses</code> as brainstorming, but <code>planStatuses</code> is empty until <code>loadPlanStatuses</code> (called without waiting from <code>app/routes/app/project/idea.js</code> <code>setupController</code>) resolves.</p><ul><li>In <code>app/controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> add a <code>@tracked</code> flag (e.g. <code>planStatusesLoaded</code>, YUIDoc'd), initially false. Set it to true when <code>loadPlanStatuses</code> finishes: after it fills <code>planStatuses</code>, when <code>loadPlans</code> returns nothing, and when it rejects (catch the rejection so it isn't unhandled). Keep the existing sequence check, so a stale load never overwrites newer state, and check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after the await. Reset the flag when the route loads a different project's ideas, so the old project's labels aren't shown.</li><li>In <code>progressByIdea</code>, while the flag is false, give non-archived ideas a loading entry (e.g. <code>{ label: 'views.app.idea.progress.loading', class: 'default', loading: true }</code>). Archived ideas keep the Archived label immediately.</li><li>In <code>app/templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>, render the loading entry in the same <code>label pull-right</code> span (<code>data-idea-status</code>) with <code>&lt;i class=\\"fa fa-spinner fa-spin\\" aria-hidden=\\"true\\"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;</code> before the text, as in <code>app/components/idea/plan-box.hbs</code>. No new styles.</li><li>Add <code>views.app.idea.progress.loading</code>: \\"Loading\\" to <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Reloads triggered by the Hermes handlers (<code>idea.plan.created</code>, <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code>) and <code>setPlanStatus</code> do not reset the flag: the current labels stay while the reload runs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>While the plans request is pending, open ideas show the spinner and \\"Loading\\", never \\"Brainstorming\\". Archived ideas show \\"Archived\\".</li><li>Once it resolves, each idea shows its real status. Ideas with no plan show \\"Brainstorming\\".</li><li>If the plans request fails or returns nothing, the labels fall back to the current behaviour instead of loading forever.</li><li>A live plan event does not bring the spinner back.</li><li>Unit tests in <code>tests/unit/controllers/app/project/idea-live-test.js</code> cover the loading entry before the load, the real status after it, and the failed-load fallback. Each test must fail if its line is reverted. The idea browser acceptance steps (<code>tests/acceptance/steps/ideas/idea-browser-steps.js</code>) still pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> loading indicators elsewhere on the idea page, and changing how plans are queried.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-03 12:42:59	2026-11-03 12:42:59	f
716d83116ae9-3c46-fee8-f993d4c7c3aa	994b17496ae9-2420-fee8-e1f463ff8479	2	{"summary": "A single Prometheus fix. The idea browser shows a spinner 'Loading' label on open ideas until their plan statuses have loaded, instead of falling back to 'Brainstorming'.", "issues": [{"key": "idea-status-loading", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea browser: show a loading label until plan statuses have loaded", "description": "<p>Every open idea in the idea browser shows <strong>Brainstorming</strong> while its status loads, then switches to its real status (Proposed, Created, ...). The cause: <code>progressByIdea</code> in <code>app/controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> treats a missing entry in <code>planStatuses</code> as brainstorming, but <code>planStatuses</code> is empty until <code>loadPlanStatuses</code> (called without waiting from <code>app/routes/app/project/idea.js</code> <code>setupController</code>) resolves.</p><ul><li>In <code>app/controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> add a <code>@tracked</code> flag (e.g. <code>planStatusesLoaded</code>, YUIDoc'd), initially false. Set it to true when <code>loadPlanStatuses</code> finishes: after it fills <code>planStatuses</code>, when <code>loadPlans</code> returns nothing, and when it rejects (catch the rejection so it isn't unhandled). Keep the existing sequence check, so a stale load never overwrites newer state, and check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after the await. Reset the flag when the route loads a different project's ideas, so the old project's labels aren't shown.</li><li>In <code>progressByIdea</code>, while the flag is false, give non-archived ideas a loading entry (e.g. <code>{ label: 'views.app.idea.progress.loading', class: 'default', loading: true }</code>). Archived ideas keep the Archived label immediately.</li><li>In <code>app/templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>, render the loading entry in the same <code>label pull-right</code> span (<code>data-idea-status</code>) with <code>&lt;i class=\\"fa fa-spinner fa-spin\\" aria-hidden=\\"true\\"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;</code> before the text, as in <code>app/components/idea/plan-box.hbs</code>. No new styles. See the attached screens for the loading and loaded states.</li><li>Add <code>views.app.idea.progress.loading</code>: \\"Loading\\" to <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Reloads triggered by the Hermes handlers (<code>idea.plan.created</code>, <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code>) and <code>setPlanStatus</code> do not reset the flag: the current labels stay while the reload runs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>While the plans request is pending, open ideas show the spinner and \\"Loading\\", never \\"Brainstorming\\". Archived ideas show \\"Archived\\".</li><li>Once it resolves, each idea shows its real status. Ideas with no plan show \\"Brainstorming\\".</li><li>If the plans request fails or returns nothing, the labels fall back to the current behaviour instead of loading forever.</li><li>A live plan event does not bring the spinner back.</li><li>Unit tests in <code>tests/unit/controllers/app/project/idea-live-test.js</code> cover the loading entry before the load, the real status after it, and the failed-load fallback. Each test must fail if its line is reverted. The idea browser acceptance steps (<code>tests/acceptance/steps/ideas/idea-browser-steps.js</code>) still pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> loading indicators elsewhere on the idea page, and changing how plans are queried.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["idea-browser-loading", "idea-browser-loaded"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-03 12:45:37	2026-11-03 12:45:37	f
f9978d376aeb-f308-85f1-013a3d7c8a09	599b10726aeb-f308-85f1-2dd28eca8a3d	1	{"summary": "Make Agamemnon aware of Docker. The first issue adds a Docker state reader with an ok/pressured/down verdict. Two issues build on it in parallel: starting and restarting the engine on Windows and Linux, and a dispatch hold that keeps new runs from starting while Docker is down or short of memory (it starts a stopped engine by itself). The aga commands come next (docker read, start-docker, restart-docker, hold-until-docker, with held issues given back one per sweep once memory is free). The last issue teaches the classifier, premise, role and incident packet about Docker incidents, with the patterns checked against real handback logs.", "issues": [{"key": "docker-state", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: read Docker's state (daemon, memory, containers) with an ok/pressured/down verdict", "description": "<p>Agamemnon and the dispatcher know nothing about Docker today: the triage packet's <code>docker</code> field is always <code>None</code> (<code>talos/lib/agamemnon/triage.py</code> <code>run</code>), and the only probe is <code>installer/p4m.py</code> <code>docker_running</code>. Runs keep dying because Docker is down or out of memory (see adt-4234), and nothing notices. This issue adds the reader and the verdict everything else builds on.</p><ul><li>New module <code>talos/lib/docker_state.py</code>. The <code>docker</code> calls sit behind small functions (stdin given, no shell) so the logic is unit tested without Docker.</li><li><code>read()</code> returns a dict: <code>cli</code> (found or not), <code>daemon</code> (reachable or not, plus the error text), <code>serverVersion</code>, <code>memTotal</code> (from <code>docker info</code>), <code>memUsed</code> and per-container usage (name, memory, CPU; <code>docker stats --no-stream</code> in JSON format), and <code>p4mTestContainers</code> (the count of those labelled by p4m test).</li><li><code>verdict(state, high, low, was)</code> returns <code>down</code> (CLI missing or daemon unreachable), <code>pressured</code> (used/total at or above <code>high</code>, or still above <code>low</code> when the previous verdict was pressured: hysteresis), otherwise <code>ok</code>.</li><li>Config in the agent's agent.json: <code>docker: {\\"memoryHighPercent\\": 85, \\"memoryOkPercent\\": 70}</code>, read in <code>talos/lib/registry.py</code> with these defaults.</li><li><code>talos status</code> prints one Docker line: the verdict, used/total memory and the number of test containers.</li><li>README: a Docker state section.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests cover parsing <code>docker info</code>/<code>stats</code> output, a missing CLI, an unreachable daemon, and the verdict thresholds including hysteresis. Windows and Linux both work.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> starting Docker, holding dispatch, aga commands (later issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "docker-engine", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: start and restart the Docker engine (Docker Desktop on Windows, Desktop or user service on Linux)", "description": "<p>When Docker is down, every run fails and needs a person to start Docker Desktop. Talos needs one safe way to start or restart the engine and wait until it answers.</p><ul><li>In <code>talos/lib/docker_state.py</code> (or a small sibling module <code>docker_engine.py</code>): <code>start()</code> and <code>restart()</code>, each followed by <code>wait_ready(timeout)</code>, which polls <code>read()</code> until the daemon answers.</li><li>Prefer the <code>docker desktop start|restart</code> CLI when it exists (Docker Desktop 4.37+). Fallbacks behind <code>os.name == \\"nt\\"</code>, both branches written: Windows launches <code>Docker Desktop.exe</code> from Program Files (path found, not hard-coded to one drive) and restarts by stopping its process tree first. Linux uses <code>systemctl --user start|restart docker-desktop</code> when that unit exists. A rootful system <code>docker.service</code> needs sudo, so it is refused with a clear message, never prompted for.</li><li>Return a result: <code>{action, ok, seconds, method, error}</code>. Timeouts come from agent.json (<code>docker.startTimeoutSeconds</code>, default 180).</li><li>After the engine is up, report whether the p4m stack containers (gaia-dev, postgres, proxy) are running (<code>docker ps</code>). Don't start them: say which ones are missing.</li><li>README: what each platform supports.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests with stubbed processes cover each method choice, the timeout, the refused rootful case and the Windows tree kill. Tried by hand once on Windows Docker Desktop, noted in the PR.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> deciding when to start or restart (dispatch hold and aga issues), remote Docker hosts.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["docker-state"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "docker-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos dispatcher: hold dispatch while Docker is down or out of memory, start a stopped engine", "description": "<p>Starting runs while Docker is full only produces more OOM-killed runs and handbacks to the owner. The dispatcher should wait for Docker the same way it waits out a Claude usage limit.</p><ul><li>New class <code>DockerPause</code> in its own module, modelled on <code>talos/lib/usage_pause.py</code> <code>UsagePause</code> (one lock, interruptible wait, <code>stop()</code>). It holds the last verdict from <code>docker_state</code> and re-reads it at most every <code>docker.checkSeconds</code> (default 30).</li><li><code>talos/lib/dispatcher.py</code>: before a job is taken (next to the usage-limit wait ~l.193), wait while the verdict is <code>down</code> or <code>pressured</code>. Log once when the hold starts and once when it ends. No issue comments, since no issue is affected yet.</li><li>When the verdict is <code>down</code> and <code>docker.autoStart</code> is true (default true), call the engine <code>start()</code> once per hold; if it fails, log it and keep waiting. Never restart from here.</li><li>A run already in flight is not touched.</li><li><code>talos status</code> shows a Docker hold and since when; README updated.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests show the dispatcher waits while down or pressured, resumes when ok (with hysteresis), tries a start once per hold, and that <code>stop()</code> releases waiters.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> holding single issues (aga issue), freeing memory.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["docker-state", "docker-engine"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "aga-docker-verbs", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "aga: docker read, start-docker, restart-docker and hold-until-docker verbs", "description": "<p>Agamemnon's triage sessions can't read Docker or act on it: the premise grants <code>docker_down</code> a <code>pause</code> tier that no verb uses. This issue adds the commands. Their use is granted per incident type in the follow-up issue.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/verbs.py</code>: <code>docker</code> (tier read, level READ: the <code>docker_state.read()</code> output plus its verdict); <code>start-docker</code> and <code>restart-docker</code> (new tier <code>engine</code>, level PRIVATE, added to the tier list in <code>talos/agents/agamemnon/premise.json</code>); <code>hold-until-docker</code> (tier wait, level PRIVATE).</li><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/tool.py</code>: <code>start-docker</code> is refused when the daemon is already up. <code>restart-docker</code> is refused while another issue has a run in flight, unless the verdict is <code>down</code> (those runs are already failing). Both wait until ready and report the stack containers that are missing.</li><li><code>hold-until-docker</code> works like <code>_hold_until_tomorrow</code> (refused with a run in flight, in in_review or already held; assigns the issue to Agamemnon), but the journal hold has a condition <code>docker</code> instead of a time.</li><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/holds.py</code> <code>release_due</code> and <code>journal</code>: a Docker hold is due when the verdict is <code>ok</code>. Give back at most one Docker-held issue per sweep, oldest first, so they don't all start at once. A hold older than <code>docker.holdMaxHours</code> (default 12) goes to the owner with a comment. Undo releases the hold, as for time holds.</li><li>Talos README (The <code>aga</code> tool): the new verbs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for each verb's refusals, the one-per-sweep release, the max-hours handover and undo. These paths are in <code>agamemnonProtected</code>, so the merge gate's self check fails by design and the PR needs a manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the classifier, premise grants and role text (next issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["docker-state", "docker-engine"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "docker-incidents", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon: docker_pressure incident, wider docker_down, Docker state in the triage packet", "description": "<p>Runs that died from Docker running out of memory are classified as <code>other</code> and go to the owner, even though waiting for memory and retrying would have resumed them. <code>docker_down</code> may only notify. This issue lets triage handle both.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/classifier.py</code>: a new <code>docker_pressure</code> rule (OOM kill, exit code 137, <code>Killed</code> from the test runner or ember build, Docker reporting the container OOMKilled, and similar), checked before <code>test_contention</code>. Widen <code>docker_down</code> (Docker Desktop starting or stopped, <code>error during connect</code> variants, pipe or socket not found on Windows and Linux).</li><li>Check the patterns against the real run logs of recent handbacks (Talos state and talos.db; the issues handed back over roughly the last 50). List in the PR which past handbacks are now classified differently.</li><li><code>premise.json</code>: <code>docker_down</code> gets read, engine, wait, retry, notify (\\"start the engine; restart only if it stays unresponsive and nothing else is running; then retry\\"). <code>docker_pressure</code> gets read, wait, retry, notify (\\"hold-until-docker, then retry\\").</li><li><code>triage.py</code> <code>run</code>: fill the packet's <code>docker</code> with <code>docker_state.read()</code> plus its verdict instead of <code>None</code>.</li><li><code>role.md</code>: a Docker section: read <code>docker</code> first; when memory is short, hold, never restart; start before restart; never restart while other runs are in flight.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> classifier tests built from real log excerpts (secrets removed), a triage test showing the packet carries Docker state, and premise loading tests. Manual merge (<code>agamemnonProtected</code>).</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> freeing memory (stopping idle warm ember builds, extra container cleanup), remote Docker hosts.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aga-docker-verbs"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 21:09:13	2026-11-04 21:09:13	f
2080f1616ae9-025d-5952-7e6b51af6b17	994b17496ae9-2420-fee8-e1f463ff8479	3	{"summary": "A single Prometheus fix in milestone aga-v2. The idea browser shows the existing spinner and a 'Loading' label on open ideas until their plan statuses have loaded, instead of falling back to 'Brainstorming'.", "issues": [{"key": "idea-status-loading", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea browser: show a loading label until plan statuses have loaded", "description": "<p>Every open idea in the idea browser shows <strong>Brainstorming</strong> while its status loads, then switches to its real status (Proposed, Created, ...). The cause: <code>progressByIdea</code> in <code>app/controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> treats a missing entry in <code>planStatuses</code> as brainstorming, but <code>planStatuses</code> is empty until <code>loadPlanStatuses</code> (called without waiting from <code>app/routes/app/project/idea.js</code> <code>setupController</code>) resolves.</p><ul><li>In <code>app/controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> add a <code>@tracked</code> flag (e.g. <code>planStatusesLoaded</code>, YUIDoc'd), initially false. Set it to true when <code>loadPlanStatuses</code> finishes: after it fills <code>planStatuses</code>, when <code>loadPlans</code> returns nothing, and when it rejects (catch the rejection so it isn't unhandled). Keep the existing sequence check, so a stale load never overwrites newer state, and check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after the await. Reset the flag when the route loads a different project's ideas, so the old project's labels aren't shown.</li><li>In <code>progressByIdea</code>, while the flag is false, give non-archived ideas a loading entry (e.g. <code>{ label: 'views.app.idea.progress.loading', class: 'default', loading: true }</code>). Archived ideas keep the Archived label immediately.</li><li>In <code>app/templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>, render the loading entry in the same <code>label pull-right</code> span (<code>data-idea-status</code>) with the existing spinner <code>&lt;i class=\\"fa fa-spinner fa-spin\\" aria-hidden=\\"true\\"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;</code> before the text, as in <code>app/components/idea/plan-box.hbs</code>. No other icon and no new styles. See the attached screens for the loading and loaded states.</li><li>Add <code>views.app.idea.progress.loading</code>: \\"Loading\\" to <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Reloads triggered by the Hermes handlers (<code>idea.plan.created</code>, <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code>) and <code>setPlanStatus</code> do not reset the flag: the current labels stay while the reload runs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>While the plans request is pending, open ideas show the spinner and \\"Loading\\", never \\"Brainstorming\\". Archived ideas show \\"Archived\\".</li><li>Once it resolves, each idea shows its real status. Ideas with no plan show \\"Brainstorming\\".</li><li>If the plans request fails or returns nothing, the labels fall back to the current behaviour instead of loading forever.</li><li>A live plan event does not bring the spinner back.</li><li>Unit tests in <code>tests/unit/controllers/app/project/idea-live-test.js</code> cover the loading entry before the load, the real status after it, and the failed-load fallback. Each test must fail if its line is reverted. The idea browser acceptance steps (<code>tests/acceptance/steps/ideas/idea-browser-steps.js</code>) still pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> loading indicators elsewhere on the idea page, and changing how plans are queried.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["idea-browser-loading", "idea-browser-loaded"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-03 12:52:48	2026-11-03 12:53:48	f
2fa187f76aea-40c3-be98-52007f055b8d	ba63ff326aea-3ad0-be98-b6a90d50524a	1	{"summary": "The issue create and edit screens request the project with four list relationships joined into one query. The rows multiply and Gaia runs out of memory. The Prometheus issue loads those lists separately and fixes the crash. The Gaia issue changes the framework to load each list relationship in its own query, so no request can multiply rows like this again. The two issues are independent.", "issues": [{"key": "issue-form-split-rels", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue create/edit: load milestones, issue types and statuses separately instead of project rels", "description": "<p>Opening the issue create or edit screen can crash Gaia with <code>Allowed memory size of 134217728 bytes exhausted</code> in <code>RestController.php</code>. Both routes query the project with <code>rels: 'members,milestones,issuetypes,issuestatuses'</code>, <code>sort: 'members.name'</code> and <code>limit: -1</code>. Gaia joins all four list relationships into one SQL query, so it returns members × milestones × types × statuses rows for a single project. This repo's CLAUDE.md already forbids loading hasMany relations through the parent's <code>rels</code>.</p><ul><li><code>app/routes/app/project/issue/create.js</code> (<code>afterModel</code>) and <code>app/routes/app/project/issue/edit.js</code>: query the project with <code>rels: 'members'</code> and <code>sort: 'members.name'</code> only (one row per member).</li><li>In parallel (<code>Promise.all</code>), load <code>store.query('milestone', { query: '(Milestone.projectId : X)', limit: -1 })</code>, the same for <code>issuetype</code> (<code>Issuetype.projectId</code>) and <code>issuestatus</code> (<code>Issuestatus.projectId</code>). Check the field names with <code>gaia-dev model</code>. Keep the existing fallback to system statuses (<code>(Issuestatus.system : 1)</code>) when the project has none.</li><li>Pass them to the templates and controllers under the same names they read today (<code>project.milestones</code>, <code>project.issuetypes</code>, <code>project.issuestatuses</code>), or update those readers, so the form dropdowns behave as before. Put the shared loading in one place used by both routes (a small util or service method, not a mixin).</li><li>Errors still go through <code>errorManager.handleError</code>.</li><li>Mirage handlers for the new queries and an acceptance test that opens create and edit and checks that the milestone, type, status and assignee dropdowns are filled.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> neither route requests the project with milestones, issuetypes or issuestatuses as <code>rels</code>; create and edit work for a project with many members and milestones; the dropdown contents match what they showed before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Gaia framework change to how rels are loaded; other screens that still pass hasMany rels.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gaia-split-collection-rels", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Read path: load hasMany/hasManyToMany rels in separate queries instead of one cartesian join", "description": "<p>A read that asks for two or more list relationships (hasMany or hasManyToMany) through <code>rels</code> joins all of them into one query (<code>Model::read/readAll</code> → <code>Relationship::prepareJoinsForQuery</code>). The result has the product of all child counts as rows; <code>RestController::prepareData</code> then hydrates every row and runs out of memory. Example: <code>GET /project?query=(Project.id : X)&amp;rels=members,milestones,issuetypes,issuestatuses&amp;sort=members.name&amp;limit=-1</code> hit the 128 MB limit. <code>limit</code> applies to the joined rows, not to the base records. <code>Model::executeQuery</code> already has a split path (<code>executeHasManyRel</code>, <code>DataExtractor::extractModelIds</code>), but <code>passSplittingChecks</code> requires <code>getTotalNumberOfRelationship() &lt;= 3 &amp;&amp; getTotalHasManyToManyRels() &gt; 4</code>, which can never be true, so the path never runs.</p><ul><li>When a read requests more than one collection rel, keep hasOne/belongsTo rels joined to the base query. Load each collection rel (hasMany and hasManyToMany) in its own query filtered by the base model IDs, and merge the results into the response in the same JSON:API shape as today.</li><li>A sort or where on a related field (e.g. <code>members.name</code>) goes into that relationship's own query. A where on a related field that filters the base records must still filter them, as the existing pre-execution of filtered hasManyToMany rels in <code>executeQuery</code> does. Decide how to treat OR and aggregates, and fall back to the join where the semantics can't be preserved.</li><li>Replace the unsatisfiable condition in <code>passSplittingChecks</code> with the real rule. Apply field and relationship ACL to each split query, as the joined path does, so project scoping doesn't leak.</li><li><code>limit</code>/<code>offset</code> then apply to the base records only when the collection rels are split.</li><li>Tests: a failing test first that reproduces the row multiplication (a project with several members, milestones, types and statuses, all four rels); unit tests for the split decision; api-tester cases showing the response shape is unchanged for single-rel reads.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the request above returns each child once with bounded memory; responses for existing single-rel reads are unchanged; the full suite passes (RestController and Model changes reach every resource).</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> raising <code>memory_limit</code>; paging related collections.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-03 16:34:55	2026-11-03 16:34:55	f
ca0ac0186aea-cb24-4534-d682153c74f1	6de133f26aea-cb24-4534-3173523ada56	1	{"summary": "Two Prometheus issues for the comment editor's Tribute menus in initialize-toastui.js. First, keyboard navigation: make the highlighted item visible and keep the editor from moving the cursor, so Up/Down/Enter work in the emoji, user and issue menus. Second, shortcode search: emojis get shortcodes such as :) and :D, which the emoji menu matches and ranks first. The second follows the first because both change the same modifier and test file.", "issues": [{"key": "emoji-keyboard-nav", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Editor mention menus: visible Up/Down keyboard navigation for emoji, user and issue suggestions", "description": "<p>In the comment and description editor (<code>AppUi::ToastUi</code>), typing <code>:</code>, <code>@</code> or <code>#</code> opens a Tribute suggestion menu. Users can't pick an entry with the Up/Down keys. Tribute supports keyboard navigation, but <code>attachTributeEvents</code> in <code>app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js</code> gives the list Bootstrap's <code>dropdown-menu</code> class, and no stylesheet styles Tribute's <code>li.highlight</code>, so the selected item is probably invisible.</p><ul><li>First reproduce it in the running app (an issue comment box) and confirm the cause. Check whether the highlight only lacks styling, or whether the ToastUI wysiwyg editor also handles ArrowUp/ArrowDown/Enter (moving the cursor or adding a line) while the menu is open. If it does, stop those keys while Tribute is active (<code>tribute.isActive</code>), in the existing <code>editor.addHook('keydown', ...)</code> or the target element's keydown listener.</li><li>Style the highlighted item like a hovered Bootstrap dropdown item (<code>.tribute-container li.highlight &gt; a</code>), with colours from <code>app/styles/variables.scss</code> and square edges. Put the rule in the shared editor styles (an existing scss file next to the editor/ToastUI styles), not inline.</li><li>Use the mouse hover and the keyboard highlight as the same selection (Tribute's default), and keep the highlighted item in view.</li><li>Enter or Tab inserts the highlighted item, and Escape closes the menu. Ctrl+Enter submit still must not fire while the menu is open (the current <code>isTributeActive</code> logic).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Typing <code>:smi</code> in a comment opens the emoji menu with the first item visibly highlighted. Down/Up moves the highlight without moving the editor's cursor, and Enter inserts the highlighted emoji.</li><li>The same works in the <code>@</code> and <code>#</code> menus.</li><li>An integration test in <code>tests/integration/modifiers/initialize-toastui-test.js</code> sends ArrowDown and then Enter, and checks that the second suggestion was inserted. It fails if the fix is reverted.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing what the menus search or list, and the legacy <code>message-box.js</code> and <code>summer-note.js</code> editors.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "emoji-shortcodes", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Editor emoji menu: search emojis by emoticon shortcodes like :) and :D", "description": "<p>The <code>:</code> emoji menu in the comment and description editor only matches emoji names (<code>lookup: 'name'</code> in <code>setupTribute</code>, <code>app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js</code>). Typing a familiar emoticon such as <code>:)</code> sends the query <code>)</code>, which finds nothing useful. Users should be able to find emojis by their common shortcodes.</p><ul><li>Add a shortcode map from emoji id (the ids in <code>emojiList</code> of <code>app/components/app-ui/toast-ui.js</code>) to the text typed after the <code>:</code> trigger. For example: <code>slightly-smiling-face</code>: <code>)</code>, <code>-)</code>; <code>smile</code>: <code>D</code>, <code>-D</code>; <code>slightly-frowning-face</code>: <code>(</code>, <code>-(</code>; <code>stuck-out-tongue</code>: <code>P</code>, <code>p</code>; <code>open-mouth</code>: <code>O</code>, <code>o</code>; <code>neutral-face</code>: <code>|</code>; <code>confused</code>: <code>/</code>; <code>cry</code>: <code>'(</code>; <code>wink</code>: <code>-*</code> or similar, chosen sensibly. Put it in a small util (e.g. <code>app/utils/emoji-shortcodes.js</code>, with YUIDoc and the license header). Shortcodes are not translated.</li><li>Include the shortcodes in each <code>translatedEmojis</code> entry built in <code>toast-ui.js</code>.</li><li>Replace the emoji collection's static <code>values</code> with a <code>values(text, cb)</code> function. It ranks emojis whose shortcode equals the query first, then names that start with the query, then the current fuzzy name matches, and keeps <code>menuItemLimit: 5</code>.</li><li>Show the matched shortcode after the name in the menu item (e.g. <code>🙂 Slightly smiling face :)</code>), escaped. Selecting it still inserts the emoji.</li><li>Check that a query containing <code>)</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>|</code>, <code>/</code> or <code>'</code> keeps the menu open (Tribute's query regex). Fix it with Tribute options if not.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Typing <code>:)</code> shows 🙂 as the first, highlighted suggestion, and Enter inserts it. <code>:D</code> gives 😄 and <code>:(</code> gives 🙁.</li><li>Name search still works (<code>:thumb</code> finds thumbs up).</li><li>Integration tests in <code>tests/integration/modifiers/initialize-toastui-test.js</code> cover shortcode ranking and name search, plus a unit test for the util.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> shortcodes that don't start with <code>:</code> (<code>;)</code>, <code>&lt;3</code>), which would need a new trigger; automatically converting a shortcode followed by a space without the menu; and the legacy <code>message-box.js</code> and <code>summer-note.js</code> editors.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["emoji-keyboard-nav"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-03 16:41:46	2026-11-03 16:41:46	f
07ea0af26af4-a328-1af5-b84a84bbe345	5a1482d46af4-0fdf-00ad-c45029d7a40d	3	{"summary": "Docs module foundation, built from scratch beside the existing Wiki (Wiki stays unchanged until the Docs module is complete, then its code is retired in a later idea). Gaia gets a standard project-scoped Doc REST resource (title, body, projectId, ownerId, locked, tags via the shared Tag/Tagged tables) plus a decision record. Prometheus then gets the doc model/adapter/serializer with Mirage support, the doc page (app.project.doc.page), and, in parallel, the All Docs list (app.project.doc.index) and Create Doc form (app.project.doc.create), each with its sidebar entry, ACL route mapping, loading skeleton, empty state, translations and acceptance tests.", "issues": [{"key": "doc-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Doc resource (title, body, owner, locked, tags) as standard project-scoped CRUD", "description": "<p>Projects get a Docs module where teams create, list and open documents. This adds the backing <code>Doc</code> resource as plain REST CRUD, following the new-resource guide <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code> (exemplar gaia#193, Idea).</p><ul><li><code>app/metadata/model/Doc.php</code>, table <code>doc</code>: <code>title</code> varchar(255) required, <code>body</code> text (nullable), <code>projectId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>ownerId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>locked</code> bool default false, plus the standard <code>id</code>, <code>dateCreated</code>, <code>dateModified</code>, <code>createdUser</code>, <code>modifiedUser</code>, <code>deleted</code>. Behaviours: <code>createdUserBehavior</code>, <code>modifiedUserBehavior</code>, <code>dateCreatedBehavior</code>, <code>dateModifiedBehavior</code>, <code>softDeleteBehavior</code>, <code>auditBehavior</code>.</li><li>Relationships: <code>project</code> belongsTo Project, <code>owner</code> hasOne User (via <code>ownerId</code>), <code>createdBy</code>/<code>modifiedBy</code> hasOne User, <code>tag</code> hasManyToMany Tag via Tagged (<code>relatedTo = 'doc'</code>), <code>tagged</code> hasMany Tagged. Add the inverse <code>doc</code> relationship on <code>Tagged</code> and <code>docs</code> on <code>Project</code>, the same way Issue is wired.</li><li>ACL metadata: <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via <code>projectId</code>, so only project members with the <code>doc.*</code> permissions can read/create/update/delete.</li><li>Empty <code>app/models/Doc.php</code> and <code>DocController</code> (RestController subclass), the <code>'Doc'</code> line in <code>core/config/models.php</code>, the <code>doc</code> route in <code>core/config/routes.php</code>, <code>routes.v1.json</code>, the placeholders in <code>generate-backend-apis.php</code> and a regenerated <code>backend.json</code>.</li><li>api-tester: harness table and seed rows, fixture ids, <code>acl.json</code> cases (member with and without <code>doc.*</code>, non-member) and <code>client.json</code> cases (create, list by project, get with <code>owner</code> and <code>tag</code> rels, delete).</li><li>New <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>, D-001: Docs is a new, independent module built from scratch and shares no code or tables with Wiki (beyond the generic Tag/Tagged tagging). Wiki is kept unchanged while Docs is built; once the Docs module is complete, the Wiki code is retired. Whether existing wiki content is migrated into Docs or dropped is decided at retirement, once the Docs body format is settled.</li><li>No permission seed SQL (the reviewer grants <code>doc.*</code> by hand). Regenerate the gaia-dev graph and <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a project member with <code>doc.create</code> can POST a doc and list it with <code>((Doc.projectId : X))</code>; a user without <code>doc.read</code> or outside the project gets 403/empty; tags attach through Tagged; the full test suite and CI drift checks pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> live events, enforcing <code>locked</code>, owner-change rules, body format/versioning, any change to Wiki.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "A new resource has a fixed set of touchpoints (metadata, parent relationships, model, controller, models/routes config, api-tester catalog and acl/client cases) that must ship together, or dev is left with a resource that has no ACL cases; the decision doc is one small file.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-data", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: doc model, adapter, serializer and Mirage support", "description": "<p>Data layer for the new Docs module, used by the doc page, All Docs and Create Doc screens. It reads the Gaia <code>doc</code> resource. Docs is a new module built from scratch; don't reuse or change the Wiki code.</p><ul><li><code>app/models/doc.js</code> (native class, YUIDoc): <code>title</code>, <code>body</code>, <code>projectId</code>, <code>ownerId</code>, <code>locked</code> (boolean), <code>dateCreated</code>, <code>dateModified</code>, <code>createdUser</code>, <code>modifiedUser</code>; relationships <code>project</code>, <code>owner</code> (user), <code>tag</code> (hasMany tag, async). Follow the <code>idea</code> model for naming and date handling.</li><li><code>app/adapters/doc.js</code> and <code>app/serializers/doc.js</code> extending the application adapter/serializer with no custom endpoints (singular path <code>/api/v1/doc</code>).</li><li>Mirage: <code>mirage/factories/doc.js</code> (realistic titles, an owner, some tags) and handlers in <code>mirage/config.js</code> for list with the Gaia <code>query</code> filter on projectId, get by id, create and delete, written like the <code>idea</code> handlers. Tagged rows with <code>relatedTo: 'doc'</code> must work in Mirage.</li><li>Unit tests for the model and serializer.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>store.query('doc', { query: '((Doc.projectId : X))', rels: 'owner,tag' })</code>, <code>findRecord</code>, <code>createRecord().save()</code> and <code>destroyRecord</code> work against Mirage; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> routes and UI (separate issues), live updates.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-api"], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-page", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: doc page route (app.project.doc.page) with detail layout, skeleton and empty state", "description": "<p>Opening a doc in a project. This is the page the All Docs rows link to and Create Doc lands on after saving. Editing the body comes later; this page is read-only.</p><ul><li><code>app/router.js</code>: add <code>this.route('doc', function(){ this.route('page', {path: '/:doc_id'}); })</code> under <code>project</code> (the index and create routes are added by their own issues).</li><li><code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code>: <code>{ name: 'app.project.doc.page', map: 'doc.read' }</code>.</li><li>Route <code>routes/app/project/doc/page.js</code> (native class, extends <code>routes/app.js</code>): loads the doc with <code>rels</code> for <code>owner</code> and <code>tag</code> only (no unbounded hasMany); a missing or forbidden doc shows the existing not-found/error handling.</li><li>Template <code>templates/app/project/doc/page.hbs</code> on the design-system detail pattern: <code>col-md-8</code> <code>box box-primary</code> with the title (lock icon <code>fa fa-lock</code> when <code>locked</code>) and the body as escaped text (no <code>htmlSafe</code>/triple-stash); when the body is empty, the design-system §4 empty state (\\"This doc has no content yet\\"). <code>col-md-4</code> side box with owner, tags (<code>label</code>s), created and last edited.</li><li><code>templates/app/project/doc/page-loading.hbs</code> skeleton matching the layout (design-system §4).</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Acceptance <code>.feature</code> (with steps in a per-feature steps file, not <code>steps.js</code>): opens a doc and sees title, owner, tags; empty body shows the empty state; a user without <code>doc.read</code> is redirected away.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the scenarios above pass on Mirage; page matches an existing detail screen side by side; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> editing, delete button, comments, presence, live updates.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-data"], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: All Docs list page (app.project.doc.index) and Docs sidebar item", "description": "<p>The project's list of docs, reached from a new \\"Docs\\" item in the sidebar.</p><ul><li><code>app/router.js</code>: add <code>this.route('index', {path: '/'})</code> to the <code>doc</code> route. <code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code>: <code>app.project.doc.index</code> → <code>doc.read</code>.</li><li>Sidebar: in <code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> <code>views.Navigation.items</code> add <code>Doc</code> (icon <code>file-text-o</code>, route <code>app.project.doc</code>, <code>anchorRoute: 'doc'</code>, <code>projectRelated: true</code>, <code>aclContext: 'doc.read'</code>) with <code>actions.section1.list</code> \\"All Docs\\" like the Issue item. The \\"Create Doc\\" child is added by the Create Doc issue; if it is already there, keep it.</li><li>Route <code>routes/app/project/doc/index.js</code> and controller <code>controllers/app/project/doc/index.js</code> extending <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>, modelled on <code>controllers/app/agent/index.js</code>: query <code>((Doc.projectId : X))</code> with rels <code>owner,tag</code>, sort by last edited desc, pagination, search by title.</li><li>Template <code>templates/app/project/doc/index.hbs</code>: list page pattern, one full-width <code>box box-primary</code> with search toolbar, table (title linking to <code>app.project.doc.page</code> with a lock icon when locked, owner, last edited, tags) and pagination; row delete through the base list's delete with <code>aclContext=\\"doc.delete\\"</code>; a \\"New doc\\" button (<code>aclContext=\\"doc.create\\"</code>) to <code>app.project.doc.create</code> if that route exists, otherwise the Create Doc issue adds it.</li><li><code>templates/app/project/doc/index-loading.hbs</code> skeleton and an empty state (\\"No docs yet\\") per design-system §4.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; acceptance <code>.feature</code> with a per-feature steps file: list shows seeded docs with owner/tags, search filters, empty state, delete removes a row, no <code>doc.read</code> → route blocked and sidebar item hidden.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> scenarios pass on Mirage; screen matches an existing list page side by side; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> saved searches beyond what <code>list.js</code> gives for free, export, mass update, live updates.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-page"], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-create", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Create Doc form (app.project.doc.create) and sidebar entry", "description": "<p>Lets a project member with <code>doc.create</code> start a new doc. The body is written later in the editor, so the form asks only for title and tags.</p><ul><li><code>app/router.js</code>: add <code>this.route('create')</code> to the <code>doc</code> route. <code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code>: <code>app.project.doc.create</code> → <code>doc.create</code>.</li><li>Sidebar: add <code>actions.section1.create</code> \\"Create Doc\\" (route <code>app.project.doc.create</code>, <code>aclContext: 'doc.create'</code>) to the Docs item in <code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>; if the Docs item isn't there yet, add it (icon <code>file-text-o</code>, route <code>app.project.doc</code>, <code>aclContext: 'doc.read'</code>). If All Docs has shipped, add its \\"New doc\\" button (<code>aclContext=\\"doc.create\\"</code>) to the list's box-tools.</li><li>Route/controller <code>app/project/doc/create</code> (native classes) and <code>templates/app/project/doc/create.hbs</code> on the create/edit pattern: <code>col-md-8</code> form box with <code>FormFields::FieldText</code> title (required, validation message) and <code>FormFields::FieldRelateMulti</code> for tags (existing project tags), <code>col-md-4</code> side box with owner (current user) and project; Save/Cancel below the boxes.</li><li>Save: creates the doc with <code>projectId</code> and <code>ownerId</code> = current user, then the Tagged rows (<code>relatedTo: 'doc'</code>), then transitions to <code>app.project.doc.page</code>. Ignore a second submit while saving and disable Save; on failure show the error and roll back. Cancel returns to <code>app.project.doc.index</code> (or the project dashboard if that route doesn't exist yet).</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; acceptance <code>.feature</code> with a per-feature steps file: create with title and tags lands on the doc page; empty title shows validation; failed save shows an error; no <code>doc.create</code> → route blocked and sidebar child hidden.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> scenarios pass on Mirage; a created doc appears in All Docs; screen matches an existing create form side by side; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> body editing, creating new tags inline, templates, edit route.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-page"], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-11 09:57:27	2026-11-11 10:00:17	f
583d72906aea-9509-4534-53e44a397186	6de133f26aea-cb24-4534-3173523ada56	2	{"summary": "Two Prometheus issues for the comment editor's Tribute menus in initialize-toastui.js, both in milestone aga-v2. First, keyboard navigation: make the highlighted item visible and keep the editor from moving the cursor, so Up/Down/Enter work in the emoji, user and issue menus. Second, shortcode search: emojis get shortcodes such as :) and :D, which the emoji menu matches and ranks first. The second follows the first because both change the same modifier and test file.", "issues": [{"key": "emoji-keyboard-nav", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Editor mention menus: visible Up/Down keyboard navigation for emoji, user and issue suggestions", "description": "<p>In the comment and description editor (<code>AppUi::ToastUi</code>), typing <code>:</code>, <code>@</code> or <code>#</code> opens a Tribute suggestion menu. Users can't pick an entry with the Up/Down keys. Tribute supports keyboard navigation, but <code>attachTributeEvents</code> in <code>app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js</code> gives the list Bootstrap's <code>dropdown-menu</code> class, and no stylesheet styles Tribute's <code>li.highlight</code>, so the selected item is probably invisible.</p><ul><li>First reproduce it in the running app (an issue comment box) and confirm the cause. Check whether the highlight only lacks styling, or whether the ToastUI wysiwyg editor also handles ArrowUp/ArrowDown/Enter (moving the cursor or adding a line) while the menu is open. If it does, stop those keys while Tribute is active (<code>tribute.isActive</code>), in the existing <code>editor.addHook('keydown', ...)</code> or the target element's keydown listener.</li><li>Style the highlighted item like a hovered Bootstrap dropdown item (<code>.tribute-container li.highlight &gt; a</code>), with colours from <code>app/styles/variables.scss</code> and square edges. Put the rule in the shared editor styles (an existing scss file next to the editor/ToastUI styles), not inline.</li><li>Use the mouse hover and the keyboard highlight as the same selection (Tribute's default), and keep the highlighted item in view.</li><li>Enter or Tab inserts the highlighted item, and Escape closes the menu. Ctrl+Enter submit still must not fire while the menu is open (the current <code>isTributeActive</code> logic).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Typing <code>:smi</code> in a comment opens the emoji menu with the first item visibly highlighted. Down/Up moves the highlight without moving the editor's cursor, and Enter inserts the highlighted emoji.</li><li>The same works in the <code>@</code> and <code>#</code> menus.</li><li>An integration test in <code>tests/integration/modifiers/initialize-toastui-test.js</code> sends ArrowDown and then Enter, and checks that the second suggestion was inserted. It fails if the fix is reverted.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing what the menus search or list, and the legacy <code>message-box.js</code> and <code>summer-note.js</code> editors.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "emoji-shortcodes", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Editor emoji menu: search emojis by emoticon shortcodes like :) and :D", "description": "<p>The <code>:</code> emoji menu in the comment and description editor only matches emoji names (<code>lookup: 'name'</code> in <code>setupTribute</code>, <code>app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js</code>). Typing a familiar emoticon such as <code>:)</code> sends the query <code>)</code>, which finds nothing useful. Users should be able to find emojis by their common shortcodes.</p><ul><li>Add a shortcode map from emoji id (the ids in <code>emojiList</code> of <code>app/components/app-ui/toast-ui.js</code>) to the text typed after the <code>:</code> trigger. For example: <code>slightly-smiling-face</code>: <code>)</code>, <code>-)</code>; <code>smile</code>: <code>D</code>, <code>-D</code>; <code>slightly-frowning-face</code>: <code>(</code>, <code>-(</code>; <code>stuck-out-tongue</code>: <code>P</code>, <code>p</code>; <code>open-mouth</code>: <code>O</code>, <code>o</code>; <code>neutral-face</code>: <code>|</code>; <code>confused</code>: <code>/</code>; <code>cry</code>: <code>'(</code>; <code>wink</code>: <code>-*</code> or similar, chosen sensibly. Put it in a small util (e.g. <code>app/utils/emoji-shortcodes.js</code>, with YUIDoc and the license header). Shortcodes are not translated.</li><li>Include the shortcodes in each <code>translatedEmojis</code> entry built in <code>toast-ui.js</code>.</li><li>Replace the emoji collection's static <code>values</code> with a <code>values(text, cb)</code> function. It ranks emojis whose shortcode equals the query first, then names that start with the query, then the current fuzzy name matches, and keeps <code>menuItemLimit: 5</code>.</li><li>Show the matched shortcode after the name in the menu item (e.g. <code>🙂 Slightly smiling face :)</code>), escaped. Selecting it still inserts the emoji.</li><li>Check that a query containing <code>)</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>|</code>, <code>/</code> or <code>'</code> keeps the menu open (Tribute's query regex). Fix it with Tribute options if not.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Typing <code>:)</code> shows 🙂 as the first, highlighted suggestion, and Enter inserts it. <code>:D</code> gives 😄 and <code>:(</code> gives 🙁.</li><li>Name search still works (<code>:thumb</code> finds thumbs up).</li><li>Integration tests in <code>tests/integration/modifiers/initialize-toastui-test.js</code> cover shortcode ranking and name search, plus a unit test for the util.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> shortcodes that don't start with <code>:</code> (<code>;)</code>, <code>&lt;3</code>), which would need a new trigger; automatically converting a shortcode followed by a space without the menu; and the legacy <code>message-box.js</code> and <code>summer-note.js</code> editors.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["emoji-keyboard-nav"], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-03 16:44:08	2026-11-03 16:44:43	f
ae3857a36aea-6fb0-813e-45fc82bbb8eb	994b17496ae9-2420-fee8-e1f463ff8479	4	{"summary": "Follow-up to aprom-4267, in milestone aga-v2: in the idea browser, replace the spinner 'Loading' label shown while plan statuses load with the existing shimmer skeleton bar, sized like a status label.", "issues": [{"key": "idea-status-skeleton", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea browser: shimmer skeleton instead of the spinner label while plan statuses load", "description": "<p>aprom-4267 shows a spinner \\"Loading\\" label on each open idea in the idea browser until the plan statuses have loaded. The engineer wants the skeleton look used elsewhere in Prometheus instead. A status label comes from the latest <code>ideaplan</code>, queried separately by <code>loadPlans</code> in <code>app/routes/app/project/idea.js</code>, not from the idea model. So the skeleton runs until that plans query resolves (the loading state aprom-4267 added to <code>app/controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>), not until the idea model resolves.</p><ul><li>In <code>app/templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>, when an idea's progress entry is in its loading state, render <code>&lt;span class=\\"pull-right skeleton-line skeleton-line--xs idea-status-skeleton\\" data-idea-status-skeleton&gt;</code> in place of the <code>label</code> span, with a <code>sr-only</code> \\"Loading\\" text inside it (reuse <code>views.app.idea.progress.loading</code>). Remove the spinner icon from this place.</li><li>Reuse the shimmer from <code>app/styles/components/skeleton.scss</code> (<code>.skeleton-line</code>). Add only <code>.idea-status-skeleton</code>, scoped under the idea list in <code>app/styles/modules/idea.scss</code>: about label height and width, no margin, vertically aligned with the title, and <code>border-radius: 0</code> (square edges per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>).</li><li>Keep everything else from aprom-4267: archived ideas show Archived at once; the skeleton ends when plans load, fail or return nothing; live plan events do not bring it back.</li><li>Update the unit and acceptance checks that look for the spinner label so they look for <code>[data-idea-status-skeleton]</code> while loading and <code>[data-idea-status]</code> after.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>While the plans request is pending, every open idea shows a shimmering bar on the right of its row, no spinner and no \\"Brainstorming\\". Screen readers announce \\"Loading\\".</li><li>When it resolves, the bar is replaced by the real status label in the same place, without the row shifting.</li><li>The bar has square edges and uses only the existing skeleton colours.</li><li>Tests pass, and each changed check fails if its template line is reverted.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a skeleton for the whole idea list while the ideas query loads, and changes to how plans are queried.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4267"], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["idea-browser-skeleton"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 07:28:46	2026-11-04 07:28:46	f
864be3b86aeb-4599-8fd2-6de56905ffbb	599b10726aeb-f308-85f1-2dd28eca8a3d	2	{"summary": "Make Agamemnon aware of Docker. The first issue adds a Docker state reader with an ok/pressured/down verdict. Two issues build on it in parallel: engine start and restart (Docker Desktop locally, configurable commands for the future server) and a dispatch hold that keeps new runs from starting while Docker is down or at 85% memory or more. The hold waits for Docker after boot and starts a stopped engine by itself. Freeing memory then extends the hold: it stops the test containers of issues that are stale for over 72 hours or deferred or won't fix. The aga commands come next (docker read, start-docker, restart-docker, stop-stale-containers, hold-until-docker; a hold ends after 72 hours or when the issue is deferred or won't fix). The last issue teaches the classifier, premise, role and incident packet about Docker incidents, with the patterns checked against real handback logs.", "issues": [{"key": "docker-state", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: read Docker's state (daemon, memory, containers) with an ok/pressured/down verdict", "description": "<p>Agamemnon and the dispatcher know nothing about Docker today: the triage packet's <code>docker</code> field is always <code>None</code> (<code>talos/lib/agamemnon/triage.py</code> <code>run</code>), and the only probe is <code>installer/p4m.py</code> <code>docker_running</code>. Runs keep dying because Docker is down or out of memory (see adt-4234), and nothing notices. This issue adds the reader and the verdict everything else builds on.</p><ul><li>New module <code>talos/lib/docker_state.py</code>. The <code>docker</code> calls sit behind small functions (stdin given, no shell) so the logic is unit tested without Docker.</li><li><code>read()</code> returns a dict: <code>cli</code> (found or not), <code>daemon</code> (reachable or not, plus the error text), <code>serverVersion</code>, <code>memTotal</code> (from <code>docker info</code>), <code>memUsed</code> and per-container usage (name, memory, CPU; <code>docker stats --no-stream</code> in JSON format), and <code>p4mTestContainers</code> (the count of those labelled by p4m test).</li><li><code>verdict(state, high, low, was)</code> returns <code>down</code> (CLI missing or daemon unreachable), <code>pressured</code> (used/total at or above <code>high</code>, or still above <code>low</code> when the previous verdict was pressured: hysteresis), otherwise <code>ok</code>.</li><li>Config in the agent's agent.json: <code>docker: {\\"memoryHighPercent\\": 85, \\"memoryOkPercent\\": 70}</code>, read in <code>talos/lib/registry.py</code> with these defaults.</li><li><code>talos status</code> prints one Docker line: the verdict, used/total memory and the number of test containers.</li><li>README: a Docker state section.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests cover parsing <code>docker info</code>/<code>stats</code> output, a missing CLI, an unreachable daemon, and the verdict thresholds including hysteresis. Windows and Linux both work.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> starting Docker, holding dispatch, freeing memory, aga commands (later issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "docker-engine", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: start and restart the Docker engine (Docker Desktop locally, configurable commands for a server)", "description": "<p>When Docker is down, every run fails and needs a person to start it. Today Talos runs on engineers' machines (Docker Desktop, started by the user). Later it will run on a server, where Talos and Docker are part of the system's boot. Talos needs one safe way to start or restart the engine on both, and to wait until it answers.</p><ul><li>New module <code>talos/lib/docker_engine.py</code>: <code>start()</code> and <code>restart()</code>, each followed by <code>wait_ready(timeout)</code>, which polls <code>docker_state.read()</code> until the daemon answers.</li><li>Configured commands first: agent.json <code>docker.startCommand</code> / <code>docker.restartCommand</code> (argv lists, run without a shell and without a TTY so nothing can prompt; e.g. a server with a sudoers rule uses <code>[\\"sudo\\", \\"-n\\", \\"systemctl\\", \\"restart\\", \\"docker\\"]</code>).</li><li>Defaults when no command is set: the <code>docker desktop start|restart</code> CLI when it exists (Docker Desktop 4.37+). Otherwise, behind <code>os.name == \\"nt\\"</code> with both branches written: Windows launches <code>Docker Desktop.exe</code> from Program Files (path found, not hard-coded to one drive) and restarts by stopping its process tree first; Linux uses <code>systemctl --user start|restart docker-desktop</code> when that unit exists. A rootful system <code>docker.service</code> without a configured command is refused with a clear message saying which setting to add.</li><li>Return a result: <code>{action, ok, seconds, method, error}</code>. Timeout from <code>docker.startTimeoutSeconds</code> (default 180).</li><li>After the engine is up, report whether the p4m stack containers (gaia-dev, postgres, proxy) are running (<code>docker ps</code>). Don't start them: say which ones are missing.</li><li>README: the defaults per platform and the server setup (commands and the sudoers line).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests with stubbed processes cover configured commands, each default method, the timeout, the refused rootful case and the Windows tree kill. Tried by hand once on Windows Docker Desktop, noted in the PR.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> deciding when to start or restart (dispatch hold and aga issues), installing Talos as a system service, remote Docker hosts.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["docker-state"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "docker-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos dispatcher: hold dispatch while Docker is down or at 85% memory, start a stopped engine", "description": "<p>Starting runs while Docker is full only produces more OOM-killed runs and handbacks to the owner. When Talos runs on a server, it may also start before Docker is ready at boot. The dispatcher should wait for Docker the same way it waits out a Claude usage limit.</p><ul><li>New class <code>DockerPause</code> in its own module, modelled on <code>talos/lib/usage_pause.py</code> <code>UsagePause</code> (one lock, interruptible wait, <code>stop()</code>). It holds the last verdict from <code>docker_state</code> and re-reads it at most every <code>docker.checkSeconds</code> (default 30).</li><li><code>talos/lib/dispatcher.py</code>: before a job is taken (next to the usage-limit wait ~l.193), wait while the verdict is <code>down</code> or <code>pressured</code> (85% high, 70% ok, from agent.json). Log once when the hold starts and once when it ends. No issue comments, since no issue is affected yet.</li><li>When the verdict is <code>down</code> and <code>docker.autoStart</code> is true (default true), call <code>docker_engine.start()</code> once per hold, after a short grace period so a Docker that is still booting isn't started twice. If it fails, log it and keep waiting. Never restart from here.</li><li>A run already in flight is not touched.</li><li><code>talos status</code> shows a Docker hold and since when; README updated.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests show the dispatcher waits while down or pressured, resumes when ok (with hysteresis), tries one start per hold after the grace period, and that <code>stop()</code> releases waiters.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> freeing memory (next issue), holding single issues (aga issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["docker-state", "docker-engine"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "docker-free", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: free Docker memory by stopping test containers of stale, deferred or won't-fix issues", "description": "<p>A warm Prometheus test container holds about 3 GB. Talos gc (adt-4234) removes them only for done, closed or won't fix issues, or merged PRs, so containers of issues that are parked or deferred keep filling Docker. When Docker is short of memory, Talos should stop the containers nobody is using, and only those.</p><ul><li>New module <code>talos/lib/docker_free.py</code>: <code>stoppable(containers, issues, running, now)</code> (pure) chooses the issues whose p4m test containers may be stopped. An issue qualifies when it has no run in flight <strong>and</strong> either its status is deferred or won't fix, or it has not changed (Gaia modified time) for more than <code>docker.staleHours</code> (default 72). Status names are normalised like <code>workspace_gc._norm</code>.</li><li><code>stop(names)</code> runs <code>docker stop</code> (not remove: the workspace and the next <code>ai test</code> still work). Containers come from <code>workspace_gc.test_containers</code> ({issue: names}).</li><li>The dispatch hold (<code>DockerPause</code>) calls it once when a <code>pressured</code> hold starts, then re-checks the verdict. Each stopped container is logged with its issue and reason; the issue gets no comment.</li><li><code>talos gc --dry-run</code> or <code>talos status</code> lists which containers would be stopped; README updated.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for <code>stoppable</code> (in-flight issue never chosen; deferred, won't fix and stale over 72h chosen; 71h not chosen; unreadable issue not chosen) and the hold calling it once per pressured hold. Docker unreachable: nothing stopped, the hold carries on.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> stopping the warm ember build inside a container that is otherwise in use, removing containers (gc's job).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["docker-gate"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "aga-docker-verbs", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "aga: docker, start-docker, restart-docker, stop-stale-containers and hold-until-docker verbs", "description": "<p>Agamemnon's triage sessions can't read Docker or act on it: the premise grants <code>docker_down</code> a <code>pause</code> tier that no verb uses. This issue adds the commands. Their use is granted per incident type in the follow-up issue.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/verbs.py</code>: <code>docker</code> (tier read, level READ: <code>docker_state.read()</code> plus its verdict); <code>start-docker</code> and <code>restart-docker</code> (new tier <code>engine</code>, level PRIVATE, added to the tier list in <code>talos/agents/agamemnon/premise.json</code>); <code>stop-stale-containers</code> (new tier <code>free</code>, level PRIVATE, uses <code>docker_free</code>, same rule: no run in flight, and deferred, won't fix or unchanged for more than 72h); <code>hold-until-docker</code> (tier wait, level PRIVATE).</li><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/tool.py</code>: <code>start-docker</code> is refused when the daemon is already up. <code>restart-docker</code> is refused while another issue has a run in flight, unless the verdict is <code>down</code> (those runs are already failing). Both use <code>docker_engine</code>, wait until ready and report the stack containers that are missing.</li><li><code>hold-until-docker</code> works like <code>_hold_until_tomorrow</code> (refused with a run in flight, in in_review or already held; assigns the issue to Agamemnon), but the journal hold has a condition <code>docker</code> instead of a time.</li><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/holds.py</code> <code>release_due</code> and <code>journal</code>: a Docker hold is due when the verdict is <code>ok</code>. Give back at most one Docker-held issue per sweep, oldest first, so they don't all start at once. A hold ends without giving the issue back when the issue was moved to deferred or won't fix, and goes to the owner with a comment after <code>docker.holdMaxHours</code> (default 72). Undo releases the hold, as for time holds.</li><li>Talos README (The <code>aga</code> tool): the new verbs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for each verb's refusals, the one-per-sweep release, the deferred/won't-fix release, the 72h handover and undo. These paths are in <code>agamemnonProtected</code>, so the merge gate's self check fails by design and the PR needs a manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the classifier, premise grants and role text (next issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["docker-engine", "docker-free"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "docker-incidents", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon: docker_pressure incident, wider docker_down, Docker state in the triage packet", "description": "<p>Runs that died from Docker running out of memory are classified as <code>other</code> and go to the owner, even though freeing memory, waiting and retrying would have resumed them. <code>docker_down</code> may only notify. This issue lets triage handle both.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/classifier.py</code>: a new <code>docker_pressure</code> rule (OOM kill, exit code 137, <code>Killed</code> from the test runner or ember build, Docker reporting the container OOMKilled, and similar), checked before <code>test_contention</code>. Widen <code>docker_down</code> (Docker Desktop starting or stopped, <code>error during connect</code> variants, pipe or socket not found on Windows and Linux).</li><li>Check the patterns against the real run logs of recent handbacks (Talos state and talos.db; the issues handed back over roughly the last 50). List in the PR which past handbacks are now classified differently.</li><li><code>premise.json</code>: <code>docker_down</code> gets read, engine, wait, retry, notify (\\"start the engine; restart only if it stays unresponsive and nothing else is running; then retry\\"). <code>docker_pressure</code> gets read, free, wait, retry, notify (\\"stop stale containers; if still short, hold-until-docker; then retry\\").</li><li><code>triage.py</code> <code>run</code>: fill the packet's <code>docker</code> with <code>docker_state.read()</code> plus its verdict instead of <code>None</code>.</li><li><code>role.md</code>: a Docker section: read <code>docker</code> first; when memory is short, free and hold, never restart; start before restart; never restart while other runs are in flight.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> classifier tests built from real log excerpts (secrets removed), a triage test showing the packet carries Docker state, and premise loading tests. Manual merge (<code>agamemnonProtected</code>).</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> remote Docker hosts, installing Talos as a system service.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aga-docker-verbs"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 21:20:06	2026-11-04 21:21:59	f
369dc1266aeb-38b7-6034-825abfb0ae13	34bdca956ae6-8157-e410-2af2948f16f3	4	{"summary": "Six Prometheus issues for the workflow editor's Run agent step, one per reported problem, all in aga-v1. Two fix the agent picker's avatar: the real picture and its size. One finds and fixes why the step can't be saved, and shows Gaia's validation errors. One fills the agent's defaults when an agent is picked, after the save fix since both change the same form. One offers the Run agent output ({step.outcome}, {step.comment}, which Gaia already provides) in the pickers of later steps. One makes the canvas zoom only on Ctrl/⌘+scroll, so plain scroll scrolls the page.", "issues": [{"key": "actor-avatar-picture", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: Run agent's agent dropdown shows the robot instead of the agent's picture", "description": "<p>In the workflow editor's properties panel (aprom-4057), the Run agent step's Agent dropdown always draws the default robot, even for agents with a profile picture. aprom-4252 made <code>Agent::Avatar</code> take the agent's user and show <code>profilePicture</code> when there is one. The panel's option renderer, <code>related-fields/relate-actor</code> (added by aprom-4057 for user pictures, agent avatars and expressions), still renders it without the user.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Pass the agent's user to <code>Agent::Avatar</code> in <code>relate-actor</code>, for the options and for the selected value.</li><li>Make sure the agent options are loaded with their user (<code>rels: 'user'</code> on the agent query of the editor's catalog data, loaded by the route or service, not the component) so <code>profilePicture</code> is there.</li><li>Check the other actor pickers that use <code>relate-actor</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Agents with a picture show it in the dropdown and in the selected value. Agents without one show the robot.</li><li>An integration test covers both cases.</li></ul>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "actor-avatar-size", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: avatars in the actor dropdown overflow the dropdown items", "description": "<p>In the workflow editor's properties panel (aprom-4057), the avatar in the Run agent step's Agent dropdown is too big: it overflows the dropdown item. The options are rendered by <code>related-fields/relate-actor</code>.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Render the avatar at the small size the user picker uses (<code>related-fields/relate-user</code>): same classes and size, avatar and name on one line, vertically centred. Reuse the existing classes. Only if none fits, add a scoped rule in the editor's module stylesheet.</li><li>Check the selected value in the closed select and the Ask a user picker, which use the same renderer.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Avatars fit inside each dropdown item and the closed select, matching the user picker's look.</li><li>No overflow at any item height.</li></ul>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "run-agent-save", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: a Run agent step can't be saved", "description": "<p>In the workflow editor (aprom-4038, panel aprom-4057), filling in a Run agent step and saving it fails, and the user isn't told why. The node is saved as a <code>workflownode</code> with a JSON <code>config</code>, which Gaia checks against the kind's fields (<code>gaia/core/libs/workflows/NodeKindCatalog.php</code>, <code>NodeConfigRules.php</code>).</p><p><strong>Gaia's rules for <code>run_agent</code></strong></p><ul><li>Fields: <code>agentId</code> (required: an agent id or an expression), <code>prompt</code>, <code>session</code>, <code>model</code>, <code>maxTurns</code>, <code>claimTimeout</code>, <code>timeout</code>.</li><li>All the optional fields are type <code>string</code>, including <code>maxTurns</code> and the timeouts: a number is rejected with 'must be a non-empty string'.</li><li>Any key not in the list is rejected ('is not a setting of run_agent'). Empty or null optional fields are fine.</li><li>The structure of an Active workflow can't change: only moving or renaming a node is allowed.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Reproduce it against the local Gaia, read the response, and fix the cause. Likely: numbers sent for <code>maxTurns</code>/timeouts, or extra keys in <code>config</code>. Send only the kind's fields, as strings, and drop empty ones.</li><li>Show Gaia's validation messages in the panel when a node save fails, for every node kind. Today the failure is silent.</li><li>If the fix needs a change in Gaia (e.g. numeric types), stop and say so in a comment rather than working around it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A Run agent step with an agent, a prompt and any mix of optional settings saves, and reloads with the same values.</li><li>A save Gaia rejects shows its message in the panel.</li><li>Tests cover the saved config shape and the error display.</li></ul>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "run-agent-defaults", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: fill a Run agent step's settings from the agent when one is picked", "description": "<p>When an agent is picked in a Run agent step (properties panel, aprom-4057), every other setting stays blank. The user should start from the agent's defaults and be able to edit them.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>On picking an agent, fill the empty settings in the draft:<ul><li><code>maxTurns</code>: the agent's <code>maxTurns</code>.</li><li><code>session</code>: <code>new</code>.</li><li><code>claimTimeout</code>: <code>15</code> and <code>timeout</code>: <code>240</code> (Gaia's defaults in <code>RunAgentActor::CLAIM_MINUTES</code> / <code>FINISH_MINUTES</code>).</li></ul>All values are strings (Gaia types every Run agent setting as a string).</li><li>Model: leave it empty and show the agent's choice as the empty option, e.g. 'Agent's default (simple: sonnet, complex: opus)' from the agent's <code>modelConfig</code>. An empty model lets the runtime pick by the issue's complexity, and a filled one would switch that off.</li><li>Never overwrite a value the user typed. When the agent changes, only refill the settings that still hold the previous agent's defaults.</li><li>Field help as info-icon tooltips (what each default comes from).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Picking an agent fills the settings above.</li><li>They can be edited and are saved as edited.</li><li>Switching agents keeps the user's edits.</li><li>An integration test covers fill, edit and switch.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a default prompt.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["run-agent-save"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "step-output-expressions", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: offer a Run agent step's output ({step.outcome}, {step.comment}) to the steps after it", "description": "<p>A workflow should be able to use what an agent produced: create an issue from it, or branch on it. Gaia already supports this. When an agent reports its Run agent step (<code>outcome</code> and <code>comment</code>, see <code>gaia/core/libs/workflows/ActorStepReports.php</code>), the run continues by the outcome's port, and later steps can read <code>{step.outcome}</code> (done, needs_input, blocked, failed, limit) and <code>{step.comment}</code>. Talos puts the run's summary in the comment. The same goes for Ask a user (replied or reassigned). The editor's field and expression pickers only offer the trigger's payload paths, so the output can't be found.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>For a node downstream of an actor node (Run agent or Ask a user), add a 'Step output' group to the expression picker and the filter and switch field pickers: <code>step.outcome</code> and <code>step.comment</code>.</li><li>In text settings such as Create issue's subject and description, or Add comment's body, the output can be inserted as <code>{step.comment}</code>.</li><li>A tooltip on the group: the values come from the latest actor step before this one.</li><li>Show the Run agent node's outcome ports with their names on the canvas, if they aren't already, so branching on the outcome is visible.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>After a Run agent step, a Create issue step can use <code>{step.comment}</code> in its description, and a filter can test <code>step.outcome</code>.</li><li>Nodes not after an actor step don't offer the group.</li><li>A test run shows the resolved values.</li><li>Tests cover the picker.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> structured output (a JSON object from the agent, read as <code>{step.output.*}</code>), which needs Gaia and Talos changes; output of earlier actor steps than the latest.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "canvas-wheel-zoom", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: zoom only on Ctrl/⌘ + scroll; plain scroll scrolls the page", "description": "<p>The workflow canvas (aprom-4038, own SVG layer) zooms on every mouse-wheel turn. The canvas is large, so the pointer is usually over it, and scrolling down to the step settings zooms instead. The common convention (Figma, Miro, n8n) is to zoom on Ctrl+scroll (⌘+scroll on macOS). Trackpad pinch arrives as a wheel event with <code>ctrlKey</code>, so pinch keeps zooming.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In the canvas's wheel handler, zoom only when <code>ctrlKey</code> or <code>metaKey</code> is held: call <code>preventDefault</code> then, and zoom around the pointer as today.</li><li>Without a modifier, don't handle the event or prevent its default, so the page scrolls.</li><li>Panning by dragging the background and the zoom and fit buttons stay as they are.</li><li>Tooltip on the zoom controls: 'Ctrl + scroll to zoom'.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Plain scroll over the canvas scrolls the page.</li><li>Ctrl/⌘ + scroll and trackpad pinch zoom.</li><li>A test covers both wheel cases.</li></ul>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 22:35:34	2026-11-04 22:35:34	f
c0596ff76aea-a4f4-813e-d19ff80fb3ab	994b17496ae9-2420-fee8-e1f463ff8479	5	{"summary": "One Prometheus issue in milestone aga-v2. In the idea browser, each open idea shows a shimmer skeleton bar where its status label goes until the plan statuses have loaded, replacing the spinner label from aprom-4267. The issue also makes sure the loading state really holds until the plans query resolves, since the aprom-4267 change is not visible in production.", "issues": [{"key": "idea-status-skeleton", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea browser: shimmer skeleton in place of the status label while plan statuses load", "description": "<p>The idea browser (<code>app/templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>) shows a status label on each idea: Archived from the idea model, otherwise Brainstorming / Proposed / Created / ... from the latest <code>ideaplan</code>. The plans are queried separately by <code>loadPlans</code> in <code>app/routes/app/project/idea.js</code> after the ideas load, so until then open ideas wrongly show Brainstorming. aprom-4267 (prometheus#617) added a loading state with a spinner label in <code>app/controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> (<code>progressByIdea</code>, <code>loadPlanStatuses</code>), but the engineer sees no change in production. Replace that spinner with the shimmer skeleton used elsewhere in Prometheus, and make sure the loading state really works.</p><ul><li><strong>Check first:</strong> on current <code>dev</code>, open the ideas page with DevTools network throttling (Slow 3G) and confirm whether open ideas show the loading state until the plans response arrives. If they still show Brainstorming first, find out why (e.g. the loaded state set before the plans query resolves, or <code>setupController</code> not resetting it) and fix it in the controller and route, with a unit test that fails before the fix.</li><li>While an open idea's status is loading, render <code>&lt;span class=\\"pull-right skeleton-line skeleton-line--xs idea-status-skeleton\\" data-idea-status-skeleton&gt;</code> in place of its <code>label</code> span, containing a <code>sr-only</code> \\"Loading\\" text (<code>views.app.idea.progress.loading</code>; add the key to <code>translations/en-us.json</code> if missing). No spinner icon.</li><li>Reuse the shimmer from <code>app/styles/components/skeleton.scss</code> (<code>.skeleton-line</code>). Add only <code>.idea-status-skeleton</code>, scoped under the idea list in <code>app/styles/modules/idea.scss</code>: about the height and width of a status label, no margin, aligned with the title, and <code>border-radius: 0</code> (square edges per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>).</li><li>The skeleton ends when the plans query resolves, fails or returns nothing (failure falls back to Brainstorming; the route already reports the error). Archived ideas show Archived immediately. Live plan events (<code>idea.plan.created</code>, <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code>) and <code>setPlanStatus</code> keep the current labels instead of bringing the skeleton back. A switch to another project's ideas shows the skeleton again.</li><li>Update the unit tests (<code>tests/unit/controllers/app/project/idea-live-test.js</code>) and idea browser acceptance steps (<code>tests/acceptance/steps/ideas/idea-browser-steps.js</code>) so they check <code>[data-idea-status-skeleton]</code> while loading and <code>[data-idea-status]</code> after.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>With Slow 3G throttling, every open idea shows a shimmering bar on the right of its row until the plans response arrives, never Brainstorming and no spinner. Screen readers announce \\"Loading\\".</li><li>Then each bar is replaced by the real status label in the same place, without the row shifting.</li><li>The bar has square edges and uses only the existing skeleton colours.</li><li>Verified in the running app (<code>https://app.local-projects4.me</code>) with throttling; the PR says so.</li><li>Tests pass, and each new check fails if its line is reverted.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a skeleton for the whole idea list while the ideas query loads, and changing how plans are queried.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["idea-browser-skeleton", "idea-browser-loaded"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 07:37:36	2026-11-04 07:39:14	f
f430d0d66aeb-9e83-c85a-a814a9b6ec1c	393073e96aeb-daa0-504d-005f14c7084c	1	{"summary": "Show live-ish online status dots on the project dashboard's Members box, derived from Gaia's existing User.lastActivityAt (updated on every authenticated request). First a standalone presence-dot component maps a timestamp to online (<5 min) / away (5-30 min) / offline (no dot) with a tooltip; then a presence service polls the members' lastActivityAt every 60 seconds while the dashboard is open and the Members box renders the dot on each active member's avatar. Prometheus only, no Gaia or Hermes contract change.", "issues": [{"key": "presence-dot", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Users: presence dot component from lastActivityAt (online / away / offline)", "description": "<p>The project dashboard's Members box should show whether each member is around right now. Gaia already records <code>User.lastActivityAt</code> (UTC datetime, updated on every authenticated API request; Prometheus model <code>app/models/user.js</code> has it as <code>lastActivityAt</code>). This issue adds a small reusable component that turns that timestamp into a status dot. Placing it in the Members box is a separate issue.</p><ul><li>New Glimmer component <code>app/components/user-ui/presence-dot.{js,hbs}</code> (native class, YUIDoc, license header). Arguments: <code>@lastActivityAt</code> (string or Date, may be null).</li><li>Status from the age of <code>@lastActivityAt</code>: <strong>online</strong> when under 5 minutes, <strong>away</strong> from 5 up to 30 minutes, <strong>offline</strong> otherwise or when null. Put the thresholds in named constants. Parse the value as UTC (Gaia stores <code>gmdate</code>); reuse the parsing of the existing <code>format-date-time</code> helper rather than writing new date code.</li><li>Re-evaluate the status every 60 seconds while rendered (so a member drifts from online to away without new data); clear the timer on destroy.</li><li>Render: online = round dot in <code>$successColor</code>, away = round dot in <code>$warningColor</code>, offline = nothing. <code>border-radius: 50%</code> is allowed for status dots; a thin white border so it reads on any avatar. Styles in <code>app/styles/modules/user.scss</code> (or the existing user module file) under a scoped class such as <code>.presence-dot</code>, <code>.presence-dot-online</code>, <code>.presence-dot-away</code>; colours only from <code>app/styles/variables.scss</code>.</li><li>Tooltip (<code>title</code> + <code>data-toggle=\\"tooltip\\"</code>, as elsewhere): \\"Online\\" or \\"Away · active 12 minutes ago\\" (humanized like <code>format-date-time humanize=true</code>). The dot also has screen-reader text (<code>sr-only</code>) with the same status.</li><li>All strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Integration test <code>tests/integration/components/user-ui/presence-dot-test.js</code>: online for 1 minute ago, away for 10 minutes ago, nothing rendered for 45 minutes ago and for null, tooltip text for each, and the status changes after the clock advances past 5 minutes (fake timers). Each test fails if its line is reverted.</li><li>Lint passes; no new dependencies.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: using the component anywhere (next issue), fetching data, user-set statuses.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "members-presence", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project dashboard: online status dots in the Members box with 60 s refresh", "description": "<p>Show each project member's online status on the project dashboard's Members box, using the <code>UserUi::PresenceDot</code> component (from the issue this depends on). The status comes from <code>User.lastActivityAt</code>, which Gaia updates on every authenticated request, so it must be refreshed while the page is open to stay current.</p><ul><li>New service <code>app/services/presence.js</code> (single responsibility: keep the <code>lastActivityAt</code> of a set of users fresh). API: <code>track(owner, userIds)</code> starts polling every 60 seconds and returns/registers a disposer; polling stops when the owner is torn down (same lifecycle idea as <code>hermes.register</code>). Each poll is one <code>store.query('user', { query: &lt;Gaia query matching the ids&gt;, fields: 'id,lastActivityAt' })</code> (see <code>core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php</code> for the id-list syntax, and <code>routes/app/user/management.js</code> for <code>fields</code>), so the existing user records in the store update and the dots re-render. Use the store, not <code>fetch()</code>. Ignore a response that is older than the latest one (request counter), catch failures and keep the last known values, and skip the poll while the tab is hidden (<code>document.visibilityState</code>), polling once immediately when it becomes visible again.</li><li>Start tracking the member ids from the dashboard (<code>routes/app/project/index.js</code> / its controller, members come from the project's <code>members</code> rel) on route enter and stop on exit or project change.</li><li>In <code>app/templates/app/project/index.hbs</code> (~265, <code>users-list</code> / <code>member-avatar-wrap</code>) render <code>&lt;UserUi::PresenceDot @lastActivityAt={{member.lastActivityAt}} /&gt;</code> on the avatar, only for members whose <code>accountStatus</code> is active (invited/inactive keep their existing badge and get no dot). Position it at the avatar's bottom-right via a scoped rule in <code>app/styles/modules/project.scss</code> next to <code>.member-account-status</code>.</li><li>Mirage: make sure the user handler supports the poll query and <code>fields</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit test for the presence service: polls every 60 s, stops after dispose, no poll while hidden, a stale response does not overwrite a newer one, a failed request keeps the previous values.</li><li>Acceptance test (Gherkin, feature-specific steps in their own steps file, not <code>steps.js</code>): a member active 1 minute ago shows an online dot, one active 10 minutes ago an away dot, one active 2 hours ago and an invited member show none.</li><li>Checked in the running app next to the current dashboard; lint and tests pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: dots on other screens, the sidebar's own \\"Online\\" text, the control sidebar, push presence through Hermes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["presence-dot"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 14:45:08	2026-11-04 14:45:08	f
702e94606aef-9eab-9161-151c67395b7c	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	12	{"summary": "EzSearchCompact polish and two more views. First a fix in the compact component: in the multi-row layout, Search and Clear become icon-only buttons attached to the bar (the idea list shows wide text buttons today); every compact user gets it. Gantt Cal gets the multi-row compact search at the top of its task list. Task Board replaces its saved-search dropdown and client-side text filter with the linear compact search, inline with the milestone tabs (at least 30% of the row); searching becomes server-side through the existing query and searchId parameters. Gantt and Board run in parallel; Gantt waits for the icon fix.", "issues": [{"key": "ez-compact-icons", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "EzSearchCompact: Search and Clear as icon buttons attached to the bar", "description": "<p>On the idea list (aprom-4334) the compact search's Search and Clear take too much of the narrow column: they render as wide text buttons. The agreed design (screens <code>compact-multirow</code>, <code>gantt-compact</code>) has them as icon-only buttons attached to the right end of the bar, so the input keeps almost the full width. Fix it in <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> (aprom-4333) so every compact user gets it. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search-compact/index.hbs</code>, multi-row layout, row 1:<ul><li>The bar, then Search as <code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code> with only <code>fa-search</code>, then Clear as <code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code> with only <code>fa-times</code>.</li><li>Both are attached to the bar like a Bootstrap <code>input-group-btn</code>: same height as the input, no gap, square edges.</li><li>Each has a translated <code>title</code> and <code>aria-label</code> (reuse <code>global.form.search</code> and <code>global.form.clear</code>).</li></ul>The linear layout already uses icons; make both layouts share the same button markup (one partial or sub-component), not two copies.</li><li><code>app/styles/components/ez-search-compact.scss</code>: the bar fills the remaining width. Remove any width or padding that made the buttons wide.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An integration test asserts that the multi-row Search and Clear contain no text, only their icons, carry titles, and sit on the bar's row. In a 300px container the input is wider than both buttons together.</li><li>Checked in the browser on the idea list at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> rows 2 and 3 (Saved, Filter, chips), the full <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> toolbar.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4333"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["gantt-compact", "compact-multirow"]}, {"key": "ez-gantt", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Gantt Cal: search with EzSearchCompact", "description": "<p>The Gantt Cal has no search UI: it only honours a <code>?query=</code> URL parameter, which the route ANDs into each milestone's issue query (<code>routes/app/project/gantt.js</code> ~l.53-82, controller <code>queryParams = ['query']</code> ~l.130). Add <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> (aprom-4333, multi-row, the default) at the top of the task list. The engineer approved the placement in screen <code>gantt-compact</code>. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>components/app-ui/gantt-chart.hbs</code>: add a named block (e.g. <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code>) rendered at the top of <code>.gantt-task-list</code>, above <code>.gantt-header</code>. The chart knows nothing about search. In <code>styles/modules/gantt.scss</code>, keep the task rows and the timeline rows aligned when the block is present: the timeline side gets the same top offset, or the block sits outside both scroll areas. Check the row alignment in the browser.</li><li><code>templates/app/project/gantt.hbs</code>: pass <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact @schema @query @savedSearches @activeSavedSearchId @onSavedSearchChange @onApply @onSave @onUpdateSavedSearch @aclContext=\\"issue.read\\" /&gt;</code> in that block, plus the save dialog as on the Issue list. No <code>@baseQuery</code>: the route adds milestone and project.</li><li><code>routes/app/project/gantt.js</code>: load the Issue schema (<code>query-schema</code> <code>load('Issue', {projectId})</code>, metadata <code>views.Issue.search</code>) and the project's issue saved searches through <code>services/saved-search.js</code> (<code>relatedTo: 'issue'</code>, <code>projectId</code>, shared with the Issue list).</li><li><code>controllers/app/project/gantt.js</code>: add <code>searchId</code> to <code>queryParams</code>. Apply, select, save and update go through the saved-search service. Don't copy list-controller code. Live-sync reloads keep the active query.</li><li>Acceptance (<code>tests/acceptance/gantt/</code> + steps, Mirage issue handler already records the query):<ol><li>Type and run a query: issues are requested with it ANDed with milestone and project, and <code>?query=</code> is set.</li><li>Remove a chip: it re-runs.</li><li>Apply a saved search: its name shows.</li><li>An error shows and nothing is sent.</li></ol></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios pass.</li><li>The existing Gantt tests (drag, resize, dependencies, issue panel, live sync) pass.</li><li>Task rows and timeline rows stay aligned with the search present.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filtering milestones (the query applies to issues), the Calendar view, the Task Board.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ez-compact-icons", "aprom-4331"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["gantt-compact"]}, {"key": "ez-board", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task Board: search with EzSearchCompact (linear), inline with the milestone tabs", "description": "<p>The Task Board has two separate filters in the milestone tabs row (<code>components/app-ui/task-board.hbs</code> ~l.37-62):</p><ul><li>a Saved Searches <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code>, whose state lives in the component (<code>activeSearch</code>, <code>filterQuery</code>, <code>toggleSearch</code>, <code>isSearchActive</code>, <code>task-board.js</code> ~l.26-163) and which applies through <code>@applySearch</code> to the controller's <code>query</code>/<code>searchId</code> URL parameters (<code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> ~l.833; the route ANDs the query into each lane's issue query);</li><li>a free-text <code>&lt;Input&gt;</code> that hides loaded cards in the browser (<code>task-board/issues-provider.js</code> ~l.32: subject, description, number).</li></ul><p>Replace both with <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact @linear={{true}}&gt;</code> (aprom-4333). There is one search model, so typed text runs on the server (bare words become <code>Issue.subject CONTAINS …</code>) and the lanes reload. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>task-board.hbs</code>: replace the dropdown and the <code>&lt;Input&gt;</code> in <code>.milestone-filters</code> with <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact @linear={{true}} @schema @query @savedSearches @activeSavedSearchId @onSavedSearchChange @onApply @onSave @onUpdateSavedSearch @aclContext=\\"issue.read\\" /&gt;</code>, all passed in from the page.</li><li>Placement (engineer's requirement, screen <code>board-linear</code>):<ul><li>The search stays <strong>inline with the milestone tabs, on the same row</strong>, and never drops onto its own row at md widths and up.</li><li>The row is a flex row: the tab strip takes the remaining space (<code>flex: 1</code>, <code>min-width: 0</code>) and scrolls sideways when there are more tabs than fit; the search takes at least 30% of the row (<code>flex: 0 0 30%</code>, growing only if its content needs it).</li><li>The tabs keep working as drop targets (<code>.drop-zone-area</code>) while scrolled.</li><li>Only below 768px does the search wrap under the tabs at full width (screen <code>board-linear-mobile</code>).</li></ul></li><li><code>task-board.js</code>: remove <code>query</code>, <code>filterQuery</code>, <code>activeSearch</code>, <code>toggleSearch</code>, <code>isSearchActive</code> and the constructor's saved-search lookup. Remove the client text filter from <code>issues-provider.js</code> and <code>milestones.hbs</code> (<code>@query</code>). <code>initialize-sortable</code> receives <code>query</code> to re-attach Sortable when the cards change; make sure lanes re-rendered by the route reload still get Sortable (drag still works after a search).</li><li><code>templates/app/project/board.hbs</code>, <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code>, <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code>:<ul><li>Load the Issue schema (<code>query-schema</code> <code>load('Issue', {projectId})</code>) and the issue saved searches through <code>services/saved-search.js</code> (<code>relatedTo: 'issue'</code>, <code>projectId</code>), replacing the route's own saved-search queries (~l.161-166).</li><li>Apply, select, save and update go through the service, and set <code>query</code>/<code>searchId</code> as <code>applySearch</code> does now.</li><li>Add the save dialog as on the Issue list.</li><li>Hermes live updates keep the active query.</li></ul></li><li><code>styles/modules/board.scss</code>: the flex row, the tab-strip scroll and the mobile wrap, scoped under the board.</li><li>Tests: update <code>tests/acceptance/taskboard/filter-issues.feature</code> and its steps:<ol><li>Typing <code>subject words</code> and pressing Enter requests every lane with <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS 'subject words')</code>.</li><li>Applying a saved search shows its name and sets <code>searchId</code>.</li><li>Clear resets.</li><li>Cards can still be dragged after a search.</li><li>The search and the tabs share one row at desktop width (same top).</li></ol></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios pass.</li><li>The other Task Board tests (quick create, status update, milestone create and complete) pass.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width with two and with eight milestone tabs (search stays inline, at least 30%), and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> keeping an instant client-side card filter, the planning view, the Gantt.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4333", "aprom-4331"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["board-linear", "board-linear-mobile"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 20:26:24	2026-11-07 20:28:27	f
25e673436aeb-d2a8-4887-0e618ad13583	34bdca956ae6-8157-e410-2af2948f16f3	3	{"summary": "Gaia adds a 'Milestone completed' workflow trigger. That needs a small catalog addition: an update trigger can require a field to change to a value. Talos learns to run a Run agent step that isn't about an issue, with no repo workspace, branch or PR, just the step's prompt, the record and the agent's tools. Prometheus then shows the trigger in the editor and lets a test run pick a milestone. Gaia and Talos run in parallel; Prometheus follows Gaia. With these, the engineer sets up a Retrospective agent and a workflow in the UI that creates a retrospective issue when a milestone is completed. All three go in milestone aga-v1.", "issues": [{"key": "trigger-milestone-completed", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Workflows: 'Milestone completed' trigger (update triggers that match a field changing to a value)", "description": "<p>A Prometheus needs a workflow that starts when a milestone is completed, so an agent can write a retrospective and create an issue from it. The trigger catalog (<code>core/libs/workflows/TriggerEventCatalog.php</code>) has issue, comment, wiki and time-log events only. Its update events match the fields that changed, never the value they changed to. Milestone writes aren't wired to workflows at all.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Catalog: let an update event name a transition, e.g. <code>'to' =&gt; ['status' =&gt; 'completed']</code>. The event is raised only when the field changes to that value from another value. <code>raisedBy</code> then needs the audit's old and new values, not only the changed field names. Update <code>WorkflowTriggersComponent::raise</code> and <code>changed</code> to pass them. Keep the current behaviour for events without <code>to</code>.</li><li>Add <code>EventNames::MILESTONE_COMPLETED</code> (<code>milestone.completed</code>, already a live event) as a trigger: model <code>Milestone</code>, on update, field <code>status</code>, to <code>completed</code>, label 'Milestone completed'. Use the same rule as <code>MilestoneLiveEventsComponent</code> (~l.77): new status completed, old status not completed.</li><li>Add <code>Events\\\\WorkflowTriggers</code> to <code>MilestoneController</code> <code>$uses</code>.</li><li>Check that the payload, the describer (<code>TriggerEventDescriber</code>: fields and types for filters and expressions such as <code>{milestone.name}</code>), <code>ProjectIdResolver</code> (knows milestone), <code>SetFieldAction</code>'s model check and the test run (<code>TestRunPayload</code>, <code>WorkflowrunController</code> with <code>entityType</code> Milestone) all work for a milestone.</li><li><code>GET /workflowevent</code> lists the new trigger.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Completing a milestone (PATCH status to <code>completed</code>) starts the Active workflows with this trigger in the milestone's project. A Run agent step's actor step has <code>entityType</code> Milestone and the milestone's id.</li><li>Other milestone edits don't start them, and neither does saving an already completed milestone.</li><li>A test run against a milestone works.</li><li>Unit tests cover the catalog's transition matching. Regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other milestone triggers (created, started).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "talos-record-runs", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: run 'Run agent' workflow steps that aren't about an issue (no repo workspace)", "description": "<p>A workflow can now ask an agent to work on a record that isn't an issue: first case, a Retrospective agent started by 'Milestone completed', which reads the milestone and creates an issue. Gaia's Run agent step works with any record (<code>entityType</code>/<code>entityId</code> on the actor step), but Talos refuses it: <code>talos/lib/workflow_steps.py</code> <code>_subject</code> (~l.197) says 'Talos runs agents on issues only'. <code>dispatcher.run_step</code> (~l.274) and <code>_start</code> assume an issue and its repo: workspace, branch, Gaia pack, ship flow and CodeRabbit loop.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In <code>workflow_steps.py</code>, issue steps run exactly as today. Any other <code>entityType</code> becomes a record run.</li><li>A record run: Claude with the step's prompt, the agent's spec (role prompt, model, tool grants, permission mode, turn cap) and a short context block (record type, id and project; for a milestone, its name and dates through gaia-mcp <code>get_milestone</code>).</li><li>Its cwd is a scratch folder under the per-machine state (from <code>LOCAL_DIR</code>), not a repo checkout. No branch, no commit, no PR, no ship session, no CodeRabbit loop, no test slot.</li><li>Sessions are keyed by record (type + id), so <code>session: resume</code> works per record.</li><li>Report the outcome with the existing five (done, needs_input, blocked, failed, limit), and handle usage limits as issue steps do.</li><li>Keep the step logic in <code>lib/</code> functions that can be unit tested. Update the Talos README.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A Run agent step on a milestone is claimed, runs in a scratch folder without touching any repo, and reports done or a hand-off.</li><li>Issue steps behave exactly as before.</li><li>Unit tests cover the issue/record split, the record context and the outcome reporting.</li><li>Works on Windows and Linux.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> record runs that change code.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "editor-milestone-trigger", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: show the 'Milestone completed' trigger and test-run a milestone", "description": "<p>Gaia adds a 'Milestone completed' workflow trigger (listed by <code>GET /workflowevent</code>) so a workflow can start an agent when a milestone is completed. The editor from aprom-4038 and 4057 keeps its own <code>catalog.js</code> copy of Gaia's node kinds and triggers (noted on aprom-4038), and its test run may only pick issues.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Check where the palette and the trigger form get their triggers. If they're hard-coded, add <code>milestone.completed</code> (label 'Milestone completed', module Milestone). Better: take the triggers from the cached <code>workflowevent</code> catalog so later triggers need no UI change.</li><li>The properties panel's field and expression pickers offer the milestone's fields (from the trigger catalog's payload paths).</li><li>Test run: when the trigger's module is Milestone, the record picker lists the scope's milestones (<code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code>, searchable), and the run posts <code>entityType</code> Milestone with the milestone's id.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A workflow with the Milestone completed trigger and a Run agent step can be built, saved, activated and test-run against a milestone.</li><li>Mirage handlers and an integration or acceptance test cover the trigger and the milestone picker.</li></ul>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["trigger-milestone-completed"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 20:05:57	2026-11-04 20:13:49	f
26e988076aeb-2e52-6034-9b0b94fc76a9	34bdca956ae6-8157-e410-2af2948f16f3	5	{"summary": "Five Prometheus issues for the workflow editor's Run agent step, one per reported problem, all in aga-v1. Two fix the agent picker's avatar: the real picture and its size. One fixes the step save that fails silently with no request sent (client side), and makes save failures visible. One fills the agent's defaults when an agent is picked, after the save fix since both change the same form. One makes the canvas zoom only on Ctrl/⌘+scroll. The step-output picker is left out until the engineer has checked {step.outcome}/{step.comment}.", "issues": [{"key": "actor-avatar-picture", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: Run agent's agent dropdown shows the robot instead of the agent's picture", "description": "<p>In the workflow editor's properties panel (aprom-4057), the Run agent step's Agent dropdown always draws the default robot, even for agents with a profile picture. aprom-4252 made <code>Agent::Avatar</code> take the agent's user and show <code>profilePicture</code> when there is one. The panel's option renderer, <code>related-fields/relate-actor</code> (added by aprom-4057 for user pictures, agent avatars and expressions), still renders it without the user.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Pass the agent's user to <code>Agent::Avatar</code> in <code>relate-actor</code>, for the options and for the selected value.</li><li>Make sure the agent options are loaded with their user (<code>rels: 'user'</code> on the agent query of the editor's catalog data, loaded by the route or service, not the component) so <code>profilePicture</code> is there.</li><li>Check the other actor pickers that use <code>relate-actor</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Agents with a picture show it in the dropdown and in the selected value. Agents without one show the robot.</li><li>An integration test covers both cases.</li></ul>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "actor-avatar-size", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: avatars in the actor dropdown overflow the dropdown items", "description": "<p>In the workflow editor's properties panel (aprom-4057), the avatar in the Run agent step's Agent dropdown is too big: it overflows the dropdown item. The options are rendered by <code>related-fields/relate-actor</code>.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Render the avatar at the small size the user picker uses (<code>related-fields/relate-user</code>): same classes and size, avatar and name on one line, vertically centred. Reuse the existing classes. Only if none fits, add a scoped rule in the editor's module stylesheet.</li><li>Check the selected value in the closed select and the Ask a user picker, which use the same renderer.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Avatars fit inside each dropdown item and the closed select, matching the user picker's look.</li><li>No overflow at any item height.</li></ul>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "run-agent-save", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: saving a Run agent step does nothing (no request, no error)", "description": "<p>In the workflow editor (aprom-4038, properties panel aprom-4057), filling in a Run agent step and saving it does nothing. The engineer traced it: <strong>no network request is sent and nothing is logged in the console</strong>. So the save stops in Prometheus before it reaches Gaia.</p><p><strong>How saving works</strong> (from aprom-4038 and 4057)</p><ul><li>The panel edits a deep-copied draft and writes it back with Apply. The header Save persists the graph through the workflow-graph service, which orders the node, edge and workflow writes.</li><li>The aprom-4057 notes say live edits were rejected because changes to the shared <code>node.config</code> could not be tracked.</li></ul><p><strong>Where to look</strong></p><ul><li>The Apply and Save handlers: is the action wired up, or is the button disabled without a visible cue?</li><li>Client-side validation of the draft that fails and returns without a message.</li><li>The graph service skipping the node because it looks unchanged. If Apply writes into the existing <code>config</code> object, or the change isn't seen on the record, nothing is dirty and nothing is sent.</li><li>A swallowed promise rejection: a <code>catch</code> or <code>then</code> without a handler.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Start with a failing test that reproduces it: fill a Run agent step, Apply, Save, and expect a <code>workflownode</code> POST or PATCH in Mirage. Then fix the cause.</li><li>Make every failure visible: a validation problem is shown on its field or in the panel, and a failed save shows Gaia's message through <code>errorManager</code>.</li><li>Once the request goes out, follow Gaia's rules for <code>run_agent</code> (<code>gaia/core/libs/workflows/NodeKindCatalog.php</code>, <code>NodeConfigRules.php</code>):<ul><li>Fields: <code>agentId</code> (required), <code>prompt</code>, <code>session</code>, <code>model</code>, <code>maxTurns</code>, <code>claimTimeout</code>, <code>timeout</code>.</li><li>All are strings, including <code>maxTurns</code> and the timeouts: numbers are rejected.</li><li>Any other key is rejected. Drop empty optional fields.</li><li>An Active workflow's structure can't change.</li></ul></li><li>Check that the other node kinds save after the fix.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A Run agent step with an agent, a prompt and any mix of optional settings saves (a request is sent), and reloads with the same values.</li><li>Any blocked or failed save shows a message.</li><li>Tests cover the save, the config shape and the error display.</li></ul>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "run-agent-defaults", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: fill a Run agent step's settings from the agent when one is picked", "description": "<p>When an agent is picked in a Run agent step (properties panel, aprom-4057), every other setting stays blank. The user should start from the agent's defaults and be able to edit them.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>On picking an agent, fill the empty settings in the draft:<ul><li><code>maxTurns</code>: the agent's <code>maxTurns</code>.</li><li><code>session</code>: <code>new</code>.</li><li><code>claimTimeout</code>: <code>15</code> and <code>timeout</code>: <code>240</code> (Gaia's defaults in <code>RunAgentActor::CLAIM_MINUTES</code> / <code>FINISH_MINUTES</code>).</li></ul>All values are strings (Gaia types every Run agent setting as a string).</li><li>Model: leave it empty and show the agent's choice as the empty option, e.g. 'Agent's default (simple: sonnet, complex: opus)' from the agent's <code>modelConfig</code>. An empty model lets the runtime pick by the issue's complexity, and a filled one would switch that off.</li><li>Never overwrite a value the user typed. When the agent changes, only refill the settings that still hold the previous agent's defaults.</li><li>Field help as info-icon tooltips (what each default comes from).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Picking an agent fills the settings above.</li><li>They can be edited and are saved as edited.</li><li>Switching agents keeps the user's edits.</li><li>An integration test covers fill, edit and switch.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a default prompt.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["run-agent-save"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "canvas-wheel-zoom", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: zoom only on Ctrl/⌘ + scroll; plain scroll scrolls the page", "description": "<p>The workflow canvas (aprom-4038, own SVG layer) zooms on every mouse-wheel turn. The canvas is large, so the pointer is usually over it, and scrolling down to the step settings zooms instead. The common convention (Figma, Miro, n8n) is to zoom on Ctrl+scroll (⌘+scroll on macOS). Trackpad pinch arrives as a wheel event with <code>ctrlKey</code>, so pinch keeps zooming.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In the canvas's wheel handler, zoom only when <code>ctrlKey</code> or <code>metaKey</code> is held: call <code>preventDefault</code> then, and zoom around the pointer as today.</li><li>Without a modifier, don't handle the event or prevent its default, so the page scrolls.</li><li>Panning by dragging the background and the zoom and fit buttons stay as they are.</li><li>Tooltip on the zoom controls: 'Ctrl + scroll to zoom'.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Plain scroll over the canvas scrolls the page.</li><li>Ctrl/⌘ + scroll and trackpad pinch zoom.</li><li>A test covers both wheel cases.</li></ul>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-04 22:39:34	2026-11-04 22:43:14	f
b08175706aeb-160e-d9f0-42e10cb53bf7	34bdca956ae6-8157-e410-2af2948f16f3	6	{"summary": "One Prometheus issue in aga-v1: the workflow editor shows a node's open ports and can end all of them with one action, so workflows meet Gaia's activation rule (every port connected, paths end at an End node) without wiring each port by hand. Gaia's rule stays as it is.", "issues": [{"key": "end-open-ports", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow editor: show open ports and end them with one action", "description": "<p>Activating a workflow fails when any output port is unconnected. Gaia (<code>gaia/core/libs/workflows/WorkflowGraph.php</code> <code>errors</code>) requires every port connected and every path to end explicitly at an <code>end</code> node: 'Port 'done' of node 'call Hera' is not connected; connect it or end it with an end node.' A Run agent node has five ports (done, needs_input, blocked, failed, limit), a filter two, a switch one per case plus default. The editor (aprom-4038) gives no sign of open ports until activation, and the user must wire each one by hand. Keep Gaia's rule: it catches forgotten branches. Make it easy to meet in the editor.</p><p><strong>Gaia's rules the editor must respect</strong></p><ul><li>One edge per port.</li><li>An End node takes any number of incoming edges and has no ports.</li><li>Edges can't close a cycle or lead into the trigger.</li><li>An Active workflow's structure can't change (draft or disable it first, as the editor already handles).</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Open-port markers: on the canvas, mark each unconnected port of every node except End (e.g. a warning colour from <code>variables.scss</code> plus a tooltip 'Not connected'). Show a count of open ports in the editor header next to Activate.</li><li>'End open ports' action: on a selected node with open ports, a button in the properties panel. It connects every free port to an End node: reuse the workflow's existing End node if there is one, else add one near the node. It goes through the existing graph save, like a manual connection.</li><li>Also offer it for all nodes at once in the editor header, when there are open ports.</li><li>When activation fails, keep showing Gaia's messages, and select or highlight the nodes they name if that's straightforward.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A workflow whose only problem is open ports can be made activatable with one click, and activates.</li><li>Open ports are visible before activating.</li><li>Ports that are already connected are untouched.</li><li>Integration or acceptance tests cover the markers and both forms of the action.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing Gaia's activation rule; auto-ending ports on save.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-05 00:41:20	2026-11-05 00:41:20	f
b69bb3d06af5-a32c-65e3-e108334a5716	e66181d96af4-7c69-1af5-a7b779ce5171	3	{"summary": "Replace the in-browser milestone paging from aprom-4493 with real server-side paging: the Project Milestones box loads 5 milestones per request through ListLoader. Its fixed box-footer pager is QuickList::Pagination, driven by Gaia's meta.links.next, as in the ideas browser. The estimated-vs-spent chart keeps a light all-milestones query for its dropdown. One Prometheus issue in aga-v2.", "issues": [{"key": "milestones-server-paging", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project dashboard: page the Project Milestones box from the server (ListLoader + QuickList pagination footer)", "description": "<p>aprom-4493 paginated the Project Milestones box on the project dashboard in the browser only: the route still loads every milestone (<code>limit: -1</code>) and the controller slices the list. Make it real lazy loading: each page is its own request of 5 milestones. Use the ideas browser pattern (<code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> with <code>utils/state/list-loader.js</code>, footer pager <code>QuickList::Pagination</code>).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Box data</strong>: in <code>controllers/app/project/index.js</code>, add a <code>ListLoader</code> for <code>milestone</code> (page size 5). Its request is <code>(Milestone.projectId : &lt;id&gt;)</code>, sort <code>Milestone.startDate</code> DESC, <code>page</code>. Keep the page in a tracked controller property, not a query param, and reset it to 1 in the route's <code>setupController</code>. <code>hasNext</code>, the loading flag and the error come from the loader. A page that fails to load shows the error with a retry, as the QuickList does.</li><li><strong>Issue counts per row</strong>: after each page loads, attach to its milestones the matching issues from the issues the route already loads (<code>issuetime</code>, filter by <code>milestoneId</code>), as <code>loadMilestones</code> in <code>routes/app/project/index.js</code> does today. Keep the <code>willTransition</code> unload working.</li><li><strong>Footer</strong>: in <code>templates/app/project/index.hbs</code> (~368), render the current page's <code>Project::Milestones</code> rows in the <code>box-body</code>. Put <code>&lt;QuickList::Pagination @page @limit @hasNext @count @disabled={{isLoading}} @onPage&gt;</code> in a <code>box-footer</code> of the box, unchanged, so it reads <code>1-5 / 5+</code> while there is a next page and <code>6-9 / 9</code> on the last. It hides itself when there is only one page. Keep the <code>Exceptions::NothingFound</code> empty state.</li><li><strong>Remove the aprom-4493 client paging</strong>: <code>milestonesPageSize</code>, <code>milestonesPage</code>, <code>visibleMilestones</code>, the range getters, the previous/next actions (~244-372), the inline pager markup and its <code>pageRange</code> translation if nothing else uses it.</li><li><strong>Chart filter</strong>: the estimated-vs-spent milestone dropdown still lists all milestones. The route's all-milestones query becomes a light one (<code>fields: 'Milestone.id,Milestone.name,Milestone.dateCreated'</code>, <code>limit: -1</code>, as in <code>utils/state/thread-votes.js</code>) used only for <code>estimatedSpentMilestoneOptions</code> and the default selection. <code>estimatedSpentChartIssues</code> filters <code>issuetime</code> by <code>milestoneId</code> instead of reading <code>milestone.issues</code>.</li><li><strong>Adding a milestone</strong> (<code>saveMilestone</code>): reload page 1 of the box instead of <code>pushObject</code> into the full list, and add it to the chart options. Editing keeps the current page.</li><li>Mirage: make the milestone handler page with <code>meta.links.next</code> like the idea handler (<code>mirage/helpers/paginate.js</code>), if it doesn't already.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>With 9 milestones, opening the dashboard requests only 5 for the box (<code>limit: 5</code>). The footer shows <code>1-5 / 5+</code>, ‹ is disabled, and › requests page 2 and shows <code>6-9 / 9</code> with › disabled.</li><li>With 5 or fewer milestones there is no pager. With none, the empty state shows.</li><li>Each row's issue count and progress match today's values. The edit pencil and the milestone links work on every page.</li><li>The estimated-vs-spent dropdown still lists every milestone, and the chart shows the selected milestone's issues.</li><li>Adding a milestone shows page 1 again with the new milestone counted. A failed page load shows the error and retry, and the arrows are disabled while a page loads.</li><li>Tests: acceptance or integration tests on Mirage covering the first page request, next and last page, no pager at ≤5, the chart dropdown with more than 5 milestones, and a failed page load. Each test fails if its line is reverted.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: no longer loading every issue on the dashboard (totals, charts and counts still use it), server-side issue counts per milestone, and a page-size selector.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["milestones-paginated"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-12 09:24:06	2026-11-12 09:25:55	f
33887ba06aec-7eb6-a4ea-22cce576feb2	c433e6f16aec-d3c1-a4ea-f400133f2b79	1	{"summary": "One Prometheus issue: the header's quick-create (\\"New\\") dropdown shows the module's nav-menu icon before each entry (Issue, Conversation, Project). The button caret's icon styling is scoped so it no longer applies to the new icons. No shading or other visual changes.", "issues": [{"key": "quick-create-icons", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Header quick create: show module icons before the entry names", "description": "<p>The \\"New\\" quick-create dropdown in the header lists only module names. To match the navigation menu, each entry should show its module icon before the name. The attached screen <code>quick-create-icons</code> shows the result. Keep the dropdown's current look; only the icons are new.</p><ul><li><strong>Template</strong> <code>app/components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs</code> (~l.30-39): in each <code>LinkTo</code> inside <code>div.create-module-dropdown-content</code>, add a Font Awesome 4 icon before the label: <code>&lt;i class=\\"fa fa-fw fa-tasks\\"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;</code> for Issue, <code>fa-comments</code> for Conversation, <code>fa-briefcase</code> for Project. These are the icons the nav menu uses in <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> (<code>views.Navigation.items</code>). <code>fa-fw</code> keeps the labels lined up. Leave the disabled (<code>pointer-none</code>) state without a project as it is; the icon follows the link's muted colour.</li><li><strong>Styles</strong> <code>app/styles/modules/header.scss</code>: the dropdown sits inside <code>button.create-module-btn</code>, so the rule <code>.create-module-btn i</code> (margin-left 0.5rem, font-size 1.2rem) would also hit the new icons. Scope it to the caret (e.g. <code>&gt; i.fa-caret-down</code>). If needed, add a small right margin for the icons inside <code>.create-module-dropdown-content a</code>. No new colours, shadows or border-radius (design-system.md).</li><li><strong>Test</strong> <code>tests/integration/components/app-layouts/application-header-test.js</code>: when the dropdown is open, each entry renders its icon (<code>fa-tasks</code>, <code>fa-comments</code>, <code>fa-briefcase</code>) before the translated label.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Opening \\"New\\" shows Issue, Conversation and Project, each with its nav-menu icon before the name, with the labels lined up.</li><li>The caret on the \\"New\\" button looks the same as before.</li><li>Hover (crimson background, white text) and the disabled state without a project still work, and the icon follows the text colour.</li><li>The integration test passes; lint is clean.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing the dropdown's shading, borders or separators; adding new entries (e.g. Idea); building the entries from metadata.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-create-icons"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-05 16:09:23	2026-11-05 16:09:23	f
9bb6ebf26aec-7eb6-459b-f9bc5f300e2a	c433e6f16aec-d3c1-a4ea-f400133f2b79	2	{"summary": "One Prometheus issue: the header's quick-create (\\"New\\") dropdown shows the module's nav-menu icon before each entry (Issue, Conversation, Project). The button caret's icon styling is scoped so it no longer applies to the new icons. No shading or other visual changes.", "issues": [{"key": "quick-create-icons", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Header quick create: show module icons before the entry names", "description": "<p>The \\"New\\" quick-create dropdown in the header lists only module names. To match the navigation menu, each entry should show its module icon before the name. The attached screen <code>quick-create-icons</code> shows the result. Keep the dropdown's current look; only the icons are new.</p><ul><li><strong>Template</strong> <code>app/components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs</code> (~l.30-39): in each <code>LinkTo</code> inside <code>div.create-module-dropdown-content</code>, add a Font Awesome 4 icon before the label: <code>&lt;i class=\\"fa fa-fw fa-tasks\\"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;</code> for Issue, <code>fa-comments</code> for Conversation, <code>fa-briefcase</code> for Project. These are the icons the nav menu uses in <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> (<code>views.Navigation.items</code>). <code>fa-fw</code> keeps the labels lined up. Leave the disabled (<code>pointer-none</code>) state without a project as it is; the icon follows the link's muted colour.</li><li><strong>Styles</strong> <code>app/styles/modules/header.scss</code>: the dropdown sits inside <code>button.create-module-btn</code>, so the rule <code>.create-module-btn i</code> (margin-left 0.5rem, font-size 1.2rem) would also hit the new icons. Scope it to the caret (e.g. <code>&gt; i.fa-caret-down</code>). If needed, add a small right margin for the icons inside <code>.create-module-dropdown-content a</code>. No new colours, shadows or border-radius (design-system.md).</li><li><strong>Test</strong> <code>tests/integration/components/app-layouts/application-header-test.js</code>: when the dropdown is open, each entry renders its icon (<code>fa-tasks</code>, <code>fa-comments</code>, <code>fa-briefcase</code>) before the translated label.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Opening \\"New\\" shows Issue, Conversation and Project, each with its nav-menu icon before the name, with the labels lined up.</li><li>The caret on the \\"New\\" button looks the same as before.</li><li>Hover (crimson background, white text) and the disabled state without a project still work, and the icon follows the text colour.</li><li>The integration test passes; lint is clean.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing the dropdown's shading, borders or separators; adding new entries (e.g. Idea); building the entries from metadata.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-create-icons"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-05 16:11:07	2026-11-05 16:11:49	f
6e7c3bc66aee-bd4d-6d43-e693c55b93b7	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	1	{"summary": "A native, page-independent query builder for Prometheus (phase 1: the component and its logic, no page uses it yet). The text chain is the query model (tree, one operator registry, schema helpers, Gaia serializer, composer), then the parser (loose text and Gaia wire format into the tree, with errors and positions, plus round trips of the board, Gantt and saved-search queries), then the completer, then the SearchBar. The builder chain is the model, then the Issue and Project schemas with the query-schema service, then the type-aware ValueEditor, then the Panel (groups and conditions). Last, Query::Builder ties the two editors to one tracked tree with the toolbar and the public API. Everything is tested with unit and integration tests; the old jQuery builder and the pages are not touched.", "issues": [{"key": "query-model", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Query: tree model, operator registry, schema helpers and Gaia serializer", "description": "<p>First step in replacing jQuery QueryBuilder with a native query builder. The query is one tree (groups and conditions) edited by a search bar and a visual builder; this issue adds the pure model and the serializer to Gaia's existing wire format, for example <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND (Issue.status !: done))</code>. The wire format, saved searches and the API do not change. No component or page changes; leave <code>utils/query/parser.js</code>, <code>utils/query/builder.js</code> and <code>utils/metadata/querybuilder-operators.js</code> alone (they are removed in a later phase).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/query/ast.js</code>: node factories <code>group(conjunction 'AND'|'OR', children)</code> and <code>condition(field, operator, value)</code>. <code>value</code> is a string, an array for IN, <code>[from, to]</code> for BETWEEN, or null for nullary operators. Each node gets a stable <code>id</code> for UI keys. Immutable helpers: add, replace, remove and move a node, set a conjunction, <code>isComplete(condition)</code>, and <code>normalize(tree)</code>, which merges nested groups that have the same conjunction, unwraps one-child groups and drops empty ones.</li><li><code>app/utils/query/operators.js</code>: ONE registry. Each entry has a key, the Gaia symbol, the text aliases accepted when typing, a translation key for its label, arity (0, 1, 2 or n) and the field types it applies to (text, number, enum, user, date). It covers all Gaia operators: <code>: !: &lt; &lt;: &gt; &gt;: CONTAINS !CONTAINS STARTS !STARTS ENDS !ENDS BETWEEN !BETWEEN NULL !NULL EMPTY !EMPTY</code>, plus IN and NOT IN. Text aliases: <code>= != &gt;= &lt;= ~ IN</code>, case-insensitive. Lookup helpers: by symbol, by alias, valid for a type, and the default operator for a type.</li><li><code>app/utils/query/schema.js</code>: <code>createSchema({module, fields, textField, values})</code>. A field is <code>{id, aliases, labelKey, type, valueSource}</code>. The helpers resolve a field from its id, alias or label (case-insensitive; a unique prefix also matches) and resolve a value for enum and user fields (exact match first, then a unique prefix gives the stored value; an ambiguous prefix returns the candidates). Pure: values are passed in, nothing is loaded here.</li><li><code>app/utils/query/serializer.js</code>: <code>serialize(tree)</code> returns <code>{query, errors}</code> and never throws. Rules:<ul><li>Every group is in brackets, with one conjunction per group; normalize first. Incomplete conditions are left out, and an empty tree gives an empty string.</li><li>IN is written as <code>CONTAINS 'a','b'</code> and NOT IN as <code>!CONTAINS 'a','b'</code>; a one-value IN or NOT IN is written as <code>:</code> or <code>!:</code>.</li><li>BETWEEN is written as <code>BETWEEN a AND b</code>; values with spaces are quoted with <code>'</code>.</li><li>Single spaces between field, operator and value.</li><li>It refuses, with an error code and the node id, values that contain <code>(</code>, <code>)</code> or <code>'</code> (Gaia's <code>core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php</code> concatenates values into SQL) and values that contain uppercase <code>NULL</code> or <code>EMPTY</code> (Clause.php ~l.159 then parses the leaf as a nullary operator).</li></ul></li><li><code>app/utils/query/composer.js</code>: <code>compose(baseTree, userTree)</code> returns an AND of both, normalized. Boards use it in a later phase.</li><li>Errors are <code>{code, params, nodeId?}</code> objects with no intl inside the utils. Add the English messages and the operator labels to <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.query.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests for ast (helpers, normalize), operators (alias and symbol lookups, types), schema (alias, label and prefix resolution, ambiguous prefixes), serializer (every rule above, including the one-value IN, the nested merge and each refusal) and composer.</li><li>The serializer output for <code>group(AND,[priority:High, group(OR,[type:Bug,type:Story])])</code> is <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND ((issuetype.name : Bug) OR (issuetype.name : Story)))</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> parsing text, real schemas, components, and the Gaia escaping fix (planned in the Issue list phase).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "query-parser", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Query: lexer and parser for loose text and Gaia format, with round-trip tests", "description": "<p>The native query builder's search bar lets people type loosely and formats the query on Enter. This issue turns text (loose input or Gaia's wire format from saved searches and <code>?query=</code> URLs) into the query tree from the query-model issue, with plain errors that carry positions. Pure utils only; the old <code>app/utils/query/parser.js</code> stays where it is.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/query/lexer.js</code>: tokens with <code>start</code>/<code>end</code> and a kind: field, operator, value, quoted value, comma, and/or keyword, bracket, bare word. Quotes may be <code>'</code> or <code>\\"</code>, and quoted text may contain spaces and and/or. The SearchBar reuses the tokens to colour the query, so keep the kinds stable.</li><li><code>app/utils/query/parser.js</code> (new file, same folder as the old one is fine because the old one is the default export of <code>utils/query/parser.js</code>; name it <code>parse.js</code> if the names clash): <code>parse(text, schema)</code> returns <code>{tree, errors}</code>, using <code>createSchema</code> from the query-model issue. Grammar:<ul><li>Brackets nest groups, and redundant brackets are allowed.</li><li>AND/OR in any case. AND is implied between conditions, and AND binds tighter than OR when they are mixed without brackets.</li><li>Inside a bracketed leaf the value runs to the closing bracket and is trimmed (Gaia wire format, e.g. <code>(assignedTo.name : Hammad Hassan)</code>, <code>(Issue.milestoneId : 5 )</code>). Outside brackets a value is one word unless quoted.</li><li>Comma lists after IN or CONTAINS; <code>BETWEEN a AND b</code>; NULL and EMPTY take no value.</li><li>Consecutive bare words become one <code>textField CONTAINS 'phrase'</code> condition.</li></ul></li><li>Binding through the schema:<ul><li>A field is matched by its id, alias, label or a unique prefix.</li><li>The operator must be valid for the field type.</li><li>Enum and user values are resolved to the stored value (exact first, then a unique prefix).</li><li>Dates accept <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>, <code>MM/DD/YYYY</code> and <code>today</code>, and are always output as <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>.</li><li>Unknown <code>Module.field</code> ids from old saved searches still parse as text fields.</li></ul></li><li>Error codes with params and positions: missing operator (\\"Choose an operator after Priority\\"), missing value, unknown field, unknown value with the allowed choices (\\"'zzz' isn't a Status. Pick one of: …\\"), ambiguous value, operator not valid for the type, bad date, BETWEEN needs two values, unbalanced bracket. Add their English messages to <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.query.errors.*</code>.</li><li><code>tests/helpers/query-schema.js</code>: a fixture Issue schema (priority, status, type, milestone, assignee, start date, subject) with static values, reused by later issues.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (unit tests)</p><ul><li>The loose examples serialize exactly:<ul><li><code>priority:high</code> gives <code>(Issue.priority : High)</code>.</li><li><code>prio = hi status != done</code> gives <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND (Issue.status !: done))</code>.</li><li><code>assignee in rana, hammad</code> gives <code>(assignedTo.name CONTAINS 'Rana Nouman','Hammad Hassan')</code>.</li><li><code>timezone</code> gives <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS timezone)</code>.</li><li><code>start between 05/01/2026 and 2026-08-31</code> gives <code>(Issue.startDate BETWEEN 2026-05-01 AND 2026-08-31)</code>.</li><li><code>(type:bug OR type:story) milestone:v0.1.1</code> gives <code>(((issuetype.name : Bug) OR (issuetype.name : Story)) AND (issuemilestone.name : v0.1.1))</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Round trip: for every query built in <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code> (l.58, 71, 77, 83, 90-97, 140, 161, 166) and <code>gantt.js</code> (l.59, 76-78), the header search query in <code>components/app-layouts/application-header.js</code>, and saved-search formats produced by the jQuery builder (equal, not_equal and contains on strings; date comparisons and BETWEEN; nested groups), <code>parse(serialize(parse(q)))</code> deep-equals <code>parse(q)</code> and serializing again is stable.</li><li>Each error code is tested with its position.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> suggestions, components, removing the old parser.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["query-model"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "query-schemas", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Query: Issue and Project schemas and the query-schema service", "description": "<p>The native query builder needs to know, per module, which fields can be queried, their types and their values. Today that lives in each controller's <code>metadata.filters</code> in the jQuery plugin's format (<code>controllers/app/project/issue/index.js:35-144</code>, <code>controllers/app/projects/index.js:30</code>). This issue moves it into schemas built with <code>createSchema</code> (query-model issue) and a service that loads the values. No page uses it yet, and the controllers stay as they are.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/query/schemas/issue.js</code>: the same field ids as today's Issue filters:<ul><li><code>Issue.issueNumber</code> and <code>parentissue.issueNumber</code> are number fields.</li><li><code>Issue.subject</code> is the text field.</li><li><code>Issue.status</code>, <code>issuemilestone.name</code>, <code>issuetype.name</code> and <code>Issue.priority</code> are enum fields.</li><li><code>Issue.startDate</code> and <code>Issue.endDate</code> are dates.</li><li><code>assignedTo.name</code>, <code>ownedBy.name</code> and <code>reportedBy.name</code> are user fields.</li><li>Aliases: number/#, subject, status, milestone, type, priority/prio, start, end, parent, assignee, owner, reporter.</li><li>Labels use the existing <code>views.app.issue.fields.*</code> keys.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/utils/query/schemas/project.js</code>: <code>Project.name</code> (the text field), <code>Project.shortCode</code>, <code>Project.status</code> and <code>manager.name</code>, matching today's projects filters.</li><li><code>app/services/query-schema.js</code>: <code>load(module, {projectId})</code> returns a Promise of a schema with its values loaded in parallel through the store, using the same stored values as today:<ul><li>status by name (as <code>statusOptionsByName</code>, issue statuses of the project);</li><li>milestone names of the project;</li><li>issue type names;</li><li>priority from <code>views.app.issue.lists.priority</code>;</li><li>member names, carrying each user's id and profile picture for avatars.</li></ul>Values are cached per module and project; callers check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after awaiting.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests: each schema resolves its aliases and labels, and the service returns the loaded values from Mirage (add handlers only where missing) and caches per project.</li><li>The <code>parse</code> fixture examples also pass against the real Issue schema with Mirage data.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> schemas for other modules, changing the controllers.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["query-model"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "query-completer", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Query: completer for search bar suggestions", "description": "<p>The native query search bar shows a suggestion menu while typing. This issue adds the pure logic behind it: given the text, the cursor and a schema, what comes next and what to suggest. No UI.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/query/completer.js</code>: <code>complete(text, cursor, schema)</code> returns <code>{context, replaceStart, replaceEnd, suggestions}</code>. Context is field, operator, value or connector; built on the lexer from the parser issue.</li><li>Order of suggestions by context:<ul><li>At a field: fields, plus a \\"Search &lt;text field label&gt; for '&lt;word&gt;'\\" item.</li><li>After a field: only the operators valid for its type (registry from the query-model issue).</li><li>After an operator: the field's values (enum order, users alphabetical, <code>today</code> for dates; inside quotes too).</li><li>After a complete condition: AND, OR, and <code>)</code> only when a bracket is open.</li></ul></li><li>Each suggestion is <code>{kind, label (translation key or text), insert, detail (e.g. the field id)}</code>, and accepting one replaces <code>replaceStart..replaceEnd</code>.</li><li>Ranking: exact match, then label prefix, then alias or id prefix, then word start inside the label, then substring; ties keep schema order. At most 8 items.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests with the fixture schema (<code>tests/helpers/query-schema.js</code>):<ul><li><code>prio|</code> gives Priority first.</li><li><code>priority |</code> gives the enum operators only.</li><li><code>priority = h|</code> gives High.</li><li><code>start between 2026-05-01 and |</code> gives date values.</li><li><code>(type:bug |</code> gives AND, OR and <code>)</code>.</li><li><code>status:new |</code> gives AND and OR without <code>)</code>.</li><li>A cursor in the middle of the text replaces the right range.</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> recent or saved queries as suggestions.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["query-parser"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "query-search-bar", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Query::SearchBar: typed queries with suggestions, formatting and errors", "description": "<p>The native query builder's text editor. Today the Issue list search input is readonly and only opens the jQuery panel. This component lets people type a loose query that is formatted into Gaia's exact format. It is standalone: <code>&lt;Query::SearchBar @tree @schema @placeholder @onChange @onRun /&gt;</code>. The <code>Query::Builder</code> container (later issue) keeps it in sync with the visual builder, and no page uses it yet. The name <code>Query::*</code> is used because the classic <code>QueryBuilder</code> component still exists.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/query/search-bar.{js,hbs}</code> (Glimmer):<ul><li>Uses <code>FormFields::FieldText</code> (modifiers through <code>...attributes</code> for keydown and the caret position) and holds the draft text while editing.</li><li>On Enter (menu closed) or blur, <code>parse</code> against <code>@schema</code>. If it parses, call <code>@onChange(tree)</code> and replace the text with <code>serialize(tree)</code>, which uses exact ids such as <code>Issue.priority</code>, not labels. Enter also calls <code>@onRun()</code>.</li><li>When there are errors, show the translated message with its position under the input (<code>span.error.text-red</code>, see screen <code>bar-error</code>), keep the text, and never call <code>@onChange</code> or <code>@onRun</code>.</li><li>When <code>@tree</code> changes from outside while not editing, show <code>serialize(@tree)</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Suggestion menu from <code>complete()</code> (completer issue): a Bootstrap <code>dropdown-menu</code> under the input with section headers and key hints (screen <code>toolbar-typing</code>). Up and Down move, Tab or Enter accept, Enter with the menu closed runs, Esc closes. Keep the menu open while typing and close it on blur.</li><li><code>app/components/query/query-text.{js,hbs}</code>: shows the formatted query when the bar is not focused, with fields, operators and and/or keywords coloured from lexer tokens. Render plain text in spans, never <code>htmlSafe</code>. Clicking it focuses the input.</li><li><code>app/styles/components/query-search-bar.scss</code>, imported in <code>app/styles/app.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.query-search-bar</code>. Colours are <code>$secondaryColor</code> for fields, <code>$primaryColor</code> for operators and <code>$highlightColor</code> for keywords; square edges. It is a separate file so the Panel PR doesn't conflict.</li><li>Strings (menu headers, hints) go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.query.searchBar.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests with the fixture schema)</p><ul><li>Typing <code>prio = hi status != done</code> and pressing Enter calls <code>@onChange</code> and <code>@onRun</code> and shows <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND (Issue.status !: done))</code>.</li><li>Typing <code>prio</code> opens the menu with Priority highlighted; Tab inserts it.</li><li>Arrow keys and Esc behave as described.</li><li><code>status:zzz</code> shows the unknown-value error and calls nothing.</li><li>An outside <code>@tree</code> change updates the text.</li><li>Coloured tokens are rendered as text, not HTML.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the toolbar (Saved Searches, Builder, Search, Clear), page integration.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["query-completer"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["toolbar-typing", "bar-error"]}, {"key": "query-value-editor", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Query::ValueEditor: value input by field type and operator", "description": "<p>The visual query builder needs a value input that matches the condition's field type and operator. This standalone component is used by <code>Query::Condition</code> in the Panel issue. No page uses it yet.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/query/value-editor.{js,hbs}</code>: <code>&lt;Query::ValueEditor @field @operator @value @onChange /&gt;</code>, where <code>@field</code> is a schema field with its values (query-schemas issue) and <code>@operator</code> is a registry entry (query-model issue). The input by type and operator:<ul><li>Enum fields: <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> (<code>@relateType=\\"relate-simple\\"</code>).</li><li>User fields: the same, with avatars as in the existing user selects.</li><li>IN and NOT IN: <code>FormFields::FieldMultiSelect</code> (or <code>FieldRelateMulti</code>, whichever the forms use for static options), giving an array.</li><li>Dates: <code>FormFields::FieldDate</code>, and two of them with a translated \\"and\\" for BETWEEN. The output is always <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>.</li><li>Text and number fields: <code>FormFields::FieldText</code>.</li><li>Operators with arity 0 (NULL, EMPTY): no input.</li></ul></li><li><code>@onChange(value)</code> passes values in the shape <code>ast.condition</code> expects (string, array, or [from, to]). It never mutates <code>@value</code>.</li><li>Placeholders go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.query.valueEditor.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>Each type and operator combination renders the right control and emits the right value shape.</li><li>A date picked through FieldDate is emitted as <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>.</li><li>Switching the operator from <code>:</code> to IN turns a single value into a one-item array.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> rows, groups, the panel.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["query-schemas"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["builder-open"]}, {"key": "query-panel", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Query::Panel: visual builder with groups and conditions", "description": "<p>The visual editor of the native query builder: nested groups with an AND/OR switch and rows of field / operator / value. It is standalone: <code>&lt;Query::Panel @tree @schema @onChange /&gt;</code>. The <code>Query::Builder</code> container (later issue) keeps it in sync with the search bar, opens it inline under the bar and adds Save Search. No page uses it yet.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/query/panel.{js,hbs}</code>: renders the root group; an empty tree shows one empty AND group.</li><li><code>app/components/query/group.{js,hbs}</code>:<ul><li>A bordered block with a crimson (<code>$primaryColor</code>) left edge for AND and a plum (<code>$highlightColor</code>) one for OR.</li><li>The header has an AND/OR <code>btn-group btn-xs</code> switch, \\"Condition\\" and \\"Group\\" buttons, and a remove button (not on the root).</li><li>Groups nest to any depth.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/components/query/condition.{js,hbs}</code>:<ul><li>A row with the field (<code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> over the schema fields by label), the operator (<code>FieldRelate</code> over the operators valid for the field type), <code>Query::ValueEditor</code> and a remove <code>btn-box-tool</code>.</li><li>Changing the field resets the operator to the type's default and clears an incompatible value.</li><li>An incomplete row stays in the tree, shows a muted \\"Incomplete: left out of the query\\" note, and is skipped by the serializer.</li><li>Serializer refusals for the row (brackets, apostrophes, NULL/EMPTY) show under it.</li></ul></li><li>All changes go through the immutable helpers in <code>app/utils/query/ast.js</code> and come out as <code>@onChange(newTree)</code>; the components never mutate <code>@tree</code>.</li><li><code>app/styles/components/query-panel.scss</code>, imported in <code>app/styles/app.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.query-panel</code>. Square edges, existing tokens only, no shadows. Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.query.panel.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>The tree from screen <code>builder-open</code> renders: an AND group with status IN, start date BETWEEN, one incomplete assignee row and a nested OR group with two type rows.</li><li>Toggling AND/OR, adding and removing conditions and groups, and changing the field each emit the expected tree.</li><li>The incomplete row is kept in the tree and absent from <code>serialize</code>.</li><li>A value with <code>(</code> shows the refusal message.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> drag and drop of rows, the toolbar, page integration.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["query-value-editor"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["builder-open"]}, {"key": "query-builder-container", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Query::Builder: one tree for search bar and panel, toolbar and public API", "description": "<p>Ties the native query builder together: one query tree as tracked state, edited live by <code>Query::SearchBar</code> and <code>Query::Panel</code>, with the list toolbar around them. This is the component pages will use from the next phase: <code>&lt;Query::Builder @schema @query @baseQuery @savedSearches @onApply @onSave @aclContext /&gt;</code>. No page uses it in this issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/query/builder.{js,hbs}</code> (Glimmer):<ul><li><code>@tracked tree</code>, parsed from <code>@query</code> (the Gaia string) when it changes. If a stored query fails to parse, its errors are shown under the bar.</li><li>SearchBar and Panel both get <code>tree</code> and both update it through <code>onChange</code>, so they stay in sync live.</li><li>Check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after every await.</li></ul></li><li>Toolbar, in the existing <code>.search</code> layout (screens <code>toolbar-typing</code>, <code>builder-open</code>):<ul><li>Saved Searches <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> over <code>@savedSearches</code> (<code>{name, query}</code>): picking one loads its query into the tree and marks it active with <code>fa-check</code>.</li><li>Then the SearchBar.</li><li>A Builder <code>btn-default</code> (<code>fa-sliders</code>, <code>active</code> while open) that toggles the Panel inline under the bar, closed by default.</li><li>Search (<code>AppUi::Button btn-primary</code>, <code>@aclContext</code>), disabled while the bar has errors.</li><li>Clear, which empties the tree and applies.</li></ul></li><li>Applying (Search, or Enter in the bar) calls <code>@onApply(queryString)</code>. The query string is <code>serialize(compose(parse(@baseQuery), tree))</code>; <code>@baseQuery</code> is never shown in the bar or panel. Nothing is applied when serializing gives errors.</li><li>When <code>@onSave</code> is given, a Save Search <code>btn-primary</code> at the bottom right of the open panel calls <code>@onSave(serialize(tree))</code>. The page owns the save dialog.</li><li>Labels: reuse <code>global.form.search</code>, <code>global.form.clear</code>, <code>global.form.savesearch</code> and <code>views.app.issue.list.savedsearch.label</code>, and add <code>components.query.builder.toggle</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>Typing in the bar updates the open panel, and editing the panel updates the bar text.</li><li><code>@query</code> in Gaia format loads into both.</li><li>Choosing a saved search loads it.</li><li>Search calls <code>@onApply</code> with the base query ANDed in.</li><li>Clear empties both editors and applies the base query only.</li><li>An invalid bar disables Search.</li><li>Builder toggles the panel; Save Search appears only with <code>@onSave</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> using it on the Issue list or other views, removing jQuery QueryBuilder (next phases).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["query-search-bar", "query-panel"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["toolbar-typing", "builder-open", "bar-error"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-06 21:15:26	2026-11-06 21:15:26	f
1e0083526aee-63af-5ba1-db77a2a27f51	d87ad5636ae5-1449-ae8f-5808a9dddbf1	5	{"summary": "Fix the endless reload of images pasted into idea messages. render-markdown re-runs because the image lookup it starts inside its tracked run changes store data the modifier depends on, so each run starts another. Make the modifier read only its argument, skip unchanged text and resolve each image once.", "issues": [{"key": "inline-image-loop", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea messages: pasted images reload forever because render-markdown re-runs on its own store query", "description": "<p>When a user pastes an image into the idea composer, it is uploaded and stored in the message as <code>![name](upload:&lt;id&gt;)</code> (aprom-4114). In the thread the message never settles. The image request succeeds, but the message keeps re-rendering and requesting the image again.</p><p><strong>Likely cause (confirm first):</strong> <code>modifiers/render-markdown.js</code> is a classic ember-modifier. Its <code>didReceiveArguments</code> runs inside autotracking and synchronously calls <code>showImages</code>, which calls <code>uploadPreview.previewUrl</code>. That runs <code>store.query('upload', { id, download: true })</code> (<code>services/upload-preview.js</code>). Store state read there seems to become a dependency of the modifier, and the query result changes it. The modifier then re-runs, mints a new single-use download token, calls <code>viewer.setMarkdown</code> again (re-rendering the message and reloading the image), and repeats. Verify this with a counter or a breakpoint before fixing; if the cause is different, say so in the issue.</p><ul><li>Start with a failing integration test: render a message body with one <code>upload:</code> image (Mirage upload and download token). Assert that the preview address is requested once, and the image is shown once, after settling.</li><li>In <code>didReceiveArguments</code>, read only the positional argument. Do nothing when the markdown equals the one already shown. Start the image lookup outside the tracking frame, e.g. after an <code>await Promise.resolve()</code> or a scheduled task, so nothing it reads becomes a dependency.</li><li>Keep the resolved address per upload id for the modifier's lifetime, so a later run with the same image doesn't fetch a new token or redraw the image. Tokens are single-use, so a redrawn <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> pointing at a used address gets a 404.</li><li>Keep the existing behaviour: the image name shows first, the image replaces it once resolved, an unreadable upload stays as its name, a click opens the full size, and the stale-markdown check stays. Clean up on <code>willRemove</code>.</li><li>Check that the composer preview and the create page's first message (both render markdown) don't loop either.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a message with a pasted image shows the image once and stays still. The network tab shows one token request and one image request per image, and no repeating requests while the page is idle. The ember suite passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> opening pasted images in the preview modal instead of a new tab, migrating the modifier to the ember-modifier 4 API, and Gaia changes.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 07:32:46	2026-11-07 07:36:03	f
542e0e276aee-41e5-0b34-cf4c4ab70fb7	f1592e496aee-cb3c-b49a-239fcfcb2381	2	{"summary": "With CodeRabbit's auto review turned off, our tools ask for every review themselves. A shared counter with a tier policy (rabbit-request) decides who reviews each PR: under 10 reviews in the last 24 hours CodeRabbit reviews everything, from 10 to 24 only large PRs, from 25 on everything goes to the human reviewer. It posts the trigger and records it. ai ship (ship-gate), the Talos fix-round loop (loop-gate) and Agamemnon's branch updates and conflict fixes (aga-gate) all go through it and hand the issue to the reviewer when it answers human. Agamemnon's sweep then sends PRs that went to the reviewer because of the limit to CodeRabbit once there is credit again (aga-backlog).", "issues": [{"key": "rabbit-request", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "ai rabbit request: daily CodeRabbit counter with a tier policy that posts the review trigger", "description": "<p>CodeRabbit includes about 26 PR reviews a day; after that it charges per file. Its auto review is turned off, so our tools now ask for every review by posting a trigger comment. This issue adds the one place that decides whether a PR goes to CodeRabbit or to the human reviewer, posts the trigger and counts it.</p><ul><li>New <code>ai/lib/rabbitbudget.py</code>: a ledger in <code>STATE_DIR</code> (<code>ai/lib/common.py</code>; under <code>LOCAL_DIR</code>, so the runtime copy and the checkout share it). Two lists: <code>sent</code> <code>{at (UTC ISO), repo, pr, sha, source}</code> and <code>deferred</code> <code>{at, repo, pr, issue, files}</code> (PRs that went to the human because of the limit). Writes are atomic and safe across processes (lock file plus write-to-temp-then-replace). Prune <code>sent</code> entries older than 48 hours.</li><li>Policy, a pure function of (used in the rolling last 24 hours, hand-written file count, rereview flag, settings): <code>used &lt; everyPrUntil</code> → coderabbit; <code>used &lt; limit</code> → coderabbit when <code>rereview</code> or <code>files &gt;= largePrFiles</code>, else human; otherwise human.</li><li>Settings in <code>ai/config.json</code>: <code>codeRabbitBudget: {everyPrUntil: 10, limit: 25, largePrFiles: 6}</code> and <code>codeRabbitTrigger: \\"@coderabbitai full review always\\"</code>. A missing <code>codeRabbitBudget</code> means no limit.</li><li><code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source pr-opened|bot-round|reenter|update-branch|conflict|backlog [--files N] [--rereview] [--issue N] [--json]</code>. For a repo where <code>coderabbit.enabled(repo)</code> is false it answers <code>absent</code>. It applies the policy. On coderabbit, it posts the trigger as Agent Odysseus (<code>ody(repo, 'gh', 'pr', 'comment', ...)</code>), records it in <code>sent</code> with the head sha, and drops any <code>deferred</code> entry for the PR. On human, it adds a <code>deferred</code> entry (only when <code>--issue</code> is given; one per PR). It prints, or returns as JSON, <code>{decision: coderabbit|human|absent, used, limit, reason}</code>. A failed comment means the decision is human, with the error in <code>reason</code>; nothing is recorded in <code>sent</code>.</li><li><code>ai rabbit budget [--json]</code>: used, limit, the current tier, when the next slot frees up, and the deferred list.</li><li>Unit tests (ody mocked): every tier boundary (9/10, 24/25), large vs small, rereview in the middle tier, rolling window, deferred added and cleared, failed comment, disabled repo.</li><li>Document both commands and the settings in <code>ai/README.md</code> (CodeRabbit section).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>ai rabbit request</code> posts exactly one trigger comment when the policy says coderabbit and records it; <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code> reports the rolling count and the deferred PRs; <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the callers (ai ship, Talos, Agamemnon: separate issues); counting reviews people trigger by hand on GitHub.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ship-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "ai ship: ask ai rabbit request who reviews a new PR, hand it to the reviewer when it answers human", "description": "<p>CodeRabbit's auto review is off, so a new agent PR only gets a CodeRabbit review when <code>ai ship</code> asks for one. Depending on the daily count and the PR's size, the answer may be the human reviewer instead.</p><ul><li>In <code>ai/lib/ship.py</code> <code>cmd_ship</code>, after the PR is open (~l.195-200, where <code>defer</code> is decided today): for a CodeRabbit repo, call the <code>rabbitbudget</code> request logic with <code>source pr-opened</code>, <code>files</code> = the hand-written count <code>sizecheck.check</code> already returned, and the issue number.</li><li>On coderabbit: defer the hand-off as today (the issue stays in progress for the Talos loop).</li><li>On human: don't defer. <code>pr_hand_off</code> sets in_review and assigns the reviewer. Add to the tracker notes: <em>Not sent to CodeRabbit: N of 25 reviews used in the last 24 hours (small PRs go to you from 10). Please review by hand; CodeRabbit may add a review later when credit frees up.</em> Print that the session finishes as <code>done</code>, not <code>awaiting_bot_review</code> (like the existing branch for repos without CodeRabbit).</li><li>On resume, when <code>existing_pr</code> finds the PR, don't ask again if the pending hand-off or the ledger already has the PR.</li><li><code>ai pr</code> (<code>workflow.cmd_pr</code>) does the same, with the file count from the PR's changed files.</li><li>Check that Odysseus' ship prompt and role (<code>talos/agents/odysseus/</code>) follow the printed outcome; adjust the wording if needed.</li><li>Unit tests with the request logic mocked: coderabbit → deferred; human → handed off with the note; resume doesn't ask twice.</li><li>Update <code>ai/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with 12 reviews used, a 3-file gaia PR goes to the reviewer as in_review with the note and no trigger comment; an 8-file PR gets the trigger and stays with the agent.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fix rounds and Agamemnon (separate issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-request"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "loop-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos CodeRabbit loop: request a review after each fix round, hand off when the budget says human", "description": "<p>With CodeRabbit's auto review off, a fix round's push gets no review unless Talos asks for one, and the merge check needs a CodeRabbit result on the latest commit. Each follow-up review counts toward the daily limit.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/bot_review.py</code> <code>Watcher.check_one</code> (~l.204): when <code>next_step</code> returns RUN_ROUND, first read <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code> (through <code>talos/lib/ai_cli.py</code>, like <code>ai_rabbit</code>). If a follow-up review would be answered human (limit reached), don't run the round. Hand off to the reviewer (never the merger route) with the comment <em>CodeRabbit limit reached: open CodeRabbit findings left for you.</em></li><li>After a round ends with <code>awaiting_bot_review</code> (<code>dispatcher._await_bot_review</code> ~l.507, when rounds &gt; 0), call <code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source bot-round --rereview --issue N --json</code>. On human, hand off with the same note instead of waiting.</li><li><code>Watcher.reenter</code> (~l.157, after address-review in auto-merge milestones): call <code>ai rabbit request ... --source reenter --rereview</code>; on human, hand off to the reviewer instead of re-entering.</li><li>If the ai command fails, log it and hand off to the reviewer; don't wait for a review that was never requested.</li><li>Unit tests in <code>talos/tests/test_bot_review.py</code>: round skipped at the limit, request after a round, reenter to human, command failure.</li><li>Update the CodeRabbit loop section of the Talos README.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> each fix round's push gets exactly one trigger comment while under the limit; at the limit the issue goes to the reviewer as in_review with the note and no new commit.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the first review (ai ship), Agamemnon.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-request"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "aga-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon: request a CodeRabbit review after branch updates and conflict fixes, or hand the issue to the owner", "description": "<p>Agamemnon's keeper pushes new commits to agent PRs: it updates PRs that are behind their base and sends resolved conflicts back for review. With CodeRabbit's auto review off, those commits get no review unless asked for, and the merge check (<code>ai/lib/mergegate.py</code> <code>gate</code>) needs a CodeRabbit result on the latest commit. Agamemnon must spend reviews through the shared counter and know when the limit is reached.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/orchestrator/keeper.py</code> <code>_update</code> (~l.86): before the update-branch call, read <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code>; at the limit, skip the update (log once per PR per day). After a successful update, call <code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source update-branch --rereview --issue N</code>.</li><li><code>_conflict</code> / <code>_resolve</code> (~l.96-155): at the limit, don't resolve; hand the issue to the owner as in_review with <em>merge conflict, CodeRabbit limit reached: please resolve and review by hand.</em> After a resolution is pushed, call <code>ai rabbit request ... --source conflict --rereview</code>. On human, hand off with the same note.</li><li>The premise and role (<code>talos/agents/agamemnon/</code>): add the budget (tiers, that each push needs a trigger, what happens at the limit) where they describe updates, conflicts and merging.</li><li>An ai command failure means hand off to the owner, logged.</li><li>Unit tests (see <code>talos/tests/test_agamemnon_conflicts.py</code>): update skipped at the limit, request after update, conflict to the owner, request after resolution.</li><li>Update <code>agamemnon/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> at the limit, Agamemnon's sweep pushes nothing to agent PRs and conflicting PRs land with the owner with the note; under the limit, every push it makes is followed by one trigger comment.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> letting the merge check accept an earlier CodeRabbit pass after base-only merges; auto-merge itself (PRs that went to the human never come back clean).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-request"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "aga-backlog", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon: send PRs that went to the reviewer because of the limit to CodeRabbit once credit frees up", "description": "<p>When the daily CodeRabbit limit sends a PR to the human reviewer, it is recorded as deferred in the shared ledger. Once there is credit again, it should still get a CodeRabbit review to help the human; the issue stays with the human.</p><ul><li>In Agamemnon's sweep (<code>talos/lib/orchestrator/</code>, next to the keeper's sweep): read <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code>. For each deferred PR, oldest first, while the tier allows it (its stored file count against the tier, as for a new PR), call <code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source backlog --files N --issue N</code>. Stop at the first human answer.</li><li>Before sending, drop the entry without spending a review when the PR is closed or merged, or when the issue is no longer in_review.</li><li>Comment on the issue when a review was requested: <em>CodeRabbit review requested now that credit is available; the issue stays with you.</em> Don't reassign it or start the Talos loop.</li><li>Agamemnon role: mention the backlog sending.</li><li>Unit tests: oldest first, stops at the tier, closed/merged/moved PRs dropped, the comment.</li><li>Update <code>agamemnon/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after the 24-hour window frees slots, deferred PRs that fit the tier get a trigger comment, oldest first; their issues stay assigned to the reviewer.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> giving the issue back to the agent to answer CodeRabbit's findings; notifications.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-request", "ship-gate"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 10:24:20	2026-11-07 10:24:20	f
f501fad46aee-a9ea-e0b2-c359d0594351	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	2	{"summary": "ezSearch phase 1: a native, page-independent query builder for Prometheus, plus three Gaia requests that make Gaia's query parser safe and complete. Prometheus, text chain: query model (tree, operator registry, schema helpers, Gaia serializer, composer), then the parser (loose text and Gaia format into the tree; mixing AND and OR in a group without brackets is an error; a field without a module defaults to the current module), then the completer, then EzSearch::SearchBar. Prometheus, builder chain: model, then the Issue and Project schemas with the query-schema service, then EzSearch::ValueEditor, then EzSearch::Panel. <EzSearch> joins both chains with the toolbar and the public API. All UI works on mobile. Gaia, in order (same method): NULL/EMPTY recognised by the operator, then bound values and validated fields, then quote-aware leaf parsing. No page uses ezSearch yet, and jQuery QueryBuilder stays until the removal phase.", "issues": [{"key": "query-model", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: query tree model, operator registry, schema helpers and Gaia serializer", "description": "<p>First step of ezSearch, the native replacement for jQuery QueryBuilder. A query is one tree (groups and conditions) edited by a search bar and a visual builder. This issue adds the pure model and the serializer to Gaia's existing wire format, for example <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND (Issue.status !: done))</code>. The wire format, saved searches and the API do not change. There are no component or page changes. Leave <code>utils/query/parser.js</code>, <code>utils/query/builder.js</code> and <code>utils/metadata/querybuilder-operators.js</code> alone; they are removed in a later phase.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/query/ast.js</code>:<ul><li>Node factories <code>group(conjunction 'AND'|'OR', children)</code> and <code>condition(field, operator, value)</code>. <code>value</code> is a string, an array for IN, <code>[from, to]</code> for BETWEEN, or null for nullary operators.</li><li>Each node gets a stable <code>id</code> for UI keys.</li><li>Immutable helpers: add, replace, remove and move a node; set a conjunction; <code>isComplete(condition)</code>.</li><li><code>normalize(tree)</code> merges nested groups that have the same conjunction, unwraps one-child groups and drops empty ones. A group always has exactly one conjunction.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/utils/query/operators.js</code>: ONE registry. Each entry has:<ul><li>a key and the Gaia symbol;</li><li>the text aliases accepted when typing;</li><li>a translation key for its label;</li><li>its arity (0, 1, 2 or n);</li><li>the field types it applies to (text, number, enum, user, date).</li></ul>It covers all Gaia operators (<code>: !: &lt; &lt;: &gt; &gt;: CONTAINS !CONTAINS STARTS !STARTS ENDS !ENDS BETWEEN !BETWEEN NULL !NULL EMPTY !EMPTY</code>) plus IN and NOT IN. Text aliases: <code>= != &gt;= &lt;= ~ IN</code>, case-insensitive. Lookup helpers: by symbol, by alias, valid for a type, and the default operator for a type.</li><li><code>app/utils/query/schema.js</code>: <code>createSchema({module, fields, textField, values})</code>, where a field is <code>{id, aliases, labelKey, type, valueSource}</code>. Field resolution, case-insensitive, in this order:<ol><li>the id;</li><li>the id without its module prefix (<code>startdate</code> gives <code>Issue.startDate</code>);</li><li>an alias or the label;</li><li>a unique prefix of an alias or label.</li></ol>Otherwise a word without a module prefix defaults to <code>&lt;Module&gt;.&lt;word&gt;</code> as a text field, and an unknown <code>Module.field</code> is kept as a text field (so there is no unknown-field error). Value resolution for enum and user fields: an exact match first, then a unique prefix gives the stored value, and an ambiguous prefix returns the candidates. The module is pure: values are passed in, nothing is loaded here.</li><li><code>app/utils/query/serializer.js</code>: <code>serialize(tree)</code> returns <code>{query, errors}</code> and never throws. Rules:<ul><li>Every group and every condition is in brackets, with one conjunction per group (normalize first).</li><li>Incomplete conditions are left out, and an empty tree gives an empty string.</li><li>IN is written as <code>CONTAINS 'a','b'</code> and NOT IN as <code>!CONTAINS 'a','b'</code>; a one-value IN or NOT IN is written as <code>:</code> or <code>!:</code>.</li><li><code>BETWEEN a AND b</code>; values with spaces are quoted with <code>'</code>; single spaces between field, operator and value.</li><li>It refuses, with an error code and the node id, values that contain <code>(</code>, <code>)</code> or <code>'</code>, or uppercase <code>NULL</code> or <code>EMPTY</code>. Gaia's <code>core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php</code> can't handle these yet; the agaia requests in the same plan fix that, and this refusal is relaxed in a later phase.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/utils/query/composer.js</code>: <code>compose(baseTree, userTree)</code> returns an AND of both, normalized. Boards use it in a later phase.</li><li>Errors are <code>{code, params, nodeId?}</code> with no intl inside the utils. Add the English messages and the operator labels to <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (unit tests)</p><ul><li>ast (helpers, normalize), operators (alias and symbol lookups, types), schema (every resolution step, including the default-module rule and ambiguous prefixes), serializer (every rule, the one-value IN, the nested merge, each refusal) and composer.</li><li><code>group(AND,[priority:High, group(OR,[type:Bug,type:Story])])</code> serializes to <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND ((issuetype.name : Bug) OR (issuetype.name : Story)))</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> parsing text, real schemas, components.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "query-parser", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: lexer and parser for loose text and Gaia format, with round-trip tests", "description": "<p>The ezSearch bar lets people type loosely and formats the query on Enter. This issue turns text into the query tree from the query-model issue, with plain errors that carry positions. The text is either loose input or Gaia's wire format from saved searches and <code>?query=</code> URLs. Pure utils only; the old <code>app/utils/query/parser.js</code> stays untouched.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/query/lexer.js</code>: tokens with <code>start</code>/<code>end</code> and a kind (field, operator, value, quoted value, comma, and/or keyword, bracket, bare word). Quotes may be <code>'</code> or <code>\\"</code>, and quoted text may contain spaces and and/or. The SearchBar reuses the tokens to colour the query, so keep the kinds stable.</li><li><code>app/utils/query/parse.js</code> (a new name, because <code>parser.js</code> is the old one): <code>parse(text, schema)</code> returns <code>{tree, errors}</code>, using <code>createSchema</code> from the query-model issue. Grammar:<ul><li>Brackets nest groups, and redundant brackets are allowed.</li><li>AND/OR in any case, and AND is implied between conditions.</li><li><strong>Every group has one conjunction: mixing AND and OR in the same group without brackets is an error, never interpreted. An implied AND counts as AND.</strong></li><li>Inside a bracketed leaf the value runs to the closing bracket and is trimmed (Gaia wire format, e.g. <code>(assignedTo.name : Hammad Hassan)</code>, <code>(Issue.milestoneId : 5 )</code>). Outside brackets a value is one word unless quoted.</li><li>Comma lists after IN or CONTAINS; <code>BETWEEN a AND b</code>; NULL and EMPTY take no value.</li><li>Consecutive bare words become one <code>textField CONTAINS 'phrase'</code> condition.</li></ul></li><li>Binding through the schema:<ul><li>Fields resolve as in <code>schema.js</code>, including the default-module rule.</li><li>The operator must be valid for the field type.</li><li>Enum and user values resolve to the stored value (exact first, then a unique prefix).</li><li>Dates accept <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>, <code>MM/DD/YYYY</code> and <code>today</code>, and are output as <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Error codes with params and positions:<ul><li>missing operator (\\"Choose an operator after Priority\\") and missing value;</li><li>mixed AND/OR (\\"AND and OR can't be mixed in one group. Add brackets\\", at the second conjunction);</li><li>unknown value with the allowed choices (\\"'zzz' isn't a Status. Pick one of: …\\") and ambiguous value;</li><li>operator not valid for the type;</li><li>bad date, and BETWEEN needs two values;</li><li>unbalanced bracket.</li></ul>Add the English messages to <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.errors.*</code>.</li><li><code>tests/helpers/query-schema.js</code>: a fixture Issue schema (priority, status, type, milestone, assignee, start date, subject) with static values, reused by later issues.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (unit tests)</p><ul><li>These loose inputs serialize exactly:<ul><li><code>priority:high</code> gives <code>(Issue.priority : High)</code>.</li><li><code>prio = hi status != done</code> gives <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND (Issue.status !: done))</code>.</li><li><code>assignee in rana, hammad</code> gives <code>(assignedTo.name CONTAINS 'Rana Nouman','Hammad Hassan')</code>.</li><li><code>timezone</code> gives <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS timezone)</code>.</li><li><code>start between 05/01/2026 and 2026-08-31</code> gives <code>(Issue.startDate BETWEEN 2026-05-01 AND 2026-08-31)</code>.</li><li><code>(type:bug OR type:story) milestone:v0.1.1</code> gives <code>(((issuetype.name : Bug) OR (issuetype.name : Story)) AND (issuemilestone.name : v0.1.1))</code>.</li><li><code>description ~ crash</code> gives <code>(Issue.description CONTAINS crash)</code>.</li></ul></li><li><code>status:new or type:bug milestone:v0.1.1</code> gives the mixed error at the implied AND.</li><li>Round trip: <code>parse(serialize(parse(q)))</code> deep-equals <code>parse(q)</code>, and serializing again is stable, for:<ul><li>every query built in <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code> (l.58, 71, 77, 83, 90-97, 140, 161, 166) and <code>gantt.js</code> (l.59, 76-78);</li><li>the header search query in <code>components/app-layouts/application-header.js</code>;</li><li>the saved-search formats the jQuery builder produced (equal, not_equal and contains on strings; date comparisons and BETWEEN; nested groups).</li></ul></li><li>Each error code is tested with its position.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> suggestions, components, removing the old parser.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["query-model"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "query-schemas", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: Issue and Project schemas and the query-schema service", "description": "<p>ezSearch needs to know, per module, which fields can be queried, their types and their values. Today that lives in each controller's <code>metadata.filters</code> in the jQuery plugin's format (<code>controllers/app/project/issue/index.js:35-144</code>, <code>controllers/app/projects/index.js:30</code>). This issue moves it into schemas built with <code>createSchema</code> (query-model issue) and a service that loads the values. No page uses it yet, and the controllers stay as they are.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/query/schemas/issue.js</code>, module <code>Issue</code>, with the same field ids as today's Issue filters:<ul><li><code>Issue.issueNumber</code> and <code>parentissue.issueNumber</code> are number fields.</li><li><code>Issue.subject</code> is the text field.</li><li><code>Issue.status</code>, <code>issuemilestone.name</code>, <code>issuetype.name</code> and <code>Issue.priority</code> are enum fields.</li><li><code>Issue.startDate</code> and <code>Issue.endDate</code> are dates.</li><li><code>assignedTo.name</code>, <code>ownedBy.name</code> and <code>reportedBy.name</code> are user fields.</li><li>Aliases: number/#, subject, status, milestone, type, priority/prio, start, end, parent, assignee, owner, reporter.</li><li>Labels use the existing <code>views.app.issue.fields.*</code> keys.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/utils/query/schemas/project.js</code>, module <code>Project</code>: <code>Project.name</code> (the text field), <code>Project.shortCode</code>, <code>Project.status</code> and <code>manager.name</code>, matching today's projects filters.</li><li><code>app/services/query-schema.js</code>: <code>load(module, {projectId})</code> returns a Promise of a schema with its values loaded in parallel through the store, using the same stored values as today:<ul><li>status by name (as <code>statusOptionsByName</code>, issue statuses of the project);</li><li>milestone names of the project;</li><li>issue type names;</li><li>priority from <code>views.app.issue.lists.priority</code>;</li><li>member names, carrying each user's id and profile picture for avatars.</li></ul>Values are cached per module and project; callers check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after awaiting.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests: each schema resolves its aliases and labels, and the service returns the loaded values from Mirage (add handlers only where missing) and caches per project.</li><li>The parser's loose examples also pass against the real Issue schema with Mirage data.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> schemas for other modules, changing the controllers.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["query-model"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "query-completer", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: completer for search bar suggestions", "description": "<p>The ezSearch bar shows a suggestion menu while typing. This issue adds the pure logic behind it: given the text, the cursor and a schema, what comes next and what to suggest. No UI.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/query/completer.js</code>: <code>complete(text, cursor, schema)</code> returns <code>{context, replaceStart, replaceEnd, suggestions}</code>. Context is field, operator, value or connector; built on the lexer from the parser issue.</li><li>Order of suggestions by context:<ul><li>At a field: fields, plus a \\"Search &lt;text field label&gt; for '&lt;word&gt;'\\" item.</li><li>After a field: only the operators valid for its type (registry from the query-model issue).</li><li>After an operator: the field's values (enum order, users alphabetical, <code>today</code> for dates; inside quotes too).</li><li>After a complete condition: <code>)</code> when a bracket is open, plus only the conjunction the current group already uses. Groups never mix AND and OR, and an implied AND counts. Both AND and OR are offered only when the group has one condition.</li></ul></li><li>Each suggestion is <code>{kind, label (translation key or text), insert, detail (e.g. the field id)}</code>, and accepting one replaces <code>replaceStart..replaceEnd</code>.</li><li>Ranking: exact match, then label prefix, then alias or id prefix, then word start inside the label, then substring; ties keep schema order. At most 8 items.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests with the fixture schema (<code>tests/helpers/query-schema.js</code>):<ul><li><code>prio|</code> gives Priority first.</li><li><code>priority |</code> gives the enum operators only.</li><li><code>priority = h|</code> gives High.</li><li><code>start between 2026-05-01 and |</code> gives date values.</li><li><code>(type:bug |</code> gives AND, OR and <code>)</code>.</li><li><code>(type:bug OR type:story |</code> gives OR and <code>)</code> only.</li><li><code>status:new milestone:v1 |</code> gives AND only.</li><li>A cursor in the middle of the text replaces the right range.</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> recent or saved queries as suggestions.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["query-parser"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "query-search-bar", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "EzSearch::SearchBar: typed queries with suggestions, formatting and errors", "description": "<p>The text editor of ezSearch. Today the Issue list search input is readonly and only opens the jQuery panel. This component lets people type a loose query that is formatted into Gaia's exact format. It is standalone: <code>&lt;EzSearch::SearchBar @tree @schema @placeholder @onChange @onRun /&gt;</code>. The <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> container (later issue) keeps it in sync with the visual builder, and no page uses it yet.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search/search-bar.{js,hbs}</code> (Glimmer):<ul><li>Uses <code>FormFields::FieldText</code> (modifiers through <code>...attributes</code> for keydown and the caret position) and holds the draft text while editing.</li><li>On Enter (menu closed) or blur, <code>parse</code> against <code>@schema</code>. If it parses, call <code>@onChange(tree)</code> and replace the text with <code>serialize(tree)</code>, which uses exact ids such as <code>Issue.priority</code>, not labels. Enter also calls <code>@onRun()</code>.</li><li>When there are errors, show the translated message with its position under the input (<code>span.error.text-red</code>, screen <code>bar-error</code>), keep the text, and never call <code>@onChange</code> or <code>@onRun</code>.</li><li>When <code>@tree</code> changes from outside while not editing, show <code>serialize(@tree)</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Suggestion menu from <code>complete()</code> (completer issue): a Bootstrap <code>dropdown-menu</code> under the input with section headers and key hints (screen <code>toolbar-typing</code>). Up and Down move, Tab or Enter accept, Enter with the menu closed runs, Esc closes. Keep it open while typing and close it on blur.</li><li><code>app/components/ez-search/query-text.{js,hbs}</code>: shows the formatted query when the bar is not focused, with fields, operators and and/or keywords coloured from lexer tokens. Render plain text in spans, never <code>htmlSafe</code>. Clicking it focuses the input.</li><li><code>app/styles/components/ez-search-bar.scss</code>, imported in <code>app/styles/app.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.ez-search-bar</code>. Colours are <code>$secondaryColor</code> for fields, <code>$primaryColor</code> for operators and <code>$highlightColor</code> for keywords; square edges. It is a separate file so the Panel PR doesn't conflict.</li><li>Mobile (below 768px, screen <code>mobile-views</code>): the bar takes the full width, the suggestion menu spans the bar's width, and the hint line is hidden.</li><li>Strings (menu headers, hints) go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.searchBar.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests with the fixture schema)</p><ul><li>Typing <code>prio = hi status != done</code> and pressing Enter calls <code>@onChange</code> and <code>@onRun</code> and shows <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND (Issue.status !: done))</code>.</li><li>Typing <code>prio</code> opens the menu with Priority highlighted; Tab inserts it.</li><li>Arrow keys and Esc behave as described.</li><li><code>status:zzz</code> shows the unknown-value error, and <code>status:new or type:bug milestone:v1</code> shows the mixed AND/OR error; neither calls anything.</li><li>An outside <code>@tree</code> change updates the text.</li><li>Coloured tokens are rendered as text, not HTML.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the toolbar (Saved Searches, Builder, Search, Clear), page integration.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["query-completer"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["toolbar-typing", "bar-error", "mobile-views"]}, {"key": "query-value-editor", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "EzSearch::ValueEditor: value input by field type and operator", "description": "<p>The ezSearch visual builder needs a value input that matches the condition's field type and operator. This standalone component is used by <code>EzSearch::Condition</code> in the Panel issue. No page uses it yet.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search/value-editor.{js,hbs}</code>: <code>&lt;EzSearch::ValueEditor @field @operator @value @onChange /&gt;</code>, where <code>@field</code> is a schema field with its values (query-schemas issue) and <code>@operator</code> is a registry entry (query-model issue). The input by type and operator:<ul><li>Enum fields: <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> (<code>@relateType=\\"relate-simple\\"</code>).</li><li>User fields: the same, with avatars as in the existing user selects.</li><li>IN and NOT IN: <code>FormFields::FieldMultiSelect</code> (or <code>FieldRelateMulti</code>, whichever the forms use for static options), giving an array.</li><li>Dates: <code>FormFields::FieldDate</code>, and two of them with a translated \\"and\\" for BETWEEN. The output is always <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>.</li><li>Text and number fields: <code>FormFields::FieldText</code>.</li><li>Operators with arity 0 (NULL, EMPTY): no input.</li></ul></li><li><code>@onChange(value)</code> passes values in the shape <code>ast.condition</code> expects (string, array, or [from, to]). It never mutates <code>@value</code>.</li><li>The controls fill their column so they stack on mobile (screen <code>mobile-views</code>).</li><li>Placeholders go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.valueEditor.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>Each type and operator combination renders the right control and emits the right value shape.</li><li>A date picked through FieldDate is emitted as <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>.</li><li>Switching the operator from <code>:</code> to IN turns a single value into a one-item array.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> rows, groups, the panel.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["query-schemas"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["builder-open", "mobile-views"]}, {"key": "query-panel", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "EzSearch::Panel: visual builder with groups and conditions", "description": "<p>The visual editor of ezSearch: nested groups with an AND/OR switch, and rows of field / operator / value. It is standalone: <code>&lt;EzSearch::Panel @tree @schema @onChange /&gt;</code>. The <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> container (later issue) keeps it in sync with the search bar, opens it inline under the bar and adds Save Search. No page uses it yet.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search/panel.{js,hbs}</code>: renders the root group; an empty tree shows one empty AND group.</li><li><code>app/components/ez-search/group.{js,hbs}</code>:<ul><li>A bordered block with a crimson (<code>$primaryColor</code>) left edge for AND and a plum (<code>$highlightColor</code>) one for OR. A group has exactly one conjunction.</li><li>The header has an AND/OR <code>btn-group btn-xs</code> switch, \\"Condition\\" and \\"Group\\" buttons, and a remove button (not on the root).</li><li>Groups nest to any depth.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/components/ez-search/condition.{js,hbs}</code>:<ul><li>A row with the field (<code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> over the schema fields by label), the operator (<code>FieldRelate</code> over the operators valid for the field type), <code>EzSearch::ValueEditor</code> and a remove <code>btn-box-tool</code>.</li><li>Changing the field resets the operator to the type's default and clears an incompatible value.</li><li>An incomplete row stays in the tree with a muted \\"Incomplete: left out of the query\\" note, and the serializer skips it.</li><li>Serializer refusals for the row (brackets, apostrophes, NULL/EMPTY) show under it.</li></ul></li><li>All changes go through the immutable helpers in <code>app/utils/query/ast.js</code> and come out as <code>@onChange(newTree)</code>; the components never mutate <code>@tree</code>.</li><li>Responsive, using the Bootstrap grid (screens <code>builder-open</code>, <code>mobile-views</code>):<ul><li>From 768px a row is field <code>col-sm-3</code>, operator <code>col-sm-2</code>, value <code>col-sm-6</code> and remove <code>col-sm-1</code>.</li><li>Below 768px the field and the remove button share the first line, and the operator and the value each take a full line.</li><li>Below 768px the group buttons are icon-only (texts <code>hidden-xs</code>) and nested groups are indented less.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/styles/components/ez-search-panel.scss</code>, imported in <code>app/styles/app.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.ez-search-panel</code>. Square edges, existing tokens only, no shadows. Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.panel.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>The tree from screen <code>builder-open</code> renders: an AND group with status IN, start date BETWEEN, one incomplete assignee row and a nested OR group with two type rows.</li><li>Toggling AND/OR, adding and removing conditions and groups, and changing the field each emit the expected tree.</li><li>The incomplete row is in the tree and absent from <code>serialize</code>.</li><li>A value with <code>(</code> shows the refusal.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> drag and drop of rows, the toolbar, page integration.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["query-value-editor"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["builder-open", "mobile-views"]}, {"key": "query-ez-search", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "EzSearch: one tree for search bar and panel, toolbar and public API", "description": "<p>Ties ezSearch together: one query tree as tracked state, edited live by <code>EzSearch::SearchBar</code> and <code>EzSearch::Panel</code>, with the list toolbar around them. This is the component pages use from the next phase: <code>&lt;EzSearch @schema @query @baseQuery @savedSearches @onApply @onSave @aclContext /&gt;</code>. No page uses it in this issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search/index.{js,hbs}</code> (Glimmer):<ul><li><code>@tracked tree</code>, parsed from <code>@query</code> (the Gaia string) when it changes. If a stored query fails to parse, its errors are shown under the bar.</li><li>SearchBar and Panel both get <code>tree</code> and both update it through <code>onChange</code>, so they stay in sync live. Applying text from the bar replaces the tree, so incomplete builder rows are dropped (accepted).</li><li>Check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after every await.</li></ul></li><li>Toolbar, in the existing <code>.search</code> layout (screens <code>toolbar-typing</code>, <code>builder-open</code>):<ul><li>Saved Searches <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> over <code>@savedSearches</code> (<code>{name, query}</code>): picking one loads its query into the tree and marks it active with <code>fa-check</code>.</li><li>Then the SearchBar.</li><li>A Builder <code>btn-default</code> (<code>fa-sliders</code>, <code>active</code> while open) that toggles the Panel inline under the bar, closed by default.</li><li>Search (<code>AppUi::Button btn-primary</code>, <code>@aclContext</code>), disabled while the bar has errors.</li><li>Clear, which empties the tree and applies.</li></ul></li><li>Mobile (below 768px, screen <code>mobile-views</code>): the toolbar wraps. The bar takes the first full-width row; the second row has Saved Searches as <code>fa-bookmark</code> plus a caret and Builder as an icon on the left, and Search and Clear on the right. Save Search is full width. Styles go in <code>app/styles/components/ez-search.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.ez-search</code>.</li><li>Applying (Search, or Enter in the bar) calls <code>@onApply(queryString)</code>. The query string is <code>serialize(compose(parse(@baseQuery), tree))</code>; <code>@baseQuery</code> is never shown in the bar or panel. Nothing is applied when serializing gives errors.</li><li>When <code>@onSave</code> is given, a Save Search <code>btn-primary</code> at the bottom right of the open panel calls <code>@onSave(serialize(tree))</code>. The page owns the save dialog.</li><li>Labels: reuse <code>global.form.search</code>, <code>global.form.clear</code>, <code>global.form.savesearch</code> and <code>views.app.issue.list.savedsearch.label</code>, and add <code>components.ezSearch.builderToggle</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>Typing in the bar updates the open panel, and editing the panel updates the bar text.</li><li><code>@query</code> in Gaia format loads into both.</li><li>Choosing a saved search loads it.</li><li>Search calls <code>@onApply</code> with the base query ANDed in.</li><li>Clear empties both editors and applies the base query only.</li><li>An invalid bar disables Search.</li><li>Builder toggles the panel; Save Search appears only with <code>@onSave</code>.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> using it on the Issue list or other views, removing jQuery QueryBuilder (next phases).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["query-search-bar", "query-panel"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["toolbar-typing", "builder-open", "bar-error", "mobile-views"]}, {"key": "gaia-null-empty", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Query: recognise NULL and EMPTY by the operator, not by text anywhere in the leaf", "description": "<p><strong>Request from A Prometheus (ezSearch).</strong> Prometheus is replacing jQuery QueryBuilder with ezSearch, a search bar plus a visual builder that produce Gaia's existing query format. Gaia misparses any leaf that contains the uppercase words NULL or EMPTY, even inside a value. For example, <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS NULL pointer)</code> is treated as a nullary operator and fails. Until this is fixed, ezSearch refuses such values. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Where</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php</code> <code>prepareWhere</code> ~l.159: <code>preg_match('@NULL|EMPTY@', $substatement)</code> decides the value offset from the whole leaf text.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed change</strong></p><ul><li>Split the leaf into field and operator first, and treat it as nullary only when the operator token itself is <code>NULL</code>, <code>!NULL</code>, <code>EMPTY</code> or <code>!EMPTY</code>.</li><li>Every other operator keeps its value, even when the value contains those words.</li><li>The wire format does not change.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Tests (api-tester cases on <code>GET /issue?query=</code>, see the run-tests skill):<ul><li><code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS NULL pointer)</code> and <code>(Issue.subject : EMPTY box)</code> filter by those strings.</li><li><code>(Issue.milestoneId NULL)</code>, <code>(Issue.milestoneId !NULL)</code>, <code>(Issue.milestoneId EMPTY)</code> and <code>(Issue.milestoneId !EMPTY)</code> behave as today.</li><li><code>: null</code> still means IS NULL (<code>isNullSentinelValue</code>).</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> binding values (separate request), quoted values with brackets.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gaia-bind-values", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Query: bind query values as parameters and validate field names in Clause.php", "description": "<p><strong>Request from A Prometheus (ezSearch).</strong> ezSearch lets people type free-text queries, which Gaia turns into PHQL. Today <code>Clause.php</code> concatenates both the values and the field names into the where string. A value with an apostrophe breaks the query, and crafted values or fields reach the SQL, which breaks the house rule \\"never build SQL/PHQL by string concatenation\\". ezSearch refuses apostrophes until this is fixed. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Where</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php</code> <code>prepareWhere</code> ~l.188-273 builds <code>$translatedStatement</code> with the values inlined.</li><li><code>core/mvc/models/Query.php:141</code> calls <code>queryBuilder-&gt;where($this-&gt;clause-&gt;where)</code> with no bind parameters.</li><li>The translated leaves are reused by <code>getWhereClause</code> (~l.551), by query splitting in <code>updateBaseWhereWithIds</code>, <code>updateRelatedWhere</code> and <code>updateBaseWhereWithId</code> (~l.599-632, the last also inlines the id), by <code>core/mvc/models/Model.php:379</code> (HasManyToMany <code>prepareWhere</code>) and by <code>query/Meta.php:176-223</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed change</strong></p><ul><li>Each leaf emits PHQL placeholders (<code>:qN:</code>) and records the values in a bind map on the Clause.</li><li>BETWEEN gets two placeholders, IN gets one per item (or an array bind), and LIKE patterns are built in PHP with <code>%</code> and <code>_</code> escaped.</li><li>The bind map travels with the where string to every place that reuses it, including split queries and many-to-many where clauses.</li><li>Field names are checked against <code>alias.field</code> (identifier characters only) and resolved against the model metadata or the relationship aliases; an unknown field returns a clear 400 error.</li><li>The wire format does not change.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Values containing <code>'</code> (e.g. <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS O'Brien)</code>) filter correctly.</li><li>A value such as <code>x') OR ('1'='1</code> matches literally and widens nothing.</li><li>An invalid field name returns 400.</li><li>The existing api-tester query cases (issue list, board and gantt queries, saved searches, related-model filters, query splitting) all pass.</li><li>Tests added per the run-tests skill.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> brackets inside quoted values (separate request), new operators.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["gaia-null-empty"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gaia-quoted-values", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Query: quote-aware leaf parsing so values may contain brackets and apostrophes", "description": "<p><strong>Request from A Prometheus (ezSearch).</strong> ezSearch writes values with spaces in single quotes and would like to allow any text in a value. Gaia's leaf extraction is a regex (<code>@\\\\([^(]*[^)]\\\\)@</code> in <code>Clause.php</code> ~l.152, another one in <code>query/Meta.php</code> <code>extractWhereSubstatements</code> ~l.223 and in <code>Clause::extractWhereSubstatements</code> ~l.360). So a value containing <code>(</code> or <code>)</code>, even when quoted, splits the leaf, and an apostrophe can't be written at all. ezSearch refuses these characters until this is fixed. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li>A value may be wrapped in single quotes, and inside quotes <code>(</code>, <code>)</code>, <code>,</code> and the words AND, OR, NULL and EMPTY are plain text.</li><li>An apostrophe inside a quoted value is written as two apostrophes (<code>'O''Brien'</code>).</li><li>IN lists stay <code>CONTAINS 'a','b'</code>, now split on commas outside quotes.</li><li>Unquoted values keep today's behaviour, so existing saved searches and URLs keep working.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed change</strong></p><ul><li>One small quote-aware tokenizer for the where string (e.g. <code>core/mvc/models/query/WhereTokenizer.php</code>) that yields the leaves with their positions, used by <code>Clause::prepareWhere</code>, <code>Clause::extractWhereSubstatements</code> and <code>Meta</code> in place of the regexes.</li><li>It works on top of the bound values from the bind-values request.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li><code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS 'fix (urgent)')</code>, <code>(Issue.subject : 'O''Brien')</code> and <code>(assignedTo.name CONTAINS 'Rana Nouman','Hammad Hassan')</code> filter correctly.</li><li>All existing query cases pass unchanged.</li><li>Tests added per the run-tests skill.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> double-quoted values, changes to the operators. Prometheus relaxes its refusals in a later phase, once this is merged.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["gaia-bind-values"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-06 21:34:45	2026-11-06 21:41:26	f
bba3bad06aee-2243-248d-3cf90022a70a	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	3	{"summary": "ezSearch phase 2: the Issue list uses <EzSearch> in place of the readonly input and the jQuery query-builder panel, with the Issue schema from the query-schema service. Saved searches, Save Search, Clear, paging and ?query= keep working through a new applyQuery path in the shared list controller. The Project and admin lists stay on jQuery QueryBuilder, and nothing is removed. Gherkin acceptance tests on Mirage cover typing, keyboard suggestions, builder-to-bar sync, saved searches and errors. A small follow-up lifts the serializer's apostrophe refusal once Gaia binds query values (agaia-4302, already planned; no new Gaia request).", "issues": [{"key": "ez-issue-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue list: replace jQuery QueryBuilder with ezSearch", "description": "<p>ezSearch (the <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> component from aprom-4300, built on aprom-4293..4299) replaces jQuery QueryBuilder, starting with the Issue list. Today the list's search input is readonly and only opens the jQuery panel, so nobody can type a query. The Project list and the admin module lists share <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code> and stay on jQuery QueryBuilder until a later phase, so their path must keep working and nothing is removed.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs</code> ~l.7-67: replace the Saved Searches dropdown, the readonly <code>FormFields::FieldText</code>, the Search and Clear buttons and the <code>.list-view-filters</code> block with <code>{{query-builder module=\\"issue\\"}}</code> and its Save Search button with <code>&lt;EzSearch @schema={{this.querySchema}} @query={{this.query}} @savedSearches={{this.ezSavedSearches}} @activeSavedSearchId={{this.searchId}} @onSavedSearchChange={{this.selectSavedSearch}} @onApply={{this.applyQuery}} @onSave={{this.showEzSaveSearchDialog}} @aclContext=\\"issue.read\\" /&gt;</code>. Use the argument names 4300 actually shipped. Keep the save dialog (<code>bootstrap-modal</code>) in the page and show the query passed to <code>@onSave</code>. Don't pass <code>@baseQuery</code>: the route already ANDs <code>(Issue.projectId : X)</code> (<code>routes/app/project/issue/index.js</code> l.191-196).</li><li><code>routes/app/project/issue/index.js</code>: load the schema with <code>query-schema</code> <code>load('issue', {projectId})</code> next to the saved searches (l.232) and set <code>controller.querySchema</code> in <code>setupController</code>. <code>?query=</code> loads into the bar and the builder through <code>@query</code>; the <code>reloadPage</code> trailing-space hack must still parse.</li><li><code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>: add <code>@action applyQuery(query)</code>, which sets <code>queryString</code> and <code>query</code>, resets <code>page</code> to 1 and clears <code>searchId</code>/<code>activeSearch</code>. It doesn't touch <code>utils/query/builder.js</code>. Clear on the Issue list goes through <code>applyQuery('')</code>, because <code>clearSearch</code> calls the jQuery singleton, which throws when it was never initialised. Keep <code>searchByRules</code>, <code>openFilters</code>, <code>clearSearch</code>, <code>showSaveSearchDialog</code> and <code>toggleSearch</code> unchanged for the other lists.</li><li><code>controllers/app/project/issue/index.js</code>:<ul><li>Remove the <code>metadata.filters</code> array (l.35-144); the issue schema replaces it.</li><li>Add <code>ezSavedSearches</code>, mapping saved searches to <code>{id, name, query: searchquery}</code>.</li><li>Add <code>selectSavedSearch(search|null)</code>, which sets <code>searchId</code>/<code>activeSearch</code> and applies the query, or clears it like <code>toggleSearch</code> does.</li><li>Add a save path that saves the query handed over by <code>@onSave</code> without calling <code>searchByRules</code> (today's <code>saveSearch</code> l.235 sends it).</li><li>Keep <code>statusOptionsByName</code>, <code>milestonesOptions</code>, <code>usersOptions</code> and <code>issueTypeOptions</code> if anything else still uses them.</li></ul></li><li><code>mirage/route-handlers/issue.js</code>: record the last <code>query</code> param in the scenario context so steps can assert what was sent; keep today's behaviour.</li><li>Tests:<ul><li>Update <code>tests/acceptance/issue/search-issue-from-list.feature</code> and its steps for the new Saved Searches dropdown.</li><li>New <code>tests/acceptance/issue/ez-search-issue-list.feature</code> + steps with these scenarios:<ol><li>Type <code>prio = hi status != done</code>, press Enter: the bar shows <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND (Issue.status !: done))</code>, <code>/issue</code> was queried with it ANDed with the project, and the URL has <code>?query=</code>.</li><li>Type <code>prio</code>, use Down and Tab to accept Priority, finish and run.</li><li>Open Builder, add a Status condition: the bar text updates.</li><li>Pick a saved search: the bar and the builder show it, the query is sent and <code>searchId</code> is set.</li><li>Type <code>status:zzz</code>: the error shows under the bar, Search is disabled and no new <code>/issue</code> request is made.</li></ol></li><li>A unit test for <code>applyQuery</code>.</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios above pass.</li><li>Existing issue-list acceptance tests (paging, sort, mass update, export with a query, saved search) pass.</li><li>The Project list and admin lists still open and use jQuery QueryBuilder.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px against screens <code>issue-list-applied</code> and <code>issue-list-applied-mobile</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Project and admin lists, the board, Gantt and calendar, removing jQuery QueryBuilder or <code>utils/query/*</code>, and editing or deleting saved searches.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4300"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["issue-list-applied", "issue-list-applied-mobile"]}, {"key": "ez-apostrophes", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: allow apostrophes in values once Gaia binds query values", "description": "<p>The ezSearch serializer (<code>app/utils/query/serializer.js</code>, aprom-4293) refuses values with an apostrophe, because Gaia's <code>Clause.php</code> concatenated values into SQL. agaia-4302 binds the values as parameters, so names like <code>O'Brien</code> can be searched safely. Gaia still trims <code>'</code> from both ends of a value and splits IN lists on <code>','</code> until agaia-4303 adds the <code>''</code> escape, so a few cases stay refused.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>serializer.js</code>: allow <code>'</code> inside a single value, e.g. <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS O'Brien)</code> and <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS 'Rana''s board')</code>.</li><li>Keep refusing, with a clearer message (\\"Apostrophes can't start or end a value or appear in a list yet\\"):<ul><li>an apostrophe at the start or end of a value;</li><li>an apostrophe in any item of an IN or NOT IN list.</li></ul></li><li>Brackets and uppercase NULL/EMPTY stay refused (agaia-4303 and agaia-4301).</li><li>Update the message in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> and the serializer and round-trip unit tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests: <code>subject ~ O'Brien</code> serializes and round-trips.</li><li>Unit tests: <code>subject ~ \\"'quoted'\\"</code> and <code>assignee in O'Brien, rana</code> are refused with the new message.</li><li>On the Issue list (local Gaia with agaia-4302), searching <code>O'Brien</code> returns matching issues without a server error.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>''</code> escape and brackets (after agaia-4303).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["agaia-4302", "aprom-4293"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 01:54:03	2026-11-07 01:54:03	f
036203086aee-88b0-248d-67de2e16ce14	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	4	{"summary": "ezSearch phase 2: the Issue list uses <EzSearch> in place of the readonly input and the jQuery query-builder panel. First, a small change to <EzSearch> lets the page know which saved search is active and when the user picks or clears one, so ?searchId= keeps working. Then the Issue list integration: Issue schema from the query-schema service, saved searches, Save Search, Clear, paging and ?query= through a new applyQuery path in the shared list controller, plus Gherkin acceptance tests on Mirage. The Project and admin lists stay on jQuery QueryBuilder, and nothing is removed. A small follow-up lifts the serializer's apostrophe refusal once Gaia binds query values (agaia-4302, already planned).", "issues": [{"key": "ez-saved-search-api", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "EzSearch: report the picked saved search and accept the active one", "description": "<p><code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> (aprom-4300) loads a picked saved search into its tree and marks it active internally. The Issue list keeps the active saved search in its <code>searchId</code> URL parameter (<code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code> <code>toggleSearch</code> ~l.974, route <code>routes/app/project/issue/index.js</code> ~l.278), so the page must be told when one is picked or cleared and must be able to set the active one when the page loads. This issue adds that to the component only; no page uses it yet.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search/index.{js,hbs}</code>:<ul><li>New optional <code>@activeSavedSearchId</code>: when it is set, that saved search is marked active (<code>fa-check</code>) and its query is loaded, unless <code>@query</code> is also given, in which case <code>@query</code> wins.</li><li>New optional <code>@onSavedSearchChange(search|null)</code>: called when the user picks a saved search, when they pick the active one again (which deselects it, as <code>toggleSearch</code> does today: called with null, tree emptied), and when Clear is used (called with null). Picking a search still applies it through <code>@onApply</code>, as 4300 does.</li><li>Editing the query in the bar or the builder after picking a search keeps the mark until the query is applied. Once it is applied and differs from the saved query, the mark is removed and <code>@onSavedSearchChange(null)</code> is called.</li><li>Without the new arguments the component behaves exactly as 4300 shipped it. Use the <code>@savedSearches</code> item shape 4300 defined (<code>{id, name, query}</code> or whatever it actually uses).</li></ul></li><li>Extend the component's integration test.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests)</p><ul><li><code>@activeSavedSearchId</code> marks the search and loads its query.</li><li>Picking a search calls <code>@onSavedSearchChange(search)</code> and <code>@onApply</code>.</li><li>Picking it again calls <code>@onSavedSearchChange(null)</code>.</li><li>Clear calls <code>@onSavedSearchChange(null)</code>.</li><li>Applying an edited query drops the mark.</li><li>All existing EzSearch tests pass unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> editing or deleting saved searches, page integration.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4300"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ez-issue-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Issue list: replace jQuery QueryBuilder with ezSearch", "description": "<p>ezSearch (the <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> component from aprom-4300, built on aprom-4293..4299, with the saved-search arguments from the issue this one depends on) replaces jQuery QueryBuilder, starting with the Issue list. Today the list's search input is readonly and only opens the jQuery panel, so nobody can type a query. The Project list and the admin module lists share <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code> and stay on jQuery QueryBuilder until a later phase, so their path must keep working and nothing is removed.</p><p><strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look. Where they disagree with <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code> or with what <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> actually renders, the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs</code> ~l.7-67: replace the Saved Searches dropdown, the readonly <code>FormFields::FieldText</code>, the Search and Clear buttons and the <code>.list-view-filters</code> block with <code>{{query-builder module=\\"issue\\"}}</code> and its Save Search button with <code>&lt;EzSearch @schema={{this.querySchema}} @query={{this.query}} @savedSearches={{this.ezSavedSearches}} @activeSavedSearchId={{this.searchId}} @onSavedSearchChange={{this.selectSavedSearch}} @onApply={{this.applyQuery}} @onSave={{this.showEzSaveSearchDialog}} @aclContext=\\"issue.read\\" /&gt;</code>. Keep the save dialog (<code>bootstrap-modal</code>) in the page and show the query passed to <code>@onSave</code>. Don't pass <code>@baseQuery</code>: the route already ANDs <code>(Issue.projectId : X)</code> (<code>routes/app/project/issue/index.js</code> l.191-196).</li><li><code>routes/app/project/issue/index.js</code>: load the schema with <code>query-schema</code> <code>load('issue', {projectId})</code> next to the saved searches (l.232) and set <code>controller.querySchema</code> in <code>setupController</code>. <code>?query=</code> loads into the bar and the builder through <code>@query</code>; the <code>reloadPage</code> trailing-space hack must still parse.</li><li><code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>: add <code>@action applyQuery(query)</code>, which sets <code>queryString</code> and <code>query</code> and resets <code>page</code> to 1. It doesn't touch <code>utils/query/builder.js</code>. Clear on the Issue list goes through <code>applyQuery('')</code> plus <code>selectSavedSearch(null)</code>, because <code>clearSearch</code> calls the jQuery singleton, which throws when it was never initialised. Keep <code>searchByRules</code>, <code>openFilters</code>, <code>clearSearch</code>, <code>showSaveSearchDialog</code> and <code>toggleSearch</code> unchanged for the other lists.</li><li><code>controllers/app/project/issue/index.js</code>:<ul><li>Remove the <code>metadata.filters</code> array (l.35-144); the issue schema replaces it.</li><li>Add <code>ezSavedSearches</code>, mapping saved searches to the item shape <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> expects (query from <code>searchquery</code>).</li><li>Add <code>selectSavedSearch(search|null)</code>, which sets or clears <code>searchId</code>/<code>activeSearch</code>.</li><li>Add a save path that saves the query handed over by <code>@onSave</code> without calling <code>searchByRules</code> (today's <code>saveSearch</code> l.235 sends it).</li><li>Keep <code>statusOptionsByName</code>, <code>milestonesOptions</code>, <code>usersOptions</code> and <code>issueTypeOptions</code> if anything else still uses them.</li></ul></li><li><code>mirage/route-handlers/issue.js</code>: record the last <code>query</code> param in the scenario context so steps can assert what was sent; keep today's behaviour (Mirage doesn't filter by query).</li><li>Tests:<ul><li>Update <code>tests/acceptance/issue/search-issue-from-list.feature</code> and its steps for the new Saved Searches dropdown.</li><li>New <code>tests/acceptance/issue/ez-search-issue-list.feature</code> + steps with these scenarios:<ol><li>Type <code>prio = hi status != done</code>, press Enter: the bar shows <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND (Issue.status !: done))</code>, <code>/issue</code> was queried with it ANDed with the project, and the URL has <code>?query=</code>.</li><li>Type <code>prio</code>, use Down and Tab to accept Priority, finish and run.</li><li>Open Builder, add a Status condition: the bar text updates.</li><li>Pick a saved search: the bar and the builder show it, the query is sent and <code>searchId</code> is in the URL.</li><li>Type <code>status:zzz</code>: the error shows under the bar, Search is disabled and no new <code>/issue</code> request is made.</li></ol></li><li>A unit test for <code>applyQuery</code>.</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios above pass.</li><li>Existing issue-list acceptance tests (paging, sort, mass update, export with a query, saved search) pass.</li><li>The Project list and admin lists still open and use jQuery QueryBuilder.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px, using the screens <code>issue-list-applied</code> and <code>issue-list-applied-mobile</code> as a guide.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Project and admin lists, the board, Gantt and calendar, removing jQuery QueryBuilder or <code>utils/query/*</code>, and editing or deleting saved searches.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ez-saved-search-api"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["issue-list-applied", "issue-list-applied-mobile"]}, {"key": "ez-apostrophes", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: allow apostrophes in values once Gaia binds query values", "description": "<p>The ezSearch serializer (<code>app/utils/query/serializer.js</code>, aprom-4293) refuses values with an apostrophe, because Gaia's <code>Clause.php</code> concatenated values into SQL. agaia-4302 binds the values as parameters, so names like <code>O'Brien</code> can be searched safely. Gaia still trims <code>'</code> from both ends of a value and splits IN lists on <code>','</code> until agaia-4303 adds the <code>''</code> escape, so a few cases stay refused.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>serializer.js</code>: allow <code>'</code> inside a single value, e.g. <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS O'Brien)</code> and <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS 'Rana''s board')</code>.</li><li>Keep refusing, with a clearer message (\\"Apostrophes can't start or end a value or appear in a list yet\\"):<ul><li>an apostrophe at the start or end of a value;</li><li>an apostrophe in any item of an IN or NOT IN list.</li></ul></li><li>Brackets and uppercase NULL/EMPTY stay refused (agaia-4303 and agaia-4301).</li><li>Update the message in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> and the serializer and round-trip unit tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests: <code>subject ~ O'Brien</code> serializes and round-trips.</li><li>Unit tests: <code>subject ~ \\"'quoted'\\"</code> and <code>assignee in O'Brien, rana</code> are refused with the new message.</li><li>On the Issue list (local Gaia with agaia-4302), searching <code>O'Brien</code> returns matching issues without a server error.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>''</code> escape and brackets (after agaia-4303).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["agaia-4302", "aprom-4293"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 01:59:31	2026-11-07 02:03:55	f
0ab0d1526aee-cdab-4f28-cd42fb6a4e59	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	5	{"summary": "One bug fix: the ezSearch toolbar on the Issue list takes three rows (buttons, then the formatted query on its own line, plus a stray underline and empty space). It must be a single line as tall as the old toolbar: Saved Searches, the bar filling the remaining width, Builder, Search, Clear.", "issues": [{"key": "ez-single-line", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: toolbar renders on three rows instead of one line", "description": "<p>On the Issue list (aprom-4305) the ezSearch toolbar takes three rows instead of one. It should be a single line, the same height as the old toolbar (see <code>docs/ui/screens/issue-list.png</code>). The earlier mock-ups looked taller, but they were only a guide.</p><p><strong>What happens today</strong> (engineer's screenshot, query <code>((issuemilestone.name : aga-v1) AND (Issue.priority : high))</code> applied, builder closed)</p><ul><li>Row 1 has Saved Searches on the left and Builder, Search and Clear on the right, with an empty gap where the bar should be.</li><li>Row 2 has the coloured query (<code>EzSearch::QueryText</code>) on its own line, below the buttons and offset to the right.</li><li>A stray short underline sits at the right of row 2, near the Builder button: likely the <code>FormFields::FieldText</code> <code>.bar</code> of an input that has collapsed to almost no width.</li><li>About one more row of empty space follows before the list controls.</li></ul><p><strong>Check first</strong></p><ul><li>Whether QueryText is rendered outside the input's <code>.form-field</code>/<code>.has-feedback</code> box rather than in it.</li><li>Whether the bar's flex item (the <code>.search</code> layout in <code>styles/modules/document.scss</code> ~l.329) has no width or <code>flex: 1</code>.</li><li>Whether the error <code>span</code> or the menu reserves height while empty.</li></ul><p><strong>Expected</strong></p><ul><li>One row, in order: Saved Searches, the bar filling all the remaining width, Builder, Search, Clear. All are vertically aligned, and the box header has the old toolbar's height.</li><li>The formatted query is shown inside the bar, in the same box and on the same underline as the input. It is not a separate block, and there is no second underline.</li><li>While not focused, a long query stays on one line, is cut off with an ellipsis, and shows the full text as a <code>title</code> tooltip. While editing, the input scrolls horizontally.</li><li>Nothing reserves height when there is no error or the menu is closed. An error message and the suggestion menu still appear under the bar (the menu as an overlay that doesn't push the list down).</li><li>Mobile (below 768px) still wraps to two rows as specified in aprom-4300 (the bar, then the buttons) with no extra gaps.</li><li>Fix it in the ezSearch components and their styles (<code>app/components/ez-search/search-bar</code>, <code>query-text</code>, <code>index</code>, <code>app/styles/components/ez-search*.scss</code>), not with page-specific CSS on the Issue list. Square edges, existing tokens.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An integration test renders <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> with a query and asserts that the bar and the buttons share one row (same top within a few px) and that the bar is wider than the buttons together.</li><li>Checked in the browser on the Issue list with a short query, a long query, the menu open and an error, at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other toolbar changes, the builder panel.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4300"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 07:15:22	2026-11-07 07:15:22	f
884230936aee-4713-5ba1-61377f782fc1	d87ad5636ae5-1449-ae8f-5808a9dddbf1	4	{"summary": "Fix the endless reload of images pasted into idea messages. render-markdown re-runs because the image lookup it starts inside its tracked run changes store data the modifier depends on, so each run starts another. Make the modifier read only its argument, skip unchanged text and resolve each image once.", "issues": [{"key": "inline-image-loop", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Idea messages: pasted images reload forever because render-markdown re-runs on its own store query", "description": "<p>When a user pastes an image into the idea composer, it is uploaded and stored in the message as <code>![name](upload:&lt;id&gt;)</code> (aprom-4114). In the thread the message never settles. The image request succeeds, but the message keeps re-rendering and requesting the image again.</p><p><strong>Likely cause (confirm first):</strong> <code>modifiers/render-markdown.js</code> is a classic ember-modifier. Its <code>didReceiveArguments</code> runs inside autotracking and synchronously calls <code>showImages</code>, which calls <code>uploadPreview.previewUrl</code>. That runs <code>store.query('upload', { id, download: true })</code> (<code>services/upload-preview.js</code>). Store state read there seems to become a dependency of the modifier, and the query result changes it. The modifier then re-runs, mints a new single-use download token, calls <code>viewer.setMarkdown</code> again (re-rendering the message and reloading the image), and repeats. Verify this with a counter or a breakpoint before fixing; if the cause is different, say so in the issue.</p><ul><li>Start with a failing integration test: render a message body with one <code>upload:</code> image (Mirage upload and download token). Assert that the preview address is requested once, and the image is shown once, after settling.</li><li>In <code>didReceiveArguments</code>, read only the positional argument. Do nothing when the markdown equals the one already shown. Start the image lookup outside the tracking frame, e.g. after an <code>await Promise.resolve()</code> or a scheduled task, so nothing it reads becomes a dependency.</li><li>Keep the resolved address per upload id for the modifier's lifetime, so a later run with the same image doesn't fetch a new token or redraw the image. Tokens are single-use, so a redrawn <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> pointing at a used address gets a 404.</li><li>Keep the existing behaviour: the image name shows first, the image replaces it once resolved, an unreadable upload stays as its name, a click opens the full size, and the stale-markdown check stays. Clean up on <code>willRemove</code>.</li><li>Check that the composer preview and the create page's first message (both render markdown) don't loop either.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a message with a pasted image shows the image once and stays still. The network tab shows one token request and one image request per image, and no repeating requests while the page is idle. The ember suite passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> opening pasted images in the preview modal instead of a new tab, migrating the modifier to the ember-modifier 4 API, and Gaia changes.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 07:30:16	2026-11-07 07:30:16	f
aeb148596aee-083f-0b34-b160c77d65e7	f1592e496aee-cb3c-b49a-239fcfcb2381	3	{"summary": "With CodeRabbit's auto review turned off, the agents ask for every review themselves. A shared counter with a tier policy (rabbit-request) decides who reviews each PR: under 10 reviews in the last 24 hours CodeRabbit reviews everything, from 10 to 24 only large PRs, from 25 on everything goes to the human reviewer. It posts '@coderabbitai full review' as Agent Odysseus and records it. ai ship (ship-gate), the Talos fix-round loop (loop-gate) and Agamemnon's branch updates and conflict fixes (aga-gate) all go through it and hand the issue to the reviewer when it answers human. Agamemnon's sweep later sends those PRs to CodeRabbit once there is credit again (aga-backlog). Separately, Agamemnon sets an issue to done when a person merges its agent PR (merged-done). Only agent activity is counted; the engineer's own GitHub activity is not counted or limited.", "issues": [{"key": "rabbit-request", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "ai rabbit request: daily CodeRabbit counter with a tier policy that posts the review trigger", "description": "<p>CodeRabbit includes about 26 PR reviews a day; after that it charges per file. Its auto review is turned off, so the agents now ask for every review by posting a trigger comment as Agent Odysseus. This issue adds the one place that decides whether an agent PR goes to CodeRabbit or to the human reviewer, posts the trigger and counts it. Only these agent triggers are counted; reviews people request themselves on GitHub are neither counted nor limited.</p><ul><li>New <code>ai/lib/rabbitbudget.py</code>: a ledger in <code>STATE_DIR</code> (<code>ai/lib/common.py</code>; under <code>LOCAL_DIR</code>, so the runtime copy and the checkout share it). Two lists: <code>sent</code> <code>{at (UTC ISO), repo, pr, sha, source}</code> and <code>deferred</code> <code>{at, repo, pr, issue, files}</code> (PRs that went to the human because of the limit). Writes are atomic and safe across processes (lock file plus write-to-temp-then-replace). Prune <code>sent</code> entries older than 48 hours.</li><li>Policy, a pure function of (used in the rolling last 24 hours, hand-written file count, rereview flag, settings): <code>used &lt; everyPrUntil</code> → coderabbit; <code>used &lt; limit</code> → coderabbit when <code>rereview</code> or <code>files &gt;= largePrFiles</code>, else human; otherwise human.</li><li>Settings in <code>ai/config.json</code>: <code>codeRabbitBudget: {everyPrUntil: 10, limit: 25, largePrFiles: 6}</code> and <code>codeRabbitTrigger: \\"@coderabbitai full review\\"</code>. A missing <code>codeRabbitBudget</code> means no limit.</li><li><code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source pr-opened|bot-round|reenter|update-branch|conflict|backlog [--files N] [--rereview] [--issue N] [--json]</code>. For a repo where <code>coderabbit.enabled(repo)</code> is false it answers <code>absent</code>. It applies the policy. On coderabbit, it posts the trigger as Agent Odysseus (<code>ody(repo, 'gh', 'pr', 'comment', ...)</code>), records it in <code>sent</code> with the head sha, and drops any <code>deferred</code> entry for the PR. On human, it adds a <code>deferred</code> entry (only when <code>--issue</code> is given; one per PR). It prints, or returns as JSON, <code>{decision: coderabbit|human|absent, used, limit, reason}</code>. A failed comment means the decision is human, with the error in <code>reason</code>; nothing is recorded in <code>sent</code>.</li><li><code>ai rabbit budget [--json]</code>: used, limit, the current tier, when the next slot frees up, and the deferred list.</li><li>Unit tests (ody mocked): every tier boundary (9/10, 24/25), large vs small, rereview in the middle tier, rolling window, deferred added and cleared, failed comment, disabled repo.</li><li>Document both commands and the settings in <code>ai/README.md</code> (CodeRabbit section); say that CodeRabbit's auto review is expected to be off.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>ai rabbit request</code> posts exactly one <code>@coderabbitai full review</code> comment when the policy says coderabbit and records it; <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code> reports the rolling count and the deferred PRs; <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the callers (ai ship, Talos, Agamemnon: separate issues); counting reviews people trigger themselves; cheaper merge-check options.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ship-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "ai ship: ask ai rabbit request who reviews a new PR, hand it to the reviewer when it answers human", "description": "<p>CodeRabbit's auto review is off, so a new agent PR only gets a CodeRabbit review when <code>ai ship</code> asks for one. Depending on the daily count and the PR's size, the answer may be the human reviewer instead.</p><ul><li>In <code>ai/lib/ship.py</code> <code>cmd_ship</code>, after the PR is open (~l.195-200, where <code>defer</code> is decided today): for a CodeRabbit repo, call the <code>rabbitbudget</code> request logic with <code>source pr-opened</code>, <code>files</code> = the hand-written count <code>sizecheck.check</code> already returned, and the issue number.</li><li>On coderabbit: defer the hand-off as today (the issue stays in progress for the Talos loop).</li><li>On human: don't defer. <code>pr_hand_off</code> sets in_review and assigns the reviewer. Add to the tracker notes: <em>Not sent to CodeRabbit: N of 25 reviews used in the last 24 hours (small PRs go to you from 10). Please review by hand; CodeRabbit may add a review later when credit frees up.</em> Print that the session finishes as <code>done</code>, not <code>awaiting_bot_review</code> (like the existing branch for repos without CodeRabbit).</li><li>On resume, when <code>existing_pr</code> finds the PR, don't ask again if the pending hand-off or the ledger already has the PR.</li><li><code>ai pr</code> (<code>workflow.cmd_pr</code>) does the same, with the file count from the PR's changed files.</li><li>Check that Odysseus' ship prompt and role (<code>talos/agents/odysseus/</code>) follow the printed outcome; adjust the wording if needed.</li><li>Unit tests with the request logic mocked: coderabbit → deferred; human → handed off with the note; resume doesn't ask twice.</li><li>Update <code>ai/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with 12 reviews used, a 3-file gaia PR goes to the reviewer as in_review with the note and no trigger comment; an 8-file PR gets the trigger and stays with the agent.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fix rounds and Agamemnon (separate issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-request"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "loop-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos CodeRabbit loop: request a review after each fix round, hand off when the budget says human", "description": "<p>With CodeRabbit's auto review off, a fix round's push gets no review unless Talos asks for one, and the merge check needs a CodeRabbit result on the latest commit. Each follow-up review counts toward the daily limit.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/bot_review.py</code> <code>Watcher.check_one</code> (~l.204): when <code>next_step</code> returns RUN_ROUND, first read <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code> (through <code>talos/lib/ai_cli.py</code>, like <code>ai_rabbit</code>). If a follow-up review would be answered human (limit reached), don't run the round. Hand off to the reviewer (never the merger route) with the comment <em>CodeRabbit limit reached: open CodeRabbit findings left for you.</em></li><li>After a round ends with <code>awaiting_bot_review</code> (<code>dispatcher._await_bot_review</code> ~l.507, when rounds &gt; 0), call <code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source bot-round --rereview --issue N --json</code>. On human, hand off with the same note instead of waiting.</li><li><code>Watcher.reenter</code> (~l.157, after address-review in auto-merge milestones): call <code>ai rabbit request ... --source reenter --rereview</code>; on human, hand off to the reviewer instead of re-entering.</li><li>If the ai command fails, log it and hand off to the reviewer; don't wait for a review that was never requested.</li><li>Unit tests in <code>talos/tests/test_bot_review.py</code>: round skipped at the limit, request after a round, reenter to human, command failure.</li><li>Update the CodeRabbit loop section of the Talos README.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> each fix round's push gets exactly one trigger comment while under the limit; at the limit the issue goes to the reviewer as in_review with the note and no new commit.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the first review (ai ship), Agamemnon.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-request"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "aga-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon: request a CodeRabbit review after branch updates and conflict fixes, or hand the issue to the owner", "description": "<p>Agamemnon's keeper pushes new commits to agent PRs: it updates PRs that are behind their base and sends resolved conflicts back for review. With CodeRabbit's auto review off, those commits get no review unless asked for, and the merge check (<code>ai/lib/mergegate.py</code> <code>gate</code>) needs a CodeRabbit result on the latest commit. Agamemnon must spend reviews through the shared counter and know when the limit is reached.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/orchestrator/keeper.py</code> <code>_update</code> (~l.86): before the update-branch call, read <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code>; at the limit, skip the update (log once per PR per day). After a successful update, call <code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source update-branch --rereview --issue N</code>.</li><li><code>_conflict</code> / <code>_resolve</code> (~l.96-155): at the limit, don't resolve; hand the issue to the owner as in_review with <em>merge conflict, CodeRabbit limit reached: please resolve and review by hand.</em> After a resolution is pushed, call <code>ai rabbit request ... --source conflict --rereview</code>. On human, hand off with the same note.</li><li>The premise and role (<code>talos/agents/agamemnon/</code>): add the budget (tiers, that each agent push needs a trigger, what happens at the limit, that the owner's own GitHub activity is not counted) where they describe updates, conflicts and merging.</li><li>An ai command failure means hand off to the owner, logged.</li><li>Unit tests (see <code>talos/tests/test_agamemnon_conflicts.py</code>): update skipped at the limit, request after update, conflict to the owner, request after resolution.</li><li>Update <code>agamemnon/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> at the limit, Agamemnon's sweep pushes nothing to agent PRs and conflicting PRs land with the owner with the note; under the limit, every push it makes is followed by one trigger comment.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> letting the merge check accept an earlier CodeRabbit pass after base-only merges; auto-merge itself (PRs that went to the human never come back clean).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-request"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "aga-backlog", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon: send PRs that went to the reviewer because of the limit to CodeRabbit once credit frees up", "description": "<p>When the daily CodeRabbit limit sends an agent PR to the human reviewer, it is recorded as deferred in the shared ledger. Once there is credit again, it should still get a CodeRabbit review to help the human; the issue stays with the human.</p><ul><li>In Agamemnon's sweep (<code>talos/lib/orchestrator/</code>, next to the keeper's sweep): read <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code>. For each deferred PR, oldest first, while the tier allows it (its stored file count against the tier, as for a new PR), call <code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source backlog --files N --issue N</code>. Stop at the first human answer.</li><li>Before sending, drop the entry without spending a review when the PR is closed or merged, or the issue is no longer in_review.</li><li>Comment on the issue when a review was requested: <em>CodeRabbit review requested now that credit is available; the issue stays with you.</em> Don't reassign it or start the Talos loop.</li><li>Agamemnon role: mention the backlog sending.</li><li>Unit tests: oldest first, stops at the tier, closed/merged/moved PRs dropped, the comment.</li><li>Update <code>agamemnon/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after the 24-hour window frees slots, deferred PRs that fit the tier get a trigger comment, oldest first; their issues stay assigned to the reviewer.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> giving the issue back to the agent to answer CodeRabbit's findings; notifications.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-request", "ship-gate"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "merged-done", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon: set an agent issue done when a person merges its PR", "description": "<p>Agamemnon sets an issue done only after a merge it did itself (<code>talos/lib/orchestrator/merging.py</code> <code>_finish</code> ~l.152). More agent PRs will now go to the human reviewer, and when the reviewer merges one by hand on GitHub the issue stays in_review. Agamemnon should close the loop for those too.</p><ul><li>New sweep step in <code>talos/lib/orchestrator/</code> (its own small module, wired where the merge sweep is set up in <code>orchestrator/setup.py</code>): for in_review issues in the worker's projects assigned to the owner (<code>owners</code>), find the agent PR: branch <code>claude-issue-N</code>, author = the Agent Odysseus GitHub account (reuse the PR lookup the CodeRabbit watcher uses).</li><li>When that PR is merged and Agamemnon didn't merge it (no open/closed merge record in its store): set the issue done and comment <em>PR repo#N merged by &lt;GitHub login&gt;; set done.</em> This is worded differently from Agamemnon's own \\"merged automatically\\" comment, so a person's merge and an agent's merge are told apart.</li><li>Skip issues with no agent PR, with more than one open agent PR, or whose PR is closed without merging (leave those to the owner). Each step safe to repeat.</li><li>Agamemnon role and README: describe the step.</li><li>Unit tests: merged by a person → done + comment; merged by Agamemnon → untouched (its own flow); not merged, closed, no PR → untouched.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after the owner merges an agent PR on GitHub, the issue is done within one Agamemnon sweep, with the comment naming who merged it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> PRs not opened by Agent Odysseus; issues outside the worker's projects; webhooks (polling only).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 10:34:22	2026-11-07 10:34:22	f
f434b7596aee-698e-6251-6053691c3edb	599b10726aeb-f308-85f1-2dd28eca8a3d	3	{"summary": "Fix the two failures, then let Agamemnon move CI failures along. Three issues can start in parallel: held issues survive a reconnect or restart (the waiting list is saved, and the worker's own changes don't block the re-check); Agamemnon's sweep gives stranded ready issues back to the worker; CI re-runs get up to 3 attempts per commit, and a failing re-run command is counted and handed back instead of looping. Then: read verbs for CI (failing job log, the same job on the base branch); a file-bug verb and a hold-until-done verb (building on adt-4278's condition holds) that merges the base branch and re-runs CI once the bug is done; finally the ci_failed premise and role that tell temporary, PR-caused and base-branch failures apart.", "issues": [{"key": "held-reconcile", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos dispatcher: issues waiting on dependencies survive a reconnect or restart", "description": "<p>agaia-4303 was held waiting on agaia-4302. At the next Hermes reconnect, reconcile re-checked it with <code>require_allowed_modifier</code>. The last modifier was the worker itself, because of its own \\"waiting on #4302\\" comment, so <code>policy.decide</code> (<code>talos/lib/policy.py</code> ~l.80) skipped it and it left the held set. When 4302 was done, nothing released 4303. Talos log 2026-11-07 11:55: <code>#4303 skipped: last changed by a user who can't hand this agent work (left the held set)</code>. The held set is also in memory only, so a Talos restart loses it the same way.</p><ul><li>Save the held set (issue, dependencies, last commented waiting set) in talos.db, so <code>DependencyGate</code> (<code>talos/lib/dependency_gate.py</code>) loads it at start. The dispatcher's <code>release_held(\\"reconnect\\", None)</code> then re-checks all of them on reconcile.</li><li>Reconcile no longer drops an issue the worker itself held. For an issue in the saved held set, the last-modifier check is skipped: the hold started from an accepted assignment. The check still applies to issues Talos has never seen.</li><li>An issue leaves the saved set when it is released, worked, unassigned from the agent, or no longer actionable.</li><li>README: dependency gating survives restarts.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests: an issue held, then a reconcile where the last modifier is the agent itself, stays held and is released when its dependency turns done; the held set survives a new Dispatcher on the same db; an unknown issue last changed by a stranger is still skipped.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the orchestrator's stranded-issue sweep (separate issue).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "stranded-sweep", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon sweep: give stranded ready issues back to the worker", "description": "<p>When the worker loses an issue (agaia-4303: held, then dropped on a reconnect), Agamemnon's sweep doesn't see it. The sweep only assigns new issues that have no assignee, so it reported \\"nothing ready\\" with free slots while 4303 sat assigned to the worker with every dependency done.</p><ul><li>In the orchestrator sweep (<code>talos/lib/orchestrator</code>): find issues in its milestones that are assigned to the worker, in a status the worker acts on (new, pending), with every \\"Depends on\\" issue done, and with nothing queued, running or held in the worker for at least <code>strandedMinutes</code> (agent.json, default 15).</li><li>Give each one back through the same path <code>aga retry</code> uses (<code>tool.py</code> <code>_assign_worker</code>), at most as many as there are free slots, counted like a normal feed. Post the comment \\"{Agamemnon}: picked up a stranded issue\\" with why it was ready.</li><li>Don't touch issues held by Agamemnon itself, those in triage, or those in review.</li><li><code>talos status</code> lists stranded issues; README updated.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for the stranded rule (deps done vs not, queued or running vs not, below vs above the minutes) and the free-slot limit. <code>agamemnonProtected</code> paths: manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the worker-side fix (held-reconcile issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ci-rerun-fix", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon merges: up to 3 CI re-runs per head, a failing re-run is counted and handed back", "description": "<p>On agaia-4301 (PR gaia#245) CI failed on a GitHub-side timeout. <code>_ci_failed</code> (<code>talos/lib/orchestrator/merging.py</code> ~l.113) called <code>merge.py</code> <code>rerun</code>, and <code>gh run rerun --failed</code> exited 1 on every sweep for hours. The exception comes before <code>store.note_merge</code>, so the re-run was never recorded and there was no comment and no handback; the engineer re-ran it by hand. The likely cause is that the Agamemnon token has no Actions permission. Also, one re-run per head is too few for flaky external fetches.</p><ul><li><code>merge.py</code> <code>rerun</code>: keep gh's stderr in the error.</li><li><code>_ci_failed</code>: a re-run that errors is recorded (count plus error) and logged with the error. After <code>ciRerunErrors</code> (default 2) errors on the same head, hand back with the error text, which goes to triage first as today.</li><li><code>policy.ci_step</code> and <code>state.py</code> (auto_merges): count re-runs per head. RERUN while the count is below <code>ciRerunAttempts</code> (agent.json, default 3), WAIT for the grace minutes after each, HAND_BACK after the last one. The comment says \\"attempt n of 3\\".</li><li><code>agamemnon/README.md</code>: add <strong>Actions: Read and write</strong> (re-run failed jobs) to the token's permission table. Talos README: the new settings.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for 1, 2 and 3 re-runs at a head, a new head starting over, a rerun command that errors (counted, then handed back with stderr, never looping), and the dry run. <code>agamemnonProtected</code> paths: manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> deciding whether the failure is temporary (ci-triage issues).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "aga-ci-read", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "aga: ci-log and base-ci read verbs", "description": "<p>To tell a temporary CI failure from one the PR caused, or one already broken on the base branch, a triage session must read the failing job's log and compare it with the base branch. <code>aga</code> has no CI reads today (only <code>mergecheck</code>).</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/verbs.py</code> + <code>tool.py</code>: <code>ci-log</code> (tier read): the failed jobs on the PR head with name, URL and the tail of <code>gh run view --log-failed</code> (last ~150 lines per job, secrets masked as gh does). <code>base-ci</code> (tier read): the same workflow's latest completed run on the PR's base branch (dev or main), whether its jobs passed, and whether the failing job names on the PR head also fail there.</li><li>The gh calls go in <code>talos/lib/orchestrator/merge.py</code> next to <code>failed_jobs</code>, behind small functions.</li><li>Talos README (the <code>aga</code> tool): the verbs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests with stubbed gh output: no failed jobs, one failed job, base passing vs failing the same job. <code>agamemnonProtected</code> paths: manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> premise grants and role text (ci-premise issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "aga-file-bug", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "aga: file-bug verb (Agamemnon files a Bug for a failure already on the base branch)", "description": "<p>When CI fails on something already broken on the base branch (e.g. an earlier image preview test failing for every PR), the fix is a separate bug issue, after which the blocked PR merges the base branch and carries on. Agamemnon should be able to file that bug itself. This is a new, visible power, so it is tightly limited.</p><ul><li><code>verbs.py</code>: <code>file-bug</code> (new tier <code>file</code>, level VISIBLE, added to the tier list in <code>premise.json</code>). Args: <code>--title</code>, <code>--signature</code> (the failing job plus test name), <code>--body</code> (what fails, the log excerpt, the base commit where it also fails, the blocked issue).</li><li><code>tool.py</code>: create a Bug through the tracker (gaia-mcp, as Talos does elsewhere) in the blocked issue's project and milestone, priority high, assigned to the worker. The description opens with \\"Filed by Agent Agamemnon: blocks #N\\" and ends with acceptance criteria (the job passes on the base branch). Post a comment on the blocked issue linking it.</li><li>Refused when the base-ci read in this incident did not show the job failing on the base branch too; when the same signature already has an open Agamemnon-filed bug (link that one instead, recorded in the journal); or when <code>agaFileBugsPerDay</code> (agent.json, default 3) is reached.</li><li>Undo: none on GitHub. Undo sets the filed bug to won't fix with a comment.</li><li>Talos README: the verb and its limits.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for creation, every refusal, dedupe by signature, the daily cap and undo. <code>agamemnonProtected</code> paths: manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> holding and resuming the blocked issue (hold-until-done issue), fixing the bug (the worker does that like any issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["aga-ci-read"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "aga-hold-until-done", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "aga: hold-until-done verb, then merge the base branch and re-run CI", "description": "<p>After a bug blocking a PR is filed and fixed, the blocked issue must pick up the fix: merge the base branch into the PR branch (never a rebase) and let CI run again. Today a person does this. adt-4278 adds condition holds to the journal (<code>hold-until-docker</code>); this adds a second condition.</p><ul><li><code>verbs.py</code> + <code>tool.py</code>: <code>hold-until-done &lt;issue&gt;</code> (tier wait): the blocked issue stays with Agamemnon (it is in review with an open PR), and the journal hold has the condition \\"issue N done\\".</li><li><code>holds.py</code> <code>release_due</code>: when N is done (worker's <code>dependency_done_statuses</code>), run <code>update-branch</code> on the held issue's PR, the same as the verb (merge the base on GitHub; on a conflict, hand it to the conflict flow as today), reset its CI re-run count and leave it to the merge sweep. Comment \\"#N is done: merged the base branch into the PR, CI runs again\\". When N is won't fix or deferred, release the hold to the owner with a comment.</li><li>A hold older than <code>docker.holdMaxHours</code>'s sibling <code>holdMaxHours</code> (default 72) goes to the owner.</li><li>Talos README: the verb.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests: a release on done runs update-branch once and resets the count; won't fix releases to the owner; the 72h handover; undo releases the hold. <code>agamemnonProtected</code> paths: manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filing the bug (file-bug issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["adt-4278", "ci-rerun-fix"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ci-premise", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon: ci_failed triage tells temporary, PR-caused and base-branch failures apart", "description": "<p>With the CI reads, file-bug and hold-until-done in place, the <code>ci_failed</code> incident can move things along instead of re-running once and handing over.</p><ul><li><code>premise.json</code> <code>ci_failed</code>: tiers read, retry, wait, handoff, file, update, notify. \\"does\\": read ci-log and base-ci; temporary (timeouts, network, registry or GitHub 5xx, rate limits): rerun-ci within the 3 attempts; fails on the base branch too: file-bug (or link the open one), hold-until-done; caused by the PR's diff: send to the worker with the failing test and log excerpt.</li><li><code>role.md</code>: a CI section with these three cases, \\"never file a bug without base-ci showing the same failure\\", \\"merge the base, never rebase\\", and \\"escalate when the cause is unclear\\".</li><li><code>triage.py</code>: put the failed job names and the re-run count in the packet.</li><li><code>classifier.py</code>: CI handbacks from the merge sweep (\\"CI failed again after …\\", re-run errors) map to <code>ci_failed</code>; check the patterns against the real handbacks in the Talos log.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> premise loading and classifier tests, a triage prompt test showing the packet fields. Checked once on a real failing PR if one comes up, noted in the PR. <code>agamemnonProtected</code> paths: manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> stack containers that are down (e.g. Postgres) as an incident.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ci-rerun-fix", "aga-ci-read", "aga-file-bug", "aga-hold-until-done"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 07:57:40	2026-11-07 08:12:38	f
5854a5816aee-8611-5ba1-999303bf0514	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	6	{"summary": "Two small ezSearch bugs, one per problem. (1) The bar input is a FormFields::FieldText, so the global .form-field margin of 3rem applies to it and pushes the bar onto its own tall row; remove that margin for this field only, so the toolbar is one line. (2) The Saved Searches menu is right-aligned (AppUi::Dropdown's global right: 0), so on mobile it opens off-screen; inside ezSearch, open it from the button's left edge. Both changes apply only inside ezSearch; the global rules stay.", "issues": [{"key": "ez-input-margin", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: remove the 3rem form-field margin from the search bar input", "description": "<p>On the Issue list the ezSearch toolbar takes about three rows instead of one: the formatted query drops below the buttons and leaves empty space around it. Cause (found by the engineer): the bar's input (<code>data-field=\\"ez-search-input\\"</code>) is a <code>FormFields::FieldText</code>, which renders a <code>div.form-field</code> wrapper, and <code>styles/modules/form-fields.scss</code> l.11-13 gives every <code>.form-field</code> <code>margin: 3rem</code>. That margin is right for form layouts but not for this toolbar field.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In the ezSearch bar styles (<code>app/styles/components/ez-search-bar.scss</code>, scoped under the bar's root class), set the margin of the bar's <code>.form-field</code> to 0. Also remove any other form-layout spacing that makes the row taller, such as label space. Don't change the global <code>.form-field</code> rule or <code>FormFields::FieldText</code>.</li><li>Result: one row with Saved Searches, the bar filling the remaining width, then Builder, Search and Clear, vertically aligned. The coloured query sits inside the bar on its single underline, and the box header has the old toolbar's height (<code>docs/ui/screens/issue-list.png</code>).</li><li>An error message and the suggestion menu still show under the bar. Mobile (below 768px) still wraps to two rows (bar, then buttons), without extra gaps.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An integration test for <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> asserts that the bar's <code>.form-field</code> has no margin and that the bar and the Search button share one row (same top within a few px).</li><li>Other forms using <code>FieldText</code> (e.g. issue create) are unchanged.</li><li>Checked in the browser on the Issue list at desktop width and at 390px, with and without a query.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Saved Searches menu alignment (separate issue), long-query behaviour.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ez-saved-menu-align", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: Saved Searches menu opens off-screen on mobile", "description": "<p>On mobile the ezSearch Saved Searches menu opens to the left of its button, so most of it is outside the viewport. Cause: <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> positions <code>.app-dropdown-content</code> with <code>right: 0</code> (<code>app/styles/components/dropdown.scss</code> l.26), so the menu lines up with the button's right edge and grows leftwards. The Saved Searches button sits at the left edge of the screen. The menu should line up with the button's left edge and grow to the right.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In the ezSearch toolbar styles (<code>app/styles/components/ez-search.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.ez-search</code>), set the Saved Searches dropdown content to <code>left: 0; right: auto</code>, at every screen width (the button is always first in the toolbar).</li><li>Keep the menu inside the viewport on narrow screens: <code>max-width</code> of the toolbar's width, with long saved-search names wrapping or truncated with an ellipsis.</li><li>Don't change the global <code>.app-dropdown-content</code> rule: other dropdowns rely on it (<code>styles/modules/board.scss</code> ~l.49, <code>conversation.scss</code> ~l.359).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>At 390px and at desktop width the open menu's left edge lines up with the button's left edge, and the whole menu is visible.</li><li>Other <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> menus (board, conversation) are unchanged.</li><li>An integration test for <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> checks that the open menu's left edge is not left of the button's left edge.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> itself, the search bar margin (separate issue).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 07:25:12	2026-11-07 07:37:02	f
95a337c66aee-b0cf-b49a-ab98db7d11a2	f1592e496aee-cb3c-b49a-239fcfcb2381	1	{"summary": "A shared CodeRabbit review counter (rabbit-budget) that every tool checks before starting a CodeRabbit review. Once the daily allowance (25, last 24 hours) is used up, ai ship hands new PRs straight to the reviewer as in_review (ship-gate), the Talos review loop stops running fix rounds and hands off (loop-gate), and Agamemnon stops updating PRs that are behind and sending conflict fixes back through CodeRabbit (aga-gate). The three gates can be built in parallel once the counter exists.", "issues": [{"key": "rabbit-budget", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "ai rabbit budget: shared daily counter of CodeRabbit reviews", "description": "<p>CodeRabbit includes about 26 PR reviews a day; after that it charges per file, which is often not worth it. We need one count of the reviews our tools start, shared by ai, Talos and Agamemnon, so each can stop sending PRs to CodeRabbit once the allowance is used up.</p><ul><li>New module <code>ai/lib/rabbitbudget.py</code>: a ledger in <code>STATE_DIR</code> (<code>ai/lib/common.py</code>, under <code>LOCAL_DIR</code> so the runtime copy and the checkout share it) with entries <code>{at (UTC ISO), repo, pr, sha, source}</code>. Writes are atomic and safe across processes (reuse the dev-tools file lock helper if it is on main, else write-to-temp-then-replace under a lock file).</li><li>Functions: <code>used(now)</code> (entries in the last 24 hours, rolling window), <code>limit()</code>, <code>available(now)</code>, <code>record(repo, pr, sha, source)</code> (idempotent per repo+pr+sha+source), <code>next_free(now)</code> (when the oldest entry leaves the window). Entries older than 48 hours are pruned on write.</li><li>Config: <code>codeRabbitDailyBudget</code> in <code>ai/config.json</code>, default 25. 0 or a missing key means no limit.</li><li>CLI: <code>ai rabbit budget</code> prints used/limit/next free slot; <code>--json</code> prints <code>{used, limit, available, nextFree}</code> for Talos. <code>ai rabbit budget record --repo --pr --sha --source</code> records an entry (Talos and Agamemnon call ai through the CLI).</li><li>Unit tests: the rolling window, idempotent record, pruning, no limit, the JSON output.</li><li>Document it in <code>ai/README.md</code> next to the CodeRabbit section.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code> reports the reviews recorded in the last 24 hours; <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> reading the count from GitHub or CodeRabbit; the gates themselves (separate issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ship-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "ai ship: hand new PRs straight to the reviewer when the CodeRabbit budget is used up", "description": "<p>When the daily CodeRabbit allowance is used up, a new agent PR must not go to CodeRabbit: the issue goes to the reviewer as in_review instead of waiting for a review.</p><ul><li>In <code>ai/lib/ship.py</code> <code>cmd_ship</code> (~l.197, where <code>defer</code> is decided) and in the trigger comment adt-4245 adds to <code>workflow.open_pr</code>: for a repo where <code>coderabbit.enabled(repo)</code>, check <code>rabbitbudget.available()</code> first.</li><li>Available: post the trigger as today and <code>record(repo, pr, head sha, 'pr-opened')</code>.</li><li>Used up: don't post the trigger, don't defer the hand-off (the issue goes in_review, assigned to the reviewer via <code>pr_hand_off</code>), add a line to the tracker notes: <em>CodeRabbit budget used (N/25 in the last 24 hours): not sent to CodeRabbit, please review by hand.</em> Print the same message, saying to finish as <code>done</code>, not <code>awaiting_bot_review</code> (as the non-CodeRabbit branch already does).</li><li><code>ai pr</code> (<code>cmd_pr</code>) behaves the same.</li><li>Check that Odysseus' ship prompt and role (<code>talos/agents/odysseus/</code>) already follow that printed message; adjust the wording if they don't.</li><li>Unit tests with ody and the budget mocked: budget available → trigger posted, entry recorded, hand-off deferred; used up → no trigger, no entry, hand-off done, note present.</li><li>Update <code>ai/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the budget used up, <code>ai ship --defer-handoff</code> in gaia leaves the issue in_review, assigned to the reviewer, with the budget note and no CodeRabbit comment on the PR.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Talos loop and Agamemnon (separate issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-budget", "adt-4245"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "loop-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos CodeRabbit loop: no more bot rounds or re-entries when the budget is used up", "description": "<p>Each bot round pushes a fix, and CodeRabbit reviews every push again. Once the daily CodeRabbit allowance is used up, the loop must hand the issue to the reviewer instead of starting another review.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/bot_review.py</code>: read the budget through the ai CLI (<code>ai rabbit budget --json</code>, via <code>talos/lib/ai_cli.py</code> like <code>ai_rabbit</code>). In <code>Watcher.check_one</code>, when <code>next_step</code> returns RUN_ROUND and nothing is available, hand off instead (to the reviewer, never the merger route), with a comment: <em>CodeRabbit budget used: open CodeRabbit findings left for you.</em></li><li>When a round does start, record it (<code>ai rabbit budget record ... --source bot-round</code>).</li><li><code>Watcher.reenter</code> (after address-review in auto-merge milestones): with nothing available, don't re-enter: hand off to the reviewer with the same note. When it re-enters, record it.</li><li>If the budget can't be read (CLI error), treat it as available and log it, so a broken counter doesn't stall issues.</li><li>Unit tests in <code>talos/tests/test_bot_review.py</code>: round turned into a hand-off, reenter turned into a hand-off, round recorded, unreadable budget.</li><li>Update the CodeRabbit loop section of the Talos README.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the budget used up, an issue whose PR has CodeRabbit findings goes to the reviewer as in_review with the note, and no new commit is pushed.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> issues already waiting for a review that is in progress (they finish as today).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-budget"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "aga-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon: don't update or resend PRs through CodeRabbit when the budget is used up", "description": "<p>Agamemnon's keeper starts CodeRabbit reviews itself: it updates PRs that are behind their base on GitHub (new merge commit) and sends a resolved conflict back through CodeRabbit. Once the daily CodeRabbit allowance is used up, it must stop doing both and hand the issue to the engineer instead.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/orchestrator/keeper.py</code> <code>_update</code> (~l.86): with nothing available, skip the update-branch call (the PR stays behind; log it once per PR per day). When it does update, record it (<code>ai rabbit budget record ... --source update-branch</code>).</li><li><code>_conflict</code> / <code>_resolve</code> (~l.96-155): with nothing available, don't resolve the conflict and send the PR through CodeRabbit; hand the issue to the owner as in_review with a comment: <em>merge conflict, CodeRabbit budget used: please resolve and review by hand.</em> When it does resolve, record it.</li><li>Read the budget the same way as the Talos loop (ai CLI, JSON). An unreadable budget counts as available.</li><li>Check the Agamemnon premise and role (<code>talos/agents/agamemnon/</code>): mention the budget where they describe updating PRs and resolving conflicts.</li><li>Unit tests (see <code>talos/tests/test_agamemnon_conflicts.py</code>): update skipped, conflict handed off, both recorded when available.</li><li>Update <code>agamemnon/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the budget used up, Agamemnon's sweep pushes nothing to agent PRs, and a conflicting PR's issue lands with the owner as in_review with the note.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> auto-merge changes (a PR that skipped CodeRabbit never comes back clean, so it never reaches the merger).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-budget"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 09:59:49	2026-11-07 09:59:49	f
54043fb36aee-e6e4-0b34-d6db25262abd	f1592e496aee-cb3c-b49a-239fcfcb2381	4	{"summary": "With CodeRabbit's auto review turned off, the agents ask for every review themselves. A shared counter with a tier policy (rabbit-request) decides who reviews each PR: under 10 reviews in the last 24 hours CodeRabbit reviews everything, from 10 to 24 only large PRs, from 25 on everything goes to the human reviewer. It posts '@coderabbitai full review' as Agent Odysseus and records it. ai ship (ship-gate), the Talos fix-round loop (loop-gate) and Agamemnon's branch updates and conflict fixes (aga-gate) all go through it and hand the issue to the reviewer when it answers human. Agamemnon's sweep later sends those PRs to CodeRabbit once there is credit again (aga-backlog). Separately, Agamemnon sets an issue to done when a person merges its agent PR (merged-done). Only agent activity is counted; the engineer's own GitHub activity is not counted or limited. All issues go in milestone aga-agentic system.", "issues": [{"key": "rabbit-request", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "ai rabbit request: daily CodeRabbit counter with a tier policy that posts the review trigger", "description": "<p>CodeRabbit includes about 26 PR reviews a day; after that it charges per file. Its auto review is turned off, so the agents now ask for every review by posting a trigger comment as Agent Odysseus. This issue adds the one place that decides whether an agent PR goes to CodeRabbit or to the human reviewer, posts the trigger and counts it. Only these agent triggers are counted; reviews people request themselves on GitHub are neither counted nor limited.</p><ul><li>New <code>ai/lib/rabbitbudget.py</code>: a ledger in <code>STATE_DIR</code> (<code>ai/lib/common.py</code>; under <code>LOCAL_DIR</code>, so the runtime copy and the checkout share it). Two lists: <code>sent</code> <code>{at (UTC ISO), repo, pr, sha, source}</code> and <code>deferred</code> <code>{at, repo, pr, issue, files}</code> (PRs that went to the human because of the limit). Writes are atomic and safe across processes (lock file plus write-to-temp-then-replace). Prune <code>sent</code> entries older than 48 hours.</li><li>Policy, a pure function of (used in the rolling last 24 hours, hand-written file count, rereview flag, settings): <code>used &lt; everyPrUntil</code> → coderabbit; <code>used &lt; limit</code> → coderabbit when <code>rereview</code> or <code>files &gt;= largePrFiles</code>, else human; otherwise human.</li><li>Settings in <code>ai/config.json</code>: <code>codeRabbitBudget: {everyPrUntil: 10, limit: 25, largePrFiles: 6}</code> and <code>codeRabbitTrigger: \\"@coderabbitai full review\\"</code>. A missing <code>codeRabbitBudget</code> means no limit.</li><li><code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source pr-opened|bot-round|reenter|update-branch|conflict|backlog [--files N] [--rereview] [--issue N] [--json]</code>. For a repo where <code>coderabbit.enabled(repo)</code> is false it answers <code>absent</code>. It applies the policy. On coderabbit, it posts the trigger as Agent Odysseus (<code>ody(repo, 'gh', 'pr', 'comment', ...)</code>), records it in <code>sent</code> with the head sha, and drops any <code>deferred</code> entry for the PR. On human, it adds a <code>deferred</code> entry (only when <code>--issue</code> is given; one per PR). It prints, or returns as JSON, <code>{decision: coderabbit|human|absent, used, limit, reason}</code>. A failed comment means the decision is human, with the error in <code>reason</code>; nothing is recorded in <code>sent</code>.</li><li><code>ai rabbit budget [--json]</code>: used, limit, the current tier, when the next slot frees up, and the deferred list.</li><li>Unit tests (ody mocked): every tier boundary (9/10, 24/25), large vs small, rereview in the middle tier, rolling window, deferred added and cleared, failed comment, disabled repo.</li><li>Document both commands and the settings in <code>ai/README.md</code> (CodeRabbit section); say that CodeRabbit's auto review is expected to be off.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>ai rabbit request</code> posts exactly one <code>@coderabbitai full review</code> comment when the policy says coderabbit and records it; <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code> reports the rolling count and the deferred PRs; <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the callers (ai ship, Talos, Agamemnon: separate issues); counting reviews people trigger themselves; cheaper merge-check options.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ship-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "ai ship: ask ai rabbit request who reviews a new PR, hand it to the reviewer when it answers human", "description": "<p>CodeRabbit's auto review is off, so a new agent PR only gets a CodeRabbit review when <code>ai ship</code> asks for one. Depending on the daily count and the PR's size, the answer may be the human reviewer instead.</p><ul><li>In <code>ai/lib/ship.py</code> <code>cmd_ship</code>, after the PR is open (~l.195-200, where <code>defer</code> is decided today): for a CodeRabbit repo, call the <code>rabbitbudget</code> request logic with <code>source pr-opened</code>, <code>files</code> = the hand-written count <code>sizecheck.check</code> already returned, and the issue number.</li><li>On coderabbit: defer the hand-off as today (the issue stays in progress for the Talos loop).</li><li>On human: don't defer. <code>pr_hand_off</code> sets in_review and assigns the reviewer. Add to the tracker notes: <em>Not sent to CodeRabbit: N of 25 reviews used in the last 24 hours (small PRs go to you from 10). Please review by hand; CodeRabbit may add a review later when credit frees up.</em> Print that the session finishes as <code>done</code>, not <code>awaiting_bot_review</code> (like the existing branch for repos without CodeRabbit).</li><li>On resume, when <code>existing_pr</code> finds the PR, don't ask again if the pending hand-off or the ledger already has the PR.</li><li><code>ai pr</code> (<code>workflow.cmd_pr</code>) does the same, with the file count from the PR's changed files.</li><li>Check that Odysseus' ship prompt and role (<code>talos/agents/odysseus/</code>) follow the printed outcome; adjust the wording if needed.</li><li>Unit tests with the request logic mocked: coderabbit → deferred; human → handed off with the note; resume doesn't ask twice.</li><li>Update <code>ai/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with 12 reviews used, a 3-file gaia PR goes to the reviewer as in_review with the note and no trigger comment; an 8-file PR gets the trigger and stays with the agent.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fix rounds and Agamemnon (separate issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-request"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "loop-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos CodeRabbit loop: request a review after each fix round, hand off when the budget says human", "description": "<p>With CodeRabbit's auto review off, a fix round's push gets no review unless Talos asks for one, and the merge check needs a CodeRabbit result on the latest commit. Each follow-up review counts toward the daily limit.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/bot_review.py</code> <code>Watcher.check_one</code> (~l.204): when <code>next_step</code> returns RUN_ROUND, first read <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code> (through <code>talos/lib/ai_cli.py</code>, like <code>ai_rabbit</code>). If a follow-up review would be answered human (limit reached), don't run the round. Hand off to the reviewer (never the merger route) with the comment <em>CodeRabbit limit reached: open CodeRabbit findings left for you.</em></li><li>After a round ends with <code>awaiting_bot_review</code> (<code>dispatcher._await_bot_review</code> ~l.507, when rounds &gt; 0), call <code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source bot-round --rereview --issue N --json</code>. On human, hand off with the same note instead of waiting.</li><li><code>Watcher.reenter</code> (~l.157, after address-review in auto-merge milestones): call <code>ai rabbit request ... --source reenter --rereview</code>; on human, hand off to the reviewer instead of re-entering.</li><li>If the ai command fails, log it and hand off to the reviewer; don't wait for a review that was never requested.</li><li>Unit tests in <code>talos/tests/test_bot_review.py</code>: round skipped at the limit, request after a round, reenter to human, command failure.</li><li>Update the CodeRabbit loop section of the Talos README.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> each fix round's push gets exactly one trigger comment while under the limit; at the limit the issue goes to the reviewer as in_review with the note and no new commit.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the first review (ai ship), Agamemnon.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-request"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "aga-gate", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon: request a CodeRabbit review after branch updates and conflict fixes, or hand the issue to the owner", "description": "<p>Agamemnon's keeper pushes new commits to agent PRs: it updates PRs that are behind their base and sends resolved conflicts back for review. With CodeRabbit's auto review off, those commits get no review unless asked for, and the merge check (<code>ai/lib/mergegate.py</code> <code>gate</code>) needs a CodeRabbit result on the latest commit. Agamemnon must spend reviews through the shared counter and know when the limit is reached.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/orchestrator/keeper.py</code> <code>_update</code> (~l.86): before the update-branch call, read <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code>; at the limit, skip the update (log once per PR per day). After a successful update, call <code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source update-branch --rereview --issue N</code>.</li><li><code>_conflict</code> / <code>_resolve</code> (~l.96-155): at the limit, don't resolve; hand the issue to the owner as in_review with <em>merge conflict, CodeRabbit limit reached: please resolve and review by hand.</em> After a resolution is pushed, call <code>ai rabbit request ... --source conflict --rereview</code>. On human, hand off with the same note.</li><li>The premise and role (<code>talos/agents/agamemnon/</code>): add the budget (tiers, that each agent push needs a trigger, what happens at the limit, that the owner's own GitHub activity is not counted) where they describe updates, conflicts and merging.</li><li>An ai command failure means hand off to the owner, logged.</li><li>Unit tests (see <code>talos/tests/test_agamemnon_conflicts.py</code>): update skipped at the limit, request after update, conflict to the owner, request after resolution.</li><li>Update <code>agamemnon/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> at the limit, Agamemnon's sweep pushes nothing to agent PRs and conflicting PRs land with the owner with the note; under the limit, every push it makes is followed by one trigger comment.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> letting the merge check accept an earlier CodeRabbit pass after base-only merges; auto-merge itself (PRs that went to the human never come back clean).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-request"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "aga-backlog", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon: send PRs that went to the reviewer because of the limit to CodeRabbit once credit frees up", "description": "<p>When the daily CodeRabbit limit sends an agent PR to the human reviewer, it is recorded as deferred in the shared ledger. Once there is credit again, it should still get a CodeRabbit review to help the human; the issue stays with the human.</p><ul><li>In Agamemnon's sweep (<code>talos/lib/orchestrator/</code>, next to the keeper's sweep): read <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code>. For each deferred PR, oldest first, while the tier allows it (its stored file count against the tier, as for a new PR), call <code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source backlog --files N --issue N</code>. Stop at the first human answer.</li><li>Before sending, drop the entry without spending a review when the PR is closed or merged, or the issue is no longer in_review.</li><li>Comment on the issue when a review was requested: <em>CodeRabbit review requested now that credit is available; the issue stays with you.</em> Don't reassign it or start the Talos loop.</li><li>Agamemnon role: mention the backlog sending.</li><li>Unit tests: oldest first, stops at the tier, closed/merged/moved PRs dropped, the comment.</li><li>Update <code>agamemnon/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after the 24-hour window frees slots, deferred PRs that fit the tier get a trigger comment, oldest first; their issues stay assigned to the reviewer.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> giving the issue back to the agent to answer CodeRabbit's findings; notifications.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["rabbit-request", "ship-gate"], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "merged-done", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Agamemnon: set an agent issue done when a person merges its PR", "description": "<p>Agamemnon sets an issue done only after a merge it did itself (<code>talos/lib/orchestrator/merging.py</code> <code>_finish</code> ~l.152). More agent PRs will now go to the human reviewer, and when the reviewer merges one by hand on GitHub the issue stays in_review. Agamemnon should close the loop for those too.</p><ul><li>New sweep step in <code>talos/lib/orchestrator/</code> (its own small module, wired where the merge sweep is set up in <code>orchestrator/setup.py</code>): for in_review issues in the worker's projects assigned to the owner (<code>owners</code>), find the agent PR: branch <code>claude-issue-N</code>, author = the Agent Odysseus GitHub account (reuse the PR lookup the CodeRabbit watcher uses).</li><li>When that PR is merged and Agamemnon didn't merge it (no open/closed merge record in its store): set the issue done and comment <em>PR repo#N merged by &lt;GitHub login&gt;; set done.</em> This is worded differently from Agamemnon's own \\"merged automatically\\" comment, so a person's merge and an agent's merge are told apart.</li><li>Skip issues with no agent PR, with more than one open agent PR, or whose PR is closed without merging (leave those to the owner). Each step safe to repeat.</li><li>Agamemnon role and README: describe the step.</li><li>Unit tests: merged by a person → done + comment; merged by Agamemnon → untouched (its own flow); not merged, closed, no PR → untouched.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after the owner merges an agent PR on GitHub, the issue is done within one Agamemnon sweep, with the comment naming who merged it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> PRs not opened by Agent Odysseus; issues outside the worker's projects; webhooks (polling only).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-agentic system", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 10:37:08	2026-11-07 10:45:42	f
0fb2a8496aef-9bb6-9b16-7c7c8caa0908	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	7	{"summary": "ezSearch phase 3: move the last jQuery QueryBuilder users and remove the plugin. The Project list moves to <EzSearch> with the project schema, following the Issue list (aprom-4305). The generic admin module list (app.module) loses its jQuery search: no module defines 'filters' view metadata, so it can't work today. Both have acceptance tests. Then the removal: the npm packages and ember-cli-build imports, the old utils and component, the old search code and global keydown handler in controllers/prometheus/list.js, and the plugin's styles. The removal depends on both migrations.", "issues": [{"key": "ez-project-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project list: replace jQuery QueryBuilder with ezSearch", "description": "<p>ezSearch replaced jQuery QueryBuilder on the Issue list (aprom-4305). The Project list is one of the two remaining jQuery users; once it and the admin list are moved, the plugin can be removed. Follow aprom-4305's pattern exactly, using the <code>project</code> schema from <code>services/query-schema.js</code> (aprom-4295) and the saved-search arguments of <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> (aprom-4304).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>templates/app/projects/index.hbs</code> ~l.17-75: replace the Saved Searches dropdown, the readonly <code>FieldText</code>, Search, Clear and the <code>.list-view-filters</code> block (<code>{{query-builder module=\\"project\\"}}</code> and its Save Search button) with <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code>, wired as on the Issue list: <code>@schema</code>, <code>@query</code>, <code>@savedSearches</code>, <code>@activeSavedSearchId</code>, <code>@onSavedSearchChange</code>, <code>@onApply</code>, <code>@onSave</code> and <code>@aclContext=\\"project.read\\"</code>. No <code>@baseQuery</code>. Keep the save dialog in the page.</li><li><code>routes/app/projects/index.js</code>: load the schema with <code>query-schema</code> <code>load('project')</code> next to the saved searches (~l.178) and set <code>controller.querySchema</code>.</li><li><code>controllers/app/projects/index.js</code>:<ul><li>Remove the <code>metadata.filters</code> array (l.29-56).</li><li>Add <code>ezSavedSearches</code> (query from <code>searchquery</code>) and <code>selectSavedSearch(search|null)</code>.</li><li>Add a save path that saves the query from <code>@onSave</code> without <code>searchByRules</code>.</li><li>Clear goes through <code>applyQuery('')</code>, the action 4305 added to <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Check that the <code>project</code> schema covers today's filters (<code>Project.name</code>, <code>Project.shortCode</code>, <code>Project.status</code> with the <code>views.app.project.lists.status</code> values, <code>manager.name</code>). Fix it in <code>app/utils/query/schemas/project.js</code> if not.</li><li><code>mirage/route-handlers/project.js</code>: record the last <code>query</code> param in the scenario context, as 4305 did for issues.</li><li>Tests:<ul><li>Update <code>tests/acceptance/project/search-project-from-list.feature</code> and its steps.</li><li>New <code>tests/acceptance/project/ez-search-project-list.feature</code> + steps:<ol><li>Type <code>status:active manager in hammad</code> (or values that exist in the Mirage scenario), press Enter: the formatted query shows and is sent.</li><li>Accept a field suggestion with the keyboard.</li><li>Edit in the builder and see the bar update.</li><li>Load a saved search: the bar shows it and <code>searchId</code> is in the URL.</li><li>Show an error and send nothing.</li></ol></li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios pass.</li><li>The existing project list tests (render, mass update, select and navigate) pass.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px next to the Issue list.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> removing the plugin (separate issue), the generic admin list.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4304", "aprom-4305"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "module-list-search", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Generic module list: remove the jQuery search that has no filters", "description": "<p>The generic admin list (route <code>app.module</code>, path <code>/app/:module</code>) has a jQuery QueryBuilder search panel (<code>#builder</code>). It can't work: <code>controllers/app/module.js</code> <code>setupQuery</code> (~l.253) reads <code>MD.create().getViewMeta(this.module, 'filters', intl).enabledFilters</code>, and no module in <code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> defines <code>filters</code> view metadata. <code>getViewMeta</code> returns <code>false</code>, so the plugin gets no filters and throws. jQuery QueryBuilder is being removed (ezSearch replaces it on the Issue and Project lists), so this dead search goes first. The engineer chose removal over building an ezSearch schema from metadata that doesn't exist.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>templates/app/module.hbs</code> ~l.19-50: remove the search input (<code>text-field</code> with <code>populateQuery</code>/<code>openFilters</code>/<code>filter</code>), the <code>toggleFilters</code> button and the <code>.list-view-filters</code> row with <code>#builder</code> and its Search button. Keep the list, sorting and paging.</li><li><code>controllers/app/module.js</code>: remove <code>searchByRules</code>, <code>setupQuery</code>, <code>openFilters</code>, <code>toggleFilters</code> and <code>populateQuery</code>, the <code>filter</code> action if only the search used it, and the imports of <code>utils/query/parser</code> and <code>utils/query/builder</code>. <code>navigate</code> keeps passing <code>query</code> from the URL, so <code>?query=</code> still filters.</li><li>Acceptance test (<code>tests/acceptance/module/</code> + steps): visiting a module list that resolves to <code>app.module</code> renders the list and pages without errors, and a <code>?query=</code> in the URL is sent to the API. If no module can be reached through <code>app.module</code> with Mirage, write a controller unit test instead and say so in the PR (the route may be dead; don't delete it here).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>No references to <code>utils/query/builder</code>, <code>utils/query/parser</code> or <code>#builder</code> remain in the module list.</li><li>The test above passes.</li><li>The other lists are unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> an ezSearch schema for generic modules, removing the <code>app.module</code> route, removing the plugin (separate issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "remove-jquery-qb", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Remove jQuery QueryBuilder and the old query utils", "description": "<p>ezSearch now serves the Issue list (aprom-4305) and the Project list, and the generic module list no longer has a jQuery search. Nothing uses jQuery QueryBuilder any more, so remove it with its helpers, the old search code and its styles.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>package.json</code>: remove <code>jQuery-QueryBuilder</code> (l.107) and <code>jquery-extendext</code> (l.105), and update the lockfile. <code>ember-cli-build.js</code>: remove both <code>app.import</code> lines (l.45-46). Keep <code>jquery</code> itself.</li><li>Delete <code>app/utils/query/builder.js</code>, the old <code>app/utils/query/parser.js</code> (not ezSearch's <code>parse.js</code>), <code>app/utils/metadata/querybuilder-operators.js</code> and <code>app/components/query-builder.js</code> (and its template if there is one).</li><li><code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>:<ul><li>Remove the imports of the old builder and parser.</li><li>Remove <code>searchByRules</code>, <code>openFilters</code>, the <code>_searchRulesHandler</code> property (~l.147-152) and the global <code>keydown</code> listener it adds.</li><li>Remove <code>queryBuilder.clear()</code> from <code>clearSearch</code>, or drop <code>clearSearch</code> if no template uses it any more.</li><li>Remove the <code>send('searchByRules')</code> in <code>showSaveSearchDialog</code>, or drop that action if unused.</li></ul>Keep <code>applyQuery</code>, <code>applySearch</code>, <code>toggleSearch</code> and <code>isSearchActive</code> if the lists still use them.</li><li>Styles: remove the \\"jQuery query Builder custom styles\\" block in <code>app/styles/modules/document.scss</code> (~l.456-466) and the <code>.query-builder</code> rules in <code>app/styles/modules/module.scss</code> (~l.11-46). Remove <code>.dropToggle</code> (<code>document.scss</code> ~l.360) only if nothing uses it any more. Keep the <code>.search</code> block (<code>document.scss</code> ~l.329): the ezSearch toolbar uses it.</li><li>Search the app for any remaining reference (<code>queryBuilder</code>, <code>query-builder</code>, <code>getRules</code>, <code>metadata.filters</code>, <code>.list-view-filters</code>) and remove it. The generated YUIDoc in <code>docs/</code> is left as is.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The app builds without the two packages.</li><li>No source references to the plugin or the deleted files remain.</li><li>The full test suite passes, including the Issue and Project list ezSearch acceptance tests.</li><li>Issue list, Project list and a generic module list checked in the browser: no console errors.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> board, Gantt and calendar search (later phase), regenerating <code>docs/</code>.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ez-project-list", "module-list-search"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 12:26:55	2026-11-07 12:26:55	f
f281d8936aef-218c-aab1-369e2150ba48	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	11	{"summary": "EzSearchCompact on two more views. Gantt Cal gets the multi-row compact search at the top of its task list (it has no search UI today, only ?query=), with the Issue search metadata and the project's issue saved searches. Task Board replaces its saved-search dropdown and its client-side text filter with the linear compact search in the milestone tabs row; searching becomes server-side through the existing query and searchId parameters. Both use the saved-search service, and the two issues run in parallel.", "issues": [{"key": "ez-gantt", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Gantt Cal: search with EzSearchCompact", "description": "<p>The Gantt Cal has no search UI: it only honours a <code>?query=</code> URL parameter, which the route ANDs into each milestone's issue query (<code>routes/app/project/gantt.js</code> ~l.53-82, controller <code>queryParams = ['query']</code> ~l.130). Add <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> (aprom-4333, multi-row, the default) at the top of the task list. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>components/app-ui/gantt-chart.hbs</code>: add a named block (e.g. <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code>) rendered at the top of <code>.gantt-task-list</code>, above <code>.gantt-header</code>. The chart knows nothing about search. In <code>styles/modules/gantt.scss</code>, keep the task rows and the timeline rows aligned when the block is present: the timeline side gets the same top offset, or the block sits outside both scroll areas. Check the row alignment in the browser.</li><li><code>templates/app/project/gantt.hbs</code>: pass <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact @schema @query @savedSearches @activeSavedSearchId @onSavedSearchChange @onApply @onSave @onUpdateSavedSearch @aclContext=\\"issue.read\\" /&gt;</code> in that block, plus the save dialog as on the Issue list. No <code>@baseQuery</code>: the route adds milestone and project.</li><li><code>routes/app/project/gantt.js</code>: load the Issue schema (<code>query-schema</code> <code>load('Issue', {projectId})</code>, metadata <code>views.Issue.search</code>) and the project's issue saved searches through <code>services/saved-search.js</code> (<code>relatedTo: 'issue'</code>, <code>projectId</code>, shared with the Issue list).</li><li><code>controllers/app/project/gantt.js</code>: add <code>searchId</code> to <code>queryParams</code>. Apply, select, save and update go through the saved-search service. Don't copy list-controller code. Live-sync reloads keep the active query.</li><li>Acceptance (<code>tests/acceptance/gantt/</code> + steps, Mirage issue handler already records the query):<ol><li>Type and run a query: issues are requested with it ANDed with milestone and project, and <code>?query=</code> is set.</li><li>Remove a chip: it re-runs.</li><li>Apply a saved search: its name shows.</li><li>An error shows and nothing is sent.</li></ol></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios pass.</li><li>The existing Gantt tests (drag, resize, dependencies, issue panel, live sync) pass.</li><li>Task rows and timeline rows stay aligned with the search present.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filtering milestones (the query applies to issues), the Calendar view, the Task Board.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4333", "aprom-4331"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["gantt-compact"]}, {"key": "ez-board", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task Board: search with EzSearchCompact (linear)", "description": "<p>The Task Board has two separate filters in the milestone tabs row (<code>components/app-ui/task-board.hbs</code> ~l.37-62):</p><ul><li>a Saved Searches <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code>, whose state lives in the component (<code>activeSearch</code>, <code>filterQuery</code>, <code>toggleSearch</code>, <code>isSearchActive</code>, <code>task-board.js</code> ~l.26-163) and which applies through <code>@applySearch</code> to the controller's <code>query</code>/<code>searchId</code> URL parameters (<code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> ~l.833; the route ANDs the query into each lane's issue query);</li><li>a free-text <code>&lt;Input&gt;</code> that hides loaded cards in the browser (<code>task-board/issues-provider.js</code> ~l.32: subject, description, number).</li></ul><p>Replace both with <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact @linear={{true}}&gt;</code> (aprom-4333). There is one search model, so typed text runs on the server (bare words become <code>Issue.subject CONTAINS …</code>) and the lanes reload. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>task-board.hbs</code>: replace the dropdown and the <code>&lt;Input&gt;</code> in <code>.milestone-filters</code> with <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact @linear={{true}} @schema @query @savedSearches @activeSavedSearchId @onSavedSearchChange @onApply @onSave @onUpdateSavedSearch @aclContext=\\"issue.read\\" /&gt;</code>, all passed in from the page.<ul><li>It stays at the right of the tabs row with a sensible minimum width (about 32rem).</li><li>Below the md breakpoint it wraps onto its own full-width row under the tabs (screen <code>board-linear-mobile</code>).</li></ul></li><li><code>task-board.js</code>: remove <code>query</code>, <code>filterQuery</code>, <code>activeSearch</code>, <code>toggleSearch</code>, <code>isSearchActive</code> and the constructor's saved-search lookup. Remove the client text filter from <code>issues-provider.js</code> and <code>milestones.hbs</code> (<code>@query</code>). <code>initialize-sortable</code> receives <code>query</code> to re-attach Sortable when the cards change; make sure lanes re-rendered by the route reload still get Sortable (drag still works after a search).</li><li><code>templates/app/project/board.hbs</code>, <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code>, <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code>:<ul><li>Load the Issue schema (<code>query-schema</code> <code>load('Issue', {projectId})</code>) and the issue saved searches through <code>services/saved-search.js</code> (<code>relatedTo: 'issue'</code>, <code>projectId</code>), replacing the route's own saved-search queries (~l.161-166).</li><li>Apply, select, save and update go through the service, and set <code>query</code>/<code>searchId</code> as <code>applySearch</code> does now.</li><li>Add the save dialog as on the Issue list.</li><li>Hermes live updates keep the active query.</li></ul></li><li><code>styles/modules/board.scss</code>: the placement and wrap rules, scoped.</li><li>Tests: update <code>tests/acceptance/taskboard/filter-issues.feature</code> and its steps:<ol><li>Typing <code>subject words</code> and pressing Enter requests every lane with <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS 'subject words')</code>.</li><li>Applying a saved search shows its name and sets <code>searchId</code>.</li><li>Clear resets.</li><li>Cards can still be dragged after a search.</li></ol></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios pass.</li><li>The other Task Board tests (quick create, status update, milestone create and complete) pass.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width with several milestone tabs, and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> keeping an instant client-side card filter, the planning view, the Gantt.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4333", "aprom-4331"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["board-linear", "board-linear-mobile"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-07 19:50:10	2026-11-07 19:50:10	f
746f69196af4-a328-1af5-c06fddda2d7b	e66181d96af4-7c69-1af5-a7b779ce5171	1	{"summary": "Paginate the Project Milestones box on the project dashboard in the browser, 5 per page, using the shared Pagination component. The route already loads every milestone and the chart filter needs them all, so there is no Gaia change. One Prometheus issue.", "issues": [{"key": "milestones-pagination", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project dashboard: paginate the Project Milestones box (5 per page)", "description": "<p>The Project Milestones box on the project dashboard (<code>app/templates/app/project/index.hbs</code>, <code>project-milestones-section</code>, in the col-md-4 side column) lists every milestone of the project. On projects with many milestones the box runs far down the page. Paginate it in the browser using the existing shared <code>Pagination</code> component.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>The route <code>routes/app/project/index.js</code> keeps loading all milestones (<code>limit: -1</code>, sort <code>Milestone.startDate</code> DESC). The estimated-vs-spent chart filter (<code>milestonesByDateCreatedDesc</code>) and the per-milestone issue counts need the full list. No API change.</li><li>In <code>controllers/app/project/index.js</code>, track the current milestone page and add a getter for the visible slice (page size 5, in the list's existing order). Add an <code>onPageChange({page, pageSize})</code> action that sets the page and returns <code>{ hasMore }</code>. The getter must react to the <code>milestones</code> list, so milestones added through <code>saveMilestone</code> or edited show up without a reload.</li><li>In the milestones <code>box-body</code>, wrap the <code>{{#each}}</code> of <code>Project::Milestones</code> in <code>&lt;Pagination @pageSize={{5}} @onPageChange=... @containerClass=\\"project-milestones-pagination\\"&gt;</code>. Use the <code>&lt;:center&gt;</code> block to show <code>first – last / total</code> (e.g. <code>1 – 5 / 14</code>) from a translation in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Render the pager only when there are more than 5 milestones. Keep the <code>Exceptions::NothingFound</code> empty state as it is.</li><li>After adding a milestone, the total and the › button update. If the current page becomes empty (should not happen today; there is no delete), fall back to the last page.</li><li>Only add styles if needed, scoped under <code>.project-milestones-section</code> in <code>styles/modules/project.scss</code>, and follow the design system (square edges, existing colours).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>With 14 milestones the box shows the first 5, the footer reads <code>1 – 5 / 14</code>, ‹ is disabled, and › moves to <code>6 – 10 / 14</code>. The last page shows <code>11 – 14 / 14</code> with › disabled.</li><li>With 5 or fewer milestones there is no pager. With none, the existing empty state shows.</li><li>Adding a milestone through the + dialog updates the total right away. The edit pencil and the milestone links still work on every page.</li><li>The estimated-vs-spent chart filter still lists all milestones.</li><li>Tests: an integration or acceptance test (Mirage, 14 milestones) covering page 1, next, last page and no pager at ≤5. Each test fails if the slicing is reverted.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: server-side paging of milestones, a page-size selector, filtering by status, and reducing the full milestone/issue load on this route.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["milestones-paginated"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-11 09:59:16	2026-11-11 09:59:16	f
dbc8e9356af5-dbba-d19d-a8f35dec595b	8870b9e26af5-dbba-d19d-df4cdc28a203	1	{"summary": "One Gaia fix, written as a request from A Prometheus. Upload reads (GET /upload, GET /upload/:id) return fileThumbnail as a base64 data URI, the same as issue reads with included uploads. Today they return the raw 0/1 flag. The preview modal's token request then overwrites the thumbnail in the Ember store with \\"1\\", so the thumbnail breaks after the modal closes. Prometheus needs no change.", "issues": [{"key": "upload-read-thumbnail", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Uploads: return fileThumbnail as a data URI on upload reads, not the raw 0/1 flag", "description": "<p><strong>Request from A Prometheus.</strong> On the issue detail page, clicking an attachment opens the preview modal (<code>Issue::FilePreview</code>). The modal fetches a one-time token with <code>GET /api/v1/upload/:id?download=true</code>. Ember Data merges that response into the same <code>upload</code> record the attachment list uses. The response has <code>fileThumbnail: \\"1\\"</code> (the raw DB flag), not the base64 data URI the issue read returned. So after the modal closes, the thumbnail renders as <code>&lt;img src=\\"1\\"&gt;</code> and shows as a broken image. Prometheus needs <code>fileThumbnail</code> to mean the same thing on every read.</p><p><strong>Cause:</strong> <code>FilethumbComponent::afterRead</code> (<code>app/api/v1/controllers/components/FilethumbComponent.php</code>) only converts upload entries in <code>finalData['included']</code>. <code>IssueController</code> and <code>WikiController</code> use it, but <code>UploadController</code> (<code>$uses = ['Fileattachment']</code>, custom <code>getAction</code>/<code>listAction</code>) does not. Its reads return the smallint flag.</p><p><strong>Proposed change</strong> (please accept, adapt or decline):</p><ul><li>Extend <code>FilethumbComponent::afterRead</code> so it also converts <code>type == 'upload'</code> entries in <code>finalData['data']</code>, handling both a list and a single resource. Move the conversion into one private method shared by <code>data</code> and <code>included</code>.</li><li>Add <code>'Filethumb'</code> to <code>UploadController::$uses</code>. Check that <code>getAction</code> and <code>listAction</code> fire <code>rest:afterRead</code> after <code>finalData</code> is built (<code>getAction</code> does; verify <code>listAction</code>). The <code>downloadLink</code> attribute must still be returned.</li><li>If the thumbnail file under <code>filesystem/uploads/thumbnail/thumb_&lt;id&gt;.jpg</code> is missing or unreadable, return <code>\\"0\\"</code> (the value the UI already reads as \\"no thumbnail\\") instead of a data URI of an empty string. Apply the same rule to issue and wiki reads.</li><li>Keep the <code>\\"0\\"</code>/null behaviour for uploads without a thumbnail.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li><code>GET /upload/:id</code> and <code>GET /upload/:id?download=true</code> for an image with a thumbnail return <code>fileThumbnail</code> starting with <code>data:</code>, identical to the value in the issue read's <code>included</code>.</li><li><code>GET /upload</code> (list) does the same for every upload with a thumbnail.</li><li>Uploads without a thumbnail, or whose thumbnail file is missing, return <code>\\"0\\"</code>.</li><li>Issue and wiki reads are unchanged except for the missing-file case.</li><li>A test (api-tester case and/or unit test) fails before the fix and passes after. gaia-dev graph and generated docs are refreshed (the <code>uses</code> list of <code>upload</code> changes).</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing the flag/data-URI field with a thumbnail URL endpoint, and any Prometheus changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-12 14:40:27	2026-11-12 14:40:27	f
be1240786aef-6ee9-711b-4a4cc54c0f40	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	14	{"summary": "One bug: on the Task Board the lane headers (.board .lane .box-header, z-index 999) show above ezSearch's suggestion menu. Give the ezSearch menus a z-index above 999 and make sure no ancestor (the board's .milestone-filters slot, the compact search's input group) puts them in a lower stacking context.", "issues": [{"key": "ez-menu-zindex", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task Board: lane headers show above the ezSearch suggestion menu", "description": "<p>On the Task Board the lane headers draw over ezSearch's suggestion menu, so the menu is hidden behind them. The lane headers have <code>z-index: 999</code> (<code>.board .lane .box-header</code>, <code>app/styles/modules/board.scss</code> ~l.81-86). The menu has <code>z-index: 1000</code> (<code>.ez-search-menu</code>, <code>app/styles/components/ez-search-bar.scss</code> ~l.56-64), so one of its ancestors most likely creates a stacking context below the lanes: the board's absolutely positioned <code>.milestone-filters</code> slot (aprom-4339), or the compact search's input group (Bootstrap sets <code>position: relative</code> and small z-indexes there).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Find the ancestor that traps the menu (browser devtools: stacking context of <code>.ez-search-menu</code>) and fix it there:<ul><li>The board's search slot (<code>.board .milestone-filters</code>) gets its own <code>z-index</code> above 999, so everything inside it (suggestion menu, Saved menu, Filter badge menu) stacks above the lanes.</li><li>Inside ezSearch, no wrapper sets a z-index lower than the menu's.</li></ul></li><li>The ezSearch menus (suggestions in <code>ez-search-bar.scss</code>, and the Saved dropdown in the compact and full toolbars) keep a z-index above 999, kept as one shared value in the ezSearch styles rather than repeated numbers.</li><li>Don't lower the lane headers' 999: they rely on it to stay over the cards.</li><li>Modals (the compact builder) are unaffected: Bootstrap modals sit at body level at 1050.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A Task Board acceptance or integration check: with the suggestion menu open, <code>document.elementFromPoint</code> at a menu item's centre, where it overlaps a lane header, returns the menu item.</li><li>In the browser on the Task Board, the suggestion menu and the Saved menu show fully above the lane headers and cards.</li><li>The Issue list, the idea list and the Gantt are unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the lane headers' own z-index, the menu colours (aprom-4343).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4339", "aprom-4343"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 00:22:22	2026-11-08 00:25:25	f
5e20cb446aef-1a22-399b-5f26e1625466	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	15	{"summary": "Three ezSearch bugs. (1) In the suggestion menu, a row whose field id wraps onto a second line is only half highlighted, leaving the id white on white: highlight the whole row. (2) In both Saved menus, hovering turns the text white but keeps a transparent background: give hover/focus the crimson background. (3) On the Task Board the compact builder modal sits under the backdrop because it renders inside the board's search slot: render it at body level, like the idea screen preview does.", "issues": [{"key": "ez-menu-row-highlight", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: two-line suggestion rows are only half highlighted", "description": "<p>In the suggestion menu, when a row's label and field id don't fit on one line (e.g. \\"Milestone\\" + <code>issuemilestone.name</code> in a narrow column), the id wraps below. The highlight (crimson background, white text, aprom-4343) only covers the first line, so the id is white on white. Cause: the id is <code>float: right</code> (<code>.ez-search-item-detail</code>, <code>app/styles/components/ez-search-bar.scss</code> ~l.91), and the row's <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> (<code>app/components/ez-search/search-bar.hbs</code> ~l.29-33) doesn't contain the float, so the wrapped id falls outside the highlighted box.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Lay out each row's <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> so it always contains both parts, e.g. <code>display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap</code>, with the detail no longer floated (it goes to the right when it fits, below the label when it doesn't).</li><li>The whole row, both lines, gets the active/hover background, and both texts turn white.</li><li>Long ids wrap (<code>overflow-wrap: anywhere</code>) rather than overflow.</li><li>No markup change is needed beyond what the layout requires. Keep it in <code>ez-search-bar.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.ez-search-menu</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An integration test renders the menu at 240px wide, makes a row with a long id active, and asserts that the id's bounding box lies inside the row's <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> box.</li><li>In the browser, the idea list (narrow) and the Task Board both highlight the whole row with readable text.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Saved menus, menu content.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ez-saved-hover", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: Saved menu items turn white on hover without a highlight", "description": "<p>In the Saved searches menu (both <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code>), hovering an item turns its text white but the background stays transparent, so the item disappears. Cause: the shared dropdown gives hovered items a crimson background and white text (<code>app/styles/components/dropdown.scss</code> ~l.44-49, <code>.app-dropdown .app-dropdown-content &gt; *:hover</code>). The ezSearch styles reset the item buttons to <code>background: transparent</code> with a more specific selector, so the background is lost while the white text stays:</p><ul><li><code>.ez-search-compact-saved .app-dropdown-content button</code>, <code>app/styles/components/ez-search-compact.scss</code> ~l.62-68;</li><li><code>.ez-search .ez-search-saved .dropdown-menu button</code>, <code>app/styles/components/ez-search.scss</code> ~l.90-97.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In both places keep the transparent reset for the normal state only, and add <code>:hover</code> and <code>:focus</code> (keyboard) with <code>$primaryColor</code> background and white text, matching <code>dropdown.scss</code>.</li><li>Share one rule (or a mixin) for both menus instead of two copies.</li><li>The active search keeps its <code>fa-check</code>, and its icon stays visible on hover. Disabled entries, if any, get no highlight.</li><li>The Update, Save as new, Revert and Save current search entries behave the same.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An integration test, for both components: a focused saved item has the crimson background and white text (computed styles).</li><li>Checked in the browser with the mouse and the keyboard on the Issue list (full) and the idea list and Task Board (compact).</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the suggestion menu, menu alignment.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ez-compact-modal-body", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task Board: the ezSearch Filter modal opens behind the overlay", "description": "<p>On the Task Board, clicking Filter in the compact search opens the builder modal under the dark overlay, so it can't be used. It works on the idea list. Cause: <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> renders its <code>bootstrap-modal</code> inline inside the component (<code>app/components/ez-search-compact/index.hbs</code> ~l.82-97). On the board the component sits in <code>.milestone-filters</code>, which has its own stacking level (aprom-4344, needed for the suggestion menu). The modal is trapped inside it, while Bootstrap's backdrop is added to <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> and covers it.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Render the builder modal at body level with <code>{{#in-element}}</code>, the same way <code>app/components/idea/message-screen.hbs</code> ~l.11 renders its screen modal (<code>{{#in-element this.modalRoot insertBefore=null}}</code>, with <code>modalRoot</code> resolved in the component class). The modal then works in any container, whatever its stacking.</li><li>Check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> in any async close path. Closing (Cancel, Search, Clear, Esc, backdrop click) still removes the modal and the backdrop. Focus returns to the Filter button.</li><li>Check <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code>'s own modals (save dialog pages) aren't affected. They are rendered by pages, outside the search.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An acceptance test on the Task Board: open Filter, and the modal's dialog element is the top element at its centre (<code>document.elementFromPoint</code>). Add a condition and Search: the query applies and the modal and backdrop are gone.</li><li>The same flow still works on the idea list and the Gantt.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing <code>bootstrap-modal</code> itself, the board's z-index values.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4344"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 00:46:22	2026-11-08 00:48:40	f
2af305b36aef-4618-07ee-667ce0a57d0a	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	16	{"summary": "One Gantt Cal bug: since the search was added (aprom-4337) the timeline side (Days/Weeks tabs and date header) starts below the search's height, leaving an empty band at the top right. Make the chart's top one header band: tabs aligned with the top of the search, date header aligned with the task list's column header, so rows stay aligned with no extra space above the tabs.", "issues": [{"key": "gantt-header-align", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Gantt Cal: timeline starts below the search, leaving empty space at the top", "description": "<p>Since aprom-4337 put the compact search at the top of the Gantt's task list, the whole timeline side (the Days/Weeks tabs <code>.gantt-time-scale-selector</code> and the date header <code>AppUi::GanttChart::TimelineHeader</code>) is pushed down by the search block's height. That leaves an empty band at the top right. 4337's description asked for exactly that offset to keep task rows and timeline rows aligned, and it was the wrong approach. The engineer wants the timeline to start at the top, level with the top of the filter.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In <code>components/app-ui/gantt-chart.hbs</code> and <code>app/styles/modules/gantt.scss</code>, remove the top offset 4337 added to the timeline side.</li><li>Make the chart's top one header band across both columns:<ul><li>Left: the <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> block at the top, the <code>.gantt-header</code> column row (Milestone / Start - End) at the bottom.</li><li>Right: the Days/Weeks tabs at the top, level with the top of the search; the timeline date header at the bottom, level with the left column row.</li></ul>For example, a shared header row (grid or flex with <code>align-items: stretch</code>) where each side puts its column or date header at the bottom (<code>margin-top: auto</code>).</li><li>Any extra height (the search is taller than the tabs) sits between the tabs and the date header on the right, never above the tabs. When the chips row is empty, the band is no taller than the left side needs.</li><li>Task rows and timeline rows stay aligned row for row, also while the chips row appears or disappears (applying or clearing a search), and after switching Days/Weeks.</li><li>The issue panel mode (<code>gantt-timeline-hidden</code>), scrolling (slimscroll on <code>.gantt-tasks</code>, horizontal timeline scroll) and the scale conversion overlay are unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An integration or acceptance check:<ul><li>The top of the Days/Weeks tabs equals the top of the search block (within 2px).</li><li>The bottom of the left column header row equals the bottom of the timeline date header.</li><li>The first task row and the first timeline row share the same top. This holds with no search applied and with chips showing.</li></ul></li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the search itself, the Task Board.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4337"], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 01:32:27	2026-11-08 01:34:05	f
aa243df96af0-d214-00cd-6d59c33d79cc	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	4	{"summary": "Fixes and follow-ups after QuickList shipped (aprom-4350..4359). Pagination never shows on the idea browser because no total is known. Following the engineer's architecture decision, Prometheus asks Gaia for one row more than the page size, shows the page size, and the extra row means a next page exists (list-page style 1-20 / 20+): a page-window helper, pagination without a total, and an ADR. Two idea issues apply the engineer's decisions: a search lists open ideas only unless 'show archived' is on, with server order only, and 'show archived' moves into the URL. One bug fixes the crimson-on-crimson Group/Sort menu hover, plus five small follow-ups from the review notes. No Gaia change.", "issues": [{"key": "ql-ideas-pager", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: pagination never shows; page by fetching one extra row (limit + 1) and record the decision", "description": "<p>The idea browser (aprom-4359) shows no ‹ › pagination, while Settings &gt; Developer &gt; UI does. Gaia's list response has no total (<code>meta.count</code> is the rows on this page only), so the browser falls back to counting the loaded ideas, <code>@total</code> is never above 20, and <code>QuickList::Pagination</code> hides because everything seems to fit on one page.</p><p><strong>Architecture decision (engineer, 2026-11-08):</strong> Prometheus never asks for totals or runs count queries to page. To show N rows it asks Gaia for N + 1. If N + 1 rows come back, there is a next page and only N are shown; fewer means this is the last page. One extra row costs nothing, while a count query (with joins) is wasted work.</p><ul><li>New pure helper <code>app/utils/quick-list/page-window.js</code>: <code>requestLimit(pageSize)</code> returns <code>pageSize + 1</code>, and <code>pageWindow(records, pageSize)</code> returns <code>{ items: first pageSize records, hasNext: records.length &gt; pageSize }</code>. Unit tests.</li><li><code>QuickList::Pagination</code> (<code>components/quick-list/pagination.{hbs,js}</code>) and the root <code>QuickList</code>: new <code>@hasNext</code>; <code>@total</code> becomes optional. Without a total, show the list-page style <code>1-20 / 20+</code> when there's a next page and <code>21-25 / 25</code> on the last page; enable ‹ when page &gt; 1 and › when <code>@hasNext</code>; hide only on page 1 with no next page. The header count uses the same text. With a total, behaviour is unchanged (the dev showcase keeps working).</li><li>Idea browser (<code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code>, <code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>): request <code>limit = requestLimit(20)</code>, render <code>pageWindow(...).items</code>, pass <code>@hasNext</code>; drop the total fallback that counts loaded ideas and any count queries used for paging.</li><li>Record the decision in <code>prometheus/docs/architecture/lists/decisions.md</code> (new; same format as <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md</code>): context, the limit + 1 rule, why not totals, and the helper to use.</li><li>Mirage idea handler: honour <code>limit</code> as sent (it may return limit rows of the N + 1 asked).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: with 25 ideas the browser shows <code>1-20 / 20+</code> with › enabled, then <code>21-25 / 25</code> with › disabled; the request carries <code>limit=21</code>. Unit tests for the helper, integration tests for pagination without a total, acceptance test for the browser.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: other lists (they adopt the helper when they move to QuickList).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ideas-search-open", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: a search lists open ideas only unless \\"show archived\\" is on; server order only", "description": "<p>Today a search in the idea browser matches every status, and when search or \\"show archived\\" is on, the browser lists open ideas before archived ones within each page. With server paging, that reordering makes the rows disagree with the pages (aprom-4356/4359 notes). Engineer's decision: a search returns open ideas only unless \\"show archived\\" is on, and the order comes only from the server.</p><ul><li>In the idea query (<code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> / <code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code>): always AND <code>(Idea.status : open)</code> with the search unless show archived is on; with show archived, no status condition.</li><li>Remove the client-side open-before-archived ordering; render the page in the order Gaia returns.</li><li>Keep the \\"show archived\\" toggle visible during a search (today it's hidden then), so archived ideas can still be found.</li><li>Update the idea browser acceptance tests (search hides archived ideas; with show archived the search finds them; order follows the sort).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: as above; the request's query carries the status condition when show archived is off.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: putting show archived in the URL (separate issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ideas-archived-url", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: keep \\"show archived\\" in the URL", "description": "<p>\\"Show archived\\" in the idea browser is controller state only (aprom-4356), so a reload or a shared link drops it. Engineer's decision: put it in the URL like <code>group</code>, <code>sort</code> and <code>page</code>.</p><ul><li>New query param <code>archived</code> (boolean, default false) on the idea controller, used by the footer toggle and the idea query; the route refreshes the list when it changes (page back to 1).</li><li>Links inside the idea area (<code>linkQuery</code>, the idea page links) keep it. Reset it with the other list params when leaving the idea area.</li><li>Acceptance test: turn show archived on, reload, archived ideas are still listed and the toggle shows \\"Hide archived\\".</li></ul>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ql-menu-hover", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: selected Group/Sort option is invisible on hover (crimson on crimson)", "description": "<p>In the QuickList toolbar (<code>QuickList::Toolbar</code>, aprom-4353), the current Group by / Sort option is marked with crimson text. On hover, the dropdown's hover rule (<code>styles/components/dropdown.scss</code>, crimson background) applies, but the marker colour wins over the hover's white text, so the option becomes a blank crimson bar (seen on Settings &gt; Developer &gt; UI with \\"None\\" selected). It's the same kind of bug as aprom-4346 (Saved menus).</p><ul><li>In <code>app/styles/components/quick-list/_toolbar.scss</code>, keep the crimson marker only at rest. On <code>:hover</code> and <code>:focus</code> the selected option (text, check and order icon) uses the same white text as the other hovered options. Don't change <code>dropdown.scss</code> globally.</li><li>Check the Sort menu as well as Group by, with keyboard focus too.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: hovering or focusing the selected option shows white text and icon on crimson in both menus; other options are unchanged. A test asserts the hovered/focused selected option gets the white-text rule.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ideas-creator-unknown", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: \\"Created by\\" group shows the raw user id when the creator isn't loaded", "description": "<p>In the idea browser (aprom-4359), grouping by Created by reads creator names with a synchronous peek of the <code>createdBy</code> relation. When it isn't loaded, the group heading (and the row's secondary line) shows the raw user id.</p><ul><li>Fall back to a translated \\"Unknown user\\" (<code>translations/en-us.json</code>) instead of the id, in both the group label and the secondary line.</li><li>Make sure the idea query loads <code>createdBy</code> (hasOne rel) so the fallback is rare.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: a test with an idea whose creator isn't in the store shows \\"Unknown user\\", never an id.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ideas-reset-sort", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: leaving the page resets group but not sort and order", "description": "<p>The idea route's <code>resetController</code> (aprom-4359) resets the <code>group</code> query param but leaves <code>sort</code> and <code>order</code> (and possibly <code>page</code>), so the browser comes back half reset. The defaults for sort/order/page are also repeated in the route and the controller (aprom-4356 notes).</p><ul><li>Reset <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>order</code> and <code>group</code> together when leaving the idea area, keeping the search params as they are today.</li><li>Keep the defaults (sort <code>Idea.dateModified</code>, order DESC, page 1) in one place used by both route and controller.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: an acceptance test changes sort, order and group, leaves the idea area and returns: all three are back to their defaults.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "mirage-multi-sort", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Mirage: idea handler ignores two-field sort", "description": "<p>Grouping ideas by Created by sends a two-field sort (<code>Idea.createdUser</code> first, then the chosen sort). The Mirage <code>/idea</code> handler ignores the comma-separated sort, so no test checks the grouped order across pages (aprom-4359 notes).</p><ul><li>Make the Mirage idea handler (and the shared sort helper if one exists) apply comma-separated <code>sort</code> fields in order, with <code>order</code> applied to each as Gaia does.</li><li>Add an acceptance test: group by Created by over two pages; each creator's ideas are contiguous and in the chosen order.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: the new test passes and fails if the handler ignores the first sort field.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ql-state-owners", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: move selection and group-collapse state out of the root component", "description": "<p>The assemble issue (aprom-4357) left the root <code>QuickList</code> component holding the selected ids, the collapsed groups per groupBy, and the rendering, plus a group heading fallback written both in <code>index.hbs</code> and <code>group.hbs</code>. Its design review suggested splitting these.</p><ul><li>Move the selection into a small class (e.g. <code>app/utils/quick-list/selection.js</code>: tracked <code>Set</code> of ids, toggle, toggleAll(items), clear, state 'none'|'some'|'all') and the collapse state into another (<code>collapse-state.js</code>, per groupBy). The root creates and uses them; its arguments and blocks don't change.</li><li>Keep the group heading fallback in <code>QuickList::Group</code> only.</li><li>Unit tests for both classes; the existing integration tests must pass unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: no change in behaviour or public contract; the root component code shrinks to wiring and rendering.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ideas-group-util", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: move the browser's sort and group definitions into a util with unit tests", "description": "<p>The idea browser's QuickList options (sort list, group list with <code>groupKey</code>/<code>groupLabel</code> closures, creators map, <code>buildSort</code>) live in a getter in <code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> and have no unit tests (aprom-4359 notes).</p><ul><li>Move them to <code>app/utils/ideas/list-options.js</code> as pure functions taking what they need (intl, progress lookup, creator lookup); the controller only calls them.</li><li>Unit tests for the sort list, the group list (none, plan status, created by) and <code>buildSort</code> (created-by grouping puts <code>Idea.createdUser</code> first).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: no change in behaviour; new unit tests pass.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 15:00:58	2026-11-08 15:03:49	f
c43d80336af0-06f4-8669-7eee42fb7ef0	c89b1b196aee-e15e-6d43-8adc416a487e	17	{"summary": "ezSearch runs searches too eagerly on Enter, including an empty bar on first load. Change the shared search bar so Enter only accepts a suggestion or formats/validates the text, and a search runs only on Ctrl/Cmd+Enter or the Search button. Never run when the bar is empty with nothing applied, or when the query is unchanged since it was applied. Applies to <EzSearch> and <EzSearchCompact> everywhere; acceptance steps that pressed Enter move to Ctrl+Enter.", "issues": [{"key": "ez-enter-run", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "ezSearch: Enter no longer runs the search; Ctrl/Cmd+Enter or the Search button does", "description": "<p>Pressing Enter in ezSearch runs the search too eagerly: while typing, Enter starts a search, and on first load Enter runs a query even when the bar is empty. That is the behaviour aprom-4297 specified (Enter with the suggestion menu closed formats and runs). The engineer wants searches to run only on purpose. Change it in the shared search bar (<code>app/components/ez-search/search-bar.{js,hbs}</code>), so <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> (both layouts) behave the same everywhere.</p><p><strong>New keyboard behaviour</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Enter</strong>:<ul><li>With the suggestion menu open: accept the highlighted suggestion (unchanged).</li><li>With the menu closed: parse and format the text into the exact query and show any error, without calling <code>@onRun</code>/<code>@onApply</code>.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Ctrl+Enter</strong> (<strong>Cmd+Enter</strong> on macOS, i.e. <code>ctrlKey || metaKey</code>): format and run, the same as clicking Search. It works with the menu open too: the typed text runs, the highlighted suggestion is not accepted.</li><li><strong>Search button</strong>: unchanged; it runs.</li><li><strong>Guard</strong> (in the shared base, <code>app/components/ez-search/base.js</code>, so the button and the shortcut both use it): don't apply when the bar is empty and no query is currently applied, or when the formatted query equals the one last applied. Clear still applies the empty query when something was applied.</li><li>Tab, Up, Down and Esc are unchanged. Blur still formats without running.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>The search bar's keydown handling and the base's apply guard, as above.</li><li>The menu's hint line (<code>components.ezSearch.searchBar.hint</code> in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>): \\"Enter to accept · Ctrl+Enter to search · Esc to close\\". The Search button's <code>title</code> mentions Ctrl+Enter.</li><li>Update the search bar's and the base's integration tests.</li><li>Update the acceptance step definitions that run a query by pressing Enter (Issue, Project, Agents, Workflows, idea list, Gantt, Task Board scenarios) to use Ctrl+Enter or the Search button. Prefer one shared step so the features don't each change.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Integration tests:<ul><li>Enter with the menu closed formats and doesn't call <code>@onApply</code>.</li><li>Enter with the menu open accepts the suggestion.</li><li>Ctrl+Enter and Cmd+Enter apply.</li><li>Ctrl+Enter or Search on an empty bar with nothing applied does nothing.</li><li>An unchanged query is not applied twice.</li><li>Clear after an applied search applies the empty query.</li></ul></li><li>An acceptance check on the Issue list: loading the page and pressing Enter in the empty bar makes no new <code>/issue</code> request.</li><li>All ezSearch acceptance suites pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the builder modal's buttons, other shortcuts.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 10:19:48	2026-11-08 10:28:56	f
b1249ca66af0-e87c-60c0-cf097445dee8	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	1	{"summary": "A reusable QuickList component for narrow, box-sized lists. The core issue sets the contract: the root box, header, row frame and named blocks for each module's content, and the empty, loading and error states. Pagination and group/sort build on it side by side, then selection with bulk actions. A developer page under Settings > Developer > UI > QuickList shows every feature with fixture data, and the idea browser is the first real user, without selection. Notifications, Gantt and the project overview come later.", "issues": [{"key": "ql-core", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: core component (box, header, item frame, named blocks, states)", "description": "<p>Several narrow lists in Prometheus (the idea browser, the Gantt task list, notifications, latest issues) each build their own markup. This issue adds the shared <code>QuickList</code> component they will use, starting with its contract. The attached screens are a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the existing components decide that.</p><ul><li>New Glimmer components in <code>app/components/quick-list/</code>: <code>QuickList</code> (root <code>box box-primary quick-list</code>), <code>QuickList::Header</code> (box title with the count: <code>64</code>, or <code>0 of 64</code> when <code>@total</code> and a filtered count differ, plus <code>box-tools</code>) and <code>QuickList::Item</code> (the row frame: link via <code>@route</code>/<code>@model</code>, a 3px crimson left bar when <code>@active</code>, light row separator).</li><li>Named blocks: <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> (header tools), <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> (a slot for <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code>, which is not wrapped), <code>&lt;:item as |record|&gt;</code> rendering <code>QuickList::Item</code> with <code>&lt;:primary&gt;</code> (bold title that wraps, status label on the right) and <code>&lt;:secondary&gt;</code> (12px grey line cut off with an ellipsis, plus optional tags), and <code>&lt;:empty&gt;</code>.</li><li>Arguments: <code>@items</code>, <code>@total</code>, <code>@activeId</code>, <code>@isLoading</code>, <code>@error</code>, <code>@onRetry</code>, <code>@title</code>. The component never loads data; the caller owns the queries.</li><li>States: loading = three skeleton rows (reuse the existing <code>skeleton-line</code> styles / <code>AppUi::Skeleton</code>); empty = grey <code>fa-info-circle</code> text, with a \\"Clear the search\\" action when the caller passes <code>@onClearSearch</code>; error = red <code>fa-exclamation-triangle</code> text with \\"Try again\\" (<code>@onRetry</code>).</li><li>Styles in <code>app/styles/components/quick-list.scss</code> (imported in <code>app.scss</code>), all under <code>.quick-list</code>: square edges, colours from <code>variables.scss</code>, no shadows.</li><li>YUIDoc on every class and argument, describing the contract for future users. Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests render items through the named blocks, mark the active item, and show the loading, empty (default and replaced) and error states with working actions.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: pagination, grouping, sorting and selection (separate issues), and adopting the component in any page.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-default", "quick-list-states"]}, {"key": "ql-pager", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: pagination footer", "description": "<p>QuickList needs pagination like the list pages have: <code>1-20 / 64</code> with square ‹ › buttons. The attached screen is a guide only; the design system wins.</p><ul><li>New <code>QuickList::Pagination</code>, rendered by <code>QuickList</code> under the items when <code>@limit</code> is set. Arguments on QuickList: <code>@page</code> (1-based), <code>@limit</code>, <code>@total</code>, <code>@onPage(page)</code>.</li><li>Shows the range and total in grey 12px text. ‹ is disabled on page 1 and › on the last page; both are disabled while <code>@isLoading</code>. Square <code>btn btn-default btn-xs</code> buttons with <code>fa-angle-left</code>/<code>fa-angle-right</code>.</li><li>No footer when everything fits on one page.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: an integration test covers the range text, the disabled states and <code>@onPage</code> calls.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: numbered pages, page size picker, infinite scroll.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ql-core"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-default"]}, {"key": "ql-group-sort", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: toolbar with group-by and sort, grouped rendering", "description": "<p>QuickList lists can be grouped (by status, creator, ...) and sorted. Grouping works on the page the caller loaded: Gaia's <code>group</code> parameter is a SQL GROUP BY and can't produce headed groups. So the caller sorts by the group field first, and QuickList groups the returned items in JS and counts them there. The attached screens are a guide only.</p><ul><li>New <code>QuickList::Toolbar</code> row under the search: <strong>Group by ▾</strong> (<code>fa-object-group</code> + current label) and <strong>Sort ▾</strong> (<code>fa-sort-amount-desc</code>/<code>-asc</code> + current label) as square <code>btn-default btn-xs</code> dropdowns, using the existing <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code>. The current choice is marked in crimson with a check or sort icon. The left side is left free for the select-all box (selection issue).</li><li>Arguments on QuickList: <code>@groupOptions</code> (<code>[{key, label, groupKey(record), groupLabel(key)}]</code>), <code>@groupBy</code>, <code>@onGroup(key)</code>, <code>@sortOptions</code> (<code>[{key, label}]</code>), <code>@sort</code>, <code>@order</code>, <code>@onSort(key, order)</code>. Picking the current sort again flips the order. The toolbar is hidden when neither option list is given.</li><li>A pure helper <code>app/utils/quick-list/group-items.js</code>: (items, groupOption) -&gt; ordered groups <code>{key, label, items, count}</code>, keeping first-seen order, with unit tests.</li><li>New <code>QuickList::Group</code> heading (<code>#f4f4f4</code> band, <code>#ddd</code> bottom border, 12px bold uppercase, caret, <code>badge</code> with the count), collapsible; collapsed groups are kept per groupBy for the component's lifetime. A <code>&lt;:group as |group|&gt;</code> block can replace the heading content.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests for group-items; integration tests for the menus, the onGroup/onSort calls, grouped rendering with counts, collapsing, and a replaced group heading.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: totals per group across all pages, sorting more than one field.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ql-core"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-selection-grouped", "quick-list-states"]}, {"key": "ql-selection", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: selection and bulk actions", "description": "<p>QuickList can let users select rows and run actions on them. It's optional: the idea browser won't turn it on. The attached screen is a guide only.</p><ul><li><code>@selectable</code> turns it on: each <code>QuickList::Item</code> gets a checkbox before the body (<code>fa-square-o</code> / crimson <code>fa-check-square</code>; checked rows get a <code>#f9fafc</code> background), and the toolbar gets a select-all box on the left that shows none, part (<code>fa-minus-square-o</code>) or all of the loaded items.</li><li>New <code>QuickList::SelectionBar</code>: while anything is selected it replaces the toolbar row: select-all box, \\"N selected\\", the <code>&lt;:selectionActions as |selected clear|&gt;</code> block, and a × button that clears the selection. Group/sort return when the selection is empty.</li><li>The selection lives in QuickList (ids), is reported through <code>@onSelect(ids)</code>, and is cleared when <code>@items</code> changes to a different page or search. Clicking the checkbox must not follow the row link.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for selecting and unselecting rows, the three select-all states, the selection bar replacing the toolbar, clearing, and the yielded actions receiving the selected records.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: selecting across pages, shift-click ranges, any real action.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ql-group-sort"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-selection-grouped"]}, {"key": "ql-dev-page", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Settings > Developer > UI: QuickList showcase page", "description": "<p>Developers need one place to see QuickList with every feature on, including selection, which no product list uses yet. This adds a Developer group to Settings with a UI page whose first entry is QuickList, using fixture data.</p><ul><li>Metadata: new group <code>developer</code> (label \\"Developer\\") in <code>views.Navigation.settingsItems</code> (<code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> ~l.234) with item <strong>UI</strong> (icon <code>paint-brush</code>, aclContext <code>setting.read</code>). The Settings layout (<code>templates/app/settings.hbs</code>) already renders groups from metadata.</li><li>Routes in <code>router.js</code> under <code>settings</code>: <code>ui</code> with child <code>quick-list</code> (the <code>ui</code> index redirects to it); add both to <code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code> as <code>setting.read</code>. The UI page shows a <code>nav nav-tabs</code> of showcased components (just QuickList for now) inside the settings content column.</li><li>QuickList page: a local fixture of about 45 records (title, status, creator, dates, tags) in <code>app/utils/dev/quick-list-fixture.js</code>. The controller does paging (20 per page), sort, group (status, creator) and a title filter in memory. The list is rendered at the idea-browser width (<code>col-md-4</code>) with header actions, all named blocks, <code>@selectable</code> and dummy selection actions (\\"Archive\\", \\"Delete\\") that only show a toast with the count. Buttons on the page switch the list into the loading, empty and error states.</li><li>No Gaia calls, so no Mirage handler is needed. Add an acceptance test (Gherkin, like the existing settings features).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: Settings shows Developer &gt; UI; the QuickList page shows paging, grouping, sorting, selection with actions, and each state.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: showcases of other components, hiding the group in production builds.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ql-pager", "ql-selection"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-selection-grouped", "quick-list-states"]}, {"key": "ql-ideas", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: idea browser uses QuickList with server paging, sort and grouping", "description": "<p>The idea browser (<code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>, <code>ul.nav.nav-stacked.idea-list</code>) is the first page to use QuickList. Today the route loads every idea (<code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code>, limit -1) and the controller filters open and archived in the browser (<code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> <code>listedIdeas</code>). The attached screens are a guide only.</p><ul><li>Replace the list markup with <code>&lt;QuickList&gt;</code> in the same <code>col-md-3 box</code>: <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> = the New Idea button (same ACL), <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> = the existing <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;:item&gt;</code> primary = title + the plan progress label (current <code>progressByIdea</code> labels and skeleton), secondary = creator name + last updated (<code>ember-moment</code> \\"x ago\\"). Active row = the selected idea. No selection.</li><li>Server paging: 20 per page via Gaia <code>limit</code>/<code>page</code>, <code>@total</code> from the response meta, a <code>page</code> query param kept with the search. The open/archived split moves into the query (open by default; the existing \\"show archived\\" toggle adds archived ideas).</li><li>Sort: last updated (default, desc), date created, title, via Gaia <code>sort</code>/<code>order</code>. Group by: none, plan status, created by. For created by, sort by <code>Idea.createdUser</code> first so groups continue across pages; plan status is worked out in the browser, so it groups only the loaded page. Counts come from the loaded page.</li><li>Load the creator with the hasOne rel (<code>createdBy</code>) only, no hasMany rels. Hermes idea events re-run the current page query.</li><li>Update the Mirage idea handler to honour limit/page/sort, and the existing acceptance tests for the idea browser.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: the browser shows 20 ideas per page with working ‹ ›, sort and group menus, search still applies, the selected idea is marked, archived ideas appear only when toggled, and live updates refresh the page.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: tags on ideas, selection/bulk actions, other lists (notifications, Gantt, project overview).</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ql-pager", "ql-group-sort"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-default", "quick-list-selection-grouped"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 11:40:33	2026-11-08 11:40:33	f
88c111f46af2-c9f1-5ed1-1d8d5c2984e8	341481c56af2-8040-cd6a-5ea33d81936b	3	{"summary": "Threads moves to the QuickList list + detail layout: list col-md-3, thread col-md-6, info column col-md-3 (inside the col-md-9 outlet as 8/4). ezSearch metadata first, then the QuickList list (default QuickList styling, grouped by milestone by default, child thread route, ?c_id= redirect). Row counts (separate Gaia calls for now) run in parallel with the discussion thread page, which follows the engineer's mockup. The vote body + Result box, Participants, Create issue from thread and a limited Activity box follow in a chain because they share the page and info column. Two requests go to A Gaia (room counts incl. agree/disagree; thread activities). Then a counts switch and a cleanup.", "issues": [{"key": "threads-search", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: ezSearch metadata (views.Conversationroom.search) incl. 'Liked by'", "description": "<p>Threads (app.project.conversation) is moving to the QuickList list + detail layout used by Ideas and Roles (aprom-4428, aprom-4430). Its search must come from view metadata like every other list, replacing the hard-coded filters in <code>controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code> (<code>conversationFilters</code> ~l.295, <code>conversationDateFilters</code> ~l.344).</p><ul><li>Add <code>views.Conversationroom.search</code> in <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>, same format as <code>views.Idea.search</code> / <code>views.Role.search</code>: subject, description, roomType (values vote | discussion, translated), linked issue (Conversationroom.issueNumber, with empty / not empty), dateCreated, dateModified, created by, and <strong>Liked by</strong> = <code>votes.createdUser</code> (Gaia already accepts <code>(votes.createdUser : &lt;userId&gt;)</code>, used by today's My Likes filter), with the project members as value source and the current user first.</li><li>If the metadata format or <code>services/query-schema.js</code> cannot express a relation field like <code>votes.createdUser</code>, extend it generically (no thread-specific code in ez-search) and document it in <code>docs/architecture/metadata-views/</code>.</li><li>Translations in en-us.json.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit test that the schema built from the metadata produces <code>(Conversationroom.roomType : vote)</code>, <code>(Conversationroom.issueNumber NULL)</code> and <code>(votes.createdUser : X)</code> clauses. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> wiring it into the page (next issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "threads-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: QuickList list + detail layout, grouped by milestone, first thread opened", "description": "<p>Replace the infinite-scroll feed on the Threads page with the QuickList list + detail layout of Ideas/Roles, so threads can be searched, paged, sorted and grouped and one thread is read at a time. The list uses <strong>QuickList's default styling</strong> (no custom row look): use its standard blocks only.</p><ul><li>Routing: <code>app.project.conversation</code> becomes the layout with children <code>index</code> and <code>page</code> (<code>conversations/:conversation_id</code>); add <code>app.project.conversation.page</code> to <code>services/acl.js</code> routeMaps (conversationroom.read) and the breadcrumb. Index route: <code>replaceWith</code> the first row; if <code>?c_id=X</code> is present, replaceWith the page for X (old links from project overview, issue list, weekly-conversations widget, tag-parser keep working). Empty state (QuickList <code>&lt;:empty&gt;</code> with Clear search) only when nothing matches; the outlet then says no thread is open.</li><li>Page header: \\"Threads\\" with a <strong>New thread</strong> btn-primary on the right (ACL conversationroom.create) opening the existing create modal.</li><li>Layout <code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code>: .row with col-md-3 QuickList + col-md-9 outlet. QuickList with the range (limit+1, no totals, QuickList pagination), <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> = <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> with <code>views.Conversationroom.search</code> and saved searches as on the idea browser.</li><li>State on the toolkit (<code>utils/state/</code> ListLoader + UrlState, aprom-4425/4426): query, page, sort, order, group in the URL, list reloads in place (no refreshModel), newest response wins. Query <code>conversationroom</code> with hasOne rels only (<code>createdBy,issue</code>), never comments/votes rels.</li><li>Rows: <code>&lt;:leading&gt;</code> = type icon (<code>fa-comment-o</code> discussion, <code>fa-thumbs-o-up</code> vote); primary = subject; secondary = linked issue <code>#number · subject</code> for discussions (nothing yet for votes, tallies come with the counts issue), then creator name · modified time/date. Active row = open thread.</li><li>Grouping <strong>on by default</strong> by the linked issue's milestone: load the project's milestones once, map <code>issue.milestoneId</code> to its name, threads without issue or milestone in \\"No milestone\\" last; per loaded page (QuickList grouping helper). Other group option: type. Sort: last updated (default), created, subject.</li><li>Page route for now renders the existing <code>Conversation::ConversationItem</code> for the selected thread in the col-md-9 (replaced by the thread page issue), so dev never breaks.</li><li>Hermes: keep the existing project registrations; a new/updated thread reloads the list through the loader.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Mirage handlers + acceptance feature: first thread opens by default, <code>?c_id=</code> redirects, grouping by milestone with \\"No milestone\\" last, search reloads only the list. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> counts in rows, the new thread page, removing old code.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-search"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Route split, layout, toolkit state and the c_id redirect must ship together so the page never breaks; counts, thread page, votes and cleanup are already separate issues.", "screens": []}, {"key": "threads-row-counts", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: comment counts and vote tallies on list rows (separate Gaia calls for now)", "description": "<p>Thread rows should show how active a thread is. Gaia has no count field yet (requested separately), so for now load them with separate calls per row, as the current page already does for comments (<code>fetchAndLinkComments</code>).</p><ul><li>A small service or util (single responsibility: counts for a set of room ids) that, for each row of the loaded page, queries the room's comments with minimal fields (<code>createdUser</code>, comment text) and returns <code>{commentCount, agreeCount, disagreeCount}</code> (vote rooms: comments with text \\"I agree\\" / \\"I disagree\\"); runs in parallel, results dropped when the page changes (newest wins), rows render while counts load.</li><li>Rows: discussion meta line gets <code>fa-comment-o N</code>; vote rows' secondary line = <code>N agree · M disagree</code>.</li><li>Live: Hermes comment created/deleted for a listed thread updates its count.</li><li>Keep the count source behind one function so a later issue can swap it for one Gaia call per page.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit test for the counts helper (stale page dropped, agree/disagree split) and an acceptance step showing counts for both room types. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> Gaia changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-list"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "threads-detail", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: thread page for discussions (header, comments, reply, Linked issue box)", "description": "<p>Replace the temporary <code>Conversation::ConversationItem</code> in <code>app.project.conversation.page</code> with the thread page. Inside the col-md-9 outlet: thread col-md-8 + info column col-md-4. This issue builds the page and the discussion body; the vote body, Participants, Create issue and Activity come in follow-up issues. The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>Thread box (box-primary) header: small uppercase type label (Discussion / Vote) above the subject as a large title; box-tools = like toggle with count (existing toggleVote logic) and edit (existing edit modal from ConversationItem); linked-issue line (<code>fa-link</code>, <code>#number</code> link, subject, status label); \\"Started by &lt;user link&gt; · date\\".</li><li>Body: description (rendered as today). Comments section: uppercase \\"N comments\\" heading, each comment with a round initials/profile avatar, name link, time and text with mentions highlighted (reuse <code>ConversationUi::CommentItem</code>), loaded with <strong>their own query</strong> (newest 10, sort Comment.dateCreated, \\"Load older comments\\"), never through rels. Reply box at the bottom with the current user's avatar and <code>ConversationUi::CommentComposer</code> (mentions + issue links), Reply button.</li><li>Leave a body slot chosen by roomType where the vote body plugs in; until then vote rooms show the description only.</li><li>Info column: <strong>Linked issue</strong> box (box-info: key link, subject, status label, milestone; \\"No linked issue\\" otherwise). Leave room below it for the boxes added later.</li><li>Page route loads the room with hasOne rels only (<code>createdBy,issue</code>); move the Hermes comment handlers (<code>handleCommentCreated/Updated/Deleted</code>) for the open thread to the page controller. Guard async work after destroy.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Mirage + acceptance: opening a discussion shows the header, comments, load older, posting a reply appears, Linked issue box filled. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> vote body, Participants, Create issue, Activity, reply threading (aprom-3750), removing ConversationItem.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-list"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-list"]}, {"key": "threads-vote", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: vote thread body (agree/disagree, voter list) and Result box", "description": "<p>Vote threads are a key use of Threads. In vote rooms a vote is a comment whose text is \\"I agree\\" or \\"I disagree\\" (ConversationItem's <code>@vote</code>), one per user, not changeable, and tallies are counted over all of the room's comments. The thread page loads comments in pages, so tallies need their own data. The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>Vote body (in the slot from the thread page issue), below the description: the existing agree/disagree <code>info-box</code>es side by side (icon, count, progress bar, percentage), moved out of ConversationItem into a vote component. Not voted: thumbs clickable (existing vote action) and a hint \\"You haven't voted yet. Click a thumb to vote; one vote per person.\\"; voted: thumbs locked and \\"You voted: I agree\\" (or disagree).</li><li>Tallies from a dedicated query of the room's vote comments (all, minimal fields: createdUser, text, date), shared with the voter list.</li><li>Voter list: uppercase \\"N votes\\" heading, rows with avatar, name link, time and a label (<code>label-success</code> I agree / <code>label-danger</code> I disagree), newest first, \\"Show all N votes\\" expands the rest. No reply box on vote threads (as today).</li><li>Info column for votes: <strong>Result</strong> box (box-warning) first: \\"Leaning: I agree (3 of 4)\\" (or \\"Tied\\" / \\"No votes yet\\") and \\"N of M project members voted\\" (members from the project members list). No Linked issue box on vote threads.</li><li>Live: a new vote (Hermes comment created) updates tallies, list and result without reload.</li><li>Translations: reuse <code>views.app.conversation.vote.*</code>, new keys for result, hint and heading.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> acceptance test: vote once, counts and result update, thumbs locked after voting, a live vote from another user updates tallies. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> closing a vote, changing a vote, deadlines, linking issues to votes.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-detail"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-vote"]}, {"key": "threads-participants", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: Participants box in the thread info column", "description": "<p>Show who takes part in a thread, in the info column of the thread page (below Linked issue for discussions, below Result for votes). The attached screens are a guide for layout and content only.</p><ul><li>Participants = the thread's creator first, then distinct authors of its comments (votes on vote threads), newest activity first.</li><li>Data: one comments query for the room with minimal fields (<code>createdUser</code>, <code>createdUserName</code>, date), not the paged comments; reuse the vote tally data on vote threads.</li><li>Render with the existing member avatar component (e.g. <code>Project::MemberAvatars</code>), names as tooltips, linking to the user page; collapse to \\"+N\\" past 8.</li><li>Live: a new comment/vote by a new person adds them.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> integration test for the participant list (creator first, distinct) and an acceptance step on both room types. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> following, mentions as participants.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-vote"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-list", "threads-vote"]}, {"key": "threads-create-issue", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: 'Create issue from thread' in the Linked issue box", "description": "<p>Discussions often end in work. Let people create an issue straight from a discussion thread, linked to it, from the Linked issue box. The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only.</p><ul><li>Button \\"Create issue from thread\\" (btn-default btn-sm, <code>fa-plus</code>) in the Linked issue box footer, on discussion threads only, shown when the user may create issues (ACL issue.create) and the thread has no linked issue.</li><li>It opens the existing issue create flow (prefer reusing the issue create route/form; decide between navigating with prefilled values or a modal based on what the create controller supports, and say which in the PR) with subject = thread subject and description = thread description plus a link back to the thread.</li><li>After the issue is saved, PATCH the room's <code>issueId</code>/<code>issueNumber</code> (same fields the create modal sets) and return to the thread, which now shows the linked issue.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> acceptance test: create issue from a discussion, the thread shows the new issue in the Linked issue box and the list row shows its key. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> vote threads, unlinking.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["threads-participants"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-list"]}, {"key": "gaia-activities", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Conversation rooms: record a few activities (started, edited, issue linked)", "description": "<p><strong>Request from A Prometheus.</strong> The new Threads page shows a small Activity box per thread. Gaia records activities for issues (<code>IssueactivitiesComponent</code>, generic Activity with <code>relatedTo</code>), but <code>ConversationroomController</code> only uses <code>Events\\\\\\\\ConversationLiveEvents</code>, so threads have no history. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract:</strong></p><ul><li>A component like <code>IssueactivitiesComponent</code>, added to <code>ConversationroomController</code> <code>$uses</code>, writing Activity rows with <code>relatedTo</code> = <code>conversationroom</code> and <code>relatedId</code> = room id for a <strong>limited</strong> set: thread created; subject edited; description edited; linked issue set, changed or cleared (with the issue key). No rows for comments or votes (they are visible in the thread).</li><li>Readable through the existing activity resource with project scoping like the room.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> api-tester cases for each activity type and that comments/votes write none. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> backfilling existing rooms.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "threads-activity", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: limited Activity box in the thread info column", "description": "<p>Show a short history of a thread in the info column, last box, on both room types. The attached screens are a guide for layout and content only.</p><ul><li>Data: Activity rows with <code>relatedTo conversationroom</code> and the room id (Gaia request in this plan), newest 5, \\"Show more\\" for the rest. Only the kinds Gaia records: started the thread/vote, edited subject/description, linked/changed/cleared issue.</li><li>Rendering: date (DD MMM, time for today) + sentence (\\"Rana Nouman edited the description\\"), reusing the existing activity rendering/translations where they fit (e.g. the activities box from aprom-4242).</li><li>Live: reload on the room's update events.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Mirage + integration test for the box (limit, sentence per kind). <strong>Out of scope:</strong> comments/votes in activity.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-create-issue", "gaia-activities"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-list", "threads-vote"]}, {"key": "threads-create-form", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: create modal uses FormFields for the linked issue and opens the new thread", "description": "<p>The New thread modal in <code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code> uses a raw <code>&lt;PowerSelect&gt;</code> and a hand-written label for the linked issue, which the design system forbids (selects are <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code>).</p><ul><li>Linked issue: <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> with search over issues (existing <code>linkIssueSearch</code> task), enabled only for roomType discussion as today.</li><li>After save: the list reloads in place and the app navigates to the new thread's page.</li><li>Move the modal into its own component if it keeps the layout template simpler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> acceptance test creating a discussion with a linked issue lands on the new thread. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other fields.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-row-counts"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gaia-counts", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Conversation rooms: read-only comment, vote and like counts per room", "description": "<p><strong>Request from A Prometheus.</strong> The Threads page (Prometheus) is moving to a QuickList and shows comment counts and vote tallies on each row and on vote threads. Gaia has no count for a room, so Prometheus currently queries each row's comments (20 extra calls per page) and loads every vote comment to count agree/disagree. We ask for one read-only resource that returns counts for many rooms in one call. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract:</strong></p><ul><li>Read-only resource <code>conversationroomcount</code> (view model, like <code>app/metadata/model/Userlatestproject.php</code> with COUNT subqueries): fields <code>id</code> (= room id), <code>commentCount</code>, <code>likeCount</code> (votes on the room), <code>agreeCount</code> and <code>disagreeCount</code> (comments of vote rooms with the text \\"I agree\\" / \\"I disagree\\"), <code>lastCommentDate</code>, <code>projectId</code>.</li><li><code>GET /conversationroomcount?query=(Conversationroomcount.id CONTAINS 'a','b',...)</code> returns one row per room; list + get only (no create/update/delete), standard CRUD controller, no custom routes.</li><li>ACL: project-scoped like Conversationroom; reading needs <code>conversationroom.read</code> (or a new <code>conversationroomcount.list</code>, your call).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> api-tester cases for counts (no comments = 0, deleted comments not counted, agree/disagree split) and for project scoping. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> live events for counts (Prometheus updates counts from comment events).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "threads-counts-switch", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: load row counts and vote tallies with one Gaia call", "description": "<p>Once Gaia serves room counts (the A Gaia counts request in this plan), replace the per-row comment queries (row counts issue) with one <code>conversationroomcount</code> query per loaded page, and take the vote thread's tallies and Result from it (<code>agreeCount</code>/<code>disagreeCount</code>) instead of counting all vote comments; the voter list and Participants keep their own queries.</p><ul><li>New model + adapter/serializer if needed, Mirage handler.</li><li>Swap only the count sources; rows, vote UI and live updates unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a 20-row page makes one count request (test on the Mirage request log); vote tallies match. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> anything else on the page.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-row-counts", "threads-vote", "gaia-counts"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "threads-cleanup", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: remove the old feed, filters and unused conversation code", "description": "<p>After the list, thread page, vote body and create form are in place, remove what the old Threads feed left behind.</p><ul><li>Controller <code>controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code>: InfiniteScroll paging (<code>loadMoreConversations</code>, <code>fetchAllConversations</code>, <code>fetchFilteredConversations</code>, <code>fetchAndLinkComments</code>, <code>setHasMoreFlag</code>), hard-coded filters/date filters, <code>restoreStateFromQueryParams</code>, scroll-to-top/refresh, unused QPs (filter, date, q).</li><li><code>Conversation::ConversationItem</code> and <code>app-ui/skeleton/conversation-grid</code> if nothing uses them anymore; <code>conversation-loading.hbs</code> if replaced; dead styles in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code>; unused translation keys.</li><li><code>components/app-ui/tag-parser.js</code> ~l.229 and the <code>c_id</code> LinkTos (project overview, issue list, weekly-conversations widget) point to the thread page route directly; the index redirect stays for old URLs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> full test suite and lint pass; no reference to the removed code. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> behaviour changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-activity", "threads-create-form"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 23:17:28	2026-11-09 23:21:49	f
ee3554a06af0-67ba-60c0-a614c6ef3915	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	2	{"summary": "QuickList is a reusable component for narrow, box-sized lists, planned in three waves so that up to three issues run at once. Wave 1 has seven issues with no dependencies: the core root component and contract, and four standalone pieces (pagination, group heading + grouping helper, group/sort toolbar, selection bar), each built and tested on its own. Also in wave 1: the Settings > Developer > UI section with an empty QuickList page, and server-side paging/sort for idea queries that keeps loading all ideas by default. Wave 2 connects the pieces to the root QuickList. Wave 3 fills the developer showcase page and switches the idea browser to QuickList, side by side. No selection on ideas; notifications, Gantt and the project overview come later.", "issues": [{"key": "ql-core", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: core component (box, header, item frame, named blocks, states)", "description": "<p>Several narrow lists in Prometheus (the idea browser, the Gantt task list, notifications, latest issues) each build their own markup. This issue adds the root <code>QuickList</code> component and sets its contract. Other issues build the pagination, group heading, toolbar and selection bar separately as standalone components, and a later issue connects them to this root, so don't build those parts here. The attached screens are a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the existing components decide that.</p><ul><li>New Glimmer components in <code>app/components/quick-list/</code>: <code>QuickList</code> (root <code>box box-primary quick-list</code>), <code>QuickList::Header</code> (box title with the count: <code>64</code>, or <code>0 of 64</code> when the shown count and <code>@total</code> differ, plus <code>box-tools</code>) and <code>QuickList::Item</code> (the row frame: link via <code>@route</code>/<code>@model</code>, a 3px crimson left bar when active, light row separator).</li><li>Named blocks: <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> (header tools), <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> (a slot for <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code>, which is not wrapped), <code>&lt;:item as |record|&gt;</code> rendering <code>QuickList::Item</code> with <code>&lt;:primary&gt;</code> (bold title that wraps, status label on the right) and <code>&lt;:secondary&gt;</code> (12px grey line cut off with an ellipsis, plus optional tags), and <code>&lt;:empty&gt;</code>.</li><li>Arguments: <code>@items</code>, <code>@total</code>, <code>@activeId</code>, <code>@isLoading</code>, <code>@error</code>, <code>@onRetry</code>, <code>@onClearSearch</code>, <code>@title</code>. The component never loads data; the caller owns the queries.</li><li>States: loading = three skeleton rows (reuse the existing <code>skeleton-line</code> styles / <code>AppUi::Skeleton</code>); empty = grey <code>fa-info-circle</code> text, with \\"Clear the search\\" when <code>@onClearSearch</code> is passed; error = red <code>fa-exclamation-triangle</code> text with \\"Try again\\" (<code>@onRetry</code>).</li><li>Styles in <code>app/styles/components/quick-list.scss</code> (imported in <code>app.scss</code>), all under <code>.quick-list</code>: square edges, colours from <code>variables.scss</code>, no shadows. Strings under <code>components.quickList.*</code> in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>YUIDoc on the class and every argument and block, describing the contract for future users.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests render items through the named blocks, mark the active item, and show the loading, empty (default and replaced) and error states with working actions.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: pagination, grouping, sorting, selection, and adopting the component in any page.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-default", "quick-list-states"]}, {"key": "ql-pagination", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: standalone pagination component", "description": "<p>QuickList needs pagination like the list pages have: <code>1-20 / 64</code> with square ‹ › buttons. Build it as a standalone component; a later issue connects it to the root <code>QuickList</code>, so don't touch <code>components/quick-list/index.*</code>. The attached screen is a guide only; the design system wins.</p><ul><li>New <code>app/components/quick-list/pagination.{hbs,js}</code> (<code>QuickList::Pagination</code>). Arguments: <code>@page</code> (1-based), <code>@limit</code>, <code>@total</code>, <code>@disabled</code>, <code>@onPage(page)</code>.</li><li>Shows the range and total in grey 12px text. ‹ is disabled on page 1 and › on the last page, both disabled while <code>@disabled</code>. Square <code>btn btn-default btn-xs</code> buttons with <code>fa-angle-left</code>/<code>fa-angle-right</code>. Renders nothing when everything fits on one page.</li><li>Styles in a new partial <code>app/styles/components/quick-list/_pagination.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.quick-list-pagination</code>. Don't import it anywhere: the assemble issue does that. Strings under <code>components.quickList.pagination.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: an integration test covers the range text, the disabled states, rendering nothing for a single page, and <code>@onPage</code> calls.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: numbered pages, page size picker, infinite scroll.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-default"]}, {"key": "ql-group", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: grouping helper and group heading component", "description": "<p>QuickList lists can be grouped (by status, creator, ...). Grouping works on the page the caller loaded: Gaia's <code>group</code> parameter is a SQL GROUP BY and can't produce headed groups, so items are grouped and counted in JS. Build the helper and the heading as standalone pieces; a later issue connects them to the root <code>QuickList</code>. The attached screen is a guide only.</p><ul><li>Pure helper <code>app/utils/quick-list/group-items.js</code>: <code>groupItems(items, option)</code> with <code>option = {key, groupKey(record), groupLabel(key)}</code> -&gt; ordered groups <code>[{key, label, items, count}]</code>, keeping first-seen order (the caller sorts by the group field first so groups continue across pages). Unit tests, including empty input and null keys (one \\"None\\" group).</li><li>New <code>QuickList::Group</code> (<code>app/components/quick-list/group.{hbs,js}</code>): heading with caret (<code>fa-caret-down</code>/<code>-right</code>), label in 12px bold uppercase, Bootstrap <code>badge</code> with the count; <code>#f4f4f4</code> band with a <code>#ddd</code> bottom border. Arguments <code>@group</code>, <code>@collapsed</code>, <code>@onToggle</code>. It yields the default block for the group's items (hidden while collapsed) and a <code>&lt;:heading as |group|&gt;</code> block that replaces the label.</li><li>Styles in a new partial <code>app/styles/components/quick-list/_group.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.quick-list-group</code>, not imported (the assemble issue imports it).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests for the helper; integration tests for the heading, the count, collapsing and a replaced heading.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: totals per group across all pages; connecting it to QuickList.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-selection-grouped"]}, {"key": "ql-toolbar", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: standalone group-by and sort toolbar", "description": "<p>QuickList lists get a toolbar row with Group by and Sort menus. Build it as a standalone component; a later issue connects it to the root <code>QuickList</code>. The attached screens are a guide only.</p><ul><li>New <code>QuickList::Toolbar</code> (<code>app/components/quick-list/toolbar.{hbs,js}</code>): a flex row with a <code>&lt;:start&gt;</code> block on the left (for the select-all box later) and, on the right, <strong>Group by ▾</strong> (<code>fa-object-group</code> + current label) and <strong>Sort ▾</strong> (<code>fa-sort-amount-desc</code>/<code>-asc</code> + current label) as square <code>btn-default btn-xs</code> dropdowns using the existing <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code>.</li><li>Arguments: <code>@groupOptions</code> (<code>[{key, label}]</code>, with \\"None\\" first), <code>@groupBy</code>, <code>@onGroup(key)</code>, <code>@sortOptions</code> (<code>[{key, label}]</code>), <code>@sort</code>, <code>@order</code>, <code>@onSort(key, order)</code>. Picking the current sort again flips the order. Each menu is hidden when it has no options. The current choice is marked in crimson with a check (group) or the order icon (sort).</li><li>Styles in a new partial <code>app/styles/components/quick-list/_toolbar.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.quick-list-toolbar</code>, not imported (the assemble issue imports it). Strings under <code>components.quickList.toolbar.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for both menus, the marked current choice, order flipping, hidden menus and the <code>&lt;:start&gt;</code> block.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: sorting more than one field; connecting it to QuickList.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-states"]}, {"key": "ql-selection-bar", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: standalone select-all box and selection bar", "description": "<p>QuickList can let users select rows and run actions on them; it's optional and the idea browser won't use it. Build the select-all box and the selection bar as standalone components; a later issue connects them (and the per-row checkbox) to the root <code>QuickList</code>. The attached screen is a guide only.</p><ul><li>New <code>QuickList::SelectAll</code> (<code>app/components/quick-list/select-all.{hbs,js}</code>): square <code>btn-default btn-xs</code> showing <code>fa-square-o</code> (none), <code>fa-minus-square-o</code> (some) or <code>fa-check-square</code> (all). Arguments <code>@state</code> ('none'|'some'|'all') and <code>@onToggle</code>; it has an accessible label.</li><li>New <code>QuickList::SelectionBar</code> (<code>selection-bar.{hbs,js}</code>): a row with <code>#f9fafc</code> background: <code>SelectAll</code>, bold \\"N selected\\", the <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> block, and a × <code>btn-default btn-xs</code> that calls <code>@onClear</code>. Arguments <code>@count</code>, <code>@state</code>, <code>@onToggleAll</code>, <code>@onClear</code>.</li><li>Styles in a new partial <code>app/styles/components/quick-list/_selection.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.quick-list-selection</code>, not imported (the assemble issue imports it). Strings under <code>components.quickList.selection.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for the three select-all states, the count text, the yielded actions and clearing.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: keeping the selection state, row checkboxes, and connecting them to QuickList (the assemble issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-selection-grouped"]}, {"key": "ql-dev-settings", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Settings: Developer group with a UI section and an empty QuickList page", "description": "<p>Developers need one place to see shared UI components with every feature on. This issue adds the Settings &gt; Developer &gt; UI section and an empty QuickList page; another issue fills the page once QuickList is assembled.</p><ul><li>Metadata: new group <code>developer</code> (label \\"Developer\\") in <code>views.Navigation.settingsItems</code> (<code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> ~l.234) with item <strong>UI</strong> (icon <code>paint-brush</code>, aclContext <code>setting.read</code>). The Settings layout (<code>templates/app/settings.hbs</code>) already renders groups from metadata.</li><li>Routes in <code>router.js</code> under <code>settings</code> (~l.69): <code>ui</code> with child <code>quick-list</code>; the <code>ui</code> index redirects to <code>quick-list</code>. Add them to <code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code> as <code>setting.read</code>.</li><li><code>templates/app/settings/ui.hbs</code>: a <code>box box-primary</code> titled \\"UI\\" with a <code>nav nav-tabs</code> listing the showcased components (only QuickList for now) and an outlet. <code>templates/app/settings/ui/quick-list.hbs</code>: an intro line and an empty-state placeholder (\\"Showcase coming soon\\"), with a route and controller ready to fill.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>. Acceptance test (Gherkin, like the existing settings features): Settings shows Developer &gt; UI, which opens the QuickList tab.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: the QuickList showcase content; hiding the group in production builds.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ql-ideas-data", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: server-side paging, sort and archived filter for the idea browser query", "description": "<p>The idea browser loads every idea (<code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code> ~l.47, limit -1) and filters open/archived in the browser (<code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> <code>listedIdeas</code> ~l.300). Before it moves to QuickList with 20 ideas per page, the query has to page and sort on the server. This issue changes only the data side; the browser looks the same.</p><ul><li>Controller query params <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>order</code> next to the existing search params. The idea query sends <code>limit</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code> (default <code>Idea.dateModified</code>), <code>order</code> (default DESC) and exposes the total from the response meta as <code>totalIdeas</code>.</li><li>A <code>pageSize</code> property on the controller that defaults to <code>-1</code> (all ideas, as today), so the current list keeps working; the QuickList issue sets it to 20.</li><li>Move the open/archived split into the query: open ideas by default (<code>Idea.status : open</code> ANDed with the search); when \\"show archived\\" is on, the status condition is dropped. The footer toggle and counts keep working.</li><li>Load the creator via the hasOne rel <code>createdBy</code> only (no hasMany rels). Hermes idea events re-run the current query, not a full reload.</li><li>Mirage: make the idea handler honour <code>limit</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code>/<code>order</code> and the status condition and return the total in meta; update the existing idea browser acceptance tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: the browser looks and works as before; tests show the query sends the sort, order and status condition, and that page/sort query params reach the request.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: the QuickList UI, page size 20, grouping.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ql-assemble", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: assemble pagination, grouping, toolbar and selection into the root", "description": "<p>The root <code>QuickList</code> and its standalone parts (pagination, group heading + <code>group-items</code> helper, toolbar, select-all + selection bar) were built separately. This issue connects them into one component and imports their style partials. The attached screens are a guide only.</p><ul><li><code>components/quick-list/index.{hbs,js}</code>: new arguments <code>@page</code>, <code>@limit</code>, <code>@onPage</code> (renders <code>QuickList::Pagination</code> under the items, disabled while <code>@isLoading</code>); <code>@groupOptions</code> (<code>[{key, label, groupKey, groupLabel}]</code>), <code>@groupBy</code>, <code>@onGroup</code>, <code>@sortOptions</code>, <code>@sort</code>, <code>@order</code>, <code>@onSort</code> (render <code>QuickList::Toolbar</code> under the search when any options are given). When <code>@groupBy</code> is set, items are grouped with <code>groupItems</code> and rendered in <code>QuickList::Group</code>; collapsed groups are remembered per groupBy for the component's lifetime; a <code>&lt;:group as |group|&gt;</code> block passes through to the heading.</li><li>Selection: <code>@selectable</code> adds a checkbox before each <code>QuickList::Item</code> body (<code>fa-square-o</code> / crimson <code>fa-check-square</code>, checked rows <code>#f9fafc</code>; clicking it doesn't follow the row link) and <code>QuickList::SelectAll</code> in the toolbar's <code>&lt;:start&gt;</code>. While anything is selected, <code>QuickList::SelectionBar</code> replaces the toolbar with the <code>&lt;:selectionActions as |selected clear|&gt;</code> block. QuickList keeps the selected ids, reports them via <code>@onSelect(ids)</code>, and clears them when <code>@items</code> changes to another page or search.</li><li>Import the partials <code>styles/components/quick-list/_pagination.scss</code>, <code>_group.scss</code>, <code>_toolbar.scss</code>, <code>_selection.scss</code> from <code>quick-list.scss</code>. Update the YUIDoc contract.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for paging, grouped rendering with counts and collapse, group/sort callbacks, selection (rows, select-all states, bar swap, yielded actions, clearing on new items).</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: selecting across pages, shift-click ranges.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ql-core", "ql-pagination", "ql-group", "ql-toolbar", "ql-selection-bar"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-default", "quick-list-selection-grouped", "quick-list-states"]}, {"key": "ql-dev-showcase", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Settings > Developer > UI: QuickList showcase with fixture data", "description": "<p>Fill the empty QuickList page under Settings &gt; Developer &gt; UI so developers see QuickList with every feature on, including selection, which no product list uses yet. The attached screens are a guide only.</p><ul><li>Fixture <code>app/utils/dev/quick-list-fixture.js</code>: about 45 records (title, status from the issue status classes, creator, created/updated dates, tags).</li><li><code>controllers/app/settings/ui/quick-list.js</code>: in-memory paging (20 per page), sort (updated, created, title), group (status, creator) and a title filter, all on the fixture. No Gaia calls, so no Mirage handler.</li><li><code>templates/app/settings/ui/quick-list.hbs</code>: QuickList in a <code>col-md-4</code> (the idea browser's width) with a header action, every named block (primary with status label, secondary with creator/date, tags), <code>@selectable</code>, and dummy selection actions \\"Archive\\" and \\"Delete\\" that only show a toast with the count. A small <code>btn-group</code> beside it switches the list into the loading, empty and error states.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; extend the settings acceptance test to cover paging, grouping, selection and the state switches.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: showcases of other components.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ql-assemble", "ql-dev-settings"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-selection-grouped", "quick-list-states"]}, {"key": "ql-ideas-ui", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: idea browser uses QuickList (20 per page, sort, grouping)", "description": "<p>The idea browser becomes QuickList's first real user. The query already pages and sorts on the server (previous ideas data issue), with <code>pageSize</code> -1 on the controller. The attached screens are a guide only.</p><ul><li>In <code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>, replace <code>ul.nav.nav-stacked.idea-list</code> with <code>&lt;QuickList&gt;</code> in the same <code>col-md-3 box</code>: <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> = New Idea button (same ACL), <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> = the existing <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;:item&gt;</code> primary = title + plan progress label (the current <code>progressByIdea</code> labels and skeleton), secondary = creator name + last updated (\\"x ago\\"). Active row = selected idea. No selection. Keep the archived footer toggle and the <code>data-idea*</code> test hooks where possible.</li><li>Set <code>pageSize</code> to 20 and connect <code>@page</code>/<code>@onPage</code>/<code>@total</code> to the controller's page query param.</li><li>Sort options: last updated (default), date created, title -&gt; the controller's sort/order. Group options: none, plan status (client-side from <code>progressByIdea</code>, groups only the loaded page), created by (sorts by <code>Idea.createdUser</code> first, then the chosen sort, so groups continue across pages). Group choice kept in a <code>group</code> query param.</li><li>Remove styles in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code> that only served the old list; update the idea browser acceptance tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: 20 ideas per page with working ‹ ›, sort and group menus, search still applies, the selected idea is marked, archived ideas appear only when toggled, live updates refresh the current page.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: tags on ideas, selection/bulk actions, other lists (notifications, Gantt, project overview).</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ql-assemble", "ql-ideas-data"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["quick-list-default", "quick-list-selection-grouped"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 11:45:50	2026-11-08 11:49:15	f
95b677166af0-b986-77e7-189ea47a30d4	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	3	{"summary": "Fixes and follow-ups after QuickList shipped (aprom-4350..4359). Pagination never shows on the idea browser because Gaia's list responses carry no total: aprom makes pagination work from Gaia's next link, and in parallel Gaia is asked for an opt-in total, which the browser already reads when present. A separate aprom bug fixes the Group/Sort menus, where the selected option is crimson on crimson on hover. Five small, independent follow-ups from the review notes: the creator fallback label, resetting sort/order, Mirage two-field sort, moving the selection and collapse state out of the QuickList root, and moving the idea group definitions into a util with tests. All issues are independent, so they can run three at a time.", "issues": [{"key": "ql-ideas-pager", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: pagination never shows because Gaia sends no total; page from the next link", "description": "<p>The idea browser (aprom-4359) shows no ‹ › pagination, while the Settings &gt; Developer &gt; UI page does. Cause: Gaia's list response has no total. <code>RestController::buildHAL</code> sets <code>meta.count</code> to the rows on this page only. aprom-4356 then falls back to counting the loaded ideas, so <code>@total</code> is never more than 20, and <code>QuickList::Pagination</code> renders nothing when everything fits on one page. Gaia does say whether a next page exists: it fetches <code>limit + 1</code> rows and adds <code>meta.links.next</code> only when there are more.</p><ul><li><code>QuickList::Pagination</code> (<code>components/quick-list/pagination.{hbs,js}</code>): new optional <code>@hasNext</code>. When <code>@total</code> is unknown (null/undefined), show the range without a total (<code>21-40</code>), enable ‹ when page &gt; 1 and › when <code>@hasNext</code>, and hide only on page 1 with no next. With a known total, behaviour is unchanged. Pass <code>@hasNext</code> through the root <code>QuickList</code>.</li><li>Idea browser (<code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>, route <code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code>): take <code>hasNext</code> from the query result's <code>meta.links.next</code>; pass <code>@total</code> only when <code>meta.total</code> is present (a separate Gaia request adds it, opt-in with <code>total=true</code>; send that parameter now, Gaia ignores it until then). Keep the header count as shown/total only when the total is known.</li><li>Mirage idea handler: return <code>meta.links.next</code> when more rows exist, and no <code>meta.total</code> unless <code>total=true</code> is sent and the handler is told to.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: with 25 ideas and no total, the browser shows <code>1-20</code> with › enabled, then <code>21-25</code> with › disabled; with a total it shows <code>1-20 / 25</code>. Integration tests for pagination with unknown total; acceptance test for the browser.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: the Gaia total itself.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gaia-list-total", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "List responses: opt-in total count in meta", "description": "<p>Prometheus (project A Prometheus) has started showing paged lists such as the idea browser's QuickList, and needs the total number of matching records to show <code>1-20 / 64</code> and correct counts. Today <code>RestController::buildHAL</code> (~l.1102) sets <code>meta.count</code> to the rows on the current page only, and there is no total. This is a request from A Prometheus: please accept, adapt or decline the proposed contract.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li>GET list requests accept <code>total=true</code>. When it is set, the response has <code>meta.total</code>: the number of records matching the same <code>query</code> and the ACL record scope (<code>applyRecordScope</code>), ignoring <code>limit</code>, <code>page</code> and <code>sort</code>. Without the parameter, nothing changes and no extra query runs.</li><li>The count must not be inflated by hasOne/hasMany <code>rels</code> joins (count distinct base ids, or count without rels). The existing <code>count</code> request parameter (~l.665) has another meaning; check it and don't break it.</li><li>Values stay bound (no string-built SQL). Add api-tester cases: total with a query, with record scope (a user who sees fewer records gets a smaller total), with rels, and without the parameter.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: <code>GET /idea?query=...&amp;limit=20&amp;total=true</code> returns <code>meta.total</code> equal to the number of ideas the user can see that match; responses without <code>total=true</code> are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: totals per group, exports.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ql-menu-hover", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: selected Group/Sort option is invisible on hover (crimson on crimson)", "description": "<p>In the QuickList toolbar (<code>QuickList::Toolbar</code>, aprom-4353), the current Group by / Sort option is marked with crimson text. When you hover it, the dropdown's hover rule (<code>styles/components/dropdown.scss</code>, crimson background) applies, but the marker colour wins over the hover's white text, so the option turns into a blank crimson bar (seen on Settings &gt; Developer &gt; UI with \\"None\\" selected). It's the same kind of bug as aprom-4346 (Saved menus).</p><ul><li>In <code>app/styles/components/quick-list/_toolbar.scss</code>, keep the crimson marker only at rest. On <code>:hover</code> and <code>:focus</code> the selected option (text, check and order icon) uses the same white text as the other hovered options. Don't change <code>dropdown.scss</code> globally.</li><li>Check the Sort menu as well as Group by, with keyboard focus too.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: hovering or focusing the selected option shows white text and icon on crimson in both menus; other options are unchanged. A test asserts the computed colour of a hovered or focused selected option differs from its background (or the class/rule that guarantees it).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ideas-creator-unknown", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: \\"Created by\\" group shows the raw user id when the creator isn't loaded", "description": "<p>In the idea browser (aprom-4359), grouping by Created by reads creator names with a synchronous peek of the <code>createdBy</code> relation. When it isn't loaded, the group heading (and the row's secondary line) shows the raw user id.</p><ul><li>Fall back to a translated \\"Unknown user\\" (<code>translations/en-us.json</code>) instead of the id, in both the group label and the secondary line.</li><li>Make sure the idea query loads <code>createdBy</code> (hasOne rel) so the fallback is rare.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: a test with an idea whose creator isn't in the store shows \\"Unknown user\\", never an id.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ideas-reset-sort", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: leaving the page resets group but not sort and order", "description": "<p>The idea route's <code>resetController</code> (aprom-4359) resets the <code>group</code> query param but leaves <code>sort</code> and <code>order</code> (and possibly <code>page</code>), so the browser comes back in a half-reset state. The defaults for sort/order/page are also repeated in the route and the controller (aprom-4356 notes).</p><ul><li>Reset <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>order</code> and <code>group</code> together when leaving the idea area, keeping the search params as they are today.</li><li>Keep the defaults (sort <code>Idea.dateModified</code>, order DESC, page 1) in one place used by both route and controller.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: an acceptance test changes sort, order and group, leaves the idea area and returns: all three are back to their defaults.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "mirage-multi-sort", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Mirage: idea handler ignores two-field sort", "description": "<p>Grouping ideas by Created by sends a two-field sort (<code>Idea.createdUser</code> first, then the chosen sort). The Mirage <code>/idea</code> handler ignores the comma-separated sort, so no test checks the grouped order across pages (aprom-4359 notes).</p><ul><li>Make the Mirage idea handler (and the shared sort helper if one exists) apply comma-separated <code>sort</code> fields in order, with <code>order</code> applied to each as Gaia does.</li><li>Add an acceptance test: group by Created by over two pages; each creator's ideas are contiguous and in the chosen order.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: the new test passes and fails if the handler ignores the first sort field.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ql-state-owners", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: move selection and group-collapse state out of the root component", "description": "<p>The assemble issue (aprom-4357) left the root <code>QuickList</code> component holding the selected ids, the collapsed groups per groupBy, and the rendering, plus a group heading fallback written both in <code>index.hbs</code> and <code>group.hbs</code>. Its design review suggested splitting these.</p><ul><li>Move the selection into a small class (e.g. <code>app/utils/quick-list/selection.js</code>: tracked <code>Set</code> of ids, toggle, toggleAll(items), clear, state 'none'|'some'|'all') and the collapse state into another (<code>collapse-state.js</code>, per groupBy). The root creates and uses them; its arguments and blocks don't change.</li><li>Keep the group heading fallback in <code>QuickList::Group</code> only.</li><li>Unit tests for both classes; the existing integration tests must pass unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: no change in behaviour or public contract; root component code shrinks to wiring and rendering.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ideas-group-util", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: move the browser's sort and group definitions into a util with unit tests", "description": "<p>The idea browser's QuickList options (sort list, group list with <code>groupKey</code>/<code>groupLabel</code> closures, creators map, <code>buildSort</code>) live in a getter in <code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> and have no unit tests (aprom-4359 notes).</p><ul><li>Move them to <code>app/utils/ideas/list-options.js</code> as pure functions taking what they need (intl, progress lookup, creator lookup); the controller only calls them.</li><li>Unit tests for the sort list, the group list (none, plan status, created by) and <code>buildSort</code> (created-by grouping puts <code>Idea.createdUser</code> first).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: no change in behaviour; new unit tests pass.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 14:52:05	2026-11-08 14:52:05	f
c1b3a2766af0-09ac-bf1d-c03051b9e30d	ded9f4396af0-2b69-3bb7-c36bdb48cfdf	1	{"summary": "An isolated Developer section in Prometheus hosting a Component Library. Wave 1 builds the framework in parallel: the section itself (route, admin nav item, component registry, Components box with search), the shared entry boxes (header, Controls with forced states, Event log) and the Documentation box that loads static markdown from public/ui-docs on demand and splits it into tabs. Wave 2 adds the first five entries (QuickList, ezSearch, Form fields, Modal, Dropdown), each a demo component plus its markdown doc, registered in the registry. Wave 3 removes the old Settings -> Developer -> UI page once QuickList has moved. No Gaia changes; developer-facing text is English only (no translations), docs never enter the app bundle.", "issues": [{"key": "dev-section", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Developer section: route, admin nav item, component registry and Components box", "description": "<p>We are building a Component Library for developers: one page per reusable UI component with a live demo, controls, an event log and docs. It must be isolated from Settings (developer-only, and it keeps Settings light). This issue builds the section and its navigation; the entry boxes and the docs box are built in parallel issues and the entries come after.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li><strong>Routes</strong> in <code>app/router.js</code> under <code>app</code>: <code>developer</code> (path <code>/developer</code>) with <code>components</code> and <code>component</code> (<code>/components/:name</code>). <code>developer.index</code> and <code>developer.components</code> redirect to the first registered component. An unknown <code>:name</code> shows an error box with a link back to the first component, not a crash.</li><li><strong>Nav</strong>: a <code>Developer</code> item in <code>views.Navigation.adminItems</code> (<code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> ~l.173; icon <code>code</code>, route <code>app.developer</code>, anchorRoute <code>developer</code>, aclContext <code>setting.read</code>, projectRelated false). Add every new route to <code>routeMaps</code> in <code>services/acl.js</code> mapped to <code>setting.read</code>. No new Gaia permission.</li><li><strong>Registry</strong> <code>app/utils/developer/component-registry.js</code>: an ordered list of entries <code>{ name, label, group, status (stable|experimental), summary, usedIn: [{label, route}], demo (component name), doc (file name in public/ui-docs), variants (optional count/labels) }</code> plus helpers <code>find(name)</code> and <code>grouped(filter)</code>. Groups: Lists, Search, Forms, Overlays, Menus. Ship it empty of real components except a placeholder entry if needed for tests; entries are added by later issues.</li><li><strong>Layout</strong> <code>templates/app/developer.hbs</code>: content-header \\"Developer Component Library\\", <code>col-md-3</code> <code>box box-primary</code> \\"Components\\" (count badge, a search input filtering the registry by label/summary client-side, group headings, active item marked) + <code>col-md-9</code> outlet. Put the box in <code>components/developer/component-nav.{hbs,js}</code>. Below md the box stacks above the entry.</li><li><strong>Entry route</strong> <code>routes/app/developer/component.js</code> resolves the registry entry and the template renders the entry's demo component with <code>{{component}}</code>; the demo composes the entry boxes from the parallel issue itself.</li><li>Developer-facing text is English only in this section (engineer's decision: no translations for the Developer section); the nav item label still uses a translation key like the other nav items.</li><li>Styles scoped under <code>.developer</code> in <code>app/styles/modules/developer.scss</code>; design system, square edges.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: an admin sees Developer in the Admin nav; the Components box lists registry entries grouped, the search filters them, the active one is marked; deep links work; a user without <code>setting.read</code> neither sees the item nor reaches the route. Acceptance test (Gherkin) for nav, search and unknown name.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: the entry boxes, the docs box, real entries, removing Settings -&gt; UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["library-entry"]}, {"key": "entry-shell", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Developer section: entry header, Controls and Event log components", "description": "<p>Every Component Library entry has the same frame: a header box, the demo, a Controls box and an Event log. This issue builds those shared pieces so each entry only writes its demo and its controls.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li><code>Developer::EntryHeader</code> (<code>components/developer/entry-header.{hbs,js}</code>): <code>box box-primary</code> with the label, a status label (stable = <code>label-success</code>, experimental = <code>label-warning</code>) in <code>box-tools</code>, the summary and \\"Used in\\" links (LinkTo per <code>usedIn</code> item). Takes a registry entry.</li><li><code>Developer::Entry</code> (<code>components/developer/entry.{hbs,js}</code>): the frame. Named blocks <code>&lt;:demo&gt;</code> (in a <code>box box-default</code> \\"Demo\\" <code>col-md-7</code>, with a Reset box-tool calling <code>@onReset</code>), <code>&lt;:controls&gt;</code> (in <code>box box-default</code> \\"Controls\\" <code>col-md-5</code>) and <code>&lt;:docs&gt;</code> (full width below). Yields an event logger to the blocks.</li><li><code>Developer::StateSwitch</code>: btn-group for forced states (<code>@states</code>, default normal/loading/empty/error; <code>@value</code>, <code>@onChange</code>).</li><li>Event log: a small class <code>utils/developer/event-log.js</code> (tracked list, newest first, capped at 50; <code>log(name, ...args)</code>, <code>wrap(name, fn)</code> returning a function that logs then calls <code>fn</code>, <code>clear()</code>) and <code>Developer::EventLog</code> (box \\"Event log\\", table time / <code>@name</code> / payload as short JSON, Clear box-tool, empty state \\"No events yet\\").</li><li>Controls inside entries use existing <code>FormFields::*</code> (checkbox, relate-simple selects) per the design system.</li><li>English-only text (no translations in the Developer section). Styles in <code>app/styles/modules/developer.scss</code> under <code>.developer</code>; if that file does not exist yet (parallel issue), create <code>app/styles/components/developer-entry.scss</code> and import it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for EntryHeader, StateSwitch, EventLog (log, wrap, cap, clear) and Entry (blocks render, Reset calls <code>@onReset</code>).</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: routes and nav, the docs box, real entries.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["library-entry"]}, {"key": "docs-box", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Developer section: Documentation box loading static markdown from public/ui-docs", "description": "<p>Component docs must not grow the app bundle (engineer's decision), so they are markdown files served as static assets from <code>public/ui-docs/&lt;name&gt;.md</code> and downloaded only when an entry opens. This issue builds the box that shows them and fixes the doc format.</p><ul><li><code>Developer::Docs</code> (<code>components/developer/docs.{hbs,js}</code>): <code>box box-info</code> \\"Documentation\\" with the file path in <code>box-tools</code>. Loads <code>/ui-docs/&lt;@doc&gt;</code> with <code>fetch</code> (a static file of the app itself, not Gaia, so the store/adapter rule does not apply; say so in a code comment); add the app version as a query param for cache busting. Splits the markdown on <code>## </code> headings into Bootstrap <code>nav nav-tabs</code> (first tab active, tab state internal) and renders each section with the existing <code>render-markdown</code> modifier (toastui viewer). States: loading (<code>AppUi::Loader</code>), missing file (\\"No documentation yet\\" with the expected path), fetch error. Guard async work after destroy.</li><li>Doc format in <code>public/ui-docs/README.md</code>: sections <code>## Overview</code>, <code>## Arguments</code> (table: Argument, Type, Default, Meaning), <code>## Blocks</code>, <code>## Events</code> (callback, payload), <code>## Do and Avoid</code>. No copy-ready code snippets (engineer's decision). Link the folder from <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code> section 9.</li><li>Check that <code>broccoli-asset-rev</code> leaves <code>.md</code> files unfingerprinted and that they are in the production build output.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration test with a stubbed fetch (tabs from headings, missing file state, error state); <code>ember build</code> output contains <code>ui-docs/README.md</code>; the app bundle size does not change from the docs.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: the docs of real components (each entry issue writes its own), lazy-loaded engines.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "entry-quick-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Component Library: QuickList entry (moved from Settings -> UI)", "description": "<p>QuickList already has a demo page under Settings -&gt; Developer -&gt; UI (<code>templates/app/settings/ui/quick-list.hbs</code>, <code>controllers/app/settings/ui/quick-list.js</code>, fixture <code>utils/dev/quick-list-fixture.js</code>). Move it into the new Developer section as the first Component Library entry.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li><code>components/developer/demos/quick-list.{hbs,js}</code>: the demo inside <code>Developer::Entry</code>. Move the paging, sorting, grouping, filtering and selection logic from the settings controller, keeping the in-memory fixture (no Gaia calls).</li><li>Search block: replace the plain <code>&lt;input&gt;</code> with <code>EzSearchCompact</code> on a fixture schema (title, status, creator, tag), filtering the fixture.</li><li>Controls: StateSwitch (normal/loading/empty/error), <code>@selectable</code>, search block on/off, <code>@groupBy</code> (none/status/creator), <code>@limit</code> (5/10/20). Every callback (<code>@onPage</code>, <code>@onSort</code>, <code>@onGroup</code>, selection actions, <code>@onRetry</code>, <code>@onClearSearch</code>) goes through the event log.</li><li>Registry entry (group Lists, stable, used in: Ideas browser) and <code>public/ui-docs/quick-list.md</code> in the doc format: all arguments, the named blocks (<code>actions</code>, <code>search</code>, <code>item</code> with <code>primary</code>/<code>secondary</code>, <code>group</code>, <code>selectionActions</code>, <code>empty</code>, <code>footer</code>), events, and the paging rule (ask Gaia for limit+1, no totals) under Do and Avoid.</li><li>Leave the old Settings page in place; a later issue removes it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: the entry shows every state and option from the controls; events appear in the log; docs tabs render; integration test of the demo.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: removing Settings -&gt; UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["dev-section", "entry-shell", "docs-box"], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["library-entry"]}, {"key": "entry-ez-search", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Component Library: ezSearch entry (EzSearch, compact multi-row, compact linear)", "description": "<p>ezSearch (<code>components/ez-search/</code>, <code>components/ez-search-compact/</code>) is our search bar and builder, used on the Issue, Project, Agent, Workflow and Idea lists, the Gantt and the Task Board. Document it in the Component Library with one entry and three variants.</p><ul><li><code>components/developer/demos/ez-search.{hbs,js}</code>: a variant switch in Controls (EzSearch full / EzSearchCompact multi-row / EzSearchCompact linear) over a fixture schema in the <code>views.&lt;Module&gt;.search</code> metadata shape (text, select with static values, date, user fields) and fixture saved searches. No Gaia calls: saving a search only logs.</li><li>Controls: <code>@query</code> preset (empty, simple, AND/OR with brackets, invalid mix), <code>@baseQuery</code> on/off, active saved search.</li><li>Event log: <code>@onApply</code> (show the exact query string Gaia would receive), <code>@onSave</code>, <code>@onSavedSearchChange</code>, <code>@onUpdateSavedSearch</code>.</li><li>Registry entry (group Search, stable, used in: Issues, Projects, Ideas, Gantt, Task Board; variants 3) and <code>public/ui-docs/ez-search.md</code>: arguments of both components (see <code>components/ez-search/base.js</code>), the metadata format and value sources (<code>services/query-schema.js</code>), keyboard behaviour, and rules under Do and Avoid (no AND/OR mixing without brackets, bare words are one phrase, do not wrap EzSearchCompact).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: all three variants work on the fixture; Apply logs the query string; docs tabs render; integration test of the demo.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: changes to ezSearch itself (log bugs found as separate issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["dev-section", "entry-shell", "docs-box"], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "entry-form-fields", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Component Library: Form fields entry (FormFields::*)", "description": "<p>The house rules require <code>FormFields::*</code> for every form, so developers and agents need to see them and their options in one place. Add a Form fields entry to the Component Library.</p><ul><li><code>components/developer/demos/form-fields.{hbs,js}</code>: a field picker in Controls switching between FieldText, FieldTextArea, FieldRelate (<code>@relateType=\\"relate-simple\\"</code>), FieldRelateMulti, FieldMultiSelect, FieldDate, FieldCheckbox, FieldSwitch, FieldUpload, FieldSearch, with fixture options (users with avatars for relate).</li><li>Common controls: disabled/read-only, a validation error (<code>@validate</code> + <code>@message</code>, <code>FormFields::ValidationMessages</code>), placeholder, <code>@searchEnabled</code> where supported. Show the current value under the demo. Value changes go to the event log. FieldUpload must not upload: log the file instead.</li><li>Registry entry (group Forms, stable, variants = the field count) and <code>public/ui-docs/form-fields.md</code>: per field its arguments, <code>@data-field</code> and <code>@aclContext</code> (field-level ACL), and Do and Avoid (never a bare <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;PowerSelect&gt;</code>, no helper text under fields: info-icon tooltips, labels come from translations in product screens).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: every listed field renders and reports its value; validation state shown; docs tabs render; integration test of the demo.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: the legacy root-level field components (<code>components/field-*.js</code>), changes to the fields.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["dev-section", "entry-shell", "docs-box"], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "entry-modal", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Component Library: Modal entry (bootstrap-modal)", "description": "<p><code>bootstrap-modal</code> is our only modal, and we have had bugs with its confirm handling and with modals trapped inside a parent's stacking context or styles (fixed by rendering through <code>in-element</code>, see <code>components/idea/message-screen.hbs</code>). Document it in the Component Library.</p><ul><li><code>components/developer/demos/modal.{hbs,js}</code>: an Open button and Controls for title, <code>@containerClass</code>, <code>@removeConfirmBtn</code>, confirm behaviour (resolves after 1s / rejects / returns true synchronously) and \\"render inside a constrained box\\" vs \\"render with in-element\\" to show the stacking problem and its fix.</li><li>Event log: open, confirm (with result), cancel, hide.</li><li>Registry entry (group Overlays) with status taken from the current confirm behaviour (experimental if async confirm is not in the component yet) and <code>public/ui-docs/modal.md</code>: arguments, the confirm contract as it is in the code today, and Do and Avoid (render outside scroll/stacking containers, title is translated via <code>t</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: each control combination demonstrable; events logged; docs tabs render; integration test of the demo.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing bootstrap-modal (log bugs found as separate issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["dev-section", "entry-shell", "docs-box"], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "entry-dropdown", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Component Library: Dropdown entry (AppUi::Dropdown)", "description": "<p><code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> (<code>components/app-ui/dropdown.{hbs,js}</code>, styles <code>styles/components/dropdown.scss</code>) is used for Saved Searches menus and board filters; alignment (<code>right: 0</code> by default) and hover/selected colours caused several bugs (aprom-4309, 4346). Document it in the Component Library.</p><ul><li><code>components/developer/demos/dropdown.{hbs,js}</code>: a trigger with fixture items (plain, with icons, a selected item, a divider, a long label). Controls: placement near the left edge / right edge of the demo box, scoped left alignment as used by ezSearch, many items (scroll).</li><li>Event log: open, close, item chosen.</li><li>Registry entry (group Menus, stable, used in: ezSearch saved searches, Task Board) and <code>public/ui-docs/dropdown.md</code>: arguments and blocks, and Do and Avoid (scope alignment overrides under the user's root class, never restyle globally; hover/selected colours).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: all variants demonstrable; events logged; docs tabs render; integration test of the demo.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing the dropdown.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["dev-section", "entry-shell", "docs-box"], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "remove-settings-ui", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Settings: remove the Developer -> UI page (moved to the Developer section)", "description": "<p>The QuickList demo now lives in the Developer section's Component Library, which is kept apart from Settings on purpose. Remove the old Settings page.</p><ul><li>Remove the <code>developer</code> group from <code>views.Navigation.settingsItems</code> in <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> (~l.280).</li><li>Remove the <code>ui</code> routes from <code>app/router.js</code> (~l.74), <code>routes/app/settings/ui/index.js</code>, <code>controllers/app/settings/ui/quick-list.js</code>, <code>templates/app/settings/ui.hbs</code>, <code>templates/app/settings/ui/quick-list.hbs</code>, their <code>services/acl.js</code> routeMaps entries (~l.91-93), their translation keys (<code>views.app.settings.ui.*</code>, <code>views.nav.menu.settings.ui</code>, <code>views.nav.menu.settings.group.developer</code>) and their tests. Keep <code>utils/dev/quick-list-fixture.js</code> if the new entry uses it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: Settings shows Access, Projects and System only; <code>/app/settings/ui</code> no longer exists; the Developer -&gt; Components -&gt; QuickList entry still works; tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: anything else in Settings.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["entry-quick-list"], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 16:01:05	2026-11-08 17:22:18	f
23ae5e456af2-54cf-3ec9-7ae4278e1ac5	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	10	{"summary": "Fixes the white space in the role detail's Role box (aprom-4432). The record keeps FormFields with @allowInlineEdit, which render as full form fields even when reading. Switch the name and description to AppUi::InlineEditable, as the user profile page does: plain text with a pencil when reading, a FormFields input with check/cancel only while editing. Then tighten the layout: 48px initials square, bold name and caption beside it, description under the name, facts on one compact row.", "issues": [{"key": "role-record-compact", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Role detail: Role box wastes space; use AppUi::InlineEditable for name and description", "description": "<p>After aprom-4432 the Role box on the role detail page is mostly white space. The name and description are <code>FormFields::FieldText</code>/<code>FieldTextArea</code> with <code>@allowInlineEdit</code>, so they render as full form fields even when only reading: the <code>.form-field</code> margin, a full-width field that pushes the pencil to the far right, and a textarea with placeholder and resize handle. The facts are 18px <code>&lt;h4&gt;</code> headings spread in thirds. Prometheus has the right component for inline editing: <code>AppUi::InlineEditable</code> (<code>components/app-ui/inline-editable.hbs</code>), used on the user profile page (<code>templates/app/user/page.hbs</code> ~l.30-160). The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and the existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li><strong>Name</strong>: <code>&lt;AppUi::InlineEditable&gt;</code> inside an <code>&lt;h3&gt;</code> next to the initials square. <code>&lt;:display&gt;</code> = the name (18px, bold); <code>&lt;:edit as |f|&gt;</code> = <code>FormFields::FieldText</code> exactly as the user page's name (<code>@value={{f.value}}</code>, <code>@onInput={{f.update}}</code>, validation via the role's <code>roleCreate</code> schema, <code>autofocus</code>, <code>f.onKeydown</code>). Wire <code>@onSave</code>, <code>@validate</code>, <code>@message</code>, <code>@onClearMessage</code> with the base create controller's <code>saveModelAttribute</code>/<code>validateInlineField</code>/<code>clearFieldMessage</code>; <code>@aclContext=\\"role.update\\"</code>.</li><li><strong>Description</strong>: <code>&lt;AppUi::InlineEditable&gt;</code> lined up under the name (indented past the initials). <code>&lt;:display&gt;</code> = plain paragraph; empty state through the component's <code>@label</code>/empty hint (\\"Add a description\\"). <code>&lt;:edit&gt;</code> = <code>FormFields::FieldTextArea</code>. <code>@submitOnEnter={{false}}</code> so Enter adds a line.</li><li><strong>Layout</strong>: initials square 48px in the tier colour beside the name; caption \\"Created … by … · Modified …\\" (12px grey) under the name; facts (Access labels, Members, Actions granted) on one row under a light <code>#f4f4f4</code> separator, each a 12px grey label above a bold value, with a fixed gap (not spread in thirds). Remove the old <code>editRole</code>/<code>resetModelAttributes</code> wiring and the styles that served the FormFields-in-record layout from <code>styles/modules/role.scss</code>; new rules scoped under <code>.role-record</code>.</li><li>Tests: editing the name and the description saves (check and Enter for the name; check for the description), cancel restores the value, a blank name shows the validation message, no ACL hides the pencil, the empty description shows the hint.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: the Role box is about as tall as the attached screen; reading shows plain text with pencils, editing shows the field only while editing.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4434"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["role-record-inline"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 21:41:55	2026-11-09 21:44:22	f
049cc0656af0-f978-689a-32cf2f8b8bec	c31674596af0-6d25-f538-e6760785c02e	1	{"summary": "Gives every Projects4Me service its own identity and lets Talos run Gaia-declared agents without ever holding agent secrets. Gaia gets service clients (no user behind the token), a deny-by-default service access path, scope ceilings on tokens, enrollment by on-screen approval (A) or single-use enrollment token (B), self-rotation, agent delegation (Agent.delegationScopes, 1-hour tokens with sub = agent, client = runtime), runtime reads (delegable agents, specs, grants) and an introspection response with actor type and project ids. Hermes is hardened now, then enrolls, authenticates sockets through introspection (disconnecting at token expiry), drops access live on user.access.changed and serves a runtimes room for run requests. Talos enrolls, discovers Gaia agents, runs them on delegated tokens and takes run requests from the runtimes room. Prometheus gets Settings > Services (clients, enrollments, enrollment tokens) and a Delegation scopes field on agents. Order: Gaia base (service clients, token scopes) -> enrollment, access, delegation, introspection -> Hermes and Talos -> runtimes room. Contract pairs (access-changed, runtimes room) merge together.", "issues": [{"key": "h-hardening", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Ingest: timing-safe secret check and no default secret outside local dev", "description": "<p>Gaia publishes to <code>POST /publish</code> with a shared secret (<code>X-Hermes-Secret</code>). The check in <code>src/http/middleware/require-secret.js</code> uses <code>!==</code> (not timing-safe), and <code>src/config.js</code> falls back to <code>hermes-dev-secret</code> in every non-production environment. This hardens the secret until Hermes gets a service identity (later issues in this idea).</p><ul><li>Compare the secret with <code>crypto.timingSafeEqual</code> on equal-length buffers (different lengths = reject without leaking timing).</li><li><code>config.js</code>: use the dev default only when <code>NODE_ENV</code> is <code>development</code> or <code>test</code>; any other value without <code>HERMES_SECRET</code> fails at startup with a clear message. Also refuse to start with <code>HERMES_SECRET=hermes-dev-secret</code> outside development/test.</li><li>Never log the secret; ADR entry in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests for wrong, missing, different-length and correct secrets; startup tests for each NODE_ENV case. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing the shared secret.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-service-clients", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Service clients: OAuth client kind service, client_credentials tokens without a user", "description": "<p>Services (Talos runtimes, Hermes, later Ares) need their own identity, never to be confused with agents, which are users and also use client_credentials (agaia-4028, <code>core/libs/authorization/AgentClientCredentials.php</code>). This adds the service client concept.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Serviceclient</code> (bundle B): name, kind (<code>runtime</code> | <code>hermes</code>), status (active | disabled), scopes (JSON list, defaults per kind from <code>config/*.php</code>: runtime gets <code>agent.delegate</code> plus the runtime read scopes, hermes gets <code>token.introspect</code>), lastUsedAt, oauth client id. Admin-only ACL: list, get, PATCH status; no POST (clients are created by enrollment, later issue). api-tester acl cases.</li><li>Mark every OAuth client with a kind (app | agent | service). The client_credentials handler branches on it: agent clients keep today's behaviour (token user_id = agent email); service clients get a token with <strong>no user_id</strong> and the client's scopes; disabled clients get nothing. A service client can never get a user token and an agent client never a service token.</li><li>Store only a hash of service secrets (follow agaia-4028's Agentcredential storage if it already hashes; otherwise hash in <code>core/libs/oauth2.0/storage/pdo.php</code> for service clients).</li><li>Service clients are not users: no row in users, not in user lists or pickers.</li><li>Decision entries in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for the grant branching (agent, service, disabled, app client); a service token on any existing CRUD resource still fails as today. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> what service tokens may access, enrollment, rotation.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-token-scopes", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "ACL: tokens with scopes are held to them on top of the actor's ACL", "description": "<p>Delegated agent tokens (later issue) must never do more than their scopes allow, even when the agent's roles would. Today scopes on tokens are ignored. Effective access becomes: the actor's ACL AND the token's scopes. Scopes only narrow; tokens without scopes (people, agents' own credentials) are unchanged.</p><ul><li>Scope vocabulary = existing permission names (<code>issue.get</code>, <code>comment.create</code>) with <code>*</code> wildcards (<code>issue.*</code>, <code>*.get</code>).</li><li>In <code>RestController::authorize()</code> (after <code>verifyResourceRequest</code>), when the access token has a scope, the requested <code>controller.action</code> must match one; related and included resources (RBAC D-020) are checked the same way and omitted when not covered (D-021).</li><li>Hard exclusions for scoped tokens regardless of scope: agentcredential.*, serviceclient.*, enrollment resources, role.*, userrole.*, permission.*, agent create/update/delete.</li><li>Keep the check in one class under <code>core/libs/security</code> (not inline in the controller); decision entry in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for matching, wildcards, related reads and exclusions; api-tester cases with a scoped token. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> issuing scoped tokens.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-service-access", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "ACL: deny-by-default access path for service tokens", "description": "<p>A service token has no user, so <code>RestController::setUser()</code> rejects it today. Runtimes must read a few things as themselves (delegable agents, specs, grants). This adds a separate, deny-by-default path that never touches RBAC roles or the resolution mode.</p><ul><li>Resources opt in to service access in their model ACL metadata (which actions, which service kinds). A service token is allowed only when the resource opted in AND <code>controller.action</code> is in the service client's scopes; everything else 401.</li><li>Optional per-resource record filter for service tokens (metadata hook), so a resource can limit rows (e.g. only delegable agents).</li><li>No current user for service requests: behaviours and components that need one must not run or must handle it (list them in the PR).</li><li>Requests by a disabled client fail; <code>lastUsedAt</code> updated.</li><li>Decision entry in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit with a test resource opted in and one not; api-tester acl cases with a service token. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> opting real resources in (later issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-service-clients"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-enrollment", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Service enrollment: request, admin approval with a code, secret delivered to the service", "description": "<p>No secret may be copied by hand. A service enrolls itself: it asks Gaia, shows a short code, an admin approves the matching request, and the service receives its secret straight from Gaia (device-authorization style, RFC 8628).</p><ul><li>Resource <code>Serviceenrollment</code>: name, kind, status (pending | approved | denied | expired | delivered), userCode (e.g. <code>KQ7-3MX</code>), expiresAt (15 minutes), approvedBy, serviceclientId.</li><li>Anonymous POST creates a pending request and returns id, userCode, expiresAt and a pollToken (shown once, stored hashed). Rate limited per IP.</li><li>Anonymous GET by id with the pollToken: returns status; once approved, returns clientId and clientSecret <strong>once</strong> (status delivered), creating the Serviceclient with its kind's default scopes.</li><li>Admin list + PATCH status approved/denied (ACL like other admin resources). Expired requests can't be approved.</li><li>Only these two actions are anonymous: decide how (controller <code>$authorization</code> is controller-wide today) and record it in the decisions doc. Standard CRUD only, no custom routes.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for the state machine (expiry, double delivery, wrong pollToken, deny); api-tester cases for anonymous and admin paths. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> enrollment tokens, UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-service-clients"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-enrollment-tokens", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Service enrollment: single-use enrollment tokens for unattended deploys", "description": "<p>Deployed services (Hermes, later Ares) can't wait for someone to approve a code. A deploy pipeline gets a single-use enrollment token and passes it to the container; the service enrolls with it and is approved automatically.</p><ul><li>Resource <code>Serviceenrollmenttoken</code>: kind, name, expiresAt (15 minutes), usedAt, createdUser. Admin POST returns the token once (stored hashed); list and DELETE (revoke).</li><li>An enrollment request (agaia <code>Serviceenrollment</code> POST) carrying a valid, unused, unexpired token of the same kind is approved at once; the token is marked used. Invalid tokens are refused without saying why.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for single use, expiry, kind mismatch, revoke; api-tester acl cases. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["g-enrollment"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-secret-rotation", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Service clients rotate their own secret", "description": "<p>No service secret should live forever and nobody should handle rotation. A service replaces its own secret with its current service token.</p><ul><li>Opt <code>Serviceclient</code> PATCH in to service access (agaia service access path) for the client's own record only, field <code>rotateSecret: true</code>; the response carries the new secret once. The old secret stays valid for 10 minutes so a crash mid-rotation doesn't lock the service out.</li><li>Scope <code>serviceclient.rotate</code> in every kind's defaults.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit (own record only, grace period, old secret refused after it); api-tester case. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> rotation schedule (each service decides).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["g-service-access"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-delegation", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Agents: delegationScopes and the delegation grant for runtimes", "description": "<p>Talos (a runtime service client) must run Gaia-declared agents without holding their secrets. It asks Gaia for a short-lived token acting as the agent.</p><ul><li><code>Agent.delegationScopes</code>: JSON list of permission names with <code>*</code> (agaia scope vocabulary). Empty = the agent can't be delegated. Editable by those with agent.update; an agent can't change its own (extend <code>AgentEscalationGuard</code>).</li><li>New grant type (e.g. <code>urn:projects4me:params:oauth:grant-type:agent-delegation</code>, params <code>agent_id</code>, optional <code>scope</code>), registered in <code>core/libs/authorization/OAuthServer.php</code> like <code>AgentClientCredentials</code>. Client must be an active service client with scope <code>agent.delegate</code>; agent must be active with non-empty delegationScopes; requested scope must be a subset (default = all of them).</li><li>Token: user_id = agent email (as today), client_id = the runtime's client, scope = granted, 1 hour, no refresh token. Keep these token rows (no purge) so the token table shows which runtime acted for which agent when.</li><li>Decision entry in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for every refusal case and the happy path; a delegated token can't reach anything outside its scopes (relies on the token scopes issue). <strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-step scopes, runtime-to-agent binding.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-service-clients", "g-token-scopes"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-runtime-reads", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Runtime reads: delegable agents, agent specs and grants for runtime service tokens", "description": "<p>A Talos runtime discovers the agents it may run from Gaia with its own service token (no user), instead of naming them locally.</p><ul><li>Opt in to service access for kind <code>runtime</code> (agaia service access path): Agent list/get limited by a record filter to active agents with non-empty delegationScopes; agentspec get (agaia-4043) for those agents; Agenttool, Agentskill and Skill (with files) list/get for those agents.</li><li>Never Agentcredential, Useridentity or any secret field; field ACL keeps secrets out of the agent payload.</li><li>Add the matching scopes to the runtime kind's defaults.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> api-tester cases with a runtime token: delegable agent visible, non-delegable and inactive agents hidden, credentials refused, a hermes-kind token refused. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other service kinds.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["g-service-access", "g-delegation"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-introspection", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Introspection: callable with a service token, returns actor type, client, scopes and project ids", "description": "<p>Hermes will check socket tokens with Gaia introspection (agaia-4029) using its own service token, replacing <code>/user/me</code> plus a membership query with the user's token. Contract change with A Hermes (socket auth issue).</p><ul><li>Accept a service token with scope <code>token.introspect</code>; keep the agaia-4029 shared-secret door for Ares until Ares is reworked.</li><li>Response (RFC 7662 names plus ours): <code>active</code>, <code>sub</code> (user id), <code>actorType</code> (user | agent | service), <code>clientId</code>, <code>act</code> (the service client id when the token is delegated), <code>scope</code>, <code>exp</code>, <code>projectIds</code> (memberships, for users and agents), <code>serviceKind</code> for service tokens. Inactive or disabled = <code>{active: false}</code> only.</li><li>Agent tool grants stay in the response as 4029 built them.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit and api-tester cases for user, agent, delegated, service and expired tokens. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> Ares changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-service-clients"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-access-changed", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Live events: publish user.access.changed when a user's access changes", "description": "<p>Hermes checks a socket only at connect and caches access for 5 minutes, so removed members and disabled users keep receiving events. Gaia tells Hermes when a user's access changes. Contract change: merges together with the matching A Hermes issue (allowlist + handler).</p><ul><li>Name <code>user.access.changed</code> in <code>support/EventNames.php</code>, user-scoped like Hermes D-009 (<code>user:&lt;id&gt;</code>).</li><li>Publish it after: account status changes, session revocation (agaia-3954 path), membership create and delete. No payload beyond the user id.</li><li>Live events component per bundle E; fail open like other events.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit plus api-tester <code>hermes.expect</code> cases for each trigger. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> role changes (don't affect Hermes).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-runtimes-room", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Live events: also publish workflow.agent.run.requested to the runtimes scope", "description": "<p>Talos runtimes take run requests on one socket (runtimes room) instead of one socket per agent. Contract change: merges together with the matching A Hermes issue.</p><ul><li>Where Gaia publishes <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> to the agent's user scope (agaia-4052, Hermes D-017), also publish it with the scope <code>runtimes</code> (exact form agreed with the Hermes issue).</li><li>Only for agents with non-empty delegationScopes. The existing claim (RunAgentActor claim window) decides which runtime takes the step when several listen.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> api-tester <code>hermes.expect</code> cases for delegable and non-delegable agents. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> routing to a specific runtime.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-delegation"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "h-service-identity", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Hermes enrolls with Gaia and keeps a service token", "description": "<p>Hermes gets its own identity from Gaia (service client of kind <code>hermes</code>) so it can call Gaia as itself. No secret is copied by hand.</p><ul><li>One gateway module in <code>src/auth/</code>: on start, if no stored credential, enroll with <code>GAIA_ENROLLMENT_TOKEN</code> (auto-approved) or, without one, create a request and log its user code for an admin to approve, then poll until delivered.</li><li>Store the client id and secret in a file at a configured path (mounted volume, mode 600). ADR in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>: credential file is not domain storage (Hermes stays a relay).</li><li>Get and refresh a client_credentials token before expiry; rotate its secret weekly via Gaia's rotation.</li><li>Never log the secret, token or user code beyond the one log line for approval.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> in-process tests with a stub Gaia (D-015) for both enrollment paths, restart with stored credential, token refresh and rotation. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> using the token (next issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-enrollment-tokens", "g-secret-rotation"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "h-socket-auth", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Socket auth through Gaia introspection, disconnect at token expiry", "description": "<p>Replace the per-socket <code>/user/me</code> + membership lookup with the user's token (<code>src/auth/gaia-session.js</code>) by one Gaia introspection call made with Hermes' service token. Contract with A Gaia introspection issue.</p><ul><li>Session = <code>sub</code>, <code>actorType</code>, <code>projectIds</code>, <code>exp</code> from introspection; cache as today (<code>session-cache.js</code>), never past <code>exp</code>.</li><li>Accept user and agent tokens (delegated included); refuse service tokens on normal intents (the runtimes room comes later).</li><li>Disconnect a socket when its token's <code>exp</code> passes (Prometheus already reconnects with the refreshed token, <code>services/hermes.js</code>).</li><li>ADR update for D-002, D-011, D-012.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests with a stub introspection: active, inactive, service token refused, expiry disconnect, cache bounded by exp. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> live revocation.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["h-service-identity", "g-introspection"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "h-access-changed", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Allowlist user.access.changed and re-check that user's sockets", "description": "<p>Gaia publishes <code>user.access.changed</code> (user-scoped) when a user is disabled, sessions are revoked or memberships change. Contract change: merges together with the matching A Gaia issue.</p><ul><li>Add the name to <code>src/contract/names.js</code> (must match Gaia <code>EventNames.php</code>); ADR entry.</li><li>On it: evict the user's cached sessions, re-introspect each of the user's sockets; disconnect if inactive, otherwise re-apply intents so rooms of projects no longer in <code>projectIds</code> are left.</li><li>Not forwarded to clients.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests for membership removal (room left), disable (disconnect), unchanged access (no effect). <strong>Out of scope:</strong> role changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["h-socket-auth"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "h-runtimes-room", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Runtimes room: runtime service tokens receive workflow.agent.run.requested", "description": "<p>Talos runtimes take run requests on one socket. Gaia also publishes <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> with the scope <code>runtimes</code>. Contract change: merges together with the matching A Gaia issue.</p><ul><li>Accept that scope on <code>/publish</code> for this event only.</li><li>Only sockets whose introspection says <code>actorType: service</code> and <code>serviceKind: runtime</code> may set an intent for it; everyone else is refused it; runtime tokens may set no other intent.</li><li>ADR entry (alongside D-009 and D-017).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests: runtime token receives the event, user and agent tokens refused, runtime token refused on project intents. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-runtime routing.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["h-socket-auth"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "d-enroll", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: enroll as a runtime service client and keep a service token", "description": "<p>Talos becomes a registered runtime in Gaia with no hand-copied secret, the first step towards running Gaia-declared agents (and later running inside Ares).</p><ul><li>Through gaia-mcp (the only tracker client): enrollment (create request, poll, receive secret once), service client_credentials token, token refresh, self-rotation of the secret (weekly).</li><li><code>talos enroll</code> (and on <code>talos run</code> when no credential): uses <code>TALOS_ENROLLMENT_TOKEN</code> if set, otherwise prints the user code for an admin to approve in Prometheus and waits.</li><li>Credential stored under <code>LOCAL_DIR</code> state (git-ignored, owner-only permissions on both platforms); never logged.</li><li>README for Talos and gaia-mcp; stdlib only.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests with a fake Gaia for both enrollment paths, restart with a stored credential, refresh and rotation. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> agent discovery.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-enrollment-tokens", "g-secret-rotation"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "d-discover", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: discover Gaia agents and run them on delegated tokens", "description": "<p>Talos stops naming Gaia agents locally (<code>gaiaAgent</code> in agent.json, <code>talos/lib/registry.py</code> ~l.131-165) and asks Gaia which agents it may run, with its runtime service token.</p><ul><li>Periodically list delegable agents and load each spec (reuse <code>talos/lib/agent_spec.py</code> <code>settings_from</code>), tool grants and skills.</li><li>Per agent, get a delegated token (agaia delegation grant) and cache it; renew about 5 minutes before expiry; every Gaia call and the Hermes connection made for that agent's runs use it.</li><li>Gaia-declared agents take work from workflow run requests only (adt-4047 path); agent.json stays for Talos' own agents (Odysseus, Nestor, Agamemnon) with their own credentials. Remove <code>gaiaAgent</code> support and its README section.</li><li>Agent disabled or delegation emptied in Gaia: stop starting new runs for it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests: discovery adds and removes agents, token cache renewal, refusal handling. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> runtimes room (next issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["d-enroll", "g-runtime-reads"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "d-runtimes-room", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: take workflow run requests from the Hermes runtimes room", "description": "<p>One socket per runtime instead of one per agent: Talos listens to <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> in the runtimes room with its service token and hands each request to the discovered agent it names.</p><ul><li>Listener in <code>talos/lib/hermes.py</code> with the service token (fresh on every reconnect, as today).</li><li>Requests for agents this runtime doesn't run are ignored; the step claim decides between runtimes.</li><li>Drop the per-agent run-request subscription for Gaia agents.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for routing, unknown agent and reconnect. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-runtime routing.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["d-discover", "h-runtimes-room", "g-runtimes-room"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "p-services", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Settings > Services: list service clients and disable them", "description": "<p>Admins need to see which services (Talos runtimes, Hermes) have an identity in Gaia and cut one off at once.</p><ul><li>New settings item Services (<code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> <code>settingsItems</code>, group system) and route under <code>settings</code>.</li><li>List of <code>serviceclient</code>: name, kind, status label, last used; Disable / Enable with a confirm modal (<code>bootstrap-modal</code>).</li><li>Design system boxes and table; empty state.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> model, Mirage, acceptance test for list and disable. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> enrollments (next issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["g-service-clients"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "p-enrollments", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Settings > Services: approve enrollment requests and create enrollment tokens", "description": "<p>Services enroll by showing a code; an admin approves the matching request here. Deploy pipelines use single-use enrollment tokens created here.</p><ul><li>Pending requests box on the Services page: name, kind, user code, time left; Approve / Deny (confirm modal asks the admin to check the code matches what the service shows).</li><li>Enrollment tokens box: create (kind, name) shows the token once with a copy button and a warning that it is single-use for 15 minutes; list with used/expired state; revoke.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> acceptance tests for approve, deny, expired request, token create and revoke. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> editing scopes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["p-services", "g-enrollment-tokens"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "p-delegation-scopes", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Agents: Delegation scopes field on the agent form", "description": "<p>Sponsors choose what a runtime may do when running an agent: <code>Agent.delegationScopes</code>, a list of permission names with <code>*</code>; empty means the agent can't run on a runtime.</p><ul><li>Field on agent create/edit (<code>templates/app/agent/create.hbs</code>, shared create controller): multi-select of permission names plus wildcard entries per module (<code>issue.*</code>), free entry allowed; info-icon tooltip explains empty = no delegation.</li><li>Agent page shows the scopes, or No delegation.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> integration test for the field, acceptance test saving scopes. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> validating scopes against the catalog.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["g-delegation"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 20:13:56	2026-11-08 20:13:56	f
0bb2c9086af2-440d-d733-dd1c3c6d9a07	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	8	{"summary": "The Roles page moves from a card grid to the QuickList list + detail layout. Every piece of card information stays in the row: an initials square in the tier colour, the name, granted % and denied % labels, a one-line description, member avatars and the modified date. The first role opens by default. A small QuickList addition (an optional <:leading> block on QuickList::Item) is built alongside the state toolkit (aprom-4425/4426). The Roles change then uses both, and a final cleanup removes Role::Card and rewrites the role architecture doc.", "issues": [{"key": "ql-item-leading", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: optional leading block on QuickList::Item (icon/avatar column)", "description": "<p>Some lists need a visual on the left of each row with the text lines lined up beside it: the Roles list needs an initials square in its access-tier colour, issue lists a priority icon, user lists an avatar. <code>QuickList::Item</code> only has <code>&lt;:primary&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;:secondary&gt;</code> today. This adds an optional leading column to the QuickList contract.</p><ul><li><code>QuickList::Item</code> (<code>components/quick-list/item.{hbs,js}</code>): optional <code>&lt;:leading&gt;</code> block rendered in a fixed-width column before the body (after the selection checkbox when <code>@selectable</code>), top-aligned; the body takes the remaining width so the primary/secondary lines align under each other. Without the block, the row is exactly as today.</li><li>Pass the block through the root <code>QuickList</code>'s <code>&lt;:item&gt;</code> usage (callers write <code>&lt;item.leading&gt;</code> or the documented equivalent; keep it consistent with how <code>&lt;:primary&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;:secondary&gt;</code> are exposed).</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/components/quick-list.scss</code> (or the item partial): leading column width set by content, 8px gap, square edges. No new colours.</li><li>Show it on the Settings &gt; Developer &gt; UI QuickList page (an initials square on the fixture rows).</li><li>Update the YUIDoc contract; integration tests: row with leading (column rendered before the body, body lines intact), row without leading unchanged, with selection (checkbox, then leading, then body).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: as above; existing QuickList tests pass unchanged.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "roles-quicklist", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Roles: list + detail layout with QuickList, card details in each row, first role opened by default", "description": "<p>The Roles page (<code>templates/app/role.hbs</code>) shows a grid of <code>Role::Card</code>s (<code>components/role/card.{hbs,js}</code>) that squeezes into a <code>col-lg-2</code> column when a role opens (<code>controllers/app/role.js</code> <code>isRolePage</code>/<code>rolesClass</code>/<code>roleCardClass</code>). The route (<code>routes/app/role.js</code>) loads every role, every userrole with its user, and one permission query per role for access coverage; the search only filters the loaded names. Move it to the QuickList list + detail layout used by the idea browser, built on the state toolkit (<code>ListLoader</code>, <code>UrlState</code> from aprom-4425/4426) and the new <code>&lt;:leading&gt;</code> item block. The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and the existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li><strong>Layout</strong>: <code>.row</code> with <code>col-md-3</code> QuickList and <code>col-md-9</code> outlet (the existing <code>app.role.page</code>, unchanged). Remove <code>isRolePage</code>/<code>rolesClass</code>/<code>roleCardClass</code> and the <code>roles--detail-open</code> classes.</li><li><strong>Row</strong>, keeping all the card's information: <code>&lt;:leading&gt;</code> = square initials box (same initials logic as <code>Role::Card</code>) in the access-tier colour (existing tiers in <code>styles/modules/role.scss</code>: high/elevated/medium/low/no data). Primary = role name, the granted <code>{percent}%</code> label in the tier colour and, when above 0, a red <code>{percent}% denied</code> label (same values as the card's granted/denied). Secondary line 1 = description, one line cut off with an ellipsis, or grey italic \\"No description\\". Secondary line 2 = <code>Project::MemberAvatars</code> with <code>@maxVisible={{2}}</code> (or \\"No members\\") on the left and the modified date (<code>dateModified</code>, fallback <code>dateCreated</code>, <code>DD MMM YYYY</code>) on the right. Active row = the open role (QuickList's crimson bar replaces the card's chevron and fading). Reuse the card's translation keys.</li><li><strong>Header and search</strong>: \\"Roles\\" with count; <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> = <strong>New Role</strong> (<code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code>, ACL <code>role.create</code>) opening the existing add-role modal; <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> = <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> with new metadata <code>views.Role.search</code> (<code>Role.name</code>, <code>Role.description</code>, in <code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>, same format as <code>views.Idea.search</code>) plus saved searches as in the idea browser. No selection.</li><li><strong>Group and sort</strong>: group by none or access tier (client-side, loaded page only); sort by name (default ASC) or last modified (DESC) via Gaia <code>Role.name</code>/<code>Role.dateModified</code>.</li><li><strong>Data</strong>: <code>UrlState</code> for <code>query</code>, <code>searchId</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>order</code>, <code>group</code> (all <code>refreshModel: false</code>); a <code>ListLoader</code> for roles (20 per page, limit + 1, one shared <code>buildRequest</code>). After each page loads, query permissions only for that page's roles (<code>permission?roleId=</code> per role, as today) and userroles with <code>rels: 'user'</code> only for that page's role ids; compute coverage and members with the existing <code>coverageByRole</code>/<code>isActionAllowed</code>/<code>membersByRole</code> logic. Reset on leaving the roles area.</li><li><strong>First role by default</strong>: a new <code>app.role.index</code> route. Once the list has loaded and no role is open, it calls <code>replaceWith('app.role.page', firstRow.id)</code>, so Back doesn't bounce onto the list again. This also applies after a search, a page change or deleting the open role, but never moves a user away from a role they opened. When no roles match, the index shows a <code>box box-primary</code> with a centred grey <code>fa-info-circle</code> \\"No roles match this search\\".</li><li><strong>Keep working</strong>: create (the new role appears; reload the current page and open it), delete from the role page (<code>deleteRole</code> reloads the list instead of filtering arrays, then the first role opens), permission and member edits on the role page refresh that role's row (<code>syncRoleCoverage</code> and member reload for the open role).</li><li>Update the roles acceptance tests and Mirage handlers (role paging/sort, userrole by role ids). Add tests for: row content (initials, both labels, description fallback, avatars, date), search, paging, group by tier, first role opened on landing and after deleting the open role, and the no-match state.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: as above; the URL keeps the list params; opening a role doesn't reload the list.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: removing <code>Role::Card</code> and its styles (follow-up), bulk actions on roles.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4425", "aprom-4426", "ql-item-leading"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "The list, its per-page coverage and member data, and the auto-open index route ship together: a list without coverage or members would lose information from the cards, and without auto-open the detail column is empty on landing.", "screens": ["roles-quick-list"]}, {"key": "roles-card-cleanup", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Roles: remove Role::Card and rewrite the role-cards architecture doc", "description": "<p>After the Roles page moves to QuickList, <code>Role::Card</code> is no longer used. Remove it and update the docs.</p><ul><li>Delete <code>app/components/role/card.{hbs,js}</code> and its tests, and the card-only rules in <code>app/styles/modules/role.scss</code>. Keep the tier colours used by the row's initials box and labels, and move the initials helper if the Roles list imports it from the card.</li><li>Remove <code>views.app.role.card.*</code> translation keys only if no longer referenced (the list reuses some).</li><li>Rewrite <code>prometheus/docs/architecture/role-cards/architecture.md</code> as <code>role-list/architecture.md</code>: QuickList list + detail, row contents, per-page permission and userrole queries, first role opened by default, the coverage formula and tiers (unchanged), ownership table.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: no references to <code>Role::Card</code> remain; the full suite passes; the doc describes the current page.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["roles-quicklist"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 19:24:59	2026-11-09 19:37:31	f
69ad28596af0-871c-7b74-a31ef7f86660	c31674596af0-6d25-f538-e6760785c02e	2	{"summary": "Gives every Projects4Me service its own identity and lets Talos run Gaia-declared agents without ever holding agent secrets. Gaia gets service clients (no user behind the token), a deny-by-default service access path, scope ceilings on tokens, enrollment by on-screen approval (A) or single-use enrollment token (B), self-rotation, agent delegation (Agent.delegationScopes, 1-hour tokens with sub = agent, client = runtime), runtime reads (delegable agents, specs, grants) and an introspection response with actor type and project ids. Hermes is hardened now, then enrolls, authenticates sockets through introspection (disconnecting at token expiry), drops access live on user.access.changed and serves a runtimes room for run requests. Talos enrolls, discovers Gaia agents, runs them on delegated tokens (Gaia agents take work from workflows only) and takes run requests from the runtimes room. Prometheus gets Settings > Services (clients, enrollments, enrollment tokens) and a Delegation scopes field on agents. Order: Gaia base (service clients, token scopes) -> enrollment, access, delegation, introspection -> Hermes and Talos -> runtimes room. Contract pairs (access-changed, runtimes room) merge together. All in milestone aga-Identity.", "issues": [{"key": "h-hardening", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Ingest: timing-safe secret check and no default secret outside local dev", "description": "<p>Gaia publishes to <code>POST /publish</code> with a shared secret (<code>X-Hermes-Secret</code>). The check in <code>src/http/middleware/require-secret.js</code> uses <code>!==</code> (not timing-safe), and <code>src/config.js</code> falls back to <code>hermes-dev-secret</code> in every non-production environment. This hardens the secret until Hermes gets a service identity (later issues in this milestone).</p><ul><li>Compare the secret with <code>crypto.timingSafeEqual</code> on equal-length buffers (different lengths = reject without leaking timing).</li><li><code>config.js</code>: use the dev default only when <code>NODE_ENV</code> is <code>development</code> or <code>test</code>; any other value without <code>HERMES_SECRET</code> fails at startup with a clear message. Also refuse to start with <code>HERMES_SECRET=hermes-dev-secret</code> outside development/test.</li><li>Never log the secret; ADR entry in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests for wrong, missing, different-length and correct secrets; startup tests for each NODE_ENV case. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing the shared secret.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-service-clients", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Service clients: OAuth client kind service, client_credentials tokens without a user", "description": "<p>Services (Talos runtimes, Hermes, later Ares) need their own identity, never to be confused with agents, which are users and also use client_credentials (agaia-4028, <code>core/libs/authorization/AgentClientCredentials.php</code>). This adds the service client concept.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Serviceclient</code> (bundle B): name, kind (<code>runtime</code> | <code>hermes</code>), status (active | disabled), scopes (JSON list, defaults per kind from <code>config/*.php</code>: runtime gets <code>agent.delegate</code> plus the runtime read scopes, hermes gets <code>token.introspect</code>), lastUsedAt, oauth client id. Admin-only ACL: list, get, PATCH status; no POST (clients are created by enrollment, later issue). api-tester acl cases.</li><li>Mark every OAuth client with a kind (app | agent | service). The client_credentials handler branches on it: agent clients keep today's behaviour (token user_id = agent email); service clients get a token with <strong>no user_id</strong> and the client's scopes; disabled clients get nothing. A service client can never get a user token and an agent client never a service token.</li><li>Store only a hash of service secrets (follow agaia-4028's Agentcredential storage if it already hashes; otherwise hash in <code>core/libs/oauth2.0/storage/pdo.php</code> for service clients).</li><li>Service clients are not users: no row in users, not in user lists or pickers.</li><li>Decision entries in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for the grant branching (agent, service, disabled, app client); a service token on any existing CRUD resource still fails as today. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> what service tokens may access, enrollment, rotation.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-token-scopes", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "ACL: tokens with scopes are held to them on top of the actor's ACL", "description": "<p>Delegated agent tokens (later issue) must never do more than their scopes allow, even when the agent's roles would. Today scopes on tokens are ignored. Effective access becomes: the actor's ACL AND the token's scopes. Scopes only narrow; tokens without scopes (people, agents' own credentials) are unchanged.</p><ul><li>Scope vocabulary = existing permission names (<code>issue.get</code>, <code>comment.create</code>) with <code>*</code> wildcards (<code>issue.*</code>, <code>*.get</code>).</li><li>In <code>RestController::authorize()</code> (after <code>verifyResourceRequest</code>), when the access token has a scope, the requested <code>controller.action</code> must match one; related and included resources (RBAC D-020) are checked the same way and omitted when not covered (D-021).</li><li>Hard exclusions for scoped tokens regardless of scope: agentcredential.*, serviceclient.*, enrollment resources, role.*, userrole.*, permission.*, agent create/update/delete.</li><li>Keep the check in one class under <code>core/libs/security</code> (not inline in the controller); decision entry in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for matching, wildcards, related reads and exclusions; api-tester cases with a scoped token. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> issuing scoped tokens.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-service-access", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "ACL: deny-by-default access path for service tokens", "description": "<p>A service token has no user, so <code>RestController::setUser()</code> rejects it today. Runtimes must read a few things as themselves (delegable agents, specs, grants). This adds a separate, deny-by-default path that never touches RBAC roles or the resolution mode.</p><ul><li>Resources opt in to service access in their model ACL metadata (which actions, which service kinds). A service token is allowed only when the resource opted in AND <code>controller.action</code> is in the service client's scopes; everything else 401.</li><li>Optional per-resource record filter for service tokens (metadata hook), so a resource can limit rows (e.g. only delegable agents).</li><li>No current user for service requests: behaviours and components that need one must not run or must handle it (list them in the PR).</li><li>Requests by a disabled client fail; <code>lastUsedAt</code> updated.</li><li>Decision entry in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit with a test resource opted in and one not; api-tester acl cases with a service token. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> opting real resources in (later issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-service-clients"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-enrollment", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Service enrollment: request, admin approval with a code, secret delivered to the service", "description": "<p>No secret may be copied by hand. A service enrolls itself: it asks Gaia, shows a short code, an admin approves the matching request, and the service receives its secret straight from Gaia (device-authorization style, RFC 8628).</p><ul><li>Resource <code>Serviceenrollment</code>: name, kind, status (pending | approved | denied | expired | delivered), userCode (e.g. <code>KQ7-3MX</code>), expiresAt (15 minutes), approvedBy, serviceclientId.</li><li>Anonymous POST creates a pending request and returns id, userCode, expiresAt and a pollToken (shown once, stored hashed). Rate limited per IP.</li><li>Anonymous GET by id with the pollToken: returns status; once approved, returns clientId and clientSecret <strong>once</strong> (status delivered), creating the Serviceclient with its kind's default scopes.</li><li>Admin list + PATCH status approved/denied (ACL like other admin resources). Expired requests can't be approved.</li><li>Only these two actions are anonymous: decide how (controller <code>$authorization</code> is controller-wide today) and record it in the decisions doc. Standard CRUD only, no custom routes.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for the state machine (expiry, double delivery, wrong pollToken, deny); api-tester cases for anonymous and admin paths. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> enrollment tokens, UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-service-clients"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-enrollment-tokens", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Service enrollment: single-use enrollment tokens for unattended deploys", "description": "<p>Deployed services (Hermes, later Ares) can't wait for someone to approve a code. A deploy pipeline gets a single-use enrollment token and passes it to the container; the service enrolls with it and is approved automatically.</p><ul><li>Resource <code>Serviceenrollmenttoken</code>: kind, name, expiresAt (15 minutes), usedAt, createdUser. Admin POST returns the token once (stored hashed); list and DELETE (revoke).</li><li>An enrollment request (<code>Serviceenrollment</code> POST) carrying a valid, unused, unexpired token of the same kind is approved at once; the token is marked used. Invalid tokens are refused without saying why.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for single use, expiry, kind mismatch, revoke; api-tester acl cases. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["g-enrollment"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-secret-rotation", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Service clients rotate their own secret", "description": "<p>No service secret should live forever and nobody should handle rotation. A service replaces its own secret with its current service token.</p><ul><li>Opt <code>Serviceclient</code> PATCH in to service access (the service access path in this milestone) for the client's own record only, field <code>rotateSecret: true</code>; the response carries the new secret once. The old secret stays valid for 10 minutes so a crash mid-rotation doesn't lock the service out.</li><li>Scope <code>serviceclient.rotate</code> in every kind's defaults.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit (own record only, grace period, old secret refused after it); api-tester case. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> rotation schedule (each service decides).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["g-service-access"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-delegation", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Agents: delegationScopes and the delegation grant for runtimes", "description": "<p>Talos (a runtime service client) must run Gaia-declared agents without holding their secrets. It asks Gaia for a short-lived token acting as the agent.</p><ul><li><code>Agent.delegationScopes</code>: JSON list of permission names with <code>*</code> (same vocabulary as token scopes). Empty = the agent can't be delegated. Editable by those with agent.update; an agent can't change its own (extend <code>AgentEscalationGuard</code>).</li><li>New grant type (e.g. <code>urn:projects4me:params:oauth:grant-type:agent-delegation</code>, params <code>agent_id</code>, optional <code>scope</code>), registered in <code>core/libs/authorization/OAuthServer.php</code> like <code>AgentClientCredentials</code>. Client must be an active service client with scope <code>agent.delegate</code>; agent must be active with non-empty delegationScopes; requested scope must be a subset (default = all of them).</li><li>Token: user_id = agent email (as today), client_id = the runtime's client, scope = granted, 1 hour, no refresh token. Keep these token rows (no purge) so the token table shows which runtime acted for which agent when.</li><li>Decision entry in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for every refusal case and the happy path; a delegated token can't reach anything outside its scopes (relies on the token scopes issue). <strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-step scopes, runtime-to-agent binding.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-service-clients", "g-token-scopes"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-runtime-reads", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Runtime reads: delegable agents, agent specs and grants for runtime service tokens", "description": "<p>A Talos runtime discovers the agents it may run from Gaia with its own service token (no user), instead of naming them locally.</p><ul><li>Opt in to service access for kind <code>runtime</code>: Agent list/get limited by a record filter to active agents with non-empty delegationScopes; agentspec get (agaia-4043) for those agents; Agenttool, Agentskill and Skill (with files) list/get for those agents.</li><li>Never Agentcredential, Useridentity or any secret field; field ACL keeps secrets out of the agent payload.</li><li>Add the matching scopes to the runtime kind's defaults.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> api-tester cases with a runtime token: delegable agent visible, non-delegable and inactive agents hidden, credentials refused, a hermes-kind token refused. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other service kinds.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["g-service-access", "g-delegation"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-introspection", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Introspection: callable with a service token, returns actor type, client, scopes and project ids", "description": "<p>Hermes will check socket tokens with Gaia introspection (agaia-4029) using its own service token, replacing <code>/user/me</code> plus a membership query with the user's token. Contract change with A Hermes (socket auth issue).</p><ul><li>Accept a service token with scope <code>token.introspect</code>; keep the agaia-4029 shared-secret door for Ares until Ares is reworked.</li><li>Response (RFC 7662 names plus ours): <code>active</code>, <code>sub</code> (user id), <code>actorType</code> (user | agent | service), <code>clientId</code>, <code>act</code> (the service client id when the token is delegated), <code>scope</code>, <code>exp</code>, <code>projectIds</code> (memberships, for users and agents), <code>serviceKind</code> for service tokens. Inactive or disabled = <code>{active: false}</code> only.</li><li>Agent tool grants stay in the response as 4029 built them.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit and api-tester cases for user, agent, delegated, service and expired tokens. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> Ares changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-service-clients"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-access-changed", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Live events: publish user.access.changed when a user's access changes", "description": "<p>Hermes checks a socket only at connect and caches access for 5 minutes, so removed members and disabled users keep receiving events. Gaia tells Hermes when a user's access changes. Contract change: merges together with the matching A Hermes issue (allowlist + handler).</p><ul><li>Name <code>user.access.changed</code> in <code>support/EventNames.php</code>, user-scoped like Hermes D-009 (<code>user:&lt;id&gt;</code>).</li><li>Publish it after: account status changes, session revocation (agaia-3954 path), membership create and delete. No payload beyond the user id.</li><li>Live events component per bundle E; fail open like other events.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit plus api-tester <code>hermes.expect</code> cases for each trigger. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> role changes (don't affect Hermes).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "g-runtimes-room", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Live events: also publish workflow.agent.run.requested to the runtimes scope", "description": "<p>Talos runtimes take run requests on one socket (runtimes room) instead of one socket per agent. Contract change: merges together with the matching A Hermes issue.</p><ul><li>Where Gaia publishes <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> to the agent's user scope (agaia-4052, Hermes D-017), also publish it with the scope <code>runtimes</code> (exact form agreed with the Hermes issue).</li><li>Only for agents with non-empty delegationScopes. The existing claim (RunAgentActor claim window) decides which runtime takes the step when several listen.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> api-tester <code>hermes.expect</code> cases for delegable and non-delegable agents. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> routing to a specific runtime.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-delegation"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "h-service-identity", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Hermes enrolls with Gaia and keeps a service token", "description": "<p>Hermes gets its own identity from Gaia (service client of kind <code>hermes</code>) so it can call Gaia as itself. No secret is copied by hand.</p><ul><li>One gateway module in <code>src/auth/</code>: on start, if no stored credential, enroll with <code>GAIA_ENROLLMENT_TOKEN</code> (auto-approved) or, without one, create a request and log its user code for an admin to approve, then poll until delivered.</li><li>Store the client id and secret in a file at a configured path (mounted volume, mode 600), so unattended restarts need no new enrollment token. ADR in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>: credential file is not domain storage (Hermes stays a relay).</li><li>Get a new client_credentials token at every start and refresh it before expiry; rotate its secret weekly via Gaia's rotation.</li><li>Never log the secret, token or user code beyond the one log line for approval.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> in-process tests with a stub Gaia (D-015) for both enrollment paths, restart with stored credential, token refresh and rotation. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> using the token (next issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-enrollment-tokens", "g-secret-rotation"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "h-socket-auth", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Socket auth through Gaia introspection, disconnect at token expiry", "description": "<p>Replace the per-socket <code>/user/me</code> + membership lookup with the user's token (<code>src/auth/gaia-session.js</code>) by one Gaia introspection call made with Hermes' service token. Contract with the A Gaia introspection issue.</p><ul><li>Session = <code>sub</code>, <code>actorType</code>, <code>projectIds</code>, <code>exp</code> from introspection; cache as today (<code>session-cache.js</code>), never past <code>exp</code>.</li><li>Accept user and agent tokens (delegated included); refuse service tokens on normal intents (the runtimes room comes later).</li><li>Disconnect a socket when its token's <code>exp</code> passes (Prometheus already reconnects with the refreshed token, <code>services/hermes.js</code>).</li><li>ADR update for D-002, D-011, D-012.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests with a stub introspection: active, inactive, service token refused, expiry disconnect, cache bounded by exp. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> live revocation.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["h-service-identity", "g-introspection"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "h-access-changed", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Allowlist user.access.changed and re-check that user's sockets", "description": "<p>Gaia publishes <code>user.access.changed</code> (user-scoped) when a user is disabled, sessions are revoked or memberships change. Contract change: merges together with the matching A Gaia issue.</p><ul><li>Add the name to <code>src/contract/names.js</code> (must match Gaia <code>EventNames.php</code>); ADR entry.</li><li>On it: evict the user's cached sessions, re-introspect each of the user's sockets; disconnect if inactive, otherwise re-apply intents so rooms of projects no longer in <code>projectIds</code> are left.</li><li>Not forwarded to clients.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests for membership removal (room left), disable (disconnect), unchanged access (no effect). <strong>Out of scope:</strong> role changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["h-socket-auth"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "h-runtimes-room", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Runtimes room: runtime service tokens receive workflow.agent.run.requested", "description": "<p>Talos runtimes take run requests on one socket. Gaia also publishes <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> with the scope <code>runtimes</code>. Contract change: merges together with the matching A Gaia issue.</p><ul><li>Accept that scope on <code>/publish</code> for this event only.</li><li>Only sockets whose introspection says <code>actorType: service</code> and <code>serviceKind: runtime</code> may set an intent for it; everyone else is refused it; runtime tokens may set no other intent.</li><li>ADR entry (alongside D-009 and D-017).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests: runtime token receives the event, user and agent tokens refused, runtime token refused on project intents. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-runtime routing.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["h-socket-auth"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "d-enroll", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: enroll as a runtime service client and keep a service token", "description": "<p>Talos becomes a registered runtime in Gaia with no hand-copied secret, the first step towards running Gaia-declared agents (and later running inside Ares).</p><ul><li>Through gaia-mcp (the only tracker client): enrollment (create request, poll, receive secret once), service client_credentials token, token refresh, self-rotation of the secret (weekly).</li><li><code>talos enroll</code> (and on <code>talos run</code> when no credential): uses <code>TALOS_ENROLLMENT_TOKEN</code> if set, otherwise prints the user code for an admin to approve in Prometheus and waits.</li><li>Credential stored under <code>LOCAL_DIR</code> state (git-ignored, owner-only permissions on both platforms); never logged.</li><li>README for Talos and gaia-mcp; stdlib only.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests with a fake Gaia for both enrollment paths, restart with a stored credential, refresh and rotation. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> agent discovery.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["g-enrollment-tokens", "g-secret-rotation"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "d-discover", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: discover Gaia agents and run them on delegated tokens", "description": "<p>Talos stops naming Gaia agents locally (<code>gaiaAgent</code> in agent.json, <code>talos/lib/registry.py</code> ~l.131-165) and asks Gaia which agents it may run, with its runtime service token.</p><ul><li>Periodically list delegable agents and load each spec (reuse <code>talos/lib/agent_spec.py</code> <code>settings_from</code>), tool grants and skills.</li><li>Per agent, get a delegated token (Gaia delegation grant) and cache it; renew about 5 minutes before expiry; every Gaia call and the Hermes connection made for that agent's runs use it.</li><li>Gaia-declared agents take work from Gaia workflow run requests only (adt-4047 path); agent.json stays for Talos' own agents (Odysseus, Nestor, Agamemnon) with their own credentials. Remove <code>gaiaAgent</code> support and its README section (Hera moves to a workflow on the milestone-completed trigger, agaia-4271).</li><li>Agent disabled or delegation emptied in Gaia: stop starting new runs for it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests: discovery adds and removes agents, token cache renewal, refusal handling. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> runtimes room (next issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["d-enroll", "g-runtime-reads"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "d-runtimes-room", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "Talos: take workflow run requests from the Hermes runtimes room", "description": "<p>One socket per runtime instead of one per agent: Talos listens to <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> in the runtimes room with its service token and hands each request to the discovered agent it names.</p><ul><li>Listener in <code>talos/lib/hermes.py</code> with the service token (fresh on every reconnect, as today).</li><li>Requests for agents this runtime doesn't run are ignored; the step claim decides between runtimes.</li><li>Drop the per-agent run-request subscription for Gaia agents.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for routing, unknown agent and reconnect. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-runtime routing.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["d-discover", "h-runtimes-room", "g-runtimes-room"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "p-services", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Settings > Services: list service clients and disable them", "description": "<p>Admins need to see which services (Talos runtimes, Hermes) have an identity in Gaia and cut one off at once.</p><ul><li>New settings item Services (<code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> <code>settingsItems</code>, group system) and route under <code>settings</code>.</li><li>List of <code>serviceclient</code>: name, kind, status label, last used; Disable / Enable with a confirm modal (<code>bootstrap-modal</code>).</li><li>Design system boxes and table; empty state.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> model, Mirage, acceptance test for list and disable. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> enrollments (next issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["g-service-clients"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "p-enrollments", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Settings > Services: approve enrollment requests and create enrollment tokens", "description": "<p>Services enroll by showing a code; an admin approves the matching request here. Deploy pipelines use single-use enrollment tokens created here.</p><ul><li>Pending requests box on the Services page: name, kind, user code, time left; Approve / Deny (confirm modal asks the admin to check the code matches what the service shows).</li><li>Enrollment tokens box: create (kind, name) shows the token once with a copy button and a warning that it is single-use for 15 minutes; list with used/expired state; revoke.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> acceptance tests for approve, deny, expired request, token create and revoke. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> editing scopes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["p-services", "g-enrollment-tokens"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "p-delegation-scopes", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Agents: Delegation scopes field on the agent form", "description": "<p>Sponsors choose what a runtime may do when running an agent: <code>Agent.delegationScopes</code>, a list of permission names with <code>*</code>; empty means the agent can't run on a runtime.</p><ul><li>Field on agent create/edit (<code>templates/app/agent/create.hbs</code>, shared create controller): multi-select of permission names plus wildcard entries per module (<code>issue.*</code>), free entry allowed; info-icon tooltip explains empty = no delegation.</li><li>Agent page shows the scopes, or No delegation.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> integration test for the field, acceptance test saving scopes. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> validating scopes against the catalog.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["g-delegation"], "milestone": "aga-Identity", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-08 20:28:25	2026-11-08 20:42:12	f
364ed5106af1-88d1-a5cc-ae5ca09a3373	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	5	{"summary": "Paging, sorting and grouping in the idea browser reload the whole page: the list is loaded by the layout route's model with refreshModel query params, so every change refreshes the route and shows the parent loading screen. A reusable ListLoader (store query with limit + 1, stale-response guard, tracked items/hasNext/isLoading/error) lets a QuickList reload in place. The idea browser then moves its list params off route refresh and reloads only the list (skeleton rows in the QuickList body), keeping the open idea page, browser back/forward and live updates working. The rule is recorded in the lists ADR.", "issues": [{"key": "ql-list-loader", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: reusable ListLoader to reload a list in place", "description": "<p>QuickList pages should reload only the list when the page, sort, group or search changes, not the whole route (today the idea browser refreshes its route on every change). This issue adds a small reusable loader that callers own (in a controller or component), so the route model doesn't have to change on each list change.</p><ul><li>New <code>app/utils/quick-list/list-loader.js</code>, class <code>ListLoader</code> (native class, <code>@tracked</code>): constructor <code>{ store, modelName, pageSize, buildRequest(params) }</code>, where <code>buildRequest</code> returns the store query options (query, sort, order, rels) for the given params.</li><li><code>load(params)</code>: sets <code>isLoading</code>, asks the store for <code>page</code> and <code>limit = requestLimit(pageSize)</code> (the page-window helper from aprom-4360), then sets <code>items</code> and <code>hasNext</code> via <code>pageWindow</code>. A request token makes sure only the newest call writes its result (a slower older response is dropped). On failure it sets <code>error</code> and keeps the previous items. <code>reload()</code> re-runs the last params.</li><li>It can be seeded with an already-loaded first page (<code>seed(records, params)</code>) so a route can still load the first page for the initial render.</li><li>No API calls in components: the loader uses the injected store passed in. YUIDoc on the class.</li><li>Unit tests (store stubbed): page window and hasNext, isLoading flips, a stale response doesn't overwrite a newer one, error keeps the old items, reload re-uses the last params, seed.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests above pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: using it in any page (separate issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4360"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ideas-inplace-reload", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: page, sort, group and search reload only the list, not the whole page", "description": "<p>In the idea browser, changing page, sort, group or search reloads the whole page. Likely cause (confirm first): the list is loaded in the layout route's <code>model()</code> (<code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code>) with <code>refreshModel: true</code> query params (<code>query</code>, and probably <code>page</code>/<code>sort</code>/<code>order</code>/<code>group</code> from aprom-4356/4359). Each change refreshes the route; there is no <code>idea-loading.hbs</code>, so the parent loading substate replaces the content and the child idea page re-renders. Ember can update just the list.</p><ul><li>Set <code>refreshModel: false</code> on every list param (<code>query</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>order</code>, <code>group</code>, <code>archived</code>). The route keeps loading the first page for the initial render (and the search schema/saved searches as today) and seeds a <code>ListLoader</code> (from the list-loader issue) owned by the idea controller.</li><li>The controller's actions for page, sort, group, search apply/clear and the archived toggle update the query params and call <code>loader.load(params)</code>. A group change that needs no new order (plan status, which only groups the loaded page) doesn't fetch at all.</li><li>Browser back/forward: when the list params in the URL change without an action (listen to the router service's <code>routeDidChange</code> for this route), reload the list if they differ from the last loaded params.</li><li>QuickList gets <code>@items</code>/<code>@hasNext</code>/<code>@isLoading</code>/<code>@error</code>/<code>@onRetry</code> from the loader: while loading, skeleton rows in the list body; the header, search, toolbar and the idea page beside it stay put; the pager is disabled. Hermes idea events call <code>loader.reload()</code> instead of re-running the route's loader closures (drop those closures).</li><li>Add to <code>prometheus/docs/architecture/lists/decisions.md</code> (from aprom-4360): list params never refresh the route; lists reload in place through a <code>ListLoader</code>.</li><li>Acceptance tests: changing page/sort/group/search does not re-render the open idea page (e.g. a marker set on its DOM survives) and only the list's loading state shows; back/forward restores the previous page of ideas; a failed load shows the QuickList error with a working retry.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: as above; the URL still carries every list param.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: other lists.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ql-list-loader", "aprom-4360", "aprom-4361", "aprom-4362", "aprom-4365"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 17:00:38	2026-11-09 17:00:38	f
dd4d1c826af2-bf67-cd6a-cb95854d457c	8ed0e1366af2-ca37-d7c4-675b9ea9985d	1	{"summary": "Global search over issues, milestones and projects in Postgres, in two phases. Phase 1 (fuzzy): Gaia learns trigram GIN indexes and extensions in metadata (trgm-indexes), gets a search library with one ACL-scoped source per type (search-core) and a read-only search resource (search-api); Prometheus replaces the issues-only header search with a grouped dropdown (header-search). Phase 2 (semantic): pgvector in the Postgres images (pgvector-image) and a vector field type in Gaia metadata (vector-type); Ares gets POST /embed behind a swappable embedding adapter with Ollama first (embed-endpoint), p4m runs Ollama locally (p4m-ollama); Gaia stores embeddings filled by a cron task that fails open (embedding-store), then blends trigram and vector rankings with a fuzzy-only fallback (hybrid-search). Provider swaps need only env changes: rows record their model and the vector column has no fixed dimension.", "issues": [{"key": "trgm-indexes", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migration: trigram GIN indexes and required Postgres extensions from model metadata", "description": "<p>Global search needs fuzzy matching with <code>pg_trgm</code>, and that needs GIN trigram indexes. Gaia's metadata-driven migration can only create plain btree and unique indexes, and nothing creates Postgres extensions. <code>pg_trgm</code> exists only in the db dumps and the api-tester's <code>prepare-test-db.sh</code>. This is the framework capability on its own; the search work adds the actual indexes.</p><ul><li>Model metadata <code>indexes</code> entries accept <code>method</code> (<code>btree</code> default, <code>gin</code>) and <code>opclass</code> (e.g. <code>gin_trgm_ops</code>), single or multi-column. Extend <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> (<code>syncIndexes</code>, <code>syncMultiColumnIndex</code> ~l.260) and <code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> <code>prepareTableDefinition</code> for new tables. Identifiers stay escaped. Allow only a whitelist of methods and opclasses, never raw SQL from metadata.</li><li>Required extensions: a config list (e.g. <code>database.extensions</code>, default <code>[\\"uuid-ossp\\", \\"pg_trgm\\"]</code>). Migrate runs <code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS</code> for each before syncing tables, and fails with a clear message when it can't.</li><li>An index whose method or opclass changes in metadata is recreated, not silently kept.</li><li>Record the decision in <code>docs/architecture/</code> (a new <code>search/decisions.md</code>, which later search issues extend), and refresh the generated docs and graph.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests cover GIN with opclass, the whitelist rejection and extension creation; migrating twice is a no-op; existing indexes are untouched.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> expression indexes, tsvector, the pgvector extension (a later issue), and adding indexes to any model.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-core", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: fuzzy search library with ACL-scoped sources for issues, milestones and projects", "description": "<p>The domain layer of the new global search: given a query string, return the best fuzzy matches across issues, milestones and projects that the current user may read. This uses <code>pg_trgm</code> only; semantic search comes later and plugs into the same coordinator.</p><ul><li><code>core/libs/search/</code>: a <code>SearchSource</code> interface (<code>type()</code>, <code>search(query, user, limit)</code> returning hits) and <code>IssueSearchSource</code>, <code>MilestoneSearchSource</code>, <code>ProjectSearchSource</code>. A <code>GlobalSearch</code> coordinator runs the requested types, each capped at its own limit.</li><li>Fields: Issue <code>subject</code> (strong), <code>description</code> (weak), with an exact match on the issue number or <code>SHORTCODE-1234</code> ranked first. Milestone <code>name</code>, <code>description</code>. Project <code>name</code>, <code>shortCode</code>, <code>description</code>. Score with <code>word_similarity</code>/<code>similarity</code>, plus a bonus for prefix matches on titles. Drop hits under a minimum threshold (a config value).</li><li>SQL uses bound parameters only. Soft-deleted rows are excluded.</li><li><strong>ACL:</strong> a source runs only when the user has the model's read permission, and its rows are limited to the same project record scope the normal list endpoints apply (see <code>Acl.php</code> <code>resolveRecordScopeBinding</code>). No bypass, and no result from a project the user can't read.</li><li>A hit is <code>{entityType, entityId, title, snippet, number, projectId, projectShortcode, status, score}</code>; the snippet is a short plain-text excerpt around the match.</li><li>Add trigram GIN indexes (from trgm-indexes) to the searched fields in the Issue, Milestone and Project metadata.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests cover a typo still matching (e.g. <code>notifcation</code> finds Notification), number lookup, the limit per type, and the scope: a non-member sees nothing from that project and a user without <code>milestone</code> read gets no milestones.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the HTTP resource, embeddings, and other models (comments, wikis, ideas).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["trgm-indexes"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: read-only search resource (GET /search) for the global search", "description": "<p>Expose the search library as a read-only resource so Prometheus can call it. Follow <code>WorkfloweventController</code>: list only, the id route returns 404, and there are no custom actions.</p><ul><li><code>SearchController</code> with aclMap get/list mapped to <code>search.get</code>. <code>GET /api/v1/search?q=...&amp;types=issue,milestone,project&amp;limit=5</code>: <code>types</code> defaults to all three; <code>limit</code> is per type, default 5, max 20; a missing <code>q</code> or one under 2 characters returns an empty list, not an error.</li><li>The response is a JSON:API collection of type <code>search</code>, with ids <code>&lt;entityType&gt;:&lt;entityId&gt;</code> and the hit fields as attributes, ordered by type then score, plus <code>meta.count</code>. This is the contract Prometheus (header-search) reads, so document it in <code>docs/architecture/search/decisions.md</code>.</li><li>Route in <code>core/config/routes.php</code>, ACL metadata, api-tester acl and behaviour cases. No permission seed SQL: the reviewer grants <code>search.get</code> by hand.</li><li>Keep the controller thin: parse, authorize, call <code>GlobalSearch</code>, shape the response.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> api-tester cases cover a typo match, a per-type limit, an unknown type (400), no permission (403) and a non-member seeing no hits.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> paging and semantic ranking.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-core"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "header-search", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Header global search: issues, milestones and projects in a grouped dropdown", "description": "<p>The header search only finds issues today, through a <code>CONTAINS</code> query on <code>issue</code> (<code>components/app-layouts/application-header.js</code> <code>loadSearchData</code>). Gaia now has a fuzzy <code>GET /search</code> resource (type <code>search</code>, ids <code>&lt;entityType&gt;:&lt;entityId&gt;</code>, attributes entityType, entityId, title, snippet, number, projectId, projectShortcode, status, score). Switch the header to it.</p><ul><li><code>models/search.js</code> for the hit, plus an adapter/serializer only if the default doesn't fit. The ember-concurrency <code>search</code> task stays (debounce, at least 2 characters) and calls <code>store.query('search', {q, limit: 5})</code>.</li><li><code>application-header.hbs</code> (~l.14-22): PowerSelect with group options, in the order Issues, Milestones, Projects, with headings from translations; empty groups are hidden. An issue row shows <code>SHORTCODE-number</code>, the subject and a status label; a milestone row shows the name and project; a project row shows the name and short code. States: no results, loading, and an error message when the call fails.</li><li>Selecting a hit (<code>itemSelected</code> -&gt; <code>@searchedItem</code> -&gt; the app controller's <code>itemSearched</code>, <code>templates/app.hbs:8</code>) goes to the issue page (<code>app.project.issue.page</code> by shortcode and number), the project overview, or, for a milestone, its project's board.</li><li>Follow <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code> and add translations to <code>en-us</code>. Update the Mirage handler for <code>/search</code> and the integration test of the header.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a typo finds the issue; all three groups render; each kind navigates correctly; the old <code>CONTAINS</code> query is gone.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a full results page, filters, and selecting the milestone tab on the board.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "pgvector-image", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Postgres images with pgvector for local, test and CI databases", "description": "<p>Semantic search stores embeddings with the <code>pgvector</code> extension, which the plain <code>postgres:16-alpine</code> image doesn't ship.</p><ul><li><code>docker-compose.yaml</code> (~l.133): switch to <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code>, keeping the volume and data compatible (same major version).</li><li><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code> (~l.63): the same image for the Postgres service.</li><li><code>tools/api-tester/harness/prepare-test-db.sh</code>: <code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector</code> next to <code>pg_trgm</code>.</li><li>Add <code>vector</code> to the required extensions config from trgm-indexes so migrate creates it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the local stack and CI start, existing tests pass, and <code>SELECT '[1,2]'::vector</code> works in dev and test.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the production image in the <code>docker-images</code> repo (no tracker project; changed by hand, say so in the PR) and any vector columns.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["trgm-indexes"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "vector-type", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migration: vector field type in model metadata (pgvector)", "description": "<p>The embedding table needs a pgvector column, and Gaia's metadata migration only knows MySQL-style types (<code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> <code>getColumnTypeString</code> ~l.396, <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> <code>normalizeColumnType</code> ~l.286). <code>syncExistingTable</code> drops columns it doesn't understand, so the type has to be supported properly.</p><ul><li>Field type <code>vector</code> with an optional <code>dimensions</code>. Without dimensions the column is plain <code>vector</code>, so the embedding model can change without a migration.</li><li>Create, keep and compare the column correctly: no drop or alter loop on a second migrate.</li><li>Models read and write it as a pgvector text literal (<code>[0.1,0.2,...]</code>); add a small helper to convert PHP float arrays to and from it.</li><li>Update the decisions doc and refresh the generated docs and graph.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests cover create, a second migrate as a no-op, and a float array round trip.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> HNSW/IVFFlat indexes and the embedding model itself.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["pgvector-image"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "embed-endpoint", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Embeddings: POST /embed behind a swappable embedding adapter, Ollama first", "description": "<p>Request from A Gaia: the global search adds semantic ranking, and Gaia needs text turned into vectors. Ares is the AI gateway, so we propose it gains an embeddings use case. The engineer chose a local Ollama model for now, so no text leaves our servers, but the provider must be easy to swap later. Please accept, adapt or decline this contract.</p><ul><li>Contract: <code>POST /embed</code> with <code>{texts: [string]}</code> (max 64 texts, each truncated to a configured length) returns <code>{model, dimensions, vectors: [[float]]}</code> in input order. Failures return a clear status (400 bad input, 502/503 provider down), never fake vectors. Gaia ships the matching client in a linked PR.</li><li>Layering per the Ares Design rules: <code>routers/embed.py</code> (Pydantic request/response) -&gt; <code>services/embedding_service.py</code> -&gt; <code>adapters/base_embedding_adapter.py</code> (<code>embed(texts)</code>, <code>model_name()</code>, <code>health_check()</code>) with <code>adapters/ollama_embedding_adapter.py</code>, chosen by the factory from env <code>EMBEDDING_PROVIDER</code> (default <code>ollama</code>). <code>OLLAMA_URL</code> and <code>EMBEDDING_MODEL</code> (default <code>nomic-embed-text</code>) come from env.</li><li>Async HTTP to Ollama's <code>/api/embed</code>. <code>httpx</code> already comes in through the Anthropic SDK: declare it explicitly in requirements and say so in the PR (new dependency approval).</li><li><code>docker-compose.yml</code>: an <code>ollama</code> service on the <code>backend</code> network with a volume for models, which pulls the model on first start.</li><li>Update the Architecture section of <code>CLAUDE.md</code>: Gaia's <code>LLM.php</code> is no longer the only endpoint.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests with a fake adapter (no live calls) cover order, limits, the provider-down error and factory selection.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other providers, caching, and auth on Ares (deferred elsewhere).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "p4m-ollama", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "p4m: run Ollama in the local stack for Ares embeddings", "description": "<p>Request from A Gaia: semantic search uses Ares <code>POST /embed</code> backed by a local Ollama container (added to <code>ares/docker-compose.yml</code>). The local stack started by <code>p4m</code> must run it too, or semantic search silently falls back to fuzzy. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><ul><li><code>installer/p4m.py</code>: make sure <code>p4m up</code> / <code>p4m up ares</code> starts the <code>ollama</code> service from the Ares compose file and that it is in the service names list.</li><li>Add <code>OLLAMA_URL</code> and <code>EMBEDDING_MODEL</code> to the generated env, with defaults.</li><li><code>installer/P4M-CLI.md</code>: the new service, its first-start model download (a few hundred MB) and that it runs on CPU.</li><li>Unit tests for the stack and env changes, on Windows and Linux.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a fresh setup, <code>p4m up</code> brings up Ollama with the model pulled, and Ares <code>/embed</code> answers.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> GPU support and production deployment.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["embed-endpoint"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "embedding-store", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: store embeddings for issues, milestones and projects, filled by a cron task", "description": "<p>Semantic search needs a vector per searchable record. Embedding on every save would slow writes and break them when Ares is down, so a batch task fills them and fails open.</p><ul><li>Internal model <code>Searchembedding</code> (no public routes): <code>entityType</code>, <code>entityId</code>, <code>projectId</code>, <code>model</code>, <code>contentHash</code>, <code>embedding</code> (<code>vector</code> without dimensions), with a unique index on entityType+entityId.</li><li><code>core/services/Embeddings.php</code>: the one gateway to Ares <code>POST /embed</code>, following <code>core/services/LLM.php</code> (Guzzle, URL from env, timeouts). It returns the vectors plus the model, or throws a clear exception.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SearchDocuments</code> builds the text per type (issue subject + description, milestone name + description, project name + short code + description, plain text, length-capped) and its hash.</li><li><code>core/tasks/SearchTask.php</code>: <code>php cli.php search embed</code> embeds records with no row, a changed hash or a different model, in batches, and soft-deleted records lose their row. It logs and stops cleanly when Ares is down. Run it every minute from cron, as <code>WorkflowTask</code> documents.</li><li>Changing the provider or model only needs env changes: the next runs re-embed, because rows record their model.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests with a fake gateway cover new, changed, unchanged, model-changed and deleted records, and Ares down (no exception escapes, nothing written).</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> query-time search, vector indexes and other models.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["vector-type", "embed-endpoint", "search-core"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hybrid-search", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: blend semantic and fuzzy ranking, fall back to fuzzy when embeddings are unavailable", "description": "<p>Add the semantic part to the global search: embed the query, find the nearest records, and merge them with the trigram hits, so a search like <code>login broken</code> also finds an issue titled 'Users can't sign in'.</p><ul><li><code>GlobalSearch</code> embeds the query once through the <code>Embeddings</code> gateway, with a short timeout (config, about 1.5s). Each source also returns its nearest records by cosine distance (<code>&lt;=&gt;</code>), limited to embeddings of the current model and the same ACL scope as its fuzzy query.</li><li>Merge per type with reciprocal rank fusion in a small <code>RankFusion</code> class. A record found both ways appears once. Keep a distance cutoff (config) so unrelated records don't appear.</li><li>When the query embedding fails, return fuzzy results as before. The response <code>meta.semantic</code> is true or false; the contract is otherwise unchanged, so Prometheus needs no change.</li><li>Update <code>docs/architecture/search/decisions.md</code> (fusion, fallback, exact scan without an index for now).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests cover fusion, dedup, the fallback, and the scope (a non-member never gets semantic hits from that project); api-tester cases run with the gateway faked or down.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> HNSW indexes, query caching and UI changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["embedding-store", "search-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 22:40:29	2026-11-09 22:40:29	f
d9d725926af2-8040-cd6a-d24cfe038bc8	8ed0e1366af2-ca37-d7c4-675b9ea9985d	2	{"summary": "Global search over issues, milestones and projects in Postgres, in two phases. Phase 1 (fuzzy): Gaia learns trigram GIN indexes and extensions in metadata (trgm-indexes), gets a search library with one ACL-scoped source per type (search-core) and a read-only search resource (search-api); Prometheus replaces the issues-only header search with a grouped dropdown (header-search). Phase 2 (semantic): pgvector in the Postgres images (pgvector-image) and a vector field type in Gaia metadata (vector-type); Ares gets POST /embed behind a swappable embedding adapter with Ollama first (embed-endpoint), p4m runs Ollama locally (p4m-ollama); Gaia stores embeddings filled by a cron task that fails open (embedding-store), then blends trigram and vector rankings with a fuzzy-only fallback (hybrid-search). Provider swaps need only env changes: rows record their model and the vector column has no fixed dimension. All issues in milestone aga-Fuzzies.", "issues": [{"key": "trgm-indexes", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migration: trigram GIN indexes and required Postgres extensions from model metadata", "description": "<p>Global search needs fuzzy matching with <code>pg_trgm</code>, and that needs GIN trigram indexes. Gaia's metadata-driven migration can only create plain btree and unique indexes, and nothing creates Postgres extensions. <code>pg_trgm</code> exists only in the db dumps and the api-tester's <code>prepare-test-db.sh</code>. This is the framework capability on its own; the search work adds the actual indexes.</p><ul><li>Model metadata <code>indexes</code> entries accept <code>method</code> (<code>btree</code> default, <code>gin</code>) and <code>opclass</code> (e.g. <code>gin_trgm_ops</code>), single or multi-column. Extend <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> (<code>syncIndexes</code>, <code>syncMultiColumnIndex</code> ~l.260) and <code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> <code>prepareTableDefinition</code> for new tables. Identifiers stay escaped. Allow only a whitelist of methods and opclasses, never raw SQL from metadata.</li><li>Required extensions: a config list (e.g. <code>database.extensions</code>, default <code>[\\"uuid-ossp\\", \\"pg_trgm\\"]</code>). Migrate runs <code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS</code> for each before syncing tables, and fails with a clear message when it can't.</li><li>An index whose method or opclass changes in metadata is recreated, not silently kept.</li><li>Record the decision in <code>docs/architecture/</code> (a new <code>search/decisions.md</code>, which later search issues extend), and refresh the generated docs and graph.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests cover GIN with opclass, the whitelist rejection and extension creation; migrating twice is a no-op; existing indexes are untouched.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> expression indexes, tsvector, the pgvector extension (a later issue), and adding indexes to any model.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Fuzzies", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-core", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: fuzzy search library with ACL-scoped sources for issues, milestones and projects", "description": "<p>The domain layer of the new global search: given a query string, return the best fuzzy matches across issues, milestones and projects that the current user may read. This uses <code>pg_trgm</code> only; semantic search comes later and plugs into the same coordinator.</p><ul><li><code>core/libs/search/</code>: a <code>SearchSource</code> interface (<code>type()</code>, <code>search(query, user, limit)</code> returning hits) and <code>IssueSearchSource</code>, <code>MilestoneSearchSource</code>, <code>ProjectSearchSource</code>. A <code>GlobalSearch</code> coordinator runs the requested types, each capped at its own limit.</li><li>Fields: Issue <code>subject</code> (strong), <code>description</code> (weak), with an exact match on the issue number or <code>SHORTCODE-1234</code> ranked first. Milestone <code>name</code>, <code>description</code>. Project <code>name</code>, <code>shortCode</code>, <code>description</code>. Score with <code>word_similarity</code>/<code>similarity</code>, plus a bonus for prefix matches on titles. Drop hits under a minimum threshold (a config value).</li><li>SQL uses bound parameters only. Soft-deleted rows are excluded.</li><li><strong>ACL:</strong> a source runs only when the user has the model's read permission, and its rows are limited to the same project record scope the normal list endpoints apply (see <code>Acl.php</code> <code>resolveRecordScopeBinding</code>). No bypass, and no result from a project the user can't read.</li><li>A hit is <code>{entityType, entityId, title, snippet, number, projectId, projectShortcode, status, score}</code>; the snippet is a short plain-text excerpt around the match.</li><li>Add trigram GIN indexes (from trgm-indexes) to the searched fields in the Issue, Milestone and Project metadata.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests cover a typo still matching (e.g. <code>notifcation</code> finds Notification), number lookup, the limit per type, and the scope: a non-member sees nothing from that project and a user without <code>milestone</code> read gets no milestones.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the HTTP resource, embeddings, and other models (comments, wikis, ideas).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["trgm-indexes"], "milestone": "aga-Fuzzies", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: read-only search resource (GET /search) for the global search", "description": "<p>Expose the search library as a read-only resource so Prometheus can call it. Follow <code>WorkfloweventController</code>: list only, the id route returns 404, and there are no custom actions.</p><ul><li><code>SearchController</code> with aclMap get/list mapped to <code>search.get</code>. <code>GET /api/v1/search?q=...&amp;types=issue,milestone,project&amp;limit=5</code>: <code>types</code> defaults to all three; <code>limit</code> is per type, default 5, max 20; a missing <code>q</code> or one under 2 characters returns an empty list, not an error.</li><li>The response is a JSON:API collection of type <code>search</code>, with ids <code>&lt;entityType&gt;:&lt;entityId&gt;</code> and the hit fields as attributes, ordered by type then score, plus <code>meta.count</code>. This is the contract Prometheus (header-search) reads, so document it in <code>docs/architecture/search/decisions.md</code>.</li><li>Route in <code>core/config/routes.php</code>, ACL metadata, api-tester acl and behaviour cases. No permission seed SQL: the reviewer grants <code>search.get</code> by hand.</li><li>Keep the controller thin: parse, authorize, call <code>GlobalSearch</code>, shape the response.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> api-tester cases cover a typo match, a per-type limit, an unknown type (400), no permission (403) and a non-member seeing no hits.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> paging and semantic ranking.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-core"], "milestone": "aga-Fuzzies", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "header-search", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Header global search: issues, milestones and projects in a grouped dropdown", "description": "<p>The header search only finds issues today, through a <code>CONTAINS</code> query on <code>issue</code> (<code>components/app-layouts/application-header.js</code> <code>loadSearchData</code>). Gaia now has a fuzzy <code>GET /search</code> resource (type <code>search</code>, ids <code>&lt;entityType&gt;:&lt;entityId&gt;</code>, attributes entityType, entityId, title, snippet, number, projectId, projectShortcode, status, score). Switch the header to it.</p><ul><li><code>models/search.js</code> for the hit, plus an adapter/serializer only if the default doesn't fit. The ember-concurrency <code>search</code> task stays (debounce, at least 2 characters) and calls <code>store.query('search', {q, limit: 5})</code>.</li><li><code>application-header.hbs</code> (~l.14-22): PowerSelect with group options, in the order Issues, Milestones, Projects, with headings from translations; empty groups are hidden. An issue row shows <code>SHORTCODE-number</code>, the subject and a status label; a milestone row shows the name and project; a project row shows the name and short code. States: no results, loading, and an error message when the call fails.</li><li>Selecting a hit (<code>itemSelected</code> -&gt; <code>@searchedItem</code> -&gt; the app controller's <code>itemSearched</code>, <code>templates/app.hbs:8</code>) goes to the issue page (<code>app.project.issue.page</code> by shortcode and number), the project overview, or, for a milestone, its project's board.</li><li>Follow <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code> and add translations to <code>en-us</code>. Update the Mirage handler for <code>/search</code> and the integration test of the header.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a typo finds the issue; all three groups render; each kind navigates correctly; the old <code>CONTAINS</code> query is gone.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a full results page, filters, and selecting the milestone tab on the board.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-api"], "milestone": "aga-Fuzzies", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "pgvector-image", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Postgres images with pgvector for local, test and CI databases", "description": "<p>Semantic search stores embeddings with the <code>pgvector</code> extension, which the plain <code>postgres:16-alpine</code> image doesn't ship.</p><ul><li><code>docker-compose.yaml</code> (~l.133): switch to <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code>, keeping the volume and data compatible (same major version).</li><li><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code> (~l.63): the same image for the Postgres service.</li><li><code>tools/api-tester/harness/prepare-test-db.sh</code>: <code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector</code> next to <code>pg_trgm</code>.</li><li>Add <code>vector</code> to the required extensions config from trgm-indexes so migrate creates it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the local stack and CI start, existing tests pass, and <code>SELECT '[1,2]'::vector</code> works in dev and test.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the production image in the <code>docker-images</code> repo (no tracker project; changed by hand, say so in the PR) and any vector columns.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["trgm-indexes"], "milestone": "aga-Fuzzies", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "vector-type", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migration: vector field type in model metadata (pgvector)", "description": "<p>The embedding table needs a pgvector column, and Gaia's metadata migration only knows MySQL-style types (<code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> <code>getColumnTypeString</code> ~l.396, <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> <code>normalizeColumnType</code> ~l.286). <code>syncExistingTable</code> drops columns it doesn't understand, so the type has to be supported properly.</p><ul><li>Field type <code>vector</code> with an optional <code>dimensions</code>. Without dimensions the column is plain <code>vector</code>, so the embedding model can change without a migration.</li><li>Create, keep and compare the column correctly: no drop or alter loop on a second migrate.</li><li>Models read and write it as a pgvector text literal (<code>[0.1,0.2,...]</code>); add a small helper to convert PHP float arrays to and from it.</li><li>Update the decisions doc and refresh the generated docs and graph.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests cover create, a second migrate as a no-op, and a float array round trip.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> HNSW/IVFFlat indexes and the embedding model itself.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["pgvector-image"], "milestone": "aga-Fuzzies", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "embed-endpoint", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Embeddings: POST /embed behind a swappable embedding adapter, Ollama first", "description": "<p>Request from A Gaia: the global search adds semantic ranking, and Gaia needs text turned into vectors. Ares is the AI gateway, so we propose it gains an embeddings use case. The engineer chose a local Ollama model for now, so no text leaves our servers, but the provider must be easy to swap later. Please accept, adapt or decline this contract.</p><ul><li>Contract: <code>POST /embed</code> with <code>{texts: [string]}</code> (max 64 texts, each truncated to a configured length) returns <code>{model, dimensions, vectors: [[float]]}</code> in input order. Failures return a clear status (400 bad input, 502/503 provider down), never fake vectors. Gaia ships the matching client in a linked PR.</li><li>Layering per the Ares Design rules: <code>routers/embed.py</code> (Pydantic request/response) -&gt; <code>services/embedding_service.py</code> -&gt; <code>adapters/base_embedding_adapter.py</code> (<code>embed(texts)</code>, <code>model_name()</code>, <code>health_check()</code>) with <code>adapters/ollama_embedding_adapter.py</code>, chosen by the factory from env <code>EMBEDDING_PROVIDER</code> (default <code>ollama</code>). <code>OLLAMA_URL</code> and <code>EMBEDDING_MODEL</code> (default <code>nomic-embed-text</code>) come from env.</li><li>Async HTTP to Ollama's <code>/api/embed</code>. <code>httpx</code> already comes in through the Anthropic SDK: declare it explicitly in requirements and say so in the PR (new dependency approval).</li><li><code>docker-compose.yml</code>: an <code>ollama</code> service on the <code>backend</code> network with a volume for models, which pulls the model on first start.</li><li>Update the Architecture section of <code>CLAUDE.md</code>: Gaia's <code>LLM.php</code> is no longer the only endpoint.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests with a fake adapter (no live calls) cover order, limits, the provider-down error and factory selection.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other providers, caching, and auth on Ares (deferred elsewhere).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Fuzzies", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "p4m-ollama", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "p4m: run Ollama in the local stack for Ares embeddings", "description": "<p>Request from A Gaia: semantic search uses Ares <code>POST /embed</code> backed by a local Ollama container (added to <code>ares/docker-compose.yml</code>). The local stack started by <code>p4m</code> must run it too, or semantic search silently falls back to fuzzy. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><ul><li><code>installer/p4m.py</code>: make sure <code>p4m up</code> / <code>p4m up ares</code> starts the <code>ollama</code> service from the Ares compose file and that it is in the service names list.</li><li>Add <code>OLLAMA_URL</code> and <code>EMBEDDING_MODEL</code> to the generated env, with defaults.</li><li><code>installer/P4M-CLI.md</code>: the new service, its first-start model download (a few hundred MB) and that it runs on CPU.</li><li>Unit tests for the stack and env changes, on Windows and Linux.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a fresh setup, <code>p4m up</code> brings up Ollama with the model pulled, and Ares <code>/embed</code> answers.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> GPU support and production deployment.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["embed-endpoint"], "milestone": "aga-Fuzzies", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "embedding-store", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: store embeddings for issues, milestones and projects, filled by a cron task", "description": "<p>Semantic search needs a vector per searchable record. Embedding on every save would slow writes and break them when Ares is down, so a batch task fills them and fails open.</p><ul><li>Internal model <code>Searchembedding</code> (no public routes): <code>entityType</code>, <code>entityId</code>, <code>projectId</code>, <code>model</code>, <code>contentHash</code>, <code>embedding</code> (<code>vector</code> without dimensions), with a unique index on entityType+entityId.</li><li><code>core/services/Embeddings.php</code>: the one gateway to Ares <code>POST /embed</code>, following <code>core/services/LLM.php</code> (Guzzle, URL from env, timeouts). It returns the vectors plus the model, or throws a clear exception.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SearchDocuments</code> builds the text per type (issue subject + description, milestone name + description, project name + short code + description, plain text, length-capped) and its hash.</li><li><code>core/tasks/SearchTask.php</code>: <code>php cli.php search embed</code> embeds records with no row, a changed hash or a different model, in batches, and soft-deleted records lose their row. It logs and stops cleanly when Ares is down. Run it every minute from cron, as <code>WorkflowTask</code> documents.</li><li>Changing the provider or model only needs env changes: the next runs re-embed, because rows record their model.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests with a fake gateway cover new, changed, unchanged, model-changed and deleted records, and Ares down (no exception escapes, nothing written).</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> query-time search, vector indexes and other models.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["vector-type", "embed-endpoint", "search-core"], "milestone": "aga-Fuzzies", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hybrid-search", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: blend semantic and fuzzy ranking, fall back to fuzzy when embeddings are unavailable", "description": "<p>Add the semantic part to the global search: embed the query, find the nearest records, and merge them with the trigram hits, so a search like <code>login broken</code> also finds an issue titled 'Users can't sign in'.</p><ul><li><code>GlobalSearch</code> embeds the query once through the <code>Embeddings</code> gateway, with a short timeout (config, about 1.5s). Each source also returns its nearest records by cosine distance (<code>&lt;=&gt;</code>), limited to embeddings of the current model and the same ACL scope as its fuzzy query.</li><li>Merge per type with reciprocal rank fusion in a small <code>RankFusion</code> class. A record found both ways appears once. Keep a distance cutoff (config) so unrelated records don't appear.</li><li>When the query embedding fails, return fuzzy results as before. The response <code>meta.semantic</code> is true or false; the contract is otherwise unchanged, so Prometheus needs no change.</li><li>Update <code>docs/architecture/search/decisions.md</code> (fusion, fallback, exact scan without an index for now).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests cover fusion, dedup, the fallback, and the scope (a non-member never gets semantic hits from that project); api-tester cases run with the gateway faked or down.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> HNSW indexes, query caching and UI changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["embedding-store", "search-api"], "milestone": "aga-Fuzzies", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 22:44:41	2026-11-09 22:44:41	f
78ebc3e56af1-661c-36e2-10b3e7592dff	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	6	{"summary": "A small state-management toolkit for Prometheus pages, since each page (idea browser, Task Board and Gantt quick views) handles URL state, async loads, newest-response-wins, loading/error and reset by hand. AsyncResource (+ ListLoader on top) and UrlState are built in parallel, then the architecture doc and the idea browser's in-place reload use them: page, sort, group and search reload only the list, back/forward and live updates keep working, and nothing refreshes the route. Board and Gantt adoption is left for a next phase.", "issues": [{"key": "state-async", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "State toolkit: AsyncResource and ListLoader (newest call wins, loading, error, retry)", "description": "<p>Pages load data in controllers with hand-written flags and no protection against stale responses. For example, the Task Board's <code>selectIssue</code>/<code>loadIssueDetails</code> (<code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> ~l.845/911) sets <code>isLoadingIssueDetails</code> by hand, and two quick clicks can show the wrong issue. This issue adds the shared async pieces of a small state toolkit in <code>app/utils/state/</code>. The URL part (<code>UrlState</code>) is a separate issue built in parallel.</p><ul><li><code>app/utils/state/async-resource.js</code>, class <code>AsyncResource</code> (native class, <code>@tracked</code>): constructor <code>{ load(params) }</code> (an async function the caller supplies, e.g. a store query). <code>run(params)</code> sets <code>isLoading</code>, awaits <code>load</code>, and only the newest call writes <code>value</code>/<code>error</code> (request token; older responses are dropped). <code>retry()</code> re-runs the last params; <code>reset()</code> clears everything; <code>seed(value, params)</code> sets an already-loaded value. On error the previous <code>value</code> is kept. Guard writes after the owner is destroyed (<code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> on an optional owner).</li><li><code>app/utils/state/list-loader.js</code>, class <code>ListLoader</code> built on <code>AsyncResource</code>: constructor <code>{ store, modelName, pageSize, buildRequest(params) }</code>. It asks for <code>requestLimit(pageSize)</code> rows (the page-window helper from aprom-4360) and exposes <code>items</code> and <code>hasNext</code> through <code>pageWindow</code>, plus <code>isLoading</code>, <code>error</code>, <code>retry</code>, <code>reset</code> and <code>seed(records, params)</code>. <code>buildRequest</code> is the single place that builds the query options; routes that load a first page must use the same function.</li><li>YUIDoc on both classes. No component or route changes here.</li><li>Unit tests (load stubbed): newest call wins over a slower older one, loading flags, error keeps the old value, retry, reset, seed, no writes after destroy; ListLoader page window and hasNext.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: URL state (separate issue), using the classes in any page.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4360"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "state-url", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "State toolkit: UrlState for query-param-backed page state (defaults, reset, back/forward)", "description": "<p>Pages keep list and view state in query params (idea browser: query, page, sort, order, group, archived; board/gantt: query) and either refresh the whole route on every change (<code>refreshModel: true</code>) or juggle the params by hand. This issue adds <code>UrlState</code> to the toolkit in <code>app/utils/state/</code>, so a page can keep its state in the URL without refreshing the route. <code>AsyncResource</code>/<code>ListLoader</code> are a separate issue built in parallel.</p><ul><li><code>app/utils/state/url-state.js</code>, class <code>UrlState</code>: built in a controller with a schema <code>{ name: { default, type: 'string'|'number'|'boolean' } }</code> for that controller's query params. It exposes typed <code>values</code>, <code>set(changes)</code> (updates the params; resets <code>page</code> to its default when another list param changes, if the schema says so), <code>resetToDefaults()</code>, and <code>isDefault(name)</code>.</li><li>Change detection: <code>onChange(callback)</code> is called with <code>(values, changedNames)</code> whenever the params differ from the last values handled, whether the change came from <code>set</code>, a link, or browser back/forward (listen to the router service's <code>routeDidChange</code> for the owning route; clean up on destroy). Calling <code>set</code> with the same values does nothing.</li><li>Helpers for routes: <code>UrlState.queryParamsConfig(schema)</code> returns the route <code>queryParams</code> with <code>refreshModel: false</code> for every entry. A documented reset hook for <code>resetController</code> (leaving the route or switching project).</li><li>YUIDoc. Unit tests with a stubbed router and controller: typed parsing and defaults, set + page reset, same-value no-op, external change (simulated routeDidChange) reports only the changed names, reset, cleanup on destroy.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: using it in any page.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "state-docs", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: page state architecture (URL vs controller state, in-place loading)", "description": "<p>Write down how Prometheus pages manage state, so later pages (Task Board, Gantt Cal, other QuickLists) use the toolkit the same way.</p><ul><li><code>prometheus/docs/architecture/state/architecture.md</code>: the toolkit (<code>AsyncResource</code>, <code>ListLoader</code>, <code>UrlState</code>), when state belongs in the URL (anything a user would bookmark, reload or go back to: list params, an open quick view) and when it stays in the controller (transient UI such as hover, collapsed groups), and how a page wires them (route seeds the first load with the same <code>buildRequest</code>; controller owns the loaders; <code>UrlState.onChange</code> drives reloads; reset on exit and project switch).</li><li><code>prometheus/docs/architecture/state/decisions.md</code> (same format as <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md</code>): list and view params never refresh the route; newest request wins; paging by limit + 1 (link to <code>docs/architecture/lists/decisions.md</code> from aprom-4360).</li><li>Link the new docs from <code>prometheus/CLAUDE.md</code> Architecture section in one line.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: docs match the merged toolkit APIs.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["state-async", "state-url"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ideas-inplace-reload", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Ideas: page, sort, group and search reload only the list, not the whole page", "description": "<p>In the idea browser, changing page, sort, group or search reloads the whole page. Likely cause (confirm first): the list is loaded in the layout route's <code>model()</code> (<code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code>) with <code>refreshModel: true</code> query params, and there is no <code>idea-loading.hbs</code>, so the parent loading screen replaces the content and the open idea page redraws. Move the browser onto the state toolkit (<code>UrlState</code>, <code>ListLoader</code>).</p><ul><li>Route: <code>queryParams</code> from <code>UrlState.queryParamsConfig</code> for <code>query</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>order</code>, <code>group</code>, <code>archived</code> (all <code>refreshModel: false</code>). The route still loads the first page for the initial render, using the controller's shared <code>buildRequest</code>, and seeds the controller's <code>ListLoader</code>; schema and saved searches load as today.</li><li>Controller: a <code>UrlState</code> for those params and a <code>ListLoader</code> for the ideas. Actions (page, sort, group, search apply/clear, saved search pick, archived toggle) call <code>urlState.set(...)</code>; <code>urlState.onChange</code> reloads the list when a param that affects the request changed (grouping by plan status only regroups the loaded page, no fetch). Back/forward and links go through the same path. Reset both on leaving the idea area and on project switch.</li><li>QuickList gets <code>@items</code>/<code>@hasNext</code>/<code>@isLoading</code>/<code>@error</code>/<code>@onRetry</code> from the loader: skeleton rows in the list body only, the header/search/toolbar and the idea page beside it stay put, pager disabled while loading. Hermes idea events call <code>loader.retry()</code> instead of the route's loader closures (remove those closures).</li><li>Acceptance tests: page/sort/group/search/saved-search don't redraw the open idea page (a marker on its DOM survives) and only the list shows loading; back/forward restores the previous page and sort; reload keeps every param; leaving and returning (or switching project) starts from defaults with no previous items shown; a failed load shows the QuickList error with a working retry.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: Task Board and Gantt Cal (next phase).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["state-async", "state-url", "aprom-4360", "aprom-4361", "aprom-4362", "aprom-4365"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 17:14:32	2026-11-09 17:17:56	f
d6835e266af2-560a-5423-664af141f463	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	7	{"summary": "The Roles page moves from a card grid to the QuickList list + detail layout used by the idea browser: QuickList in col-md-3 (role name + access % label, members and modified date, ezSearch on name and description, group by access tier, sort by name or modified, 20 per page via the state toolkit, New Role in the header), with the existing role page in col-md-9. It loads permissions and user-role links only for the roles on the current page instead of all of them. A follow-up removes the then-unused Role::Card and rewrites the role-cards architecture doc.", "issues": [{"key": "roles-quicklist", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Roles: list + detail layout with QuickList (search, group, sort, paging)", "description": "<p>The Roles page (<code>templates/app/role.hbs</code>) shows a grid of <code>Role::Card</code>s that squeezes into a <code>col-lg-2</code> column when a role opens (<code>controllers/app/role.js</code> <code>isRolePage</code>/<code>rolesClass</code>/<code>roleCardClass</code>). The route (<code>routes/app/role.js</code>) loads every role, every userrole with its user, and one permission query per role to compute access coverage, and the search only filters the loaded names. Move it to the QuickList list + detail layout used by the idea browser, built on the state toolkit (<code>ListLoader</code>, <code>UrlState</code> from aprom-4425/4426). The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and the existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>Layout: <code>.row</code> with <code>col-md-3</code> QuickList and <code>col-md-9</code> outlet (the existing <code>app.role.page</code>, unchanged). New <code>app.role.index</code> template: a <code>box box-primary</code> with a centred grey <code>fa-info-circle</code> \\"Pick a role to see its permissions and members\\". Remove <code>isRolePage</code>/<code>rolesClass</code>/<code>roleCardClass</code> and the <code>roles--detail-open</code> classes.</li><li>QuickList: header \\"Roles\\" with count, <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> = <strong>New Role</strong> (<code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code>, ACL <code>role.create</code>) opening the existing add-role modal; <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> = <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> with new metadata <code>views.Role.search</code> (<code>Role.name</code>, <code>Role.description</code>, in <code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>, same format as <code>views.Idea.search</code>) and saved searches as the idea browser does; item primary = role name + access label (<code>{percent}% access</code>, colour from the existing coverage tiers in <code>styles/modules/role.scss</code>: high/elevated/medium/low/no data), secondary = <code>fa-users</code> + member count (\\"No members\\" when none) + \\"Modified \\" (<code>dateModified</code>, fallback <code>dateCreated</code>, format <code>DD MMM YYYY</code>). Active row = the open role. No selection.</li><li>Group by: none, access tier (client-side from coverage, loaded page only). Sort: name (default ASC), last modified (DESC), sent to Gaia as <code>Role.name</code>/<code>Role.dateModified</code>.</li><li>Data: <code>UrlState</code> for <code>query</code>, <code>searchId</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>order</code>, <code>group</code> (all <code>refreshModel: false</code>); a <code>ListLoader</code> for roles (20 per page, limit + 1, one shared <code>buildRequest</code> for route and controller). After each page loads, query permissions only for that page's roles (as today, <code>permission?roleId=</code> per role) and userroles with <code>rels: 'user'</code> only for that page's role ids, then compute coverage and member counts with the existing <code>coverageByRole</code>/<code>isActionAllowed</code> logic. Reset on leaving the roles area.</li><li>Keep working: create (new role appears; reload the current page), delete from the role page (<code>deleteRole</code> reloads the list instead of filtering arrays), permission/member edits on the role page refresh that role's row (call the list's reload or <code>syncRoleCoverage</code> for the open role).</li><li>Update the roles acceptance tests and Mirage handlers (role paging/sort, userrole by role ids); add tests for search, paging, group by tier and the empty detail state.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: as above; the URL keeps the list params; opening a role doesn't reload the list.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: removing <code>Role::Card</code> and its styles (follow-up), bulk actions on roles.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4425", "aprom-4426"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["roles-quick-list"]}, {"key": "roles-card-cleanup", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Roles: remove Role::Card and rewrite the role-cards architecture doc", "description": "<p>After the Roles page moves to QuickList, <code>Role::Card</code> is no longer used. Remove it and update the docs.</p><ul><li>Delete <code>app/components/role/card.{hbs,js}</code> and its tests, and the card-only rules in <code>app/styles/modules/role.scss</code> (keep the coverage tier variables/classes the QuickList access label uses). Check nothing else renders <code>Role::Card</code>.</li><li>Remove card-only translation keys (<code>views.app.role.card.*</code>) no longer referenced.</li><li>Rewrite <code>prometheus/docs/architecture/role-cards/architecture.md</code> (rename to <code>role-list/architecture.md</code>): QuickList list + detail, per-page permission and userrole queries, the coverage formula and tiers (unchanged), ownership table.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: no references to <code>Role::Card</code> remain; the full suite passes; the doc describes the current page.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["roles-quicklist"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 19:19:50	2026-11-09 19:19:50	f
4a2789386af2-2815-7557-e2a3162f909a	c82823c16af0-9a8b-6f54-9c6fbacd2282	9	{"summary": "The role detail page (app.role.page) follows the design system as three full-width boxes stacked in the detail column: Role (box-primary: initials square in the tier colour, inline-editable name and description, created/modified caption, Access/Members/Actions granted facts), Members (box-warning, existing grid and dialogs), and Permissions (box-info, Save in the box-footer). Separately, the Fields tab's raw selects become FormFields::FieldRelate, and Delete role moves from the Permissions box into the Role box header. Layout and select fix run side by side; the delete move follows both.", "issues": [{"key": "role-detail-layout", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Role detail: Role, Members and Permissions as full-width boxes", "description": "<p>The role detail page (<code>templates/app/role/page.hbs</code>) doesn't follow the design system: the name and description are bare form fields outside any box, a floating × close toolbar sits on top (useless now that the first role opens by default, aprom-4430), and Save sits in the Permissions box body. Restructure it into three full-width boxes stacked in the detail column (<code>col-md-9</code> beside the Roles QuickList). The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and the existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li><strong>Role</strong> (<code>box box-primary role-record</code>, title \\"Role\\"): an avatar block with the role's initials in a square box in its access-tier colour (same initials and tier logic the Roles list uses; square edges), the role name in bold and a grey caption \\"Created  by  · Modified \\" (<code>DD MMM YYYY</code>; created-by name via the hasOne rel). The name and description keep their current inline edit (<code>FormFields::FieldText</code>/<code>FieldTextArea</code> with <code>@allowInlineEdit</code>, validation and <code>editRole</code>), shown as the name in the avatar block and a \\"Description\\" <code>&lt;h4&gt;</code> with the text below. Facts as <code>&lt;h4&gt;</code> + value: Access (granted label in the tier colour + red \\"N% denied\\" label when above 0), Members (count), Actions granted (\\"46 of 80\\", from the same action-permission count as the coverage). Leave the box header tools empty here (delete moves there in a separate issue).</li><li><strong>Members</strong> (<code>box box-warning role-members</code>): unchanged content (users-list grid, <code>AppUi::DottedAddButton</code> in the header, remove buttons, \\"View all members\\" footer, the add-userrole and view-all modals), full width.</li><li><strong>Permissions</strong> (<code>box box-info</code>): <code>Role::Permissions</code> as today, but its Save button moves into a <code>box-footer</code> of this box (pass the save action through or render the footer in <code>page.hbs</code>; keep the Delete button where it is for now).</li><li>Remove the × close toolbar and <code>closeRoleDetail</code> if unused elsewhere. Remove the old <code>role-details</code>/<code>field-group</code> layout rules from <code>styles/modules/role.scss</code>; new rules scoped under <code>.role-record</code>. Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Update the role page acceptance tests (inline edit of name and description still saves, facts show the right values, members add/remove still work, Save permissions still works).</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: the Fields tab selects and moving Delete (separate issues).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4430"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["role-detail"]}, {"key": "role-field-select", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Role permissions: Fields tab uses a raw <select>; use FormFields::FieldRelate", "description": "<p>The Fields tab of <code>Role::Permissions</code> (<code>components/role/permissions.hbs</code> ~l.104) renders each field's access mode with a raw <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> and hand-written <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>. The house rules require <code>FormFields::*</code>: a select is <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> with <code>@relateType=\\"relate-simple\\"</code>.</p><ul><li>Replace the select and label with <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> (<code>@relateType=\\"relate-simple\\"</code>, options from <code>fieldAccessOptions</code>, label = the control's <code>displayLabel</code>, selected = <code>control.accessMode</code>), calling the existing <code>setFieldAccessMode(control, value)</code> on change. Keep the <code>data-field-access-select</code> hook (or update tests to the FieldRelate's).</li><li>Check the Actions tab's <code>Role::PermissionOptions</code> renders through FormFields too; if it also uses a raw select, fix it the same way in this issue.</li><li>Update the role permission tests (changing a field's access mode still marks it for save and saves).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: no raw <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> left in role permissions; changing access modes still saves.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "role-delete-header", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Role detail: move Delete role into the Role box header", "description": "<p>The \\"Delete role\\" button sits in the Permissions box next to Save (<code>components/role/permissions.hbs</code> ~l.148, passed as <code>@onDelete</code> from <code>templates/app/role/page.hbs</code>). Record actions belong in the record box's header tools.</p><ul><li>Remove the Delete button and the <code>@onDelete</code> argument from <code>Role::Permissions</code>.</li><li>Add a trash <code>btn btn-box-tool</code> (<code>AppUi::Button</code> with <code>@aclContext=\\"role.delete\\"</code>, tooltip \\"Delete role\\") to the Role box's <code>box-tools</code>, calling the existing <code>deleteRole(model)</code> (Messenger confirmation unchanged; after deleting, the list reloads and the first role opens, as in aprom-4430).</li><li>Update tests (delete from the header with confirmation; the Permissions box has no delete button).</li></ul>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["role-detail-layout", "role-field-select"], "milestone": "aga-Quick List", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["role-detail"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 20:42:50	2026-11-09 20:44:56	f
00982e776af3-573c-d5f1-412815e8eefb	341481c56af2-8040-cd6a-5ea33d81936b	4	{"summary": "Eight bug fixes for the new Threads UI found in the live review, one issue per problem. Layout template chain: drop the page header, stop the duplicate breadcrumb, move New thread into the QuickList header. Thread page chain: drop the 'Discussion' label, drop the issue link from the header, translate the Linked issue status. In parallel: remove the thread box's extra shadow/border, and make the QuickList sort toolbar wrap (component fix, helps every QuickList).", "issues": [{"key": "thr-no-header", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: remove the page header/title above the list and thread", "description": "<p>The new Threads page (aprom-4437) renders a page header (\\"Threads\\" title row) above the list and the thread. Task Board and Gantt Cal have no such header, so Threads shouldn't either. This came from the spec and screens of aprom-4437; ignore the header in the screens attached to other Threads issues too.</p><ul><li>Remove the page title/header section from the Threads layout template (<code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code> or wherever 4437 put it), so the list + thread row starts right under the app's own top area, as on the Task Board and Gantt pages.</li><li>Keep any button that lived there working until the New thread issue moves it (it moves into the QuickList header).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the Threads page has no page title row; compare side by side with the Task Board. The acceptance test asserts no page header is rendered. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> breadcrumb, New thread placement (separate issues).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4437"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "thr-breadcrumb", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: the breadcrumb is rendered twice", "description": "<p>The Threads page shows the breadcrumb twice. The app layout already renders the breadcrumb (from <code>services/breadcrumb.js</code>), so the page itself must not render one.</p><ul><li>Remove the page's own breadcrumb (added with aprom-4437's page header) and check the breadcrumb definitions for <code>app.project.conversation</code>, <code>.index</code> and <code>.page</code> in <code>services/breadcrumb.js</code> so the single app breadcrumb shows Threads (and the thread on the page route) once.</li><li>If removing the page header (the previous issue) already removed the duplicate, verify it and add only the test.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> exactly one breadcrumb on the Threads index and a thread page (acceptance test counts it). <strong>Out of scope:</strong> breadcrumb on other pages.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["thr-no-header"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "thr-new-in-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: move the New thread button into the QuickList header", "description": "<p>On Roles and Ideas the create button sits in the QuickList header (<code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> block, e.g. New Role from aprom-4430: <code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code>). On Threads it sits in the page header, which is being removed.</p><ul><li>Put New thread in the Threads QuickList <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> block with the same markup and size as New Role / New Idea, ACL <code>conversationroom.create</code>, opening the existing create modal.</li><li>Remove the old button.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> New thread shows in the list header and opens the modal; hidden without create permission; existing create tests updated. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> the modal's fields (aprom-4445).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["thr-breadcrumb"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "thr-box-style", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: the thread box has an extra shadow and border unlike other boxes", "description": "<p>The thread (discussion) box on the Threads page (aprom-4439) has a shadow and border that don't match the rest of the application's boxes.</p><ul><li>Find the custom rules added for the thread box (likely in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code> or a new thread partial) and remove the extra shadow/border, so it looks exactly like a standard <code>box box-primary</code> (design system: no new shadows, square edges).</li><li>Don't restyle AdminLTE's <code>.box</code> globally.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the thread box matches the issue page's record box side by side in the running app. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other layout changes.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4439"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "thr-no-eyebrow", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: remove the 'Discussion' / 'Vote' label above the thread title", "description": "<p>The thread box shows a small uppercase type label (\\"Discussion\\") above the subject. No other page in the app has such a label, so Threads shouldn't either. It came from the spec and screen of aprom-4439; ignore it in the screens attached to the other Threads issues (vote, participants, create issue, activity).</p><ul><li>Remove the label from the thread header (and its styles and translation keys if unused). The title stays as the box title.</li><li>The room type stays visible in the list row icon and the vote body.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> no type label in the thread header for discussions or votes; tests updated. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> the list rows.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4439"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "thr-no-header-link", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: remove the linked issue line from the thread header", "description": "<p>The thread header shows the linked issue (<code>fa-link</code>, key, subject, status) and the Linked issue box in the info column shows it again. The side box is enough.</p><ul><li>Remove the linked-issue line from the thread header (template, styles, translations if unused). Keep \\"Started by ... · date\\".</li><li>The Linked issue box is unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the linked issue appears only in the Linked issue box; tests updated. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Linked issue box itself.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["thr-no-eyebrow"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "thr-status-label", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: Linked issue box shows the issue status untranslated", "description": "<p>The Linked issue box in the thread info column shows the raw issue status (e.g. <code>in_progress</code>) instead of the translated label.</p><ul><li>Render it like the issue page does (<code>components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> ~l.19): <code>status-label</code> helper for the text and <code>status-style</code> + the status class for the colour.</li><li>Check the list rows and any other place the Threads code shows an issue status for the same mistake.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> integration test: a linked issue with status <code>in_progress</code> shows the translated label. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other boxes.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["thr-no-header-link"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ql-toolbar-wrap", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: group/sort toolbar overflows its box instead of wrapping", "description": "<p>In the Threads QuickList, when the column is narrow, the group-by/sort toolbar (<code>QuickList::Toolbar</code>, aprom-4353) overflows the box instead of wrapping. It's a component bug, so the fix belongs in QuickList and helps every user (Ideas, Roles, Threads, the component library entry).</p><ul><li>Let the toolbar's controls wrap onto a second line (flex-wrap with a gap, right-aligned) inside the QuickList box at any width; long option labels truncate with an ellipsis rather than pushing the box wider.</li><li>Styles stay in the QuickList partial, scoped under the component's class.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a narrow col-md-3 (e.g. 1280px window) the toolbar stays inside the box on Threads, Ideas and Roles; integration test or demo state in the component library entry covers a narrow width. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> new toolbar options.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-10 14:36:48	2026-11-10 14:36:48	f
2f09faf16af2-deea-cd6a-93defe2ddcd9	341481c56af2-8040-cd6a-5ea33d81936b	1	{"summary": "Threads moves to the Ideas/Roles list + detail layout. ezSearch metadata for threads (including 'Liked by') comes first. Then the QuickList list with a child thread route, grouped by the linked issue's milestone by default, with old ?c_id= links redirected. Per-row comment/like counts (separate Gaia calls for now) and the Idea-like thread page follow in parallel, then the create form fix. A request to A Gaia adds a read-only counts resource, and a follow-up switches the rows to it. A cleanup removes the old feed.", "issues": [{"key": "threads-search", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: ezSearch metadata (views.Conversationroom.search) incl. 'Liked by'", "description": "<p>Threads (app.project.conversation) is moving to the QuickList list + detail layout used by Ideas and Roles (aprom-4428, aprom-4430). Its search must come from view metadata like every other list, replacing the hard-coded filters in <code>controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code> (<code>conversationFilters</code> ~l.295, <code>conversationDateFilters</code> ~l.344).</p><ul><li>Add <code>views.Conversationroom.search</code> in <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>, same format as <code>views.Idea.search</code> / <code>views.Role.search</code>: subject, description, roomType (values vote | discussion, translated), linked issue (Conversationroom.issueNumber, with empty / not empty), dateCreated, dateModified, and <strong>Liked by</strong> = <code>votes.createdUser</code> (Gaia already accepts <code>(votes.createdUser : &lt;userId&gt;)</code>, used by today's My Likes filter), with the project members as value source and the current user first.</li><li>If the metadata format or <code>services/query-schema.js</code> cannot express a relation field like <code>votes.createdUser</code>, extend it generically (no thread-specific code in ez-search) and document it in <code>docs/architecture/metadata-views/</code>.</li><li>Translations in en-us.json.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit test that the schema built from the metadata produces <code>(Conversationroom.roomType : vote)</code>, <code>(Conversationroom.issueNumber NULL)</code> and <code>(votes.createdUser : X)</code> clauses. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> wiring it into the page (next issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "threads-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: QuickList list + detail layout, grouped by milestone, first thread opened", "description": "<p>Replace the infinite-scroll feed on the Threads page with the QuickList list + detail layout of Ideas/Roles, so threads can be searched, paged, sorted and grouped and one thread is read at a time. The attached screens are a guide for layout and content only; the design system and the real components (QuickList, EzSearchCompact) decide the final look.</p><ul><li>Routing: <code>app.project.conversation</code> becomes the layout with children <code>index</code> and <code>page</code> (<code>conversations/:conversation_id</code>); add <code>app.project.conversation.page</code> to <code>services/acl.js</code> routeMaps (conversationroom.read) and the breadcrumb. Index route: <code>replaceWith</code> the first row; if <code>?c_id=X</code> is present, replaceWith the page for X (old links from project overview, issue list, weekly-conversations widget, tag-parser keep working). Empty state only when nothing matches.</li><li>Layout <code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code>: .row with col-md-3 QuickList + col-md-9 outlet. Header \\"Threads\\" with range (<code>1-20 / 20+</code>, limit+1, no totals), <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> New Thread (btn-primary btn-sm, ACL conversationroom.create) opening the existing create modal, <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> = <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> with <code>views.Conversationroom.search</code> and saved searches as on the idea browser.</li><li>State on the toolkit (<code>utils/state/</code> ListLoader + UrlState, aprom-4425/4426): query, page, sort, order, group in the URL, list reloads in place (no refreshModel), newest response wins. Query <code>conversationroom</code> with hasOne rels only (<code>createdBy,issue</code>), never comments/votes rels.</li><li>Rows: creator avatar (existing user image / initials), subject (one line, ellipsis), Vote/Discussion label, linked issue key, modified date (DD MMM YYYY). Active row = open thread.</li><li>Grouping <strong>on by default</strong> by the linked issue's milestone: load the project's milestones once, map <code>issue.milestoneId</code> to its name, threads without issue or milestone in \\"No milestone\\" last; per loaded page, counts in JS (QuickList grouping helper). Other group option: type. Sort: last updated (default), created, subject.</li><li>Page route for now renders the existing <code>Conversation::ConversationItem</code> for the selected thread in the col-md-9 (replaced by the Idea-like page in a later issue), so dev never breaks.</li><li>Hermes: keep the existing project registrations; a new/updated thread reloads the list through the loader.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Mirage handlers + acceptance feature: first thread opens by default, <code>?c_id=</code> redirects, grouping by milestone with \\"No milestone\\" last, search reloads only the list. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> counts in rows, the new detail page, removing old code.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-search"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Route split, layout, toolkit state and the c_id redirect must ship together so the page never breaks; counts, detail and cleanup are already separate issues.", "screens": ["threads-list", "threads-empty"]}, {"key": "threads-row-counts", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: comment and like counts on each list row (separate Gaia calls for now)", "description": "<p>The thread rows should show how many comments and likes a thread has. Gaia has no count field yet (requested separately), so for now load them with separate calls per row, as the current page already does for comments (<code>fetchAndLinkComments</code>).</p><ul><li>A small service or util (single responsibility: counts for a set of room ids) that, for each row of the loaded page, queries comments (<code>(Comment.relatedId : id)</code>) and votes (<code>(Vote.relatedId : id)</code> or the field the Vote model uses) with minimal fields and returns <code>{commentCount, likeCount}</code>; runs in parallel, results dropped when the page changes (newest wins), rows render while counts load.</li><li>Row secondary line shows <code>fa-comment-o N</code> and <code>fa-heart-o N</code>.</li><li>Live: Hermes comment created/deleted for a listed thread updates its count.</li><li>Keep the count source behind one function so a later issue can swap it for one Gaia call per page.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> integration/unit test for the counts helper (stale page dropped) and an acceptance step showing counts. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> Gaia changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-list"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-list"]}, {"key": "threads-detail", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: Idea-like thread page (thread box + Linked issue, Details, Votes side boxes)", "description": "<p>Replace the temporary <code>Conversation::ConversationItem</code> in <code>app.project.conversation.page</code> with a thread page laid out like the idea page (conversation col-md-8 + side col-md-4). The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>Thread box (box-primary, col-md-8): subject as title; box-tools = like toggle with count (existing toggleVote logic) and edit (existing edit flow); body = author + date and description (rendered as today); comments in box-comments loaded with <strong>their own query</strong> (newest 10, sort Comment.dateCreated, \\"Load older comments\\"), never through rels; composer at the bottom (existing comment save, Ctrl+Enter sends, reuse the comment components used in ConversationItem).</li><li>Side col-md-4: <strong>Linked issue</strong> (box-info: status label, key link, subject, milestone; \\"No linked issue\\" otherwise), <strong>Details</strong> (box-default: type, started by, updated, likes), <strong>Votes</strong> for roomType vote (box-warning: the agree/disagree info-boxes from ConversationItem).</li><li>Page route loads the room with hasOne rels only (<code>createdBy,issue</code>); move the Hermes comment handlers (<code>handleCommentCreated/Updated/Deleted</code>) for the open thread to the page controller.</li><li>Guard async work after destroy.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Mirage + acceptance: opening a thread shows comments, load older, posting a reply, Votes box only on vote threads. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> reply threading (aprom-3750), removing ConversationItem.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-list"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-list"]}, {"key": "threads-create-form", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: create modal uses FormFields for the linked issue and opens the new thread", "description": "<p>The New Thread modal in <code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code> uses a raw <code>&lt;PowerSelect&gt;</code> and a hand-written label for the linked issue, which the design system forbids (selects are <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code>).</p><ul><li>Linked issue: <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> with search over issues (existing <code>linkIssueSearch</code> task), enabled only for roomType discussion as today.</li><li>After save: the list reloads in place and the app navigates to the new thread's page.</li><li>Move the modal into its own component if it keeps the layout template simpler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> acceptance test creating a discussion with a linked issue lands on the new thread. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other fields.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-row-counts"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gaia-counts", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Conversation rooms: read-only comment and like counts per room", "description": "<p><strong>Request from A Prometheus.</strong> The Threads page (Prometheus) is moving to a QuickList and shows comment and like counts on each row. Gaia has no count for a room, so Prometheus currently makes two extra queries per row (40 calls for a 20-row page). We ask for one read-only resource that returns counts for many rooms in one call. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract:</strong></p><ul><li>Read-only resource <code>conversationroomcount</code> (view model, like <code>app/metadata/model/Userlatestproject.php</code> with COUNT subqueries): fields <code>id</code> (= room id), <code>commentCount</code>, <code>likeCount</code>, <code>lastCommentDate</code>, <code>projectId</code>.</li><li><code>GET /conversationroomcount?query=(Conversationroomcount.id CONTAINS 'a','b',...)</code> returns one row per room; list + get only (no create/update/delete), standard CRUD controller, no custom routes.</li><li>ACL: project-scoped like Conversationroom; reading needs <code>conversationroom.read</code> (or a new <code>conversationroomcount.list</code>, your call).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> api-tester cases for counts (no comments = 0, deleted comments not counted) and for project scoping. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> live events for counts (Prometheus updates counts from comment events).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "threads-counts-switch", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: load row counts with one Gaia call per page", "description": "<p>Once Gaia serves room counts (the A Gaia request in this plan), replace the per-row comment/vote queries from the row-counts issue with one <code>conversationroomcount</code> query per loaded page (ids of the page's rows).</p><ul><li>New model + adapter/serializer if needed, Mirage handler.</li><li>Swap only the count source function; rows and live updates unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a 20-row page makes one count request (test on the Mirage request log). <strong>Out of scope:</strong> anything else on the page.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-row-counts", "gaia-counts"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "threads-cleanup", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: remove the old feed, filters and unused conversation code", "description": "<p>After the list, detail and create form are in place, remove what the old Threads feed left behind.</p><ul><li>Controller <code>controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code>: InfiniteScroll paging (<code>loadMoreConversations</code>, <code>fetchAllConversations</code>, <code>fetchFilteredConversations</code>, <code>fetchAndLinkComments</code>, <code>setHasMoreFlag</code>), hard-coded filters/date filters, <code>restoreStateFromQueryParams</code>, scroll-to-top/refresh, unused QPs (filter, date, q).</li><li><code>Conversation::ConversationItem</code> and <code>app-ui/skeleton/conversation-grid</code> if nothing uses them anymore; <code>conversation-loading.hbs</code> if replaced; dead styles in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code>; unused translation keys.</li><li><code>components/app-ui/tag-parser.js</code> ~l.229 and the <code>c_id</code> LinkTos (project overview, issue list, weekly-conversations widget) point to the thread page route directly; the index redirect stays for old URLs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> full test suite and lint pass; no reference to the removed code. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> behaviour changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-detail", "threads-create-form"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 22:50:23	2026-11-09 22:50:23	f
