 20+</code>, limit+1, no totals), <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> New Thread (btn-primary btn-sm, ACL conversationroom.create) opening the existing create modal, <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> = <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> with <code>views.Conversationroom.search</code> and saved searches as on the idea browser.</li><li>State on the toolkit (<code>utils/state/</code> ListLoader + UrlState, aprom-4425/4426): query, page, sort, order, group in the URL, list reloads in place (no refreshModel), newest response wins. Query <code>conversationroom</code> with hasOne rels only (<code>createdBy,issue</code>), never comments/votes rels.</li><li>Rows: creator avatar (existing user image / initials), subject (one line, ellipsis), Vote/Discussion label, linked issue key, modified date (DD MMM YYYY). Active row = open thread.</li><li>Grouping <strong>on by default</strong> by the linked issue's milestone: load the project's milestones once, map <code>issue.milestoneId</code> to its name, threads without issue or milestone in \\"No milestone\\" last; per loaded page, counts in JS (QuickList grouping helper). Other group option: type. Sort: last updated (default), created, subject.</li><li>Page route for now renders the existing <code>Conversation::ConversationItem</code> for the selected thread in the col-md-9 (replaced in later issues), so dev never breaks.</li><li>Hermes: keep the existing project registrations; a new/updated thread reloads the list through the loader.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Mirage handlers + acceptance feature: first thread opens by default, <code>?c_id=</code> redirects, grouping by milestone with \\"No milestone\\" last, search reloads only the list. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> counts in rows, the new detail page, removing old code.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-search"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Route split, layout, toolkit state and the c_id redirect must ship together so the page never breaks; counts, detail, votes and cleanup are already separate issues.", "screens": ["threads-list", "threads-empty"]}, {"key": "threads-row-counts", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: comment, vote and like counts on each list row (separate Gaia calls for now)", "description": "<p>The thread rows should show how active a thread is. Gaia has no count field yet (requested separately), so for now load them with separate calls per row, as the current page already does for comments (<code>fetchAndLinkComments</code>).</p><ul><li>A small service or util (single responsibility: counts for a set of room ids) that, for each row of the loaded page, queries comments (<code>(Comment.relatedId : id)</code>) and likes (the <code>vote</code> model, related to the room) with minimal fields and returns <code>{commentCount, likeCount}</code>; runs in parallel, results dropped when the page changes (newest wins), rows render while counts load.</li><li>Row secondary line: discussion = <code>fa-comment-o N</code>; vote room = <code>fa-check-square-o N</code> (its comments are the votes); both show <code>fa-heart-o N</code> when likes &gt; 0.</li><li>Live: Hermes comment created/deleted for a listed thread updates its count.</li><li>Keep the count source behind one function so a later issue can swap it for one Gaia call per page.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit test for the counts helper (stale page dropped) and an acceptance step showing counts for both room types. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> Gaia changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-list"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-list", "threads-vote"]}, {"key": "threads-detail", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: Idea-like thread page for discussions (thread box + Linked issue, Details)", "description": "<p>Replace the temporary <code>Conversation::ConversationItem</code> in <code>app.project.conversation.page</code> with a thread page laid out like the idea page (thread col-md-8 + side col-md-4). This issue builds the shared page and the discussion body; vote rooms get their body in a separate issue. The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>Thread box (box-primary, col-md-8): subject as title; box-tools = like toggle with count (existing toggleVote logic) and edit (existing edit modal from ConversationItem); body = author + date and description (rendered as today).</li><li>Discussion body: comments in box-comments loaded with <strong>their own query</strong> (newest 10, sort Comment.dateCreated, \\"Load older comments\\"), never through rels, using <code>ConversationUi::CommentItem</code>; <code>ConversationUi::CommentComposer</code> at the bottom (existing saveComment, mentions + issue search).</li><li>Leave a clear slot (e.g. a body component chosen by roomType) where the vote body plugs in; until then vote rooms show the description only.</li><li>Side col-md-4: <strong>Linked issue</strong> (box-info: status label, key link, subject, milestone; \\"No linked issue\\" otherwise) and <strong>Details</strong> (box-default: type, started by, updated, likes).</li><li>Page route loads the room with hasOne rels only (<code>createdBy,issue</code>); move the Hermes comment handlers (<code>handleCommentCreated/Updated/Deleted</code>) for the open thread to the page controller. Guard async work after destroy.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Mirage + acceptance: opening a discussion shows comments, load older, posting a reply appears, side boxes filled. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> the vote body, reply threading (aprom-3750), removing ConversationItem.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-list"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-list"]}, {"key": "threads-vote", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: vote thread body (agree/disagree, voter list, Result box) on the thread page", "description": "<p>Vote threads are a key use of Threads. In vote rooms a vote is a comment whose text is \\"I agree\\" or \\"I disagree\\" (ConversationItem's <code>@vote</code>), one per user, not changeable, and the tallies are counted over all of the room's comments. The new thread page loads comments in pages, so the tallies need their own data. The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>Vote body in the thread box (in the slot from the discussion page issue): the existing agree/disagree <code>info-box</code>es side by side (icon, count, progress bar, percentage), moved out of ConversationItem into a vote component. Not voted: thumbs are clickable (existing vote action) and a hint says one vote per person; voted: thumbs locked and \\"You voted: I agree\\" (or disagree).</li><li>Tallies from a dedicated query of the room's vote comments (all of them, minimal fields: createdUser, comment text), so counts are right whatever the comment page size; shared with the voter list.</li><li>Voter list in box-comments: newest votes (name, choice, date), \\"Show all N votes\\" expands the rest.</li><li>Side: <strong>Result</strong> box (box-warning) above Linked issue: \\"Leaning: I agree (4 of 5)\\" (or \\"Tied\\" / \\"No votes yet\\") and \\"N of M project members voted\\" (members from the project members list).</li><li>Live: a new vote comment (Hermes comment created) updates tallies, list and result without reload.</li><li>Translations: reuse <code>views.app.conversation.vote.*</code>, new keys for result and hint.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> acceptance test: vote once, counts and result update, thumbs locked after voting, a live vote from another user updates tallies. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> closing a vote, changing a vote, linking issues to votes.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-detail"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-vote"]}, {"key": "threads-create-form", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: create modal uses FormFields for the linked issue and opens the new thread", "description": "<p>The New Thread modal in <code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code> uses a raw <code>&lt;PowerSelect&gt;</code> and a hand-written label for the linked issue, which the design system forbids (selects are <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code>).</p><ul><li>Linked issue: <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> with search over issues (existing <code>linkIssueSearch</code> task), enabled only for roomType discussion as today.</li><li>After save: the list reloads in place and the app navigates to the new thread's page.</li><li>Move the modal into its own component if it keeps the layout template simpler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> acceptance test creating a discussion with a linked issue lands on the new thread. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other fields.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-row-counts"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gaia-counts", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Conversation rooms: read-only comment, vote and like counts per room", "description": "<p><strong>Request from A Prometheus.</strong> The Threads page (Prometheus) is moving to a QuickList and shows comment/vote and like counts on each row, and vote tallies on vote threads. Gaia has no count for a room, so Prometheus currently makes two extra queries per row (40 calls for a 20-row page) and loads every vote comment to count agree/disagree. We ask for one read-only resource that returns counts for many rooms in one call. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract:</strong></p><ul><li>Read-only resource <code>conversationroomcount</code> (view model, like <code>app/metadata/model/Userlatestproject.php</code> with COUNT subqueries): fields <code>id</code> (= room id), <code>commentCount</code>, <code>likeCount</code> (votes on the room), <code>agreeCount</code> and <code>disagreeCount</code> (comments of vote rooms with the text \\"I agree\\" / \\"I disagree\\"), <code>lastCommentDate</code>, <code>projectId</code>.</li><li><code>GET /conversationroomcount?query=(Conversationroomcount.id CONTAINS 'a','b',...)</code> returns one row per room; list + get only (no create/update/delete), standard CRUD controller, no custom routes.</li><li>ACL: project-scoped like Conversationroom; reading needs <code>conversationroom.read</code> (or a new <code>conversationroomcount.list</code>, your call).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> api-tester cases for counts (no comments = 0, deleted comments not counted, agree/disagree split) and for project scoping. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> live events for counts (Prometheus updates counts from comment events).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "threads-counts-switch", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: load row counts and vote tallies with one Gaia call", "description": "<p>Once Gaia serves room counts (the A Gaia request in this plan), replace the per-row comment/vote queries (row counts issue) with one <code>conversationroomcount</code> query per loaded page, and take the vote thread's tallies from it (<code>agreeCount</code>/<code>disagreeCount</code>) instead of counting all vote comments; the voter list keeps its own paged query.</p><ul><li>New model + adapter/serializer if needed, Mirage handler.</li><li>Swap only the count sources; rows, vote UI and live updates unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a 20-row page makes one count request (test on the Mirage request log); vote tallies match. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> anything else on the page.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-row-counts", "threads-vote", "gaia-counts"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "threads-cleanup", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: remove the old feed, filters and unused conversation code", "description": "<p>After the list, thread page, vote body and create form are in place, remove what the old Threads feed left behind.</p><ul><li>Controller <code>controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code>: InfiniteScroll paging (<code>loadMoreConversations</code>, <code>fetchAllConversations</code>, <code>fetchFilteredConversations</code>, <code>fetchAndLinkComments</code>, <code>setHasMoreFlag</code>), hard-coded filters/date filters, <code>restoreStateFromQueryParams</code>, scroll-to-top/refresh, unused QPs (filter, date, q).</li><li><code>Conversation::ConversationItem</code> and <code>app-ui/skeleton/conversation-grid</code> if nothing uses them anymore; <code>conversation-loading.hbs</code> if replaced; dead styles in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code>; unused translation keys.</li><li><code>components/app-ui/tag-parser.js</code> ~l.229 and the <code>c_id</code> LinkTos (project overview, issue list, weekly-conversations widget) point to the thread page route directly; the index redirect stays for old URLs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> full test suite and lint pass; no reference to the removed code. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> behaviour changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["threads-vote", "threads-create-form"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-09 23:00:53	2026-11-09 23:00:53	f
c5d438046af3-2733-a385-0a767ae38d5c	341481c56af2-8040-cd6a-5ea33d81936b	5	{"summary": "Seven bug fixes for the new Threads UI from the live review. Layout template chain: remove the extra Threads header that aprom-4437 added (its title row and second breadcrumb; the project layout's own header with the project link and breadcrumb stays), then move New thread into the QuickList header. Thread page chain: drop the 'Discussion' label, drop the issue link from the header, translate the Linked issue status. In parallel: remove the thread box's extra shadow/border, and make the QuickList sort toolbar wrap (component fix, helps every QuickList).", "issues": [{"key": "thr-extra-header", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: remove the extra page header (title + second breadcrumb) added by the list layout", "description": "<p>The project layout <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> already renders the page header for every project page: the project name linking to the project (<code>h1 &gt; small &gt; LinkTo</code>) and the one <code>&lt;BreadCrumb/&gt;</code>. The new Threads layout (aprom-4437) added a <strong>second</strong> header with a \\"Threads\\" title and its own breadcrumb, so the breadcrumb shows twice and Threads has a title row that Task Board and Gantt Cal don't have. This came from the spec and screens of aprom-4437; ignore that header in the screens attached to the other Threads issues too.</p><ul><li>Remove only the header section the Threads templates render themselves (title row + breadcrumb, in <code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code> or wherever 4437 put it). <strong>Do not touch</strong> <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code>: the project link and the single breadcrumb stay exactly as on the Task Board.</li><li>Check the breadcrumb definitions for <code>app.project.conversation</code>, <code>.index</code> and <code>.page</code> in <code>services/breadcrumb.js</code> so the one breadcrumb shows Threads (and the thread on the page route).</li><li>Keep any button that lived in the removed header working until the next issue moves it into the QuickList header.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Threads shows the project link and exactly one breadcrumb, like the Task Board, and no extra title row (acceptance test counts the breadcrumbs on the index and a thread page). <strong>Out of scope:</strong> New thread placement (next issue).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4437"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-fixed"]}, {"key": "thr-new-in-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: move the New thread button into the QuickList header", "description": "<p>On Roles and Ideas the create button sits in the QuickList header (<code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> block, e.g. New Role from aprom-4430: <code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code>). On Threads it sat in the extra page header, which the previous issue removes.</p><ul><li>Put New thread in the Threads QuickList <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> block, same markup and size as New Role / New Idea, ACL <code>conversationroom.create</code>, opening the existing create modal.</li><li>The QuickList header shows only the title and this button; the page range and prev/next stay in QuickList's pagination in the box footer.</li><li>Remove the old button.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> New thread shows in the list header and opens the modal; hidden without create permission; existing create tests updated. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> the modal's fields (aprom-4445).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["thr-extra-header"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-fixed"]}, {"key": "thr-box-style", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: the thread box has an extra shadow and border unlike other boxes", "description": "<p>The thread (discussion) box on the Threads page (aprom-4439) has a shadow and border that don't match the rest of the application's boxes.</p><ul><li>Find the custom rules added for the thread box (likely in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code> or a new thread partial) and remove the extra shadow/border, so it looks exactly like a standard <code>box box-primary</code> (design system: no new shadows, square edges).</li><li>Don't restyle AdminLTE's <code>.box</code> globally.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the thread box matches the issue page's record box side by side in the running app. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other layout changes.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4439"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-fixed"]}, {"key": "thr-no-eyebrow", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: remove the 'Discussion' / 'Vote' label above the thread title", "description": "<p>The thread box shows a small uppercase type label (\\"Discussion\\") above the subject. No other page in the app has such a label, so Threads shouldn't either. It came from the spec and screen of aprom-4439; ignore it in the screens attached to the other Threads issues (vote, participants, create issue, activity).</p><ul><li>Remove the label from the thread header (and its styles and translation keys if unused). The subject is the box title (<code>h3.box-title</code>), followed by \\"Started by ... · date\\".</li><li>The room type stays visible in the list row icon and the vote body.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> no type label in the thread header for discussions or votes; tests updated. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> the list rows.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4439"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-fixed"]}, {"key": "thr-no-header-link", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: remove the linked issue line from the thread header", "description": "<p>The thread header shows the linked issue (<code>fa-link</code>, key, subject, status) and the Linked issue box in the info column shows it again. The side box is enough.</p><ul><li>Remove the linked-issue line from the thread header (template, styles, translations if unused). Keep \\"Started by ... · date\\".</li><li>The Linked issue box is unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the linked issue appears only in the Linked issue box; tests updated. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Linked issue box itself.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["thr-no-eyebrow"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-fixed"]}, {"key": "thr-status-label", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Threads: Linked issue box shows the issue status untranslated", "description": "<p>The Linked issue box in the thread info column shows the raw issue status (e.g. <code>in_progress</code>) instead of the translated label.</p><ul><li>Render it like the issue page does (<code>components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> ~l.19): <code>status-label</code> helper for the text and <code>status-style</code> + the status class for the colour.</li><li>Check the list rows and any other place the Threads code shows an issue status for the same mistake.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> integration test: a linked issue with status <code>in_progress</code> shows the translated label. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other boxes.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["thr-no-header-link"], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["threads-fixed"]}, {"key": "ql-toolbar-wrap", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: group/sort toolbar overflows its box instead of wrapping", "description": "<p>In the Threads QuickList, when the column is narrow, the group-by/sort toolbar (<code>QuickList::Toolbar</code>, aprom-4353) overflows the box instead of wrapping. It's a component bug, so the fix belongs in QuickList and helps every user (Ideas, Roles, Threads, the component library entry).</p><ul><li>Let the toolbar's controls wrap onto a second line (flex-wrap with a gap, right-aligned) inside the QuickList box at any width; long option labels truncate with an ellipsis rather than pushing the box wider.</li><li>Styles stay in the QuickList partial, scoped under the component's class.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a narrow col-md-3 (e.g. 1280px window) the toolbar stays inside the box on Threads, Ideas and Roles; integration test or demo state in the component library entry covers a narrow width. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> new toolbar options.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-threads", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-10 14:52:53	2026-11-10 14:56:46	f
6bc637a06af3-640b-1996-4d3c09c1b6c6	00d17cb06af3-c415-1996-69951fb2ab5f	1	{"summary": "Stop the deprecation flood in the Prometheus test runs without new dependencies. One issue removes the app's only use of the deprecated assign from @ember/polyfills (the oauth2 authenticator). The other adds a deprecation handler to the test helper that hides the listed deprecation IDs (starting with ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign), counts every deprecation by ID and prints one summary at the end of the run, so the output stops carrying thousands of stack traces and shows which IDs remain. The two are independent. Upgrading the addons that raise the deprecations is left to the separate stack upgrade.", "issues": [{"key": "oauth2-object-assign", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "OAuth2 authenticator: use Object.assign instead of the deprecated assign from @ember/polyfills", "description": "<p><code>assign</code> from <code>@ember/polyfills</code> is deprecated in Ember 4 (ID <code>ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign</code>). The only use in <code>app/</code> is the OAuth2 authenticator. Removing it is part of cutting the deprecation noise in the test runs.</p><ul><li><code>app/authenticators/oauth2.js</code>: remove the <code>import { assign } from '@ember/polyfills'</code> (line 11) and replace <code>response = assign(response, { 'expires_at': expiresAt })</code> in <code>authenticate()</code> (~line 106) with <code>Object.assign</code>. The behaviour stays the same: the response object gets <code>expires_at</code>.</li><li>Extend <code>tests/unit/authenticators/oauth2-test.js</code> to check that <code>authenticate()</code> resolves with <code>expires_at</code> when the server returns <code>expires_in</code>, if that case isn't covered yet.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>grep -r \\"@ember/polyfills\\" app tests mirage</code> finds nothing; the oauth2 unit test and the sign-in acceptance feature pass; the full suite passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> deprecations raised by addons (handled in the test helper issue and the later stack upgrade); lodash <code>_.assign</code> in <code>adapters/application.js</code> (not deprecated).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "test-deprecation-handler", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Tests: hide known deprecations and print one count per deprecation ID instead of a stack trace each", "description": "<p>A full Prometheus test run writes about 18.7k deprecation stack traces: Ember's debug build sends each deprecation to <code>console.warn</code> with a stack, and testem captures all of them. That bloats the run log that <code>ai test</code>, Talos and CI read, and hides real failures. Most of them come from addons, not from <code>app/</code> code (the app's only <code>assign</code> from <code>@ember/polyfills</code> is in the oauth2 authenticator, which acceptance tests skip by logging in with <code>authenticateSession</code>). Fixing the addons belongs to a later stack upgrade. This issue only stops the noise in tests and reports what remains.</p><ul><li>In <code>tests/test-helper.js</code>, register a handler with <code>registerDeprecationHandler</code> from <code>@ember/debug</code>, before <code>start()</code>. Use no new dependency (not ember-cli-deprecation-workflow).</li><li>Keep a short list of hidden deprecation IDs in a small test-support module (e.g. <code>tests/helpers/deprecations.js</code>), starting with <code>ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign</code>. For a hidden ID, count it and don't call <code>next</code>, so nothing is logged.</li><li>Count every deprecation by ID, hidden or not. Other IDs still go to <code>next</code>, so they log as before.</li><li>On <code>QUnit.done</code>, print one <code>console.log</code> line per ID with its count (e.g. <code>DEPRECATIONS ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign: 18734</code>), and print nothing when there were none.</li><li>Before the change, run the full suite and record in the PR the number of deprecation lines per ID and the log size. Record them again after the change.</li><li>Unit test for the counting and hiding logic in the helper module.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the full suite passes with the same number of tests; the run log has no stack traces for hidden IDs; the end-of-run summary lists the counts per ID; the PR shows the before and after numbers.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> upgrading the addons that raise the deprecations; making deprecations fail tests; hiding deprecations outside tests (dev and production builds are unchanged); ember-exam / parallel test runs.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-10 16:20:59	2026-11-10 16:20:59	f
94c8e0b86af4-c2ce-00ad-b3189993660a	5a1482d46af4-0fdf-00ad-c45029d7a40d	1	{"summary": "Docs module foundation. Gaia gets a standard project-scoped Doc REST resource (title, body, projectId, ownerId, locked, tags via Tag/Tagged) plus the decision to keep Wiki until a later migration. Prometheus then gets the doc model/adapter/serializer with Mirage support, the doc page (app.project.doc.page), and, in parallel, the All Docs list (app.project.doc.index) and Create Doc form (app.project.doc.create), each with its sidebar entry, ACL route mapping, loading skeleton, empty state, translations and acceptance tests.", "issues": [{"key": "doc-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Doc resource (title, body, owner, locked, tags) as standard project-scoped CRUD", "description": "<p>Projects get a Docs module where teams create, list and open documents. This adds the backing <code>Doc</code> resource as plain REST CRUD, following the new-resource guide <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code> (exemplar gaia#193, Idea).</p><ul><li><code>app/metadata/model/Doc.php</code>, table <code>doc</code>: <code>title</code> varchar(255) required, <code>body</code> text (nullable), <code>projectId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>ownerId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>locked</code> bool default false, plus the standard <code>id</code>, <code>dateCreated</code>, <code>dateModified</code>, <code>createdUser</code>, <code>modifiedUser</code>, <code>deleted</code>. Behaviours as on <code>Wiki</code>: created/modified user and date, soft delete, audit.</li><li>Relationships: <code>project</code> belongsTo Project, <code>owner</code> hasOne User (via <code>ownerId</code>), <code>createdBy</code>/<code>modifiedBy</code> hasOne User, <code>tag</code> hasManyToMany Tag via Tagged (<code>relatedTo = 'doc'</code>), <code>tagged</code> hasMany Tagged. Add the inverse <code>doc</code> relationship on <code>Tagged</code> and <code>docs</code> on <code>Project</code>, as done for Wiki.</li><li>ACL metadata: <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via <code>projectId</code>, so only project members with the <code>doc.*</code> permissions can read/create/update/delete.</li><li>Empty <code>app/models/Doc.php</code> and <code>DocController</code> (RestController subclass), the <code>'Doc'</code> line in <code>core/config/models.php</code>, the <code>doc</code> route in <code>core/config/routes.php</code>, <code>routes.v1.json</code>, the placeholders in <code>generate-backend-apis.php</code> and a regenerated <code>backend.json</code>.</li><li>api-tester: harness table and seed rows, fixture ids, <code>acl.json</code> cases (member with and without <code>doc.*</code>, non-member) and <code>client.json</code> cases (create, list by project, get with <code>owner</code> and <code>tag</code> rels, delete).</li><li>New <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>, D-001: Docs is a new module beside Wiki. Wiki stays as is (no new features), its content is migrated into Docs in a later issue once the Docs body format is settled, and then Wiki is retired.</li><li>No permission seed SQL (the reviewer grants <code>doc.*</code> by hand). Regenerate the gaia-dev graph and <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a project member with <code>doc.create</code> can POST a doc and list it with <code>((Doc.projectId : X))</code>; a user without <code>doc.read</code> or outside the project gets 403/empty; tags attach through Tagged; the full test suite and CI drift checks pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> live events, enforcing <code>locked</code>, owner-change rules, Wiki migration, body format/versioning.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "A new resource has a fixed set of touchpoints (metadata, parent relationships, model, controller, models/routes config, api-tester catalog and acl/client cases) that must ship together, or dev is left with a resource that has no ACL cases; the decision doc is one small file.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-data", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: doc model, adapter, serializer and Mirage support", "description": "<p>Data layer for the new Docs module, used by the doc page, All Docs and Create Doc screens. It reads the Gaia <code>doc</code> resource.</p><ul><li><code>app/models/doc.js</code> (native class, YUIDoc): <code>title</code>, <code>body</code>, <code>projectId</code>, <code>ownerId</code>, <code>locked</code> (boolean), <code>dateCreated</code>, <code>dateModified</code>, <code>createdUser</code>, <code>modifiedUser</code>; relationships <code>project</code>, <code>owner</code> (user), <code>tag</code> (hasMany tag, async). Follow the closest existing model (e.g. <code>idea</code>, <code>wiki</code>) for naming and date handling.</li><li><code>app/adapters/doc.js</code> and <code>app/serializers/doc.js</code> extending the application adapter/serializer with no custom endpoints (singular path <code>/api/v1/doc</code>).</li><li>Mirage: <code>mirage/factories/doc.js</code> (realistic titles, an owner, some tags) and handlers in <code>mirage/config.js</code> for list with the Gaia <code>query</code> filter on projectId, get by id, create and delete, matching how the <code>idea</code> and <code>wiki</code> handlers are written. Tagged rows with <code>relatedTo: 'doc'</code> must work in Mirage.</li><li>Unit tests for the model and serializer.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>store.query('doc', { query: '((Doc.projectId : X))', rels: 'owner,tag' })</code>, <code>findRecord</code>, <code>createRecord().save()</code> and <code>destroyRecord</code> work against Mirage; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> routes and UI (separate issues), live updates.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-api"], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-page", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: doc page route (app.project.doc.page) with detail layout, skeleton and empty state", "description": "<p>Opening a doc in a project. This is the page the All Docs rows link to and Create Doc lands on after saving. Editing the body comes later; this page is read-only.</p><ul><li><code>app/router.js</code>: add <code>this.route('doc', function(){ this.route('page', {path: '/:doc_id'}); })</code> under <code>project</code> (the index and create routes are added by their own issues).</li><li><code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code>: <code>{ name: 'app.project.doc.page', map: 'doc.read' }</code>.</li><li>Route <code>routes/app/project/doc/page.js</code> (native class, extends <code>routes/app.js</code>): loads the doc with <code>rels</code> for <code>owner</code> and <code>tag</code> only (hasOne/belongsTo and tags, no unbounded hasMany); a missing or forbidden doc shows the existing not-found/error handling.</li><li>Template <code>templates/app/project/doc/page.hbs</code> on the design-system detail pattern: <code>col-md-8</code> <code>box box-primary</code> with the title (lock icon <code>fa fa-lock</code> when <code>locked</code>) and the body as escaped text (no <code>htmlSafe</code>/triple-stash); when the body is empty, the design-system §4 empty state (\\"This doc has no content yet\\"). <code>col-md-4</code> side box with owner, tags (<code>label</code>s), created and last edited.</li><li><code>templates/app/project/doc/page-loading.hbs</code> skeleton matching the layout (design-system §4).</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Acceptance <code>.feature</code> (with steps in a per-feature steps file, not <code>steps.js</code>): opens a doc and sees title, owner, tags; empty body shows the empty state; a user without <code>doc.read</code> is redirected away.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the scenarios above pass on Mirage; page matches an existing detail screen side by side; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> editing, delete button, comments, presence, live updates.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-data"], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-list", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: All Docs list page (app.project.doc.index) and Docs sidebar item", "description": "<p>The project's list of docs, reached from a new \\"Docs\\" item in the sidebar.</p><ul><li><code>app/router.js</code>: add <code>this.route('index', {path: '/'})</code> to the <code>doc</code> route. <code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code>: <code>app.project.doc.index</code> → <code>doc.read</code>.</li><li>Sidebar: in <code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> <code>views.Navigation.items</code> add <code>Doc</code> (icon <code>file-text-o</code>, route <code>app.project.doc</code>, <code>anchorRoute: 'doc'</code>, <code>projectRelated: true</code>, <code>aclContext: 'doc.read'</code>) with <code>actions.section1.list</code> \\"All Docs\\" like the Issue item. The \\"Create Doc\\" child is added by the Create Doc issue.</li><li>Route <code>routes/app/project/doc/index.js</code> and controller <code>controllers/app/project/doc/index.js</code> extending <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>, modelled on <code>controllers/app/agent/index.js</code>: query <code>((Doc.projectId : X))</code> with rels <code>owner,tag</code>, sort by last edited desc, pagination, search by title.</li><li>Template <code>templates/app/project/doc/index.hbs</code>: list page pattern, one full-width <code>box box-primary</code> with search toolbar, table (title linking to <code>app.project.doc.page</code> with a lock icon when locked, owner, last edited, tags) and pagination; row delete through the base list's delete with <code>aclContext=\\"doc.delete\\"</code>; \\"New doc\\" button with <code>aclContext=\\"doc.create\\"</code> to <code>app.project.doc.create</code> only once that route exists, otherwise leave it to the Create Doc issue.</li><li><code>templates/app/project/doc/index-loading.hbs</code> skeleton and an empty state (\\"No docs yet\\") per design-system §4.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; acceptance <code>.feature</code> with a per-feature steps file: list shows seeded docs with owner/tags, search filters, empty state, delete removes a row, no <code>doc.read</code> → route blocked and sidebar item hidden.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> scenarios pass on Mirage; screen matches an existing list page side by side; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> saved searches beyond what <code>list.js</code> gives for free, export, mass update, live updates.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-page"], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-create", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Create Doc form (app.project.doc.create) and sidebar entry", "description": "<p>Lets a project member with <code>doc.create</code> start a new doc. The body is written later in the editor, so the form asks only for title and tags.</p><ul><li><code>app/router.js</code>: add <code>this.route('create')</code> to the <code>doc</code> route. <code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code>: <code>app.project.doc.create</code> → <code>doc.create</code>.</li><li>Sidebar: add <code>actions.section1.create</code> \\"Create Doc\\" (route <code>app.project.doc.create</code>, <code>aclContext: 'doc.create'</code>) to the Docs item in <code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>; if the Docs item isn't there yet, add it as described for All Docs (icon <code>file-text-o</code>, <code>aclContext: 'doc.read'</code>).</li><li>Route/controller <code>app/project/doc/create</code> (native classes) and <code>templates/app/project/doc/create.hbs</code> on the create/edit pattern: <code>col-md-8</code> form box with <code>FormFields::FieldText</code> title (required, validation message) and <code>FormFields::FieldRelateMulti</code> for tags (existing project tags), <code>col-md-4</code> side box with owner (current user) and project; Save/Cancel below the boxes.</li><li>Save: creates the doc with <code>projectId</code> and <code>ownerId</code> = current user, then the Tagged rows (<code>relatedTo: 'doc'</code>), then transitions to <code>app.project.doc.page</code>. Ignore a second submit while saving and disable Save; on failure show the error and roll back. Cancel returns to <code>app.project.doc.index</code>.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; acceptance <code>.feature</code> with a per-feature steps file: create with title and tags lands on the doc page and the doc appears in All Docs; empty title shows validation; failed save shows an error; no <code>doc.create</code> → route blocked and sidebar child hidden.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> scenarios pass on Mirage; screen matches an existing create form side by side; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> body editing, creating new tags inline, templates, edit route.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-page"], "milestone": "Docs MVP", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-11 09:51:16	2026-11-11 09:51:16	f
f95a03f26af7-b6c3-7359-e26fe950af67	44c783b46af7-b6c3-7359-e3d9f0af5900	1	{"summary": "One Prometheus issue: show each milestone's issue count on its task board tab, taken from the milestone.issues the board already loads and keeps in sync, so it updates when issues are created, moved (including drag onto a tab) or deleted. No API change.", "issues": [{"key": "tab-issue-count", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task board: show issue count on each milestone tab", "description": "<p>The task board's milestone tabs show only the type and name, so users must open each tab to see how much work it holds. Add the issue count to every tab, backlog included.</p><ul><li>In <code>app/components/app-ui/task-board.hbs</code> (the <code>ul.milestone-tabs</code> loop), render <code>milestone.issues.length</code> after the milestone name as an AdminLTE <code>label</code> (per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>), with a <code>data-milestone-issue-count</code> attribute and a translated title/tooltip such as \\"12 issues\\" (new key in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>).</li><li>Use the same <code>milestone.issues</code> array as the milestone header's \\"x/y issues\\" (<code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code>). <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> already keeps it in sync on create, move between milestones (including drop on a tab via <code>modifiers/initialize-sortable.js</code>) and delete, so the count must update without a reload.</li><li>If a style is needed (spacing next to the name, contrast on the active tab), add it under <code>.milestone-tabs</code> in <code>app/styles/modules/board.scss</code>. Use palette colours only and keep square edges. The label must not break the tab drop zones (<code>.drop-zone-area</code>).</li><li>When a board filter is active, the count reflects the issues loaded on the board, consistent with the lane counts.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Every milestone tab, including the backlog, shows its issue count. A milestone with no issues shows 0.</li><li>Creating an issue in a milestone, dragging an issue onto another milestone's tab or between milestones, and deleting an issue update the affected tab counts right away.</li><li>Integration test in <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/task-board/layout-test.js</code> covering the counts, including 0 and a count change after an issue moves.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-status or open/closed counts on the tab, and server-side totals that ignore the active filter.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-13 12:56:25	2026-11-13 12:56:25	f
0888cb166afc-5e99-d022-193a8eec8ffb	368036d36afc-ae59-6053-37801a47463a	1	{"summary": "Rework the app shell in Prometheus. The project selector moves from the sidebar into the header as a crimson project switcher. The sidebar is split into Workspace, Project <CODE> and Admin groups; project items are disabled until a project is selected. The search is centred in the header on desktop and gets its own row on phones. The sidebar user panel goes and its online status moves to the header avatar and the profile menu. On phones the sidebar closes after navigation. The switcher comes first because it removes the sidebar selector. The grouped sidebar and the search layout follow in parallel, and the profile status comes last because it touches the same header and sidebar templates. The phone auto-close is independent.", "issues": [{"key": "header-switcher", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Header: project switcher replaces the sidebar project selector", "description": "<p>The project selector sits in the sidebar (<code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.hbs</code> <code>.sidebar-form</code>), so the loaded project can't be seen when the sidebar is collapsed or closed on a phone. Move it into the header as a project switcher, so the current project is always visible. The attached screens are a guide to layout and content only; the design system and the real components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>In <code>components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs</code>, right after the sidebar toggle, add a crimson switcher. Desktop label: the project name plus its short code (e.g. <code>A Prometheus APROM</code>, name and code on one baseline). Below 768px label: the short code only. With no project selected, the label is <strong>Select a project</strong>.</li><li>The switcher opens a searchable list of the user's projects (name left, code right, the current one ticked) with an <strong>All projects</strong> link (<code>app.projects</code>) at the bottom. Build it with the existing <code>AppUi::Select</code> (power-select, search on <code>label</code>, same <code>projectsList</code> data the sidebar uses today). Do not hand-roll a dropdown. If the footer link can't be added through power-select's existing extension points, finish with needs_input.</li><li>Move <code>projectChanged</code> and <code>getTransitionUrl</code> from <code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.js</code> to the header component (or a small shared helper) unchanged in behaviour. Remove the selector and <code>projectsList</code> plumbing from the sidebar (<code>nav-bar.hbs</code>, <code>application-sidebar.hbs</code>).</li><li>Styles go in <code>styles/modules/header.scss</code>. Colours come from <code>variables.scss</code> only, square edges. Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Update tests: <code>tests/integration/components/app-layouts/application-header-test.js</code>, <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/nav-bar-test.js</code>, and <code>tests/acceptance/app/select-project-from-sidebar.feature</code> plus its steps (now selecting from the header). Use <code>data-test-*</code> selectors.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the current project's name and code are visible in the header with the sidebar expanded, collapsed or closed. Picking a project navigates exactly as the sidebar selector did. The sidebar no longer has a selector.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the sidebar grouping, the search position and the profile status (separate issues).</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["nav-desktop", "nav-no-project", "nav-desktop-collapsed", "nav-mobile"]}, {"key": "nav-groups", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Sidebar: Workspace / Project / Admin groups, project items disabled without a project", "description": "<p>Dashboard and Projects work across projects, while Issues, Task Board, Gantt Cal, Threads and Ideas belong to the selected project, yet they are mixed in one \\"Main Navigation\\" list. Group them, and disable the project items when no project is selected. Today those items link to <code>/project/undefined/...</code>. The attached screens are a guide to layout and content only; the design system and the real components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>In <code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.{hbs,js}</code>, split <code>navigationMeta</code> by the existing metadata flag <code>projectRelated</code> (<code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> <code>Navigation.items</code>). Do not hard-code item names. Render the groups as <code>li.header</code> sections: <strong>Workspace</strong> (non-project items), then <strong>Project</strong> followed by the current project's short code in crimson, then the existing <strong>Admin</strong> group. Keep the order within each group by <code>order</code>.</li><li>No project selected (<code>trackedProject</code> has no short code): still render the project items, but disabled through <code>components/app-ui/navbar-items.{hbs,js}</code>. Disabled items are muted with a not-allowed cursor, <code>aria-disabled=\\"true\\"</code>, no navigation and no treeview expansion, with a \\"Select a project\\" title. The group header shows <strong>Select a project</strong> on the right instead of the code.</li><li>Collapsed sidebar (<code>sidebar-collapse</code>): AdminLTE hides <code>li.header</code>, so put a thin divider between the groups.</li><li>Styles go in <code>styles/modules/nav.scss</code>. Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> (rename the \\"Main Navigation\\" label to Workspace).</li><li>Tests: <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/nav-bar-test.js</code> and <code>navbar-items-test.js</code> cover the grouping, the code in the header, and the disabled state without a project.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Dashboard and Projects are under Workspace; Issues, Task Board, Gantt Cal, Threads and Ideas are under Project &lt;CODE&gt;. Without a project those items are visible but do nothing. Dividers separate the groups when the sidebar is collapsed.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the user panel removal (profile status issue) and closing the sidebar on phones.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["header-switcher"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["nav-desktop", "nav-no-project", "nav-desktop-collapsed", "nav-mobile"]}, {"key": "search-layout", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Header: centre the global search, own row on phones", "description": "<p>With the project switcher in the header, the search and the switcher no longer both fit on one phone row. On desktop the search should sit in the centre of the header. The attached screens are a guide to layout and content only; the design system and the real components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>Desktop (768px and up): centre <code>div.global-search</code> (<code>components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs</code>) in the navbar, about 420px wide, without overlapping the switcher or the right-hand menu at narrower desktop widths.</li><li>Below 768px: the search moves to its own full-width row under the switcher, New, bell and avatar row. That row has the hamburger, the switcher (short code), a compact New (<code>fa-plus</code>) and the bell. The content and the opened sidebar start below the taller header.</li><li>The search keeps its behaviour (<code>AppUi::Select</code> issue search, <code>search</code> task).</li><li>Styles go in <code>styles/modules/header.scss</code> (media queries at the Bootstrap xs breakpoint).</li><li>Test: <code>tests/integration/components/app-layouts/application-header-test.js</code> (the search is still rendered and works).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on desktop the search is centred in the header. On a 390px wide phone the header has the action row plus a full-width search row, with nothing cramped or clipped.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> hiding the logo row on phones, and changing what the search finds.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["header-switcher"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["nav-desktop", "nav-mobile"]}, {"key": "header-presence", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Header: online status on the avatar and in the profile menu, remove the sidebar user panel", "description": "<p>The sidebar repeats the user's picture and name from the header, only to show a static \\"Online\\" status. Move the status into the header and drop the sidebar user panel. Presence stays fixed (always Online) for now. The attached screens are a guide to layout and content only; the design system and the real components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>In <code>components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs</code>, the user menu keeps the real profile picture (<code>AppUi::Avatar</code> <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code>) with a small green status dot at its bottom-right. The picture and name are vertically centred in the navbar.</li><li>In the profile dropdown, the large avatar gets the same dot. Add a row under <code>li.user-header</code>: green dot, <strong>Online</strong>, and a muted \\"Visible to your team\\" on the right, above Profile / Sign out.</li><li>Remove the <code>.user-panel</code> block (<code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.hbs</code> lines 2-12). Keep the <code>initialize-sidebar</code> modifier on an element that stays in the sidebar.</li><li>Colours: the success green from <code>variables.scss</code>. Styles go in <code>styles/modules/header.scss</code>. Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> (reuse <code>views.app.online</code>).</li><li>Tests: <code>application-header-test.js</code> (dot plus status row) and <code>nav-bar-test.js</code> / <code>application-sidebar-test.js</code> (no user panel).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the header avatar shows the profile picture with a green dot, the profile menu shows the Online row, and the sidebar starts with the Workspace group.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> real presence (online, away, offline from Hermes).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["nav-groups", "search-layout"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["nav-desktop", "nav-mobile"]}, {"key": "mobile-close", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Sidebar: close the menu after navigation on phones", "description": "<p>On phones, the sidebar opened with the hamburger stays open after you pick a page, so it has to be closed by hand. Close it automatically, on phones only. The attached screen is a guide to layout and content only.</p><ul><li>On every route change (router service <code>routeDidChange</code>), when the viewport is below 768px and <code>body</code> has <code>sidebar-open</code>, remove it. Desktop expand/collapse and the persisted <code>sidebar-collapsed</code> preference (<code>modifiers/initialize-sidebar.js</code>) stay unchanged.</li><li>While the menu is open on a phone, dim the page under it. Tapping the dimmed page closes the menu, the same way AdminLTE's content click does.</li><li>Clean up the listener on teardown. Use no new jQuery; native listeners and the router service only.</li><li>Test: an integration or acceptance test that opens the sidebar at phone width, navigates, and asserts it closed, plus a desktop case where nothing changes.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a phone, tapping any menu item navigates and closes the menu, and tapping outside closes it too. On desktop the sidebar state never changes on navigation.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> swipe gestures.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["nav-mobile"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 09:48:56	2026-11-17 09:48:56	f
3b7763776afd-5c6b-838a-ee875da766e5	6c7240d86afd-3eec-75db-a5acaf1064a6	2	{"summary": "Remove the blank screens between opening Prometheus and seeing a page. A static boot loader in index.html covers bundle download, session restore and translation loading, and loading-assets shows the page skeleton instead of a bare heading. The app.project route gets a loading skeleton and renders its outlet without a redundant project query. It also stops making nested routes wait for the all-issues preload. The boot issue is independent of the two project-route issues, which run in order because both change routes/app/project.js.", "issues": [{"key": "boot-loader", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "App start: static boot loader until the first screen, skeleton on loading-assets", "description": "<p>On a cold load, Prometheus shows a blank page until several steps finish one after another. First the bundles load: the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> of <code>app/index.html</code> holds only the two script tags. Then <code>routes/application.js</code> <code>beforeModel</code> awaits <code>session.setup()</code>, which restores the session and may refresh the token. Then it awaits <code>translations.load()</code>. No loading template exists at the top level. After that, <code>app.loading-assets</code> shows only a hardcoded <code>&lt;h1&gt;Loading Assets...&lt;/h1&gt;</code> while it loads the user, users, roles, projects and settings.</p><ul><li><code>app/index.html</code>: add a static boot loader element inside <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> before the scripts (e.g. <code>&lt;div class=\\"boot-loader\\" data-boot-loader&gt;</code>). Use no text, because translations aren't loaded yet: a centred spinner or a header bar with skeleton lines. Style it with design-system colours in a new partial under <code>app/styles/</code>, imported from <code>app.scss</code>. <code>prometheus.css</code> is linked in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, so it applies before the JS runs.</li><li>Remove the element once the application route has finished <code>beforeModel</code> (e.g. in its <code>setupController</code>), so it stays up through session restore and translation loading. Removal must be safe when the element is missing (<code>tests/index.html</code> has none), and it must also happen when <code>beforeModel</code> ends in a redirect (signin, public routes).</li><li><code>app/templates/app/loading-assets.hbs</code>: replace the hardcoded heading with <code>&lt;AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader={{true}} /&gt;</code>.</li><li>Tests: an integration or acceptance test that loading-assets renders the skeleton while its model is pending, and a unit test that the application route removes the boot loader and tolerates its absence.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> from the first paint of a cold load (signed in or not) until the first real screen, the page always shows the boot loader or a skeleton, never a blank white page. The boot loader is gone once the sign-in page or the app shell renders. No user-facing text is hardcoded.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> making the boot requests themselves faster (session restore, translations, loading-assets data), and the app.project route wait.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "project-route-skeleton", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project route: show a skeleton while the project loads and render the outlet without the extra project query", "description": "<p>On a fresh load of any project URL (e.g. <code>/app/project/aprom/issue/4198</code>), the content area stays blank until the parent <code>app.project</code> route finishes its hooks, before the nested route's own request even starts. Ember finds no loading substate for <code>app.project</code>: <code>app/project-loading.hbs</code>, <code>app/loading.hbs</code> and <code>loading.hbs</code> don't exist. The existing <code>app/project/loading.hbs</code> and <code>*-loading.hbs</code> templates only cover child routes. They are also hidden, because <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> renders <code>{{outlet}}</code> only inside <code>{{#if this.projectId}}</code>, and <code>setupController</code> in <code>routes/app/project.js</code> sets <code>projectId</code> in the <code>.then()</code> of a second project query, although <code>beforeModel</code> already loaded the project.</p><ul><li>Add <code>app/templates/app/project-loading.hbs</code>: a <code>content-header</code> with a heading skeleton line plus <code>&lt;AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @bodyOnly={{true}} /&gt;</code>, following <code>app/templates/app/settings-loading.hbs</code> and the design system.</li><li><code>routes/app/project.js</code>: keep the project record loaded in <code>beforeModel</code> on the route. In <code>setupController</code>, set <code>model</code>, <code>projectId</code> and <code>projectName</code> from it straight away, and remove the second <code>store.query('project', { fields: 'Project.id,Project.name' ... })</code>.</li><li>When no project matches the short code, keep today's error handling (<code>errorManager</code>) and don't throw on <code>objectAt(project, 0).id</code>.</li><li>Tests: an acceptance or route test that visits a project child route with a delayed project response and asserts the project skeleton is shown. Also check that the child's loading template renders while its own model is pending.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a cold load or reload of a project page never shows an empty content area. The project skeleton shows while the project loads, then the child skeleton, then the page. Only one project request is made per project entry. The project name and breadcrumb are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the all-issues preload in <code>afterModel</code> (separate issue), the app start before the app shell.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "project-issues-nonblocking", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project route: stop blocking nested routes on the all-issues preload", "description": "<p><code>routes/app/project.js</code> <code>afterModel</code> loads every issue of the project (<code>limit: -1</code>; fields id, subject, issueNumber, statusId, projectId) and returns that promise, so every nested route (board, issue list, issue page, ideas, conversations, ...) waits for it before its own request starts. The list only feeds the <code>issuesList</code> getter in <code>controllers/app/project.js</code> (<code>@computed('projectId', 'issues')</code>). It is read by <code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code> and <code>controllers/prometheus/projectrelated.js</code>, and from there by <code>components/message-box.js</code> and <code>components/summer-note.js</code>.</p><ul><li>Start the issues query without returning it from <code>afterModel</code>. When it resolves, set <code>issues</code> on the <code>app.project</code> controller (and the route, if still read there); report errors with <code>errorManager.handleError</code> as today. Ignore a result that arrives after the user has switched to another project.</li><li>Make sure the <code>issuesList</code> getter updates when <code>issues</code> arrives later, and that every reader handles the empty list (only the blank entry) until then without errors.</li><li>Tests: a route/acceptance test that a nested route's model request starts before the issues preload resolves, and that the list fills in once it does.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a cold load of a project page, the nested route's request starts right after the project request, without waiting for the all-issues request. Issue pickers that use <code>issuesList</code> show the issues once loaded. Switching projects never shows another project's issues.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing the preload with server-side search in the pickers, the store.request migration (aprom-4552).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["project-route-skeleton"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 10:00:27	2026-11-18 10:00:27	f
c22de8386afc-5e99-ea61-a75bfaea9cb9	368036d36afc-ae59-6053-37801a47463a	2	{"summary": "Rework the app shell in Prometheus. The project selector moves from the sidebar into the header as a crimson project switcher. The sidebar is split into Workspace, Project <CODE> and Admin groups; project items are disabled until a project is selected. The search is centred in the header on desktop and gets its own row on phones. The sidebar user panel goes and its online status moves to the header avatar and the profile menu. On phones the sidebar closes after navigation. The switcher comes first because it removes the sidebar selector. The grouped sidebar and the search layout follow in parallel, and the profile status comes last because it touches the same header and sidebar templates. The phone auto-close is independent.", "issues": [{"key": "header-switcher", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Header: project switcher replaces the sidebar project selector", "description": "<p>The project selector sits in the sidebar (<code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.hbs</code> <code>.sidebar-form</code>), so the loaded project can't be seen when the sidebar is collapsed or closed on a phone. Move it into the header as a project switcher, so the current project is always visible. The attached screens are a guide to layout and content only; the design system and the real components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>In <code>components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs</code>, right after the sidebar toggle, add a crimson switcher. Desktop label: the project name plus its short code (e.g. <code>A Prometheus APROM</code>, name and code on one baseline). Below 768px label: the short code only. With no project selected, the label is <strong>Select a project</strong>.</li><li>The switcher opens a searchable list of the user's projects (name left, code right, the current one ticked) with an <strong>All projects</strong> link (<code>app.projects</code>) at the bottom. Build it with the existing <code>AppUi::Select</code> (power-select, search on <code>label</code>, same <code>projectsList</code> data the sidebar uses today). Do not hand-roll a dropdown. If the footer link can't be added through power-select's existing extension points, finish with needs_input.</li><li>Move <code>projectChanged</code> and <code>getTransitionUrl</code> from <code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.js</code> to the header component (or a small shared helper) unchanged in behaviour. Remove the selector and <code>projectsList</code> plumbing from the sidebar (<code>nav-bar.hbs</code>, <code>application-sidebar.hbs</code>).</li><li>Styles go in <code>styles/modules/header.scss</code>. Colours come from <code>variables.scss</code> only, square edges. Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Update tests: <code>tests/integration/components/app-layouts/application-header-test.js</code>, <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/nav-bar-test.js</code>, and <code>tests/acceptance/app/select-project-from-sidebar.feature</code> plus its steps (now selecting from the header). Use <code>data-test-*</code> selectors.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the current project's name and code are visible in the header with the sidebar expanded, collapsed or closed. Picking a project navigates exactly as the sidebar selector did. The sidebar no longer has a selector.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the sidebar grouping, the search position and the profile status (separate issues).</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Navbar", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["nav-desktop", "nav-no-project", "nav-desktop-collapsed", "nav-mobile"]}, {"key": "nav-groups", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Sidebar: Workspace / Project / Admin groups, project items disabled without a project", "description": "<p>Dashboard and Projects work across projects, while Issues, Task Board, Gantt Cal, Threads and Ideas belong to the selected project, yet they are mixed in one \\"Main Navigation\\" list. Group them, and disable the project items when no project is selected. Today those items link to <code>/project/undefined/...</code>. The attached screens are a guide to layout and content only; the design system and the real components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>In <code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.{hbs,js}</code>, split <code>navigationMeta</code> by the existing metadata flag <code>projectRelated</code> (<code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> <code>Navigation.items</code>). Do not hard-code item names. Render the groups as <code>li.header</code> sections: <strong>Workspace</strong> (non-project items), then <strong>Project</strong> followed by the current project's short code in crimson, then the existing <strong>Admin</strong> group. Keep the order within each group by <code>order</code>.</li><li>No project selected (<code>trackedProject</code> has no short code): still render the project items, but disabled through <code>components/app-ui/navbar-items.{hbs,js}</code>. Disabled items are muted with a not-allowed cursor, <code>aria-disabled=\\"true\\"</code>, no navigation and no treeview expansion, with a \\"Select a project\\" title. The group header shows <strong>Select a project</strong> on the right instead of the code.</li><li>Collapsed sidebar (<code>sidebar-collapse</code>): AdminLTE hides <code>li.header</code>, so put a thin divider between the groups.</li><li>Styles go in <code>styles/modules/nav.scss</code>. Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> (rename the \\"Main Navigation\\" label to Workspace).</li><li>Tests: <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/nav-bar-test.js</code> and <code>navbar-items-test.js</code> cover the grouping, the code in the header, and the disabled state without a project.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Dashboard and Projects are under Workspace; Issues, Task Board, Gantt Cal, Threads and Ideas are under Project &lt;CODE&gt;. Without a project those items are visible but do nothing. Dividers separate the groups when the sidebar is collapsed.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the user panel removal (profile status issue) and closing the sidebar on phones.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["header-switcher"], "milestone": "aga-Navbar", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["nav-desktop", "nav-no-project", "nav-desktop-collapsed", "nav-mobile"]}, {"key": "search-layout", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Header: centre the global search, own row on phones", "description": "<p>With the project switcher in the header, the search and the switcher no longer both fit on one phone row. On desktop the search should sit in the centre of the header. The attached screens are a guide to layout and content only; the design system and the real components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>Desktop (768px and up): centre <code>div.global-search</code> (<code>components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs</code>) in the navbar, about 420px wide, without overlapping the switcher or the right-hand menu at narrower desktop widths.</li><li>Below 768px: the search moves to its own full-width row under the switcher, New, bell and avatar row. That row has the hamburger, the switcher (short code), a compact New (<code>fa-plus</code>) and the bell. The content and the opened sidebar start below the taller header.</li><li>The search keeps its behaviour (<code>AppUi::Select</code> issue search, <code>search</code> task).</li><li>Styles go in <code>styles/modules/header.scss</code> (media queries at the Bootstrap xs breakpoint).</li><li>Test: <code>tests/integration/components/app-layouts/application-header-test.js</code> (the search is still rendered and works).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on desktop the search is centred in the header. On a 390px wide phone the header has the action row plus a full-width search row, with nothing cramped or clipped.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> hiding the logo row on phones, and changing what the search finds.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["header-switcher"], "milestone": "aga-Navbar", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["nav-desktop", "nav-mobile"]}, {"key": "header-presence", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Header: online status on the avatar and in the profile menu, remove the sidebar user panel", "description": "<p>The sidebar repeats the user's picture and name from the header, only to show a static \\"Online\\" status. Move the status into the header and drop the sidebar user panel. Presence stays fixed (always Online) for now. The attached screens are a guide to layout and content only; the design system and the real components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>In <code>components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs</code>, the user menu keeps the real profile picture (<code>AppUi::Avatar</code> <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code>) with a small green status dot at its bottom-right. The picture and name are vertically centred in the navbar.</li><li>In the profile dropdown, the large avatar gets the same dot. Add a row under <code>li.user-header</code>: green dot, <strong>Online</strong>, and a muted \\"Visible to your team\\" on the right, above Profile / Sign out.</li><li>Remove the <code>.user-panel</code> block (<code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.hbs</code> lines 2-12). Keep the <code>initialize-sidebar</code> modifier on an element that stays in the sidebar.</li><li>Colours: the success green from <code>variables.scss</code>. Styles go in <code>styles/modules/header.scss</code>. Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> (reuse <code>views.app.online</code>).</li><li>Tests: <code>application-header-test.js</code> (dot plus status row) and <code>nav-bar-test.js</code> / <code>application-sidebar-test.js</code> (no user panel).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the header avatar shows the profile picture with a green dot, the profile menu shows the Online row, and the sidebar starts with the Workspace group.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> real presence (online, away, offline from Hermes).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["nav-groups", "search-layout"], "milestone": "aga-Navbar", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["nav-desktop", "nav-mobile"]}, {"key": "mobile-close", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Sidebar: close the menu after navigation on phones", "description": "<p>On phones, the sidebar opened with the hamburger stays open after you pick a page, so it has to be closed by hand. Close it automatically, on phones only. The attached screen is a guide to layout and content only.</p><ul><li>On every route change (router service <code>routeDidChange</code>), when the viewport is below 768px and <code>body</code> has <code>sidebar-open</code>, remove it. Desktop expand/collapse and the persisted <code>sidebar-collapsed</code> preference (<code>modifiers/initialize-sidebar.js</code>) stay unchanged.</li><li>While the menu is open on a phone, dim the page under it. Tapping the dimmed page closes the menu, the same way AdminLTE's content click does.</li><li>Clean up the listener on teardown. Use no new jQuery; native listeners and the router service only.</li><li>Test: an integration or acceptance test that opens the sidebar at phone width, navigates, and asserts it closed, plus a desktop case where nothing changes.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a phone, tapping any menu item navigates and closes the menu, and tapping outside closes it too. On desktop the sidebar state never changes on navigation.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> swipe gestures.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Navbar", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["nav-mobile"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 09:52:02	2026-11-17 09:57:30	f
34f26db06af7-29da-7359-68bb3943fd34	44c783b46af7-b6c3-7359-e3d9f0af5900	2	{"summary": "One Prometheus issue: show each milestone's issue count on its task board tab, taken from the milestone.issues the board already loads and keeps in sync, so it updates when issues are created, moved (including drag onto a tab) or deleted. No API change.", "issues": [{"key": "tab-issue-count", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task board: show issue count on each milestone tab", "description": "<p>The task board's milestone tabs show only the type and name, so users must open each tab to see how much work it holds. Add the issue count to every tab, backlog included.</p><ul><li>In <code>app/components/app-ui/task-board.hbs</code> (the <code>ul.milestone-tabs</code> loop), render <code>milestone.issues.length</code> after the milestone name as an AdminLTE <code>label</code> (per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>), with a <code>data-milestone-issue-count</code> attribute and a translated title/tooltip such as \\"12 issues\\" (new key in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>).</li><li>Use the same <code>milestone.issues</code> array as the milestone header's \\"x/y issues\\" (<code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code>). <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> already keeps it in sync on create, move between milestones (including drop on a tab via <code>modifiers/initialize-sortable.js</code>) and delete, so the count must update without a reload.</li><li>If a style is needed (spacing next to the name, contrast on the active tab), add it under <code>.milestone-tabs</code> in <code>app/styles/modules/board.scss</code>. Use palette colours only and keep square edges. The label must not break the tab drop zones (<code>.drop-zone-area</code>).</li><li>When a board filter is active, the count reflects the issues loaded on the board, consistent with the lane counts.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Every milestone tab, including the backlog, shows its issue count. A milestone with no issues shows 0.</li><li>Creating an issue in a milestone, dragging an issue onto another milestone's tab or between milestones, and deleting an issue update the affected tab counts right away.</li><li>Integration test in <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/task-board/layout-test.js</code> covering the counts, including 0 and a count change after an issue moves.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-status or open/closed counts on the tab, and server-side totals that ignore the active filter.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-v2", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-13 12:57:25	2026-11-13 12:58:21	f
f19a1c176af7-b1e2-90ec-b4398bff2c3c	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	5	{"summary": "Collaborative Docs, first slice plus the AI features, with no separate AI panel. Gaia stores each doc's Yjs state and its derived HTML and plain text in a new Doccontent resource (Doc.body is dropped), and enforces doc.update and the lock on writes. A Hocuspocus collab server in hermes/collab syncs the docs and saves them to Gaia. Prometheus gets a Tiptap editor whose schema includes suggestion marks (with a reason), real-time co-editing with offline recovery, and presence. For AI, Ares gets /docs/ask, /docs/complete and /docs/review; Gaia exposes them through a standard Docassist resource that checks access, rate-limits and logs who asked. Prometheus adds a Suggestions box with accept/reject, then always-on ghost text, an Ask AI floating menu on selections (results land as suggestions) and an AI Reviewer toolbar button (fixes as suggestions with reasons, other findings as notes), all on a shared doc-ai data layer.", "issues": [{"key": "doc-content-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Doccontent resource (Yjs state, HTML and plain text) and drop Doc.body", "description": "<p>Docs become real-time co-edited documents. A doc's content is a Yjs CRDT state kept live by a collab server and saved to Gaia. The content gets its own resource so that the frequent autosaves don't rewrite the doc metadata, aren't copied into the audit log (<code>auditBehavior</code> stores old and new values of every changed field) and never travel with list queries.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Doccontent</code> (table <code>doccontent</code>), following <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code> (exemplar gaia#264, the Doc resource): <code>docId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>projectId</code> varchar(36) required (the doc's project, for the ACL group), <code>state</code> text nullable (base64-encoded Yjs update), <code>html</code> text nullable, <code>plainText</code> text nullable, <code>byteSize</code> int, plus the standard id, dates, createdUser, modifiedUser and deleted fields. Behaviours: createdUser, modifiedUser, dateCreated, dateModified, softDelete. <strong>No auditBehavior.</strong></li><li>Relationships: <code>doc</code> hasOne Doc (docId); inverse <code>content</code> hasOne Doccontent on <code>Doc</code>.</li><li>Validation: one Doccontent per doc (a second create for the same <code>docId</code> fails validation); <code>docId</code> must be a doc in the same <code>projectId</code>.</li><li>Remove the <code>body</code> field from <code>Doc</code> metadata and its api-tester cases. Existing doc rows are test data only, so their body is dropped.</li><li>ACL metadata <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via projectId, permissions <code>doccontent.get/create/update/delete</code>. No permission seed SQL.</li><li>Model, empty controller, <code>core/config/models.php</code>, <code>core/config/routes.php</code>, <code>routes.v1.json</code>, backend api placeholders and regenerated outputs as in B.md. api-tester harness/seed rows plus acl.json (member with and without doccontent.*, non-member) and client.json cases (create, get by docId, update, duplicate docId rejected).</li><li><code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>: D-002 (the Yjs state in Doccontent is the master copy; <code>html</code> and <code>plainText</code> are derived copies for export, search and AI, written by the collab server and never edited directly; base64 in text because the REST API is JSON), D-003 (content is written with the connected user's own token, so Gaia ACL and modifiedUser stay authoritative; no service account), D-004 (one merged snapshot row per doc, no update log).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a project member with doccontent.* can create, read and update one content row per doc; non-members are denied; Doc has no body field; the regenerated docs and graph have no drift.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> version history, lock enforcement (separate issue), sharing, full-text indexes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "A standard new-resource bundle per B.md (metadata, model, controller, config, routes, api-tester cases) plus removing Doc.body and the decisions doc; splitting it would leave a half resource that breaks dev.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-write-guard", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: require doc.update for Doc/Doccontent writes and reject writes on locked docs", "description": "<p>The collab server and the UI rely on Gaia to refuse writes a user isn't allowed to make. The review of agaia-4488 (gaia#264) found that a project member with only <code>doc.get</code>/<code>doc.create</code> got 200 on <code>PATCH /api/v1/doc/{id}</code>, and that <code>Doc.locked</code> is stored but not enforced.</p><ul><li>Find why update was authorized without <code>doc.update</code> (check how RestController/ACL authorizes PATCH for project-group resources, and whether other resources are affected) and fix it at the root. If the cause is in shared ACL code, fix it there and add denial cases for one other resource too.</li><li>Enforce <code>locked</code>: while a doc is locked, updates to its <code>Doccontent</code> are rejected (403 or a validation error, following the layering in the Design section). Only the doc's owner (<code>ownerId</code>) or a user with the project admin role may change <code>locked</code>, like the wiki lock today.</li><li>api-tester acl.json cases: Doc update and delete denied without doc.update/doc.delete; Doccontent update denied without doccontent.update; Doccontent update rejected on a locked doc; lock/unlock by the owner allowed, by another editor denied.</li><li>Record the lock rule as a decision in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the new denial cases pass and the existing Doc cases still pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-doc sharing roles, ownerId validation against project members.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-content-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "collab-server", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Docs collab server: self-contained collab/ package (Hocuspocus) with Gaia auth and Doccontent persistence", "description": "<p>Projects4Me Docs need Google-Docs-style co-editing. Each doc is a Yjs CRDT document that must be held in memory, synced between browsers and saved to Gaia. The relay can't do this (D-001 locked stateless relay, D-002 browsers never publish), so a collab server is added to this repo as a <strong>self-contained package in <code>collab/</code></strong>: its own process, port and container, sharing no code or dependencies with the relay, so it can later move to its own repo by moving the folder.</p><ul><li><strong>Isolation:</strong> its own <code>collab/package.json</code> (dependencies <code>@hocuspocus/server</code>, <code>yjs</code>, <code>@tiptap/html</code> and the Tiptap extensions below, approved for this module; pick versions that run on Node 18, Hermes' runtime), its own entrypoint <code>collab/server.js</code>, its own Dockerfile and docker-compose service. No imports from the relay's <code>src/</code> and no changes to relay code: its own small Gaia client module, modelled on <code>src/auth/gaia-session.js</code>.</li><li><strong>ADR D-016</strong> in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>: the collab server lives in <code>collab/</code> as a separate process; it holds Yjs documents and awareness in memory only and persists only through Gaia; the relay rules D-001 to D-015 are unchanged. It moves to its own repo when it takes on agents or export, or when its releases start to clash with the relay's.</li><li><code>CLAUDE.md</code>: scope the rule \\"Hermes stays a locked relay: no domain logic, no storage\\" to the relay (<code>src/</code>), and add a short <code>collab/</code> section (what it may do, its own package.json, no imports across the two).</li><li>Root test script also runs <code>collab/</code> tests, so the existing hermes test command covers both.</li><li>Document name contract: <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>. The client sends the user's Gaia OAuth access token as the Hocuspocus token. Never log tokens or document content.</li><li>onAuthenticate: call Gaia <code>GET /api/v1/user/me</code> with the token. Reject without <code>doc.get</code> in <code>aclPermissions</code>, then <code>GET /api/v1/doc/&lt;id&gt;</code> with the same token (reject on 403/404). The connection is read-only when the user lacks <code>doc.update</code> or the doc is <code>locked</code>.</li><li>onLoadDocument: load the Doccontent for the doc (<code>GET /api/v1/doccontent</code> filtered by docId) and apply the base64 <code>state</code>; start empty if there is none.</li><li>onStoreDocument (debounce about 2 s, max 10 s): encode the state and create or PATCH the Doccontent <code>state</code> and <code>byteSize</code>. After about 30 s without changes and on the last disconnect, also write <code>html</code> (generated from the Yjs fragment) and <code>plainText</code>. Use the token of a connected user who has write access.</li><li><strong>Schema</strong> in <code>collab/schema.js</code>, matching the Prometheus editor: StarterKit, Underline, Link, Table/TableRow/TableHeader/TableCell, TaskList/TaskItem, and two marks <code>suggestionInsert</code> / <code>suggestionDelete</code> (attrs <code>id</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>authorId</code>, <code>actedFor</code>, <code>requestId</code>, <code>reason</code>, <code>createdAt</code>; rendered as <code>&lt;ins data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;del data-suggestion-id&gt;</code>). Document it in <code>collab/README.md</code> with the env config (<code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>COLLAB_PORT</code>) and how to run it.</li><li>Unit tests with a stubbed Gaia: rejected token, missing doc.get, read-only for no doc.update and for locked, load applies stored state, store creates then updates the content, html/plainText written on idle and on last disconnect.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two clients editing <code>doc:&lt;id&gt;</code> converge; after a restart the content reloads from Gaia; unauthorized users can't connect; read-only users can't change the document; the relay's tests and image are unchanged apart from the test script.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> agents as server-side peers, version snapshots, comments, scaling beyond one instance.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-content-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "A new self-contained service package: entrypoint, auth, Gaia client/persistence and schema modules, its package.json, Dockerfile and compose service, README, ADR, CLAUDE.md, root test script and two test files. Auth and persistence can't ship apart, because the server is unusable without both.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-editor", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Tiptap editor component with toolbar, tables, checklists, outline and suggestion marks", "description": "<p>The Docs module needs a structured rich-text editor that can co-edit through Yjs. Toast UI can't, so Docs uses Tiptap (open-source packages only). This issue builds the editor as a standalone component. Real-time wiring and suggestion behaviour come in later issues.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>@tiptap/core</code>, <code>@tiptap/starter-kit</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-underline</code>, <code>-link</code>, <code>-table</code>, <code>-table-row</code>, <code>-table-header</code>, <code>-table-cell</code>, <code>-task-list</code>, <code>-task-item</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>utils/docs/schema.js</code>: the single list of extensions, plus two marks <code>suggestionInsert</code> and <code>suggestionDelete</code> (attrs <code>id</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>authorId</code>, <code>actedFor</code>, <code>requestId</code>, <code>reason</code>, <code>createdAt</code>; rendered as <code>&lt;ins data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;del data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> with a <code>doc-suggestion</code> class). The collab server builds the stored HTML from the same list (<code>hermes/collab/schema.js</code>), so a change here needs the same change there.</li><li><code>Docs::Editor</code> (<code>components/docs/editor.{js,hbs}</code>): mounts Tiptap on an element. Args <code>@content</code> (initial HTML), <code>@editable</code>, <code>@extensions</code> (extra extensions added to the schema list), <code>@onReady(editor)</code>. Destroys the editor on teardown. No persistence.</li><li><code>Docs::Toolbar</code>: bold, italic, underline, strike, H1 to H3, bullet and ordered list, checklist, blockquote, code block, link, insert table and add/remove rows and columns. Buttons are <code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code> with Font Awesome 4 icons, <code>aria-pressed</code> for active marks, and the toolbar is hidden when not editable. It yields a slot for extra button groups.</li><li><code>Docs::Outline</code>: a <code>col-md-4</code> side box listing the document's headings; clicking or pressing Enter scrolls to the heading.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code> (square edges, colours from <code>variables.scss</code> only), including the suggestion marks (inserted text underlined, deleted text struck through, in existing colours). Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Integration tests: renders the content, a toolbar action applies a mark, read-only hides the toolbar and blocks typing, the outline lists headings and scrolls, suggestion marks render with their attributes.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the component renders and edits formatted content, tables and checklists, renders suggestion marks, and follows <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> saving, real-time collaboration, accepting/rejecting suggestions, images and attachments, comments.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Editor, toolbar and outline components (js+hbs each), the schema module, styles, translations and tests. The toolbar and outline are small and only make sense with the editor they drive.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-collab-client", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: real-time co-editing on the doc page with autosave status and offline recovery", "description": "<p>Connects the Docs editor to the collab server (<code>hermes/collab</code>), so several people edit one doc live and changes save themselves with no Save button.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>yjs</code>, <code>@hocuspocus/provider</code>, <code>y-indexeddb</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>config/environment.js</code>: <code>ENV.docs.collabUrl</code> (no secrets).</li><li><code>services/doc-collab.js</code>: <code>open(docId)</code> creates a Y.Doc, an <code>IndexeddbPersistence</code> for offline recovery and a <code>HocuspocusProvider</code> (name <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>, token = the session's current access token, refreshed through <code>services/session.js</code> before a reconnect). Exposes tracked <code>status</code> (connecting, saving, saved, offline) and <code>readOnly</code> (from the server). <code>close()</code> destroys both. One responsibility: the connection; no UI.</li><li>Doc page from aprom-4490 (<code>app.project.doc.page</code>): renders <code>Docs::Editor</code> with the Collaboration extension bound to the Y.Doc. Editable only when <code>acl</code> allows doc.update, the doc isn't locked and the server didn't mark the connection read-only. Opens on route enter and closes on exit. A new doc starts empty.</li><li><code>Docs::SaveStatus</code> in the record box header: \\"Saving…\\", \\"All changes saved\\", \\"Offline – changes are kept on this device\\".</li><li>Tests: the service with a stubbed provider (status transitions, readOnly, close on exit) and an acceptance test of the page in read-only and editable modes with the service stubbed (Mirage has no websocket).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two browsers on the same doc see each other's edits live; reloading keeps the content; edits made offline sync after reconnecting; a locked doc, or a user without doc.update, gets a read-only editor.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence and cursors (next issue), version history.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-editor", "collab-server", "aprom-4489", "aprom-4490"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-presence", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: who's in the doc, live cursors and selections, and 'is typing'", "description": "<p>Collaborators should see who else is in a doc and where they are working, like Google Docs. This uses the collab server's awareness channel from <code>services/doc-collab.js</code>; nothing is stored.</p><ul><li>Dependency: <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration-cursor</code> (approved for this module).</li><li>Awareness state: <code>{ user: { id, name, color }, typing: boolean }</code>. Pick the colour deterministically from the user id out of a fixed palette of existing <code>variables.scss</code> colours; no new colours.</li><li>Live cursors and selections in the editor, each with a name label in the user's colour (styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>).</li><li>A \\"who's in the doc\\" avatar stack in the record box header, reusing the existing avatar markup (<code>components/project/member-avatars.hbs</code> pattern, <code>userimage/get</code>). One entry per user even with several tabs, with a tooltip of the name.</li><li>\\"<em>Name</em> is typing…\\": set <code>typing</code> on local input and clear it after about 2 s of no input; show it under the avatars.</li><li>Tests: the avatar stack de-duplicates users and hides the current user; the typing flag clears after the timeout; the colour is stable for an id.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with two users in a doc each sees the other's avatar, cursor, selection and typing indicator, and these disappear when the other leaves.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence on the All Docs list, follow-a-user mode.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-docs", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Docs AI endpoints: /docs/ask, /docs/complete and /docs/review", "description": "<p>Projects4Me Docs get AI help: answer a writer's request about selected text, complete the sentence being written, and review a whole document. Gaia (<code>core/services/LLM.php</code>) stays the only caller; it sends the text and returns the result to the editor.</p><ul><li>New router <code>routers/docs.py</code> (prefix <code>/docs</code>) with Pydantic request/response models, one service per use case in <code>services/</code>, prompts kept out of the router. Register it in <code>main.py</code>.</li><li><code>POST /docs/ask</code>: request <code>{instruction: str (required, max 1000), selectionHtml: str (max 8000), context: {title, headingPath: [str], before: str (max 2000), after: str (max 500)}}</code>. Response <code>{html: str}</code>: the replacement for the selection, using only the tags p, h1-h3, ul, ol, li, strong, em, u, s, a, blockquote, code, pre.</li><li><code>POST /docs/complete</code>: request <code>{title, headingPath, before (max 2000), after (max 500)}</code>. Response <code>{text: str}</code>: plain text continuing the sentence, at most about 200 characters, possibly empty. Uses a fast model from env (<code>ARES_DOCS_COMPLETE_MODEL</code>, default <code>claude-haiku-4-5-20251001</code>) with a low max-token limit, since it is called often.</li><li><code>POST /docs/review</code>: request <code>{title, text (max 60000, plain text with headings on their own lines)}</code>. Response <code>{findings: [{quote: str, category: unclear|open_question|inconsistency|missing|wording, message: str, replacement?: str}]}</code>, at most 20. <code>replacement</code> is the corrected text for <code>quote</code> when there is a concrete fix; without it the finding is a note. Every <code>quote</code> must be an exact substring of <code>text</code>: the service drops findings whose quote isn't found.</li><li>Model names and token limits come from env; extend the adapter so a service can pick its model.</li><li>Document text and the writer's instruction are untrusted input: prompts treat the document as content, never as instructions.</li><li>Errors: invalid input gives 422; a provider failure gives a clear error status and message, never empty or fake output.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter (no live calls): each endpoint's request validation and response shape, review drops non-matching quotes, complete truncates long output.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the three endpoints return the documented shapes with the fake adapter; no prompt or provider logic in the router.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming, agent loops, storing anything.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Three endpoints that share one router, one set of request/response models and one adapter change; each service and its test is small.", "screens": []}, {"key": "docassist-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Docassist resource for AI help (ask, complete, review) via Ares", "description": "<p>The Docs editor asks for AI help: a writer's request about selected text, sentence completion while writing, and a document review. Gaia owns access and must record who asked, so each request is a <code>Docassist</code> record created through standard CRUD. The create calls Ares and returns the result in the response.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Docassist</code> (table <code>docassist</code>) per <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code>: <code>docId</code>, <code>projectId</code> (varchar(36), required), <code>kind</code> (ask|complete|review), <code>instruction</code> varchar(1000) nullable (required for ask), <code>status</code> (done|failed), <code>result</code> text nullable (ask: HTML; review: JSON findings; complete: not stored), <code>inputChars</code> and <code>outputChars</code> int, standard fields and behaviours (no audit). The person who asked is <code>createdUser</code> (the <code>actedFor</code> of the resulting suggestions).</li><li>Request-only inputs, never stored: <code>selectionHtml</code>, <code>context</code> {title, headingPath, before, after}, <code>text</code> (review). Decide how the framework accepts non-persisted create inputs (e.g. a component on create) and record it in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>.</li><li>On create: check the doc exists in <code>projectId</code> and the caller has <code>doc.update</code> on it; enforce input limits (instruction 1000, selection 8000, before 2000, after 500, text 60000 chars); rate-limit per user (complete 40/min, ask and review 10/min, counted from the user's recent Docassist rows) with 429; call Ares through <code>core/services/LLM.php</code> (new methods for <code>/docs/ask</code>, <code>/docs/complete</code>, <code>/docs/review</code>); save the row with <code>status</code> and return the result in the response (<code>result</code> for ask and review; a transient <code>completion</code> field for complete).</li><li>A failed Ares call saves <code>status = failed</code> and returns an error status with a message, never an empty success.</li><li>ACL metadata <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via projectId; permissions <code>docassist.create/get</code> (get is used to load the latest review of a doc). No permission seed SQL.</li><li>api-tester with a stubbed LLM service in the test environment (no live Ares): acl cases (member with and without docassist.create, without doc.update, non-member) and client cases (each kind returns its shape, ask without instruction is rejected, input over the limit is rejected, rate limit returns 429, Ares failure gives an error and a failed row, completion text is not stored).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the three kinds work end to end with the stub; only users who can edit the doc can ask; every request leaves a row with who, when, kind and status.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming, cost accounting in money, agents.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ares-docs", "doc-content-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 14, "sizeReason": "A new-resource bundle per B.md plus the LLM service methods, the request-only input handling, the rate limit and a test stub for the LLM service; the AI call and the resource that carries it can't ship apart.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-suggestions", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: apply, accept and reject suggestions with a Suggestions box", "description": "<p>Changes made by AI in a doc never land directly: they arrive as suggestions that people accept or reject, each showing who it was made for and, when given, why. The editor schema already has the <code>suggestionInsert</code>/<code>suggestionDelete</code> marks; this issue adds the behaviour and the Suggestions box, the single place where suggestions are reviewed. Suggesting mode for people's own typing is not part of this issue.</p><ul><li><code>utils/docs/suggestions.js</code>: <code>proposeReplacement(editor, from, to, html, attrs)</code> marks the old range with <code>suggestionDelete</code> and inserts the new content with <code>suggestionInsert</code>, both with the same <code>id</code>; <code>proposeInsertion</code>; <code>accept(id)</code> (removes inserted marks, deletes text marked deleted); <code>reject(id)</code> (deletes inserted text, removes deleted marks); <code>acceptAll</code>/<code>rejectAll(requestId)</code>; <code>list(editor)</code> groups pending suggestions by <code>requestId</code>. All as single editor transactions, so they sync and undo like normal edits.</li><li><code>Docs::SuggestionsBox</code>: a <code>box-info</code> side box on the doc page (see the ai-reviewer screen) listing pending suggestions grouped by request, with Accept/Reject per suggestion and Accept all/Reject all per group. The group header shows the source name (\\"Ask AI\\" or \\"AI Reviewer\\", from <code>source</code>) with <code>Agent::Badge</code> and the \\"for {name}\\" sponsor text (as <code>components/agent/user-tag.hbs</code> does) and the time. Each entry shows its <code>reason</code> when present. It yields a slot per group for extra entries (used for reviewer notes). Empty state: \\"No suggestions in this doc\\".</li><li>Clicking an entry scrolls to and selects the suggestion; clicking a suggestion in the text shows a small Accept/Reject popover (keyboard reachable).</li><li>Buttons only for users who can edit; others see the suggestions read-only.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>, strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the helpers (replacement then accept and reject give the expected document; acceptAll per request) and an integration test of the box (grouping, reason, sponsor text, read-only hides buttons, empty state).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a suggestion added through the helper shows inline and in the box; accept and reject change the document as expected for everyone in the doc.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> Suggesting mode for people's typing, comments on suggestions, notifications.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ai-reviewer"]}, {"key": "doc-ai-data", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: docassist model, adapter, Mirage and a doc-ai service", "description": "<p>The Docs AI features (ghost text, Ask AI, AI Reviewer) all call Gaia's <code>Docassist</code> resource. This issue adds the shared data layer so each feature only builds its UI.</p><ul><li>Ember Data <code>docassist</code> model (docId, projectId, kind, instruction, status, result, inputChars, outputChars, createdUser, dateCreated, plus the request-only <code>selectionHtml</code>, <code>context</code>, <code>text</code>), adapter and serializer following the existing ones; request-only attributes are sent on create and never read back.</li><li><code>services/doc-ai.js</code>: <code>ask(doc, instruction, selectionHtml, context)</code>, <code>complete(doc, context)</code>, <code>review(doc, text)</code>, <code>latestReview(doc)</code>. Latest request wins per kind (a newer call makes an older pending result be ignored); errors are thrown with Gaia's message, and 429 becomes a \\"too many requests, try again shortly\\" error.</li><li>Mirage: a <code>docassist</code> factory and a POST handler that returns canned results per kind (and a 429 scenario).</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the service (latest wins, error mapping, review result parsed from JSON).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the service returns parsed results from Mirage for each kind and surfaces errors.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["docassist-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-ask-ai", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Ask AI floating menu on selected text, result inserted as a suggestion", "description": "<p>When a writer selects text, a small floating menu appears with an <strong>Ask AI</strong> option. They type what they want (\\"make this clearer\\", \\"turn into a checklist\\") and the answer replaces the selection as a suggestion that needs approval. There is no separate AI panel and no preview step.</p><ul><li>Dependency: <code>@tiptap/extension-bubble-menu</code> (open source, approved for this module).</li><li><code>Docs::SelectionMenu</code>: a bubble menu shown for a non-empty text selection, only to users who can edit. It holds bold, italic, link and an <strong>Ask AI</strong> button (<code>fa-magic</code>). Ask AI turns the menu into a request field (<code>FormFields::FieldText</code> with label \\"Ask AI\\" and help text \\"The answer is added as a suggestion. Enter to send, Esc to close.\\"). Enter sends (ignored during IME composition), Esc closes and returns focus to the editor.</li><li>On send: call <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>ask()</code> with the instruction, the selection as HTML and context (doc title, heading path, up to 2000 characters before and 500 after). Show <code>AppUi::Loader</code> in the menu and disable the field while waiting.</li><li>On success: replace the original range with <code>proposeReplacement</code> from <code>utils/docs/suggestions.js</code> (<code>source: ask</code>, <code>actedFor</code> = current user, <code>requestId</code> = the Docassist id), close the menu and highlight the new group in the Suggestions box. If the selected text changed while waiting, don't insert; show \\"The text changed, try again\\" in the menu.</li><li>Errors (including 429) show in the menu with a retry; one request at a time.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>, styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>.</li><li>Integration test with Mirage: select text, menu shows Ask AI, send a request, a suggestion with the right attrs appears; error path; read-only users get no Ask AI.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> matches the ask-ai screen; nothing becomes final until someone accepts the suggestion.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> preset actions, streaming, Ask AI without a selection.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-ai-data", "doc-suggestions"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ask-ai"]}, {"key": "doc-ai-complete", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: always-on ghost-text AI completion while writing (Tab to accept)", "description": "<p>While writing, AI suggests how the sentence continues, shown right away as grey text after the cursor. It is always on for people who can edit. Accepting it is the writer's own choice, so accepted text is a normal edit, not a suggestion.</p><ul><li>A Tiptap extension <code>utils/docs/ghost-text.js</code>, added to the doc page editor for users who can edit: after about 500 ms without typing, with the cursor at the end of a non-empty text block and no selection, ask <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>complete()</code> with the title, heading path, up to 2000 characters before and 500 after. Show the result as a widget decoration (local only, not synced, not saved).</li><li>Tab inserts the text at the cursor; Esc, any typing, moving the cursor or losing focus dismisses it. A newer request makes older responses be ignored, and a pending request is dropped when the writer types again. Ignore while composing (IME), in read-only mode and while the Ask AI menu is open.</li><li>On 429 or errors, show nothing and back off for 30 s; no toasts.</li><li>Ghost text style in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code> (muted colour from <code>variables.scss</code>); a short hint \\"Tab to accept\\" comes from <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the extension (debounce, shown only at block end, Tab inserts, typing dismisses, stale response ignored, back-off after an error) and a page test that read-only users get no ghost text.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> pausing at the end of a paragraph shows a completion that Tab inserts; typing dismisses it; read-only users never trigger requests.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> multi-paragraph completions, completions in the middle of text, a per-user on/off setting.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-ai-data", "doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ask-ai"]}, {"key": "doc-ai-review", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: AI Reviewer toolbar button with fixes as suggestions and notes", "description": "<p>An <strong>AI Reviewer</strong> button in the editor toolbar reviews the whole document: unclear wording, open questions, inconsistencies and missing parts. Concrete fixes arrive as suggestions with their reason; findings without a fix show as notes. Everything is reviewed in the Suggestions box; there is no separate AI panel.</p><ul><li>Toolbar button (<code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code>, <code>fa-magic</code>, \\"AI Reviewer\\") in the toolbar's extra slot, for users who can edit. While running it shows \\"Reviewing…\\" with <code>aria-busy</code> and is disabled; afterwards it shows the number of findings as a <code>label</code>.</li><li>On click: send the doc's plain text (headings on their own lines) through <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>review()</code>.</li><li>For each finding with a <code>replacement</code>: find its <code>quote</code> in the current document. If it occurs exactly once and doesn't overlap another fix, apply <code>proposeReplacement</code> with <code>source: review</code>, <code>actedFor</code> = current user, <code>requestId</code> = the Docassist id and <code>reason</code> = the category and message. Otherwise treat it as a note, so a fix never lands in the wrong place.</li><li>Notes (findings without a replacement, or not placeable) appear in the Suggestions box group for this review through the box's group slot: category <code>label</code>, message, and Dismiss. Clicking a note selects its quote if it is still in the doc, otherwise it shows \\"Text changed since the review\\". Dismiss hides it for this user (local only).</li><li>On page load, notes of the doc's latest review (<code>latestReview</code>) are shown for everyone who opens the doc.</li><li>Errors (including 429) show next to the button with a retry. Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>, styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>.</li><li>Integration tests with Mirage: fixes become suggestions with reasons, an ambiguous quote becomes a note, notes render and select their text, the latest review's notes load on open, read-only users get no button.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> matches the ai-reviewer screen; fixes need approval in the Suggestions box and are attributed to the person who ran the review.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> turning notes into comments, scheduled or automatic reviews.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-ai-data", "doc-suggestions"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ai-reviewer"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-13 13:17:37	2026-11-13 13:17:37	f
54dfde486af7-e1c1-cc28-88b3d893e724	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	6	{"summary": "Collaborative Docs: real-time co-editing with presence, plus AI ghost text, Ask AI on a selection and an AI Reviewer, all live for everyone in the doc. Gaia stores each doc's Yjs state and its derived HTML and plain text in a new Doccontent resource (Doc.body is dropped), enforces doc.update and the lock, publishes doc.created/updated/deleted through Hermes and tells the collab server when a doc is locked or deleted. A Hocuspocus collab server in hermes/collab syncs content, suggestions, review notes and presence over one WebSocket, saves to Gaia, and switches open editors to read-only or closes them when Gaia says access changed; the Hermes relay only gains the doc.* event names. Prometheus gets a Tiptap editor with suggestion marks, the collab client with offline recovery, live doc metadata, and presence including an AI busy flag. For AI, Ares gets /docs/ask, /docs/complete and /docs/review behind a standard Gaia Docassist resource (access, rate limit, log of who asked); Prometheus adds the Suggestions box, then always-on ghost text, the Ask AI floating menu and the AI Reviewer, whose notes are stored in the shared Y.Doc.", "issues": [{"key": "doc-content-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Doccontent resource (Yjs state, HTML and plain text) and drop Doc.body", "description": "<p>Docs become real-time co-edited documents. A doc's content is a Yjs CRDT state kept live by a collab server and saved to Gaia. The content gets its own resource so that the frequent autosaves don't rewrite the doc metadata, aren't copied into the audit log (<code>auditBehavior</code> stores old and new values of every changed field) and never travel with list queries.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Doccontent</code> (table <code>doccontent</code>), following <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code> (exemplar gaia#264, the Doc resource): <code>docId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>projectId</code> varchar(36) required (the doc's project, for the ACL group), <code>state</code> text nullable (base64-encoded Yjs update), <code>html</code> text nullable, <code>plainText</code> text nullable, <code>byteSize</code> int, plus the standard id, dates, createdUser, modifiedUser and deleted fields. Behaviours: createdUser, modifiedUser, dateCreated, dateModified, softDelete. <strong>No auditBehavior.</strong></li><li>Relationships: <code>doc</code> hasOne Doc (docId); inverse <code>content</code> hasOne Doccontent on <code>Doc</code>.</li><li>Validation: one Doccontent per doc (a second create for the same <code>docId</code> fails validation); <code>docId</code> must be a doc in the same <code>projectId</code>.</li><li>Remove the <code>body</code> field from <code>Doc</code> metadata and its api-tester cases. Existing doc rows are test data only, so their body is dropped.</li><li>ACL metadata <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via projectId, permissions <code>doccontent.get/create/update/delete</code>. No permission seed SQL.</li><li>Model, empty controller, <code>core/config/models.php</code>, <code>core/config/routes.php</code>, <code>routes.v1.json</code>, backend api placeholders and regenerated outputs as in B.md. api-tester harness/seed rows plus acl.json (member with and without doccontent.*, non-member) and client.json cases (create, get by docId, update, duplicate docId rejected).</li><li><code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>: D-002 (the Yjs state in Doccontent is the master copy; <code>html</code> and <code>plainText</code> are derived copies for export, search and AI, written by the collab server and never edited directly; base64 in text because the REST API is JSON), D-003 (content is written with the connected user's own token, so Gaia ACL and modifiedUser stay authoritative; no service account), D-004 (one merged snapshot row per doc, no update log).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a project member with doccontent.* can create, read and update one content row per doc; non-members are denied; Doc has no body field; the regenerated docs and graph have no drift.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> version history, lock enforcement (separate issue), sharing, full-text search.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "A standard new-resource bundle per B.md (metadata, model, controller, config, routes, api-tester cases) plus removing Doc.body and the decisions doc; splitting it would leave a half resource that breaks dev.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-write-guard", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: require doc.update for Doc/Doccontent writes and reject writes on locked docs", "description": "<p>The collab server and the UI rely on Gaia to refuse writes a user isn't allowed to make. The review of agaia-4488 (gaia#264) found that a project member with only <code>doc.get</code>/<code>doc.create</code> got 200 on <code>PATCH /api/v1/doc/{id}</code>, and that <code>Doc.locked</code> is stored but not enforced.</p><ul><li>Find why update was authorized without <code>doc.update</code> (check how RestController/ACL authorizes PATCH for project-group resources, and whether other resources are affected) and fix it at the root. If the cause is in shared ACL code, fix it there and add denial cases for one other resource too.</li><li>Enforce <code>locked</code>: while a doc is locked, updates to its <code>Doccontent</code> are rejected (403 or a validation error, following the layering in the Design section). Only the doc's owner (<code>ownerId</code>) or a user with the project admin role may change <code>locked</code>, like the wiki lock today.</li><li>api-tester acl.json cases: Doc update and delete denied without doc.update/doc.delete; Doccontent update denied without doccontent.update; Doccontent update rejected on a locked doc; lock/unlock by the owner allowed, by another editor denied.</li><li>Record the lock rule as a decision in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the new denial cases pass and the existing Doc cases still pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-doc sharing roles, ownerId validation against project members.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-content-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "collab-server", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Docs collab server: self-contained collab/ package (Hocuspocus) with Gaia auth and Doccontent persistence", "description": "<p>Projects4Me Docs need Google-Docs-style co-editing. Each doc is a Yjs CRDT document that must be held in memory, synced between browsers and saved to Gaia. The relay can't do this (D-001 locked stateless relay, D-002 browsers never publish), so a collab server is added to this repo as a <strong>self-contained package in <code>collab/</code></strong>: its own process, port and container, sharing no code or dependencies with the relay, so it can later move to its own repo by moving the folder.</p><ul><li><strong>Isolation:</strong> its own <code>collab/package.json</code> (dependencies <code>@hocuspocus/server</code>, <code>yjs</code>, <code>@tiptap/html</code> and the Tiptap extensions below, approved for this module; pick versions that run on Node 18, Hermes' runtime), its own entrypoint <code>collab/server.js</code>, its own Dockerfile and docker-compose service. No imports from the relay's <code>src/</code> and no changes to relay code: its own small Gaia client module, modelled on <code>src/auth/gaia-session.js</code>.</li><li><strong>ADR D-016</strong> in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>: the collab server lives in <code>collab/</code> as a separate process; it holds Yjs documents and awareness in memory only and persists only through Gaia; the relay rules D-001 to D-015 are unchanged. It moves to its own repo when it takes on agents or export, or when its releases start to clash with the relay's.</li><li><code>CLAUDE.md</code>: scope the rule \\"Hermes stays a locked relay: no domain logic, no storage\\" to the relay (<code>src/</code>), and add a short <code>collab/</code> section (what it may do, its own package.json, no imports across the two).</li><li>Root test script also runs <code>collab/</code> tests, so the existing hermes test command covers both.</li><li>Document name contract: <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>. The client sends the user's Gaia OAuth access token as the Hocuspocus token. Never log tokens or document content.</li><li>onAuthenticate: call Gaia <code>GET /api/v1/user/me</code> with the token. Reject without <code>doc.get</code> in <code>aclPermissions</code>, then <code>GET /api/v1/doc/&lt;id&gt;</code> with the same token (reject on 403/404). The connection is read-only when the user lacks <code>doc.update</code> or the doc is <code>locked</code>; updates from read-only connections are dropped by the server.</li><li>onLoadDocument: load the Doccontent for the doc (<code>GET /api/v1/doccontent</code> filtered by docId) and apply the base64 <code>state</code>; start empty if there is none. Unload a doc from memory after it has been saved and nobody is connected.</li><li>onStoreDocument (debounce about 2 s, max 10 s): encode the state and create or PATCH the Doccontent <code>state</code> and <code>byteSize</code>. After about 30 s without changes and on the last disconnect, also write <code>html</code> and <code>plainText</code>, generated from the editor fragment only (other shared types in the Y.Doc, such as the review <code>notes</code> map, are saved with the state but not rendered). Use the token of a connected user who has write access; on 401, try another connected writer.</li><li><strong>Schema</strong> in <code>collab/schema.js</code>, matching the Prometheus editor: StarterKit, Underline, Link, Table/TableRow/TableHeader/TableCell, TaskList/TaskItem, and two marks <code>suggestionInsert</code> / <code>suggestionDelete</code> (attrs <code>id</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>authorId</code>, <code>actedFor</code>, <code>requestId</code>, <code>reason</code>, <code>createdAt</code>; rendered as <code>&lt;ins data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;del data-suggestion-id&gt;</code>). Document it in <code>collab/README.md</code> with the env config (<code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>COLLAB_PORT</code>) and how to run it.</li><li>Unit tests with a stubbed Gaia: rejected token, missing doc.get, read-only for no doc.update and for locked, load applies stored state, store creates then updates the content, html/plainText written on idle and on last disconnect.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two clients editing <code>doc:&lt;id&gt;</code> converge; after a restart the content reloads from Gaia; unauthorized users can't connect; read-only users can't change the document; the relay's tests and image are unchanged apart from the test script.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> access changes while connected (separate issue), agents as server-side peers, version snapshots, comments, scaling beyond one instance.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-content-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "A new self-contained service package: entrypoint, auth, Gaia client/persistence and schema modules, its package.json, Dockerfile and compose service, README, ADR, CLAUDE.md, root test script and two test files. Auth and persistence can't ship apart, because the server is unusable without both.", "screens": []}, {"key": "collab-access", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Docs collab server: internal access-change endpoint, client messages and write limits", "description": "<p>When a doc is locked or deleted, people who already have it open must switch to read-only or be closed at once. Otherwise their edits keep spreading to others in memory while Gaia refuses to save them. Gaia tells the collab server (<code>collab/</code>) through a server-to-server call; the collab server re-checks each connection with Gaia and informs the clients.</p><ul><li><code>POST /internal/docs/:docId/access</code> on the collab server's HTTP port, authenticated with a shared secret (<code>COLLAB_SECRET</code> env, header <code>X-Collab-Secret</code>, compared in constant time). Body <code>{reason: locked|unlocked|deleted|access}</code>. Returns 202. Rejects without the secret.</li><li>On a call: for every connection to <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>, re-check with Gaia using that connection's token (same checks as onAuthenticate). Switch it to read-only or back to editable, or close it when the doc is gone or access was lost.</li><li>Stateless messages to clients (JSON, documented in <code>collab/README.md</code> as the contract with Prometheus): <code>{type: 'access', readOnly: bool, reason}</code>, <code>{type: 'deleted'}</code>, <code>{type: 'unsaved', since: ISO date}</code> when saving to Gaia has failed for over 2 minutes (and <code>{type: 'saved'}</code> once it recovers). Retry failed saves with back-off.</li><li>Limits: maximum size per incoming Yjs update (env, default 512 KB) and a per-connection update rate limit; offending connections are closed with a reason. Check the WebSocket <code>Origin</code> against an allowed list from env.</li><li>Add an ADR entry next to D-016 for the internal endpoint and its secret.</li><li>Unit tests with a stubbed Gaia: missing or wrong secret rejected, lock switches connections to read-only and sends the message, unlock restores editing, delete closes connections, unsaved message after the save-failure threshold, oversized update rejected.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after the endpoint is called for a locked doc, open editors stop being able to change it within a second and are told why.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-doc sharing changes (later), multi-instance coordination.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["collab-server"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-doc-events", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Relay: allow doc.created, doc.updated and doc.deleted events", "description": "<p>Docs lists and open doc pages update live when a doc is created, renamed, locked or deleted. Gaia publishes these as domain events; the relay only needs to accept the names (D-003 allowlist).</p><ul><li>Add <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code> and <code>doc.deleted</code> to <code>src/contract/names.js</code>, matching Gaia's <code>EventNames.php</code>. Payloads follow the existing closed envelope (project-scoped, ids plus changed field names for <code>doc.updated</code>).</li><li>ADR entry in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code> for the new names, as the contract rules require.</li><li>Tests: the names are accepted by <code>/publish</code> and delivered to sockets with a matching intent; unknown <code>doc.*</code> names are still rejected.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a published <code>doc.updated</code> reaches a project member's socket registered for it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any doc content traffic (that goes through the collab server).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-live-events", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: publish doc.created/updated/deleted live events and notify the collab server on lock and delete", "description": "<p>Docs lists and open doc pages must update live when a doc is created, renamed, locked or deleted, and open editors must turn read-only as soon as a doc is locked. Gaia publishes doc events through Hermes and calls the collab server's internal access endpoint.</p><ul><li><code>DocLiveEventsComponent</code> in <code>app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/</code>, following <code>docs/generated/bundles/E.md</code> (precedent <code>UserAccessLiveEventsComponent</code>, <code>IdeaLiveEventsComponent</code>): publish <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code> (with the changed field names: title, locked, ownerId, parent and status as they exist) and <code>doc.deleted</code>, scoped to the doc's project. Add the names to <code>support/EventNames.php</code>; they must match <code>hermes/src/contract/names.js</code>, so this ships together with the Hermes allowlist change.</li><li>New <code>CollabNotifier</code> class (one class owns the collab server's URL, secret and transport, like <code>HermesPublisher</code>): <code>POST {COLLAB_URL}/internal/docs/{docId}/access</code> with header <code>X-Collab-Secret</code> and body <code>{reason: locked|unlocked|deleted}</code>. Called after a doc's <code>locked</code> changes and after a doc is deleted. Config via <code>getenv()</code> in <code>config/*.php</code>; never logged.</li><li>Side effects fail open: Hermes or the collab server being down must not fail the user's write; log the failure.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the component (right event and payload per change, no event for unchanged saves) and the notifier (sends on lock, unlock and delete; failures don't throw), with the transports stubbed.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> renaming, locking or deleting a doc publishes the matching event; locking or deleting calls the collab server; both failing leaves the write successful.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> events for Doccontent saves, sharing events.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-write-guard", "hermes-doc-events", "collab-access"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-editor", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Tiptap editor component with toolbar, tables, checklists, outline and suggestion marks", "description": "<p>The Docs module needs a structured rich-text editor that can co-edit through Yjs. Toast UI can't, so Docs uses Tiptap (open-source packages only). This issue builds the editor as a standalone component. Real-time wiring and suggestion behaviour come in later issues.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>@tiptap/core</code>, <code>@tiptap/starter-kit</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-underline</code>, <code>-link</code>, <code>-table</code>, <code>-table-row</code>, <code>-table-header</code>, <code>-table-cell</code>, <code>-task-list</code>, <code>-task-item</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>utils/docs/schema.js</code>: the single list of extensions, plus two marks <code>suggestionInsert</code> and <code>suggestionDelete</code> (attrs <code>id</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>authorId</code>, <code>actedFor</code>, <code>requestId</code>, <code>reason</code>, <code>createdAt</code>; rendered as <code>&lt;ins data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;del data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> with a <code>doc-suggestion</code> class). The collab server builds the stored HTML from the same list (<code>hermes/collab/schema.js</code>), so a change here needs the same change there.</li><li><code>Docs::Editor</code> (<code>components/docs/editor.{js,hbs}</code>): mounts Tiptap on an element. Args <code>@content</code> (initial HTML), <code>@editable</code>, <code>@extensions</code> (extra extensions added to the schema list), <code>@onReady(editor)</code>. Destroys the editor on teardown. No persistence.</li><li><code>Docs::Toolbar</code>: bold, italic, underline, strike, H1 to H3, bullet and ordered list, checklist, blockquote, code block, link, insert table and add/remove rows and columns. Buttons are <code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code> with Font Awesome 4 icons, <code>aria-pressed</code> for active marks, and the toolbar is hidden when not editable. It yields a slot for extra button groups.</li><li><code>Docs::Outline</code>: a <code>col-md-4</code> side box listing the document's headings; clicking or pressing Enter scrolls to the heading.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code> (square edges, colours from <code>variables.scss</code> only), including the suggestion marks (inserted text underlined, deleted text struck through, in existing colours). Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Integration tests: renders the content, a toolbar action applies a mark, read-only hides the toolbar and blocks typing, the outline lists headings and scrolls, suggestion marks render with their attributes.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the component renders and edits formatted content, tables and checklists, renders suggestion marks, and follows <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> saving, real-time collaboration, accepting/rejecting suggestions, images and attachments, comments.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Editor, toolbar and outline components (js+hbs each), the schema module, styles, translations and tests. The toolbar and outline are small and only make sense with the editor they drive.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-collab-client", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: real-time co-editing on the doc page with autosave status and offline recovery", "description": "<p>Connects the Docs editor to the collab server (<code>hermes/collab</code>), so several people edit one doc live and changes save themselves with no Save button.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>yjs</code>, <code>@hocuspocus/provider</code>, <code>y-indexeddb</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>config/environment.js</code>: <code>ENV.docs.collabUrl</code> (no secrets).</li><li><code>services/doc-collab.js</code>: <code>open(docId)</code> creates a Y.Doc, an <code>IndexeddbPersistence</code> for offline recovery and a <code>HocuspocusProvider</code> (name <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>, token = the session's current access token; refresh it through <code>services/session.js</code> and reconnect before it expires). Exposes the Y.Doc, the provider's awareness, tracked <code>status</code> (connecting, saving, saved, offline) and <code>readOnly</code> (from the server). <code>close()</code> destroys both. One responsibility: the connection; no UI.</li><li>Doc page from aprom-4490 (<code>app.project.doc.page</code>): renders <code>Docs::Editor</code> with the Collaboration extension bound to the Y.Doc. Editable only when <code>acl</code> allows doc.update, the doc isn't locked and the server didn't mark the connection read-only. Opens on route enter and closes on exit. A new doc starts empty.</li><li><code>Docs::SaveStatus</code> in the record box header: \\"Saving…\\", \\"All changes saved\\", \\"Offline – changes are kept on this device\\".</li><li>Tests: the service with a stubbed provider (status transitions, readOnly, close on exit) and an acceptance test of the page in read-only and editable modes with the service stubbed (Mirage has no websocket).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two browsers on the same doc see each other's edits live; reloading keeps the content; edits made offline sync after reconnecting; a locked doc, or a user without doc.update, gets a read-only editor.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence and cursors, live metadata and server messages (separate issues), version history.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-editor", "collab-server", "aprom-4489", "aprom-4490"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-live-client", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: live doc metadata on list and page, and collab server messages (locked, deleted, not saved)", "description": "<p>Everything about a doc should update live: a rename or lock shows at once in the All Docs list and on the open page, a deleted doc closes, and editors learn immediately when they can no longer edit or when their changes aren't reaching the server.</p><ul><li>Register for Hermes <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code> and <code>doc.deleted</code> with <code>hermes.register(owner, projectId, handlers)</code> from the controllers of the All Docs list (aprom-4491) and the doc page (aprom-4490), following <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/</code>; filter on the doc id on the page (precedent <code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>). The list reloads or updates the affected row; the page reloads the doc record (title, lock). Add the registrations to the live-updates registration table.</li><li>Handle the collab server's stateless messages in <code>services/doc-collab.js</code> (contract in <code>hermes/collab/README.md</code>): <code>access</code> switches the editor to read-only or back and shows a Messenger notice with the reason (\\"This doc was locked\\"); <code>deleted</code> closes the connection and goes to the All Docs list with a notice; <code>unsaved</code>/<code>saved</code> drive a \\"Not saved to server yet\\" state in <code>Docs::SaveStatus</code>.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: handlers update the list and page (Hermes stubbed), each message type changes the editor state and notice as expected.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with two browsers, renaming or locking in one updates the other's list and page without reload; locking turns the other's open editor read-only with a notice; deleting closes it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> live updates for sharing (later).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-collab-client", "doc-live-events", "aprom-4491"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-presence", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: who's in the doc, live cursors and selections, 'is typing' and 'asking AI'", "description": "<p>Collaborators should see who else is in a doc, where they are working and when someone is waiting on AI, like Google Docs. This uses the collab server's awareness channel from <code>services/doc-collab.js</code>; nothing is stored.</p><ul><li>Dependency: <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration-cursor</code> (approved for this module).</li><li>Awareness state: <code>{ user: { id, name, color }, typing: boolean, ai: null | 'ask' | 'review' }</code>. Pick the colour deterministically from the user id out of a fixed palette of existing <code>variables.scss</code> colours; no new colours. Expose a small setter on the service so other features can set <code>ai</code>.</li><li>Live cursors and selections in the editor, each with a name label in the user's colour (styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>).</li><li>A \\"who's in the doc\\" avatar stack in the record box header, reusing the existing avatar markup (<code>components/project/member-avatars.hbs</code> pattern, <code>userimage/get</code>). One entry per user even with several tabs, with a tooltip of the name.</li><li>Status line under the avatars: \\"<em>Name</em> is typing…\\" (set <code>typing</code> on local input, clear it after about 2 s), \\"<em>Name</em> is asking AI…\\" and \\"<em>Name</em> is running the AI Reviewer…\\" from <code>ai</code>.</li><li>Tests: the avatar stack de-duplicates users and hides the current user; the typing flag clears after the timeout; the ai flag shows the right text; the colour is stable for an id.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with two users in a doc each sees the other's avatar, cursor, selection, typing and AI status, and these disappear when the other leaves.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence on the All Docs list, follow-a-user mode.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-docs", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Docs AI endpoints: /docs/ask, /docs/complete and /docs/review", "description": "<p>Projects4Me Docs get AI help: answer a writer's request about selected text, complete the sentence being written, and review a whole document. Gaia (<code>core/services/LLM.php</code>) stays the only caller; it sends the text and returns the result to the editor.</p><ul><li>New router <code>routers/docs.py</code> (prefix <code>/docs</code>) with Pydantic request/response models, one service per use case in <code>services/</code>, prompts kept out of the router. Register it in <code>main.py</code>.</li><li><code>POST /docs/ask</code>: request <code>{instruction: str (required, max 1000), selectionHtml: str (max 8000), context: {title, headingPath: [str], before: str (max 2000), after: str (max 500)}}</code>. Response <code>{html: str}</code>: the replacement for the selection, using only the tags p, h1-h3, ul, ol, li, strong, em, u, s, a, blockquote, code, pre.</li><li><code>POST /docs/complete</code>: request <code>{title, headingPath, before (max 2000), after (max 500)}</code>. Response <code>{text: str}</code>: plain text continuing the sentence, at most about 200 characters, possibly empty. Uses a fast model from env (<code>ARES_DOCS_COMPLETE_MODEL</code>, default <code>claude-haiku-4-5-20251001</code>) with a low max-token limit, since it is called often.</li><li><code>POST /docs/review</code>: request <code>{title, text (max 60000, plain text with headings on their own lines)}</code>. Response <code>{findings: [{quote: str, category: unclear|open_question|inconsistency|missing|wording, message: str, replacement?: str}]}</code>, at most 20. <code>replacement</code> is the corrected text for <code>quote</code> when there is a concrete fix; without it the finding is a note. Every <code>quote</code> must be an exact substring of <code>text</code>: the service drops findings whose quote isn't found.</li><li>Model names and token limits come from env; extend the adapter so a service can pick its model.</li><li>Document text and the writer's instruction are untrusted input: prompts treat the document as content, never as instructions.</li><li>Errors: invalid input gives 422; a provider failure gives a clear error status and message, never empty or fake output.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter (no live calls): each endpoint's request validation and response shape, review drops non-matching quotes, complete truncates long output.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the three endpoints return the documented shapes with the fake adapter; no prompt or provider logic in the router.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming, agent loops, storing anything.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Three endpoints that share one router, one set of request/response models and one adapter change; each service and its test is small.", "screens": []}, {"key": "docassist-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Docassist resource for AI help (ask, complete, review) via Ares", "description": "<p>The Docs editor asks for AI help: a writer's request about selected text, sentence completion while writing, and a document review. Gaia owns access and must record who asked, so each request is a <code>Docassist</code> record created through standard CRUD. The create calls Ares and returns the result in the response.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Docassist</code> (table <code>docassist</code>) per <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code>: <code>docId</code>, <code>projectId</code> (varchar(36), required), <code>kind</code> (ask|complete|review), <code>instruction</code> varchar(1000) nullable (required for ask), <code>status</code> (done|failed), <code>result</code> text nullable (ask: HTML; review: JSON findings; complete: not stored), <code>inputChars</code> and <code>outputChars</code> int, standard fields and behaviours (no audit). The person who asked is <code>createdUser</code> (the <code>actedFor</code> of the resulting suggestions).</li><li>Request-only inputs, never stored: <code>selectionHtml</code>, <code>context</code> {title, headingPath, before, after}, <code>text</code> (review). Decide how the framework accepts non-persisted create inputs (e.g. a component on create) and record it in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>.</li><li>On create: check the doc exists in <code>projectId</code> and the caller has <code>doc.update</code> on it; enforce input limits (instruction 1000, selection 8000, before 2000, after 500, text 60000 chars); rate-limit per user (complete 40/min, ask and review 10/min, counted from the user's recent Docassist rows) with 429; call Ares through <code>core/services/LLM.php</code> (new methods for <code>/docs/ask</code>, <code>/docs/complete</code>, <code>/docs/review</code>, with timeouts of about 5 s, 30 s and 60 s); save the row with <code>status</code> and return the result in the response (<code>result</code> for ask and review; a transient <code>completion</code> field for complete).</li><li>A failed or timed-out Ares call saves <code>status = failed</code> and returns an error status with a message, never an empty success.</li><li>ACL metadata <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via projectId; permissions <code>docassist.create/get</code>. No permission seed SQL.</li><li>api-tester with a stubbed LLM service in the test environment (no live Ares): acl cases (member with and without docassist.create, without doc.update, non-member) and client cases (each kind returns its shape, ask without instruction is rejected, input over the limit is rejected, rate limit returns 429, Ares failure gives an error and a failed row, completion text is not stored).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the three kinds work end to end with the stub; only users who can edit the doc can ask; every request leaves a row with who, when, kind and status.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming, cost accounting in money, agents.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ares-docs", "doc-content-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 14, "sizeReason": "A new-resource bundle per B.md plus the LLM service methods, the request-only input handling, the rate limit and a test stub for the LLM service; the AI call and the resource that carries it can't ship apart.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-suggestions", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: apply, accept and reject suggestions with a Suggestions box", "description": "<p>Changes made by AI in a doc never land directly: they arrive as suggestions that people accept or reject, each showing who it was made for and, when given, why. The editor schema already has the <code>suggestionInsert</code>/<code>suggestionDelete</code> marks; this issue adds the behaviour and the Suggestions box, the single place where suggestions are reviewed. Because suggestions are marks in the shared Y.Doc, they and their accept/reject are live for everyone. Suggesting mode for people's own typing is not part of this issue.</p><ul><li><code>utils/docs/suggestions.js</code>: <code>proposeReplacement(editor, from, to, html, attrs)</code> marks the old range with <code>suggestionDelete</code> and inserts the new content with <code>suggestionInsert</code>, both with the same <code>id</code>; <code>proposeInsertion</code>; <code>accept(id)</code> (removes inserted marks, deletes text marked deleted); <code>reject(id)</code> (deletes inserted text, removes deleted marks); <code>acceptAll</code>/<code>rejectAll(requestId)</code>; <code>list(editor)</code> groups pending suggestions by <code>requestId</code>. All as single editor transactions, so they sync and undo like normal edits.</li><li><code>Docs::SuggestionsBox</code>: a <code>box-info</code> side box on the doc page (see the ai-reviewer screen) listing pending suggestions grouped by request, with Accept/Reject per suggestion and Accept all/Reject all per group. The group header shows the source name (\\"Ask AI\\" or \\"AI Reviewer\\", from <code>source</code>) with <code>Agent::Badge</code> and the \\"for {name}\\" sponsor text (as <code>components/agent/user-tag.hbs</code> does) and the time. Each entry shows its <code>reason</code> when present. It yields a slot per group for extra entries (used for reviewer notes) and re-renders when the document changes. Empty state: \\"No suggestions in this doc\\".</li><li>Clicking an entry scrolls to and selects the suggestion; clicking a suggestion in the text shows a small Accept/Reject popover (keyboard reachable).</li><li>Buttons only for users who can edit; others see the suggestions read-only.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>, strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the helpers (replacement then accept and reject give the expected document; acceptAll per request) and an integration test of the box (grouping, reason, sponsor text, read-only hides buttons, empty state).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a suggestion added through the helper shows inline and in the box; accept and reject change the document as expected for everyone in the doc.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> Suggesting mode for people's typing, comments on suggestions, notifications.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ai-reviewer"]}, {"key": "doc-ai-data", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: docassist model, adapter, Mirage and a doc-ai service", "description": "<p>The Docs AI features (ghost text, Ask AI, AI Reviewer) all call Gaia's <code>Docassist</code> resource. This issue adds the shared data layer so each feature only builds its UI.</p><ul><li>Ember Data <code>docassist</code> model (docId, projectId, kind, instruction, status, result, inputChars, outputChars, createdUser, dateCreated, plus the request-only <code>selectionHtml</code>, <code>context</code>, <code>text</code>), adapter and serializer following the existing ones; request-only attributes are sent on create and never read back.</li><li><code>services/doc-ai.js</code>: <code>ask(doc, instruction, selectionHtml, context)</code>, <code>complete(doc, context)</code>, <code>review(doc, text)</code>. Latest request wins per kind (a newer call makes an older pending result be ignored); errors are thrown with Gaia's message, and 429 becomes a \\"too many requests, try again shortly\\" error.</li><li>Mirage: a <code>docassist</code> factory and a POST handler that returns canned results per kind (and a 429 scenario).</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the service (latest wins, error mapping, review result parsed from JSON).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the service returns parsed results from Mirage for each kind and surfaces errors.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["docassist-api"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-ask-ai", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Ask AI floating menu on selected text, result inserted as a suggestion", "description": "<p>When a writer selects text, a small floating menu appears with an <strong>Ask AI</strong> option. They type what they want (\\"make this clearer\\", \\"turn into a checklist\\") and the answer replaces the selection as a suggestion that needs approval. There is no separate AI panel and no preview step.</p><ul><li>Dependency: <code>@tiptap/extension-bubble-menu</code> (open source, approved for this module).</li><li><code>Docs::SelectionMenu</code>: a bubble menu shown for a non-empty text selection, only to users who can edit. It holds bold, italic, link and an <strong>Ask AI</strong> button (<code>fa-magic</code>). Ask AI turns the menu into a request field (<code>FormFields::FieldText</code> with label \\"Ask AI\\" and help text \\"The answer is added as a suggestion. Enter to send, Esc to close.\\"). Enter sends (ignored during IME composition), Esc closes and returns focus to the editor.</li><li>On send: set the awareness <code>ai</code> flag to <code>ask</code> (so others see \\"<em>Name</em> is asking AI…\\") and clear it when done; call <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>ask()</code> with the instruction, the selection as HTML and context (doc title, heading path, up to 2000 characters before and 500 after). Show <code>AppUi::Loader</code> in the menu and disable the field while waiting.</li><li>On success: replace the original range with <code>proposeReplacement</code> from <code>utils/docs/suggestions.js</code> (<code>source: ask</code>, <code>actedFor</code> = current user, <code>requestId</code> = the Docassist id), close the menu and highlight the new group in the Suggestions box. Track the selection with Yjs relative positions while waiting; if the selected text changed, don't insert and show \\"The text changed, try again\\" in the menu.</li><li>Errors (including 429) show in the menu with a retry; one request at a time.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>, styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>.</li><li>Integration test with Mirage: select text, menu shows Ask AI, send a request, a suggestion with the right attrs appears, the ai flag is set and cleared; error path; read-only users get no Ask AI.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> matches the ask-ai screen; nothing becomes final until someone accepts the suggestion.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> preset actions, streaming, Ask AI without a selection.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-ai-data", "doc-suggestions", "doc-presence"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ask-ai"]}, {"key": "doc-ai-complete", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: always-on ghost-text AI completion while writing (Tab to accept)", "description": "<p>While writing, AI suggests how the sentence continues, shown right away as grey text after the cursor. It is always on for people who can edit. Accepting it is the writer's own choice, so accepted text is a normal edit, not a suggestion.</p><ul><li>A Tiptap extension <code>utils/docs/ghost-text.js</code>, added to the doc page editor for users who can edit: after about 500 ms without typing, with the cursor at the end of a non-empty text block and no selection, ask <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>complete()</code> with the title, heading path, up to 2000 characters before and 500 after. Show the result as a widget decoration (local only, not synced, not saved).</li><li>Tab inserts the text at the cursor; Esc, any typing, moving the cursor or losing focus dismisses it. A newer request makes older responses be ignored, and a pending request is dropped when the writer types again. Ignore while composing (IME), in read-only mode and while the Ask AI menu is open.</li><li>On 429 or errors, show nothing and back off for 30 s; no toasts.</li><li>Ghost text style in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code> (muted colour from <code>variables.scss</code>); a short hint \\"Tab to accept\\" comes from <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the extension (debounce, shown only at block end, Tab inserts, typing dismisses, stale response ignored, back-off after an error) and a page test that read-only users get no ghost text.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> pausing at the end of a paragraph shows a completion that Tab inserts; typing dismisses it; read-only users never trigger requests.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> multi-paragraph completions, completions in the middle of text, a per-user on/off setting.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-ai-data", "doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ask-ai"]}, {"key": "doc-ai-review", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: AI Reviewer toolbar button with fixes as suggestions and shared review notes", "description": "<p>An <strong>AI Reviewer</strong> button in the editor toolbar reviews the whole document: unclear wording, open questions, inconsistencies and missing parts. Concrete fixes arrive as suggestions with their reason; findings without a fix become notes. Fixes and notes live in the shared Y.Doc, so everyone in the doc sees them appear and get resolved live. Everything is reviewed in the Suggestions box; there is no separate AI panel.</p><ul><li>Toolbar button (<code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code>, <code>fa-magic</code>, \\"AI Reviewer\\") in the toolbar's extra slot, for users who can edit. While running it shows \\"Reviewing…\\" with <code>aria-busy</code>, is disabled, and sets the awareness <code>ai</code> flag to <code>review</code> (cleared when done). Afterwards it shows the number of open findings as a <code>label</code>.</li><li>On click: send the doc's plain text (headings on their own lines) through <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>review()</code>.</li><li>For each finding with a <code>replacement</code>: find its <code>quote</code> in the current document. If it occurs exactly once and doesn't overlap another fix, apply <code>proposeReplacement</code> with <code>source: review</code>, <code>actedFor</code> = current user, <code>requestId</code> = the Docassist id and <code>reason</code> = the category and message. Otherwise treat it as a note, so a fix never lands in the wrong place.</li><li><strong>Notes</strong> are stored in a shared <code>Y.Map</code> named <code>notes</code> in the doc's Y.Doc (saved with the doc state by the collab server, not rendered into the HTML): <code>{id, requestId, category, message, quote, anchorFrom, anchorTo (encoded Yjs relative positions), actedFor, createdAt, resolved, resolvedBy}</code>. Anchors follow the text as people edit.</li><li>The Suggestions box shows the open notes of each review group through its group slot: category <code>label</code>, message and a Resolve button (resolving is shared and live). Clicking a note selects its anchored text, or shows \\"Text changed since the review\\" if that text was deleted.</li><li>Errors (including 429) show next to the button with a retry. Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>, styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the notes map helpers (add, anchor, resolve) and integration tests with Mirage: fixes become suggestions with reasons, an ambiguous quote becomes a note, notes render and select their text, resolving hides the note, read-only users get no button.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> matches the ai-reviewer screen; fixes need approval in the Suggestions box and are attributed to the person who ran the review; another person in the doc sees the fixes and notes appear and get resolved without reloading.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> turning notes into comments, scheduled or automatic reviews.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-ai-data", "doc-suggestions", "doc-presence"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ai-reviewer"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-13 13:57:40	2026-11-13 13:57:40	f
4d1904176af7-395e-cc28-e583a8fd8a2d	361eb9326af4-3b69-e9a2-8e04f96d31a4	7	{"summary": "Collaborative Docs: real-time co-editing with presence, plus AI ghost text, Ask AI on a selection and an AI Reviewer, all live for everyone in the doc. Gaia stores each doc's Yjs state and its derived HTML and plain text in a new Doccontent resource (Doc.body is dropped), enforces doc.update and the lock, publishes doc.created/updated/deleted through Hermes and tells the collab server when a doc is locked or deleted. A Hocuspocus collab server in hermes/collab syncs content, suggestions, review notes and presence over one WebSocket, saves to Gaia, and switches open editors to read-only or closes them when Gaia says access changed; the Hermes relay only gains the doc.* event names. Prometheus gets a Tiptap editor with suggestion marks, the collab client with offline recovery, live doc metadata, and presence including an AI busy flag. For AI, Ares gets /docs/ask, /docs/complete and /docs/review behind a standard Gaia Docassist resource (access, rate limit, log of who asked); Prometheus adds the Suggestions box, then always-on ghost text, the Ask AI floating menu and the AI Reviewer, whose notes are stored in the shared Y.Doc.", "issues": [{"key": "doc-content-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Doccontent resource (Yjs state, HTML and plain text) and drop Doc.body", "description": "<p>Docs become real-time co-edited documents. A doc's content is a Yjs CRDT state kept live by a collab server and saved to Gaia. The content gets its own resource so that the frequent autosaves don't rewrite the doc metadata, aren't copied into the audit log (<code>auditBehavior</code> stores old and new values of every changed field) and never travel with list queries.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Doccontent</code> (table <code>doccontent</code>), following <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code> (exemplar gaia#264, the Doc resource): <code>docId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>projectId</code> varchar(36) required (the doc's project, for the ACL group), <code>state</code> text nullable (base64-encoded Yjs update), <code>html</code> text nullable, <code>plainText</code> text nullable, <code>byteSize</code> int, plus the standard id, dates, createdUser, modifiedUser and deleted fields. Behaviours: createdUser, modifiedUser, dateCreated, dateModified, softDelete. <strong>No auditBehavior.</strong></li><li>Relationships: <code>doc</code> hasOne Doc (docId); inverse <code>content</code> hasOne Doccontent on <code>Doc</code>.</li><li>Validation: one Doccontent per doc (a second create for the same <code>docId</code> fails validation); <code>docId</code> must be a doc in the same <code>projectId</code>.</li><li>Remove the <code>body</code> field from <code>Doc</code> metadata and its api-tester cases. Existing doc rows are test data only, so their body is dropped.</li><li>ACL metadata <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via projectId, permissions <code>doccontent.get/create/update/delete</code>. No permission seed SQL.</li><li>Model, empty controller, <code>core/config/models.php</code>, <code>core/config/routes.php</code>, <code>routes.v1.json</code>, backend api placeholders and regenerated outputs as in B.md. api-tester harness/seed rows plus acl.json (member with and without doccontent.*, non-member) and client.json cases (create, get by docId, update, duplicate docId rejected).</li><li><code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>: D-002 (the Yjs state in Doccontent is the master copy; <code>html</code> and <code>plainText</code> are derived copies for export, search and AI, written by the collab server and never edited directly; base64 in text because the REST API is JSON), D-003 (content is written with the connected user's own token, so Gaia ACL and modifiedUser stay authoritative; no service account), D-004 (one merged snapshot row per doc, no update log).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a project member with doccontent.* can create, read and update one content row per doc; non-members are denied; Doc has no body field; the regenerated docs and graph have no drift.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> version history, lock enforcement (separate issue), sharing, full-text search.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "A standard new-resource bundle per B.md (metadata, model, controller, config, routes, api-tester cases) plus removing Doc.body and the decisions doc; splitting it would leave a half resource that breaks dev.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-write-guard", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: require doc.update for Doc/Doccontent writes and reject writes on locked docs", "description": "<p>The collab server and the UI rely on Gaia to refuse writes a user isn't allowed to make. The review of agaia-4488 (gaia#264) found that a project member with only <code>doc.get</code>/<code>doc.create</code> got 200 on <code>PATCH /api/v1/doc/{id}</code>, and that <code>Doc.locked</code> is stored but not enforced.</p><ul><li>Find why update was authorized without <code>doc.update</code> (check how RestController/ACL authorizes PATCH for project-group resources, and whether other resources are affected) and fix it at the root. If the cause is in shared ACL code, fix it there and add denial cases for one other resource too.</li><li>Enforce <code>locked</code>: while a doc is locked, updates to its <code>Doccontent</code> are rejected (403 or a validation error, following the layering in the Design section). Only the doc's owner (<code>ownerId</code>) or a user with the project admin role may change <code>locked</code>, like the wiki lock today.</li><li>api-tester acl.json cases: Doc update and delete denied without doc.update/doc.delete; Doccontent update denied without doccontent.update; Doccontent update rejected on a locked doc; lock/unlock by the owner allowed, by another editor denied.</li><li>Record the lock rule as a decision in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the new denial cases pass and the existing Doc cases still pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-doc sharing roles, ownerId validation against project members.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-content-api"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "collab-server", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Docs collab server: self-contained collab/ package (Hocuspocus) with Gaia auth and Doccontent persistence", "description": "<p>Projects4Me Docs need Google-Docs-style co-editing. Each doc is a Yjs CRDT document that must be held in memory, synced between browsers and saved to Gaia. The relay can't do this (D-001 locked stateless relay, D-002 browsers never publish), so a collab server is added to this repo as a <strong>self-contained package in <code>collab/</code></strong>: its own process, port and container, sharing no code or dependencies with the relay, so it can later move to its own repo by moving the folder.</p><ul><li><strong>Isolation:</strong> its own <code>collab/package.json</code> (dependencies <code>@hocuspocus/server</code>, <code>yjs</code>, <code>@tiptap/html</code> and the Tiptap extensions below, approved for this module; pick versions that run on Node 18, Hermes' runtime), its own entrypoint <code>collab/server.js</code>, its own Dockerfile and docker-compose service. No imports from the relay's <code>src/</code> and no changes to relay code: its own small Gaia client module, modelled on <code>src/auth/gaia-session.js</code>.</li><li><strong>ADR D-016</strong> in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>: the collab server lives in <code>collab/</code> as a separate process; it holds Yjs documents and awareness in memory only and persists only through Gaia; the relay rules D-001 to D-015 are unchanged. It moves to its own repo when it takes on agents or export, or when its releases start to clash with the relay's.</li><li><code>CLAUDE.md</code>: scope the rule \\"Hermes stays a locked relay: no domain logic, no storage\\" to the relay (<code>src/</code>), and add a short <code>collab/</code> section (what it may do, its own package.json, no imports across the two).</li><li>Root test script also runs <code>collab/</code> tests, so the existing hermes test command covers both.</li><li>Document name contract: <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>. The client sends the user's Gaia OAuth access token as the Hocuspocus token. Never log tokens or document content.</li><li>onAuthenticate: call Gaia <code>GET /api/v1/user/me</code> with the token. Reject without <code>doc.get</code> in <code>aclPermissions</code>, then <code>GET /api/v1/doc/&lt;id&gt;</code> with the same token (reject on 403/404). The connection is read-only when the user lacks <code>doc.update</code> or the doc is <code>locked</code>; updates from read-only connections are dropped by the server.</li><li>onLoadDocument: load the Doccontent for the doc (<code>GET /api/v1/doccontent</code> filtered by docId) and apply the base64 <code>state</code>; start empty if there is none. Unload a doc from memory after it has been saved and nobody is connected.</li><li>onStoreDocument (debounce about 2 s, max 10 s): encode the state and create or PATCH the Doccontent <code>state</code> and <code>byteSize</code>. After about 30 s without changes and on the last disconnect, also write <code>html</code> and <code>plainText</code>, generated from the editor fragment only (other shared types in the Y.Doc, such as the review <code>notes</code> map, are saved with the state but not rendered). Use the token of a connected user who has write access; on 401, try another connected writer.</li><li><strong>Schema</strong> in <code>collab/schema.js</code>, matching the Prometheus editor: StarterKit, Underline, Link, Table/TableRow/TableHeader/TableCell, TaskList/TaskItem, and two marks <code>suggestionInsert</code> / <code>suggestionDelete</code> (attrs <code>id</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>authorId</code>, <code>actedFor</code>, <code>requestId</code>, <code>reason</code>, <code>createdAt</code>; rendered as <code>&lt;ins data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;del data-suggestion-id&gt;</code>). Document it in <code>collab/README.md</code> with the env config (<code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>COLLAB_PORT</code>) and how to run it.</li><li>Unit tests with a stubbed Gaia: rejected token, missing doc.get, read-only for no doc.update and for locked, load applies stored state, store creates then updates the content, html/plainText written on idle and on last disconnect.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two clients editing <code>doc:&lt;id&gt;</code> converge; after a restart the content reloads from Gaia; unauthorized users can't connect; read-only users can't change the document; the relay's tests and image are unchanged apart from the test script.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> access changes while connected (separate issue), agents as server-side peers, version snapshots, comments, scaling beyond one instance.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-content-api"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "A new self-contained service package: entrypoint, auth, Gaia client/persistence and schema modules, its package.json, Dockerfile and compose service, README, ADR, CLAUDE.md, root test script and two test files. Auth and persistence can't ship apart, because the server is unusable without both.", "screens": []}, {"key": "collab-access", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Docs collab server: internal access-change endpoint, client messages and write limits", "description": "<p>When a doc is locked or deleted, people who already have it open must switch to read-only or be closed at once. Otherwise their edits keep spreading to others in memory while Gaia refuses to save them. Gaia tells the collab server (<code>collab/</code>) through a server-to-server call; the collab server re-checks each connection with Gaia and informs the clients.</p><ul><li><code>POST /internal/docs/:docId/access</code> on the collab server's HTTP port, authenticated with a shared secret (<code>COLLAB_SECRET</code> env, header <code>X-Collab-Secret</code>, compared in constant time). Body <code>{reason: locked|unlocked|deleted|access}</code>. Returns 202. Rejects without the secret.</li><li>On a call: for every connection to <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>, re-check with Gaia using that connection's token (same checks as onAuthenticate). Switch it to read-only or back to editable, or close it when the doc is gone or access was lost.</li><li>Stateless messages to clients (JSON, documented in <code>collab/README.md</code> as the contract with Prometheus): <code>{type: 'access', readOnly: bool, reason}</code>, <code>{type: 'deleted'}</code>, <code>{type: 'unsaved', since: ISO date}</code> when saving to Gaia has failed for over 2 minutes (and <code>{type: 'saved'}</code> once it recovers). Retry failed saves with back-off.</li><li>Limits: maximum size per incoming Yjs update (env, default 512 KB) and a per-connection update rate limit; offending connections are closed with a reason. Check the WebSocket <code>Origin</code> against an allowed list from env.</li><li>Add an ADR entry next to D-016 for the internal endpoint and its secret.</li><li>Unit tests with a stubbed Gaia: missing or wrong secret rejected, lock switches connections to read-only and sends the message, unlock restores editing, delete closes connections, unsaved message after the save-failure threshold, oversized update rejected.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after the endpoint is called for a locked doc, open editors stop being able to change it within a second and are told why.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-doc sharing changes (later), multi-instance coordination.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["collab-server"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-doc-events", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Relay: allow doc.created, doc.updated and doc.deleted events", "description": "<p>Docs lists and open doc pages update live when a doc is created, renamed, locked or deleted. Gaia publishes these as domain events; the relay only needs to accept the names (D-003 allowlist).</p><ul><li>Add <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code> and <code>doc.deleted</code> to <code>src/contract/names.js</code>, matching Gaia's <code>EventNames.php</code>. Payloads follow the existing closed envelope (project-scoped, ids plus changed field names for <code>doc.updated</code>).</li><li>ADR entry in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code> for the new names, as the contract rules require.</li><li>Tests: the names are accepted by <code>/publish</code> and delivered to sockets with a matching intent; unknown <code>doc.*</code> names are still rejected.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a published <code>doc.updated</code> reaches a project member's socket registered for it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any doc content traffic (that goes through the collab server).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-live-events", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: publish doc.created/updated/deleted live events and notify the collab server on lock and delete", "description": "<p>Docs lists and open doc pages must update live when a doc is created, renamed, locked or deleted, and open editors must turn read-only as soon as a doc is locked. Gaia publishes doc events through Hermes and calls the collab server's internal access endpoint.</p><ul><li><code>DocLiveEventsComponent</code> in <code>app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/</code>, following <code>docs/generated/bundles/E.md</code> (precedent <code>UserAccessLiveEventsComponent</code>, <code>IdeaLiveEventsComponent</code>): publish <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code> (with the changed field names: title, locked, ownerId, parent and status as they exist) and <code>doc.deleted</code>, scoped to the doc's project. Add the names to <code>support/EventNames.php</code>; they must match <code>hermes/src/contract/names.js</code>, so this ships together with the Hermes allowlist change.</li><li>New <code>CollabNotifier</code> class (one class owns the collab server's URL, secret and transport, like <code>HermesPublisher</code>): <code>POST {COLLAB_URL}/internal/docs/{docId}/access</code> with header <code>X-Collab-Secret</code> and body <code>{reason: locked|unlocked|deleted}</code>. Called after a doc's <code>locked</code> changes and after a doc is deleted. Config via <code>getenv()</code> in <code>config/*.php</code>; never logged.</li><li>Side effects fail open: Hermes or the collab server being down must not fail the user's write; log the failure.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the component (right event and payload per change, no event for unchanged saves) and the notifier (sends on lock, unlock and delete; failures don't throw), with the transports stubbed.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> renaming, locking or deleting a doc publishes the matching event; locking or deleting calls the collab server; both failing leaves the write successful.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> events for Doccontent saves, sharing events.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-write-guard", "hermes-doc-events", "collab-access"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-editor", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Tiptap editor component with toolbar, tables, checklists, outline and suggestion marks", "description": "<p>The Docs module needs a structured rich-text editor that can co-edit through Yjs. Toast UI can't, so Docs uses Tiptap (open-source packages only). This issue builds the editor as a standalone component. Real-time wiring and suggestion behaviour come in later issues.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>@tiptap/core</code>, <code>@tiptap/starter-kit</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-underline</code>, <code>-link</code>, <code>-table</code>, <code>-table-row</code>, <code>-table-header</code>, <code>-table-cell</code>, <code>-task-list</code>, <code>-task-item</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>utils/docs/schema.js</code>: the single list of extensions, plus two marks <code>suggestionInsert</code> and <code>suggestionDelete</code> (attrs <code>id</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>authorId</code>, <code>actedFor</code>, <code>requestId</code>, <code>reason</code>, <code>createdAt</code>; rendered as <code>&lt;ins data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;del data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> with a <code>doc-suggestion</code> class). The collab server builds the stored HTML from the same list (<code>hermes/collab/schema.js</code>), so a change here needs the same change there.</li><li><code>Docs::Editor</code> (<code>components/docs/editor.{js,hbs}</code>): mounts Tiptap on an element. Args <code>@content</code> (initial HTML), <code>@editable</code>, <code>@extensions</code> (extra extensions added to the schema list), <code>@onReady(editor)</code>. Destroys the editor on teardown. No persistence.</li><li><code>Docs::Toolbar</code>: bold, italic, underline, strike, H1 to H3, bullet and ordered list, checklist, blockquote, code block, link, insert table and add/remove rows and columns. Buttons are <code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code> with Font Awesome 4 icons, <code>aria-pressed</code> for active marks, and the toolbar is hidden when not editable. It yields a slot for extra button groups.</li><li><code>Docs::Outline</code>: a <code>col-md-4</code> side box listing the document's headings; clicking or pressing Enter scrolls to the heading.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code> (square edges, colours from <code>variables.scss</code> only), including the suggestion marks (inserted text underlined, deleted text struck through, in existing colours). Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Integration tests: renders the content, a toolbar action applies a mark, read-only hides the toolbar and blocks typing, the outline lists headings and scrolls, suggestion marks render with their attributes.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the component renders and edits formatted content, tables and checklists, renders suggestion marks, and follows <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> saving, real-time collaboration, accepting/rejecting suggestions, images and attachments, comments.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Editor, toolbar and outline components (js+hbs each), the schema module, styles, translations and tests. The toolbar and outline are small and only make sense with the editor they drive.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-collab-client", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: real-time co-editing on the doc page with autosave status and offline recovery", "description": "<p>Connects the Docs editor to the collab server (<code>hermes/collab</code>), so several people edit one doc live and changes save themselves with no Save button.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>yjs</code>, <code>@hocuspocus/provider</code>, <code>y-indexeddb</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>config/environment.js</code>: <code>ENV.docs.collabUrl</code> (no secrets).</li><li><code>services/doc-collab.js</code>: <code>open(docId)</code> creates a Y.Doc, an <code>IndexeddbPersistence</code> for offline recovery and a <code>HocuspocusProvider</code> (name <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>, token = the session's current access token; refresh it through <code>services/session.js</code> and reconnect before it expires). Exposes the Y.Doc, the provider's awareness, tracked <code>status</code> (connecting, saving, saved, offline) and <code>readOnly</code> (from the server). <code>close()</code> destroys both. One responsibility: the connection; no UI.</li><li>Doc page from aprom-4490 (<code>app.project.doc.page</code>): renders <code>Docs::Editor</code> with the Collaboration extension bound to the Y.Doc. Editable only when <code>acl</code> allows doc.update, the doc isn't locked and the server didn't mark the connection read-only. Opens on route enter and closes on exit. A new doc starts empty.</li><li><code>Docs::SaveStatus</code> in the record box header: \\"Saving…\\", \\"All changes saved\\", \\"Offline – changes are kept on this device\\".</li><li>Tests: the service with a stubbed provider (status transitions, readOnly, close on exit) and an acceptance test of the page in read-only and editable modes with the service stubbed (Mirage has no websocket).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two browsers on the same doc see each other's edits live; reloading keeps the content; edits made offline sync after reconnecting; a locked doc, or a user without doc.update, gets a read-only editor.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence and cursors, live metadata and server messages (separate issues), version history.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-editor", "collab-server", "aprom-4489", "aprom-4490"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-live-client", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: live doc metadata on list and page, and collab server messages (locked, deleted, not saved)", "description": "<p>Everything about a doc should update live: a rename or lock shows at once in the All Docs list and on the open page, a deleted doc closes, and editors learn immediately when they can no longer edit or when their changes aren't reaching the server.</p><ul><li>Register for Hermes <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code> and <code>doc.deleted</code> with <code>hermes.register(owner, projectId, handlers)</code> from the controllers of the All Docs list (aprom-4491) and the doc page (aprom-4490), following <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/</code>; filter on the doc id on the page (precedent <code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>). The list reloads or updates the affected row; the page reloads the doc record (title, lock). Add the registrations to the live-updates registration table.</li><li>Handle the collab server's stateless messages in <code>services/doc-collab.js</code> (contract in <code>hermes/collab/README.md</code>): <code>access</code> switches the editor to read-only or back and shows a Messenger notice with the reason (\\"This doc was locked\\"); <code>deleted</code> closes the connection and goes to the All Docs list with a notice; <code>unsaved</code>/<code>saved</code> drive a \\"Not saved to server yet\\" state in <code>Docs::SaveStatus</code>.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: handlers update the list and page (Hermes stubbed), each message type changes the editor state and notice as expected.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with two browsers, renaming or locking in one updates the other's list and page without reload; locking turns the other's open editor read-only with a notice; deleting closes it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> live updates for sharing (later).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-collab-client", "doc-live-events", "aprom-4491"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-presence", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: who's in the doc, live cursors and selections, 'is typing' and 'asking AI'", "description": "<p>Collaborators should see who else is in a doc, where they are working and when someone is waiting on AI, like Google Docs. This uses the collab server's awareness channel from <code>services/doc-collab.js</code>; nothing is stored.</p><ul><li>Dependency: <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration-cursor</code> (approved for this module).</li><li>Awareness state: <code>{ user: { id, name, color }, typing: boolean, ai: null | 'ask' | 'review' }</code>. Pick the colour deterministically from the user id out of a fixed palette of existing <code>variables.scss</code> colours; no new colours. Expose a small setter on the service so other features can set <code>ai</code>.</li><li>Live cursors and selections in the editor, each with a name label in the user's colour (styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>).</li><li>A \\"who's in the doc\\" avatar stack in the record box header, reusing the existing avatar markup (<code>components/project/member-avatars.hbs</code> pattern, <code>userimage/get</code>). One entry per user even with several tabs, with a tooltip of the name.</li><li>Status line under the avatars: \\"<em>Name</em> is typing…\\" (set <code>typing</code> on local input, clear it after about 2 s), \\"<em>Name</em> is asking AI…\\" and \\"<em>Name</em> is running the AI Reviewer…\\" from <code>ai</code>.</li><li>Tests: the avatar stack de-duplicates users and hides the current user; the typing flag clears after the timeout; the ai flag shows the right text; the colour is stable for an id.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with two users in a doc each sees the other's avatar, cursor, selection, typing and AI status, and these disappear when the other leaves.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence on the All Docs list, follow-a-user mode.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-docs", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Docs AI endpoints: /docs/ask, /docs/complete and /docs/review", "description": "<p>Projects4Me Docs get AI help: answer a writer's request about selected text, complete the sentence being written, and review a whole document. Gaia (<code>core/services/LLM.php</code>) stays the only caller; it sends the text and returns the result to the editor.</p><ul><li>New router <code>routers/docs.py</code> (prefix <code>/docs</code>) with Pydantic request/response models, one service per use case in <code>services/</code>, prompts kept out of the router. Register it in <code>main.py</code>.</li><li><code>POST /docs/ask</code>: request <code>{instruction: str (required, max 1000), selectionHtml: str (max 8000), context: {title, headingPath: [str], before: str (max 2000), after: str (max 500)}}</code>. Response <code>{html: str}</code>: the replacement for the selection, using only the tags p, h1-h3, ul, ol, li, strong, em, u, s, a, blockquote, code, pre.</li><li><code>POST /docs/complete</code>: request <code>{title, headingPath, before (max 2000), after (max 500)}</code>. Response <code>{text: str}</code>: plain text continuing the sentence, at most about 200 characters, possibly empty. Uses a fast model from env (<code>ARES_DOCS_COMPLETE_MODEL</code>, default <code>claude-haiku-4-5-20251001</code>) with a low max-token limit, since it is called often.</li><li><code>POST /docs/review</code>: request <code>{title, text (max 60000, plain text with headings on their own lines)}</code>. Response <code>{findings: [{quote: str, category: unclear|open_question|inconsistency|missing|wording, message: str, replacement?: str}]}</code>, at most 20. <code>replacement</code> is the corrected text for <code>quote</code> when there is a concrete fix; without it the finding is a note. Every <code>quote</code> must be an exact substring of <code>text</code>: the service drops findings whose quote isn't found.</li><li>Model names and token limits come from env; extend the adapter so a service can pick its model.</li><li>Document text and the writer's instruction are untrusted input: prompts treat the document as content, never as instructions.</li><li>Errors: invalid input gives 422; a provider failure gives a clear error status and message, never empty or fake output.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter (no live calls): each endpoint's request validation and response shape, review drops non-matching quotes, complete truncates long output.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the three endpoints return the documented shapes with the fake adapter; no prompt or provider logic in the router.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming, agent loops, storing anything.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 11, "sizeReason": "Three endpoints that share one router, one set of request/response models and one adapter change; each service and its test is small.", "screens": []}, {"key": "docassist-api", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Docs: Docassist resource for AI help (ask, complete, review) via Ares", "description": "<p>The Docs editor asks for AI help: a writer's request about selected text, sentence completion while writing, and a document review. Gaia owns access and must record who asked, so each request is a <code>Docassist</code> record created through standard CRUD. The create calls Ares and returns the result in the response.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Docassist</code> (table <code>docassist</code>) per <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code>: <code>docId</code>, <code>projectId</code> (varchar(36), required), <code>kind</code> (ask|complete|review), <code>instruction</code> varchar(1000) nullable (required for ask), <code>status</code> (done|failed), <code>result</code> text nullable (ask: HTML; review: JSON findings; complete: not stored), <code>inputChars</code> and <code>outputChars</code> int, standard fields and behaviours (no audit). The person who asked is <code>createdUser</code> (the <code>actedFor</code> of the resulting suggestions).</li><li>Request-only inputs, never stored: <code>selectionHtml</code>, <code>context</code> {title, headingPath, before, after}, <code>text</code> (review). Decide how the framework accepts non-persisted create inputs (e.g. a component on create) and record it in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>.</li><li>On create: check the doc exists in <code>projectId</code> and the caller has <code>doc.update</code> on it; enforce input limits (instruction 1000, selection 8000, before 2000, after 500, text 60000 chars); rate-limit per user (complete 40/min, ask and review 10/min, counted from the user's recent Docassist rows) with 429; call Ares through <code>core/services/LLM.php</code> (new methods for <code>/docs/ask</code>, <code>/docs/complete</code>, <code>/docs/review</code>, with timeouts of about 5 s, 30 s and 60 s); save the row with <code>status</code> and return the result in the response (<code>result</code> for ask and review; a transient <code>completion</code> field for complete).</li><li>A failed or timed-out Ares call saves <code>status = failed</code> and returns an error status with a message, never an empty success.</li><li>ACL metadata <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via projectId; permissions <code>docassist.create/get</code>. No permission seed SQL.</li><li>api-tester with a stubbed LLM service in the test environment (no live Ares): acl cases (member with and without docassist.create, without doc.update, non-member) and client cases (each kind returns its shape, ask without instruction is rejected, input over the limit is rejected, rate limit returns 429, Ares failure gives an error and a failed row, completion text is not stored).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the three kinds work end to end with the stub; only users who can edit the doc can ask; every request leaves a row with who, when, kind and status.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming, cost accounting in money, agents.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ares-docs", "doc-content-api"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 14, "sizeReason": "A new-resource bundle per B.md plus the LLM service methods, the request-only input handling, the rate limit and a test stub for the LLM service; the AI call and the resource that carries it can't ship apart.", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-suggestions", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: apply, accept and reject suggestions with a Suggestions box", "description": "<p>Changes made by AI in a doc never land directly: they arrive as suggestions that people accept or reject, each showing who it was made for and, when given, why. The editor schema already has the <code>suggestionInsert</code>/<code>suggestionDelete</code> marks; this issue adds the behaviour and the Suggestions box, the single place where suggestions are reviewed. Because suggestions are marks in the shared Y.Doc, they and their accept/reject are live for everyone. Suggesting mode for people's own typing is not part of this issue.</p><ul><li><code>utils/docs/suggestions.js</code>: <code>proposeReplacement(editor, from, to, html, attrs)</code> marks the old range with <code>suggestionDelete</code> and inserts the new content with <code>suggestionInsert</code>, both with the same <code>id</code>; <code>proposeInsertion</code>; <code>accept(id)</code> (removes inserted marks, deletes text marked deleted); <code>reject(id)</code> (deletes inserted text, removes deleted marks); <code>acceptAll</code>/<code>rejectAll(requestId)</code>; <code>list(editor)</code> groups pending suggestions by <code>requestId</code>. All as single editor transactions, so they sync and undo like normal edits.</li><li><code>Docs::SuggestionsBox</code>: a <code>box-info</code> side box on the doc page (see the ai-reviewer screen) listing pending suggestions grouped by request, with Accept/Reject per suggestion and Accept all/Reject all per group. The group header shows the source name (\\"Ask AI\\" or \\"AI Reviewer\\", from <code>source</code>) with <code>Agent::Badge</code> and the \\"for {name}\\" sponsor text (as <code>components/agent/user-tag.hbs</code> does) and the time. Each entry shows its <code>reason</code> when present. It yields a slot per group for extra entries (used for reviewer notes) and re-renders when the document changes. Empty state: \\"No suggestions in this doc\\".</li><li>Clicking an entry scrolls to and selects the suggestion; clicking a suggestion in the text shows a small Accept/Reject popover (keyboard reachable).</li><li>Buttons only for users who can edit; others see the suggestions read-only.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>, strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the helpers (replacement then accept and reject give the expected document; acceptAll per request) and an integration test of the box (grouping, reason, sponsor text, read-only hides buttons, empty state).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a suggestion added through the helper shows inline and in the box; accept and reject change the document as expected for everyone in the doc.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> Suggesting mode for people's typing, comments on suggestions, notifications.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ai-reviewer"]}, {"key": "doc-ai-data", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: docassist model, adapter, Mirage and a doc-ai service", "description": "<p>The Docs AI features (ghost text, Ask AI, AI Reviewer) all call Gaia's <code>Docassist</code> resource. This issue adds the shared data layer so each feature only builds its UI.</p><ul><li>Ember Data <code>docassist</code> model (docId, projectId, kind, instruction, status, result, inputChars, outputChars, createdUser, dateCreated, plus the request-only <code>selectionHtml</code>, <code>context</code>, <code>text</code>), adapter and serializer following the existing ones; request-only attributes are sent on create and never read back.</li><li><code>services/doc-ai.js</code>: <code>ask(doc, instruction, selectionHtml, context)</code>, <code>complete(doc, context)</code>, <code>review(doc, text)</code>. Latest request wins per kind (a newer call makes an older pending result be ignored); errors are thrown with Gaia's message, and 429 becomes a \\"too many requests, try again shortly\\" error.</li><li>Mirage: a <code>docassist</code> factory and a POST handler that returns canned results per kind (and a 429 scenario).</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the service (latest wins, error mapping, review result parsed from JSON).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the service returns parsed results from Mirage for each kind and surfaces errors.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["docassist-api"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "doc-ask-ai", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: Ask AI floating menu on selected text, result inserted as a suggestion", "description": "<p>When a writer selects text, a small floating menu appears with an <strong>Ask AI</strong> option. They type what they want (\\"make this clearer\\", \\"turn into a checklist\\") and the answer replaces the selection as a suggestion that needs approval. There is no separate AI panel and no preview step.</p><ul><li>Dependency: <code>@tiptap/extension-bubble-menu</code> (open source, approved for this module).</li><li><code>Docs::SelectionMenu</code>: a bubble menu shown for a non-empty text selection, only to users who can edit. It holds bold, italic, link and an <strong>Ask AI</strong> button (<code>fa-magic</code>). Ask AI turns the menu into a request field (<code>FormFields::FieldText</code> with label \\"Ask AI\\" and help text \\"The answer is added as a suggestion. Enter to send, Esc to close.\\"). Enter sends (ignored during IME composition), Esc closes and returns focus to the editor.</li><li>On send: set the awareness <code>ai</code> flag to <code>ask</code> (so others see \\"<em>Name</em> is asking AI…\\") and clear it when done; call <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>ask()</code> with the instruction, the selection as HTML and context (doc title, heading path, up to 2000 characters before and 500 after). Show <code>AppUi::Loader</code> in the menu and disable the field while waiting.</li><li>On success: replace the original range with <code>proposeReplacement</code> from <code>utils/docs/suggestions.js</code> (<code>source: ask</code>, <code>actedFor</code> = current user, <code>requestId</code> = the Docassist id), close the menu and highlight the new group in the Suggestions box. Track the selection with Yjs relative positions while waiting; if the selected text changed, don't insert and show \\"The text changed, try again\\" in the menu.</li><li>Errors (including 429) show in the menu with a retry; one request at a time.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>, styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>.</li><li>Integration test with Mirage: select text, menu shows Ask AI, send a request, a suggestion with the right attrs appears, the ai flag is set and cleared; error path; read-only users get no Ask AI.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> matches the ask-ai screen; nothing becomes final until someone accepts the suggestion.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> preset actions, streaming, Ask AI without a selection.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-ai-data", "doc-suggestions", "doc-presence"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ask-ai"]}, {"key": "doc-ai-complete", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: always-on ghost-text AI completion while writing (Tab to accept)", "description": "<p>While writing, AI suggests how the sentence continues, shown right away as grey text after the cursor. It is always on for people who can edit. Accepting it is the writer's own choice, so accepted text is a normal edit, not a suggestion.</p><ul><li>A Tiptap extension <code>utils/docs/ghost-text.js</code>, added to the doc page editor for users who can edit: after about 500 ms without typing, with the cursor at the end of a non-empty text block and no selection, ask <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>complete()</code> with the title, heading path, up to 2000 characters before and 500 after. Show the result as a widget decoration (local only, not synced, not saved).</li><li>Tab inserts the text at the cursor; Esc, any typing, moving the cursor or losing focus dismisses it. A newer request makes older responses be ignored, and a pending request is dropped when the writer types again. Ignore while composing (IME), in read-only mode and while the Ask AI menu is open.</li><li>On 429 or errors, show nothing and back off for 30 s; no toasts.</li><li>Ghost text style in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code> (muted colour from <code>variables.scss</code>); a short hint \\"Tab to accept\\" comes from <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the extension (debounce, shown only at block end, Tab inserts, typing dismisses, stale response ignored, back-off after an error) and a page test that read-only users get no ghost text.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> pausing at the end of a paragraph shows a completion that Tab inserts; typing dismisses it; read-only users never trigger requests.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> multi-paragraph completions, completions in the middle of text, a per-user on/off setting.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-ai-data", "doc-collab-client"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ask-ai"]}, {"key": "doc-ai-review", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Docs: AI Reviewer toolbar button with fixes as suggestions and shared review notes", "description": "<p>An <strong>AI Reviewer</strong> button in the editor toolbar reviews the whole document: unclear wording, open questions, inconsistencies and missing parts. Concrete fixes arrive as suggestions with their reason; findings without a fix become notes. Fixes and notes live in the shared Y.Doc, so everyone in the doc sees them appear and get resolved live. Everything is reviewed in the Suggestions box; there is no separate AI panel.</p><ul><li>Toolbar button (<code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code>, <code>fa-magic</code>, \\"AI Reviewer\\") in the toolbar's extra slot, for users who can edit. While running it shows \\"Reviewing…\\" with <code>aria-busy</code>, is disabled, and sets the awareness <code>ai</code> flag to <code>review</code> (cleared when done). Afterwards it shows the number of open findings as a <code>label</code>.</li><li>On click: send the doc's plain text (headings on their own lines) through <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>review()</code>.</li><li>For each finding with a <code>replacement</code>: find its <code>quote</code> in the current document. If it occurs exactly once and doesn't overlap another fix, apply <code>proposeReplacement</code> with <code>source: review</code>, <code>actedFor</code> = current user, <code>requestId</code> = the Docassist id and <code>reason</code> = the category and message. Otherwise treat it as a note, so a fix never lands in the wrong place.</li><li><strong>Notes</strong> are stored in a shared <code>Y.Map</code> named <code>notes</code> in the doc's Y.Doc (saved with the doc state by the collab server, not rendered into the HTML): <code>{id, requestId, category, message, quote, anchorFrom, anchorTo (encoded Yjs relative positions), actedFor, createdAt, resolved, resolvedBy}</code>. Anchors follow the text as people edit.</li><li>The Suggestions box shows the open notes of each review group through its group slot: category <code>label</code>, message and a Resolve button (resolving is shared and live). Clicking a note selects its anchored text, or shows \\"Text changed since the review\\" if that text was deleted.</li><li>Errors (including 429) show next to the button with a retry. Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>, styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the notes map helpers (add, anchor, resolve) and integration tests with Mirage: fixes become suggestions with reasons, an ambiguous quote becomes a note, notes render and select their text, resolving hides the note, read-only users get no button.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> matches the ai-reviewer screen; fixes need approval in the Suggestions box and are attributed to the person who ran the review; another person in the doc sees the fixes and notes appear and get resolved without reloading.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> turning notes into comments, scheduled or automatic reviews.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["doc-ai-data", "doc-suggestions", "doc-presence"], "milestone": "aga-Docs", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["ai-reviewer"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-13 14:01:49	2026-11-13 14:14:39	f
1f8fe0b06afa-b491-52a3-64b7d6edfeec	ded9f4396af0-2b69-3bb7-c36bdb48cfdf	2	{"summary": "Finalize five core components of the Component Library without touching their users: Avatar (standard sizes, default image, person vs agent) -> Tag (Task Board look, palette colours, removable); Dropdown (auto alignment, Bootstrap menu look); a shared selection model that lets DataTable keep a selection across pages -> DataTable look (QuickList checkboxes and selected rows, standard action icons, more-menu on AppUi::Dropdown); EzSearch icon-only buttons when its own box is narrow; then ListToolbar ties a built-in selection bar to the list's selection and gives the search room in narrow spaces. Each issue updates the component's demo, ui-docs page and manifest (design-system R6). Parallel issues never share a file.", "issues": [{"key": "avatar", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::Avatar: standard sizes xs/s/m/l, default image, person vs agent", "description": "<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library (Developer -&gt; Components). <code>AppUi::Avatar</code> needs standard sizes, a default image and a clear person vs agent look. Scope is the component, its demo and its docs only: do not change pages that use it (if a page then looks different, that is accepted).</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><p>Today: <code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code> renders <code>Agent::UserAvatar</code> (<code>components/agent/user-avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, uses the <code>agentDirectory</code> service) with AdminLTE <code>img-circle</code> + <code>img-sm</code>/<code>img-xs</code>; with no size the image shows at its file size; a missing image is broken; for an agent it renders <code>Agent::Avatar</code> without <code>@user</code> (so an agent's own picture never shows) and without the size.</p><ul><li><code>@size</code>: <code>xs</code> 20px, <code>s</code> 30px, <code>m</code> 40px (default), <code>l</code> 96px; <code>sm</code> stays an alias of <code>s</code>. Unknown values fall back to m.</li><li>Person: the user image (<code>/userimage/get/&lt;id&gt;</code>); when there is no id or the image fails to load (<code>error</code> event), show <code>/img/default.png</code> at the same size (see <code>isDefaultProfilePicture</code> in <code>models/user.js</code>). Never a broken image.</li><li>Agent: pass the user to <code>Agent::Avatar</code> so its picture shows; with a picture add a small round robot marker (<code>fa-android</code>, plum <code>$highlightColor</code>, white 1px ring) at the bottom right from size s up; without a picture the robot icon on plum, sized to the avatar. Title/alt says the name and that it is an agent.</li><li>Styles in a new <code>app/styles/components/app-ui-avatar.scss</code>, imported in <code>app/styles/app.scss</code> on the line right after <code>@import \\"modules/agent.scss\\";</code>. Round (50%) is the only allowed radius. Do not edit <code>modules/agent.scss</code> page rules.</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>: rows person / person without image / agent with picture / agent without picture, columns xs-l; controls for size and \\"image fails\\". Do not edit <code>styles/components/developer-entry.scss</code> (another issue changes it).</li><li>Docs: <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-avatar.md</code> and the manifest <code>app-ui-avatar.json</code> (sizes, aliases, agent behaviour).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for each size, the alias, the image error fallback, agent with and without picture. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing pages or <code>Agent::Avatar</code> users elsewhere, initials avatars.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["avatar-tag-standards"]}, {"key": "tag", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::Tag: standard tag look (Task Board style), palette colours from text, removable", "description": "<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library. <code>AppUi::Tag</code> (<code>components/app-ui/tag.hbs</code>) is a bare <code>label label-&lt;variant&gt;</code> with no styles or manifest. Standardize it on the Task Board tag look. Scope is the component, its demo and docs only: do not change pages that use it, and do not change the board.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><p>Reference markup to copy the look from: <code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code> ~l.102-110 (<code>.badge.issue-type-tag</code>, <code>.info-tag</code>) with styles in <code>styles/modules/board.scss</code> ~l.432-446 and the colour in <code>milestones.js</code> <code>getIssueTypeTagStyle</code> ~l.509 (border + text in the colour, 16% tint behind).</p><ul><li>Look: 1px border and text in the variant colour, a 16% tint of it as background (<code>rgba()</code> of the variable in SCSS), 11px semibold, padding 2px 7px, square edges, 4px gap between tags, wraps in a row. Variants <code>default</code> (#ddd border, #444 text, #f9fafc), <code>primary</code>, <code>info</code>, <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>danger</code> from <code>app/styles/variables.scss</code> only.</li><li><code>@colorKey</code>: when set (and no <code>@variant</code>), pick the variant deterministically from the key (simple string hash over the five coloured variants), so the same text always gets the same palette colour. No ColorHash free colours.</li><li><code>@onRemove</code>: shows a small <code>fa-times</code> button inside the tag (grey, darker on hover, aria-label) that calls it.</li><li>Long text: max width with ellipsis and the full text in <code>title</code>.</li><li>Add <code>components/app-ui/tag.js</code> for the logic; styles in new <code>app/styles/components/app-ui-tag.scss</code>, imported in <code>app/styles/app.scss</code> on the line right after <code>@import 'components/dropdown.scss';</code>.</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/tag.{hbs,js}</code>: variants, colour from text, removable (logs <code>@onRemove</code>), a wrapping row with a long tag. Do not edit <code>developer-entry.scss</code>.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-tag.md</code> and a new manifest <code>app-ui-tag.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for variants, colorKey stability, onRemove, truncation title. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing the Task Board or other pages; status labels (<code>AppUi::StatusLabel</code>).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar"], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["avatar-tag-standards"]}, {"key": "dropdown", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::Dropdown: menu opens where it should (auto alignment) and standard menu colours", "description": "<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library. The Dropdown demo is broken: the menu does not appear where it should and the primary colour is overused. Fix the component, its demo and docs; do not change pages that use it (ezSearch keeps its own scoped overrides).</p><p>Today: <code>components/app-ui/dropdown.{hbs,js}</code>, styles <code>app/styles/components/dropdown.scss</code>: the menu is always <code>right: 0</code> (at a left edge it opens off-screen), items hover crimson with white text, <code>z-index: 99999</code>; the demo's <code>.active</code> item is plum (<code>styles/components/developer-entry.scss</code> ~l.29-68).</p><ul><li><code>@align</code>: <code>auto</code> (default), <code>start</code>, <code>end</code>. Start = menu's left edge on the trigger's left edge; end = right edges aligned. Auto measures on open: start when the menu fits in the viewport to the right, otherwise end; and opens upward when there is no room below. Re-measure on window resize while open.</li><li>Menu look = Bootstrap <code>dropdown-menu</code>: white, 1px <code>#ddd</code> border, square, items <code>#444</code> text, hover/focus <code>#f4f4f4</code> background with <code>#444</code> text (no crimson fill), a selected item (<code>.active</code> or <code>aria-selected</code>) shows crimson text + <code>fa-check</code>, no fill; dividers. <code>z-index</code> 1000. Keep the existing shadow, add none.</li><li>Trigger: <code>btn-default</code> unless <code>@isPrimary</code>; caret as today. Close on outside click and Escape; focus returns to the trigger.</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/dropdown.{hbs,js}</code> and its rules in <code>developer-entry.scss</code>: placement left / right edge, align control (auto/start/end), near the bottom (opens up), many items (scroll); remove the plum <code>.active</code> rule.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/dropdown.md</code> + new manifest <code>dropdown.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: at both edges and near the bottom the menu is fully visible; hover/selected colours as above; integration tests for align start/end, auto flip (stub sizes), Escape. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing ezSearch's or the board's dropdown overrides.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "selection-model", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "List selection model shared by DataTable and ListToolbar, kept across pages", "description": "<p>DataTable selection only knows the current page (<code>@selectedIds</code>/<code>@onSelect</code>/<code>@onSelectAll</code> in <code>components/app-ui/data-table.{hbs,js}</code>), and ListToolbar has no link to it. We need multi-page selection that the table and the toolbar share. This issue adds the model and DataTable support; the look and the toolbar are separate issues.</p><ul><li>New <code>app/utils/state/selection.js</code> class <code>Selection</code> (next to <code>AsyncResource</code>/<code>ListLoader</code>/<code>UrlState</code>): tracked set of ids (strings); <code>has(id)</code>, <code>toggle(id)</code>, <code>set(ids, on)</code>, <code>clear()</code>, <code>count</code>, <code>ids</code>, <code>stateFor(rows)</code> returning none|some|all for the given page rows, <code>countIn(rows)</code>. Kept across page changes; no totals (lists use limit+1 paging, see <code>docs/architecture/lists/decisions.md</code>), so no \\"select all matching\\".</li><li><code>AppUi::DataTable</code> takes <code>@selection</code> (a Selection): row toggles and the header select-all (current page) use it; <code>@onSelectionChange</code> fires with the ids. The existing <code>@selectedIds</code>/<code>@onSelect</code>/<code>@onSelectAll</code> keep working when <code>@selection</code> is not given.</li><li>Document it in <code>docs/architecture/state/</code> (one section) and in <code>public/ui-docs/data-table.md</code> + <code>data-table.json</code> (new args/events).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests for Selection; integration test: select on page 1, change rows (page 2), select, go back: page 1 rows still selected, count = both. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: checkbox look, toolbar selection bar, QuickList adopting it, select all matching.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "data-table-look", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::DataTable: QuickList selection look, standard row action icons, more-menu on AppUi::Dropdown", "description": "<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library. DataTable's select icons and selection colour don't match QuickList, and the row action icons' style, colour and size are inconsistent. Fix the component, give it its own demo and update the docs; do not change pages that use it.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><p>Reference markup to align with: QuickList row check <code>components/quick-list/row.hbs</code> (<code>button.quick-list__check</code> with <code>fa-square-o</code>/<code>fa-check-square</code>; styles <code>styles/components/quick-list.scss</code> ~l.155-175: unchecked <code>$mediumColor</code>, checked <code>$primaryColor</code>, selected row <code>#f9fafc</code>) and <code>QuickList::SelectAll</code> (already used in the header).</p><ul><li>Rows: replace the native checkbox with the same icon button as QuickList (same size, colours, aria-pressed); selected rows get the QuickList selected background. Header select-all shows none/some/all (<code>fa-square-o</code>/<code>fa-minus-square</code>/<code>fa-check-square</code>).</li><li>Row actions: one standard: icon-only <code>btn btn-box-tool</code> look (grey <code>$mediumColor</code>, <code>#444</code> on hover, 14px, square, title + aria-label), right-aligned, same gap; the more-actions button uses <code>fa-ellipsis-v</code> in the same style and opens its menu with <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> (<code>@align=\\"end\\"</code>) instead of the hand-made <code>.data-table-more-menu</code>.</li><li>Styles in <code>app/styles/components/app-ui-data-table.scss</code>.</li><li>Own demo <code>components/developer/demos/data-table.{hbs,js}</code> (columns, sort, groups, selection with a Selection across 3 fixture pages, row actions + more menu, empty state) and point the <code>data-table</code> entry in <code>utils/developer/component-registry.js</code> to it (the list-page demo stays for ListToolbar; do not edit it).</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/data-table.md</code> + <code>data-table.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for check icons/states, selected row class, action button classes, more-menu opens via AppUi::Dropdown. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: ListToolbar, changing list pages.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["selection-model", "dropdown"], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["list-toolbar-table"]}, {"key": "ez-search-narrow", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "EzSearch: icon-only Saved Searches, Builder, Search and Clear when its own box is narrow", "description": "<p>EzSearch (<code>components/ez-search/index.{hbs,js}</code>) only drops its button labels at the xs viewport (<code>hidden-xs</code>). Inside a narrow box (a list in a side column, ListToolbar with actions) the buttons eat the space and the input gets squeezed. The input must take priority. Scope: the component, its demo and docs.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li>New modifier <code>app/modifiers/observe-width.js</code> (ResizeObserver on the element, calls back with the width; cleans up on destroy; no-op where ResizeObserver is missing; the only current ResizeObserver use is <code>app-ui/gantt-chart.js</code> ~l.1034-1084 for reference). Reusable by ListToolbar later.</li><li>EzSearch measures its own root: below a threshold (start at 560px, constant in the component) it adds <code>ez-search--narrow</code>: Saved Searches shows <code>fa-bookmark</code> only (saved name in the title), Builder <code>fa-sliders</code> only, Search <code>fa-search</code> only, Clear <code>fa-times</code> only; every icon button keeps its title and aria-label. The input flexes and keeps a min width (about 160px). The existing xs behaviour stays.</li><li><code>@narrow</code> (true/false) forces the mode; when not given it is automatic.</li><li>Styles in <code>app/styles/components/ez-search.scss</code> (scoped under <code>.ez-search--narrow</code>).</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/ez-search.{hbs,js}</code>: a width control (full / 50% / 320px) to show the switch. Docs <code>public/ui-docs/ez-search.md</code> (+ manifest if present).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests: forced narrow shows icon-only buttons with titles; automatic switch with a stubbed width; modifier unit test. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: EzSearchCompact, ListToolbar, page changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["list-toolbar-table"]}, {"key": "list-toolbar", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::ListToolbar: selection bar tied to the list's selection, space-conscious search", "description": "<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library. <code>AppUi::ListToolbar</code> (<code>components/app-ui/list-toolbar.hbs</code>, styles <code>styles/components/app-ui-list-toolbar.scss</code>) leaves selection to the page (the demo <code>components/developer/demos/list-page.{hbs,js}</code> hand-rolls select-all, bulk buttons and \\"(Selected : N)\\" unrelated to the table) and gives the search no priority in small spaces. Fix the component, the list-page demo and the docs; do not change pages that use it.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li><code>@selection</code> (the <code>Selection</code> from <code>utils/state/selection.js</code>, the same instance passed to <code>AppUi::DataTable</code>) + <code>@rows</code> (current page rows): when <code>count &gt; 0</code> the toolbar shows a selection bar like <code>QuickList::SelectionBar</code> (<code>components/quick-list/selection-bar.hbs</code>; reuse its markup/classes or the component): tri-state select-all for the page, \\"N selected\\" + \\"X on this page, Y on other pages\\", <code>&lt;:bulkActions as |ids clear|&gt;</code>, a clear button. With nothing selected: the page select-all icon and a muted hint. The pager stays on the right. The old <code>&lt;:selection&gt;</code> block keeps working when <code>@selection</code> is not given.</li><li>Narrow mode: measure the toolbar with <code>modifiers/observe-width.js</code>; below the threshold pass <code>@narrow={{true}}</code> to the search (document that EzSearch goes in the search block) and yield <code>narrow</code> to <code>&lt;:actions as |narrow|&gt;</code> so callers can show icon-only buttons. The search block flexes first (min width), actions never push it below that; if still too narrow, actions wrap under it.</li><li>Demo <code>list-page</code>: one Selection shared by ListToolbar and DataTable across fixture pages, bulk actions log the ids, EzSearch in the search block with the saved-search wiring, a width control (full / col-md-4) to show narrow mode.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/list-toolbar.md</code> + <code>list-toolbar.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests: bar appears with the right counts across pages, bulk block gets ids, clear empties the selection, narrow passes @narrow and yields it to actions. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing Agents/Workflows list pages, select all matching.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["selection-model", "ez-search-narrow"], "milestone": "aga-Component Library", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["list-toolbar-table"]}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-15 23:02:55	2026-11-15 23:02:55	f
079bced76afa-79f5-7528-15badc67e35e	9fd531f66afa-e792-fe2e-e0480570c2cd	3	{"summary": "Extends the bulk client (aprom-4595) to more screens. Dashboard: each widget's metadata entry (views.Dashboard.widgets.<w>.{model, options}) is its registration; the route sends every visible widget's first load plus the statuses in one bulk call, and widgets keep fetching directly afterwards. A small service extension adds plain JSON GET items so the Active Milestones widget loads its N overviews in one bulk call instead of raw fetches. Gantt, the Agent page, the Workflow list and the Project overview each move their independent queries into bulk rounds. All issues depend on aprom-4595 and can run in parallel, except the overview widget, which needs the plain JSON items. All in milestone aga-Cleanup.", "issues": [{"key": "dashboard-bulk", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Dashboard: widgets register their first load through metadata and load in one bulk request", "description": "<p>The dashboard route loads the issue statuses and then each widget's first query one at a time (<code>app/routes/app/index.js</code> ~l.61-83, a <code>for … await</code> loop), so load time grows with every widget. Dashboards will soon be customizable and have more widgets, so the set of calls has to follow the widgets the user actually shows. Use the bulk service (aprom-4595) and make each widget's metadata entry its registration for the first load.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Registration contract: a widget registers its first load by declaring <code>model</code> + <code>options</code> in <code>views.Dashboard.widgets.&lt;name&gt;</code> (<code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> ~l.592; already the format, keep it). A widget without a declaration loads itself. Write this contract into a short doc under <code>docs/architecture/</code> (the bulk doc from aprom-4595).</li><li><code>routes/app/index.js</code>: after <code>_getValidWidgets</code> (the user's list, <code>currentUser.user.dashboard.widgets</code>), build one <code>bulk.query</code> with the system issue statuses item plus one item per visible widget that declares a load (options as prepared by <code>_getWidgetSettings</code>). Map results back to <code>widgetResults[widget]</code>.</li><li>A failed item gives that widget an empty result and goes through <code>errorManager.handleError</code>. The other widgets render. The service splits batches over the limit.</li><li>Widgets keep fetching directly after the first load (paging, week switching, refresh in <code>components/widgets/*.js</code>). Don't change them.</li><li>Acceptance: extend a dashboard feature (e.g. <code>tests/acceptance/dashboard/active-milestones/check-list-of-milestones.feature</code> or <code>tolerate-invalid-widgets.feature</code>) to cover the bulk path, including one widget whose item fails.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> opening the dashboard makes one <code>POST /bulk</code> for the statuses and all widget first loads, and no per-widget GET. A user with a different widget list gets a batch with only their widgets. Unknown widgets are still dropped as today.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the customizable dashboard itself, the milestone overviews (separate issue), runtime (same-tick) batching.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4595"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "bulk-json-overviews", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Bulk service: plain JSON GET items; Active Milestones loads its overviews in one bulk request", "description": "<p>The Active Milestones widget loads one milestone overview per milestone with raw <code>fetch</code> and a hand-passed token (<code>app/utils/milestone-overview-api.js</code> <code>fetchMilestoneOverview</code>/<code>fetchMilestoneOverviewsBulk</code>, called from <code>components/widgets/active-milestones.js</code> ~l.72-110). That is N requests and it bypasses the adapter's token refresh (house rule: no raw fetch). Overviews are not Ember Data records, so the bulk service (aprom-4595) needs plain JSON items.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>services/bulk.js</code>: also accept <code>{id, url}</code> items (a relative <code>/api/v1/...</code> GET). They return <code>{status, body}</code> with the parsed JSON instead of records and are never pushed to the store. The fallback for a failed bulk call runs them through the adapter's <code>ajax</code>.</li><li><code>milestone-overview-api.js</code>: replace the raw fetches with one <code>bulk.query</code> of overview items (same URL as <code>buildMilestoneOverviewUrl</code>). Keep the return shape <code>[{id, overview}]</code> with <code>null</code> for failures. Drop the token argument.</li><li><code>active-milestones.js</code>: call it without the token, for both the first load and \\"load more\\" (<code>merge: true</code>).</li><li>Unit tests for the plain JSON items and the util. Mirage: the <code>/bulk</code> handler answers overview GETs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> the widget shows the same overviews with one <code>POST /bulk</code> per load or load more, and no <code>GET /milestoneoverview</code> calls. A failed overview shows as today (null).</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> non-GET plain items.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4595"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gantt-bulk", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Gantt: load all milestone lanes in one bulk request", "description": "<p>The Gantt route loads the active milestones and then one issue query per milestone (<code>app/routes/app/project/gantt.js</code> ~l.90-124), the same pattern the Task Board had (aprom-4596). Use the bulk service (aprom-4595) for the per-milestone queries.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Keep the milestones query (it decides the lanes). Then send one <code>bulk.query</code> with one item per milestone: the same query string (including the ezSearch <code>searchQuery</code> AND), rels and limit as today. Then <code>replaceRecords(milestone.issues, records)</code>.</li><li>A failed lane goes through <code>errorManager.handleError</code> and stays empty. Timeline bounds and <code>loadSearchData</code> (~l.152) stay unchanged.</li><li>Extend <code>tests/acceptance/gantt/gantt-search.feature</code> (or a Gantt render feature) to run through the Mirage <code>/bulk</code> handler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> opening the Gantt chart makes one milestones GET and one <code>POST /bulk</code>, and no per-milestone <code>GET /issue</code>. Lanes, search and the timeline behave as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the controller's reloads and Hermes refreshes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4595"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "agent-page-bulk", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Agent page: load the agent's related data in one bulk request", "description": "<p>The agent page route loads the agent and then 9 queries in parallel (<code>app/routes/app/agent/page.js</code> ~l.30-54: userroles, memberships, identities, tool grants, skill grants, tools, tool servers, skills, activities). That is more than the browser runs at once over HTTP/1.1, so some of them wait. Use the bulk service (aprom-4595).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Keep the agent query. Replace the <code>Promise.all</code> of 9 queries with one <code>bulk.query</code> using the same options, mapping results to the same variables.</li><li>Keep today's error behaviour for the page (a failing item is handled like the failing query today).</li><li>Make the agent page acceptance test go through the Mirage <code>/bulk</code> handler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> the agent page makes one agent GET and one <code>POST /bulk</code>, and every box shows the same data as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the agent create, edit, tools and skills routes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4595"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "workflow-list-bulk", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow list: load nodes, runs, agents and projects in bulk rounds", "description": "<p>The workflow list route loads its extra data one query after another (<code>app/routes/app/workflow/index.js</code> ~l.80-118: saved searches, nodes, runs, then agents and projects for the ids found). Group the queries that don't depend on each other into bulk rounds with the bulk service (aprom-4595).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Round 1 (after the workflow list, which gives the ids): saved searches, nodes (<code>anyOf('Workflownode', 'workflowId', ids)</code>) and runs in one <code>bulk.query</code>.</li><li>Round 2: agents and projects (ids from round 1) in one <code>bulk.query</code>, skipped when both id lists are empty.</li><li>The same options and results as today. A failed item leaves that list empty, as the current catches do.</li><li>Make <code>tests/acceptance/workflows/workflows-list.feature</code> go through the Mirage <code>/bulk</code> handler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> after the list GET the page makes at most two <code>POST /bulk</code> calls, and the list columns show the same data.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the workflow page and editor.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4595"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "project-overview-bulk", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project overview: load project, milestones, activities, issues and conversations in one bulk request", "description": "<p>The project overview route sends 5 queries in parallel (<code>app/routes/app/project/index.js</code> ~l.97-102: project, milestones, activities, issues, conversation rooms). Use the bulk service (aprom-4595) to send them as one request.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Replace the <code>hashSettled</code> of 5 queries with one <code>bulk.query</code> using the same options. Keep the settled semantics: a failed item gives that box its current failure state, and the others render.</li><li>Make the project overview acceptance test go through the Mirage <code>/bulk</code> handler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> the overview makes one <code>POST /bulk</code> instead of 5 GETs, and every box shows the same data.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the parent <code>routes/app/project.js</code> loads.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4595"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 09:55:19	2026-11-16 09:55:19	f
e871c6e16afa-b491-52a3-c3a741a14dec	5aa975066afa-b491-52a3-8ddda4f295d5	1	{"summary": "Bulk API in Gaia, three chained issues. (1) Separate building the error response from sending it, so an error can become one item's result instead of ending the whole request. (2) An in-process sub-request runner that dispatches one REST call through the normal router, controller, authentication and ACL, with its own Request and Response, and returns its status and body without sending anything. (3) The `bulk` resource (POST /api/v1/bulk, never stored): it validates the batch, runs every item through the runner in order and returns one result per item. Items are isolated, so a failing item affects only its own result. Left out: all-or-nothing mode, cross-item references, parallel execution and the Prometheus client.", "issues": [{"key": "error-responses", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Exceptions: build the error response without sending it (toResponse), handle() sends it", "description": "<p>The Bulk API (POST /api/v1/bulk, a later issue) runs several REST calls in one request. Each one's error must come back as that item's result. Today every <code>Gaia\\\\Exception\\\\*</code> class in <code>core/exceptions/</code> builds its error response in <code>handle()</code> and calls <code>send()</code> immediately, and <code>public/index.php</code> (~l.234-264) relies on that. As a result, the first failing item would end the whole batch.</p><ul><li>Give every exception class in <code>core/exceptions/</code> (Access, BadRequest, Exception, FileNotFound, InvalidGrant, MigrationDriver, Permission, ResourceLocked, ResourceNotFound, TooManyRequests, UnAuthorized) a <code>toResponse(): \\\\Phalcon\\\\Http\\\\Response</code>. It builds the same status, headers (e.g. Retry-After on TooManyRequests, WWW-Authenticate where set) and JSON body that <code>handle()</code> builds today, without sending anything.</li><li><code>handle()</code> becomes <code>toResponse()-&gt;send()</code>. The HTTP output of a normal request stays byte for byte the same.</li><li>Put the shared part (a new Response with status and JSON error) in one place, e.g. a protected helper on a common base or a small <code>ErrorResponse</code> builder, so the classes don't repeat it.</li><li>Unit tests: <code>toResponse()</code> returns the expected status and body for each class and sends nothing (headers not sent, no output).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> all existing api-tester and phpunit suites pass unchanged, and every Gaia exception can produce its response object without sending it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>\\\\Phalcon\\\\Exception</code> branch in <code>index.php</code> (agaia-4251 covers JSON for Phalcon exceptions), and any change to error messages or status codes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 13, "sizeReason": "The same mechanical change has to land in all 11 exception classes at once, plus one shared helper and one test file. Splitting it would leave some exceptions still sending their response directly.", "screens": []}, {"key": "sub-request-runner", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Framework: in-process sub-request runner (one REST call dispatched with its own Request/Response, result captured, not sent)", "description": "<p>The Bulk API needs to run an ordinary REST call (method, URL with query, JSON body) inside the current PHP request. The call must go through the normal router, <code>RestController</code>, authentication and ACL, and give back its status and body without writing anything to the client. Today the code assumes one request per process: <code>public/index.php</code> calls <code>Phalcon\\\\Mvc\\\\Application::handle()</code> once, <code>RestController</code> reads <code>request-&gt;getJsonRawBody()</code> / <code>getQuery()</code> / the method from the DI <code>request</code>, and <code>authorize()</code> sets <code>$GLOBALS['currentUser']</code>.</p><ul><li>New domain-side class (e.g. <code>core/libs/http/SubRequestRunner.php</code>): <code>run(string $method, string $url, ?array $body, string $authorization): SubResult</code>. <code>SubResult</code> holds the status, the decoded body and the duration in ms.</li><li>For each call, register a fresh request object in the DI (a <code>Phalcon\\\\Http\\\\Request</code> subclass that returns the given method, URI, query parameters, raw/JSON body and Authorization header instead of reading superglobals and php://input), and a fresh <code>response</code>. Dispatch through the existing router/dispatcher (<code>core/mvc/Router.php</code>). Restore the outer request, response and <code>$GLOBALS['currentUser']</code> afterwards, also when the call throws.</li><li>Catch <code>Gaia\\\\Exception\\\\*</code> and turn it into the result with <code>toResponse()</code> (from the error-responses issue). Any other <code>Throwable</code> becomes a 500 with a generic error. Log it, and never put a stack trace in the body. One call's failure must not leak state into the next call.</li><li>Every call runs the full authentication and ACL check of the target action with the caller's token. Nothing in the runner skips or weakens authorization.</li><li>Unit tests (fake controller/route): success, 404 route, Gaia exception -&gt; its status, unexpected exception -&gt; 500, state restored between consecutive calls, query and body passed correctly. Add a short note under <code>docs/architecture/</code> (new <code>bulk/decisions.md</code>) on why sub-requests run in-process and sequentially.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two consecutive <code>run()</code> calls in one PHP process (e.g. GET /api/v1/issue?query=... and a PATCH that fails ACL) return the same status and body as the separate HTTP calls, and nothing is sent to the client.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>bulk</code> resource and its validation (next issue), parallel execution, transactions.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["error-responses"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "bulk-resource", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Bulk API: `bulk` resource (POST /api/v1/bulk) runs up to N REST calls, one result per call", "description": "<p>Screens like the Task Board and Dashboard need several Gaia calls whose shape is known in advance. Sending them one by one costs a network round trip each. This adds a CRUD resource <code>bulk</code> (POST only, never stored, like other non-persisted resources such as agentspec) that runs a batch of REST calls with the sub-request runner and returns every result. A failing call affects only its own result.</p><ul><li><strong>Request:</strong> <code>{\\"requests\\": [{\\"id\\": \\"lanes\\", \\"method\\": \\"GET\\", \\"url\\": \\"/api/v1/issue?query=...\\", \\"body\\": null}, ...]}</code>. <code>id</code> is a client string, unique within the batch. <code>method</code> is GET, POST, PATCH or DELETE. <code>body</code> is optional JSON.</li><li><strong>Response 200:</strong> <code>{\\"responses\\": [{\\"id\\": \\"lanes\\", \\"status\\": 200, \\"body\\": {...}, \\"durationMs\\": 12}, {\\"id\\": \\"x\\", \\"status\\": 403, \\"body\\": {\\"error\\": \\"...\\"}, \\"durationMs\\": 3}]}</code>, in request order.</li><li><strong>Execution:</strong> items run sequentially in the order sent, through <code>SubRequestRunner</code>, with the caller's Authorization header. There is no rollback: a successful write stays even if a later item fails. Live events and other side effects behave as for separate calls.</li><li><strong>Batch validation</strong> (400 and nothing runs if any check fails): <code>requests</code> is a non-empty array; at most <code>BULK_MAX_REQUESTS</code> items (default 25, read via <code>getenv()</code> in a <code>config/bulk.php</code>); the request body stays under a size limit (config); ids are unique; every URL is a relative <code>/api/v1/&lt;resource&gt;...</code> path that the router resolves. Refused: <code>/api/v1/bulk</code> itself (no nesting), OAuth/token, unauthenticated routes and the streaming endpoints (upload file streams, download, preview).</li><li><strong>Security:</strong> the bulk call itself needs a valid token and the <code>bulk.create</code> permission (ACL metadata, no permission seed: the reviewer grants it). Every item is then authorized on its own exactly like a direct call, so a batch can never do more than its separate calls. Log one line per batch (user, item count, statuses, total time), never bodies.</li><li>Keep the controller thin: request parsing and response shaping in <code>BulkController</code>; batch validation in its own class (e.g. <code>core/libs/http/BulkRequestValidator.php</code>); execution in a small service that loops over the runner.</li><li><strong>Tests:</strong> phpunit for the validator, plus api-tester cases. Acl: no token -&gt; 401; no bulk.create -&gt; 403. Behaviour: mixed success + 404 + 403 items each return their own status; a write followed by a failing item keeps the write; too many items / nested bulk / unknown route -&gt; 400.</li><li>Extend <code>docs/architecture/bulk/decisions.md</code> with the contract, the limits and the no-rollback decision; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a Task Board-style batch (milestones, issues of a milestone, statuses) returns all three results in one call. One item without permission returns 403 and the others still return 200.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> all-or-nothing mode, references between items (<code>$ref</code>), parallel execution, the Prometheus client.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["sub-request-runner"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-15 23:06:16	2026-11-15 23:10:03	f
e3a3fbd46afa-c6cf-7528-996e85fe6d52	9fd531f66afa-e792-fe2e-e0480570c2cd	2	{"summary": "Extends the bulk client (aprom-4595) to more screens. Dashboard: each widget's metadata entry (views.Dashboard.widgets.<w>.{model, options}) is its registration; the route sends every visible widget's first load plus the statuses in one bulk call, and widgets keep fetching directly afterwards. A small service extension adds plain JSON GET items so the Active Milestones widget loads its N overviews in one bulk call instead of raw fetches. Gantt, the Agent page, the Workflow list and the Project overview each move their independent queries into bulk rounds. All issues depend on aprom-4595 and can run in parallel, except the overview widget, which needs the plain JSON items.", "issues": [{"key": "dashboard-bulk", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Dashboard: widgets register their first load through metadata and load in one bulk request", "description": "<p>The dashboard route loads the issue statuses and then each widget's first query one at a time (<code>app/routes/app/index.js</code> ~l.61-83, a <code>for … await</code> loop), so load time grows with every widget. Dashboards will soon be customizable and have more widgets, so the set of calls has to follow the widgets the user actually shows. Use the bulk service (aprom-4595) and make each widget's metadata entry its registration for the first load.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Registration contract: a widget registers its first load by declaring <code>model</code> + <code>options</code> in <code>views.Dashboard.widgets.&lt;name&gt;</code> (<code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> ~l.592; already the format, keep it). A widget without a declaration loads itself. Write this contract into a short doc under <code>docs/architecture/</code> (the bulk doc from aprom-4595).</li><li><code>routes/app/index.js</code>: after <code>_getValidWidgets</code> (the user's list, <code>currentUser.user.dashboard.widgets</code>), build one <code>bulk.query</code> with the system issue statuses item plus one item per visible widget that declares a load (options as prepared by <code>_getWidgetSettings</code>). Map results back to <code>widgetResults[widget]</code>.</li><li>A failed item gives that widget an empty result and goes through <code>errorManager.handleError</code>. The other widgets render. The service splits batches over the limit.</li><li>Widgets keep fetching directly after the first load (paging, week switching, refresh in <code>components/widgets/*.js</code>). Don't change them.</li><li>Acceptance: extend a dashboard feature (e.g. <code>tests/acceptance/dashboard/active-milestones/check-list-of-milestones.feature</code> or <code>tolerate-invalid-widgets.feature</code>) to cover the bulk path, including one widget whose item fails.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> opening the dashboard makes one <code>POST /bulk</code> for the statuses and all widget first loads, and no per-widget GET. A user with a different widget list gets a batch with only their widgets. Unknown widgets are still dropped as today.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the customizable dashboard itself, the milestone overviews (separate issue), runtime (same-tick) batching.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4595"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "bulk-json-overviews", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Bulk service: plain JSON GET items; Active Milestones loads its overviews in one bulk request", "description": "<p>The Active Milestones widget loads one milestone overview per milestone with raw <code>fetch</code> and a hand-passed token (<code>app/utils/milestone-overview-api.js</code> <code>fetchMilestoneOverview</code>/<code>fetchMilestoneOverviewsBulk</code>, called from <code>components/widgets/active-milestones.js</code> ~l.72-110). That is N requests and it bypasses the adapter's token refresh (house rule: no raw fetch). Overviews are not Ember Data records, so the bulk service (aprom-4595) needs plain JSON items.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>services/bulk.js</code>: also accept <code>{id, url}</code> items (a relative <code>/api/v1/...</code> GET). They return <code>{status, body}</code> with the parsed JSON instead of records and are never pushed to the store. The fallback for a failed bulk call runs them through the adapter's <code>ajax</code>.</li><li><code>milestone-overview-api.js</code>: replace the raw fetches with one <code>bulk.query</code> of overview items (same URL as <code>buildMilestoneOverviewUrl</code>). Keep the return shape <code>[{id, overview}]</code> with <code>null</code> for failures. Drop the token argument.</li><li><code>active-milestones.js</code>: call it without the token, for both the first load and \\"load more\\" (<code>merge: true</code>).</li><li>Unit tests for the plain JSON items and the util. Mirage: the <code>/bulk</code> handler answers overview GETs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> the widget shows the same overviews with one <code>POST /bulk</code> per load or load more, and no <code>GET /milestoneoverview</code> calls. A failed overview shows as today (null).</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> non-GET plain items.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4595"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gantt-bulk", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Gantt: load all milestone lanes in one bulk request", "description": "<p>The Gantt route loads the active milestones and then one issue query per milestone (<code>app/routes/app/project/gantt.js</code> ~l.90-124), the same pattern the Task Board had (aprom-4596). Use the bulk service (aprom-4595) for the per-milestone queries.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Keep the milestones query (it decides the lanes). Then send one <code>bulk.query</code> with one item per milestone: the same query string (including the ezSearch <code>searchQuery</code> AND), rels and limit as today. Then <code>replaceRecords(milestone.issues, records)</code>.</li><li>A failed lane goes through <code>errorManager.handleError</code> and stays empty. Timeline bounds and <code>loadSearchData</code> (~l.152) stay unchanged.</li><li>Extend <code>tests/acceptance/gantt/gantt-search.feature</code> (or a Gantt render feature) to run through the Mirage <code>/bulk</code> handler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> opening the Gantt chart makes one milestones GET and one <code>POST /bulk</code>, and no per-milestone <code>GET /issue</code>. Lanes, search and the timeline behave as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the controller's reloads and Hermes refreshes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4595"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "agent-page-bulk", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Agent page: load the agent's related data in one bulk request", "description": "<p>The agent page route loads the agent and then 9 queries in parallel (<code>app/routes/app/agent/page.js</code> ~l.30-54: userroles, memberships, identities, tool grants, skill grants, tools, tool servers, skills, activities). That is more than the browser runs at once over HTTP/1.1, so some of them wait. Use the bulk service (aprom-4595).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Keep the agent query. Replace the <code>Promise.all</code> of 9 queries with one <code>bulk.query</code> using the same options, mapping results to the same variables.</li><li>Keep today's error behaviour for the page (a failing item is handled like the failing query today).</li><li>Make the agent page acceptance test go through the Mirage <code>/bulk</code> handler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> the agent page makes one agent GET and one <code>POST /bulk</code>, and every box shows the same data as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the agent create, edit, tools and skills routes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4595"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "workflow-list-bulk", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Workflow list: load nodes, runs, agents and projects in bulk rounds", "description": "<p>The workflow list route loads its extra data one query after another (<code>app/routes/app/workflow/index.js</code> ~l.80-118: saved searches, nodes, runs, then agents and projects for the ids found). Group the queries that don't depend on each other into bulk rounds with the bulk service (aprom-4595).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Round 1 (after the workflow list, which gives the ids): saved searches, nodes (<code>anyOf('Workflownode', 'workflowId', ids)</code>) and runs in one <code>bulk.query</code>.</li><li>Round 2: agents and projects (ids from round 1) in one <code>bulk.query</code>, skipped when both id lists are empty.</li><li>The same options and results as today. A failed item leaves that list empty, as the current catches do.</li><li>Make <code>tests/acceptance/workflows/workflows-list.feature</code> go through the Mirage <code>/bulk</code> handler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> after the list GET the page makes at most two <code>POST /bulk</code> calls, and the list columns show the same data.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the workflow page and editor.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4595"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "project-overview-bulk", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project overview: load project, milestones, activities, issues and conversations in one bulk request", "description": "<p>The project overview route sends 5 queries in parallel (<code>app/routes/app/project/index.js</code> ~l.97-102: project, milestones, activities, issues, conversation rooms). Use the bulk service (aprom-4595) to send them as one request.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Replace the <code>hashSettled</code> of 5 queries with one <code>bulk.query</code> using the same options. Keep the settled semantics: a failed item gives that box its current failure state, and the others render.</li><li>Make the project overview acceptance test go through the Mirage <code>/bulk</code> handler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> the overview makes one <code>POST /bulk</code> instead of 5 GETs, and every box shows the same data.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the parent <code>routes/app/project.js</code> loads.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4595"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 09:46:11	2026-11-16 09:56:25	f
0f48bdd16afa-23c6-fe2e-3be5b114f3d3	9fd531f66afa-e792-fe2e-e0480570c2cd	1	{"summary": "Prometheus gets a reusable bulk client service on top of Gaia's POST /api/v1/bulk (agaia-4587): it batches store queries into one request, pushes the results into the store, splits batches larger than the server limit, and falls back to separate queries when the bulk call itself fails. The Task Board route then loads its data in two bulk rounds (milestones + backlog + statuses, then every milestone's issues) instead of 3 + N requests. The board issue depends on the client.", "issues": [{"key": "bulk-client", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Data layer: bulk query service that batches store queries into one POST /api/v1/bulk", "description": "<p>Gaia now has a <code>bulk</code> resource (agaia-4587) that runs several REST calls in one request. Screens that make many independent queries (Task Board first, later Dashboard and Gantt) pay one network round trip per query today. This adds a reusable client so routes can batch their queries and still get ordinary Ember Data records.</p><p><strong>Gaia contract</strong> (see <code>gaia/docs/architecture/bulk/decisions.md</code>): <code>POST /api/v1/bulk</code> with <code>{\\"requests\\": [{\\"id\\": \\"lane-1\\", \\"method\\": \\"GET\\", \\"url\\": \\"/api/v1/issue?query=...&amp;rels=...&amp;limit=-1\\", \\"body\\": null}]}</code> returns 200 <code>{\\"responses\\": [{\\"id\\", \\"status\\", \\"body\\", \\"durationMs\\"}]}</code> in request order. There can be at most 25 items (BULK_MAX_REQUESTS). The call needs the <code>bulk.create</code> permission, and each item is authorized like a direct call.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New service <code>app/services/bulk.js</code> with <code>query(items)</code>, where each item is <code>{id, modelName, query}</code> and <code>query</code> is the same options object passed to <code>store.query</code> (<code>query</code>, <code>rels</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>order</code>, <code>limit</code>). It returns a map id → <code>{records}</code> or <code>{error}</code>.</li><li>Build each item's URL with the model's adapter (<code>buildURL</code>/<code>urlForQuery</code>, serialized query params), so it matches what <code>store.query</code> sends, made relative as <code>/api/v1/...</code>.</li><li>Send the batch through the application adapter's <code>ajax</code> (<code>app/adapters/application.js</code> ~l.256) so token refresh, the 401 retry and the test waiter apply. No raw <code>fetch</code>.</li><li>For each 2xx item, normalize the body with <code>store.serializerFor(modelName).normalizeResponse(store, modelClass, body, null, 'query')</code> and <code>store.push</code> it. Non-2xx items become an <code>error</code> for that id only.</li><li>Split batches above the limit into several bulk calls (limit in <code>config/environment.js</code> <code>ENV.APP.bulkMaxRequests</code>, default 25) and merge the results.</li><li>Fallback: when the bulk call itself fails (403 because the role lacks <code>bulk.create</code>, network error, non-200), run the items as separate <code>store.query</code> calls in parallel and return the same shape. Log one warning.</li><li>Mirage: a <code>/bulk</code> POST handler that answers each GET item with the same data the existing Mirage handlers return for that resource (at least <code>issue</code>, <code>milestone</code>, <code>issuestatus</code>).</li><li>A short doc section in <code>docs/architecture/</code> (a new <code>bulk/</code> folder) on when to use the service and the fallback.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests: URL building matches <code>store.query</code>, results land in the store, one failing item doesn't affect the others, more than 25 items are split, and a failed or 403 bulk call falls back to separate queries.</li><li>Lint and the full test suite pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> writes (POST/PATCH/DELETE items), using it on any screen (separate issues), milestone overviews.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "board-bulk", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Task Board: load milestones, backlog, statuses and milestone lanes in two bulk requests", "description": "<p>The Task Board route makes 3 + N requests: active milestones, backlog issues and issue statuses one after another, then one issue query per milestone. With many active milestones this adds visible latency. Switch it to the <code>bulk</code> service (the bulk-client issue) so the board loads in two requests.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong> in <code>app/routes/app/project/board.js</code> <code>model</code> (~l.61-131):</p><ul><li>Round 1, one <code>bulk.query</code>: the milestones query (l.67-72), the backlog issues query (l.80-88, including the ezSearch <code>searchQuery</code> AND) and the project's issue statuses (l.92-95). Same query strings, rels, sort and limits as today.</li><li>Round 2, one <code>bulk.query</code> with one item per returned milestone (the per-milestone query of l.99-112, with <code>searchQuery</code>), then <code>replaceRecords(milestone.issues, records)</code> as today.</li><li>Keep today's error handling: a failed item goes through <code>errorManager.handleError</code> (with <code>moduleName: 'milestone'</code> for the milestones item), and a failed lane shows as empty instead of breaking the board. Backlog milestone creation (<code>getBacklogMilestone</code>), <code>afterModel</code> (system statuses fallback, sort) and <code>loadSearchData</code> stay unchanged.</li><li>Extend the board's acceptance coverage (e.g. <code>tests/acceptance/taskboard/render-milestone.feature</code>) so it runs through the Mirage <code>/bulk</code> handler and checks that lanes and backlog render as before, including with an ezSearch query applied.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Opening the board makes two <code>POST /bulk</code> requests and no per-milestone <code>GET /issue</code> (verify in the running app's network tab).</li><li>Lanes, backlog, status columns, filtering and live updates behave as before.</li><li>If the user's role lacks <code>bulk.create</code>, the board still loads (service fallback).</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the controller's own reloads (<code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> ~l.1119), Hermes-driven refreshes, Dashboard and Gantt.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["bulk-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 02:06:07	2026-11-16 02:09:27	f
39b501316afa-fe7f-5cb2-49d87769d595	ded9f4396af0-2b69-3bb7-c36bdb48cfdf	3	{"summary": "Finalize five core components of the Component Library without touching their users: Avatar (standard sizes, default image, person vs agent) -> Tag (Task Board look, palette colours, removable); Dropdown (auto alignment, Bootstrap menu look); a shared selection model that lets DataTable keep a selection across pages -> DataTable look (QuickList checkboxes and selected rows, standard action icons, more-menu on AppUi::Dropdown); EzSearch icon-only buttons when its own box is narrow; then ListToolbar ties a built-in selection bar to the list's selection and gives the search room in narrow spaces. Each issue updates the component's demo, ui-docs page and manifest (design-system R6). Parallel issues never share a file. All in milestone aga-Cleanup.", "issues": [{"key": "avatar", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::Avatar: standard sizes xs/s/m/l, default image, person vs agent", "description": "<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library (Developer -&gt; Components). <code>AppUi::Avatar</code> needs standard sizes, a default image and a clear person vs agent look. Scope is the component, its demo and its docs only: do not change pages that use it (if a page then looks different, that is accepted).</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><p>Today: <code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code> renders <code>Agent::UserAvatar</code> (<code>components/agent/user-avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, uses the <code>agentDirectory</code> service) with AdminLTE <code>img-circle</code> + <code>img-sm</code>/<code>img-xs</code>; with no size the image shows at its file size; a missing image is broken; for an agent it renders <code>Agent::Avatar</code> without <code>@user</code> (so an agent's own picture never shows) and without the size.</p><ul><li><code>@size</code>: <code>xs</code> 20px, <code>s</code> 30px, <code>m</code> 40px (default), <code>l</code> 96px; <code>sm</code> stays an alias of <code>s</code>. Unknown values fall back to m.</li><li>Person: the user image (<code>/userimage/get/&lt;id&gt;</code>); when there is no id or the image fails to load (<code>error</code> event), show <code>/img/default.png</code> at the same size (see <code>isDefaultProfilePicture</code> in <code>models/user.js</code>). Never a broken image.</li><li>Agent: pass the user to <code>Agent::Avatar</code> so its picture shows; with a picture add a small round robot marker (<code>fa-android</code>, plum <code>$highlightColor</code>, white 1px ring) at the bottom right from size s up; without a picture the robot icon on plum, sized to the avatar. Title/alt says the name and that it is an agent.</li><li>Styles in a new <code>app/styles/components/app-ui-avatar.scss</code>, imported in <code>app/styles/app.scss</code> on the line right after <code>@import \\"modules/agent.scss\\";</code>. Round (50%) is the only allowed radius. Do not edit <code>modules/agent.scss</code> page rules.</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>: rows person / person without image / agent with picture / agent without picture, columns xs-l; controls for size and \\"image fails\\". Do not edit <code>styles/components/developer-entry.scss</code> (another issue changes it).</li><li>Docs: <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-avatar.md</code> and the manifest <code>app-ui-avatar.json</code> (sizes, aliases, agent behaviour).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for each size, the alias, the image error fallback, agent with and without picture. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing pages or <code>Agent::Avatar</code> users elsewhere, initials avatars.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["avatar-tag-standards"]}, {"key": "tag", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::Tag: standard tag look (Task Board style), palette colours from text, removable", "description": "<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library. <code>AppUi::Tag</code> (<code>components/app-ui/tag.hbs</code>) is a bare <code>label label-&lt;variant&gt;</code> with no styles or manifest. Standardize it on the Task Board tag look. Scope is the component, its demo and docs only: do not change pages that use it, and do not change the board.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><p>Reference markup to copy the look from: <code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code> ~l.102-110 (<code>.badge.issue-type-tag</code>, <code>.info-tag</code>) with styles in <code>styles/modules/board.scss</code> ~l.432-446 and the colour in <code>milestones.js</code> <code>getIssueTypeTagStyle</code> ~l.509 (border + text in the colour, 16% tint behind).</p><ul><li>Look: 1px border and text in the variant colour, a 16% tint of it as background (<code>rgba()</code> of the variable in SCSS), 11px semibold, padding 2px 7px, square edges, 4px gap between tags, wraps in a row. Variants <code>default</code> (#ddd border, #444 text, #f9fafc), <code>primary</code>, <code>info</code>, <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>danger</code> from <code>app/styles/variables.scss</code> only.</li><li><code>@colorKey</code>: when set (and no <code>@variant</code>), pick the variant deterministically from the key (simple string hash over the five coloured variants), so the same text always gets the same palette colour. No ColorHash free colours.</li><li><code>@onRemove</code>: shows a small <code>fa-times</code> button inside the tag (grey, darker on hover, aria-label) that calls it.</li><li>Long text: max width with ellipsis and the full text in <code>title</code>.</li><li>Add <code>components/app-ui/tag.js</code> for the logic; styles in new <code>app/styles/components/app-ui-tag.scss</code>, imported in <code>app/styles/app.scss</code> on the line right after <code>@import 'components/dropdown.scss';</code>.</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/tag.{hbs,js}</code>: variants, colour from text, removable (logs <code>@onRemove</code>), a wrapping row with a long tag. Do not edit <code>developer-entry.scss</code>.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-tag.md</code> and a new manifest <code>app-ui-tag.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for variants, colorKey stability, onRemove, truncation title. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing the Task Board or other pages; status labels (<code>AppUi::StatusLabel</code>).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["avatar-tag-standards"]}, {"key": "dropdown", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::Dropdown: menu opens where it should (auto alignment) and standard menu colours", "description": "<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library. The Dropdown demo is broken: the menu does not appear where it should and the primary colour is overused. Fix the component, its demo and docs; do not change pages that use it (ezSearch keeps its own scoped overrides).</p><p>Today: <code>components/app-ui/dropdown.{hbs,js}</code>, styles <code>app/styles/components/dropdown.scss</code>: the menu is always <code>right: 0</code> (at a left edge it opens off-screen), items hover crimson with white text, <code>z-index: 99999</code>; the demo's <code>.active</code> item is plum (<code>styles/components/developer-entry.scss</code> ~l.29-68).</p><ul><li><code>@align</code>: <code>auto</code> (default), <code>start</code>, <code>end</code>. Start = menu's left edge on the trigger's left edge; end = right edges aligned. Auto measures on open: start when the menu fits in the viewport to the right, otherwise end; and opens upward when there is no room below. Re-measure on window resize while open.</li><li>Menu look = Bootstrap <code>dropdown-menu</code>: white, 1px <code>#ddd</code> border, square, items <code>#444</code> text, hover/focus <code>#f4f4f4</code> background with <code>#444</code> text (no crimson fill), a selected item (<code>.active</code> or <code>aria-selected</code>) shows crimson text + <code>fa-check</code>, no fill; dividers. <code>z-index</code> 1000. Keep the existing shadow, add none.</li><li>Trigger: <code>btn-default</code> unless <code>@isPrimary</code>; caret as today. Close on outside click and Escape; focus returns to the trigger.</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/dropdown.{hbs,js}</code> and its rules in <code>developer-entry.scss</code>: placement left / right edge, align control (auto/start/end), near the bottom (opens up), many items (scroll); remove the plum <code>.active</code> rule.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/dropdown.md</code> + new manifest <code>dropdown.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: at both edges and near the bottom the menu is fully visible; hover/selected colours as above; integration tests for align start/end, auto flip (stub sizes), Escape. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing ezSearch's or the board's dropdown overrides.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "selection-model", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "List selection model shared by DataTable and ListToolbar, kept across pages", "description": "<p>DataTable selection only knows the current page (<code>@selectedIds</code>/<code>@onSelect</code>/<code>@onSelectAll</code> in <code>components/app-ui/data-table.{hbs,js}</code>), and ListToolbar has no link to it. We need multi-page selection that the table and the toolbar share. This issue adds the model and DataTable support; the look and the toolbar are separate issues.</p><ul><li>New <code>app/utils/state/selection.js</code> class <code>Selection</code> (next to <code>AsyncResource</code>/<code>ListLoader</code>/<code>UrlState</code>): tracked set of ids (strings); <code>has(id)</code>, <code>toggle(id)</code>, <code>set(ids, on)</code>, <code>clear()</code>, <code>count</code>, <code>ids</code>, <code>stateFor(rows)</code> returning none|some|all for the given page rows, <code>countIn(rows)</code>. Kept across page changes; no totals (lists use limit+1 paging, see <code>docs/architecture/lists/decisions.md</code>), so no \\"select all matching\\".</li><li><code>AppUi::DataTable</code> takes <code>@selection</code> (a Selection): row toggles and the header select-all (current page) use it; <code>@onSelectionChange</code> fires with the ids. The existing <code>@selectedIds</code>/<code>@onSelect</code>/<code>@onSelectAll</code> keep working when <code>@selection</code> is not given.</li><li>Document it in <code>docs/architecture/state/</code> (one section) and in <code>public/ui-docs/data-table.md</code> + <code>data-table.json</code> (new args/events).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests for Selection; integration test: select on page 1, change rows (page 2), select, go back: page 1 rows still selected, count = both. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: checkbox look, toolbar selection bar, QuickList adopting it, select all matching.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "data-table-look", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::DataTable: QuickList selection look, standard row action icons, more-menu on AppUi::Dropdown", "description": "<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library. DataTable's select icons and selection colour don't match QuickList, and the row action icons' style, colour and size are inconsistent. Fix the component, give it its own demo and update the docs; do not change pages that use it.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><p>Reference markup to align with: QuickList row check <code>components/quick-list/row.hbs</code> (<code>button.quick-list__check</code> with <code>fa-square-o</code>/<code>fa-check-square</code>; styles <code>styles/components/quick-list.scss</code> ~l.155-175: unchecked <code>$mediumColor</code>, checked <code>$primaryColor</code>, selected row <code>#f9fafc</code>) and <code>QuickList::SelectAll</code> (already used in the header).</p><ul><li>Rows: replace the native checkbox with the same icon button as QuickList (same size, colours, aria-pressed); selected rows get the QuickList selected background. Header select-all shows none/some/all (<code>fa-square-o</code>/<code>fa-minus-square</code>/<code>fa-check-square</code>).</li><li>Row actions: one standard: icon-only <code>btn btn-box-tool</code> look (grey <code>$mediumColor</code>, <code>#444</code> on hover, 14px, square, title + aria-label), right-aligned, same gap; the more-actions button uses <code>fa-ellipsis-v</code> in the same style and opens its menu with <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> (<code>@align=\\"end\\"</code>) instead of the hand-made <code>.data-table-more-menu</code>.</li><li>Styles in <code>app/styles/components/app-ui-data-table.scss</code>.</li><li>Own demo <code>components/developer/demos/data-table.{hbs,js}</code> (columns, sort, groups, selection with a Selection across 3 fixture pages, row actions + more menu, empty state) and point the <code>data-table</code> entry in <code>utils/developer/component-registry.js</code> to it (the list-page demo stays for ListToolbar; do not edit it).</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/data-table.md</code> + <code>data-table.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for check icons/states, selected row class, action button classes, more-menu opens via AppUi::Dropdown. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: ListToolbar, changing list pages.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["selection-model", "dropdown"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["list-toolbar-table"]}, {"key": "ez-search-narrow", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "EzSearch: icon-only Saved Searches, Builder, Search and Clear when its own box is narrow", "description": "<p>EzSearch (<code>components/ez-search/index.{hbs,js}</code>) only drops its button labels at the xs viewport (<code>hidden-xs</code>). Inside a narrow box (a list in a side column, ListToolbar with actions) the buttons eat the space and the input gets squeezed. The input must take priority. Scope: the component, its demo and docs.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li>New modifier <code>app/modifiers/observe-width.js</code> (ResizeObserver on the element, calls back with the width; cleans up on destroy; no-op where ResizeObserver is missing; the only current ResizeObserver use is <code>app-ui/gantt-chart.js</code> ~l.1034-1084 for reference). Reusable by ListToolbar later.</li><li>EzSearch measures its own root: below a threshold (start at 560px, constant in the component) it adds <code>ez-search--narrow</code>: Saved Searches shows <code>fa-bookmark</code> only (saved name in the title), Builder <code>fa-sliders</code> only, Search <code>fa-search</code> only, Clear <code>fa-times</code> only; every icon button keeps its title and aria-label. The input flexes and keeps a min width (about 160px). The existing xs behaviour stays.</li><li><code>@narrow</code> (true/false) forces the mode; when not given it is automatic.</li><li>Styles in <code>app/styles/components/ez-search.scss</code> (scoped under <code>.ez-search--narrow</code>).</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/ez-search.{hbs,js}</code>: a width control (full / 50% / 320px) to show the switch. Docs <code>public/ui-docs/ez-search.md</code> (+ manifest if present).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests: forced narrow shows icon-only buttons with titles; automatic switch with a stubbed width; modifier unit test. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: EzSearchCompact, ListToolbar, page changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["list-toolbar-table"]}, {"key": "list-toolbar", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::ListToolbar: selection bar tied to the list's selection, space-conscious search", "description": "<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library. <code>AppUi::ListToolbar</code> (<code>components/app-ui/list-toolbar.hbs</code>, styles <code>styles/components/app-ui-list-toolbar.scss</code>) leaves selection to the page (the demo <code>components/developer/demos/list-page.{hbs,js}</code> hand-rolls select-all, bulk buttons and \\"(Selected : N)\\" unrelated to the table) and gives the search no priority in small spaces. Fix the component, the list-page demo and the docs; do not change pages that use it.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li><code>@selection</code> (the <code>Selection</code> from <code>utils/state/selection.js</code>, the same instance passed to <code>AppUi::DataTable</code>) + <code>@rows</code> (current page rows): when <code>count &gt; 0</code> the toolbar shows a selection bar like <code>QuickList::SelectionBar</code> (<code>components/quick-list/selection-bar.hbs</code>; reuse its markup/classes or the component): tri-state select-all for the page, \\"N selected\\" + \\"X on this page, Y on other pages\\", <code>&lt;:bulkActions as |ids clear|&gt;</code>, a clear button. With nothing selected: the page select-all icon and a muted hint. The pager stays on the right. The old <code>&lt;:selection&gt;</code> block keeps working when <code>@selection</code> is not given.</li><li>Narrow mode: measure the toolbar with <code>modifiers/observe-width.js</code>; below the threshold pass <code>@narrow={{true}}</code> to the search (document that EzSearch goes in the search block) and yield <code>narrow</code> to <code>&lt;:actions as |narrow|&gt;</code> so callers can show icon-only buttons. The search block flexes first (min width), actions never push it below that; if still too narrow, actions wrap under it.</li><li>Demo <code>list-page</code>: one Selection shared by ListToolbar and DataTable across fixture pages, bulk actions log the ids, EzSearch in the search block with the saved-search wiring, a width control (full / col-md-4) to show narrow mode.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/list-toolbar.md</code> + <code>list-toolbar.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests: bar appears with the right counts across pages, bulk block gets ids, clear empties the selection, narrow passes @narrow and yields it to actions. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing Agents/Workflows list pages, select all matching.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["selection-model", "ez-search-narrow"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["list-toolbar-table"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-15 23:07:37	2026-11-15 23:17:36	f
d5a276686afa-5047-dae4-da5baa0942d2	61698d956afa-5047-dae4-71e5f7daf8d5	1	{"summary": "One Prometheus issue. A new app-update service checks whether a newer build of Prometheus has been deployed: every 5 minutes, and whenever the tab becomes visible, it fetches index.html with no-store and compares the fingerprinted script names with the ones the running page loaded. When they differ, it shows a warning Messenger message with a Reload button and a close button. The message stays until the user closes it, and appears once per new build. No changes are needed in the build, deploy, Gaia or Hermes.", "issues": [{"key": "new-build-prompt", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "App: warn open sessions when a new build is deployed, with a sticky Reload prompt", "description": "<p>After we deploy a new Prometheus build, tabs that are already open keep running the old code until the user reloads, which causes stale behaviour and errors against a newer API. The open app should notice a new build and ask the user to reload, with a warning message that stays on screen until they close it.</p><p><strong>How a new build is detected (no build or deploy change needed)</strong>: production builds (<code>ember build -prod</code> in <code>docker/&lt;branch&gt;/Dockerfile</code>) fingerprint their scripts, e.g. <code>assets/prometheus-&lt;hash&gt;.js</code> and <code>assets/vendor-&lt;hash&gt;.js</code>. Fetch <code>${rootURL}index.html</code> with <code>cache: 'no-store'</code>, take the <code>src</code> of every <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> under <code>assets/</code>, and compare that set with the script tags of the page that is running (<code>document.scripts</code>). If they differ, a new build has been deployed. A plain <code>fetch</code> is right here: this is a static file, not a Gaia API call, so the store and adapter rule doesn't apply.</p><ul><li><strong>New service</strong> <code>app/services/app-update.js</code>, with one job: detect a new build and show the prompt.<ul><li><code>start()</code> is idempotent. It records the current script set, then checks every <code>ENV.appUpdate.interval</code> ms (default 5 minutes) and on <code>visibilitychange</code> when the tab becomes visible.</li><li>Put the pure logic in a small util (e.g. <code>app/utils/app-update/scripts.js</code>): extract the asset script srcs from an HTML string or document, and compare two sets. Ignore the order of the scripts and any query strings.</li><li>A failed fetch (offline, 5xx) or HTML with no asset scripts is ignored silently. Never prompt on errors.</li><li>Clear the timer and the listener in <code>willDestroy</code>.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Prompt</strong>: <code>new Messenger().post({ type: 'warning', hideAfter: false, showCloseButton: true, message, actions: { reload: { label, action: () =&gt; window.location.reload() } } })</code>. Follow the pattern in <code>services/live-reload-prompt.js</code> and leave that service unchanged. Show it once per new build: after it is shown or closed, don't show it again unless the server's script set changes again (another deploy). Text in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>, e.g. <code>services.appUpdate.message</code>: \\"A new version of Projects4Me is available. Reload the page to use it.\\" and <code>services.appUpdate.reload</code>: \\"Reload\\".</li><li><strong>Wiring</strong>: call <code>appUpdate.start()</code> from <code>routes/application.js</code> <code>beforeModel</code> (~l.86), so it also runs on the sign-in page.</li><li><strong>Config</strong>: <code>config/environment.js</code> gets <code>appUpdate: { enabled: true, interval: 300000 }</code>, with <code>enabled: false</code> in the test environment so acceptance tests never poll. In <code>ember serve</code> the scripts aren't fingerprinted, so the sets never differ and no prompt appears. That is expected.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>With the app open on build A, deploying build B makes a yellow warning Messenger message appear within 5 minutes, or straight away when the user comes back to the tab.</li><li>The message stays until the user clicks × or Reload. Reload loads the new build.</li><li>After closing, the message doesn't come back for build B. It appears again if build C is deployed.</li><li>Network errors never show a prompt and leave nothing in the console beyond a debug log.</li><li>Unit tests cover the util (extract and compare: same set, different hash, different order, no scripts) and the service: a changed set shows the prompt once, an unchanged set or a fetch error shows nothing, and it isn't shown again after closing. Stub <code>fetch</code> and <code>Messenger</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: forced reloads, release notes or a \\"what changed\\" view, service workers, server-side build ids, and any change to the Dockerfiles or the CD workflow.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-15 23:27:17	2026-11-15 23:27:17	f
bebdb3e46afa-54dd-5288-e2cc68ad359a	61698d956afa-5047-dae4-71e5f7daf8d5	2	{"summary": "Two parallel Prometheus issues. (1) build-header: the CD workflow passes the commit sha into the Docker build as BUILD_ID. The dev and qa images bake it into the Ember build and Apache sends it on every response as X-Prometheus-Build. (2) new-build-prompt: the app knows its own build id (ENV.APP.buildId, from BUILD_ID at build time). Whenever it makes a Gaia request, or the tab becomes visible, it sends a HEAD request for index.html, at most once a minute, and compares the header with its own id. When they differ it shows a warning Messenger message with Reload and close; the message stays until the user closes it and appears once per build. Without the header (local ember serve, or before (1) is deployed) nothing is shown, so the two issues can ship in either order.", "issues": [{"key": "build-header", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Deploy: stamp each build with BUILD_ID and serve it as the X-Prometheus-Build header", "description": "<p>Open browser tabs need to find out that a newer Prometheus build has been deployed, so they can ask the user to reload. The signal is a build signature: the same id is baked into the Ember build and sent by Apache as a response header, so the running app can compare its own id with the server's. This issue covers the build and deploy side. The app side is a separate issue that reads <code>ENV.APP.buildId</code> and the <code>X-Prometheus-Build</code> header.</p><p><strong>Contract</strong>: response header <code>X-Prometheus-Build: &lt;build id&gt;</code> on every response from the Prometheus server (at least on <code>index.html</code>, including <code>HEAD</code> requests). The build id is the git commit sha. The Ember build reads the same value from the environment variable <code>BUILD_ID</code>, and <code>config/environment.js</code> (changed in the app issue) puts it into <code>ENV.APP.buildId</code>.</p><ul><li><code>.github/workflows/cd-ovh.yml</code>: pass <code>build-args: BUILD_ID=${{ github.event.workflow_run.head_sha || github.sha }}</code> to <code>docker/build-push-action</code>. The workflow runs on both <code>pull_request: closed</code> and <code>workflow_run</code>, and on <code>workflow_run</code> <code>github.sha</code> isn't the built commit, so check which sha each trigger gives.</li><li><code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code> and <code>docker/qa/Dockerfile</code>: <code>ARG BUILD_ID</code> plus <code>ENV BUILD_ID=$BUILD_ID</code> in the build stage, before <code>ember build -prod</code>. Repeat <code>ARG</code>/<code>ENV BUILD_ID</code> in the Apache stage so the server can read it.</li><li><code>docker/apache/prometheus.conf</code>: <code>Header always set X-Prometheus-Build \\"${BUILD_ID}\\"</code> inside the VirtualHost (<code>mod_headers</code> is already enabled). Make sure Apache started by <code>apache2ctl -D FOREGROUND</code> sees the variable, using <code>PassEnv</code> or a define if <code>${BUILD_ID}</code> doesn't expand from the process environment. Same-origin requests, so no CORS expose header is needed.</li><li>Leave the root <code>Dockerfile</code> (dev/test image, <code>ember serve</code>) unchanged: no header there, so no prompt in local dev.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Building <code>docker/qa/Dockerfile</code> with <code>--build-arg BUILD_ID=abc123</code> and running it, <code>curl -I http://localhost:4000/index.html</code> and a deep link such as <code>/app/projects</code> both return <code>X-Prometheus-Build: abc123</code>.</li><li>A build without the arg still works. The header is then empty or missing, and the app treats that as \\"unknown\\".</li><li>The CD run log shows the sha passed as the build arg for both triggers.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: the app-side check and prompt (separate issue), Gaia and Hermes, production/master images (no CD for them today).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "new-build-prompt", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "App: compare the build signature on activity and show a sticky warning to reload", "description": "<p>After we deploy a new Prometheus build, tabs that are already open keep running the old code until the user reloads. The deploy stamps each build with an id: Apache sends it as the <code>X-Prometheus-Build</code> response header (separate deploy issue), and the same value is in the environment variable <code>BUILD_ID</code> at build time. The running app compares its own id with the server's while the user is active and asks them to reload, with a warning message that stays until they close it.</p><ul><li><strong>Config</strong> <code>config/environment.js</code>: <code>APP.buildId: process.env.BUILD_ID || null</code> and <code>appUpdate: { enabled: true, throttle: 60000 }</code>, with <code>enabled: false</code> in the test environment.</li><li><strong>New service</strong> <code>app/services/app-update.js</code>, with one job: detect a new build and show the prompt.<ul><li><code>check()</code> is throttled to once per <code>ENV.appUpdate.throttle</code> ms. It sends <code>fetch(`${rootURL}index.html`, { method: 'HEAD', cache: 'no-store' })</code> and reads <code>X-Prometheus-Build</code>. A plain fetch is right here: this is the app's own static server, not a Gaia API call, so the store and adapter rule doesn't apply.</li><li>No prompt when the app's own <code>buildId</code> is empty, the header is missing or empty, the request fails, or the ids match.</li><li>A different id shows the prompt once for that server id. After it is shown or closed, it isn't shown again unless the server's id changes again (another deploy).</li><li>Listen to <code>visibilitychange</code> and call <code>check()</code> when the tab becomes visible. Remove the listener in <code>willDestroy</code>. There is no timer.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Trigger on requests</strong>: in <code>app/adapters/application.js</code> <code>handleResponse</code> (~l.149), call <code>this.appUpdate.check()</code> without awaiting it, so every Gaia request (route loads, saves) is a chance to check, subject to the throttle.</li><li><strong>Start</strong>: inject and start the service from <code>routes/application.js</code> <code>beforeModel</code> (~l.86), so the visibility listener is in place on every page, the sign-in page included.</li><li><strong>Prompt</strong>: <code>new Messenger().post({ type: 'warning', hideAfter: false, showCloseButton: true, message, actions: { reload: { label, action: () =&gt; window.location.reload() } } })</code>. Follow the pattern in <code>services/live-reload-prompt.js</code> and leave that service unchanged. Text in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>, e.g. <code>services.appUpdate.message</code>: \\"A new version of Projects4Me is available. Reload the page to use it.\\" and <code>services.appUpdate.reload</code>: \\"Reload\\".</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>With build A open and build B deployed, the next Gaia request (more than 60 s after the last check), or coming back to the tab, shows a yellow warning Messenger message with Reload and ×.</li><li>It stays until the user clicks × or Reload. Reload loads build B. After ×, it doesn't come back for B, but it does for a later build C.</li><li>With no header, an empty own id (local <code>ember serve</code>) or a network error, nothing is shown.</li><li>No more than one HEAD request per minute, however many API calls are made.</li><li>Unit tests for the service, with <code>fetch</code>, <code>Messenger</code> and time stubbed: same id shows nothing, a different id shows the prompt once, no prompt again after closing, a new id shows it again, a missing header or a fetch error shows nothing, and the throttle holds. The adapter test covers the <code>check()</code> call.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: the header and build arg (deploy issue), Gaia-side headers, forced reloads, release notes, service workers.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 01:22:06	2026-11-16 01:22:06	f
5b9df9526afa-2876-35fc-539c942c2679	dcdfbac46afa-a4f4-35fc-b54d188e59a0	1	{"summary": "Replace the edit-comment modal with in-place editing by reusing AppUi::InlineEditable, the design system's inline edit component. First extend InlineEditable, without changing its current behaviour, so it can be started from an external trigger, its click-to-edit surface can be turned off, and it can show Save/Cancel buttons below a multi-line editor. Then switch ConversationUi::CommentItem (used on issue detail and in conversation threads) to edit the comment in place with the existing ToastUi editor and remove the modal.", "issues": [{"key": "inline-editable-external-trigger", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::InlineEditable: external edit trigger, optional click-to-edit and a Save/Cancel button toolbar", "description": "<p><code>AppUi::InlineEditable</code> (<code>app/components/app-ui/inline-editable.{js,hbs}</code>, styles <code>app/styles/components/inline-editable.scss</code>) is the design system's inline edit component, but it only suits short fields. Comments need to be edited in place from a pencil button in the comment header, with a multi-line rich editor. This issue adds the options needed for that; every current caller (role page, user page, idea title) must keep working unchanged.</p><ul><li><strong><code>@editOnClick</code></strong> (default <code>true</code>). When <code>false</code>, the display surface is not interactive: no <code>role=\\"button\\"</code>, no <code>tabindex</code>, no click or keydown handler, no hover background and no <code>__edit-hint</code> pencil.</li><li><strong>The display block yields an API</strong>: <code>&lt;:display as |d|&gt;</code> with <code>d.startEdit</code> (the existing <code>startEdit</code> action, guarded by <code>canEdit</code>) and <code>d.canEdit</code>, so a button inside the display content can open the editor.</li><li><strong><code>@toolbar</code></strong>: <code>\\"icons\\"</code> (default, today's check/cross icons beside the slot) or <code>\\"buttons\\"</code>: the slot takes the full width and below it sit a <code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code> Save and a <code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code> Cancel (labels <code>global.form.save</code> / <code>global.form.cancel</code>), both disabled while saving, with <code>aria-busy</code> on the edit row while saving. Any new layout classes go in <code>inline-editable.scss</code> under the BEM block. Square edges, no new colours.</li><li>Keep the existing save semantics: validation via <code>@validate</code>/<code>@message</code>, stay in edit mode when <code>@onSave</code> throws, drop a second save while one is pending.</li><li>After <code>startEdit</code> from an external trigger, move focus into the edit slot; on cancel or a successful save, return focus to the element that triggered the edit when it still exists.</li><li>Add <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/inline-editable-test.js</code> (the component has none today): default click-to-edit still works; <code>@editOnClick={{false}}</code> ignores clicks and Enter on the surface; <code>d.startEdit</code> opens the editor; the buttons toolbar saves, cancels and is disabled while saving; a rejecting <code>@onSave</code> keeps the editor open; <code>@disabled</code>/ACL block <code>d.startEdit</code>.</li><li>Document the new arguments in the component's YUIDoc and add a short note on the inline-edit row in <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong>: existing role, user and idea-title inline edits behave exactly as before (their acceptance tests pass); the new options work as described and are covered by the integration test.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: using the new options in any screen (the comment change is a separate issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "comment-inline-edit", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Comments: edit a comment in place instead of in a modal", "description": "<p>Editing a comment opens a <code>bootstrap-modal</code> with a ToastUi editor just to change one comment. Users should edit it in place, where it sits in the thread. <code>ConversationUi::CommentItem</code> (<code>app/components/conversation-ui/comment-item.{js,hbs}</code>) renders comments on the issue detail page (<code>issue/issue-details.hbs</code>) and in conversation threads (<code>conversation/thread-comments.hbs</code>), so changing it covers both.</p><ul><li>Wrap the comment in <code>AppUi::InlineEditable</code> with <code>@editOnClick={{false}}</code>, <code>@toolbar=\\"buttons\\"</code>, <code>@submitOnEnter={{false}}</code> and <code>@disabled</code> unless <code>isOwnComment</code>. <code>&lt;:display as |d|&gt;</code> renders the existing <code>ConversationUi::CommentFrame</code> with its <code>&lt;:tools&gt;</code>: the pencil button (<code>data-btn=\\"edit\\"</code>) calls <code>d.startEdit</code>; the delete button and delete modal stay as they are. <code>&lt;:edit as |f|&gt;</code> renders the same CommentFrame header, with <code>AppUi::ToastUi</code> in the body (same args as the current modal: <code>@usersList</code>, <code>@issueSearch</code>, wysiwyg, <code>@hide={{array 'footer'}}</code>, <code>@initialValue={{f.value}}</code>, <code>@onContentChange={{f.updateDirect}}</code>) and the tool buttons hidden while editing.</li><li>Clicking the comment text never starts editing; only the pencil does.</li><li><code>onSave(content)</code>: reject an empty or whitespace-only comment with the existing <code>views.app.conversation.comment.edit.empty</code> error and stay in edit mode; otherwise set <code>comment.comment</code> and <code>save()</code>. On failure, <code>rollbackAttributes()</code>, show the existing <code>edit.error</code> Messenger toast and rethrow so the editor stays open with the user's text. Drop the \\"updating\\" and \\"updated\\" toasts: the saving state of the buttons and the updated comment are the feedback. Check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after the await.</li><li>Escape cancels the edit (wire <code>f.onKeydown</code> on the edit wrapper) but must not cancel while the editor's mention/emoji/issue menu (Tribute) is open; Escape then only closes the menu.</li><li>Remove the edit modal, <code>showEditCommentModal</code>, <code>showEditCommentDialog</code>, <code>removeEditCommentModal</code>, <code>editedCommentContent</code> and the now unused translation keys (<code>views.app.conversation.comment.edit.title</code>, <code>.update</code>, <code>.comment</code>, <code>.updating</code>, <code>.updated</code>) from <code>translations/en-us.json</code> and the legacy <code>app/locales/en-us/translations.js</code> if present there. Any spacing for the in-place editor goes in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code>.</li><li>Update <code>tests/acceptance/conversation/edit-comment.feature</code> and <code>steps/conversation/edit-comment-steps.js</code> for in-place editing (no modal), and add scenarios for Cancel restoring the original text and a failed save keeping the editor open. Add <code>tests/integration/components/conversation-ui/comment-item-test.js</code> covering: the pencil opens the editor in place, another user's comment shows no pencil, an empty comment is rejected, a rejected save rolls back and stays in edit mode.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong>: on the issue detail page and in a conversation thread, the pencil on your own comment turns it into an editor in place; Save updates it in place, and Cancel or Escape restores the original; no modal opens; the delete flow is unchanged; tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: idea messages, editing other users' comments, an \\"edited\\" marker, live updates of edits for other viewers.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["inline-editable-external-trigger"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 10:56:27	2026-11-16 10:56:27	f
da81b0156afa-5122-b3db-7c577473353c	dcdfbac46afa-a4f4-35fc-b54d188e59a0	2	{"summary": "Replace the edit-comment modal with in-place editing by reusing AppUi::InlineEditable, the design system's inline edit component, with the existing Toast UI editor (AppUi::ToastUi, mentions and emojis included) in its edit slot. First extend InlineEditable, without changing its current behaviour, so it can be started from an external trigger, its click-to-edit surface can be turned off, and it can show Save/Cancel buttons below a multi-line editor. Then switch ConversationUi::CommentItem (used on issue detail and in conversation threads) to edit the comment in place and remove the modal.", "issues": [{"key": "inline-editable-external-trigger", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::InlineEditable: external edit trigger, optional click-to-edit and a Save/Cancel button toolbar", "description": "<p><code>AppUi::InlineEditable</code> (<code>app/components/app-ui/inline-editable.{js,hbs}</code>, styles <code>app/styles/components/inline-editable.scss</code>) is the design system's inline edit component, but it only suits short fields. Comments need to be edited in place from a pencil button in the comment header, with a multi-line rich editor. This issue adds the options needed for that; every current caller (role page, user page, idea title) must keep working unchanged.</p><ul><li><strong><code>@editOnClick</code></strong> (default <code>true</code>). When <code>false</code>, the display surface is not interactive: no <code>role=\\"button\\"</code>, no <code>tabindex</code>, no click or keydown handler, no hover background and no <code>__edit-hint</code> pencil.</li><li><strong>The display block yields an API</strong>: <code>&lt;:display as |d|&gt;</code> with <code>d.startEdit</code> (the existing <code>startEdit</code> action, guarded by <code>canEdit</code>) and <code>d.canEdit</code>, so a button inside the display content can open the editor.</li><li><strong><code>@toolbar</code></strong>: <code>\\"icons\\"</code> (default, today's check/cross icons beside the slot) or <code>\\"buttons\\"</code>: the slot takes the full width and below it sit a <code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code> Save and a <code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code> Cancel (labels <code>global.form.save</code> / <code>global.form.cancel</code>), both disabled while saving, with <code>aria-busy</code> on the edit row while saving. Any new layout classes go in <code>inline-editable.scss</code> under the BEM block. Square edges, no new colours.</li><li>Keep the existing save semantics: validation via <code>@validate</code>/<code>@message</code>, stay in edit mode when <code>@onSave</code> throws, drop a second save while one is pending.</li><li>After <code>startEdit</code> from an external trigger, move focus into the edit slot; on cancel or a successful save, return focus to the element that triggered the edit when it still exists.</li><li>Add <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/inline-editable-test.js</code> (the component has none today): default click-to-edit still works; <code>@editOnClick={{false}}</code> ignores clicks and Enter on the surface; <code>d.startEdit</code> opens the editor; the buttons toolbar saves, cancels and is disabled while saving; a rejecting <code>@onSave</code> keeps the editor open; <code>@disabled</code>/ACL block <code>d.startEdit</code>.</li><li>Document the new arguments in the component's YUIDoc and add a short note on the inline-edit row in <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong>: existing role, user and idea-title inline edits behave exactly as before (their acceptance tests pass); the new options work as described and are covered by the integration test.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: using the new options in any screen (the comment change is a separate issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "comment-inline-edit", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Comments: edit a comment in place with the Toast UI editor instead of in a modal", "description": "<p>Editing a comment opens a <code>bootstrap-modal</code> with a Toast UI editor just to change one comment. Users should edit it in place, where it sits in the thread, with the same Toast UI editor (toolbar, @ user mentions, # issue links, : emojis). <code>ConversationUi::CommentItem</code> (<code>app/components/conversation-ui/comment-item.{js,hbs}</code>) renders comments on the issue detail page (<code>issue/issue-details.hbs</code>) and in conversation threads (<code>conversation/thread-comments.hbs</code>), so changing it covers both.</p><ul><li>Wrap the comment in <code>AppUi::InlineEditable</code> with <code>@editOnClick={{false}}</code>, <code>@toolbar=\\"buttons\\"</code>, <code>@submitOnEnter={{false}}</code> and <code>@disabled</code> unless <code>isOwnComment</code>. <code>&lt;:display as |d|&gt;</code> renders the existing <code>ConversationUi::CommentFrame</code> with its <code>&lt;:tools&gt;</code>: the pencil button (<code>data-btn=\\"edit\\"</code>) calls <code>d.startEdit</code>; the delete button and delete modal stay as they are. <code>&lt;:edit as |f|&gt;</code> renders the same CommentFrame header, with the tool buttons hidden while editing.</li><li><strong>Editor</strong>: the edit body is <code>AppUi::ToastUi</code> with the same args as the current modal: <code>@usersList</code>, <code>@issueSearch</code>, <code>@editType='wysiwyg'</code>, <code>@hide={{array 'footer'}}</code>, <code>@placeholder</code>, plus <code>@initialValue={{f.value}}</code> and <code>@onContentChange={{f.updateDirect}}</code>. (<code>modifiers/initialize-toastui.js</code> builds the editor once in <code>modify</code> and ignores later arg changes, so the draft does not reset the content.) Do <strong>not</strong> wrap it in a <code>.form-field</code> div as the modal does: <code>inline-editable.scss</code> hides every <code>label</code> inside <code>.form-field</code> in the slot, which would hide the labels of Toast UI's link and image popups. Check that the mention, issue and emoji menus open and insert correctly inside the comment box.</li><li>Clicking the comment text never starts editing; only the pencil does.</li><li><code>onSave(content)</code>: reject an empty or whitespace-only comment with the existing <code>views.app.conversation.comment.edit.empty</code> error and stay in edit mode; otherwise set <code>comment.comment</code> and <code>save()</code>. On failure, <code>rollbackAttributes()</code>, show the existing <code>edit.error</code> Messenger toast and rethrow so the editor stays open with the user's text. Drop the \\"updating\\" and \\"updated\\" toasts: the saving state of the buttons and the updated comment are the feedback. Check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after the await.</li><li>Escape cancels the edit (wire <code>f.onKeydown</code> on the edit wrapper) but must not cancel while the editor's mention/emoji/issue menu (Tribute) is open; Escape then only closes the menu.</li><li>The Toast UI modifier has no teardown (editor and Tribute are not destroyed on removal), as with the modal today. Check that opening and cancelling the editor several times leaves no stray mention menus; if it does, log a separate issue rather than fixing the modifier here.</li><li>Remove the edit modal, <code>showEditCommentModal</code>, <code>showEditCommentDialog</code>, <code>removeEditCommentModal</code>, <code>editedCommentContent</code>, <code>handleEditContentChange</code> and the now unused translation keys (<code>views.app.conversation.comment.edit.title</code>, <code>.update</code>, <code>.comment</code>, <code>.updating</code>, <code>.updated</code>) from <code>translations/en-us.json</code> and the legacy <code>app/locales/en-us/translations.js</code> if present there. Any spacing for the in-place editor goes in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code>.</li><li>Update <code>tests/acceptance/conversation/edit-comment.feature</code> and <code>steps/conversation/edit-comment-steps.js</code> for in-place editing (no modal), and add scenarios for Cancel restoring the original text and a failed save keeping the editor open. Add <code>tests/integration/components/conversation-ui/comment-item-test.js</code> covering: the pencil opens the Toast UI editor in place with the comment's content, another user's comment shows no pencil, an empty comment is rejected, a rejected save rolls back and stays in edit mode.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong>: on the issue detail page and in a conversation thread, the pencil on your own comment turns it into a Toast UI editor in place, prefilled with the comment, with mentions and emojis working; Save updates it in place, and Cancel or Escape restores the original; no modal opens; the delete flow is unchanged; tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: idea messages, editing other users' comments, an \\"edited\\" marker, live updates of edits for other viewers, fixing the Toast UI modifier's missing teardown.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["inline-editable-external-trigger"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 11:11:22	2026-11-16 11:11:22	f
a11397646afa-bdaf-7528-8696074fd152	ded9f4396af0-2b69-3bb7-c36bdb48cfdf	4	{"summary": "Change request on the Avatar: when a person has no image or it fails to load, AppUi::Avatar shows their initials on a background generated at run time from a hash of the user id (palette base colour + one pattern shape in a second palette colour), so every user looks different and always the same. Follows aprom-4588, which builds the sizes and agent look.", "issues": [{"key": "avatar-initials", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::Avatar: initials on a stable per-user generated background when there is no image", "description": "<p>Change request on <code>AppUi::Avatar</code> (built in aprom-4588: sizes xs/s/m/l, agent look). When a person has no image or the image fails to load, show the user's initials instead of <code>/img/default.png</code>. A shared grey placeholder makes users hard to tell apart, and a background that changes between views is confusing, so the background is generated at run time from the user and is always the same for that user. Scope: the component, its demo and docs; do not change pages that use it.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li>New pure util <code>app/utils/ui/avatar-identity.js</code>: <code>initials(name, size)</code> (first letter of the first and last word, uppercase, Unicode-safe; one word = one letter; xs always one letter; empty name = null) and <code>identity(key)</code> returning <code>{ base, accent, pattern }</code> from a stable string hash (e.g. FNV-1a) of the key. Base colour from the dark palette colours that keep white text readable (<code>$primaryColor</code>, <code>$highlightColor</code>, <code>$secondaryColor</code>, <code>$dangerColor</code>, <code>$warningColor</code>, <code>$darkColor</code>, mirrored as constants with a comment pointing to <code>app/styles/variables.scss</code>), accent = a different colour from the same list, pattern from a fixed list (half-bottom, half-left, corner circle top-right, corner circle bottom-left, ring). Document that the order of these lists must never change (reordering changes every user's avatar).</li><li>Key = the user id; fall back to the name when there is no id. Nothing is stored.</li><li><code>AppUi::Avatar</code>: for a person, render the initials avatar when there is no id or the image <code>error</code> event fires (replaces 4588's default.png fallback); round (50%), the avatar size, base colour background, the pattern as an absolutely positioned shape in the accent colour at 50% opacity, white semibold initials scaled to the size; no name = <code>fa-user</code> icon on the same background. <code>title</code>/<code>alt</code> = the name. Colours via classes (e.g. <code>app-ui-avatar--c3</code>, <code>app-ui-avatar--p2</code>) defined in <code>app/styles/components/app-ui-avatar.scss</code>, not inline styles. Agents keep the robot look from 4588 (no initials).</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>: a row of sample people without images in every size, and an \\"image fails\\" control showing the switch. Docs <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-avatar.md</code> + <code>app-ui-avatar.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests for initials (one/two words, extra spaces, non-Latin, xs) and identity (same key = same result, different keys spread over colours/patterns, accent never equals base); integration tests: no id, image error, name missing, agent unaffected. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: users whose stored picture is the default placeholder (they still load an image; handled separately if approved), uploading pictures, page changes.</p>", "type": "Change Request", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["aprom-4588"], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["avatar-initials"]}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 09:53:37	2026-11-16 10:17:27	f
2f3eb4756afa-1926-b3db-9e39dd74c969	de3303a86afa-5122-b3db-e6498ef24096	1	{"summary": "Adopt AppUi::Avatar everywhere a user's picture is shown (~35 call sites), each mapped from its current rendered size to the standard scale (xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96) plus a new ml 64px size for the member grids, which have no fitting size today. One issue per area; issues that share a stylesheet are chained (issue.scss: issue details -> assignee avatars; project.scss: issue details -> project overview -> member stacks -> role page; agent.scss: relate fields -> agent pages). A final cleanup removes Agent::UserAvatar and the dead avatar CSS and records the rule in the design system.", "issues": [{"key": "avatar-ml", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "AppUi::Avatar: add size ml (64px) for member grids", "description": "<p>We are moving every user picture in the app to <code>AppUi::Avatar</code>. The member grids (project overview Members, issue Members box, role page Members) render avatars at about 70-80px today, between m (40px) and l (96px), so the scale needs one more size.</p><ul><li><code>components/app-ui/avatar.js</code>: add <code>ml</code> to <code>SIZES</code> (order xs, s, m, ml, l). Unknown values still fall back to m.</li><li><code>styles/components/app-ui-avatar.scss</code>: <code>.app-ui-avatar-ml</code> 64px x 64px; agent icon font size and initials text scaled between m and l; the robot marker shows (as from s up).</li><li>Update the header comment of the scss and the component YUIDoc.</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>: add the ml column and size option.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-avatar.md</code> and its manifest json: list ml 64px and when to use it (stacked member grids with the name below).</li><li>Integration test: ml renders 64px, with initials and with the agent marker.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>@size=\\"ml\\"</code> renders a 64px avatar for a person, a person without an image and an agent; the existing sizes are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing any page that uses the avatar.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-shell", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar in the header, user menu, sidebar user panel and control bar", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in). Today the app shell renders raw <code>/userimage/get</code> images sized by AdminLTE.</p><ul><li><code>components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs:56</code> navbar <code>img.user-image</code> (25px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code>; keep it beside the name, vertically centred in the 50px navbar.</li><li>Same file l.64 user menu <code>li.user-header img.img-circle</code> (90px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"l\\"</code>, centred as today.</li><li><code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.hbs:5</code> sidebar <code>.user-panel .image img</code> (45px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>.</li><li><code>components/application-controlbar.hbs:16</code> <code>img.contacts-list-img</code> (40px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>.</li><li>Pass <code>this.currentUser.user</code> (or the listed user) as <code>@user</code>.</li><li>If an AdminLTE rule (<code>.navbar .user-image</code>, <code>.user-header &gt; img</code>, <code>.user-panel &gt; .image &gt; img</code>, <code>.contacts-list-img</code>) no longer matches, re-add the float/margin it gave by scoping a rule in the layout's own module scss, not by restyling the avatar.</li><li>Update the tests that select these images (use <code>data-test-avatar</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the 4 spots show AppUi::Avatar at the sizes above; the header, menu and sidebar layouts look as before apart from the size change; a user without an image shows initials.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> deleting legacy CSS used elsewhere (cleanup issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-comments", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar in comments, the comment composer and the weekly conversations widget", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in).</p><ul><li><code>components/conversation-ui/comment-frame.hbs:3</code> <code>Agent::UserAvatar @class=\\"img-circle img-sm\\"</code> (30px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code> with <code>(hash id=@userId name=@userName)</code>. This frame is shared by issue comments, thread comments and idea messages; check all three.</li><li><code>components/conversation-ui/comment-composer.hbs:12</code> current user image (30px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code>.</li><li><code>components/widgets/weekly-conversations.hbs:~60</code> <code>img.img-circle.img-sm</code> (30px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code> with <code>(hash id=comment.createdUser name=...)</code>.</li><li>AdminLTE floats <code>.box-comment img</code> and offsets the comment text by 40px; keep the avatar floated left with the text beside it (scope a rule in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code> if needed). Its 30px <code>!important</code> rule matches s.</li><li>Update tests that select the old images (use <code>data-test-avatar</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> comments, the composer and the widget show 30px AppUi avatars with the same layout as before; agents show the agent look; a missing image shows initials.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> removing <code>Agent::UserAvatar</code> (cleanup issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-notifications", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar in notifications", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in).</p><ul><li><code>components/app-ui/notifications/notification.hbs:5</code> <code>img.img-circle.img-xs.user-image</code>, rendered 40px by <code>styles/components/notifications-sidebar.scss:100</code> -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code> with <code>(hash id=@notification.createdUser name=@notification.createdUserName)</code>.</li><li>Keep the wrapper <code>span.user-image[data-notification-user-image]</code>: <code>notification.js</code> (~l.236-260) decides that a click on the avatar opens the user, partly by checking for an <code>IMG</code> with class <code>user-image</code>. Make that check rely on the wrapper's data attribute only, so initials (no img) behave the same.</li><li>Rescope the 4rem sidebar rule so it no longer resizes the avatar's inner img.</li><li>Update the notification integration and acceptance tests (avatar click still opens the user).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> notifications show 40px AppUi avatars; clicking the avatar (image or initials) opens the user, clicking elsewhere opens the item as before.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-issue-details", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar in issue details (assignee, members, time logs, watchers)", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, ml 64, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in). Issue details (<code>components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code>) is shared by the issue page, the list and board quick views and the gantt panel.</p><ul><li>l.129 assignee in <code>.project-manager</code> (img stretched to the col-md-2 width, about 100-130px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"l\\"</code>, centred above the name.</li><li>l.275-293 Members box <code>users-list</code> (assigned to, owned by, modified by, reported by; fluid, about 70-80px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"ml\\"</code>, centred in its cell with the name and label below.</li><li>l.376 and l.490 time logs (<code>.time-log .user-img img</code> 50px, <code>styles/modules/issue.scss:99</code>) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>; drop the <code>user-img</code> wrapper class there (keep the tooltip) and remove the issue.scss <code>.user-img img</code> rule if nothing else uses it.</li><li>l.710 add-watcher modal <code>img.img-circle.img-sm</code> (30px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code>.</li><li>Replace every <code>Agent::UserAvatar</code> here; pass <code>(hash id=... name=... type=...)</code> where only fields are at hand.</li><li>Make sure <code>.project-manager img { width: 100% }</code> (<code>styles/modules/project.scss:11</code>, also used by the project overview) doesn't stretch the avatar's inner img: scope it to the old markup or move it under a class only the old markup has. Don't delete it (the project overview still uses it until its own issue).</li><li>Update tests that select the old images.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the issue page and quick views, the avatars show at the sizes above with the layout as before; agents show the agent look; missing images show initials.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-ml"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-assignee", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar for issue assignees (assignee select, issue list, gantt bar)", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in).</p><ul><li><code>components/issue/assignee-select.hbs:8</code> compact trigger on board cards (24px from <code>styles/modules/issue.scss:693</code> <code>img.img-circle</code>) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"s\\"</code>; remove that rule. Keep the caret and the dropdown toggle behaviour (aprom-4155: don't stop click propagation).</li><li>Same file l.28 menu options (<code>.assignee-select-option-avatar</code> 20px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"xs\\"</code>, still left of the name with the same gap.</li><li><code>templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs:108</code> issue list assignee (<code>img.img-circle.user-img</code>, 40px from the global <code>.user-img</code> in profile.scss) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>, title = the name. Don't delete <code>.user-img</code> (still used elsewhere).</li><li><code>components/app-ui/gantt-chart/gantt-bar.hbs:47</code> (40px, <code>styles/modules/gantt.scss:466</code> <code>!important</code>) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>; keep the tooltip (initialize-tooltip on the wrapper) and the position right of the bar; remove the img size rule.</li><li>Check the board card with Sortable: the avatar must still open the menu, not start a drag (the sortable filter is <code>[data-issue-assignee-dropdown]</code>).</li><li>Update tests that select these images.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> board cards, the issue list, the gantt bars and the assignee menu show AppUi avatars at the sizes above; the assignee menu still opens and changes the assignee.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-issue-details"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-project-overview", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar on the project overview (manager, conversations, members)", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, ml 64, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in). Page: <code>templates/app/project/index.hbs</code>.</p><ul><li>l.30 manager in <code>.project-manager</code> (img stretched to the col-md-2 width) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"l\\"</code>, centred above the name. <code>.project-manager img { width: 100% }</code> (<code>styles/modules/project.scss:11</code>) must no longer hit the avatar; remove it if issue details no longer needs it.</li><li>l.92 latest conversations <code>.user-block img.img-circle</code> (40px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code> with <code>(hash id=conversation.createdBy ...)</code>; keep the subject and description offset beside it.</li><li>l.273 Members box grid (<code>users-list</code>, about 70-80px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"ml\\"</code>, keeping the inactive/invited status badge on the avatar (<code>.member-avatar-wrap</code>, <code>.member-account-status</code>) and the delete button.</li><li>Update tests that select these images.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the three boxes show AppUi avatars at the sizes above with the layout as before; the member status badges still sit on the avatar.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-ml", "avatar-issue-details"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-member-stack", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project::MemberAvatars: pass a size to AppUi::Avatar instead of resizing it with CSS", "description": "<p><code>components/project/member-avatars.hbs</code> already renders <code>AppUi::Avatar</code>, but its size is forced by CSS on the wrapper: <code>.member-avatars .member-avatar</code> 4rem (<code>styles/modules/project.scss:318</code>) and 2.4rem in role rows (<code>styles/modules/role.scss:70</code>). Use the component's sizes instead.</p><ul><li>Add <code>@size</code> to MemberAvatars (default m), passed to each <code>AppUi::Avatar</code>; the overflow badge (<code>.member-avatars-overflow</code>) takes the same diameter.</li><li>Callers: projects list (<code>templates/app/projects/index.hbs:111</code>, 40px) -&gt; m; role rows (<code>templates/app/role.hbs:79</code>, 24px) -&gt; s; thread participants (<code>components/conversation/participants-box.hbs:7</code>) -&gt; m.</li><li>Remove the width/height overrides from project.scss and role.scss; keep the overlap margin and hover.</li><li>YUIDoc for <code>@size</code>; integration test per size.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the stacks render at 40px (projects, participants) and 30px (role rows) through <code>@size</code>, with no CSS size override left.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-project-overview"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-role-page", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar on the role page (members and view-all modal)", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, ml 64, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in). Page: <code>templates/app/role/page.hbs</code>.</p><ul><li>l.145 Members grid (<code>.member-avatar-wrap img</code> 7rem, <code>styles/modules/role.scss:188</code>) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"ml\\"</code>, name below; remove the img size rule.</li><li>l.229 view-all modal (<code>.role-members-view-all__avatar</code> 3.6rem, role.scss:227) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>, beside the name; keep the class on the wrapper for layout (flex-shrink) but drop its size.</li><li>Pass <code>userrole.user</code> (or <code>(hash id=... name=...)</code>).</li><li>Update tests that select these images.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> role members and the modal list show AppUi avatars at 64px and 40px with the layout as before.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-ml", "avatar-member-stack"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-users", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar in user management and the profile's close members", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in).</p><ul><li><code>templates/app/user/management.hbs:97</code> <code>img.user-img</code> (40px, global <code>.user-img</code> in profile.scss:456) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>; keep the 1rem gap before the name (<code>styles/modules/user-management.scss:48</code>, move it to the wrapper).</li><li><code>components/user-profile/close-members.hbs:4</code> <code>img.user-img</code> (40px) -&gt; <code>@size=\\"m\\"</code>.</li><li>alt/title = the user's name (today the alt is the literal user-img).</li><li>Don't delete <code>.user-img</code> (cleanup issue).</li><li>Update tests that select these images.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> both lists show 40px AppUi avatars, layout as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the profile picture editor (<code>components/user/edit/profile-picture.hbs</code>), which previews an unsaved upload.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-relate-fields", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar in the user and actor relate fields", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in). The relate renderers show people as a 25px raw image and agents through <code>Agent::Avatar</code>; <code>relate-user</code> passes no user, so an agent's picture never shows.</p><ul><li><code>components/related-fields/relate-user.hbs</code>: one <code>AppUi::Avatar @size=\\"xs\\"</code> for people and agents, with <code>(hash id=@data.value name=@data.label)</code> (add <code>type</code> when <code>@data.isAgent</code>); keep the sponsor text.</li><li><code>components/related-fields/relate-actor.hbs</code>: same for <code>kind</code> user and agent (<code>@data.user</code> for agents); the expression icon stays.</li><li>Remove <code>.user-relate-icon</code> (<code>styles/modules/form-fields.scss:226</code>) if unused afterwards, and the <code>.relate-user.relate-agent .agent-avatar</code> size rule (<code>styles/modules/agent.scss:97</code>), which would override the avatar size; keep the sponsor line-height aligned.</li><li>Check select rows in issue create (assignee), the workflow properties panel (actor) and agent sponsor pickers: same row height, no overflow (aprom-4283).</li><li>Update tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> people and agents show 20px AppUi avatars in these selects (agents with their picture when they have one); rows don't grow.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-agents", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Use AppUi::Avatar on the agent list and agent page", "description": "<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px). It renders <code>Agent::Avatar</code> for agents itself, plus the robot marker when the agent has a picture.</p><ul><li><code>templates/app/agent/index.hbs:49</code> <code>Agent::Avatar @user=agent.user</code> (36px) -&gt; <code>AppUi::Avatar @user=agent.user @size=\\"m\\"</code>; keep the 10px gap to the name (<code>.agents-list .agent-cell</code> in agent.scss, move it to the wrapper).</li><li><code>templates/app/agent/page.hbs:54</code> and <code>:58</code> <code>Agent::Avatar @large</code> (96px), inside <code>User::Edit::ProfilePicture</code> and its fallback -&gt; <code>@size=\\"l\\"</code>; the upload click and crop flow keep working.</li><li>Remove agent.scss page rules that only sized these avatars, if unused afterwards. Keep <code>Agent::Avatar</code> itself (AppUi::Avatar uses it).</li><li>Update the agent list and page tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the agent list shows 40px and the agent page 96px avatars with the agent look; uploading a picture still works and shows it.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-relate-fields"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "avatar-cleanup", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Remove Agent::UserAvatar and the dead avatar CSS; record AppUi::Avatar as the only user picture", "description": "<p>After every user picture has moved to <code>AppUi::Avatar</code>, remove what is left of the old ways.</p><ul><li>Delete <code>components/agent/user-avatar.{hbs,js}</code> and its tests (no callers left; check with a search).</li><li>Search <code>app/</code> for <code>/userimage/get</code> outside <code>components/app-ui/avatar.js</code> and the profile picture editor; any left is a missed call site: move it (pick the size closest to its current rendered size) or list it in a comment.</li><li>Remove CSS rules that no longer match anything: e.g. <code>.user-img</code> (profile.scss:456), <code>.user-relate-icon</code>, <code>.assignee-select-option-avatar</code>, <code>.users-list .agent-avatar</code>, <code>.box-comment &gt; .agent-avatar</code>, <code>.project-manager img</code>, gantt <code>.users-list &gt; li &gt; img</code>. Check each with a search of the templates first.</li><li><code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>: add the rule that every user picture is <code>AppUi::Avatar</code> with a standard size (xs, s, m, ml, l and when to use each), and add it to the checklist.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> no <code>Agent::UserAvatar</code>, no raw user images outside the two allowed places, no dead avatar CSS; full test suite and lint pass.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "low", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["avatar-shell", "avatar-comments", "avatar-notifications", "avatar-assignee", "avatar-role-page", "avatar-users", "avatar-agents"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 11:17:03	2026-11-16 11:17:03	f
de01bff36afd-3eec-75db-2de637cf275a	6c7240d86afd-3eec-75db-a5acaf1064a6	1	{"summary": "Fix the blank content area on project pages. On a cold load, the parent app.project route waits for three requests in a row (project, an optional issuestatus fallback, all project issues) and has no loading template of its own. Its outlet also stays hidden until a second, redundant project query returns. The first issue adds a project-level skeleton and renders the outlet straight away. The second stops nested routes from waiting for the all-issues preload. Both change routes/app/project.js, so they run in order.", "issues": [{"key": "project-route-skeleton", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project route: show a skeleton while the project loads and render the outlet without the extra project query", "description": "<p>On a fresh load of any project URL (e.g. <code>/app/project/aprom/issue/4198</code>), the content area stays blank until the parent <code>app.project</code> route finishes its hooks, before the nested route's own request even starts. Ember finds no loading substate for <code>app.project</code>: <code>app/project-loading.hbs</code>, <code>app/loading.hbs</code> and <code>loading.hbs</code> don't exist. The existing <code>app/project/loading.hbs</code> and <code>*-loading.hbs</code> templates only cover child routes. They are also hidden, because <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> renders <code>{{outlet}}</code> only inside <code>{{#if this.projectId}}</code>, and <code>setupController</code> in <code>routes/app/project.js</code> sets <code>projectId</code> in the <code>.then()</code> of a second project query, although <code>beforeModel</code> already loaded the project.</p><ul><li>Add <code>app/templates/app/project-loading.hbs</code>: a <code>content-header</code> with a heading skeleton line plus <code>&lt;AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @bodyOnly={{true}} /&gt;</code>, following <code>app/templates/app/settings-loading.hbs</code> and the design system.</li><li><code>routes/app/project.js</code>: keep the project record loaded in <code>beforeModel</code> on the route. In <code>setupController</code>, set <code>model</code>, <code>projectId</code> and <code>projectName</code> from it straight away, and remove the second <code>store.query('project', { fields: 'Project.id,Project.name' ... })</code>.</li><li>When no project matches the short code, keep today's error handling (<code>errorManager</code>) and don't throw on <code>objectAt(project, 0).id</code>.</li><li>Tests: an acceptance or route test that visits a project child route with a delayed project response and asserts the project skeleton is shown. Also check that the child's loading template renders while its own model is pending.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a cold load or reload of a project page never shows an empty content area. The project skeleton shows while the project loads, then the child skeleton, then the page. Only one project request is made per project entry. The project name and breadcrumb are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the all-issues preload in <code>afterModel</code> (separate issue), the <code>app.loading-assets</code> flow.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "project-issues-nonblocking", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project route: stop blocking nested routes on the all-issues preload", "description": "<p><code>routes/app/project.js</code> <code>afterModel</code> loads every issue of the project (<code>limit: -1</code>; fields id, subject, issueNumber, statusId, projectId) and returns that promise, so every nested route (board, issue list, issue page, ideas, conversations, ...) waits for it before its own request starts. The list only feeds the <code>issuesList</code> getter in <code>controllers/app/project.js</code> (<code>@computed('projectId', 'issues')</code>). It is read by <code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code> and <code>controllers/prometheus/projectrelated.js</code>, and from there by <code>components/message-box.js</code> and <code>components/summer-note.js</code>.</p><ul><li>Start the issues query without returning it from <code>afterModel</code>. When it resolves, set <code>issues</code> on the <code>app.project</code> controller (and the route, if still read there); report errors with <code>errorManager.handleError</code> as today. Ignore a result that arrives after the user has switched to another project.</li><li>Make sure the <code>issuesList</code> getter updates when <code>issues</code> arrives later, and that every reader handles the empty list (only the blank entry) until then without errors.</li><li>Tests: a route/acceptance test that a nested route's model request starts before the issues preload resolves, and that the list fills in once it does.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a cold load of a project page, the nested route's request starts right after the project request, without waiting for the all-issues request. Issue pickers that use <code>issuesList</code> show the issues once loaded. Switching projects never shows another project's issues.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing the preload with server-side search in the pickers, the store.request migration (aprom-4552).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["project-route-skeleton"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 09:50:22	2026-11-18 09:50:22	f
b736d2196afb-66c3-948b-c8f30116f4c9	de3303a86afa-5122-b3db-e6498ef24096	5	{"summary": "Two small QuickList fixes: the sort/group toolbar and the pagination footer have no horizontal padding, so their buttons touch the box border. Both get 10px sides, matching the QuickList selection bar, group headings and AdminLTE's box header. Independent, can go in parallel.", "issues": [{"key": "ql-toolbar-padding", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: sort and group toolbar touches the box border", "description": "<p>In every QuickList (ideas, roles, threads, Developer demo) the toolbar with the Group by / Sort by menus sits flush against the box's left and right borders: <code>styles/components/quick-list/_toolbar.scss:10</code> sets <code>.quick-list-toolbar { padding: 0.4rem 0 }</code>. The selection bar (<code>_selection.scss</code>) and group headings (<code>_group.scss</code>) already use 10px on the sides, as does AdminLTE's <code>.box-header</code>.</p><ul><li>Change the toolbar padding to <code>0.4rem 10px</code> so the select-all control on the left and the menus on the right line up with the box header and the selection bar.</li><li>Check the toolbar still wraps without overflow in the narrow lists (idea browser col-md-3) and that switching between toolbar and selection bar doesn't shift the content sideways.</li><li>Check the Developer -&gt; Components QuickList entry and the ideas and roles lists.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the toolbar's buttons have 10px between them and the box border on both sides, aligned with the header title and the selection bar; nothing else in the list moves.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 1, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ql-pager-padding", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "QuickList: pagination footer touches the box border", "description": "<p>The QuickList pager (<code>AppUi::Pager class=\\"quick-list-pagination\\"</code> in <code>components/quick-list/index.hbs:88</code>) sits flush against the box's right border: <code>styles/components/quick-list/_pagination.scss:6</code> sets <code>.quick-list-pagination { padding: 6px 0 }</code>. The selection bar and group headings use <code>6px 10px</code>.</p><ul><li>Change the pagination padding to <code>6px 10px</code>, so the range text and the previous/next buttons have 10px to the border, aligned with the box header.</li><li>Don't change <code>AppUi::Pager</code> itself or its styles (<code>app-ui-pager.scss</code>); the fix is the QuickList's footer only.</li><li>Check the ideas, roles and threads lists and the Developer -&gt; Components QuickList entry, including a narrow list (col-md-3).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the pager's buttons have 10px between them and the box border; the range text and buttons stay on one line in the narrow lists.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> moving the pager into a <code>.box-footer</code>.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Cleanup", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 1, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 20:12:39	2026-11-16 20:14:35	f
ed55c6206afb-b5db-dcfe-b7e74ca23f6b	1cecd6c76afb-1ee8-c328-6f16c99cd135	1	{"summary": "Backend-only issue links in Gaia. A framework ACL capability lets a project-grouped model be scoped by several project keys (a row is readable when any key is in scope, with write rules and per-row filtering of embedded relations). In parallel, an issue graph service detects cycles and is applied right away to the existing Issue.parentId. The new Issuelink CRUD resource (blocks, relates, splits; cross-project, with projectId and targetProjectId set by the server) builds on both. Parent/child stays on parentId; blocking is not enforced. UI, live events, workflow triggers and gaia-mcp tools come later.", "issues": [{"key": "acl-any-project", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "ACL: scope a project-grouped model by several project keys (row readable when any key is in scope)", "description": "<p>Issue links (a new <code>Issuelink</code> resource, planned separately) connect issues in two different projects. Today a project-grouped model is scoped through exactly one project key per row: <code>acl.groupKeys</code> takes a direct <code>projectId</code> or a set of <code>paths</code>, and <code>when</code> picks one of them (see <code>app/metadata/model/Activity.php</code> ~l.169, decision D-060). A row that belongs to two projects can't be expressed. This issue adds that capability to the framework, with no resource using it yet.</p><ul><li><strong>Metadata:</strong> a way for a model to bind the <code>Project</code> group through several keys with \\"any of\\" semantics, e.g. <code>'groupKeys' =&gt; ['Project' =&gt; ['anyOf' =&gt; ['projectId', 'targetProjectId']]]</code>. The exact shape is yours to settle; keep it consistent with the existing <code>paths</code>/<code>when</code> format.</li><li><strong>Read (members scope, <code>project.get</code> = 2):</strong> list and get return a row when the user is a member of <em>any</em> of the bound projects. Scope 1 (all) adds no filter, and scope 0 denies, as today.</li><li><strong>Write:</strong> <code>assertWriteInScope</code> / <code>assertRecordIdInScope</code> support a configurable rule for such models. The first use needs \\"in scope for at least one bound project\\". Keep the rule declared in metadata, not hard-coded per model.</li><li><strong>Embedded relations, per row:</strong> check whether eager <code>rels</code> to a project-grouped model (e.g. an <code>Issue</code> in a project the user isn't a member of) are filtered row by row under members scope. D-021 only covers model-level denial. If they aren't filtered, make them so: the related record is left out while the parent row stays. Write down what you found.</li><li>Record the decision in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code> (new D-0xx) and refresh <code>docs/generated/</code> (<code>gaia-dev graph export</code>, <code>docs generate</code>).</li><li>Unit tests for the scope filter and the write assertion with a test-only model or fixture metadata.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a model declaring two project keys returns a row to a member of either project and not to a member of neither; a write is accepted or refused per the declared rule; an embedded related record in an out-of-scope project is not returned. Existing single-key models behave exactly as before (existing acl api-tester cases pass).</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Issuelink resource itself and any UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "issue-graph", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Issues: cycle detection service and guard on Issue.parentId", "description": "<p>Issue relationships must never form cycles. Today nothing stops <code>Issue.parentId</code> from pointing to the issue itself or to one of its own descendants (only metadata in <code>app/metadata/model/Issue.php</code> ~l.191 and the live events component touch it). The upcoming <code>Issuelink</code> resource (blocks, splits) needs the same check, so build it once as a domain service.</p><ul><li>A domain service in <code>core/libs</code> (e.g. <code>IssueGraph</code>) answering \\"would adding edge from A to B create a cycle?\\" over an edge source behind a small interface. Implement it with a bound recursive CTE (no string-built SQL) and a depth cap.</li><li>A first edge source for <code>Issue.parentId</code>. The Issuelink edge source is added by the Issuelink issue.</li><li>The walk ignores ACL: it must see the whole graph, including issues the user can't read. Error messages never name or identify those issues.</li><li><strong>Guard on parentId:</strong> on Issue create/update, reject <code>parentId</code> equal to the issue's own id, or to any of its descendants, with 422 and a clear message. Apply it through a model behaviour or validator, not in the controller.</li><li>Serialise the check against concurrent writes with a transaction-level advisory lock (<code>pg_advisory_xact_lock</code>) on a key the Issuelink resource can reuse.</li><li>Unit tests for the service (self, direct, deep cycle, no cycle, depth cap) and api-tester cases for the parentId guard.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> PATCH or POST issue with <code>parentId</code> = itself or a descendant returns 422; valid parent changes still work; the service is reusable for other edge types.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> moving parent/child into Issuelink, and any UI.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "issuelink-resource", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Issuelink resource: blocks, relates and splits links between issues, across projects", "description": "<p>Issues need typed links beyond parent/child: an issue blocks (and is blocked by) another, relates to another, or is split into several issues. Links may cross projects. This is backend only: the Prometheus UI, live events and workflow enforcement of blocking come later. Parent/child stays on <code>Issue.parentId</code> for now.</p><ul><li><strong>New CRUD resource <code>Issuelink</code></strong> (standard REST, no custom actions) with:<ul><li><code>sourceIssueId</code>, <code>targetIssueId</code>;</li><li><code>type</code>: <code>blocks</code> | <code>relates</code> | <code>splits</code>;</li><li><code>projectId</code> (the source issue's project) and <code>targetProjectId</code> (the target's);</li><li>audit fields; soft delete; indexes on both issue ids.</li></ul>Each link is stored once. \\"Blocked by\\" and \\"split from\\" are the inverse view of <code>blocks</code> and <code>splits</code>.</li><li><strong>Server-set fields:</strong> <code>projectId</code> and <code>targetProjectId</code> are always derived from the two issues; values in the request body are ignored. When an issue's <code>projectId</code> changes, its links' project columns follow.</li><li><strong>Relations:</strong> Issuelink hasOne <code>sourceIssue</code>, <code>targetIssue</code>, <code>project</code>, <code>targetProject</code>. Issue hasMany <code>outgoingLinks</code> (sourceIssueId) and <code>incomingLinks</code> (targetIssueId).</li><li><strong>ACL:</strong> <code>groups =&gt; ['Project']</code> bound by any of <code>projectId</code> / <code>targetProjectId</code>, using the multi-key capability from the ACL issue.<ul><li><strong>Read:</strong> a member of either project sees the link. The issue on the side the user can't read is left out, but its project id stays, so a client can show \\"an issue in another project\\".</li><li><strong>Create/delete:</strong> <code>issuelink.create</code>/<code>delete</code>, read scope on both issues, and write scope on at least one of the two projects.</li><li>No permission seeds (the reviewer grants them); add <code>acl</code> api-tester cases.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Validation (422), in a domain validator using <code>IssueGraph</code> from the cycle issue:</strong><ul><li>no self-links;</li><li>no duplicate (same pair and type; for <code>relates</code> in either direction);</li><li>no cycle in <code>blocks</code>;</li><li>no cycle in <code>splits</code>, and a target can be split from only one source.</li></ul>Add an Issuelink edge source to <code>IssueGraph</code> and reuse its advisory lock. Messages never identify issues the user can't read.</li><li>Changing <code>type</code> or the issue ids by PATCH is refused: delete and create instead.</li><li>When an issue is soft-deleted, its links are soft-deleted too.</li><li>Decision note in the docs (link model, ACL rule) and refreshed <code>docs/generated/</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> links can be created, listed (by <code>sourceIssueId</code> or <code>targetIssueId</code>), read and deleted within and across projects under the rules above; every 422 rule has an api-tester case; acl cases cover members of the source project, the target project, both, and neither.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> Prometheus UI, live events, workflow triggers or enforcement of blocking, gaia-mcp tools, migrating parentId into links.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["acl-any-project", "issue-graph"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-16 21:13:17	2026-11-16 21:13:17	f
4abddbf96afc-9973-ac6f-c808aa5ef21d	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	1	{"summary": "Module-agnostic search in Gaia driven by a per-model `search` metadata block. Ares gets a POST /embeddings endpoint backed by an Ollama nomic-embed-text sidecar, and the dev stack gets Ollama plus a pgvector Postgres image. The Gaia framework learns Postgres extensions, a vector field type and GIN/trigram/HNSW indexes generated from `search` metadata; Issue is the first searchable model. Embeddings live in one shared Searchembedding table, kept fresh by a model behaviour that queues changed records, a CLI worker that drains the queue every minute and a daily reconcile, run by a container scheduler. Search itself is a lexical core (exact pin, FTS, fuzzy, RRF fusion, module ACL and record scope applied in SQL), exposed by GET /api/v1/search, then a semantic searcher added to the fusion that degrades to lexical results when Ares is down.", "issues": [{"key": "ares-embeddings", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Embeddings endpoint POST /embeddings backed by Ollama nomic-embed-text", "description": "<p>Gaia is adding semantic search across its modules and needs vector embeddings for record text and search queries. It requests a stateless embeddings endpoint in Ares using the open <code>nomic-embed-text</code> model served by an Ollama sidecar container, so no ML runtime ships inside the Ares image. Please accept, adapt or decline the contract below.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li><code>POST /embeddings</code> request: <code>{\\"texts\\": [\\"...\\"], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code>; 1 to 64 texts, each non-empty and at most 8000 characters; 422 otherwise.</li><li>200 response: <code>{\\"model\\": \\"nomic-embed-text\\", \\"dimensions\\": 768, \\"embeddings\\": [[...], ...]}</code>, same order as <code>texts</code>.</li><li>503 with a clear message when Ollama is unreachable or the model is not pulled; never an empty or fake vector.</li><li>Ares adds the model's task prefixes itself (<code>search_document: </code> / <code>search_query: </code>), so callers send plain text.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Router <code>routers/embeddings.py</code> (Pydantic request/response only) -&gt; <code>services/embedding_service.py</code> -&gt; a new embedding gateway: <code>adapters/base_embedding_adapter.py</code> plus <code>adapters/ollama_embedding_adapter.py</code> (async HTTP to Ollama <code>/api/embed</code> via httpx, already installed through the anthropic SDK), chosen by the factory.</li><li>Env: <code>OLLAMA_URL</code> (default <code>http://ollama:11434</code>), <code>EMBEDDING_MODEL</code> (default <code>nomic-embed-text</code>), timeout from env.</li><li><code>docker-compose.yml</code>: an <code>ollama</code> service on the <code>backend</code> network with a named volume for models, pulling <code>nomic-embed-text</code> on start.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter (no live Ollama): validation errors, prefixing per task, order kept, 503 on adapter failure.</li><li>Update <code>CLAUDE.md</code> Architecture (second endpoint, Gaia caller <code>core/services/Embeddings.php</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the compose stack up, POST /embeddings returns 768-dimension vectors for both tasks; tests pass without network.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other models or providers, batching above 64, caching.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "stack-ollama-pgvector", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "p4m stack: Ollama service for Ares and pgvector Postgres image", "description": "<p>Gaia is adding semantic search: it stores embeddings in Postgres with the <code>vector</code> extension and gets them from a new Ares <code>/embeddings</code> endpoint served by an Ollama sidecar. The local stack that <code>p4m</code> generates needs both so engineers and agents can run it. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>installer/p4m.py</code>: Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code> instead of <code>postgres:16-alpine</code> for the dev DB and the gaia-test containers (same data volume layout; pg16 keeps existing data readable).</li><li>An <code>ollama</code> service in the generated ares compose (~line 528) on the backend network, a named model volume, <code>nomic-embed-text</code> pulled on first start; <code>OLLAMA_URL</code> passed to Ares.</li><li><code>p4m status</code>/health shows the Ollama service; README notes the ~300 MB model download.</li><li>Unit tests for the generated compose (image name, ollama service, env).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>p4m up</code> on a fresh machine starts Postgres with <code>CREATE EXTENSION vector</code> available and Ollama answering with the model pulled; existing local databases keep working.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> GPU support, production infrastructure.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-framework", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search framework: Postgres extensions, vector field type and search indexes from `search` metadata", "description": "<p>Gaia is getting module-agnostic search (FTS, fuzzy, semantic, exact) configured per model in metadata. The declarative migrations only know primary, unique and plain/multi-column indexes (<code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> ~215-271, <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> ~242), so they need new capabilities first.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Extensions: migrations run <code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector</code> and <code>pg_trgm</code> (declared once in config, idempotent).</li><li>Field type <code>vector</code> with a <code>dimensions</code> property (maps to <code>vector(N)</code>) in <code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code> <code>getFieldType</code> and the Postgres migration dialect.</li><li>A model-level <code>search</code> metadata block, validated by the meta manager: <code>type</code> (name used in <code>/search?types=</code>, unique across models), <code>fts</code> (field =&gt; weight A-D), <code>fuzzy</code> (fields), <code>semantic</code> (ordered fields), <code>exact</code> (fields), <code>display</code> (<code>title</code>, <code>snippet</code> fields). Unknown fields or weights fail with a clear message.</li><li>Generated indexes from that block: one GIN expression index over the weighted tsvector (<code>setweight(to_tsvector(config, coalesce(field,'')), weight)</code> concatenated, text search config from <code>config</code>, default <code>english</code>) and a GIN <code>gin_trgm_ops</code> index per fuzzy field. Expose the exact tsvector expression through one helper so the query side (later issue) uses the identical expression and hits the index.</li><li>Index type <code>hnsw_cosine</code> for vector columns (<code>USING hnsw (col vector_cosine_ops)</code>).</li><li><code>docker-compose.yaml</code> Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code>.</li><li>Unit tests for type mapping, metadata validation and the generated DDL; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a model with a <code>search</code> block migrates to the expected GIN indexes, re-running migrate is a no-op, a vector field with an HNSW index migrates, models without a block are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the search query code, any model's search block.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "embeddings-client", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Embeddings service: Gaia client for the Ares /embeddings endpoint", "description": "<p>Search needs document and query embeddings from Ares (<code>POST /embeddings</code>, nomic-embed-text, 768 dimensions). Like <code>core/services/LLM.php</code>, the external system sits behind one class that owns its configuration and transport.</p><p><strong>Contract (Ares)</strong>: request <code>{\\"texts\\": [...], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code> (1-64 texts, max 8000 chars each); 200 <code>{\\"model\\", \\"dimensions\\", \\"embeddings\\": [[...]]}</code>; 422 invalid; 503 model unavailable.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/services/Embeddings.php</code>: <code>embedDocuments(array $texts): array</code> and <code>embedQuery(string $text): array</code>; Guzzle, base URL <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL</code>, short timeouts from env (query ~3 s, documents ~30 s).</li><li>Failures throw a dedicated exception (e.g. <code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code>) with the reason; never return an empty vector. Validates the response shape and dimension count.</li><li>Register it in <code>ServiceFactory</code> if that is how services are resolved.</li><li>Unit tests with a mocked Guzzle handler: success, 422, 503, timeout, malformed body, wrong dimensions.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests pass without network; callers get vectors or a typed exception.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> where embeddings are stored or used.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ares-embeddings"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "issue-searchable", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Issue: add the `search` metadata block", "description": "<p>Issue is the first searchable module. Add its <code>search</code> block to <code>app/metadata/model/Issue.php</code> so the migration builds its FTS and trigram indexes.</p><ul><li><code>'search' =&gt; ['type' =&gt; 'issue', 'fts' =&gt; ['subject' =&gt; 'A', 'description' =&gt; 'B'], 'fuzzy' =&gt; ['subject'], 'semantic' =&gt; ['subject', 'description'], 'exact' =&gt; ['issueNumber'], 'display' =&gt; ['title' =&gt; 'subject', 'snippet' =&gt; 'description']]</code></li><li>Run migrate locally and confirm the GIN indexes exist; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> and the graph.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> migrate creates the Issue indexes; an <code>EXPLAIN</code> of the framework's tsvector expression against <code>issues</code> uses the GIN index.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other modules (Doc, Wiki, Milestone come later by adding their own block).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-framework"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "index-queue", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search index: Searchembedding table and change-driven queueing behaviour", "description": "<p>Semantic search keeps one embedding per searchable record. Changes must be picked up from every write path (REST, MCP, workflows, CLI), so a model behaviour queues them; the embedding itself is computed later by a worker, so a save never waits on or fails because of Ares.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Model <code>Searchembedding</code> (metadata + model, no REST controller): <code>relatedTo</code> (search type), <code>relatedId</code>, <code>contentHash</code> (sha256 of the semantic text), <code>model</code>, <code>embedding</code> <code>vector(768)</code> null, <code>status</code> (pending, done, failed), <code>attempts</code>, <code>error</code>, <code>dateIndexed</code>; unique (<code>relatedTo</code>, <code>relatedId</code>), HNSW cosine index on <code>embedding</code>. No audit behaviour.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SearchableRegistry</code>: reads every model's <code>search</code> block; lookup by type and by model class.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticText</code>: builds the text from the <code>semantic</code> fields in order, HTML stripped, whitespace collapsed, cut to <code>SEARCH_EMBED_MAX_CHARS</code> (default 4000), and its hash.</li><li><code>searchIndexBehavior</code> attached automatically to every model with a <code>search</code> block (where behaviours are loaded), so a module is searchable by metadata alone. After save: upsert the row as pending only when the hash changed or no row exists. On soft delete: delete the row. Errors are caught and logged (fail open), never failing the user's write.</li><li>Unit tests: hash unchanged = no write, changed = pending, delete removes, failure does not break the save; models without a block get no behaviour.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> creating or editing an Issue's subject/description leaves a pending row; editing other fields does not.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> calling Ares, querying vectors.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-framework", "issue-searchable"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "index-worker", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search CLI: `search embed` queue worker and `search reindex` daily reconcile", "description": "<p>Pending Searchembedding rows need embeddings, and a periodic reconcile catches anything an event missed (direct DB changes, a model gaining a <code>search</code> block, failed rows).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong> in <code>core/tasks/SearchTask.php</code> (logic in <code>core/libs/search/</code>, the task only parses and prints):</p><ul><li><code>php cli.php search embed [--limit=N]</code>: claims pending rows and failed rows with <code>attempts &lt; 5</code> in batches of 32 (<code>FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED</code>, so two runs never overlap), rebuilds the text via <code>SemanticText</code>, calls <code>Embeddings::embedDocuments</code>, stores vector, model and <code>done</code>. On <code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code>: mark failed, increment attempts, keep the error, stop the run. Skips rows whose record is gone or deleted (deletes the row).</li><li><code>php cli.php search reindex [type]</code>: walks every searchable model in pages, upserts pending where the hash differs or no row exists, deletes orphan rows.</li><li>Both print counts (embedded, failed, queued, removed).</li><li>Unit tests with a fake Embeddings: batching, retry cap, unavailable stops the run, reindex queues only changed records.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after <code>search reindex</code> and <code>search embed</code> every non-deleted Issue has a <code>done</code> row with 768 dimensions.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> scheduling the commands (separate issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["index-queue", "embeddings-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "cli-scheduler", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Run Gaia CLI tasks on a schedule in the containers", "description": "<p>No container runs cron today (<code>docker/dev/start.sh</code> only migrates), so scheduled tasks never run. Search needs <code>php cli.php search embed</code> every minute and <code>php cli.php search reindex</code> every 24 hours.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Pick a scheduler that needs no new package if possible (busybox <code>crond</code> or cron from the base image) and run it in the deployed image (<code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code>, <code>start.sh</code>) and the local stack; a crontab file in the repo with the two search entries (UTC), output to the container log.</li><li>Ask the reviewer whether to also enable the existing <code>workflow schedule</code> (every minute) here; it is documented as cron-driven but never runs.</li><li>Document the schedule in the README; one test or check that the crontab lines parse.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> in the running container, editing an Issue gets its embedding within about a minute, and the daily reconcile is listed in the crontab.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a job queue system, production infrastructure outside the images.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["index-worker"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-lexical", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search core: exact, FTS and fuzzy searchers with ACL scope and rank fusion", "description": "<p>The domain layer for module-agnostic search, driven by the <code>search</code> metadata (via <code>SearchableRegistry</code> if it exists, else read it the same way). The controller comes in a later issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong> in <code>core/libs/search/</code>:</p><ul><li><code>SearchRequest</code>: types, query text (trimmed, 2-200 chars), modes (fts, fuzzy, semantic, default all), limit (default 20, max 50).</li><li><code>ExactMatcher</code>: rows whose <code>exact</code> fields equal the query (type-aware: a numeric field matches only an integer query, also <code>#123</code>); pinned first.</li><li><code>FtsSearcher</code>: <code>websearch_to_tsquery</code> against the framework's tsvector expression (identical, so the GIN index is used), <code>ts_rank_cd</code>, snippet via <code>ts_headline</code> on the display snippet field.</li><li><code>FuzzySearcher</code>: <code>pg_trgm</code> <code>word_similarity</code> on fuzzy fields, threshold from config (default 0.3).</li><li><code>RankFusion</code>: Reciprocal Rank Fusion (k = 60) over each mode's ranked ids; result items carry <code>matchedBy</code> modes and the fused score; exact matches stay on top.</li><li><code>SearchService</code>: for each type, require <code>&lt;module&gt;.get</code> through <code>Acl</code> (denied type = 403, as for unauthorized query criteria, D-027); apply the module's record scope (<code>Acl::applyRecordScope</code>, <code>acl.groupKeys</code>, D-060) and <code>deleted = 0</code> inside each candidate query, before ranking and LIMIT (D-022). A mode is skipped for a type when the user lacks read on any field it searches (field ACL); denied display fields are omitted. Bound parameters only.</li><li>Unit/integration tests: ranking order, exact pin, typo tolerance, members-scope user never sees other projects' issues, field-ACL skip.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>SearchService</code> returns fused, ACL-scoped results for <code>issue</code> with modes fts and fuzzy.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic mode, HTTP endpoint.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-framework", "issue-searchable"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-endpoint", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "SearchController: GET /api/v1/search across searchable modules", "description": "<p>Expose the search core over HTTP. The controller has no module permission of its own; authorization is the searched module's (done in <code>SearchService</code>). This is a deliberate exception to standard CRUD resources: record it as a decision in a new <code>docs/architecture/search/decisions.md</code> (and register it wherever the decisions-docs test expects).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>SearchController</code> with a list action only: <code>GET /api/v1/search?types=issue&amp;q=...&amp;modes=fts,fuzzy&amp;limit=20</code>; route in <code>core/config/routes.php</code>; OAuth still required; <code>$aclMap</code> declared so the action catalog does not publish a <code>search.*</code> permission.</li><li>Thin: parse into <code>SearchRequest</code>, call <code>SearchService</code>, shape the response. 400 for missing/short <code>q</code>, unknown type or mode; 403 when a requested type's <code>.get</code> is denied.</li><li>Response: <code>data</code> items <code>{type: 'searchresult', id: '&lt;type&gt;:&lt;recordId&gt;', attributes: {module, recordId, title, snippet, score, matchedBy, pinned}}</code>, <code>meta</code> <code>{query, types, modes}</code>.</li><li>api-tester cases incl. <code>acl</code> profiles (denied module = 403, members scope hides other projects' issues); regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass; searching an issue number pins that issue; a typo in a subject word still finds it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic mode (next issue), Prometheus UI.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-lexical"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-semantic", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: semantic mode with pgvector, fused with lexical results", "description": "<p>Add the semantic mode to search: the query is embedded through Ares and compared to stored Searchembedding vectors, then fused with the FTS/fuzzy results.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticSearcher</code>: <code>Embeddings::embedQuery</code>, then cosine distance (<code>&lt;=&gt;</code>, HNSW index) on <code>searchembedding</code> rows with <code>status = done</code>, joined to the module table with the same record scope, ACL and <code>deleted = 0</code> as the lexical searchers (before LIMIT); max distance from config. Skipped when the user lacks read on any <code>semantic</code> field.</li><li>Plug it into <code>SearchService</code>/<code>RankFusion</code> as a mode, on by default.</li><li>Ares failure (<code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code>): lexical results are still returned and <code>meta.semantic</code> is <code>unavailable</code> (otherwise <code>ok</code>), never a silent success; logged.</li><li>Tests with a fake Embeddings: a paraphrase finds the issue, scope is respected, Ares down gives lexical results plus the meta flag; api-tester case for the meta field; update the search decisions doc.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> searching \\"login fails after password reset\\" finds an issue titled \\"Reset password link broken\\" with <code>matchedBy</code> containing <code>semantic</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records, re-ranking models.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-endpoint", "index-worker"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 13:48:58	2026-11-17 13:48:58	f
670a60566afc-9c53-0c6d-5fad5d8c6e20	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	2	{"summary": "Module-agnostic search in Gaia, configured by a per-model `search` metadata block, with the search columns living on the module's own table. Ares embeds text in-process with nomic-embed-text (fastembed/ONNX) behind POST /embeddings; the dev stack switches Postgres to the pgvector image. Gaia framework work adds Postgres extensions, vector and generated-tsvector columns and GIN/trigram/HNSW indexes to migrations, then a `search` block that injects system-managed search columns (hidden from REST, not writable, not audited) into the model; Issue is the first searchable model. Saves mark changed records stale; a `search embed` command fills embeddings (scheduled every minute, pending the engineer's inline-vs-queued call) and `search reindex` reconciles every 24 hours. Search runs every mode (exact pin, FTS, fuzzy, semantic) fused by RRF, with the searched module's ACL and record scope applied in SQL, behind GET /api/v1/search?types=&q=.", "issues": [{"key": "ares-embeddings", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Embeddings endpoint POST /embeddings running nomic-embed-text in-process", "description": "<p>Gaia is adding semantic search across its modules and needs vector embeddings for record text and search queries. It requests a stateless embeddings endpoint in Ares that runs the <code>nomic-embed-text</code> model inside Ares itself (no external model server). Please accept, adapt or decline the contract below.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li><code>POST /embeddings</code> request: <code>{\\"texts\\": [\\"...\\"], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code>; 1 to 64 texts, each non-empty and at most 8000 characters; 422 otherwise.</li><li>200 response: <code>{\\"model\\": \\"nomic-embed-text-v1.5\\", \\"dimensions\\": 768, \\"embeddings\\": [[...], ...]}</code>, same order as <code>texts</code>, L2-normalised.</li><li>503 with a clear message when the model failed to load; never an empty or fake vector.</li><li>Ares adds the model's task prefixes itself (<code>search_document: </code> / <code>search_query: </code>), so callers send plain text.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>fastembed</code> (ONNX Runtime, CPU, no PyTorch; approved by the engineer for this feature) in <code>requirements.txt</code>.</li><li>Router <code>routers/embeddings.py</code> (Pydantic request/response only) -&gt; <code>services/embedding_service.py</code> -&gt; a new gateway <code>adapters/base_embedding_adapter.py</code> + <code>adapters/fastembed_adapter.py</code>, chosen by the factory. The model is loaded once (lazily or at startup) and inference runs in a thread pool so async routes are not blocked.</li><li>Env: <code>EMBEDDING_MODEL</code> (default <code>nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5</code>), <code>EMBEDDING_CACHE_DIR</code>, thread count.</li><li><code>Dockerfile</code>: download the model weights at build time into the cache dir so the first request does not download; <code>/health</code> reports whether the model is loaded.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter (no model download): validation errors, prefixing per task, order kept, 503 on adapter failure.</li><li>Update <code>CLAUDE.md</code> Architecture (second endpoint; Gaia caller <code>core/services/Embeddings.php</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> in the built image POST /embeddings returns 768-dimension vectors for both tasks without network access; tests pass offline.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> GPU, other models, batching above 64, caching results.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "stack-pgvector", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "p4m stack: pgvector Postgres image for the dev and test databases", "description": "<p>Gaia is adding semantic search and stores embeddings in Postgres with the <code>vector</code> extension, which <code>postgres:16-alpine</code> does not ship. The stack <code>p4m</code> generates needs an image that has it. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>installer/p4m.py</code>: Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code> for the dev DB and the gaia-test containers (same major version, existing data volumes stay readable).</li><li>README: note the image change and that Ares' image now carries an embedding model (bigger first build).</li><li>Unit test for the generated compose image name.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after <code>p4m up</code>, <code>CREATE EXTENSION vector</code> succeeds in the dev and test databases; existing local databases keep working.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> production infrastructure.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-migrations", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migrations: Postgres extensions, vector and generated tsvector columns, GIN/trigram/HNSW indexes", "description": "<p>Search needs column and index kinds the declarative migrations cannot create today: they only know primary, unique and plain/multi-column indexes (<code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> ~215-271, <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> ~242). This issue adds the generic capabilities; the search metadata that uses them is the next issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Extensions: migrate runs <code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector</code> and <code>pg_trgm</code> (declared in config, idempotent).</li><li>Field type <code>vector</code> with <code>dimensions</code> (maps to <code>vector(N)</code>) in <code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code> <code>getFieldType</code> and the Postgres dialect.</li><li>Field type <code>tsvector</code> with a <code>generated</code> definition: list of source field =&gt; weight (A-D) and a text search config (default <code>english</code>), migrated as <code>GENERATED ALWAYS AS (setweight(to_tsvector(config, coalesce(field,'')), 'A') || ...) STORED</code>.</li><li>Index kinds: <code>gin</code> (for tsvector), <code>gin_trgm</code> (<code>gin_trgm_ops</code> on a text field), <code>hnsw_cosine</code> (<code>USING hnsw (col vector_cosine_ops)</code>).</li><li>Re-running migrate is a no-op; changing a generated column's sources recreates it.</li><li><code>docker-compose.yaml</code> Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code>.</li><li>Unit tests for type mapping and generated DDL; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a vector field, a generated tsvector field and the three index kinds migrates as expected and re-migrates cleanly; existing models are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>search</code> metadata block, any real model.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-metadata", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search metadata block injects system-managed search columns into the model", "description": "<p>A model becomes searchable by declaring a <code>search</code> block in its metadata. The search data lives on the module's own table, so the block must add the search columns and indexes to the model, and those columns must never be exposed, written or audited like normal fields (an audited 768-float vector on every change would bloat the audit log).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Validate the block in the meta manager: <code>type</code> (name in <code>/search?types=</code>, unique across models), <code>fts</code> (field =&gt; weight A-D), <code>fuzzy</code> (fields), <code>semantic</code> (ordered fields), <code>exact</code> (fields), <code>display</code> (<code>title</code>, <code>snippet</code>). Unknown fields or weights fail with a clear message.</li><li>Inject columns for a model with the block: <code>searchVector</code> (generated tsvector from <code>fts</code>, GIN index), <code>searchEmbedding</code> (<code>vector(768)</code>, HNSW cosine index; only when <code>semantic</code> is set), <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> (varchar 64), <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> (datetime), plus a <code>gin_trgm</code> index per fuzzy field.</li><li>A new field flag for system-managed fields (e.g. <code>'system' =&gt; true</code>) set on the injected columns: left out of REST serialization and <code>fields=</code>, discarded from request bodies, not in the field-ACL catalog, skipped by <code>auditBehavior</code>, not usable in <code>query</code> clauses.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SearchableRegistry</code>: lookup of the <code>search</code> block by type and by model.</li><li>Unit tests: validation, injected columns, a system field is absent from GET responses, ignored on PATCH and not audited; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> and record the flag in the relevant decisions doc.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a <code>search</code> block migrates with the four columns and indexes; its REST payloads and audit rows never contain them.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filling the embedding, querying.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-migrations"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "issue-searchable", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Issue: add the `search` metadata block", "description": "<p>Issue is the first searchable module. Add its <code>search</code> block to <code>app/metadata/model/Issue.php</code> so the migration adds the search columns and indexes to <code>issues</code>.</p><ul><li><code>'search' =&gt; ['type' =&gt; 'issue', 'fts' =&gt; ['subject' =&gt; 'A', 'description' =&gt; 'B'], 'fuzzy' =&gt; ['subject'], 'semantic' =&gt; ['subject', 'description'], 'exact' =&gt; ['issueNumber'], 'display' =&gt; ['title' =&gt; 'subject', 'snippet' =&gt; 'description']]</code></li><li>Run migrate locally and confirm the columns and indexes; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> and the graph.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>issues</code> has <code>searchVector</code> (filled for existing rows), <code>searchEmbedding</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> and the indexes; Issue GET/PATCH payloads are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other modules (they come later by adding their own block).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-metadata"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "embeddings-client", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Embeddings service: Gaia client for the Ares /embeddings endpoint", "description": "<p>Search needs document and query embeddings from Ares (<code>POST /embeddings</code>, nomic-embed-text, 768 dimensions). Like <code>core/services/LLM.php</code>, the external system sits behind one class that owns its configuration and transport.</p><p><strong>Contract (Ares)</strong>: request <code>{\\"texts\\": [...], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code> (1-64 texts, max 8000 chars each); 200 <code>{\\"model\\", \\"dimensions\\", \\"embeddings\\": [[...]]}</code>; 422 invalid; 503 model unavailable.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/services/Embeddings.php</code>: <code>embedDocuments(array $texts): array</code> and <code>embedQuery(string $text): array</code>; Guzzle, base URL <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL</code>, timeouts from env (query ~3 s, documents ~30 s).</li><li>Failures throw a dedicated exception (e.g. <code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code>) with the reason; never return an empty vector. Validates the response shape and dimension count.</li><li>Register it in <code>ServiceFactory</code> if that is how services are resolved.</li><li>Unit tests with a mocked Guzzle handler: success, 422, 503, timeout, malformed body, wrong dimensions.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests pass without network; callers get vectors or a typed exception.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> where embeddings are stored or used.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ares-embeddings"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "index-sync", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: mark records stale on change, `search embed` and `search reindex` commands", "description": "<p>A searchable record's <code>searchEmbedding</code> must follow its text. Changes are caught from every write path (REST, MCP, workflows, CLI) by a model behaviour that marks the record stale; commands fill and reconcile the embeddings. <code>searchVector</code> is a generated column and needs nothing here.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticText</code>: text from the <code>semantic</code> fields in order, HTML stripped, whitespace collapsed, cut to <code>SEARCH_EMBED_MAX_CHARS</code> (default 4000); and its sha256.</li><li><code>searchIndexBehavior</code>, attached automatically to every model with a <code>search</code> block: before save, when a <code>semantic</code> field changed (or on create), set <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> to null in the same write. No extra query, no Ares call, cannot fail the save.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/EmbeddingIndexer</code>: picks stale, non-deleted records (<code>searchEmbeddedAt IS NULL</code>) per searchable model in batches of 32 (<code>FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED</code>), calls <code>Embeddings::embedDocuments</code>, writes <code>searchEmbedding</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> with a direct bound <code>UPDATE</code> by id that bypasses model behaviours (no audit, no dateModified/modifiedUser, no live events). On <code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code> it stops the run, logs, and leaves the rows stale.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/EmbeddingReconciler</code>: walks every searchable record in pages, marks stale where the stored hash differs from the current <code>SemanticText</code> hash or the embedding is missing.</li><li><code>core/tasks/SearchTask.php</code> (parses and prints only): <code>php cli.php search embed [--limit=N]</code> and <code>php cli.php search reindex [type]</code> (reconcile, then embed), printing counts.</li><li>Unit tests with a fake Embeddings: behaviour marks stale only on semantic-field changes, embedding write leaves audit/dateModified untouched, Ares down leaves rows stale, reindex catches a changed hash.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after <code>search reindex</code> every non-deleted Issue has a 768-dimension embedding; editing its description marks it stale and the next <code>search embed</code> refreshes it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> scheduling the commands (separate issue).</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable", "embeddings-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "cli-scheduler", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Run the search commands on a schedule in the Gaia containers", "description": "<p>No container runs cron today (<code>docker/dev/start.sh</code> only migrates), so scheduled CLI tasks never run. Search needs <code>php cli.php search embed</code> every minute (picks up records marked stale by saves) and <code>php cli.php search reindex</code> every 24 hours.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Pick a scheduler that needs no new package if possible (busybox <code>crond</code> or the base image's cron) and run it in the deployed image (<code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code>, <code>start.sh</code>) and the local stack; a crontab file in the repo with the two entries (UTC), output to the container log, no overlapping runs.</li><li>Ask the reviewer whether to also enable the existing <code>workflow schedule</code> (documented as cron-driven, never run).</li><li>Document the schedule in the README; a check that the crontab lines parse.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> in the running container an edited Issue gets its new embedding within about a minute, and the daily reindex is scheduled.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a job queue system, production infrastructure outside the images.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["index-sync"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-lexical", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search core: exact, FTS and fuzzy searchers with module ACL scope and rank fusion", "description": "<p>The domain layer for module-agnostic search, driven by the <code>search</code> metadata via <code>SearchableRegistry</code>. Every search runs all modes; the caller only gives types and the query. The HTTP controller is the next issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong> in <code>core/libs/search/</code>:</p><ul><li><code>SearchRequest</code>: types, query text (trimmed, 2-200 chars), limit (default 20, max 50).</li><li><code>ExactMatcher</code>: rows whose <code>exact</code> fields equal the query (type-aware: a numeric field matches only an integer query, also <code>#123</code>); pinned first.</li><li><code>FtsSearcher</code>: <code>websearch_to_tsquery</code> against the model's <code>searchVector</code> column (same text search config), <code>ts_rank_cd</code>, snippet via <code>ts_headline</code> on the display snippet field.</li><li><code>FuzzySearcher</code>: <code>pg_trgm</code> <code>word_similarity</code> on the fuzzy fields, threshold from config (default 0.3).</li><li><code>RankFusion</code>: Reciprocal Rank Fusion (k = 60) over each searcher's ranked ids, open to more searchers (semantic comes next); items carry <code>matchedBy</code> and the fused score; exact matches stay on top.</li><li><code>SearchService</code>: for each type require <code>&lt;module&gt;.get</code> through <code>Acl</code> (denied type = 403, as for unauthorized query criteria, D-027); apply the module's record scope (<code>Acl::applyRecordScope</code>, <code>acl.groupKeys</code>, D-060) and <code>deleted = 0</code> inside each candidate query, before ranking and LIMIT (D-022). A searcher is skipped for a type when the user lacks read on a field it matches; denied display fields are omitted. Bound parameters only.</li><li>Tests: ranking order, exact pin, typo tolerance, a members-scope user never sees other projects' issues, field-ACL skip.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>SearchService</code> returns fused, ACL-scoped Issue results from exact, FTS and fuzzy matching.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching, the HTTP endpoint.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-endpoint", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "SearchController: GET /api/v1/search across searchable modules", "description": "<p>Expose the search core over HTTP. The controller has no permission of its own; authorization is the searched module's (done in <code>SearchService</code>). This is a deliberate exception to standard CRUD resources: record it as a decision in a new <code>docs/architecture/search/decisions.md</code> (and register it wherever the decisions-docs test expects), together with the search metadata, system-managed columns and ranking decisions.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>SearchController</code> with a list action only: <code>GET /api/v1/search?types=issue&amp;q=...&amp;limit=20</code>; route in <code>core/config/routes.php</code>; OAuth still required; <code>$aclMap</code> declared so the action catalog does not publish a <code>search.*</code> permission.</li><li>Thin: parse into <code>SearchRequest</code>, call <code>SearchService</code>, shape the response. 400 for missing or too short <code>q</code> or an unknown type; 403 when a requested type's <code>.get</code> is denied.</li><li>Response: <code>data</code> items <code>{type: 'searchresult', id: '&lt;type&gt;:&lt;recordId&gt;', attributes: {module, recordId, title, snippet, score, matchedBy, pinned}}</code>, <code>meta</code> <code>{query, types}</code>.</li><li>api-tester cases incl. <code>acl</code> profiles (denied module = 403, members scope hides other projects' issues); regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass; searching an issue number pins that issue; a typo in a subject word still finds it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching (next issue), Prometheus UI.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-lexical"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-semantic", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: semantic matching on the module's searchEmbedding column", "description": "<p>Add semantic matching to every search: the query is embedded through Ares and compared to the module's <code>searchEmbedding</code> column, then fused with the exact/FTS/fuzzy results.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticSearcher</code>: <code>Embeddings::embedQuery</code>, then cosine distance (<code>&lt;=&gt;</code>, HNSW index) on the module table's <code>searchEmbedding</code> (non-null), with the same record scope, ACL and <code>deleted = 0</code> as the other searchers, before LIMIT; max distance from config. Skipped when the user lacks read on any <code>semantic</code> field.</li><li>Register it in <code>SearchService</code>/<code>RankFusion</code>; it always runs for types with a <code>semantic</code> list.</li><li>Ares failure (<code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code>): the other results are still returned and <code>meta.semantic</code> is <code>unavailable</code> (otherwise <code>ok</code>), never a silent success; logged.</li><li>Tests with a fake Embeddings: a paraphrase finds the issue, scope is respected, Ares down gives the other results plus the meta flag; api-tester case for the meta field; update the search decisions doc.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> searching \\"login fails after password reset\\" finds an issue titled \\"Reset password link broken\\" with <code>matchedBy</code> containing <code>semantic</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records, re-ranking models.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-endpoint", "index-sync"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 14:36:23	2026-11-17 14:36:23	f
2922d9656afc-aa6f-0c6d-c355d92eec03	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	3	{"summary": "Module-agnostic search configured by a per-model `search` metadata block, with search columns on the module's own table (Issue first) marked with Gaia's system-field flag. Gaia gets migration support (extensions, vector, generated tsvector, GIN/trigram/HNSW), the `search` block, an `ares` service kind allowed to update only the search columns (unstamped), and a generic `search.document.changed` event published from a model hook on create or semantic-field change, plus a daily `search reindex` that republishes stale records. Hermes accepts service sockets and `service:<kind>` scoped intents. Ares runs nomic-embed-text in-process (fastembed), signs in to Gaia as a service, listens for the event, checks the dirty state by hash and writes the embedding back through Gaia; it also serves POST /embeddings for query embedding. Search runs exact, FTS, fuzzy and semantic matching fused by RRF behind GET /api/v1/search?types=&q=, with the searched module's ACL and record scope applied in SQL.", "issues": [{"key": "search-migrations", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migrations: Postgres extensions, vector and generated tsvector columns, GIN/trigram/HNSW indexes", "description": "<p>Search needs column and index kinds the declarative migrations cannot create today: they only know primary, unique and plain/multi-column indexes (<code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> ~215-271, <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> ~242). This issue adds the generic capabilities; the search metadata that uses them is the next issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Extensions: migrate runs <code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector</code> and <code>pg_trgm</code> (declared in config, idempotent).</li><li>Field type <code>vector</code> with <code>dimensions</code> (maps to <code>vector(N)</code>) in <code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code> <code>getFieldType</code> and the Postgres dialect.</li><li>Field type <code>tsvector</code> with a <code>generated</code> definition (source field =&gt; weight A-D, text search config default <code>english</code>), migrated as <code>GENERATED ALWAYS AS (setweight(to_tsvector(config, coalesce(field,'')), 'A') || ...) STORED</code>.</li><li>Index kinds <code>gin</code> (tsvector), <code>gin_trgm</code> (<code>gin_trgm_ops</code> on a text field), <code>hnsw_cosine</code> (<code>USING hnsw (col vector_cosine_ops)</code>).</li><li>Re-running migrate is a no-op; changing a generated column's sources recreates it.</li><li><code>docker-compose.yaml</code> Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code>.</li><li>Unit tests for type mapping and generated DDL; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a vector field, a generated tsvector field and the three index kinds migrates as expected and re-migrates cleanly; existing models are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>search</code> metadata block, any real model.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-metadata", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search metadata block injects system search columns into the model", "description": "<p>A model becomes searchable by declaring a <code>search</code> block in its metadata. The search data lives on the module's own table, so the block adds the search columns and indexes to the model; they are system fields and never appear in API responses.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Validate the block in the meta manager: <code>type</code> (name used in <code>/search?types=</code> and in search events, unique across models), <code>fts</code> (field =&gt; weight A-D), <code>fuzzy</code> (fields), <code>semantic</code> (ordered fields), <code>exact</code> (fields), <code>display</code> (<code>title</code>, <code>snippet</code>). Unknown fields or weights fail with a clear message.</li><li>Inject columns: <code>searchVector</code> (generated tsvector from <code>fts</code>, GIN index), <code>searchEmbedding</code> (<code>vector(768)</code>, HNSW cosine index; only when <code>semantic</code> is set), <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> (varchar 64), <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> (datetime), plus a <code>gin_trgm</code> index per fuzzy field.</li><li>Mark the injected columns with Gaia's existing system-field flag (keeps a field out of responses); also make sure they are discarded from user request bodies, are not in the field-ACL catalog, cannot be used in <code>query</code> clauses by users, and are skipped by <code>auditBehavior</code> (a 768-float vector must never be audited).</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SearchableRegistry</code>: lookup of the <code>search</code> block by type and by model.</li><li>Unit tests: validation, injected columns, a system search field is absent from GET responses, ignored on a user PATCH and not audited; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a <code>search</code> block migrates with the four columns and indexes; its REST payloads and audit rows never contain them.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filling the embedding, querying, service access.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-migrations"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "issue-searchable", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Issue: add the `search` metadata block", "description": "<p>Issue is the first searchable module. Add its <code>search</code> block to <code>app/metadata/model/Issue.php</code> so the migration adds the search columns and indexes to <code>issues</code>.</p><ul><li><code>'search' =&gt; ['type' =&gt; 'issue', 'fts' =&gt; ['subject' =&gt; 'A', 'description' =&gt; 'B'], 'fuzzy' =&gt; ['subject'], 'semantic' =&gt; ['subject', 'description'], 'exact' =&gt; ['issueNumber'], 'display' =&gt; ['title' =&gt; 'subject', 'snippet' =&gt; 'description']]</code></li><li>Run migrate locally and confirm the columns and indexes; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> and the graph.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>issues</code> has <code>searchVector</code> (filled for existing rows), <code>searchEmbedding</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> and the indexes; Issue GET/PATCH payloads are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other modules (they come later by adding their own block).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-metadata"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "service-search-access", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Ares service kind: read searchable records and write only their search columns", "description": "<p>Ares computes embeddings and stores them through Gaia, signing in as a service client (D-065/D-066). Service tokens can only <code>get</code> today, and writes are closed until it is decided who a service write is stamped as (D-066). This issue opens one narrow write: the system search columns, unstamped.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Service kind <code>ares</code> in <code>config/serviceclients.php</code> with default scopes for the searchable modules' <code>get</code>/<code>update</code>.</li><li>Every model with a <code>search</code> block opens <code>get</code> to kind <code>ares</code> (injected from the block, same as <code>acl.service</code>), including reading the system search columns (<code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>) via <code>fields=</code>; system fields stay hidden from users.</li><li>A filtered <code>update</code> for kind <code>ares</code> on those models (like D-068): the body may contain only <code>searchEmbedding</code> (768 numbers, validated), <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>; anything else is 400. The write is a bound <code>UPDATE</code> of those columns that skips audit, created/modified-user and dateModified behaviours, live events and the search event (no loop).</li><li>Record the decision in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code> (new D-number, referencing D-066).</li><li>api-tester cases: ares service token reads an issue's hash, PATCHes the embedding (200), cannot PATCH <code>subject</code> (400), a user cannot write the search columns, other service kinds are denied (401); unit tests for validation.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass and an embedding PATCH leaves the issue's audit, dateModified and modifiedUser unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> issuing the Ares client credentials in deployments.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-service-sockets", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Service sockets: accept service tokens and `service:<kind>` scoped intents", "description": "<p>Gaia's search needs Ares (a backend service) to hear a <code>search.document.changed</code> event for records in every project. Today sockets authenticate users through <code>user/me</code> and intents must name a project the user is a member of (D-008), so a service would have to join every project and stay under 100 intents. Gaia requests service-scoped subscriptions, mirroring user-scoped events (D-009). Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li>Handshake: a token with no user is checked with Gaia's introspection (<code>POST /api/v1/introspect</code>, D-065: <code>actorType: service</code>, <code>serviceKind</code>); user tokens work as today.</li><li>A new list of service-scoped events in <code>src/contract/names.js</code> (first: <code>search.document.changed</code>, added to the allowlist). Their <code>projectId</code> is <code>service:&lt;kind&gt;</code>; a socket may subscribe only when its <code>serviceKind</code> equals that kind (<code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code>). Service sockets cannot subscribe to project or user events.</li><li>Gaia publishes such events with <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> through the existing <code>POST /publish</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/auth</code> (introspection with Hermes' own service token, cached like D-012), <code>src/contract/names.js</code>, <code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code>, a new ADR in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>, tests with the stub loader.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a service socket of kind ares subscribes to <code>service:ares</code>/<code>search.document.changed</code> and receives a published envelope; a user socket is rejected for it; a service socket is rejected for project events.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other service events.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-events", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: publish `search.document.changed` and a daily `search reindex` command", "description": "<p>Embeddings are created by Ares when it hears that a searchable record's semantic text may have changed. Gaia publishes one generic event for every searchable module, from a model hook so every write path (REST, MCP, workflows, CLI) is covered, and re-publishes stale records daily because Hermes keeps no history.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Event name <code>search.document.changed</code> in <code>support/EventNames.php</code> (lockstep with Hermes <code>names.js</code>, service-scoped).</li><li><code>searchIndexBehavior</code>, attached automatically to every model with a <code>search</code> block: after create, and after update when a <code>semantic</code> field changed, publish through <code>HermesPublisher</code> with <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> and payload <code>{type, resource, recordId, semanticFields, maxChars}</code> (<code>maxChars</code> from <code>SEARCH_EMBED_MAX_CHARS</code>, default 4000). Fail open: a Hermes failure is logged and never fails the write. Not fired by the Ares search-column write.</li><li><code>core/tasks/SearchTask.php</code> (parses and prints; logic in <code>core/libs/search/</code>): <code>php cli.php search reindex [type]</code> publishes the event, paced, for every non-deleted record whose <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> is null or older than <code>dateModified</code>; prints counts.</li><li>Unit tests with a fake publisher: create publishes, a semantic edit publishes, a non-semantic edit does not, publish failure does not break the save, reindex selects only stale records.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> creating an issue or editing its description publishes one event; <code>search reindex</code> republishes every issue without an up-to-date embedding.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> scheduling the command (separate issue), the Ares consumer.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable", "hermes-service-sockets"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "cli-scheduler", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Run `search reindex` every 24 hours in the Gaia containers", "description": "<p>No container runs cron today (<code>docker/dev/start.sh</code> only migrates), so scheduled CLI tasks never run. Search needs <code>php cli.php search reindex</code> once a day to catch records whose event Ares missed.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Pick a scheduler that needs no new package if possible (busybox <code>crond</code> or the base image's cron) and run it in the deployed image (<code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code>, <code>start.sh</code>) and the local stack; a crontab file in the repo (UTC), output to the container log, no overlapping runs.</li><li>Ask the reviewer whether to also enable the existing <code>workflow schedule</code> (documented as cron-driven, never run).</li><li>Document the schedule in the README; a check that the crontab lines parse.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the container's crontab runs <code>search reindex</code> daily and its output appears in the container log.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a job queue system, production infrastructure outside the images.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-events"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-embeddings", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Run nomic-embed-text in-process and serve POST /embeddings", "description": "<p>Gaia is adding semantic search. Ares will compute all embeddings itself with the <code>nomic-embed-text</code> model running inside Ares (no external model server): for records (from search events, a later issue) and for search queries, which Gaia sends over HTTP. Please accept, adapt or decline the contract.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li><code>POST /embeddings</code> request <code>{\\"texts\\": [\\"...\\"], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code>; 1 to 64 non-empty texts of at most 8000 characters; 422 otherwise.</li><li>200 <code>{\\"model\\": \\"nomic-embed-text-v1.5\\", \\"dimensions\\": 768, \\"embeddings\\": [[...]]}</code>, same order, L2-normalised. 503 with a clear message if the model is not loaded; never a fake vector.</li><li>Ares adds the task prefixes (<code>search_document: </code> / <code>search_query: </code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>fastembed</code> (ONNX Runtime, CPU, no PyTorch; approved by the engineer for this feature).</li><li><code>routers/embeddings.py</code> (Pydantic only) -&gt; <code>services/embedding_service.py</code> (reused by the search listener) -&gt; <code>adapters/base_embedding_adapter.py</code> + <code>adapters/fastembed_adapter.py</code> via the factory. Model loaded once; inference in a thread pool so async routes are not blocked.</li><li>Env <code>EMBEDDING_MODEL</code> (default <code>nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5</code>), <code>EMBEDDING_CACHE_DIR</code>, thread count. <code>Dockerfile</code> downloads the weights at build time; <code>/health</code> reports the model loaded.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter: validation, prefixes, order, 503.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the built image returns 768-dimension vectors offline; tests pass without downloading the model.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> GPU, other models, result caching.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-gaia-client", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Sign in to Gaia as the `ares` service client and a Gaia gateway for search columns", "description": "<p>To store embeddings through Gaia, Ares needs its own Gaia identity: a service client of kind <code>ares</code> (Gaia D-065/D-066), allowed to read searchable records and update only their search columns (<code>searchEmbedding</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>). Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>adapters/gaia_auth.py</code>: OAuth <code>client_credentials</code> with <code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code> (env only, never logged); caches the token and refreshes before expiry or on 401.</li><li><code>adapters/gaia_client.py</code> (one class owning transport): <code>get_record(resource, id, fields)</code> and <code>update_search_fields(resource, id, embedding, hash, embedded_at)</code> (<code>PATCH /api/v1/&lt;resource&gt;/&lt;id&gt;</code>), typed errors for 401/403/404/5xx.</li><li>Update <code>CLAUDE.md</code> Boundaries: Ares stays stateless but now reads from and writes to Gaia as the ares service.</li><li>Tests with a mocked HTTP transport: token reuse and refresh, 404 handled, secrets never in logs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> against local Gaia with an ares client, Ares reads an issue's hash and writes an embedding.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the event listener.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["service-search-access"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-search-listener", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Listen for `search.document.changed` and keep record embeddings up to date", "description": "<p>Ares creates and updates embeddings when Gaia announces a change. Gaia publishes <code>search.document.changed</code> through Hermes to <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> with <code>{type, resource, recordId, semanticFields, maxChars}</code>; Ares checks whether the text really changed, embeds it and stores it through Gaia. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>python-socketio</code> (async client; approved by the engineer). <code>adapters/hermes_listener.py</code> connects to <code>HERMES_URL</code> with the ares service token (fresh token on every reconnect), sends <code>intents:set</code> for <code>service:ares</code>/<code>search.document.changed</code>, reconnects with backoff; started from the FastAPI lifespan.</li><li><code>services/search_index_service.py</code>: fetch the record with <code>semanticFields</code> and <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>; build the text (fields in order, HTML stripped, whitespace collapsed, cut to <code>maxChars</code>); sha256. Same hash: PATCH only <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>. Different or missing: embed with the <code>document</code> task and PATCH embedding, hash and <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>. 404 or deleted: skip.</li><li>Events processed through a bounded async queue with limited concurrency, duplicates within a short window collapsed; failures logged and left for Gaia's daily reindex (no retries storm).</li><li>Tests with fake listener, Gaia client and embedder: changed text embeds, same text only stamps, missing record skipped, embedder failure leaves the record untouched.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the local stack, editing an issue's description gives it a new embedding within seconds; editing it back to the same text does not re-embed.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ares-embeddings", "ares-gaia-client", "search-events"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "stack-pgvector-ares", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "p4m stack: pgvector Postgres image and Ares Gaia/Hermes settings", "description": "<p>Gaia's new search stores embeddings with the Postgres <code>vector</code> extension, and Ares now signs in to Gaia as a service and listens to Hermes. The stack <code>p4m</code> generates needs both. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>installer/p4m.py</code>: Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code> for the dev DB and gaia-test containers (same major version, existing volumes stay readable).</li><li>Ares env in the generated compose: <code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>HERMES_URL</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>/<code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code> read from <code>p4m.env</code> (secrets only there); <code>p4m configure</code> asks for them; README explains creating the ares service client and the bigger Ares image (embedding model).</li><li>Unit tests for the generated compose.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after <code>p4m up</code>, <code>CREATE EXTENSION vector</code> works in dev and test databases and Ares has its Gaia/Hermes settings.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> production infrastructure.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "embeddings-client", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Embeddings service: Gaia client for the Ares /embeddings endpoint (query embedding)", "description": "<p>Semantic search embeds the user's query at search time through Ares (<code>POST /embeddings</code>, task <code>query</code>, 768 dimensions). Like <code>core/services/LLM.php</code>, the external system sits behind one class that owns configuration and transport.</p><p><strong>Contract (Ares)</strong>: request <code>{\\"texts\\": [...], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code>; 200 <code>{\\"model\\", \\"dimensions\\", \\"embeddings\\": [[...]]}</code>; 422 invalid; 503 model unavailable.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/services/Embeddings.php</code>: <code>embedQuery(string $text): array</code>; Guzzle, base URL <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL</code>, short timeout from env (~3 s).</li><li>Failures throw <code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code> with the reason; never an empty vector. Validates shape and dimension count.</li><li>Register it in <code>ServiceFactory</code> if that is how services are resolved.</li><li>Unit tests with a mocked Guzzle handler: success, 422, 503, timeout, malformed body, wrong dimensions.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests pass without network.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> document embeddings (Ares makes those itself).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ares-embeddings"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-lexical", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search core: exact, FTS and fuzzy searchers with module ACL scope and rank fusion", "description": "<p>The domain layer for module-agnostic search, driven by the <code>search</code> metadata via <code>SearchableRegistry</code>. Every search runs all matching kinds; the caller only gives types and the query. The HTTP controller is the next issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong> in <code>core/libs/search/</code>:</p><ul><li><code>SearchRequest</code>: types, query text (trimmed, 2-200 chars), limit (default 20, max 50).</li><li><code>ExactMatcher</code>: rows whose <code>exact</code> fields equal the query (type-aware: numeric fields match only an integer query, also <code>#123</code>); pinned first.</li><li><code>FtsSearcher</code>: <code>websearch_to_tsquery</code> against the model's <code>searchVector</code> column (same text search config), <code>ts_rank_cd</code>, snippet via <code>ts_headline</code> on the display snippet field.</li><li><code>FuzzySearcher</code>: <code>pg_trgm</code> <code>word_similarity</code> on fuzzy fields, threshold from config (default 0.3).</li><li><code>RankFusion</code>: Reciprocal Rank Fusion (k = 60) over each searcher's ranked ids, open to more searchers (semantic comes later); items carry <code>matchedBy</code> and the fused score; exact matches stay on top.</li><li><code>SearchService</code>: per type require <code>&lt;module&gt;.get</code> through <code>Acl</code> (denied type = 403, as for unauthorized query criteria, D-027); apply the module's record scope (<code>Acl::applyRecordScope</code>, <code>acl.groupKeys</code>, D-060) and <code>deleted = 0</code> inside each candidate query, before ranking and LIMIT (D-022). A searcher is skipped for a type when the user lacks read on a field it matches; denied display fields are omitted. Bound parameters only.</li><li>Tests: ranking order, exact pin, typo tolerance, a members-scope user never sees other projects' issues, field-ACL skip.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>SearchService</code> returns fused, ACL-scoped Issue results from exact, FTS and fuzzy matching.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching, the HTTP endpoint.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-endpoint", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "SearchController: GET /api/v1/search across searchable modules", "description": "<p>Expose the search core over HTTP. The controller has no permission of its own; authorization is the searched module's (done in <code>SearchService</code>). This is a deliberate exception to standard CRUD resources: record it in a new <code>docs/architecture/search/decisions.md</code> (registered wherever the decisions-docs test expects), with the search metadata, system search columns, event-driven embedding by Ares and ranking decisions.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>SearchController</code> with a list action only: <code>GET /api/v1/search?types=issue&amp;q=...&amp;limit=20</code>; route in <code>core/config/routes.php</code>; OAuth required; <code>$aclMap</code> declared so the action catalog publishes no <code>search.*</code> permission.</li><li>Thin: parse into <code>SearchRequest</code>, call <code>SearchService</code>, shape the response. 400 for missing or too short <code>q</code> or an unknown type; 403 when a requested type's <code>.get</code> is denied.</li><li>Response: <code>data</code> items <code>{type: 'searchresult', id: '&lt;type&gt;:&lt;recordId&gt;', attributes: {module, recordId, title, snippet, score, matchedBy, pinned}}</code>, <code>meta</code> <code>{query, types}</code>.</li><li>api-tester cases incl. <code>acl</code> profiles (denied module = 403, members scope hides other projects' issues); regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass; searching an issue number pins that issue; a typo in a subject word still finds it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching (next issue), Prometheus UI.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-lexical"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-semantic", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: semantic matching on the module's searchEmbedding column", "description": "<p>Add semantic matching to every search: the query is embedded through Ares and compared to the module's <code>searchEmbedding</code> column (filled by Ares from search events), then fused with the exact/FTS/fuzzy results.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticSearcher</code>: <code>Embeddings::embedQuery</code>, then cosine distance (<code>&lt;=&gt;</code>, HNSW index) on the module table's non-null <code>searchEmbedding</code>, with the same record scope, ACL and <code>deleted = 0</code> as the other searchers, before LIMIT; max distance from config. Skipped when the user lacks read on any <code>semantic</code> field.</li><li>Register it in <code>SearchService</code>/<code>RankFusion</code>; it always runs for types with a <code>semantic</code> list.</li><li>Ares failure (<code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code>): the other results are still returned and <code>meta.semantic</code> is <code>unavailable</code> (otherwise <code>ok</code>); logged, never a silent success.</li><li>Tests with a fake Embeddings: a paraphrase finds the issue, scope respected, Ares down gives the other results plus the meta flag; api-tester case for the meta field; update the search decisions doc.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> searching \\"login fails after password reset\\" finds an issue titled \\"Reset password link broken\\" with <code>matchedBy</code> containing <code>semantic</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records, re-ranking.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-endpoint", "embeddings-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 14:48:09	2026-11-17 14:48:09	f
f97422e06afc-e6e8-3ed5-bac671370e1b	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	4	{"summary": "Module-agnostic search configured by a per-model `search` metadata block, with search columns on the module's own table (Issue first). Gaia framework work: a new `system` field flag (hidden from responses, not user-writable, not audited) and migration support (extensions, vector, generated tsvector, GIN/trigram/HNSW); then the `search` block that injects system search columns, an `ares` service kind allowed to update only those columns (unstamped), and a generic `search.document.changed` event published from a model hook on create or semantic-field change, plus a daily `search reindex` that republishes stale records. Hermes accepts service sockets and `service:<kind>` scoped intents. Ares runs nomic-embed-text in-process (fastembed), signs in to Gaia as a service, listens for the event, checks the dirty state by hash and writes the embedding back through Gaia; it also serves POST /embeddings for query embedding. Search runs exact, FTS, fuzzy and semantic matching fused by RRF behind GET /api/v1/search?types=&q=, with the searched module's ACL and record scope applied in SQL.", "issues": [{"key": "system-fields", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Metadata: `system` field flag for fields hidden from the API and not audited", "description": "<p>Gaia has no way to mark a column as managed by the system. Search is about to add columns to module tables (an embedding vector, hashes, timestamps) that must never reach API clients, never be written by users and never be audited. This issue adds a generic field flag for that.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Field property <code>'system' =&gt; true</code> in model metadata, read through the meta manager (<code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code>), with a helper listing a model's system fields.</li><li>Responses: system fields are never serialized, for the record itself, included relationships, <code>fields=</code> (silently omitted, like denied fields in D-033) and CSV export.</li><li>Writes: system fields in a user request body (POST/PUT/PATCH) are discarded, like denied write fields (D-034).</li><li>Not in the field-ACL catalog (<code>AclMapCatalog</code>) and not usable by users in <code>query</code> clauses or sort (rejected like an unknown field).</li><li><code>auditBehavior</code> skips system fields.</li><li>Opt-in access for specific internal paths is left to the code that needs it (first: the Ares search-column write); no generic bypass.</li><li>Record it as a decision in the relevant <code>docs/architecture/*/decisions.md</code>; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li><li>Tests on a fixture model: absent from GET/list/include/fields=, discarded on PATCH, rejected in a query clause, not in the audit diff, not in the permission catalog.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a field flagged <code>system</code> is invisible and read-only through the REST API and never appears in audit rows; unflagged fields behave as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any real model using the flag.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-migrations", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migrations: Postgres extensions, vector and generated tsvector columns, GIN/trigram/HNSW indexes", "description": "<p>Search needs column and index kinds the declarative migrations cannot create today: they only know primary, unique and plain/multi-column indexes (<code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> ~215-271, <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> ~242). This issue adds the generic capabilities; the search metadata that uses them comes later.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Extensions: migrate runs <code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector</code> and <code>pg_trgm</code> (declared in config, idempotent).</li><li>Field type <code>vector</code> with <code>dimensions</code> (maps to <code>vector(N)</code>) in <code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code> <code>getFieldType</code> and the Postgres dialect.</li><li>Field type <code>tsvector</code> with a <code>generated</code> definition (source field =&gt; weight A-D, text search config default <code>english</code>), migrated as <code>GENERATED ALWAYS AS (setweight(to_tsvector(config, coalesce(field,'')), 'A') || ...) STORED</code>.</li><li>Index kinds <code>gin</code> (tsvector), <code>gin_trgm</code> (<code>gin_trgm_ops</code> on a text field), <code>hnsw_cosine</code> (<code>USING hnsw (col vector_cosine_ops)</code>).</li><li>Re-running migrate is a no-op; changing a generated column's sources recreates it.</li><li><code>docker-compose.yaml</code> Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code>.</li><li>Unit tests for type mapping and generated DDL; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a vector field, a generated tsvector field and the three index kinds migrates as expected and re-migrates cleanly; existing models are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>search</code> metadata block, any real model.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-metadata", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search metadata block injects system search columns into the model", "description": "<p>A model becomes searchable by declaring a <code>search</code> block in its metadata. The search data lives on the module's own table, so the block adds the search columns and indexes to the model, flagged as system fields so they never appear in the API.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Validate the block in the meta manager: <code>type</code> (name used in <code>/search?types=</code> and in search events, unique across models), <code>fts</code> (field =&gt; weight A-D), <code>fuzzy</code> (fields), <code>semantic</code> (ordered fields), <code>exact</code> (fields), <code>display</code> (<code>title</code>, <code>snippet</code>). Unknown fields or weights fail with a clear message.</li><li>Inject columns, all with <code>'system' =&gt; true</code>: <code>searchVector</code> (generated tsvector from <code>fts</code>, GIN index), <code>searchEmbedding</code> (<code>vector(768)</code>, HNSW cosine index; only when <code>semantic</code> is set), <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> (varchar 64), <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> (datetime); plus a <code>gin_trgm</code> index per fuzzy field.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SearchableRegistry</code>: lookup of the <code>search</code> block by type and by model.</li><li>Unit tests: validation, injected columns and indexes, columns flagged system; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a <code>search</code> block migrates with the four system columns and indexes; its REST payloads and audit rows never contain them.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filling the embedding, querying, service access.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["system-fields", "search-migrations"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "issue-searchable", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Issue: add the `search` metadata block", "description": "<p>Issue is the first searchable module. Add its <code>search</code> block to <code>app/metadata/model/Issue.php</code> so the migration adds the search columns and indexes to <code>issues</code>.</p><ul><li><code>'search' =&gt; ['type' =&gt; 'issue', 'fts' =&gt; ['subject' =&gt; 'A', 'description' =&gt; 'B'], 'fuzzy' =&gt; ['subject'], 'semantic' =&gt; ['subject', 'description'], 'exact' =&gt; ['issueNumber'], 'display' =&gt; ['title' =&gt; 'subject', 'snippet' =&gt; 'description']]</code></li><li>Run migrate locally and confirm the columns and indexes; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> and the graph.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>issues</code> has <code>searchVector</code> (filled for existing rows), <code>searchEmbedding</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> and the indexes; Issue GET/PATCH payloads are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other modules (they come later by adding their own block).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-metadata"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "service-search-access", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Ares service kind: read searchable records and write only their search columns", "description": "<p>Ares computes embeddings and stores them through Gaia, signing in as a service client (D-065/D-066). Service tokens can only <code>get</code> today, writes are closed until it is decided who a service write is stamped as (D-066), and the search columns are <code>system</code> fields hidden from the API. This issue opens one narrow, explicit path to them.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Service kind <code>ares</code> in <code>config/serviceclients.php</code> with default scopes for the searchable modules' <code>get</code>/<code>update</code>.</li><li>Every model with a <code>search</code> block opens <code>get</code> to kind <code>ares</code> (injected from the block, same mechanism as <code>acl.service</code>); for that kind only, <code>fields=searchEmbeddingHash,searchEmbeddedAt</code> returns those system fields. Users still never see them.</li><li>A filtered <code>update</code> for kind <code>ares</code> on those models (like D-068): the body may contain only <code>searchEmbedding</code> (768 numbers, validated), <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>; anything else is 400. The write is a bound <code>UPDATE</code> of those columns that skips audit, created/modified-user and dateModified behaviours, live events and the search event (no loop).</li><li>Record the decision in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code> (new D-number, referencing D-066).</li><li>api-tester cases: ares service token reads an issue's hash, PATCHes the embedding (200), cannot PATCH <code>subject</code> (400), a user cannot read or write the search columns, other service kinds are denied (401); unit tests for validation.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass and an embedding PATCH leaves the issue's audit, dateModified and modifiedUser unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> issuing the Ares client credentials in deployments.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-service-sockets", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Service sockets: accept service tokens and `service:<kind>` scoped intents", "description": "<p>Gaia's search needs Ares (a backend service) to hear a <code>search.document.changed</code> event for records in every project. Today sockets authenticate users through <code>user/me</code> and intents must name a project the user is a member of (D-008), so a service would have to join every project and stay under 100 intents. Gaia requests service-scoped subscriptions, mirroring user-scoped events (D-009). Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li>Handshake: a token with no user is checked with Gaia's introspection (<code>POST /api/v1/introspect</code>, D-065: <code>actorType: service</code>, <code>serviceKind</code>); user tokens work as today.</li><li>A new list of service-scoped events in <code>src/contract/names.js</code> (first: <code>search.document.changed</code>, added to the allowlist). Their <code>projectId</code> is <code>service:&lt;kind&gt;</code>; a socket may subscribe only when its <code>serviceKind</code> equals that kind (<code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code>). Service sockets cannot subscribe to project or user events.</li><li>Gaia publishes such events with <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> through the existing <code>POST /publish</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/auth</code> (introspection with Hermes' own service token, cached like D-012), <code>src/contract/names.js</code>, <code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code>, a new ADR in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>, tests with the stub loader.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a service socket of kind ares subscribes to <code>service:ares</code>/<code>search.document.changed</code> and receives a published envelope; a user socket is rejected for it; a service socket is rejected for project events.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other service events.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-events", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: publish `search.document.changed` and a daily `search reindex` command", "description": "<p>Embeddings are created by Ares when it hears that a searchable record's semantic text may have changed. Gaia publishes one generic event for every searchable module, from a model hook so every write path (REST, MCP, workflows, CLI) is covered, and re-publishes stale records daily because Hermes keeps no history.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Event name <code>search.document.changed</code> in <code>support/EventNames.php</code> (lockstep with Hermes <code>names.js</code>, service-scoped).</li><li><code>searchIndexBehavior</code>, attached automatically to every model with a <code>search</code> block: after create, and after update when a <code>semantic</code> field changed, publish through <code>HermesPublisher</code> with <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> and payload <code>{type, resource, recordId, semanticFields, maxChars}</code> (<code>maxChars</code> from <code>SEARCH_EMBED_MAX_CHARS</code>, default 4000). Fail open: a Hermes failure is logged and never fails the write. Not fired by the Ares search-column write.</li><li><code>core/tasks/SearchTask.php</code> (parses and prints; logic in <code>core/libs/search/</code>): <code>php cli.php search reindex [type]</code> publishes the event, paced, for every non-deleted record whose <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> is null or older than <code>dateModified</code>; prints counts.</li><li>Unit tests with a fake publisher: create publishes, a semantic edit publishes, a non-semantic edit does not, publish failure does not break the save, reindex selects only stale records.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> creating an issue or editing its description publishes one event; <code>search reindex</code> republishes every issue without an up-to-date embedding.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> scheduling the command (separate issue), the Ares consumer.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable", "hermes-service-sockets"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "cli-scheduler", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Run `search reindex` every 24 hours in the Gaia containers", "description": "<p>No container runs cron today (<code>docker/dev/start.sh</code> only migrates), so scheduled CLI tasks never run. Search needs <code>php cli.php search reindex</code> once a day to catch records whose event Ares missed.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Pick a scheduler that needs no new package if possible (busybox <code>crond</code> or the base image's cron) and run it in the deployed image (<code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code>, <code>start.sh</code>) and the local stack; a crontab file in the repo (UTC), output to the container log, no overlapping runs.</li><li>Ask the reviewer whether to also enable the existing <code>workflow schedule</code> (documented as cron-driven, never run).</li><li>Document the schedule in the README; a check that the crontab lines parse.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the container's crontab runs <code>search reindex</code> daily and its output appears in the container log.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a job queue system, production infrastructure outside the images.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-events"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-embeddings", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Run nomic-embed-text in-process and serve POST /embeddings", "description": "<p>Gaia is adding semantic search. Ares will compute all embeddings itself with the <code>nomic-embed-text</code> model running inside Ares (no external model server): for records (from search events, a later issue) and for search queries, which Gaia sends over HTTP. Please accept, adapt or decline the contract.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li><code>POST /embeddings</code> request <code>{\\"texts\\": [\\"...\\"], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code>; 1 to 64 non-empty texts of at most 8000 characters; 422 otherwise.</li><li>200 <code>{\\"model\\": \\"nomic-embed-text-v1.5\\", \\"dimensions\\": 768, \\"embeddings\\": [[...]]}</code>, same order, L2-normalised. 503 with a clear message if the model is not loaded; never a fake vector.</li><li>Ares adds the task prefixes (<code>search_document: </code> / <code>search_query: </code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>fastembed</code> (ONNX Runtime, CPU, no PyTorch; approved by the engineer for this feature).</li><li><code>routers/embeddings.py</code> (Pydantic only) -&gt; <code>services/embedding_service.py</code> (reused by the search listener) -&gt; <code>adapters/base_embedding_adapter.py</code> + <code>adapters/fastembed_adapter.py</code> via the factory. Model loaded once; inference in a thread pool so async routes are not blocked.</li><li>Env <code>EMBEDDING_MODEL</code> (default <code>nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5</code>), <code>EMBEDDING_CACHE_DIR</code>, thread count. <code>Dockerfile</code> downloads the weights at build time; <code>/health</code> reports the model loaded.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter: validation, prefixes, order, 503.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the built image returns 768-dimension vectors offline; tests pass without downloading the model.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> GPU, other models, result caching.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-gaia-client", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Sign in to Gaia as the `ares` service client and a Gaia gateway for search columns", "description": "<p>To store embeddings through Gaia, Ares needs its own Gaia identity: a service client of kind <code>ares</code> (Gaia D-065/D-066), allowed to read searchable records and update only their search columns (<code>searchEmbedding</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>). Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>adapters/gaia_auth.py</code>: OAuth <code>client_credentials</code> with <code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code> (env only, never logged); caches the token and refreshes before expiry or on 401.</li><li><code>adapters/gaia_client.py</code> (one class owning transport): <code>get_record(resource, id, fields)</code> and <code>update_search_fields(resource, id, embedding, hash, embedded_at)</code> (<code>PATCH /api/v1/&lt;resource&gt;/&lt;id&gt;</code>), typed errors for 401/403/404/5xx.</li><li>Update <code>CLAUDE.md</code> Boundaries: Ares stays stateless but now reads from and writes to Gaia as the ares service.</li><li>Tests with a mocked HTTP transport: token reuse and refresh, 404 handled, secrets never in logs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> against local Gaia with an ares client, Ares reads an issue's hash and writes an embedding.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the event listener.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["service-search-access"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-search-listener", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Listen for `search.document.changed` and keep record embeddings up to date", "description": "<p>Ares creates and updates embeddings when Gaia announces a change. Gaia publishes <code>search.document.changed</code> through Hermes to <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> with <code>{type, resource, recordId, semanticFields, maxChars}</code>; Ares checks whether the text really changed, embeds it and stores it through Gaia. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>python-socketio</code> (async client; approved by the engineer). <code>adapters/hermes_listener.py</code> connects to <code>HERMES_URL</code> with the ares service token (fresh token on every reconnect), sends <code>intents:set</code> for <code>service:ares</code>/<code>search.document.changed</code>, reconnects with backoff; started from the FastAPI lifespan.</li><li><code>services/search_index_service.py</code>: fetch the record with <code>semanticFields</code> and <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>; build the text (fields in order, HTML stripped, whitespace collapsed, cut to <code>maxChars</code>); sha256. Same hash: PATCH only <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>. Different or missing: embed with the <code>document</code> task and PATCH embedding, hash and <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>. 404 or deleted: skip.</li><li>Events processed through a bounded async queue with limited concurrency, duplicates within a short window collapsed; failures logged and left for Gaia's daily reindex (no retry storm).</li><li>Tests with fake listener, Gaia client and embedder: changed text embeds, same text only stamps, missing record skipped, embedder failure leaves the record untouched.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the local stack, editing an issue's description gives it a new embedding within seconds; editing it back to the same text does not re-embed.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ares-embeddings", "ares-gaia-client", "search-events"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "stack-pgvector-ares", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "p4m stack: pgvector Postgres image and Ares Gaia/Hermes settings", "description": "<p>Gaia's new search stores embeddings with the Postgres <code>vector</code> extension, and Ares now signs in to Gaia as a service and listens to Hermes. The stack <code>p4m</code> generates needs both. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>installer/p4m.py</code>: Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code> for the dev DB and gaia-test containers (same major version, existing volumes stay readable).</li><li>Ares env in the generated compose: <code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>HERMES_URL</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>/<code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code> read from <code>p4m.env</code> (secrets only there); <code>p4m configure</code> asks for them; README explains creating the ares service client and the bigger Ares image (embedding model).</li><li>Unit tests for the generated compose.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after <code>p4m up</code>, <code>CREATE EXTENSION vector</code> works in dev and test databases and Ares has its Gaia/Hermes settings.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> production infrastructure.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "embeddings-client", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Embeddings service: Gaia client for the Ares /embeddings endpoint (query embedding)", "description": "<p>Semantic search embeds the user's query at search time through Ares (<code>POST /embeddings</code>, task <code>query</code>, 768 dimensions). Like <code>core/services/LLM.php</code>, the external system sits behind one class that owns configuration and transport.</p><p><strong>Contract (Ares)</strong>: request <code>{\\"texts\\": [...], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code>; 200 <code>{\\"model\\", \\"dimensions\\", \\"embeddings\\": [[...]]}</code>; 422 invalid; 503 model unavailable.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/services/Embeddings.php</code>: <code>embedQuery(string $text): array</code>; Guzzle, base URL <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL</code>, short timeout from env (~3 s).</li><li>Failures throw <code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code> with the reason; never an empty vector. Validates shape and dimension count.</li><li>Register it in <code>ServiceFactory</code> if that is how services are resolved.</li><li>Unit tests with a mocked Guzzle handler: success, 422, 503, timeout, malformed body, wrong dimensions.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests pass without network.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> document embeddings (Ares makes those itself).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ares-embeddings"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-lexical", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search core: exact, FTS and fuzzy searchers with module ACL scope and rank fusion", "description": "<p>The domain layer for module-agnostic search, driven by the <code>search</code> metadata via <code>SearchableRegistry</code>. Every search runs all matching kinds; the caller only gives types and the query. The HTTP controller is the next issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong> in <code>core/libs/search/</code>:</p><ul><li><code>SearchRequest</code>: types, query text (trimmed, 2-200 chars), limit (default 20, max 50).</li><li><code>ExactMatcher</code>: rows whose <code>exact</code> fields equal the query (type-aware: numeric fields match only an integer query, also <code>#123</code>); pinned first.</li><li><code>FtsSearcher</code>: <code>websearch_to_tsquery</code> against the model's system <code>searchVector</code> column (same text search config), <code>ts_rank_cd</code>, snippet via <code>ts_headline</code> on the display snippet field.</li><li><code>FuzzySearcher</code>: <code>pg_trgm</code> <code>word_similarity</code> on fuzzy fields, threshold from config (default 0.3).</li><li><code>RankFusion</code>: Reciprocal Rank Fusion (k = 60) over each searcher's ranked ids, open to more searchers (semantic comes later); items carry <code>matchedBy</code> and the fused score; exact matches stay on top.</li><li><code>SearchService</code>: per type require <code>&lt;module&gt;.get</code> through <code>Acl</code> (denied type = 403, as for unauthorized query criteria, D-027); apply the module's record scope (<code>Acl::applyRecordScope</code>, <code>acl.groupKeys</code>, D-060) and <code>deleted = 0</code> inside each candidate query, before ranking and LIMIT (D-022). A searcher is skipped for a type when the user lacks read on a field it matches; denied display fields are omitted. Bound parameters only.</li><li>Tests: ranking order, exact pin, typo tolerance, a members-scope user never sees other projects' issues, field-ACL skip.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>SearchService</code> returns fused, ACL-scoped Issue results from exact, FTS and fuzzy matching.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching, the HTTP endpoint.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-endpoint", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "SearchController: GET /api/v1/search across searchable modules", "description": "<p>Expose the search core over HTTP. The controller has no permission of its own; authorization is the searched module's (done in <code>SearchService</code>). This is a deliberate exception to standard CRUD resources: record it in a new <code>docs/architecture/search/decisions.md</code> (registered wherever the decisions-docs test expects), with the search metadata, system search columns, event-driven embedding by Ares and ranking decisions.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>SearchController</code> with a list action only: <code>GET /api/v1/search?types=issue&amp;q=...&amp;limit=20</code>; route in <code>core/config/routes.php</code>; OAuth required; <code>$aclMap</code> declared so the action catalog publishes no <code>search.*</code> permission.</li><li>Thin: parse into <code>SearchRequest</code>, call <code>SearchService</code>, shape the response. 400 for missing or too short <code>q</code> or an unknown type; 403 when a requested type's <code>.get</code> is denied.</li><li>Response: <code>data</code> items <code>{type: 'searchresult', id: '&lt;type&gt;:&lt;recordId&gt;', attributes: {module, recordId, title, snippet, score, matchedBy, pinned}}</code>, <code>meta</code> <code>{query, types}</code>.</li><li>api-tester cases incl. <code>acl</code> profiles (denied module = 403, members scope hides other projects' issues); regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass; searching an issue number pins that issue; a typo in a subject word still finds it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching (next issue), Prometheus UI.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-lexical"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-semantic", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: semantic matching on the module's searchEmbedding column", "description": "<p>Add semantic matching to every search: the query is embedded through Ares and compared to the module's system <code>searchEmbedding</code> column (filled by Ares from search events), then fused with the exact/FTS/fuzzy results.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticSearcher</code>: <code>Embeddings::embedQuery</code>, then cosine distance (<code>&lt;=&gt;</code>, HNSW index) on the module table's non-null <code>searchEmbedding</code>, with the same record scope, ACL and <code>deleted = 0</code> as the other searchers, before LIMIT; max distance from config. Skipped when the user lacks read on any <code>semantic</code> field.</li><li>Register it in <code>SearchService</code>/<code>RankFusion</code>; it always runs for types with a <code>semantic</code> list.</li><li>Ares failure (<code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code>): the other results are still returned and <code>meta.semantic</code> is <code>unavailable</code> (otherwise <code>ok</code>); logged, never a silent success.</li><li>Tests with a fake Embeddings: a paraphrase finds the issue, scope respected, Ares down gives the other results plus the meta flag; api-tester case for the meta field; update the search decisions doc.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> searching \\"login fails after password reset\\" finds an issue titled \\"Reset password link broken\\" with <code>matchedBy</code> containing <code>semantic</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records, re-ranking.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-endpoint", "embeddings-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 15:04:25	2026-11-17 15:04:25	f
dc0c6a366afc-07a6-74f5-1e90e0dcdb01	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	5	{"summary": "Module-agnostic search configured by a per-model `search` metadata block, with search columns on the module's own table (Issue first). Gaia framework work: a new `system` field flag (hidden from responses, not user-writable, not audited) and migration support (extensions, vector, generated tsvector, GIN/trigram/HNSW); then the `search` block that injects system search columns and owns the canonical semantic text and hash, an `ares` service kind that reads that text and writes the embedding only when the hash it embedded matches the record's current hash (409 otherwise), and a generic `search.semantic.changed` event published from a model hook on create or semantic-field change, plus a daily `search reindex` that republishes records whose stored hash is stale. Hermes accepts service sockets and `service:<kind>` scoped intents. Ares runs nomic-embed-text in-process (fastembed), signs in to Gaia as a service, listens for the event, compares hashes, embeds and writes back through Gaia, dropping 409s; it also serves POST /embeddings for query embedding. Search runs exact, FTS, fuzzy and semantic matching fused by RRF behind GET /api/v1/search?types=&q=, with the searched module's ACL and record scope applied in SQL.", "issues": [{"key": "system-fields", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Metadata: `system` field flag for fields hidden from the API and not audited", "description": "<p>Gaia has no way to mark a column as managed by the system. Search is about to add columns to module tables (an embedding vector, hashes, timestamps) that must never reach API clients, never be written by users and never be audited. This issue adds a generic field flag for that.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Field property <code>'system' =&gt; true</code> in model metadata, read through the meta manager (<code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code>), with a helper listing a model's system fields.</li><li>Responses: system fields are never serialized, for the record itself, included relationships, <code>fields=</code> (silently omitted, like denied fields in D-033) and CSV export.</li><li>Writes: system fields in a user request body (POST/PUT/PATCH) are discarded, like denied write fields (D-034).</li><li>Not in the field-ACL catalog (<code>AclMapCatalog</code>) and not usable by users in <code>query</code> clauses or sort (rejected like an unknown field).</li><li><code>auditBehavior</code> skips system fields.</li><li>Opt-in access for specific internal paths is left to the code that needs it (first: the Ares search-column write); no generic bypass.</li><li>Record it as a decision in the relevant <code>docs/architecture/*/decisions.md</code>; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li><li>Tests on a fixture model: absent from GET/list/include/fields=, discarded on PATCH, rejected in a query clause, not in the audit diff, not in the permission catalog.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a field flagged <code>system</code> is invisible and read-only through the REST API and never appears in audit rows; unflagged fields behave as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any real model using the flag.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-migrations", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migrations: Postgres extensions, vector and generated tsvector columns, GIN/trigram/HNSW indexes", "description": "<p>Search needs column and index kinds the declarative migrations cannot create today: they only know primary, unique and plain/multi-column indexes (<code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> ~215-271, <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> ~242). This issue adds the generic capabilities; the search metadata that uses them comes later.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Extensions: migrate runs <code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector</code> and <code>pg_trgm</code> (declared in config, idempotent).</li><li>Field type <code>vector</code> with <code>dimensions</code> (maps to <code>vector(N)</code>) in <code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code> <code>getFieldType</code> and the Postgres dialect.</li><li>Field type <code>tsvector</code> with a <code>generated</code> definition (source field =&gt; weight A-D, text search config default <code>english</code>), migrated as <code>GENERATED ALWAYS AS (setweight(to_tsvector(config, coalesce(field,'')), 'A') || ...) STORED</code>.</li><li>Index kinds <code>gin</code> (tsvector), <code>gin_trgm</code> (<code>gin_trgm_ops</code> on a text field), <code>hnsw_cosine</code> (<code>USING hnsw (col vector_cosine_ops)</code>).</li><li>Re-running migrate is a no-op; changing a generated column's sources recreates it.</li><li><code>docker-compose.yaml</code> Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code>.</li><li>Unit tests for type mapping and generated DDL; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a vector field, a generated tsvector field and the three index kinds migrates as expected and re-migrates cleanly; existing models are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>search</code> metadata block, any real model.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-metadata", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search metadata block: system search columns and the canonical semantic text", "description": "<p>A model becomes searchable by declaring a <code>search</code> block in its metadata. The search data lives on the module's own table, so the block adds the search columns and indexes to the model, flagged as system fields. Gaia is also the single owner of the text that gets embedded and its hash, so every consumer (Ares, the stale-write check, the reindex) agrees on it.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Validate the block in the meta manager: <code>type</code> (name used in <code>/search?types=</code> and in search events, unique across models), <code>fts</code> (field =&gt; weight A-D), <code>fuzzy</code> (fields), <code>semantic</code> (ordered fields), <code>exact</code> (fields), <code>display</code> (<code>title</code>, <code>snippet</code>). Unknown fields or weights fail with a clear message.</li><li>Inject columns, all with <code>'system' =&gt; true</code>: <code>searchVector</code> (generated tsvector from <code>fts</code>, GIN index), <code>searchEmbedding</code> (<code>vector(768)</code>, HNSW cosine index; only when <code>semantic</code> is set), <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> (varchar 64, the hash of the text the stored vector was made from), <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> (datetime); plus a <code>gin_trgm</code> index per fuzzy field.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticText</code>: builds a record's canonical semantic text (the <code>semantic</code> fields in order, HTML stripped, whitespace collapsed, cut to <code>SEARCH_EMBED_MAX_CHARS</code>, default 4000) and its sha256. Deterministic; the only implementation of this rule.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SearchableRegistry</code>: lookup of the <code>search</code> block by type and by model.</li><li>Unit tests: validation, injected columns and indexes, columns flagged system, <code>SemanticText</code> output and hash stability (HTML, whitespace, truncation, null fields); regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a <code>search</code> block migrates with the four system columns and indexes; its REST payloads and audit rows never contain them; <code>SemanticText</code> gives the same hash for the same field values.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filling the embedding, querying, service access.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["system-fields", "search-migrations"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "issue-searchable", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Issue: add the `search` metadata block", "description": "<p>Issue is the first searchable module. Add its <code>search</code> block to <code>app/metadata/model/Issue.php</code> so the migration adds the search columns and indexes to <code>issues</code>.</p><ul><li><code>'search' =&gt; ['type' =&gt; 'issue', 'fts' =&gt; ['subject' =&gt; 'A', 'description' =&gt; 'B'], 'fuzzy' =&gt; ['subject'], 'semantic' =&gt; ['subject', 'description'], 'exact' =&gt; ['issueNumber'], 'display' =&gt; ['title' =&gt; 'subject', 'snippet' =&gt; 'description']]</code></li><li>Run migrate locally and confirm the columns and indexes; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> and the graph.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>issues</code> has <code>searchVector</code> (filled for existing rows), <code>searchEmbedding</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> and the indexes; Issue GET/PATCH payloads are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other modules (they come later by adding their own block).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-metadata"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "service-search-access", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Ares service kind: read the semantic text and write embeddings only for the current text (409 when stale)", "description": "<p>Ares computes embeddings and stores them through Gaia, signing in as a service client (D-065/D-066). Service tokens can only <code>get</code> today, writes are closed until it is decided who a service write is stamped as (D-066), and the search columns are <code>system</code> fields hidden from the API. This issue opens one narrow, explicit path. Because events can be handled out of order, an embedding is stored only if it was made from the record's current semantic text; a slow, older write must never overwrite a newer embedding.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Service kind <code>ares</code> in <code>config/serviceclients.php</code> with default scopes for the searchable modules' <code>get</code>/<code>update</code>.</li><li>Every model with a <code>search</code> block opens <code>get</code> to kind <code>ares</code> (injected from the block, same mechanism as <code>acl.service</code>). For that kind only, <code>fields=</code> can return the computed read-only attributes <code>searchSemanticText</code> and <code>searchSemanticHash</code> (from <code>SemanticText</code>) and the stored <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>. Users never see any of them.</li><li>A filtered <code>update</code> for kind <code>ares</code> (like D-068): body <code>{searchEmbedding (768 numbers, validated), searchEmbeddingHash}</code> only; anything else is 400. In one transaction: lock the row (<code>SELECT ... FOR UPDATE</code>), recompute the current hash with <code>SemanticText</code>; if it differs from the sent <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, return <strong>409</strong> and write nothing; otherwise store vector and hash and set <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> to now. Deleted or missing record: 404.</li><li>The write is a bound <code>UPDATE</code> of the search columns that skips audit, created/modified-user and dateModified behaviours, live events and the search event (no loop).</li><li>Record the decisions in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code> (new D-number, referencing D-066): unstamped service write of system search columns, hash precondition with 409.</li><li>api-tester cases: ares token reads <code>searchSemanticHash</code>; PATCH with the current hash 200; PATCH with an old hash after a subject change 409 and the stored vector unchanged; PATCH of <code>subject</code> 400; a user cannot read or write the search fields; other service kinds 401. Unit test for the lock-and-compare path.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass; an accepted PATCH leaves the issue's audit, dateModified and modifiedUser unchanged; a stale PATCH never overwrites a newer embedding.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> issuing the Ares client credentials in deployments.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-service-sockets", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Service sockets: accept service tokens and `service:<kind>` scoped intents", "description": "<p>Gaia's search needs Ares (a backend service) to hear a <code>search.semantic.changed</code> event for records in every project. Today sockets authenticate users through <code>user/me</code> and intents must name a project the user is a member of (D-008), so a service would have to join every project and stay under 100 intents. Gaia requests service-scoped subscriptions, mirroring user-scoped events (D-009). Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li>Handshake: a token with no user is checked with Gaia's introspection (<code>POST /api/v1/introspect</code>, D-065: <code>actorType: service</code>, <code>serviceKind</code>); user tokens work as today.</li><li>A new list of service-scoped events in <code>src/contract/names.js</code> (first: <code>search.semantic.changed</code>, added to the allowlist). Their <code>projectId</code> is <code>service:&lt;kind&gt;</code>; a socket may subscribe only when its <code>serviceKind</code> equals that kind (<code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code>). Service sockets cannot subscribe to project or user events.</li><li>Gaia publishes such events with <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> through the existing <code>POST /publish</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/auth</code> (introspection with Hermes' own service token, cached like D-012), <code>src/contract/names.js</code>, <code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code>, a new ADR in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>, tests with the stub loader.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a service socket of kind ares subscribes to <code>service:ares</code>/<code>search.semantic.changed</code> and receives a published envelope; a user socket is rejected for it; a service socket is rejected for project events.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other service events.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-events", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: publish `search.semantic.changed` and a daily `search reindex` command", "description": "<p>Embeddings are created by Ares when it hears that a searchable record's semantic text may have changed. Gaia publishes one generic event for every searchable module, from a model hook so every write path (REST, MCP, workflows, CLI) is covered, and re-publishes stale records daily because Hermes keeps no history.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Event name <code>search.semantic.changed</code> in <code>support/EventNames.php</code> (lockstep with Hermes <code>names.js</code>, service-scoped).</li><li><code>searchIndexBehavior</code>, attached automatically to every model with a <code>search</code> block: after create, and after update when a <code>semantic</code> field changed, publish through <code>HermesPublisher</code> with <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> and payload <code>{type, resource, recordId}</code> (Ares reads the text and hash from Gaia). Fail open: a Hermes failure is logged and never fails the write. Not fired by the Ares search-column write.</li><li><code>core/tasks/SearchTask.php</code> (parses and prints; logic in <code>core/libs/search/</code>): <code>php cli.php search reindex [type]</code> pages through every non-deleted searchable record and publishes the event, paced, where <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> is null or differs from the current <code>SemanticText</code> hash; prints counts.</li><li>Unit tests with a fake publisher: create publishes, a semantic edit publishes, a non-semantic edit does not, publish failure does not break the save, reindex selects only records whose hash is missing or stale.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> creating an issue or editing its description publishes one event; <code>search reindex</code> republishes every issue without an up-to-date embedding and nothing else.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> scheduling the command (separate issue), the Ares consumer.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable", "hermes-service-sockets"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "cli-scheduler", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Run `search reindex` every 24 hours in the Gaia containers", "description": "<p>No container runs cron today (<code>docker/dev/start.sh</code> only migrates), so scheduled CLI tasks never run. Search needs <code>php cli.php search reindex</code> once a day to catch records whose event Ares missed.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Pick a scheduler that needs no new package if possible (busybox <code>crond</code> or the base image's cron) and run it in the deployed image (<code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code>, <code>start.sh</code>) and the local stack; a crontab file in the repo (UTC), output to the container log, no overlapping runs.</li><li>Ask the reviewer whether to also enable the existing <code>workflow schedule</code> (documented as cron-driven, never run).</li><li>Document the schedule in the README; a check that the crontab lines parse.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the container's crontab runs <code>search reindex</code> daily and its output appears in the container log.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a job queue system, production infrastructure outside the images.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-events"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-embeddings", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Run nomic-embed-text in-process and serve POST /embeddings", "description": "<p>Gaia is adding semantic search. Ares will compute all embeddings itself with the <code>nomic-embed-text</code> model running inside Ares (no external model server): for records (from search events, a later issue) and for search queries, which Gaia sends over HTTP. Please accept, adapt or decline the contract.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li><code>POST /embeddings</code> request <code>{\\"texts\\": [\\"...\\"], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code>; 1 to 64 non-empty texts of at most 8000 characters; 422 otherwise.</li><li>200 <code>{\\"model\\": \\"nomic-embed-text-v1.5\\", \\"dimensions\\": 768, \\"embeddings\\": [[...]]}</code>, same order, L2-normalised. 503 with a clear message if the model is not loaded; never a fake vector.</li><li>Ares adds the task prefixes (<code>search_document: </code> / <code>search_query: </code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>fastembed</code> (ONNX Runtime, CPU, no PyTorch; approved by the engineer for this feature).</li><li><code>routers/embeddings.py</code> (Pydantic only) -&gt; <code>services/embedding_service.py</code> (reused by the search listener) -&gt; <code>adapters/base_embedding_adapter.py</code> + <code>adapters/fastembed_adapter.py</code> via the factory. Model loaded once; inference in a thread pool so async routes are not blocked.</li><li>Env <code>EMBEDDING_MODEL</code> (default <code>nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5</code>), <code>EMBEDDING_CACHE_DIR</code>, thread count. <code>Dockerfile</code> downloads the weights at build time; <code>/health</code> reports the model loaded.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter: validation, prefixes, order, 503.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the built image returns 768-dimension vectors offline; tests pass without downloading the model.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> GPU, other models, result caching.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-gaia-client", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Sign in to Gaia as the `ares` service client and a Gaia gateway for search fields", "description": "<p>To store embeddings through Gaia, Ares needs its own Gaia identity: a service client of kind <code>ares</code> (Gaia D-065/D-066). Gaia lets it read a searchable record's canonical <code>searchSemanticText</code>, <code>searchSemanticHash</code> and stored <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, and PATCH <code>{searchEmbedding, searchEmbeddingHash}</code>; Gaia answers 409 when the hash no longer matches the record's current text. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>adapters/gaia_auth.py</code>: OAuth <code>client_credentials</code> with <code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code> (env only, never logged); caches the token and refreshes before expiry or on 401.</li><li><code>adapters/gaia_client.py</code> (one class owning transport): <code>get_search_state(resource, id)</code> (the four fields above) and <code>store_embedding(resource, id, embedding, text_hash)</code> (<code>PATCH /api/v1/&lt;resource&gt;/&lt;id&gt;</code>); typed results/errors for 404, <strong>409 stale</strong>, 401/403 and 5xx.</li><li>Update <code>CLAUDE.md</code> Boundaries: Ares stays stateless but now reads from and writes to Gaia as the ares service.</li><li>Tests with a mocked HTTP transport: token reuse and refresh, 404 and 409 mapped to typed results, secrets never in logs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> against local Gaia with an ares client, Ares reads an issue's semantic text and hash and stores an embedding; a stale hash comes back as the 409 result.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the event listener.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["service-search-access"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-search-listener", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Listen for `search.semantic.changed` and keep record embeddings up to date", "description": "<p>Ares creates and updates embeddings when Gaia announces a change. Gaia publishes <code>search.semantic.changed</code> through Hermes to <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> with <code>{type, resource, recordId}</code>. Ares checks the record's dirty state, embeds the canonical text Gaia gives it and stores it with the hash of that text; Gaia rejects it with 409 if the text changed meanwhile. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>python-socketio</code> (async client; approved by the engineer). <code>adapters/hermes_listener.py</code> connects to <code>HERMES_URL</code> with the ares service token (fresh token on every reconnect), sends <code>intents:set</code> for <code>service:ares</code>/<code>search.semantic.changed</code>, reconnects with backoff; started from the FastAPI lifespan.</li><li><code>services/search_index_service.py</code>: <code>get_search_state</code>; if <code>searchSemanticHash</code> equals <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, nothing to do. Otherwise embed <code>searchSemanticText</code> with the <code>document</code> task (no own text building) and <code>store_embedding</code> with <code>searchSemanticHash</code>. <strong>409: drop the result</strong> (a newer event or the daily reindex brings the current text). 404: skip.</li><li>Events processed through a bounded async queue with limited concurrency, duplicates within a short window collapsed; other failures logged and left for Gaia's daily reindex (no retry storm).</li><li>Tests with fake listener, Gaia client and embedder: dirty record embeds and stores with the read hash, clean record does nothing, 409 is dropped without retry, missing record skipped, embedder failure stores nothing.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the local stack, editing an issue's description gives it a new embedding within seconds; two quick edits never leave the older text's embedding stored.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ares-embeddings", "ares-gaia-client", "search-events"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "stack-pgvector-ares", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "p4m stack: pgvector Postgres image and Ares Gaia/Hermes settings", "description": "<p>Gaia's new search stores embeddings with the Postgres <code>vector</code> extension, and Ares now signs in to Gaia as a service and listens to Hermes. The stack <code>p4m</code> generates needs both. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>installer/p4m.py</code>: Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code> for the dev DB and gaia-test containers (same major version, existing volumes stay readable).</li><li>Ares env in the generated compose: <code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>HERMES_URL</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>/<code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code> read from <code>p4m.env</code> (secrets only there); <code>p4m configure</code> asks for them; README explains creating the ares service client and the bigger Ares image (embedding model).</li><li>Unit tests for the generated compose.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after <code>p4m up</code>, <code>CREATE EXTENSION vector</code> works in dev and test databases and Ares has its Gaia/Hermes settings.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> production infrastructure.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "embeddings-client", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Embeddings service: Gaia client for the Ares /embeddings endpoint (query embedding)", "description": "<p>Semantic search embeds the user's query at search time through Ares (<code>POST /embeddings</code>, task <code>query</code>, 768 dimensions). Like <code>core/services/LLM.php</code>, the external system sits behind one class that owns configuration and transport.</p><p><strong>Contract (Ares)</strong>: request <code>{\\"texts\\": [...], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code>; 200 <code>{\\"model\\", \\"dimensions\\", \\"embeddings\\": [[...]]}</code>; 422 invalid; 503 model unavailable.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/services/Embeddings.php</code>: <code>embedQuery(string $text): array</code>; Guzzle, base URL <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL</code>, short timeout from env (~3 s).</li><li>Failures throw <code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code> with the reason; never an empty vector. Validates shape and dimension count.</li><li>Register it in <code>ServiceFactory</code> if that is how services are resolved.</li><li>Unit tests with a mocked Guzzle handler: success, 422, 503, timeout, malformed body, wrong dimensions.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests pass without network.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> document embeddings (Ares makes those itself).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ares-embeddings"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-lexical", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search core: exact, FTS and fuzzy searchers with module ACL scope and rank fusion", "description": "<p>The domain layer for module-agnostic search, driven by the <code>search</code> metadata via <code>SearchableRegistry</code>. Every search runs all matching kinds; the caller only gives types and the query. The HTTP controller is the next issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong> in <code>core/libs/search/</code>:</p><ul><li><code>SearchRequest</code>: types, query text (trimmed, 2-200 chars), limit (default 20, max 50).</li><li><code>ExactMatcher</code>: rows whose <code>exact</code> fields equal the query (type-aware: numeric fields match only an integer query, also <code>#123</code>); pinned first.</li><li><code>FtsSearcher</code>: <code>websearch_to_tsquery</code> against the model's system <code>searchVector</code> column (same text search config), <code>ts_rank_cd</code>, snippet via <code>ts_headline</code> on the display snippet field.</li><li><code>FuzzySearcher</code>: <code>pg_trgm</code> <code>word_similarity</code> on fuzzy fields, threshold from config (default 0.3).</li><li><code>RankFusion</code>: Reciprocal Rank Fusion (k = 60) over each searcher's ranked ids, open to more searchers (semantic comes later); items carry <code>matchedBy</code> and the fused score; exact matches stay on top.</li><li><code>SearchService</code>: per type require <code>&lt;module&gt;.get</code> through <code>Acl</code> (denied type = 403, as for unauthorized query criteria, D-027); apply the module's record scope (<code>Acl::applyRecordScope</code>, <code>acl.groupKeys</code>, D-060) and <code>deleted = 0</code> inside each candidate query, before ranking and LIMIT (D-022). A searcher is skipped for a type when the user lacks read on a field it matches; denied display fields are omitted. Bound parameters only.</li><li>Tests: ranking order, exact pin, typo tolerance, a members-scope user never sees other projects' issues, field-ACL skip.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>SearchService</code> returns fused, ACL-scoped Issue results from exact, FTS and fuzzy matching.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching, the HTTP endpoint.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-endpoint", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "SearchController: GET /api/v1/search across searchable modules", "description": "<p>Expose the search core over HTTP. The controller has no permission of its own; authorization is the searched module's (done in <code>SearchService</code>). This is a deliberate exception to standard CRUD resources: record it in a new <code>docs/architecture/search/decisions.md</code> (registered wherever the decisions-docs test expects), with the search metadata, system search columns, event-driven embedding by Ares with the hash precondition, and ranking decisions.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>SearchController</code> with a list action only: <code>GET /api/v1/search?types=issue&amp;q=...&amp;limit=20</code>; route in <code>core/config/routes.php</code>; OAuth required; <code>$aclMap</code> declared so the action catalog publishes no <code>search.*</code> permission.</li><li>Thin: parse into <code>SearchRequest</code>, call <code>SearchService</code>, shape the response. 400 for missing or too short <code>q</code> or an unknown type; 403 when a requested type's <code>.get</code> is denied.</li><li>Response: <code>data</code> items <code>{type: 'searchresult', id: '&lt;type&gt;:&lt;recordId&gt;', attributes: {module, recordId, title, snippet, score, matchedBy, pinned}}</code>, <code>meta</code> <code>{query, types}</code>.</li><li>api-tester cases incl. <code>acl</code> profiles (denied module = 403, members scope hides other projects' issues); regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass; searching an issue number pins that issue; a typo in a subject word still finds it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching (next issue), Prometheus UI.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-lexical"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-semantic", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: semantic matching on the module's searchEmbedding column", "description": "<p>Add semantic matching to every search: the query is embedded through Ares and compared to the module's system <code>searchEmbedding</code> column (filled by Ares from search events), then fused with the exact/FTS/fuzzy results.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticSearcher</code>: <code>Embeddings::embedQuery</code>, then cosine distance (<code>&lt;=&gt;</code>, HNSW index) on the module table's non-null <code>searchEmbedding</code>, with the same record scope, ACL and <code>deleted = 0</code> as the other searchers, before LIMIT; max distance from config. Skipped when the user lacks read on any <code>semantic</code> field.</li><li>Register it in <code>SearchService</code>/<code>RankFusion</code>; it always runs for types with a <code>semantic</code> list.</li><li>Ares failure (<code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code>): the other results are still returned and <code>meta.semantic</code> is <code>unavailable</code> (otherwise <code>ok</code>); logged, never a silent success.</li><li>Tests with a fake Embeddings: a paraphrase finds the issue, scope respected, Ares down gives the other results plus the meta flag; api-tester case for the meta field; update the search decisions doc.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> searching \\"login fails after password reset\\" finds an issue titled \\"Reset password link broken\\" with <code>matchedBy</code> containing <code>semantic</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records, re-ranking.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-endpoint", "embeddings-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 15:12:28	2026-11-17 15:12:28	f
43b953236afc-f0b3-74f5-95cb48aa6d7f	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	1	{"summary": "A file-based event registry in Gaia (app/metadata/events.php) becomes the single list of the events Gaia raises: name, scope, source, channels (hermes, workflow), consumers and an on/off switch. EventNames and HermesPublisher read it first; then, in parallel, gaia-dev learns it and exports docs/generated/events.json, the workflow TriggerEventCatalog moves onto it, and Hermes CI checks its allowlist against that export. Four event changes follow, each Gaia issue after the registry and each Hermes issue after its Gaia pair: role changes publish user.access.changed (Gaia only), user.mentioned (Gaia finds mentions in comments server-side), workflow.run.finished, and user.created on a new system scope that Gaia gates by ACL and Hermes enforces.", "issues": [{"key": "registry", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: file-based event registry that decides which events Gaia raises and on which channels", "description": "<p>Gaia raises events in two hand-kept lists: <code>EventNames</code> (live events sent to Hermes) and <code>TriggerEventCatalog</code> (in-process workflow triggers). We want one registry that records every event we raise, so adding or removing one is an edit in one place, and nothing goes to Hermes unless the registry says so. It must not live in the database: it is read on almost every API call.</p><ul><li>New <code>app/metadata/events.php</code> (next to <code>FTS.php</code>): a PHP array keyed by event name. Each entry has <code>description</code>, <code>scope</code> (<code>project</code> | <code>user</code>), optional <code>source</code> (<code>model</code>, <code>on</code> create|update, <code>fields</code>, <code>to</code>: the same shape as <code>TriggerEventCatalog::EVENTS</code>), <code>channels</code> (<code>hermes</code> and/or <code>workflow</code>), <code>consumers</code> (free list for documentation, e.g. prometheus, talos, workflows) and <code>enabled</code>.</li><li>Fill it with every event raised today: the 23 <code>EventNames</code> constants (channel hermes; also workflow for issue.created, issue.assignee.changed, issue.status.changed, milestone.completed) and the trigger-only events issue.modified, comment.added, wiki.created, wiki.modified, time.logged (channel workflow only). Copy the source definitions from <code>TriggerEventCatalog::EVENTS</code>. user.access.changed and notification.created are user scope.</li><li>A domain class (e.g. <code>core/libs/events/EventRegistry.php</code>) loads the file once per request (plain <code>require</code>, opcache) and answers: <code>has</code>, <code>definition</code>, <code>enabled</code>, <code>names(channel)</code>, <code>scope</code>.</li><li><code>EventNames</code> keeps its constants (code refers to them), but <code>ALL</code>/<code>isAllowed</code> come from the registry: the names that are enabled and have the hermes channel.</li><li><code>HermesPublisher</code> drops (quietly, debug log) an event that is disabled or not on the hermes channel, before any HTTP call. Fail-open behaviour is unchanged.</li><li>New ADR in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md</code> (the registry replaces the hand-kept allowlist, why it's a file and not the database); update <code>architecture.md</code> key files.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> every event published today is still published with the same envelope; turning <code>enabled</code> off for one stops it being sent (unit test); unit tests for the registry class; existing live-event tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> <code>TriggerEventCatalog</code> reading the registry and gaia-dev tooling (separate issues); merging comment.added with conversation.comment.created (stored in workflow trigger nodes, needs a data migration).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gaia-dev-registry", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "gaia-dev: scaffold and check live events against the event registry, export docs/generated/events.json", "description": "<p>After the event registry (<code>app/metadata/events.php</code>) exists, the gaia-dev tooling still writes and checks <code>EventNames::ALL</code> by hand, and Hermes needs a machine-readable copy of the registry to check its allowlist in CI.</p><ul><li><code>tools/gaia-dev/src/Scaffold/LiveEventsScaffold.php</code> (+ <code>ScaffoldLiveEventsCommand</code>): <code>scaffold live-events</code> adds the registry entry (scope, channels hermes, enabled true) alongside the <code>EventNames</code> constant, instead of editing <code>ALL</code>.</li><li><code>tools/gaia-dev/src/Check/LiveEventsCheck.php</code>: every registry entry on the hermes channel has an <code>EventNames</code> constant emitted by a component and a test case; every constant has a registry entry; unknown channels/scopes are reported.</li><li><code>docs generate</code> writes <code>docs/generated/events.json</code>: a sorted list of <code>{name, scope, channels, enabled, description}</code>. CI's existing \\"generated docs are current\\" check then covers it.</li><li>Update <code>tools/gaia-dev/README.md</code> and the live-events bundle guide (<code>docs/dev/bundles.md</code> E, regenerated <code>docs/generated/bundles/E.md</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> gaia-dev tests cover the scaffold, check and export; <code>events.json</code> is generated and committed; the check passes on dev.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Hermes side of the drift check.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "trigger-catalog", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Workflows: TriggerEventCatalog reads its events from the event registry", "description": "<p>Workflow trigger events are defined in <code>core/libs/workflows/TriggerEventCatalog.php</code> (<code>EVENTS</code> const). The event registry (<code>app/metadata/events.php</code>, class <code>EventRegistry</code>) now holds the same definitions; the catalog should read them so there is one list.</p><ul><li><code>TriggerEventCatalog</code> takes the registry entries that are enabled and have the <code>workflow</code> channel; <code>model</code>, <code>on</code>, <code>fields</code>, <code>to</code> come from the entry's <code>source</code>, <code>label</code> from its description (or a <code>label</code> key if you add one). Remove the private <code>EVENTS</code> const; keep the public API (<code>names</code>, <code>has</code>, <code>definition</code>, <code>models</code>, <code>raisedBy</code>) and constants unchanged.</li><li>A disabled event is neither offered by <code>GET /workflowevent</code> nor raised by <code>WorkflowTriggersComponent</code>.</li><li>Update <code>tests/libraries/workflows/TriggerEventCatalogTest.php</code>; inject the registry so the test can use a fixture.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the workflow trigger list and the events raised are unchanged on dev; a test shows a disabled event disappears from both.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> renaming or merging trigger names.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-drift-check", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "CI: check the event allowlist against Gaia's event registry export", "description": "<p>Gaia now has a file-based event registry and exports it as <code>docs/generated/events.json</code> in the gaia repo. Hermes keeps its own allowlist (<code>src/contract/names.js</code>) by design; CI should fail when the two drift (the local copy already misses <code>user.access.changed</code>, which Gaia publishes).</p><ul><li>A small Node script (e.g. <code>scripts/check-event-registry.js</code>) reads Gaia's <code>events.json</code> (path or URL argument) and compares: the names that are enabled and on the <code>hermes</code> channel must equal <code>EVENT_ALLOWLIST</code>; those with scope <code>user</code> must equal <code>USER_SCOPED_EVENTS</code>. It prints the differences and exits non-zero.</li><li><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code>: a step that fetches <code>events.json</code> from gaia's <code>dev</code> branch and runs the script. If the gaia repository isn't publicly readable, use a read-only token secret and say so in the PR.</li><li>Fix the allowlist if it's really missing <code>user.access.changed</code> (and its user scope).</li><li>Unit test the comparison; mention the check in the docs where the allowlist rule is described.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> CI passes on dev; the test shows a missing and an extra name both fail.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> generating names.js from Gaia.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["gaia-dev-registry"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "role-access", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: publish user.access.changed when a user's role is added or removed", "description": "<p><code>user.access.changed</code> (scope <code>user:&lt;userId&gt;</code>, ids only) tells Hermes and Prometheus to re-check a user's access. Today it fires on account status and membership changes, but not on role changes, which also change what the user may do.</p><ul><li>New live-events component for <code>UserroleController</code>, following <code>MembershipLiveEventsComponent</code>: on create, delete and an update that changes <code>userId</code> or <code>roleId</code>, call <code>UserAccessLiveEventsComponent::publishAccessChanged</code> for the affected user (both users when <code>userId</code> changes). Add it to the controller's <code>$uses</code>.</li><li>Update the user.access.changed entry in <code>app/metadata/events.php</code> (description, consumers).</li><li>Tests in the live-events test and api-tester cases with <code>hermes.expect</code>, as for membership.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> adding or removing a role publishes one user.access.changed to that user; failures to reach Hermes don't fail the write.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> permission changes on a role itself (affects many users).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "user-mentioned", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: record user mentions in comments and publish user.mentioned", "description": "<p>Agents (e.g. Talos reacting to an @-mention of an agent), workflows and the UI need to know when someone is mentioned. Today user mentions exist only as HTML in the comment body: Prometheus' editor (<code>prometheus/app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js</code> ~l.515-535) writes <code>&lt;a class=\\"badge\\" href=\\"/app/user/&lt;userId&gt;\\"&gt;@Name&lt;/a&gt;</code>. Nothing writes the existing <code>Mention</code> resource (<code>app/metadata/model/Mention.php</code>: relatedTo, relatedId, userId, notified). Gaia should find mentions itself, so any client (Prometheus, gaia-mcp, agents) counts.</p><ul><li>A domain class (e.g. <code>core/libs/mentions/MentionParser.php</code>) extracts the user ids from a comment body: links to <code>/app/user/&lt;id&gt;</code> (relative or absolute). Only ids of existing, non-deleted users; no duplicates.</li><li>A component on <code>CommentController</code> (add to <code>$uses</code>): after create, write a <code>Mention</code> row (relatedTo <code>comment</code>, relatedId = comment id) per mentioned user and publish <code>user.mentioned</code>; after update, only for users newly mentioned (compare with the stored rows). Skip the author mentioning themselves.</li><li>Event: <code>user.mentioned</code>, scope <code>user:&lt;mentionedUserId&gt;</code>, ids only (Hermes D-017 style): commentId, the comment's relatedTo/relatedId, issueId and projectId when the room belongs to an issue, actor id. Add the constant to <code>EventNames</code> and the registry entry (channel hermes, consumers talos, prometheus).</li><li>Tests: parser unit tests (HTML variants, unknown ids), component test, api-tester cases with <code>hermes.expect</code>.</li><li>Contract change: linked Hermes PR (allowlist + user scope).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a comment mentioning two users creates two Mention rows and two events, each to that user; editing it to add a third sends one more; a Hermes outage doesn't fail the comment.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> mentions in idea messages or wiki/docs, notifications or emails for mentions, the workflow channel.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-user-mentioned", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Allowlist the user-scoped event user.mentioned", "description": "<p>Gaia publishes <code>user.mentioned</code> when a comment mentions a user (linked Gaia issue). It is user-scoped: projectId <code>user:&lt;mentionedUserId&gt;</code>, ids only (commentId, relatedTo/relatedId, issueId, projectId, actor).</p><ul><li>Add it to <code>EVENT_ALLOWLIST</code> and <code>USER_SCOPED_EVENTS</code> in <code>src/contract/names.js</code>.</li><li>ADR entry in decisions.md and tests (only the mentioned user's socket may subscribe).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the drift check against Gaia's events.json passes; tests pass.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["user-mentioned"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "run-finished", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: publish workflow.run.finished when a workflow run completes or fails", "description": "<p>A run's end is invisible outside Gaia: the run view, Talos and Agamemnon can only poll. Runs end in <code>core/libs/workflows/RunJournal.php</code> <code>finish</code> (called from <code>WorkflowRunner</code> ~l.243; check every caller, e.g. timeouts via <code>ActorStepTimeouts</code>).</p><ul><li>When a run moves to <code>RunStatus::COMPLETED</code> or <code>FAILED</code> (not <code>WAITING</code>), publish <code>workflow.run.finished</code>, project-scoped by the run's <code>projectId</code> (skip runs without one). Payload ids only: runId, workflowId, status, test flag, entityType/entityId; no error text.</li><li>Inject a publisher the way <code>AgentRunLiveEvents</code> is injected into <code>WorkflowRunner</code> (see <code>WorkflowTriggersComponent::runner</code>); the domain class gets an abstraction, not <code>HermesPublisher</code>.</li><li>Constant in <code>EventNames</code>, registry entry (scope project, channel hermes, consumers prometheus, talos).</li><li>Tests for completed, failed, waiting (no event) and the fail-open path.</li><li>Contract change: linked Hermes PR.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> each finished run publishes exactly one event; a Hermes outage doesn't affect the run.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> step-level events, Prometheus live run view.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-run-finished", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Allowlist the project-scoped event workflow.run.finished", "description": "<p>Gaia publishes <code>workflow.run.finished</code> when a workflow run completes or fails (linked Gaia issue). Project-scoped (the run's projectId), ids only: runId, workflowId, status, test, entityType, entityId.</p><ul><li>Add it to <code>EVENT_ALLOWLIST</code> in <code>src/contract/names.js</code>.</li><li>ADR entry in decisions.md and tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the drift check passes; project members can subscribe, others can't.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["run-finished"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "system-scope", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: system scope for system-wide events, gated by ACL and exposed on /user/me", "description": "<p>Some events belong to no project and no single user (first one: <code>user.created</code>). Hermes only knows project scope and <code>user:&lt;id&gt;</code>. We add a <code>system</code> scope; Gaia owns who may receive it, Hermes enforces it (linked Hermes issue).</p><ul><li>Registry: scope <code>system</code> is valid; such events are published with envelope projectId <code>system</code> (extend <code>LiveEventsComponent::publish</code>/envelope handling as needed).</li><li>Who may receive them: a new ACL resource (proposed <code>Systemevent</code>, action read) checked through the normal ACL; no permission seed SQL (the reviewer grants it to admin roles and agents such as Talos by hand). Add api-tester acl cases.</li><li><code>GET /api/v1/user/me</code> returns whether the caller may receive system events (proposed: <code>meta.systemEvents: true|false</code>); Hermes reads it at handshake.</li><li>ADR in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md</code>: why a system scope, the flag, why not a custom endpoint.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> /user/me shows the flag true only for users granted the permission; tests for both; nothing is published on the system scope yet.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the user.created event (next issue), Hermes changes.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "user-created", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: publish user.created on the system scope when a user or agent is created", "description": "<p>Integrations and Talos need to know when a user or an agent account is created (provisioning, onboarding). Uses the <code>system</code> scope from the previous issue.</p><ul><li>Publish <code>user.created</code> after a user is created (<code>UserController</code>) and after an agent is created (<code>AgentController</code>; agents are users via CTI, so publish once per new account). Payload ids only: userId and <code>type</code> (person | agent). Projectid <code>system</code>.</li><li>Constant in <code>EventNames</code>, registry entry (scope system, channel hermes, consumers talos, integrations).</li><li>Live-events tests and api-tester cases with <code>hermes.expect</code>.</li><li>Contract change: linked Hermes PR.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> creating a user or an agent publishes one event each; a Hermes outage doesn't fail the create.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> user updated/deleted events, the workflow channel (workflow runs need a project).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["system-scope"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-system-scope", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "System-scoped events: authorize the 'system' scope from Gaia's flag and allowlist user.created", "description": "<p>Gaia adds a <code>system</code> scope for events that belong to no project or user (first: <code>user.created</code>, ids only: userId, type person|agent). Gaia decides who may receive them and reports it as <code>meta.systemEvents</code> on <code>GET /api/v1/user/me</code> (linked Gaia issues).</p><ul><li><code>src/auth/gaia-session.js</code>: read the flag into the session (cached as today).</li><li><code>src/contract/names.js</code>: <code>SYSTEM_SCOPED_EVENTS</code> with <code>user.created</code>, added to the allowlist; <code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code> <code>isIntentAuthorized</code>: such an intent needs projectId <code>system</code> and the flag.</li><li>Extend the drift check (scope <code>system</code> must equal <code>SYSTEM_SCOPED_EVENTS</code>).</li><li>ADR in decisions.md; tests for allowed, denied and a wrong projectId.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> only flagged sessions receive user.created; other events behave as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> re-checking the flag before the cache expires.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["user-created", "hermes-drift-check"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 15:22:43	2026-11-17 15:22:43	f
643ad1006afc-02d0-311d-1687c7c44e28	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	2	{"summary": "A file-based event registry in Gaia (app/metadata/events.php) becomes the single list of the events Gaia raises: name, scope, source, channels (hermes, workflow), consumers and an on/off switch. EventNames/HermesPublisher read it first; then gaia-dev learns it and exports docs/generated/events.json (Hermes CI checks its allowlist against it), and the workflow TriggerEventCatalog moves onto it. Mentions: a model behavior finds user mentions in the text fields of a record on every create and update and records them as Mention rows (framework issue), turned on for issues, comments and threads, and for ideas and idea messages; each new Mention publishes user.mentioned (Hermes allowlist after it) and notifies the mentioned user. Role changes publish user.access.changed, and finished workflow runs publish workflow.run.finished (Hermes allowlist after it).", "issues": [{"key": "registry", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: file-based event registry that decides which events Gaia raises and on which channels", "description": "<p>Gaia raises events in two hand-kept lists: <code>EventNames</code> (live events sent to Hermes) and <code>TriggerEventCatalog</code> (in-process workflow triggers). We want one registry that records every event we raise, so adding or removing one is an edit in one place, and nothing goes to Hermes unless the registry says so. It must not live in the database: it is read on almost every API call.</p><ul><li>New <code>app/metadata/events.php</code> (next to <code>FTS.php</code>): a PHP array keyed by event name. Each entry has <code>description</code>, <code>scope</code> (<code>project</code> | <code>user</code>), optional <code>source</code> (<code>model</code>, <code>on</code> create|update, <code>fields</code>, <code>to</code>: the same shape as <code>TriggerEventCatalog::EVENTS</code>), <code>channels</code> (<code>hermes</code> and/or <code>workflow</code>), <code>consumers</code> (free list for documentation, e.g. prometheus, talos, workflows) and <code>enabled</code>.</li><li>Fill it with every event raised today: the 23 <code>EventNames</code> constants (channel hermes; also workflow for issue.created, issue.assignee.changed, issue.status.changed, milestone.completed) and the trigger-only events issue.modified, comment.added, wiki.created, wiki.modified, time.logged (channel workflow only). Copy the source definitions from <code>TriggerEventCatalog::EVENTS</code>. user.access.changed, notification.created and workflow.agent.run.requested are user scope.</li><li>A domain class (e.g. <code>core/libs/events/EventRegistry.php</code>) loads the file once per request (plain <code>require</code>, opcache) and answers <code>has</code>, <code>definition</code>, <code>enabled</code>, <code>names(channel)</code>, <code>scope</code>.</li><li><code>EventNames</code> keeps its constants (code refers to them), but <code>ALL</code>/<code>isAllowed</code> come from the registry: the names that are enabled and on the hermes channel.</li><li><code>HermesPublisher</code> drops (quietly, debug log) an event that is disabled or not on the hermes channel, before any HTTP call. Fail-open behaviour is unchanged.</li><li>New ADR in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md</code> (the registry replaces the hand-kept allowlist; why a file and not the database); update <code>architecture.md</code> key files.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> every event published today is still published with the same envelope; turning <code>enabled</code> off for one stops it being sent (unit test); unit tests for the registry class; existing live-event tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> <code>TriggerEventCatalog</code> reading the registry and gaia-dev tooling (separate issues); merging comment.added with conversation.comment.created (the name is stored in workflow trigger nodes, needs a data migration).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gaia-dev-registry", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "gaia-dev: scaffold and check live events against the event registry, export docs/generated/events.json", "description": "<p>After the event registry (<code>app/metadata/events.php</code>) exists, the gaia-dev tooling still writes and checks <code>EventNames::ALL</code> by hand, and Hermes needs a machine-readable copy of the registry to check its allowlist in CI.</p><ul><li><code>tools/gaia-dev/src/Scaffold/LiveEventsScaffold.php</code> (+ <code>ScaffoldLiveEventsCommand</code>): <code>scaffold live-events</code> adds the registry entry (scope, channel hermes, enabled true) alongside the <code>EventNames</code> constant, instead of editing <code>ALL</code>.</li><li><code>tools/gaia-dev/src/Check/LiveEventsCheck.php</code>: every registry entry on the hermes channel has an <code>EventNames</code> constant emitted by a component (or model class) and a test case; every constant has a registry entry; unknown channels/scopes are reported.</li><li><code>docs generate</code> writes <code>docs/generated/events.json</code>: a sorted list of <code>{name, scope, channels, enabled, description}</code>. CI's existing \\"generated docs are current\\" check then covers it.</li><li>Update <code>tools/gaia-dev/README.md</code> and the live-events bundle guide (<code>docs/dev/bundles.md</code> E, regenerated <code>docs/generated/bundles/E.md</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> gaia-dev tests cover the scaffold, check and export; <code>events.json</code> is generated and committed; the check passes on dev.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Hermes side of the drift check.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "trigger-catalog", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Workflows: TriggerEventCatalog reads its events from the event registry", "description": "<p>Workflow trigger events are defined in <code>core/libs/workflows/TriggerEventCatalog.php</code> (<code>EVENTS</code> const). The event registry (<code>app/metadata/events.php</code>, class <code>EventRegistry</code>) now holds the same definitions; the catalog should read them so there is one list.</p><ul><li><code>TriggerEventCatalog</code> takes the registry entries that are enabled and on the <code>workflow</code> channel; <code>model</code>, <code>on</code>, <code>fields</code>, <code>to</code> come from the entry's <code>source</code>, the label from the entry (add a <code>label</code> key if needed). Remove the private <code>EVENTS</code> const; keep the public API (<code>names</code>, <code>has</code>, <code>definition</code>, <code>models</code>, <code>raisedBy</code>) and constants unchanged.</li><li>A disabled event is neither offered by <code>GET /workflowevent</code> nor raised by <code>WorkflowTriggersComponent</code>.</li><li>Update <code>tests/libraries/workflows/TriggerEventCatalogTest.php</code>; inject the registry so the test can use a fixture.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the workflow trigger list and the events raised are unchanged on dev; a test shows a disabled event disappears from both.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> renaming or merging trigger names.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-drift-check", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "CI: check the event allowlist against Gaia's event registry export", "description": "<p>Gaia now has a file-based event registry and exports it as <code>docs/generated/events.json</code> in the gaia repo. Hermes keeps its own allowlist (<code>src/contract/names.js</code>) by design; CI should fail when the two drift (the local copy seems to miss <code>user.access.changed</code>, which Gaia publishes).</p><ul><li>A small Node script (e.g. <code>scripts/check-event-registry.js</code>) reads Gaia's <code>events.json</code> (path or URL argument) and compares: the names that are enabled and on the <code>hermes</code> channel must equal <code>EVENT_ALLOWLIST</code>; those with scope <code>user</code> must equal <code>USER_SCOPED_EVENTS</code>. It prints the differences and exits non-zero.</li><li><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code>: a step that fetches <code>events.json</code> from gaia's <code>dev</code> branch and runs the script. If the gaia repository isn't publicly readable, use a read-only token secret and say so in the PR.</li><li>Fix the allowlist if it really misses <code>user.access.changed</code> (and its user scope).</li><li>Unit test the comparison; mention the check where the docs describe the allowlist rule.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> CI passes on dev; tests show a missing and an extra name both fail.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> generating names.js from Gaia.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["gaia-dev-registry"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "role-access", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: publish user.access.changed when a user's role is added or removed", "description": "<p><code>user.access.changed</code> (scope <code>user:&lt;userId&gt;</code>, ids only) tells Hermes and Prometheus to re-check a user's access. Today it fires on account status and membership changes, but not on role changes, which also change what the user may do.</p><ul><li>New live-events component for <code>UserroleController</code>, following <code>MembershipLiveEventsComponent</code>: on create, delete and an update that changes <code>userId</code> or <code>roleId</code>, call <code>UserAccessLiveEventsComponent::publishAccessChanged</code> for the affected user (both users when <code>userId</code> changes). Add it to the controller's <code>$uses</code>.</li><li>Update the user.access.changed entry in <code>app/metadata/events.php</code> (description, consumers).</li><li>Tests in the live-events test and api-tester cases with <code>hermes.expect</code>, as for membership.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> adding or removing a role publishes one user.access.changed to that user; a Hermes outage doesn't fail the write.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> permission changes on a role itself (affects many users).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "mention-framework", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Mentions: model behavior that records user mentions in a record's text fields on every create and update", "description": "<p>Users are mentioned in comments, issue descriptions, thread descriptions and ideas. Prometheus' editor writes a mention as a link, <code>&lt;a class=\\"badge\\" href=\\"/app/user/&lt;userId&gt;\\"&gt;@Name&lt;/a&gt;</code>; markdown bodies (idea messages) would hold <code>[@Name](/app/user/&lt;userId&gt;)</code>. Gaia stores none of this today: the <code>Mention</code> resource (<code>app/metadata/model/Mention.php</code>: relatedTo, relatedId, userId, notified) is never written. This issue builds the capability; the next issues turn it on per model. It must catch <strong>every</strong> write path: REST create/update, collection PATCH, and saves outside controllers such as the workflow Set field action. So it is a model behavior, not a controller component.</p><ul><li><code>MentionParser</code> (domain, e.g. <code>core/libs/mentions/</code>): user ids from HTML anchors and markdown links whose target is <code>/app/user/&lt;id&gt;</code> (relative or absolute URL). Distinct, in order.</li><li>A behavior (e.g. <code>core/mvc/models/behaviors/mentionsBehavior.php</code>, listed in a model's metadata <code>behaviors</code> like <code>ideaScreensBehavior</code>) reading a new metadata key <code>'mentions' =&gt; ['fields' =&gt; [...]]</code>. After create, and after an update where one of those fields changed, it hands the record to a recorder.</li><li>Recorder: for each parsed user id, create a <code>Mention</code> row (relatedTo = the model's lowercase name, relatedId = record id, userId, createdUser = the actor) unless one exists for that record and user. Rows are append-only: removing a mention doesn't delete its row, and re-adding it doesn't create a new one, so nobody is notified twice. Skip the actor mentioning themselves, unknown or deleted users, and users who aren't members of the record's project (resolve the project with the existing <code>ProjectIdResolver</code> logic or an equivalent domain helper).</li><li>Add <code>projectId</code> to <code>Mention</code> (metadata + migration) so later consumers don't have to walk the record.</li><li>Fails safe: an error while recording mentions is logged and must not fail the user's save.</li><li>ADR (e.g. <code>docs/architecture/mentions/decisions.md</code>): behavior vs component, append-only rows, membership rule.</li><li>Tests: parser (HTML and markdown, absolute/relative, junk links), recorder (create, update adds only new users, self, non-member), behavior on a test model.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the behavior on a model, saving text with two mentions creates two rows; saving again creates none; editing in a third creates one.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> turning it on for real models, notifications and events (separate issues); the Mention resource's read ACL.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "mentions-issues", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Mentions: record mentions in issue descriptions, comments and thread descriptions", "description": "<p>Turn on the mentions behavior (from the mention-framework issue) for the records where people mention each other on issues and threads, so mentions are recorded on create and on every update.</p><ul><li><code>app/metadata/model/Issue.php</code>: <code>mentions</code> fields <code>description</code>, behavior added.</li><li><code>app/metadata/model/Comment.php</code>: field <code>comment</code> (comments live in conversation rooms: issue rooms and threads).</li><li><code>app/metadata/model/Conversationroom.php</code>: field <code>description</code> (thread starter).</li><li>api-tester cases: create with a mention, update adding one, update without a change, collection PATCH of issue descriptions; check the Mention rows.</li><li>A unit test that a workflow Set field on an issue description records the mention.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> every create/update path above records new mentions once; existing tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> wiki and docs, ideas (separate issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["mention-framework"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "mentions-ideas", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Mentions: record mentions in idea descriptions and idea messages", "description": "<p>Turn on the mentions behavior (from the mention-framework issue) for ideas. Idea messages are markdown, so mentions there are markdown links to <code>/app/user/&lt;id&gt;</code>; the parser already handles them. Messages written by agents (e.g. Nestor) count too.</p><ul><li><code>app/metadata/model/Idea.php</code>: <code>mentions</code> field <code>description</code>, behavior added.</li><li><code>app/metadata/model/Ideamessage.php</code>: field <code>body</code>, behavior added after the existing ones.</li><li>api-tester cases for create and update of both.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> mentions of project members in ideas and idea messages are recorded once.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> an @-mention picker in Prometheus' idea composer (a Prometheus follow-up).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["mention-framework"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "mention-event", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: publish user.mentioned when a mention is recorded", "description": "<p>Agents, workflows and the UI need to know when someone is mentioned. Mentions are now recorded as <code>Mention</code> rows (mention-framework issue) from every write path, so the event is published when a row is created, the way <code>app/models/Systemnotificationrecipient.php</code> publishes <code>notification.created</code> through <code>NotificationLiveEvents</code> after create.</p><ul><li>After a <code>Mention</code> is created, publish <code>user.mentioned</code>, scope <code>user:&lt;userId&gt;</code> (the mentioned user). Ids only: mentionId, relatedTo, relatedId, projectId, actor id.</li><li>A small publisher class next to <code>NotificationLiveEvents</code>; constant in <code>EventNames</code>; registry entry in <code>app/metadata/events.php</code> (scope user, channel hermes, consumers talos, prometheus).</li><li>Tests (published once per row, fail-open when Hermes is down) and api-tester <code>hermes.expect</code> on a comment with a mention.</li><li>Contract change: linked Hermes PR (allowlist + user scope).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a comment mentioning two members sends two events, each to that user; an edit that adds nobody sends none.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the workflow channel for mentions.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry", "mention-framework"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "mention-notification", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Notifications: notify a user when they are mentioned", "description": "<p>A mentioned user should get a notification. Mentions are recorded as <code>Mention</code> rows from every write path; create the notification when a row is created, next to the <code>user.mentioned</code> publish.</p><ul><li>A notification builder (e.g. <code>components/notifications/modules/MentionNotification.php</code> or a service beside it): <code>CreateModel::execute('systemnotification', ...)</code> + <code>RecipientService::notifyUsers($notification, [$userId])</code>, which already publishes <code>notification.created</code>. Description per relatedTo, following the existing templates: <code>{{User@actor}} mentioned you in {{Issue@id}}</code>; for a comment, the issue (or thread) it is on; for an idea or idea message, the idea. <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code> and <code>context</code> (projectShortcode, issueNumber or ideaId, commentId, userId, userName) as in <code>CommentNotification</code>. Set the Mention's <code>notified</code> to true.</li><li>No double notification: <code>CommentNotification::onCreate</code> and <code>IssueNotification::onCreate</code> exclude users mentioned in that same record (Mention rows exist by then, the behavior runs at model save) via the <code>excludeIds</code> of <code>notifyIssueRecipients</code>.</li><li>Tests for each relatedTo and for the exclusion.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a mentioned member gets one mention notification and no second \\"commented\\" one; others are notified as before; a failure doesn't fail the save.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> emails; Prometheus rendering of idea/thread notification links (Prometheus follow-up).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["mention-event"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-user-mentioned", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Allowlist the user-scoped event user.mentioned", "description": "<p>Gaia publishes <code>user.mentioned</code> when a user is mentioned in a comment, issue or thread description, idea or idea message (linked Gaia issue). It is user-scoped: projectId <code>user:&lt;mentionedUserId&gt;</code>, ids only (mentionId, relatedTo, relatedId, projectId, actor).</p><ul><li>Add it to <code>EVENT_ALLOWLIST</code> and <code>USER_SCOPED_EVENTS</code> in <code>src/contract/names.js</code>.</li><li>ADR entry in decisions.md and tests (only the mentioned user's socket may subscribe).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the drift check against Gaia's events.json passes; tests pass.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["mention-event", "hermes-drift-check"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "run-finished", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: publish workflow.run.finished when a workflow run completes or fails", "description": "<p>A run's end is invisible outside Gaia: the run view, Talos and Agamemnon can only poll. Runs end in <code>core/libs/workflows/RunJournal.php</code> <code>finish</code> (called from <code>WorkflowRunner</code> ~l.243; check every caller, e.g. timeouts via <code>ActorStepTimeouts</code>).</p><ul><li>When a run moves to <code>RunStatus::COMPLETED</code> or <code>FAILED</code> (not <code>WAITING</code>), publish <code>workflow.run.finished</code>, project-scoped by the run's <code>projectId</code> (skip runs without one). Ids only: runId, workflowId, status, test flag, entityType/entityId; no error text.</li><li>Inject a publisher the way <code>AgentRunLiveEvents</code> is injected into <code>WorkflowRunner</code> (see <code>WorkflowTriggersComponent::runner</code>); the domain class gets an abstraction, not <code>HermesPublisher</code>.</li><li>Constant in <code>EventNames</code>, registry entry (scope project, channel hermes, consumers prometheus, talos).</li><li>Tests for completed, failed, waiting (no event) and fail-open.</li><li>Contract change: linked Hermes PR.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> each finished run publishes exactly one event; a Hermes outage doesn't affect the run.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> step-level events.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-run-finished", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Allowlist the project-scoped event workflow.run.finished", "description": "<p>Gaia publishes <code>workflow.run.finished</code> when a workflow run completes or fails (linked Gaia issue). Project-scoped (the run's projectId), ids only: runId, workflowId, status, test, entityType, entityId.</p><ul><li>Add it to <code>EVENT_ALLOWLIST</code> in <code>src/contract/names.js</code>.</li><li>ADR entry in decisions.md and tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the drift check passes; project members can subscribe, others can't.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["run-finished", "hermes-drift-check"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 15:31:48	2026-11-17 15:31:48	f
4096fa976afd-a500-49c2-c27e71b5ffc6	6c7240d86afd-3eec-75db-a5acaf1064a6	3	{"summary": "Remove the blank screens between opening Prometheus and seeing a page, using the existing skeleton standard throughout. index.html gets a static copy of the app shell with the PageLoading skeleton, built from existing classes only. It covers the bundle download, session restore and translations. app.loading-assets and the app.project route then show the same PageLoading skeleton through the component. The project route also renders its outlet without a redundant project query and stops making nested routes wait for the all-issues preload. The boot issue is independent of the two project-route issues, which run in order because both change routes/app/project.js.", "issues": [{"key": "boot-loader", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "App start: static skeleton in index.html until the application route is ready, skeleton on loading-assets", "description": "<p>On a cold load, Prometheus shows a blank page until several steps finish one after another. First the bundles load: the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> of <code>app/index.html</code> holds only the two script tags. Then <code>routes/application.js</code> <code>beforeModel</code> awaits <code>session.setup()</code>, which restores the session and may refresh the token. Then it awaits <code>translations.load()</code>. No loading template exists at the top level. After that, <code>app.loading-assets</code> shows only a hardcoded <code>&lt;h1&gt;Loading Assets...&lt;/h1&gt;</code> in the app shell while it loads the user, users, roles, projects and settings. Loading must follow the existing skeleton standard (design system section 9: <code>AppUi::Skeleton</code>), with no new loader, class or CSS.</p><ul><li><code>app/index.html</code>: inside <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>, before the scripts, add static markup marked with <code>data-boot-loader</code>. It copies the app shell (<code>wrapper</code>, <code>main-header</code> with the static logo <code>img/app/logo-256.png</code> in <code>.logo</code>, <code>main-sidebar</code> with a <code>sidebar-menu</code> of <code>skeleton-line</code> rows, <code>content-wrapper</code>) and puts the markup of <code>AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader</code> (<code>page-skeleton-header</code> plus <code>components/app-ui/skeleton/page-loading-body.hbs</code>) in the content area. Use existing <code>.skeleton-*</code> and AdminLTE classes only, no inline styles and no text (translations aren't loaded yet). Add a comment in <code>index.html</code> and in <code>page-loading-body.hbs</code> pointing to each other, so the copies stay in sync.</li><li><code>routes/application.js</code>: remove the <code>[data-boot-loader]</code> element once <code>beforeModel</code> has finished, including when it ends in a redirect (signin, public routes) and when restore fails. It must be a no-op when the element is missing (<code>tests/index.html</code> has none).</li><li><code>app/templates/app/loading-assets.hbs</code>: replace the hardcoded heading with <code>&lt;AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader={{true}} /&gt;</code>.</li><li>Tests: a unit test that the application route removes the boot skeleton after <code>beforeModel</code> and tolerates its absence. An integration or acceptance test that loading-assets renders <code>[data-test-page-loading]</code> while its model is pending.</li><li>Compare the static skeleton with the real shell in the running app (sidebar width, header height, content offset) so the handover to the app doesn't jump.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> from the first paint of a cold load (signed in or not) until the first real screen, the page always shows a skeleton, never a blank white page. The static skeleton is gone once the sign-in page or the app shell renders. There is no hardcoded user-facing text and no new CSS.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> making the boot requests themselves faster (session restore, translations, loading-assets data), and the app.project route wait.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["boot-splash"]}, {"key": "project-route-skeleton", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project route: show a skeleton while the project loads and render the outlet without the extra project query", "description": "<p>On a fresh load of any project URL (e.g. <code>/app/project/aprom/issue/4198</code>), the content area stays blank until the parent <code>app.project</code> route finishes its hooks, before the nested route's own request even starts. Ember finds no loading substate for <code>app.project</code>: <code>app/project-loading.hbs</code>, <code>app/loading.hbs</code> and <code>loading.hbs</code> don't exist. The existing <code>app/project/loading.hbs</code> and <code>*-loading.hbs</code> templates only cover child routes. They are also hidden, because <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> renders <code>{{outlet}}</code> only inside <code>{{#if this.projectId}}</code>, and <code>setupController</code> in <code>routes/app/project.js</code> sets <code>projectId</code> in the <code>.then()</code> of a second project query, although <code>beforeModel</code> already loaded the project.</p><ul><li>Add <code>app/templates/app/project-loading.hbs</code> with <code>&lt;AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader={{true}} /&gt;</code>, following <code>app/templates/app/settings-loading.hbs</code> and the design system.</li><li><code>routes/app/project.js</code>: keep the project record loaded in <code>beforeModel</code> on the route. In <code>setupController</code>, set <code>model</code>, <code>projectId</code> and <code>projectName</code> from it straight away, and remove the second <code>store.query('project', { fields: 'Project.id,Project.name' ... })</code>.</li><li>When no project matches the short code, keep today's error handling (<code>errorManager</code>) and don't throw on <code>objectAt(project, 0).id</code>.</li><li>Tests: an acceptance or route test that visits a project child route with a delayed project response and asserts the project skeleton is shown. Also check that the child's loading template renders while its own model is pending.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a cold load or reload of a project page never shows an empty content area. The project skeleton shows while the project loads, then the child skeleton, then the page. Only one project request is made per project entry. The project name and breadcrumb are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the all-issues preload in <code>afterModel</code> (separate issue), the app start before the app shell.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["project-loading"]}, {"key": "project-issues-nonblocking", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project route: stop blocking nested routes on the all-issues preload", "description": "<p><code>routes/app/project.js</code> <code>afterModel</code> loads every issue of the project (<code>limit: -1</code>; fields id, subject, issueNumber, statusId, projectId) and returns that promise, so every nested route (board, issue list, issue page, ideas, conversations, ...) waits for it before its own request starts. The list only feeds the <code>issuesList</code> getter in <code>controllers/app/project.js</code> (<code>@computed('projectId', 'issues')</code>). It is read by <code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code> and <code>controllers/prometheus/projectrelated.js</code>, and from there by <code>components/message-box.js</code> and <code>components/summer-note.js</code>.</p><ul><li>Start the issues query without returning it from <code>afterModel</code>. When it resolves, set <code>issues</code> on the <code>app.project</code> controller (and the route, if still read there); report errors with <code>errorManager.handleError</code> as today. Ignore a result that arrives after the user has switched to another project.</li><li>Make sure the <code>issuesList</code> getter updates when <code>issues</code> arrives later, and that every reader handles the empty list (only the blank entry) until then without errors.</li><li>Tests: a route/acceptance test that a nested route's model request starts before the issues preload resolves, and that the list fills in once it does.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a cold load of a project page, the nested route's request starts right after the project request, without waiting for the all-issues request. Issue pickers that use <code>issuesList</code> show the issues once loaded. Switching projects never shows another project's issues.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing the preload with server-side search in the pickers, the store.request migration (aprom-4552).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["project-route-skeleton"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 10:26:08	2026-11-18 10:26:08	f
5ad498126afc-30ee-311d-0013182bf066	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	3	{"summary": "A file-based event registry in Gaia (app/metadata/events.php) becomes the single list of the events Gaia raises: name, scope, source, channels (hermes, workflow), consumers and an on/off switch. EventNames/HermesPublisher read it first; then gaia-dev learns it and exports docs/generated/events.json (Hermes CI checks its allowlist against it), and the workflow TriggerEventCatalog moves onto it. Mentions: a model behavior finds user mentions in the text fields of a record on every create and update and records them as Mention rows (framework issue), turned on for issues, comments and threads, and for ideas and idea messages; each new Mention publishes user.mentioned (Hermes allowlist after it) and notifies the mentioned user. Role changes publish user.access.changed, and finished workflow runs publish workflow.run.finished (Hermes allowlist after it). All issues in milestone aga-MentionEvents.", "issues": [{"key": "registry", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: file-based event registry that decides which events Gaia raises and on which channels", "description": "<p>Gaia raises events in two hand-kept lists: <code>EventNames</code> (live events sent to Hermes) and <code>TriggerEventCatalog</code> (in-process workflow triggers). We want one registry that records every event we raise, so adding or removing one is an edit in one place, and nothing goes to Hermes unless the registry says so. It must not live in the database: it is read on almost every API call.</p><ul><li>New <code>app/metadata/events.php</code> (next to <code>FTS.php</code>): a PHP array keyed by event name. Each entry has <code>description</code>, <code>scope</code> (<code>project</code> | <code>user</code>), optional <code>source</code> (<code>model</code>, <code>on</code> create|update, <code>fields</code>, <code>to</code>: the same shape as <code>TriggerEventCatalog::EVENTS</code>), <code>channels</code> (<code>hermes</code> and/or <code>workflow</code>), <code>consumers</code> (free list for documentation, e.g. prometheus, talos, workflows) and <code>enabled</code>.</li><li>Fill it with every event raised today: the 23 <code>EventNames</code> constants (channel hermes; also workflow for issue.created, issue.assignee.changed, issue.status.changed, milestone.completed) and the trigger-only events issue.modified, comment.added, wiki.created, wiki.modified, time.logged (channel workflow only). Copy the source definitions from <code>TriggerEventCatalog::EVENTS</code>. user.access.changed, notification.created and workflow.agent.run.requested are user scope.</li><li>A domain class (e.g. <code>core/libs/events/EventRegistry.php</code>) loads the file once per request (plain <code>require</code>, opcache) and answers <code>has</code>, <code>definition</code>, <code>enabled</code>, <code>names(channel)</code>, <code>scope</code>.</li><li><code>EventNames</code> keeps its constants (code refers to them), but <code>ALL</code>/<code>isAllowed</code> come from the registry: the names that are enabled and on the hermes channel.</li><li><code>HermesPublisher</code> drops (quietly, debug log) an event that is disabled or not on the hermes channel, before any HTTP call. Fail-open behaviour is unchanged.</li><li>New ADR in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md</code> (the registry replaces the hand-kept allowlist; why a file and not the database); update <code>architecture.md</code> key files.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> every event published today is still published with the same envelope; turning <code>enabled</code> off for one stops it being sent (unit test); unit tests for the registry class; existing live-event tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> <code>TriggerEventCatalog</code> reading the registry and gaia-dev tooling (separate issues); merging comment.added with conversation.comment.created (the name is stored in workflow trigger nodes, needs a data migration).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "gaia-dev-registry", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "gaia-dev: scaffold and check live events against the event registry, export docs/generated/events.json", "description": "<p>After the event registry (<code>app/metadata/events.php</code>) exists, the gaia-dev tooling still writes and checks <code>EventNames::ALL</code> by hand, and Hermes needs a machine-readable copy of the registry to check its allowlist in CI.</p><ul><li><code>tools/gaia-dev/src/Scaffold/LiveEventsScaffold.php</code> (+ <code>ScaffoldLiveEventsCommand</code>): <code>scaffold live-events</code> adds the registry entry (scope, channel hermes, enabled true) alongside the <code>EventNames</code> constant, instead of editing <code>ALL</code>.</li><li><code>tools/gaia-dev/src/Check/LiveEventsCheck.php</code>: every registry entry on the hermes channel has an <code>EventNames</code> constant emitted by a component (or model class) and a test case; every constant has a registry entry; unknown channels/scopes are reported.</li><li><code>docs generate</code> writes <code>docs/generated/events.json</code>: a sorted list of <code>{name, scope, channels, enabled, description}</code>. CI's existing \\"generated docs are current\\" check then covers it.</li><li>Update <code>tools/gaia-dev/README.md</code> and the live-events bundle guide (<code>docs/dev/bundles.md</code> E, regenerated <code>docs/generated/bundles/E.md</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> gaia-dev tests cover the scaffold, check and export; <code>events.json</code> is generated and committed; the check passes on dev.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Hermes side of the drift check.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "trigger-catalog", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Workflows: TriggerEventCatalog reads its events from the event registry", "description": "<p>Workflow trigger events are defined in <code>core/libs/workflows/TriggerEventCatalog.php</code> (<code>EVENTS</code> const). The event registry (<code>app/metadata/events.php</code>, class <code>EventRegistry</code>) now holds the same definitions; the catalog should read them so there is one list.</p><ul><li><code>TriggerEventCatalog</code> takes the registry entries that are enabled and on the <code>workflow</code> channel; <code>model</code>, <code>on</code>, <code>fields</code>, <code>to</code> come from the entry's <code>source</code>, the label from the entry (add a <code>label</code> key if needed). Remove the private <code>EVENTS</code> const; keep the public API (<code>names</code>, <code>has</code>, <code>definition</code>, <code>models</code>, <code>raisedBy</code>) and constants unchanged.</li><li>A disabled event is neither offered by <code>GET /workflowevent</code> nor raised by <code>WorkflowTriggersComponent</code>.</li><li>Update <code>tests/libraries/workflows/TriggerEventCatalogTest.php</code>; inject the registry so the test can use a fixture.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the workflow trigger list and the events raised are unchanged on dev; a test shows a disabled event disappears from both.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> renaming or merging trigger names.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-drift-check", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "CI: check the event allowlist against Gaia's event registry export", "description": "<p>Gaia now has a file-based event registry and exports it as <code>docs/generated/events.json</code> in the gaia repo. Hermes keeps its own allowlist (<code>src/contract/names.js</code>) by design; CI should fail when the two drift (the local copy seems to miss <code>user.access.changed</code>, which Gaia publishes).</p><ul><li>A small Node script (e.g. <code>scripts/check-event-registry.js</code>) reads Gaia's <code>events.json</code> (path or URL argument) and compares: the names that are enabled and on the <code>hermes</code> channel must equal <code>EVENT_ALLOWLIST</code>; those with scope <code>user</code> must equal <code>USER_SCOPED_EVENTS</code>. It prints the differences and exits non-zero.</li><li><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code>: a step that fetches <code>events.json</code> from gaia's <code>dev</code> branch and runs the script. If the gaia repository isn't publicly readable, use a read-only token secret and say so in the PR.</li><li>Fix the allowlist if it really misses <code>user.access.changed</code> (and its user scope).</li><li>Unit test the comparison; mention the check where the docs describe the allowlist rule.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> CI passes on dev; tests show a missing and an extra name both fail.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> generating names.js from Gaia.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["gaia-dev-registry"], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "role-access", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: publish user.access.changed when a user's role is added or removed", "description": "<p><code>user.access.changed</code> (scope <code>user:&lt;userId&gt;</code>, ids only) tells Hermes and Prometheus to re-check a user's access. Today it fires on account status and membership changes, but not on role changes, which also change what the user may do.</p><ul><li>New live-events component for <code>UserroleController</code>, following <code>MembershipLiveEventsComponent</code>: on create, delete and an update that changes <code>userId</code> or <code>roleId</code>, call <code>UserAccessLiveEventsComponent::publishAccessChanged</code> for the affected user (both users when <code>userId</code> changes). Add it to the controller's <code>$uses</code>.</li><li>Update the user.access.changed entry in <code>app/metadata/events.php</code> (description, consumers).</li><li>Tests in the live-events test and api-tester cases with <code>hermes.expect</code>, as for membership.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> adding or removing a role publishes one user.access.changed to that user; a Hermes outage doesn't fail the write.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> permission changes on a role itself (affects many users).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 5, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "mention-framework", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Mentions: model behavior that records user mentions in a record's text fields on every create and update", "description": "<p>Users are mentioned in comments, issue descriptions, thread descriptions and ideas. Prometheus' editor writes a mention as a link, <code>&lt;a class=\\"badge\\" href=\\"/app/user/&lt;userId&gt;\\"&gt;@Name&lt;/a&gt;</code>; markdown bodies (idea messages) would hold <code>[@Name](/app/user/&lt;userId&gt;)</code>. Gaia stores none of this today: the <code>Mention</code> resource (<code>app/metadata/model/Mention.php</code>: relatedTo, relatedId, userId, notified) is never written. This issue builds the capability; the next issues turn it on per model. It must catch <strong>every</strong> write path: REST create/update, collection PATCH, and saves outside controllers such as the workflow Set field action. So it is a model behavior, not a controller component.</p><ul><li><code>MentionParser</code> (domain, e.g. <code>core/libs/mentions/</code>): user ids from HTML anchors and markdown links whose target is <code>/app/user/&lt;id&gt;</code> (relative or absolute URL). Distinct, in order.</li><li>A behavior (e.g. <code>core/mvc/models/behaviors/mentionsBehavior.php</code>, listed in a model's metadata <code>behaviors</code> like <code>ideaScreensBehavior</code>) reading a new metadata key <code>'mentions' =&gt; ['fields' =&gt; [...]]</code>. After create, and after an update where one of those fields changed, it hands the record to a recorder.</li><li>Recorder: for each parsed user id, create a <code>Mention</code> row (relatedTo = the model's lowercase name, relatedId = record id, userId, createdUser = the actor) unless one exists for that record and user. Rows are append-only: removing a mention doesn't delete its row, and re-adding it doesn't create a new one, so nobody is notified twice. Skip the actor mentioning themselves, unknown or deleted users, and users who aren't members of the record's project (resolve the project with the existing <code>ProjectIdResolver</code> logic or an equivalent domain helper).</li><li>Add <code>projectId</code> to <code>Mention</code> (metadata + migration) so later consumers don't have to walk the record.</li><li>Fails safe: an error while recording mentions is logged and must not fail the user's save.</li><li>ADR (e.g. <code>docs/architecture/mentions/decisions.md</code>): behavior vs component, append-only rows, membership rule.</li><li>Tests: parser (HTML and markdown, absolute/relative, junk links), recorder (create, update adds only new users, self, non-member), behavior on a test model.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the behavior on a model, saving text with two mentions creates two rows; saving again creates none; editing in a third creates one.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> turning it on for real models, notifications and events (separate issues); the Mention resource's read ACL.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "mentions-issues", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Mentions: record mentions in issue descriptions, comments and thread descriptions", "description": "<p>Turn on the mentions behavior (from the mention-framework issue) for the records where people mention each other on issues and threads, so mentions are recorded on create and on every update.</p><ul><li><code>app/metadata/model/Issue.php</code>: <code>mentions</code> fields <code>description</code>, behavior added.</li><li><code>app/metadata/model/Comment.php</code>: field <code>comment</code> (comments live in conversation rooms: issue rooms and threads).</li><li><code>app/metadata/model/Conversationroom.php</code>: field <code>description</code> (thread starter).</li><li>api-tester cases: create with a mention, update adding one, update without a change, collection PATCH of issue descriptions; check the Mention rows.</li><li>A unit test that a workflow Set field on an issue description records the mention.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> every create/update path above records new mentions once; existing tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> wiki and docs, ideas (separate issue).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["mention-framework"], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "mentions-ideas", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Mentions: record mentions in idea descriptions and idea messages", "description": "<p>Turn on the mentions behavior (from the mention-framework issue) for ideas. Idea messages are markdown, so mentions there are markdown links to <code>/app/user/&lt;id&gt;</code>; the parser already handles them. Messages written by agents (e.g. Nestor) count too.</p><ul><li><code>app/metadata/model/Idea.php</code>: <code>mentions</code> field <code>description</code>, behavior added.</li><li><code>app/metadata/model/Ideamessage.php</code>: field <code>body</code>, behavior added after the existing ones.</li><li>api-tester cases for create and update of both.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> mentions of project members in ideas and idea messages are recorded once.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> an @-mention picker in Prometheus' idea composer (a Prometheus follow-up).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["mention-framework"], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "mention-event", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: publish user.mentioned when a mention is recorded", "description": "<p>Agents, workflows and the UI need to know when someone is mentioned. Mentions are now recorded as <code>Mention</code> rows (mention-framework issue) from every write path, so the event is published when a row is created, the way <code>app/models/Systemnotificationrecipient.php</code> publishes <code>notification.created</code> through <code>NotificationLiveEvents</code> after create.</p><ul><li>After a <code>Mention</code> is created, publish <code>user.mentioned</code>, scope <code>user:&lt;userId&gt;</code> (the mentioned user). Ids only: mentionId, relatedTo, relatedId, projectId, actor id.</li><li>A small publisher class next to <code>NotificationLiveEvents</code>; constant in <code>EventNames</code>; registry entry in <code>app/metadata/events.php</code> (scope user, channel hermes, consumers talos, prometheus).</li><li>Tests (published once per row, fail-open when Hermes is down) and api-tester <code>hermes.expect</code> on a comment with a mention.</li><li>Contract change: linked Hermes PR (allowlist + user scope).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a comment mentioning two members sends two events, each to that user; an edit that adds nobody sends none.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the workflow channel for mentions.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry", "mention-framework"], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "mention-notification", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Notifications: notify a user when they are mentioned", "description": "<p>A mentioned user should get a notification. Mentions are recorded as <code>Mention</code> rows from every write path; create the notification when a row is created, next to the <code>user.mentioned</code> publish.</p><ul><li>A notification builder (e.g. <code>components/notifications/modules/MentionNotification.php</code> or a service beside it): <code>CreateModel::execute('systemnotification', ...)</code> + <code>RecipientService::notifyUsers($notification, [$userId])</code>, which already publishes <code>notification.created</code>. Description per relatedTo, following the existing templates: <code>{{User@actor}} mentioned you in {{Issue@id}}</code>; for a comment, the issue (or thread) it is on; for an idea or idea message, the idea. <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code> and <code>context</code> (projectShortcode, issueNumber or ideaId, commentId, userId, userName) as in <code>CommentNotification</code>. Set the Mention's <code>notified</code> to true.</li><li>No double notification: <code>CommentNotification::onCreate</code> and <code>IssueNotification::onCreate</code> exclude users mentioned in that same record (Mention rows exist by then, the behavior runs at model save) via the <code>excludeIds</code> of <code>notifyIssueRecipients</code>.</li><li>Tests for each relatedTo and for the exclusion.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a mentioned member gets one mention notification and no second \\"commented\\" one; others are notified as before; a failure doesn't fail the save.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> emails; Prometheus rendering of idea/thread notification links (Prometheus follow-up).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["mention-event"], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-user-mentioned", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Allowlist the user-scoped event user.mentioned", "description": "<p>Gaia publishes <code>user.mentioned</code> when a user is mentioned in a comment, issue or thread description, idea or idea message (linked Gaia issue). It is user-scoped: projectId <code>user:&lt;mentionedUserId&gt;</code>, ids only (mentionId, relatedTo, relatedId, projectId, actor).</p><ul><li>Add it to <code>EVENT_ALLOWLIST</code> and <code>USER_SCOPED_EVENTS</code> in <code>src/contract/names.js</code>.</li><li>ADR entry in decisions.md and tests (only the mentioned user's socket may subscribe).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the drift check against Gaia's events.json passes; tests pass.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["mention-event", "hermes-drift-check"], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "run-finished", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events: publish workflow.run.finished when a workflow run completes or fails", "description": "<p>A run's end is invisible outside Gaia: the run view, Talos and Agamemnon can only poll. Runs end in <code>core/libs/workflows/RunJournal.php</code> <code>finish</code> (called from <code>WorkflowRunner</code> ~l.243; check every caller, e.g. timeouts via <code>ActorStepTimeouts</code>).</p><ul><li>When a run moves to <code>RunStatus::COMPLETED</code> or <code>FAILED</code> (not <code>WAITING</code>), publish <code>workflow.run.finished</code>, project-scoped by the run's <code>projectId</code> (skip runs without one). Ids only: runId, workflowId, status, test flag, entityType/entityId; no error text.</li><li>Inject a publisher the way <code>AgentRunLiveEvents</code> is injected into <code>WorkflowRunner</code> (see <code>WorkflowTriggersComponent::runner</code>); the domain class gets an abstraction, not <code>HermesPublisher</code>.</li><li>Constant in <code>EventNames</code>, registry entry (scope project, channel hermes, consumers prometheus, talos).</li><li>Tests for completed, failed, waiting (no event) and fail-open.</li><li>Contract change: linked Hermes PR.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> each finished run publishes exactly one event; a Hermes outage doesn't affect the run.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> step-level events.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["registry"], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-run-finished", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Allowlist the project-scoped event workflow.run.finished", "description": "<p>Gaia publishes <code>workflow.run.finished</code> when a workflow run completes or fails (linked Gaia issue). Project-scoped (the run's projectId), ids only: runId, workflowId, status, test, entityType, entityId.</p><ul><li>Add it to <code>EVENT_ALLOWLIST</code> in <code>src/contract/names.js</code>.</li><li>ADR entry in decisions.md and tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the drift check passes; project members can subscribe, others can't.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["run-finished", "hermes-drift-check"], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 15:35:54	2026-11-17 15:38:20	f
8d25cf846afc-b85d-5f9c-933b67487895	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	6	{"summary": "Module-agnostic search configured by a per-model `search` metadata block, with search columns on the module's own table (Issue first). Gaia framework work: a new `system` field flag (hidden from responses, not user-writable, not audited) and migration support (extensions, vector, generated tsvector, GIN/trigram/HNSW); then the `search` block that injects system search columns, including the stored canonical semantic text and its hash. A model behaviour keeps text and hash current in the same write and publishes `search.semantic.changed`; a daily `search reindex` backfills them and republishes records whose embedding hash is stale. An `ares` service kind reads those columns and writes the embedding only when the hash it embedded equals the stored current hash (409 otherwise). Hermes accepts service sockets and `service:<kind>` scoped intents. Ares runs nomic-embed-text in-process (fastembed), signs in to Gaia as a service, listens for the event, compares hashes, embeds and writes back, dropping 409s; it also serves POST /embeddings for query embedding. Search runs exact, FTS, fuzzy and semantic matching fused by RRF behind GET /api/v1/search?types=&q=, with the searched module's ACL and record scope applied in SQL.", "issues": [{"key": "system-fields", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Metadata: `system` field flag for fields hidden from the API and not audited", "description": "<p>Gaia has no way to mark a column as managed by the system. Search is about to add columns to module tables (an embedding vector, the text it was made from, hashes, timestamps) that must never reach API clients, never be written by users and never be audited. This issue adds a generic field flag for that.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Field property <code>'system' =&gt; true</code> in model metadata, read through the meta manager (<code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code>), with a helper listing a model's system fields.</li><li>Responses: system fields are never serialized, for the record itself, included relationships, <code>fields=</code> (silently omitted, like denied fields in D-033) and CSV export.</li><li>Writes: system fields in a user request body (POST/PUT/PATCH) are discarded, like denied write fields (D-034).</li><li>Not in the field-ACL catalog (<code>AclMapCatalog</code>) and not usable by users in <code>query</code> clauses or sort (rejected like an unknown field).</li><li><code>auditBehavior</code> skips system fields.</li><li>Opt-in access for specific internal paths is left to the code that needs it (first: the Ares search-column access); no generic bypass.</li><li>Record it as a decision in the relevant <code>docs/architecture/*/decisions.md</code>; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li><li>Tests on a fixture model: absent from GET/list/include/fields=, discarded on PATCH, rejected in a query clause, not in the audit diff, not in the permission catalog.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a field flagged <code>system</code> is invisible and read-only through the REST API and never appears in audit rows; unflagged fields behave as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any real model using the flag.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-migrations", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migrations: Postgres extensions, vector and generated tsvector columns, GIN/trigram/HNSW indexes", "description": "<p>Search needs column and index kinds the declarative migrations cannot create today: they only know primary, unique and plain/multi-column indexes (<code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> ~215-271, <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> ~242). This issue adds the generic capabilities; the search metadata that uses them comes later.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Extensions: migrate runs <code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector</code> and <code>pg_trgm</code> (declared in config, idempotent).</li><li>Field type <code>vector</code> with <code>dimensions</code> (maps to <code>vector(N)</code>) in <code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code> <code>getFieldType</code> and the Postgres dialect.</li><li>Field type <code>tsvector</code> with a <code>generated</code> definition (source field =&gt; weight A-D, text search config default <code>english</code>), migrated as <code>GENERATED ALWAYS AS (setweight(to_tsvector(config, coalesce(field,'')), 'A') || ...) STORED</code>.</li><li>Index kinds <code>gin</code> (tsvector), <code>gin_trgm</code> (<code>gin_trgm_ops</code> on a text field), <code>hnsw_cosine</code> (<code>USING hnsw (col vector_cosine_ops)</code>).</li><li>Re-running migrate is a no-op; changing a generated column's sources recreates it.</li><li><code>docker-compose.yaml</code> Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code>.</li><li>Unit tests for type mapping and generated DDL; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a vector field, a generated tsvector field and the three index kinds migrates as expected and re-migrates cleanly; existing models are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>search</code> metadata block, any real model.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-metadata", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search metadata block: system search columns and the canonical semantic text rule", "description": "<p>A model becomes searchable by declaring a <code>search</code> block in its metadata. The search data lives on the module's own table, so the block adds the search columns and indexes to the model, flagged as system fields. Gaia is the single owner of the text that gets embedded: it stores that text and its hash (Gaia has no computed fields), so every consumer (Ares, the stale-write check, the reindex) agrees on it.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Validate the block in the meta manager: <code>type</code> (name used in <code>/search?types=</code> and in search events, unique across models), <code>fts</code> (field =&gt; weight A-D), <code>fuzzy</code> (fields), <code>semantic</code> (ordered fields), <code>exact</code> (fields), <code>display</code> (<code>title</code>, <code>snippet</code>). Unknown fields or weights fail with a clear message.</li><li>Inject columns, all with <code>'system' =&gt; true</code>: <code>searchVector</code> (generated tsvector from <code>fts</code>, GIN index); and when <code>semantic</code> is set: <code>searchSemanticText</code> (text, the canonical text), <code>searchSemanticHash</code> (varchar 64, its sha256), <code>searchEmbedding</code> (<code>vector(768)</code>, HNSW cosine index), <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> (varchar 64, hash of the text the stored vector was made from), <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> (datetime); plus a <code>gin_trgm</code> index per fuzzy field.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticText</code>: builds a record's canonical semantic text (the <code>semantic</code> fields in order, HTML stripped, whitespace collapsed, cut to <code>SEARCH_EMBED_MAX_CHARS</code>, default 4000) and its sha256. Deterministic; the only implementation of this rule.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SearchableRegistry</code>: lookup of the <code>search</code> block by type and by model.</li><li>Unit tests: validation, injected columns and indexes, columns flagged system, <code>SemanticText</code> output and hash stability (HTML, whitespace, truncation, null fields); regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a <code>search</code> block migrates with the system columns and indexes; its REST payloads and audit rows never contain them; <code>SemanticText</code> gives the same hash for the same field values.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filling the columns (the search behaviour, a later issue), querying, service access.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["system-fields", "search-migrations"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "issue-searchable", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Issue: add the `search` metadata block", "description": "<p>Issue is the first searchable module. Add its <code>search</code> block to <code>app/metadata/model/Issue.php</code> so the migration adds the search columns and indexes to <code>issues</code>.</p><ul><li><code>'search' =&gt; ['type' =&gt; 'issue', 'fts' =&gt; ['subject' =&gt; 'A', 'description' =&gt; 'B'], 'fuzzy' =&gt; ['subject'], 'semantic' =&gt; ['subject', 'description'], 'exact' =&gt; ['issueNumber'], 'display' =&gt; ['title' =&gt; 'subject', 'snippet' =&gt; 'description']]</code></li><li>Run migrate locally and confirm the columns and indexes; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> and the graph.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>issues</code> has <code>searchVector</code> (filled for existing rows), <code>searchSemanticText</code>, <code>searchSemanticHash</code>, <code>searchEmbedding</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> and the indexes; Issue GET/PATCH payloads are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filling the semantic columns (search behaviour and reindex), other modules.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-metadata"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-service-sockets", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Service sockets: accept service tokens and `service:<kind>` scoped intents", "description": "<p>Gaia's search needs Ares (a backend service) to hear a <code>search.semantic.changed</code> event for records in every project. Today sockets authenticate users through <code>user/me</code> and intents must name a project the user is a member of (D-008), so a service would have to join every project and stay under 100 intents. Gaia requests service-scoped subscriptions, mirroring user-scoped events (D-009). Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li>Handshake: a token with no user is checked with Gaia's introspection (<code>POST /api/v1/introspect</code>, D-065: <code>actorType: service</code>, <code>serviceKind</code>); user tokens work as today.</li><li>A new list of service-scoped events in <code>src/contract/names.js</code> (first: <code>search.semantic.changed</code>, added to the allowlist). Their <code>projectId</code> is <code>service:&lt;kind&gt;</code>; a socket may subscribe only when its <code>serviceKind</code> equals that kind (<code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code>). Service sockets cannot subscribe to project or user events.</li><li>Gaia publishes such events with <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> through the existing <code>POST /publish</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/auth</code> (introspection with Hermes' own service token, cached like D-012), <code>src/contract/names.js</code>, <code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code>, a new ADR in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>, tests with the stub loader.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a service socket of kind ares subscribes to <code>service:ares</code>/<code>search.semantic.changed</code> and receives a published envelope; a user socket is rejected for it; a service socket is rejected for project events.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other service events.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-events", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: keep semantic text current, publish `search.semantic.changed`, daily `search reindex`", "description": "<p>Ares embeds a searchable record when Gaia announces that its semantic text changed. Gaia keeps the stored canonical text and hash current in the same write as the change, from a model hook so every write path (REST, MCP, workflows, CLI) is covered, and re-publishes stale records daily because Hermes keeps no history.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Event name <code>search.semantic.changed</code> in <code>support/EventNames.php</code> (lockstep with Hermes <code>names.js</code>, service-scoped).</li><li><code>searchIndexBehavior</code>, attached automatically to every model with a <code>search</code> block that has <code>semantic</code> fields. Before create, and before update when a <code>semantic</code> field changed: set <code>searchSemanticText</code> and <code>searchSemanticHash</code> from <code>SemanticText</code> (same write, no extra query). After the save, if the hash changed: publish through <code>HermesPublisher</code> with <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> and payload <code>{type, resource, recordId}</code>. Fail open: a Hermes failure is logged and never fails the write. Not triggered by the Ares embedding write.</li><li><code>core/tasks/SearchTask.php</code> (parses and prints; logic in <code>core/libs/search/</code>): <code>php cli.php search reindex [type]</code> pages through every non-deleted searchable record; recomputes text and hash and updates them (bound UPDATE, no audit/dateModified) where missing or different (backfills existing rows, follows rule changes); then publishes the event, paced, where <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> is null or differs from <code>searchSemanticHash</code>; prints counts.</li><li>Unit tests with a fake publisher: create sets text/hash and publishes, a semantic edit updates and publishes, a non-semantic edit does neither, an edit that leaves the text identical does not publish, publish failure does not break the save, reindex backfills and selects only stale records.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> creating an issue or editing its description stores its new text and hash and publishes one event; after <code>search reindex</code> every issue has text and hash, and events go out only for issues without an up-to-date embedding.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> scheduling the command (separate issue), the Ares consumer.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable", "hermes-service-sockets"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "service-search-access", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Ares service kind: read the stored semantic text and write embeddings only for the current hash (409 when stale)", "description": "<p>Ares computes embeddings and stores them through Gaia, signing in as a service client (D-065/D-066). Service tokens can only <code>get</code> today, writes are closed until it is decided who a service write is stamped as (D-066), and the search columns are <code>system</code> fields hidden from the API. This issue opens one narrow, explicit path. Because events can be handled out of order, an embedding is stored only if it was made from the record's current semantic text; a slow, older write must never overwrite a newer embedding.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Service kind <code>ares</code> in <code>config/serviceclients.php</code> with default scopes for the searchable modules' <code>get</code>/<code>update</code>.</li><li>Every model with a <code>search</code> block opens <code>get</code> to kind <code>ares</code> (injected from the block, same mechanism as <code>acl.service</code>). For that kind only, <code>fields=</code> may return the stored system fields <code>searchSemanticText</code>, <code>searchSemanticHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>. Users never see them.</li><li>A filtered <code>update</code> for kind <code>ares</code> (like D-068): body <code>{searchEmbedding (768 numbers, validated), searchEmbeddingHash}</code> only; anything else is 400. In one transaction: lock the row (<code>SELECT ... FOR UPDATE</code>) and compare the sent <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> with the stored <code>searchSemanticHash</code>; if they differ, return <strong>409</strong> and write nothing; otherwise store vector and hash and set <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> to now. Deleted or missing record: 404.</li><li>The write is a bound <code>UPDATE</code> of the search columns that skips audit, created/modified-user and dateModified behaviours, live events and the search behaviour (no loop).</li><li>Record the decisions in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code> (new D-number, referencing D-066): unstamped service write of system search columns, hash precondition with 409.</li><li>api-tester cases: ares token reads <code>searchSemanticText</code>/<code>searchSemanticHash</code>; PATCH with the current hash 200; PATCH with an old hash after a subject change 409 and the stored vector unchanged; PATCH of <code>subject</code> 400; a user cannot read or write the search fields; other service kinds 401. Unit test for the lock-and-compare path.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass; an accepted PATCH leaves the issue's audit, dateModified and modifiedUser unchanged; a stale PATCH never overwrites a newer embedding.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> issuing the Ares client credentials in deployments.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-events"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "cli-scheduler", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Run `search reindex` every 24 hours in the Gaia containers", "description": "<p>No container runs cron today (<code>docker/dev/start.sh</code> only migrates), so scheduled CLI tasks never run. Search needs <code>php cli.php search reindex</code> once a day to backfill semantic text and catch records whose event Ares missed.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Pick a scheduler that needs no new package if possible (busybox <code>crond</code> or the base image's cron) and run it in the deployed image (<code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code>, <code>start.sh</code>) and the local stack; a crontab file in the repo (UTC), output to the container log, no overlapping runs.</li><li>Ask the reviewer whether to also enable the existing <code>workflow schedule</code> (documented as cron-driven, never run).</li><li>Document the schedule in the README; a check that the crontab lines parse.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the container's crontab runs <code>search reindex</code> daily and its output appears in the container log.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a job queue system, production infrastructure outside the images.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-events"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-embeddings", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Run nomic-embed-text in-process and serve POST /embeddings", "description": "<p>Gaia is adding semantic search. Ares will compute all embeddings itself with the <code>nomic-embed-text</code> model running inside Ares (no external model server): for records (from search events, a later issue) and for search queries, which Gaia sends over HTTP. Please accept, adapt or decline the contract.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li><code>POST /embeddings</code> request <code>{\\"texts\\": [\\"...\\"], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code>; 1 to 64 non-empty texts of at most 8000 characters; 422 otherwise.</li><li>200 <code>{\\"model\\": \\"nomic-embed-text-v1.5\\", \\"dimensions\\": 768, \\"embeddings\\": [[...]]}</code>, same order, L2-normalised. 503 with a clear message if the model is not loaded; never a fake vector.</li><li>Ares adds the task prefixes (<code>search_document: </code> / <code>search_query: </code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>fastembed</code> (ONNX Runtime, CPU, no PyTorch; approved by the engineer for this feature).</li><li><code>routers/embeddings.py</code> (Pydantic only) -&gt; <code>services/embedding_service.py</code> (reused by the search listener) -&gt; <code>adapters/base_embedding_adapter.py</code> + <code>adapters/fastembed_adapter.py</code> via the factory. Model loaded once; inference in a thread pool so async routes are not blocked.</li><li>Env <code>EMBEDDING_MODEL</code> (default <code>nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5</code>), <code>EMBEDDING_CACHE_DIR</code>, thread count. <code>Dockerfile</code> downloads the weights at build time; <code>/health</code> reports the model loaded.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter: validation, prefixes, order, 503.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the built image returns 768-dimension vectors offline; tests pass without downloading the model.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> GPU, other models, result caching.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-gaia-client", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Sign in to Gaia as the `ares` service client and a Gaia gateway for search fields", "description": "<p>To store embeddings through Gaia, Ares needs its own Gaia identity: a service client of kind <code>ares</code> (Gaia D-065/D-066). Gaia lets it read a searchable record's stored <code>searchSemanticText</code>, <code>searchSemanticHash</code> and <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, and PATCH <code>{searchEmbedding, searchEmbeddingHash}</code>; Gaia answers 409 when the hash no longer matches the record's current text. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>adapters/gaia_auth.py</code>: OAuth <code>client_credentials</code> with <code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code> (env only, never logged); caches the token and refreshes before expiry or on 401.</li><li><code>adapters/gaia_client.py</code> (one class owning transport): <code>get_search_state(resource, id)</code> (the three fields above) and <code>store_embedding(resource, id, embedding, text_hash)</code> (<code>PATCH /api/v1/&lt;resource&gt;/&lt;id&gt;</code>); typed results/errors for 404, <strong>409 stale</strong>, 401/403 and 5xx.</li><li>Update <code>CLAUDE.md</code> Boundaries: Ares stays stateless but now reads from and writes to Gaia as the ares service.</li><li>Tests with a mocked HTTP transport: token reuse and refresh, 404 and 409 mapped to typed results, secrets never in logs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> against local Gaia with an ares client, Ares reads an issue's semantic text and hash and stores an embedding; a stale hash comes back as the 409 result.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the event listener.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["service-search-access"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-search-listener", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Listen for `search.semantic.changed` and keep record embeddings up to date", "description": "<p>Ares creates and updates embeddings when Gaia announces a change. Gaia publishes <code>search.semantic.changed</code> through Hermes to <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> with <code>{type, resource, recordId}</code>. Ares checks the record's dirty state, embeds the canonical text Gaia stores and sends it back with the hash of that text; Gaia rejects it with 409 if the text changed meanwhile. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>python-socketio</code> (async client; approved by the engineer). <code>adapters/hermes_listener.py</code> connects to <code>HERMES_URL</code> with the ares service token (fresh token on every reconnect), sends <code>intents:set</code> for <code>service:ares</code>/<code>search.semantic.changed</code>, reconnects with backoff; started from the FastAPI lifespan.</li><li><code>services/search_index_service.py</code>: <code>get_search_state</code>; if <code>searchSemanticHash</code> equals <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, nothing to do. Otherwise embed <code>searchSemanticText</code> with the <code>document</code> task (no own text building) and <code>store_embedding</code> with <code>searchSemanticHash</code>. <strong>409: drop the result</strong> (a newer event or the daily reindex brings the current text). 404 or empty text: skip.</li><li>Events processed through a bounded async queue with limited concurrency, duplicates within a short window collapsed; other failures logged and left for Gaia's daily reindex (no retry storm).</li><li>Tests with fake listener, Gaia client and embedder: dirty record embeds and stores with the read hash, clean record does nothing, 409 is dropped without retry, missing record skipped, embedder failure stores nothing.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the local stack, editing an issue's description gives it a new embedding within seconds; two quick edits never leave the older text's embedding stored.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ares-embeddings", "ares-gaia-client", "search-events"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "stack-pgvector-ares", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "p4m stack: pgvector Postgres image and Ares Gaia/Hermes settings", "description": "<p>Gaia's new search stores embeddings with the Postgres <code>vector</code> extension, and Ares now signs in to Gaia as a service and listens to Hermes. The stack <code>p4m</code> generates needs both. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>installer/p4m.py</code>: Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code> for the dev DB and gaia-test containers (same major version, existing volumes stay readable).</li><li>Ares env in the generated compose: <code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>HERMES_URL</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>/<code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code> read from <code>p4m.env</code> (secrets only there); <code>p4m configure</code> asks for them; README explains creating the ares service client and the bigger Ares image (embedding model).</li><li>Unit tests for the generated compose.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after <code>p4m up</code>, <code>CREATE EXTENSION vector</code> works in dev and test databases and Ares has its Gaia/Hermes settings.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> production infrastructure.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "embeddings-client", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Embeddings service: Gaia client for the Ares /embeddings endpoint (query embedding)", "description": "<p>Semantic search embeds the user's query at search time through Ares (<code>POST /embeddings</code>, task <code>query</code>, 768 dimensions). Like <code>core/services/LLM.php</code>, the external system sits behind one class that owns configuration and transport.</p><p><strong>Contract (Ares)</strong>: request <code>{\\"texts\\": [...], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code>; 200 <code>{\\"model\\", \\"dimensions\\", \\"embeddings\\": [[...]]}</code>; 422 invalid; 503 model unavailable.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/services/Embeddings.php</code>: <code>embedQuery(string $text): array</code>; Guzzle, base URL <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL</code>, short timeout from env (~3 s).</li><li>Failures throw <code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code> with the reason; never an empty vector. Validates shape and dimension count.</li><li>Register it in <code>ServiceFactory</code> if that is how services are resolved.</li><li>Unit tests with a mocked Guzzle handler: success, 422, 503, timeout, malformed body, wrong dimensions.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests pass without network.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> document embeddings (Ares makes those itself).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ares-embeddings"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-lexical", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search core: exact, FTS and fuzzy searchers with module ACL scope and rank fusion", "description": "<p>The domain layer for module-agnostic search, driven by the <code>search</code> metadata via <code>SearchableRegistry</code>. Every search runs all matching kinds; the caller only gives types and the query. The HTTP controller is the next issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong> in <code>core/libs/search/</code>:</p><ul><li><code>SearchRequest</code>: types, query text (trimmed, 2-200 chars), limit (default 20, max 50).</li><li><code>ExactMatcher</code>: rows whose <code>exact</code> fields equal the query (type-aware: numeric fields match only an integer query, also <code>#123</code>); pinned first.</li><li><code>FtsSearcher</code>: <code>websearch_to_tsquery</code> against the model's system <code>searchVector</code> column (same text search config), <code>ts_rank_cd</code>, snippet via <code>ts_headline</code> on the display snippet field.</li><li><code>FuzzySearcher</code>: <code>pg_trgm</code> <code>word_similarity</code> on fuzzy fields, threshold from config (default 0.3).</li><li><code>RankFusion</code>: Reciprocal Rank Fusion (k = 60) over each searcher's ranked ids, open to more searchers (semantic comes later); items carry <code>matchedBy</code> and the fused score; exact matches stay on top.</li><li><code>SearchService</code>: per type require <code>&lt;module&gt;.get</code> through <code>Acl</code> (denied type = 403, as for unauthorized query criteria, D-027); apply the module's record scope (<code>Acl::applyRecordScope</code>, <code>acl.groupKeys</code>, D-060) and <code>deleted = 0</code> inside each candidate query, before ranking and LIMIT (D-022). A searcher is skipped for a type when the user lacks read on a field it matches; denied display fields are omitted. Bound parameters only.</li><li>Tests: ranking order, exact pin, typo tolerance, a members-scope user never sees other projects' issues, field-ACL skip.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>SearchService</code> returns fused, ACL-scoped Issue results from exact, FTS and fuzzy matching.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching, the HTTP endpoint.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-endpoint", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "SearchController: GET /api/v1/search across searchable modules", "description": "<p>Expose the search core over HTTP. The controller has no permission of its own; authorization is the searched module's (done in <code>SearchService</code>). This is a deliberate exception to standard CRUD resources: record it in a new <code>docs/architecture/search/decisions.md</code> (registered wherever the decisions-docs test expects), with the search metadata, stored system search columns, event-driven embedding by Ares with the hash precondition, and ranking decisions.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>SearchController</code> with a list action only: <code>GET /api/v1/search?types=issue&amp;q=...&amp;limit=20</code>; route in <code>core/config/routes.php</code>; OAuth required; <code>$aclMap</code> declared so the action catalog publishes no <code>search.*</code> permission.</li><li>Thin: parse into <code>SearchRequest</code>, call <code>SearchService</code>, shape the response. 400 for missing or too short <code>q</code> or an unknown type; 403 when a requested type's <code>.get</code> is denied.</li><li>Response: <code>data</code> items <code>{type: 'searchresult', id: '&lt;type&gt;:&lt;recordId&gt;', attributes: {module, recordId, title, snippet, score, matchedBy, pinned}}</code>, <code>meta</code> <code>{query, types}</code>.</li><li>api-tester cases incl. <code>acl</code> profiles (denied module = 403, members scope hides other projects' issues); regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass; searching an issue number pins that issue; a typo in a subject word still finds it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching (next issue), Prometheus UI.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-lexical"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-semantic", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: semantic matching on the module's searchEmbedding column", "description": "<p>Add semantic matching to every search: the query is embedded through Ares and compared to the module's system <code>searchEmbedding</code> column (filled by Ares from search events), then fused with the exact/FTS/fuzzy results.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticSearcher</code>: <code>Embeddings::embedQuery</code>, then cosine distance (<code>&lt;=&gt;</code>, HNSW index) on the module table's non-null <code>searchEmbedding</code>, with the same record scope, ACL and <code>deleted = 0</code> as the other searchers, before LIMIT; max distance from config. Skipped when the user lacks read on any <code>semantic</code> field.</li><li>Register it in <code>SearchService</code>/<code>RankFusion</code>; it always runs for types with a <code>semantic</code> list.</li><li>Ares failure (<code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code>): the other results are still returned and <code>meta.semantic</code> is <code>unavailable</code> (otherwise <code>ok</code>); logged, never a silent success.</li><li>Tests with a fake Embeddings: a paraphrase finds the issue, scope respected, Ares down gives the other results plus the meta flag; api-tester case for the meta field; update the search decisions doc.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> searching \\"login fails after password reset\\" finds an issue titled \\"Reset password link broken\\" with <code>matchedBy</code> containing <code>semantic</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records, re-ranking.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-endpoint", "embeddings-client"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 16:02:21	2026-11-17 16:02:21	f
feb63c356afd-a500-49c2-500b7d7c7b2c	6c7240d86afd-3eec-75db-a5acaf1064a6	4	{"summary": "Remove the blank screens between opening Prometheus and seeing a page, using the existing skeleton standard throughout. index.html gets a static, all-skeleton copy of the app shell (header, sidebar and the PageLoading content), built from existing classes only. It covers the bundle download, session restore and translations. app.loading-assets and the app.project route then show the same PageLoading skeleton through the component. The project route also renders its outlet without a redundant project query and stops making nested routes wait for the all-issues preload. The boot issue is independent of the two project-route issues, which run in order because both change routes/app/project.js.", "issues": [{"key": "boot-loader", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "App start: static skeleton in index.html until the application route is ready, skeleton on loading-assets", "description": "<p>On a cold load, Prometheus shows a blank page until several steps finish one after another. First the bundles load: the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> of <code>app/index.html</code> holds only the two script tags. Then <code>routes/application.js</code> <code>beforeModel</code> awaits <code>session.setup()</code>, which restores the session and may refresh the token. Then it awaits <code>translations.load()</code>. No loading template exists at the top level. After that, <code>app.loading-assets</code> shows only a hardcoded <code>&lt;h1&gt;Loading Assets...&lt;/h1&gt;</code> in the app shell while it loads the user, users, roles, projects and settings. Loading must follow the existing skeleton standard (design system section 9: <code>AppUi::Skeleton</code>), with no new loader, class or CSS.</p><ul><li><code>app/index.html</code>: inside <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>, before the scripts, add static markup marked with <code>data-boot-loader</code> that copies the app shell, with every part a skeleton (see the attached screen):<ul><li><code>wrapper</code>;</li><li><code>main-header</code>: <code>.logo</code> holding a <code>skeleton-line</code>, a <code>global-search</code> skeleton bar, and <code>navbar-custom-menu</code> &gt; <code>ul.nav.navbar-nav</code> with three <code>li &gt; a &gt; skeleton-line--xs</code> for New, notifications and user;</li><li><code>main-sidebar</code> with a <code>sidebar-menu</code> of <code>skeleton-line</code> rows;</li><li><code>content-wrapper</code> containing the markup of <code>AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader</code> (<code>page-skeleton-header</code> plus <code>components/app-ui/skeleton/page-loading-body.hbs</code>).</li></ul>Use existing <code>.skeleton-*</code>, AdminLTE and header classes only, with no inline styles, no new CSS and no text (translations aren't loaded yet). Add a comment in <code>index.html</code> and in <code>page-loading-body.hbs</code> pointing to each other, so the copies stay in sync.</li><li><code>routes/application.js</code>: remove the <code>[data-boot-loader]</code> element once <code>beforeModel</code> has finished, including when it ends in a redirect (signin, public routes) and when restore fails. It must be a no-op when the element is missing (<code>tests/index.html</code> has none).</li><li><code>app/templates/app/loading-assets.hbs</code>: replace the hardcoded heading with <code>&lt;AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader={{true}} /&gt;</code>.</li><li>Tests: a unit test that the application route removes the boot skeleton after <code>beforeModel</code> and tolerates its absence. An integration or acceptance test that loading-assets renders <code>[data-test-page-loading]</code> while its model is pending.</li><li>Compare the static skeleton with the real shell in the running app (sidebar width, header height, content offset) so the handover to the app doesn't jump.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> from the first paint of a cold load (signed in or not) until the first real screen, the page always shows a skeleton (header, sidebar and content), never a blank white page. The static skeleton is gone once the sign-in page or the app shell renders. There is no hardcoded user-facing text and no new CSS.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a skeleton state for the real <code>ApplicationHeader</code> during loading-assets, making the boot requests themselves faster (session restore, translations, loading-assets data), and the app.project route wait.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["boot-splash"]}, {"key": "project-route-skeleton", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project route: show a skeleton while the project loads and render the outlet without the extra project query", "description": "<p>On a fresh load of any project URL (e.g. <code>/app/project/aprom/issue/4198</code>), the content area stays blank until the parent <code>app.project</code> route finishes its hooks, before the nested route's own request even starts. Ember finds no loading substate for <code>app.project</code>: <code>app/project-loading.hbs</code>, <code>app/loading.hbs</code> and <code>loading.hbs</code> don't exist. The existing <code>app/project/loading.hbs</code> and <code>*-loading.hbs</code> templates only cover child routes. They are also hidden, because <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> renders <code>{{outlet}}</code> only inside <code>{{#if this.projectId}}</code>, and <code>setupController</code> in <code>routes/app/project.js</code> sets <code>projectId</code> in the <code>.then()</code> of a second project query, although <code>beforeModel</code> already loaded the project.</p><ul><li>Add <code>app/templates/app/project-loading.hbs</code> with <code>&lt;AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader={{true}} /&gt;</code>, following <code>app/templates/app/settings-loading.hbs</code> and the design system.</li><li><code>routes/app/project.js</code>: keep the project record loaded in <code>beforeModel</code> on the route. In <code>setupController</code>, set <code>model</code>, <code>projectId</code> and <code>projectName</code> from it straight away, and remove the second <code>store.query('project', { fields: 'Project.id,Project.name' ... })</code>.</li><li>When no project matches the short code, keep today's error handling (<code>errorManager</code>) and don't throw on <code>objectAt(project, 0).id</code>.</li><li>Tests: an acceptance or route test that visits a project child route with a delayed project response and asserts the project skeleton is shown. Also check that the child's loading template renders while its own model is pending.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a cold load or reload of a project page never shows an empty content area. The project skeleton shows while the project loads, then the child skeleton, then the page. Only one project request is made per project entry. The project name and breadcrumb are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the all-issues preload in <code>afterModel</code> (separate issue), the app start before the app shell.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["project-loading"]}, {"key": "project-issues-nonblocking", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project route: stop blocking nested routes on the all-issues preload", "description": "<p><code>routes/app/project.js</code> <code>afterModel</code> loads every issue of the project (<code>limit: -1</code>; fields id, subject, issueNumber, statusId, projectId) and returns that promise, so every nested route (board, issue list, issue page, ideas, conversations, ...) waits for it before its own request starts. The list only feeds the <code>issuesList</code> getter in <code>controllers/app/project.js</code> (<code>@computed('projectId', 'issues')</code>). It is read by <code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code> and <code>controllers/prometheus/projectrelated.js</code>, and from there by <code>components/message-box.js</code> and <code>components/summer-note.js</code>.</p><ul><li>Start the issues query without returning it from <code>afterModel</code>. When it resolves, set <code>issues</code> on the <code>app.project</code> controller (and the route, if still read there); report errors with <code>errorManager.handleError</code> as today. Ignore a result that arrives after the user has switched to another project.</li><li>Make sure the <code>issuesList</code> getter updates when <code>issues</code> arrives later, and that every reader handles the empty list (only the blank entry) until then without errors.</li><li>Tests: a route/acceptance test that a nested route's model request starts before the issues preload resolves, and that the list fills in once it does.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a cold load of a project page, the nested route's request starts right after the project request, without waiting for the all-issues request. Issue pickers that use <code>issuesList</code> show the issues once loaded. Switching projects never shows another project's issues.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing the preload with server-side search in the pickers, the store.request migration (aprom-4552).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["project-route-skeleton"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 10:29:18	2026-11-18 10:29:18	f
fec8a3c16afc-dc22-b62c-c261cf290435	411da3826afc-9a36-ac6f-3a7c323d23c4	7	{"summary": "Module-agnostic search configured by a per-model `search` metadata block, with search columns on the module's own table (Issue first). Gaia framework work: a new `system` field flag (hidden from responses, not user-writable, not audited) and migration support (extensions, vector, generated tsvector, GIN/trigram/HNSW); then the `search` block that injects system search columns, including the stored canonical semantic text and its hash. A model behaviour keeps text and hash current in the same write and publishes `search.semantic.changed`; a daily `search reindex` backfills them and republishes records whose embedding hash is stale. An `ares` service kind reads those columns and writes the embedding only when the hash it embedded equals the stored current hash (409 otherwise). Hermes accepts service sockets and `service:<kind>` scoped intents. Ares runs nomic-embed-text in-process (fastembed), signs in to Gaia as a service, listens for the event, compares hashes, embeds and writes back, dropping 409s; it also serves POST /embeddings for query embedding. Search runs exact, FTS, fuzzy and semantic matching fused by RRF behind GET /api/v1/search?types=&q=, with the searched module's ACL and record scope applied in SQL.", "issues": [{"key": "system-fields", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Metadata: `system` field flag for fields hidden from the API and not audited", "description": "<p>Gaia has no way to mark a column as managed by the system. Search is about to add columns to module tables (an embedding vector, the text it was made from, hashes, timestamps) that must never reach API clients, never be written by users and never be audited. This issue adds a generic field flag for that.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Field property <code>'system' =&gt; true</code> in model metadata, read through the meta manager (<code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code>), with a helper listing a model's system fields.</li><li>Responses: system fields are never serialized, for the record itself, included relationships, <code>fields=</code> (silently omitted, like denied fields in D-033) and CSV export.</li><li>Writes: system fields in a user request body (POST/PUT/PATCH) are discarded, like denied write fields (D-034).</li><li>Not in the field-ACL catalog (<code>AclMapCatalog</code>) and not usable by users in <code>query</code> clauses or sort (rejected like an unknown field).</li><li><code>auditBehavior</code> skips system fields.</li><li>Opt-in access for specific internal paths is left to the code that needs it (first: the Ares search-column access); no generic bypass.</li><li>Record it as a decision in the relevant <code>docs/architecture/*/decisions.md</code>; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li><li>Tests on a fixture model: absent from GET/list/include/fields=, discarded on PATCH, rejected in a query clause, not in the audit diff, not in the permission catalog.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a field flagged <code>system</code> is invisible and read-only through the REST API and never appears in audit rows; unflagged fields behave as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any real model using the flag.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-migrations", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migrations: Postgres extensions, vector and generated tsvector columns, GIN/trigram/HNSW indexes", "description": "<p>Search needs column and index kinds the declarative migrations cannot create today: they only know primary, unique and plain/multi-column indexes (<code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> ~215-271, <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> ~242). This issue adds the generic capabilities; the search metadata that uses them comes later.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Extensions: migrate runs <code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector</code> and <code>pg_trgm</code> (declared in config, idempotent).</li><li>Field type <code>vector</code> with <code>dimensions</code> (maps to <code>vector(N)</code>) in <code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code> <code>getFieldType</code> and the Postgres dialect.</li><li>Field type <code>tsvector</code> with a <code>generated</code> definition (source field =&gt; weight A-D, text search config default <code>english</code>), migrated as <code>GENERATED ALWAYS AS (setweight(to_tsvector(config, coalesce(field,'')), 'A') || ...) STORED</code>.</li><li>Index kinds <code>gin</code> (tsvector), <code>gin_trgm</code> (<code>gin_trgm_ops</code> on a text field), <code>hnsw_cosine</code> (<code>USING hnsw (col vector_cosine_ops)</code>).</li><li>Re-running migrate is a no-op; changing a generated column's sources recreates it.</li><li><code>docker-compose.yaml</code> Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code>.</li><li>Unit tests for type mapping and generated DDL; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a vector field, a generated tsvector field and the three index kinds migrates as expected and re-migrates cleanly; existing models are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>search</code> metadata block, any real model.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-metadata", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search metadata block: system search columns and the canonical semantic text rule", "description": "<p>A model becomes searchable by declaring a <code>search</code> block in its metadata. The search data lives on the module's own table, so the block adds the search columns and indexes to the model, flagged as system fields. Gaia is the single owner of the text that gets embedded: it stores that text and its hash (Gaia has no computed fields), so every consumer (Ares, the stale-write check, the reindex) agrees on it.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Validate the block in the meta manager: <code>type</code> (name used in <code>/search?types=</code> and in search events, unique across models), <code>fts</code> (field =&gt; weight A-D), <code>fuzzy</code> (fields), <code>semantic</code> (ordered fields), <code>exact</code> (fields), <code>display</code> (<code>title</code>, <code>snippet</code>). Unknown fields or weights fail with a clear message.</li><li>Inject columns, all with <code>'system' =&gt; true</code>: <code>searchVector</code> (generated tsvector from <code>fts</code>, GIN index); and when <code>semantic</code> is set: <code>searchSemanticText</code> (text, the canonical text), <code>searchSemanticHash</code> (varchar 64, its sha256), <code>searchEmbedding</code> (<code>vector(768)</code>, HNSW cosine index), <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> (varchar 64, hash of the text the stored vector was made from), <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> (datetime); plus a <code>gin_trgm</code> index per fuzzy field.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticText</code>: builds a record's canonical semantic text (the <code>semantic</code> fields in order, HTML stripped, whitespace collapsed, cut to <code>SEARCH_EMBED_MAX_CHARS</code>, default 4000) and its sha256. Deterministic; the only implementation of this rule.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SearchableRegistry</code>: lookup of the <code>search</code> block by type and by model.</li><li>Unit tests: validation, injected columns and indexes, columns flagged system, <code>SemanticText</code> output and hash stability (HTML, whitespace, truncation, null fields); regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a <code>search</code> block migrates with the system columns and indexes; its REST payloads and audit rows never contain them; <code>SemanticText</code> gives the same hash for the same field values.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filling the columns (the search behaviour, a later issue), querying, service access.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["system-fields", "search-migrations"], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "issue-searchable", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Issue: add the `search` metadata block", "description": "<p>Issue is the first searchable module. Add its <code>search</code> block to <code>app/metadata/model/Issue.php</code> so the migration adds the search columns and indexes to <code>issues</code>.</p><ul><li><code>'search' =&gt; ['type' =&gt; 'issue', 'fts' =&gt; ['subject' =&gt; 'A', 'description' =&gt; 'B'], 'fuzzy' =&gt; ['subject'], 'semantic' =&gt; ['subject', 'description'], 'exact' =&gt; ['issueNumber'], 'display' =&gt; ['title' =&gt; 'subject', 'snippet' =&gt; 'description']]</code></li><li>Run migrate locally and confirm the columns and indexes; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> and the graph.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>issues</code> has <code>searchVector</code> (filled for existing rows), <code>searchSemanticText</code>, <code>searchSemanticHash</code>, <code>searchEmbedding</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> and the indexes; Issue GET/PATCH payloads are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filling the semantic columns (search behaviour and reindex), other modules.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-metadata"], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 2, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "hermes-service-sockets", "project": "A Hermes", "projectCode": "ah", "subject": "Service sockets: accept service tokens and `service:<kind>` scoped intents", "description": "<p>Gaia's search needs Ares (a backend service) to hear a <code>search.semantic.changed</code> event for records in every project. Today sockets authenticate users through <code>user/me</code> and intents must name a project the user is a member of (D-008), so a service would have to join every project and stay under 100 intents. Gaia requests service-scoped subscriptions, mirroring user-scoped events (D-009). Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li>Handshake: a token with no user is checked with Gaia's introspection (<code>POST /api/v1/introspect</code>, D-065: <code>actorType: service</code>, <code>serviceKind</code>); user tokens work as today.</li><li>A new list of service-scoped events in <code>src/contract/names.js</code> (first: <code>search.semantic.changed</code>, added to the allowlist). Their <code>projectId</code> is <code>service:&lt;kind&gt;</code>; a socket may subscribe only when its <code>serviceKind</code> equals that kind (<code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code>). Service sockets cannot subscribe to project or user events.</li><li>Gaia publishes such events with <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> through the existing <code>POST /publish</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/auth</code> (introspection with Hermes' own service token, cached like D-012), <code>src/contract/names.js</code>, <code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code>, a new ADR in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>, tests with the stub loader.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a service socket of kind ares subscribes to <code>service:ares</code>/<code>search.semantic.changed</code> and receives a published envelope; a user socket is rejected for it; a service socket is rejected for project events.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other service events.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-events", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: keep semantic text current, publish `search.semantic.changed`, daily `search reindex`", "description": "<p>Ares embeds a searchable record when Gaia announces that its semantic text changed. Gaia keeps the stored canonical text and hash current in the same write as the change, from a model hook so every write path (REST, MCP, workflows, CLI) is covered, and re-publishes stale records daily because Hermes keeps no history.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Event name <code>search.semantic.changed</code> in <code>support/EventNames.php</code> (lockstep with Hermes <code>names.js</code>, service-scoped).</li><li><code>searchIndexBehavior</code>, attached automatically to every model with a <code>search</code> block that has <code>semantic</code> fields. Before create, and before update when a <code>semantic</code> field changed: set <code>searchSemanticText</code> and <code>searchSemanticHash</code> from <code>SemanticText</code> (same write, no extra query). After the save, if the hash changed: publish through <code>HermesPublisher</code> with <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> and payload <code>{type, resource, recordId}</code>. Fail open: a Hermes failure is logged and never fails the write. Not triggered by the Ares embedding write.</li><li><code>core/tasks/SearchTask.php</code> (parses and prints; logic in <code>core/libs/search/</code>): <code>php cli.php search reindex [type]</code> pages through every non-deleted searchable record; recomputes text and hash and updates them (bound UPDATE, no audit/dateModified) where missing or different (backfills existing rows, follows rule changes); then publishes the event, paced, where <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> is null or differs from <code>searchSemanticHash</code>; prints counts.</li><li>Unit tests with a fake publisher: create sets text/hash and publishes, a semantic edit updates and publishes, a non-semantic edit does neither, an edit that leaves the text identical does not publish, publish failure does not break the save, reindex backfills and selects only stale records.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> creating an issue or editing its description stores its new text and hash and publishes one event; after <code>search reindex</code> every issue has text and hash, and events go out only for issues without an up-to-date embedding.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> scheduling the command (separate issue), the Ares consumer.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable", "hermes-service-sockets"], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "service-search-access", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Ares service kind: read the stored semantic text and write embeddings only for the current hash (409 when stale)", "description": "<p>Ares computes embeddings and stores them through Gaia, signing in as a service client (D-065/D-066). Service tokens can only <code>get</code> today, writes are closed until it is decided who a service write is stamped as (D-066), and the search columns are <code>system</code> fields hidden from the API. This issue opens one narrow, explicit path. Because events can be handled out of order, an embedding is stored only if it was made from the record's current semantic text; a slow, older write must never overwrite a newer embedding.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Service kind <code>ares</code> in <code>config/serviceclients.php</code> with default scopes for the searchable modules' <code>get</code>/<code>update</code>.</li><li>Every model with a <code>search</code> block opens <code>get</code> to kind <code>ares</code> (injected from the block, same mechanism as <code>acl.service</code>). For that kind only, <code>fields=</code> may return the stored system fields <code>searchSemanticText</code>, <code>searchSemanticHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>. Users never see them.</li><li>A filtered <code>update</code> for kind <code>ares</code> (like D-068): body <code>{searchEmbedding (768 numbers, validated), searchEmbeddingHash}</code> only; anything else is 400. In one transaction: lock the row (<code>SELECT ... FOR UPDATE</code>) and compare the sent <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> with the stored <code>searchSemanticHash</code>; if they differ, return <strong>409</strong> and write nothing; otherwise store vector and hash and set <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> to now. Deleted or missing record: 404.</li><li>The write is a bound <code>UPDATE</code> of the search columns that skips audit, created/modified-user and dateModified behaviours, live events and the search behaviour (no loop).</li><li>Record the decisions in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code> (new D-number, referencing D-066): unstamped service write of system search columns, hash precondition with 409.</li><li>api-tester cases: ares token reads <code>searchSemanticText</code>/<code>searchSemanticHash</code>; PATCH with the current hash 200; PATCH with an old hash after a subject change 409 and the stored vector unchanged; PATCH of <code>subject</code> 400; a user cannot read or write the search fields; other service kinds 401. Unit test for the lock-and-compare path.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass; an accepted PATCH leaves the issue's audit, dateModified and modifiedUser unchanged; a stale PATCH never overwrites a newer embedding.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> issuing the Ares client credentials in deployments.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-events"], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "cli-scheduler", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Run `search reindex` every 24 hours in the Gaia containers", "description": "<p>No container runs cron today (<code>docker/dev/start.sh</code> only migrates), so scheduled CLI tasks never run. Search needs <code>php cli.php search reindex</code> once a day to backfill semantic text and catch records whose event Ares missed.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Pick a scheduler that needs no new package if possible (busybox <code>crond</code> or the base image's cron) and run it in the deployed image (<code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code>, <code>start.sh</code>) and the local stack; a crontab file in the repo (UTC), output to the container log, no overlapping runs.</li><li>Ask the reviewer whether to also enable the existing <code>workflow schedule</code> (documented as cron-driven, never run).</li><li>Document the schedule in the README; a check that the crontab lines parse.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the container's crontab runs <code>search reindex</code> daily and its output appears in the container log.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a job queue system, production infrastructure outside the images.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-events"], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-embeddings", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Run nomic-embed-text in-process and serve POST /embeddings", "description": "<p>Gaia is adding semantic search. Ares will compute all embeddings itself with the <code>nomic-embed-text</code> model running inside Ares (no external model server): for records (from search events, a later issue) and for search queries, which Gaia sends over HTTP. Please accept, adapt or decline the contract.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li><code>POST /embeddings</code> request <code>{\\"texts\\": [\\"...\\"], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code>; 1 to 64 non-empty texts of at most 8000 characters; 422 otherwise.</li><li>200 <code>{\\"model\\": \\"nomic-embed-text-v1.5\\", \\"dimensions\\": 768, \\"embeddings\\": [[...]]}</code>, same order, L2-normalised. 503 with a clear message if the model is not loaded; never a fake vector.</li><li>Ares adds the task prefixes (<code>search_document: </code> / <code>search_query: </code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>fastembed</code> (ONNX Runtime, CPU, no PyTorch; approved by the engineer for this feature).</li><li><code>routers/embeddings.py</code> (Pydantic only) -&gt; <code>services/embedding_service.py</code> (reused by the search listener) -&gt; <code>adapters/base_embedding_adapter.py</code> + <code>adapters/fastembed_adapter.py</code> via the factory. Model loaded once; inference in a thread pool so async routes are not blocked.</li><li>Env <code>EMBEDDING_MODEL</code> (default <code>nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5</code>), <code>EMBEDDING_CACHE_DIR</code>, thread count. <code>Dockerfile</code> downloads the weights at build time; <code>/health</code> reports the model loaded.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter: validation, prefixes, order, 503.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the built image returns 768-dimension vectors offline; tests pass without downloading the model.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> GPU, other models, result caching.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 9, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-gaia-client", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Sign in to Gaia as the `ares` service client and a Gaia gateway for search fields", "description": "<p>To store embeddings through Gaia, Ares needs its own Gaia identity: a service client of kind <code>ares</code> (Gaia D-065/D-066). Gaia lets it read a searchable record's stored <code>searchSemanticText</code>, <code>searchSemanticHash</code> and <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, and PATCH <code>{searchEmbedding, searchEmbeddingHash}</code>; Gaia answers 409 when the hash no longer matches the record's current text. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>adapters/gaia_auth.py</code>: OAuth <code>client_credentials</code> with <code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code> (env only, never logged); caches the token and refreshes before expiry or on 401.</li><li><code>adapters/gaia_client.py</code> (one class owning transport): <code>get_search_state(resource, id)</code> (the three fields above) and <code>store_embedding(resource, id, embedding, text_hash)</code> (<code>PATCH /api/v1/&lt;resource&gt;/&lt;id&gt;</code>); typed results/errors for 404, <strong>409 stale</strong>, 401/403 and 5xx.</li><li>Update <code>CLAUDE.md</code> Boundaries: Ares stays stateless but now reads from and writes to Gaia as the ares service.</li><li>Tests with a mocked HTTP transport: token reuse and refresh, 404 and 409 mapped to typed results, secrets never in logs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> against local Gaia with an ares client, Ares reads an issue's semantic text and hash and stores an embedding; a stale hash comes back as the 409 result.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the event listener.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["service-search-access"], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ares-search-listener", "project": "A Ares", "projectCode": "aa", "subject": "Listen for `search.semantic.changed` and keep record embeddings up to date", "description": "<p>Ares creates and updates embeddings when Gaia announces a change. Gaia publishes <code>search.semantic.changed</code> through Hermes to <code>projectId: \\"service:ares\\"</code> with <code>{type, resource, recordId}</code>. Ares checks the record's dirty state, embeds the canonical text Gaia stores and sends it back with the hash of that text; Gaia rejects it with 409 if the text changed meanwhile. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>python-socketio</code> (async client; approved by the engineer). <code>adapters/hermes_listener.py</code> connects to <code>HERMES_URL</code> with the ares service token (fresh token on every reconnect), sends <code>intents:set</code> for <code>service:ares</code>/<code>search.semantic.changed</code>, reconnects with backoff; started from the FastAPI lifespan.</li><li><code>services/search_index_service.py</code>: <code>get_search_state</code>; if <code>searchSemanticHash</code> equals <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, nothing to do. Otherwise embed <code>searchSemanticText</code> with the <code>document</code> task (no own text building) and <code>store_embedding</code> with <code>searchSemanticHash</code>. <strong>409: drop the result</strong> (a newer event or the daily reindex brings the current text). 404 or empty text: skip.</li><li>Events processed through a bounded async queue with limited concurrency, duplicates within a short window collapsed; other failures logged and left for Gaia's daily reindex (no retry storm).</li><li>Tests with fake listener, Gaia client and embedder: dirty record embeds and stores with the read hash, clean record does nothing, 409 is dropped without retry, missing record skipped, embedder failure stores nothing.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the local stack, editing an issue's description gives it a new embedding within seconds; two quick edits never leave the older text's embedding stored.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["ares-embeddings", "ares-gaia-client", "search-events"], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "stack-pgvector-ares", "project": "A Dev Tool", "projectCode": "adt", "subject": "p4m stack: pgvector Postgres image and Ares Gaia/Hermes settings", "description": "<p>Gaia's new search stores embeddings with the Postgres <code>vector</code> extension, and Ares now signs in to Gaia as a service and listens to Hermes. The stack <code>p4m</code> generates needs both. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>installer/p4m.py</code>: Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code> for the dev DB and gaia-test containers (same major version, existing volumes stay readable).</li><li>Ares env in the generated compose: <code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>HERMES_URL</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>/<code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code> read from <code>p4m.env</code> (secrets only there); <code>p4m configure</code> asks for them; README explains creating the ares service client and the bigger Ares image (embedding model).</li><li>Unit tests for the generated compose.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after <code>p4m up</code>, <code>CREATE EXTENSION vector</code> works in dev and test databases and Ares has its Gaia/Hermes settings.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> production infrastructure.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "embeddings-client", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Embeddings service: Gaia client for the Ares /embeddings endpoint (query embedding)", "description": "<p>Semantic search embeds the user's query at search time through Ares (<code>POST /embeddings</code>, task <code>query</code>, 768 dimensions). Like <code>core/services/LLM.php</code>, the external system sits behind one class that owns configuration and transport.</p><p><strong>Contract (Ares)</strong>: request <code>{\\"texts\\": [...], \\"task\\": \\"document\\"|\\"query\\"}</code>; 200 <code>{\\"model\\", \\"dimensions\\", \\"embeddings\\": [[...]]}</code>; 422 invalid; 503 model unavailable.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/services/Embeddings.php</code>: <code>embedQuery(string $text): array</code>; Guzzle, base URL <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL</code>, short timeout from env (~3 s).</li><li>Failures throw <code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code> with the reason; never an empty vector. Validates shape and dimension count.</li><li>Register it in <code>ServiceFactory</code> if that is how services are resolved.</li><li>Unit tests with a mocked Guzzle handler: success, 422, 503, timeout, malformed body, wrong dimensions.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests pass without network.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> document embeddings (Ares makes those itself).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ares-embeddings"], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-lexical", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search core: exact, FTS and fuzzy searchers with module ACL scope and rank fusion", "description": "<p>The domain layer for module-agnostic search, driven by the <code>search</code> metadata via <code>SearchableRegistry</code>. Every search runs all matching kinds; the caller only gives types and the query. The HTTP controller is the next issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong> in <code>core/libs/search/</code>:</p><ul><li><code>SearchRequest</code>: types, query text (trimmed, 2-200 chars), limit (default 20, max 50).</li><li><code>ExactMatcher</code>: rows whose <code>exact</code> fields equal the query (type-aware: numeric fields match only an integer query, also <code>#123</code>); pinned first.</li><li><code>FtsSearcher</code>: <code>websearch_to_tsquery</code> against the model's system <code>searchVector</code> column (same text search config), <code>ts_rank_cd</code>, snippet via <code>ts_headline</code> on the display snippet field.</li><li><code>FuzzySearcher</code>: <code>pg_trgm</code> <code>word_similarity</code> on fuzzy fields, threshold from config (default 0.3).</li><li><code>RankFusion</code>: Reciprocal Rank Fusion (k = 60) over each searcher's ranked ids, open to more searchers (semantic comes later); items carry <code>matchedBy</code> and the fused score; exact matches stay on top.</li><li><code>SearchService</code>: per type require <code>&lt;module&gt;.get</code> through <code>Acl</code> (denied type = 403, as for unauthorized query criteria, D-027); apply the module's record scope (<code>Acl::applyRecordScope</code>, <code>acl.groupKeys</code>, D-060) and <code>deleted = 0</code> inside each candidate query, before ranking and LIMIT (D-022). A searcher is skipped for a type when the user lacks read on a field it matches; denied display fields are omitted. Bound parameters only.</li><li>Tests: ranking order, exact pin, typo tolerance, a members-scope user never sees other projects' issues, field-ACL skip.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>SearchService</code> returns fused, ACL-scoped Issue results from exact, FTS and fuzzy matching.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching, the HTTP endpoint.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["issue-searchable"], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-endpoint", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "SearchController: GET /api/v1/search across searchable modules", "description": "<p>Expose the search core over HTTP. The controller has no permission of its own; authorization is the searched module's (done in <code>SearchService</code>). This is a deliberate exception to standard CRUD resources: record it in a new <code>docs/architecture/search/decisions.md</code> (registered wherever the decisions-docs test expects), with the search metadata, stored system search columns, event-driven embedding by Ares with the hash precondition, and ranking decisions.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>SearchController</code> with a list action only: <code>GET /api/v1/search?types=issue&amp;q=...&amp;limit=20</code>; route in <code>core/config/routes.php</code>; OAuth required; <code>$aclMap</code> declared so the action catalog publishes no <code>search.*</code> permission.</li><li>Thin: parse into <code>SearchRequest</code>, call <code>SearchService</code>, shape the response. 400 for missing or too short <code>q</code> or an unknown type; 403 when a requested type's <code>.get</code> is denied.</li><li>Response: <code>data</code> items <code>{type: 'searchresult', id: '&lt;type&gt;:&lt;recordId&gt;', attributes: {module, recordId, title, snippet, score, matchedBy, pinned}}</code>, <code>meta</code> <code>{query, types}</code>.</li><li>api-tester cases incl. <code>acl</code> profiles (denied module = 403, members scope hides other projects' issues); regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass; searching an issue number pins that issue; a typo in a subject word still finds it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching (next issue), Prometheus UI.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["search-lexical"], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "search-semantic", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Search: semantic matching on the module's searchEmbedding column", "description": "<p>Add semantic matching to every search: the query is embedded through Ares and compared to the module's system <code>searchEmbedding</code> column (filled by Ares from search events), then fused with the exact/FTS/fuzzy results.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticSearcher</code>: <code>Embeddings::embedQuery</code>, then cosine distance (<code>&lt;=&gt;</code>, HNSW index) on the module table's non-null <code>searchEmbedding</code>, with the same record scope, ACL and <code>deleted = 0</code> as the other searchers, before LIMIT; max distance from config. Skipped when the user lacks read on any <code>semantic</code> field.</li><li>Register it in <code>SearchService</code>/<code>RankFusion</code>; it always runs for types with a <code>semantic</code> list.</li><li>Ares failure (<code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code>): the other results are still returned and <code>meta.semantic</code> is <code>unavailable</code> (otherwise <code>ok</code>); logged, never a silent success.</li><li>Tests with a fake Embeddings: a paraphrase finds the issue, scope respected, Ares down gives the other results plus the meta flag; api-tester case for the meta field; update the search decisions doc.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> searching \\"login fails after password reset\\" finds an issue titled \\"Reset password link broken\\" with <code>matchedBy</code> containing <code>semantic</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records, re-ranking.</p>", "type": "Story", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["search-endpoint", "embeddings-client"], "milestone": "aga-semantic", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-17 16:21:18	2026-11-17 16:24:17	f
5bd17a206afd-7db8-49c2-40001c5118be	6c7240d86afd-3eec-75db-a5acaf1064a6	5	{"summary": "Remove the blank screens between opening Prometheus and seeing a page, using the existing skeleton standard throughout. index.html gets a static, all-skeleton copy of the app shell (header, sidebar and the PageLoading content), built from existing classes only. It covers the bundle download, session restore and translations. app.loading-assets and the app.project route then show the same PageLoading skeleton through the component. The project route also renders its outlet without a redundant project query and stops making nested routes wait for the all-issues preload. The boot issue is independent of the two project-route issues, which run in order because both change routes/app/project.js.", "issues": [{"key": "boot-loader", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "App start: static skeleton in index.html until the application route is ready, skeleton on loading-assets", "description": "<p>On a cold load, Prometheus shows a blank page until several steps finish one after another. First the bundles load: the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> of <code>app/index.html</code> holds only the two script tags. Then <code>routes/application.js</code> <code>beforeModel</code> awaits <code>session.setup()</code>, which restores the session and may refresh the token. Then it awaits <code>translations.load()</code>. No loading template exists at the top level. After that, <code>app.loading-assets</code> shows only a hardcoded <code>&lt;h1&gt;Loading Assets...&lt;/h1&gt;</code> in the app shell while it loads the user, users, roles, projects and settings. Loading must follow the existing skeleton standard (design system section 9: <code>AppUi::Skeleton</code>), with no new loader, class or CSS.</p><ul><li><code>app/index.html</code>: inside <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>, before the scripts, add static markup marked with <code>data-boot-loader</code> that copies the app shell, with every part a skeleton (see the attached screen):<ul><li><code>wrapper</code>;</li><li><code>main-header</code>: <code>.logo</code> holding a <code>skeleton-line</code>, a <code>global-search</code> skeleton bar, and <code>navbar-custom-menu</code> &gt; <code>ul.nav.navbar-nav</code> with three <code>li &gt; a &gt; skeleton-line--xs</code> for New, notifications and user;</li><li><code>main-sidebar</code> with a <code>sidebar-menu</code> of <code>skeleton-line</code> rows;</li><li><code>content-wrapper</code> containing the markup of <code>AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader</code> (<code>page-skeleton-header</code> plus <code>components/app-ui/skeleton/page-loading-body.hbs</code>).</li></ul>Use existing <code>.skeleton-*</code>, AdminLTE and header classes only, with no inline styles, no new CSS and no text (translations aren't loaded yet). Add a comment in <code>index.html</code> and in <code>page-loading-body.hbs</code> pointing to each other, so the copies stay in sync.</li><li><code>routes/application.js</code>: remove the <code>[data-boot-loader]</code> element once <code>beforeModel</code> has finished, including when it ends in a redirect (signin, public routes) and when restore fails. It must be a no-op when the element is missing (<code>tests/index.html</code> has none).</li><li><code>app/templates/app/loading-assets.hbs</code>: replace the hardcoded heading with <code>&lt;AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader={{true}} /&gt;</code>.</li><li>Tests: a unit test that the application route removes the boot skeleton after <code>beforeModel</code> and tolerates its absence. An integration or acceptance test that loading-assets renders <code>[data-test-page-loading]</code> while its model is pending.</li><li>Compare the static skeleton with the real shell in the running app (sidebar width, header height, content offset) so the handover to the app doesn't jump.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> from the first paint of a cold load (signed in or not) until the first real screen, the page always shows a skeleton (header, sidebar and content), never a blank white page. The static skeleton is gone once the sign-in page or the app shell renders. There is no hardcoded user-facing text and no new CSS.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a skeleton state for the real <code>ApplicationHeader</code> during loading-assets, making the boot requests themselves faster (session restore, translations, loading-assets data), and the app.project route wait.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-ui-loading", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["boot-splash"]}, {"key": "project-route-skeleton", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project route: show a skeleton while the project loads and render the outlet without the extra project query", "description": "<p>On a fresh load of any project URL (e.g. <code>/app/project/aprom/issue/4198</code>), the content area stays blank until the parent <code>app.project</code> route finishes its hooks, before the nested route's own request even starts. Ember finds no loading substate for <code>app.project</code>: <code>app/project-loading.hbs</code>, <code>app/loading.hbs</code> and <code>loading.hbs</code> don't exist. The existing <code>app/project/loading.hbs</code> and <code>*-loading.hbs</code> templates only cover child routes. They are also hidden, because <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> renders <code>{{outlet}}</code> only inside <code>{{#if this.projectId}}</code>, and <code>setupController</code> in <code>routes/app/project.js</code> sets <code>projectId</code> in the <code>.then()</code> of a second project query, although <code>beforeModel</code> already loaded the project.</p><ul><li>Add <code>app/templates/app/project-loading.hbs</code> with <code>&lt;AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader={{true}} /&gt;</code>, following <code>app/templates/app/settings-loading.hbs</code> and the design system.</li><li><code>routes/app/project.js</code>: keep the project record loaded in <code>beforeModel</code> on the route. In <code>setupController</code>, set <code>model</code>, <code>projectId</code> and <code>projectName</code> from it straight away, and remove the second <code>store.query('project', { fields: 'Project.id,Project.name' ... })</code>.</li><li>When no project matches the short code, keep today's error handling (<code>errorManager</code>) and don't throw on <code>objectAt(project, 0).id</code>.</li><li>Tests: an acceptance or route test that visits a project child route with a delayed project response and asserts the project skeleton is shown. Also check that the child's loading template renders while its own model is pending.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a cold load or reload of a project page never shows an empty content area. The project skeleton shows while the project loads, then the child skeleton, then the page. Only one project request is made per project entry. The project name and breadcrumb are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the all-issues preload in <code>afterModel</code> (separate issue), the app start before the app shell.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-ui-loading", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": ["project-loading"]}, {"key": "project-issues-nonblocking", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Project route: stop blocking nested routes on the all-issues preload", "description": "<p><code>routes/app/project.js</code> <code>afterModel</code> loads every issue of the project (<code>limit: -1</code>; fields id, subject, issueNumber, statusId, projectId) and returns that promise, so every nested route (board, issue list, issue page, ideas, conversations, ...) waits for it before its own request starts. The list only feeds the <code>issuesList</code> getter in <code>controllers/app/project.js</code> (<code>@computed('projectId', 'issues')</code>). It is read by <code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code> and <code>controllers/prometheus/projectrelated.js</code>, and from there by <code>components/message-box.js</code> and <code>components/summer-note.js</code>.</p><ul><li>Start the issues query without returning it from <code>afterModel</code>. When it resolves, set <code>issues</code> on the <code>app.project</code> controller (and the route, if still read there); report errors with <code>errorManager.handleError</code> as today. Ignore a result that arrives after the user has switched to another project.</li><li>Make sure the <code>issuesList</code> getter updates when <code>issues</code> arrives later, and that every reader handles the empty list (only the blank entry) until then without errors.</li><li>Tests: a route/acceptance test that a nested route's model request starts before the issues preload resolves, and that the list fills in once it does.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a cold load of a project page, the nested route's request starts right after the project request, without waiting for the all-issues request. Issue pickers that use <code>issuesList</code> show the issues once loaded. Switching projects never shows another project's issues.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing the preload with server-side search in the pickers, the store.request migration (aprom-4552).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["project-route-skeleton"], "milestone": "aga-ui-loading", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 10:30:51	2026-11-18 10:32:18	f
9b0ffe816afd-c3e4-2996-2b38e00ec6c1	d98352c16af4-9ee0-e9a2-4dddf1b444ee	4	{"summary": "Moves Gaia from PHP 7.4.21 / Phalcon 4.1.2 to PHP 8.5.12 / Phalcon 5.23.0 with both stacks running side by side on dev, in the new milestone aga-Upgrade8.5. Six independent first steps: a Dockerfile in the repo for both images (env-image), the full PHPUnit suite in CI (ci-full-suite), removing Elasticsearch, removing env-based SMTP, api-tester response recording and comparison (response-diff), and a Throwable catch-all for Phalcon 5 exceptions (php8-errors). Then dropping phalcon/migrations in favour of the adapter's createTable() with schema snapshots (after drop-elasticsearch), migrate --dry-run (after that), the deprecation log with a lint script for the new image, and the PHP 8.4/8.5 deprecation fixes in two halves. dual-stack-boot adds the Phalcon 5 alias shim and composer ranges so the same code starts on both images. next-stack-ci adds a non-blocking job on the new image that posts one summary of what still differs, and bulk-next fixes the known empty POST /bulk response on the new stack. The switch-over and removing the shim are planned from that summary.", "issues": [{"key": "env-image", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Runtime image: Dockerfile in the repo for the current and the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5.23 stack", "description": "<p>Gaia, its CI and the test containers build on <code>rananoman/gaia:env-dev</code>, whose recipe isn't in any repo. For the PHP 8.5 upgrade, which runs both stacks side by side, we need both images built from one recipe in the Gaia repo.</p><ul><li><code>docker/env/Dockerfile</code> with build args <code>PHP_VERSION</code>, <code>PHALCON_VERSION</code> and the extension versions. It installs pdo_pgsql, imagick, zip, mbstring, curl, xml, xdebug, xhprof, composer and Apache with mod_rewrite, plus psr only for Phalcon 4.</li><li>Two targets, versions confirmed by a test run: <strong>current</strong> = PHP 7.4.21, Phalcon 4.1.2, Debian 10 (the same as env-dev today); <strong>next</strong> = PHP 8.5.12, Phalcon 5.23.0, xdebug 3.5.3, xhprof 2.3.10.</li><li><code>docker/env/build.sh</code> builds and tags <code>gaia-env:current</code> and <code>gaia-env:next</code>.</li><li><code>docker/env/README.md</code>: the versions, how to build, and that the reviewer publishes the tags. Note that <code>docker-images/gaia/Dockerfile</code> in the workspace is an obsolete MySQL-era recipe (<code>mileschou/phalcon:7.4</code>, PHPUnit 5.7) replaced by this one. Also start <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>, the upgrade notes page that later issues add to.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> both images build. Gaia on <code>gaia-env:current</code> gives the same PHPUnit and api-tester results as on env-dev. <code>php -v</code> and <code>php --ri phalcon</code> in next print 8.5.12 and 5.23.0.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> switching Dockerfiles, compose or CI to these images, pushing to a registry, and changing the docker-images repo.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ci-full-suite", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "CI: run the whole PHPUnit suite and modernise phpunit.xml", "description": "<p>CI runs only <code>tests/libraries/security</code>, <code>utils</code>, <code>libraries/tools</code> and <code>tests/tools</code>. <code>models/</code>, <code>foundation/</code>, <code>api/</code>, <code>libraries/workflows</code>, <code>query</code> and <code>authorization</code> never run in CI. Before the PHP 8.5 upgrade the whole suite has to be green on today's stack, so that a failure on the new stack means something.</p><ul><li><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code>: run the whole suite from <code>tests/phpunit.xml</code>, excluding <code>tests/tools/gaia-dev/fixtures</code>. Write a JUnit report and upload it as an artifact.</li><li>Move <code>tests/phpunit.xml</code> to the PHPUnit 9.6 schema: <code>whitelist</code> becomes <code>coverage</code>, and <code>syntaxCheck</code> and other removed attributes go.</li><li>Fix failures caused by the tests themselves. A failure that reveals a product bug: create an issue for it and put the test in a <code>quarantine</code> group, excluded in CI, with the issue number.</li><li>Add the image name to the vendor cache key (today it is <code>hashFiles('composer.json')</code> only).</li><li>Each test file must still pass when run alone.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> CI runs every test folder and is green on the current image. Quarantined tests are listed in the PR with their issue numbers.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> upgrading PHPUnit past 9.6, and fixing the product bugs found.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "drop-elasticsearch", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Remove the unused Elasticsearch indexing and its dependencies", "description": "<p>Gaia no longer uses Elasticsearch. <code>elasticsearch/elasticsearch ~6.0</code> and <code>monolog/monolog ~1.0</code> are used only by the legacy indexing in <code>core/tasks/AdminTask.php</code>, and both are old majors that block the PHP 8.5 upgrade.</p><ul><li>Remove the Elasticsearch/Monolog commands and code from <code>AdminTask</code>, and any config used only by them.</li><li>Remove both packages from <code>composer.json</code>.</li><li>Leave the <code>fts</code> flags in model metadata and <code>app/metadata/FTS.php</code> alone unless they reference removed code.</li><li>Update the gaia-dev graph and generated docs if they change.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>composer install</code> and CI are green, and no <code>Elasticsearch\\\\</code> or <code>Monolog\\\\</code> reference remains outside vendor.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "smtp-env-removal", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Email: drop the env-based SMTP config, Settings is the only source", "description": "<p>SMTP is now set up on the Settings page (<code>core/libs/utils/SmtpSettings.php</code> merges saved settings over the <code>smtp</code> config). The env-based config in <code>core/config/smtp.php</code> (<code>SMTP_*</code> env vars, defaulting to <code>smtp.gmail.com</code>) is no longer needed, and <code>docker-compose.yaml</code> commits a real Gmail username and app password for gaia-dev.</p><ul><li>Remove every <code>SMTP_*</code> variable from <code>docker-compose.yaml</code> (gaia, gaia-test, gaia-test-hermes-down).</li><li>Remove the env reads and the Gmail default from <code>core/config/smtp.php</code>. Keep only non-secret defaults such as port, encryption and auth if <code>SmtpSettings::resolve</code> still needs them, or remove the config and its fallback in <code>SmtpSettings</code>.</li><li>With no host saved in Settings, <code>Mailer</code> sends nothing and logs a warning. It must fail open and never fail the user's write. Today the test containers rely on <code>SMTP_HOST=127.0.0.1:9</code> to stay off real mail servers; after this change that comes from empty Settings. The api-tester mail suite still works by saving the mailpit host in Settings.</li><li>Update <code>tests/libraries/utils/SmtpSettingsTest.php</code>, <code>TestEmailSenderTest.php</code> and <code>tools/api-tester/README.md</code> (the SMTP paragraph).</li><li>The PR says that the password is still in git history and must be rotated by its owner, and that any deployed environment needs its SMTP saved in Settings before this deploys.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> no SMTP credentials or hosts in tracked files. With Settings empty, a notification-triggering write succeeds and no mail is attempted. With Settings filled in, mail is sent. CI is green.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "response-diff", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "api-tester: save response bodies and compare two runs", "description": "<p>The silent risk in the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5 upgrade is responses that still pass the api-tester checks but have changed. A test run already found one: <code>POST /bulk</code> returns an empty <code>200</code> on Phalcon 5. Prometheus reads these responses, so we need to compare the same catalog run on two stacks.</p><ul><li><code>tools/api-tester</code>: an opt-in flag <code>--record-bodies</code> that writes each case's status, content type and body (parsed JSON, or raw text when the body isn't JSON) into the report.</li><li><code>tools/api-tester/bin/compare-reports.php a.json b.json</code>: matches cases by id and reports differences in status, content type, empty vs non-empty body, keys, value types (for example <code>1</code> vs <code>\\\\u00221\\\\u0022</code>) and values. It ignores runtime ids/GUIDs, timestamps and tokens through a documented ignore list, prints a summary grouped per endpoint and per kind of difference, and exits non-zero when there are differences.</li><li>The comparison logic is its own class with unit tests; the bin script only parses arguments and prints.</li><li>Document both in the api-tester README.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two recorded runs of the same stack compare clean (no flaky differences). An empty body in one report and a changed value type are each reported.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> CI wiring (next-stack-ci).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "php8-errors", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Error handling: catch Throwable so Phalcon 5 exceptions still return JSON", "description": "<p>In Phalcon 5, its own exceptions (<code>Mvc\\\\Dispatcher\\\\Exception</code>, <code>Mvc\\\\Model\\\\Exception</code>, ...) no longer extend <code>Phalcon\\\\Exception</code>. A test run on PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5.23 showed that the <code>catch (\\\\Phalcon\\\\Exception)</code> in <code>public/index.php</code> then misses them: an unknown route returns HTTP 200 with a PHP fatal-error HTML page instead of a JSON 404, and a PHQL error does the same instead of a 500. The fix has to work on PHP 7.4 / Phalcon 4 too.</p><ul><li><code>public/index.php</code> and <code>cli.php</code>: a final <code>catch (\\\\Throwable)</code> that goes through the same JSON error path as today (<code>core/exceptions/PhalconError.php</code>), with the status the error deserves (404 for a dispatcher not-found, 500 otherwise).</li><li>Review the other files that catch <code>Phalcon\\\\Exception</code>: <code>RestController</code>, <code>SubRequestRunner</code>, <code>Model</code>, <code>Relationship</code>, <code>query/Clause</code>, <code>UploadController</code>, <code>PreviewController</code>, <code>ImageController</code>, <code>UserimageController</code>, <code>DownloadController</code>, <code>IndexController</code> and <code>ProjectActivitiesComponent</code>. Where the block is meant to catch an exception Phalcon throws, widen it so it also catches it on Phalcon 5. Leave blocks that only catch Gaia's own throws.</li><li>Extend <code>tests/libraries/utils/PhalconErrorTest.php</code>: an exception that doesn't extend <code>Phalcon\\\\Exception</code> produces the JSON error with the right status.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the current stack, an unknown route and a malformed query still return the same JSON errors as before, and CI is green. List each reviewed catch block and the decision in the PR.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "migrations", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migrations: create tables without phalcon/migrations, plus a schema snapshot script", "description": "<p><code>phalcon/migrations</code> (installed through <code>phalcon/devtools</code>) blocks PHP 8.5. 3.x only installs through 2021 <code>nette</code> versions never tested on 8.5, and v4 is a rewrite with a different API (no static connection). On Postgres, Gaia only uses its <code>morphTable</code> to create new tables; existing tables go through Gaia's own <code>syncExistingTable</code>.</p><ul><li><code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code>: create new tables with the DB adapter's <code>createTable()</code> (on both Phalcon 4 and 5) instead of extending <code>Phalcon\\\\Migrations\\\\Mvc\\\\Model\\\\Migration</code>, with the same columns, indexes and references as today. Check whether <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Mysql.php</code> relies on the package; if it does, move it to the adapter too, or say in the PR what MySQL loses.</li><li>Remove <code>phalcon/devtools</code> from <code>composer.json</code>.</li><li><code>tools/upgrade/schema-snapshot.sh &lt;db&gt;</code>: <code>pg_dump --schema-only</code> with owner and comment noise removed, so two snapshots can be diffed. Document it in <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>.</li><li>A PHPUnit test showing that creating a table produces the expected definition (fake adapter).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> starting from the baseline dump plus an empty database, the schema snapshot after <code>migration migrate</code> is identical before and after this change. CI is green.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a dry-run mode (migrate-dry-run).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["drop-elasticsearch"], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "migrate-dry-run", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migrations: --dry-run that prints the planned DDL without running it", "description": "<p><code>docker/dev/start.sh</code> runs <code>php cli.php migration migrate</code> every time Gaia starts, and <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> <code>syncExistingTable</code> drops columns that aren't in the metadata. Before switching stacks, and for any risky metadata change, we want to see what migrate would do before it does it.</p><ul><li><code>php cli.php migration migrate --dry-run</code> (<code>core/tasks/MigrationTask.php</code>) prints every CREATE, ALTER, DROP, index and function statement that <code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> and the Postgres driver (<code>syncExistingTable</code>, <code>syncIndexes</code>, <code>syncMultiColumnIndex</code>, <code>migrateFunctions</code>) would run, one per line with its table, and runs none.</li><li>Exit code 0 when nothing is planned, a separate non-zero code when changes are planned, and the usual failure code on errors.</li><li>The switch between running and collecting statements lives in the migration layer, not in the task.</li><li>A PHPUnit test with a fake adapter: planned statements are collected and nothing is executed.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a freshly migrated local database, <code>--dry-run</code> plans nothing. After removing a field from a model's metadata, it lists the DROP without running it. CI is green.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing what migrate does, and changing <code>start.sh</code>.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["migrations"], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "deprecation-log", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Collect PHP deprecations and warnings into a grouped report, plus a lint run on the new image", "description": "<p>PHP 8.x reports many upgrade problems only as E_DEPRECATED or E_WARNING. A test run showed that over HTTP none reach the PHP log, because Gaia's error handling hides them. For the PHP 8.5 upgrade they need to be collected and grouped.</p><ul><li><code>docker/php/conf.d/diagnostics.ini</code>, mounted only on the gaia-test services in <code>docker-compose.yaml</code>: <code>error_reporting=E_ALL</code>, <code>log_errors=On</code>, <code>display_errors=Off</code>, log to <code>logs/php-diagnostics.log</code>. Make sure Gaia's own error handler passes deprecations and warnings on to that log instead of hiding them.</li><li>PHPUnit runs write deprecations and warnings to the same kind of log without failing tests, configured through <code>tests/phpunit.xml</code>.</li><li><code>tools/upgrade/lint-next.sh</code>: runs <code>php -l</code> with <code>error_reporting=E_ALL</code> on every PHP file (outside vendor and the gaia-dev fixtures) inside <code>gaia-env:next</code>, and writes the results to a log in the same format.</li><li><code>tools/upgrade/deprecations-report.php &lt;log&gt;...</code>: groups entries by message pattern and <code>file:line</code>, separates Gaia code from vendor, counts them, and prints markdown suitable for a CI job summary. Unit-test the grouping.</li><li>Add the commands to <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a PHPUnit plus api-tester run against gaia-test produces a log, and the lint run on next lists the known implicitly nullable parameters and the <code>private final</code> warnings. The report groups both.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing them, and CI wiring.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ci-full-suite", "smtp-env-removal", "env-image"], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "php8-deprecations-core", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "PHP 8.4/8.5 deprecations in core/ (code that still runs on PHP 7.4)", "description": "<p>A <code>php -l</code> run on PHP 8.5 found deprecations that can be fixed now in a form PHP 7.4 accepts. This issue fixes the ones under <code>core/</code>.</p><ul><li>Implicitly nullable parameters (<code>Type $x = null</code>) become <code>?Type $x = null</code>.</li><li>The <code>private final</code> methods (mostly <code>core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php</code>) lose <code>final</code>.</li><li><code>#[\\\\AllowDynamicProperties]</code> on the base model <code>core/mvc/models/Model.php</code> (models keep their columns as dynamic properties; the attribute is inherited and is a comment on 7.4).</li><li>Declare the dynamic properties found elsewhere, such as <code>core/mvc/db/factory/DialectFactory.php</code> <code>$dialect</code>.</li><li><code>#[\\\\ReturnTypeWillChange]</code> on the Iterator methods of <code>core/mvc/models/ResultStream.php</code>.</li><li>Find the files with <code>php -d error_reporting=E_ALL -l</code> in <code>gaia-env:next</code>. If more than 15 files under <code>core/</code> need changes, fix 15 and list the rest in the PR for a follow-up.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> those files lint clean on 8.5 and still lint on 7.4, and CI is green on the current stack.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> files outside <code>core/</code>, and Phalcon class renames (the shim covers them).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["env-image", "php8-errors"], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 15, "sizeReason": "Mechanical one-line signature changes spread across files; the issue caps itself at 15 files and lists the rest for a follow-up.", "screens": []}, {"key": "php8-deprecations-app", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "PHP 8.4/8.5 deprecations outside core/ (code that still runs on PHP 7.4)", "description": "<p>The same kind of fixes as for <code>core/</code>, for <code>app/</code>, <code>tools/</code>, <code>tests/</code> (excluding <code>tests/tools/gaia-dev/fixtures</code>), <code>public/</code> and <code>cli.php</code>. All of them must still run on PHP 7.4.</p><ul><li>Implicitly nullable parameters become <code>?Type $x = null</code>.</li><li>Remove <code>final</code> from <code>private</code> methods.</li><li>Declare dynamic properties on non-model classes.</li><li><code>#[\\\\ReturnTypeWillChange]</code> where internal interfaces (Iterator, ArrayAccess, Countable, JsonSerializable) are implemented without return types.</li><li>Find the files with <code>php -d error_reporting=E_ALL -l</code> in <code>gaia-env:next</code>. If more than 15 files need changes, fix 15 and list the rest in the PR for a follow-up.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> those files lint clean on 8.5 and still lint on 7.4, and CI is green on the current stack.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> <code>core/</code> and the Phalcon class renames.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["env-image", "php8-errors"], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 15, "sizeReason": "Mechanical one-line signature changes spread across files; the issue caps itself at 15 files and lists the rest for a follow-up.", "screens": []}, {"key": "dual-stack-boot", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Boot Gaia on both Phalcon 4.1 / PHP 7.4 and Phalcon 5.23 / PHP 8.5 with an alias shim", "description": "<p>For the side-by-side upgrade, the same code on <code>dev</code> must start on both <code>gaia-env:current</code> and <code>gaia-env:next</code> until the switch-over. Gaia uses Phalcon 4 class names that Phalcon 5 removed, in many files: <code>Phalcon\\\\Di</code> (49), <code>Phalcon\\\\Exception</code> (16), <code>Phalcon\\\\Config</code> (10), <code>Phalcon\\\\Text</code> (8), <code>Phalcon\\\\Logger</code> (5), <code>Phalcon\\\\Loader</code> (3). A test run showed that one shim file handles them without editing those files.</p><ul><li><code>core/libs/compat/phalcon5.php</code>, required at the top of <code>autoload.php</code> (and <code>tests/autoload.php</code> if it doesn't go through it). It does nothing on Phalcon 4. On Phalcon 5 it defines the old names: <code>class_alias</code> for <code>Di</code>, <code>DiInterface</code>, <code>Config</code>, <code>Logger</code> and <code>Exception</code>, plus small subclasses where the API changed (<code>Loader</code>: <code>registerNamespaces</code> calls <code>setNamespaces</code>; <code>Text</code>: the methods Gaia uses, built on <code>Phalcon\\\\Support\\\\Helper\\\\Str</code>).</li><li>Delete <code>tests/UnitTestCase.php</code> and its require in <code>tests/TestHelper.php</code>. Nothing extends it, and it doesn't compile on PHP 8.</li><li><code>composer.json</code>: <code>php</code> becomes <code>~7.4.0 || ~8.5.0</code>. Drop <code>ext-psr</code> and the six unused <code>phalcon/incubator*</code> packages, and move <code>bshaffer/oauth2-server-php</code> to a 1.x that supports PHP 8.5. There's no lock file, so each image resolves its own versions; check that nothing falls back to outdated releases on 8.5.</li><li>A PHPUnit test for the shim that passes on both stacks.</li><li>Add the shim and its removal at switch-over to <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the current image, CI is green as before. On <code>gaia-env:next</code>, <code>composer install</code> succeeds, the API serves a token request and a list read, <code>migration migrate</code> runs, and PHPUnit runs to completion (failures allowed). List the remaining failures in the PR.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing everything that fails on next, replacing the old class names in code, and making next the default.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["env-image", "ci-full-suite", "migrations"], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "next-stack-ci", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "CI: non-blocking PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5.23 job that reports what fails", "description": "<p>Shows on every PR what still fails on the new stack, compared with the current one, so the upgrade work is visible and shrinks PR by PR. The current-stack job stays the only blocking check.</p><ul><li>A <code>next-stack</code> job in <code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code> on the published <code>gaia-env:next</code>, with <code>continue-on-error: true</code> and its own vendor cache key. It loads the baseline dump, runs <code>migration migrate --dry-run</code> then <code>migrate</code>, and takes a schema snapshot (<code>tools/upgrade/schema-snapshot.sh</code>). Then it prepares <code>pr4m_test</code>, runs the full PHPUnit suite (JUnit), runs the api-tester backend and acl modes with <code>--record-bodies</code>, runs <code>tools/upgrade/lint-next.sh</code>, and keeps the PHP diagnostics log.</li><li>The current-stack job also uploads a schema snapshot and an api-tester report with bodies.</li><li>A compare step diffs the two schema snapshots and the two api-tester reports (<code>compare-reports.php</code>), runs <code>deprecations-report.php</code>, and writes one markdown summary to <code>$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY</code>: PHPUnit failures, dry-run statements, schema differences, api-tester failures, response differences and deprecations, each with a count and its artifact.</li><li>Add how to reproduce the summary locally to <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a PR shows the summary, a failure in the next job doesn't block the PR, and the known <code>POST /bulk</code> empty response shows up as a response difference.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing what it reports, and making the job blocking.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["dual-stack-boot", "deprecation-log", "response-diff", "migrate-dry-run", "ci-full-suite"], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "bulk-next", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "POST /bulk returns an empty 200 on Phalcon 5", "description": "<p>On PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5.23, <code>POST /bulk</code> returns <code>200</code> with <code>Content-Length: 0</code> and logs nothing, while the current stack returns the sub-responses. The likely cause is the nested <code>Application::handle()</code> in <code>core/mvc/http/SubRequestRunner.php</code>: Phalcon 5 handles responses, the dispatcher and DI services differently in a nested handle.</p><ul><li>Start with a failing test (PHPUnit or an api-tester case run against <code>gaia-env:next</code>) that shows the empty body.</li><li>Fix <code>SubRequestRunner</code> so sub-requests return their responses on both stacks, without a Phalcon version check in the class if possible.</li><li>A sub-request that throws is reported in the bulk response as it is today.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the bulk api-tester cases pass on both stacks with identical responses (<code>compare-reports.php</code> shows no difference for <code>/bulk</code>).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["dual-stack-boot"], "milestone": "aga-Upgrade8.5", "newMilestone": true, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 11:01:47	2026-11-18 11:01:47	f
fdad78e56afd-cdc7-49c2-2c6f2a925171	d98352c16af4-9ee0-e9a2-4dddf1b444ee	2	{"summary": "Moves Gaia from PHP 7.4.21 / Phalcon 4.1.2 to PHP 8.5.12 / Phalcon 5.23.0 with both stacks running side by side on dev. Six independent first steps: a Dockerfile in the repo for both images (env-image), the full PHPUnit suite in CI (ci-full-suite), removing Elasticsearch, removing env-based SMTP, api-tester response recording and comparison (response-diff), and a Throwable catch-all for Phalcon 5 exceptions (php8-errors). Then migrations without phalcon/migrations plus --dry-run and schema snapshots (after drop-elasticsearch), the deprecation log with a lint script for the new image, and the PHP 8.4/8.5 deprecation fixes in two halves. dual-stack-boot adds the Phalcon 5 alias shim and composer ranges so the same code starts on both images. next-stack-ci adds a non-blocking job on the new image that posts one summary of what still differs, and bulk-next fixes the known empty POST /bulk response on the new stack. The switch-over and removing the shim are planned from that summary.", "issues": [{"key": "env-image", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Runtime image: Dockerfile in the repo for the current and the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5.23 stack", "description": "<p>Gaia, its CI and the test containers build on <code>rananoman/gaia:env-dev</code>, whose recipe isn't in any repo. For the PHP 8.5 upgrade, which runs both stacks side by side, we need both images built from one recipe in the Gaia repo.</p><ul><li><code>docker/env/Dockerfile</code> with build args <code>PHP_VERSION</code>, <code>PHALCON_VERSION</code> and the extension versions. It installs pdo_pgsql, imagick, zip, mbstring, curl, xml, xdebug, xhprof, composer and Apache with mod_rewrite, plus psr only for Phalcon 4.</li><li>Two targets, versions confirmed by a test run: <strong>current</strong> = PHP 7.4.21, Phalcon 4.1.2, Debian 10 (the same as env-dev today); <strong>next</strong> = PHP 8.5.12, Phalcon 5.23.0, xdebug 3.5.3, xhprof 2.3.10.</li><li><code>docker/env/build.sh</code> builds and tags <code>gaia-env:current</code> and <code>gaia-env:next</code>.</li><li><code>docker/env/README.md</code>: the versions, how to build, and that the reviewer publishes the tags. Also start <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>, the upgrade notes page that later issues add to.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> both images build. Gaia on <code>gaia-env:current</code> gives the same PHPUnit and api-tester results as on env-dev. <code>php -v</code> and <code>php --ri phalcon</code> in next print 8.5.12 and 5.23.0.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> switching Dockerfiles, compose or CI to these images, and pushing to a registry.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ci-full-suite", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "CI: run the whole PHPUnit suite and modernise phpunit.xml", "description": "<p>CI runs only <code>tests/libraries/security</code>, <code>utils</code>, <code>libraries/tools</code> and <code>tests/tools</code>. <code>models/</code>, <code>foundation/</code>, <code>api/</code>, <code>libraries/workflows</code>, <code>query</code> and <code>authorization</code> never run in CI. Before the PHP 8.5 upgrade the whole suite has to be green on today's stack, so that a failure on the new stack means something.</p><ul><li><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code>: run the whole suite from <code>tests/phpunit.xml</code>, excluding <code>tests/tools/gaia-dev/fixtures</code>. Write a JUnit report and upload it as an artifact.</li><li>Move <code>tests/phpunit.xml</code> to the PHPUnit 9.6 schema: <code>whitelist</code> becomes <code>coverage</code>, and <code>syntaxCheck</code> and other removed attributes go.</li><li>Fix failures caused by the tests themselves. A failure that reveals a product bug: create an issue for it and put the test in a <code>quarantine</code> group, excluded in CI, with the issue number.</li><li>Add the image name to the vendor cache key (today it is <code>hashFiles('composer.json')</code> only).</li><li>Each test file must still pass when run alone.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> CI runs every test folder and is green on the current image. Quarantined tests are listed in the PR with their issue numbers.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> upgrading PHPUnit past 9.6, and fixing the product bugs found.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "drop-elasticsearch", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Remove the unused Elasticsearch indexing and its dependencies", "description": "<p>Gaia no longer uses Elasticsearch. <code>elasticsearch/elasticsearch ~6.0</code> and <code>monolog/monolog ~1.0</code> are used only by the legacy indexing in <code>core/tasks/AdminTask.php</code>, and both are old majors that block the PHP 8.5 upgrade.</p><ul><li>Remove the Elasticsearch/Monolog commands and code from <code>AdminTask</code>, and any config used only by them.</li><li>Remove both packages from <code>composer.json</code>.</li><li>Leave the <code>fts</code> flags in model metadata and <code>app/metadata/FTS.php</code> alone unless they reference removed code.</li><li>Update the gaia-dev graph and generated docs if they change.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>composer install</code> and CI are green, and no <code>Elasticsearch\\\\</code> or <code>Monolog\\\\</code> reference remains outside vendor.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "smtp-env-removal", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Email: drop the env-based SMTP config, Settings is the only source", "description": "<p>SMTP is now set up on the Settings page (<code>core/libs/utils/SmtpSettings.php</code> merges saved settings over the <code>smtp</code> config). The env-based config in <code>core/config/smtp.php</code> (<code>SMTP_*</code> env vars, defaulting to <code>smtp.gmail.com</code>) is no longer needed, and <code>docker-compose.yaml</code> commits a real Gmail username and app password for gaia-dev.</p><ul><li>Remove every <code>SMTP_*</code> variable from <code>docker-compose.yaml</code> (gaia, gaia-test, gaia-test-hermes-down).</li><li>Remove the env reads and the Gmail default from <code>core/config/smtp.php</code>. Keep only non-secret defaults such as port, encryption and auth if <code>SmtpSettings::resolve</code> still needs them, or remove the config and its fallback in <code>SmtpSettings</code>.</li><li>With no host saved in Settings, <code>Mailer</code> sends nothing and logs a warning. It must fail open and never fail the user's write. Today the test containers rely on <code>SMTP_HOST=127.0.0.1:9</code> to stay off real mail servers; after this change that comes from empty Settings. The api-tester mail suite still works by saving the mailpit host in Settings.</li><li>Update <code>tests/libraries/utils/SmtpSettingsTest.php</code>, <code>TestEmailSenderTest.php</code> and <code>tools/api-tester/README.md</code> (the SMTP paragraph).</li><li>The PR says that the password is still in git history and must be rotated by its owner, and that any deployed environment needs its SMTP saved in Settings before this deploys.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> no SMTP credentials or hosts in tracked files. With Settings empty, a notification-triggering write succeeds and no mail is attempted. With Settings filled in, mail is sent. CI is green.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "response-diff", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "api-tester: save response bodies and compare two runs", "description": "<p>The silent risk in the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5 upgrade is responses that still pass the api-tester checks but have changed. A test run already found one: <code>POST /bulk</code> returns an empty <code>200</code> on Phalcon 5. Prometheus reads these responses, so we need to compare the same catalog run on two stacks.</p><ul><li><code>tools/api-tester</code>: an opt-in flag <code>--record-bodies</code> that writes each case's status, content type and body (parsed JSON, or raw text when the body isn't JSON) into the report.</li><li><code>tools/api-tester/bin/compare-reports.php a.json b.json</code>: matches cases by id and reports differences in status, content type, empty vs non-empty body, keys, value types (for example <code>1</code> vs <code>\\\\u00221\\\\u0022</code>) and values. It ignores runtime ids/GUIDs, timestamps and tokens through a documented ignore list, prints a summary grouped per endpoint and per kind of difference, and exits non-zero when there are differences.</li><li>The comparison logic is its own class with unit tests; the bin script only parses arguments and prints.</li><li>Document both in the api-tester README.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two recorded runs of the same stack compare clean (no flaky differences). An empty body in one report and a changed value type are each reported.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> CI wiring (next-stack-ci).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "php8-errors", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Error handling: catch Throwable so Phalcon 5 exceptions still return JSON", "description": "<p>In Phalcon 5, its own exceptions (<code>Mvc\\\\Dispatcher\\\\Exception</code>, <code>Mvc\\\\Model\\\\Exception</code>, ...) no longer extend <code>Phalcon\\\\Exception</code>. A test run on PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5.23 showed that the <code>catch (\\\\Phalcon\\\\Exception)</code> in <code>public/index.php</code> then misses them: an unknown route returns HTTP 200 with a PHP fatal-error HTML page instead of a JSON 404, and a PHQL error does the same instead of a 500. The fix has to work on PHP 7.4 / Phalcon 4 too.</p><ul><li><code>public/index.php</code> and <code>cli.php</code>: a final <code>catch (\\\\Throwable)</code> that goes through the same JSON error path as today (<code>core/exceptions/PhalconError.php</code>), with the status the error deserves (404 for a dispatcher not-found, 500 otherwise).</li><li>Review the other files that catch <code>Phalcon\\\\Exception</code>: <code>RestController</code>, <code>SubRequestRunner</code>, <code>Model</code>, <code>Relationship</code>, <code>query/Clause</code>, <code>UploadController</code>, <code>PreviewController</code>, <code>ImageController</code>, <code>UserimageController</code>, <code>DownloadController</code>, <code>IndexController</code> and <code>ProjectActivitiesComponent</code>. Where the block is meant to catch an exception Phalcon throws, widen it so it also catches it on Phalcon 5. Leave blocks that only catch Gaia's own throws.</li><li>Extend <code>tests/libraries/utils/PhalconErrorTest.php</code>: an exception that doesn't extend <code>Phalcon\\\\Exception</code> produces the JSON error with the right status.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the current stack, an unknown route and a malformed query still return the same JSON errors as before, and CI is green. List each reviewed catch block and the decision in the PR.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "migrations", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migrations: create tables without phalcon/migrations, add --dry-run and schema snapshots", "description": "<p><code>phalcon/migrations</code> (installed through <code>phalcon/devtools</code>) blocks PHP 8.5. 3.x caps PHP below 8.3/8.4, and on 8.5 composer only installs it by falling back to 2021 dependencies. v4 is a rewrite that removes the static connection Gaia uses. On Postgres, Gaia only uses its <code>morphTable</code> to create new tables (existing tables go through Gaia's own <code>syncExistingTable</code>). Also, <code>docker/dev/start.sh</code> runs migrate every time Gaia starts and it drops columns that aren't in the metadata, so we need to see the planned changes before they run.</p><ul><li><code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code>: create new tables with the DB adapter's <code>createTable()</code> (on both Phalcon 4 and 5) instead of extending <code>Phalcon\\\\Migrations\\\\Mvc\\\\Model\\\\Migration</code>, with the same columns, indexes and references as today. Check whether <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Mysql.php</code> relies on the package; if it does, move it to the adapter too, or say in the PR what MySQL loses.</li><li>Remove <code>phalcon/devtools</code> from <code>composer.json</code>.</li><li><code>php cli.php migration migrate --dry-run</code> (<code>core/tasks/MigrationTask.php</code>) prints every CREATE, ALTER, DROP, index and function statement it would run, one per line with its table, and runs none. Exit code 0 when nothing is planned, a separate non-zero code when changes are planned. The switch between running and collecting statements lives in the migration layer, not in the task.</li><li><code>tools/upgrade/schema-snapshot.sh &lt;db&gt;</code>: <code>pg_dump --schema-only</code> with owner and comment noise removed, so two snapshots can be diffed.</li><li>PHPUnit tests: creating a table produces the expected definition, and a dry run collects statements without executing them (fake adapter).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> starting from the baseline dump, the schema snapshot after <code>migrate</code> is identical before and after this change. On a migrated database, <code>--dry-run</code> plans nothing. Removing a field from a model's metadata makes it list the DROP without running it. CI is green.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["drop-elasticsearch"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "deprecation-log", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Collect PHP deprecations and warnings into a grouped report, plus a lint run on the new image", "description": "<p>PHP 8.x reports many upgrade problems only as E_DEPRECATED or E_WARNING. A test run showed that over HTTP none reach the PHP log, because Gaia's error handling hides them. For the PHP 8.5 upgrade they need to be collected and grouped.</p><ul><li><code>docker/php/conf.d/diagnostics.ini</code>, mounted only on the gaia-test services in <code>docker-compose.yaml</code>: <code>error_reporting=E_ALL</code>, <code>log_errors=On</code>, <code>display_errors=Off</code>, log to <code>logs/php-diagnostics.log</code>. Make sure Gaia's own error handler passes deprecations and warnings on to that log instead of hiding them.</li><li>PHPUnit runs write deprecations and warnings to the same kind of log without failing tests, configured through <code>tests/phpunit.xml</code>.</li><li><code>tools/upgrade/lint-next.sh</code>: runs <code>php -l</code> with <code>error_reporting=E_ALL</code> on every PHP file (outside vendor and the gaia-dev fixtures) inside <code>gaia-env:next</code>, and writes the results to a log in the same format.</li><li><code>tools/upgrade/deprecations-report.php &lt;log&gt;...</code>: groups entries by message pattern and <code>file:line</code>, separates Gaia code from vendor, counts them, and prints markdown suitable for a CI job summary. Unit-test the grouping.</li><li>Add the commands to <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a PHPUnit plus api-tester run against gaia-test produces a log, and the lint run on next lists the known implicitly nullable parameters and the <code>private final</code> warnings. The report groups both.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing them, and CI wiring.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ci-full-suite", "smtp-env-removal", "env-image"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "php8-deprecations-core", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "PHP 8.4/8.5 deprecations in core/ (code that still runs on PHP 7.4)", "description": "<p>A <code>php -l</code> run on PHP 8.5 found deprecations that can be fixed now in a form PHP 7.4 accepts. This issue fixes the ones under <code>core/</code>.</p><ul><li>Implicitly nullable parameters (<code>Type $x = null</code>) become <code>?Type $x = null</code>.</li><li>The <code>private final</code> methods (mostly <code>core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php</code>) lose <code>final</code>.</li><li><code>#[\\\\AllowDynamicProperties]</code> on the base model <code>core/mvc/models/Model.php</code> (models keep their columns as dynamic properties; the attribute is inherited and is a comment on 7.4).</li><li>Declare the dynamic properties found elsewhere, such as <code>core/mvc/db/factory/DialectFactory.php</code> <code>$dialect</code>.</li><li><code>#[\\\\ReturnTypeWillChange]</code> on the Iterator methods of <code>core/mvc/models/ResultStream.php</code>.</li><li>Find the files with <code>php -d error_reporting=E_ALL -l</code> in <code>gaia-env:next</code>. If more than 15 files under <code>core/</code> need changes, fix 15 and list the rest in the PR for a follow-up.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> those files lint clean on 8.5 and still lint on 7.4, and CI is green on the current stack.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> files outside <code>core/</code>, and Phalcon class renames (the shim covers them).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["env-image", "php8-errors"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 15, "sizeReason": "Mechanical one-line signature changes spread across files; the issue caps itself at 15 files and lists the rest for a follow-up.", "screens": []}, {"key": "php8-deprecations-app", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "PHP 8.4/8.5 deprecations outside core/ (code that still runs on PHP 7.4)", "description": "<p>The same kind of fixes as for <code>core/</code>, for <code>app/</code>, <code>tools/</code>, <code>tests/</code> (excluding <code>tests/tools/gaia-dev/fixtures</code>), <code>public/</code> and <code>cli.php</code>. All of them must still run on PHP 7.4.</p><ul><li>Implicitly nullable parameters become <code>?Type $x = null</code>.</li><li>Remove <code>final</code> from <code>private</code> methods.</li><li>Declare dynamic properties on non-model classes.</li><li><code>#[\\\\ReturnTypeWillChange]</code> where internal interfaces (Iterator, ArrayAccess, Countable, JsonSerializable) are implemented without return types.</li><li>Find the files with <code>php -d error_reporting=E_ALL -l</code> in <code>gaia-env:next</code>. If more than 15 files need changes, fix 15 and list the rest in the PR for a follow-up.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> those files lint clean on 8.5 and still lint on 7.4, and CI is green on the current stack.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> <code>core/</code> and the Phalcon class renames.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["env-image", "php8-errors"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 15, "sizeReason": "Mechanical one-line signature changes spread across files; the issue caps itself at 15 files and lists the rest for a follow-up.", "screens": []}, {"key": "dual-stack-boot", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Boot Gaia on both Phalcon 4.1 / PHP 7.4 and Phalcon 5.23 / PHP 8.5 with an alias shim", "description": "<p>For the side-by-side upgrade, the same code on <code>dev</code> must start on both <code>gaia-env:current</code> and <code>gaia-env:next</code> until the switch-over. Gaia uses Phalcon 4 class names that Phalcon 5 removed, in many files: <code>Phalcon\\\\Di</code> (49), <code>Phalcon\\\\Exception</code> (16), <code>Phalcon\\\\Config</code> (10), <code>Phalcon\\\\Text</code> (8), <code>Phalcon\\\\Logger</code> (5), <code>Phalcon\\\\Loader</code> (3). A test run showed that one shim file handles them without editing those files.</p><ul><li><code>core/libs/compat/phalcon5.php</code>, required at the top of <code>autoload.php</code> (and <code>tests/autoload.php</code> if it doesn't go through it). It does nothing on Phalcon 4. On Phalcon 5 it defines the old names: <code>class_alias</code> for <code>Di</code>, <code>DiInterface</code>, <code>Config</code>, <code>Logger</code> and <code>Exception</code>, plus small subclasses where the API changed (<code>Loader</code>: <code>registerNamespaces</code> calls <code>setNamespaces</code>; <code>Text</code>: the methods Gaia uses, built on <code>Phalcon\\\\Support\\\\Helper\\\\Str</code>).</li><li>Delete <code>tests/UnitTestCase.php</code> and its require in <code>tests/TestHelper.php</code>. Nothing extends it, and it doesn't compile on PHP 8.</li><li><code>composer.json</code>: <code>php</code> becomes <code>~7.4.0 || ~8.5.0</code>. Drop <code>ext-psr</code> and the six unused <code>phalcon/incubator*</code> packages, and move <code>bshaffer/oauth2-server-php</code> to a 1.x that supports PHP 8.5. There's no lock file, so each image resolves its own versions; check that nothing falls back to outdated releases on 8.5.</li><li>A PHPUnit test for the shim that passes on both stacks.</li><li>Add the shim and its removal at switch-over to <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the current image, CI is green as before. On <code>gaia-env:next</code>, <code>composer install</code> succeeds, the API serves a token request and a list read, <code>migration migrate --dry-run</code> runs, and PHPUnit runs to completion (failures allowed). List the remaining failures in the PR.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing everything that fails on next, replacing the old class names in code, and making next the default.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["env-image", "ci-full-suite", "migrations"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "next-stack-ci", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "CI: non-blocking PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5.23 job that reports what fails", "description": "<p>Shows on every PR what still fails on the new stack, compared with the current one, so the upgrade work is visible and shrinks PR by PR. The current-stack job stays the only blocking check.</p><ul><li>A <code>next-stack</code> job in <code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code> on the published <code>gaia-env:next</code>, with <code>continue-on-error: true</code> and its own vendor cache key. It loads the baseline dump, runs <code>migration migrate --dry-run</code> then <code>migrate</code>, and takes a schema snapshot. Then it prepares <code>pr4m_test</code>, runs the full PHPUnit suite (JUnit), runs the api-tester backend and acl modes with <code>--record-bodies</code>, runs <code>tools/upgrade/lint-next.sh</code>, and keeps the PHP diagnostics log.</li><li>The current-stack job also uploads a schema snapshot and an api-tester report with bodies.</li><li>A compare step diffs the two schema snapshots and the two api-tester reports (<code>compare-reports.php</code>), runs <code>deprecations-report.php</code>, and writes one markdown summary to <code>$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY</code>: PHPUnit failures, dry-run statements, schema differences, api-tester failures, response differences and deprecations, each with a count and its artifact.</li><li>Add how to reproduce the summary locally to <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a PR shows the summary, a failure in the next job doesn't block the PR, and the known <code>POST /bulk</code> empty response shows up as a response difference.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing what it reports, and making the job blocking.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["dual-stack-boot", "deprecation-log", "response-diff", "ci-full-suite"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "bulk-next", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "POST /bulk returns an empty 200 on Phalcon 5", "description": "<p>On PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5.23, <code>POST /bulk</code> returns <code>200</code> with <code>Content-Length: 0</code> and logs nothing, while the current stack returns the sub-responses. The likely cause is the nested <code>Application::handle()</code> in <code>core/mvc/http/SubRequestRunner.php</code>: Phalcon 5 handles responses, the dispatcher and DI services differently in a nested handle.</p><ul><li>Start with a failing test (PHPUnit or an api-tester case run against <code>gaia-env:next</code>) that shows the empty body.</li><li>Fix <code>SubRequestRunner</code> so sub-requests return their responses on both stacks, without a Phalcon version check in the class if possible.</li><li>A sub-request that throws is reported in the bulk response as it is today.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the bulk api-tester cases pass on both stacks with identical responses (<code>compare-reports.php</code> shows no difference for <code>/bulk</code>).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["dual-stack-boot"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-18 10:20:45	2026-11-18 10:38:03	t
5a8339b36afd-200a-42c4-6b37dad283b2	d98352c16af4-9ee0-e9a2-4dddf1b444ee	3	{"summary": "Moves Gaia from PHP 7.4.21 / Phalcon 4.1.2 to PHP 8.5.12 / Phalcon 5.23.0 with both stacks running side by side on dev. Six independent first steps: a Dockerfile in the repo for both images (env-image), the full PHPUnit suite in CI (ci-full-suite), removing Elasticsearch, removing env-based SMTP, api-tester response recording and comparison (response-diff), and a Throwable catch-all for Phalcon 5 exceptions (php8-errors). Then dropping phalcon/migrations in favour of the adapter's createTable() with schema snapshots (after drop-elasticsearch), migrate --dry-run (after that), the deprecation log with a lint script for the new image, and the PHP 8.4/8.5 deprecation fixes in two halves. dual-stack-boot adds the Phalcon 5 alias shim and composer ranges so the same code starts on both images. next-stack-ci adds a non-blocking job on the new image that posts one summary of what still differs, and bulk-next fixes the known empty POST /bulk response on the new stack. The switch-over and removing the shim are planned from that summary.", "issues": [{"key": "env-image", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Runtime image: Dockerfile in the repo for the current and the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5.23 stack", "description": "<p>Gaia, its CI and the test containers build on <code>rananoman/gaia:env-dev</code>, whose recipe isn't in any repo. For the PHP 8.5 upgrade, which runs both stacks side by side, we need both images built from one recipe in the Gaia repo.</p><ul><li><code>docker/env/Dockerfile</code> with build args <code>PHP_VERSION</code>, <code>PHALCON_VERSION</code> and the extension versions. It installs pdo_pgsql, imagick, zip, mbstring, curl, xml, xdebug, xhprof, composer and Apache with mod_rewrite, plus psr only for Phalcon 4.</li><li>Two targets, versions confirmed by a test run: <strong>current</strong> = PHP 7.4.21, Phalcon 4.1.2, Debian 10 (the same as env-dev today); <strong>next</strong> = PHP 8.5.12, Phalcon 5.23.0, xdebug 3.5.3, xhprof 2.3.10.</li><li><code>docker/env/build.sh</code> builds and tags <code>gaia-env:current</code> and <code>gaia-env:next</code>.</li><li><code>docker/env/README.md</code>: the versions, how to build, and that the reviewer publishes the tags. Note that <code>docker-images/gaia/Dockerfile</code> in the workspace is an obsolete MySQL-era recipe (<code>mileschou/phalcon:7.4</code>, PHPUnit 5.7) replaced by this one. Also start <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>, the upgrade notes page that later issues add to.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> both images build. Gaia on <code>gaia-env:current</code> gives the same PHPUnit and api-tester results as on env-dev. <code>php -v</code> and <code>php --ri phalcon</code> in next print 8.5.12 and 5.23.0.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> switching Dockerfiles, compose or CI to these images, pushing to a registry, and changing the docker-images repo.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "ci-full-suite", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "CI: run the whole PHPUnit suite and modernise phpunit.xml", "description": "<p>CI runs only <code>tests/libraries/security</code>, <code>utils</code>, <code>libraries/tools</code> and <code>tests/tools</code>. <code>models/</code>, <code>foundation/</code>, <code>api/</code>, <code>libraries/workflows</code>, <code>query</code> and <code>authorization</code> never run in CI. Before the PHP 8.5 upgrade the whole suite has to be green on today's stack, so that a failure on the new stack means something.</p><ul><li><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code>: run the whole suite from <code>tests/phpunit.xml</code>, excluding <code>tests/tools/gaia-dev/fixtures</code>. Write a JUnit report and upload it as an artifact.</li><li>Move <code>tests/phpunit.xml</code> to the PHPUnit 9.6 schema: <code>whitelist</code> becomes <code>coverage</code>, and <code>syntaxCheck</code> and other removed attributes go.</li><li>Fix failures caused by the tests themselves. A failure that reveals a product bug: create an issue for it and put the test in a <code>quarantine</code> group, excluded in CI, with the issue number.</li><li>Add the image name to the vendor cache key (today it is <code>hashFiles('composer.json')</code> only).</li><li>Each test file must still pass when run alone.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> CI runs every test folder and is green on the current image. Quarantined tests are listed in the PR with their issue numbers.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> upgrading PHPUnit past 9.6, and fixing the product bugs found.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "drop-elasticsearch", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Remove the unused Elasticsearch indexing and its dependencies", "description": "<p>Gaia no longer uses Elasticsearch. <code>elasticsearch/elasticsearch ~6.0</code> and <code>monolog/monolog ~1.0</code> are used only by the legacy indexing in <code>core/tasks/AdminTask.php</code>, and both are old majors that block the PHP 8.5 upgrade.</p><ul><li>Remove the Elasticsearch/Monolog commands and code from <code>AdminTask</code>, and any config used only by them.</li><li>Remove both packages from <code>composer.json</code>.</li><li>Leave the <code>fts</code> flags in model metadata and <code>app/metadata/FTS.php</code> alone unless they reference removed code.</li><li>Update the gaia-dev graph and generated docs if they change.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>composer install</code> and CI are green, and no <code>Elasticsearch\\\\</code> or <code>Monolog\\\\</code> reference remains outside vendor.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 3, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "smtp-env-removal", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Email: drop the env-based SMTP config, Settings is the only source", "description": "<p>SMTP is now set up on the Settings page (<code>core/libs/utils/SmtpSettings.php</code> merges saved settings over the <code>smtp</code> config). The env-based config in <code>core/config/smtp.php</code> (<code>SMTP_*</code> env vars, defaulting to <code>smtp.gmail.com</code>) is no longer needed, and <code>docker-compose.yaml</code> commits a real Gmail username and app password for gaia-dev.</p><ul><li>Remove every <code>SMTP_*</code> variable from <code>docker-compose.yaml</code> (gaia, gaia-test, gaia-test-hermes-down).</li><li>Remove the env reads and the Gmail default from <code>core/config/smtp.php</code>. Keep only non-secret defaults such as port, encryption and auth if <code>SmtpSettings::resolve</code> still needs them, or remove the config and its fallback in <code>SmtpSettings</code>.</li><li>With no host saved in Settings, <code>Mailer</code> sends nothing and logs a warning. It must fail open and never fail the user's write. Today the test containers rely on <code>SMTP_HOST=127.0.0.1:9</code> to stay off real mail servers; after this change that comes from empty Settings. The api-tester mail suite still works by saving the mailpit host in Settings.</li><li>Update <code>tests/libraries/utils/SmtpSettingsTest.php</code>, <code>TestEmailSenderTest.php</code> and <code>tools/api-tester/README.md</code> (the SMTP paragraph).</li><li>The PR says that the password is still in git history and must be rotated by its owner, and that any deployed environment needs its SMTP saved in Settings before this deploys.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> no SMTP credentials or hosts in tracked files. With Settings empty, a notification-triggering write succeeds and no mail is attempted. With Settings filled in, mail is sent. CI is green.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "response-diff", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "api-tester: save response bodies and compare two runs", "description": "<p>The silent risk in the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5 upgrade is responses that still pass the api-tester checks but have changed. A test run already found one: <code>POST /bulk</code> returns an empty <code>200</code> on Phalcon 5. Prometheus reads these responses, so we need to compare the same catalog run on two stacks.</p><ul><li><code>tools/api-tester</code>: an opt-in flag <code>--record-bodies</code> that writes each case's status, content type and body (parsed JSON, or raw text when the body isn't JSON) into the report.</li><li><code>tools/api-tester/bin/compare-reports.php a.json b.json</code>: matches cases by id and reports differences in status, content type, empty vs non-empty body, keys, value types (for example <code>1</code> vs <code>\\\\u00221\\\\u0022</code>) and values. It ignores runtime ids/GUIDs, timestamps and tokens through a documented ignore list, prints a summary grouped per endpoint and per kind of difference, and exits non-zero when there are differences.</li><li>The comparison logic is its own class with unit tests; the bin script only parses arguments and prints.</li><li>Document both in the api-tester README.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two recorded runs of the same stack compare clean (no flaky differences). An empty body in one report and a changed value type are each reported.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> CI wiring (next-stack-ci).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "php8-errors", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Error handling: catch Throwable so Phalcon 5 exceptions still return JSON", "description": "<p>In Phalcon 5, its own exceptions (<code>Mvc\\\\Dispatcher\\\\Exception</code>, <code>Mvc\\\\Model\\\\Exception</code>, ...) no longer extend <code>Phalcon\\\\Exception</code>. A test run on PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5.23 showed that the <code>catch (\\\\Phalcon\\\\Exception)</code> in <code>public/index.php</code> then misses them: an unknown route returns HTTP 200 with a PHP fatal-error HTML page instead of a JSON 404, and a PHQL error does the same instead of a 500. The fix has to work on PHP 7.4 / Phalcon 4 too.</p><ul><li><code>public/index.php</code> and <code>cli.php</code>: a final <code>catch (\\\\Throwable)</code> that goes through the same JSON error path as today (<code>core/exceptions/PhalconError.php</code>), with the status the error deserves (404 for a dispatcher not-found, 500 otherwise).</li><li>Review the other files that catch <code>Phalcon\\\\Exception</code>: <code>RestController</code>, <code>SubRequestRunner</code>, <code>Model</code>, <code>Relationship</code>, <code>query/Clause</code>, <code>UploadController</code>, <code>PreviewController</code>, <code>ImageController</code>, <code>UserimageController</code>, <code>DownloadController</code>, <code>IndexController</code> and <code>ProjectActivitiesComponent</code>. Where the block is meant to catch an exception Phalcon throws, widen it so it also catches it on Phalcon 5. Leave blocks that only catch Gaia's own throws.</li><li>Extend <code>tests/libraries/utils/PhalconErrorTest.php</code>: an exception that doesn't extend <code>Phalcon\\\\Exception</code> produces the JSON error with the right status.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the current stack, an unknown route and a malformed query still return the same JSON errors as before, and CI is green. List each reviewed catch block and the decision in the PR.</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 10, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "migrations", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migrations: create tables without phalcon/migrations, plus a schema snapshot script", "description": "<p><code>phalcon/migrations</code> (installed through <code>phalcon/devtools</code>) blocks PHP 8.5. 3.x only installs through 2021 <code>nette</code> versions never tested on 8.5, and v4 is a rewrite with a different API (no static connection). On Postgres, Gaia only uses its <code>morphTable</code> to create new tables; existing tables go through Gaia's own <code>syncExistingTable</code>.</p><ul><li><code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code>: create new tables with the DB adapter's <code>createTable()</code> (on both Phalcon 4 and 5) instead of extending <code>Phalcon\\\\Migrations\\\\Mvc\\\\Model\\\\Migration</code>, with the same columns, indexes and references as today. Check whether <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Mysql.php</code> relies on the package; if it does, move it to the adapter too, or say in the PR what MySQL loses.</li><li>Remove <code>phalcon/devtools</code> from <code>composer.json</code>.</li><li><code>tools/upgrade/schema-snapshot.sh &lt;db&gt;</code>: <code>pg_dump --schema-only</code> with owner and comment noise removed, so two snapshots can be diffed. Document it in <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>.</li><li>A PHPUnit test showing that creating a table produces the expected definition (fake adapter).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> starting from the baseline dump plus an empty database, the schema snapshot after <code>migration migrate</code> is identical before and after this change. CI is green.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a dry-run mode (migrate-dry-run).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["drop-elasticsearch"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "migrate-dry-run", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Migrations: --dry-run that prints the planned DDL without running it", "description": "<p><code>docker/dev/start.sh</code> runs <code>php cli.php migration migrate</code> every time Gaia starts, and <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> <code>syncExistingTable</code> drops columns that aren't in the metadata. Before switching stacks, and for any risky metadata change, we want to see what migrate would do before it does it.</p><ul><li><code>php cli.php migration migrate --dry-run</code> (<code>core/tasks/MigrationTask.php</code>) prints every CREATE, ALTER, DROP, index and function statement that <code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> and the Postgres driver (<code>syncExistingTable</code>, <code>syncIndexes</code>, <code>syncMultiColumnIndex</code>, <code>migrateFunctions</code>) would run, one per line with its table, and runs none.</li><li>Exit code 0 when nothing is planned, a separate non-zero code when changes are planned, and the usual failure code on errors.</li><li>The switch between running and collecting statements lives in the migration layer, not in the task.</li><li>A PHPUnit test with a fake adapter: planned statements are collected and nothing is executed.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a freshly migrated local database, <code>--dry-run</code> plans nothing. After removing a field from a model's metadata, it lists the DROP without running it. CI is green.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing what migrate does, and changing <code>start.sh</code>.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["migrations"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "deprecation-log", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Collect PHP deprecations and warnings into a grouped report, plus a lint run on the new image", "description": "<p>PHP 8.x reports many upgrade problems only as E_DEPRECATED or E_WARNING. A test run showed that over HTTP none reach the PHP log, because Gaia's error handling hides them. For the PHP 8.5 upgrade they need to be collected and grouped.</p><ul><li><code>docker/php/conf.d/diagnostics.ini</code>, mounted only on the gaia-test services in <code>docker-compose.yaml</code>: <code>error_reporting=E_ALL</code>, <code>log_errors=On</code>, <code>display_errors=Off</code>, log to <code>logs/php-diagnostics.log</code>. Make sure Gaia's own error handler passes deprecations and warnings on to that log instead of hiding them.</li><li>PHPUnit runs write deprecations and warnings to the same kind of log without failing tests, configured through <code>tests/phpunit.xml</code>.</li><li><code>tools/upgrade/lint-next.sh</code>: runs <code>php -l</code> with <code>error_reporting=E_ALL</code> on every PHP file (outside vendor and the gaia-dev fixtures) inside <code>gaia-env:next</code>, and writes the results to a log in the same format.</li><li><code>tools/upgrade/deprecations-report.php &lt;log&gt;...</code>: groups entries by message pattern and <code>file:line</code>, separates Gaia code from vendor, counts them, and prints markdown suitable for a CI job summary. Unit-test the grouping.</li><li>Add the commands to <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a PHPUnit plus api-tester run against gaia-test produces a log, and the lint run on next lists the known implicitly nullable parameters and the <code>private final</code> warnings. The report groups both.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing them, and CI wiring.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["ci-full-suite", "smtp-env-removal", "env-image"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 7, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "php8-deprecations-core", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "PHP 8.4/8.5 deprecations in core/ (code that still runs on PHP 7.4)", "description": "<p>A <code>php -l</code> run on PHP 8.5 found deprecations that can be fixed now in a form PHP 7.4 accepts. This issue fixes the ones under <code>core/</code>.</p><ul><li>Implicitly nullable parameters (<code>Type $x = null</code>) become <code>?Type $x = null</code>.</li><li>The <code>private final</code> methods (mostly <code>core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php</code>) lose <code>final</code>.</li><li><code>#[\\\\AllowDynamicProperties]</code> on the base model <code>core/mvc/models/Model.php</code> (models keep their columns as dynamic properties; the attribute is inherited and is a comment on 7.4).</li><li>Declare the dynamic properties found elsewhere, such as <code>core/mvc/db/factory/DialectFactory.php</code> <code>$dialect</code>.</li><li><code>#[\\\\ReturnTypeWillChange]</code> on the Iterator methods of <code>core/mvc/models/ResultStream.php</code>.</li><li>Find the files with <code>php -d error_reporting=E_ALL -l</code> in <code>gaia-env:next</code>. If more than 15 files under <code>core/</code> need changes, fix 15 and list the rest in the PR for a follow-up.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> those files lint clean on 8.5 and still lint on 7.4, and CI is green on the current stack.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> files outside <code>core/</code>, and Phalcon class renames (the shim covers them).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["env-image", "php8-errors"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 15, "sizeReason": "Mechanical one-line signature changes spread across files; the issue caps itself at 15 files and lists the rest for a follow-up.", "screens": []}, {"key": "php8-deprecations-app", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "PHP 8.4/8.5 deprecations outside core/ (code that still runs on PHP 7.4)", "description": "<p>The same kind of fixes as for <code>core/</code>, for <code>app/</code>, <code>tools/</code>, <code>tests/</code> (excluding <code>tests/tools/gaia-dev/fixtures</code>), <code>public/</code> and <code>cli.php</code>. All of them must still run on PHP 7.4.</p><ul><li>Implicitly nullable parameters become <code>?Type $x = null</code>.</li><li>Remove <code>final</code> from <code>private</code> methods.</li><li>Declare dynamic properties on non-model classes.</li><li><code>#[\\\\ReturnTypeWillChange]</code> where internal interfaces (Iterator, ArrayAccess, Countable, JsonSerializable) are implemented without return types.</li><li>Find the files with <code>php -d error_reporting=E_ALL -l</code> in <code>gaia-env:next</code>. If more than 15 files need changes, fix 15 and list the rest in the PR for a follow-up.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> those files lint clean on 8.5 and still lint on 7.4, and CI is green on the current stack.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> <code>core/</code> and the Phalcon class renames.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": ["env-image", "php8-errors"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 15, "sizeReason": "Mechanical one-line signature changes spread across files; the issue caps itself at 15 files and lists the rest for a follow-up.", "screens": []}, {"key": "dual-stack-boot", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Boot Gaia on both Phalcon 4.1 / PHP 7.4 and Phalcon 5.23 / PHP 8.5 with an alias shim", "description": "<p>For the side-by-side upgrade, the same code on <code>dev</code> must start on both <code>gaia-env:current</code> and <code>gaia-env:next</code> until the switch-over. Gaia uses Phalcon 4 class names that Phalcon 5 removed, in many files: <code>Phalcon\\\\Di</code> (49), <code>Phalcon\\\\Exception</code> (16), <code>Phalcon\\\\Config</code> (10), <code>Phalcon\\\\Text</code> (8), <code>Phalcon\\\\Logger</code> (5), <code>Phalcon\\\\Loader</code> (3). A test run showed that one shim file handles them without editing those files.</p><ul><li><code>core/libs/compat/phalcon5.php</code>, required at the top of <code>autoload.php</code> (and <code>tests/autoload.php</code> if it doesn't go through it). It does nothing on Phalcon 4. On Phalcon 5 it defines the old names: <code>class_alias</code> for <code>Di</code>, <code>DiInterface</code>, <code>Config</code>, <code>Logger</code> and <code>Exception</code>, plus small subclasses where the API changed (<code>Loader</code>: <code>registerNamespaces</code> calls <code>setNamespaces</code>; <code>Text</code>: the methods Gaia uses, built on <code>Phalcon\\\\Support\\\\Helper\\\\Str</code>).</li><li>Delete <code>tests/UnitTestCase.php</code> and its require in <code>tests/TestHelper.php</code>. Nothing extends it, and it doesn't compile on PHP 8.</li><li><code>composer.json</code>: <code>php</code> becomes <code>~7.4.0 || ~8.5.0</code>. Drop <code>ext-psr</code> and the six unused <code>phalcon/incubator*</code> packages, and move <code>bshaffer/oauth2-server-php</code> to a 1.x that supports PHP 8.5. There's no lock file, so each image resolves its own versions; check that nothing falls back to outdated releases on 8.5.</li><li>A PHPUnit test for the shim that passes on both stacks.</li><li>Add the shim and its removal at switch-over to <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the current image, CI is green as before. On <code>gaia-env:next</code>, <code>composer install</code> succeeds, the API serves a token request and a list read, <code>migration migrate</code> runs, and PHPUnit runs to completion (failures allowed). List the remaining failures in the PR.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing everything that fails on next, replacing the old class names in code, and making next the default.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["env-image", "ci-full-suite", "migrations"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 6, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "next-stack-ci", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "CI: non-blocking PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5.23 job that reports what fails", "description": "<p>Shows on every PR what still fails on the new stack, compared with the current one, so the upgrade work is visible and shrinks PR by PR. The current-stack job stays the only blocking check.</p><ul><li>A <code>next-stack</code> job in <code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code> on the published <code>gaia-env:next</code>, with <code>continue-on-error: true</code> and its own vendor cache key. It loads the baseline dump, runs <code>migration migrate --dry-run</code> then <code>migrate</code>, and takes a schema snapshot (<code>tools/upgrade/schema-snapshot.sh</code>). Then it prepares <code>pr4m_test</code>, runs the full PHPUnit suite (JUnit), runs the api-tester backend and acl modes with <code>--record-bodies</code>, runs <code>tools/upgrade/lint-next.sh</code>, and keeps the PHP diagnostics log.</li><li>The current-stack job also uploads a schema snapshot and an api-tester report with bodies.</li><li>A compare step diffs the two schema snapshots and the two api-tester reports (<code>compare-reports.php</code>), runs <code>deprecations-report.php</code>, and writes one markdown summary to <code>$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY</code>: PHPUnit failures, dry-run statements, schema differences, api-tester failures, response differences and deprecations, each with a count and its artifact.</li><li>Add how to reproduce the summary locally to <code>docs/upgrade/php85-phalcon5.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a PR shows the summary, a failure in the next job doesn't block the PR, and the known <code>POST /bulk</code> empty response shows up as a response difference.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing what it reports, and making the job blocking.</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["dual-stack-boot", "deprecation-log", "response-diff", "migrate-dry-run", "ci-full-suite"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}, {"key": "bulk-next", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "POST /bulk returns an empty 200 on Phalcon 5", "description": "<p>On PHP 8.5 / Phalcon 5.23, <code>POST /bulk</code> returns <code>200</code> with <code>Content-Length: 0</code> and logs nothing, while the current stack returns the sub-responses. The likely cause is the nested <code>Application::handle()</code> in <code>core/mvc/http/SubRequestRunner.php</code>: Phalcon 5 handles responses, the dispatcher and DI services differently in a nested handle.</p><ul><li>Start with a failing test (PHPUnit or an api-tester case run against <code>gaia-env:next</code>) that shows the empty body.</li><li>Fix <code>SubRequestRunner</code> so sub-requests return their responses on both stacks, without a Phalcon version check in the class if possible.</li><li>A sub-request that throws is reported in the bulk response as it is today.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the bulk api-tester cases pass on both stacks with identical responses (<code>compare-reports.php</code> shows no difference for <code>/bulk</code>).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": ["dual-stack-boot"], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 4, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 10:47:54	2026-11-18 10:47:54	f
f0c6ce096afd-9969-0c24-dd934c43d79f	7281afa46afd-7a77-8aba-64fa90d6419b	1	{"summary": "Gaia has no rels=none option: rels must name real relationships (an unknown name such as 'none' fails the request) and omitted rels load every relationship, hasMany included. The idea browser's archived count sends rels: 'none', so it fails silently. One Prometheus issue adds a Gaia request-options builder that encodes this contract (explicit belongsTo rels required, no 'none', known option keys only), documents the contract, and moves the idea browser to it, which fixes the archived count. The other callers move in later issues.", "issues": [{"key": "request-options", "project": "A Prometheus", "projectCode": "aprom", "subject": "Data: Gaia request-options builder that encodes the query contract; idea browser uses it (fixes archived count)", "description": "<p>Every <code>store.query</code> in Prometheus builds Gaia's options by hand, and nothing in the client knows Gaia's rules. The idea browser's archived-ideas count (<code>utils/idea/browser-requests.js</code> <code>buildArchivedCountRequest</code>) sends <code>rels: 'none'</code>, an option Gaia doesn't support. Gaia treats it as a relationship name, fails the request, and <code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> (~416) swallows the error, so the count silently disappears. The other trap is leaving out <code>rels</code>: Gaia then loads <strong>every</strong> relationship, hasMany included. This issue puts the contract in one place so each call is right by construction.</p><ul><li>New <code>app/utils/gaia/request-options.js</code>: a pure function that takes the Ember model class (from <code>store.modelFor</code>) and the options, and returns what to pass to <code>store.query</code>/<code>findRecord</code>. Rules, checked with <code>assert</code> from <code>@ember/debug</code> (stripped in production):<ul><li>only the keys Gaia reads (<code>query</code>, <code>rels</code>, <code>fields</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>order</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>limit</code>);</li><li><code>rels</code> is required and non-empty: a call that needs no relations names the cheapest belongsTo (Gaia has no way to ask for none, and omitting it loads all);</li><li>each rel must be a <code>belongsTo</code> of the model (<code>relationshipsByName</code>), so <code>'none'</code>, typos and hasMany rels all fail loudly. The hasMany message points at the <code>CLAUDE.md</code> rule (query the children separately);</li><li>arrays are joined into Gaia's comma strings.</li></ul></li><li>Move <code>utils/idea/browser-requests.js</code> (idea list, archived count, plans) to the builder. The archived count uses <code>rels: ['createdBy']</code>.</li><li>Contract doc <code>docs/architecture/gaia-requests/README.md</code> + <code>decisions.md</code>: what each param means (rels omitted = all relationships, names only, no <code>none</code>, an unknown name fails the request; <code>limit</code> applies to joined rows; <code>limit: -1</code>; paging via <code>meta.links.next</code> with no totals, linking <code>docs/architecture/lists/decisions.md</code>; the query language). Add one line to <code>CLAUDE.md</code> Architecture: new queries go through the builder.</li><li>Unit tests for the builder (every rule, including each assert) and for the moved idea requests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The idea browser shows the archived ideas count again (no request with <code>rels=none</code> is sent).</li><li>In development, a <code>rels</code> value that is missing, <code>none</code>, unknown or hasMany, or an unknown option key, fails with a clear message.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any Gaia change; moving the other ~27 callers that build <code>rels</code> by hand (later issues, some need hasMany loads reworked first).</p>", "type": "Bug", "priority": "medium", "complexity": "simple", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "Claude-v1", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	proposed	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 14:15:12	2026-11-18 14:15:12	f
4c7859a26afd-d3df-b689-ab9cc2457a5a	45e5a2256afc-2d64-3ed5-063c904309cb	4	{"summary": "One Gaia issue that lets the event registry describe every scope Hermes knows (project, user, runtimes, service:<kind>, several per event) and events Hermes already allows but Gaia doesn't raise yet (planned), and adds doc.created/updated/deleted and search.semantic.changed as planned entries, so Hermes' drift check (ah-4643) can pass on dev once ah-4650 and ah-4652 are in.", "issues": [{"key": "registry-scopes-planned", "project": "A Gaia", "projectCode": "agaia", "subject": "Events registry: multiple scopes (runtimes, service:<kind>) and planned entries; list doc.* and search.semantic.changed", "description": "<p>Hermes' drift check (ah-4643) compares <code>hermes/src/contract/names.js</code> with Gaia's registry export <code>docs/generated/events.json</code> (agaia-4640, agaia-4641). The registry can't describe what Hermes already has: it knows only scope <code>project</code> or <code>user</code>, one per event, and only events Gaia raises today. Hermes also allows <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code>, <code>doc.deleted</code> (Gaia publishing: agaia-4531, pending) and <code>search.semantic.changed</code> on the service scope <code>service:ares</code> (Gaia publishing: agaia-4658), and routes <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> to both <code>user:&lt;id&gt;</code> and the <code>runtimes</code> scope (<code>AgentRunLiveEvents</code> already publishes to both).</p><ul><li><code>app/metadata/events.php</code>: replace <code>scope</code> with <code>scopes</code>, a list of <code>project</code>, <code>user</code>, <code>runtimes</code>, <code>service</code>; an entry with <code>service</code> also has <code>serviceKind</code> (e.g. <code>ares</code>). Update every entry; <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> gets <code>user</code> + <code>runtimes</code>. Update the header comment.</li><li>New optional flag <code>planned: true</code>: Hermes may already allow the event, but Gaia doesn't raise it yet. A planned entry is not in <code>EventNames::ALL</code> and <code>HermesPublisher</code> treats it as not allowed.</li><li>Add planned entries: <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code>, <code>doc.deleted</code> (scopes project, channel hermes, consumers prometheus, collab) and <code>search.semantic.changed</code> (scopes service, serviceKind ares, channel hermes, consumers ares).</li><li><code>core/libs/events/EventRegistry.php</code>: <code>scopes(name)</code>, <code>serviceKind(name)</code>, <code>planned(name)</code>; <code>names(channel)</code> excludes planned and disabled entries. Validate on load: known scopes only, <code>serviceKind</code> required with <code>service</code> and only then.</li><li><code>tools/gaia-dev/src/Check/LiveEventsCheck.php</code>: a planned entry must have no <code>EventNames</code> constant emitted by code; when code emits it, fail with \\"remove planned from &lt;name&gt; in app/metadata/events.php\\". Planned entries need no test case.</li><li><code>tools/gaia-dev/src/Docs/EventsExport.php</code>: each item becomes <code>{name, scopes, serviceKind?, channels, enabled, planned, description}</code>; regenerate <code>docs/generated/events.json</code>.</li><li>ADR update in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md</code> (the registry decision): scopes list, planned entries, and the drift rule Hermes applies: Gaia's enabled, non-planned hermes names must be in the allowlist; every allowlisted name must be in the registry on the hermes channel (planned included); user/runtimes/service scope sets must match.</li><li>Tests: registry (scopes, serviceKind validation, planned excluded from names), check (planned and emitted fails), export shape.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> events published today are unchanged; <code>events.json</code> lists doc.* and search.semantic.changed as planned with their scopes and <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> with user + runtimes; gaia-dev check passes on dev.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> publishing doc.* (agaia-4531) or search.semantic.changed (agaia-4658), which must each drop <code>planned</code> when they publish; the Hermes script (ah-4643).</p>", "type": "Task", "priority": "high", "complexity": "complex", "dependsOn": [], "milestone": "aga-MentionEvents", "newMilestone": false, "estimatedFiles": 8, "sizeReason": "", "screens": []}]}	created	\N	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	Agent Nestor	2026-11-18 18:54:04	2026-11-18 18:55:53	f
