d9ea2c186ad9-192a-43e2-564cf383d0a0	Ideas: publish idea, message, plan and plan issue events to Hermes	2026-10-22 00:24:57	2026-10-22 06:54:52	0	<p>The Ideas resources (agaia-4069) store everything, but nothing tells Prometheus or Talos when an idea changes: sending a message or approving a plan in Prometheus must reach the agent tooling and refresh other open pages. Gaia publishes live events for issues, milestones and conversations already; ideas get the same.</p><ul><li>Add to <code>support/EventNames.php</code> (must match Hermes <code>src/contract/names.js</code>, linked Hermes PR): <code>idea.created</code>, <code>idea.updated</code>, <code>idea.message.created</code>, <code>idea.plan.created</code>, <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code>, <code>idea.planissue.created</code>.</li><li>Live events components in <code>app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/</code> extending <code>LiveEventsComponent</code>, listed in <code>$uses</code> of <code>IdeaController</code>, <code>IdeamessageController</code>, <code>IdeaplanController</code>, <code>IdeaplanissueController</code> (one component per resource, like <code>IssueLiveEventsComponent</code>/<code>ConversationCommentLiveEventsComponent</code>).</li><li>Payloads (projectId = the idea's project; every event has <code>meta.ideaId</code>): <code>idea.created</code> changes <code>{title, status}</code>; <code>idea.updated</code> changed <code>title</code>/<code>description</code>/<code>status</code> from the audit diff, only when one changed; <code>idea.message.created</code> resource <code>ideamessage</code>, changes <code>{kind}</code>; <code>idea.plan.created</code> resource <code>ideaplan</code>, changes <code>{version, status}</code>, meta adds <code>version</code>; <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code> when <code>status</code> or <code>error</code> changed, changes <code>{status, error}</code>, meta adds <code>version</code>; <code>idea.planissue.created</code> resource <code>ideaplanissue</code>, changes <code>{key, issueId}</code>, meta adds <code>ideaplanId</code>. No message bodies or plan bodies in events: subscribers re-read through the API.</li><li><code>support/ProjectIdResolver.php</code>: resolve <code>ideaId</code> to the Idea's <code>projectId</code> for the child resources.</li><li>Side effects fail open: Hermes down must not fail the write.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> each write publishes exactly the event above with the right projectId and meta (PHPUnit with a fake publisher, like the existing live events tests); PR description lists the contract impact and links the Hermes PR; both merge together.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> user-scoped or agent events, live progress, notifications for ideas.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4088	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	a66851e96ad8-d753-535b-55dc78bc78d9	\N	cbb506d05acd-06d6-1141-68969b9fd562	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	46eaf5576ad9-4e9a-93ae-a5cf891aa58e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-22 06:54:52	agaia	0	0
ae51c2776ada-1ba3-1fa7-9ee658065edc	Ideas: plan issues like the Nestor UI with links to created issues, approve/archive modal leaves its backdrop, no list highlight	2026-10-22 14:54:38	2026-10-23 17:19:36	0	<ol><li><strong>Plan issues</strong> look like the first Nestor UI (dev-tools/nestor): each issue a collapsed row with a caret, the subject in bold, and a meta line with the project code, type, priority (icon + translated name, coloured), complexity (cog/cogs), milestone (flag, "(new)" when it will be created), "after &lt;keys&gt;" for dependencies, screens, and the created issue's link (e.g. aprom-4102) once the plan was approved, else the issue key. A click expands the description.</li><li><strong>Approve (and archive) modal</strong>: after confirming, the dialog disappears but the backdrop stays. <code>confirmApprove</code>/<code>confirmArchive</code> remove the modal from the page before Bootstrap hides it. Let <code>bootstrap-modal</code> hide it and close it through <code>close</code>.</li><li><strong>Created issue link missing</strong>: the page queries <code>ideaplanissue</code> without <code>rels: 'issue'</code>; the async <code>issue</code> relation has no data, so the Created Issues box shows an empty link. Query with the issue related.</li><li><strong>Ideas list</strong>: no highlight on the selected idea.</li></ol><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4103	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	741405586ada-33fb-3e11-3a332174db83	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-23 17:19:36	aprom	0	0
6a6109176adc-9973-8304-d17b0e7c98cc	bootstrap-modal: wait for an async confirm, with loading state, and close on success	2026-10-24 07:16:58	2026-10-24 12:51:23	0	<p>Confirm modals can't show that work is running, and some don't close after confirming. In <code>templates/components/bootstrap-modal.hbs</code> the confirm button calls the passed-in <code>confirm</code> directly (<code>@onClick={{this.confirm}}</code>). The component's own <code>actions.confirm</code> in <code>components/bootstrap-modal.js</code>, which hides the modal when <code>confirm()</code> returns true, never runs. So callers that return <code>true</code> to close (e.g. <code>components/idea/plan-box.js</code> <code>confirmApprove</code>, after aprom-4103) stay open. Check this in the browser first.</p><ul><li>Route the confirm button through the component's own confirm handler.</li><li>If <code>confirm()</code> returns a Promise: mark the modal busy, which disables Confirm and Cancel and shows a <code>fa fa-spinner fa-spin</code> on Confirm. Ignore repeated clicks. Hide the modal as soon as it resolves truthy. When it rejects or resolves falsy, clear the busy state and keep the modal open.</li><li>Synchronous returns behave as documented: <code>true</code> hides, anything else leaves it open. Check the ~31 existing usages for any that relied on the old behaviour (e.g. a caller that closes itself and would now be hidden twice, or returns true but expects to stay open) and adjust them in this PR.</li><li>The close path still goes through <code>hidden.bs.modal</code> -&gt; <code>close</code>, so no backdrop is left behind (aprom-4103). No new jQuery outside this component. Remove the stray backtick after <code>modal-footer</code> in the template.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a modal whose confirm returns a Promise shows the spinner, ignores double clicks, closes on resolve and stays open (buttons enabled again) on reject. A sync-true modal closes. A sync-false modal stays open. The idea archive modal closes after confirming. Integration test for the component covers all four cases. Full suite passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> rewriting bootstrap-modal as a Glimmer component.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4112	2026-10-31	2026-10-24	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	ac6af3216ad8-d753-535b-b21c3700739d	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	aeabf1396adc-6ca4-f080-baaa2fa4c436	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-24 12:51:23	aprom	0	0
5e1758736a58-fa98-a09f-658fe6f47e42	Revamp RBAC implementation	2026-07-16 07:08:14	2026-07-20 15:20:23	0	<h2 data-tomark-pass="">**Problem Statement**\n</h2>The current Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) implementation supports multiple permission levels (e.g., <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">0</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">1</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">2</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">3</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">9</code>), making authorization logic unnecessarily complex and difficult to maintain. Over time, the permission evaluation has become harder to reason about, increases implementation complexity, and introduces inconsistencies across APIs and resources.\n<p>Additionally, authorization of related resources (<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">rels</code>) and field-level visibility is not consistently enforced, resulting in unpredictable API behavior and increased security risk.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 data-tomark-pass="">**Goal / Objective**\n</h2>Simplify and standardize the authorization model by introducing a binary permission system while establishing clear authorization rules for resources, relationships, and field-level access.\n<p>The new RBAC implementation should be easier to understand, maintain, and extend while providing predictable and secure API responses.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 data-tomark-pass="">**Scope of Work**\n</h2><h3 data-tomark-pass="">**1\\. Simplify Permission Levels**\n</h3>Replace the existing permission level hierarchy with a binary access model.\n<h4 data-tomark-pass="">New Permission Values\n</h4><ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">**0** → No Access</li><li data-tomark-pass="">**1** → Access Granted</li></ul>Remove support for permission values such as:\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">2</li><li data-tomark-pass="">3</li><li data-tomark-pass="">9</li></ul>Authorization decisions should be based solely on whether access is granted or denied.\n<hr>\n<h3 data-tomark-pass="">**2\\. Resource\\-Level Authorization**\n</h3>RBAC will be responsible for determining whether a user has permission to perform an action on a resource.\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Project → Read</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Project → Create</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Project → Update</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Project → Delete</li></ul>Each resource/action combination should be evaluated independently.\n<hr>\n<h3 data-tomark-pass="">**3\\. Relationship \\(<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">rels</code>) Authorization**\n</h3>Authorization must also be evaluated for requested relationships.\n<p>If the parent resource is accessible but a related resource is not, the related data should <strong>not</strong> be returned.</p>\n<h4 data-tomark-pass="">Example\n</h4>Request:\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""><br>\n<code data-te-codeblock="" data-tomark-pass="">GET /api/v1/projects?rels=issues</code>Permissions:</p>\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">✅ Project Read</li><li data-tomark-pass="">❌ Issue Read</li></ul>Expected response:\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""><br>\n<code data-te-codeblock="" data-tomark-pass="">{<br>\n"projects": [<br>\n{<br>\n"id": 1,<br>\n"name": "Website Redesign"<br>\n}<br>\n]<br>\n}</code>The <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">issues</code> relationship should be omitted from the response rather than causing the entire request to fail.</p>\n<p>Each requested relationship should be authorized independently.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3 data-tomark-pass="">**4\\. Field\\-Level Authorization**\n</h3>Introduce field-level access control to determine which resource attributes are visible to a user.\n<p>RBAC should evaluate access to individual fields before serialization.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Budget</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Salary</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Cost</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Internal Notes</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Profit Margin</li></ul>Unauthorized fields should be excluded from the API response.\n<blockquote data-tomark-pass="">**Note:** Field-level authorization applies only to resource attributes and does **not** govern relationship (<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">rels</code>) access.\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h3 data-tomark-pass="">**5\\. Consistent Authorization Flow**\n</h3>Ensure every API follows a consistent authorization pipeline:\n<ol data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Resource authorization</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Action authorization</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Relationship authorization</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Field-level authorization</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Serialize permitted data</li></ol>\n<hr>\n<h2 data-tomark-pass="">**Expected Outcome**\n</h2><ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Simplified permission model</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Easier-to-maintain authorization logic</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Predictable API responses</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Secure relationship handling</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Consistent field-level visibility</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Improved extensibility for future resources</li></ul>\n<hr>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""><br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3905	2026-07-17	2026-07-16	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	63413fd6673b-6180-ffb0-440801685dd8	\N	cbc507475acd-06d6-1141-be4fe5e9193b	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	f91122756a58-3147-094e-6cf7358eee4d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-07-20 15:13:44	agaia	0	0
03f27c316a1e-5959-df1f-a8639da1ac7e	Remove Reports & Timelogs Navigation from Navbar	2026-06-02 04:45:55	2026-06-02 17:14:20	0	<p>Remove the <strong>Reports</strong> and <strong>Timelogs</strong> navigation items from the application's main navigation bar.</p>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""><br>\nThe current navigation structure contains links that are no longer required. Removing these items will simplify the navigation experience, reduce visual clutter, and help users focus on the most relevant sections of the application.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3897	2026-06-03	2026-06-02	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	0a337ec36a1d-0176-a590-3f299fa1b9ce	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	becded286a1e-ceed-e188-5542a3a7b7b7	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-06-02 17:14:17	aprom	0	0
4292e7736ad7-3791-42b0-dc417a56bae0	Notifications sidebar: group notifications by issue	2026-10-20 21:29:38	2026-10-23 19:10:58	0	<p>Every change to an issue (assignment, status change, comment, time log) creates its own notification, so one issue often fills several rows of the notifications sidebar. The sidebar should show one collapsible group per issue. This is UI only: Gaia keeps creating one notification per change.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Add a pure grouping function (e.g. <code>app/utils/notifications/group-by-issue.js</code>) that takes the flat <code>notifications.notifications</code> list and returns entries in display order. Notifications whose <code>context.relatedTo</code> is <code>issue</code>, <code>comment</code> or <code>timelog</code> and that have <code>context.projectShortcode</code> and <code>context.issueNumber</code> are grouped by <code>projectShortcode</code> (case-insensitive) + <code>issueNumber</code>. All other notifications are standalone entries. Entries are sorted by their newest notification, newest first, and notifications in a group are newest first too.</li><li>Expose the grouped entries from <code>services/notifications.js</code> as a getter computed from the tracked <code>notifications</code> array, so live <code>notification.created</code> pushes, pagination merges and read-state updates regroup automatically. Do not change how the service loads, deduplicates or marks notifications.</li><li>Add a component <code>AppUi::Notifications::Group</code> (co-located in <code>app/components/app-ui/notifications/</code>). Collapsed it shows the issue key (<code>SHORTCODE-number</code>), the newest notification's text (via <code>AppUi::TagParser</code>), an update count, an unread count, and the newest timestamp. It gets the unread style when any item in the group is unread. Clicking the header toggles expansion (collapsed by default), and expanded it lists the existing <code>AppUi::Notifications::Notification</code> items unchanged. Expanding does not mark anything read. A group with one notification renders as a plain <code>Notification</code>.</li><li>Update <code>app-layouts/notifications-sidebar.hbs</code> to iterate the grouped entries instead of the flat list. <code>InfiniteScroll</code> keeps <code>@model</code> on the flat list so paging is unchanged.</li><li>Follow <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>: reuse the existing notification item styling in <code>styles/components/notifications-sidebar.scss</code>, square edges, existing colours, Font Awesome 4 caret icons. Put new strings (update count, unread count) in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>When an issue is assigned to the user and its status then changed, the sidebar shows one group for that issue with 2 updates, not two rows.</li><li>Comment and time log notifications on the same issue join that issue's group. Project, milestone and membership notifications stay as separate rows in time order.</li><li>A live notification for an issue that already has a group joins it, and the group moves to the top. Unread counts update.</li><li>Opening an item inside a group marks only that item read and navigates as today. Mark all as read and cross-tab sync still clear the group's unread state.</li><li>Unit tests for the grouping function (mixed types, case of the shortcode, ordering, missing context) and integration tests for the group component (collapsed/expanded, single-item case, unread state). Update the existing notification acceptance features and Mirage data to cover grouping.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: grouping or merging in Gaia, a per-group "mark read" action (needs a bulk endpoint), grouping non-issue notifications, and remembering expanded state across reloads.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4063	2026-10-28	2026-10-21	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	059fbf476ada-ed55-8ece-8502e6795087	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-23 19:10:59	aprom	0	0
8bdbbe936ad9-4a8c-9b61-163c8f801287	ai test: Git Bash mangles /regex/ filters, empty filters hang ember test, and hung runs leave processes in the container	2026-10-21 21:24:27	2026-10-21 23:02:38	0	<p>aprom-4073 (Sonnet, Talos) lost about 20 minutes and ended blocked. It ran <code>dev-tools/ai/ai test prometheus --filter "/idea/i" 2>&amp;1 | tail -40</code> from Git Bash, and the run never finished:</p><ul><li><strong>Path conversion.</strong> Git Bash rewrites an argument that starts with <code>/</code> before passing it to a native Windows program. The filter reached <code>ember test</code> as <code>C:/Program Files/Git/idea/i</code>; the stuck test page showed <code>filter=c:/program files/git/idea/i</code>. You can see it with <code>python -c "import sys;print(sys.argv[1:])" --filter "/idea/i"</code>, which prints <code>['--filter', 'C:/Program Files/Git/idea/i']</code>.</li><li><strong>An empty filter hangs.</strong> When no test matches, QUnit marks the run failed (<code>Prometheus Tests (0/1)</code>), but testem never reports completion. <code>ember test</code> then waits forever, with Chrome idle.</li><li><strong>Leftover processes.</strong> Killing the caller doesn't stop the <code>ember test</code> or Chrome started through <code>docker exec</code> inside <code>p4m-test-prometheus-*</code>. They keep the testem port (7357), so the next run collides with them. They had to be killed by hand.</li><li><strong>No partial output.</strong> <code>ai test</code> writes its log only at the end. With the output also piped through <code>tail</code>, the agent's background output file stayed empty, and it polled that file for 10 minutes.</li></ul><p>Changes:</p><ul><li>Set <code>MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1</code> (and <code>MSYS2_ARG_CONV_EXCL='*'</code>) in the <code>ai/ai</code>, <code>installer/p4m</code>, <code>talos/talos</code>, <code>nestor/nestor</code> and <code>sim/sim</code> launchers before <code>exec</code>.</li><li>As a safeguard, <code>ai test --filter</code> rejects a value that looks like a converted Windows path (e.g. contains <code>:/</code> or <code>Program Files</code>) with a clear message.</li><li>A filter that matches no tests fails fast with "no tests matched", instead of hanging. Also give the <code>ember test</code> step its own timeout.</li><li>On timeout or interrupt, kill the in-container <code>ember test</code> and its Chrome (<code>pkill</code> by pattern, taking care that the pattern doesn't match the <code>sh -c</code> that runs it). Before starting a run, also clear any <code>ember test</code> left over from an earlier one.</li><li>Write <code>test-&lt;repo&gt;-ember.log</code> as the run progresses.</li><li>Agent instructions (<code>/start-issue</code> command card, Odysseus role): don't pipe long-running commands through <code>tail</code>/<code>head</code>; prefer <code>ai test --changed</code> or a plain-text filter.</li></ul><p>Also seen: an orphaned <code>ember</code> process (pid 2214, about 2.9 GB, a day old, parent pid 1) in the test container, with swap nearly full. <code>p4m</code> should find and clear processes like this.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> from Git Bash, <code>ai test prometheus --filter "/idea/i"</code> runs the idea tests. <code>--filter "/nomatch/"</code> fails within seconds. Interrupting a run leaves no <code>ember test</code> or Chrome processes in the container.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4081	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	885a68b86ad9-5cff-cf2d-1923547c6131	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-21 23:02:38	adt	0	0
76c957046aee-a7e9-ca02-9e8494b7ae42	External Request: Query: bind query values as parameters and validate field names in Clause.php	2026-11-06 21:41:10	2026-11-07 07:26:11	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Prometheus (idea "Query Builder", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p><strong>Request from A Prometheus (ezSearch).</strong> ezSearch lets people type free-text queries, which Gaia turns into PHQL. Today <code>Clause.php</code> concatenates both the values and the field names into the where string. A value with an apostrophe breaks the query, and crafted values or fields reach the SQL, which breaks the house rule "never build SQL/PHQL by string concatenation". ezSearch refuses apostrophes until this is fixed. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Where</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php</code> <code>prepareWhere</code> ~l.188-273 builds <code>$translatedStatement</code> with the values inlined.</li><li><code>core/mvc/models/Query.php:141</code> calls <code>queryBuilder-&gt;where($this-&gt;clause-&gt;where)</code> with no bind parameters.</li><li>The translated leaves are reused by <code>getWhereClause</code> (~l.551), by query splitting in <code>updateBaseWhereWithIds</code>, <code>updateRelatedWhere</code> and <code>updateBaseWhereWithId</code> (~l.599-632, the last also inlines the id), by <code>core/mvc/models/Model.php:379</code> (HasManyToMany <code>prepareWhere</code>) and by <code>query/Meta.php:176-223</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed change</strong></p><ul><li>Each leaf emits PHQL placeholders (<code>:qN:</code>) and records the values in a bind map on the Clause.</li><li>BETWEEN gets two placeholders, IN gets one per item (or an array bind), and LIKE patterns are built in PHP with <code>%</code> and <code>_</code> escaped.</li><li>The bind map travels with the where string to every place that reuses it, including split queries and many-to-many where clauses.</li><li>Field names are checked against <code>alias.field</code> (identifier characters only) and resolved against the model metadata or the relationship aliases; an unknown field returns a clear 400 error.</li><li>The wire format does not change.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Values containing <code>'</code> (e.g. <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS O'Brien)</code>) filter correctly.</li><li>A value such as <code>x') OR ('1'='1</code> matches literally and widens nothing.</li><li>An invalid field name returns 400.</li><li>The existing api-tester query cases (issue list, board and gantt queries, saved searches, related-model filters, query splitting) all pass.</li><li>Tests added per the run-tests skill.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> brackets inside quoted values (separate request), new operators.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4301</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4302	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	77c73c366ae8-73b7-51f2-b6608da2587e	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	5ff1d0d86aee-7d6c-248d-4e49ac0999e8	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 07:26:11	agaia	0	0
