08b9bc386ae5-9c1a-ae8f-2361a937558f	External Request: Preview: fix /preview/get/<token> (missing Downloadtoken import, upload lookup, bound token, images only)	2026-10-31 14:24:08	2026-10-31 15:32:53	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Prometheus (idea "Idea screen preview", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Every <code>GET /preview/get/&lt;token&gt;</code> fails with <code>Class 'Gaia\\MVC\\REST\\Controllers\\Downloadtoken' not found</code> (<code>app/api/v1/controllers/PreviewController.php:45</code>). Prometheus uses this endpoint to show idea screens, images pasted into idea messages and wiki images, so none of them load. The token is created by the authenticated, ACL-checked <code>GET /upload?id=X&amp;download=true</code> (<code>UploadController::listAction</code>). It is single-use and lasts 10 minutes. That design stays: an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> can't send a Bearer token.</p><ul><li>Add <code>use Gaia\\MVC\\Models\\Downloadtoken;</code>, as in <code>DownloadController</code>.</li><li>Look the token up with a bound parameter. Never put the URL value into the query or <code>find()</code> string.</li><li>Read the <code>readAll()</code> result as <code>DownloadController</code> does (<code>['baseModel']</code>), or use a single bound <code>findFirst</code>.</li><li>Load the upload by the token's <code>uploadId</code>, not through the <code>&lt;relatedTo&gt;Upload</code> relation. <code>Downloadtoken</code> metadata only has <code>issueUpload</code> and <code>wikiUpload</code>, so idea uploads would still fail.</li><li>Serve images only: when <code>fileMime</code> isn't <code>image/*</code>, return the same not-found response as an invalid token. Send <code>Content-Disposition: inline</code> and <code>X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</code>.</li><li>Return the content with <code>setContent</code> and return the response once, as <code>DownloadController</code> does. Drop the <code>readfile</code> + <code>send()</code> double send.</li><li>Keep the token single-use: delete it after a successful response or when it has expired.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong> (start with a failing one): a valid token for an idea upload returns 200 with the image bytes and mime. The same token a second time returns not found. Expired, unknown and non-image tokens return not found. A token containing quotes or query syntax is treated as not found.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the idea page, screens and pasted images load. Wiki images load again.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing token-based access with authenticated blob fetching, and <code>DownloadController</code>'s own unbound queries (log a separate issue).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4236	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	469f6e096ae5-5b75-e81d-2e78a6fff912	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 15:32:53	agaia	0	0
cf4c4cc26adb-4599-3884-aae2276cd86f	Notifications sidebar: show issue groups as an always-open heading with all notifications listed	2026-10-23 18:05:03	2026-10-23 19:10:40	0	<p>aprom-4063 groups notifications by issue, but each group is a collapsed toggle header showing only the newest notification's text and counts. Users have to expand it to see anything, and expanded items lose the normal item styling. The engineer wants each group to be a plain heading with the issue key and every notification of that issue listed under it, always visible.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/app-ui/notifications/group.{hbs,js}</code>: remove the collapse. No caret, <code>isExpanded</code>, <code>toggle</code>/<code>onKeyDown</code>, <code>role="button"</code>/<code>tabindex</code>/<code>aria-expanded</code>, newest-text preview, update count or unread count. Render <code>li.notification-group</code> with a heading <code>h5.notification-group-heading</code> holding only the issue key (<code>SHORTCODE-number</code>, upper case, <code>fa fa-ticket</code> icon). Take the key from the same values the issue link is built from: <code>context.projectShortcode</code> + <code>context.issueNumber</code>, already on the group entry as <code>shortcode</code>/<code>issueNumber</code>. Make the key a link to the issue page, using the same route/link the notification item builds for issue notifications in <code>notification.js</code>; reuse that logic rather than duplicating it. Following the heading link must not mark anything read. Under the heading, list every notification of the group with the existing <code>AppUi::Notifications::Notification</code>, unchanged, newest first.</li><li>Render the heading for every issue group, including groups with a single notification (remove the <code>length 1</code> shortcut that renders a plain item).</li><li>Fix item styling inside groups: today items sit in <code>ul.notification-group-items</code>, which the <code>.notifications-list &gt; li &gt; a</code> rules in <code>app/styles/components/notifications-sidebar.scss</code> don't match, so grouped items lose their padding and flex layout. Grouped items must look exactly like ungrouped ones (e.g. give the inner list the <code>notifications-list</code> class or widen the selector) with no left indent.</li><li>Styles in <code>notifications-sidebar.scss</code>: replace <code>.notification-group-header</code>/<code>.notification-group-caret</code> with <code>.notification-group-heading</code>: a small padded heading with a 1px divider above it (use the existing <code>rgba(210, 214, 222, …)</code> border colour), key in bold link blue (<code>$secondaryColor</code>), square edges, no new colours or shadows (<code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>). The heading has no unread style; unread stays on the items.</li><li>Order: keep <code>utils/notifications/group-by-issue.js</code> as is. Entries (groups and standalone notifications) sort by their newest notification, newest first, and items inside a group sort newest first. A new notification for an issue whose group sits lower moves that group to the top. Remove anything from the component that only the collapsed header used (e.g. unread count), along with the translation keys <code>views.app.notifications.updateCount</code>/<code>unreadCount</code> if unused.</li><li>Tests: update <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/notifications/</code> group tests (heading with the key shown, all items rendered without interaction, single-item group has a heading, heading links to the issue and doesn't mark read) and the acceptance features under <code>tests/acceptance/notification/</code>. Add one unit or acceptance case for the order: issue A's latest notification is 3 minutes old and its oldest is yesterday, issue B's latest is 1 hour old, so A comes before B.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Opening the sidebar shows, for every issue (even one with a single notification), a heading with the issue key followed by all its loaded notifications, with no click needed.</li><li>Groups and standalone notifications are ordered by their most recent notification, newest first, including after a live <code>notification.created</code> push and after loading more pages.</li><li>Grouped items look identical to ungrouped items (avatar, text, timestamp, unread marker).</li><li>Clicking an item still marks it read and navigates as before. Clicking the heading only navigates to the issue.</li><li>Lint and the full Prometheus suite pass. Compare in the running app with the screen attached.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> issue subject in the heading (not in the notification context; needs Gaia, later), per-group mark-as-read, collapsing, and changes to how the service loads or pages notifications.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4063</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> grouped-sidebar.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4104	2026-10-30	2026-10-23	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	939ea5596adb-4dcd-958f-a6e1bf84c249	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-23 19:10:40	aprom	0	0
3c94d0396ade-5527-77b9-ed33d202c6ac	gaia-mcp: load issue comments, time logs and idea messages in separate queries, not as hasMany rels with limit=1	2026-10-25 18:45:16	2026-10-26 21:49:11	0	<p>Gaia applies <code>limit</code> to the joined rows, not to the parent records. A lookup with <code>limit=1</code> and hasMany <code>rels</code> therefore truncates the children. This is a known Gaia design caveat and won't be changed now. <code>issue_by_number</code> sends <code>limit=1</code> with <code>rels=comments,spent,estimated</code>, so <code>gaia_get_issue</code> (and <code>ai issue</code> / <code>ai context</code>) only ever return the first 2 comments. On agaia-4075, Talos missed three answers on the thread and kept asking again. <code>_idea</code> (<code>gaia_get_idea</code>, Nestor) does the same with <code>rels=messages,plans</code>.</p><p><strong>Fix</strong> (Gaia's established pattern): load the parent without hasMany rels, then load the children in their own query with a much bigger limit.</p><ul><li><code>gaia_get_issue</code>: comments from <code>comment</code> by the issue's conversation room, newest first, last 10 by default (a <code>comments</code> argument can ask for more, up to 100). Return them oldest first, with the total count. Spent/estimated time from <code>timelog</code> by <code>issueId</code>.</li><li><code>gaia_get_idea</code>: messages and plans in their own queries.</li><li><code>ai issue --comments N / --full</code> pass the count through.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>gaia_get_issue 4075</code> returns the latest 10 comments (it has more than 2); time totals match Prometheus; tests cover the separate queries.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4124	2026-11-01	2026-10-25	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	a5d408356ade-57fe-4b7b-5cbf3c271072	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-26 21:49:11	adt	0	0
5ae910206adb-b6fb-3a5e-a22b8af5e654	Idea page: 'View the plan' opens its version, plan shows its screens, status label alignment	2026-10-23 21:49:14	2026-10-24 08:59:14	0	<p>The idea page's plan box has three problems: the 'View the plan' link on a message does nothing, the screens a plan lists can't be seen before the plan is approved, and the status label in the box header is off-center.</p><ul><li><strong>View the plan:</strong> <code>components/idea/message-item.hbs</code> links to <code>#ideaplan-&lt;id&gt;</code>, which matches nothing. Replace it with an action passed down from the idea page controller (<code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>, through <code>Idea::ConversationBox</code>). The action sets the plan to show (for example a tracked <code>shownPlanId</code>) and scrolls the plan box (<code>data-idea-plan</code>) into view. <code>Idea::PlanBox</code> takes the requested plan as an argument and shows that version's tab. Keep the current behaviour otherwise: the latest version by default, the user's tab pick, and a newer version arriving resets the pick.</li><li><strong>Screens in the plan:</strong> under the plan summary, add a row of thumbnails for every screen key listed by any planned issue of the shown version, each key once. Resolve each key to its latest version from the idea's message screens (<code>message.screens</code>: uploadId, key, title, version), because that is what Talos attaches on approval. Reuse <code>Idea::MessageScreens</code> / <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code> (thumbnail plus click to preview) and pass the messages or a resolved list from the page. If a key has no screen, show it as plain text. Keep the existing key list in each issue's meta row.</li><li><strong>Status label:</strong> in <code>components/idea/plan-box.hbs</code>, put the status <code>label</code> inside <code>&lt;div class="box-tools pull-right"&gt;</code>, as <code>conversation-box.hbs</code> does, so it is vertically centred in the header. Add no new CSS.</li><li>Translations in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> (<code>views.app.idea.plan.*</code>), Mirage data, and integration tests for plan-box and message-item.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> clicking 'View the plan' on a message for v2 while v3 exists shows the v2 tab and scrolls to the plan box. A plan whose issues list screens shows their latest thumbnails before approval. The status label is centred in the header, like the conversation box tools.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> thumbnails inside each issue's detail, a picker for older screen versions, and the Gaia upload 404 (a separate issue; thumbnails depend on <code>/upload/{id}</code> working).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4105	2026-10-31	2026-10-24	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	ac6af3216ad8-d753-535b-b21c3700739d	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	acdcdd936adc-e6e8-3718-572beda3f561	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-24 08:59:14	aprom	0	0
0a890c186981-88d1-7028-71164d501df1	Handle Image upload size	2026-02-03 13:45:46	2026-03-04 11:27:02	0	<p>An error occurred when Image uploaded of size 7MB. Set limit to that so that user shouln't face any error while adding comment.<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>Fatal error: Uncaught PDOException: SQLSTATE[08S01]: Communication link failure: 1153 Got a packet bigger than 'max_allowed_packet' bytes in /var/www/html/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php:790 Stack trace: #0 [internal function]: PDOStatement-&gt;execute() #1 [internal function]: Phalcon\\Db\\Adapter\\Pdo\\AbstractPdo-&gt;executePrepared(Object(PDOStatement), Array, Array) #2 [internal function]: Phalcon\\Db\\Adapter\\Pdo\\AbstractPdo-&gt;execute('INSERT INTO `co...', Array, Array) #3 [internal function]: Phalcon\\Db\\Adapter\\AbstractAdapter-&gt;insert('comments', Array, Array, Array) #4 [internal function]: Phalcon\\Mvc\\Model-&gt;doLowInsert(Object(Phalcon\\Mvc\\Model\\MetaData\\Memory), Object(Phalcon\\Db\\Adapter\\Pdo\\Mysql), 'comments', false) #5 /var/www/html/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php(790): Phalcon\\Mvc\\Model-&gt;save(Array) #6 [internal function]: Gaia\\Core\\MVC\\REST\\Controllers\\RestController-&gt;postAction() #7 [internal function]: Phalcon\\Dispatcher\\AbstractDispatcher-&gt;callActionMethod(Object(Gaia\\MVC\\REST\\Controllers\\CommentControll in&nbsp;/var/www/html/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php&nbsp;on line&nbsp;790\n</code></pre>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3806	2026-02-04	2026-02-03	pending	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	1c5ba55169a5-edd6-cd30-52e2cd27f10c	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	2f68d74162c6-8e43-a8e0-a879eaeffc5e	2026-03-04 11:27:02	aprom	0	0
af8c51386ad6-6765-7e60-74c42c064e76	Settings: Email page – Test Settings button (modal with recipient, translated test result)	2026-10-19 18:25:51	2026-10-19 20:30:55	0	<p>Follow-up to aprom-3964. The Email page is merged (prometheus#532) without the test-email box. This adds a <strong>Test Settings</strong> button, so admins can check their SMTP settings by sending a test email <strong>without saving them</strong>.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Depends on</strong>: agaia-4017 (test flag on <code>PATCH /api/v1/setting</code>). Build against its contract with Mirage; the PR merges after agaia-4017.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Scope</strong> (<code>app/controllers/app/settings/email.js</code>, <code>app/templates/app/settings/email.hbs</code>)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A <strong>Test Settings</strong> button (<code>btn-default</code>) next to Save on the Email Settings page. It replaces the old "Send a test email" box in 3964's scope.</li>\n<li>Clicking it opens a modal (follow <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>: AdminLTE box styling, square edges):\n  <ul>\n  <li>it asks for a recipient email address, defaulting to the current user's email;</li>\n  <li>submit is disabled until the address is valid (the same email validation as the form).</li>\n  </ul>\n</li>\n<li>On submit, send the <strong>current form values</strong> (the draft, saved or not) in one request to the existing save endpoint, plus the test flag and the recipient:\n<pre>PATCH /api/v1/setting\n{ "collection": [ { "id": "...", "settingValue": "..." }, ... ], "test": true, "recipient": "..." }</pre>\n  <ul>\n  <li>Include every email field.</li>\n  <li>Send a blank password as blank: Gaia then uses the stored one.</li>\n  <li><strong>Don't</strong> use <code>record.save()</code> here. It would save the settings and mark the records as clean.</li>\n  </ul>\n</li>\n<li>Read <code>testResult</code> from the response and show its translated message in the modal (success styling for <code>TEST_EMAIL_SENT</code>, error styling otherwise). Show a spinner and disable the button while sending.</li>\n<li>Translations in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>views.app.settings.email.test.*</code>, one per code: <code>TEST_EMAIL_SENT</code>, <code>INVALID_RECIPIENT</code>, <code>SMTP_AUTH_FAILED</code>, <code>SMTP_CONNECTION_FAILED</code> and <code>UNKNOWN_ERROR</code>. An unknown or missing code, or a network failure, shows the <code>UNKNOWN_ERROR</code> message.</li>\n<li>A test leaves the form exactly as it was: the draft, its dirty state and the navigation guard are unchanged.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Test Settings never changes the stored settings. Reloading after a test shows the previously saved values.</li>\n<li>Save behaves the same as before.</li>\n<li>Every possible test result has a matching translated message.</li>\n<li>Submit is impossible with an invalid recipient.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Tests</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Gherkin scenarios in <code>tests/acceptance/settings/email.feature</code>, steps in <code>tests/acceptance/steps/settings/email-steps.js</code>:\n  <ul>\n  <li>the modal opens with the current user's email;</li>\n  <li>an invalid recipient blocks submit;</li>\n  <li>each result code shows its message;</li>\n  <li>unsaved edits are sent in the test and stay unsaved afterwards (the Mirage DB is unchanged).</li>\n  </ul>\n</li>\n<li>Mirage: extend <code>mirage/route-handlers/setting.js</code> so that PATCH with <code>test: true</code> returns a configurable <code>testResult</code> with the status from agaia-4017 (200/422/502), and saves nothing.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><em>Mockups:</em> the test-email part of the aprom-3964 mockups (<code>dev-tools/mockups/settings/</code>), with the box replaced by the button and modal described here.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	4018	2026-10-26	2026-10-19	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	7f53bcb86ace-34bf-02fa-83a17db4682e	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	012426626ad6-97e0-4576-b25d78220453	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-19 20:30:55	aprom	0	0
ec5122556ae0-36a5-29af-f516a39e9847	Talos: dependency gating, hold issues whose "Depends on" issues aren't merged	2026-10-27 16:18:52	2026-10-28 05:53:58	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. With runs in parallel, an issue can be started before the issue it builds on is merged. Nestor and the gaia MCP already write "Depends on #N" lines into descriptions.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Parse "Depends on" lines (pure function in <code>talos/lib/policy.py</code>).</li>\n<li>An issue whose dependency isn't done/merged goes into a held set instead of running, with one "waiting on #N" comment (not repeated).</li>\n<li>The held set is re-checked when any issue changes status (Hermes events) and on reconnect; held time counts toward neither iterations nor runs.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Done when</strong>: assigning B (depends on A) while A is in review holds B; A becoming done releases B; policy unit tests cover parsing, holding and release.</p>\n<p>Depends on: none</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4161	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	bcb698486ae0-36a5-29af-ebb1949fa852	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	fb8853f86ae1-acf1-d2bd-c9237a7af282	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 05:53:58	adt	0	0
0c8f58f969c3-246c-d842-a0d1d4371aaf	Password auto generated indication	2026-03-25 15:15:24	2026-04-07 07:22:30	0	<p>For now there is no inidication for the end user that the password will be generated by system and will be recevied via email. So handle these two scenarios that will mature ux.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3850	2026-03-26	2026-03-25	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	1c5ba55169a5-edd6-cd30-52e2cd27f10c	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	4173069869ce-339c-1059-0f4c46b6dd2a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-04-07 07:22:29	aprom	0	0
0c9e65c169c3-5df4-3053-2caa1c84b3b9	Add more validation on email | User creation	2026-03-25 14:02:52	2026-04-08 13:55:42	0	<p>Yup doesn't validate dot specific email. Add more custom validation on top of the yup's default one.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3847	2026-03-26	2026-03-25	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	1c5ba55169a5-edd6-cd30-52e2cd27f10c	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	90d04b8369c4-10bd-27e5-91b8ddbb1f7f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-04-08 13:55:42	aprom	0	0
65482f026ad6-ee49-a263-c3cd1c333885	Agent tooling: make tests, shipping and context deterministic (cut tokens and time per issue)	2026-10-19 19:49:57	2026-10-19 20:43:00	0	<p>The Talos runs of aprom-3964, agaia-4017 and aprom-4018 cost $7.84 and 61 minutes for simple issues. Most of the cost went on tooling workarounds, not on the issues: test-environment wrangling (17% of context tokens), workflow chores (15%) and reading dev-tools source to learn how to use it (14%). About 75–80% of wall time went on test runs. This issue covers dev-tools and the Pr4M skills.</p>\n<p><strong>Defects</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>ai test</code> and <code>p4m test</code> run in the shared <code>gaia-test</code> / <code>prometheus-dev</code> containers. Those mount the checkout they were created from (<code>Projects4Me/</code>), not the workspace the agent is working in (<code>Pr4M/</code>), so the suites test the wrong code.</li>\n<li><code>ai commit</code> and <code>ai pr</code> write to <code>&lt;repo&gt;/.git/…</code>, which fails in a submodule (where <code>.git</code> is a file).</li>\n<li>The Prometheus baseline is a failure count, so a different failing test looks "known", and a known one can look new (aprom-3964 ended blocked).</li>\n<li>CRLF shell scripts in the checkouts break the api-tester harness (<code>p4m repos sync</code> doesn't run <code>fix-eol</code>).</li>\n<li>The entrypoint scripts are committed without the exec bit, which breaks them on Ubuntu/macOS.</li>\n<li><code>p4m configure</code> keeps an existing gaia MCP registration even when it points at another checkout.</li>\n<li>The gaia MCP (and so Talos) sets only <code>statusId</code>. Gaia's status notification and activity entry look for <code>status</code>, so you get no "status changed" notification.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Changes</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><code>p4m test</code> and <code>ai test</code> always test the workspace checkout. When the shared container mounts a different path, run in a throwaway container from the same image, with the same network and env and the right mount.</li>\n<li>Name-based baselines: <code>ai baseline &lt;repo&gt;</code> runs the suite on a clean <code>origin/dev</code> worktree and caches the failing test names by dev SHA. <code>ai test</code> reports only failures not in that set.</li>\n<li>Targeted tests: <code>ai test &lt;repo&gt; --changed</code> maps changed files to the related tests (Ember feature/module, api-tester resource, PHPUnit folder). Reruns of the Ember tests reuse one build.</li>\n<li>Fix <code>ai commit</code> and <code>ai pr</code> in submodules.</li>\n<li><code>ai ship</code>: one command, from a single JSON file, for notes → time → commit → push → PR → hand-off.</li>\n<li><code>ai context &lt;issue&gt;</code>: a deterministic context pack. It gives outlines (signatures with line numbers) of the files, classes and endpoints the issue names, plus the related tests and recent commits.</li>\n<li><code>ai review --open</code>: fold the CodeRabbit boilerplate (collapsed <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> blocks, analysis chains) without dropping any finding text.</li>\n<li>Skills carry an exact command card. Add a Windows note: <code>python</code>, never <code>python3</code> (the Store stub hangs).</li>\n<li>Model routing: <code>complex</code> means a design decision, not a large change. Document it in the issue-creation guidance and in Talos.</li>\n<li>Talos turn budget: when a run passes N turns, it stops with <code>needs_input</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Line endings in the gaia and prometheus repos themselves have their own issues.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	4019	2026-10-27	2026-10-20	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	385694586ad6-bc7c-58a5-943df47fcc78	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10