220d75306ad8-298c-c7bd-1c45788680f3	Notifications: add relatedTo and relatedId columns to system notifications and set them on create	2026-10-21 07:30:42	2026-10-23 19:41:46	0	<p>Notifications today have no column that says which entity they are about; the link exists only inside the <code>description</code> tags and the <code>context</code> JSON text. Generic <code>relatedTo</code> and <code>relatedId</code> columns let Gaia find and update notifications by entity (first use: mark an issue's notifications read when the user views the issue), and new entity types can be added later without schema changes.</p><ul><li><strong>Metadata:</strong> in <code>app/metadata/model/Systemnotification.php</code> add <code>relatedTo</code> (varchar 50, null true) and <code>relatedId</code> (varchar 36, null true) with labels in the existing <code>LBL_SYSTEM_NOTIFICATION_*</code> style, and add indexes on both (the <code>'field' =&gt; 'index'</code> style used in <code>Issuewatcher.php</code>). Run the migration locally.</li><li><strong>Meaning:</strong> the columns hold the <em>parent entity</em> the user would open, not the thing that triggered the notification. Set them in <code>app/api/v1/controllers/components/notifications/modules/</code>: <code>IssueNotification</code> uses <code>issue</code> / the issue id; <code>CommentNotification</code> uses <code>issue</code> / <code>$conversationroom-&gt;issueId</code>; <code>TimelogNotification</code> uses <code>issue</code> / <code>$issue-&gt;id</code>; <code>MilestoneNotification</code> uses <code>milestone</code> / the milestone id; <code>MembershipNotification</code> uses <code>project</code> / the project id. Cover every <code>CreateModel::execute('systemnotification', ...)</code> call.</li><li>Leave <code>context.relatedTo</code> (issue, comment, timelog, milestone, project) unchanged: Prometheus builds notification links from it. The new column is a separate, coarser field. Document the difference in the metadata labels or docblocks.</li><li>Both fields come back on <code>GET /systemnotification</code> through the normal metadata, so Prometheus can read them.</li><li>Tests: notification unit/api tests assert both columns for each module (the comment and timelog cases point at the issue). Regenerate the <code>tools/api-tester</code> backend catalog.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after migrating, every newly created notification has <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code> set according to the mapping above, both are indexed, and both are returned by the API.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> backfilling existing notifications (they keep NULL); any read-marking endpoint change (separate issue).</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4064	2026-10-28	2026-10-21	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	0a0ed8a26adb-0f28-3e99-fc75be2255b5	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-23 19:41:47	agaia	0	0
57e578c66ae6-76ba-935c-65691c3ca81b	Ideas: collapse the ideas list with the board's gutter handle instead of text buttons	2026-10-31 16:59:03	2026-10-31 17:14:37	0	<p>aprom-4224 added a collapse button with a long text label ("Hide the ideas list") to the ideas browser header, and a separate "Show" button above the content when collapsed. The engineer wants the small handle that the task board and issue list use between their panels: <code>button.board-panel-divider &gt; span.divider-handle &gt; i.fa-angle-left|right</code> (<code>templates/app/project/board.hbs</code> ~l.45, <code>templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs</code> ~l.231, styles <code>styles/modules/issue.scss</code> ~l.566-608). The attached screen <code>ideas-dividers</code> shows it in the gap between the ideas list and the idea page. That screen also shows a second handle between the conversation and the plan: ignore it, it is a separate issue.</p><ul><li>In <code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>, remove the browser header's collapse button (<code>data-collapse-browser</code>) and the <code>.idea-browser-expand</code> block with its button (<code>data-expand-browser</code>), including the <code>idea-browser-toggle-label</code> spans.</li><li>Put one <code>board-panel-divider</code> button at the top of the outlet column (col-md-9 or col-md-12). It sits in the gutter because Bootstrap columns are <code>position: relative</code>. It shows <code>fa-angle-left</code> when the list is visible and <code>fa-angle-right</code> when it's hidden. Its title comes from the existing <code>views.app.idea.browser.collapse</code>/<code>expand</code> translations, reworded if needed. It calls the existing <code>toggleBrowser</code>. Keep the <code>data-collapse-browser</code>/<code>data-expand-browser</code> attributes on it for the tests.</li><li>Keep the state as is: <code>browserCollapsed</code> on <code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>, saved in localStorage.</li><li>Positioning in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code> under <code>.idea-wrapper</code> (the board's offsets are scoped to <code>.issue-details-container</code>): centred in the gutter when the list shows, flush with the left edge of the content when hidden. Remove the styles of the deleted buttons. Reuse the handle's look as it is.</li><li>Below the md breakpoint the columns stack: always show the list there and hide the handle, so a saved collapsed state can't hide the list on a phone.</li><li>Tests: update <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-browser.feature</code> (and steps): the handle hides the list and widens the content, clicking it again restores it, and the state survives a reload.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the ideas list has no text collapse buttons. A small crimson handle in the gap hides and shows the list, as on the task board. The idea page and New Idea page both follow it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Brainstorm/Plan divider between conversation and plan (separate issue), and squaring the handle's legacy rounded corners.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> ideas-dividers.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4239	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	298622786ae6-57e5-e410-8a6db3c1e068	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 17:14:37	aprom	0	0
b225b1c46adf-8b84-9a0f-2483784b9d45	adt-4143 follow-ups: workspace doc PR, how Talos runs the full gaia suite, design-review refactors, baseline container label mismatch	2026-10-26 22:01:22	2026-10-26 22:32:34	0	<p><b>Context.</b> adt-4143 (<a href="https://github.com/projects4me/dev-tools/pull/26">dev-tools#26</a>) made <code>ai test gaia</code> safe to run in the background: fingerprint at start, a dead-PID lock takeover, process-tree kill and the 0xC0000142 retry. Its handoff listed four items as not done. This issue covers them.</p>\n<p><b>1. Workspace doc edits: second PR in pr4m.</b> The agent and skill instructions live in the workspace repo (projects4me/pr4m), not dev-tools, so they need their own PR:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>.claude/agents/test-runner.md</code>, <code>.claude/skills/run-tests/SKILL.md</code>, <code>.claude/skills/ship-issue/SKILL.md</code>;</li>\n<li>run the full <code>ai test gaia</code> with <code>run_in_background</code> instead of a 600000 ms foreground call;</li>\n<li>replace "1-4 minutes" with the measured times (api ~9.5 min, baseline re-run ~16 min, until adt-4144 lands);</li>\n<li><code>--changed</code> while iterating;</li>\n<li>no repo edits while a full run is in flight.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>2. Decision: how Talos runs the full gaia suite.</b> Talos sets <code>CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_BACKGROUND_TASKS=1</code>, so its agents can't background the ~10 min run, and a 600 s foreground call can't hold it. Options to decide between:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>(a) land adt-4144 (copy-in test container, measured ~25× faster requests), which should bring the full run to ~1–2 min and make this moot;</li>\n<li>(b) Talos runs <code>ai test gaia</code> itself, outside the Claude session, before or after the agent's ship step, and feeds the result in (<code>test-last-gaia.json</code> is fingerprinted, so <code>ai ship</code> can trust it);</li>\n<li>(c) allow background tasks for the test step only;</li>\n<li>(d) split the run into per-mode calls (backend / acl / client), each under 600 s, plus a combining step that records one result.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Record the decision on the issue and implement it, or link it to adt-4144 if (a).</p>\n<p><b>3. Design-review follow-ups from dev-tools#26.</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Restore the previous signal handlers when <code>cmd_test</code> returns (try/finally), so a caller in the same process, such as <code>ai ship</code>, doesn't inherit them.</li>\n<li>Split <code>results.record()</code>: compute staleness (start vs end fingerprint) in one function, and write the result in another (single responsibility).</li>\n<li>Move the 0xC0000142 retry out of <code>prepare_test_db</code> into a <code>run_bash()</code> helper next to <code>find_bash()</code>, so every Git Bash launch from p4m gets it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>4. Baseline container left running: testenv label mismatch.</b> In the 2026-10-27 run, <code>p4m-test-gaia-test-8b10322f</code> stayed up after <code>baseline.require</code>'s <code>finally: p4m test clean --src &lt;baseline worktree&gt;</code>. adt-4143 traced it to a mismatch between the <code>p4m.test</code> label and the <code>--src</code> path (normalisation of the worktree path) but couldn't reproduce it. Reproduce it with a baseline run on Windows, compare the label against <code>norm(--src)</code>, fix it, and add a unittest.</p>\n<p><b>Checks:</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>pr4m PR merged for item 1;</li>\n<li>Talos decision recorded, with a Talos run of a gaia issue completing its full test step;</li>\n<li>dev-tools unittests for the signal restore, staleness split, <code>run_bash</code> retry and label/clean match;</li>\n<li>after a baseline run, <code>docker ps</code> shows no leftover <code>p4m-test-gaia-test-*</code> container for the baseline worktree.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Depends on:</b> adt-4143 (merged first). Item 2 may be resolved by adt-4144.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4145	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	8fe2ae046adf-8154-4904-8f5112ed5746	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	d7bb57b96adf-bcf9-d60d-7e15e7c69bc0	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-26 22:32:34	adt	0	0
9dcdbc566af1-35f0-87ea-14b325c2b25a	Talos: Gaia-agent discovery must never stop or change the local agents (isolation tests)	2026-11-09 11:46:37	2026-11-09 12:15:49	0	<p>Rule: the local agents (Nestor, Achilles/Odysseus, Agamemnon) must always work. Gaia-declared agents (e.g. Hera) are additive.</p><p><strong>Change:</strong> tests in <code>talos/tests</code> that start Talos's agents with the local agents plus Gaia discovery, and check that the local agents start and keep running when discovery:</p><ul><li>has no template, no <code>gaia-runtime/agent.local.json</code>, or no service identity;</li><li>raises while listing agents, building one (bad spec, unknown projects) or starting one;</li><li>loses its delegated token.</li></ul><p>Fix anything the tests expose so a discovery failure is only logged.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4411</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 2</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4416	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	712014526af0-7d1c-cccd-ee6dc2488b11	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	e57408d66af1-1f08-3228-4684b45b3d05	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 12:15:49	adt	0	0
