26acca216ad8-298c-c7bd-326be9a73cfb	Notifications: mark the current user's notifications for one entity as read (relatedTo/relatedId on POST systemnotificationrecipient)	2026-10-21 07:30:46	2026-10-23 20:25:02	0	<p>When a user opens an issue, Prometheus will ask Gaia to mark all of that user's unread notifications about it as read. Gaia already has a bulk mark-read call (<code>POST /api/v1/systemnotificationrecipient</code> with <code>markAllAsRead</code>). This issue adds an entity-scoped variant to that call, with no new route, using the <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code> columns on <code>Systemnotification</code> added by the linked issue.</p><ul><li><strong>Model:</strong> add <code>Systemnotificationrecipient::markRelatedAsRead($userId, $relatedTo, $relatedId)</code> next to <code>updateAllAsRead</code> in <code>app/models/Systemnotificationrecipient.php</code>. It sets <code>isRead = 1</code> on the user's unread recipient rows whose notification has the given <code>relatedTo</code> and <code>relatedId</code>, and returns the number of rows changed. Use bound parameters only.</li><li><strong>Controller:</strong> in <code>SystemnotificationrecipientController::postAction</code>, when both <code>relatedTo</code> and <code>relatedId</code> are sent, call <code>markRelatedAsRead</code>. Keep <code>markAllAsRead</code> as it is. If neither form is sent (or only one of the pair), return 400; today <code>$result</code> is undefined in that case.</li><li><strong>Security fix:</strong> both branches use the logged-in <code>$currentUser-&gt;id</code> and ignore any <code>userId</code> in the body. Today any user can mark another user's notifications as read.</li><li><strong>Response contract (Prometheus reads this):</strong> <code>{ "success": true, "markedCount": &lt;int&gt;, "meta": { "unreadCount": &lt;int&gt; } }</code>. <code>unreadCount</code> is computed the same way as in <code>patchAction</code>. Add the same <code>meta.unreadCount</code> to the <code>markAllAsRead</code> response.</li><li><code>tools/api-tester</code> cases: relatedTo=issue marks only that issue's notifications for the caller (including its comment and timelog notifications); other users and other entities are untouched; a body <code>userId</code> of another user has no effect; a missing or partial body returns 400.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a POST with <code>{"relatedTo": "issue", "relatedId": "&lt;id&gt;"}</code> marks the caller's unread notifications for that issue as read, returns <code>markedCount</code> and the new <code>unreadCount</code>, and changes nothing else. Mark-all still works, now scoped to the caller.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> Hermes events for read state; notifications created before the columns existed (NULL relatedId) are not matched.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4064</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4065	2026-10-28	2026-10-21	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	5625e2066adb-9b5b-6527-b5ea3d1b84f4	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-23 20:25:02	agaia	0	0
