2bc927e46ad8-298c-c7bd-447e80b75f65	Notifications: mark an issue's notifications read when the issue is viewed, and ring the bell	2026-10-21 07:30:51	2026-10-23 21:33:57	0	<p>When a user views an issue, their unread notifications about it should become read without clicking each one. Every place that shows an issue (detail page <code>templates/app/project/issue/page.hbs</code>, the list and board quick views, the Gantt <code>issue-details-panel</code>) renders <code>Issue::IssueDetails</code> (<code>app/components/issue/issue-details.js</code>), so the trigger goes there and not on model fetches, which also run when nobody is looking at the issue.</p><ul><li><strong>Model:</strong> add <code>@attr('string') relatedTo</code> and <code>@attr('string') relatedId</code> to <code>app/models/systemnotification.js</code> (new Gaia columns; <code>relatedTo</code> is the parent entity, so comment and timelog notifications carry <code>issue</code> and the issue id). This is separate from <code>context.relatedTo</code>, which the link generators keep using.</li><li><strong>Service:</strong> add <code>markRelatedAsRead(relatedTo, relatedId)</code> to <code>app/services/notifications.js</code>. If <code>unreadCount</code> is 0, it returns without a call. Otherwise it POSTs <code>{ relatedTo, relatedId }</code> to <code>systemnotificationrecipient</code> through the adapter, the same way <code>markAllAsRead</code> does (no Messenger toast). On success it: sets <code>unreadCount</code> from <code>meta.unreadCount</code>; flips <code>isRead</code> to '1' on loaded notifications with the same <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code> and removes their <code>unread-notification</code> class; posts a new BroadcastChannel message <code>MARK_RELATED_AS_READ</code> (relatedTo, relatedId, unreadCount), handled in <code>_handleCrossTabMessage</code>. Failures are logged and swallowed, because viewing an issue must never show an error for this.</li><li><strong>Trigger:</strong> <code>Issue::IssueDetails</code> calls <code>notifications.markRelatedAsRead('issue', @issue.id)</code> when it first renders an issue and again when <code>@issue</code> changes to a different id (for example clicking another card in a quick view). It does not call again for the same issue on re-render.</li><li><strong>Bell ring:</strong> when <code>markedCount &gt; 0</code>, the service sets a tracked flag that <code>components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs</code> (bell at line 46) uses to add a short ring class (CSS keyframe rotation, about 1s, then removed). Put the CSS in the header's existing module scss, honour <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>, and add no new colours or libraries. The bell does not ring when nothing was marked.</li><li><strong>Gaia contract</strong> (from the linked Gaia issue): <code>POST /api/v1/systemnotificationrecipient {"relatedTo", "relatedId"}</code> returns <code>{ success, markedCount, meta: { unreadCount } }</code>. Add a matching Mirage handler and the new fields to the Mirage notification factory or fixtures.</li><li><strong>Tests:</strong> an acceptance feature under <code>tests/acceptance/notification/</code> (opening an issue with unread notifications clears them in the sidebar and badge; the bell gets the ring class; with no unread, no request is sent) and unit coverage of the service method and the cross-tab message.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> opening an issue from the detail page, list quick view, board quick view or Gantt panel marks its notifications read in this tab and other open tabs, updates the badge and browser title count, and rings the bell only when something changed.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> marking read when an issue only appears in a list row; auto-read for milestones or projects (the service method is generic, so that is a later one-line trigger); any change to the per-notification click or mark-all behaviour.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4065</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	