6259a7486adf-9842-9a0f-5a2b0aaf0c87	Deployed Gaia image (devapi/qa): enable OPcache and stop loading Xdebug in develop mode	2026-10-26 22:08:34	2026-10-28 17:57:58	0	<p><b>Problem (likely, to be confirmed on the cluster first).</b> devapi.projects4.me (and qa) run <code>rananoman/gaia:&lt;branch&gt;</code>, built by <code>.github/workflows/cd-ovh.yml</code> from <code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code>: <code>FROM rananoman/gaia:env-dev</code> + <code>COPY</code> + <code>composer install</code> + <code>start.sh</code> (migrations, then <code>apache2-foreground</code>). Nothing in that chain enables OPcache. The local images built on the same <code>env-dev</code> base have <code>opcache.so</code> present but <b>not loaded</b>, and have <b>Xdebug 3.1.5 and xhprof loaded</b> (from the base layers). Without an ini setting, Xdebug 3 runs in <code>develop</code> mode, which adds overhead to every request on a shared server.</p>\n<p>Found while investigating slow <code>ai test gaia</code> runs (see adt-4144). There, OPcache alone cut per-request time on a slow filesystem from ~0.74 s to ~0.4–0.5 s. devapi has no bind mount, so the gain there is unmeasured, but PHP compile time is paid on every request without OPcache.</p>\n<p><b>What</b></p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Confirm on the cluster:</b> <code>kubectl exec deploy/&lt;gaia-dev deployment&gt; -- php -m | grep -iE "opcache|xdebug|xhprof"</code> and <code>php -i | grep -E "opcache.enable|xdebug.mode"</code>. Note that <code>php -m</code> is the CLI; check the Apache SAPI too, for example a temporary phpinfo or <code>opcache_get_status()</code>. Record the result on the issue.</li>\n<li><b>Measure before:</b> time a few representative requests on devapi (for example <code>curl -w "%{time_total}"</code> on a 401 and on an authenticated list) and record them.</li>\n<li><b>docker/dev/Dockerfile</b> (deployed image only, not the local dev compose setup):\n<ul>\n<li>enable OPcache: <code>docker-php-ext-enable opcache</code>, or a <code>conf.d/opcache.ini</code> with <code>opcache.enable=1</code>, <code>opcache.memory_consumption=128</code>, <code>opcache.max_accelerated_files=20000</code>, <code>opcache.validate_timestamps=0</code>. The code is baked into the image, so a deploy is a new container;</li>\n<li>remove the Xdebug ini (<code>docker-php-ext-xdebug.ini</code>) or set <code>ENV XDEBUG_MODE=off</code>. Prefer removing the ini so the extension isn't loaded at all. Same decision for xhprof, unless it's used for profiling on dev.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><b>Measure after</b> the deploy, with the same requests, and record them.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><b>Don't change:</b> local <code>gaia-dev</code> keeps Xdebug for debugging, and the test container's OPcache is handled in adt-4144.</p>\n<p><b>Also verify (not confirmed as a bug):</b> <code>cd-ovh.yml</code> runs <code>helm upgrade … -f values-${TARGET_BRANCH}.yaml</code>, but the repo has <code>helm/values-dev.yml</code> (<code>.yml</code>) next to <code>values-qa.yaml</code>. The command runs in <code>OVH_GAIA_HELM_PATH</code> on the server, so the server copy may be named correctly. Check it.</p>\n<p><b>Checks:</b> on devapi, OPcache is enabled for the Apache SAPI and Xdebug isn't loaded (or its mode is off); before and after timings are recorded; migrations still run on start; smoke-test login and an issue list.</p>\n<p><b>Depends on:</b> nothing. It deploys through the normal dev pipeline, so the reviewer merges and watches the deploy.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4146	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	706e04d26ae2-0ec0-7254-d02be976aca0	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 17:57:58	agaia	0	0
