1b7eab7368f0-e7f8-08bc-99fbf245acb6	Implement breadcrumb functionality	2025-10-16 13:11:55	2025-11-06 07:35:16	0	<p>Breadcrumb functionality was there in the product by using the ember-crumbly, but after our upgrade to the Ember Octane, that library doesn't support that at all.</p>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""><br>\nThat's why we have to come up with a custom implementation or use the existing library to implement that feature</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3725	2025-11-19	2025-10-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	f79e81a568f0-f6b3-5cb9-e5a2c76ef237	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	3d844677690b-2a67-a6e3-c12e9ab63bf8	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2025-11-06 07:35:13	aprom	0	0
753bcb466a67-865a-ea66-48f21c40fd33	Migrate RBAC from CRUD Resource Flags to Action-Based Permissions	2026-07-27 15:42:45	2026-08-03 10:47:25	0	<h3>Problem Statement</h3>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Today’s authorization model is&nbsp;resource-centric: permissions target a model (via&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resources</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resourceId</code>) and grant access through CRUD-style flags (<code data-backticks="1">readF</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">createF</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">updateF</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">deleteF</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">importF</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">exportF</code>). That design forces admins to reason about “Issue → Create flag” and “Issue.subject → Delete flag,” even though field-level delete (and most non-read field flags) are product-meaningless.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Enterprise products (Jira, Azure DevOps, Linear) grant&nbsp;named module actions&nbsp;(“Create Issue”, “Close Issue”), not opaque flag matrices. Gaia’s current model increases admin cognitive load, complicates role setup, and couples permission storage to an unnecessary&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resources</code>&nbsp;indirection.</span></p>\n<h3>Goal / Objective</h3>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Replace flag-based, resource-linked ACL with&nbsp;action-based RBAC&nbsp;where:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each module exposes grantable&nbsp;actions&nbsp;derived from controller&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">$aclMap</code>&nbsp;(defaults + customs).</li>\n<li>A permission is simply&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resourceName</code>&nbsp;(e.g.&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;issue.create&lt;/span&gt;</code>) +&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">allowed</code>&nbsp;(yes/no).</li>\n<li>Runtime authorization resolves the current request to&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">{module}.{action}</code>&nbsp;and checks that action.</li>\n<li>The action catalog is code-driven (no DB seeding of actions) and published to clients via system settings.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Scope of Work</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Introduce module/action catalog generation from REST controllers’&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">$aclMap</code>&nbsp;(<code data-backticks="1">AclMapCatalog</code>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;system.php&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;→&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">moduleActions</code>).</li>\n<li>Reshape&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">Permission</code>&nbsp;persistence:&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resourceName</code>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">allowed</code>; remove dependency on&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resourceId</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resources</code>&nbsp;table and CRUD&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">*F</code>&nbsp;columns.</li>\n<li>Update&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">PermissionController</code>&nbsp;defaults/list/create/update to use action catalog (no field-level permission rows in this revamp).</li>\n<li>Update runtime ACL to authorize by action resource (e.g.&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;issue.create&lt;/span&gt;</code>) instead of model + flag.</li>\n<li>Align&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">RestController</code>&nbsp;/ module controllers so defaults (<code data-backticks="1">get</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">create</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">update</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">delete</code>) and customs (e.g.&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">close</code>) map cleanly to actions.</li>\n<li>Expose catalog to frontend via&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">SystemsettingController</code>&nbsp;(<code data-backticks="1">moduleActions</code>, simplified&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">apiOptions</code>).</li>\n<li>Remove obsolete Resource API/model/routes and related wiring; update migrations/API contract artifacts as needed.</li>\n<li>Preserve membership → role path for user effective permissions (project-scoped ACL refinements deferred).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Permissions are granted per&nbsp;module action, not per CRUD flag on a resource/field.</li>\n<li>Default actions for ACL-enabled modules: get, create, update, delete (product-facing names may differ in UI later).</li>\n<li>Modules may declare additional custom actions in their controller&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">$aclMap</code>.</li>\n<li><code data-backticks="1">GET</code>&nbsp;permission defaults / role permission payloads list only catalog actions.</li>\n<li>Saving a permission persists&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resourceName</code>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">allowed</code>&nbsp;(binary allow / not set).</li>\n<li>Unauthorized action requests are denied according to configured resolution mode (permissive/restrictive).</li>\n<li>System settings expose&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">moduleActions</code>&nbsp;so clients can render role permission UIs without hardcoding action lists.</li>\n<li>Field-level resources (e.g.&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;Issue.subject&lt;/span&gt;</code>) are&nbsp;not&nbsp;part of the permission catalog in this release.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Admin/role APIs return action-based permission identities (<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;issue.get&lt;/span&gt;</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;issue.create&lt;/span&gt;</code>, …).</li>\n<li>Creating/updating permissions no longer requires&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resourceId</code>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">*F</code>&nbsp;flags.</li>\n<li>API requests are authorized by resolved module action for the controller method.</li>\n<li>Modules that opt out of ACL remain excluded from the catalog.</li>\n<li>Clients receive a stable action catalog from system settings for role configuration screens.</li>\n</ul>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3909	2026-07-28	2026-07-27	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	f1d8e6336a5f-5863-d50a-b12ddae1fd5c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	b9d22d426a67-1ac2-3423-96c8985ab713	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-08-03 10:47:25	agaia	0	0
dd999f196ad9-78e7-8fcc-651eb8c536b0	Translations: model, migration and public endpoint with a file cache	2026-10-22 07:06:05	2026-11-11 12:27:07	0	<p>Store UI translations in the database and serve them per locale through a public endpoint, cached as JSON files in the filesystem.</p>\n<h3>Scope</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Translation model + migration</b>: table <code>translations</code> with <code>id</code>, <code>locale</code> (e.g. <code>en-us</code>), <code>path</code> (dotted key, e.g. <code>views.app.issue.lists.status.in_progress</code>), <code>value</code>, the usual audit columns and <code>deleted</code>. Unique on <code>(locale, path)</code>.</li>\n<li><b>Supported locales</b> in Gaia config, starting with <code>en-us</code>.</li>\n<li><b>Public endpoints</b> (no auth, in the <code>app</code> routes next to <code>/image</code>):\n<ul>\n<li><code>GET /translations</code>: the supported locales.</li>\n<li><code>GET /translations/{locale}</code>: if <code>filesystem/translations/{locale}.json</code> exists, serve it. Otherwise build it from the DB as nested JSON (<code>a.b.c</code> → <code>{"a":{"b":{"c":…}}}</code>), write the file and serve it.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>{locale}</code> against the supported list before touching any path. Unsupported locale → 404.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><b>Cache invalidation</b>: creating, updating or deleting a translation deletes that locale's cached file.</li>\n<li><b>Seed</b>: idempotent <code>en-us</code> rows at <code>views.app.issue.lists.status.&lt;name&gt;</code> for the system statuses: new (New), in_progress (In Progress), in_review (In Review), done (Done), feedback (Feedback), pending (Pending), deferred (Deferred), wont_fix (Won't Fix).</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Notes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>RestController::setLanguage()</code> is unused (its call is commented out) and builds an include path from <code>Accept-Language</code>. Don't reuse it.</li>\n<li>Thin controller: validate the locale and return the file. One class reads/writes the cache file, one builds the nested document from rows; the path-to-nested conversion is a pure, unit-tested function.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Tests</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>First request builds and writes the file; the second serves the file without querying the DB.</li>\n<li>Changing a translation deletes the cached file; the next request returns the new value.</li>\n<li>Unsupported locale and path traversal (<code>../</code>) → 404, nothing read or written.</li>\n<li>Endpoints work without a token.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: complex</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4095	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	3f446a786ad9-497b-5f53-979db55a549e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-22 14:55:52	agaia	0	0
