1b80ab2369a5-550c-db9a-c63a028907e6	Activities in record views	2026-03-02 14:56:27	2026-03-06 15:23:43	0	<p>In the Project and Issue&nbsp; record view add bubble to the activities</p>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<ol>\n<li><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(92, 213, 251);" data-tomark-pass="">box-shadow</span>: <u data-tomark-pass="">rgba</u>(14,&nbsp;30,&nbsp;37,&nbsp;.12)&nbsp;0&nbsp;.2rem&nbsp;.4rem&nbsp;0,&nbsp;<u data-tomark-pass="">rgba</u>(14,&nbsp;30,&nbsp;37,&nbsp;.32)&nbsp;0&nbsp;.2rem&nbsp;1.6rem&nbsp;0;</li>\n<li><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(92, 213, 251);" data-tomark-pass="">background</span>: #f7f7f7;</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""><br>\n<img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="image.png"></p>\n<p>Also add the padding at the bottom of the issue activities screen in the project record view</p>\n	1	1	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	1	3826	2026-03-13	2026-03-02	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	1c5ba55169a5-edd6-cd30-52e2cd27f10c	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Hammad Hassan	Hammad Hassan	e554d33369a9-da5e-326e-c3e45e09c528	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-03-06 15:23:43	aprom	0	0
6ca2c4996a68-fe39-3c7d-102d97095b35	Align Role Permissions and ACL with Action-Based RBAC	2026-07-28 07:21:16	2026-07-28 13:51:47	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Update the frontend to consume Gaia’s new&nbsp;action-based&nbsp;authorization model. Role administration must stop presenting CRUD flag matrices and field-level permission rows, and instead allow admins to grant named module actions (e.g. Get Issue, Create Issue) via a simple allow/deny control.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">In parallel, the client ACL service must evaluate access using action identities (<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;issue.get&lt;/span&gt;</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;issue.create&lt;/span&gt;</code>) and the single&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">allowed</code>&nbsp;flag, while remaining compatible with existing template/route contexts (e.g.&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;Issue.read&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;→&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;issue.get&lt;/span&gt;</code>).</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">This delivers a clearer admin experience aligned with enterprise tools (Jira, Azure DevOps, Linear), removes meaningless field flags from the UI, and keeps navigation/button gating consistent with the backend catalog.</span></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Permission Ember Data models use&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resourceName</code>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">allowed</code>&nbsp;(remove&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">readF</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">createF</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">updateF</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">deleteF</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">importF</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">exportF</code>&nbsp;and related fields).</li>\n<li>Role Permissions tab groups grants by&nbsp;module, with one row per catalog action (<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;module.action&lt;/span&gt;</code>).</li>\n<li>Each action row exposes a single control bound to&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">allowed</code>&nbsp;(Not set / Allow / None) from flat&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">apiOptions</code>.</li>\n<li>Module and action labels are i18n-driven (<code data-backticks="1">modules.*</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">labels.{resourceName}</code>), not raw technical keys where product copy exists.</li>\n<li>Saving a new grant sends&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resourceName</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">roleId</code>, and&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">allowed</code>&nbsp;as required by the API adapter.</li>\n<li>Client&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">acl</code>&nbsp;service normalizes legacy contexts (<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;Issue.read&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;→&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;issue.get&lt;/span&gt;</code>) and checks&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">entity</code>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">allowed</code>.</li>\n<li>Route and&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">@aclContext</code>&nbsp;gating continue to work without requiring every template to be rewritten immediately.</li>\n<li>Mirage factories/handlers and acceptance coverage reflect action-catalog defaults and the simplified permission shape.</li>\n<li>System settings consumption no longer depends on&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">permissionFlags</code>; options come from simplified&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">apiOptions</code>&nbsp;(and catalog where used by Mirage/tests).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Opening a role’s Permissions tab shows modules as accordion sections; expanding a module lists only&nbsp;actions&nbsp;(no field rows, no multi-flag columns).</li>\n<li>Admin changes Allow/None/Not set for an action, saves, and sees progress/success/error feedback per row as today.</li>\n<li>UI elements and routes gated by ACL hide or allow access based on whether the mapped action is allowed for the current user.</li>\n<li>Unknown/unsupported actions (e.g. legacy import/export contexts) deny access rather than falling through on old flag columns.</li>\n<li>Tests for role permission rendering and sign-in ACL setup pass against the new Mirage permission contract.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>UI/UX Considerations</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Replace the wide 6-flag permission table with a compact&nbsp;Action | Access&nbsp;layout to reduce cognitive load.</li>\n<li>Use human-readable module/action labels (i18n); keep&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resourceName</code>&nbsp;as the stable identity, not the primary display string.</li>\n<li>Preserve accordion + save/cancel per module to avoid accidental mass edits.</li>\n<li>Keep loading (spinner), success (check), and error (times) states on each permission row during save.</li>\n<li>Ensure the table remains usable on smaller widths (<code data-backticks="1">table-responsive</code>); avoid reintroducing dense multi-column flag grids.</li>\n<li>Empty module / no-permission states should remain understandable (no cryptic empty flag cells).</li>\n<li>Prefer product language in labels (“Get”, “Create”, “Update”, “Delete”) over internal flag names.</li>\n</ul>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3910	2026-07-29	2026-07-28	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	1de107506a58-f3e9-094e-c2fc0df77006	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	df03c1576a68-4b25-d965-949947e62e92	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-07-28 13:51:45	aprom	0	0
