ad6c6ab86ad8-8856-55d8-8c72c21cf36a	Ideas: check that plan-issue and message references belong to the idea, and number concurrent plan versions safely	2026-10-21 15:18:05	2026-10-25 20:18:56	0	<p>Follow-up from the agaia-4069 design review. The Ideas resources check only <code>ideaId</code> against the project scope (through the <code>Idea</code> groupKeys path):</p><ul><li><code>Ideaplanissue.issueId</code> can name an issue in another project, and <code>Ideaplanissue.ideaplanId</code> / <code>Ideamessage.ideaplanId</code> can name a plan of another idea. Records can then link across projects, and <code>rels=issue</code> could show an issue the user can't otherwise see. Fix: add a domain-layer check (behaviour or validation) that the referenced plan belongs to the same idea, and that the referenced issue is in the idea's project or one the user can read. Note that plan items carry their own <code>project</code>, so decide first whether a plan may create issues in other projects (cross-project ideas were out of scope for 4069).</li><li><code>planVersionBehavior</code> computes max + 1 in a separate query. If two plans are created for one idea at the same moment, the unique <code>(ideaId, version)</code> index rejects the second, which returns a 500. Fix: retry on the unique violation, or lock the idea row while numbering.</li><li>Partial PATCH of a Comment or Activity that sends <code>relatedId</code> without <code>relatedTo</code> skips the parent-scope check on the new parent; merge the payload over the stored record before matching paths.</li></ul><p>Complexity: complex because it needs a design decision on cross-project plan items and the concurrency approach.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4075	2026-10-28	2026-10-21	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Achilles	