fd0311d46a69-4f66-99e1-2665e7041d6c	Remove Role Assignment from Project Membership	2026-07-29 07:38:37	2026-07-29 14:49:19	0	<p>Simplify the role assignment model by removing the concept of project-specific roles from project membership.</p>\n<p>Currently, a user's project membership includes a role assignment, making roles scoped to individual projects. This creates unnecessary complexity in role management and authorization, particularly as the product moves toward a model where users can have multiple roles assigned at the application level.</p>\n<p>Under the simplified model, roles will be assigned to users globally across the application rather than separately for each project. Project membership will therefore only represent the user's membership and relationship with the project, while role assignments will be managed independently.</p>\n<p>This change is a prerequisite for implementing the new group-based and hierarchical authorization model.<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove the role association from project membership.</li>\n<li>Remove project-specific role assignment and management logic from the backend.</li>\n<li>Ensure a project membership represents only the user's membership/access relationship with the project.</li>\n<li>Roles must be assigned to users at the application level rather than at the project level.</li>\n<li>A user may have multiple application-wide roles.</li>\n<li>Authorization checks must resolve the user's roles from their application-level role assignments.</li>\n<li>Remove project membership role data from relevant API request and response payloads.</li>\n<li>Update project membership creation and update operations so they no longer accept or process a role.</li>\n<li>Ensure removing a user from a project does not remove or modify their application-wide roles.</li>\n<li>Ensure assigning or removing an application-wide role does not directly modify project memberships.</li>\n<li>Update database relationships and constraints to remove the project membership → role dependency.</li>\n<li>Update existing migrations or provide a migration to safely remove the obsolete project membership role association.</li>\n<li>Update backend services, models, serializers, validators, and authorization logic that depend on project-specific roles.</li>\n<li>Ensure existing users and project memberships remain valid after the migration.</li>\n<li>Ensure the new model supports users having multiple roles simultaneously.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3>\n<p>A user's relationship with a project should no longer contain a role assignment.</p>\n<p>The conceptual model should be:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>User\n├── Application-wide Role 1\n├── Application-wide Role 2\n└── Project Membership\n    ├── Project A\n    ├── Project B\n    └── Project C\n</code></pre>\n<p>Instead of:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>User\n├── Project A\n│   └── Role A\n├── Project B\n│   └── Role B\n└── Project C\n    └── Role C\n</code></pre>\n<p>A user may have multiple application-wide roles, and those roles are not tied to a specific project membership.</p>\n<p>For example:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>User: John\n\nApplication Roles:\n- Project Manager\n- Developer\n\nProject Memberships:\n- Project A\n- Project B\n</code></pre>\n<p>John's roles are assigned globally and are not separately configured for Project A or Project B.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3912	2026-07-30	2026-07-29	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	f1d8e6336a5f-5863-d50a-b12ddae1fd5c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-07-29 14:49:17	agaia	0	0
