2e3651706adc-e2c6-179a-7062bd59d4a1	Nestor: plan cross-project issues as External Requests from the idea's project	2026-10-24 06:03:26	2026-10-27 14:39:13	0	<p>Ideas live in one project, but the work often spans several. For example, a Prometheus idea may need a new Gaia API. The engineer decided that Agent Nestor may keep planning issues in any project it can reach. An issue created outside the idea's own project, though, must be clearly marked as a request from that project and must be evaluated before anyone implements it. It stays a Task or Story, and its subject starts with <strong>External Request:</strong>. Today Nestor isn't told which project the idea belongs to, and approval creates every issue the same way.</p><ul><li><strong>Home project in the session prompt:</strong> <code>talos/lib/ideas/conversation.py</code> <code>Conversation.system_prompt</code> adds a line like <em>This idea belongs to A Prometheus (short code aprom)</em>. Resolve it from the idea's <code>projectId</code> (already returned by <code>lib/ideas/client.py</code> <code>idea()</code>) through the tracker's project ids and codes. <code>system_prompt</code> doesn't take the idea today, so pass it in. With the sim source, where an idea may have no project, leave the line out.</li><li><strong>Role rule:</strong> add a short section to <code>talos/agents/nestor/role.md</code> (Splitting the work). Plan the home project's work as usual. When the work needs a change in another project you can plan in, plan it there, but write it as a request: open with what the home project needs and why, then the proposed contract, and ask the receiving team to accept, adapt or decline it. Keep the type Task or Story. Don't add the External Request prefix yourself, because Talos adds it. Don't set it to blocker or critical, because that is the receiving project's call. The home-project issue that needs it lists it in <code>dependsOn</code>. In the reply, say which issues are external requests.</li><li><strong>Marking on approval, done by code:</strong> in <code>talos/lib/ideas/approval.py</code>, when an issue's project differs from the idea's project: (1) the subject passed to <code>tracker.create_issue</code> becomes <code>External Request: &lt;subject&gt;</code>; don't add it twice if the subject already starts with it. (2) <code>Approval.description</code> puts a first paragraph before the description: <code>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;External Request&lt;/strong&gt; from &lt;home project name&gt; (idea "&lt;title&gt;", raised by &lt;owner name&gt;). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.&lt;/p&gt;</code>. Same-project issues stay unchanged.</li><li><strong>Approval message:</strong> in <code>Approval._tell</code>, tag external requests in the chat line and in the note to Nestor, e.g. <code>agaia-4101 (rule-api, external request to A Gaia)</code>.</li><li><strong>Tests</strong> (Talos ideas tests, <code>ai test dev-tools</code>): an issue in another project gets the subject prefix (only once) and the paragraph, a home-project issue gets neither, the system prompt names the home project, and the <code>_tell</code> text tags external requests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> a plan for an idea in A Prometheus with one aprom issue and one agaia issue creates the aprom issue unchanged. The agaia issue's subject starts with <code>External Request: </code>, its description opens with the request paragraph, and its type is the one the plan gave (Task or Story). Nestor's prompt names the idea's project. The approval message shows which issues are external requests. Works on Windows and Linux as per the dev-tools rules.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> blocking or limiting cross-project creation (explicitly not wanted), showing refs to issues the user can't read as plain text in Prometheus (filed separately by the engineer), Gaia reference checks (agaia-4075), linking projects, a request badge on the plan card, and a dedicated issue type.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4107	2026-10-31	2026-10-24	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	5ad7f7536ae0-3811-7641-d221d7a42689	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-27 14:39:13	adt	0	0
