868de2746adc-6ec6-f97e-baeeb017a127	Notifications: open the issue in the current screen's quick view by relatedTo/relatedId (issue-preview service, task board first)	2026-10-24 14:07:02	2026-10-25 16:51:52	0	<p>Clicking a notification always goes to a URL built from its context. Notifications now carry <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code>, which name the entity they belong to (comment and time-log notifications point at their issue). When the screen you are on has an issue quick view and shows that issue, the click should open it there; otherwise it should open the issue detail page. This issue adds the mechanism and the task board as the first preview view.</p><ul><li><strong>New service <code>app/services/issue-preview.js</code></strong> (one responsibility: send an issue to the open screen that can preview it).<ul><li><code>register(owner, {hasIssue(issueId), open(issueId)})</code> returns a dispose function, following the pattern of <code>hermes.register</code>. One active registration: the screen that is open.</li><li><code>open(issueId)</code> returns <code>true</code> when the registered view has the issue and opened it, and <code>false</code> otherwise.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Task board:</strong> <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code> registers in <code>setupController</code> and disposes in <code>resetController</code> on exit, next to the Hermes intents. <code>hasIssue</code> looks for the id in the lanes on screen (<code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> <code>milestones</code>: open milestones plus backlog, already filtered by the search, as <code>findIssueById</code> does). <code>open</code> calls the existing <code>selectIssue(issue)</code>.</li><li><strong>Notification click</strong> (<code>components/app-ui/notifications/notification.js</code> <code>markAsRead</code>):<ul><li>When <code>notification.relatedTo === 'issue'</code>: mark the notification read, then call <code>issuePreview.open(notification.relatedId)</code>. If no view took it, transition to <code>app.project.issue.page</code> with the project shortcode and issue number from the notification's context. These are only route parameters; the target is always <code>relatedId</code>.</li><li>A notification without <code>relatedId</code> is only marked read.</li><li>Clicks on a user avatar or user link, and notifications whose <code>relatedTo</code> is milestone or project, behave as today.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Group heading</strong> (<code>components/app-ui/notifications/group.js</code> <code>goToIssue</code>): same flow, using the <code>relatedId</code> of the group's notifications. Modifier and middle clicks still let the browser open the <code>href</code> in a new tab.</li><li><strong>Live notifications:</strong> check that the <code>notification.created</code> envelope's <code>changes</code> includes <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code> (<code>services/notifications.js</code> <code>onNotificationCreated</code>). If it doesn't, file a Gaia issue rather than reading the context.</li><li>Keep the <code>config.app.notifications.enableNav</code> gate.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>On the task board, clicking an issue, comment or time-log notification (or the group heading) whose issue is in a lane on the board opens the board's quick view. The URL doesn't change, and the notifications are marked read.</li><li>If the issue isn't on the board (other project, filtered out, completed milestone), or you aren't on the board, the click opens the issue detail page.</li><li>After you leave the board, its registration is disposed.</li><li>Unit tests for the service. Mirage acceptance tests under <code>tests/acceptance/notification/</code> for the quick view and the fallback.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the issue list and gantt (next issue), scrolling to the comment or time log in the quick view, and milestone and project notifications.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4117</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4118	2026-10-31	2026-10-24	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	98dbfcd76adc-5af1-8c3d-53b434d35ac1	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-25 16:51:52	aprom	0	0
