cad135f26adc-e07b-a0a9-8a51ae1aaf9d	Ideas: created issues in projects the user can't read show as plain text, not links	2026-10-24 06:10:18	2026-10-24 07:10:03	0	<p>A plan approved in one project can create issues in other projects (for example a frontend idea that needs a new API in the backend project). Users should still see every issue their idea created. But a link to an issue in a project they are not a member of only leads to a permission-denied page. So on the idea page, a created issue is a link only when the user can read its project. Otherwise it is plain text. Gaia still decides who can read what. This change only decides whether a link is shown.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>: add a getter for the project ids the user can read: the idea's <code>projectId</code> plus the ids in <code>currentUser.user.projects</code> (<code>services/current-user.js</code> already loads them with <code>include: 'projects'</code>). Pass it to <code>Idea::CreatedIssuesBox</code> and <code>Idea::PlanBox</code> in <code>templates/app/project/idea/page.hbs</code> (for example <code>@readableProjectIds</code>). Don't add new API calls.</li><li><code>components/idea/created-issues-box.{hbs,js}</code>: render the <code>LinkTo</code> (line ~11) only when <code>link.issue.projectId</code> is in the readable ids. Otherwise show the same <code>SHORTCODE-NUMBER</code> and subject as muted text (<code>text-muted</code>), with no anchor.</li><li><code>components/idea/plan-box.{hbs,js}</code>: in the <code>createdIssues</code> getter (~l.141), also record whether each created issue is readable. In the template (~l.42), render the <code>fa-external-link</code> <code>LinkTo</code> only for readable ones. Show the others as muted text with the issue key.</li><li>Handle a link with no issue: Gaia may stop returning issues the user can't read through <code>rels=issue</code>. An <code>ideaplanissue</code> with no loaded issue must not crash or show an empty link. In Created Issues, show the plan item's key and subject from the plan body (item with the same <code>key</code>) as muted text. In the plan box, show no created-issue reference for that item.</li><li>Don't add a tooltip or a new style. Use the existing <code>text-muted</code> class. Put any new string in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A created issue in the idea's project, or in a project the user belongs to, is a link to <code>app.project.issue.page</code>, as it is today.</li><li>A created issue in a project the user doesn't belong to shows its key (and subject in Created Issues) as plain text in both boxes, with no anchor element.</li><li>An <code>ideaplanissue</code> whose <code>issue</code> is missing renders without errors, as plain text from the plan item.</li><li>Mirage data covers all three cases. Integration tests for <code>Idea::CreatedIssuesBox</code> and <code>Idea::PlanBox</code> check link vs. plain text. The existing idea tests still pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong></p><ul><li>Gaia-side checks on <code>Ideaplanissue.issueId</code> / <code>ideaplanId</code> scope (filed separately in A Gaia).</li><li>Marking plan items that target another project as external requests.</li><li>Special read rules for admins who aren't members of a project (they see plain text).</li></ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4108	2026-10-31	2026-10-24	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	a4e6f2c26adc-d3fe-2863-36dc2a0cdd54	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-24 07:10:03	aprom	0	0
