e2b741406ad3-3667-878f-ae22ee198b78	Make task board and issue status labels data-driven (colour, order, translated names)	2026-10-17 20:56:02	2026-11-11 12:27:38	0	<p>Follow-up split from #3966 (Settings: Issue Statuses page). Acceptance criterion: <b>changes made in Settings &gt; Issue Statuses appear on the task board and issue labels after reload.</b> Depends on #3966 and Gaia #3960 (<code>color</code>, <code>sortOrder</code> on Issuestatus).</p>\n<p><b>Current state (hardcoded):</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Board lanes: <code>statuses</code> getter in <code>app/controllers/app/project/board.js</code> is a hardcoded array (new, in_progress, in_review, done, feedback, pending, deferred).</li>\n<li>Lane header colour comes from CSS classes by status name (<code>app/styles/issue/issue-status.scss</code>, used via <code>get-prop @statusClass status.name</code> in <code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code>).</li>\n<li>Badges in about 10 templates use <code>class="badge {{status}}"</code>: issue-details, task-row (gantt), conversation-item, widgets recent-issues, active-milestones, weekly-issue-timelogs, etc.</li>\n<li>Labels use translation keys <code>views.app.issue.lists.status.&lt;name&gt;</code>. Hammad confirmed the displayed label must remain the translated value (multi-language); a status without a translation key should fall back to its name.</li>\n<li>The board loads the project's own status copies (<code>Issuestatus.projectId</code>) and falls back to system statuses (<code>Issuestatus.system : 1</code>) only if the project has none. Decide how project copies follow system status edits (open question; likely needs Gaia input).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Scope:</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Board lanes built from the loaded statuses ordered by <code>sortOrder</code>, not the hardcoded list.</li>\n<li>A helper/style source that applies a status <code>color</code> (inline) to lane headers and badges, falling back to the existing CSS class.</li>\n<li>Translated label with name fallback for statuses that have no translation.</li>\n<li>Mirage factory gains <code>color</code>/<code>sortOrder</code>; acceptance tests for board order and badge colour.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Design points for the implementer: single responsibility (one helper for colour, one for label), no per-template logic; check every template listed above.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	3976	2026-10-25	2026-10-18	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	cf0cb1306ad7-7919-8702-4eaeb438fafd	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-22 06:52:56	aprom	0	0
