2c2efb536ad8-7aac-fae6-82e385f2f1c2	Keep issues.status in step when an issue status is renamed	2026-10-21 09:51:40	2026-10-21 13:35:59	0	<p>Found while addressing review on Prometheus #3976 (PR projects4me/prometheus#536).</p>\n<p><code data-tomark-pass="">issues.status</code> is a copy of the status name. The <code data-tomark-pass="">add_issue_status</code> / <code data-tomark-pass="">update_issue_status</code> triggers on Issue (app/models/Issue.php, from #3600) only set it on insert or when <code data-tomark-pass="">statusId</code> changes. Renaming a status in Settings &gt; Issue Statuses (#3960) leaves its issues with the old name. Any screen that reads <code data-tomark-pass="">issue.status</code> then shows a stale label and colour: the badges in issue details, widgets and the gantt chart. The task board in Prometheus now matches issues to lanes by <code data-tomark-pass="">statusId</code>, so the board itself is fine.</p>\n<h3 data-tomark-pass="">Chosen implementation\n</h3>Use a database trigger on <code data-tomark-pass="">issue_statuses</code>, not an Issuestatus model hook. The existing triggers on <code data-tomark-pass="">issues</code> can't be reused: they only fire when an issue row changes, and a rename only changes the issue\\_statuses row.\n<ol data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Check whether an update trigger already exists on <code data-tomark-pass="">issue_statuses</code> (e.g. <code data-tomark-pass="">update_issue_statuses</code>). If it does, extend it. Otherwise add a new <code data-tomark-pass="">AFTER UPDATE</code> trigger.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">The trigger logic: when <code data-tomark-pass="">NEW.name &lt;&gt; OLD.name</code>, run <code data-tomark-pass="">UPDATE issues SET status = NEW.name WHERE statusId = NEW.id</code>. Check the real column names against the schema.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Define the trigger in the Issuestatus model, the same way the Issue triggers are defined in app/models/Issue.php, and add a migration that creates it on existing databases.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">The existing <code data-tomark-pass="">update_issue_status</code> trigger on issues will still fire for each updated row. It only sets <code data-tomark-pass="">status</code> when <code data-tomark-pass="">statusId</code> changes, so it won't overwrite the new name. Confirm this while testing.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Test: rename a status in Settings &gt; Issue Statuses and check that its issues show the new name in issue details, widgets and the gantt chart.</li></ol><h3 data-tomark-pass="">Decision: project copies\n</h3>System issue statuses and project statuses are separate. Renaming a system status does **not** rename the project copies of it, so project statuses and their issues keep their names. The trigger only updates issues whose <code data-tomark-pass="">statusId</code> is the renamed row, so it does this without any extra logic. Do not add code that spreads a rename to project copies.\n<p>Renaming a project's own status works the same way: its issues follow, because they point at that status by <code data-tomark-pass="">statusId</code>.</p>\n<p>Test this too: rename a system status and check that a project copy of it, and that project's issues, are unchanged.</p>\n<h3 data-tomark-pass="">Decision: status name length (30 characters)\n</h3><code data-tomark-pass="">issues.status</code> was <code data-tomark-pass="">varchar(12)</code> and <code data-tomark-pass="">issue_statuses.name</code> was <code data-tomark-pass="">varchar(255)</code>, so with the trigger a rename to more than 12 characters failed. Both columns become <code data-tomark-pass="">varchar(30)</code> in this PR:\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Widen <code data-tomark-pass="">issues.status</code> to 30. This means extending <code data-tomark-pass="">core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> so it can alter column type and length, and handling the dependent view <code data-tomark-pass="">user_latest_issues</code>.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Shrink <code data-tomark-pass="">issue_statuses.name</code> to 30. First check for existing names over 30 characters, and report them rather than truncating them.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">The API returns 422 for names over 30 characters. Check this on create, and on update only when the name changes.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Test that a 30-character name works for rename and issue create, and that a 31-character name gets a 422.</li></ul>Complex because it needs a migration-tool change, a trigger and a schema change.\n<p>Complexity: complex</p>\n	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4067	2026-10-28	2026-10-21	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Odysseus	Rana Nouman	a37893056ad8-b698-0c8e-590b00d38a54	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-21 13:35:47	agaia	0	0
