a436a6216ade-bc23-4a93-a91bf7571305	Live events: include relatedTo and relatedId on notification.created	2026-10-25 17:34:28	2026-10-25 20:37:28	0	<p>agaia-4064 added <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code> to <code>system_notifications</code>, and Prometheus now relies on them. Viewing an issue marks its notifications read (aprom-4066), and clicking a notification opens its issue in the current screen's quick view (aprom-4118, aprom-4119). The live <code>notification.created</code> event doesn't send these two fields, so a notification that arrives through Hermes while the page is open has neither. It is then never marked read when its issue is viewed, and its click skips the quick view. After a page reload the REST load includes them and both features work, which is how the bug was spotted.</p><ul><li>Add <code>relatedTo</code> and <code>relatedId</code> to <code>NOTIFICATION_FIELDS</code> in <code>app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/NotificationLiveEvents.php</code> (they are copied into <code>changes</code> when set, like the other fields).</li><li>Extend <code>tests/api/controllers/components/events/LiveEventsComponentsTest.php</code> (<code>testNotificationLiveEventsPicksAllowlistedFields</code> or a new case): the posted <code>changes</code> contain both fields when the notification has them and leave them out when they are NULL. Write it first and watch it fail.</li><li>Update the notification row in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/architecture.md</code> if it lists the payload fields.</li></ul><p><strong>Contract:</strong> two extra keys in the existing <code>changes</code> of <code>notification.created</code>. The event name is unchanged, so Hermes needs no change. Prometheus <code>services/notifications.js</code> <code>onNotificationCreated</code> already pushes every key of <code>changes</code> onto the <code>systemnotification</code> record, whose model has both attributes.</p><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A <code>notification.created</code> envelope for an issue, comment or time-log notification carries <code>relatedTo: issue</code> and the issue id in <code>changes</code>. Milestone and membership notifications carry their own values.</li><li>Manual check in the running app: with an issue's notification arriving live (no reload), opening that issue marks it read and rings the bell, and clicking it on the task board opens the board's quick view.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> backfilling old rows (agaia-4117), and any other notification field.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4122	2026-11-01	2026-10-25	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	0ff3f0a16ade-9b04-57f3-d1d74aed8292	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-25 20:37:28	agaia	0	0
