432bd1776a6c-f42c-f859-9809d085125b	Revamp ACL Authorization with Group-Based Access Control	2026-07-31 09:52:03	2026-08-04 12:27:17	0	<p>Revamp Gaia's ACL authorization model to support group-based access control for resources that belong to or depend on one or more parent groups.</p>\n<p>Currently, ACL authorization evaluates a resource's permission independently. This can result in users being able to access a child resource even when they do not have access to its parent resource.</p>\n<p>For example, if a user has <code data-backticks="1">0</code> access to a <code data-backticks="1">Project</code> but <code data-backticks="1">1</code> access to an <code data-backticks="1">Issue</code>, the current implementation may still return the Issue. This is not logically correct because an Issue belongs to a Project and should not be accessible when the user cannot access the Project.</p>\n<p>The same principle applies to conversations and their dependent resources. If a user cannot access a <code data-backticks="1">Conversation</code>, they should not be able to access its <code data-backticks="1">Comments</code>, even if they have direct permission on the Comment resource.</p>\n<p>The ACL model should therefore introduce the concept of <strong>authorization groups</strong>. A group represents a parent/context resource that controls access to its dependent child resources.</p>\n<p>For the initial implementation, the supported groups are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code data-backticks="1">Project</code></li>\n<li><code data-backticks="1">Conversation</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>A resource may belong to one or multiple groups. Access to a resource should only be granted when the user has the required permission for the resource itself <strong>and</strong> has the required access to <strong>all of its associated groups</strong>.<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Revamp the ACL service to support group-based authorization.</li>\n<li>Introduce the concept of authorization groups for dependent resources.</li>\n<li>Initially support the following authorization groups:\n<ul>\n<li>Project</li>\n<li>Conversation</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Allow a resource to define one or multiple group dependencies.</li>\n<li>Evaluate the user's access to the requested resource.</li>\n<li>Evaluate the user's access to every required group associated with that resource.</li>\n<li>Require all applicable authorization checks to pass before returning or exposing the resource.</li>\n<li>If access to any required group is denied, the dependent resource must also be denied.</li>\n<li>Apply group-based authorization to direct API access.</li>\n<li>Apply group-based authorization to resources returned through relationships.</li>\n<li>Apply group-based authorization to nested relationships.</li>\n<li>Ensure relationship loading cannot bypass group-level authorization.</li>\n<li>Ensure collection endpoints filter out resources that fail any required group authorization check.</li>\n<li>Ensure detail endpoints deny access when any required group authorization check fails.</li>\n<li>Ensure the authorization logic is centralized and reusable across models.</li>\n<li>Avoid hardcoding authorization dependency logic directly into individual API controllers wherever possible.</li>\n<li>Ensure the implementation supports resources with multiple group dependencies.</li>\n<li>Ensure a resource with multiple groups requires access to all groups before it can be returned.</li>\n<li>Ensure the model is extensible so additional authorization groups can be introduced in the future.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3>\n<p>The effective authorization model should be:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>Resource Access\n      +\nAccess to ALL Required Groups\n      =\nResource Can Be Accessed\n</code></pre>\n<p>If any required group is inaccessible:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>Resource Access = Allowed\nGroup A Access = Allowed\nGroup B Access = Denied\n\nResult → Resource Access Denied\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Example 1 — Issue Belongs to Project</h3>\n<pre><code>Project Access: 0\nIssue Access:   1\n</code></pre>\n<p>Result:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>Issue → NOT returned\n</code></pre>\n<p>The user cannot access the Issue because the Issue's authorization group is the Project, and the user does not have access to that Project.</p>\n<p>If:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>Project Access: 1\nIssue Access:   1\n</code></pre>\n<p>Result:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>Issue → Returned\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Example 2 — Comment Belongs to Conversation</h3>\n<pre><code>Conversation Access: 0\nComment Access:     1\n</code></pre>\n<p>Result:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>Comment → NOT returned\n</code></pre>\n<p>The user cannot access the Comment because they cannot access the Conversation that contains it.<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<h3>Example 3 — Comment Has Multiple Groups</h3>\n<p>A Comment may have multiple authorization groups:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>Project\n   └── Conversation\n         └── Comment\n</code></pre>\n<p>The Comment therefore has two required authorization groups:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>Comment Groups:\n- Project\n- Conversation\n</code></pre>\n<p>The user must have access to both:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>Project Access:     1\nConversation Access: 1\nComment Access:      1\n\nResult → Comment returned\n</code></pre>\n<p>If either group is inaccessible:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>Project Access:     1\nConversation Access: 0\nComment Access:      1\n\nResult → Comment NOT returned\n</code></pre>\n<p>Or:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>Project Access:     0\nConversation Access: 1\nComment Access:      1\n\nResult → Comment NOT returned\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Relationship Behavior</h3>\n<p>Group-based ACL checks must also apply when resources are returned as relationships.</p>\n<p>For example:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>GET /api/v1/projects?rels=issues\n</code></pre>\n<p>Only Issues for which the user has:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Required Issue access</li>\n<li>Required Project group access</li>\n</ul>\n<p>should be returned.</p>\n<p>Similarly:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>GET /api/v1/conversations?rels=comments\n</code></pre>\n<p>Comments should only be returned when the user has:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Required Comment access</li>\n<li>Required Conversation group access</li>\n<li>Any additional required group access, such as Project</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Unauthorized child resources should be filtered out rather than allowing relationship loading to bypass group authorization.</p>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""><br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3916	2026-08-01	2026-07-31	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	8d2dc2996a70-1635-52c1-7e0683d8ced6	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	131c05456a70-1635-52c1-e3641a956da9	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-08-04 12:27:17	agaia	0	0
