28b27d706aee-a7e9-ca02-43ba8c8b654c	EzSearch::ValueEditor: value input by field type and operator	2026-11-06 21:39:52	2026-11-07 00:15:52	0	<p>The ezSearch visual builder needs a value input that matches the condition's field type and operator. This standalone component is used by <code>EzSearch::Condition</code> in the Panel issue. No page uses it yet.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search/value-editor.{js,hbs}</code>: <code>&lt;EzSearch::ValueEditor @field @operator @value @onChange /&gt;</code>, where <code>@field</code> is a schema field with its values (query-schemas issue) and <code>@operator</code> is a registry entry (query-model issue). The input by type and operator:<ul><li>Enum fields: <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> (<code>@relateType="relate-simple"</code>).</li><li>User fields: the same, with avatars as in the existing user selects.</li><li>IN and NOT IN: <code>FormFields::FieldMultiSelect</code> (or <code>FieldRelateMulti</code>, whichever the forms use for static options), giving an array.</li><li>Dates: <code>FormFields::FieldDate</code>, and two of them with a translated "and" for BETWEEN. The output is always <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>.</li><li>Text and number fields: <code>FormFields::FieldText</code>.</li><li>Operators with arity 0 (NULL, EMPTY): no input.</li></ul></li><li><code>@onChange(value)</code> passes values in the shape <code>ast.condition</code> expects (string, array, or [from, to]). It never mutates <code>@value</code>.</li><li>The controls fill their column so they stack on mobile (screen <code>mobile-views</code>).</li><li>Placeholders go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.valueEditor.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>Each type and operator combination renders the right control and emits the right value shape.</li><li>A date picked through FieldDate is emitted as <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>.</li><li>Switching the operator from <code>:</code> to IN turns a single value into a one-item array.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> rows, groups, the panel.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4295</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> builder-open.png, mobile-views.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4298	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	ec8f13d96aee-170f-af4c-311adf05713e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 00:15:52	aprom	0	0
