4edde8616adc-9973-8304-aa49e4158097	Ideas: rich text editor with toolbar for the message composer	2026-10-24 07:16:30	2026-10-24 11:23:44	0	<p>The idea message composer is a 2-row plain textarea, which is too small for real messages and has no formatting. Give it the same editor issue comments use. Gaia's <code>Ideamessage.body</code> is already an unlimited <code>text</code> column, so this is UI only.</p><ul><li><code>components/idea/composer.{hbs,js}</code>: replace <code>FormFields::FieldTextArea</code> with <code>AppUi::ToastUi</code> (<code>@editType='wysiwyg'</code>, toolbar shown, <code>@hide={{array 'footer'}}</code>), as in <code>components/conversation-ui/message-box.hbs</code>. Keep the Send button (<code>AppUi::Button</code>, <code>@aclContext="ideamessage.create"</code>). <strong>Ctrl+Enter or Send</strong> sends, as in issue comments (<code>@onKeyboardSubmit</code>). Plain Enter adds a new line. While sending or when the idea is archived, the composer is disabled. After a successful send the editor is cleared (the modifier resets on <code>clearContents</code> from its pubSub; see how comments clear). On failure the text is kept.</li><li><strong>Messages stay markdown.</strong> The thread renders bodies with <code>modifiers/render-markdown.js</code>, and the planning agent reads and writes markdown. <code>modifiers/initialize-toastui.js</code> only emits <code>editor.getHtml()</code> (change event ~l.189 and keyboard submit ~l.239). Add an optional named argument (e.g. <code>output='markdown'</code>) that emits <code>editor.getMarkdown()</code> instead, passed through by <code>components/app-ui/toast-ui.hbs</code>. The default stays HTML, so the other editors don't change. The create page and inline images (separate issues) build on this.</li><li>No user mentions or issue search for now: pass no <code>usersList</code>/<code>issueSearch</code>, and make sure the editor and its Tribute setup work without them.</li><li>The editor's height should be comfortable for a few paragraphs, like the issue comment box. Square edges per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a message with headings, a list, bold text and a code block is sent from the toolbar and renders formatted in the thread. The stored body is markdown. Ctrl+Enter and the Send button both send. The editor clears after a successful send and keeps the text on a failure. An archived idea's composer is disabled. Other ToastUi editors still emit HTML. Integration tests for the composer, and the markdown option covered.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> mentions, issue links, images (separate issue), editing sent messages, the create page.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4110	2026-10-31	2026-10-24	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	ac6af3216ad8-d753-535b-b21c3700739d	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	1a9941d56adc-2d6f-802e-32a4692dd47e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-24 11:23:44	aprom	0	0
