acbb0b086ad9-a767-e557-927702485caf	Talos: run from a separate runtime copy of dev-tools, so dev-tools issues don't change the tooling under running agents	2026-10-21 22:33:16	2026-10-21 23:24:33	0	<p>Since adt-4083, Odysseus works A Dev Tool issues. But Talos, <code>ai</code>, gaia-mcp, Nestor, sim and the agent prompts all run from the same <code>dev-tools</code> checkout, the one a dev-tools issue edits and checks out branches in. While such an issue is worked:</p><ul><li>every <code>ai test</code>/<code>ai ship</code> (including the agent's own later steps) runs half-edited tooling;</li><li><code>agent.json</code> and the role prompts are read for each run, so a branch switch changes how other agents behave;</li><li>the running Talos keeps its old code in memory while its files change on disk. An issue that changes Talos itself (e.g. adt-4077) is the worst case.</li></ul><p>Changes:</p><ul><li>A runtime copy of dev-tools for Talos and the agents' tooling: <code>git worktree add</code> on <code>main</code> at e.g. <code>Pr4M/.dev-tools-runtime</code>, or a separate clone. Talos, the <code>ai</code> wrapper the agents call, gaia-mcp and the agent configs run from it. The <code>dev-tools</code> checkout stays a normal working copy for issues.</li><li>Keep the per-machine files in one place. <code>state/</code> (talos.db, logs, kb.db, timers), <code>*.local.json</code>, <code>gaia-mcp/*.env</code> and the sim state stay in their current location, or move to a shared state folder. Their paths must not depend on which copy is running.</li><li>Update the runtime copy explicitly: <code>p4m runtime update</code> (or <code>talos update</code>) fast-forwards it to <code>origin/main</code>, refusing while a Talos run is active. After that, <code>talos run</code> needs a restart, or restarts itself between runs.</li><li>Agents still work on the real repos (<code>gaia</code>, <code>prometheus</code>, <code>dev-tools</code>…), but call <code>ai</code> from the runtime copy. The prompts and skills mention <code>dev-tools/ai/ai</code>; route them through a stable path or an environment variable.</li><li>Set it up in <code>p4m setup</code>/<code>p4m configure</code>, and document it in the Talos README and <code>dev-tools/CLAUDE.md</code>. Windows and Linux.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> while Odysseus works a dev-tools issue on its branch, another issue's <code>ai test</code>/<code>ai ship</code> and Talos itself keep using <code>main</code>'s tooling. A merged dev-tools PR takes effect only after the runtime update.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4084	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	221316c56ad9-83b8-ef89-6c6ac1ec05ba	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-21 23:24:33	adt	0	0
