e0ce9be66adc-7635-8c3d-af4913939821	Notifications: include relatedTo and relatedId in the notification.created live event	2026-10-24 16:25:04	2026-10-25 20:41:36	0	<p>The <code>notification.created</code> envelope's <code>changes</code> carries only <code>NotificationLiveEvents::NOTIFICATION_FIELDS</code> (description, context, createdUser, createdUserName, dateCreated). It doesn't include <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code>, which agaia-4064 added to system notifications.</p><p>Prometheus (aprom-4118) opens a notification's issue from <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code>. A notification that arrives live has neither field until the page reloads, so clicking it only marks it read and doesn't open the issue.</p><ul><li>Add <code>relatedTo</code> and <code>relatedId</code> to <code>NOTIFICATION_FIELDS</code> in <code>app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/NotificationLiveEvents.php</code>.</li><li>Update the live-updates contract doc and the PHPUnit test for the envelope's fields.</li></ul><p>This adds fields to an existing event and doesn't rename anything, so Hermes needs no change.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4121	2026-10-31	2026-10-24	wont_fix	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	b080e6826ade-8333-57f3-ae9027d55a54	57f2151162c6-8e43-a8e0-a01f2b171f5b	2026-10-25 20:41:36	agaia	0	0
523739126ad7-63bd-e708-4d55d427eee4	Agent Nestor in Talos: ideas brainstorming through sim Gaia/Hermes, Nestor UI, issue creation on approval	2026-10-20 20:38:42	2026-10-21 13:42:27	0	<p>Brainstorm an idea with <strong>Agent Nestor</strong>, refine it into an implementation plan, and on approval create the issues in Gaia. The flow is built the way it will run once Prometheus, Gaia and Hermes support ideas, with local stand-ins for the parts that don't exist yet:</p><ul><li><strong>dev-tools/nestor</strong>: <em>only the UI</em> (static files and a small server that proxies to the stand-ins as the engineer). Later the Prometheus Ideas page.</li><li><strong>dev-tools/sim</strong>: temporary stand-ins.<ul><li><strong>Sim Gaia</strong>: CRUD resources <code>idea</code>, <code>ideamessage</code>, <code>ideaplan</code> and <code>ideaissue</code> (SQLite). Every write publishes a domain event.</li><li><strong>Sim Hermes</strong>: the same envelope (<code>schemaVersion</code>, <code>eventName</code>, <code>projectId</code> <code>user:&lt;id&gt;</code>, <code>resource</code>, <code>actorId</code>, <code>changes</code>, <code>meta</code>), the intents model and the <code>/publish</code> with a secret. Delivery is over SSE.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Talos</strong>: the agent lives here. <code>agents/nestor</code> is a new agent kind <code>ideas</code>, with per-agent event subscriptions and an event source (real Hermes for Odysseus, sim Hermes for Nestor).<ul><li>On <code>idea.message.created</code> from the engineer, Talos runs <code>claude -p</code> in the workspace (read-only, streamed), publishes <code>idea.agent.progress</code>, and posts the reply and any plan version back to sim Gaia.</li><li>On <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code> to approved, Talos creates the plan's issues <strong>deterministically through the gaia MCP client</strong> as Agent Nestor (dependency order, resumable) and records them on the idea.</li></ul></li><li>Odysseus is unchanged.</li></ul><p>Follow-ups for later issues:</p><ul><li>Gaia idea resources and events, plus the Hermes allowlist.</li><li>A Hermes path for agent progress events.</li><li>A Prometheus Ideas page.</li><li><code>p4m configure</code> for Nestor.</li></ul><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4061 (in review).</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4062	2026-10-28	2026-10-21	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7eedd6116ad7-b7ec-4943-1bf14eaae825	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	a0dad7676ad8-aaa6-095f-ed9b6955cf0a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-21 13:42:27	adt	0	0
be4df81768f0-3892-adb3-2af50c7985f8	Dashboard Changes	2025-10-16 12:49:02	2025-11-04 07:04:20	0	<h3><strong>Problem Statement</strong></h3>\n<p>Currently, the Dashboard’s widget interactions present several usability issues that affect data visibility and user flow.<br>\nUsers are required to manually open conversations within the <em>Weekly Conversations</em> widget each time, and filters applied in the <em>Recent Issues</em> widget are not retained when loading more items.<br>\nThese inconsistencies disrupt the user’s dashboard experience, reduce efficiency, and require repetitive manual actions.</p>\n<h3><strong>Scope of Work</strong></h3>\n<p>This Epic includes the following improvements and fixes:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Always Open Conversations in the Weekly Conversations Widget</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Automatically expand or open conversations when the Dashboard loads, so users can immediately view active discussions without manual clicks.</li>\n<li>Improves accessibility and saves time for users who frequently monitor project communications.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Auto-Apply Filters on “Load More” in Recent Issues Widget</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Ensure that when users click the <strong>“Load More”</strong> button, any active filters remain applied to the new batch of issues.</li>\n<li>Prevents users from reapplying filters repeatedly and maintains consistent, filtered views during data expansion.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3718	2025-11-20	2025-10-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	f79e81a568f0-f6b3-5cb9-e5a2c76ef237	\N	ae4ca1725acb-1902-6b9c-1a5d19be2920	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	\N	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2025-11-04 07:04:20	aprom	1	0
28009bc36ad9-8c52-e557-daf7a712fcfd	Talos: Odysseus works A Dev Tool, A Hermes and A Ares issues too	2026-10-21 22:26:48	2026-10-21 22:36:17	0	<p>Assigning adt-4077 to the agent did nothing. Odysseus only lists A Gaia and A Prometheus in <code>projects</code>, so Talos never subscribed to assignment events for other projects, and its periodic catch-up never looked at them either.</p><ul><li><code>talos/agents/odysseus/agent.json</code>: add <code>"A Dev Tool": "dev-tools"</code>, <code>"A Hermes": "hermes"</code> and <code>"A Ares": "ares"</code> to <code>projects</code>.</li><li><code>ai/lib/common.py</code>: <code>PROJECT_FOR_REPO</code> maps <code>dev-tools</code> to "A Gaia", which predates A Dev Tool. Map it to "A Dev Tool". <code>ai/lib/ship.py</code>: add <code>"A Dev Tool": "adt"</code> to <code>SHORTCODE</code>, so commits and PRs refer to <code>adt-NNNN</code>.</li><li>Ares has no tests yet (<code>ares/CLAUDE.md</code>). <code>ai test ares</code> says so plainly and tells the agent to ship with <code>--no-tests</code>, stating how it checked the change. Hermes and dev-tools already have suites.</li><li>README: the projects Odysseus works.</li></ul><p><strong>Risk, accepted for now:</strong> Talos, <code>ai</code> and the agent prompts run from the same <code>dev-tools</code> checkout that a dev-tools issue changes and checks out branches in. A separate runtime copy of dev-tools for Talos is the follow-up. Restart <code>talos run</code> after merging.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4083	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	c7c27b026ad9-8c52-e557-430d1a3d1ced	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-21 22:36:17	adt	0	0
5d3b6d756adc-9973-8304-c017efe958f4	Ideas: create page fills the content column, no 'How it works', full editor for the first message	2026-10-24 07:16:45	2026-10-24 12:03:03	0	<p>The Start an Idea page wastes space and treats the first message as a small field. The ideas layout (<code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>) already renders each page in a <code>col-md-9</code> content column. <code>templates/app/project/idea/create.hbs</code> nests another <code>.row</code> with a <code>col-md-8</code> form and a <code>col-md-4</code> 'How it works' box inside it, which leaves empty space on both sides of the form. The description becomes the idea's first message (<code>controllers/app/project/idea/create.js</code> <code>afterSave</code>), so it needs the full editor, not a small field.</p><ul><li><code>create.hbs</code>: remove the 'How it works' box and the nested <code>.row</code>/<code>col-md-8</code>/<code>col-md-4</code>. The form box fills the content column, like the 'Brainstorm an idea' box in <code>templates/app/project/idea/index.hbs</code>. Start/Cancel stay below the box. Keep <code>AccessControl @aclContext="idea.create"</code>.</li><li>Remove the <code>views.app.idea.create.how.*</code> strings from <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Description (<code>idea.description</code>): replace <code>FormFields::FieldTextArea</code> with <code>AppUi::ToastUi</code> (wysiwyg, toolbar, footer hidden), using the markdown output option added by the composer issue. No mentions or issue search. Wrap it in <code>div.form-field</code> with <code>data-field="idea.description"</code>, as in <code>templates/app/project/issue/create.hbs</code>. Give it a height for a real first message, similar to the issue description editor. The value saved to <code>idea.description</code> and the first message is markdown.</li><li>Compare against the issue create page in the running app before calling it done.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> no 'How it works' box. The form box spans the whole content column next to the ideas list, with no empty columns beside it. The description uses the toolbar editor, and its markdown becomes the first message, rendered formatted in the thread. Title validation still works. Existing idea create tests are updated.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> images in the description (the idea doesn't exist yet when it is written), the idea page boxes, mentions.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4110</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4111	2026-10-31	2026-10-24	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	ac6af3216ad8-d753-535b-b21c3700739d	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	f0d764476adc-0b4e-5c6d-737685d2600c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-24 12:03:04	aprom	0	0
