82b0fa606a72-48f6-fed9-805438519857	Expose field ACL as mode resources on the Permission API	2026-08-05 07:51:30	2026-08-05 10:45:48	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Field-level access control is administered as three coherent modes per field (None,&nbsp;Read,&nbsp;Write), not as independent get/create/update toggles. Admins and the role-permission UI need a simple contract: one permission resource per field with a mode value.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Today, clients must understand and manage three internal storage rows (<code data-backticks="1">{module}.{field}.get|create|update</code>). That increases integration cost, risks inconsistent triples, and leaks enforcement details into the admin experience.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">This change makes the Permission API the adapter between the public mode model and internal action storage: clients list/create/update field permissions as&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">{module}.{field}</code>&nbsp;with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">allowed</code>&nbsp;∈&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">'' | none | read | write</code>. The API expands writes into action triples and collapses reads back into modes. Direct writes to field-action resources are rejected. Unset (<code data-backticks="1">allowed=''</code>) removes the triple (permissive missing, consistent with existing policy).</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Business value:&nbsp;simpler RBAC administration, fewer misconfigurations, a stable API for the permissions UI, and enforcement storage that remains action-precise for runtime evaluation.</span></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>ACL field catalog exposes one mode resource per business field (<code data-backticks="1">{module}.{field}</code>) with modes&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">none | read | write</code>&nbsp;(not three action entries).</li>\n<li>Permission list/default for a role returns field permissions as collapsed modes; get/create/update triples are never returned to the client.</li>\n<li>POST/PATCH of a field mode resource expands to the three stored action rows (or deletes them when&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">allowed</code>&nbsp;is unset).</li>\n<li>Module-level action permissions continue to use binary allowed (<code data-backticks="1">0 | 1 | ''</code>) unchanged.</li>\n<li>Direct create/update of&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">{module}.{field}.{get|create|update}</code>&nbsp;is rejected with a clear error guiding use of the mode resource.</li>\n<li>Invalid field mode values are rejected; only&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">''</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">none</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">read</code>, and&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">write</code>&nbsp;are accepted.</li>\n<li>Response for field mode save returns a synthetic JSON:API Permission with the mode resource name and mode value.</li>\n</ul>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3919	2026-08-06	2026-08-05	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	8d2dc2996a70-1635-52c1-7e0683d8ced6	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	6de900736a73-cd6d-0a94-88e4ec896960	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-08-05 10:45:46	agaia	0	0
