9ae37e156ad8-5eae-b551-e791d8478b52	Nestor: Claude-v1 milestone by default (or as asked), and UI screens as PNGs in the Projects4Me look	2026-10-21 14:09:30	2026-10-21 15:02:00	0	<p>Two changes to Agent Nestor in Talos.</p><p><strong>1. Milestone.</strong> Issues created from an approved plan go in <strong>Claude-v1</strong>, unless the engineer asks for a different milestone. Today Talos never passes a milestone: issues get gaia-mcp's default, or land in the backlog when the project has no Claude-v1.</p><ul><li>Plan issues get an optional <code>milestone</code> field. Nestor sets it only when asked; the default is Claude-v1.</li><li>The plan check validates the milestone against the project's milestones. An unknown milestone is flagged, with the ones that exist.</li><li>Talos passes the milestone explicitly when it creates the issue.</li><li>One-time, done: Claude-v1 created in A Ares, A Hermes and A Dev Tool.</li></ul><p><strong>2. UI screens.</strong> When asked, Nestor designs screens following <code>prometheus/docs/ui/design-system.md</code>. Talos renders them to <strong>PNG</strong>.</p><ul><li>Nestor writes a <code>nestor-screen</code> block (key, title, size) of HTML using Prometheus' markup and classes.</li><li>Talos sanitises it and renders it with a headless browser (Edge or Chrome on Windows, Chromium or Chrome on Linux). The page uses Prometheus' own Bootstrap 3, AdminLTE and skin-black-light CSS from the workspace, plus a Projects4Me overlay: crimson palette, gradient box tops, square edges.</li><li>The PNG is stored on the idea (a sim Gaia <code>ideascreen</code> resource) and shown in the Nestor UI. A revision with the same key replaces it.</li><li>Plan issues can list <code>screens</code>. On approval, Talos attaches those PNGs to the created issues through the gaia MCP client.</li><li>No browser available: Nestor's reply says so, and nothing breaks.</li></ul><p>Windows and Linux both, per dev-tools/CLAUDE.md. Tests and README updates.</p><p>Comple