104ecf436ae2-06a7-79e3-1219e4b05e7d	Task Board: Planning view with backlog and milestone boxes side by side	2026-10-28 15:04:48	2026-10-28 15:23:08	0	<p>Sprint planning is hard today: the backlog and each milestone are separate tabs on the Task Board. The only way to plan is to drag one card at a time onto a tab header without seeing the sprint's contents. This issue adds a second view of the board where the backlog and every open milestone are visible together. It is Prometheus only, with no Gaia changes; see the attached <code>planning-view</code> screen.</p><ul><li><strong>Toggle:</strong> add a <code>view</code> query param (<code>board</code> default, <code>planning</code>) to <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code> / <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code>. Show <strong>Board | Planning</strong> as Bootstrap <code>nav nav-tabs</code> above the board, with the existing Saved Searches dropdown and search input on the right. Search and saved searches filter both views.</li><li><strong>Data:</strong> reuse what the route already loads (open milestones with status in_progress|planned, the backlog issues, and each issue's <code>estimated</code>/<code>spent</code> timelogs). Add no new requests.</li><li><strong>New component</strong> <code>AppUi::TaskBoard::Planning</code> (co-located in <code>app/components/app-ui/task-board/</code>). Layout: <code>.row</code> &gt; <code>col-md-5</code> + <code>col-md-7</code>.<ul><li>Left: a <code>box box-primary</code> "Backlog". The header shows the issue count and total estimated hours. Below it, a <code>table table-hover</code> of rows: checkbox, <code>AppUi::PriorityIcon</code>, linked number - subject, status label underneath, estimate on the right. Sort by priority (blocker → low), then issue number. Show the first 20 rows, with a "Show N more" link in the box footer.</li><li>Right: a <code>box box-info</code> per open milestone, in the board's order. Sprints and in_progress milestones come first and are expanded; other types are <code>box-default</code> and collapsed. Each header shows the milestone type, name, dates, a status label, the issue count and the total estimate. Rows match the backlog's, plus the assignee and without the checkbox. An empty milestone shows a drop hint row.</li><li>A <strong>New Sprint</strong> button under the boxes opens the existing create-milestone modal from <code>task-board.hbs</code>, preset to type sprint. Extract the modal if needed; don't duplicate it.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Moving issues:</strong><ul><li>Drag rows between the backlog and any milestone box, and between milestone boxes, with SortableJS (shared group). Reuse <code>modifiers/initialize-sortable.js</code> where it fits; otherwise add a small modifier for list rows. On drop, save only <code>milestoneId</code> (null for the backlog) through the controller's existing <code>updateIssue</code> path, so the board view, saving overlay and Hermes updates stay consistent.</li><li>Multi-select: ticking backlog rows enables <strong>Move N to ▾</strong> (a Bootstrap dropdown listing the open milestones), which saves each selected issue's milestone.</li><li>Totals update straight away. A failed save moves the row back and shows the error through the notifications service.</li></ul></li><li>Clicking an issue subject opens the existing quick view (<code>selectIssue</code>), as on the board.</li><li>All strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>. Styles are scoped under <code>.board-planning</code> in <code>app/styles/modules/board.scss</code>, with square edges and no new colours.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li><code>?view=planning</code> shows the backlog and all open milestones together; the Board tab returns to the current board unchanged.</li><li>Dragging or Move to changes the issue's milestone in Gaia, and the issue appears in the right lane when you switch back to Board.</li><li>Counts and estimate totals are correct after every move; search filters both columns.</li><li>Mirage handlers plus an integration test for the component and an acceptance test for the toggle and Move to.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> capacity (separate issue), ordering the backlog by hand (there is no rank field), closing a milestone from this view, and a mobile layout.</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> planning-view.png</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4179	2026-11-04	2026-10-28	wont_fix	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	0f85cf816ae2-06a7-79e3-aa137e2b676c	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	\N	57f2151162c6-8e43-a8e0-a01f2b171f5b	2026-10-28 15:23:08	aprom	0	0
6d04c4c16afc-4f2e-ea61-aa8afa1d71a6	Sidebar: Workspace / Project / Admin groups, project items disabled without a project	2026-11-17 09:54:53	2026-11-17 13:18:04	0	<p>Dashboard and Projects work across projects, while Issues, Task Board, Gantt Cal, Threads and Ideas belong to the selected project, yet they are mixed in one "Main Navigation" list. Group them, and disable the project items when no project is selected. Today those items link to <code>/project/undefined/...</code>. The attached screens are a guide to layout and content only; the design system and the real components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>In <code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.{hbs,js}</code>, split <code>navigationMeta</code> by the existing metadata flag <code>projectRelated</code> (<code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> <code>Navigation.items</code>). Do not hard-code item names. Render the groups as <code>li.header</code> sections: <strong>Workspace</strong> (non-project items), then <strong>Project</strong> followed by the current project's short code in crimson, then the existing <strong>Admin</strong> group. Keep the order within each group by <code>order</code>.</li><li>No project selected (<code>trackedProject</code> has no short code): still render the project items, but disabled through <code>components/app-ui/navbar-items.{hbs,js}</code>. Disabled items are muted with a not-allowed cursor, <code>aria-disabled="true"</code>, no navigation and no treeview expansion, with a "Select a project" title. The group header shows <strong>Select a project</strong> on the right instead of the code.</li><li>Collapsed sidebar (<code>sidebar-collapse</code>): AdminLTE hides <code>li.header</code>, so put a thin divider between the groups.</li><li>Styles go in <code>styles/modules/nav.scss</code>. Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> (rename the "Main Navigation" label to Workspace).</li><li>Tests: <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/nav-bar-test.js</code> and <code>navbar-items-test.js</code> cover the grouping, the code in the header, and the disabled state without a project.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Dashboard and Projects are under Workspace; Issues, Task Board, Gantt Cal, Threads and Ideas are under Project &lt;CODE&gt;. Without a project those items are visible but do nothing. Dividers separate the groups when the sidebar is collapsed.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the user panel removal (profile status issue) and closing the sidebar on phones.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4628</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> nav-desktop.png, nav-no-project.png, nav-desktop-collapsed.png, nav-mobile.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4629	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	31c03b936afc-4f2e-ea61-7608b55d6a64	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	64ee22886afc-e2c6-50d8-b220c49ef739	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-17 13:18:04	aprom	0	1
