1c7b44456ae2-06a7-79e3-685a91ab3a86	Task Board Planning view: calculated sprint capacity from past velocity	2026-10-28 15:05:00	2026-10-28 15:23:01	0	<p>When planning a sprint, the Planning view (previous issue) shows each milestone's estimate total but not whether the team can deliver it. We don't want a capacity field in Gaia, so capacity is calculated from past velocity. See the attached <code>planning-view</code> screen: "31h of 38h capacity", the bar, and the info line in the box footer.</p><ul><li><strong>Calculation</strong> in a pure util <code>app/utils/board/sprint-capacity.js</code> (unit tested):<ul><li>Take the project's last 3 milestones with <code>milestoneType</code> sprint and <code>status</code> completed (status set by mark-as-complete, <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> ~l.990), latest <code>endDate</code> first.</li><li>For each one: velocity = the sum of estimated hours of its closed issues (statuses done, complete, closed, as in <code>getCompletedIssuesCount</code>, but excluding deferred), divided by its working days (Mon-Fri between startDate and endDate, inclusive).</li><li>Rate = the average velocity of those sprints. A milestone's capacity = rate × its working days, rounded to whole hours.</li><li>No completed sprint (or none with dates): no capacity. The box shows the estimate only.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Data:</strong> in <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code>, query the 3 completed sprints (sort by <code>Milestone.endDate</code> DESC, limit 3). Then query their issues separately with <code>rels: 'estimated'</code> only (no hasMany rels on the milestone request, per CLAUDE.md). Load these only when the Planning view is opened, not for the plain board.</li><li><strong>UI</strong> in each milestone box header of <code>AppUi::TaskBoard::Planning</code>:<ul><li>"<strong>Xh</strong> of Yh capacity" and a <code>progress progress-xs</code> bar under the header: success up to 90%, warning from 90 to 100%, danger with <code>fa-exclamation-triangle</code> above 100%.</li><li>A <code>box-footer</code> line with <code>fa-info-circle</code> explains the figure ("3.8h per working day (average of the last 3 completed sprints) × 10 working days").</li><li>Update straight away when issues are moved.</li></ul></li><li>Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; no new colours.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests cover the util: working days across weekends, sprints without dates skipped, no history means no capacity, deferred issues excluded.</li><li>The capacity figure and bar colour change as issues move in and out of a sprint.</li><li>The plain Board view makes no extra requests.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a stored capacity field, capacity per assignee, holidays and per-member availability.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4179</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> planning-view.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4180	2026-11-04	2026-10-28	wont_fix	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	0f85cf816ae2-06a7-79e3-aa137e2b676c	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	\N	57f2151162c6-8e43-a8e0-a01f2b171f5b	2026-10-28 15:23:01	aprom	0	0
