ad22ffe96ad8-d753-535b-993dddba1011	Ideas: menu item, project routes, data layer and idea browser	2026-10-21 14:56:45	2026-10-21 18:09:22	0	<p>Brings the Nestor idea UI (reference: <code>dev-tools/nestor/web/index.html</code>, run with <code>dev-tools/nestor/nestor serve</code>) into Prometheus as a project section. This issue builds the skeleton the other Ideas issues fill. The UI only stores and shows data for now: nothing replies to an idea yet. The attached screens show the target (<code>ideas-empty</code>, and the browser column in <code>idea-page</code>).</p><ul><li><strong>Data layer:</strong> ember-data models <code>idea</code>, <code>ideamessage</code>, <code>ideaplan</code>, <code>ideaplanissue</code> matching the Gaia resources (Idea: <code>projectId, title, description, status, createdUser, dateCreated, dateModified</code>; Ideamessage: <code>ideaId, body, kind, steps, ideaplanId, costUsd, createdUser, dateCreated</code>; Ideaplan: <code>ideaId, version, body, status, error, dateCreated</code>; Ideaplanissue: <code>ideaId, ideaplanId, key, issueId</code> + issue relationship). Mirage models, factories and handlers for all four.</li><li><strong>Navigation:</strong> an <code>Idea</code> entry in <code>views.Navigation.items</code> in <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> (icon <code>lightbulb-o</code>, <code>projectRelated: true</code>, list and create actions like Issue), strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li><strong>Routes:</strong> <code>app.project.idea</code> with <code>index</code>, <code>create</code> and <code>page</code> (<code>/:idea_id</code>) in <code>app/router.js</code>; add each to <code>routeMaps</code> in <code>services/acl.js</code> (<code>idea.list</code>, <code>idea.create</code>, <code>idea.get</code>). Content header with the project link and breadcrumb as on the issue pages.</li><li><strong>Layout:</strong> the <code>app.project.idea</code> template shows the idea browser in <code>col-md-3</code> and the child route in <code>col-md-9</code>. Browser: a <code>box-primary</code> with a New idea button in its box-tools and the project's open ideas (newest updated first) as a stacked nav with the status label, the active one highlighted; a Show archived (n) footer link toggles archived ones. Status labels reuse existing classes: open = <code>new</code>, archived = <code>deferred</code>. Index shows the empty-state box from <code>ideas-empty</code>. <code>page</code> and <code>create</code> render the empty column layout (<code>col-md-8</code> main, <code>col-md-4</code> side) for the next issues.</li><li>Follow <code>prometheus/docs/ui/design-system.md</code>: AdminLTE boxes, square edges, existing components only; new classes scoped in <code>app/styles/modules/idea.scss</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Ideas appears in the menu for the selected project and lists that project's ideas from Gaia; navigating between ideas works; hidden when ACL denies <code>idea.list</code>; Mirage acceptance test; checked in the running app against the attached screens; screenshots of the finished screen attached to this issue.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the create form, conversation and plan boxes (separate issues), Hermes live updates, any agent concept.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4069</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> ideas-empty.png, idea-page.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4070	2026-10-28	2026-10-21	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	ac6af3216ad8-d753-535b-b21c3700739d	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	8bbe15e46ad8-0491-7194-35b52e5fc793	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-21 18:09:22	aprom	0	0
42183e856ade-5527-77b9-9b3efe993b30	Coding rules: don't load unbounded hasMany relations in the same API call as the parent	2026-10-25 18:45:22	2026-10-25 19:08:57	0	<p>Gaia applies <code>limit</code> to the joined rows, not to the parent records. A query with hasMany <code>rels</code> (comments, time logs, activities, messages…) and a <code>limit</code> truncates the children, and without a limit it pulls an unbounded set. This is a known Gaia design caveat (found through adt/agaia-4075). The established pattern is to load the parent first, then load the children in their own query with their own, bigger limit.</p><p>Add this to the Rules in <code>prometheus/CLAUDE.md</code> so new code follows it. Existing screens that pass hasMany rels (issue page, board, conversation) are out of scope; they can be followed up separately.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4125	2026-11-01	2026-10-25	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	f3bdf5d86ade-03cb-4b7b-e3c056e72b20	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-25 19:08:57	aprom	0	0
ce59b5976adf-abaa-3ddd-38a164114ed9	CI: bump actions/cache and actions/checkout to Node24-based releases in all workflows	2026-10-26 12:59:58	2026-10-26 13:26:56	0	<p>Raised by CodeRabbit on gaia#207 (issue #4129): <code>actions/cache@v3</code> runs on the retired Node16 runtime.</p><ul><li><code>actions/cache@v3</code>: <code>ci.yml</code> (graph-drift and api-testing jobs), <code>cache-dependencies.yml</code></li><li><code>actions/checkout@v3</code>: <code>ci.yml</code>, <code>cache-dependencies.yml</code>, <code>cd-ovh.yml</code></li></ul><p>Bump all references together (cache to v5, checkout to a current major). First verify that the <code>rananoman/gaia:env-dev</code> container image has a runtime compatible with Node24-based actions, and that CI passes.</p><p>Split out from #4129 to keep that PR scoped.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4141	2026-11-02	2026-10-26	done	low	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	8d88c0836adf-8154-4904-0abe50edd8bc	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	3d1245276adf-b4a2-3ddd-094d2aee4d2c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-26 13:26:57	agaia	0	0
9a9474c46ae2-1975-ad45-8a9c246ce6ed	Remember Me sessions log out with several tabs open: legacy authenticator refresh timer still races across tabs	2026-10-28 15:58:18	2026-10-28 18:42:21	0	<h3>Problem</h3><p>With Remember Me ticked and two or more tabs open, the user is logged out within about a day. Follow-up to aprom-3942, which added the coordinated <code>session.ensureFreshToken()</code> and assumed ESA's scheduled refresh was disabled. It is only disabled inside <code>authenticate()</code>.</p><h3>Root cause</h3><ul><li><code>app/authenticators/oauth2.js</code> overrides <code>_scheduleAccessTokenRefresh</code> with a working implementation. The call is commented out in <code>authenticate()</code> (line 97), but ESA 4.2.2's <code>restore()</code> still calls it. <code>restore()</code> runs in every tab on page load and on every cross-tab <code>sessionDataUpdated</code> (internal-session <code>_bindToStoreEvents</code>).</li><li>So every tab schedules its own <code>_refreshAccessToken</code> at <code>expires_at - tokenRefreshOffset</code>. The offset is <code>floor(random*5)+5</code> seconds, so there are only 5 possible values, and the timer doesn't take the <code>navigator.locks</code> lock.</li><li>Gaia rotates the refresh token and deletes the old one (<code>always_issue_new_refresh_token</code>, which also turns on <code>unset_refresh_token_after_use</code>). When two tabs pick the same second, both send the same token and the second gets "Invalid Token". The failure branch (oauth2.js:181-190) calls <code>session.invalidate()</code>, which logs out every tab. With a 1-hour access token that is about a 1-in-5 chance per hour with two tabs.</li><li>Also: <code>restore()</code> with an already-expired token (new tab, or a laptop waking up) calls <code>_refreshAccessToken</code> straight away, again without the lock.</li></ul><h3>Fix</h3><ul><li>Make <code>services/session.js</code> the only refresher: turn off the authenticator's own refresh (<code>refreshAccessTokens: false</code>, or make <code>_scheduleAccessTokenRefresh</code> a no-op and remove <code>_refreshAccessToken</code> / <code>getUpdatedRefreshToken</code>).</li><li>Override <code>restore()</code> so an expired access token with a refresh token is resolved as is, and the adapter's <code>ensureFreshToken()</code> refreshes it under the lock. It must not reject, because that would log the user out.</li></ul><h3>Acceptance criteria</h3><ul><li>Test first (failing before the fix): restoring the session schedules no authenticator refresh, and restoring with an expired token does not POST <code>/api/v1/token</code> from the authenticator.</li><li>Every refresh_token POST goes through <code>session.ensureFreshToken()</code>.</li><li>Two tabs kept open across several token expiries stay signed in (manual check: DevTools "Preserve log" shows one <code>/token</code> refresh per expiry, none rejected).</li></ul><p>Related: agaia issue for the per-user <code>sessionExpires</code> (filed alongside this one).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4181	2026-11-04	2026-10-28	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	533f16e26ae2-e688-c950-d2d203effa87	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 18:42:21	aprom	0	0
8eafdcd36ad7-b7ec-4943-6854ff73a3a9	Agent module: users.type, agents table, creation service, ACL and self-escalation guard	2026-10-20 11:37:50	2026-10-27 12:49:07	0	<p>Part of agaia-4026 (Agents).</p>\n<p><strong>Design decisions (from the Agents brainstorm, 2026-10-20):</strong></p>\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Class Table Inheritance: every agent is a <code data-tomark-pass="">users</code> row (<code data-tomark-pass="">users.type</code> = Human \\| Agent\\) extended 1:1 by an <code data-tomark-pass="">agents</code> row. Agents therefore work like team members: ACL roles, project membership, assignment, time logs, comments.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">An agent may have a *sponsor* (the user it acts on behalf of) or none; either way it is governed by its own ACL. 'Agent admin' is not a role, just ACL permission on the <code data-tomark-pass="">agent.*</code> resources.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Agents keep an email for now (the OAuth tables key tokens by email).</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Gaia holds the full runtime config and the tool/skill catalogs and grants; Projects4Me-owned server-side tools are implemented in Ares as an MCP server; workspace tools (Read/Edit/Bash, git) run in the agent runtime; external MCP servers are referenced by URL.</li></ul><ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Add <code data-tomark-pass="">users.type</code> \\(Human \\| Agent\\, default Human\\)\\.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">New <code data-tomark-pass="">Agent</code> module (<code data-tomark-pass="">agents</code>): <code data-tomark-pass="">userId</code> (1:1, required), <code data-tomark-pass="">name</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">purpose</code> varchar(255), <code data-tomark-pass="">sponsorId</code> (nullable FK to users), <code data-tomark-pass="">rolePrompt</code> (text), <code data-tomark-pass="">modelConfig</code> (JSON, model by complexity), <code data-tomark-pass="">maxTurns</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">permissionMode</code>, plus the usual audit fields and behaviors.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">One creation service creates the user (type Agent, no password) and the agent row in a transaction; disable/delete cascade. Every type=Agent user must have an agents row.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">User endpoints refuse setting a password on an agent user.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">ACL: <code data-tomark-pass="">agent.*</code> resources from routes; record scope by sponsor via <code data-tomark-pass="">acl.assignment</code> where a sponsor is set.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Self-escalation guard (AclLockoutGuard): an agent cannot modify its own Agent record, its roles or its tool/skill grants.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Seed a 'Coding Agent' role and migrate Agent Odysseus to type Agent with an agents row.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">api-tester catalog regenerated; backend and ACL cases.</li></ul><h4 data-tomark-pass="">Changes after the UI mockups (2026-10-20)\n</h4><ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Fields on the screens: name, email, purpose (max 255), sponsor ('On behalf of', optional), role prompt (markdown), model for simple / complex issues and escalation, max turns per run, max runs per issue, permission mode, status (Active / Disabled), roles and projects.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">No workflow fields on the agent: workflows live in agaia-4048 and reference agents.</li></ul><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(191, 191, 191);" data-tomark-pass="">Important: Harness permission blocks must not reuse the&nbsp;</span>`) AS m(module)`<span class="colour" style="color: rgb(191, 191, 191);" data-tomark-pass="">&nbsp;alias because the resource scaffolder anchors on it.</span>\nMockups: the screenshots attached to this issue (from the 'Agents Screens' design canvas, https://claude.ai/artifact/9WYrFcT3LacRG9QLeBSQUL, private until shared).\n<p>Complexity: complex</p>\n	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	1	1	4027	2026-10-27	2026-10-20	done	mediu