f2bf18c66aee-88b0-a4f9-e6e65bf8ee9c	Issue list: replace jQuery QueryBuilder with ezSearch	2026-11-07 02:03:30	2026-11-07 03:46:38	0	<p>ezSearch (the <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> component from aprom-4300, built on aprom-4293..4299, with the saved-search arguments from the issue this one depends on) replaces jQuery QueryBuilder, starting with the Issue list. Today the list's search input is readonly and only opens the jQuery panel, so nobody can type a query. The Project list and the admin module lists share <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code> and stay on jQuery QueryBuilder until a later phase, so their path must keep working and nothing is removed.</p><p><strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look. Where they disagree with <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code> or with what <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> actually renders, the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs</code> ~l.7-67: replace the Saved Searches dropdown, the readonly <code>FormFields::FieldText</code>, the Search and Clear buttons and the <code>.list-view-filters</code> block with <code>{{query-builder module="issue"}}</code> and its Save Search button with <code>&lt;EzSearch @schema={{this.querySchema}} @query={{this.query}} @savedSearches={{this.ezSavedSearches}} @activeSavedSearchId={{this.searchId}} @onSavedSearchChange={{this.selectSavedSearch}} @onApply={{this.applyQuery}} @onSave={{this.showEzSaveSearchDialog}} @aclContext="issue.read" /&gt;</code>. Keep the save dialog (<code>bootstrap-modal</code>) in the page and show the query passed to <code>@onSave</code>. Don't pass <code>@baseQuery</code>: the route already ANDs <code>(Issue.projectId : X)</code> (<code>routes/app/project/issue/index.js</code> l.191-196).</li><li><code>routes/app/project/issue/index.js</code>: load the schema with <code>query-schema</code> <code>load('issue', {projectId})</code> next to the saved searches (l.232) and set <code>controller.querySchema</code> in <code>setupController</code>. <code>?query=</code> loads into the bar and the builder through <code>@query</code>; the <code>reloadPage</code> trailing-space hack must still parse.</li><li><code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>: add <code>@action applyQuery(query)</code>, which sets <code>queryString</code> and <code>query</code> and resets <code>page</code> to 1. It doesn't touch <code>utils/query/builder.js</code>. Clear on the Issue list goes through <code>applyQuery('')</code> plus <code>selectSavedSearch(null)</code>, because <code>clearSearch</code> calls the jQuery singleton, which throws when it was never initialised. Keep <code>searchByRules</code>, <code>openFilters</code>, <code>clearSearch</code>, <code>showSaveSearchDialog</code> and <code>toggleSearch</code> unchanged for the other lists.</li><li><code>controllers/app/project/issue/index.js</code>:<ul><li>Remove the <code>metadata.filters</code> array (l.35-144); the issue schema replaces it.</li><li>Add <code>ezSavedSearches</code>, mapping saved searches to the item shape <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> expects (query from <code>searchquery</code>).</li><li>Add <code>selectSavedSearch(search|null)</code>, which sets or clears <code>searchId</code>/<code>activeSearch</code>.</li><li>Add a save path that saves the query handed over by <code>@onSave</code> without calling <code>searchByRules</code> (today's <code>saveSearch</code> l.235 sends it).</li><li>Keep <code>statusOptionsByName</code>, <code>milestonesOptions</code>, <code>usersOptions</code> and <code>issueTypeOptions</code> if anything else still uses them.</li></ul></li><li><code>mirage/route-handlers/issue.js</code>: record the last <code>query</code> param in the scenario context so steps can assert what was sent; keep today's behaviour (Mirage doesn't filter by query).</li><li>Tests:<ul><li>Update <code>tests/acceptance/issue/search-issue-from-list.feature</code> and its steps for the new Saved Searches dropdown.</li><li>New <code>tests/acceptance/issue/ez-search-issue-list.feature</code> + steps with these scenarios:<ol><li>Type <code>prio = hi status != done</code>, press Enter: the bar shows <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND (Issue.status !: done))</code>, <code>/issue</code> was queried with it ANDed with the project, and the URL has <code>?query=</code>.</li><li>Type <code>prio</code>, use Down and Tab to accept Priority, finish and run.</li><li>Open Builder, add a Status condition: the bar text updates.</li><li>Pick a saved search: the bar and the builder show it, the query is sent and <code>searchId</code> is in the URL.</li><li>Type <code>status:zzz</code>: the error shows under the bar, Search is disabled and no new <code>/issue</code> request is made.</li></ol></li><li>A unit test for <code>applyQuery</code>.</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios above pass.</li><li>Existing issue-list acceptance tests (paging, sort, mass update, export with a query, saved search) pass.</li><li>The Project list and admin lists still open and use jQuery QueryBuilder.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px, using the screens <code>issue-list-applied</code> and <code>issue-list-applied-mobile</code> as a guide.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Project and admin lists, the board, Gantt and calendar, removing jQuery QueryBuilder or <code>utils/query/*</code>, and editing or deleting saved searches.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4304</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> issue-list-applied.png, issue-list-applied-mobile.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4305	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	ce7342c36aee-0d76-79ac-84e3ebbccfa7	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 03:46:38	aprom	0	0
afeed4e86a7b-ceb0-be98-504a6cdfb6c7	Materialize full-catalog default permissions at role creation	2026-08-11 11:34:07	2026-08-12 16:55:12	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Today, missing permission rows are resolved at evaluation time via the global permissive/restrictive mode (missing = allow under permissive; missing = deny under restrictive). That couples every role’s effective access to a live system setting: changing the mode later silently changes behavior for any resource without an explicit row.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Administrators and auditors need role permissions to be&nbsp;explicit and durable. The resolution mode should apply&nbsp;once at role creation&nbsp;to seed a complete permission set for the full ACL catalog. After that, the role’s access lives only in stored&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">permissions</code>&nbsp;rows. Updating the system permissive/restrictive setting must not rewrite or reinterpret existing roles’ defaults.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Business value:&nbsp;predictable RBAC, no cross-role side effects when the org changes security posture, clearer admin UX, and a clean separation between “default seed policy” and “runtime evaluation of stored grants.”</span></p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3925	2026-08-12	2026-08-11	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	8d2dc2996a70-1635-52c1-7e0683d8ced6	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	4106b0006a7b-807d-56d7-73e71ef0cdd6	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-08-12 16:55:11	agaia	0	0
0403cb506ad6-89d7-93af-34c4143879a5	Settings > Email: remove the "Emails sent by the system" box	2026-10-19 20:43:48	2026-10-20 17:22:37	0	<p>The Email settings page has a <code>box-default</code> "Emails sent by the system" box (welcome email with the account password, reset password email), shown all the time next to the SMTP form. The list of system emails will change, and it isn't relevant whenever an admin edits SMTP settings, so it shouldn't be on this page.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove the <code>data-email-sent</code> box from <code>app/templates/app/settings/email.hbs</code>. The SMTP box then uses the page width (or the layout the other Settings pages use for a single box).</li>\n<li>Remove its now-unused translations (<code>views.app.settings.email.sentTitle</code> and the email list keys) from <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li>\n<li>Remove any Gherkin step or assertion about that box in <code>tests/acceptance/settings/email.feature</code> / <code>email-steps.js</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p>\n<ul><li>The Email page shows only the SMTP form and the Save / Test Settings / Cancel buttons; the email acceptance scenarios pass.</li></ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	4022	2026-10-27	2026-10-20	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	7f53bcb86ace-34bf-02fa-83a17db4682e	ae6454575acb-1902-6b9c-f2ffa11a2697	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	13011de76ad7-0131-2b49-e60815ba497d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-20 17:22:38	aprom	0	0
