9221c3b06a7b-992e-50b0-0f7a60843683	Add “View All” Modal for Role Members When Count Exceeds 10	2026-08-11 15:11:14	2026-08-12 16:41:49	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Role detail now shows assigned users inline below the description (project-members style). On roles with large memberships, the compact members box becomes hard to scan and lengthens the page before permissions.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">This story caps the inline preview at&nbsp;10 members&nbsp;and, when more exist, adds a&nbsp;View All&nbsp;action that opens a modal listing every user assigned to the role. The modal includes a&nbsp;search box&nbsp;so admins can quickly find a specific user without leaving the role page.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Business value: keeps the role detail layout dense for typical roles, while remaining usable for org-wide or heavily shared roles.</span></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Show at most&nbsp;10&nbsp;assigned users in the inline role members list</li>\n<li>When assigned users&nbsp;&gt; 10, show a&nbsp;View All&nbsp;control in the members section</li>\n<li>When assigned users&nbsp;≤ 10, do not show View All</li>\n<li>View All opens a modal listing&nbsp;all&nbsp;users attached to the role</li>\n<li>Modal includes a search box that filters the full member list (e.g. by name; email if available in the list model)</li>\n<li>Preserve existing add (“+”) and remove-member behaviors from the inline list / existing flows</li>\n<li>Empty search results in the modal show a clear empty/no-match state</li>\n<li>Closing the modal returns to the role detail without losing role context</li>\n</ul>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3926	2026-08-12	2026-08-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1