de5d13426aee-63af-5ba1-04ae07f6b405	Idea messages: pasted images reload forever because render-markdown re-runs on its own store query	2026-11-07 07:35:58	2026-11-07 08:25:42	0	<p>When a user pastes an image into the idea composer, it is uploaded and stored in the message as <code>![name](upload:&lt;id&gt;)</code> (aprom-4114). In the thread the message never settles. The image request succeeds, but the message keeps re-rendering and requesting the image again.</p><p><strong>Likely cause (confirm first):</strong> <code>modifiers/render-markdown.js</code> is a classic ember-modifier. Its <code>didReceiveArguments</code> runs inside autotracking and synchronously calls <code>showImages</code>, which calls <code>uploadPreview.previewUrl</code>. That runs <code>store.query('upload', { id, download: true })</code> (<code>services/upload-preview.js</code>). Store state read there seems to become a dependency of the modifier, and the query result changes it. The modifier then re-runs, mints a new single-use download token, calls <code>viewer.setMarkdown</code> again (re-rendering the message and reloading the image), and repeats. Verify this with a counter or a breakpoint before fixing; if the cause is different, say so in the issue.</p><ul><li>Start with a failing integration test: render a message body with one <code>upload:</code> image (Mirage upload and download token). Assert that the preview address is requested once, and the image is shown once, after settling.</li><li>In <code>didReceiveArguments</code>, read only the positional argument. Do nothing when the markdown equals the one already shown. Start the image lookup outside the tracking frame, e.g. after an <code>await Promise.resolve()</code> or a scheduled task, so nothing it reads becomes a dependency.</li><li>Keep the resolved address per upload id for the modifier's lifetime, so a later run with the same image doesn't fetch a new token or redraw the image. Tokens are single-use, so a redrawn <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> pointing at a used address gets a 404.</li><li>Keep the existing behaviour: the image name shows first, the image replaces it once resolved, an unreadable upload stays as its name, a click opens the full size, and the stale-markdown check stays. Clean up on <code>willRemove</code>.</li><li>Check that the composer preview and the create page's first message (both render markdown) don't loop either.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a message with a pasted image shows the image once and stays still. The network tab shows one token request and one image request per image, and no repeating requests while the page is idle. The ember suite passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> opening pasted images in the preview modal instead of a new tab, migrating the modifier to the ember-modifier 4 API, and Gaia changes.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4307	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	3f7313b66aee-8d2e-aab0-2126c765194f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 08:25:42	aprom	0	0
