577766a56a7c-69f4-4848-8baa62d523f7	Replace Role Detail Icon Delete Control with Labeled Delete Button	2026-08-12 13:55:35	2026-08-13 12:47:54	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Role detail currently exposes delete as a compact toolbar icon (<code data-backticks="1">btn-box-tool</code>&nbsp;with trash), next to the close (×) control. That makes delete easy to miss or confuse with dismiss actions, and it does not match primary action patterns used elsewhere on the page (e.g. permissions&nbsp;Save&nbsp;as a labeled&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">btn-primary</code>).</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">This task replaces the icon-only delete control with a proper labeled button styled consistently with the Save button pattern, so delete is explicit, discoverable, and visually intentional—not a secondary icon beside close.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Business value: clearer destructive action affordance and fewer mis-clicks between close and delete.</span></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove the role detail toolbar delete icon control (<code data-backticks="1">btn-box-tool</code>&nbsp;/ trash icon)</li>\n<li>Add a labeled&nbsp;Delete&nbsp;button using the same button treatment as the permissions&nbsp;Save&nbsp;button (<code data-backticks="1">btn btn-primary</code>&nbsp;pattern / equivalent primary button styling)</li>\n<li>Keep existing delete behavior: ACL (<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;role.delete&lt;/span&gt;</code>), confirmation Messenger, success redirect/list update, and lockout error handling</li>\n<li>Keep the close (×) toolbar control unchanged unless layout adjustment is required to place the new Delete button cleanly</li>\n<li>Update tests/selectors as needed so acceptance still targets the delete action</li>\n</ul>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-