cba482a36ad9-34ba-5137-c0fa52586656	p4m: generate a per-machine SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY in p4m.env	2026-10-22 09:09:31	2026-10-22 12:16:15	0	<p>Saving secure settings (e.g. the email/SMTP password) in a local stack fails with <em>Secure settings cannot be saved: SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY is not configured</em>. <code>gaia/docker-compose.yaml</code> passes <code>SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY: ${SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY:-}</code> from the environment, and nothing sets it.</p><p>The key must not be committed: the gaia repo is public, and a known key decrypts every stored secret. Instead <code>p4m</code> generates a random 32-byte, base64-encoded key (the format <code>SettingsCipher</code> requires) into the git-ignored <code>dev-tools/p4m.env</code>, which is loaded into every <code>docker compose</code> call: for new files, and added once to existing ones. An existing key is never replaced (secrets saved with it would become unreadable).</p><p>The dev server (devapi) needs its own key as a deployment secret; that is outside this repo.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4096	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	a959ee166ad9-cda7-5137-ba93143c60db	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-22 12:16:16	adt	0	0
