0e3b36426af7-01e1-767c-154951947c4d	Ember 7 readiness: convert app/app.js to a native class and fix the file-preview iframe test host	2026-11-14 00:02:22	2026-11-14 00:35:03	0	<h4>Why</h4><p>The aprom-4549 trial upgrade to Ember 7.4 found only two breakages. Both can be fixed on 6.12 now, before the upgrade.</p><h4>Do</h4><ul><li><b><code>app/app.js</code>:</b> replace <code>Application.extend({ modulePrefix, podModulePrefix, Resolver })</code> with the blueprint native class: <code>export default class App extends Application { modulePrefix = config.modulePrefix; podModulePrefix = config.podModulePrefix; Resolver = Resolver; }</code>, keeping <code>loadInitializers(App, config.modulePrefix)</code>, the license header and the YUIDoc.<ul><li>Ember 7's <code>Engine</code> declares <code>Resolver = StrictResolver</code> as a class field, which shadows a prototype <code>Resolver</code> set through <code>.extend()</code>.</li><li>The boot then fails with <code>&lt;Application#modules&gt; must be set when using the StrictResolver</code>.</li></ul></li><li><b><code>tests/integration/components/issue/file-preview-test.js</code>:</b> the stub adapter host is a <code>data:</code> URL. Ember 7 sanitizes <code>data:</code> URLs in an iframe <code>src</code> to <code>unsafe:data:…</code>, so <code>it shows a pdf in an iframe</code> fails.<ul><li>Use an http(s) or <code>about:</code> host for the iframe case, keeping the image case free of network fetches.</li><li>Production is unaffected: it uses the API host.</li></ul></li></ul><h4>Done when</h4><p>The full suite passes on 6.12. No dependency changes.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4550	2026-11-21	2026-11-14	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	4e310f586af7-5caf-db55-35a5c687a1b3	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1