0fc1dec16ad9-cce6-3816-2c8d3de74921	CLAUDE.md: new modules ship no permission seed SQL	2026-10-21 22:56:15	2026-10-28 17:57:15	0	<p>Split from #4079. Reword gaia/CLAUDE.md (~line 22, "When adding a resource, check its permissions...") to say: new modules ship no permission seed SQL, the reviewer grants permissions by hand, and api-tester acl cases are still required.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4085	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	3cb87d666ae2-5d23-7254-4f4767d59b5c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 17:57:15	agaia	0	0
81aa43376adc-9973-8304-d76ba4da31eb	Ideas: paste or drop images into a message, stored as uploads of the idea and shown inline	2026-10-24 07:17:21	2026-10-24 16:12:03	0	<p>Engineers want to show UI problems in an idea conversation with screenshots (e.g. with the problem circled). This issue waits on <strong>agaia-4106</strong> (<code>GET /upload/{id}</code> returns 404 for idea uploads), which must be fixed first. Today the toastui editor has no image hook, so a pasted image becomes a base64 <code>data:</code> URI inside the body. That bloats messages and is unreadable to the planning agent. Store images as Gaia uploads instead and keep only a reference in the markdown.</p><ul><li><strong>Contract (shared with the Talos issue of this plan):</strong> an image in a message body is <code>![&lt;file name&gt;](upload:&lt;uploadId&gt;)</code>. No tokens or host in the body.</li><li><code>modifiers/initialize-toastui.js</code>: an optional named argument (e.g. <code>onImage</code>) registered as toastui's <code>addImageBlobHook</code>. It gets the blob, awaits <code>onImage(blob)</code> which resolves to <code>{url, alt}</code>, and inserts the image through the hook's callback. Without the argument, behaviour is unchanged. Passed through by <code>components/app-ui/toast-ui.hbs</code>. The modifier makes no API calls itself.</li><li><code>components/idea/composer.js</code> provides <code>onImage</code>. The upload itself goes in a service (not in the component; e.g. extend <code>services/upload-preview.js</code> or add a small upload service). It creates an <code>Upload</code> with <code>relatedTo: 'idea'</code> and <code>relatedId</code> = the idea, the same way <code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code> <code>handleUpload</code> (~l.256) uploads issue attachments through the upload adapter (no raw <code>fetch</code>). Resolve to <code>upload:&lt;id&gt;</code>. Only images (png, jpg, gif, webp). Show the upload in progress, and report a failed upload without losing the text. The composer needs the idea id (pass it from <code>Idea::ConversationBox</code>).</li><li><code>modifiers/render-markdown.js</code>: before handing the markdown to the viewer, replace <code>upload:&lt;id&gt;</code> image sources with the address from <code>services/upload-preview.js</code> <code>previewUrl(id)</code>. Render the text first and the images when their addresses resolve. Check that the result survives <code>useDefaultHTMLSanitizer</code>. A missing or unreadable upload shows its name as text, not a broken page. Clicking an image opens the full size, as message screens do.</li><li>Verify that Gaia refuses an upload with <code>relatedTo idea</code> for an idea in a project the user can't write to. If it doesn't, file an agaia bug; don't work around it here.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a pasted or dropped screenshot uploads and appears inline in the editor. The sent body contains <code>![name](upload:&lt;id&gt;)</code> and no <code>data:</code> URI. The thread shows the image for every member who can read the idea. Other ToastUi editors are unchanged. Integration or acceptance tests with Mirage cover upload, the stored reference and rendering.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> images in the create page description, non-image attachments, deleting images, images in issue comments.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4110, agaia-4106</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4114	2026-10-31	2026-10-24	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	ac6af3216ad8-d753-535b-b21c3700739d	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	aacee6316adc-41db-8a1b-46d62efd10f7	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-24 16:12:04	aprom	0	0
