202bac776ad9-497b-5f53-d7579dbe5f4b	Load translations from Gaia on boot, in the user's language	2026-10-22 11:44:32	2026-11-11 12:27:28	0	<p>Load translations from the backend before the app renders, in the user's language.</p>\n<h3>Backend contract</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>GET /translations</code> (no auth): the supported locales.</li>\n<li><code>GET /translations/{locale}</code> (no auth): nested JSON in the same shape as <code>translations/*.json</code>; 404 for an unsupported locale.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Scope</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Before the app renders (application route <code>beforeModel</code> or an equivalent boot step), fetch <code>/translations/{locale}</code> and merge it with <code>intl.addTranslations</code>. The static bundle loads first; backend values override it.</li>\n<li>Locale: the logged-in user's <code>language</code> if supported, otherwise <code>en-us</code>. Before login use <code>en-us</code>; after login, if the user's language differs, load it and <code>setLocale</code>. Replace the hard-coded <code>intl.setLocale('en-us')</code> in <code>app/instance-initializers/intl.js</code>.</li>\n<li>If the request fails or the locale is unsupported, keep the static <code>en-us</code> translations and log a warning; the app must still boot.</li>\n<li>Expose the supported locales from one service, for forms that need a field per locale.</li>\n<li>One service owns fetching and merging translations; the route only calls it.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Tests</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>A backend translation overrides the static one (e.g. a status label).</li>\n<li>User with a supported <code>language</code> → that locale is loaded and set; unsupported or empty → <code>en-us</code>.</li>\n<li>Endpoint error → app boots with static <code>en-us</code>.</li>\n<li>Mirage handlers for both endpoints.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: complex</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2