51414ae46ad8-aece-ca06-71ab832aaf02	Scaffold and blueprint for new Gaia resources (ai scaffold gaia-resource)	2026-10-21 16:20:33	2026-10-27 14:46:19	0	<p>Token analysis of agaia-4069 (four new Ideas resources, $6.72 across three Talos runs): about $2–2.5 of it was the agent learning how a Gaia resource is wired and writing boilerplate. That breaks down as:</p><ul><li>33 exploration calls ($1.19): it read the Comment and Milestone metadata, routes, controllers, <code>models.php</code>, behaviours, the migration code, <code>Acl.php</code>, <code>Project.php</code>, the seeders and the live permissions table. The 62K tokens it added were re-read on about 85 later calls, which cost about another $1.</li><li>15 calls for api-tester wiring ($0.91): about 600 lines of acl/client case JSON, a fixture and seed rows in <code>prepare-test-db.sh</code>.</li></ul><p>A generator removes the calls and the output tokens, not just the reading. A skill on its own only adds instructions to the context.</p><ul><li><code>dev-tools/ai/ai scaffold gaia-resource spec.json</code>. The spec gives the name, table, fields, relationships, ACL path and indexes. From it, the command generates:<ul><li>the metadata;</li><li><code>app/models/X.php</code> and <code>app/api/v1/controllers/XController.php</code>;</li><li>the routes in <code>core/config/routes.php</code> and the <code>core/config/models.php</code> entry;</li><li>a fixture and the standard api-tester acl/client cases.</li></ul>It then regenerates <code>tools/api-tester/apis/backend.json</code>. It is idempotent and refuses to overwrite files that exist.</li><li><code>gaia/docs/blueprints/new-resource.md</code>, one page: the conventions the generator can't decide.<ul><li>relationships;</li><li><code>groupKeys</code> ACL paths, including child paths with <code>when</code>;</li><li>multi-column indexes (<code>'name' => ['type' => 'unique', 'columns' => [...]]</code>);</li><li>behaviours;</li><li>no permission seeds (the reviewer grants pe