1dbce2f26a91-f801-c673-dbf6bfd770a5	Integrate Hermes Live Updates	2026-08-28 14:28:45	2026-09-03 07:44:42	0	<h3>Problem Statement</h3>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Collaborators currently see stale project data until they refresh. Notifications relied on polling (or were idle), and there was no shared, authenticated real-time channel for domain changes across board, gantt, and conversations. That creates collaboration lag and conflicting edits in multi-user project work.</span></p>\n<h3>Goal / Objective</h3>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Consume Hermes (Socket.IO relay) from Prometheus with one session socket: screens register only the events they can apply; remote domain events update the UI in near real time—without Prometheus publishing events or managing Hermes rooms.</span></p>\n<h3>Scope of Work</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Session lifecycle:&nbsp;Connect Hermes after login (<code data-backticks="1">loading-assets</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">app</code>) with OAuth token; start notification live sync; disconnect and clear registrations on logout</li>\n<li>Hermes client service:&nbsp;Single socket; aggregate&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">intents:set</code>&nbsp;snapshots (<code data-backticks="1">protocolVersion: 2</code>); dedupe&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">eventId</code>; drop local write echoes; fan&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">domain:event</code>&nbsp;to matching owners</li>\n<li>Screen handlers (controller-owned):\n<ul>\n<li>Board&nbsp;— status/assignee/milestone/issue create events</li>\n<li>Gantt&nbsp;— dates, dependencies, assignee, issue create</li>\n<li>Conversation&nbsp;— comments, votes, conversation create</li>\n<li>Notifications&nbsp;—&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;notification.created&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;for&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">user:&lt;currentUser.id&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Safe merge gaps:&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">live-reload-prompt</code>&nbsp;when a remote change cannot be applied to the current filtered/loaded set (Reload / Dismiss)</li>\n<li>Config:&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;ENV.hermes.url&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;(+ loopback hostname rewrite for CORS)</li>\n<li>Cleanup:&nbsp;Remove legacy chat-box / polling-oriented notification path in favor of live sync</li>\n<li>Docs &amp; tests:&nbsp;Architecture + decisions; Fake Hermes; acceptance features for board/gantt/conversation/notifications; unit/integration coverage</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Out of scope:&nbsp;Issue list/detail, wiki, and non-conversation comments remaining non-live; Gaia publishing and Hermes room implementation (sibling repos)</span></p>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Deliver enterprise-grade collaborative awareness on core project surfaces. After sign-in, Prometheus holds one Hermes connection. Mounted board, gantt, and conversation routes register project intents; the notifications service registers user-scoped intents. Remote updates apply through controller handlers; the saving tab suppresses its own echo so local saves are not clobbered.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Business value: multi-user boards and plans stay current, notification latency drops vs polling, and the live stack is maintainable (relay client vs domain logic separation).</span></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>One Socket.IO connection per signed-in tab; no per-route sockets</li>\n<li>Connect after assets load; disconnect on logout with registration teardown</li>\n<li>Board/gantt/conversation register and unregister intents on route enter/exit</li>\n<li>Notifications register&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;notification.created&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;for the current user for the session</li>\n<li>Apply matching remote events to Ember Data / UI without full-page reload when safe</li>\n<li>Show a persistent Reload prompt when live data cannot be merged into the current view</li>\n<li>Suppress echo of this tab’s REST writes for a short TTL</li>\n<li>Ignore duplicate/retried events by&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">eventId</code></li>\n<li>Configure Hermes URL per environment; rewrite loopback host to page hostname</li>\n<li>Cover session + each live surface with Fake Hermes acceptance tests</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>After login, Hermes is connected and notification intents are registered</li>\n<li>On board/gantt/conversations, another user’s changes appear (or a Reload prompt is offered when merge is unsafe)</li>\n<li>Leaving a project screen removes that screen’s intents from the snapshot</li>\n<li>Logout stops live sync and closes the socket</li>\n<li>Issue list/detail/wiki stay unchanged (not live) in this delivery</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>UI/UX Considerations</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Prefer silent in-place updates for status, dates, comments, and notification badge/count</li>\n<li>When merge is unsafe: non-blocking Messenger with&nbsp;Reload&nbsp;/&nbsp;Dismiss&nbsp;(one prompt per owner)</li>\n<li>No new chat UI; remove obsolete chat-box surface from the control bar/app shell</li>\n<li>Loading/error: connection failures recorded on the Hermes service; user-facing reload failure messaging when Reload fails</li>\n<li>Collaborative feel should match modern PM tools (Linear/Jira-style live board awareness) without noisy toasts for every remote patch</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Acceptance Criteria</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Signed-in session connects Hermes and registers notification live sync</li>\n<li>Board applies remote&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;issue.status.changed&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;(and covered board events) for the tracked project</li>\n<li>Gantt applies remote date (and covered gantt) events to the visible model</li>\n<li>Conversation applies remote comment create (and covered conversation) events</li>\n<li>Remote&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;notification.created&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;increases unread/latest notification state for the recipient</li>\n<li>Route exit unregisters that screen’s intents; logout disconnects cleanly</li>\n<li>Local save echo does not double-apply on the saving tab</li>\n<li>Live acceptance features under&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;tests/acceptance/live/&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;pass with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">@setupHermesFake</code></li>\n<li>Architecture/decisions docs reflect the shipped client contract</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Outcome</h3>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Prometheus consumes Hermes live updates on board, gantt, conversations, and notifications with a single authenticated session socket, screen-owned handlers, and testable client contracts—improving multi-user collaboration without refreshing the page.</span></p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3929	2026-08-28	2026-08-17	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	a5c362b86a91-2952-7d17-301ac1af4e15	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	7e075d796a91-287d-c673-15cad5b83def	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-09-03 07:44:41	aprom	0	0
