a7cfdef76a91-1c2f-b46f-3444c107f8bb	Publish selective domain events to Hermes after persist	2026-08-28 14:43:51	2026-09-03 12:34:13	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Real-time collaboration depends on clients learning about work changes without polling. Legacy Gaia code talked to Hermes over Socket.IO from controllers (ElephantIO&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">createRoom</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">invite</code>), which mixed room fan-out into the API layer, used hardcoded hosts/tenants, and did not scale with Prometheus’s event-driven screens.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Gaia must become the&nbsp;source of truth for domain facts only: after a successful persist, post a V2 envelope to Hermes&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">POST /publish</code>. Gaia must not name Socket.IO rooms, hold socket sessions, or target browsers. Fan-out stays in Hermes; UI application stays in Prometheus.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Business value:&nbsp;reliable live boards/conversations, fail-open writes when the relay is down, a maintainable allowlisted event contract, and removal of brittle in-controller Socket.IO coupling.</span></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>After successful persist, publish allowlisted V2 domain events via shared&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">HermesPublisher</code>&nbsp;(<code data-backticks="1">X-Hermes-Secret</code>, config/env URL + secret).</li>\n<li>Ingest is&nbsp;fail-open: Hermes errors, unknown names, or missing project scope are logged; REST/model save still succeeds.</li>\n<li>Emit&nbsp;selective named events&nbsp;(e.g.&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;issue.status.changed&lt;/span&gt;</code>), not a generic “resource changed.”</li>\n<li>Wire REST resources via controller&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">$uses</code>&nbsp;live-event components:\n<ul>\n<li>Issues → created, status, assignee, dates, dependency created/deleted</li>\n<li>Milestones → created, completed (real transition only)</li>\n<li>Conversation rooms →&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;conversation.created&lt;/span&gt;</code></li>\n<li>Comments / votes → only when related to a conversation room</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Publish&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;notification.created&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;from&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">Systemnotificationrecipient</code>&nbsp;afterCreate (not REST), scoped as&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">projectId = user:&lt;recipientUserId&gt;</code>.</li>\n<li>Keep event names in&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">EventNames</code>&nbsp;in lockstep with Hermes allowlist.</li>\n<li>Remove legacy ElephantIO publish paths from Chatroom / Conversationroom / Converser controllers.</li>\n<li>Provide local config + compose so OG Gaia → Hermes&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">:9000</code>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">gaia-test</code>&nbsp;→&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">hermes-test</code>&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">:9001</code>&nbsp;without retargeting main Hermes&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">GAIA_URL</code>.</li>\n<li>Cover publish rules with PHPUnit; cover REST → Hermes (and fail-open) with api-tester live mode.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Successful issue/milestone/conversation/comment/vote/notification writes that match rules produce the correct envelope(s) on Hermes.</li>\n<li>No-op updates and out-of-scope comments/votes publish nothing.</li>\n<li>Hermes down / 401 / timeout → client still gets normal REST success; failure is logged only.</li>\n<li>Controllers no longer open Socket.IO clients or emit&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">createRoom</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">invite</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Acceptance Criteria</h3>\n<ul>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">V2 envelope includes&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">schemaVersion</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">eventId</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">eventName</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">occurredAt</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">projectId</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resource</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">actorId</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">changes</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">meta.source=gaia</code>.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Unknown event names are rejected before HTTP and never POSTed.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Issue create/patch publishes only allowlisted field events; multi-field patches can emit multiple events; dependency replace emits delete then create.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Milestone completed fires only on transition into completed.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Conversation comments/votes publish; issue/wiki (non-room) comments/votes do not.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Notification envelopes use&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">user:&lt;id&gt;</code>&nbsp;scope, not a project id.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Fail-open verified in unit tests and api-tester (<code data-backticks="1">gaia-test-hermes-down</code>).</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Live happy-path api-tester cases pass against&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">hermes-test</code>&nbsp;with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">--hermes-url</code>.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Legacy ElephantIO controller emit code removed;&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;config/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;hermes.php&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;+ architecture/decisions docs present (D-001–D-009).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Outcome</h3>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Gaia publishes durable, selective domain facts to Hermes after persist. Live UX can update in real time without coupling API writes to sockets, and a down relay cannot break user mutations.</span></p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3930	2026-08-28	2026-08-17	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	63413fd6673b-6180-ffb0-440801685dd8	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	8a4b85f76a91-7cd4-b46f-72467dd0894f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-09-03 12:34:11	agaia	0	0
