e49bce086afa-b805-5654-9136e5d20adc	Use AppUi::Avatar on the role page (members and view-all modal)	2026-11-16 11:28:36	2026-11-16 16:45:42	0	<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, ml 64, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in). Page: <code>templates/app/role/page.hbs</code>.</p><ul><li>l.145 Members grid (<code>.member-avatar-wrap img</code> 7rem, <code>styles/modules/role.scss:188</code>) -&gt; <code>@size="ml"</code>, name below; remove the img size rule.</li><li>l.229 view-all modal (<code>.role-members-view-all__avatar</code> 3.6rem, role.scss:227) -&gt; <code>@size="m"</code>, beside the name; keep the class on the wrapper for layout (flex-shrink) but drop its size.</li><li>Pass <code>userrole.user</code> (or <code>(hash id=... name=...)</code>).</li><li>Update tests that select these images.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> role members and the modal list show AppUi avatars at 64px and 40px with the layout as before.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4606, aprom-4613</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4614	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	5a6edf926afb-3e81-74f5-f4902b4401cc	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 16:45:43	aprom	0	0
5ce9fa606ad8-aece-ca06-f9477370e002	Agent rules in the right place: no permission seeds, test-container note, split framework work from feature issues	2026-10-21 16:20:44	2026-10-21 22:57:58	0	<p>From the agaia-4069 token analysis. Some rules live only in one engineer's local Claude memory, and others are worded so agents misread them.</p><ul><li><strong>Permission seeds.</strong> <code>gaia/CLAUDE.md</code> line 22 says <em>"When adding a resource, check its permissions on existing roles and add tools/api-tester acl cases"</em>. The agent read that as "grant them" and wrote <code>db/seeds/idea_permissions.sql</code>, which the review then removed. That cost about $0.3 plus a $0.66 review round. Reword it: new modules ship no permission seed SQL, the reviewer grants permissions by hand, and the api-tester acl cases are still required. (The rule is currently only in a local memory, <code>no-permission-seeds</code>.)</li><li><strong>Test containers.</strong> The shared test containers can mount another checkout, which is also only in local memory. Move this into the <code>p4m-stack</code>/<code>run-tests</code> skills (or <code>dev-tools/CLAUDE.md</code>) so every machine's Odysseus sees it.</li><li><strong>Planning rule for Nestor</strong> (<code>dev-tools/talos/agents/nestor/role.md</code>). A new framework capability gets its own issue, marked <code>complex</code>. Examples: a new ACL concept such as child paths with <code>when</code> or write scope for path-bound models, a new index type, a new behaviour. The resources that only use it come after, marked <code>simple</code>. agaia-4069 bundled three framework changes into a "create four modules" story, so the whole thing ran on Opus.</li></ul><p>This touches files in gaia and the workspace as well as dev-tools. Split it per repo when it is picked up.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4079	2026-10-28	2026-10-2