4cb960d26913-cfd1-8ae2-db5845dddece	Remove owner (assignee) from project model	2025-11-11 14:29:32	2025-11-12 06:59:59	0	<p>As project manager field is added, so there is no need to have owner (assignee) of the project. Remove that and before removal, update the data of the production by mapping assignee data to project manager field.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3735	2025-11-12	2025-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	538616876911-7db8-be2c-5ad706f2be7c	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	e860ee946913-9770-8f66-160d252fcd2d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2025-11-12 06:59:57	aprom	0	0
c7e913356a96-c219-8a6c-3d2e4ddc1ac4	Push live project updates to the right users in real time	2026-09-01 14:10:15	2026-09-02 12:14:47	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Hermes is the realtime relay between&nbsp;Gaia&nbsp;(source of truth) and&nbsp;Prometheus&nbsp;(UI). The legacy model — Gaia pushing imperative Socket.IO room commands (<code data-backticks="1">createRoom</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">invite</code>) and generic&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">POST /broadcast</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resourceChanged</code>&nbsp;payloads — is removed. Hermes no longer interprets UI screens or project-wide “live sync” blobs.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">The new model has two halves:</span></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Client subscription (Prometheus → Hermes):&nbsp;Each browser tab opens one authenticated Socket.IO connection and sends&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">intents:set</code>&nbsp;snapshots declaring which&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">(projectId, eventName)</code>&nbsp;pairs it can apply. Hermes validates against the user’s Gaia session, stores intents&nbsp;per socket&nbsp;(per tab), and joins internal composite rooms only after the full snapshot passes validation.</li>\n<li>Domain ingest (Gaia → Hermes):&nbsp;After a successful persist, Gaia POSTs a&nbsp;V2 domain-event envelope&nbsp;to&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">POST /publish</code>. Hermes validates the contract, routes to the matching composite room, and emits&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">domain:event</code>&nbsp;with the full envelope to subscribed sockets.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Hermes remains a dumb relay: it does not know issues, boards, Gantt, or comments. Prometheus registers events per mounted route; Gaia publishes named facts after persist (fail-open — REST succeeds even if Hermes is down).</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Business value:&nbsp;Live updates are selective and route-scoped (Taskboard, Gantt, Threads, notifications) instead of project-wide noise. Gaia is decoupled from Socket.IO room semantics. The contract is documented, test-covered, and verifiable locally via&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">hermes-test</code>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">:9001</code>.</span></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Gaia ingest (<code data-backticks="1">POST /publish</code>)</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Accept&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">POST /publish</code>&nbsp;with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">X-Hermes-Secret</code>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">Authorization: Bearer</code>&nbsp;matching configured&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">HERMES_SECRET</code>&nbsp;(server-to-server; not user OAuth)</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Validate V2 envelope schema:&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">schemaVersion</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">eventId</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">eventName</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">occurredAt</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">projectId</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resource</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">actorId</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">changes</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">meta</code>&nbsp;— reject unknown top-level fields</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Reject unknown&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">eventName</code>&nbsp;values not in allowlist (<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;src/contract/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;names.js&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;— keep in lockstep with Gaia&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;EventNames.php&lt;/span&gt;</code>)</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Route to internal room&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">v2:intent:&lt;encodedProjectId&gt;:&lt;eventName&gt;</code>; support&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">projectId</code>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">user:&lt;userId&gt;</code>&nbsp;for notifications</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Emit&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">domain:event</code>&nbsp;with the full envelope payload (no transformation)</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Return&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">200 { ok, eventId, room, subscribers }</code>&nbsp;on success;&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">400 { error: 'invalid_event', details }</code>&nbsp;on validation failure;&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">401 { error: 'unauthorized' }</code>&nbsp;on bad/missing secret</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Increment publish counters (<code data-backticks="1">accepted</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">rejected</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">emitted</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">zeroSubscribers</code>); warn-log publishes with zero subscribers (not an error)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Client subscription (<code data-backticks="1">intents:set</code>)</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Authenticate Socket.IO handshakes against Gaia (<code data-backticks="1">GET /api/v1/user/me</code>) with in-memory session cache (<code data-backticks="1">AUTH_CACHE_TTL_MS</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">AUTH_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES</code>)</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Accept&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">intents:set</code>&nbsp;with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">protocolVersion: 2</code>, monotonic&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">revision</code>, and up to 100 intents&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">{ projectId, eventName }</code></li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Authorize intents: project events require&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">projectId</code>&nbsp;in socket’s Gaia membership list;&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;notification.created&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;requires&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">projectId === user:&lt;socketUserId&gt;</code></li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Deduplicate accepted intents within a snapshot; reject stale revisions (<code data-backticks="1">revision &lt;= lastAccepted</code>)</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Replace socket room membership atomically per snapshot (serialized queue per socket); ack&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">{ revision, accepted, rejected }</code></li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Store intent state per Socket.IO connection (revision starts at&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">-1</code>&nbsp;on connect/reconnect; client must resubscribe)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Legacy removal &amp; ops</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Remove legacy HTTP ingest (<code data-backticks="1">POST /events</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">POST /broadcast</code>) — return&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">404</code></li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Expose&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">GET /health</code>&nbsp;with socket count, auth-cache stats, and auth/intent/publish counters</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Document contract in&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;ARCHITECTURE.md&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;(ingest, intents, rooms, config, cross-repo file map)</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Local compose:&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">hermes-test</code>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">:9001</code>&nbsp;with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">GAIA_URL</code>&nbsp;→&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">gaia-test</code>&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">:8081</code>&nbsp;for api-tester live mode</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Explicit non-goals</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>No&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">eventId</code>&nbsp;dedup on publish (stateless relay; Gaia owns uniqueness)</li>\n<li>No per-IP rate limits on&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;publish&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;(trust network boundary + shared secret)</li>\n<li>No interpretation of&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">changes</code>&nbsp;or UI semantics</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Current Behavior (pre-migration)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Gaia called Hermes with ElephantIO-style room management and/or generic broadcast payloads (<code data-backticks="1">POST /broadcast</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resourceChanged</code>).</li>\n<li>Hermes fanned out project-wide live events; Prometheus applied broad&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">resourceChanged</code>&nbsp;handlers.</li>\n<li>No per-route event allowlist; no&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">intents:set</code>&nbsp;protocol; no V2 envelope contract.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Behavior (shipped)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Prometheus connects with OAuth token → emits&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">intents:set</code>&nbsp;for route-specific&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">(projectId, eventName)</code>&nbsp;pairs</li>\n<li>Gaia successful persist →&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">POST /publish</code>&nbsp;→ Hermes validates →&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">domain:event</code>&nbsp;to sockets in&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">v2:intent:&lt;projectId&gt;:&lt;eventName&gt;</code></li>\n<li>Invalid/missing secret →&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">401</code>; Gaia fail-open — REST still succeeds</li>\n<li>Unknown&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">eventName</code>&nbsp;or schema violation →&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">400</code>&nbsp;before relay</li>\n<li><code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;notification.created&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">projectId: user:&lt;userId&gt;</code>&nbsp;→ only that user’s subscribed socket(s) receive the event; cross-user intent registration rejected (<code data-backticks="1">project_not_authorized</code>)</li>\n<li>Publish with zero subscribers →&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">200</code>&nbsp;accepted +&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">zeroSubscribers</code>&nbsp;counter + warn log</li>\n<li>Tab close / disconnect → socket leaves all intent rooms automatically</li>\n<li>Reconnect → new socket, revision&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">-1</code>, client resends current intent snapshot</li>\n</ul>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3931	2026-09-02	2026-09-01	in_review	medium	c48eb0f26a96-01ce-9f01-d009c8adc923	50e507716a96-c219-8a6c-1d2a19fbfcb5	\N	c52c40b06a96-01ce-9f01-843b02ae1837	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	e478c8f26a98-872a-2ca6-7a1e90b22c1a	f605b4e862c6-4e44-047e-0b80b34dd385	2026-09-02 12:14:47	aherm	0	0
