53a390046a20-2be4-00dc-1f3b01730378	Mass Status Update in User Management Does Not Reset Loading State	2026-06-03 13:12:51	2026-06-08 09:12:09	0	<p>Investigate and resolve an issue in the User Management module where the loading indicator remains active after performing a bulk status update operation.</p>\n<p>Currently, when an administrator selects multiple users (or all users) and performs a mass status change (e.g., Active → Inactive or Inactive → Active), the update is successfully processed, but the loading spinner associated with the action does not return to its default state upon completion.</p>\n<p>This results in misleading UI feedback and may cause users to believe the operation is still in progress.<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Ensure the loading spinner is displayed while the bulk status update request is in progress.</li>\n<li>Reset the loading state once the request completes successfully.</li>\n<li>Reset the loading state if the request fails.</li>\n<li>Ensure the bulk action controls become interactive again after completion.</li>\n<li>Verify the behavior when updating:\n<ul>\n<li>Active → Inactive</li>\n<li>Inactive → Active</li>\n<li>Single selected user</li>\n<li>Multiple selected users</li>\n<li>All selected users</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Outcome</h3>\n<p>After a mass status update operation completes, the loading indicator should be removed, the UI should return to its normal state, and users should be able to continue interacting with the User Management page without requiring a refresh.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3899	2026-06-04	2026-06-03	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	0a337ec36a1d-0176-a590-3f299fa1b9ce	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	408201386a20-e4f2-a2da-b56b397a7e65	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be