c96075c06a99-dc0e-9781-683ba14930be	Push live project updates to the right users in real time	2026-09-03 12:53:29	2026-09-03 12:57:03	0	<p>Hermes is the realtime relay between&nbsp;Gaia&nbsp;(source of truth) and&nbsp;Prometheus&nbsp;(UI). The legacy model — Gaia pushing imperative Socket.IO room commands (createRoom,&nbsp;invite) and generic&nbsp;POST /broadcast&nbsp;/&nbsp;resourceChanged&nbsp;payloads — is removed. Hermes no longer interprets UI screens or project-wide “live sync” blobs.</p>\n<p>The new model has two halves:</p>\n<ol data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Client subscription (Prometheus → Hermes): Each browser tab opens one authenticated Socket.IO connection and sends <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">intents:set</code> snapshots declaring which <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">(projectId, eventName)</code> pairs it can apply. Hermes validates against the user’s Gaia session, stores intents per socket (per tab), and joins internal composite rooms only after the full snapshot passes validation.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Domain ingest (Gaia → Hermes): After a successful persist, Gaia POSTs a V2 domain-event envelope to <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">POST /publish</code>. Hermes validates the contract, routes to the matching composite room, and emits <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">domain:event</code> with the full envelope to subscribed sockets.</li></ol>Hermes remains a dumb relay: it does not know issues, boards, Gantt, or comments. Prometheus registers events per mounted route; Gaia publishes named facts after persist (fail-open — REST succeeds even if Hermes is down).\n<p>Business value:&nbsp;Live updates are selective and route-scoped (Taskboard, Gantt, Threads, notifications) instead of project-wide noise. Gaia is decoupled from Socket.IO room semantics. The contract is documented, test-covered, and verifiable locally via&nbsp;hermes-test&nbsp;on&nbsp;:9001.</p>\n<h3 data-tomark-pass="">Functional Requirements\n</h3>**Gaia ingest**<span class="colour" style="color:rgba(228, 228, 228, 0.92)" data-tomark-pass="">&nbsp;(<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">POST /publish</code>)</span>\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Accept <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">POST /publish</code> with <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">X-Hermes-Secret</code> or <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">Authorization: Bearer</code> matching configured <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">HERMES_SECRET</code> (server-to-server; not user OAuth)</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Validate V2 envelope schema: <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">schemaVersion</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">eventId</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">eventName</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">occurredAt</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">projectId</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">resource</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">actorId</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">changes</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">meta</code> — reject unknown top-level fields</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Reject unknown <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">eventName</code> values not in allowlist (<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass=""><span class="colour" style="color: inherit;" data-tomark-pass="">src/contract/</span><span class="colour" style="color: inherit;" data-tomark-pass="">names.js</span></code> — keep in lockstep with Gaia <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass=""><span class="colour" style="color: inherit;" data-tomark-pass="">EventNames.php</span></code>)</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Route to internal room <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">v2:intent:<encodedprojectid data-tomark-pass="">:<eventname data-tomark-pass=""></eventname></encodedprojectid></code>; support <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">projectId</code> = <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">user:<userid data-tomark-pass=""></userid></code> for notifications</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Emit <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">domain:event</code> with the full envelope payload (no transformation)</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Return <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">200 { ok, eventId, room, subscribers }</code> on success; <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">400 { error: 'invalid_event', details }</code> on validation failure; <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">401 { error: 'unauthorized' }</code> on bad/missing secret</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Increment publish counters (<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">accepted</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">rejected</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">emitted</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">zeroSubscribers</code>); warn-log publishes with zero subscribers (not an error)</li></ul>**Client subscription**<span class="colour" style="color:rgba(228, 228, 228, 0.92)" data-tomark-pass="">&nbsp;(<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">intents:set</code>)</span>\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Authenticate Socket.IO handshakes against Gaia (<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">GET /api/v1/user/me</code>) with in-memory session cache (<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">AUTH_CACHE_TTL_MS</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">AUTH_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES</code>)</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Accept <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">intents:set</code> with <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">protocolVersion: 2</code>, monotonic <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">revision</code>, and up to 100 intents <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">{ projectId, eventName }</code></li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Authorize intents: project events require <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">projectId</code> in socket’s Gaia membership list; <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass=""><span class="colour" style="color: inherit;" data-tomark-pass="">notification.created</span></code> requires <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">projectId === user:<socketuserid data-tomark-pass=""></socketuserid></code></li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Deduplicate accepted intents within a snapshot; reject stale revisions (<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">revision &lt;= lastAccepted</code>)</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Replace socket room membership atomically per snapshot (serialized queue per socket); ack <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">{ revision, accepted, rejected }</code></li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Store intent state per Socket.IO connection (revision starts at <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">-1</code> on connect/reconnect; client must resubscribe)</li></ul>**Legacy removal &amp; ops**\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Remove legacy HTTP ingest (<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">POST /events</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">POST /broadcast</code>) — return <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">404</code></li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Expose <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">GET /health</code> with socket count, auth-cache stats, and auth/intent/publish counters</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Document contract in <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass=""><span class="colour" style="color: inherit;" data-tomark-pass="">ARCHITECTURE.md</span></code> (ingest, intents, rooms, config, cross-repo file map)</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Local compose: <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">hermes-test</code> on <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">:9001</code> with <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">GAIA_URL</code> → <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">gaia-test</code> <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">:8081</code> for api-tester live mode</li></ul>**Explicit non-goals**\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">No <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">eventId</code> dedup on publish (stateless relay; Gaia owns uniqueness)</li><li data-tomark-pass="">No per-IP rate limits on <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass=""><span class="colour" style="color: inherit;" data-tomark-pass="">/</span><span class="colour" style="color: inherit;" data-tomark-pass="">publish</span></code> (trust network boundary + shared secret)</li><li data-tomark-pass="">No interpretation of <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">changes</code> or UI semantics</li></ul><h3 data-tomark-pass="">Current Behavior (pre-migration)\n</h3><ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Gaia called Hermes with ElephantIO-style room management and/or generic broadcast payloads (<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">POST /broadcast</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">resourceChanged</code>).</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Hermes fanned out project-wide live events; Prometheus applied broad <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">resourceChanged</code> handlers.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">No per-route event allowlist; no <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">intents:set</code> protocol; no V2 envelope contract.</li></ul><h3 data-tomark-pass="">Expected Behavior\n</h3><ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Prometheus connects with OAuth token → emits <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">intents:set</code> for route-specific <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">(projectId, eventName)</code> pairs</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Gaia successful persist → <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">POST /publish</code> → Hermes validates → <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">domain:event</code> to sockets in <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">v2:intent:<projectid data-tomark-pass="">:<eventname data-tomark-pass=""></eventname></projectid></code></li><li data-tomark-pass="">Invalid/missing secret → <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">401</code>; Gaia fail-open — REST still succeeds</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Unknown <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">eventName</code> or schema violation → <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">400</code> before relay</li><li data-tomark-pass=""><code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass=""><span class="colour" style="color: inherit;" data-tomark-pass="">notification.created</span></code> with <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">projectId: user:<userid data-tomark-pass=""></userid></code> → only that user’s subscribed socket(s) receive the event; cross-user intent registration rejected (<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">project_not_authorized</code>)</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Publish with zero subscribers → <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">200</code> accepted + <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">zeroSubscribers</code> counter + warn log</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Tab close / disconnect → socket leaves all intent rooms automatically</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Reconnect → new socket, revision <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">-1</code>, client resends current intent snapshot</li></ul>\n	7ea8b586623c