c46c1dc36a9e-11db-93e2-bc61a38eee7e	Enable Project Search in Sidebar Project Selector	2026-09-07 07:46:12	2026-09-07 11:05:03	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Users&nbsp;switch&nbsp;projects&nbsp;from&nbsp;the&nbsp;left&nbsp;sidebar&nbsp;project&nbsp;selector.&nbsp;Today,&nbsp;finding&nbsp;a&nbsp;project&nbsp;means&nbsp;opening&nbsp;the&nbsp;dropdown&nbsp;and&nbsp;manually&nbsp;scrolling&nbsp;through&nbsp;the&nbsp;full&nbsp;list.&nbsp;As&nbsp;organizations&nbsp;grow&nbsp;and&nbsp;users&nbsp;join&nbsp;many&nbsp;projects,&nbsp;this&nbsp;becomes&nbsp;slow&nbsp;and&nbsp;error-prone.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">This&nbsp;story&nbsp;adds&nbsp;searchable&nbsp;project&nbsp;selection&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;sidebar&nbsp;so&nbsp;users&nbsp;can&nbsp;type&nbsp;a&nbsp;name&nbsp;(or&nbsp;related&nbsp;label)&nbsp;and&nbsp;quickly&nbsp;jump&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;matching&nbsp;project—consistent&nbsp;with&nbsp;modern&nbsp;PM&nbsp;tools&nbsp;(Jira,&nbsp;Linear,&nbsp;Asana).</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Business&nbsp;value:&nbsp;faster&nbsp;project&nbsp;switching,&nbsp;less&nbsp;friction&nbsp;for&nbsp;multi-project&nbsp;users,&nbsp;and&nbsp;better&nbsp;scalability&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;primary&nbsp;navigation&nbsp;affordance.</span></p>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Allow users to search/filter projects from the sidebar project selector</li>\n<li>Match against project display label (name / short code as shown in the list)</li>\n<li>Keep existing select behavior: choosing a project updates tracked project and navigates correctly</li>\n<li>Show clear empty/no-match state when search returns no projects</li>\n<li>Preserve current placeholder (“Select a project…”) and selected-project display</li>\n<li>Ensure search works with large project lists without requiring manual scroll-only discovery</li>\n<li>Keep keyboard usability (type to filter, arrow/enter to select) where PowerSelect supports it</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>User opens the sidebar project dropdown and can type to filter the list in place</li>\n<li>Matching projects remain selectable; non-matches are hidden from the list</li>\n<li>Clearing the search restores the full project list</li>\n<li>Selecting a filtered project still switches context and routes as today</li>\n<li>If no projects match, user sees a no-results message instead of an empty/confusing list</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>UI/UX Considerations</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the existing sidebar PowerSelect project picker (do not invent a second project list)</li>\n<li>Search input should be immediately available when the dropdown opens (typeahead)</li>\n<li>Keep sidebar density: no large extra search bar outside the selector unless required for usability</li>\n<li>Loading: if the projects list is still loading, retain existing loading/empty handling</li>\n<li>Empty: no-match state with a short message (e.g. “No projects found”)</li>\n<li>Responsive: usable in both expanded and collapsed/mini sidebar contexts as supported today</li>\n<li>Align interaction with familiar select-search patterns (Jira project switcher / Linear team switcher)</li>\n</ul>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3934	2026-09-08	2026-09-07	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	a5c362b86a91-2952-7d17-301ac1af4e15	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	\N	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-09-07 11:05:02	aprom	0	0
