0d90f2e16ae6-b1a1-5224-9575bfc60c66	List toolbar: mass update and export (Agents and Workflows lists)	2026-10-31 17:49:01	2026-11-02 16:29:08	0	<p>Part of agaia-4026 (Agents). Split out of aprom-4044 and aprom-4056.</p><p>The list mockups have a four-button row toolbar: select all, delete, mass update and export. aprom-4044 and aprom-4056 build select all and delete. This issue adds the other two as a reusable piece for both lists. Prometheus has no existing mass-update or export pattern.</p><ul><li>Mass update: pick a field and a value for the selected rows, then save each through the standard PATCH. Gaia has no bulk endpoint and gets none.</li><li>Export: CSV of the selected rows, or of the current search when none are selected.</li><li>Design the shared component first, and get approval in a comment before building it.</li></ul><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4044, aprom-4056</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4243	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Agent Agamemnon	201682886ae8-59cb-56d8-210c05ebab86	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-02 16:29:08	aprom	0	0
81731a236ad9-58a0-ccbe-591f110e16d1	p4m test ember: "ember build stopped" on every run since adt-4082 (watch build no longer matched by pgrep)	2026-10-21 23:32:17	2026-10-21 23:37:08	0	<p>Regression from adt-4082 (dev-tools#14). The fix starts the watch build as <code>sh -c 'echo $$ &gt; /tmp/p4m-build.pid; … exec ember build …'</code>, so the recorded pid is ember itself. Ember then renames its process title to plain <code>ember</code>, and no <code>sh -c … ember build</code> parent is left. <code>_builder_running()</code> still uses <code>pgrep -f '[e]mber build'</code>, which now never matches. So every <code>ai test prometheus</code>:</p><ul><li>sees "no builder" and starts another watch build;</li><li>kills the previous one as stale on the next run (<code>kill_stale_builders</code>);</li><li>stops early in the wait loop with <code>ember build stopped</code>, before any test runs.</li></ul><p>aprom-4073's review round is blocked on this. Container state: two <code>ember</code> watchers (34078 and 34201), with the pid file naming 34201. The unit tests replaced <code>_builder_running</code> with a stub that always returns True, so they didn't catch it.</p><ul><li><code>_builder_running()</code>: the build is running if the pid in <code>/tmp/p4m-build.pid</code> is alive and is ember (<code>kill -0</code> plus <code>/proc/&lt;pid&gt;/cmdline</code>). Keep the <code>pgrep -f '[e]mber build'</code> check as a fallback for builds started the old way.</li><li>Restart on <code>RESTART_ON</code> changes: kill the recorded pid (and any old-style build), not just <code>pkill -f '[e]mber build'</code>.</li><li>Tests: the running check is driven by the recorded pid, the restart kills it, and a recorded pid that's dead or reused isn't treated as running. Run the check script against a fake <code>/proc</code>-free stub, or test the commands sent.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two <code>ai test prometheus --changed</code> runs in a row against the live test container both run their tests, leaving exactly one watch build, the one the pid file names.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4086	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	blocker	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	4a7555716ad9-0527-ccbe-208eb6605826	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-21 23:37:09	adt	0	0
