8906a3c36ad9-2d24-5c46-7ce89f29fcb3	Nestor on Gaia ideas: full thread in get_idea, plan from the whole turn, no silent turns, visible in talos status/runs	2026-10-22 11:59:05	2026-10-22 12:16:18	0	<p>Found on idea "Issue Hierarchy Subpanel" (4f0ce600…) on 2026-10-22: the second message got no answer, the first reply had no plan, and <code>talos status</code> showed nothing for Nestor.</p><ol><li><strong>gaia-mcp <code>get_idea</code> drops messages and plans.</strong> It reads the idea with <code>limit=1</code> and its messages/plans through <code>rels</code>; Gaia applies the limit to the related records too, so Talos saw 2 of 5 messages and no plans. A later message is invisible, the turn finds nothing to answer and ends. Fix: fetch messages and plans with their own unlimited queries (as plan issues already are). Test with a fake Gaia that truncates related records like the real one.</li><li><strong>Plan and screens lost when they aren't in the final message.</strong> Nestor wrote the answer with its <code>nestor-screen</code> and <code>nestor-plan</code> blocks, then edited his knowledge map, then ended with a short summary ("plan and screen above"). Talos parses only the final message. Fix: take the blocks from the whole turn's top-level text (the latest of each); tell Nestor (role.md) to finish with the answer.</li><li><strong>"Working" posted before checking there is anything to answer.</strong> A turn with nothing new posts "Agent Nestor is working on it." and ends silently; the notice stays. Fix: check first; log "nothing new to answer".</li><li><strong>Nestor invisible in <code>talos status</code> / <code>talos runs</code>.</strong> Idea turns are recorded in neither. Fix: record each idea turn in <code>runs</code> (keyed by idea: model, cost, duration, outcome, log) and show a running turn in <code>talos status</code> with its idea, start time, live log and latest steps.</li></ol><p>Check: after merging and restarting Talos, the unanswered message on 4f0ce600… is answered.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4099	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	blocker	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	6aa8e5126ad9-920a-5c46-d98466c5b631	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-22 12:16:18	adt	0	0
70ae09e86aee-19e9-5a2a-2d591662a537	Agamemnon: ci_failed triage tells temporary, PR-caused and base-branch failures apart	2026-11-07 08:12:32	2026-11-07 11:08:07	0	<p>With the CI reads, file-bug and hold-until-done in place, the <code>ci_failed</code> incident can move things along instead of re-running once and handing over.</p><ul><li><code>premise.json</code> <code>ci_failed</code>: tiers read, retry, wait, handoff, file, update, notify. "does": read ci-log and base-ci; temporary (timeouts, network, registry or GitHub 5xx, rate limits): rerun-ci within the 3 attempts; fails on the base branch too: file-bug (or link the open one), hold-until-done; caused by the PR's diff: send to the worker with the failing test and log excerpt.</li><li><code>role.md</code>: a CI section with these three cases, "never file a bug without base-ci showing the same failure", "merge the base, never rebase", and "escalate when the cause is unclear".</li><li><code>triage.py</code>: put the failed job names and the re-run count in the packet.</li><li><code>classifier.py</code>: CI handbacks from the merge sweep ("CI failed again after …", re-run errors) map to <code>ci_failed</code>; check the patterns against the real handbacks in the Talos log.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> premise loading and classifier tests, a triage prompt test showing the packet fields. Checked once on a real failing PR if one comes up, noted in the PR. <code>agamemnonProtected</code> paths: manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> stack containers that are down (e.g. Postgres) as an incident.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4312, adt-4313, adt-4314, adt-4315</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4316	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a1