f403e8266ae8-fb0c-741d-b637910423db	Ideas: animated 'working on it' indicator that disappears when the reply arrives	2026-11-02 19:13:56	2026-11-03 12:37:02	0	<p>On the idea page the agent's "Agent Nestor is working on it." line stays in the thread forever as an info notice, which clutters the conversation. It should look like a live typing indicator while the agent works and go away once its reply (or any later message) arrives. The agent posts this notice as an idea message of kind <code>working</code>; existing threads have it as kind <code>system</code>.</p><ul><li><code>components/idea/message-item.{js,hbs}</code>: add an <code>isWorking</code> state for kind <code>working</code>, and for legacy kind <code>system</code> messages whose body ends with <code>is working on it.</code>. Render it in the comment layout (<code>ConversationUi::CommentFrame</code>, so the author's avatar and name show, no date) with the translated text "{name} is working on it" in muted text, followed by three animated dots, instead of the info notice. Give it <code>role="status"</code> and <code>aria-busy="true"</code>. See the attached screens.</li><li><code>components/idea/conversation-box.js</code>: leave working messages out of <code>orderedMessages</code> unless they are the last message in the thread, so a superseded indicator disappears and only the newest one shows while the agent works. This updates live because the page already reloads messages on <code>idea.message.created</code>.</li><li>Dots: reuse the <code>comment-posting-dot</code> keyframes from <code>styles/_animations.scss</code> (as used by <code>.comment-posting-dots</code> in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code>). Put the new classes in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code> under <code>.idea-page</code>. Square edges, existing colours only, per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</li><li>Translation in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: integration tests for <code>Idea::MessageItem</code> (working and legacy-system render the indicator; other system notices and errors render as before) and <code>Idea::ConversationBox</code> (a working message followed by a reply is hidden; a working message that is last is shown). Add a Mirage fixture with a <code>working</code> message if the acceptance tests need one.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> while the agent works, the thread ends with an animated "Agent Nestor is working on it" row. When the reply arrives (live or after refresh), the row is gone. Old threads no longer show the stale lines. Other system notices and errors look unchanged. Lint and tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming progress text or steps, a timeout for an agent that stopped mid-turn, any Gaia or Hermes change.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> idea-working.png, idea-replied.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4255	2026-11-10	2026-11-03	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	b43cc5046ae8-20b5-32a1-13b222266c79	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	b6e91d496ae8-6485-4143-276b5811b986	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-03 12:37:02	aprom	0	0
61a663456917-de9a-fbfa-110b391c0213	Conversation Module Improvements & Feature Expansion	2025-11-14 10:37:21	2026-03-04 10:13:32	0	<p>The Conversations module currently lacks several essential collaboration and usability features, which limits communication flow and reduces overall productivity for end users. This Epic focuses on enhancing the Conversations experience by introducing missing interaction capabilities, improving content formatting tools, strengthening issue linkage, resolving UI/UX inconsistencies, and enabling more intuitive comment management.</p>\n<p>The primary objective of this Epic is to deliver a modern, reliable, and user-friendly Conversations system that supports richer communication, smoother workflows, and seamless integration with issues and project context.</p>\n<p>This Epic includes exactly the following improvements:</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>✅ <strong>Scope of Work</strong></h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Create a new issue from the conversation</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Link an issue with an unattached conversation</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Filter on Conversation</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Watching a conversation</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Enable Toast UI on conversation description as well as comments</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Ability to delete your own comments</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Ability to edit your own comments</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Enable User–User conversations</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Emoji not working</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Mentioning another issue in a comment should reflect in the issue detail</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Enable quick post through Enter or Shift+Enter or Ctrl+Enter</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Disable the pointer on the Heart Icon in the titles</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Possibly rename Topic to Description</strong></li>\n<li><strong>NaN appearing in the Vote</strong></li>\n<li><strong>User should be able to UnLove the conversation</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Add reactions to the comment</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Add reply on comment</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Pin a conversation</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Link page to date (API specific)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Edit Conversation subject description</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2><strong>Epic Goal</strong></h2>\n<p>To enhance communication efficiency and provide users a more intuitive and feature-rich Conversations module that aligns with modern collaboration standards.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2><strong>Epic Outcomes</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Richer and more interactive discussion experiences</li>\n<li>Better traceability between conversations and issues</li>\n<li>Clean, predictable UI behaviors</li>\n<li>Faster posting and editing workflows</li>\n<li>Improved user engagement through reactions and conversation controls</li>\n</ul>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3739	2025-12-14	2025-11-14	pending	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	4b60d556673c-e6e8-d08b-52b27c67dd56	\N	ae4ca1725acb-1902-6b9c-1a5d19be2920	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	2f68d74162c6-8e43-a8e0-a879eaeffc5e	2026-03-04 10:13:16	aprom	1	0
0c93d8c66ae8-863a-741d-f1c75336fc32	Issue detail: open an attachment in a preview modal by clicking it, without downloading	2026-11-02 19:14:20	2026-11-11 10:38:14	0	<p>On the issue detail page, users have to download an attachment to see it. Only the small file name opens the existing preview, which is a 35% wide iframe modal. And types the browser can't render get downloaded. Clicking an attachment should open it for viewing.</p><p><strong>Today</strong>: <code>app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> (Files box ~302-360) shows each file with a thumbnail or <code>AppUi::AttachmentIcon</code>, a name link calling <code>previewFile</code> and a download button calling <code>downloadFile</code>. <code>previewFile</code> in <code>issue-details.js</code> (~488) queries <code>upload</code> with <code>download: true</code> for a one-time token and sets the iframe <code>#file_preview</code> src to <code>&lt;upload adapter host&gt;/preview/get/&lt;token&gt;</code> through jQuery. Gaia's PreviewController serves the file with its mime type and no attachment disposition. The token is deleted after one use.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Make the whole attachment (thumbnail or icon, and name) a keyboard-reachable control that opens the preview. Keep the separate download and delete buttons.</li><li>Move the preview modal out of <code>issue-details</code> into its own component (e.g. <code>Issue::FilePreview</code>). It gets the file and builds the preview URL through the store (no raw fetch, no jQuery) and picks the view from <code>fileMime</code>: <code>image/*</code> as an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> scaled to fit; <code>application/pdf</code>, <code>text/*</code>, <code>video/*</code>, <code>audio/*</code> in the iframe/media element; any other type shows a 'No preview available for this file type' message with a Download button that reuses the existing download flow. Don't request a preview token for types that can't be previewed.</li><li>Make the modal wide enough to read in (e.g. Bootstrap <code>modal-lg</code> or most of the viewport), replacing the 35% width rule in <code>styles/modules/issue.scss</code> (<code>.filePreviewModal</code>). Square edges, design-system modal look.</li><li>Show a loading state while the token is fetched, and an error message if the request fails. Ignore a stale response if another file was opened meanwhile.</li><li>All new strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Clicking an image attachment's thumbnail or name opens the image in the modal; nothing is downloaded.</li><li>A PDF opens in the modal's viewer.</li><li>A .docx/.zip shows the no-preview message with a working Download button.</li><li>The modal can be opened and closed by keyboard; focus returns to the attachment on close.</li><li>Integration test for the preview component (image, PDF and unsupported mime cases) and an acceptance scenario with Mirage for opening an attachment from the issue page.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: previews of Office documents, any Gaia change, and changes to upload or delete.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4256	2026-11-10	2026-11-03	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	b43cc5046ae8-20b5-32a1-13b222266c79	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	bfbee9a76ae8-6485-4143-43aa45f79ebd	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-03 14:39:40	aprom	0	0
8878c7256ad9-9335-54b1-0f965efb5684	Nestor UI: reconnect the event stream after a failed connect; sim: don't log each progress publish	2026-10-22 00:06:32	2026-10-22 00:14:50	0	<p>Found while checking why the Nestor UI seemed not to reach Talos (ideas #4 and #5 on 2026-10-22). Talos had queued and run the turn; Nestor's reply was lost only because the sim was stopped mid-reply, because its console looked like it was failing.</p><ol><li><strong>Nestor UI stops listening for good.</strong> When the page's <code>EventSource</code> on <code>/sim/hermes/events</code> connects while the sim is down, the Nestor server answers 502. A browser <code>EventSource</code> that gets a non-200 response on connect closes and never retries, so the page shows no live progress or replies until it is reloaded. This also happens to any open page when the sim restarts. Fix: when the stream is closed, re-create it after a short delay (and catch up on <code>ready</code> as now).</li><li><strong>Sim console noise.</strong> <code>sim serve</code> logs every non-GET request, so Talos's live progress (<code>POST /publish</code> about once a second while Nestor writes) floods it and looks like a fault. Fix: don't log successful <code>/publish</code> requests; keep logging failures and other writes.</li></ol><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4087	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	ed5826886ad9-b3be-54b1-aaba5dbaac3a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-22 00:14:50	adt	0	0
