32dbc8306a98-fbbf-3cf5-580817a9e168	Align Prometheus Hermes Client with Protocol v1 and Configure Dev Hermes URL	2026-09-02 13:14:26	2026-09-07 10:52:03	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Prometheus live updates were integrated with Hermes using&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">protocolVersion: 2</code>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">schemaVersion: 2</code>&nbsp;on intents and domain events. The Hermes relay contract now uses&nbsp;v1&nbsp;for both. Until Prometheus matches that contract, intent registration and inbound event dispatch can be rejected or ignored, breaking board, gantt, conversation, and notification live sync in environments running the current Hermes build.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">This task aligns the Prometheus client, tests, and architecture docs with Hermes v1, and adds the dev Docker Hermes URL so the dev stack can reach the relay.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Business value: restores reliable real-time collaboration after the Hermes contract change and keeps dev/prod configuration consistent for live updates.</span></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Send&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">intents:set</code>&nbsp;with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">protocolVersion: 1</code>&nbsp;(not 2)</li>\n<li>Accept and dispatch only domain events with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">schemaVersion: 1</code></li>\n<li>Reject/ignore envelopes with unsupported schema versions (e.g. v0, v2)</li>\n<li>Update Fake Hermes test helpers and live acceptance steps to emit v1 envelopes</li>\n<li>Update integration/unit tests for Hermes and notifications to use v1</li>\n<li>Refresh live-updates architecture and decision docs to document v1</li>\n<li>Remove outdated “V2” references from live-update code comments</li>\n<li>Set&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">HERMES_URL_PRODUCTION</code>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;docker/dev/Dockerfile&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;for the dev Hermes endpoint</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>After login, Hermes intent snapshots use&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">protocolVersion: 1</code>&nbsp;and are accepted by Hermes</li>\n<li>Inbound&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">domain:event</code>&nbsp;envelopes with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">schemaVersion: 1</code>&nbsp;are routed to board/gantt/conversation/notification handlers</li>\n<li>Envelopes with non-v1 schema versions are ignored (no handler invocation)</li>\n<li>Existing live behaviors (echo suppression, dedupe, reload prompt, logout teardown) continue unchanged</li>\n<li>Dev Docker builds resolve Hermes at the configured dev relay URL</li>\n</ul>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3932	2026-09-11	2026-09-02	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	a5c362b86a91-2952-7d17-301ac1af4e15	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	cc7755766a98-fbbf-0e41-2dc2aa195803	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-09-07 10:52:02	aprom	0	0
0d67f7206a9f-ef96-2786-5b746d6aacb2	Fix User Create Navigation After Save and Unsaved-Leave Guard	2026-09-08 11:27:09	2026-09-08 11:32:34	0	<h2>Description</h2>\n<p>On User Create, post-save navigation and leave-guard behavior are inconsistent with other create flows (project/issue). Navigation currently runs inside <code>afterSave</code> while optional project/role selections are still treated as dirty, which can block or interfere with redirect to the new user profile. Cancel and route-exit cleanup are also incomplete (orphaned unsaved user records).</p>\n<p>This task aligns User Create with the standard create lifecycle: persist membership/role in <code>afterSave</code>, navigate in <code>navigateToSuccess</code> after success feedback, tighten <code>isDirty</code> to real form fields, add cancel navigation, and destroy unsaved models on exit.</p>\n<p><strong>Business value:</strong> reliable create → profile handoff, fewer false “unsaved changes” blocks, and cleaner Ember Data state when users abandon the form.</p>\n\n<h2>Functional Requirements</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>After successful user create (including optional membership/userrole), navigate to the new user’s profile via <code>navigateToSuccess</code></li>\n<li>Keep membership/userrole persistence in <code>afterSave</code>; clear <code>selectedProject</code> / <code>selectedRole</code> there</li>\n<li>Stop treating selected project/role alone as dirty for navigation blocking</li>\n<li><code>isDirty</code> should consider only relevant user fields (name, email, dateOfBirth) and safely handle a missing model</li>\n<li>On cancel, navigate to User Management (<code>afterCancel</code>)</li>\n<li>On leaving the create route with an unsaved (no id) user model, destroy the record and clear selection state</li>\n<li>Match projects/issue create navigation lifecycle conventions</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Current Behavior</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Success navigation is performed inside <code>afterSave</code>; <code>navigateToSuccess</code> is a no-op</li>\n<li>Selecting a project or role marks the form dirty and can block navigation even when core fields are clean / after save side-effects</li>\n<li>Cancel does not use a dedicated <code>afterCancel</code> path to User Management</li>\n<li>Exiting create without saving can leave an unsaved user record in the store</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Expected Behavior</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Successful save redirects to <code>app.user.page</code> for the created user without a false navigation block</li>\n<li>Optional project/role selection does not by itself trigger unsaved-leave confirmation</li>\n<li>Editing name/email/DOB still blocks navigation until save or discard (existing guard behavior)</li>\n<li>Cancel returns to User Management</li>\n<li>Aborting create cleans up the unsaved user model on route exit</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>UI/UX Considerations</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>No visual redesign; behavior-only change to create/cancel/leave flows</li>\n<li>Success toast + redirect should feel the same as project/issue create</li>\n<li>Unsaved-leave confirm should appear only for meaningful user field edits, not merely picking optional project/role</li>\n<li>Loading/error paths for save failures remain unchanged</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Acceptance Criteria</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Creating a user with no project/role navigates to the new profile successfully</li>\n<li>Creating a user with project and/or role still saves associations and then navigates to the profile without being blocked</li>\n<li>Selecting only project/role (without dirtying name/email/DOB) does not block leaving the page</li>\n<li>Dirty name/email/DOB still triggers navigation confirmation</li>\n<li>Cancel navigates to User Management</li>\n<li>Leaving create without saving removes the unsaved user record from the store</li>\n<li>Regression: existing validation and membership/userrole create behavior still works</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Expected Outcome</h2>\n<p>User Create follows the shared create navigation pattern: reliable post-save redirect, accurate dirty-guard behavior, and clean cancel/exit handling.</p>	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3937	2026-09-15	2026-09-08	in_review	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	a5c362b86a91-2952-7d17-301ac1af4e15	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	4e4b2d326a9f-fc31-1f49-b261ca1a1899	f605b4e862c6-4e44-047e-0b80b34dd385	2026-09-08 11:32:58	aprom	0	0
