15e18d396aa0-c635-a284-465834f2952a	Align Projects List Mass Actions — Mass Edit on Top, Matching Bottom Toolbar	2026-09-08 12:48:21	2026-09-15 08:21:07	0	<h2>Description</h2>\n<p>The Projects list exposes bulk actions above and below the table, but the toolbars are inconsistent. The top bar includes Delete, Mass Update, and Export; the bottom adds Discuss and Refresh. Mass Edit/Update on projects is also not wired like the Issues list (<code>showMassUpdateDialog</code>), so the control is incomplete.</p>\n<p>This task standardizes the Projects list mass-action toolbars: keep Mass Edit available at the top of the list, make the bottom toolbar match the top, and limit bulk actions to Mass Edit, Mass Export, and Delete (remove extraneous bottom-only actions).</p>\n<p><strong>Business value:</strong> predictable list UX, parity with Issues list patterns, and clearer bulk operations for project administrators.</p>\n\n<h2>Functional Requirements</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Ensure a Mass Edit (mass update) control is present in the top list toolbar</li>\n<li>Wire Mass Edit to the shared list mass-update flow (same pattern as Issues: <code>showMassUpdateDialog</code> / ACL <code>project.update</code>)</li>\n<li>Make the bottom list toolbar match the top action buttons (same set, same order, same handlers)</li>\n<li>Bulk action buttons allowed: Delete, Mass Edit, Mass Export only</li>\n<li>Remove bottom-only extras (e.g. Discuss, Refresh) so top and bottom stay aligned</li>\n<li>Preserve select-all, selection count, and pagination controls</li>\n<li>Keep ACL gating: <code>project.delete</code>, <code>project.update</code>, export as today</li>\n<li>Do not change project create/edit form UI under this ticket</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Expected Behavior</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Top toolbar: select-all + Delete + Mass Edit + Export (+ pagination/count as today)</li>\n<li>Bottom toolbar: same bulk action buttons as top (Delete + Mass Edit + Export)</li>\n<li>Mass Edit opens the mass-update dialog for selected projects</li>\n<li>Export continues to open the existing export dialog</li>\n<li>Delete remains ACL-gated (behavior per existing list delete support)</li>\n<li>No Discuss/Refresh controls appear only on the bottom bar</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>UI/UX Considerations</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Mirror Issues list control density and icon button styling (<code>btn-group</code> of <code>btn-default btn-sm</code>)</li>\n<li>Keep tooltips via existing i18n (<code>global.form.delete</code>, <code>global.form.massupdate</code>, <code>global.form.export</code>)</li>\n<li>Top and bottom must feel identical for bulk actions to avoid “where did the button go?” confusion</li>\n<li>Empty list: controls may remain visible; mass actions should no-op/guard when nothing is selected (existing list behavior)</li>\n<li>Responsive: toolbars remain usable on standard admin widths</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Acceptance Criteria</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Top Projects list toolbar includes a working Mass Edit button</li>\n<li>Bottom toolbar bulk actions exactly match top (Delete, Mass Edit, Export only)</li>\n<li>Discuss and Refresh are not present as bottom-only extras</li>\n<li>Mass Edit is ACL-gated with <code>project.update</code> and opens the mass-update dialog</li>\n<li>Export and Delete continue to work from both top and bottom</li>\n<li>Select-all / pagination / selected count remain functional</li>\n<li>Acceptance or UI verification covers top/bottom parity on <code>app/projects</code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Expected Outcome</h2>\n<p>Projects list bulk actions are consistent top-to-bottom, Mass Edit is available and usable from the top of the list, and the action set is limited to Delete, Mass Edit, and Mass Export.</p>	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3938	2026-09-15	2026-09-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	a5c362b86a91-2952-7d17-301ac1af4e15	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	d9ab8c656aa0-92e7