7fb068846ae8-0360-4071-9c41bc0fc110	gaia-mcp: milestone read tools and a milestone filter on gaia_list_issues	2026-11-02 21:02:55	2026-11-02 21:19:57	0	<p>Agents need to look up milestones and read every issue in one. Today gaia-mcp shows milestones only inside <code>gaia_project_options</code> (name, id, endDate) and can only filter issues by project, status, assignee and subject. The first user is Agent Hera, who writes a retrospective once a milestone completes.</p><ul><li><code>gaia_list_milestones</code> (project, optional status, e.g. <code>completed</code>): name, id, status, milestoneType, start and end dates.</li><li><code>gaia_get_milestone</code> (project + name, or id): the fields above plus its description and issue counts per status.</li><li><code>gaia_list_issues</code>: new optional <code>milestone</code> argument (name or id, resolved within the project) and a <code>page</code> argument, so a milestone with more than 100 issues can be read fully. Values go through the existing sanitising and lookups; never paste raw input into the query.</li><li>Code: <code>gaia-mcp/server.py</code> (<code>Gaia.find</code>, the tools class, the <code>TOOLS</code> table) plus README; unit tests in the gaia-mcp tests with a stubbed Gaia.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the new tools appear in <code>tools/list</code>; listing completed milestones of a project works; <code>gaia_list_issues</code> with a milestone returns only that milestone's issues and pages through all of them. Tests pass on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing milestones (existing <code>gaia_create_milestone</code> stays as is).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4259	2026-11-10	2026-11-03	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Ne