70d0d7806aa0-501d-41bd-136e0d65cc76	Taskboard shows duplicate milestone tabs when milestone creator receives Hermes event	2026-09-08 14:45:04	2026-09-16 12:43:04	0	<h3>Description</h3><p>Users report inconsistent milestone tab behavior on the project taskboard: in some projects a single milestone renders one tab as expected, while in others the same action produces two visually identical tabs for one milestone. This degrades navigation clarity, erodes trust in taskboard state, and increases support burden. Investigation indicates Hermes may emit a milestone-created event to the initiating user when it should be excluded, causing a duplicate tab alongside the locally created milestone. A consistent, idempotent milestone tab lifecycle is required across all projects to preserve accurate board structure and reliable real-time collaboration.</p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3><ul><li>Ensure exactly one taskboard tab is created per milestone, regardless of project configuration or board settings.</li><li>Exclude the milestone creator from Hermes milestone-created (or equivalent) event delivery when the client already applied the create action locally.</li><li>Apply idempotent tab creation on the client so duplicate events for the same milestone ID cannot create a second tab.</li><li>Normalize milestone tab state after create, update, and reconnect so persisted and realtime views converge to a single source of truth.</li><li>Verify milestone tab behavior is consistent across projects with different permissions, templates, and feature flags.</li><li>Add server-side or event-routing safeguards so self-initiated milestone actions are not redundantly broadcast to the actor when exclusion rules apply.</li><li>Preserve existing milestone ordering, naming, and selection behavior when fixing duplicate tab creation.</li></ul>\n<h3>Current Behavior</h3><p>When a user creates a milestone on the taskboard, some projects display two nearly identical milestone tabs for a single milestone. Other projects correctly show one tab. The inconsistency suggests the creating user may be receiving a Hermes event that re-applies milestone creation after the UI has already added the tab locally.</p>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3><p>Creating a milestone on any project taskboard results in exactly one milestone tab for that milestone. The creating user does not receive a redundant Hermes event that duplicates UI state. All participants, including the creator after refresh or reconnect, see a single canonical tab per milestone.</p>\n<h3>UI/UX Considerations</h3><p>Taskboard milestone tabs must remain visually distinct, correctly labeled, and selectable without duplicate entries. Tab strip layout must not overflow or misalign when milestones are created. Loading and optimistic-create states should transition cleanly to a single persisted tab. Empty, error, and reconnect states must not spawn duplicate tabs. Behavior should be consistent across viewport sizes and supported browsers.</p>\n<h3>Acceptance Criteria</h3><ul><li>Given a user creates a milestone on the taskboard in any affected project, only one tab appears for that milestone immediately after creation.</li><li>Given the milestone creator remains on the taskboard, no second tab is added when the Hermes milestone event is processed.</li><li>Given another project user creates a milestone, observers receive the event once and see one new tab without duplication.</li><li>Given page refresh or websocket reconnect after milestone creation, the taskboard loads exactly one tab per milestone.</li><li>Given repeated or out-of-order Hermes events for the same milestone ID, the UI does not create additional tabs.</li><li>Regression verified: projects that previously showed a single tab continue to behave correctly.</li><li>Automated or manual test coverage documents creator-exclusion and idempotent tab creation scenarios.</li></ul>\n<h3>Expected Outcome</h3><p>Milestone creation on the taskboard is reliable and consistent across all projects, with one tab per milestone and no duplicate tabs caused by redundant realtime events to the creator. Users experience predictable board navigation and support tickets related to duplicate milestone tabs are eliminated.</p>\n<h3>Estimated Effort (AI-assisted)</h3><p>6 hour(s)</p>\n<h3>Expected Git Commit Message</h3><p>PROM-XXXX | fix(taskboard): prevent duplicate milestone tabs for event originator</p>\n<h3>Recommendations</h3><ul><li>Audit Hermes event payloads and subscription filters for milestone create/update/delete to confirm actor-exclusion is enforced consistently across environments and project types.</li><li>Implement client-side deduplication keyed by milestone ID before inserting tabs, as a defense-in-depth measure beyond event filtering.</li><li>Add structured logging or telemetry for milestone tab insertions including event source, actor ID, and project ID to detect recurrence in production.</li><li>Document the expected realtime contract: which milestone lifecycle events are sent to the actor versus collaborators only.</li><li>Include a regression test matrix covering multiple project templates, roles, and concurrent creators to prevent environment-specific regressions.</li></ul>	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3939	2026-09-15	2026-09-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	a5c362b86a91-2952-7d17-301ac1af4e15	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	\N	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-09-16 12:43:05	aprom	0	0
