46de4ec66aa7-0b47-71e4-17c9308dc6fd	Prevent flaky logout from concurrent OAuth refresh (single-tab + multi-tab coordination)	2026-09-14 10:15:34	2026-09-14 12:46:01	0	<h3>Description</h3><p>Prometheus users experience intermittent, unexplained logouts when access tokens are near expiry. Multiple concurrent refresh attempts (within one browser tab or across tabs) are not coordinated. Gaia rotates refresh tokens on each successful refresh, invalidating the previous refresh token; a losing parallel attempt receives an invalid-token response and the client session is cleared. This erodes trust in session stability and increases support burden. Remediation belongs in the Prometheus Ember frontend: centralize refresh on an extended session service with in-tab single-flight and cross-tab locking, align refresh request format with login, and add a controlled 401 retry—without backend Gaia changes for v1.</p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3><ul><li>Extend ember-simple-auth session service with ensureFreshToken({ force }) that performs refresh when the access token is within the refresh window (e.g. 60s of expiry) or when force is true.</li><li>Implement in-tab single-flight so concurrent callers share one in-flight refresh Promise rather than issuing parallel POST /api/v1/token requests.</li><li>Coordinate cross-tab refresh using navigator.locks, with a documented localStorage lock fallback when locks are unavailable.</li><li>After acquiring the cross-tab lock, re-read persisted session; if another tab already refreshed, skip a redundant refresh POST.</li><li>Application adapter must await ensureFreshToken() before API requests; on 401/UnauthorizedError only, call ensureFreshToken({ force: true }) and retry the request once (no infinite retry).</li><li>OAuth refresh requests must use application/x-www-form-urlencoded Content-Type consistent with password login, not JSON.</li><li>On refresh failure, preserve existing session.invalidate() behavior; successful refresh must update stored tokens and expiry used by adapter headers.</li><li>Password grant login remains on authenticator:oauth2; session owns refresh only (no separate token-refresh service).</li><li>Document out-of-scope follow-up: ad-hoc fetch callers (exports, wiki, etc.) that bypass the adapter.</li></ul>\n<h3>Current Behavior</h3><p>When expires_at is within ~60 seconds, ApplicationAdapter.ajax triggers a refresh POST without coordinating other callers. ESA scheduled refresh is disabled. Gaia issues a new refresh token on each refresh (always_issue_new_refresh_token), invalidating the prior refresh token. A second parallel refresh (same tab or another tab) using the stale refresh token fails; the adapter calls session.invalidate(), logging the user out. Adapter refresh may use JSON Content-Type while login uses form-urlencoded. There is no custom extended session service today.</p>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3><p>At most one refresh executes per browser context at a time; across tabs, only one tab performs refresh while others wait, re-read session, and reuse updated tokens when available. Users remain signed in through normal near-expiry and multi-tab usage. A single 401 after a forced refresh retry may still fail and invalidate session; no unbounded retry loops.</p>\n<h3>UI/UX Considerations</h3><p>Users should not see unexpected redirects to login during routine work with multiple tabs open or bursty API activity near token expiry. No new loading chrome required; avoid flicker or duplicate error toasts from retried adapter calls. Session persistence in localStorage must remain consistent across tabs after refresh.</p>\n<h3>Acceptance Criteria</h3><ul><li>Concurrent adapter requests in one tab near token expiry result in exactly one refresh POST to /api/v1/token; all callers receive success with updated bearer token.</li><li>Two tabs both near expiry: one tab refreshes; the other waits on lock, re-reads session, skips duplicate refresh when tokens are already fresh, and completes API calls without logout.</li><li>Refresh request uses application/x-www-form-urlencoded and succeeds against Gaia refresh_token grant (parity with login).</li><li>Adapter awaits ensureFreshToken() before ajax; simulated 401 triggers one force refresh and one retry; second consecutive 401 invalidates session without further retries.</li><li>Invalid refresh token from true session expiry still invalidates session (no silent infinite retry).</li><li>No changes required to Gaia OAuthServer rotation behavior for v1 acceptance.</li><li>Follow-up note captured in issue or README for non-adapter fetch paths (exports, wiki).</li></ul>\n<h3>Expected Outcome</h3><p>Stable authenticated sessions under concurrent and multi-tab load near access-token expiry; elimination of race-driven invalid-token logouts; maintainable auth refresh owned by session service aligned with enterprise OAuth rotation practices.</p>\n<h3>Recommendations</h3><ul><li>Add unit/integration tests around ensureFreshToken single-flight and lock re-read skip path if the repo has adapter/session test harness.</li><li>Monitor client-side refresh failure rates post-release to confirm logout spike reduction.</li><li>Plan a thin shared helper or migration guide for ad-hoc fetch callers in a separate story to avoid future bypass of ensureFreshToken.</li><li>Verify navigator.locks behavior in supported enterprise browsers; document fallback limitations if localStorage lock is used.</li></ul>	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3942	2026-09-21	2026-09-14	in_review	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	a5c362b86a91-2952-7d17-301ac1af4e15	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	a97414476aa7-ae6c-2e01-5f696d5f1e7c	f605b4e862c6-4e44-047e-0b80b34dd385	2026-09-14 12:45:55	aprom	0	0
0ace2b346ad8-560e-f1b0-d616cdb58f7f	CI build fails: pin sass to 1.105.2 (sass 1.106.0 breaks on the Node 16 build image)	2026-10-21 17:48:58	2026-10-22 12:18:05	0	<p>Every Prometheus CI build ("Deploy Prometheus | OVH", run 39642787992 for aprom-4070) has failed since 2026-10-21 in <code>ember build -prod</code>, with <code>Sass Syntax Error (SassCompiler) undefined</code>.</p><p>Cause: <code>package.json</code> allows <code>"sass": "^1.32.5"</code> and <code>package-lock.json</code> is git-ignored, so each build installs the newest Sass. <code>sass@1.106.0</code>, published 2026-10-21 01:45 UTC, fails on the Node 16.13 that the build image <code>rananoman/prometheus:env</code> runs. The last green build used 1.105.2.</p><p>Checked locally with <code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code> on clean copies of the code:</p><ul><li><code>dev</code> before aprom-4070 (bb9e1ef1): installs sass 1.106.0 and <strong>fails</strong>.</li><li>The aprom-4070 commit: installs sass 1.106.0 and <strong>fails</strong>.</li><li>The aprom-4070 commit with <code>"sass": "1.105.2"</code>: <strong>builds</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Change:</strong> pin <code>"sass": "1.105.2"</code> in <code>package.json</code>.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the CI build succeeds on <code>dev</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> making builds reproducible, by committing a lockfile or moving the build image to Node 20.19 or newer, is a separate issue.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4080	2026-10-28	2026-10-21	done	blocker	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	4847e7f46ad8-560e-4271-54564e850293	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-22 12:18:06	aprom	0	0
