529777426aa7-45d5-13ce-3a72fe9cf564	Multi-tab sign-in: non-initiating tabs route to root instead of /app after auth sync	2026-09-14 12:45:06	2026-09-14 12:53:02	0	<h3>Description</h3><p>When users authenticate in one browser tab while other tabs remain on the sign-in route, session propagation must drive consistent post-login navigation across all affected tabs. Inconsistent routing degrades trust, increases support burden, and blocks access to the primary application shell. A single source of truth for authenticated session state and coordinated redirect targets preserves enterprise UX expectations for SSO and multi-tab workflows.</p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3><ul><li>Detect authenticated session establishment or refresh in any tab and reconcile navigation state in all tabs that were on /sign or equivalent unauthenticated routes</li><li>After successful sign-in (initiating or passive sync), redirect all reconciled tabs to /app (or the configured default post-auth destination), not to /</li><li>Ensure only one tab performs primary OAuth/callback handling where applicable; passive tabs must not duplicate token exchange or race navigation</li><li>Persist or broadcast post-auth intended destination consistently (e.g., BroadcastChannel, storage events, or shared auth state subscription)</li><li>Handle tab order and timing: late-opening tabs, refresh during sync, and expired sessions must not leave tabs on blank or unauthenticated views</li><li>Log or telemetry for cross-tab auth sync failures to support diagnosis without exposing tokens</li></ul>\n<h3>Current Behavior</h3><p>With two or more tabs open, sign-in completed in tab 1 navigates tab 1 to /app because the sign-in control is bound to that tab’s controller. Other tabs transition from /sign to / without reaching /app, rendering a blank page instead of the application.</p>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3><p>When authentication succeeds in any tab, every tab that was awaiting sign-in or holding an unauthenticated route updates to the authenticated default landing route (/app), showing the same application content as the initiating tab without manual refresh.</p>\n<h3>UI/UX Considerations</h3><p>Avoid blank or skeleton-only states after redirect; show loading during cross-tab sync and clear recovery if sync fails (retry sign-in or deep link to /app). Preserve focus in the tab where the user clicked sign-in; passive tabs should update silently. Ensure responsive layout and error/empty states on /app if bootstrap data is still loading.</p>\n<h3>Expected Outcome</h3><p>Users with multiple tabs open experience unified post-login navigation to /app across all tabs, eliminating blank pages and reducing confusion after enterprise sign-in.</p>\n<h3>Recommendations</h3><ul><li>Centralize auth state in a shared store or service subscribed by all tab controllers rather than tab-local redirect logic on the sign-in button</li><li>Define explicit post-auth route constants (/app) used by both initiating and passive tab handlers</li><li>Add integration tests simulating multi-tab storage/BroadcastChannel events</li><li>Document expected multi-tab SSO behavior for support and QA regression suites</li></ul>	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3943	2026-09-21	2026-09-14	in_review	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	a5c362b86a91-2952-7d17-301ac1af4e15	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	f605b4e862c6-4e44-047e-0b80b34dd385	2026-09-14 12:45:08	aprom	0	0
