864de2486adc-0a8e-e36e-21ad5009b741	Notifications sidebar: mark an issue group as read from its heading without navigating	2026-10-24 08:42:46	2026-10-24 09:46:32	0	<p>The notifications sidebar groups notifications by issue (aprom-4063, aprom-4104). Today there are only three ways to mark notifications read: click one notification, click the group heading, or use "Mark all as read". The first two also navigate to the linked entity. Users need to clear one issue's notifications without leaving the page.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/app-ui/notifications/group.hbs</code>: put a <code>button</code> on the right side of <code>h5.notification-group-heading</code>, next to the issue-key link but outside it. Icon only, <code>fa fa-check-circle</code> (the same icon as the sidebar's <code>mark-all-read-btn</code>). Give it a <code>title</code> tooltip "Mark as read" and the attribute <code>data-notification-group-mark-read</code>.</li><li>Render the button only when at least one notification in the group is unread (<code>recipientRecords.firstObject.isRead === "0"</code>, the same check <code>notification.hbs</code> uses). Add a getter such as <code>hasUnread</code> in <code>group.js</code>.</li><li><code>app/components/app-ui/notifications/group.js</code>: add an action <code>markGroupAsRead(event)</code> that calls <code>event.preventDefault()</code> and <code>event.stopPropagation()</code>, then awaits the existing <code>_markGroupAsRead()</code>. It must not navigate. The unread count, the bell and cross-tab sync are already handled by <code>notifications.markAsRead</code>.</li><li>Ignore further clicks while a save is in progress, e.g. with a tracked flag that disables the button.</li><li>Styles in <code>app/styles/components/notifications-sidebar.scss</code> under <code>.notification-group-heading</code>: lay the heading out so the link sits left and the button right; the button is a plain icon in the existing colours. Square edges. No new colours.</li><li>Add the tooltip text to <code>translations/en-us.json</code> (e.g. <code>views.app.notifications.markGroupAsRead</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A group with unread notifications shows the button in its heading. A group whose notifications are all read does not.</li><li>Clicking the button marks every notification in the group as read. The items lose their unread style, the unread count and bell update, the button disappears, and the route does not change.</li><li>Clicking the issue key still marks the group as read and navigates, as before.</li><li>Single-item groups behave the same way.</li><li>Integration test in <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/notifications/</code> for showing and hiding the button and for no navigation. Acceptance scenario in <code>tests/acceptance/notification/</code> (Mirage) for marking a group read from the sidebar.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: a mark-as-read control on single ungrouped notifications (e.g. membership) and any Gaia change.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4116	2026-10-31	2026-10-24	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	05d86c386adc-7fa9-91a7-9c23ea9feb9e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-24 09:46:32	aprom	0	0
