ffbc5df36aa7-8d4d-98f6-b0836252b498	Disable Sign-In control until post-authentication routing completes to prevent premature auth API calls	2026-09-14 14:04:47	2026-09-14 14:18:07	0	<h3>Description</h3><p>Users can activate Sign-In while navigation to the application shell is in progress or when routing state is inconsistent, which fires authentication-related API requests before the client is in a valid sign-in context. This creates unnecessary load, duplicate or failed requests, and inconsistent session handling. Controlling Sign-In availability based on routing state aligns the UI with the auth lifecycle, reduces erroneous backend traffic, and improves reliability of the login experience.</p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3><ul><li>Sign-In action must be non-interactive (disabled or equivalent) whenever the client is navigating to or has landed on the authenticated app route until routing and any auth bootstrap for that destination have settled.</li><li>Sign-In must remain available only on designated unauthenticated entry routes where sign-in is intended.</li><li>No authentication or sign-in-associated API requests may be initiated by the Sign-In control while it is disabled or while a redirect-to-app navigation is in progress.</li><li>Routing or auth state changes that re-enable Sign-In must be deterministic and derived from a single source of truth (router location, auth status, or equivalent).</li><li>If Sign-In was in progress when routing begins, in-flight requests should be cancelled or ignored per existing auth patterns to avoid race conditions.</li></ul>\n<h3>Current Behavior</h3><p>The Sign-In button stays enabled during transitions to the app page and in routing states where sign-in is not appropriate, allowing clicks that trigger sign-in-related API calls before the user is in a valid sign-in context.</p>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3><p>Sign-In is disabled whenever the user is being routed to the app page or is on the app route without a deliberate sign-in flow; API calls tied to Sign-In occur only after explicit user action on an eligible route with Sign-In enabled.</p>\n<h3>UI/UX Considerations</h3><p>Provide clear disabled styling and cursor feedback on Sign-In; optionally show a loading or redirecting state during navigation to app. Preserve accessibility (aria-disabled, focus management) and avoid layout shift. Handle slow networks without enabling duplicate clicks; surface a recoverable error if redirect fails.</p>\n<h3>Acceptance Criteria</h3><ul><li>Given navigation to the app page is in progress, Sign-In is disabled and cannot trigger auth API calls.</li><li>Given the user is on the app page without an active sign-in intent, Sign-In is disabled or not presented per product rules, and no sign-in API calls occur from that control.</li><li>Given the user is on an authorized sign-in route with routing settled, Sign-In is enabled and a single click initiates the expected auth flow once.</li><li>Automated or manual verification confirms zero sign-in-associated API calls when Sign-In is disabled across representative route transitions.</li><li>No regression to successful sign-in completion and redirect to app for valid credentials on supported browsers.</li></ul>\n<h3>Expected Outcome</h3><p>Sign-In cannot fire auth APIs during inappropriate routing states; fewer spurious requests, cleaner auth/session behavior, and a clearer login UX.</p>\n<h3>Recommendations</h3><ul><li>Centralize eligibility to show or enable Sign-In in a route guard or auth layout hook shared by all entry points.</li><li>Debounce or gate sign-in handlers on router navigation events (e.g. isNavigating, pending location) in addition to button disabled state.</li><li>Add lightweight telemetry for sign-in attempts blocked by routing state to validate fix in production.</li><li>Document which routes expose Sign-In and which API endpoints are bound to the control for future regression testing.</li></ul>	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3944	2026-09-21	2026-09-14	in_review	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	d766f5c36aa7-8d4d-98f6-5dd803999bdf	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	f605b4e862c6-4e44-047e-0b80b34dd385	2026-09-14 14:04:49	aprom	0	0
