5561ff146aa9-daad-3be4-d526cf2fe907	Support All / Members / None options for Project Get in role ACL	2026-09-15 12:51:33	2026-09-23 09:53:47	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">With Gaia’s&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;project.get&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;record scopes, role administrators must configure&nbsp;All,&nbsp;Members, or&nbsp;None&nbsp;instead of binary Allow/None for Project Get. Typical roles use Members; org-wide roles use All.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Prometheus must present the correct option set for scoped resources, persist numeric values (<code data-backticks="1">1</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">2</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">0</code>), and treat Members the same as All for UI gating so navigation and controls remain usable while the API enforces which projects appear.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Business value:&nbsp;admins can model real org access without custom workarounds; the UI matches the backend product contract.</span></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Project&nbsp;Get&nbsp;permission control uses scoped options: All (<code data-backticks="1">1</code>), Members (<code data-backticks="1">2</code>), None (<code data-backticks="1">0</code>).</li>\n<li>Project Create / Update / Delete remain Allow (<code data-backticks="1">1</code>) / None (<code data-backticks="1">0</code>).</li>\n<li>Options resolve from system settings (<code data-backticks="1">scopedApiOptions</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">scopedResources</code>), not hard-coded only for Project.</li>\n<li>Client ACL service treats&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">allowed</code>&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">1</code>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">2</code>&nbsp;as permitted for UI checks (e.g.&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;project.read&lt;/span&gt;</code>).</li>\n<li>i18n labels for All / Members; Mirage ACL settings mirror backend shape.</li>\n<li>Do not re-implement membership filtering in Ember — rely on API response sets for project lists/nav.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Role Permissions → Project → Get shows All / Members / None (plus Not set only while unset).</li>\n<li>Saving Members stores&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">2</code>; All stores&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">1</code>; None stores&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">0</code>.</li>\n<li>Users with Members still see project chrome when the module is allowed; listed projects come from the API’s membership-filtered set.</li>\n<li>Users with None continue to be denied project UI where ACL contexts apply.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>UI/UX Considerations</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Keep the existing dense permission row layout; only change the Get dropdown options for scoped resources.</li>\n<li>Labels should be product language (“All”, “Members”, “None”), not raw codes.</li>\n<li>Preserve per-control save feedback (spinner / success / error) as today.</li>\n<li>No new empty/error states beyond existing role-permission patterns; project nav empty states remain driven by API results + existing AccessControl.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Acceptance Criteria</h3>\n<ul>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Project Get dropdown shows All / Members / None with values&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">1</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">2</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">0</code>.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Other Project actions and non-scoped modules still use Allow / None.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task=""><code data-backticks="1">acl.checkAccess('project.read')</code>&nbsp;returns true for both&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">1</code>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">2</code>, false for&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">0</code>.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Settings/Mirage include&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">scopedApiOptions</code>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">scopedResources</code>.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">i18n includes&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">all</code>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">members</code>&nbsp;option labels.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Unit (or equivalent) coverage for ACL service allowing&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">1</code>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">2</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Outcome</h3>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Admins can assign org-wide vs membership-scoped project visibility from the role UI, and the client gates consistently with Gaia’s numeric scope contract.</span></p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3946	2026-09-16	2026-09-15	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	d766f5c36aa7-8d4d-98f6-5dd803999bdf	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	732f7a556aaa-69ba-957c-06c9cbb75f0f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-09-23 09:53:47	aprom	0	0
