0cc147386aa9-0f3c-3be4-1c2b82a24a9f	Add project.get record scopes (None / All / Members) with membership cascade	2026-09-15 12:54:36	2026-09-23 09:54:06	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Organizations need project visibility that matches real access: typical users should only see projects they belong to, while org-wide roles (e.g. CTO) must see every project, and some roles must see none.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Today&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;project.get&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;is binary Allow/None and does not filter rows by membership, so any user with Allow can list all projects and related project data. That overshares and blocks correct role design.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">This change introduces numeric&nbsp;record scopes&nbsp;on&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;project.get&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;(<code data-backticks="1">0</code>&nbsp;= None,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">1</code>&nbsp;= All,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">2</code>&nbsp;= Members), enforces membership filtering at the API for Project and Project-grouped children, and keeps policy orchestration in ACL while Project owns membership semantics. Existing&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">1</code>&nbsp;grants remain All (no migration). New roles seed Members by default under permissive create.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Business value:&nbsp;least-privilege project access, correct CTO vs member visibility, and a scalable pattern for future group scopes without rewriting controllers.</span></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;project.get&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;accepts&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">allowed</code>&nbsp;values&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">0 | 1 | 2</code>&nbsp;(None / All / Members); other module actions stay&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">0 | 1</code>.</li>\n<li>Expose&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">scopedApiOptions</code>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">scopedResources</code>&nbsp;via system ACL settings for clients.</li>\n<li>Under Members (<code data-backticks="1">2</code>), list/get/write for Project and Project-grouped models are limited to the user’s memberships (<code data-backticks="1">groupKeys</code>&nbsp;/ path metadata for indirect models).</li>\n<li>Under All (<code data-backticks="1">1</code>), no project-id row filter; under None (<code data-backticks="1">0</code>), module access denied as today.</li>\n<li>Multi-role aggregation uses privilege rank&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">1 &gt; 2 &gt; 0</code>&nbsp;(not raw numeric max).</li>\n<li>Permissive role seeding sets&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">project.get = 2</code>; existing stored&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">1</code>&nbsp;continues to mean All.</li>\n<li>Membership resolution and ACL predicates live on the Project model; Acl only decides when to filter/deny.</li>\n<li>Document decision D-060; cover Members scenarios in api-tester / unit tests.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Role with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">project.get = 0</code>&nbsp;→ Project API 403; Project-grouped child APIs fail group check.</li>\n<li>Role with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">project.get = 2</code>&nbsp;+ membership in project A only → lists/gets A; non-member project/issue access 403; issue create on non-member project 403.</li>\n<li>Role with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">project.get = 1</code>&nbsp;→ unfiltered project (and allowed child) access.</li>\n<li>Multi-role user with Members + All → behaves as All.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Acceptance Criteria</h3>\n<ul>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Permission write for&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;project.get&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;accepts&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">0|1|2</code>; other module actions reject&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">2</code>.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">System settings expose&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">scopedApiOptions</code>&nbsp;(<code data-backticks="1">all=1</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">members=2</code>,&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">none=0</code>) and&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">scopedResources</code>&nbsp;including&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;project.get&lt;/span&gt;</code>.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Members scope filters Project list/detail and Project-grouped modules (direct&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">projectId</code>&nbsp;and path-based Comment/Activity).</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Write paths assert project scope for create/update/delete where applicable; project create under Members remains allowed when&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">&lt;span class="colour" style="color: inherit;"&gt;project.create&lt;/span&gt;</code>&nbsp;is granted.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">New permissive roles seed&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">project.get = 2</code>; legacy&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">1</code>&nbsp;still means All.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">D-060 documents scopes, aggregation, cascade, and Project-owned membership helpers.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Api-tester (or equivalent) covers Members list/get/deny create cases.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Outcome</h3>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Gaia enforces None / All / Members for project visibility and cascades membership limits to project-owned data, with durable role grants and a clear backend contract for the role UI.</span></p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3947	2026-09-16	2026-09-15	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	63413fd6673b-6180-ffb0-440801685dd8	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	d26631d66aaa-ad44-957c-7ad5cf71b721	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-09-23 09:54:05	agaia	0	0
