70254d256af1-7d5c-b4fe-733f1b59e5ad	Live events: send empty changes as a JSON object so Hermes accepts workflow.agent.run.requested	2026-11-09 15:02:08	2026-11-09 15:59:40	0	<p><strong>Problem.</strong> Hermes refuses every <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> event from Gaia with <code>400 invalid_event</code>, so a 'Run agent' step is saved as pending but no runtime is told about it.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>AgentRunLiveEvents::publish</code> calls <code>HermesPublisher::publishDomainEvent(..., array(), ...)</code> with no changes.</li>\n<li><code>LiveEventEnvelope::build</code> puts it in the envelope as <code>'changes' =&gt; $changes</code>. PHP's <code>json_encode</code> turns the empty <code>array()</code> into the JSON list <code>[]</code>.</li>\n<li>Hermes's envelope contract (<code>src/contract/envelope.js</code>) requires <code>changes</code> to be an object (<code>isPlainObject</code> refuses lists), so it answers 400. <code>HermesPublisher::postEnvelope</code> logs "Hermes ingest failed" and goes on.</li>\n<li>Issue events always carry some changes, so they become <code>{...}</code> and get through. That is why only run requests fail.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Seen on dev (OVH), 2026-11-09.</strong> Milestone aga-v1 in A Prometheus was completed at 12:05:54 UTC. The Milestone Retro workflow saved a pending step for Hera. <code>/var/www/html/logs/application.log</code> has two "Hermes ingest failed: ... POST http://hermes.projects4.me/publish resulted in a 400 Bad Request" lines at that second, one for the <code>user:</code> scope and one for <code>runtimes</code>. Hermes's log has no publish of the event. The same pairs appear at 02:47 and 11:32:49. Talos (listening on <code>runtimes</code>) never received it.</p>\n<p><strong>Change.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>LiveEventEnvelope::build</code> always encodes <code>changes</code> as a JSON object: an empty one as <code>{}</code>, for example <code>(object) $changes</code> when it is empty. Keep <code>meta</code> an object the same way.</li>\n<li>When the publish fails, also log the response body (Hermes returns <code>error</code> and <code>details</code>), so the next contract mismatch shows its cause.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Acceptance.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>PHPUnit: the envelope for a <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> with no changes encodes <code>"changes":{}</code>, for both the <code>user:</code> and the <code>runtimes</code> publish.</li>\n<li>PHPUnit: existing events with changes encode exactly as before.</li>\n<li>On dev, completing a milestone in A Prometheus leads to a Hermes "published workflow.agent.run.requested -&gt; v1:intent:runtimes:..." line, and Talos logs "step ... queued (runtimes)" for Hera.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4421	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	dee441406af0-cd0b-cccd-253efc87745a	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	098f3c576af1-1431-b4fe-ae8c040ec4cf	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 15:59:41	agaia	0	0
