8daafc476aaa-e45c-3235-e0d8177aede3	Issue details panel: set container background to white so loading state is visible	2026-09-16 09:25:33	2026-09-23 09:44:54	0	<h3>Description</h3><p>The issue details container inherits or uses a background color from issue.scss that reduces contrast or obscures the loading placeholder. Users cannot reliably perceive that content is loading, which erodes trust and increases perceived slowness. Aligning the container background to #ffffff restores clear visual separation between chrome, skeleton/loader, and eventual content, supporting consistent issue-view UX across themes and states.</p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3><ul><li>Apply background-color #ffffff to the issue details container styled via issue.scss (or equivalent scoped styles for the issue details view).</li><li>Ensure the change applies to the container that wraps issue detail content and loading UI, not unrelated global surfaces.</li><li>Preserve existing layout, spacing, and scroll behavior after the background update.</li><li>Verify loading, loaded, and error states remain readable against the white background without new regressions in dark or high-contrast modes if those are supported elsewhere.</li></ul>\n<h3>Current Behavior</h3><p>The issue details container background (from issue.scss) prevents the loading container from appearing clearly; users may see a blank or indistinguishable area while data loads.</p>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3><p>While issue details are loading, the loading container/skeleton is clearly visible on a #ffffff background; after load, content displays on the same consistent white container background.</p>\n<h3>UI/UX Considerations</h3><p>Loading states must meet minimum contrast for spinners, skeletons, and placeholders on #ffffff. Confirm behavior on common viewport widths and when the panel is embedded in split or full-width layouts. Avoid flash of wrong background during hydration or route transitions.</p>\n<h3>Acceptance Criteria</h3><ul><li>Given a user opens issue details, when content is loading, then the loading container is visibly distinct on a #ffffff background.</li><li>Given issue details have finished loading, then the container background remains #ffffff and content layout is unchanged from pre-fix baseline except for improved loading visibility.</li><li>Given regression checks on issue list → detail navigation, then no unintended background color changes occur on adjacent panels or modals.</li><li>Visual review confirms loading, empty (if applicable), and error overlays remain legible on the updated background.</li></ul>\n<h3>Expected Outcome</h3><p>Issue details loading feedback is immediately recognizable, reducing confusion during fetch latency and aligning the detail panel with standard light-surface patterns used in enterprise PM tools.</p>\n<h3>Recommendations</h3><ul><li>Define a design token (e.g. --surface-issue-details) instead of hard-coded #ffffff if the app uses a theming system, mapping token to #ffffff in the default theme.</li><li>Add a brief UI snapshot or Storybook story for issue details in loading state to prevent future style regressions.</li><li>Audit other issue-view subpanels for the same background/loader contrast issue.</li></ul>	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3948	2026-09-23	2026-09-16	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	d766f5c36aa7-8d4d-98f6-5dd803999bdf	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	\N	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-09-23 09:44:54	aprom	0	0
