11ad65b66aaa-e792-98a7-20bc80eb752b	Issue create: show Backlog by default on new projects before any milestone exists	2026-09-16 09:40:33	2026-09-23 09:47:51	0	<h3>Description</h3><p>Newly created projects should expose a consistent placement target on issue creation. Users expect Backlog to be selectable immediately; hiding it until the first milestone is created breaks onboarding, increases support burden, and misaligns with standard agile tooling where backlog exists independent of milestones/releases.</p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3><ul><li>On issue/create for any project—including those with zero milestones—the placement or milestone selector must include Backlog as a selectable option.</li><li>Backlog availability must not depend on the presence of at least one user-defined milestone.</li><li>When the user adds their first milestone, Backlog remains in the list alongside the new milestone without requiring a full page refresh or re-navigation.</li><li>API or data layer that feeds issue create must return Backlog (or equivalent default bucket) in the milestone/placement collection for empty milestone sets.</li><li>Behavior must be consistent for newly created projects and existing projects that legitimately have no milestones configured.</li></ul>\n<h3>Current Behavior</h3><p>On a newly created project, navigating to issue/create shows no milestone options and Backlog is absent. After the user creates the first milestone and returns to issue/create, Backlog appears together with the new milestone.</p>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3><p>On issue/create for a newly created project with no milestones, Backlog is visible and selectable by default. After adding milestones, Backlog continues to appear alongside all milestones.</p>\n<h3>UI/UX Considerations</h3><p>Default selection should favor Backlog when no milestone is chosen. Empty milestone state should not look broken—show Backlog clearly labeled, avoid blank dropdowns, and handle loading/error states if milestone fetch fails. Ensure responsive layout for milestone/placement controls on mobile and desktop.</p>\n<h3>Acceptance Criteria</h3><ul><li>Given a newly created project with zero milestones, when the user opens issue/create, then Backlog is listed in the milestone/placement control.</li><li>Given a newly created project with zero milestones, when the user creates an issue with Backlog selected, then the issue is created successfully in the backlog.</li><li>Given a project with one or more milestones, when the user opens issue/create, then Backlog and all milestones are listed.</li><li>Given a user who adds the first milestone without leaving issue/create (if supported) or after returning to issue/create, then Backlog and the new milestone both appear without requiring hard refresh.</li><li>Regression: existing projects with milestones continue to show Backlog plus milestones as before.</li></ul>\n<h3>Expected Outcome</h3><p>Users can create backlog issues immediately after project creation, matching expected agile workflow and reducing confusion during project setup.</p>\n<h3>Recommendations</h3><ul><li>Treat Backlog as a system-defined placement in the domain model rather than a side effect of milestone list population.</li><li>Add integration or E2E coverage for new-project issue create with empty milestone API response.</li><li>Document product rule: Backlog is always available; milestones are optional overlays on the same selector.</li></ul>	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3949	2026-09-23	2026-09-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	d766f5c36aa7-8d4d-98f6-5dd803999bdf	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	\N	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-09-23 09:47:49	aprom	0	0
