06c2e5816aaa-a3f8-1c9b-29b823aa0a0a	Replace assignee dropdown anchor with non-link control to prevent Ember route reload	2026-09-16 11:31:18	2026-09-23 10:04:56	0	<h3>Description</h3><p>The issue detail assignee dropdown uses anchor elements with href=&quot;#&quot; for the updateAssignee action. In Ember, that pattern is treated as in-app navigation and can invoke the route model hook, causing an unnecessary full reload and degraded UX. Replacing links with semantic non-navigating controls (e.g., list items with click handlers) preserves assignee updates without side effects on routing or data refresh.</p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3><ul><li>Bind updateAssignee to a non-anchor element (e.g., li) in the issue detail assignee dropdown without href-based navigation.</li><li>Ensure assignee selection still invokes updateAssignee with the correct issue and user context.</li><li>Prevent route transitions and model hook re-execution when interacting with assignee dropdown items.</li><li>Preserve keyboard accessibility and screen reader semantics for dropdown options (role, focus, activation).</li><li>Update dropdown styles so li-based options match prior anchor appearance (hover, active, disabled, selected).</li><li>Verify behavior across supported browsers without regression to other issue detail actions.</li></ul>\n<h3>Current Behavior</h3><p>Clicking an assignee option in the issue detail dropdown uses an anchor with href=&quot;#&quot;, which Ember may interpret as a route change and trigger the route model hook, resulting in a full reload or unnecessary data refetch instead of only updating the assignee.</p>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3><p>Selecting an assignee from the dropdown updates the assignee via updateAssignee only, with no route change, no model hook re-run, and no full page reload.</p>\n<h3>UI/UX Considerations</h3><p>Dropdown options should remain visually and interactively consistent with the previous link styling (padding, hover/focus states, cursor). Maintain clear focus indicators for keyboard users. Ensure the control does not look like external navigation. Confirm layout in narrow viewports if the assignee menu is responsive.</p>\n<h3>Acceptance Criteria</h3><ul><li>Assignee dropdown items are implemented as non-link elements (e.g., li) with click/action handlers, not anchors with href=&quot;#&quot;.</li><li>Changing assignee from issue detail completes successfully and does not change the URL or reload the issue detail route.</li><li>Route model hook is not invoked solely due to assignee dropdown interaction (verified in dev tools or logging).</li><li>Dropdown styling matches or improves upon previous anchor-based presentation for default, hover, focus, and disabled states.</li><li>Keyboard Enter/Space activates an option where applicable; focus management within the dropdown remains usable.</li><li>No regressions to other issue detail header actions or dropdown close behavior after selection.</li></ul>\n<h3>Expected Outcome</h3><p>Assignee updates from issue detail are instant and isolated from routing, improving reliability and perceived performance while keeping the dropdown UI polished and accessible.</p>\n<h3>Recommendations</h3><ul><li>Audit other issue detail menus for href=&quot;#&quot; or javascript:void patterns and standardize on button or li + action handlers.</li><li>Add a lightweight regression test or acceptance test that asserts no transition occurs on assignee change.</li><li>Document a UI pattern guideline: interactive menu items must not use navigational anchors unless they perform real routing.</li></ul>	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3950	2026-09-23	2026-09-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	d766f5c36aa7-8d4d-98f6-5dd803999bdf	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	\N	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-09-23 10:04:56	aprom	0	0
6487a0f56ae8-1760-4ed1-d89decd245af	Issue statuses: run the system colour fill once (migration), not on every seed run	2026-11-02 13:21:40	2026-11-03 13:07:28	0	<p>CodeRabbit finding on gaia#239 (outside-diff, <code>db/seeds/issue_statuses.sql</code>, line 11), left unchanged in #4216 because the fill comes from #180 (a4e9618).</p><p><b>Problem:</b> the seed refills a system status's colour (and sortOrder) whenever it is cleared, so a Settings change that cleared a colour is overwritten the next time the seed runs.</p><p><b>Wanted:</b> the colour/sortOrder fill runs once, in a migration, instead of on every seed run. Settings changes then stay.</p><p><b>Open design:</b> how to move it into a declarative migration safely (the migrations only apply defaults when adding a column) without losing the backfill on databases that already have the column. Add a test that a cleared colour stays cleared after re-seeding.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4247	2026-11-09	2026-11-02	deferred	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Rana Nouman	\N	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-03 13:07:28	agaia	0	0
5bae72176ab2-c439-78f2-44b3f32f9118	Group role ACL modules into System, User, and Project sections	2026-09-22 10:24:27	2026-09-23 10:29:45	0	<p># Group role ACL modules into System, User, and Project sections</p>\n<h3 data-tomark-pass="">Description\n</h3>On the role permissions page, ACL modules are shown as one flat alphabetical list. Admins cannot tell which modules are platform/admin concerns versus user-profile extensions versus project-scoped work, so elevated permissions are easy to grant by mistake.\n<p>This change visually groups permission modules into <strong>System</strong>, <strong>User</strong>, and <strong>Project</strong> sections on both the Actions and Fields tabs, using a single classification map so the UI communicates authority boundaries without changing how permissions are stored or enforced.</p>\n<p><strong>Business value:</strong> clearer role setup, fewer accidental admin grants, and a durable pattern for classifying future ACL modules.</p>\n<h3 data-tomark-pass="">Functional Requirements\n</h3><ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Classify every known ACL module into one of: System, User, Project (unknown modules may fall into Other).</li><li data-tomark-pass="">**System:** <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">user</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">role</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">userrole</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">permission</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">issuetype</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">issuestatus</code>.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">**User:** <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">userqualification</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">userskill</code>.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">**Project:** <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">project</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">issue</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">milestone</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">milestoneoverview</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">wiki</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">comment</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">membership</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">conversationroom</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">timelog</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">chatroom</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">upload</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">activity</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">tag</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">issuewatcher</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">vote</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">issueplanning</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">savedsearch</code>.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Keep classification in a shared util (<code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">app/utils/acl/module-types.js</code>) used by the role permissions component.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Render labeled sections (System → User → Project) on both Actions and Fields tabs.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Add i18n labels for section headers; System section may show an admin/elevated-authority hint.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Style section headers distinctly (System amber, User green, Project blue) within existing role permission layout.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Do not change permission save/load semantics, allowed values, or backend ACL enforcement — visual grouping only.</li></ul><h3 data-tomark-pass="">Expected Behavior\n</h3><ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Opening a role’s Permissions tab shows System Modules, then User Modules, then Project Modules (Other only if uncategorized modules exist).</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Modules appear under the correct section on both Actions and Fields tabs.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Saving permissions continues to work as today for each control.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Future modules not listed in the map still render under Other rather than disappearing.</li></ul><h3 data-tomark-pass="">UI/UX Considerations\n</h3><ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Preserve the existing dense module-row layout; only introduce section headers and spacing between groups.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Section headers use short product language (“System Modules”, “User Modules”, “Project Modules”) with icons.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">System header tooltip explains elevated-authority intent without blocking edits.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">No new empty states beyond existing “no actions / no fields” nothing-found patterns.</li></ul><h3 data-tomark-pass="">Acceptance Criteria\n</h3><ul data-tomark-pass=""><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Role Permissions Actions tab shows System / User / Project sections with correct module membership.</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Role Permissions Fields tab uses the same grouping.</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass=""><code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">user</code> is under System; <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">userqualification</code> and <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">userskill</code> are under User; <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">savedsearch</code> and project-owned modules are under Project.</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Classification lives in <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">app/utils/acl/module-types.js</code> via <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">getModuleScope()</code>.</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">i18n keys exist for <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">scope.system</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">scope.user</code>, <code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">scope.project</code> (and Other if shown).</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Section header styles distinguish System / User / Project visually.</li><li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="" data-tomark-pass="">Permission update/save behavior is unchanged.</li></ul><h3 data-tomark-pass="">Expected Outcome\n</h3>Admins can visually distinguish platform, user-profile, and project ACL modules when configuring roles, reducing mistaken elevated grants while keeping the existing permission model intact.\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3951	2026-09-23	2026-09-22	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	d766f5c36aa7-8d4d-98f6-5dd803999bdf	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	f09839e86ab3-816d-3791-59d5409a0ff5	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-09-23 10:29:45	aprom	0	0
9778b9036af1-35f0-87ea-fed893ae3de3	Talos: one Gaia URL - configure writes gaiaUrl next to hermesUrl, Talos falls back to gaia-mcp.env GAIA_URL	2026-11-09 11:46:31	2026-11-09 15:09:00	0	<p><code>talos/config.json</code> defaults <code>gaiaUrl</code> to the local stack (<code>https://api.local-projects4.me</code>) while the agents' env files use devapi. Talos's service identity therefore enrolled with the local Gaia; requests expired because admins approved on devapi.</p><p><strong>Change:</strong></p><ul><li><code>p4m configure</code> writes <code>gaiaUrl</code> into <code>talos/config.local.json</code> (merging, like <code>hermesUrl</code>), taken from <code>GAIA_URL</code> in <code>gaia-mcp.env</code>.</li><li>When <code>gaiaUrl</code> is not set locally, Talos uses <code>GAIA_URL</code> from <code>gaia-mcp.env</code> instead of the config.json default.</li><li><code>talos enroll</code> prints the Gaia URL it enrolls with.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests for the fallback order (config.local.json, gaia-mcp.env, config.json) and that configure keeps <code>hermesUrl</code>.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4414</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4415	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	712014526af0-7d1c-cccd-ee6dc2488b11	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	1d3a3c136af1-7d5c-b4fe-d65cfac66fa4	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 15:09:00	adt	0	0
