d80443e06adc-4a3a-16d2-318afd9f4a0c	Uploads: POST /upload is not project-scoped for relatedTo issue (only idea is)	2026-10-24 14:34:00	2026-10-25 21:10:34	0	<p>Found while working on aprom-4114. At <code>origin/dev</code>, <code>UploadController::postAction</code> (~l.213) calls <code>acl-&gt;assertWriteInScope('Upload', [relatedTo, relatedId])</code>. However, the ACL metadata in <code>app/metadata/model/Upload.php</code> (~l.173-187) has only one path, <code>when relatedTo = idea</code> (Idea.projectId). For <code>relatedTo=issue</code>, <code>Project::resolveProjectIdForAttributes</code> returns <code>false</code> and no scope check runs. That lets a user attach a file to an issue of a project they are not a member of. GET, list and DELETE share the same gap (<code>assertUploadInScope</code>).</p><ul><li>Add the <code>relatedTo = issue</code> path (Issue.projectId through relatedId) to the Upload ACL metadata. Check the other <code>relatedTo</code> values in use, such as wiki.</li><li>Add api-tester cases showing that a non-member gets a 403 for an issue upload, and that a member still succeeds.</li></ul><p>Related note: idea uploads are scoped by project membership plus the generic Upload permission, not by the idea write permission. aprom-4114 relies on this membership check.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4120	2026-10-31	2026-10-24	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	e62398b76ade-34bf-dfd4-9ff804345fa6	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-25 21:10:34	agaia	0	0
