09c724166ad6-89d7-93af-8c588b51b491	Settings > Email: remove the "Leave a value blank to use the server configuration." callout	2026-10-19 20:43:53	2026-10-20 17:38:35	0	<p>The SMTP box opens with a <code>callout-info</code>: "Leave a value blank to use the server configuration." Admins are expected to know how to configure SMTP, so the hint isn't needed. It also contradicts the form: Host and Port show "This field is required" when blank.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove the callout from <code>app/templates/app/settings/email.hbs</code> and its translation key from <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li>\n<li>Keep the current field validation (Host and Port required).</li>\n<li>Not required: prefilling the fields with the server's effective values. That would be the better design if it's ever wanted, but it's out of scope here.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p>\n<ul><li>No callout above the SMTP fields; the email acceptance scenarios pass (remove any step that checks the callout text).</li></ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	4023	2026-10-27	2026-10-20	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	7f53bcb86ace-34bf-02fa-83a17db4682e	ae6454575acb-1902-6b9c-f2ffa11a2697	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	86efe1706ad7-370c-f013-a9bd06f8f295	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-20 17:38:35	aprom	0	0
d872d0d76af1-db9b-4036-1291a1b4bf8b	ai rabbit off / on: a switch that stops all CodeRabbit submissions, like talos pause/resume	2026-11-09 16:12:08	2026-11-09 16:22:37	0	<p><strong>Why:</strong> CodeRabbit now limits us to 2 reviews an hour, because we sent more than 77 reviews in the last 7 days. It adds little value right now, so the engineer needs to turn agent submissions off and back on at will. Today the only way to stop them is to fill the 24-hour ledger with fake entries.</p>\n<p><strong>Where:</strong> every agent submission already goes through <code>rabbitbudget.request()</code> (<code>ai/lib/rabbitbudget.py</code>). That covers <code>pr-opened</code> from <code>ai ship</code>, <code>bot-round</code> / <code>reenter</code> from the Talos fix loop, and <code>update-branch</code> / <code>conflict</code> / <code>backlog</code> from Agamemnon. Nothing else posts the trigger, so the switch only needs a check there.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><code>ai rabbit off [--reason "…"]</code> and <code>ai rabbit on</code>. The state goes in <code>ai/state/rabbit-switch.json</code>: <code>{"off": true, "since": "&lt;UTC %Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ&gt;", "reason": "…"}</code>. Write it under <code>common.state_locked("rabbit-switch")</code> with an atomic replace. A missing file means on. The state survives restarts and isn't committed config.</li>\n<li><code>request()</code> while off: return <code>{"decision": "human", "reason": "CodeRabbit is off (&lt;reason&gt;)", ...}</code>. Post no comment and record no send.</li>\n<li><strong>Don't defer while off:</strong> PRs that go to the human because the switch is off are <em>not</em> added to <code>deferred</code>. Otherwise Agamemnon's backlog sweep would send them all to CodeRabbit the moment it's turned back on.</li>\n<li><code>ai rabbit on</code> clears the existing <code>deferred</code> list by default, for the same reason. <code>--keep-deferred</code> keeps it.</li>\n<li><code>ai rabbit budget</code> and <code>--json</code> report the switch, adding <code>"off": bool, "offSince", "offReason"</code> to the JSON. When off, the text output starts with a line saying "CodeRabbit is OFF since … (reason)". Talos, Agamemnon and TalosExt read this.</li>\n<li>Callers handle the result the same way as the existing <code>human</code> decision (HUMAN ONLY tier). Check that the Talos bot-review loop and Agamemnon's backlog sweep stop cleanly and don't log the result as a failure.</li>\n<li>Update the README / help text for <code>ai rabbit</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Tests</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Switch round trip (off with a reason, on, missing file means on).</li>\n<li><code>request()</code> while off: no <code>gh pr comment</code>, nothing in <code>sent</code> or <code>deferred</code>, and decision <code>human</code> for every source.</li>\n<li><code>on</code> clears <code>deferred</code>, and <code>--keep-deferred</code> keeps it.</li>\n<li><code>budget()</code> reports <code>off</code> / <code>offSince</code> / <code>offReason</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>TalosExt (local, not part of this issue) already reads <code>ai/state/rabbit-switch.json</code> and shows an OFF badge.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4422	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	df3c50c46af1-3ffe-8580-92b18f966c95	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 16:22:37	adt	0	0
6e4d76e96aea-9509-4534-72629c210ef9	Editor mention menus: visible Up/Down keyboard navigation for emoji, user and issue suggestions	2026-11-03 16:44:30	2026-11-11 10:38:09	0	<p>In the comment and description editor (<code>AppUi::ToastUi</code>), typing <code>:</code>, <code>@</code> or <code>#</code> opens a Tribute suggestion menu. Users can't pick an entry with the Up/Down keys. Tribute supports keyboard navigation, but <code>attachTributeEvents</code> in <code>app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js</code> gives the list Bootstrap's <code>dropdown-menu</code> class, and no stylesheet styles Tribute's <code>li.highlight</code>, so the selected item is probably invisible.</p><ul><li>First reproduce it in the running app (an issue comment box) and confirm the cause. Check whether the highlight only lacks styling, or whether the ToastUI wysiwyg editor also handles ArrowUp/ArrowDown/Enter (moving the cursor or adding a line) while the menu is open. If it does, stop those keys while Tribute is active (<code>tribute.isActive</code>), in the existing <code>editor.addHook('keydown', ...)</code> or the target element's keydown listener.</li><li>Style the highlighted item like a hovered Bootstrap dropdown item (<code>.tribute-container li.highlight &gt; a</code>), with colours from <code>app/styles/variables.scss</code> and square edges. Put the rule in the shared editor styles (an existing scss file next to the editor/ToastUI styles), not inline.</li><li>Use the mouse hover and the keyboard highlight as the same selection (Tribute's default), and keep the highlighted item in view.</li><li>Enter or Tab inserts the highlighted item, and Escape closes the menu. Ctrl+Enter submit still must not fire while the menu is open (the current <code>isTributeActive</code> logic).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Typing <code>:smi</code> in a comment opens the emoji menu with the first item visibly highlighted. Down/Up moves the highlight without moving the editor's cursor, and Enter inserts the highlighted emoji.</li><li>The same works in the <code>@</code> and <code>#</code> menus.</li><li>An integration test in <code>tests/integration/modifiers/initialize-toastui-test.js</code> sends ArrowDown and then Enter, and checks that the second suggestion was inserted. It fails if the fix is reverted.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing what the menus search or list, and the legacy <code>message-box.js</code> and <code>summer-note.js</code> editors.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4268	2026-11-10	2026-11-03	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	b43cc5046ae8-20b5-32a1-13b222266c79	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	d40900b46aea-b7a0-4534-9135a37b34f4	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-04 07:17:39	aprom	0	0
