66e970506ada-4a9c-1fa7-6bea231b1571	Task board: change the assignee from the issue card (shared Issue::AssigneeSelect)	2026-10-22 14:49:10	2026-10-24 10:29:17	0	<p>On the task board the card only shows the assignee's avatar. To reassign an issue, users have to open the quick view and use the dropdown in the issue details. The same dropdown should work directly on the card. The dropdown exists only inside <code>Issue::IssueDetails</code> (aprom-3681 built it there), so this issue moves it into a shared component used in both places.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New Glimmer component <code>app/components/issue/assignee-select.{js,hbs}</code> with one job: show an issue's assignee and let the user pick another project member. Args: <code>@issue</code>, <code>@members</code> (the project members), <code>@compact</code> (avatar-only trigger for cards) and an optional <code>@onUpdated(issue)</code> callback.</li><li>Move the following from <code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code> (~l.1191-1279) into the new component: <code>availableAssignees</code> (active members other than the current assignee), <code>handleAssigneeOptionKeydown</code> and <code>updateAssignee</code> (sets <code>assignedTo</code>/<code>assignee</code>, <code>issue.save()</code>, Messenger toasts with the existing <code>views.app.issue.detail.assignee*</code> strings, <code>rollbackAttributes()</code> on failure). Keep the markup from <code>issue-details.hbs</code> ~l.283-307 (<code>dropdown</code>, <code>dropdown-menu</code>, the <code>data-issue-assignee*</code> attributes), and move its inline <code>style</code> on the option avatar into a scss class.</li><li><code>issue-details.hbs</code> uses the component in place of the inline dropdown and passes <code>projectController.model.members</code> plus the existing <code>postUpdateAssignee</code> as <code>@onUpdated</code>. Its behaviour and tests stay unchanged.</li><li><code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code> (~l.125, <code>.issue-card-assignee</code>): the avatar becomes the compact trigger, using <code>@membersList</code>, which the board already passes in. Open the menu with <code>dropdown-menu-right</code> so it stays inside the lane, and show the member's name on hover as today.</li><li>Clicking or using the keyboard on the trigger or the menu must not open the quick view and must not start a Sortable drag. Stop the event from propagating, and/or add the element to Sortable's <code>filter</code>/<code>preventOnFilter</code>.</li><li>After a reassignment the card updates in place and stays draggable. Do not re-render the whole card (see aprom-3700). If the reassigned issue is open in the quick view, the quick view shows the new assignee too, since both read the same model.</li><li>Styles go under the board and issue modules in <code>app/styles/modules/</code>. Follow <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>: square menu edges, 50% radius only on avatars.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>On the task board, clicking a card's assignee avatar opens a list of active project members (avatar + name), without the current assignee. Choosing one saves the issue, shows the existing updating, updated and failed toasts, and updates the avatar on the card.</li><li>Opening the menu or choosing a member does not open the quick view or move the card. The card can still be dragged afterwards.</li><li>If the save fails, the card goes back to the old assignee.</li><li>The issue detail view (page and quick view) behaves exactly as before, through the shared component.</li><li>Tests: an integration test for <code>Issue::AssigneeSelect</code> (lists members, excludes the current assignee, saves, rolls back on error), and an acceptance scenario on the board (Mirage) that reassigns from the card. Existing issue-detail assignee tests still pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing status, priority or estimate from the card; unassigning; searching or filtering the member list; live updates from other users (aprom-3978).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4102	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	103dbf626adc-12b7-2cae-fc54b263e52a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-24 10:29:17	aprom	0	0
883f53386af1-ee79-8580-c990a9ba8f47	Retro - aga-v1	2026-11-09 16:32:08	2026-11-09 16:32:08	0	<p>2026-10-31 to 2026-11-30 · 79 issues (78 done, 0 carried over, 1 wont_fix) · 25h 27m logged vs no time estimate on any issue (estimates are 0m everywhere)</p>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>aga-v1 delivered 78 of 79 issues; the one other, #4341, was closed as wont_fix because an earlier fix had already resolved it. Every issue was implemented by Agent Achilles in 5 to 70 minutes of logged time, and most Agent Agamemnon merged automatically after a clean CodeRabbit run. The largest costs were not implementation but the test and ship environment (Docker, a flaky test, shared state), missing "Depends on" links early in the milestone, and CodeRabbit quota running out late. A layout change in #4338 produced a chain of follow-up bug issues.</p>\n<h2>Numbers</h2>\n<table><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Planned / added</td><td>not computable (see Data gaps)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Delivered</td><td>78 of 79 (99%); #4341 wont_fix</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Estimate accuracy</td><td>not computable: estimated time is 0m on all 79 issues</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Logged time</td><td>25h 27m across 79 issues (sum of the time logs I read)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Late</td><td>0 (every issue end date is on or before 2026-11-15; milestone ends 2026-11-30)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Rework</td><td>at least 6 follow-up or fix-up issues from #4338 and #4326: #4339, #4340, #4341, #4344, #4347, #4335</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Waiting</td><td>at least 6 issues sent back to new or held: #4036, #4045, #4056, #4057, #4058, #4059 (missing dependencies); #4326 waited about 2.5h for input</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h2>What went well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Delivery was complete and on time: 78 of 79 done, no issue past the milestone end date — #4036 to #4349.</li>\n<li>Auto-merge after a clean CodeRabbit run kept small issues moving with no human round trip: 16 of the 22 issues in #4273 to #4309 were auto-merged — e.g. #4309, #4308, #4305, #4300, #4297, #4296.</li>\n<li>Serialising same-file work avoided conflicts in the ezSearch chain (#4293 to #4300): #4299, #4298 and #4297 were held until a predecessor merged because they shared <code>app.scss</code> and <code>en-us.json</code>. Same pattern in #4333 (behind #4331), #4337 (behind #4338), #4327/#4328/#4329 (behind #4326).</li>\n<li>Large scope was split by a design request instead of delivered in one go: #4044 was split into #4241, #4242, #4243 and #4244, and #4243's scope was narrowed after a design decision from the reviewer before coding.</li>\n<li>Agents stopped and asked rather than guess: #4326 (premise false), #4044, #4056, #4036 raised needs_input; #4288 and #4284 ended with no PR after the reviewer confirmed there was no Prometheus defect, and #4341's PR was closed cleanly.</li>\n<li>Unit and acceptance tests were added with fixes, e.g. #4307 confirmed the cause with a failing test; #4294 tested actual serializer output when the issue's examples did not match #4293.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What didn't go well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Not delivered: #4341 (wont_fix). The fix duplicated work already done by an earlier flex fix and conflicted with the fixed lane headers; the PR (#660) was closed. The issue was written assuming #4338 was the only cause, and #4340's fix had landed in parallel — #4341, #4340.</li>\n<li>Test and ship environment cost the most non-implementation time: Docker daemon down or overloaded, the 10-minute test cap close to the ~9.5–10 minute full run, and shared logs overwritten by concurrent runs — #4343 (22 of 41m on a blocked ship), #4342 (30m on the failed ship), #4337, #4340, #4244, #4242, #4222, #4221, #4207, #4287. The reviewer attributed Docker failures to parallel runs (#4244, #4242).</li>\n<li>A flaky file-preview test blocked or delayed runs and a flaky "Project | edit project" scenario (random projectManager id) caused CI failures — #4282, #4283, #4287, #4273; #4205, #4207, #4208, #4206.</li>\n<li>CodeRabbit quota ran out ("25 of 25 reviews used"), so almost every PR from #4324 onward had no bot review and was left to hand review — #4324 to #4349 (only #4337 and #4342 got a round).</li>\n<li>Browser checks were mostly not done and tests were often not shown failing before the fix — #4349, #4346, #4345, #4347, #4340, #4290, #4297, #4299.</li>\n<li>Design-review follow-ups were listed in PR comments but not picked up: #4297 (8 items), #4244 (items 1–8), #4331, #4273, #4252, #4298.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Patterns</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Missing dependencies: six issues created together on 2026-10-20 (#4036, #4045, #4056, #4057, #4058, #4059) each ended blocked or needs_input because they relied on #4038 or #4044 without listing it. Each was reset to new with the dependency added. Evidence of 6 occurrences in one batch.</li>\n<li>Test environment friction: 10+ issues (see above), with Docker down or contended during parallel runs. Time on ship and the full suite often equalled or exceeded implementation time (#4338 20m vs 13m; #4336 2m vs 14m; #4057 24 of 40m; #4223 15 of 20m).</li>\n<li>Cascading layout regressions: #4338 (inline search with the milestone tabs) was followed by #4339, #4340, #4341, #4344, #4347, #4348 (also #4337's layout), each a layout fix. Likely the original issue description carried the wrong layout (#4339 corrected it) and layout was hard to verify in Mirage (#4344).</li>\n<li>Removal broke an unchecked consumer: #4326 (remove QueryBuilder) assumed all lists were already migrated and then broke the prod build, fixed in #4335, which cost 96.4k output tokens against a 16.4k median.</li>\n<li>Merge conflicts: #4221, #4241, #4207, #4250, #4059, #4036 (mostly additive in <code>en-us.json</code>, <code>agent.scss</code>); also a tracked <code>docs/classes/Index.html</code>/<code>index.html</code> case collision tripped <code>ai ship</code> in #4221, #4207, #4222, #4224, #4223, #4204.</li>\n<li>File-count estimates drifted on some issues: #4273 (6 estimated, 13 actual), #4285 (4 vs 8), #4252 (7 vs 11), #4038 (no estimate, 41 files), #4044 (37 files, 135 turns, 81.7k output tokens, an automatic restart). Largest cost is on the biggest foundation issues #4038, #4057, #4044, #4036.</li>\n<li>Review rounds were few: only #4306 (4 rounds, merge gate failed on two open CodeRabbit threads) and #4237 (6 round entries, largely CI failures) exceeded two.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Surprises</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Single case: #4288's cause was a Gaia memory fault, not a Prometheus bug; a single case (#4287) showed idle Talos test containers holding about 12 of 15 GB of Docker memory.</li>\n<li>Single case: #4304 found the "apply on pick" behaviour the issue said #4300 had shipped was missing from the code.</li>\n<li>Single case: #4286's PR was opened with "pass 0, fail 1" and a failure labelled known, which the reviewer then asked to rebase.</li>\n<li>Single case: #4283 got a "you will need rebase" request after the PR had already merged.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Proposed actions</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Make <code>/start-issue</code> and issue creation check code dependencies and list "Depends on" before assigning (and have Agamemnon refuse to dispatch an issue whose dependency is not merged). Addresses missing dependencies (#4036 to #4059). Lives in the issue-creation skill and Agamemnon. Success: no needs_input reset caused by an unlisted dependency in the next milestone.</li>\n<li>Cap parallel Talos test runs against the shared Docker (or give each run its own container, memory-checked first) and raise or tune the 10-minute test cap. Addresses test environment friction. Lives in Talos and <code>ai test</code>. Success: no blocked ship because Docker is down or the cap was hit.</li>\n<li>Fix the known flaky tests (file-preview race, random projectManager id) and the tracked <code>docs/classes</code> case collision so tests don't rewrite tracked files. Addresses test environment friction and merge conflicts. Lives in the prometheus repo. Success: no "known failure" ship note and no tree-changed error.</li>\n<li>Before a removal issue (like #4326), require a grep of consumers listed in the issue and a <code>ember build -prod</code> in the ship checklist. Addresses removal breaking unchecked consumers. Lives in <code>ai ship</code> and the issue template.</li>\n<li>Turn design-review follow-ups into a proposed list on the PR hand-off for the reviewer, and note when CodeRabbit was skipped for quota so the reviewer can choose which PRs to hand-check. Addresses unpicked follow-ups and missing bot review. Lives in <code>ai ship</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Data gaps</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Estimate accuracy and overruns: every issue has an estimated time of 0m; only "estimated files" exist, so I could not compute time overruns.</li>\n<li>Planned vs added: the issue list does not show when each issue entered the milestone, so I could not separate planned from added or find issues moved out.</li>\n<li>Waiting time in feedback or pending: status history was not available; waits come from comments only (#4326 about 2.5h).</li>\n<li>CodeRabbit and review round counts come from time-log entries and comments, not from <code>gh</code> PR data (not read), so 0 may mean none logged. Hammad's comments are counted from the issue threads.</li>\n<li>Per-issue figures were read by three delegated passes over the issues; logged hours are my sum of their reported time totals.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Issue ledger</h2>\n<table><tr><th>#</th><th>Title</th><th>Status</th><th>Est</th><th>Actual</th><th>Review rounds</th><th>Notes</th></tr>\n<tr><td>4349</td><td>ezSearch: Enter no longer runs the search</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>15m</td><td>0</td><td>1 known failing scenario</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4348</td><td>Gantt Cal: timeline starts below the search</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>10m</td><td>0</td><td>fixes #4337 layout</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4347</td><td>Task Board: Filter modal opens behind overlay</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>23m</td><td>0</td><td>Docker issues; fail-first not shown</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4346</td><td>ezSearch: Saved menu items white on hover</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>7m</td><td>0</td><td>no browser check</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4345</td><td>ezSearch: two-line rows half highlighted</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>7m</td><td>0</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>4344</td><td>Task Board: lane headers above suggestion menu</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>6m</td><td>0</td><td>no layout test</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4343</td><td>ezSearch: suggestion menu washed out</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>41m</td><td>0</td><td>Docker down, 22m on blocked ship</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4342</td><td>Task Board: search without Milestone field</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>66m</td><td>1 CR</td><td>blocked ship, flaky timeout</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4341</td><td>Task Board: quick preview overlaps</td><td>wont_fix</td><td>0m</td><td>11m</td><td>1 human</td><td>PR #660 closed; flex fix already solved it</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4340</td><td>Task Board: lanes can't scroll horizontally</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>19m</td><td>0</td><td>already fixed; test only</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4339</td><td>Task Board: milestone tabs no longer wrap</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>13m</td><td>0</td><td>from #4338</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4338</td><td>Task Board: EzSearchCompact inline</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>33m</td><td>0</td><td>caused 5 follow-ups</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4337</td><td>Gantt Cal: EzSearchCompact</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>70m</td><td>1 CR</td><td>escalated to opus, 4 sessions</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4336</td><td>EzSearchCompact: icon buttons</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>16m</td><td>0</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>4335</td><td>Build: remove leftover doT import</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>14m</td><td>0</td><td>96.4k tokens; from #4326</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4334</td><td>Idea list: EzSearchCompact</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>20m</td><td>0</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>4333</td><td>EzSearchCompact component</td><td>done</td><td>0m</td><td>12m</td><td>0</td><td>held behind #4331</td></tr>\n<tr>