76c89b036aea-9509-4534-b3e1f70b8df2	Editor emoji menu: search emojis by emoticon shortcodes like :) and :D	2026-11-03 16:44:38	2026-11-11 10:38:24	0	<p>The <code>:</code> emoji menu in the comment and description editor only matches emoji names (<code>lookup: 'name'</code> in <code>setupTribute</code>, <code>app/modifiers/initialize-toastui.js</code>). Typing a familiar emoticon such as <code>:)</code> sends the query <code>)</code>, which finds nothing useful. Users should be able to find emojis by their common shortcodes.</p><ul><li>Add a shortcode map from emoji id (the ids in <code>emojiList</code> of <code>app/components/app-ui/toast-ui.js</code>) to the text typed after the <code>:</code> trigger. For example: <code>slightly-smiling-face</code>: <code>)</code>, <code>-)</code>; <code>smile</code>: <code>D</code>, <code>-D</code>; <code>slightly-frowning-face</code>: <code>(</code>, <code>-(</code>; <code>stuck-out-tongue</code>: <code>P</code>, <code>p</code>; <code>open-mouth</code>: <code>O</code>, <code>o</code>; <code>neutral-face</code>: <code>|</code>; <code>confused</code>: <code>/</code>; <code>cry</code>: <code>'(</code>; <code>wink</code>: <code>-*</code> or similar, chosen sensibly. Put it in a small util (e.g. <code>app/utils/emoji-shortcodes.js</code>, with YUIDoc and the license header). Shortcodes are not translated.</li><li>Include the shortcodes in each <code>translatedEmojis</code> entry built in <code>toast-ui.js</code>.</li><li>Replace the emoji collection's static <code>values</code> with a <code>values(text, cb)</code> function. It ranks emojis whose shortcode equals the query first, then names that start with the query, then the current fuzzy name matches, and keeps <code>menuItemLimit: 5</code>.</li><li>Show the matched shortcode after the name in the menu item (e.g. <code>🙂 Slightly smiling face :)</code>), escaped. Selecting it still inserts the emoji.</li><li>Check that a query containing <code>)</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>|</code>, <code>/</code> or <code>'</code> keeps the menu open (Tribute's query regex). Fix it with Tribute options if not.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Typing <code>:)</code> shows 🙂 as the first, highlighted suggestion, and Enter inserts it. <code>:D</code> gives 😄 and <code>:(</code> gives 🙁.</li><li>Name search still works (<code>:thumb</code> finds thumbs up).</li><li>Integration tests in <code>tests/integration/modifiers/initialize-toastui-test.js</code> cover shortcode ranking and name search, plus a unit test for the util.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> shortcodes that don't start with <code>:</code> (<code>;)</code>, <code>&lt;3</code>), which would need a new trigger; automatically converting a shortcode followed by a space without the menu; and the legacy <code>message-box.js</code> and <code>summer-note.js</code> editors.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4268</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4269	2026-11-10	2026-11-03	deferred	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	b43cc5046ae8-20b5-32a1-13b222266c79	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	03a034a46aea-aa31-0e96-4d7384d627c2	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-11 10:04:36	aprom	0	1
