0b6879f66ab5-011f-97b0-be5e0a483ae4	Soft-disable users by revoking sessions and blocking authentication	2026-09-24 13:56:27	2026-10-17 22:43:31	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Setting a user’s&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">accountStatus</code>&nbsp;to a non-active value (e.g. Inactive) must immediately end their ability to use the product. Today, soft-disable can leave existing OAuth access/refresh tokens and API sessions usable, so a deactivated user may continue authenticating until tokens expire.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">This change defines which statuses may authenticate (Active,&nbsp;Invited) and enforces that rule at every auth entry point: password grant, refresh token, and Bearer API authorization. When an admin deactivates a user, the system also revokes that user’s OAuth tokens and expires their session so disablement takes effect immediately—without weakening the existing admin lockout guard (cannot deactivate the last usable admin path).</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20);" data-tomark-pass="">Business value:&nbsp;immediate access revocation for offboarding and security incidents, consistent soft-disable behavior, and fewer residual sessions after account deactivation.</span></p>\n<h3>Functional Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Treat only&nbsp;Active&nbsp;and&nbsp;Invited&nbsp;as authenticatable (case-insensitive); all other statuses (Inactive, Disabled, empty, null) cannot authenticate.</li>\n<li>Reject password grant login for non-authenticatable accounts with stable error&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">account_inactive</code>.</li>\n<li>Reject refresh-token issuance for non-authenticatable accounts with the same error.</li>\n<li>Reject Bearer API requests for non-authenticatable accounts even if an access-token row still exists.</li>\n<li>On successful user PATCH that sets a non-authenticatable&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">accountStatus</code>, delete that user’s OAuth access and refresh tokens and set&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">sessionExpires</code>&nbsp;in the past.</li>\n<li>Keep Invited authenticatable so first-login / invite acceptance still works.</li>\n<li>Preserve existing AclLockoutGuard rules: cannot deactivate the last usable member of the last admin-capable role.</li>\n<li>Centralize status checks in&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">AclLockoutGuard</code>&nbsp;so login, refresh, and API auth share one definition.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Behavior</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Admin sets user to Inactive → tokens revoked, session expired → user cannot login, refresh, or call APIs.</li>\n<li>Active and Invited users can obtain tokens and use the API as today.</li>\n<li>Attempted login/refresh/API use by Inactive returns unauthorized with&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">account_inactive</code>.</li>\n<li>Deactivating the sole remaining usable admin remains blocked by lockout guard.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Acceptance Criteria</h3>\n<ul>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task=""><code data-backticks="1">AclLockoutGuard::isAuthenticatableAccountStatus</code>&nbsp;allows Active/Invited only (case-insensitive).</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Inactive (and similar) users cannot complete password grant; error is&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">account_inactive</code>.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Invited users can still obtain an access token.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Inactive users cannot refresh tokens.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Inactive users cannot authorize API requests with an existing Bearer token.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">PATCH to Inactive deletes access + refresh tokens for that user’s email and expires&nbsp;<code data-backticks="1">sessionExpires</code>.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Admin lockout on last usable admin deactivate still returns permission/422 behavior unchanged.</li>\n<li class="task-list-item" data-te-task="">Unit/API tests cover authenticatable status matrix, login, refresh, API auth, and revoke-on-deactivate.</li>\n</ul>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3954	2026-09-25	2026-09-24	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	63413fd6673b-6180-ffb0-440801685dd8	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	e66a64a26ab5-7ee0-3caa-54cce479d5bf	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-17 22:43:32	agaia	1	0
