1346eb386aea-2876-813e-68fd08cc05a1	Idea browser: shimmer skeleton in place of the status label while plan statuses load	2026-11-04 07:38:59	2026-11-11 10:38:07	0	<p>The idea browser (<code>app/templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>) shows a status label on each idea: Archived from the idea model, otherwise Brainstorming / Proposed / Created / ... from the latest <code>ideaplan</code>. The plans are queried separately by <code>loadPlans</code> in <code>app/routes/app/project/idea.js</code> after the ideas load, so until then open ideas wrongly show Brainstorming. aprom-4267 (prometheus#617) added a loading state with a spinner label in <code>app/controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> (<code>progressByIdea</code>, <code>loadPlanStatuses</code>), but the engineer sees no change in production. Replace that spinner with the shimmer skeleton used elsewhere in Prometheus, and make sure the loading state really works.</p><ul><li><strong>Check first:</strong> on current <code>dev</code>, open the ideas page with DevTools network throttling (Slow 3G) and confirm whether open ideas show the loading state until the plans response arrives. If they still show Brainstorming first, find out why (e.g. the loaded state set before the plans query resolves, or <code>setupController</code> not resetting it) and fix it in the controller and route, with a unit test that fails before the fix.</li><li>While an open idea's status is loading, render <code>&lt;span class="pull-right skeleton-line skeleton-line--xs idea-status-skeleton" data-idea-status-skeleton&gt;</code> in place of its <code>label</code> span, containing a <code>sr-only</code> "Loading" text (<code>views.app.idea.progress.loading</code>; add the key to <code>translations/en-us.json</code> if missing). No spinner icon.</li><li>Reuse the shimmer from <code>app/styles/components/skeleton.scss</code> (<code>.skeleton-line</code>). Add only <code>.idea-status-skeleton</code>, scoped under the idea list in <code>app/styles/modules/idea.scss</code>: about the height and width of a status label, no margin, aligned with the title, and <code>border-radius: 0</code> (square edges per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>).</li><li>The skeleton ends when the plans query resolves, fails or returns nothing (failure falls back to Brainstorming; the route already reports the error). Archived ideas show Archived immediately. Live plan events (<code>idea.plan.created</code>, <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code>) and <code>setPlanStatus</code> keep the current labels instead of bringing the skeleton back. A switch to another project's ideas shows the skeleton again.</li><li>Update the unit tests (<code>tests/unit/controllers/app/project/idea-live-test.js</code>) and idea browser acceptance steps (<code>tests/acceptance/steps/ideas/idea-browser-steps.js</code>) so they check <code>[data-idea-status-skeleton]</code> while loading and <code>[data-idea-status]</code> after.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>With Slow 3G throttling, every open idea shows a shimmering bar on the right of its row until the plans response arrives, never Brainstorming and no spinner. Screen readers announce "Loading".</li><li>Then each bar is replaced by the real status label in the same place, without the row shifting.</li><li>The bar has square edges and uses only the existing skeleton colours.</li><li>Verified in the running app (<code>https://app.local-projects4.me</code>) with throttling; the PR says so.</li><li>Tests pass, and each new check fails if its line is reverted.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a skeleton for the whole idea list while the ideas query loads, and changing how plans are queried.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> idea-browser-skeleton.png, idea-browser-loaded.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987