0f2108176ad6-89d7-93af-72f68b924f96	Settings > Email: Encryption uses a raw PowerSelect instead of the FormFields dropdown	2026-10-19 20:43:59	2026-10-20 18:03:47	0	<p>The Encryption field on the Email settings page doesn't look like the rest of the form. It renders a bare <code>&lt;PowerSelect&gt;</code> inside a hand-written <code>&lt;div class="form-group"&gt;&lt;label&gt;</code> (<code>app/templates/app/settings/email.hbs</code>, <code>data-field="setting.encryption"</code>). So the label is bold black instead of the crimson form label, it has no field underline styling, there's no validation wiring, and it sits apart from the other fields. <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code> §Forms says to use the <code>FormFields::*</code> components and never raw selects: select/relate → <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> with <code>@relateType="relate-simple"</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Replace the block with <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> (<code>@relateType="relate-simple"</code>, <code>@searchEnabled={{false}}</code>, <code>@label</code>, <code>@selected</code>, <code>@options</code>, <code>@data-field="setting.encryption"</code>, and <code>@validate</code>/<code>@message</code> like the other fields). See <code>components/user-profile/qualification.hbs</code> for a single-choice example.</li>\n<li>Option labels stay translated (tls / ssl / none). Adapt <code>encryptions</code> / <code>setEncryption</code> in <code>app/controllers/app/settings/email.js</code> to what <code>FieldRelate</code> expects (<code>@searchField="label"</code>, <code>@onchange</code>).</li>\n<li>Update the Gherkin steps that pick the encryption to select through the FieldRelate markup.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Encryption looks and behaves like the other selects in Prometheus forms (crimson label, square power-select, validation messages). Saving and testing still send the chosen value, and the email scenarios pass.</li></ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	4024	2026-10-27	2026-10-20	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	7f53bcb86ace-34bf-02fa-83a17db4682e	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	1c6c46f36ad7-b9b4-c0a9-6da08553d231	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-20 18:03:47	aprom	0	0
e2c507c16aeb-ef61-c1c6-50d522a75bfd	External Request: Workflows: 'Milestone completed' trigger (update triggers that match a field changing to a value)	2026-11-04 20:13:22	2026-11-04 21:05:13	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Prometheus (idea "Agents In Prometheus", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>A Prometheus needs a workflow that starts when a milestone is completed, so an agent can write a retrospective and create an issue from it. The trigger catalog (<code>core/libs/workflows/TriggerEventCatalog.php</code>) has issue, comment, wiki and time-log events only. Its update events match the fields that changed, never the value they changed to. Milestone writes aren't wired to workflows at all.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Catalog: let an update event name a transition, e.g. <code>'to' =&gt; ['status' =&gt; 'completed']</code>. The event is raised only when the field changes to that value from another value. <code>raisedBy</code> then needs the audit's old and new values, not only the changed field names. Update <code>WorkflowTriggersComponent::raise</code> and <code>changed</code> to pass them. Keep the current behaviour for events without <code>to</code>.</li><li>Add <code>EventNames::MILESTONE_COMPLETED</code> (<code>milestone.completed</code>, already a live event) as a trigger: model <code>Milestone</code>, on update, field <code>status</code>, to <code>completed</code>, label 'Milestone completed'. Use the same rule as <code>MilestoneLiveEventsComponent</code> (~l.77): new status completed, old status not completed.</li><li>Add <code>Events\\WorkflowTriggers</code> to <code>MilestoneController</code> <code>$uses</code>.</li><li>Check that the payload, the describer (<code>TriggerEventDescriber</code>: fields and types for filters and expressions such as <code>{milestone.name}</code>), <code>ProjectIdResolver</code> (knows milestone), <code>SetFieldAction</code>'s model check and the test run (<code>TestRunPayload</code>, <code>WorkflowrunController</code> with <code>entityType</code> Milestone) all work for a milestone.</li><li><code>GET /workflowevent</code> lists the new trigger.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Completing a milestone (PATCH status to <code>completed</code>) starts the Active workflows with this trigger in the milestone's project. A Run agent step's actor step has <code>entityType</code> Milestone and the milestone's id.</li><li>Other milestone edits don't start them, and neither does saving an already completed milestone.</li><li>A test run against a milestone works.</li><li>Unit tests cover the catalog's transition matching. Regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other milestone triggers (created, started).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4271	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	77c73c366ae8-73b7-51f2-b6608da2587e	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	696724766aeb-e1dc-c1c6-fdeb7e8f71d8	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-04 21:05:13	agaia	0	0
