dd896d966af1-5fd4-36e2-0260010b9eb9	Keep every local repo's dev current: ai sync --all, after merges and on a Talos timer	2026-11-09 17:07:41	2026-11-09 17:23:56	0	<h3>Problem</h3>\n<p>On 2026-11-09 the local <code>dev</code> branch in <code>Pr4M/prometheus</code> was 47 commits behind <code>origin/dev</code>. Its last fast-forward was on 2026-11-08 at 00:53, before aprom-4356 (#674) and aprom-4359 (#678) merged. As a result, Nestor reported that no local checkout had the merged paging, sorting and grouping code.</p>\n<p>The cause is that local <code>dev</code> only advances on <code>ai start</code> or <code>ai sync</code>. Both check out <code>dev</code>, so neither runs while a checkout sits on an issue branch: <code>prometheus</code> has been on <code>claude-issue-4335</code>. <code>p4m repos sync</code> switches branches, so it isn't safe to run unattended. Squash merges made things worse, because the branch heads weren't ancestors of <code>dev</code>. Squash is now stopped, and PRs use merge commits.</p>\n<h3>Change</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><b><code>ai sync --all</code></b> (and <code>ai sync &lt;repo&gt;</code>, which keeps working without a checkout) covers gaia, prometheus, hermes, ares and dev-tools (<code>main</code>). For each repo:\n<ul>\n<li>run <code>git fetch origin --prune</code>;</li>\n<li>if the base branch is <b>not</b> checked out, run <code>git fetch origin dev:dev</code>. This is fast-forward only and doesn't touch the working tree;</li>\n<li>if it <b>is</b> checked out and the tree is clean, run <code>merge --ff-only</code>;</li>\n<li>if the tree is dirty or the branch has diverged, skip with a clear warning. Never force, reset or switch branches.</li>\n</ul>\nIn a Talos <code>.runs</code> worktree, only fetch, as <code>sync_dev</code> does today.</li>\n<li><b>Sync after merge:</b> when the merge step (<code>mergegate</code>, Agamemnon) merges a PR, sync that repo.</li>\n<li><b>Sync on a timer:</b> <code>talos run</code> runs <code>ai sync --all</code> every ~10 minutes. This catches PRs merged by hand on GitHub.</li>\n<li><b>Treat the remote as the truth:</b> Nestor and other agents that read merged code fetch first and read <code>origin/dev</code>, not local <code>dev</code>.</li>\n<li><b>Show the drift:</b> <code>ai status</code> shows <code>behind origin/&lt;base&gt;: N</code> per repo. The Talos status warns when a repo has been behind for more than an hour.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Acceptance</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>With prometheus on an issue branch, <code>ai sync --all</code> fast-forwards <code>dev</code> to <code>origin/dev</code> and leaves the working tree and the current branch unchanged.</li>\n<li>A dirty or diverged repo is skipped with a warning, and the other repos still sync.</li>\n<li>Unit tests for each case, using temporary git repos. The code works on Windows and Linux, and the <code>ai/README.md</code> command table and the Talos README are updated.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Out of scope</h3>\n<p>Setting each GitHub repo to allow only merge commits. The reviewer changes that in GitHub settings.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4424	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	2ca230536af1-b1fb-36e2-ed96ae340d89	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 17:23:57	adt	0	0
