175e12c86af2-9f9a-36e2-8339f6296766	State toolkit: AsyncResource and ListLoader (newest call wins, loading, error, retry)	2026-11-09 17:17:11	2026-11-09 17:37:27	0	<p>Pages load data in controllers with hand-written flags and no protection against stale responses. For example, the Task Board's <code>selectIssue</code>/<code>loadIssueDetails</code> (<code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> ~l.845/911) sets <code>isLoadingIssueDetails</code> by hand, and two quick clicks can show the wrong issue. This issue adds the shared async pieces of a small state toolkit in <code>app/utils/state/</code>. The URL part (<code>UrlState</code>) is a separate issue built in parallel.</p><ul><li><code>app/utils/state/async-resource.js</code>, class <code>AsyncResource</code> (native class, <code>@tracked</code>): constructor <code>{ load(params) }</code> (an async function the caller supplies, e.g. a store query). <code>run(params)</code> sets <code>isLoading</code>, awaits <code>load</code>, and only the newest call writes <code>value</code>/<code>error</code> (request token; older responses are dropped). <code>retry()</code> re-runs the last params; <code>reset()</code> clears everything; <code>seed(value, params)</code> sets an already-loaded value. On error the previous <code>value</code> is kept. Guard writes after the owner is destroyed (<code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> on an optional owner).</li><li><code>app/utils/state/list-loader.js</code>, class <code>ListLoader</code> built on <code>AsyncResource</code>: constructor <code>{ store, modelName, pageSize, buildRequest(params) }</code>. It asks for <code>requestLimit(pageSize)</code> rows (the page-window helper from aprom-4360) and exposes <code>items</code> and <code>hasNext</code> through <code>pageWindow</code>, plus <code>isLoading</code>, <code>error</code>, <code>retry</code>, <code>reset</code> and <code>seed(records, params)</code>. <code>buildRequest</code> is the single place that builds the query options; routes that load a first page must use the same function.</li><li>YUIDoc on both classes. No component or route changes here.</li><li>Unit tests (load stubbed): newest call wins over a slower older one, loading flags, error keeps the old value, retry, reset, seed, no writes after destroy; ListLoader page window and hasNext.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: URL state (separate issue), using the classes in any page.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4360</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4425	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	3de583a66af2-9f9a-36e2-fa622ff30224	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 17:37:27	aprom	0	0
