8ccc92e9698f-5cb0-3cfc-abd5773f5499	Project selection & switch issue	2026-02-13 14:13:32	2026-03-02 11:30:41	0	<p>The project should be automatically selected from the dropdown when the user has not selected a project from the dropdown and opens a link, e.g. issue. When that issue link is opened, in the background, the project is selected, but the user has no idea which project is being selected.</p>\n<p>When the project is switched, the user should be on the same page where they were. This allows easy navigation ability and reduces user effort on navigating to the page they were on previously! User history will be restored just on main routes e.g. taskboard, gantt etc</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	1	3814	2026-02-14	2026-02-13	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	1d417f106953-b800-4eb2-7750214eb597	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	290a9e606995-9dba-6adb-adc8f787d257	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-03-02 11:30:41	aprom	0	0
19cdc4486aee-8d2e-aab0-488950fa2074	ezSearch: Saved Searches menu opens off-screen on mobile	2026-11-07 07:36:57	2026-11-07 09:26:23	0	<p>On mobile the ezSearch Saved Searches menu opens to the left of its button, so most of it is outside the viewport. Cause: <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> positions <code>.app-dropdown-content</code> with <code>right: 0</code> (<code>app/styles/components/dropdown.scss</code> l.26), so the menu lines up with the button's right edge and grows leftwards. The Saved Searches button sits at the left edge of the screen. The menu should line up with the button's left edge and grow to the right.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In the ezSearch toolbar styles (<code>app/styles/components/ez-search.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.ez-search</code>), set the Saved Searches dropdown content to <code>left: 0; right: auto</code>, at every screen width (the button is always first in the toolbar).</li><li>Keep the menu inside the viewport on narrow screens: <code>max-width</code> of the toolbar's width, with long saved-search names wrapping or truncated with an ellipsis.</li><li>Don't change the global <code>.app-dropdown-content</code> rule: other dropdowns rely on it (<code>styles/modules/board.scss</code> ~l.49, <code>conversation.scss</code> ~l.359).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>At 390px and at desktop width the open menu's left edge lines up with the button's left edge, and the whole menu is visible.</li><li>Other <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> menus (board, conversation) are unchanged.</li><li>An integration test for <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> checks that the open menu's left edge is not left of the button's left edge.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> itself, the search bar margin (separate issue).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 2</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-