067a1b176aee-67ee-a4f9-ee4379f897bc	ezSearch: allow apostrophes in values once Gaia binds query values	2026-11-07 02:03:50	2026-11-07 09:17:28	0	<p>The ezSearch serializer (<code>app/utils/query/serializer.js</code>, aprom-4293) refuses values with an apostrophe, because Gaia's <code>Clause.php</code> concatenated values into SQL. agaia-4302 binds the values as parameters, so names like <code>O'Brien</code> can be searched safely. Gaia still trims <code>'</code> from both ends of a value and splits IN lists on <code>','</code> until agaia-4303 adds the <code>''</code> escape, so a few cases stay refused.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>serializer.js</code>: allow <code>'</code> inside a single value, e.g. <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS O'Brien)</code> and <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS 'Rana''s board')</code>.</li><li>Keep refusing, with a clearer message ("Apostrophes can't start or end a value or appear in a list yet"):<ul><li>an apostrophe at the start or end of a value;</li><li>an apostrophe in any item of an IN or NOT IN list.</li></ul></li><li>Brackets and uppercase NULL/EMPTY stay refused (agaia-4303 and agaia-4301).</li><li>Update the message in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> and the serializer and round-trip unit tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests: <code>subject ~ O'Brien</code> serializes and round-trips.</li><li>Unit tests: <code>subject ~ "'quoted'"</code> and <code>assignee in O'Brien, rana</code> are refused with the new message.</li><li>On the Issue list (local Gaia with agaia-4302), searching <code>O'Brien</code> returns matching issues without a server error.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>''</code> escape and brackets (after agaia-4303).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4302, aprom-4293</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987