3cb007136aee-19e9-5a2a-01a583f04360	Agamemnon sweep: give stranded ready issues back to the worker	2026-11-07 08:11:40	2026-11-07 08:46:41	0	<p>When the worker loses an issue (agaia-4303: held, then dropped on a reconnect), Agamemnon's sweep doesn't see it. The sweep only assigns new issues that have no assignee, so it reported "nothing ready" with free slots while 4303 sat assigned to the worker with every dependency done.</p><ul><li>In the orchestrator sweep (<code>talos/lib/orchestrator</code>): find issues in its milestones that are assigned to the worker, in a status the worker acts on (new, pending), with every "Depends on" issue done, and with nothing queued, running or held in the worker for at least <code>strandedMinutes</code> (agent.json, default 15).</li><li>Give each one back through the same path <code>aga retry</code> uses (<code>tool.py</code> <code>_assign_worker</code>), at most as many as there are free slots, counted like a normal feed. Post the comment "{Agamemnon}: picked up a stranded issue" with why it was ready.</li><li>Don't touch issues held by Agamemnon itself, those in triage, or those in review.</li><li><code>talos status</code> lists stranded issues; README updated.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for the stranded rule (deps done vs not, queued or running vs not, below vs above the minutes) and the free-slot limit. <code>agamemnonProtected</code> paths: manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the worker-side fix (held-reconcile issue).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4311	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	55ecd6106aee-9ce1-5a2a-ab3cb7aa376c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 08:46:41	adt	0	0
