feea97636afa-3684-5afc-4d5f79e294b4	Agamemnon: triage a lint failure the worker blames on the base branch	2026-11-16 12:28:46	2026-11-16 17:09:36	0	<p><strong>What happened (aprom-4609):</strong> Achilles blocked on a <code>ai test prometheus</code> lint failure and said the base was broken ("lint now reports every suppressed violation on <code>dev</code> itself"). Agamemnon answered "incident type 'other' is outside Agamemnon's premise" and left it with the owner. The claim was wrong: CI lint on dev passed, and the branch's own edit had made a <code>.lint-todo</code> entry stale. A base check would have shown that in one step.</p><p><strong>Why it fell through:</strong> <code>talos/lib/agamemnon/classifier.py</code> maps to <code>base_test_failed</code> only on the worker's structured reason or phrases like "fails on dev too" / "not caused by the diff". "On <code>dev</code> itself" and the lint wording matched none of them. And even classified, <code>base_test_failed</code>'s <code>basetest</code> tier runs named tests, not lint.</p><ul><li>Classifier: send a handback whose failing suite is <code>lint</code> (from the run summary <code>lint: N errors</code> / handback failing suite) and that blames the base to a lint incident. That's either <code>base_test_failed</code> with lint support or a new <code>base_lint_failed</code> type in <code>premise.json</code>; pick one and record why. Widen the base-blame patterns (e.g. "on dev itself", "on dev as well", "dev is broken").</li><li>Base check for lint: run <code>p4m test lint</code> on a clean throwaway checkout of the base (as <code>basetest</code> does for tests) and compare the failing files and rules.</li><li>Lint passes on the base: send the issue back to the worker/Odysseus with the failing lines. If the errors include <code>invalid-todo-violation-rule</code>, say the diff made a recorded todo stale and the violation should be fixed. Lint fails on the base: <code>file-bug</code> (or link the open one), then hold until it's done, as for tests.</li><li>Classifier and verb tests, including the 4609 handback text as a fixture.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> replaying the 4609 handback opens a lint incident (not <code>other</code>), runs lint on the base, finds it clean and sends the issue back with the stale-todo explanation.</p><p>Related: adt-4584 (local test failures the diff did not cause), adt-4563 (lint in <code>ai test</code>).</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4620	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	5beb6f376afb-23a5-b408-43cdaef774a1	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 17:09:36	adt	0	0
