516593296aee-19e9-5a2a-0ad15e8bc637	aga: ci-log and base-ci read verbs	2026-11-07 08:12:01	2026-11-07 09:41:50	0	<p>To tell a temporary CI failure from one the PR caused, or one already broken on the base branch, a triage session must read the failing job's log and compare it with the base branch. <code>aga</code> has no CI reads today (only <code>mergecheck</code>).</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/verbs.py</code> + <code>tool.py</code>: <code>ci-log</code> (tier read): the failed jobs on the PR head with name, URL and the tail of <code>gh run view --log-failed</code> (last ~150 lines per job, secrets masked as gh does). <code>base-ci</code> (tier read): the same workflow's latest completed run on the PR's base branch (dev or main), whether its jobs passed, and whether the failing job names on the PR head also fail there.</li><li>The gh calls go in <code>talos/lib/orchestrator/merge.py</code> next to <code>failed_jobs</code>, behind small functions.</li><li>Talos README (the <code>aga</code> tool): the verbs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests with stubbed gh output: no failed jobs, one failed job, base passing vs failing the same job. <code>agamemnonProtected</code> paths: manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> premise grants and role text (ci-premise issue).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4313	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	5d1a9fe06aee-f0ca-80cc-d69b457af729	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 09:41:50	adt	0	0
