336a86116af2-9f9a-36e2-9abde61800d3	Docs: page state architecture (URL vs controller state, in-place loading)	2026-11-09 17:17:39	2026-11-15 10:37:08	0	<p>Write down how Prometheus pages manage state, so later pages (Task Board, Gantt Cal, other QuickLists) use the toolkit the same way.</p><ul><li><code>prometheus/docs/architecture/state/architecture.md</code>: the toolkit (<code>AsyncResource</code>, <code>ListLoader</code>, <code>UrlState</code>), when state belongs in the URL (anything a user would bookmark, reload or go back to: list params, an open quick view) and when it stays in the controller (transient UI such as hover, collapsed groups), and how a page wires them (route seeds the first load with the same <code>buildRequest</code>; controller owns the loaders; <code>UrlState.onChange</code> drives reloads; reset on exit and project switch).</li><li><code>prometheus/docs/architecture/state/decisions.md</code> (same format as <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md</code>): list and view params never refresh the route; newest request wins; paging by limit + 1 (link to <code>docs/architecture/lists/decisions.md</code> from aprom-4360).</li><li>Link the new docs from <code>prometheus/CLAUDE.md</code> Architecture section in one line.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: docs match the merged toolkit APIs.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4425, aprom-4426</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4427	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	400687176af2-baab-19af-004e725716b3	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 18:02:53	aprom	0	0
664ff0d86aee-19e9-5a2a-7bd4b35a16c6	aga: hold-until-done verb, then merge the base branch and re-run CI	2026-11-07 08:12:22	2026-11-07 09:42:17	0	<p>After a bug blocking a PR is filed and fixed, the blocked issue must pick up the fix: merge the base branch into the PR branch (never a rebase) and let CI run again. Today a person does this. adt-4278 adds condition holds to the journal (<code>hold-until-docker</code>); this adds a second condition.</p><ul><li><code>verbs.py</code> + <code>tool.py</code>: <code>hold-until-done &lt;issue&gt;</code> (tier wait): the blocked issue stays with Agamemnon (it is in review with an open PR), and the journal hold has the condition "issue N done".</li><li><code>holds.py</code> <code>release_due</code>: when N is done (worker's <code>dependency_done_statuses</code>), run <code>update-branch</code> on the held issue's PR, the same as the verb (merge the base on GitHub; on a conflict, hand it to the conflict flow as today), reset its CI re-run count and leave it to the merge sweep. Comment "#N is done: merged the base branch into the PR, CI runs again". When N is won't fix or deferred, release the hold to the owner with a comment.</li><li>A hold older than <code>docker.holdMaxHours</code>'s sibling <code>holdMaxHours</code> (default 72) goes to the owner.</li><li>Talos README: the verb.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests: a release on done runs update-branch once and resets the count; won't fix releases to the owner; the 72h handover; undo releases the hold. <code>agamemnonProtected</code> paths: manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filing the bug (file-bug issue).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4278, adt-4312</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4315	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103eb