ea5637f26af2-f370-ad89-eddda6c5e3e9	Roles: list + detail layout with QuickList, card details in each row, first role opened by default	2026-11-09 19:37:14	2026-11-15 10:37:28	0	<p>The Roles page (<code>templates/app/role.hbs</code>) shows a grid of <code>Role::Card</code>s (<code>components/role/card.{hbs,js}</code>) that squeezes into a <code>col-lg-2</code> column when a role opens (<code>controllers/app/role.js</code> <code>isRolePage</code>/<code>rolesClass</code>/<code>roleCardClass</code>). The route (<code>routes/app/role.js</code>) loads every role, every userrole with its user, and one permission query per role for access coverage; the search only filters the loaded names. Move it to the QuickList list + detail layout used by the idea browser, built on the state toolkit (<code>ListLoader</code>, <code>UrlState</code> from aprom-4425/4426) and the new <code>&lt;:leading&gt;</code> item block. The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and the existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li><strong>Layout</strong>: <code>.row</code> with <code>col-md-3</code> QuickList and <code>col-md-9</code> outlet (the existing <code>app.role.page</code>, unchanged). Remove <code>isRolePage</code>/<code>rolesClass</code>/<code>roleCardClass</code> and the <code>roles--detail-open</code> classes.</li><li><strong>Row</strong>, keeping all the card's information: <code>&lt;:leading&gt;</code> = square initials box (same initials logic as <code>Role::Card</code>) in the access-tier colour (existing tiers in <code>styles/modules/role.scss</code>: high/elevated/medium/low/no data). Primary = role name, the granted <code>{percent}%</code> label in the tier colour and, when above 0, a red <code>{percent}% denied</code> label (same values as the card's granted/denied). Secondary line 1 = description, one line cut off with an ellipsis, or grey italic "No description". Secondary line 2 = <code>Project::MemberAvatars</code> with <code>@maxVisible={{2}}</code> (or "No members") on the left and the modified date (<code>dateModified</code>, fallback <code>dateCreated</code>, <code>DD MMM YYYY</code>) on the right. Active row = the open role (QuickList's crimson bar replaces the card's chevron and fading). Reuse the card's translation keys.</li><li><strong>Header and search</strong>: "Roles" with count; <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> = <strong>New Role</strong> (<code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code>, ACL <code>role.create</code>) opening the existing add-role modal; <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> = <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> with new metadata <code>views.Role.search</code> (<code>Role.name</code>, <code>Role.description</code>, in <code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>, same format as <code>views.Idea.search</code>) plus saved searches as in the idea browser. No selection.</li><li><strong>Group and sort</strong>: group by none or access tier (client-side, loaded page only); sort by name (default ASC) or last modified (DESC) via Gaia <code>Role.name</code>/<code>Role.dateModified</code>.</li><li><strong>Data</strong>: <code>UrlState</code> for <code>query</code>, <code>searchId</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>order</code>, <code>group</code> (all <code>refreshModel: false</code>); a <code>ListLoader</code> for roles (20 per page, limit + 1, one shared <code>buildRequest</code>). After each page loads, query permissions only for that page's roles (<code>permission?roleId=</code> per role, as today) and userroles with <code>rels: 'user'</code> only for that page's role ids; compute coverage and members with the existing <code>coverageByRole</code>/<code>isActionAllowed</code>/<code>membersByRole</code> logic. Reset on leaving the roles area.</li><li><strong>First role by default</strong>: a new <code>app.role.index</code> route. Once the list has loaded and no role is open, it calls <code>replaceWith('app.role.page', firstRow.id)</code>, so Back doesn't bounce onto the list again. This also applies after a search, a page change or deleting the open role, but never moves a user away from a role they opened. When no roles match, the index shows a <code>box box-primary</code> with a centred grey <code>fa-info-circle</code> "No roles match this search".</li><li><strong>Keep working</strong>: create (the new role appears; reload the current page and open it), delete from the role page (<code>deleteRole</code> reloads the list instead of filtering arrays, then the first role opens), permission and member edits on the role page refresh that role's row (<code>syncRoleCoverage</code> and member reload for the open role).</li><li>Update the roles acceptance tests and Mirage handlers (role paging/sort, userrole by role ids). Add tests for: row content (initials, both labels, description fallback, avatars, date), search, paging, group by tier, first role opened on landing and after deleting the open role, and the no-match state.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: as above; the URL keeps the list params; opening a role doesn't reload the list.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: removing <code>Role::Card</code> and its styles (follow-up), bulk actions on roles.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4425, aprom-4426, aprom-4429</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 11 (The list, its per-page coverage and member data, and the auto-open index route ship together: a list without coverage or members would lose information from the cards, and without auto-open the detail column is empty on landing.)</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> roles-quick-list.png</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4430	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	af6df6106af2-bc15-ad89-0aa356344433	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 20:26:3