a28ce11869a5-c57f-e284-f402ae461644	Update Project label	2026-03-02 14:16:02	2026-03-11 15:15:32	0	<p>For now we're using Project: Project_Name as a label in the application parent container. The "Project:" label itself isn't useful because the project name is already telling on which project user is currently on.</p>\n<p>So remove that label kindof thing and just show the project name with some ui changes.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3817	2026-03-03	2026-03-02	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	1c5ba55169a5-edd6-cd30-52e2cd27f10c	\N	ae6454575acb-1902-6b9c-f2ffa11a2697	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	\N	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-03-11 15:15:29	aprom	0	0
1c4550956aef-6a89-ada2-8884e7a63ca3	ai rabbit request: daily CodeRabbit counter with a tier policy that posts the review trigger	2026-11-07 10:44:44	2026-11-07 11:10:55	0	<p>CodeRabbit includes about 26 PR reviews a day; after that it charges per file. Its auto review is turned off, so the agents now ask for every review by posting a trigger comment as Agent Odysseus. This issue adds the one place that decides whether an agent PR goes to CodeRabbit or to the human reviewer, posts the trigger and counts it. Only these agent triggers are counted; reviews people request themselves on GitHub are neither counted nor limited.</p><ul><li>New <code>ai/lib/rabbitbudget.py</code>: a ledger in <code>STATE_DIR</code> (<code>ai/lib/common.py</code>; under <code>LOCAL_DIR</code>, so the runtime copy and the checkout share it). Two lists: <code>sent</code> <code>{at (UTC ISO), repo, pr, sha, source}</code> and <code>deferred</code> <code>{at, repo, pr, issue, files}</code> (PRs that went to the human because of the limit). Writes are atomic and safe across processes (lock file plus write-to-temp-then-replace). Prune <code>sent</code> entries older than 48 hours.</li><li>Policy, a pure function of (used in the rolling last 24 hours, hand-written file count, rereview flag, settings): <code>used &lt; everyPrUntil</code> → coderabbit; <code>used &lt; limit</code> → coderabbit when <code>rereview</code> or <code>files &gt;= largePrFiles</code>, else human; otherwise human.</li><li>Settings in <code>ai/config.json</code>: <code>codeRabbitBudget: {everyPrUntil: 10, limit: 25, largePrFiles: 6}</code> and <code>codeRabbitTrigger: "@coderabbitai full review"</code>. A missing <code>codeRabbitBudget</code> means no limit.</li><li><code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source pr-opened|bot-round|reenter|update-branch|conflict|backlog [--files N] [--rereview] [--issue N] [--json]</code>. For a repo where <code>coderabbit.enabled(repo)</code> is false it answers <code>absent</code>. It applies the policy. On coderabbit, it posts the trigger as Agent Odysseus (<code>ody(repo, 'gh', 'pr', 'comment', ...)</code>), records it in <code>sent</code> with the head sha, and drops any <code>deferred</code> entry for the PR. On human, it adds a <code>deferred</code> entry (only when <code>--issue</code> is given; one per PR). It prints, or returns as JSON, <code>{decision: coderabbit|human|absent, used, limit, reason}</code>. A failed comment means the decision is human, with the error in <code>reason</code>; nothing is recorded in <code>sent</code>.</li><li><code>ai rabbit budget [--json]</code>: used, limit, the current tier, when the next slot frees up, and the deferred list.</li><li>Unit tests (ody mocked): every tier boundary (9/10, 24/25), large vs small, rereview in the middle tier, rolling window, deferred added and cleared, failed comment, disabled repo.</li><li>Document both commands and the settings in <code>ai/README.md</code> (CodeRabbit section); say that CodeRabbit's auto review is expected to be off.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>ai rabbit request</code> posts exactly one <code>@coderabbitai full review</code> comment when the policy says coderabbit and records it; <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code> reports the rolling count and the deferred PRs; <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the callers (ai ship, Talos, Agamemnon: separate issues); counting reviews people trigger themselves; cheaper merge-check options.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4317	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	8f2e83c96aef-6a89-ada2-fb7df0f9edc5	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 11:10:55	adt	0	0
