dfcabfc86af2-f370-ad89-100ee5428854	QuickList: optional leading block on QuickList::Item (icon/avatar column)	2026-11-09 19:37:03	2026-11-09 19:52:55	0	<p>Some lists need a visual on the left of each row with the text lines lined up beside it: the Roles list needs an initials square in its access-tier colour, issue lists a priority icon, user lists an avatar. <code>QuickList::Item</code> only has <code>&lt;:primary&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;:secondary&gt;</code> today. This adds an optional leading column to the QuickList contract.</p><ul><li><code>QuickList::Item</code> (<code>components/quick-list/item.{hbs,js}</code>): optional <code>&lt;:leading&gt;</code> block rendered in a fixed-width column before the body (after the selection checkbox when <code>@selectable</code>), top-aligned; the body takes the remaining width so the primary/secondary lines align under each other. Without the block, the row is exactly as today.</li><li>Pass the block through the root <code>QuickList</code>'s <code>&lt;:item&gt;</code> usage (callers write <code>&lt;item.leading&gt;</code> or the documented equivalent; keep it consistent with how <code>&lt;:primary&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;:secondary&gt;</code> are exposed).</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/components/quick-list.scss</code> (or the item partial): leading column width set by content, 8px gap, square edges. No new colours.</li><li>Show it on the Settings &gt; Developer &gt; UI QuickList page (an initials square on the fixture rows).</li><li>Update the YUIDoc contract; integration tests: row with leading (column rendered before the body, body lines intact), row without leading unchanged, with selection (checkbox, then leading, then body).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: as above; existing QuickList tests pass unchanged.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4429	2026-11-17	2026-1