317c89c66aef-6a89-ada2-636bb0bcf579	Talos CodeRabbit loop: request a review after each fix round, hand off when the budget says human	2026-11-07 10:45:05	2026-11-07 11:23:44	0	<p>With CodeRabbit's auto review off, a fix round's push gets no review unless Talos asks for one, and the merge check needs a CodeRabbit result on the latest commit. Each follow-up review counts toward the daily limit.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/bot_review.py</code> <code>Watcher.check_one</code> (~l.204): when <code>next_step</code> returns RUN_ROUND, first read <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code> (through <code>talos/lib/ai_cli.py</code>, like <code>ai_rabbit</code>). If a follow-up review would be answered human (limit reached), don't run the round. Hand off to the reviewer (never the merger route) with the comment <em>CodeRabbit limit reached: open CodeRabbit findings left for you.</em></li><li>After a round ends with <code>awaiting_bot_review</code> (<code>dispatcher._await_bot_review</code> ~l.507, when rounds &gt; 0), call <code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source bot-round --rereview --issue N --json</code>. On human, hand off with the same note instead of waiting.</li><li><code>Watcher.reenter</code> (~l.157, after address-review in auto-merge milestones): call <code>ai rabbit request ... --source reenter --rereview</code>; on human, hand off to the reviewer instead of re-entering.</li><li>If the ai command fails, log it and hand off to the reviewer; don't wait for a review that was never requested.</li><li>Unit tests in <code>talos/tests/test_bot_review.py</code>: round skipped at the limit, request after a round, reenter to human, command failure.</li><li>Update the CodeRabbit loop section of the Talos README.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> each fix round's push gets exactly one trigger comment while under the limit; at the limit the issue goes to the reviewer as in_review with the note and no new commit.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the first review (ai ship), Agamemnon.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4317</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4319	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	66aea3f86aef-1c5a-b1d4-8cc67eed2d04	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 11:23:44	adt	0	0
86b071646afb-9e2c-9895-c7a85965ee84	AppUi::Avatar: optional @minSize to step down to the space available	2026-11-16 19:16:22	2026-11-16 19:34:57	0	<p>Large avatars (l 96px) sit in columns whose width depends on where the view is rendered (full page vs narrow quick-view panels). Instead of each page choosing a fixed size, the avatar should step down through the standard sizes when its container is too narrow.</p><ul><li>New optional arg <code>@minSize</code> on <code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code> (same values and alias as <code>@size</code>). Without it, nothing changes and nothing is measured.</li><li>With it, the avatar observes the content width of its parent element (reuse <code>modifiers/observe-width.js</code>) and renders the largest standard size from <code>@size</code> down to <code>@minSize</code> (order xs, s, m, ml, l) whose width fits. If none fits, it renders <code>@minSize</code>. The rendered size is what <code>data-size</code> and the size class show.</li><li>No oscillation: decide only from the parent's width, never from the avatar's own; cover a parent whose width depends on its content in a test.</li><li>An invalid <code>@minSize</code> or one larger than <code>@size</code> is ignored (fixed <code>@size</code>).</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>: a resizable/width-controlled container showing l stepping to ml and m. Docs <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-avatar.md</code> + manifest: the new arg and when to use it (large avatars in containers of varying width).</li><li>Integration tests: fits at l, steps to ml, steps to m, stays at minSize when nothing fits, no observing without <code>@minSize</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @size="l" @minSize="m"&gt;</code> renders 96, 64 or 40px depending on its parent's width and updates when the parent resizes; existing usages are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> using it on pages (next issue).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4623	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	e97eb2496afb-9e2c-9895-611589c33e6c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 19:34:57	aprom	0	0
