aa69c3156af2-2815-69ad-a96d645594a9	Role detail: Role, Members and Permissions as full-width boxes	2026-11-09 20:44:26	2026-11-09 21:09:22	0	<p>The role detail page (<code>templates/app/role/page.hbs</code>) doesn't follow the design system: the name and description are bare form fields outside any box, a floating × close toolbar sits on top (useless now that the first role opens by default, aprom-4430), and Save sits in the Permissions box body. Restructure it into three full-width boxes stacked in the detail column (<code>col-md-9</code> beside the Roles QuickList). The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and the existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li><strong>Role</strong> (<code>box box-primary role-record</code>, title "Role"): an avatar block with the role's initials in a square box in its access-tier colour (same initials and tier logic the Roles list uses; square edges), the role name in bold and a grey caption "Created  by  · Modified " (<code>DD MMM YYYY</code>; created-by name via the hasOne rel). The name and description keep their current inline edit (<code>FormFields::FieldText</code>/<code>FieldTextArea</code> with <code>@allowInlineEdit</code>, validation and <code>editRole</code>), shown as the name in the avatar block and a "Description" <code>&lt;h4&gt;</code> with the text below. Facts as <code>&lt;h4&gt;</code> + value: Access (granted label in the tier colour + red "N% denied" label when above 0), Members (count), Actions granted ("46 of 80", from the same action-permission count as the coverage). Leave the box header tools empty here (delete moves there in a separate issue).</li><li><strong>Members</strong> (<code>box box-warning role-members</code>): unchanged content (users-list grid, <code>AppUi::DottedAddButton</code> in the header, remove buttons, "View all members" footer, the add-userrole and view-all modals), full width.</li><li><strong>Permissions</strong> (<code>box box-info</code>)