c0e7ae116af7-aa50-1f38-7d5560ee565f	Clear the ember-data 6.0 deprecations	2026-11-13 21:44:32	2026-11-13 22:35:16	0	<h4>Why</h4><p>aprom-4512 cleared the Ember 7 deprecations but left three ember-data 6.0 deprecations for a follow-up, which was never logged. They block the next ember-data LTS.</p><h4>Deprecations still reported</h4><ul><li><code>ember-data:deprecate-non-unique-relationship-entries</code>: the same record id is pushed into a relationship more than once.</li><li><code>ember-data:deprecate-many-array-duplicates</code>: duplicates are added to a hasMany array, for example by <code>pushObject</code>/<code>push</code> or the <code>pushRecords</code> helper without a uniqueness check.</li><li><code>ember-data:deprecate-relationship-remote-update-clearing-local-state</code>: a payload from the server overwrites relationship state that was changed locally and not saved.</li></ul><h4>Do</h4><ul><li>Run the suite with deprecations reported (<code>setupDeprecationReporting</code> in <code>tests/test-helper.js</code>) and list each deprecation with the code that triggers it.</li><li>Fix the source of each one, not the symptom:<ul><li>make the relationship push helpers idempotent;</li><li>stop serializers and Mirage from returning duplicate relationship ids;</li><li>handle local relationship edits explicitly before reloading.</li></ul></li><li>Don't silence them in <code>app/deprecation-workflow.js</code>.</li><li>Record the decisions in <code>docs/architecture/data-models/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><h4>Done when</h4><ul><li>The full suite reports no <code>ember-data:*</code> deprecations.</li><li>The live updates paths (Hermes handlers that push records) and the issue, file and relationship editing screens are checked by hand.</li></ul><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4546	2026-11-21	2026-11-14	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-