de42bdd96af7-aa50-1f38-6fe78f04f82a	Milestone blocks: choose the block in the template so a new status only needs a new block file	2026-11-13 21:45:02	2026-11-13 22:48:11	0	<h4>Why</h4><p>Milestone blocks are meant to work like activity blocks: one block per status under <code>app/components/milestone-blocks/</code>, and adding a status means adding its block. Since the Ember 6.12 upgrade, <code>app/components/app-ui/milestone-block.js</code> imports every block into a hard-coded <code>BLOCKS_BY_STATUS</code> map, because <code>ensureSafeComponent</code> with a string no longer works on Ember 6. So a new status now needs its block file <em>and</em> an edit to that map.</p><h4>Do</h4><ul><li>Choose the block in the template, as <code>app-ui/activity-block.hbs</code> does: <code>{{component (concat 'milestone-blocks/' this.milestoneBlockType) milestone=this.milestone}}</code>. The class keeps only the status-to-name logic and the progress calculation.</li><li>Keep <code>milestone-blocks/index</code> as the fallback for unknown statuses. A status that has no block must not render empty.</li><li>Remove the block imports and <code>BLOCKS_BY_STATUS</code>.</li></ul><h4>Tests</h4><ul><li>An integration test per status (closed, complete, completed, deferred, failed, overdue) checking the right block renders.</li><li>An integration test that an unknown status renders the index block.</li></ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4548	2026-11-21	2026-11-14	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	53961d336af7-96e3-e970-cfe714bcea9f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-13 22:48:11	aprom	0	0
513f51256aef-6a89-ada2-397d689f758a	Agamemnon: set an agent issue done when a person merges its PR	2026-11-07 10:45:37	2026-11-07 11:23:58	0	<p>Agamemnon sets an issue done only after a merge it did itself (<code>talos/lib/orchestrator/merging.py</code> <code>_finish</code> ~l.152). More agent PRs will now go to the human reviewer, and when the reviewer merges one by hand on GitHub the issue stays in_review. Agamemnon should close the loop for those too.</p><ul><li>New sweep step in <code>talos/lib/orchestrator/</code> (its own small module, wired where the merge sweep is set up in <code>orchestrator/setup.py</code>): for in_review issues in the worker's projects assigned to the owner (<code>owners</code>), find the agent PR: branch <code>claude-issue-N</code>, author = the Agent Odysseus GitHub account (reuse the PR lookup the CodeRabbit watcher uses).</li><li>When that PR is merged and Agamemnon didn't merge it (no open/closed merge record in its store): set the issue done and comment <em>PR repo#N merged by &lt;GitHub login&gt;; set done.</em> This is worded differently from Agamemnon's own "merged automatically" comment, so a person's merge and an agent's merge are told apart.</li><li>Skip issues with no agent PR, with more than one open agent PR, or whose PR is closed without merging (leave those to the owner). Each step safe to repeat.</li><li>Agamemnon role and README: describe the step.</li><li>Unit tests: merged by a person → done + comment; merged by Agamemnon → untouched (its own flow); not merged, closed, no PR → untouched.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after the owner merges an agent PR on GitHub, the issue is done within one Agamemnon sweep, with the comment naming who merged it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> PRs not opened by Agent Odysseus; issues outside the worker's projects; webhooks (polling only).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4322	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	ad655d146aef-deba-ada2-10ebecac6ef7	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 11:23:58	adt	0	0
7de53d176afb-9e2c-9895-5544f3a4c271	Issue details: assignee avatar overlaps the description in narrow views	2026-11-16 19:16:13	2026-11-16 19:48:07	0	<p>Since aprom-4610 the assignee in issue details is a fixed 96px <code>AppUi::Avatar @size="l"</code> inside <code>div.col-xs-3.col-md-2 &gt; .project-manager</code> (<code>components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code>, first row of the details box, next to <code>.col-xs-9.col-md-10.issue-description</code>). Bootstrap sizes those columns from the window width, but issue details also renders inside narrow panels (board and issue list quick views, gantt panel). There the column is about 40-60px wide and the avatar overlaps the description text. The old image was <code>width: 100%</code> and shrank with the column.</p><ul><li>Make that first row a flex row (scoped class in <code>styles/modules/issue.scss</code>): the assignee column <code>flex: 0 0 auto</code> with the gutter as padding, the description column <code>flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0</code>, so it wraps beside the avatar. Drop the <code>col-*</code> fractions from these two columns. Long words or URLs in the description wrap instead of overflowing.</li><li>The assignee name and the 'assigned to' label stay centred under the avatar, wrapping within the column's width (no wider than the avatar plus padding).</li><li>Keep <code>data-field</code> attributes, the user tag and links as they are.</li><li>Add a test (integration or acceptance) that renders issue details in a narrow container (e.g. 320px) and asserts the description column starts to the right of the avatar column (no overlap).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> in the board quick view at any window width, and on the issue page, the description never overlaps the assignee avatar; on a wide issue page the layout looks as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> resizing the avatar (separate issues); the project overview manager.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4622	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	dbf3f9d96afb-9e2c-9895-b99a1fc23658	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 19:48:07	aprom	0	0
