e48f33576af7-aa50-1f38-8543bb6de7e0	Spike: plan the move to the next Ember LTS before 6.12 support ends	2026-11-13 21:45:08	2026-11-14 00:35:02	0	<h4>Why</h4><p>Ember 6.12 LTS gets bug fixes until about 8 Dec 2026 and security fixes until about May 2027. The next move needs planning before then.</p><h4>Do (same approach as the 6.12 move)</h4><ul><li>Check the current Ember and ember-data LTS releases and their support windows. Choose the target: the newest 6.x LTS, or Ember 7 if it has an LTS.</li><li>Run a throwaway trial upgrade in an isolated container, not in a checkout or shared container. Run the full suite and record everything that breaks, grouped by cause.</li><li>Check the add-ons that pinned us before: ember-cli-yadda and yadda, ember-cli-mirage, ember-power-select and ember-basic-dropdown, ember-file-upload, ember-concurrency, ember-cli-deprecation-workflow, and the <code>package.json</code> overrides added in aprom-4512.</li><li>Decide whether to stay on the classic build or move to Embroider/Vite. Record the reasons.</li><li>Output: the list of issues that can be done on 6.12 beforehand, plus the upgrade issue itself, proposed in order for approval before anything is created.</li></ul><h4>Depends on</h4><p>The ember-data 6.0 deprecations issue and the stale deprecation-workflow issue should be done first, because those deprecations are what block the next versions.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4549	2026-12-05	2026-11-14	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae8215b05acb-1902-6b9c-d7cf4132daaf	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	a9b0b1e66af7-113d-0f34-cf930f4236c2	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-14 00:35:02	aprom	0	0
6d42c0756afb-651e-948b-15dfef864a6e	AppUi::Avatar: person image picks up page CSS on the task board (img-circle rules)	2026-11-16 20:02:53	2026-11-16 20:16:29	0	<p>On the task board, the assignee avatar of a <strong>person</strong> on an issue card looks wrong, while agents look right and the same avatar is fine in issue details. Cause: for a person, <code>components/app-ui/avatar.hbs</code> (~l.17) renders <code>&lt;img class="img-circle"&gt;</code>. Pages style that global AdminLTE class and bare <code>img</code> tags, and those rules are more specific than the component's <code>.app-ui-avatar &gt; img</code>. Agents render <code>span.agent-avatar</code>, so they escape.</p><p>Rules that reach the avatar's image today:</p><ul><li><code>styles/modules/board.scss:230</code> <code>.board .board-issue-item .img-circle</code> (3rem, 0.1rem #ddd border, object-fit). The card avatar is the compact <code>Issue::AssigneeSelect</code> in <code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs:126</code> (AppUi::Avatar @size s since aprom-4611).</li><li><code>styles/modules/board.scss:225</code> <code>.board-issue-item p &gt; img</code> (10rem !important).</li><li><code>styles/modules/issue.scss:540</code> <code>.users-list .dropdown .dropdown-menu li img</code> (20px, margin-right 0.5rem): the assignee menu options in issue details (xs avatars), where the margin pushes the image off its circle.</li></ul><p>Changes:</p><ul><li><code>avatar.hbs</code>: the person image uses a component class <code>app-ui-avatar-image</code> instead of <code>img-circle</code>.</li><li><code>styles/components/app-ui-avatar.scss</code>: style the image through <code>.app-ui-avatar .app-ui-avatar-image</code>: width and height 100%, <code>max-width: none</code>, margin 0, padding 0, border 0, round (50%), object-fit cover, display block.</li><li>Delete the board <code>.img-circle</code> rule if nothing else on the card uses <code>img-circle</code> (check the card markup), and the <code>p &gt; img</code> rule if it no longer has a target (check whether description images on cards need it; if they do, scope it to them). Remove the <code>img</code> sizing/margin in the issue.scss <code>.dropdown-menu li img</code> rule; the option avatar's own gap stays on its wrapper (<code>.assignee-select-option-avatar</code>).</li><li>Search the other stylesheets for rules on <code>.img-circle</code> or bare <code>img</code> inside containers that now render AppUi::Avatar (users-list, box-comment, user-block, gantt) and confirm they don't change the avatar's image; list any you leave in the PR.</li><li>Tests: an integration test that renders a person avatar inside a container carrying a hostile rule (e.g. a test-only class setting width, margin and border on <code>img</code> and <code>.img-circle</code>) is not realistic with scoped CSS, so instead assert the image has <code>app-ui-avatar-image</code> and no <code>img-circle</code>; an acceptance or integration check on the board card that the person avatar's computed width equals the agent's for the same size and it has no border.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-avatar.md</code>: note that pages must not style the avatar's inner elements; size comes only from <code>@size</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the task board, person and agent avatars on cards render at the same size (s, 30px) with no extra border; the assignee menus in issue details and on cards show xs avatars centred in their circle; issue details, comments and other pages look unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the wider dead-CSS cleanup (aprom-4618).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4625	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	514b98776afb-66c3-948b