b70b3be46af2-2815-69ad-1909efb73354	Role permissions: Fields tab uses a raw <select>; use FormFields::FieldRelate	2026-11-09 20:44:39	2026-11-09 21:14:41	0	<p>The Fields tab of <code>Role::Permissions</code> (<code>components/role/permissions.hbs</code> ~l.104) renders each field's access mode with a raw <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> and hand-written <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>. The house rules require <code>FormFields::*</code>: a select is <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> with <code>@relateType="relate-simple"</code>.</p><ul><li>Replace the select and label with <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> (<code>@relateType="relate-simple"</code>, options from <code>fieldAccessOptions</code>, label = the control's <code>displayLabel</code>, selected = <code>control.accessMode</code>), calling the existing <code>setFieldAccessMode(control, value)</code> on change. Keep the <code>data-field-access-select</code> hook (or update tests to the FieldRelate's).</li><li>Check the Actions tab's <code>Role::PermissionOptions</code> renders through FormFields too; if it also uses a raw select, fix it the same way in this issue.</li><li>Update the role permission tests (changing a field's access mode still marks it for save and saves).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: no raw <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> left in role permissions; changing access modes still saves.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4433	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	0c37ad186af2-eadc-69ad-69d261f2d848	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 21:14:41	aprom	0	0
26bb75856aef-6a89-ada2-9ea55889d49e	ai ship: ask ai rabbit request who reviews a new PR, hand it to the reviewer when it answers human	2026-11-07 10:44:54	2026-11-07 11:34:22	0	<p>CodeRabbit's auto review is off, so a new agent PR only gets a CodeRabbit review when <code>ai ship</code> asks for one. Depending on the daily count and the PR's size, the answer may be the human reviewer instead.</p><ul><li>In <code>ai/lib/ship.py</code> <code>cmd_ship</code>, after the PR is open (~l.195-200, where <code>defer</code> is decided today): for a CodeRabbit repo, call the <code>rabbitbudget</code> request logic with <code>source pr-opened</code>, <code>files</code> = the hand-written count <code>sizecheck.check</code> already returned, and the issue number.</li><li>On coderabbit: defer the hand-off as today (the issue stays in progress for the Talos loop).</li><li>On human: don't defer. <code>pr_hand_off</code> sets in_review and assigns the reviewer. Add to the tracker notes: <em>Not sent to CodeRabbit: N of 25 reviews used in the last 24 hours (small PRs go to you from 10). Please review by hand; CodeRabbit may add a review later when credit frees up.</em> Print that the session finishes as <code>done</code>, not <code>awaiting_bot_review</code> (like the existing branch for repos without CodeRabbit).</li><li>On resume, when <code>existing_pr</code> finds the PR, don't ask again if the pending hand-off or the ledger already has the PR.</li><li><code>ai pr</code> (<code>workflow.cmd_pr</code>) does the same, with the file count from the PR's changed files.</li><li>Check that Odysseus' ship prompt and role (<code>talos/agents/odysseus/</code>) follow the printed outcome; adjust the wording if needed.</li><li>Unit tests with the request logic mocked: coderabbit → deferred; human → handed off with the note; resume doesn't ask twice.</li><li>Update <code>ai/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with 12 reviews used, a 3-file gaia PR goes to the reviewer as 