3bef0ce06aef-6a89-ada2-9b69120f8124	Agamemnon: request a CodeRabbit review after branch updates and conflict fixes, or hand the issue to the owner	2026-11-07 10:45:15	2026-11-07 11:44:49	0	<p>Agamemnon's keeper pushes new commits to agent PRs: it updates PRs that are behind their base and sends resolved conflicts back for review. With CodeRabbit's auto review off, those commits get no review unless asked for, and the merge check (<code>ai/lib/mergegate.py</code> <code>gate</code>) needs a CodeRabbit result on the latest commit. Agamemnon must spend reviews through the shared counter and know when the limit is reached.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/orchestrator/keeper.py</code> <code>_update</code> (~l.86): before the update-branch call, read <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code>; at the limit, skip the update (log once per PR per day). After a successful update, call <code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source update-branch --rereview --issue N</code>.</li><li><code>_conflict</code> / <code>_resolve</code> (~l.96-155): at the limit, don't resolve; hand the issue to the owner as in_review with <em>merge conflict, CodeRabbit limit reached: please resolve and review by hand.</em> After a resolution is pushed, call <code>ai rabbit request ... --source conflict --rereview</code>. On human, hand off with the same note.</li><li>The premise and role (<code>talos/agents/agamemnon/</code>): add the budget (tiers, that each agent push needs a trigger, what happens at the limit, that the owner's own GitHub activity is not counted) where they describe updates, conflicts and merging.</li><li>An ai command failure means hand off to the owner, logged.</li><li>Unit tests (see <code>talos/tests/test_agamemnon_conflicts.py</code>): update skipped at the limit, request after update, conflict to the owner, request after resolution.</li><li>Update <code>agamemnon/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> at the limit, Agamemnon's sweep pushes nothing to agent PRs and conflicting PRs land with the owner with the note; under the limit, every push it makes is followed by one trigger comment.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> letting the merge check accept an earlier CodeRabbit pass after base-only merges; auto-merge itself (PRs that went to the human never come back clean).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4317</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4320	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	a01925886aef-8154-bb7a-3b46e6d54d4f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 11:44:49	adt	0	0
