b98d0fd968f0-47e3-786a-b0654a500e7c	Conversation UI Enhancements	2025-10-16 12:10:33	2025-10-31 09:46:14	0	<h3><strong>Problem Statement</strong></h3>\n<p>Currently, the Conversations UI lacks visual consistency, performance optimization, and usability refinements.<br>\nThe interface feels cluttered due to the use of a 3-column masonry layout, lacks lazy loading for performance, and does not prioritize recently active conversations. Additionally, inconsistent date formatting and comment styling reduce readability and user focus.</p>\n<p>These issues collectively affect user experience, make navigation inefficient, and hinder smooth interaction with conversation threads.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3><strong>Goal / Objective</strong></h3>\n<p>To modernize and streamline the Conversations UI for improved readability, visual hierarchy, and performance.<br>\nThis includes optimizing the layout, loading behavior, data ordering, and comment styling to enhance the overall conversation experience and make the interface more intuitive and responsive.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3><strong>Scope of Work</strong></h3>\n<p>This Epic covers the following UI and functional improvements:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Conversion to 6-Column Center-Aligned Layout</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Replace the existing masonry-style 3-column (<code data-backticks="1">col-md-4</code>) layout with a cleaner, centered 6-column (<code data-backticks="1">col-md-6</code>) layout.</li>\n<li>Improve focus and readability by reducing visual noise and aligning the conversation list centrally on the page.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Lazy Loading of Conversations</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Implement lazy loading for conversation rooms to enhance page performance and reduce initial load time.</li>\n<li>Conversations should load dynamically as the user scrolls.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Add Reload Button</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Introduce a reload button at the top of the Conversations UI to allow users to manually refresh conversation data without a full page reload.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Render Latest Modified Conversations First</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Sort and render conversation rooms based on their last modified timestamp so that the most recently updated conversations appear first.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Update Date Format in Conversation Rooms</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Standardize the date/time format displayed in conversation rooms for better readability and consistency across the UI.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Alternate Comment Colors</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Apply alternating background colors for comments (e.g., white and light gray) to visually separate messages, improve readability, and make threads easier to scan.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3711	2025-11-20	2025-10-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	f79e81a568f0-f6b3-5cb9-e5a2c76ef237	\N	ae4ca1725acb-1902-6b9c-1a5d19be2920	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2025-10-31 09:46:14	aprom	1	0
0ab5ea906af2-3028-5ed1-0742879ae733	Threads: QuickList list + detail layout, grouped by milestone, first thread opened	2026-11-09 23:19:38	2026-11-10 00:22:18	0	<p>Replace the infinite-scroll feed on the Threads page with the QuickList list + detail layout of Ideas/Roles, so threads can be searched, paged, sorted and grouped and one thread is read at a time. The list uses <strong>QuickList's default styling</strong> (no custom row look): use its standard blocks only.</p><ul><li>Routing: <code>app.project.conversation</code> becomes the layout with children <code>index</code> and <code>page</code> (<code>conversations/:conversation_id</code>); add <code>app.project.conversation.page</code> to <code>services/acl.js</code> routeMaps (conversationroom.read) and the breadcrumb. Index route: <code>replaceWith</code> the first row; if <code>?c_id=X</code> is present, replaceWith the page for X (old links from project overview, issue list, weekly-conversations widget, tag-parser keep working). Empty state (QuickList <code>&lt;:empty&gt;</code> with Clear search) only when nothing matches; the outlet then says no thread is open.</li><li>Page header: "Threads" with a <strong>New thread</strong> btn-primary on the right (ACL conversationroom.create) opening the existing create modal.</li><li>Layout <code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code>: .row with col-md-3 QuickList + col-md-9 outlet. QuickList with the range (limit+1, no totals, QuickList pagination), <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> = <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> with <code>views.Conversationroom.search</code> and saved searches as on the idea browser.</li><li>State on the toolkit (<code>utils/state/</code> ListLoader + UrlState, aprom-4425/4426): query, page, sort, order, group in the URL, list reloads in place (no refreshModel), newest response wins. Query <code>conversationroom</code> with hasOne rels only (<code>createdBy,issue</code>), never comments/votes rels.</li><li>Rows: <code>&lt;:leading&gt;</code> = type icon (<code>fa-comment-o</code> discussion, <code>fa-thumbs-o-up</code> vote); primary = subject; secondary = linked issue <code>#number · subject</code> for discussions (nothing yet for votes, tallies come with the counts issue), then creator name · modified time/date. Active row = open thread.</li><li>Grouping <strong>on by default</strong> by the linked issue's milestone: load the project's milestones once, map <code>issue.milestoneId</code> to its name, threads without issue or milestone in "No milestone" last; per loaded page (QuickList grouping helper). Other group option: type. Sort: last updated (default), created, subject.</li><li>Page route for now renders the existing <code>Conversation::ConversationItem</code> for the selected thread in the col-md-9 (replaced by the thread page issue), so dev never breaks.</li><li>Hermes: keep the existing project registrations; a new/updated thread reloads the list through the loader.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Mirage handlers + acceptance feature: first thread opens by default, <code>?c_id=</code> redirects, grouping by milestone with "No milestone" last, search reloads only the list. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> counts in rows, the new thread page, removing old code.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4436</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 11 (Route split, layout, toolkit state and the c_id redirect must ship together so the page never breaks; counts, thread page, votes and cleanup are already separate issues.)</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4437	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	e7eca8376af2-5d00-05c9-6834cfdc662a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 00:22:18	aprom	0	0
465f45a86aef-6a89-ada2-87cabcb1f490	Agamemnon: send PRs that went to the reviewer because of the limit to CodeRabbit once credit frees up	2026-11-07 10:45:26	2026-11-07 12:00:19	0	<p>When the daily CodeRabbit limit sends an agent PR to the human reviewer, it is recorded as deferred in the shared ledger. Once there is credit again, it should still get a CodeRabbit review to help the human; the issue stays with the human.</p><ul><li>In Agamemnon's sweep (<code>talos/lib/orchestrator/</code>, next to the keeper's sweep): read <code>ai rabbit budget --json</code>. For each deferred PR, oldest first, while the tier allows it (its stored file count against the tier, as for a new PR), call <code>ai rabbit request &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; --source backlog --files N --issue N</code>. Stop at the first human answer.</li><li>Before sending, drop the entry without spending a review when the PR is closed or merged, or the issue is no longer in_review.</li><li>Comment on the issue when a review was requested: <em>CodeRabbit review requested now that credit is available; the issue stays with you.</em> Don't reassign it or start the Talos loop.</li><li>Agamemnon role: mention the backlog sending.</li><li>Unit tests: oldest first, stops at the tier, closed/merged/moved PRs dropped, the comment.</li><li>Update <code>agamemnon/README.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after the 24-hour window frees slots, deferred PRs that fit the tier get a trigger comment, oldest first; their issues stay assigned to the reviewer.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> giving the issue back to the agent to answer CodeRabbit's findings; notifications.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4317, adt-4318</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4321	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9f