1c2ff3c26af2-3028-5ed1-568fa2a81ba6	Threads: thread page for discussions (header, comments, reply, Linked issue box)	2026-11-09 23:19:56	2026-11-10 10:57:49	0	<p>Replace the temporary <code>Conversation::ConversationItem</code> in <code>app.project.conversation.page</code> with the thread page. Inside the col-md-9 outlet: thread col-md-8 + info column col-md-4. This issue builds the page and the discussion body; the vote body, Participants, Create issue and Activity come in follow-up issues. The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>Thread box (box-primary) header: small uppercase type label (Discussion / Vote) above the subject as a large title; box-tools = like toggle with count (existing toggleVote logic) and edit (existing edit modal from ConversationItem); linked-issue line (<code>fa-link</code>, <code>#number</code> link, subject, status label); "Started by &lt;user link&gt; · date".</li><li>Body: description (rendered as today). Comments section: uppercase "N comments" heading, each comment with a round initials/profile avatar, name link, time and text with mentions highlighted (reuse <code>ConversationUi::CommentItem</code>), loaded with <strong>their own query</strong> (newest 10, sort Comment.dateCreated, "Load older comments"), never through rels. Reply box at the bottom with the current user's avatar and <code>ConversationUi::CommentComposer</code> (mentions + issue links), Reply button.</li><li>Leave a body slot chosen by roomType where the vote body plugs in; until then vote rooms show the description only.</li><li>Info column: <strong>Linked issue</strong> box (box-info: key link, subject, status label, milestone; "No linked issue" otherwise). Leave room below it for the boxes added later.</li><li>Page route loads the room with hasOne rels only (<code>createdBy,issue</code>); move the Hermes comment handlers (<code>handleCommentCreated/Updated/Deleted</code>) for the open thread to the page controller. Guard async work after destroy.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Mirage + acceptance: opening a discussion shows the header, comments, load older, posting a reply appears, Linked issue box filled. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> vote body, Participants, Create issue, Activity, reply threading (aprom-3750), removing ConversationItem.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4437</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> threads-list.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4439	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	a32befa46af2-682a-504e-2ee7f8469ec0	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 10:57:49	aprom	0	0
012e9f556aef-6651-38f6-982d2a070eb0	ezSearch: search fields from view metadata, documented as the list-view architecture	2026-11-07 12:48:01	2026-11-07 14:03:12	0	<p>Prometheus is partly metadata-driven: <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> <code>views</code> drives navigation, dashboard widgets and the Project list fields, and its comment states the goal of building all views from metadata. Search is not: ezSearch's fields are hard-coded in <code>app/utils/query/schemas/issue.js</code> and <code>project.js</code> (aprom-4295), and the generic admin list (<code>controllers/app/module.js</code> <code>setupQuery</code>) reads a <code>views.&lt;Module&gt;.filters</code> key that no module declares. Engineer's decision: where something is already partly metadata-driven and the change is small, make it fully metadata-driven. A list view gets search by declaring search metadata, and nothing is hard-coded per page. This issue builds that capability and documents it; the pages move in later issues.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Metadata format, in <code>views.&lt;Module&gt;.search</code> of <code>metadata.js</code>: <code>{ module: 'Issue', textField: 'Issue.subject', fields: { 'Issue.priority': { label: 'views.app.issue.fields.priority', type: 'enum', aliases: ['priority','prio'], values: { source: 'translation', key: 'views.app.issue.lists.priority' } }, ... } }</code>.<ul><li>Types are those of the operator registry (<code>app/utils/query/operators.js</code>): text, number, enum, user, date.</li><li><code>values</code> names a source plus its parameters; it is never a literal list built in code.</li><li>Field order in the metadata is the order shown in the builder and suggestions.</li></ul></li><li>Move the Issue and Project fields from <code>app/utils/query/schemas/issue.js</code> and <code>project.js</code> into <code>views.Issue.search</code> and <code>views.Project.search</code> unchanged (ids, aliases, labels, types, text fields), then delete both schema files.</li><li><code>MD.getViewMeta</code>: remove the <code>filters</code> branch (~l.478-486, which mutates labels in place). Search labels stay translation keys and are translated where they are shown.</li><li><code>app/services/query-schema.js</code>:<ul><li><code>load(module, context)</code> reads <code>getViewMeta(module, 'search')</code>, resolves each field's value source and returns <code>createSchema(...)</code> as today. It returns <code>null</code> when the module declares no search, and callers then render no search.</li><li>A value-source registry keyed by name, each entry loading values through the store with the context (e.g. <code>projectId</code>): <code>translation</code> (static, from a translation key), <code>issueStatuses</code>, <code>milestones</code>, <code>issueTypes</code>, <code>members</code> (project members with avatars) and <code>users</code>.</li><li>An unknown source name throws a clear error in development and tests. Caching per module and context stays.</li><li>The public API stays as 4295 shipped it, so the Issue list (aprom-4305) keeps working without changes.</li></ul></li><li>Documentation (new): <code>prometheus/docs/architecture/metadata-views/architecture.md</code> and <code>decisions.md</code>, in the style of <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/</code>:<ul><li>What is metadata-driven today (navigation, dashboard widgets, list fields, search) and where it lives.</li><li>The rule: a list view that extends Module (generic <code>app.module</code>, or a module list on <code>controllers/prometheus/list.js</code>) gets search only by declaring <code>views.&lt;Module&gt;.search</code>; controllers don't define filters.</li><li>The search metadata format with a full example.</li><li>How to add search to a module, and how to add a value source (the only part that needs code).</li><li>The principle: when a feature is partly metadata-driven and the change is small, finish it as metadata rather than adding hard-coded code; a full metadata-driven architecture is the direction, taken step by step.</li></ul>Add a one-line pointer to this doc in <code>prometheus/CLAUDE.md</code> under Architecture.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests:<ul><li><code>query-schema</code> builds the Issue and Project schemas from metadata with the same resolution results as before (aliases, labels, prefixes, values from Mirage).</li><li>It returns <code>null</code> for a module without search metadata.</li><li>It throws on an unknown value source.</li><li>Each registered source loads its values.</li></ul></li><li>The parser, completer and EzSearch tests and the Issue list acceptance tests pass unchanged.</li><li>No search field definitions remain in code outside <code>metadata.js</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> moving other views (forms, details) to metadata, loading metadata from the server, the Project and generic lists' UI (separate issues), YUIDoc output in <code>docs/</code>.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4323	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	21e8cba96aef-6651-38f6-a02c7b9d3de1	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 14:03:13	aprom	0	0
328654906afc-4f2e-ea61-919b144ea1de	Header: project switcher replaces the sidebar project selector	2026-11-17 09:53:54	2026-11-17 12:34:58	0	<p>The project selector sits in the sidebar (<code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.hbs</code> <code>.sidebar-form</code>), so the loaded project can't be seen when the sidebar is collapsed or closed on a phone. Move it into the header as a project switcher, so the current project is always visible. The attached screens are a guide to layout and content only; the design system and the real components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>In <code>components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs</code>, right after the sidebar toggle, add a crimson switcher. Desktop label: the project name plus its short code (e.g. <code>A Prometheus APROM</code>, name and code on one baseline). Below 768px label: the short code only. With no project selected, the label is <strong>Select a project</strong>.</li><li>The switcher opens a searchable list of the user's projects (name left, code right, the current one ticked) with an <strong>All projects</strong> link (<code>app.projects</code>) at the bottom. Build it with the existing <code>AppUi::Select</code> (power-select, search on <code>label</code>, same <code>projectsList</code> data the sidebar uses today). Do not hand-roll a dropdown. If the footer link can't be added through power-select's existing extension points, finish with needs_input.</li><li>Move <code>projectChanged</code> and <code>getTransitionUrl</code> from <code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.js</code> to the header component (or a small shared helper) unchanged in behaviour. Remove the selector and <code>projectsList</code> plumbing from the sidebar (<code>nav-bar.hbs</code>, <code>application-sidebar.hbs</code>).</li><li>Styles go in <code>styles/modules/header.scss</code>. Colours come from <code>variables.scss</code> only, square edges. Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Update tests: <code>tests/integration/components/app-layouts/application-header-test.js</code>, <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/nav-bar-test.js</code>, and <code>tests/acceptance/app/select-project-from-sidebar.feature</code> plus its steps (now selecting from the header). Use <code>data-test-*</code> selectors.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the current project's name and code are visible in the header with the sidebar expanded, collapsed or closed. Picking a project navigates exactly as the sidebar selector did. The sidebar no longer has a selector.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the sidebar grouping, the search position and the profile status (separate issues).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> nav-desktop.png, nav-no-project.png, nav-desktop-collapsed.png, nav-mobile.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4628	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	31c03b936afc-4f2e-ea61-7608b55d6a64	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	fc2968336afc-4f2e-ea61-4a23ddf28eab	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-17 12:34:58	aprom	0	0
