cb8799b76afc-4f2e-ea61-d7790cbd4749	Header: online status on the avatar and in the profile menu, remove the sidebar user panel	2026-11-17 09:56:27	2026-11-17 13:35:36	0	<p>The sidebar repeats the user's picture and name from the header, only to show a static "Online" status. Move the status into the header and drop the sidebar user panel. Presence stays fixed (always Online) for now. The attached screens are a guide to layout and content only; the design system and the real components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>In <code>components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs</code>, the user menu keeps the real profile picture (<code>AppUi::Avatar</code> <code>@size="s"</code>) with a small green status dot at its bottom-right. The picture and name are vertically centred in the navbar.</li><li>In the profile dropdown, the large avatar gets the same dot. Add a row under <code>li.user-header</code>: green dot, <strong>Online</strong>, and a muted "Visible to your team" on the right, above Profile / Sign out.</li><li>Remove the <code>.user-panel</code> block (<code>components/app-ui/nav-bar.hbs</code> lines 2-12). Keep the <code>initialize-sidebar</code> modifier on an element that stays in the sidebar.</li><li>Colours: the success green from <code>variables.scss</code>. Styles go in <code>styles/modules/header.scss</code>. Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> (reuse <code>views.app.online</code>).</li><li>Tests: <code>application-header-test.js</code> (dot plus status row) and <code>nav-bar-test.js</code> / <code>application-sidebar-test.js</code> (no user panel).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the header avatar shows the profile picture with a green dot, the profile menu shows the Online row, and the sidebar starts with the Workspace group.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> real presence (online, away, offline from Hermes).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4629, aprom-4630</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> nav-desktop.png, nav-mobile.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4631	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	31c03b936afc-4f2e-ea61-7608b55d6a64	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	7293d9336afc-d094-d414-a4d08f66ac3d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-17 13:35:36	aprom	0	0
c5c2a9706a20-0c74-d2b7-714182effe2d	Validate Timelog Input Against Field-Specific Limits	2026-06-03 14:35:49	2026-06-04 14:46:55	0	<p>Update the timelog/estimate duration selector to enforce field-specific input limits for <strong>Days</strong>, <strong>Hours</strong>, and <strong>Minutes</strong>.</p>\n<p>Currently, users can manually enter values that exceed the allowed range for a field. For example, entering <code data-backticks="1">50</code> in the <strong>Hours</strong> field automatically converts the overflow into days, resulting in an unexpected value transformation (e.g., 50 hours becoming 6 days and 2 hours).</p>\n<p>While overflow handling may be useful when using increment/decrement controls, it creates a confusing user experience when users manually enter values.</p>\n<p>The duration selector should validate user input and prevent values from exceeding the configured maximum threshold for each field.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3><strong>Functional Requirements</strong></h3>\n<h4>Days</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Allowed range: <code data-backticks="1">0 - 99</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Hours</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Allowed range: <code data-backticks="1">0 - 8</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Minutes</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Allowed range: <code data-backticks="1">0 - 59</code></li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3><strong>Current Behavior</strong></h3>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Input</th>\n<th>Current Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Hours = 50</td>\n<td>Days = 6, Hours = 2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Minutes = 120</td>\n<td>Hours incremented automatically</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hours = 25</td>\n<td>Value is redistributed across fields</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr>\n<h3><strong>Expected Behavior</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Manual input should not exceed the configured limit for each field</li>\n<li>Values greater than the maximum threshold should be rejected, capped, or prevented from being entered</li>\n<li>Users should receive immediate validation feedback</li>\n<li>No automatic redistribution should occur when manually entering invalid values</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Field</th>\n<th>Input</th>\n<th>Expected Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Hours</td>\n<td>50</td>\n<td>Validation error or capped at 8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Minutes</td>\n<td>75</td>\n<td>Validation error or capped at 59</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Days</td>\n<td>120</td>\n<td>Validation error or capped at 99</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr>\n<h3><strong>UX Considerations</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Prevent invalid values at the input level where possible</li>\n<li>Maintain existing increment/decrement (caret) behavior within valid ranges</li>\n<li>Provide clear feedback when a user attempts to exceed allowed limits</li>\n<li>Ensure consistency between manual entry and caret-based adjustments</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Hours cannot exceed <code data-backticks="1">8</code></li>\n<li>Minutes cannot exceed <code data-backticks="1">59</code></li>\n<li>Days cannot exceed <code data-backticks="1">99</code></li>\n<li>Invalid values are prevented or corrected immediately</li>\n<li>No unexpected redistribution of values occurs during manual input</li>\n<li>Existing valid timelog and estimate workflows remain unaffected</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3><strong>Expected Outcome</strong></h3>\n<p>Users can only enter valid duration values, resulting in a more predictable and intuitive experience when creating estimates or logging time.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3901	2026-06-04	2026-06-03	deferred	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	0a337ec36a1d-0176-a590-3f299fa1b9ce	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	437fea646a20-b800-d2b7-2fbb62ca8632	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-06-04 14:46:55	aprom	0	0
