fcc185866aef-41e1-a72a-3259a4ca2453	ezSearch: move EzSearch's state into a shared base class	2026-11-07 17:50:52	2026-11-07 18:32:08	0	<p>A compact variant, <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code>, is coming. It must be a drop-in replacement for <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code>: same arguments, same behaviour, only the layout differs, so a view switches by changing the component name. To guarantee that, the state and actions of <code>app/components/ez-search/index.js</code> (aprom-4300, extended by aprom-4304) move into a base class that both components extend. This issue only moves code; nothing visible changes.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New <code>app/components/ez-search/base.js</code> (Glimmer component class, no template), holding:<ul><li>the tracked tree, parsing <code>@query</code> and its errors;</li><li>the saved-search selection (<code>@savedSearches</code>, <code>@activeSavedSearchId</code>, <code>@onSavedSearchChange</code>);</li><li>apply (<code>@onApply</code> with <code>@baseQuery</code> composed), Clear, Save (<code>@onSave</code>), <code>@aclContext</code>;</li><li>the builder open/closed state.</li></ul>Document the full argument list in its YUIDoc; it is the shared contract of both components.</li><li><code>app/components/ez-search/index.js</code> extends the base and keeps only what is specific to its toolbar layout.</li><li>Add a unit or integration test for the base's state transitions (parse, apply, clear, select and deselect a saved search) so both components are covered.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>All existing EzSearch tests and the Issue, Project, Agents and Workflows list acceptance tests pass unchanged.</li><li><code>index.js</code> contains no logic that a compact layout would also need.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> new behaviour, the compact component.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4304</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8