8a6551876afc-2fdc-9eaa-4444ee76624b	Retro - aga-Cleanup	2026-11-17 10:12:26	2026-11-17 10:12:26	0	<p>2026-11-15 to 2026-12-15 (all issues created and worked 2026-11-15 to 2026-11-17) · 53 issues (53 done, 0 carried over) · 14.7h (882m) logged vs no estimate set on any issue</p>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>All 53 issues in aga-Cleanup reached done, in three days of work, well before the milestone end date. The work fell into four streams: component rules and manifests (#4566, #4567), shared components and the list-page pilot (#4568-#4582, #4588-#4594), a bulk-request data layer (#4595-#4603), and an AppUi::Avatar roll-out with follow-up layout fixes (#4604-#4627). Human feedback was rare (two issues); most friction came from stale lint-todo hashes, full-suite failures not caused by the branch, and layout changes that no one checked in a browser. No issue carried an estimate, so effort cannot be compared with a plan.</p>\n<h2>Numbers</h2>\n<table><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Delivered</td><td>53 of 53 (100%)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Late</td><td>0 (milestone ended 2026-12-15; latest issue end date 2026-11-24)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Time logged</td><td>882m (14.7h); median about 14m per issue; largest #4567 49m, #4592 48m, #4616 37m, #4610 33m</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Rework</td><td>2 issues with human-requested changes (#4567, #4592); 2 further issues bounced on lint (#4609, #4611)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Waiting</td><td>Not measurable (no status history)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Estimate accuracy / overruns</td><td>Not computable (estimate is 0m on every issue)</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h2>What went well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>100% delivery, no carry-over, every issue ending with lint and the full Ember suite passing (1505 tests at #4566 rising to 1638 at #4624) — #4566, #4624</li>\n<li>Small, single-purpose issues: the typical issue took 7-20m and one PR (all 53 issues have exactly one linked PR, apart from the rework PRs on #4567 and #4592) — e.g. #4606, #4612, #4613, #4617</li>\n<li>Dependency ordering was enforced by the orchestrator: issues were held until a prerequisite finished (#4568 behind #4567, #4589 behind #4590, #4590 behind #4588, #4598 behind #4492, #4621 behind #4611) — #4568, #4589, #4590, #4598, #4621</li>\n<li>Design-review notes were recorded as explicit follow-ups rather than silently dropped or squeezed in, keeping PRs small — #4571, #4599, #4593, #4588</li>\n<li>Root-cause fixes over workarounds: the ResizeObserver loop error was fixed in the modifier (#4594); the lint failures were traced to stale todo hashes (#4609, #4611)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What didn't go well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Nothing was left undelivered. All 53 are done, so there is no not-delivered list.</li>\n<li>Human review feedback on visual styling arrived after the PR: row action icons did not match the Issue and Project lists, then the inner icon was still 20px black, producing two extra PRs — #4592 (48m total, 3+ PRs)</li>\n<li>A CI test failed on the PR after the local run passed (modal-close test race) — #4567 (49m, the longest-logged issue)</li>\n<li>Avatar roll-out produced layout bugs fixed in the following days: avatar overlapping description (#4622), avatars shrinking in narrow columns (#4623, #4624), person image picking up page CSS (#4625), and toolbar/pager touching the box border (#4626, #4627). Of these, #4622, #4623, #4624, #4625 and #4607 trace to the earlier replacement work (#4610, #4611, #4607); this is a likely link, not proven by the issues</li>\n<li>Lint blocked hand-off twice before the cause was found to be stale todo hashes, with a first diagnosis (expired entries) later reversed — #4609, #4611 (#4611 also exceeded the prometheus median output cost: 44.7k vs 19.1k)</li>\n<li>Branch hygiene stops: origin/dev moved during shipping, and a full-suite failure came from another issue's component — #4580, #4582</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Patterns</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>No visual verification of UI changes</strong> (about 17 issues, the most frequent theme): ship notes say "not checked in a browser" or ask for a visual check — #4572 (the local app served another checkout), #4576, #4579, #4580, #4581, #4582, #4588 (mockup not compared), #4589, #4607, #4608, #4610, #4612, #4615, #4616, #4625, #4626, #4627. The two human feedback rounds in #4592 and the follow-up bugs #4622-#4627 are consistent with this, though the issues do not prove the link.</li>\n<li><strong>Stale lint todos and unrelated suite failures</strong>: #4609, #4611 (lint todo hashes), #4582 (test from #4569 failing, later removed by #4578), #4567 (CI-only race). Four issues lost time to failures not caused by their own change.</li>\n<li><strong>No estimates</strong>: 53 of 53 issues show 0m estimated, only "Estimated files" in some descriptions (e.g. #4625: 6 estimated, 5 actual files). Overrun analysis is therefore not possible.</li>\n<li><strong>Per-issue time by kind</strong> (logged time): data-layer bulk issues 12-20m (#4598-#4603); avatar replacement 7-37m (#4609-#4617); component build issues 12-28m (#4568-#4572); the larger exceptions were #4567 (49m), #4592 (48m), #4616 (37m, includes 28m fixing an acceptance step) and #4610 (33m).</li>\n<li><strong>Deferred work accumulates as follow-ups</strong> inside issue comments (Developer registry entries for #4569/#4570, EmptyState/UserChip library entries #4574, selection-state rewrite recommended by #4572, tests for the manager row #4624, lint-todo renewal #4609). None were turned into issues within the milestone.</li>\n<li><strong>Review was manual</strong>: CodeRabbit was not sent on any PR ("0 of 25 reviews used", under the threshold for small PRs), so review relied on the reviewer and on the design-review nits listed in the ship notes (#4566 and all later issues).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Surprises</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>(Single case) #4594 was escalated to Opus mid-run after a full-suite failure caused by a synchronous ResizeObserver callback; the fix went into the shared modifier.</li>\n<li>(Single case) #4580: a branch update was attempted by committing under a throwaway identity, which was denied; resolved by stash, fast-forward merge and pop.</li>\n<li>(Single case) #4595: roles need the bulk.create permission, granted manually with no seed; without it the service silently falls back to separate queries.</li>\n<li>(Single case) #4567 shipped a contract-manifest checker that uses a tokenizer, not the Glimmer AST (limits documented), and manifests later failed first full runs in #4575, #4577 and #4582 until corrected, which suggests the checker works as intended as a guard.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Proposed actions</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Add a "visual check" step to the UI-issue workflow: for issues touching templates or SCSS, the ship step records a screenshot or a named page checked, or the issue states why not; verify the local app serves the branch (the #4572 problem). Addresses: no visual verification. Lives in the /start-issue and /ship-issue skills. Worked if fewer "not checked in a browser" notes and no follow-up layout bug issues after an avatar-style change.</li>\n<li>Give every issue an estimate when created (Agamemnon/issue-creation template), even a rough one. Addresses: no estimates. Lives in the issue-creation tool or template. Worked if the next retro can compute estimate accuracy.</li>\n<li>Document how to handle lint-todo and unrelated test failures: renew todos with a stated procedure, run the suite on clean dev to tell a branch failure from a base failure (#4582), and keep that guidance in prometheus/CLAUDE.md. Addresses: stale lint todos and unrelated failures. Worked if no issue blocks on lint-todo hashes.</li>\n<li>For list-style visual rules (icon sizes, colours), name the reference page in the issue description at creation, e.g. "match the Issue and Project lists", rather than numeric values. Addresses: the rework in #4592. Lives in the issue template for UI work. Worked if no styling feedback rounds on the next component issue.</li>\n<li>Approve and create issues for the accumulated follow-ups (see Patterns), so they do not stay in comments. Addresses: deferred work. Lives in the reviewer's backlog process.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Data gaps</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Estimate accuracy, overruns and underruns: no estimates exist (0m on all issues).</li>\n<li>Planned vs added: no milestone history available, so issues added after the start date cannot be told apart (the earliest issue was created 2026-11-15 and the milestone starts the same day).</li>\n<li>Waiting time in feedback or pending: the tools give no status history, so this is left out.</li>\n<li>Reviews: only the issue comments were read, not the PR review threads with gh. Human feedback counts come from the issue comments alone and may miss PR-only comments. Merge signals ("merged by a person") appear on only some issues within the latest 10 comments, so merge dates were not used.</li>\n<li>#4592: the earliest comments (older than the latest 10) were not read.</li>\n<li>Per-issue figures were collected by delegated read-only readers and totalled from the logged times; the issue numbers cited are the evidence.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Issue ledger</h2>\n<p>All issues: status done, estimate none set, one PR unless noted, CodeRabbit not sent on any, no human feedback unless noted.</p>\n<table><tr><th>#</th><th>Title</th><th>Status</th><th>Est</th><th>Actual</th><th>Review rounds</th><th>Notes</th></tr>\n<tr><td>4566</td><td>Composition rules, test selectors, checklist</td><td>done</td><td>–</td><td>14m</td><td>0</td><td>design-reviewer follow-up outside PR</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4567</td><td>Contract manifests</td><td>done</td><td>–</td><td>49m</td><td>1 (CI test failing)</td><td>test race in modal close</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4568</td><td>AppUi::Tabs</td><td>done</td><td>–</td><td>18m</td><td>0</td><td>waited on #4567</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4569</td><td>Avatar and UserChip</td><td>done</td><td>–</td><td>12m</td><td>0</td><td>no registry entry</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4570</td><td>StatusLabel</td><td>done</td><t