f060a6036afc-4f2e-ea61-900928e84496	Sidebar: close the menu after navigation on phones	2026-11-17 09:57:04	2026-11-17 10:24:39	0	<p>On phones, the sidebar opened with the hamburger stays open after you pick a page, so it has to be closed by hand. Close it automatically, on phones only. The attached screen is a guide to layout and content only.</p><ul><li>On every route change (router service <code>routeDidChange</code>), when the viewport is below 768px and <code>body</code> has <code>sidebar-open</code>, remove it. Desktop expand/collapse and the persisted <code>sidebar-collapsed</code> preference (<code>modifiers/initialize-sidebar.js</code>) stay unchanged.</li><li>While the menu is open on a phone, dim the page under it. Tapping the dimmed page closes the menu, the same way AdminLTE's content click does.</li><li>Clean up the listener on teardown. Use no new jQuery; native listeners and the router service only.</li><li>Test: an integration or acceptance test that opens the sidebar at phone width, navigates, and asserts it closed, plus a desktop case where nothing changes.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a phone, tapping any menu item navigates and closes the menu, and tapping outside closes it too. On desktop the sidebar state never changes on navigation.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> swipe gestures.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> nav-mobile.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4632	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	31c03b936afc-4f2e-ea61-7608b55d6a64	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	4cb7b9186afc-2fdc-9eaa-3c7d4748303f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-17 10:24:39	aprom	0	0
6d76d8c96af2-3028-5ed1-88dccb166069	Threads: create modal uses FormFields for the linked issue and opens the new thread	2026-11-09 23:21:17	2026-11-10 01:09:42	0	<p>The New thread modal in <code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code> uses a raw <code>&lt;PowerSelect&gt;</code> and a hand-written label for the linked issue, which the design system forbids (selects are <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code>).</p><ul><li>Linked issue: <code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> with search over issues (existing <code>linkIssueSearch</code> task), enabled only for roomType discussion as today.</li><li>After save: the list reloads in place and the app navigates to the new thread's page.</li><li>Move the modal into its own component if it keeps the layout template simpler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> acceptance test creating a discussion with a linked issue lands on the new thread. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other fields.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4438</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4445	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	49a8bed16af2-ae46-30f7-4e63f12131c6	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 01:09:42	aprom	0	0
