16ce5eb26aef-f4f7-a72a-1afef51e5c85	ezSearch: applied-filter chips component	2026-11-07 17:51:18	2026-11-07 18:12:32	0	<p>In narrow places the formatted query is too long to read, so <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> shows the applied conditions as removable chips (screen <code>compact-multirow</code>: "Status: Open ×", "Created by: Hammad Hassan ×"). This issue builds the chips as their own component over the query tree; the compact component uses it next. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search/applied-filters.{js,hbs}</code>: <code>&lt;EzSearch::AppliedFilters @tree @schema @onChange /&gt;</code>.<ul><li>One chip per complete top-level condition of the root group: the field label from the schema, the operator in words for anything other than equals (e.g. "Title contains: search", "Start between: 2026-05-01 and 2026-08-31"), and the display value (enum and user labels from the schema values, IN values joined with commas).</li><li>A nested group is one chip: "Any of: …" for OR, "All of: …" for AND, built from its conditions.</li><li>Removing a chip calls <code>@onChange</code> with the tree without that condition or group, using the <code>app/utils/query/ast.js</code> helpers. The caller applies it.</li><li>Incomplete conditions get no chip.</li></ul></li><li>Markup: <code>btn btn-default btn-xs</code> chips with the value in <code>strong</code> and an <code>fa-times</code>, wrapping onto more lines. Long values are truncated with an ellipsis and a <code>title</code> tooltip. Render as text, never <code>htmlSafe</code>.</li><li>Styles go in <code>app/styles/components/ez-search-chips.scss</code> (imported in <code>app.scss</code>, scoped). Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.chips.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>Chips render for equals, contains, IN, BETWEEN and a nested OR group.</li><li>Removing each chip emits the expected tree.</li><li>Incomplete rows are ignored.</li><li>Labels come from the schema.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> editing a chip in place, using chips on <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code>.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> compact-multirow.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4332	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	79a3ac356aef-f4f7-a72a-e5489087c035	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 18:12:29	aprom	0	0
260bf6966aef-f4f7-a72a-d36007809894	EzSearchCompact: drop-in compact ezSearch, multi-row or linear	2026-11-07 17:51:34	2026-11-07 19:18:45	0	<p>Narrow places (the idea list now; Threads, Gantt Cal, Task Board and the app header later) need ezSearch without the full toolbar. <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> is a drop-in replacement for <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code>: it extends the same base (<code>app/components/ez-search/base.js</code>) and takes exactly the same arguments, so a view switches by changing the component name. Its only extra argument is <code>@linear</code>. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search-compact/index.{js,hbs}</code> (Glimmer, extends the base; no logic of its own beyond layout).</li><li><strong>Multi-row</strong> (default, screens <code>compact-multirow</code>, <code>compact-edited</code>, <code>compact-mobile</code>):<ul><li>Row 1: <code>EzSearch::SearchBar</code> across the full width, with <strong>Search</strong> (<code>btn-primary</code>, <code>fa-search</code>) and <strong>Clear</strong> (<code>btn-default</code>, <code>fa-times</code>) attached at its right end (Bootstrap <code>input-group input-group-sm</code> look). The suggestion menu and errors show under the bar.</li><li>Row 2: <strong>Saved</strong>: <code>fa-bookmark-o</code> "Saved" when none is active; <code>btn-primary</code> with <code>fa-bookmark</code> and the name (plus "· edited") when one is. The menu opens left-aligned with the edited entries and the list, plus "Save current search…" when <code>@onSave</code> is given. Then <strong>Filter</strong> (<code>fa-sliders</code>) with a <code>label label-primary</code> badge counting the complete conditions.</li><li>Row 3: <code>EzSearch::AppliedFilters</code>; removing a chip applies immediately.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Linear</strong> (<code>@linear={{true}}</code>, screen <code>compact-linear-header</code>): one row with the Saved icon button (the active name, truncated, when one is active), the bar filling the rest, Filter with its badge, Search and Clear as icon buttons. No chips. Icon-only buttons get translated <code>title</code> tooltips.</li><li>Filter opens the builder in a <code>bootstrap-modal</code> (screen <code>idea-search-a-builder</code>): the formatted query, <code>EzSearch::Panel</code>, and footer buttons Clear (left), Cancel and Search. Search applies and closes; Cancel discards the panel's changes.</li><li>The bar needs no form-field margin (as aprom-4308 did for EzSearch). If <code>EzSearch::SearchBar</code> can't sit inside an input group as it is, add a layout option to it rather than duplicating it.</li><li><code>app/styles/components/ez-search-compact.scss</code> (imported, scoped under <code>.ez-search-compact</code>): square edges, existing tokens. It fills its container's width at any size, down to 390px.</li><li>Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearchCompact.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>The same argument set as <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code>: render both with identical arguments and check apply, clear, saved-search select/edit/update and save produce the same callbacks.</li><li>Multi-row: the rows, the badge count, chip removal applying, and Search/Clear.</li><li>Linear: a single row (bar, Filter, Search and Clear share one top) and no chips.</li><li>The modal applies on Search and discards on Cancel.</li><li>Checked in a browser in a <code>col-md-3</code> column at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> using it on any page (next issues and later phases), the header integration.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4330, aprom-4331, aprom-4332</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> compact-multirow.png, compact-edited.png, compact-linear-header.png, compact-mobile.png, idea-search-a-builder.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4333	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	489e94366aef-085b-e956-09c4befba398	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 19:18:46	aprom	0	0
