639d7fc96afc-7dc1-276c-46fd0cdd1da6	Talos overlap gate: count only the worker's and owners' unparked issues as in flight	2026-11-17 12:06:59	2026-11-17 12:35:24	0	<p>Agamemnon's overlap gate holds a new issue when its predicted files overlap an issue that is in flight in the same repo. Today "in flight" means every issue in an <code>aga-*</code> milestone of the worker's projects, whoever owns it, whose status is not <code>new</code> or done (<code>OverlapGate.begin()</code> in <code>lib/orchestrator/overlap.py</code>, <code>policy.is_active()</code> in <code>lib/orchestrator/policy.py</code>). This has two effects:</p><ul><li>Deferred issues that belong to other people block new work. On 2026-11-17, #4628 was held for about two hours by Rana's deferred, never-started #4492. The only reason was that both issues were predicted to touch <code>translations/en-us.json</code>. Because the next issues (#4629, #4630, #4631) depend on #4628, they were blocked too. On 2026-11-16, #4598 was held by #4492 over <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>.</li><li>Every sweep runs a failing <code>git diff</code> for those issues and logs <code>[overlap] #N: no branch diff (fatal: bad revision 'origin/dev...claude-issue-N')</code>. <code>IssueFiles.branch</code> only looks for a local <code>claude-issue-N</code>, which exists only while a <code>.runs/issue-N</code> worktree does.</li></ul><p>Changes:</p><ul><li><code>policy.is_active(issue, done_statuses, parked=PARKED_STATUSES)</code> also returns false for parked statuses. The default is <code>("deferred",)</code>, and an agent setting <code>overlapParkedStatuses</code> can change it. <code>is_active</code> has no other callers.</li><li><code>OverlapGate.begin()</code> counts an issue as in flight only when it is active and assigned to the worker or to one of the orchestrator's <code>owners</code>. Other people's issues in the milestone are never in flight. Use the same assignee and owner checks the candidate filter uses (<code>policy.new_skip_reason</code>), so the two can't drift apart.</li><li><code>IssueFiles.branch</code>: first check with <code>git rev-parse --verify -q</code> that <code>origin/&lt;base&gt;</code> and the branch exist. Try the local <code>claude-issue-N</code>, then <code>odysseus/claude-issue-N</code>. If neither exists, return <code>None</code> without logging, because that is the normal case for an issue that hasn't started. Still log a diff that fails on a ref that does exist.</li><li>README, <em>Overlap hold</em> section: say which issues count as in flight, and document <code>overlapParkedStatuses</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An issue in <code>deferred</code>, or assigned to someone other than the worker or the owners, never holds a candidate. Unit tests in <code>tests/test_overlap.py</code> and <code>tests/test_policy.py</code> cover both cases.</li><li>An issue assigned to the worker and in progress still holds a candidate that overlaps it, as it does today.</li><li>For an in-flight issue with no local branch but with <code>odysseus/claude-issue-N</code>, the gate uses that branch's diff (test with a temporary repo or a stubbed <code>subprocess.run</code>).</li><li>An issue with no branch anywhere falls back to the prediction and logs nothing.</li><li><code>python -m unittest discover -s tests</code> passes from <code>dev-tools/talos</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> treating other teammates' active issues as conflict risks (a possible later option), and changing how <code>ai context</code> predicts files.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5 (<code>overlap.py</code>, <code>policy.py</code>, <code>test_overlap.py</code>, <code>test_policy.py</code>, <code>README.md</code>)</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4634	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-