7704c6e86af2-3028-5ed1-ef7dd6f0f111	External Request: Conversation rooms: read-only comment, vote and like counts per room	2026-11-09 23:21:27	2026-11-09 23:51:43	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Prometheus (idea "Threads :: UI Update ", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p><strong>Request from A Prometheus.</strong> The Threads page (Prometheus) is moving to a QuickList and shows comment counts and vote tallies on each row and on vote threads. Gaia has no count for a room, so Prometheus currently queries each row's comments (20 extra calls per page) and loads every vote comment to count agree/disagree. We ask for one read-only resource that returns counts for many rooms in one call. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract:</strong></p><ul><li>Read-only resource <code>conversationroomcount</code> (view model, like <code>app/metadata/model/Userlatestproject.php</code> with COUNT subqueries): fields <code>id</code> (= room id), <code>commentCount</code>, <code>likeCount</code> (votes on the room), <code>agreeCount</code> and <code>disagreeCount</code> (comments of vote rooms with the text "I agree" / "I disagree"), <code>lastCommentDate</code>, <code>projectId</code>.</li><li><code>GET /conversationroomcount?query=(Conversationroomcount.id CONTAINS 'a','b',...)</code> returns one row per room; list + get only (no create/update/delete), standard CRUD controller, no custom routes.</li><li>ACL: project-scoped like Conversationroom; reading needs <code>conversationroom.read</code> (or a new <code>conversationroomcount.list</code>, your call).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> api-tester cases for counts (no comments = 0, deleted comments not counted, agree/disagree split) and for project scoping. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> live events for counts (Prometheus updates counts from comment events).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity