4f1bc8f26ae5-3a9e-bbf4-ed9c4583cfce	Idea messages: parse the screens and steps JSON from Gaia so screens show in the thread and plan box	2026-10-31 09:47:59	2026-10-31 11:36:54	0	<p>Agent Nestor's screens never appear on the idea page. The plan box shows only a static <code>fa-picture-o</code> icon and the screen key (the "missing" branch in <code>components/idea/plan-box.hbs</code> ~l.29), and the conversation shows nothing. Engineers can't see a mockup while planning; they only see it once the issues are created (attachments on created issues work).</p><p>Cause: Gaia stores <code>Ideamessage.screens</code> and <code>Ideamessage.steps</code> as JSON <strong>text</strong> (<code>gaia/core/mvc/models/behaviors/ideaScreensBehavior.php</code> encodes arrays; fields are <code>type text</code>) and returns them as strings. <code>models/ideamessage.js</code> declares <code>@attr screens</code> and <code>@attr steps</code> with no transform, so they stay strings. <code>components/idea/message-screens.js</code>, <code>plan-box.js</code> <code>screens</code> and <code>message-item.js</code> <code>steps</code> all require <code>Array.isArray</code> and get nothing. The Mirage factory (<code>mirage/factories/ideamessage.js</code>) returns arrays, which hid it.</p><ul><li>Start with a failing test: make the Mirage <code>ideamessage</code> factory (and any fixtures) return <code>screens</code>/<code>steps</code> as JSON strings, as Gaia does.</li><li>Declare both as <code>@attr('json')</code> (existing <code>transforms/json.js</code>). If the transform's lack of a <code>serialize</code> breaks saving a user message, add a <code>serialize</code> that sends arrays as JSON text (Gaia's behaviour accepts both). Make sure null, empty string and invalid JSON give an empty list, not an error.</li><li>No component changes beyond what the parsed arrays need. <code>Idea::MessageScreens</code> then renders each screen and the plan box finds it by key and version, so title and version show and the click opens it (existing <code>open</code>).</li><li>Tests: a unit test for the model/transform (string, array, null, invalid). The acceptance case in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/</code> shows a Nestor message with a screen as a clickable entry in the thread and in the plan box, and its steps listed.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on an idea whose Nestor messages carry screens, each screen appears as a clickable entry with its title and version, in the message and in the plan box, and Nestor's steps show again. This works with the real Gaia response, not just Mirage.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the thumbnail image itself (separate issue), Gaia changes, attachments on created issues (they work).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4221	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	794026106ae5-0477-bbf4-0c9c774a755a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 11:36:55	aprom	0	0
c745e1466aeb-4599-8fd2-2d8e015abd5b	Talos: start and restart the Docker engine (Docker Desktop locally, configurable commands for a server)	2026-11-04 21:21:11	2026-11-04 22:02:22	0	<p>When Docker is down, every run fails and needs a person to start it. Today Talos runs on engineers' machines (Docker Desktop, started by the user). Later it will run on a server, where Talos and Docker are part of the system's boot. Talos needs one safe way to start or restart the engine on both, and to wait until it answers.</p><ul><li>New module <code>talos/lib/docker_engine.py</code>: <code>start()</code> and <code>restart()</code>, each followed by <code>wait_ready(timeout)</code>, which polls <code>docker_state.read()</code> until the daemon answers.</li><li>Configured commands first: agent.json <code>docker.startCommand</code> / <code>docker.restartCommand</code> (argv lists, run without a shell and without a TTY so nothing can prompt; e.g. a server with a sudoers rule uses <code>["sudo", "-n", "systemctl", "restart", "docker"]</code>).</li><li>Defaults when no command is set: the <code>docker desktop start|restart</code> CLI when it exists (Docker Desktop 4.37+). Otherwise, behind <code>os.name == "nt"</code> with both branches written: Windows launches <code>Docker Desktop.exe</code> from Program Files (path found, not hard-coded to one drive) and restarts by stopping its process tree first; Linux uses <code>systemctl --user start|restart docker-desktop</code> when that unit exists. A rootful system <code>docker.service</code> without a configured command is refused with a clear message saying which setting to add.</li><li>Return a result: <code>{action, ok, seconds, method, error}</code>. Timeout from <code>docker.startTimeoutSeconds</code> (default 180).</li><li>After the engine is up, report whether the p4m stack containers (gaia-dev, postgres, proxy) are running (<code>docker ps</code>). Don't start them: say which ones are missing.</li><li>README: the defaults per platform and the server setup (commands and the sudoers line).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests with stubbed processes cover configured commands, each default method, the timeout, the refused rootful case and the Windows tree kill. Tried by hand once on Windows Docker Desktop, noted in the PR.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> deciding when to start or restart (dispatch hold and aga issues), installing Talos as a system service, remote Docker hosts.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4274</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4275	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	662fe2126aeb-833c-8fd2-cb969af2b24d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-04 22:02:23	adt	0	0
3857a8196ae3-2d66-a456-b18fb52c9297	Research and ADR: project-agnostic run environments (an independent full stack per agent run)	2026-10-29 10:21:44	2026-10-29 10:21:44	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. Today's isolation is specific to Projects4Me: dev-tools knows Gaia's database names, harness, migrate command and <code>DB_NAME</code>. The goal is for Talos to run agents for any project, including ones whose dependencies we don't know (for example an app with three databases and a queue). That needs the project to declare its environment, and Talos to run whatever is declared.</p>\n<p><strong>The decision record should cover</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Isolation level</strong>: shared services split logically (today), a full stack per run from the project's compose file (<code>docker compose -p run-N</code>: private networks, volumes, names), or a VM/sandbox per run (its own Docker daemon, removing the "Docker socket = root on the host" risk). When each is worth it.</li>\n<li><strong>The environment contract</strong> the project owns: a manifest with hooks <code>up</code>, <code>prepare</code> (migrate and seed from this checkout), <code>test</code>, <code>health</code>, <code>snapshot</code>/<code>restore</code>, <code>down</code>. Reuse <code>devcontainer.json</code> plus compose, or our own file.</li>\n<li><strong>Data</strong>: no hidden dependency on a dev database (Gaia's harness copies ACL/OAuth/catalog rows from <code>pr4m</code>). Seeds and fixtures in the repo, or a versioned snapshot artifact with personal and sensitive data removed.</li>\n<li><strong>Startup cost</strong>: snapshots of prepared volumes or images keyed by a hash of schema and seeds, a warm pool, and a <code>snapshot</code> hook per database engine.</li>\n<li><strong>Resources</strong>: a resource budget per environment for concurrency (RAM and CPU, the Docker Desktop VM cap on Windows), not only <code>maxParallel</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Hostnames, ports, TLS, OAuth</strong>: per-run names (for example <code>run-N.local-projects4.me</code>) through a wildcard reverse proxy, apps that read redirect URLs and allowed origins from the environment, a browser target per run (no dev-stack lock).</li>\n<li><strong>External services</strong>: for each one, stub it (mailpit, emulators) or use a shared sandbox account with names per run.</li>\n<li><strong>Several repos</strong>: combining repos at chosen versions (<code>dev</code>'s head, or a dependency's branch), tied to dependency gating.</li>\n<li><strong>Secrets</strong> per environment without images or disk (extends adt-4175's env-only approach); an escape hatch for things that don't containerise (a declared shared service plus a lock); time limits and garbage collection for leaked volumes and networks; who keeps the definition in step with production.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Done when</strong>: an ADR in <code>dev-tools/docs/</code> with the chosen design and its trade-offs; a prototype running Gaia's suite in a per-run compose stack (its own Postgres, seeds from the repo, no <code>pr4m</code>); and proposed follow-up implementation issues.</p>\n<p>Depends on: none (the test slot template issue is the short-term fix)</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	4187	2026-11-05	2026-10-29	new	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	bcb698486ae0-36a5-29af-ebb1949fa852	a0deeed56ad7-404c-ce18-923e6af9b747	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-10-29 10:21:44	adt	0	0
8011d3e96af2-3028-5ed1-d9b78f8663e1	Threads: load row counts and vote tallies with one Gaia call	2026-11-09 23:21:36	2026-11-10 11:46:53	0	<p>Once Gaia serves room counts (the A Gaia counts request in this plan), replace the per-row comment queries (row counts issue) with one <code>conversationroomcount</code> query per loaded page, and take the vote thread's tallies and Result from it (<code>agreeCount</code>/<code>disagreeCount</code>) instead of counting all vote comments; the voter list and Participants keep their own queries.</p><ul><li>New model + adapter/serializer if needed, Mirage handler.</li><li>Swap only the count sources; rows, vote UI and live updates unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a 20-row page makes one count request (test on the Mirage request log); vote tallies match. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> anything else on the page.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4438, aprom-4440, agaia-4446</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4447	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	5ddd66856af3-e269-5f43-61da00cd1fda	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 11:46:53	aprom	0	0
e1f3f7596aeb-833c-a4f5-5f1823ac9578	Merge check: accept a recorded design review instead of CodeRabbit for repos in mergeReviewers (dev-tools)	2026-11-04 21:34:26	2026-11-04 22:06:56	0	<p>Agamemnon can't merge dev-tools PRs, and CodeRabbit won't be enabled on dev-tools. The merge check (<code>ai/lib/mergegate.py</code> <code>check_coderabbit</code>, ~l.35) fails with "CodeRabbit doesn't review this repo" for any repo not in <code>codeRabbitRepos</code>. Without a replacement, the only checks left for dev-tools would be tests and "no comments from people": dev-tools has no GitHub CI, so <code>check_ci</code> passes with "no CI checks on this commit". This issue makes the design-reviewer the review signal for such repos.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Config:</strong> a new setting in <code>ai/config.json</code>, <code>mergeReviewers</code>, for example <code>{"dev-tools": "design-review"}</code>. Validate it like <code>codeRabbitRepos</code> (<code>ai/lib/coderabbit.py</code> <code>enabled()</code>): unknown repos or reviewer kinds are an error, and a repo can't be in both. Add a small helper for the lookup that ship, the merge check and Talos can share.</li><li><strong>Record the design review against the tree:</strong> a passing design review is recorded for the exact tree it reviewed, the same way <code>ai test</code> records the last full run. Don't take the agent's word for it through a ship.json field. <code>ai ship</code> writes a fixed line, for example <code>DESIGN REVIEW: clean</code>, into the PR body's How tested section only when the recorded review is clean and matches the current tree. If the review isn't recorded, is stale or has open findings, ship still opens the PR without the line, and the merge check then sends the issue to the owner. Choose how the review is recorded (an <code>ai</code> command that runs the design-reviewer headless, or ship running it) and explain the choice on the PR.</li><li><strong>Merge check:</strong> for a repo in <code>mergeReviewers</code>, the <code>coderabbit</code> check is replaced by a <code>review</code> check: OK when the PR body has the design-review line, FAIL otherwise. Read it from the body like <code>check_tests</code> (~l.74). Repos in <code>codeRabbitRepos</code> are unchanged.</li><li>The <code>self</code> check (<code>agamemnonProtected</code>) stays as it is, so PRs that change Agamemnon's own code still go to the owner.</li><li>Update <code>dev-tools/ai/README.md</code> and the ship-issue skill.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li><code>ai mergecheck dev-tools &lt;pr&gt;</code> is ok for a PR with a passing test run, a clean design review recorded for its tree, and no protected paths.</li><li>It fails with a clear reason when the design-review line is missing, or when the PR touches <code>agamemnonProtected</code> paths.</li><li>Gaia, Prometheus and Hermes PRs are checked exactly as before.</li><li>Unit tests cover the config validation, the tree-bound record, the ship body line and the new check.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> handing dev-tools issues to Agamemnon after ship (the follow-up issue), and the auto-merge milestone setting.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4280	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	6da61e256aeb-1df9-a4f5-f22cb6872b4e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-04 22:06:56	adt	0	0
5c79ad966ae5-3a9e-bbf4-5411f6d4e102	Idea screens: show the full image instead of the boolean fileThumbnail	2026-10-31 09:48:12	2026-10-31 14:05:50	0	<p>Once the screens of idea messages are parsed (previous issue), <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code> (<code>components/idea/message-screen.{hbs,js}</code>, used in the thread and the plan box) still can't show an image. It takes the <code>img src</code> from <code>services/upload-preview.js</code> <code>thumbnail()</code>, which reads <code>upload.fileThumbnail</code> from <code>findRecord('upload', id)</code>. For <code>GET /upload/{id}</code> Gaia returns that field as the stored <strong>boolean</strong>. Only the POST response and Gaia's <code>FilethumbComponent</code> (for files <code>included</code> with a parent such as an issue) swap in base64 data. The image is broken, and even a real thumbnail would be a 198x132 crop, too small for a mockup.</p><ul><li>Show each screen as its full image, scaled to the available width, using <code>uploadPreview.previewUrl(uploadId)</code> (download token + <code>/preview/get/&lt;token&gt;</code>). <code>modifiers/render-markdown.js</code> already shows pasted images this way. Show the title and version (<code>views.app.idea.conversation.screenVersion</code>) under it, and the <code>fa-picture-o</code> placeholder while it loads or if it fails.</li><li>Keep the click that opens the full-size image in a new tab (existing <code>open</code>).</li><li>Remove the <code>thumbnail()</code> use, and the method if nothing else calls it. Don't treat <code>fileThumbnail</code> as an address in this component.</li><li>Sizes in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code>: in a message the screen spans the message width (<code>.idea-message-screen</code> is a fixed 160px today). In the plan box screen row (<code>plan-box.hbs</code> ~l.23) keep a compact size that fits the side column.</li><li>Guard the async load after destroy (check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after the await).</li><li>Tests: integration test for <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code>. With a Mirage upload whose <code>fileThumbnail</code> is <code>true</code>, it renders an <code>img</code> with the preview address. A failed token shows the placeholder.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the idea page every screen in Nestor's messages and in the plan box shows its image as soon as the page loads, before any plan is approved. A click opens it full size.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> an in-app lightbox, Gaia thumbnail changes, issue Files box thumbnails.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4221</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4222	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	f51268196ae5-1fa0-bdc7-3a13bc7c881c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 14:05:50	aprom	0	0
a9b81eb16af7-3fb3-e127-47e6ba7ab348	Replace EmberRouter.reopen with router-service events; set up tooltips with one delegated call	2026-11-14 01:04:41	2026-11-14 21:34:50	0	<p><code>app/initializers/javascript-behaviors.js</code> modifies Ember's own <code>Router</code> class with <code>EmberRouter.reopen</code> to do two things:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>call <code>Pace.restart()</code> on <code>routeWillChange</code>;</li>\n<li>run <code>$('[data-toggle="tooltip"]').tooltip()</code> on <code>routeDidChange</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The per-transition tooltip call only reaches elements that exist when the page change finishes. Rows loaded afterwards, modals, dropdowns and re-rendered lists never get a tooltip. About 100 elements in 17 templates use <code>data-toggle="tooltip"</code>.</p>\n<h4>Do</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Pace:</b> register <code>router.on('routeWillChange', () =&gt; Pace.restart())</code> once, in an instance-initializer or the application route. Pace's own request tracking stays untouched: no change to <code>vendor/pace/pace-options.js</code> or <code>utils/ui/pace-config.js</code>. It still tracks all API calls and still ignores <code>/socket.io/</code> and the Hermes origin.</li>\n<li><b>Tooltips:</b> replace the per-transition call with one delegated Bootstrap 3 call at boot: <code>$(document.body).tooltip({ selector: '[data-toggle="tooltip"]' })</code>. It keeps the same look, needs no template changes, and covers elements rendered later.</li>\n<li>Remove the <code>reopen</code> and the commented-out console code. Keep <code>applyPaceTransportExclusions()</code> and the Messenger options.</li>\n<li>Tests:\n<ul>\n<li>a page change calls <code>Pace.restart</code> (stubbed);</li>\n<li>a tooltip appears on hover over an element rendered after the page change finished;</li>\n<li>socket.io and Hermes URLs are still in Pace's ignore list.</li>\n</ul></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Not in scope: moving the tooltips to the tippy-based <code>{{initialize-tooltip}}</code> modifier, which 