021d48156af2-3028-5ed1-62aa2f047f40	Threads: ezSearch metadata (views.Conversationroom.search) incl. 'Liked by'	2026-11-09 23:19:30	2026-11-09 23:48:36	0	<p>Threads (app.project.conversation) is moving to the QuickList list + detail layout used by Ideas and Roles (aprom-4428, aprom-4430). Its search must come from view metadata like every other list, replacing the hard-coded filters in <code>controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code> (<code>conversationFilters</code> ~l.295, <code>conversationDateFilters</code> ~l.344).</p><ul><li>Add <code>views.Conversationroom.search</code> in <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>, same format as <code>views.Idea.search</code> / <code>views.Role.search</code>: subject, description, roomType (values vote | discussion, translated), linked issue (Conversationroom.issueNumber, with empty / not empty), dateCreated, dateModified, created by, and <strong>Liked by</strong> = <code>votes.createdUser</code> (Gaia already accepts <code>(votes.createdUser : &lt;userId&gt;)</code>, used by today's My Likes filter), with the project members as value source and the current user first.</li><li>If the metadata format or <code>services/query-schema.js</code> cannot express a relation field like <code>votes.createdUser</code>, extend it generically (no thread-specific code in ez-search) and document it in <code>docs/architecture/metadata-views/</code>.</li><li>Translations in en-us.json.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit test that the schema built from the metadata produces <code>(Conversationroom.roomType : vote)</code>, <code>(Conversationroom.issueNumber NULL)</code> and <code>(votes.createdUser : X)</code> clauses. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> wiring it into the page (next issue).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4436	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9