8ee825746adf-c3cd-5c87-44180b87e7a2	ai kb: index Gaia generated doc sections, graph nodes and exemplar PRs in the existing FTS5 store	2026-10-26 08:08:46	2026-10-27 08:54:52	0	<p><b>Phase 4 of "Agentic Improve" (dev-tools side).</b> <code>ai kb</code> already keeps an incrementally synced SQLite FTS5 index of tracker issues (<code>lib/kb.py</code>, <code>kbstore.py</code>, <code>kbsync.py</code>). Extend it so the same deterministic search covers the Gaia knowledge produced in A Gaia #4132. No LLM router, no server: keyword search first; local embeddings (<code>sqlite-vec</code> + a small embedding model) only as a later issue if <code>ai cost</code> shows keyword retrieval missing.</p>\n<p><b>What</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>New document kinds in the store: doc section (file + heading anchor + text, from <code>gaia/docs/generated/</code> and <code>docs/architecture/</code>), graph node (from <code>docs/generated/graph.json</code>: models, routes, controllers, components, permissions, profiles, assertions), exemplar PR (from <code>docs/dev/bundles.md</code>).</li>\n<li><code>ai kb sync</code> picks them up from the checkout (content-hash based, incremental); <code>ai kb search</code> gains <code>--kind</code>; results print the section's anchor and size so a caller can fetch exactly that section.</li>\n<li><code>ai kb section &lt;file#anchor&gt;</code> prints one section (≤ 40 lines).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Checks:</b> unittest with a fixture docs tree; sync is idempotent.</p>\n<p><b>Depends on:</b> A Gaia #4132. <b>Exit:</b> every repeat-read question from the analysis resolves to a section under 40 lines via <code>ai kb search</code>.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4138	2026-12-08	2026-11-27	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	8fe2ae046adf-8154-4904-8f5112ed5746	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	325bf9e36ae0-8390-9d4f-b292a