a0b83b716ae0-e00c-868d-b734b2aee752	ai test gaia: run tests/tools (gaia-dev consistency tests) so the local full suite matches CI; map gaia-dev and docs/generated changes to it	2026-10-27 11:23:12	2026-10-27 11:32:12	0	<p><b>Found on gaia PR #216 (agaia-4027).</b> The ship session reported <code>RESULT: PASS</code> from three full <code>ai test gaia</code> runs while CI failed with 5 failures and 2 errors. Gaia's CI runs three PHPUnit folders (<code>tests/libraries/security</code>, <code>tests/libraries/utils</code>, <code>tests/tools</code>); <code>ai test gaia</code> runs only the first two (<code>PHPUNIT_FOLDERS</code> in <code>ai/lib/tests.py</code>). <code>tests/tools</code> holds the gaia-dev consistency tests added by agaia-4128/4132/4134/4135 (graph up to date, every behaviour has a test, scaffolders can plan against the real harness), so a branch can never learn locally that it will fail CI on them. Same class of gap as agaia-4123 (tests/services).</p>\n<p><b>What</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add <code>tests/tools</code> to <code>PHPUNIT_FOLDERS</code>, so the full run, the baseline run and <code>ai ship</code>'s gate all cover it.</li>\n<li><code>ai test gaia --changed</code>: map changes under <code>tools/gaia-dev/**</code>, <code>docs/generated/**</code>, <code>app/metadata/**</code>, <code>core/config/routes.php</code> and <code>tools/api-tester/harness/**</code> to <code>tests/tools</code> in <code>lib/testmap.py</code>, so targeted runs catch a stale graph or a broken scaffolder anchor too.</li>\n<li>Unit tests in <code>ai/tests</code> for the mapping and the folder list; README/skill line updated if they list the folders.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Depends on:</b> nothing. <b>Exit:</b> on a branch that only adds a model without regenerating the graph, <code>ai test gaia</code> fails locally the same way CI does.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4147	2026-10-28	2