7d95a6196ae0-1cbd-b9b8-89636eae55fe	Talos: claude run fails with WinError 206 (command line too long) and reports log "none"	2026-10-27 12:09:33	2026-10-27 14:22:48	0	<p>On 2026-10-27 the address-review run for agaia-4027 (gaia#217, Agent Achilles) ended with <code>Claude run ended with talos error: [WinError 206] The filename or extension is too long</code> and <code>Talos log: dev-tools/talos/state/logs/none</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Cause:</b> <code>talos/lib/runner.py</code> builds <code>[claude, "-p", prompt, ...]</code>, so the whole prompt is an argv entry. Windows limits a command line to about 32k characters; a review-round prompt that embeds the open review threads (CodeRabbit security findings with suggested diffs) exceeds it. The run then fails before a log file exists, and the escalation comment prints <code>logs/none</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Fix:</b> pass the prompt on stdin (<code>claude -p</code> reads it) or from a file, never as an argument; keep argv for the flags only. Open the log file before launching so a launch failure is written there and the comment names a real path. Add a runner unit test with a 40k-character prompt on Windows (or a mocked <code>subprocess</code> that asserts the prompt is not in argv). Check the same for the CATCH_UP prompt and the nestor/sim runners.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4151	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	5e0a92326ae0-480e-d28c-869f6df6eeb2	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-27 14:22:49	adt	0	0
cf1513506aef-9eab-9161-e066abea5bf5	Gantt Cal: search with EzSearchCompact	2026-11-07 20:27:59	2026-11-08 00:14:21	0	<p>The Gantt Cal has no search UI: it only honours a <code>?query=</code> URL parameter, which the route ANDs into each milestone's issue query (<code>routes/app/project/gantt.js</code> ~l.53-82, controller <code>queryParams = ['query']</code> ~l.130). Add <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> (aprom-4333, multi-row, the default) at the top of the task list. The engineer approved the placement in screen <code>gantt-compact</code>. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>components/app-ui/gantt-chart.hbs</code>: add a named block (e.g. <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code>) rendered at the top of <code>.gantt-task-list</code>, above <code>.gantt-header</code>. The chart knows nothing about search. In <code>styles/modules/gantt.scss</code>, keep the task rows and the timeline rows aligned when the block is present: the timeline side gets the same top offset, or the block sits outside both scroll areas. Check the row alignment in the browser.</li><li><code>templates/app/project/gantt.hbs</code>: pass <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact @schema @query @savedSearches @activeSavedSearchId @onSavedSearchChange @onApply @onSave @onUpdateSavedSearch @aclContext="issue.read" /&gt;</code> in that block, plus the save dialog as on the Issue list. No <code>@baseQuery</code>: the route adds milestone and project.</li><li><code>routes/app/project/gantt.js</code>: load the Issue schema (<code>query-schema</code> <code>load('Issue', {projectId})</code>, metadata <code>views.Issue.search</code>) and the project's issue saved searches through <code>services/saved-search.js</code> (<code>relatedTo: 'issue'</code>, <code>projectId</code>, shared with the Issue list).</li><li><code>controllers/app/project/gantt.js</code>: add <code>searchId</code> to <code>queryParams</code>. Apply, select, save and update go through the saved-search service. Don't copy list-controller code. Live-sync reloads keep the active query.</li><li>Acceptance (<code>tests/acceptance/gantt/</code> + steps, Mirage issue handler already records the query):<ol><li>Type and run a query: issues are requested with it ANDed with milestone and project, and <code>?query=</code> is set.</li><li>Remove a chip: it re-runs.</li><li>Apply a saved search: its name shows.</li><li>An error shows and nothing is sent.</li></ol></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios pass.</li><li>The existing Gantt tests (drag, resize, dependencies, issue panel, live sync) pass.</li><li>Task rows and timeline rows stay aligned with the search present.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filtering milestones (the query applies to issues), the Calendar view, the Task Board.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4336, aprom-4331</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> gantt-compact.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4337	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	fa85fce26aef-24e0-f5a5-8849965ab611	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 00:14:21	aprom	0	0
