518a97186ae0-e923-b9b8-4c3ebcfb1381	Remember the show/hide state of field info ("i") bubbles	2026-10-27 11:56:01	2026-10-27 12:10:47	0	<h3>Problem</h3><p>Form fields that use <code>@showFieldInfo</code> show an info icon ("i") next to the label, with an info bubble beside it. Clicking the icon hides or shows the bubble, but the choice isn't saved. After a re-render, a route change or a page reload, every bubble shows again and the user has to hide it again.</p><p>This affects:</p><ul><li>Project create: End date, Status, Issue types</li><li>Settings → Issue statuses: Value, and the read-only value</li><li>Any other form field that passes <code>@showFieldInfo</code></li></ul><h3>Cause</h3><p><code>FormFields::Label</code> (<code>app/components/form-fields/label.js</code>) toggles the bubble by finding it with <code>document.querySelector</code> and setting <code>style.display</code> directly. The state lives only in the DOM.</p><h3>Expected behaviour</h3><ul><li>Bubbles start visible, as they do now.</li><li>When the user hides a field's bubble, it stays hidden after a reload, on other screens, and in later sessions in the same browser.</li><li>Clicking "i" again shows it and saves that choice too.</li><li>Each field's state is separate.</li></ul><h3>Implementation</h3><ul><li>New service <code>services/field-info.js</code> that only remembers which bubbles are hidden. It keeps a tracked set of hidden keys, saved to <code>localStorage</code> under <code>field-info-hidden</code>, and offers <code>isHidden(key)</code> and <code>toggle(key)</code>. Storage access is wrapped in try/catch so the app still works without it. This follows the sidebar-collapse pattern in <code>modifiers/initialize-sidebar.js</code>.</li><li><code>FormFields::Label</code>: inject the service, add an <code>isInfoHidden</code> getter and an <code>@action toggleInfo</code>, and drive the template with <code>{{#unless}}</code> instead of DOM manipulation. The key is <code>@data-field</code>, and an optional <code>@infoKey</code> can override it.</li><li>YUIDoc on the service and the changed component. The license header stays.</li></ul><h3>Acceptance criteria</h3><ol><li>Hiding a bubble on Project create → Issue types and reloading the page leaves it hidden.</li><li>Clicking "i" again shows it, and it stays visible after a reload.</li><li>Hiding one field's bubble doesn't hide any other field's bubble.</li><li>If <code>localStorage</code> is unavailable, the toggle works for the current page without errors.</li></ol><h3>Tests</h3><ul><li>Unit test for the <code>field-info</code> service.</li><li>Integration test for <code>FormFields::Label</code>: hide the bubble, re-render, and it stays hidden.</li><li>The test fails before the fix.</li></ul><h3>Out of scope / follow-ups</h3><ul><li>Saving the state per user in Gaia so it follows the user across devices. This would need a Gaia preference model.</li><li>The bubble's old styling (rounded corners, hard-coded <code>#5bc0de7d</code> / <code>#5497ab</code>), which breaks the design-system rules. This gets a separate issue.</li></ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4149	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Odysseus	Rana Nouman	905950016ae0-c582-b9b8-f2bc0e57572f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-27 12:10:46	aprom	0	0
ca6eea616ae3-b6e2-0c1c-3bd5b7863ff2	CodeRabbit loop per repo: enable it for gaia, prometheus and hermes; hand off straight away everywhere else	2026-10-29 16:39:38	2026-10-30 22:23:31	0	<p>Follow-up to adt-4189/4190. Today the loop runs for every repo and only learns that a repo has no CodeRabbit by waiting <code>botReviewWaitMinutes</code> (20) for a review that never comes. GitHub can't tell us which repos have it: <code>requested_reviewers</code> is always empty, the PR sidebar only shows CodeRabbit after it has posted a review (never on a clean pass), and the app-installation API needs CodeRabbit's app JWT. So the repos are listed explicitly, and there is no waiting on a repo that isn't listed.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>ai/config.json</code>: <code>"codeRabbitRepos": ["gaia", "prometheus", "hermes"]</code> (keys of <code>REPOS</code>). A helper in <code>ai/lib/coderabbit.py</code> (e.g. <code>enabled(repo)</code>) is the only place that reads it; unknown names in the list are an error at load time.</li><li><code>ai rabbit</code> on a repo not in the list reports <code>absent</code> ("CodeRabbit not enabled for &lt;repo&gt;") immediately, with no API calls and no <code>--wait</code> polling.</li><li><code>ai ship --defer-handoff</code> on a repo not in the list does the normal hand-off (<code>in_review</code>, reviewer) and reports that it did, so Talos ends the run as <code>done</code> rather than <code>awaiting_bot_review</code>. The Odysseus ship prompt and <code>/ship-issue</code> follow that result instead of assuming a wait.</li><li>Talos: if a waiting record still exists for a repo that isn't enabled (e.g. one written before this change), hand off on the first check.</li><li>For enabled repos nothing changes: the 20-minute wait stays as the safety net when CodeRabbit never reports.</li><li>READMEs (ai, Talos) and <code>p4m configure</code>/doctor output show which repos have the loop.</li></ul><p><strong>Prerequisite outside the code</strong>: the CodeRabbit GitHub app must be installed on <code>projects4me/hermes</code> (no hermes PR shows any CodeRabbit check, status or comment yet). Gaia and prometheus already have it.</p><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests for an enabled repo (unchanged behaviour), a disabled repo (<code>ai rabbit</code> absent without API calls; <code>--defer-handoff</code> hands off at once; Talos outcome <code>done</code>), a stale waiting record for a disabled repo, and a bad name in <code>codeRabbitRepos</code>; a dev-tools PR shipped through Talos goes to <code>in_review</code> with no wait.</p><p>Depends on adt-4193 for the loop to work on gaia (check-run reading); the two can be worked in either order.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4194	2026-11-05	2026-10-29	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	b17312f46ae3-decc-a579-ad6b25b76ddd	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-29 17:14:46	adt	0	0
dd523d506aef-9eab-9161-b19e1d1bf05b	Task Board: search with EzSearchCompact (linear), inline with the milestone tabs	2026-11-07 20:28:13	2026-11-07 21:12:56	0	<p>The Task Board has two separate filters in the milestone tabs row (<code>components/app-ui/task-board.hbs</code> ~l.37-62):</p><ul><li>a Saved Searches <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code>, whose state lives in the component (<code>activeSearch</code>, <code>filterQuery</code>, <code>toggleSearch</code>, <code>isSearchActive</code>, <code>task-board.js</code> ~l.26-163) and which applies through <code>@applySearch</code> to the controller's <code>query</code>/<code>searchId</code> URL parameters (<code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> ~l.833; the route ANDs the query into each lane's issue query);</li><li>a free-text <code>&lt;Input&gt;</code> that hides loaded cards in the browser (<code>task-board/issues-provider.js</code> ~l.32: subject, description, number).</li></ul><p>Replace both with <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact @linear={{true}}&gt;</code> (aprom-4333). There is one search model, so typed text runs on the server (bare words become <code>Issue.subject CONTAINS …</code>) and the lanes reload. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>task-board.hbs</code>: replace the dropdown and the <code>&lt;Input&gt;</code> in <code>.milestone-filters</code> with <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact @linear={{true}} @schema @query @savedSearches @activeSavedSearchId @onSavedSearchChange @onApply @onSave @onUpdateSavedSearch @aclContext="issue.read" /&gt;</code>, all passed in from the page.</li><li>Placement (engineer's requirement, screen <code>board-linear</code>):<ul><li>The search stays <strong>inline with the milestone tabs, on the same row</strong>, and never drops onto its own row at md widths and up.</li><li>The row is a flex row: the tab strip takes the remaining space (<code>flex: 1</code>, <code>min-width: 0</code>) and scrolls sideways when there are more tabs than fit; the search takes at least 30% of the row (<code>flex: 0 0 30%</code>, growing only if its content needs it).</li><li>The tabs keep working as drop targets (<code>.drop-zone-area</code>) while scrolled.</li><li>Only below 768px does the search wrap under the tabs at full width (screen <code>board-linear-mobile</code>).</li></ul></li><li><code>task-board.js</code>: remove <code>query</code>, <code>filterQuery</code>, <code>activeSearch</code>, <code>toggleSearch</code>, <code>isSearchActive</code> and the constructor's saved-search lookup. Remove the client text filter from <code>issues-provider.js</code> and <code>milestones.hbs</code> (<code>@query</code>). <code>initialize-sortable</code> receives <code>query</code> to re-attach Sortable when the cards change; make sure lanes re-rendered by the route reload still get Sortable (drag still works after a search).</li><li><code>templates/app/project/board.hbs</code>, <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code>, <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code>:<ul><li>Load the Issue schema (<code>query-schema</code> <code>load('Issue', {projectId})</code>) and the issue saved searches through <code>services/saved-search.js</code> (<code>relatedTo: 'issue'</code>, <code>projectId</code>), replacing the route's own saved-search queries (~l.161-166).</li><li>Apply, select, save and update go through the service, and set <code>query</code>/<code>searchId</code> as <code>applySearch</code> does now.</li><li>Add the save dialog as on the Issue list.</li><li>Hermes live updates keep the active query.</li></ul></li><li><code>styles/modules/board.scss</code>: the flex row, the tab-strip scroll and the mobile wrap, scoped under the board.</li><li>Tests: update <code>tests/acceptance/taskboard/filter-issues.feature</code> and its steps:<ol><li>Typing <code>subject words</code> and pressing Enter requests every lane with <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS 'subject words')</code>.</li><li>Applying a saved search shows its name and sets <code>searchId</code>.</li><li>Clear resets.</li><li>Cards can still be dragged after a search.</li><li>The search and the tabs share one row at desktop width (same top).</li></ol></li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The scenarios pass.</li><li>The other Task Board tests (quick create, status update, milestone create and complete) pass.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width with two and with eight milestone tabs (search stays inline, at least 30%), and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> keeping an instant client-side card filter, the planning view, the Gantt.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4333, aprom-4331</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> board-linear.png, board-linear-mobile.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4338	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	2a6993396aef-be8d-9161-f2c3e7d03bd9	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 21:12:57	aprom	0	0
ec2b69656aeb-2e52-8b27-d1d7b1d40e09	Workflow editor: saving a Run agent step does nothing (no request, no error)	2026-11-04 22:42:52	2026-11-05 01:04:11	0	<p>In the workflow editor (aprom-4038, properties panel aprom-4057), filling in a Run agent step and saving it does nothing. The engineer traced it: <strong>no network request is sent and nothing is logged in the console</strong>. So the save stops in Prometheus before it reaches Gaia.</p><p><strong>How saving works</strong> (from aprom-4038 and 4057)</p><ul><li>The panel edits a deep-copied draft and writes it back with Apply. The header Save persists the graph through the workflow-graph service, which orders the node, edge and workflow writes.</li><li>The aprom-4057 notes say live edits were rejected because changes to the shared <code>node.config</code> could not be tracked.</li></ul><p><strong>Where to look</strong></p><ul><li>The Apply and Save handlers: is the action wired up, or is the button disabled without a visible cue?</li><li>Client-side validation of the draft that fails and returns without a message.</li><li>The graph service skipping the node because it looks unchanged. If Apply writes into the existing <code>config</code> object, or the change isn't seen on the record, nothing is dirty and nothing is sent.</li><li>A swallowed promise rejection: a <code>catch</code> or <code>then</code> without a handler.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Start with a failing test that reproduces it: fill a Run agent step, Apply, Save, and expect a <code>workflownode</code> POST or PATCH in Mirage. Then fix the cause.</li><li>Make every failure visible: a validation problem is shown on its field or in the panel, and a failed save shows Gaia's message through <code>errorManager</code>.</li><li>Once the request goes out, follow Gaia's rules for <code>run_agent</code> (<code>gaia/core/libs/workflows/NodeKindCatalog.php</code>, <code>NodeConfigRules.php</code>):<ul><li>Fields: <code>agentId</code> (required), <code>prompt</code>, <code>session</code>, <code>model</code>, <code>maxTurns</code>, <code>claimTimeout</code>, <code>timeout</code>.</li><li>All are strings, including <code>maxTurns</code> and the timeouts: numbers are rejected.</li><li>Any other key is rejected. Drop empty optional fields.</li><li>An Active workflow's structure can't change.</li></ul></li><li>Check that the other node kinds save after the fix.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A Run agent step with an agent, a prompt and any mix of optional settings saves (a request is sent), and reloads with the same values.</li><li>Any blocked or failed save shows a message.</li><li>Tests cover the save, the config shape and the error display.</li></ul><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4284	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	273c8bb66aeb-a0c5-8b27-8d8c1f236f8d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-05 01:04:11	aprom	0	0
561419e06ae0-36a5-29af-93d4eac42bc5	Task board: card assignee dropdown never opens (click stopped before Bootstrap sees it)	2026-10-27 16:16:22	2026-10-27 18:31:40	0	<p>aprom-4102 added the shared <code>Issue::AssigneeSelect</code> component and uses it in compact form on task board cards (<code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code> ~l.126). On the board, clicking a card's assignee avatar does nothing: no menu opens and nothing shows that the avatar is clickable. The issue detail view, which uses the non-compact form, works.</p><p><strong>Cause</strong>: the wrapper <code>.dropdown</code> in <code>components/issue/assignee-select.hbs</code> has <code>{{on "click" this.stopPropagation}}</code>. When <code>@compact</code> is set, <code>stopPropagation</code> (<code>assignee-select.js</code> ~l.40) stops the event. Bootstrap 3 opens dropdowns from one delegated <code>click.bs.dropdown.data-api</code> listener on <code>document</code>, so the click from <code>[data-toggle="dropdown"]</code> never gets there. Stopping the click isn't needed: the card has no click handler (the quick view opens only from the title <code>LinkTo</code>), and Sortable already ignores the dropdown (<code>modifiers/initialize-sortable.js</code> ~l.582, <code>filter: '[data-issue-assignee-dropdown]'</code>, <code>preventOnFilter: false</code>).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Start with a test that fails: an acceptance scenario on the board (Mirage) that clicks the avatar trigger on a card (<code>[data-issue-assignee-toggle]</code>), checks that the dropdown gets the <code>open</code> class and that its menu is visible, then picks a member and checks the new avatar.</li><li>In <code>assignee-select.hbs</code>, remove the <code>click</code> handler from the wrapper. Keep the <code>mousedown</code> one only if a test shows it's needed to stop a drag; otherwise remove it and the <code>stopPropagation</code> action.</li><li>Compact trigger: add a small <code>fa fa-caret-down</code> after the avatar so it reads as a dropdown, the same way the detail view does. Size and space it in the <code>&amp;.assignee-select-compact</code> block in <code>styles/modules/issue.scss</code> (~l.639) so the card footer layout stays unchanged.</li><li>Check in the running app that the menu is fully visible on the last card of a lane. The lane body (<code>.milestone.box-body</code>, <code>styles/modules/board.scss</code> ~l.69) has <code>overflow-x: auto</code>, which also clips vertically. If the menu is cut off, open it upward on cards (Bootstrap's <code>dropup</code> on the compact wrapper). Don't change the lane's overflow or z-index.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>On the task board, clicking a card's assignee avatar (or caret) opens the member menu. Choosing a member saves the issue and updates the avatar, with the existing toasts.</li><li>Clicking the avatar doesn't open the quick view. Dragging the card by its body still works, before and after a reassignment.</li><li>The menu is fully visible for the first and last card of a lane.</li><li>The issue detail view's assignee dropdown is unchanged. Existing tests and lint pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: other quick edits on the card; the drag tolerance (separate issue); live updates from other users (aprom-3978).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4155	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	5d5d86956ae0-5335-306a-b25039df9c6c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-27 18:31:41	aprom	0	0
63762d976ae0-36a5-29af-c0eafb38c757	Task board: clicking a card title sometimes doesn't open the quick view (drag starts on a 1px move)	2026-10-27 16:16:35	2026-10-27 19:39:45	0	<p>On the task board, clicking a card's subject sometimes doesn't open the quick view. A perfectly still click works; a click where the mouse or trackpad moves by a pixel doesn't.</p><p><strong>Cause</strong>: the board passes <code>@forceFallback={{true}}</code> (<code>templates/app/project/board.hbs</code> l.15), so SortableJS does its own mouse-event dragging instead of native HTML5 drag. The lane options in <code>modifiers/initialize-sortable.js</code> <code>getSortableOptions()</code> (~l.571, used by <code>_attachSortableToLanes</code>) set no <code>fallbackTolerance</code>, and Sortable's default is <code>0</code>. Its tolerance check (<code>if (fallbackTolerance &amp;&amp; …)</code>) is then skipped, so any <code>mousemove</code> after <code>mousedown</code> starts a drag. After a fallback drag, Sortable sets <code>ignoreNextClick</code> and swallows the next <code>click</code> in a document capture listener. The <code>{{on "click" (fn @selectIssue issue)}}</code> on the title <code>LinkTo</code> (<code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code> ~l.62) then never runs. Sortable's default <code>ignore: 'a, img'</code> applies only to native drag, so it doesn't help here. Confirm this against the installed SortableJS version (<code>package.json</code>: <code>^1.14.0</code>) before changing anything.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In <code>getSortableOptions()</code>, add <code>fallbackTolerance: 5</code> and, for touch, <code>delay: 150</code> with <code>delayOnTouchOnly: true</code>. Put the values in named constants with a YUIDoc comment explaining why. Don't add the title link to <code>filter</code>: the subject is most of the card and must still start a drag.</li><li>Fix the <code>disableSortable</code> getter (~l.106), which returns <code>this.args.named</code> instead of <code>this.args.named.disableSortable</code>. Pass it to Sortable as <code>disabled</code> (the real option name) instead of <code>disableSortable</code>, in <code>getSortableOptions()</code> and in the two milestone-tab instances (~l.484, ~l.547). The board is the only caller and passes <code>false</code>, so behaviour stays the same.</li><li>Leave the milestone-tab instances' other options alone: they only receive dropped cards.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit test (modifier) asserting that the lane options include <code>fallbackTolerance</code> &gt; 0, <code>delayOnTouchOnly: true</code> and <code>disabled: false</code> when the board passes <code>@disableSortable={{false}}</code>.</li><li>Manual check in the running app: clicking a card subject with a slight mouse movement opens the quick view every time; dragging a card between lanes and onto a milestone tab still works; the parent-issue link on a card still opens its quick view.</li><li>Existing board tests (<code>tests/unit/controllers/app/project/board*.js</code>, <code>tests/acceptance/taskboard/</code>, <code>tests/acceptance/live/board-live-updates.feature</code>) and lint pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: switching off <code>forceFallback</code>, the assignee dropdown on cards (separate issue) and other Sortable refactoring.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4156	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	33def0986ae0-0184-3839-4a674cd67e39	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-27 19:39:46	aprom	0	0
c4cb9be26afc-093c-0c6d-022df0e2e3ee	Retro - aga-Navbar	2026-11-17 14:42:12	2026-11-17 14:42:12	0	<p>2026-11-17 to 2026-12-17 (all work happened on 2026-11-17) · 9 issues (9 done, 0 carried over) · 1.9h logged (114m) vs no time estimate set (only "Estimated files" in 5 descriptions)</p>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>All nine issues were delivered on the day the milestone started. Five planned issues (#4628-#4632) shipped as one PR each with a green suite, and four small follow-up issues (#4635-#4638) were then raised from visual review of the result. The follow-ups were all layout and style defects that the first five PRs flagged as "not checked in a browser". Review cost was low, but the one rework cycle (#4636) came from a missed requirement on mobile.</p>\n<h2>Numbers</h2>\n<table><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Planned / added</td><td>5 (#4628-#4632, created 09:53-09:57) / 4 (#4635-#4638, created 13:40-14:05). Milestone start-date is the same day, so "added" is inferred from creation time</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Delivered</td><td>9 of 9 (100%)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Estimate accuracy</td><td>not computable: no time estimates (all 0m)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Late</td><td>0 (all done before 2026-12-17; no done-date available, see Data gaps)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Rework</td><td>1 issue (#4636: second PR #857 after #855 was merged); 4 follow-up issues (#4635, #4637, #4638 and #4636) created after the first PRs</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Waiting</td><td>#4628 and #4629 were held by Agamemnon behind #4492 (see below); no issue used feedback or pending</td></tr></table>\n<h2>What went well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Every issue passed lint and the full ember suite on first ship (1641 to 1647 tests, 0 failures) — #4628, #4629, #4630, #4631, #4632, #4635, #4636, #4637, #4638.</li>\n<li>Issues with a precise description (files, selectors, acceptance, out of scope, dependencies) went through with no human feedback and about 6-10 min logged — #4629, #4630, #4631, #4632. #4628, the largest, took 30m.</li>\n<li>Dependency ordering ("Depends on") was respected: #4630 was assigned once #4628 was done, #4631 once #4629 and #4630 were done.</li>\n<li>The ship notes record design-review follow-ups and unverified areas explicitly (e.g. #4628, #4631), which made them easy to triage.</li>\n<li>Small CSS-only issues were cheap: 6-14m each — #4635, #4637, #4638.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What didn't go well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>#4636 needed a second PR: the width change also narrowed the logo on phones, and the reviewer asked for it to stay full width. #855 had already merged, so the fix went into new PR #857. 28m logged, the most of the four follow-ups; 3 sessions. The description did not mention the mobile logo.</li>\n<li>Four defects were found after the first five PRs merged: the mobile switcher label and dropdown were squeezed (#4635), the highlighted option's short code was unreadable (#4637), header items were misaligned and clipped on mobile (#4638), and the menu width was too large (#4636). The first four were visual and each earlier PR said it had not been checked in a browser (#4628, #4629, #4630, #4631, #4632).</li>\n<li>#4635 reverses a decision in #4628 (phone label = short code only), so the spec itself produced a defect that review then reversed.</li>\n<li>#4628 and #4629 were held by Agamemnon behind #4492, which was still deferred and assigned elsewhere when #4628 shipped; Achilles flagged the conflict risk in #4628's PR comment. #4629 was also interrupted once when Talos stopped (13:04), then resumed.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Patterns</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><b>No browser verification of UI work</b> (9 of 9 issues): each ship note says layout, mobile or overlay was not visually checked (#4628, #4629, #4630, #4631, #4632, #4635, #4636, #4637, #4638). Four follow-up issues came from exactly that gap. Suggests visual defects reach review by default.</li>\n<li><b>Mobile cases under-specified</b> (#4630, #4635, #4636, #4638): each concerns phone layout; #4630's 15rem padding assumes a 10px root font and was unverified.</li>\n<li><b>Repeated design-review follow-ups left undone</b> (#4628, #4631): logic left in component rather than a service, duplicated dot markup, an unused getter and translation, global CSS rules. Single cases each, but both were deferred, not ticketed.</li>\n<li><b>Overruns and underruns:</b> no estimate to compare. Largest logged: #4628 30m (Story, 21 files against 10 estimated, one cohesive move) and #4636 28m (rework). Smallest: #4629 6m and #4630 6m (files 6 of 7 and 4 of 4). #4632 touched 6 files against 4 estimated.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Surprises</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Single case: #4628 touched 21 files against an estimate of 10; the ship note explains the move could not be split (#4628).</li>\n<li>Single case: #4637's fix assumes power-select sets aria-current on the highlighted option and was not confirmed (#4637).</li>\n<li>Time logs are very short (6-30m per issue; 114m for nine issues), so the whole milestone is about 2 hours of logged work.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Proposed actions</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Add a browser or screenshot check step (desktop, 390px, collapsed sidebar) to the UI ship flow, or have the PR state which viewports were verified — addresses "No browser verification" — /ship-issue skill or the Prometheus CLAUDE.md. Works if fewer visual follow-up issues appear after UI milestones.</li>\n<li>Add a "mobile behaviour" line (what changes below 768px, what stays) to the issue template for layout changes — addresses "Mobile cases under-specified" — Nestor/Agamemnon issue template. Works if no reviewer feedback concerns a mobile side effect.</li>\n<li>When an issue changes a shared style (width, logo), list the other breakpoints affected in the description — addresses #4636 rework — issue template.</li>\n<li>Record design-review follow-ups (#4628, #4631) as proposed backlog issues in the retro or ship note, for approval — addresses the deferred follow-ups pattern — ship flow.</li>\n<li>Set a time estimate on issues so estimate accuracy can be computed — addresses the Data gaps — issue creation in Nestor/Agamemnon.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Data gaps</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Estimates: all issues show 0m estimated, so estimate accuracy and overruns could not be computed. Only "Estimated files" exists.</li>\n<li>Done dates and status history are not exposed, so "Late", bounce counts and waiting time in feedback could not be measured; the milestone end date (2026-12-17) is far after all work, so lateness is unlikely.</li>\n<li>Planned vs added is inferred from issue creation times; the milestone start date is the same day.</li>\n<li>PR review history on GitHub was not read (no gh access in this run), so CodeRabbit rounds and human review comments on PRs #848-#857 are known only from Gaia comments. CodeRabbit reviewed none per the ship notes.</li>\n<li>Hours for waiting on #4492 (#4628, #4629) cannot be quantified; only the comment times are available (hold at 09:57 and 12:36).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Issue ledger</h2>\n<table><tr><th>#</th><th>Title</th><th>Status</th><th>Est</th><th>Actual</th><th>Review rounds</th><th>Notes</th></tr>\n<tr><td>4628</td><td>Header: project switcher replaces the sidebar project selector</td><td>done</td><td>none (10 files)</td><td>30m</td><td>0 human; no CodeRabbit</td><td>PR #849; 21 files; held behind #4492</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4629</td><td>Sidebar: Workspace / Project / Admin groups</td><td>done</td><td>none (7 files)</td><td>6m</td><td>0</td><td>PR #851; run interrupted once; held behind #4492</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4630</td><td>Header: centre the global search</td><td>done</td><td>none (4 files)</td><td>6m</td><td>0</td><td>PR #850</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4631</td><td>Header: online status, remove user panel</td><td>done</td><td>none (7 files)</td><td>10m</td><td>0</td><td>PR #852</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4632</td><td>Sidebar: close menu after navigation on phones</td><td>done</td><td>none (4 files)</td><td>7m</td><td>0</td><td>PR #848; 6 files</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4635</td><td>Navbar Project selection mobile</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>7m</td><td>0</td><td>PR #853; CSS only; follow-up to #4628</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4636</td><td>Nav menu width</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>28m</td><td>1 human</td><td>PRs #855, #857; mobile logo width fix</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4637</td><td>Project selector highlight not affecting shortcode</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>6m</td><td>0</td><td>PR #854; selector assumption unconfirmed</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4638</td><td>Header component alignment</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>14m</td><td>0</td><td>PR #856; style only</td></tr></table><p>Complexity: simple</p>	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	1	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	4639	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	new	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729		\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Hera	Hera	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-17 14:42:13	aprom	0	0
bbdc79976aef-9eab-9161-15c63c511c5e	EzSearchCompact: Search and Clear as icon buttons attached to the bar	2026-11-07 20:27:39	2026-11-07 20:53:23	0	<p>On the idea list (aprom-4334) the compact search's Search and Clear take too much of the narrow column: they render as wide text buttons. The agreed design (screens <code>compact-multirow</code>, <code>gantt-compact</code>) has them as icon-only buttons attached to the right end of the bar, so the input keeps almost the full width. Fix it in <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> (aprom-4333) so every compact user gets it. <strong>About the attached screens:</strong> they are a rough guide to layout and content, rendered with only today's CSS, not the final look; the design system and the real components win.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search-compact/index.hbs</code>, multi-row layout, row 1:<ul><li>The bar, then Search as <code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code> with only <code>fa-search</code>, then Clear as <code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code> with only <code>fa-times</code>.</li><li>Both are attached to the bar like a Bootstrap <code>input-group-btn</code>: same height as the input, no gap, square edges.</li><li>Each has a translated <code>title</code> and <code>aria-label</code> (reuse <code>global.form.search</code> and <code>global.form.clear</code>).</li></ul>The linear layout already uses icons; make both layouts share the same button markup (one partial or sub-component), not two copies.</li><li><code>app/styles/components/ez-search-compact.scss</code>: the bar fills the remaining width. Remove any width or padding that made the buttons wide.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An integration test asserts that the multi-row Search and Clear contain no text, only their icons, carry titles, and sit on the bar's row. In a 300px container the input is wider than both buttons together.</li><li>Checked in the browser on the idea list at desktop width and at 39