409cb1b66ace-34bf-02fa-51672a59312d	Application Settings (admin area): API	2026-10-13 17:37:04	2026-10-15 17:59:40	0	<p>Backend for the new admin Settings area in Prometheus: an ACL resource for admins, a settings store, email configured from settings, and admin management of issue statuses and default issue types.</p><p><strong>Decisions (agreed 2026-10-13)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Admin access is a new ACL resource <code>setting</code> (read/update), granted on the Roles screen. No role-name checks.</li>\n<li>The main sidebar's Admin section is consolidated into a single <strong>Settings</strong> entry. Users and Roles move into the settings side nav.</li>\n<li>Settings navigation is a grouped side nav (System, Issues, Users &amp; Access, later Integrations, Plugins), GitLab/Jira style. Only built pages are shown; no "planned" placeholders ship.</li>\n<li>Email settings: values saved in the database win; unset values fall back to the current env vars.</li>\n<li>Issue statuses get a colour (from the existing status palette) and a sort order that drives task board columns.</li>\n<li>Issue types managed here are the defaults copied into new projects; existing projects keep their own copies.</li>\n</ul><p>The Prometheus side is the matching epic in A Prometheus.</p><p><em>Mockups:</em> attached in Files. Source: <code>dev-tools/mockups/settings/</code> (built from the real Prometheus CSS and shell; the footer position in the mockups is not part of the design).</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	3956	2026-10-20	2026-10-13	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cb9835c25acd-06d6-1141-d64018bb91b3	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	ec4442d76ace-34bf-02fa-4aafe5afa15d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-15 17:59:41	agaia	0	0
51815b056ace-34bf-02fa-e13315c356d4	Add 'setting' ACL resource (read/update) for the admin Settings area	2026-10-13 17:37:21	2026-10-14 20:13:44	0	<p>Admins are defined by permission, not by role name. Add a <code data-tomark-pass="">setting</code> resource so the Roles screen can grant access to the Settings area.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope</strong></p>\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Add <code data-tomark-pass="">setting</code> with <code data-tomark-pass="">read</code> and <code data-tomark-pass="">update</code> actions to <code data-tomark-pass="">AclMapCatalog</code> (system scope).</li><li data-tomark-pass="">System issue status and system issue type writes (G4, G5) are authorized by <code data-tomark-pass="">setting.update</code>, not by project membership.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Expose the permission to Prometheus the same way other resources are (so the UI can hide Settings).</li></ul>**Acceptance criteria**\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">A user whose role has <code data-tomark-pass="">setting.read</code> can GET settings; without it, 403.</li><li data-tomark-pass=""><code data-tomark-pass="">setting.update</code> is required for every settings write.</li><li data-tomark-pass=""><code data-tomark-pass="">AclLockoutGuard</code> still prevents removing the last admin-capable role's access.</li></ul>**Tests**\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">api-tester <code data-tomark-pass="">acl</code> catalog: allowed and denied cases for <code data-tomark-pass="">setting.read</code> / <code data-tomark-pass="">setting.update</code>.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">PHPUnit in <code data-tomark-pass="">tests/libraries/security</code> for the seeder defaults.</li></ul>*Mockups:* attached in Files. Source: <code data-tomark-pass="">dev-tools/mockups/settings/</code> (built from the real Prometheus CSS and shell; the footer position in the mockups is not part of the design).\n	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	1	3957	2026-10-20	2026-10-13	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	409cb1b66ace-34bf-02fa-51672a59312d	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	97036e316ace-f427-02fa-e5456929fe13	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-14 20:13:44	agaia	0	0
5a2ba3d26ace-34bf-02fa-a1a0417a59b5	Settings store and API (key/value, secrets encrypted)	2026-10-13 17:37:30	2026-10-14 19:34:37	0	<p>There is no place to store application settings. Add a settings model and endpoint the Settings pages can read and write.</p><p><strong>Scope</strong></p><ul><li>New model <code>Setting</code> (metadata, model, controller, routes, models.php): <code>group</code>, <code>key</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>secure</code> flag, audit fields, GUID id, soft delete.</li><li><code>GET /api/v1/setting?query=(Setting.group : email)</code> and <code>PATCH</code> to update; guarded by the <code>setting</code> ACL resource (G1).</li><li>Secure values (e.g. SMTP password) are encrypted at rest and never returned; the API returns a flag that a value is set.</li><li>A PATCH with an empty secure value keeps the stored one.</li><li>Regenerate the api-tester backend catalog.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Settings can be read and written by admins only.</li><li>The SMTP password never appears in any API response, log or export.</li><li>Values survive a restart and a re-run of <code>migration migrate</code> with no diff.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><ul><li>api-tester backend + acl cases for read, write, secure masking and keep-on-empty.</li><li>PHPUnit for encrypt/decrypt and masking.</li></ul><p><strong>Depends on</strong></p><ul><li>G1 (setting ACL resource)</li></ul><p><em>Mockups:</em> attached in Files. Source: <code>dev-tools/mockups/settings/</code> (built from the real Prometheus CSS and shell; the footer position in the mockups is not part of the design).</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	3958	2026-10-20	2026-10-13	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	409cb1b66ace-34bf-02fa-51672a59312d	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	089dbe036ace-a6e0-83ee-cf177b2d096c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-14 19:34:37	agaia	0	0
634cb5966ace-34bf-02fa-05671157f1a1	Email: read SMTP from settings with env fallback, and add a test-email endpoint	2026-10-13 17:37:39	2026-10-15 12:25:27	0	<p>SMTP is configured only through env vars in <code>core/config/smtp.php</code>, and the setup is duplicated in <code>core/events/notifications/Email.php</code> (<code>resetPassword()</code> and <code>emailPassword()</code>).</p><p><strong>Scope</strong></p><ul><li>One mailer factory used by both email methods (removes the duplicated setup).</li><li>Each SMTP value (host, port, encryption, username, password, from name, from email) comes from settings group <code>email</code>; if unset, from the current env/config value.</li><li><code>POST /api/v1/setting/testemail</code> with a recipient sends a test message using the current settings; returns a clear success or the SMTP error. Requires <code>setting.update</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>With no email settings saved, behaviour is exactly as today.</li><li>Saved settings take effect without a restart.</li><li>Test email reports SMTP failures as an error, never as success.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><ul><li>PHPUnit for the settings-over-env resolution.</li><li>api-tester case for the test-email endpoint (mailer stubbed in the test env).</li></ul><p><strong>Depends on</strong></p><ul><li>G2 (settings store)</li></ul><p><em>Mockups:</em> attached in Files. Source: <code>dev-tools/mockups/settings/</code> (built from the real Prometheus CSS and shell; the footer position in the mockups is not part of the design).</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	3959	2026-10-20	2026-10-13	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	409cb1b66ace-34bf-02fa-51672a59312d	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	cf5b1cd36acf-ef96-084b-f9d61a0930c2	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-15 12:25:27	agaia	0	0
7c8ad9156afc-30ee-311d-01fa3f095b2b	Events: file-based event registry that decides which events Gaia raises and on which channels	2026-11-17 15:36:28	2026-11-18 13:28:20	0	<p>Gaia raises events in two hand-kept lists: <code>EventNames</code> (live events sent to Hermes) and <code>TriggerEventCatalog</code> (in-process workflow triggers). We want one registry that records every event we raise, so adding or removing one is an edit in one place, and nothing goes to Hermes unless the registry says so. It must not live in the database: it is read on almost every API call.</p><ul><li>New <code>app/metadata/events.php</code> (next to <code>FTS.php</code>): a PHP array keyed by event name. Each entry has <code>description</code>, <code>scope</code> (<code>project</code> | <code>user</code>), optional <code>source</code> (<code>model</code>, <code>on</code> create|update, <code>fields</code>, <code>to</code>: the same shape as <code>TriggerEventCatalog::EVENTS</code>), <code>channels</code> (<code>hermes</code> and/or <code>workflow</code>), <code>consumers</code> (free list for documentation, e.g. prometheus, talos, workflows) and <code>enabled</code>.</li><li>Fill it with every event raised today: the 23 <code>EventNames</code> constants (channel hermes; also workflow for issue.created, issue.assignee.changed, issue.status.changed, milestone.completed) and the trigger-only events issue.modified, comment.added, wiki.created, wiki.modified, time.logged (channel workflow only). Copy the source definitions from <code>TriggerEventCatalog::EVENTS</code>. user.access.changed, notification.created and workflow.agent.run.requested are user scope.</li><li>A domain class (e.g. <code>core/libs/events/EventRegistry.php</code>) loads the file once per request (plain <code>require</code>, opcache) and answers <code>has</code>, <code>definition</code>, <code>enabled</code>, <code>names(channel)</code>, <code>scope</code>.</li><li><code>EventNames</code> keeps its constants (code refers to them), but <code>ALL</code>/<code>isAllowed</code> come from the registry: the names that are enabled and on the hermes channel.</li><li><code>HermesPublisher</code> drops (quietly, debug log) an event that is disabled or not on the hermes channel, before any HTTP call. Fail-open behaviour is unchanged.</li><li>New ADR in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md</code> (the registry replaces the hand-kept allowlist; why a file and not the database); update <code>architecture.md</code> key files.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> every event published today is still published with the same envelope; turning <code>enabled</code> off for one stops it being sent (unit test); unit tests for the registry class; existing live-event tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> <code>TriggerEventCatalog</code> reading the registry and gaia-dev tooling (separate issues); merging comment.added with conversation.comment.created (the name is stored in workflow trigger nodes, needs a data migration).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4640	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7b8e27936afc-30ee-311d-92e7628909b7	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	54ed5ea56afc-7fa9-cd83-8eccd921a05a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 13:28:21	agaia	0	0
6c0562696ace-34bf-02fa-67de013f8937	Issue statuses: add colour and sort order; admin CRUD for system statuses	2026-10-13 17:37:48	2026-10-14 20:41:23	0	<p>Statuses are global but have no colour or order; colours live only in Prometheus CSS (<code>styles/issue/issue-status.scss</code>), and <code>wont_fix</code> has none.</p><p><strong>Scope</strong></p><ul><li>Add <code>color</code> (hex, limited to the agreed palette) and <code>sortOrder</code> (int) to <code>Issuestatus</code> metadata; migrate.</li><li>Data migration: set colours and order for existing statuses to match today's CSS (new/in_review blue #80b5d3, in_progress crimson #B3244F, feedback/pending/deferred amber #f7bf65, done green #5ac594, closed/wont_fix salmon #e98a7e) and the current board order.</li><li>Create/update/delete of system statuses (<code>system = 1</code>) authorized by <code>setting.update</code>; reorder endpoint or PATCH of <code>sortOrder</code> in one request.</li><li>Delete is blocked (422 with a clear message) while any issue uses the status.</li><li>Return an issue count per status for the Settings list.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Statuses list returns colour, order, done flag and issue count.</li><li>Reordering persists and the list comes back in that order.</li><li>A status in use cannot be deleted.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><ul><li>api-tester backend + acl cases for create, update, reorder, delete-in-use.</li></ul><p><strong>Depends on</strong></p><ul><li>G1 (setting ACL resource)</li></ul><p><em>Mockups:</em> attached in Files. Source: <code>dev-tools/mockups/settings/</code> (built from the real Prometheus CSS and shell; the footer position in the mockups is not part of the design).</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	3960	2026-10-20	2026-10-13	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	409cb1b66ace-34bf-02fa-516