757f0db16ace-34bf-02fa-2584faa7960b	Default issue types: admin management of system types	2026-10-13 17:37:57	2026-10-14 20:55:06	0	<p>New projects copy the system issue types (<code>system = 1</code>) when they are created (done client-side in Prometheus <code>controllers/app/projects/create.js</code>). Admins need to manage those defaults.</p><p><strong>Scope</strong></p><ul><li>Create/update/delete of system issue types authorized by <code>setting.update</code> (today Issuetype's ACL group is Project).</li><li>Deleting a default type is a soft delete and never touches project copies (<code>system = 0</code>).</li><li>Return, per default type, how many projects use a type of that name (for the Projects using column).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Admins can add, rename, describe and delete default types.</li><li>Existing projects' types are unchanged by any of these operations.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><ul><li>api-tester backend + acl cases for create, update, delete and the projects-using count.</li></ul><p><strong>Depends on</strong></p><ul><li>G1 (setting ACL resource)</li></ul><p><em>Mockups:</em> attached in Files. Source: <code>dev-tools/mockups/settings/</code> (built from the real Prometheus CSS and shell; the footer position in the mockups is not part of the design).</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	3961	2026-10-20	2026-10-13	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	409cb1b66ace-34bf-02fa-51672a59312d	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	d1c7a2116acf-e4e6-e22c-d895fb2b3509	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-14 20:55:07	agaia	0	0
91c00bc46ace-34bf-02fa-ccb6f1bea159	Settings area shell: route, grouped side nav, consolidated Admin entry	2026-10-13 17:38:25	2026-10-17 19:15:43	0	<p>The frame every settings page lives in.</p><p><strong>Scope</strong></p><ul><li>Route <code>app.settings</code> (<code>/app/settings</code>, redirects to the first page the user can see) with child routes per page (<code>/app/settings/email</code>, <code>/issue-types</code>, <code>/issue-statuses</code>, <code>/users</code>, <code>/roles</code>).</li><li>Layout: <code>col-md-3</code> <code>box box-primary settings-nav</code> with grouped <code>nav-pills nav-stacked</code> (group headings like the sidebar's), <code>col-md-9</code> page content. Styles in <code>app/styles/modules/setting.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.settings-nav</code>, square edges, colours from <code>variables.scss</code>.</li><li>Nav is driven by metadata (group, route, icon, translation key, ACL context) so new pages are one entry.</li><li>Main sidebar: the Admin section shows one <strong>Settings</strong> entry (<code>fa-cogs</code>) instead of Users and Roles; it only renders for users with <code>setting.read</code>.</li><li>Users and Roles pages are reachable from the settings nav; their existing screens are reused.</li><li>Direct URL access without permission shows the access-denied page; <code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code> updated.</li><li>Breadcrumb: Dashboard &gt; Settings &gt; page. All strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; <code>-loading.hbs</code> skeleton.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Admins see Settings in the sidebar and can move between pages from the side nav; the active page is highlighted.</li><li>Non-admins don't see Settings, Users or Roles in the sidebar and get access-denied on direct URLs.</li><li>Looks identical to the attached mockups (no rounded corners, no new colours).</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><ul><li>Gherkin feature in <code>tests/acceptance/setti