b90f22f56ace-34bf-02fa-7277bca7b530	Use status colour and order from data for labels and task board columns	2026-10-13 17:39:05	2026-10-17 22:32:52	0	<p>Status colours are hard-coded per status name in <code>styles/issue/issue-status.scss</code>, so new statuses (and <code>wont_fix</code> today) render without a colour.</p><p><strong>Scope</strong></p><ul><li>Status labels across the app (issue list, detail, board, gantt, widgets) take their background from the status's <code>color</code>.</li><li>Task board columns follow <code>sortOrder</code>.</li><li>Keep the CSS classes as a fallback until all data has colours, then remove them.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A newly created status shows its chosen colour everywhere labels appear.</li><li>Board column order matches the Settings order.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><ul><li>Update affected acceptance features and Mirage issuestatus factory (colour, sortOrder).</li><li>Integration test for the status label rendering.</li></ul><p><strong>Depends on</strong></p><ul><li>#3960 (A Gaia)</li></ul><p><em>Mockups:</em> attached in Files. Source: <code>dev-tools/mockups/settings/</code> (built from the real Prometheus CSS and shell; the footer position in the mockups is not part of the design).</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	3967	2026-10-20	2026-10-13	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	7f53bcb86ace-34bf-02fa-83a17db4682e	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	e27ce0046ad3-c195-08a7-9bd02f986ab2	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-17 22:32:52	aprom	0	0
cd7faf776ace-fb40-02fa-9f7bc3779ea8	Settings access: new setting resource is allowed for every role in permissive ACL mode	2026-10-13 17:52:13	2026-10-15 14:41:17	0	<p><strong>Problem:</strong> in <code data-tomark-pass="">permissive</code> resolution mode, a resource with no permission rows for a role is <em>allowed</em> (<code data-tomark-pass="">core/libs/security/Acl.php</code> <code data-tomark-pass="">isResourceAllowed()</code>, missing grant returns true). <code data-tomark-pass="">RolePermissionSeeder</code> also gives new roles <em>allowed</em> for every resource.</p>\n<p>So when <code data-tomark-pass="">setting.get</code> / <code data-tomark-pass="">setting.update</code> ship (#3957), <strong>every existing role and every new role can open and change Settings</strong> until an admin explicitly denies it per role on the Roles screen. That contradicts "Settings only visible to admins".</p>\n<p><strong>Options discussed</strong></p>\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Deny-by-default resource list in system config (like <code data-tomark-pass="">acl.scopedResources</code>), e.g. <code data-tomark-pass="">acl.restrictedResources</code>: missing grant = deny for those resources even in permissive mode.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Configure every role manually after deploy.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">One-off migration writing deny rows for existing non-admin roles.</li></ul>To be decided and handled separately (per Hammad, 2026-10-13). Must be resolved before the Settings area goes live.\n	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	1	1	3968	2030-10-31	2026-10-13	new	low	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	63413fd6673b-6180-ffb0-440801685dd8	409cb1b66ace-34bf-02fa-51672a59312d	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	e7bd3e586ad0-23cb-8847-4b582bff1932	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-10-13 17:52:13	agaia	0	0
05a6ee596ace-a6e0-83ee-82f4d9ef13db	api-tester: membership POST case out of sync with the Membership model	2026-10-13 18:18:45	2026-10-15 17:56:31	0	<p><strong>What happens:</strong> <code>post-membership-api-v1-membership</code> in <code>tools/api-tester/apis/client.json</code> fails. It expects attributes <code>roleId</code>, <code>relatedTo</code>, <code>relatedId</code>, but the API returns <code>projectId</code> (null) and no <code>roleId</code>.</p>\n<p>Running <code>generate-backend-apis.php</code> also rewrites the membership POST body in <code>backend.json</code> (from <code>userId</code>/<code>projectId</code> to <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code>/<code>roleId</code>), so the generated catalog, the committed catalog and the model disagree.</p>\n<p>Already failing on <code>dev</code> before agaia-3958; not changed there. Decide which shape is correct and align the model, both catalogs and Prometheus.</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	3970	2026-10-20	2026-10-13	done	low	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	d89ec3f06ad1-5e79-aa23-2bf9809c9160	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-15 17:56:32	agaia	0	0
b76137526acf-81cf-527d-a9df1577f596	PATCH collection route (patchCollection) skips ACL checks and crashes on GUID ids	2026-10-14 20:01:59	2026-10-15 15:23:11	0	<p>Found while working on #3957. Every module that allows PATCH also routes <code>PATCH /api/v1/&lt;module&gt;</code> (no id) to <code>RestController::patchCollectionAction()</code> (<code>core/mvc/router.php:97</code>).</p><ul><li><code>$aclMap</code> has no <code>patchCollection</code> key, so <code>authorize()</code> doesn't resolve a real action. Writable-field ACL, <code>assertWriteInScope</code> and the system-record guard (setting.update) never run.</li><li><code>$modelName::findFirst($temp['id'])</code> puts the id into the query unquoted. GUIDs fail with a PhalconException returned as HTTP 200 (see #3969). Today this blocks writes by accident; it is not a safeguard.</li></ul><p><strong>Repro (test API):</strong> as a user with issuestatus.update but setting.update denied, <code>PATCH /api/v1/issuestatus</code> with <code>{"collection":[{"id":"&lt;system status id&gt;","description":"x"}]}</code> gets past authorization, then fails with "Column '…' doesn't belong to any of the selected models", HTTP 200.</p><p><strong>Suggested fix:</strong> either remove the collection PATCH/PUT/DELETE routes (Prometheus doesn't use them, which needs checking), or add <code>patchCollection</code> to <code>aclMap</code> as update, run the same per-record ACL checks as <code>patchAction</code>, and use bound parameters. Add acl cases.</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	3971	2026-10-22	2026-10-15	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	d34984586ad0-3892-bae6-9dd5d5148efd	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-15 15:23:11	agaia	0	0
87efff146acf-e4e6-e22c-2724cb54b6d7	Members record scope hides system issue types (projectId NULL): project create offers no types	2026-10-14 20:48:07	2026-10-14 21:06:38	0	<p>Found while working on #3961. Issuetype is project-grouped (<code>acl.groups = ['Project']</code>, groupKey <code>projectId</code>). Under <code>project.get = 2</code> (members), <code>Acl::applyRecordScope()</code> adds <code>Issuetype.projectId IN (&lt;member projects&gt;)</code>. System (default) types have <code>projectId = NULL</code>, so they are filtered out.</p><ul><li><strong>Project create:</strong> Prometheus <code>routes/app/projects/create.js</code> queries <code>(Issuetype.system : 1)</code>. A members-scope user gets an empty list, and the new project gets no issue types.</li><li><strong>Settings &gt; Issue Types</strong> (aprom-3965): an admin whose role has members scope sees no defaults. Get, update and delete of a system type by id are not blocked: <code>assertRecordIdInScope</code> returns early when projectId is null.</li><li>Reproduced on dev: Agent Odysseus (Coding Agent, project.get=2) lists 14 project types and 0 of the 9 system types.</li></ul><p><strong>Suggested fix:</strong> let rows with <code>projectId IS NULL</code> (system rows) through the project record scope for models that declare <code>acl.systemRecords</code>, e.g. <code>(Issuetype.projectId IN (...) OR Issuetype.projectId IS NULL)</code>. Reads still need <code>issuetype.get</code>; writes are already guarded by setting.update (#3957). Add acl cases for a members-scope user listing system types.</p><p>Likely introduced with the project.get none/all/members scopes (gaia#175).</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	3972	2026-10-22	2026-10-15	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	b43a1b286acf-e4e6-e22c-677b54dd8f22	402f48