b67f2e866acf-ef96-084b-c0f369f64e90	Router: app routes never register their controller/action ((array) cast of Phalcon Config)	2026-10-14 21:18:46	2026-10-15 15:48:51	0	<p>Found while working on #3959. In <code>core/mvc/router.php</code>, app routes are added with <code>$this-&gt;add($path, (array) $approute)</code>. <code>$approute</code> is a <code>Phalcon\\Config</code>, and casting it to an array returns its internal properties (<code>"\\0*\\0data"</code>, <code>"\\0*\\0insensitive"</code>, …), not <code>controller</code>/<code>action</code>. The registered routes for <code>/image</code>, <code>/download</code> and <code>/preview</code> therefore carry no usable paths.</p><p>Those URLs still respond because Phalcon's default <code>/:controller/:action</code> route catches them: <code>/download</code> dispatches to <code>DownloadController::indexAction</code>, not the configured <code>get</code> action. Any new app route with a nested path (e.g. <code>/api/v1/x/y</code>) silently goes to controller <code>api</code>.</p><p><strong>Fix:</strong> use <code>$approute-&gt;toArray()</code>. First check what <code>/image</code>, <code>/download</code> and <code>/preview</code> actually dispatch to today and whether Prometheus depends on it; fixing the cast changes their action from index to the configured one.</p><p>#3959 avoided this by adding REST module <code>actions</code> (<code>'actions' =&gt; ['testemail' =&gt; ['POST']]</code>) instead of an app route.</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	3973	2026-10-22	2026-10-15	done	low	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	a861c0f26ad0-9cba-bae6-dd674076a224	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-15 15:48:52	agaia	0	0
5ac991336ad0-9f8e-cbf0-dfbcba630038	Integration test that actually sends the notification emails (SMTP sink)	2026-10-15 09:09:46	2026-10-15 17:36:11	0	<p>Follow-up to #3959. Unit tests there run the notification emails against a stub mailer and never send a real message. Nothing yet proves a message is actually delivered through settings-configured SMTP.</p><p><strong>Scope</strong></p><ul><li>Add an SMTP sink to the local/CI stack that captures messages without delivering them (e.g. a Mailpit/MailHog-style container with an HTTP API), on the <code>backend</code> network. It must never use the real SMTP credentials.</li><li>An opt-in integration suite (like api-tester <code>--mode live</code> for Hermes) that:<ul><li>saves email settings pointing at the sink (host, port, encryption <code>none</code>, from name/email) through the settings API;</li><li>triggers the real flows: <code>POST /api/v1/forgetpassword</code> for a test user, and creating a user (welcome password email);</li><li>reads the sink's API and checks each message arrived with the right recipient, sender, subject and link/content;</li><li>restores the settings afterwards.</li></ul></li><li>No test-only endpoints or code paths in Gaia: the suite only drives public flows and the sink.</li><li>Document how to run it (README / P4M-CLI) and whether CI runs it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A successful send through settings-configured SMTP is verified end to end for both notification emails.</li><li>Default test runs never contact a real mail server.</li></ul>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	3974	2026-10-22	2026-10-15	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	f8bdd2c56ad0-5657-b053-e89662f91652	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-15 17:36:12	agaia	0	0
