5e0ecca9673f-2778-11fd-76e4bceb1be5	Upgrade the release using helm	2024-11-21 12:15:26	2024-11-21 13:13:51	0	<p>Currently, using the helm upgrade command, we were not able to pull the docker image from the docker hub because our deployments for both Gaia use the "<strong>dev-latest</strong>" tag with it, which was not updated at the time. So Helm considers this as the same image that's why in our CD workflow, when we tried to deploy our latest docker image using Helm upgrade, it was not updating the release with the updated new image the <strong>dev-latest</strong> tag.</p>\n<p><strong>Actual Behavior:</strong><br>\nhelm upgrade isn't updating the release with the latest image.</p>\n<p><strong>Expected Behavior:</strong><br>\nhelm upgrade in the CD workflow should update the&nbsp;dev/qa release.</p>\n<p><strong>Solution:</strong><br>\nHelm needs to change in the deployment object, so we're adding a new label e.g. date: "{{ now | unixEpoch }}" under <strong>labels</strong>. Every time there is a new date helm detects a change in the deployment object and will pull the image every time.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	1	3483	2024-11-21	2024-11-21	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	29393e98671f-f433-141c-87c17da1ce69	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Rana Nouman	Hammad Hassan	0f89d429673f-ef36-e2a1-70a5b6432cd4	33f2e1c062c6-81f4-bcaf-6a1b411477d8	2024-11-21 13:07:38	agaia	0	0
5e1b6214687e-dfe1-bba4-c7defc300863	Issue Planning using LLM	2025-07-21 15:48:46	2025-08-22 15:04:47	0	<p>The <strong>Issue Planning</strong> feature should present the list of generated tasks and test cases in a structured format, tabular. Each task item must include a <strong>subject</strong>, <strong>description</strong>, and an optional <strong>dependency</strong> field. Users should have the ability to <strong>edit fields inline</strong> and <strong>remove any unwanted tasks or tests</strong> from the list. However, there should be <strong>no option to manually add new items</strong> in this interface; any additional tasks or tests must be created later using the standard issue creation workflow. Once the list is finalized, the user can click <strong>“Accept and Create”</strong>, which will result in the selected items being created as <strong>child issues</strong> linked to the current parent issue. Tasks will be created as <strong>standard issues</strong>, while test cases will be created as <strong>QA-type issues</strong> or flagged accordingly. All created issues should maintain a <strong>direct association with the parent</strong> to preserve traceability.</p>\n	1	1	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3658	2025-07-24	2025-07-21	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	973277366887-2e85-fee8-668818bf5a45	\N	ae4ca1725acb-1902-6b9c-1a5d19be2920	Hammad Hassan	Rana Nouman	97edc295687e-dfe1-bba4-ac3d79bf0aac	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2025-08-22 15:04:16	aprom	0	0
