a75312f26250-83ce-4370-6b79e8c613ae	API response issue	2022-04-08 10:17:11	2022-04-08 10:17:11	0	<p>If we not specify id field when getting some specific fields from an api e.g&nbsp;<span class="colour" style="color: rgb(33, 33, 33);" data-tomark-pass=""><a href="http://api.projects4.me/api/v1/project?fields=name,status">http://api.projects4.me/api/v1/project?fields=name,status</a></span>&nbsp;<span class="colour" style="color: rgb(102, 102, 102);" data-tomark-pass=""><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(33, 33, 33);" data-tomark-pass="">then our backend doesn't give required data. For example in the previous call we are getting list of projects, by default 20(pagination). So as we have not specify&nbsp;<strong>id</strong> in fields so our backend doesn't prepare result on behalf of the id's. That's why we'll get only 1 project in this call.</span></span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(102, 102, 102);" data-tomark-pass=""><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(33, 33, 33);" data-tomark-pass=""><strong>Solution</strong>&nbsp;to the problem is that if user hasn't specify&nbsp;<strong>id,</strong>&nbsp;then we should have to&nbsp;</span></span><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(32, 33, 36);" data-tomark-pass="">Programmatically</span>&nbsp;add id of that resource to the query in order to select that resource with its id so that our backend can prepare the result set wrt to id's.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3205	2022-04-08	2022-04-07	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	3c930c88623c-093c-a755-d7059252f958	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	33f2e1c062c6-81f4-bcaf-6a1b411477d8	\N	agaia	0	0
