bd9f258469b4-e6de-c875-fd9e77d59bf5	Investigate browser title breaking issue from external links	2026-03-13 12:49:01	2026-03-16 12:22:31	0	Analyze and identify the root cause of why browser titles break when users navigate to the app from external sources. Document the current title handling mechanism in EmberJS routes and identify where the title setting logic fails during external navigation. This includes examining route transitions, application initialization, and any async data loading that might affect title setting.\n<hr>\n<div>\n<strong>Test Cases (1):</strong>\n</div>\n\n<div>\n<strong>Scenario:</strong> <span>External link navigation analysis</span>\n</div>\n<div><strong>Test Case:</strong> <pre class="issue-plan-test-case-pre">Given the application is not loaded\nWhen I navigate to various app routes from external sources (email, bookmarks, direct URLs)\nThen I should document all scenarios where the title breaks\nAnd identify the specific failure points in the code</pre></div>\n<br>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3839	2026-03-13	2026-03-13	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	1c5ba55169a5-edd6-cd30-52e2cd27f10c	e311cf8869b4-b202-c311-fa4e52f2e218	ae5a3c325acb-1902-6b9c-e93d4161f6f9	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	f9cca1f969b7-263a-1bd4-54d23a2008c7	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-03-16 12:22:31	aprom	0	0
bdb6b1d465dc-1360-8ec3-95d85e71d137	Only update the permission flag which is updated, not all	2024-02-26 09:28:29	2024-02-26 10:01:44	0	<p>If we update only one flag of permission e.g. readF then according to our current solution it is updating all of the flags which is not a good solution.</p>\n<p>Let's say if the permission is not yet created on the first then all of its flags are set to "notset". When we set read flag's value to <strong>none</strong> and make a <strong>patch/post</strong> call, then the remaining flags also become part of the payload as empty values e.g. searchF:"" and the server returns 0 against these flags which makes all of the flags set to none, which is not desired.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3395	2024-02-26	2024-02-26	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	4e31873365d2-9931-48d2-91fe572f2988	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	23a4749162c6-89cf-bcaf-50ebb8c0446b	2024-02-26 10:01:44	aprom	0	0
bde3968467e6-b66c-8877-53f7ed107a45	Field name is not a part of response when specfic fields are requested	2025-03-28 08:54:21	2025-03-28 09:35:14	0	<p>When the user requests some specific related fields without giving us an alias, the data is returning back as response but without the name of the field.\\</p>\n<p><strong>Acutal Behavior:</strong><br>\n/api/v1/project?rels=members&amp;fields=members.name</p>\n<p>"data": [<br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp;'included: [<br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp;{<br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;attributes: {<br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>" ": "nouman"</strong><br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;}<br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp;}<br>\n]</p>\n<p><strong>Expected Behavior:</strong><br>\n/api/v1/project?rels=members&amp;fields=members.name</p>\n<p>"data": [<br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp;'included: [<br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp;{<br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;attributes: {<br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>"name": "nouman"</strong><br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;}<br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp;}<br>\n]</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3578	2025-03-28	2025-03-27	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	c7087d0967da-2290-3820-a361b66b5f6a	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	33f2e1c062c6-81f4-bcaf-6a1b411477d8	2025-03-28 09:35:34	agaia	0	0
