bd3193f66ace-c075-2b63-3c1b73d15417	Show '-' instead of 'Invalid date' for empty dates	2026-10-13 15:56:45	2026-10-19 15:11:42	0	<p><strong>What happens:</strong> when an issue has no end date, the UI shows the text <em>Invalid date</em> (issue list End Date column, issue detail Duration, e.g. "13th Oct '26 - Invalid date").</p>\n<p><strong>Expected:</strong> show <code>-</code> for an empty date, consistent with other empty values (e.g. Parent shows <code>-</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>Where:</strong> dates are formatted with <code>moment-format</code> (e.g. <code>components/issue/issue-details.hbs:154</code>) and the <code>format-date</code> helper (<code>templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs</code>, widgets, user management). Fix it centrally so an empty date renders <code>-</code> everywhere, rather than patching each template.</p>\n<p>Seen on issue #4014 before its end date was set.</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	4016	2026-10-20	2026-10-13	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	b0c978e86ad5-555c-45b9-2e35aabb7d42	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-19 15:11:42	aprom	0	0
069897b36ae0-1cbd-b9b8-d3641bf04495	p4m db migrate runs in the shared gaia-dev container even when it mounts another checkout	2026-10-27 12:07:34	2026-10-27 14:16:28	0	<p><code>p4m db migrate</code> does <code>docker exec gaia-dev php cli.php migration migrate</code>. The shared <code>gaia-dev</code> container may mount another checkout (here: <code>Projects4Me/gaia</code> on an older <code>dev</code>), so the migration runs that checkout's metadata against <code>pr4m</code>. Phalcon's <code>morphTable</code> then drops every column the older metadata doesn't know.</p>\n<p><b>What happened (2026-10-27, agaia-4027 review round):</b> running <code>p4m db migrate</code> from the Pr4M workspace dropped <code>users.type</code>, <code>system_notifications.relatedTo/relatedId</code> and the other columns added to the metadata after gaia #189 (Issuestatus, Upload); the api-tester seed then failed on the missing column. The schema was restored by running the migration from the workspace checkout in a throwaway container (<code>docker run --rm --network backend -v &lt;workspace&gt;/gaia:/var/www/html -v gaia_vendor:/var/www/html/vendor</code> with gaia-dev's DB env), but the data in the dropped columns is gone.</p>\n<p><b>Fix:</b> make <code>p4m db migrate</code> behave like <code>p4m test</code> (see <code>installer/testenv.py</code>): if the shared container serves this workspace's checkout, use it; otherwise run the migration in a throwaway container started from the same image, env and network with the workspace's <code>gaia</code> mounted. Print which checkout is being migrated. Same check for <code>p4m db reset</code>, which calls <code>migrate()</code>. Add an installer unit test for the container choice.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4150	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0df54476ad7-40