68cf36006af7-3fb3-e127-98c57fd5181a	Escape user values in toast messages (htmlSafe around intl.t renders names as HTML)	2026-11-14 01:03:36	2026-11-14 01:44:38	0	<p>About 62 calls in 25 files build a toast with <code>htmlSafe(this.intl.t(key, { name: record.name }))</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The intl service escapes placeholder values only when it is called with <code>htmlSafe: true</code> (<code>app/services/intl.js</code>, around line 313).</li>\n<li>Messenger renders the message as HTML: <code>escapeText</code> defaults to false.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>So a member, agent, saved-search, project or issue name that contains HTML is rendered as HTML in the toast. That is stored XSS. It was found by reading the code and has not been confirmed with a payload yet.</p>\n<p>Affected files include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>components: <code>issue/assignee-select</code>, <code>issue/issue-details</code>, <code>saved-search/compact-bar</code>;</li>\n<li>controllers: <code>app/agent/create</code>, <code>project/board</code>, <code>conversation</code>, <code>gantt</code>, <code>idea</code>, <code>idea/create</code>, <code>project/index</code>, <code>issue/create</code>, <code>issue/edit</code>, <code>issue/index</code>, <code>wiki/create</code>, <code>wiki/edit</code>, <code>wiki/page</code>, <code>projects/create</code>, <code>projects/index</code>, <code>role</code>, <code>role/page</code>, <code>settings/issue-statuses</code>, <code>settings/issue-types</code>, <code>user/create</code>, <code>user/page</code>, <code>prometheus/list</code>;</li>\n<li>also check <code>app/services/notifications.js</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Do</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Write the failing tests first: a record whose name is <code>&lt;img src=x onerror=...&gt;</code> must appear as text in the toast, not as an element.</li>\n<li>Pass <code>htmlSafe: true</code> to <code>intl.t</code> so the values are escaped and the translation's own markup is kept. Use <code>postToast</code> (<code>app/utils/ui/post-toast.js</code>) where the message has no markup.</li>\n<li>Find every call with a multi-line search. A single-line grep misses the calls where <code>htmlSafe(</code> and <code>intl.t(</code> are on different lines.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Do not run this at the same time as the native-class / <code>{{mut}}</code> issue: both touch controllers.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4555	2026-11-21	2026-11-14	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	7894b8076af7-ed76-b152-444671a94f6a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-14 01:44:38	aprom	0	0
38b9e8d86aef-978f-b5d5-53e51c51ddab	Task Board: search without the Milestone field (view metadata with extends and exclude)	2026-11-07 21:33:44	2026-11-08 00:13:03	0	<p>On the Task Board the milestone is chosen with the milestone tabs, so offering Milestone in the search makes no sense. The board uses the Issue search fields (<code>views.Issue.search</code>) today. Under the metadata-driven list-view architecture (<code>docs/architecture/metadata-views/architecture.md</code>), a view that needs different search fields declares its own search metadata instead of hard-coding exceptions.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>: add <code>views.TaskBoard.search = { extends: 'Issue', exclude: ['issuemilestone.name'] }</code>.</li><li><code>app/services/query-schema.js</code>: support <code>extends</code> (start from the named module's search metadata: module, text field, fields, values) and <code>exclude</code> (field ids removed from it). Unknown <code>extends</code> or excluded ids throw a clear error in development and tests.</li><li>An excluded field isn't suggested and isn't in the builder. If it is typed, or comes in through <code>@query</code> or a saved search, parsing gives a clear error ("Milestone can't be searched here. Use the milestone tabs."), and nothing is applied. Add the error code to the parser and schema helpers (<code>app/utils/query/schema.js</code>, <code>parse.js</code>) and its message to <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; the message can name the view's reason through an optional <code>excludeReason</code> translation key in the metadata.</li><li>Board route: load <code>query-schema</code> <code>load('TaskBoard', {projectId})</code> instead of <code>load('Issue', …)</code>.</li><li>Docs: add a section on <code>extends</code> and <code>exclude</code> to <code>docs/architecture/metadata-views/architecture.md</code>, with this case as the example.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests: <code>extends</code>/<code>exclude</code> in the service, the error for an excluded field typed, loaded through <code>@query</code> and loaded through a saved search, and unknown names throwing.</li><li>A board acceptance scenario: typing <code>milestone</code> suggests no Milestone field, and <code>milestone:v0.4.8</code> shows the error and sends nothing.</li><li>The Issue list, Gantt and idea list still offer Milestone.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> excluding fields in other views, the board layout fixes.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4338</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4342	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	b12354c96aef-978f-b5d5-e382278b8c49	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 00:13:03	aprom	0	0
53bf4f666af2-3028-5ed1-882966d6efe4	External Request: Conversation rooms: record a few activities (started, edited, issue linked)	2026-11-09 23:20:51	2026-11-10 00:00:24	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Prometheus (idea "Threads :: UI Update ", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p><strong>Request from A Prometheus.</strong> The new Threads page shows a small Activity box per thread. Gaia records activities for issues (<code>IssueactivitiesComponent</code>, generic Activity with <code>relatedTo</code>), but <code>ConversationroomController</code> only uses <code>Events\\\\ConversationLiveEvents</code>, so threads have no history. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract:</strong></p><ul><li>A component like <code>IssueactivitiesComponent</code>, added to <code>ConversationroomController</code> <code>$uses</code>, writing Activity rows with <code>relatedTo</code> = <code>conversationroom</code> and <code>relatedId</code> = room id for a <strong>limited</strong> set: thread created; subject edited; description edited; linked issue set, changed or cleared (with the issue key). No rows for comments or votes (they are visible in the thread).</li><li>Readable through the existing activity resource with project scoping like the room.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> api-tester cases for each activity type and that comments/votes write none. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> backfilling existing rooms.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4443	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	5312b0586af2-3028-5ed1-a9e31e119edc	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	3b06c5756af2-dd7c-5ed1-a4232d03e2fd	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 00:00:24	agaia	0	1
9f2796666afc-30ee-311d-7a2868fb7296	Events: publish user.access.changed when a user's role is added or removed	2026-11-17 15:37:03	2026-11-18 13:59:46	0	<p><code>user.access.changed</code> (scope <code>user:&lt;userId&gt;</code>, ids only) tells Hermes and Prometheus to re-check a user's access. Today it fires on account status and membership changes, but not on role changes, which also change what the user may do.</p><ul><li>New live-events component for <code>UserroleController</code>, following <code>MembershipLiveEventsComponent</code>: on create, delete and an update that changes <code>userId</code> or <code>roleId</code>, call <code>UserAccessLiveEventsComponent::publishAccessChanged</code> for the affected user (both users when <code>userId</code> changes). Add it to the controller's <code>$uses</code>.</li><li>Update the user.access.changed entry in <code>app/metadata/events.php</code> (description, consumers).</li><li>Tests in the live-events test and api-tester cases with <code>hermes.expect</code>, as for membership.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> adding or removing a role publishes one user.access.changed to that user; a Hermes outage doesn't fail the write.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> permission changes on a role itself (affects many users).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4640</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4644	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7b8e27936afc-30ee-311d-92e7628909b7	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	3048e1256afd-715d-1e86-ed22e5db4c69	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 13:59:46	agaia	0	0
bd58f0c06adf-8154-4904-ac95e983c0b8	ai cost: token and turn accounting per session and issue from Claude Code transcripts, with a baseline	2026-10-26 08:05:17	2026-10-26 08:49:52	0	<p><b>Phase 0 of the "Agentic Improve" programme (measure first).</b> Analysis of 117 workspace transcripts (Oct 19–24) showed Gaia sessions cost ~1.6× Prometheus in output tokens and ~2.4× in cache reads, driven by more turns and repeated reading of <code>core/</code> and <code>tools/api-tester</code> internals. Nothing later in the programme can be judged without this measurement.</p>\n<p><b>What</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>New command <code>dev-tools/ai/ai cost [--repo R] [--issue N] [--since DATE]</code> that reads the Claude Code transcripts under <code>~/.claude/projects/&lt;workspace&gt;/*.jsonl</code> (assistant <code>message.usage</code>, tool_use inputs, tool_result sizes).</li>\n<li>Per session and per issue (issue = branch/issue number found in the transcript): output tokens, input tokens, cache-creation and cache-read tokens, turns, peak context (largest cache_read + input on one call), chars of tool results per tool and per Bash category (tests, docker, git, ai-tool, file reads…), and files read in two or more sessions.</li>\n<li>Per repo rollup (classify a session by the Pr4M/&lt;repo&gt; paths it touches) and a rolling median per repo.</li>\n<li><code>ai ship</code> posts a one-line cost summary (tokens, turns, peak context) as a comment on the issue.</li>\n<li>Baseline: run it once and commit the report to <code>dev-tools/ai/state/cost-baseline.md</code>. Reference numbers from the analysis: Gaia since Oct 22 ≈ 28k output / 46 turns / 2.4M cache reads per session; Prometheus ≈ 21.5k / 33 / 1.25M.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Checks:</b> unittest on a fixture transcript; text output terse, <code>--json</code> for tooling.</p>\n<p><b>Depends on:</b> nothing. <b>Exit:</b> baseline committed; <code>ai cost --repo gaia</code> reproduces the analysis figures within rounding.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4126	2026-11-02	2026-10-26	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	8fe2ae046adf-8154-4904-8f5112ed5746	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	6bae6d556adf-dc42-f36f-5bbfffd26d6d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-26 08:49:52	adt	0	0
c29c25956adf-8154-4904-f36b4e008bdc	Bundle catalog: recurring change bundles mined from PRs #138–#198, review threads and Talos transcripts	2026-10-26 08:05:22	2026-10-26 09:17:17	0	<p><b>Phase 1 of "Agentic Improve".</b> The file sets of the last 31 substantive Gaia PRs show six recurring bundles; this issue turns that into the catalog the scaffolders and generated docs are built from.</p>\n<p><b>Starting point (from the Oct 24 analysis of PRs #178–#198):</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>api-tester cases (<code>client.json</code>/<code>acl.json</code>) + <code>harness/prepare-test-db.sh</code> + <code>fixtures/default.json</code> + README + new <code>Asserter.php</code> assertions — in 17 of 21 PRs</li>\n<li>New resource: metadata + 22-line model + 21-line controller + <code>routes.php</code> + <code>models.php</code> + <code>backend.json</code> regen + <code>routes.v1.json</code> + fixtures + harness + acl cases (#178, #193, #196; #159 by hand)</li>\n<li>Custom controller action + route + acl case + client cases (#180, #181, #192, #198)</li>\n<li>Behaviour + unit test (#178, #193, #195, #196)</li>\n<li>Live-events component per resource + EventNames + ProjectIdResolver + test (#194, #173)</li>\n<li>Notification module edits (#197)</li>\n<li>Framework/core change (RestController, Acl, router) in 7 of 21 — templates must be derived from reference files, not static</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>What</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Read PRs #138–#198 (diffs and review threads: reviewer + CodeRabbit) and the Talos run transcripts; confirm or refine the bundles.</li>\n<li>Write <code>docs/dev/bundles.md</code>: for each bundle its exact file touchpoints in order, the golden reference files in the repo (e.g. <code>Idea*</code> for a resource, <code>ideaScreensBehavior</code> for a behaviour, <code>IdeaLiveEventsComponent</code> for events), the exemplar PR, and the checks learned from review comments and stuck agent turns (wrong fixture placeholder, missing acl case for a new permission, catalog drift…).</li>\n<li>Rank bundles by frequency × cost so the scaffolder issues are worked in payoff order.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Depends on:</b> nothing. <b>Exit:</b> catalog reviewed by Hammad; every bundle has a named exemplar PR and golden files.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4127	2026-11-02	2026-10-26	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	8d88c0836adf-8154-4904-0abe50edd8bc	\N	cbae55075acd-06d6-1141-3412c9cf4ece	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	87d75e636adf-1f1a-d6f3-de1cc6ffe1ed	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-26 09:17:17	agaia	0	0
1a5af2946ad9-497b-5f53-7a2bf149afe7	Issue statuses: save a status and its translated labels in one request	2026-10-22 11:44:26	2026-11-11 12:27:01	0	<p>Save an issue status and its translated labels in one request. Depends on #4095 (Translation model).</p>\n<h3>Scope</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Create and update of Issuestatus accept labels per locale with the status, e.g. <code>translations: {"en-us": "In Progress"}</code>, using Gaia's CRUD conventions (no custom actions). Labels are saved as Translation rows at <code>views.app.issue.lists.status.&lt;name&gt;</code> in the same transaction as the status; if either fails, nothing is saved.</li>\n<li>Validation:\n<ul>\n<li>the <code>en-us</code> label is required on create; other supported locales are optional;</li>\n<li>locales must be in the supported list;</li>\n<li>status value matches <code>^[a-z0-9_]+$</code> and is at most 30 characters. Labels have no 30-character limit.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li>The status value (<code>issue_statuses.name</code>) can't be changed after creation; an update that changes it is rejected. Decide whether the <code>rename_issue_status</code> trigger is still needed and record the decision on this issue.</li>\n<li>Deleting a status deletes its translations.</li>\n<li>Every label write clears the affected locale's cached translation file.</li>\n<li>Reading a status returns its labels.</li>\n<li>Statuses with the same value (a system status and its project copies, or the same custom value in two projects) share one label, since the path is keyed by value. Document this.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Tests</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Create with labels → status and Translation rows exist; the locale file is rebuilt with the new label.</li>\n<li>Missing <code>en-us</code> label, unsupported locale or invalid value → 4xx, nothing saved.</li>\n<li>A failed label write rolls back the status.</li>\n<li>Updating labels works; changing <code>name</code> is rejected.</li>\n<li>Deleting a status removes its translations.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: complex</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4097	2026-10-29	2026-10-22	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	030613686adb-807d-fa92-7edfe01974e1	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-26 13:34:23	agaia	0	0
a7eff7046afc-30ee-311d-42879ea3cd54	Mentions: model behavior that records user mentions in a record's text fields on every create and update	2026-11-17 15:37:11	2026-11-18 13:48:47	0	<p>Users are mentioned in comments, issue descriptions, thread descriptions and ideas. Prometheus' editor writes a mention as a link, <code>&lt;a class="badge" href="/app/user/&lt;userId&gt;"&gt;@Name&lt;/a&gt;</code>; markdown bodies (idea messages) would hold <code>[@Name](/app/user/&lt;userId&gt;)</code>. Gaia stores none of this today: the <code>Mention</code> resource (<code>app/metadata/model/Mention.php</code>: relatedTo, relatedId, userId, notified) is never written. This issue builds the capability; the next issues turn it on per model. It must catch <strong>every</strong> write path: REST create/update, collection PATCH, and saves outside controllers such as the workflow Set field action. So it is a model behavior, not a controller component.</p><ul><li><code>MentionParser</code> (domain, e.g. <code>core/libs/mentions/</code>): user ids from HTML anchors and markdown links whose target is <code>/app/user/&lt;id&gt;</code> (relative or absolute URL). Distinct, in order.</li><li>A behavior (e.g. <code>core/mvc/models/behaviors/mentionsBehavior.php</code>, listed in a model's metadata <code>behaviors</code> like <code>ideaScreensBehavior</code>) reading a new metadata key <code>'mentions' =&gt; ['fields' =&gt; [...]]</code>. After create, and after an update where one of those fields changed, it hands the record to a recorder.</li><li>Recorder: for each parsed user id, create a <code>Mention</code> row (relatedTo = the model's lowercase name, relatedId = record id, userId, createdUser = the actor) unless one exists for that record and user. Rows are append-only: removing a mention doesn't delete its row, and re-adding it doesn't create a new one, so nobody is notified twice. Skip the actor mentioning themselves, unknown or deleted users, and users who aren't members of the record's project (resolve the project with the existing <code>ProjectIdResolver</code> logic or an equivalent domain helper).</li><li>Add <code>projectId</code> to <code>Mention</code> (metadata + migration) so later consumers don't have to walk the record.</li><li>Fails safe: an error while recording mentions is logged and must not fail the user's save.</li><li>ADR (e.g. <code>docs/architecture/mentions/decisions.md</code>): behavior vs component, append-only rows, membership rule.</li><li>Tests: parser (HTML and markdown, absolute/relative, junk links), recorder (create, update adds only new users, self, non-member), behavior on a test model.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the behavior on a model, saving text with two mentions creates two rows; saving again creates none; editing in a third creates one.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> turning it on for real models, notifications and events (separate issues); the Mention resource's read ACL.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4645	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7b8e27936afc-30ee-311d-92e7628909b7	\N	cbb506d05acd-06d6-1141-68969b9fd562	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	6678c7866afc-7fa9-cd83-bcf3f0dea004	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 13:48:47	agaia	0	0
f8ba82626ae5-92fb-9f4e-aca66e967836	Agamemnon: never auto-merge changes to its own config, role or tools	2026-10-31 12:50:00	2026-10-31 13:45:37	0	<p>Agamemnon must not approve a PR that widens its own powers.</p><ul><li>The merge gate fails (as a new check, e.g. <code>self</code>) when the PR changes any protected path: talos/agents/agamemnon/**, Agamemnon's role prompt and premise config, the <code>aga</code> tool wrapper, talos/lib/orchestrator/**, ai/lib/mergegate.py. The paths live in one config list.</li><li>Such an issue goes to the owner with the reason.</li><li>Agamemnon may only <i>propose</i> a new tool: it creates an issue in its milestone describing the repeated gap; it never writes or installs tools itself. Document this in its role.</li></ul><p>Depends on: adt-4225</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4227	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	c36638756ae5-92fb-c743-0dd51d887bec	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	be23a5e76ae5-3157-5f17-e43662d3a8e1	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 13:45:37	adt	0	0
428fe4c66aef-978f-b5d5-752289ac6099	ezSearch: suggestion menu looks washed out	2026-11-07 21:33:54	2026-11-07 23:52:40	0	<p>Everywhere ezSearch is used, the suggestion menu is hard to read: item labels are light grey, and the highlighted row is light pink with white text. Cause: <code>app/styles/components/ez-search-bar.scss</code> ~l.71 sets <code>li.active &gt; a { background: $primaryColorLight; }</code> without a text colour, so Bootstrap's white text for active items lands on a light background, and the other rows use AdminLTE's grey <code>.dropdown-menu</code> link colour.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In <code>.ez-search-menu</code> (scoped, tokens only):<ul><li>Item labels <code>$darkColor</code>; the field id detail stays <code>$mediumColor</code>.</li><li>The active or hovered row gets a <code>$primaryColor</code> background with white label and detail text, matching the hover of the app's other dropdowns (<code>app/styles/components/dropdown.scss</code> ~l.44-49).</li><li>Section headers and the key hint stay muted but readable.</li><li>No opacity on the menu or its items.</li></ul></li><li>Check that the menu isn't inside an ancestor with reduced opacity (e.g. a disabled or loading state). Fix it at the source if so.</li><li>This applies to <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> (both layouts).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An integration test asserts that the active row's computed background and text colours are the crimson token and white, and that normal rows use the dark text colour.</li><li>Checked in the browser on the Issue list, the idea list, the Gantt and the Task Board.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> menu content and ranking.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 2</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4343	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-19