c7860c896adf-8154-4904-d152698a8449	gaia-dev core (1/2): data extractors for metadata, routes, models list, api-tester catalogs and fixtures; graph schema and export with drift check	2026-10-26 08:05:27	2026-10-26 10:43:52	0	<p><b>Phase 2 of "Agentic Improve": the one extraction core that scaffolders, generated docs and query commands all share.</b> This half needs no parser: <code>app/metadata/model/*.php</code> (<code>$models['X'] = array(...)</code> with fields, relationships, behaviors, acl), <code>core/config/routes.php</code> and <code>core/config/models.php</code> are plain PHP arrays, and the api-tester catalogs and fixtures are JSON.</p>\n<p><b>What</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>New tool <code>tools/gaia-dev/</code> (PHP, entry <code>bin/gaia-dev</code>), following the repo's layering: extractors (data source) → graph model (domain) → commands (presentation). One class per extractor.</li>\n<li>Extractors: metadata models (fields, relationships, behaviours, acl flags), routes (path, controller, action, type, method), models list, api-tester catalogs (<code>backend/client/acl/live/mail.json</code>: cases, endpoints, assertions used, profiles used, fixture placeholders), <code>fixtures/default.json</code>.</li>\n<li>Graph schema (<b>open design decision — settle it here and document it in <code>tools/gaia-dev/README.md</code></b>): node types model, field, relationship, behaviour, route, controller, action, component, permission, profile, case, assertion; typed edges between them. Keep it extensible for the code extractors in the follow-up issue.</li>\n<li><code>gaia-dev graph export</code> writes <code>docs/generated/graph.json</code> (committed); <code>gaia-dev graph export --check</code> exits non-zero when the committed graph is stale, and CI runs it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Checks:</b> PHPUnit per extractor under <code>tests/tools/gaia-dev/</code> (each file passes alone); CI drift job. No new runtime dependencies in this half.</p>\n<p><b>Depends on:</b> nothing (the bundle catalog only sharpens priorities). <b>Exit:</b> <code>graph.json</code> committed, drift check green, every model/route/case in the repo present in the graph.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4128	2026-11-09	2026-10-26	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	8d88c0836adf-8154-4904-0abe50edd8bc	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	e97323166adf-6651-eb25-9e74144690d5	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-26 10:43:52	agaia	0	0
152cb7356aef-978f-b5d5-05f04b717bd3	Task Board: milestone tabs no longer wrap since the inline search	2026-11-07 21:33:09	2026-11-07 21:55:45	0	<p>Since aprom-4338 the milestone tabs sit in a single row that scrolls sideways, and overflowing tabs are cut off. That came from 4338's own description, which was wrong: the engineer only asked for the search to be inline. The tabs must behave as before and wrap onto the next row when they don't fit, while the search stays inline at the top right.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Restore the pre-4338 layout model in <code>app/styles/modules/board.scss</code> (<code>.board .board-container .nav-tabs-custom</code>, ~l.13-62 before 4338):<ul><li><code>.nav-tabs-custom</code> is <code>position: relative</code>.</li><li><code>.milestone-tabs</code> is an <code>inline-block</code>, now 70% wide, with its tabs wrapping normally (no <code>flex-wrap: nowrap</code>, no <code>overflow-x</code>, no scroll arrows).</li><li><code>.milestone-filters</code> is <code>position: absolute</code> at the top right, now 30% wide, holding <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact @linear={{true}}&gt;</code> at full width.</li></ul>Remove the flex row and tab-strip scroll rules that 4338 added (compare <code>board.scss</code> and <code>components/app-ui/task-board.hbs</code> with <code>dev</code> before 4338).</li><li>The suggestion menu and the Saved menu still open over the content below.</li><li>Below 768px the search goes under the tabs at full width.</li><li>Tabs keep working as drop targets (<code>.drop-zone-area</code>), including on a second row.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>With eight milestone tabs, the tabs wrap onto a second row, all are fully visible and clickable, and the search stays at the top right on the first row at 30% width.</li><li>An acceptance or integration check that the search's top equals the first tab's top, and that no tab is clipped.</li><li>Checked in the browser with two and eight tabs, and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> lane scrolling and the quick preview (separate issues), search fields.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4338</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> board-linear.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4339	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	5b82a5686aef-978f-b5d5-05613794f8c1	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 21:55:45	aprom	0	0
134ecc926af2-3028-5ed1-1b70243103f2	Threads: comment counts and vote tallies on list rows (separate Gaia calls for now)	2026-11-09 23:19:47	2026-11-10 00:49:11	0	<p>Thread rows should show how active a thread is. Gaia has no count field yet (requested separately), so for now load them with separate calls per row, as the current page already does for comments (<code>fetchAndLinkComments</code>).</p><ul><li>A small service or util (single responsibility: counts for a set of room ids) that, for each row of the loaded page, queries the room's comments with minimal fields (<code>createdUser</code>, comment text) and returns <code>{commentCount, agreeCount, disagreeCount}</code> (vote rooms: comments with text "I agree" / "I disagree"); runs in parallel, results dropped when the page changes (newest wins), rows render while counts load.</li><li>Rows: discussion meta line gets <code>fa-comment-o N</code>; vote rows' secondary line = <code>N agree · M disagree</code>.</li><li>Live: Hermes comment created/deleted for a listed thread updates its count.</li><li>Keep the count source behind one function so a later issue can swap it for one Gaia call per page.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit test for the counts helper (stale page dropped, agree/disagree split) and an acceptance step showing counts for both room types. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> Gaia changes.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4437</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4438	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	96055cb36af2-682a-504e-7dd8d7cbb0d1	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 00:49:11	aprom	0	0
3adb66646ae5-a3a8-9f4e-5683fa7efab6	Agamemnon: the guarded aga tool, the action journal and undo	2026-10-31 12:51:06	2026-10-31 14:11:37	0	<p>One wrapper, <code>dev-tools/agamemnon/aga &lt;verb&gt;</code>, is the only way the Agamemnon AI session acts. Raw git, gh and Gaia write tools are denied in its session. Each verb checks its own preconditions (the incident type's tiers from the premise, the issue in an aga- milestone, the caps) and refuses otherwise, so the model cannot bypass a guard.</p><ul><li><b>Tier 0, read:</b> status, logs, diff, mergecheck, workspace state, in-flight overlap.</li><li><b>Tier 1, reversible and private:</b> backup (commit the workspace state to <code>refs/agamemnon/backup/&lt;issue&gt;/&lt;time&gt;</code> and push it; never <code>git stash</code>), restore, retry, wait-for (another issue or a free test slot), hold-until-tomorrow, send to Odysseus with notes, rerun CI.</li><li><b>Tier 2, reversible and visible:</b> update-branch (merge, never rebase), push a resolved merge, merge PR (only through the existing merge gate).</li><li><b>Tier 3 has no verb:</b> force push, deleting branches or workspaces with unpushed work, closing PRs, writing main/dev, changing config or limits.</li></ul><p><b>Journal:</b> a talos.db table, one row per action: incident, issue, verb, arguments, state before and after (SHAs, statuses, assignees), the reasoning given, and an undo command. <code>talos agamemnon log [--since]</code> and <code>talos agamemnon undo &lt;id&gt;</code> / <code>undo --since &lt;time&gt;</code> (undo in reverse order, refusing where the state has since moved).</p><p>Depends on: adt-4228</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4230	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	c36638756ae5-92fb-c743-0dd51d887bec	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	12cf72536ae5-e316-fd64-2108341f43fd	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 14:11:37	adt	0	0
86836fa06af7-3fb3-e127-7f8b7628e23f	Upgrade lint tooling and run lint in CI with a recorded baseline	2026-11-14 01:04:06	2026-11-14 18:33:13	0	<p>The lint tooling is out of date:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>eslint 7 with the deprecated <code>babel-eslint</code> parser;</li>\n<li><code>eslint-plugin-ember</code> 10;</li>\n<li><code>ember-template-lint</code> 3.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code> does not run lint at all. Nothing stops classic components, observers, jQuery, <code>this.get</code>/<code>set</code>, <code>{{mut}}</code> or implicit <code>this</code> from coming back.</p>\n<h4>Do</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Upgrade:\n<ul>\n<li>eslint to a current version (flat config) with <code>@babel/eslint-parser</code>;</li>\n<li><code>eslint-plugin-ember</code>, <code>eslint-plugin-qunit</code>, <code>prettier</code> and <code>ember-template-lint</code> to versions that support Ember 6.12.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li>Enable the recommended rule sets, including the Octane rules: no-classic-components, no-observers, no-jquery, no-get, no-mut, no-implicit-this, require-tagless-components and similar.</li>\n<li>Record today's violations as a baseline: the template-lint todo list and an eslint baseline or per-file overrides. CI then fails only on new violations.</li>\n<li>Add <code>lint:js</code> and <code>lint:hbs</code> steps to CI.</li>\n<li>Update the run-tests and CLAUDE.md lint commands if they change.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Do this after 4557 (dead code removal), so the baseline doesn't record code that is about to be deleted. Do it before the classic-component, router-reopen and native-class issues, so their fixes leave the baseline and stay fixed.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4558	2026-11-21	2026-11-14	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	f0db55376af7-fb0d-5