4fa467396af2-cc20-4467-ae7a12d3e93d	Prometheus full test suite is killed for out of memory about every second run (4.5g test container limit)	2026-11-10 08:39:43	2026-11-10 10:38:43	0	<p>Found while shipping aprom-4439. The full Prometheus suite (<code>ai test prometheus</code>, about 1290 tests) is often killed by the test container's memory limit, so a ship needs several attempts.</p><p><strong>Observed on 2026-11-10</strong> (checkout <code>.runs/issue-4439/prometheus</code>, one run at a time, no other Prometheus test container running):</p><ul><li>7 full runs: 4 killed for out of memory (exit 137), 3 completed (1289, 1293 and 1293 passed, 0 failed).</li><li>Message: <code>killed: out of memory (container limit 4.5g; raise PROMETHEUS_TEST_MEMORY in p4m.env if the suite has grown). Not a test failure: run it again</code>.</li><li>The kill comes partway through the run: the last one stopped after about 135 tests. Targeted runs (<code>--filter conversation</code>, 54 tests) never hit it.</li><li>Docker has 19.5 GiB; <code>prometheus-dev</code> holds about 2.4 GiB of it.</li></ul><p><strong>Likely cause:</strong> the limit was set when the test containers were tuned for the most parallel runs. <code>dev-tools/installer/testenv.py</code> has <code>PROMETHEUS_MEMORY = "4.5g"</code> and <code>PROMETHEUS_JOBS = 4</code>, with the note "with JOBS=4 a cold full suite peaks at ~3.5 GiB". The suite has grown since, and the page cache counts toward the limit, so the headroom is gone. This is not confirmed by measurement yet.</p><p><strong>To do:</strong></p><ul><li>Measure the peak memory of a cold and a warm full run today (build, Chrome, page cache) and see what grows through the run.</li><li>Decide between raising the default limit, lowering what the run uses (JOBS, Chrome flags, splitting the suite), or sizing the limit from the number of parallel runs that are actually active.</li><li>Keep parallel Talos runs safe: the limit exists so one runaway container cannot take down Docker's VM.</li><li>Update the "peaks at ~3.5 GiB" note in <code>testenv.py</code> with the new figures.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> ten full runs in a row complete without an out-of-memory kill, with two runs in parallel also completing.</p><p><strong>Where:</strong> the change is in <code>dev-tools</code> (<code>installer/testenv.py</code>, <code>installer/p4m.py</code>, <code>ai/lib/tests.py</code>), not in the Prometheus repo. Logged in this milestone because it blocks shipping its issues.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4450	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	2f581f686af2-04be-6bff-078f7f0498c8	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 10:38:43	aprom	0	0
