f26cb4066adf-8154-4904-c64029d43862	ai doctor gaia (pre-flight in ai start), ai test --explain [case] and ai test --case [id]	2026-10-26 08:06:10	2026-10-26 17:24:02	0	<p><b>Phase 6 of "Agentic Improve" (independent part): cut turns in the Gaia test loop.</b> Transcripts show test-environment wrangling and log reading as repeated multi-turn detours; every turn re-sends the whole context.</p>\n<p><b>What</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>ai doctor gaia</code>, run automatically by <code>ai start</code> for Gaia issues: checks that the test container mounts this checkout (or that the throwaway container path works), CRLF is fixed on harness scripts, <code>pr4m_test</code> is seeded and current, <code>backend.json</code> regenerates cleanly (no drift), the baseline for the merge-base exists, and the <code>odysseus</code> remote is reachable. Each failing check prints the exact fix command. Terse output; <code>--json</code>.</li>\n<li><code>ai test gaia --explain &lt;case-id&gt;</code>: reads the saved api-tester log in <code>dev-tools/ai/state/</code> and prints expected vs actual for one failed case in compact form (status, failing assertion, the differing fields), so the next turn is a fix, not a log read.</li>\n<li><code>ai test gaia --case &lt;id&gt;</code>: run a single api-tester case against the already-seeded test DB without re-seeding, if the harness permits it (document the constraint if it doesn't). <code>--changed</code> stays the middle loop; the full run stays mandatory at <code>ai ship</code>.</li>\n<li>Update the <code>run-tests</code> and <code>start-issue</code> skills to mention the three commands in one line each.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Checks:</b> unittest for each doctor check against a fake environment; unittest for <code>--explain</code> on a fixture log.</p>\n<p><b>Depends on:</b> nothing. <b>Exit:</b> a broken environment is reported with its fix in one call; a failed case is explained in one call.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef38