770a51856adf-7ec8-653d-ae2890378906	ai test gaia: fits the agent's 10-min window — background runs, fingerprint at start, orphan-proof pr4m_test lock, retry bash 0xC0000142	2026-10-26 21:39:03	2026-10-26 22:01:00	0	<p><b>Problem.</b> This blocked agaia-4135. A full <code>ai test gaia</code> takes about 10 minutes: measured 2026-10-27, phpunit ~5 s, api 9.5 min including a ~1 min seed (backend 154, acl 112, client 207 cases). A baseline re-run on <code>origin/dev</code> adds about 16 minutes more (01:53→02:09). That happens whenever a failure isn't already recorded for the current merge-base. Claude Code caps a foreground Bash call at 600000 ms, so the run times out, and the timeout cascades:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>On Windows, killing the Bash call doesn't kill the <code>p4m</code> Python child. The orphan keeps refreshing the <code>dev-tools/.p4m/pr4m_test.lock</code> heartbeat, so <code>dblock</code> never treats it as stale.</li>\n<li>The retry prints <code>waiting for another pr4m_test user to finish</code> and blocks for up to 3600 s. Observed: 13 minutes.</li>\n<li>When it finally got the lock, starting Git Bash for <code>prepare-test-db.sh</code> failed with exit <code>3221225794</code> (0xC0000142, STATUS_DLL_INIT_FAILED). That is intermittent; the next run seeded fine.</li>\n<li>The baseline's throwaway container (<code>p4m-test-gaia-test-8b10322f</code>) was left running despite the <code>finally: p4m test clean</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Separately, <code>results.record()</code> takes the tree fingerprint when the run <i>ends</i>. The test container bind-mounts the live checkout, so an edit made during a background run gets stamped as PASS, and <code>ai ship</code> accepts it.</p>\n<p><b>What</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Agent instructions:</b> <code>.claude/agents/test-runner.md</code> (and the run-tests / ship-issue skills, plus Talos prompts if they run the suite): run the full <code>ai test gaia</code> with <code>run_in_background</code>, not a 600000 ms foreground timeout. Replace "1-4 minutes" with the measured times. Use <code>--changed</code> while iterating. Don't edit the repo while a full run is in flight.</li>\n<li><b>Fingerprint at start:</b> <code>cmd_test</code> takes <code>tree_fingerprint(repo)</code> before the suites run. If the tree differs at the end, record the run as not trustworthy (<code>ok: false</code> or a <code>stale</code> flag) and say "tree changed during the run; re-run". <code>ai ship</code> then refuses it.</li>\n<li><b>Orphan-proof lock (dblock):</b> the lock already stores the holder PID. When waiting, if that PID is not alive, take the lock over regardless of heartbeat age. The on-wait message names the PID and its command line, so a user can kill it.</li>\n<li><b>Kill the tree:</b> on KeyboardInterrupt/termination, <code>ai test</code> / <code>p4m test api</code> terminate their child process tree (and the in-container runner, as adt-4081 did for ember), so a killed run releases the lock.</li>\n<li><b>Retry bash spawn:</b> in <code>prepare_test_db</code>, retry the Git Bash launch up to 2 times when the exit code is 0xC0000142 (3221225794 / -1073741502), logging the retry.</li>\n<li><b>Baseline cleanup:</b> find out why <code>p4m test clean --src &lt;baseline worktree&gt;</code> left the container running, and fix it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Checks:</b> unittest for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>dblock taking over a lock whose PID is dead but whose heartbeat is fresh;</li>\n<li>fingerprint mismatch yielding a non-shippable result;</li>\n<li>the 0xC0000142 retry (mock <code>run</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Manual: start <code>ai test gaia</code>, kill the parent shell, and confirm the next run doesn't wait on the lock.</p>\n<p><b>Depends on:</b> nothing. Related: the ai.cmd wrapper issue (separate), and the speed-up investigation that follows.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4143	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	8fe2ae046adf-8154-4904-8f5112ed5746	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	f2b511a16adf-daa6-0f35-9a095c520543	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-26 22:01:00	adt	0	0
720897336aef-b8ee-711b-33cf93a80d78	Task Board: lane headers show above the ezSearch suggestion menu	2026-11-08 00:25:22	2026-11-08 00:48:55	0	<p>On the Task Board the lane headers draw over ezSearch's suggestion menu, so the menu is hidden behind them. The lane headers have <code>z-index: 999</code> (<code>.board .lane .box-header</code>, <code>app/styles/modules/board.scss</code> ~l.81-86). The menu has <code>z-index: 1000</code> (<code>.ez-search-menu</code>, <code>app/styles/components/ez-search-bar.scss</code> ~l.56-64), so one of its ancestors most likely creates a stacking context below the lanes: the board's absolutely positioned <code>.milestone-filters</code> slot (aprom-4339), or the compact search's input group (Bootstrap sets <code>position: relative</code> and small z-indexes there).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Find the ancestor that traps the menu (browser devtools: stacking context of <code>.ez-search-menu</code>) and fix it there:<ul><li>The board's search slot (<code>.board .milestone-filters</code>) gets its own <code>z-index</code> above 999, so everything inside it (suggestion menu, Saved menu, Filter badge menu) stacks above the lanes.</li><li>Inside ezSearch, no wrapper sets a z-index lower than the menu's.</li></ul></li><li>The ezSearch menus (suggestions in <code>ez-search-bar.scss</code>, and the Saved dropdown in the compact and full toolbars) keep a z-index above 999, kept as one shared value in the ezSearch styles rather than repeated numbers.</li><li>Don't lower the lane headers' 999: they rely on it to stay over the cards.</li><li>Modals (the compact builder) are unaffected: Bootstrap modals sit at body level at 1050.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A Task Board acceptance or integration check: with the suggestion menu open, <code>document.elementFromPoint</code> at a menu item's centre, where it overlaps a lane header, returns the menu item.</li><li>In the browser on the Task Board, the suggestion menu and the Saved menu show fully above the lane headers and cards.</li><li>The Issue list, the idea list and the Gantt are unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the lane headers' own z-index, the menu colours (aprom-4343).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4339, aprom-4343</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4344	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	9122d1d06aef-b8ee-711b-35f1fadd3162	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 00:48:47	aprom	0	0
060322c66af2-3340-0581-0c5b7e6f4bca	Work Interrupted	2026-11-10 08:42:46	2026-11-10 10:06:49	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51);" data-tomark-pass="">Found while shipping aprom-4439. The full Prometheus suite (<code data-backticks="1">ai test prometheus</code>, about 1290 tests) is often killed by the test container's memory limit, so a ship needs several attempts.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51);" data-tomark-pass=""><strong>Observed on 2026-11-10</strong> (checkout <code data-backticks="1">.runs/issue-4439/prometheus</code>, one run at a time, no other Prometheus test container running):</span><br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<ul>\n<li>7 full runs: 4 killed for out of memory (exit 137), 3 completed (1289, 1293 and 1293 passed, 0 failed).</li>\n<li>Message: <code data-backticks="1">killed: out of memory (container limit 4.5g; raise PROMETHEUS_TEST_MEMORY in p4m.env if the suite has grown). Not a test failure: run it again</code>.</li>\n<li>The kill comes partway through the run: the last one stopped after about 135 tests. Targeted runs (<code data-backticks="1">--filter conversation</code>, 54 tests) never hit it.</li>\n<li>Docker has 19.5 GiB; <code data-backticks="1">prometheus-dev</code> holds about 2.4 GiB of it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51);" data-tomark-pass=""><strong>Likely cause:</strong> the limit was set when the test containers were tuned for the most parallel runs. <code data-backticks="1">dev-tools/installer/testenv.py</code> has <code data-backticks="1">PROMETHEUS_MEMORY = "4.5g"</code> and <code data-backticks="1">PROMETHEUS_JOBS = 4</code>, with the note "with JOBS=4 a cold full suite peaks at ~3.5 GiB". The suite has grown since, and the page cache counts toward the limit, so the headroom is gone. This is not confirmed by measurement yet.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51);" data-tomark-pass=""><strong>To do:</strong></span><br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Measure the peak memory of a cold and a warm full run today (build, Chrome, page cache) and see what grows through the run.</li>\n<li>Decide between raising the default limit, lowering what the run uses (JOBS, Chrome flags, splitting the suite), or sizing the limit from the number of parallel runs that are actually active.</li>\n<li>Keep parallel Talos runs safe: the limit exists so one runaway container cannot take down Docker's VM.</li>\n<li>Update the "peaks at ~3.5 GiB" note in <code data-backticks="1">testenv.py</code> with the new figures.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51);" data-tomark-pass=""><strong>Acceptance:</strong> ten full runs in a row complete without an out-of-memory kill, with two runs in parallel also completing.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51);" data-tomark-pass=""><strong>Where:</strong> the change is in <code data-backticks="1">dev-tools</code> (<code data-backticks="1">installer/testenv.py</code>, <code data-backticks="1">installer/p4m.py</code>, <code data-backticks="1">ai/lib/tests.py</code>), not in the Prometheus repo. Logged in this milestone because it blocks shipping its issues.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51);" data-tomark-pass="">Complexity: complex</span></p>\n	1	1	1	1	1	4451	2026-12-01	2026-11-10	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Hammad Hassan	Hammad Hassan	929d5db36af2-3340-0581-dd4e338973d6	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 10:06:49	adt	0	0
a1678d936af2-b094-9389-8d45fbc6915a	Agamemnon :: Improved Stress handling	2026-11-10 10:06:25	2026-11-10 10:37:02	0	<p>Currently, we are trying to statistically figure out if we are taking too much space and in order to handle a stressed run we are killing instances.<br>\nHowever, there are other ways possible. We need to create tools to allow Agamemnon to understand the current workload on docker and then route the issues accordingly but gracefully.</p>\n<p>There has to be different ways of handling the load. I think the rules should be like so.<br>\n<strong>Stressed Situation:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If tasks are running and the memory is getting full</li>\n<li>Stop routing more issues until we get at least 40% memory fee (for docker)</li>\n<li>Pause one of the containers to allow the others to finish</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Normal situation</strong><br>\nWhen routing issues take the tally of the current running containers, not just the issues. Pausing the pipeline is better than crashing</p>\n	1	1	1	1	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4452	2026-12-01	2026-11-10	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a0dfebe16ad7-404c-ce18-be5ffb6791e6	Hammad Hassan	Agent Agamemnon	f92701976af2-b094-9389-bb3b1cef75f4	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 10:37:02	adt	0	0
a2e5c1546af7-3fb3-e127-b8a318018cf7	Convert the remaining live classic components to Glimmer	2026-11-14 01:04:34	2026-11-14 21:09:03	0	<p>These classic components (<code>@ember/component</code>) are still rendered:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>application-controlbar</code></li>\n<li><code>chart-estimatedspent</code> (Chart.js; <code>didRender</code> and <code>willDestroyElement</code>)</li>\n<li><code>chart-issueratio</code> (Chart.js, ColorHash)</li>\n<li><code>priority-icon</code></li>\n<li><code>tree-list</code></li>\n<li><code>checkbox-field</code> (jQuery)</li>\n<li><code>widgets</code> (jQuery UI sortable/draggable)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Also check the top-level <code>relate-simple</code> and <code>relate-user</code>.</p>\n<h4>Do</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Write the integration tests first, where none exist, to pin down the current output.</li>\n<li>Convert each one to a Glimmer component with tracked state and <code>@action</code>s.</li>\n<li>Move DOM setup and teardown (charts, sortable, jQuery plugins) into modifiers with <code>registerDestructor</code>, and guard async work after destroy.</li>\n<li>Update the callers to angle-bracket invocation with <code>@args</code>. Remove the <code>application-controlbar</code> exception in <code>.template-lintrc.js</code> once it is converted.</li>\n<li>The charts must look and update the same: check the project dashboard and the user page.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Depends on 4557 and 4558.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4559	2026-11-21	2026-11-14	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	749adaa06af8-d160-7d58-ffcf9d69bf66	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-14 21:09:03	aprom	0	0
72c7fb856adf-7ec8-653d-3eea9d5c2c5a	ai.cmd: run dev-tools\\ai\\ai from PowerShell and cmd on Windows	2026-10-26 21:38:58	2026-10-26 21:52:20	0	<p><b>Problem.</b> <code>dev-tools/ai/ai</code> is an extensionless POSIX sh script. From PowerShell or cmd, <code>dev-tools\\ai\\ai test gaia</code> opens Windows' "How do you want to open this file?" dialog. The obvious workaround <code>bash dev-tools/ai/ai …</code> also fails in PowerShell, because <code>bash</code> there resolves to the WSL launcher (<code>WindowsApps\\bash.exe</code>): <code>WSL … execvpe(/bin/bash) failed: No such file or directory</code>. The only ways that work today are <code>&amp; "C:\\Program Files\\Git\\bin\\bash.exe" dev-tools/ai/ai …</code> or <code>python dev-tools/ai/ai.py …</code>, and the second skips the runtime-copy selection.</p>\n<p><b>What</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add <code>dev-tools/ai/ai.cmd</code> mirroring <code>dev-tools/installer/p4m.cmd</code>:\n<ul>\n<li>find Python 3 (<code>py -3</code>, else <code>python</code>; never the Microsoft Store <code>python3</code> stub);</li>\n<li>prefer <code>..\\..\\.dev-tools-runtime\\ai\\ai.py</code> unless <code>P4M_RUNTIME=off</code>, as the sh wrapper does;</li>\n<li>pass all arguments through unchanged and return the exit code.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li>No path-conversion env is needed (cmd doesn't rewrite <code>/regex/</code> args), but filters must still reach ai.py verbatim. Check <code>--filter /x/</code>.</li>\n<li>README (dev-tools/ai/README.md): one line on running it from PowerShell/cmd (<code>dev-tools\\ai\\ai …</code>), and a note that bare <code>bash</code> in PowerShell is WSL.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Checks:</b> from PowerShell, <code>dev-tools\\ai\\ai status</code> runs and uses the runtime copy; with <code>$env:P4M_RUNTIME='off'</code> it uses the checkout; the exit code propagates (<code>dev-tools\\ai\\ai test nope; $LASTEXITCODE</code> is non-zero). The Git Bash <code>dev-tools/ai/ai</code> path is unchanged.</p>\n<p><b>Depends on:</b> nothing.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4142	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	8fe2ae046adf-8154-4904-8f5112ed5746	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	5d5c8c046adf-1601-0f35-45654e859634	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-26 21:52:20	adt	0	0
d86f13866afc-30ee-311d-9f17ef917a61	External Request: Allowlist the user-scoped event user.mentioned	2026-11-17 15:38:00	2026-11-18 19:51:57	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Event Registry", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Gaia publishes <code>user.mentioned</code> when a user is mentioned in a comment, issue or thread description, idea or idea message (linked Gaia issue). It is user-scoped: projectId <code>user:&lt;mentionedUserId&gt;</code>, ids only (mentionId, relatedTo, relatedId, projectId, actor).</p><ul><li>Add it to <code>EVENT_ALLOWLIST</code> and <code>USER_SCOPED_EVENTS</code> in <code>src/contract/names.js</code>.</li><li>ADR entry in decisions.md and tests (only the mentioned user's socket may subscribe).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the drift check against Gaia's events.json passes; tests pass.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4648, ah-4643</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4650	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	861790376ad5-1449-a602-a25bd5e6e2b8	95ad44a76afc-30ee-311d-be3b6ddb7299	\N	87099ee46ad5-1449-a602-5f7a1f6605b7	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	cc7f8af76afd-5775-b791-7c59614347fe	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 19:51:58	ah	0	0
e0c5da736afc-30ee-311d-d87196102a75	Events: publish workflow.run.finished when a workflow run completes or fails	2026-11-17 15:38:08	2026-11-18 14:04:13	0	<p>A run's end is invisible outside Gaia: the run view, Talos and Agamemnon can only poll. Runs end in <code>core/libs/workflows/RunJournal.php</code> <code>finish</code> (called from <code>WorkflowRunner</code> ~l.243; check every caller, e.g. timeouts via <code>ActorStepTimeouts</code>).</p><ul><li>When a run moves to <code>RunStatus::COMPLETED</code> or <code>FAILED</code> (not <code>WAITING</code>), publish <code>workflow.run.finished</code>, project-scoped by the run's <code>projectId</code> (skip runs without one). Ids only: runId, workflowId, status, test flag, entityType/entityId; no error text.</li><li>Inject a publisher the way <code>AgentRunLiveEvents</code> is injected into <code>WorkflowRunner</code> (see <code>WorkflowTriggersComponent::runner</code>); the domain class gets an abstraction, not <code>HermesPublisher</code>.</li><li>Constant in <code>EventNames</code>, registry entry (scope project, channel hermes, consumers prometheus, talos).</li><li>Tests for completed, failed, waiting (no event) and fail-open.</li><li>Contract change: linked Hermes PR.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> each finished run publishes exactly one event; a Hermes outage doesn't affect the run.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> step-level events.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4640</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4651	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7b8e27936afc-30ee-311d-92e7628909b7	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	37e3cb016afd-715d-1e86-bad378f731f0	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 14:04:13	agaia	0	0
3ecc78716af2-9f96-d476-9c4b83574631	Nestor is failing a test which is blocking other issues. 	2026-11-10 10:21:50	2026-11-10 10:29:54	0	<blockquote>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(85, 85, 85);" data-tomark-pass="">Issue #4452 is implemented on <code data-backticks="1">claude-issue-4452</code> with the changes uncommitted in the worktree. I did not ship it because the gate needs a passing full run on the current tree, and I don't have one.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(85, 85, 85);" data-tomark-pass=""><strong>Full suite, run twice:</strong> talos 890, ai 239, installer 110, sim 8 and gaia-mcp 91 all pass. The only failure is <code data-backticks="1">nestor:test_refuses_what_it_should</code> (<code data-backticks="1">test_nestor.py:138</code>). It errors with <code data-backticks="1">ConnectionAbortedError [WinError 10053]</code> on the POST to <code data-backticks="1">/sim/publish</code> and never reaches its 404 assertion. Run on its own, the same test passes.</span></p>\n<p><span class="colour" style="color: rgb(85, 85, 85);" data-tomark-pass="">The branch touches only <code data-backticks="1">talos/</code>, not nestor. The failure looks like a Windows connection-abort flake in the nestor test server under load. I did not run the suite on the base commit to confirm it already fails there.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Apparently Nestor is failing a test. Fix it</p>\n	1	1	1	1	1	4453	2026-12-01	2026-11-10	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Hammad Hassan	Hammad Hassan	71d224346af2-9f96-d476-f7a77dce0039	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 10:29:54	adt	0	0
2084b0676afc-72fe-b62c-a048d186e54e	Metadata: `system` field flag for fields hidden from the API and not audited	2026-11-17 16:21:52	2026-11-18 09:46:18	0	<p>Gaia has no way to mark a column as managed by the system. Search is about to add columns to module tables (an embedding vector, the text it was made from, hashes, timestamps) that must never reach API clients, never be written by users and never be audited. This issue adds a generic field flag for that.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Field property <code>'system' =&gt; true</code> in model metadata, read through the meta manager (<code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code>), with a helper listing a model's system fields.</li><li>Responses: system fields are never serialized, for the record itself, included relationships, <code>fields=</code> (silently omitted, like denied fields in D-033) and CSV export.</li><li>Writes: system fields in a user request body (POST/PUT/PATCH) are discarded, like denied write fields (D-034).</li><li>Not in the field-ACL catalog (<code>AclMapCatalog</code>) and not usable by users in <code>query</code> clauses or sort (rejected like an unknown field).</li><li><code>auditBehavior</code> skips system fields.</li><li>Opt-in access for specific internal paths is left to the code that needs it (first: the Ares search-column access); no generic bypass.</li><li>Record it as a decision in the relevant <code>docs/architecture/*/decisions.md</code>; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li><li>Tests on a fixture model: absent from GET/list/include/fields=, discarded on PATCH, rejected in a query clause, not in the audit diff, not in the permission catalog.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a field flagged <code>system</code> is invisible and read-only through the REST API and never appears in audit rows; unflagged fields behave as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any real model using the flag.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4653	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	1fb236126afc-72fe-b62c-bf3c9291dd47	\N	cbb506d05acd-06d6-1141-68969b9fd562	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	2ddd1f466afc-9bce-b62c-7f88fa361e29	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 09:46:18	agaia	0	0
28798a946af2-3028-5ed1-783e389200dd	Threads: vote thread body (agree/disagree, voter list) and Result box	2026-11-09 23:20:08	2026-11-10 11:28:49	0	<p>Vote threads are a key use of Threads. In vote rooms a vote is a comment whose text is "I agree" or "I disagree" (ConversationItem's <code>@vote</code>), one per user, not changeable, and tallies are counted over all of the room's comments. The thread page loads comments in pages, so tallies need their own data. The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only; the design system and existing components decide the final look.</p><ul><li>Vote body (in the slot from the thread page issue), below the description: the existing agree/disagree <code>info-box</code>es side by side (icon, count, progress bar, percentage), moved out of ConversationItem into a vote component. Not voted: thumbs clickable (existing vote action) and a hint "You haven't voted yet. Click a thumb to vote; one vote per person."; voted: thumbs locked and "You voted: I agree" (or disagree).</li><li>Tallies from a dedicated query of the room's vote comments (all, minimal fields: createdUser, text, date), shared with the voter list.</li><li>Voter list: uppercase "N votes" heading, rows with avatar, name link, time and a label (<code>label-success</code> I agree / <code>label-danger</code> I disagree), newest first, "Show all N votes" expands the rest. No reply box on vote threads (as today).</li><li>Info column for votes: <strong>Result</strong> box (box-warning) first: "Leaning: I agree (3 of 4)" (or "Tied" / "No votes yet") and "N of M project members voted" (members from the project members list). No Linked issue box on vote threads.</li><li>Live: a new vote (Hermes comment created) updates tallies, list and result without reload.</li><li>Translations: reuse <code>views.app.conversation.vote.*</code>, new keys for result, hint and heading.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> acceptance test: vote once, counts and result update, thumbs locked after voting, a live vote from another user updates tallies. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> closing a vote, changing a vote, deadlines, linking issues to votes.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4439</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> threads-vote.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4440	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	c5cdc8086af2-2364-4d51-32dd2e156b72	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 11:28:49	aprom	0	0
4681b7a96af2-3028-5ed1-3a27c8c4556e	Threads: 'Create issue from thread' in the Linked issue box	2026-11-09 23:20:38	2026-11-15 10:37:48	0	<p>Discussions often end in work. Let people create an issue straight from a discussion thread, linked to it, from the Linked issue box. The attached screen is a guide for layout and content only.</p><ul><li>Button "Create issue from thread" (btn-default btn-sm, <code>fa-plus</code>) in the Linked issue box footer, on discussion threads only, shown when the user may create issues (ACL issue.create) and the thread has no linked issue.</li><li>It opens the existing issue create flow (prefer reusing the issue create route/form; decide between navigating with prefilled values or a modal based on what the create controller supports, and say which in the PR) with subject = thread subject and description = thread description plus a link back to the thread.</li><li>After the issue is saved, PATCH the room's <code>issueId</code>/<code>issueNumber</code> (same fields the create modal sets) and return to the thread, which now shows the linked issue.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> acceptance test: create issue from a discussion, the thread shows the new issue in the Linked issue box and the list row shows its key. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> vote threads, unlinking.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4441</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> threads-list.png</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4442	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	6b7e4ae36af3-7981-2c35-269ac88bf650	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 12:23:32	aprom	0	0
32982ef86afc-72fe-b62c-ee7e6310ed8a	Search metadata block: system search columns and the canonical semantic text rule	2026-11-17 16:22:10	2026-11-18 12:34:00	0	<p>A model becomes searchable by declaring a <code>search</code> block in its metadata. The search data lives on the module's own table, so the block adds the search columns and indexes to the model, flagged as system fields. Gaia is the single owner of the text that gets embedded: it stores that text and its hash (Gaia has no computed fields), so every consumer (Ares, the stale-write check, the reindex) agrees on it.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Validate the block in the meta manager: <code>type</code> (name used in <code>/search?types=</code> and in search events, unique across models), <code>fts</code> (field =&gt; weight A-D), <code>fuzzy</code> (fields), <code>semantic</code> (ordered fields), <code>exact</code> (fields), <code>display</code> (<code>title</code>, <code>snippet</code>). Unknown fields or weights fail with a clear message.</li><li>Inject columns, all with <code>'system' =&gt; true</code>: <code>searchVector</code> (generated tsvector from <code>fts</code>, GIN index); and when <code>semantic</code> is set: <code>searchSemanticText</code> (text, the canonical text), <code>searchSemanticHash</code> (varchar 64, its sha256), <code>searchEmbedding</code> (<code>vector(768)</code>, HNSW cosine index), <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> (varchar 64, hash of the text the stored vector was made from), <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> (datetime); plus a <code>gin_trgm</code> index per fuzzy field.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SemanticText</code>: builds a record's canonical semantic text (the <code>semantic</code> fields in order, HTML stripped, whitespace collapsed, cut to <code>SEARCH_EMBED_MAX_CHARS</code>, default 4000) and its sha256. Deterministic; the only implementation of this rule.</li><li><code>core/libs/search/SearchableRegistry</code>: lookup of the <code>search</code> block by type and by model.</li><li>Unit tests: validation, injected columns and indexes, columns flagged system, <code>SemanticText</code> output and hash stability (HTML, whitespace, truncation, null fields); regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a <code>search</code> block migrates with the system columns and indexes; its REST payloads and audit rows never contain them; <code>SemanticText</code> gives the same hash for the same field values.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filling the columns (the search behaviour, a later issue), querying, service access.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4653, agaia-4654</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4655	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	1fb236126afc-72fe-b62c-bf3c9291dd47	\N	cbb506d05acd-06d6-1141-68969b9fd562	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	db6255e46afd-2303-ca4f-6501eb544f60	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 12:34:00	agaia	0	0
87acf0b26af8-c4a5-09ef-730e7b9c8cf2	ai test prometheus: run lint:js and lint:hbs before ember test, and fail the run and ship gate on lint errors	2026-11-14 22:58:15	2026-11-14 23:19:44	0	<p>Prometheus CI runs <code>npm run lint:js</code> and <code>npm run lint:hbs</code> before the tests (<code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code>, since aprom-4558). Nothing in <code>dev-tools</code> does:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>ai test</code> calls <code>p4m test ember</code>, which only runs <code>ember test</code> (<code>installer/testenv.py</code>).</li>\n<li><code>ai ship</code> and Talos call the same thing.</li>\n<li>The <code>.runs/issue-N</code> checkouts have no <code>node_modules</code>, so the agent can't run lint by hand either.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Result: lint failures appear only on GitHub. aprom-4560 (#788) needed two review rounds for lint, and #790 (aprom-4561) is still red on template-lint.</p>\n<p>The baseline is strict in both directions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>a recorded violation that a PR fixes must be removed from <code>eslint-suppressions.json</code> / <code>.lint-todo</code>;</li>\n<li>editing a line that has a recorded template-lint violation makes it count as new.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Cleanup PRs hit both cases all the time.</p>\n<h4>Do</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Write the failing tests first.</li>\n<li>In the per-checkout Prometheus test container (adt-4509), run <code>npm run lint:js</code> and <code>npm run lint:hbs</code> on the synced source before <code>ember test</code>.</li>\n<li>A lint error fails the <code>ai test</code> run and <code>ai ship</code>'s gate. Report it as its own suite (for example <code>lint: 11 errors</code>, with the first few file:line messages), like the ember summary.</li>\n<li>When the error is a stale suppression or todo, print the exact fix command: <code>npm run lint:js:prune</code>, or <code>npx ember-template-lint &lt;file&gt; --clean-todo</code>.</li>\n<li><b>Line endings:</b> template-lint todos hash the source, line endings included. A Windows checkout with CRLF templates fails every recorded todo, even though <code>.gitattributes</code> now forces LF for <code>*.hbs</code> and <code>.lint-todo</code>. Either lint a copy with LF endings, or detect CRLF templates and fail with a clear message and the re-checkout command, so a local pass always matches CI.</li>\n<li>Talos picks this up through <code>ai test</code> / <code>ai ship</code>. Check that a Talos run sees the lint result and fixes it before shipping.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Found while observing aprom-4560 and aprom-4561 on 2026-11-15.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4563	2026-11-22	2026-11-15	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	3a0497e46af8-0491-a1ed-0aa0a6dc0e62	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-14 23:19:44	adt	0	0
