d1e1ae696adf-c3cd-5c87-bd463ad76e0d	Guard rails: PreToolUse hooks redirecting reads of Gaia framework/api-tester internals to gaia-dev, docker-suite deny, and ai cost regression gate in ai ship	2026-10-26 08:09:53	2026-10-27 09:15:54	0	<p><b>Phase 6 of "Agentic Improve", last step: make the cheaper path the default path.</b> These hooks redirect, they never truncate — the earlier decision (no output cap, every command keeps its confirmation) stands.</p>\n<p><b>What</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>PreToolUse</code> hook on Bash and Read (in <code>.claude/settings.json</code>, script under <code>dev-tools/ai/hooks/</code>): when the target is <code>gaia/core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php</code>, <code>core/libs/security/Acl.php</code>, <code>core/mvc/models/Model.php</code>, <code>tools/api-tester/{src,apis,harness}/**</code> or <code>fixtures/default.json</code>, block with a one-line message naming the <code>gaia-dev</code> command that answers the question (<code>model</code>, <code>route</code>, <code>acl</code>, <code>cases</code>, <code>assertions</code>, <code>profiles</code>). Escape hatches: the file is in the current branch's changed set (genuine framework work), or the command carries a <code>--raw</code> marker / <code># raw</code> comment.</li>\n<li><code>PreToolUse</code> hook denying <code>docker exec</code> / <code>docker run</code> of the test suites, pointing to <code>ai test</code> (today a sentence in the <code>run-tests</code> skill; make it mechanical).</li>\n<li><code>ai ship</code> gate: compare the issue's cost (from <code>ai cost</code>, #4126) with the repo's rolling median and add a warning line to the PR description and the tracker comment when it is above; never block on it.</li>\n<li><code>ai cost</code> reports the hook bypass rate (<code>--raw</code> uses and blocked attempts) so the redirect list can be tuned.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Checks:</b> unittest for the hook scripts (allow, block, escape hatches); hooks must run in under 100 ms so t