d32d1f226aef-1a22-399b-34cdb2e58be0	ezSearch: two-line suggestion rows are only half highlighted	2026-11-08 00:48:19	2026-11-08 01:05:27	0	<p>In the suggestion menu, when a row's label and field id don't fit on one line (e.g. "Milestone" + <code>issuemilestone.name</code> in a narrow column), the id wraps below. The highlight (crimson background, white text, aprom-4343) only covers the first line, so the id is white on white. Cause: the id is <code>float: right</code> (<code>.ez-search-item-detail</code>, <code>app/styles/components/ez-search-bar.scss</code> ~l.91), and the row's <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> (<code>app/components/ez-search/search-bar.hbs</code> ~l.29-33) doesn't contain the float, so the wrapped id falls outside the highlighted box.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Lay out each row's <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> so it always contains both parts, e.g. <code>display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap</code>, with the detail no longer floated (it goes to the right when it fits, below the label when it doesn't).</li><li>The whole row, both lines, gets the active/hover background, and both texts turn white.</li><li>Long ids wrap (<code>overflow-wrap: anywhere</code>) rather than overflow.</li><li>No markup change is needed beyond what the layout requires. Keep it in <code>ez-search-bar.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.ez-search-menu</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An integration test renders the menu at 240px wide, makes a row with a long id active, and asserts that the id's bounding box lies inside the row's <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> box.</li><li>In the browser, the idea list (narrow) and the Task Board both highlight the whole row with readable text.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the Saved menus, menu content.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 2</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb7