e070f1b06ae0-008b-3d46-762aaa5b4714	Idea page: Created Issues box shows 'undefined-undefined' instead of the issue refs	2026-10-27 16:22:56	2026-10-27 20:41:44	0	<p>The Created Issues box on the idea page lists every created issue as grey text <code>undefined-undefined</code>, with no link and no subject. <code>describe</code> in <code>app/components/idea/created-issues-box.js</code> reads <code>link.issue.projectShortcode</code>, <code>issueNumber</code>, <code>subject</code> and <code>projectId</code> as plain properties. <code>issue</code> on <code>app/models/ideaplanissue.js</code> is an async <code>belongsTo</code>, so <code>link.issue</code> is a promise proxy: those reads return <code>undefined</code>, <code>readable</code> is false, and because the proxy is always truthy the 'no loaded issue' fallback never runs. The plan box reads the same data through <code>get(link, 'issue.…')</code> (<code>plan-box.js</code> <code>createdIssues</code> ~l.192) and works.</p><ul><li>Add one small helper (for example in <code>app/utils/idea-plan-body.js</code>, next to <code>isProjectReadable</code>) that returns the created issue of an ideaplanissue: <code>link.belongsTo('issue').value()</code>, which gives the loaded record or <code>null</code> without triggering a fetch, plus a fallback for plain objects if the tests need one.</li><li>Use it in <code>created-issues-box.js</code> <code>describe</code>. With a record: label <code>&lt;shortcode&gt;-&lt;number&gt;</code>, the subject, and a link when <code>isProjectReadable</code> allows it. Without a record (Gaia left the issue out, for example because it isn't readable): the existing fallback, the plan item's key and subject as plain text.</li><li>Use the same helper in <code>plan-box.js</code> <code>createdIssues</code> instead of <code>get(link, 'issue.…')</code>, so both boxes read the issue the same way and a missing issue never triggers a <code>findRecord</code>.</li><li><strong>Check the version grouping:</strong> the engineer saw issues created from plans v2 and v3 listed under 'Plan v1' and 'Plan v3'. <code>groups</code> uses the plan whose id equals <code>link.ideaplanId</code>. On a real idea with several plan versions, check that the headings match the versions the issues were created from. If the box is wrong, fix it here. If the stored <code>ideaplanId</code>s are wrong (Talos records them), file an adt issue and mention it in the PR.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>On an idea with created issues, the box lists <code>aprom-4118</code>-style refs as links with their subjects, grouped under the plan version each was created from.</li><li>An issue that isn't loaded shows the plan item's key and subject as plain text, with no 'undefined'.</li><li>The integration tests in <code>tests/integration/components/idea/created-issues-box-test.js</code> (and the plan-box test if it uses plain objects) build real store records (<code>ideaplanissue</code> with a pushed <code>issue</code>, plus one without). The new test fails before the fix.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing what Gaia includes in <code>rels: 'issue'</code>, and any other change to the box's layout.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4165	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	cdbb41436ae1-dbc0-c448-1773b3943f31	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-27 20:41:44	aprom	0	0
5c14c3926ad7-c32a-4943-f07c9908d0f4	Agents module: list, create/edit and detail page	2026-10-20 11:41:16	2026-11-02 09:02:38	0	<p>Part of agaia-4026 (Agents). The Agents admin module in Prometheus, built on the Gaia <code>agent</code> CRUD from agaia-4027. Follow <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>. Field help goes in info-icon tooltips, with no helper text under fields.</p><h4>List (<code>agents-list.png</code>)</h4><ul><li>Saved searches, search and Clear. Row toolbar: select all and delete. Mass update and export are aprom-4243.</li><li>Columns:<ul><li>Agent: robot avatar, name link, Active/Disabled label, purpose.</li><li>Sponsor: avatar and name, or <em>Autonomous</em> when the agent has no sponsor.</li><li>Models: simple · complex.</li><li>Projects: labels.</li><li>Grants: n tools · n skills.</li><li>Last active.</li><li>Row menu.</li></ul></li><li><code>fa-sort</code> icons on sortable headers.</li></ul><h4>Create / edit (<code>agent-edit.png</code>)</h4><ul><li>Main box:<ul><li>Name, Email (tooltip: the agent's login, which never has a password), Purpose.</li><li>Role prompt, in the existing markdown editor.</li><li>Model and limits: model for simple issues, model for complex issues, escalate to, max turns per run, max runs per issue, permission mode.</li></ul></li><li>The three model selects read and write <code>modelConfig</code> as JSON <code>{"simple", "complex", "escalation"}</code>, the shape Gaia's seed data uses. They map to <code>maxTurns</code>, <code>maxRunsPerIssue</code> and <code>permissionMode</code>.</li><li>Sponsor box: 'On behalf of', a user picker.</li><li>Access box: roles, projects and an Active checkbox, all as the agent user's memberships and status.</li></ul><h4>Detail (<code>agent-detail.png</code>)</h4><ul><li>Header box:<ul><li>Robot avatar, name, email and the AGENT label.</li><li>A status dropdown.</li><li>Purpose, sponsor, permission mode, max turns (per run · runs per issue), model simple, model complex, escalates to.</li><li>The edit pencil.</li></ul></li><li>Role Prompt box: the first lines of the prompt, 'Show the whole prompt', and the edit pencil.</li><li>Roles &amp; Projects box.</li><li>Mount the Identities box from aprom-4037, which is merged.</li><li>Leave the other boxes to their own issues: Credentials (aprom-4045), Tools and Skills (aprom-4036), Workflows (aprom-4059) and Agent Activities (aprom-4242).</li></ul><h4>Shared pieces and plumbing</h4><ul><li>Agent badge component: the plum AGENT label, <code>$highlightColor</code>.</li><li>Robot avatar component.</li><li>The <code>type</code> field on the Prometheus user model.</li><li>Use these on the pages above only. Putting them on other screens is aprom-4244, and the grouped assignee picker is aprom-4241.</li><li>Sidebar: Admin › Agents with List Agents and Create Agent. Tool Catalog and Skills come with aprom-4036.</li><li>Agent model, routes and ACL <code>routeMaps</code> gated by the <code>agent.*</code> permissions, plus translations, Mirage and acceptance tests.</li><li>Ship no permission seeds: the reviewer grants permissions.</li></ul><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4027, adt-4240</p><p>Mockups: <code>agents-list.png</code>, <code>agent-edit.png</code> and <code>agent-detail.png</code>, attached to this issue. List them with <code>gaia_get_issue</code> (under files) and read them with <code>gaia_get_file</code>. <code>agents-in-context-and-identities.png</code> belongs to aprom-4244 and aprom-4241.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	4044	2026-10-27	2026-10-20	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	e6ddf3416ae6-5dca-104b-665d99d02ce1	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-02 09:02:38	aprom	0	0
d1f210a36ae0-7d1c-e593-fcdfa27e02e2	Issue statuses: Add/Edit dialog crashes with more than one locale (intl `_intls` updated during render)	2026-10-27 17:26:42	2026-10-27 17:58:35	0	<p>aprom-3977 (#568) made the Add/Edit issue status dialog show one label field per supported locale. It translates each field's caption into that field's locale while rendering (<code>templates/app/settings/issue-statuses.hbs</code> l.91: <code>{{t "views.app.settings.issueStatuses.label" locale=field.locale}}</code>). When Gaia offers more than one locale, the dialog crashes as it opens in development builds with <code>Assertion Failed: You attempted to update `_intls` on intl service ... after it had already been used in the same computation</code>.</p><p>This also blocks every Prometheus ship. The acceptance scenario "The status value is derived from the label until it is typed" (<code>tests/acceptance/settings/issue-statuses.feature</code>, locales <code>en-us, de-de</code>) raises a QUnit global failure on <code>dev</code> (<code>cc6a2ed5</code>), and <code>ai test prometheus</code> stops the whole run there. aprom-4155 is waiting on this.</p><p><strong>Cause</strong>: ember-intl creates a locale's formatter only when that locale is first used. It stores the formatter by writing the tracked <code>_intls</code> on the intl service (<code>getOrCreateIntl</code>). In one render, the <code>en-us</code> field reads <code>_intls</code>, then the <code>de-de</code> field writes it, which Glimmer doesn't allow. Only that scenario offers a second locale, so the other status scenarios pass.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong> (two layers: warming up is the normal path, and rendering must not depend on it)</p><ul><li><strong>Warm up</strong>: after <code>translations.loadLocales()</code> (<code>services/translations.js</code> ~l.125) sets the supported locales, create each one's formatter before the app renders. Use ember-intl's public API (for example a no-op format call with <code>{ locale }</code>), not the private <code>getOrCreateIntl</code>. A failure to warm up one locale is logged and must not stop the boot.</li><li><strong>Never translate into another locale while rendering</strong>: <code>showAddDialog</code> and <code>showEditDialog</code> (<code>controllers/app/settings/issue-statuses.js</code> ~l.171/~l.193) are actions that run outside rendering. Work out each label field's caption there and store it on <code>IssueStatusLabelField</code> (<code>utils/issue-status/form.js</code>). The template renders <code>@label={{field.caption}}</code>. This stays safe when a locale wasn't warmed up: translations failed to load, the locale list changed after boot, or a test stubbed the locales.</li><li><strong>Missing caption</strong>: if a locale has no translation for the caption key, use the default locale's caption with the locale code (for example "Label (de-de)"), never a missing-translation string. A field's caption must be unique, because its locale is the only thing that tells the fields apart.</li><li>Look for any other <code>t ... locale=</code> (or <code>intl.t(..., { locale })</code> called from a template getter) under <code>app/</code> and treat it the same way. List what you find in a comment on this issue.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong></p><ul><li>Red first: the existing scenario fails on <code>dev</code>. Record the failure on this issue.</li><li>Unit (translations service): every loaded locale is warmed up, and a locale that throws during warm-up doesn't stop the others or the boot.</li><li>Unit (<code>IssueStatusForm</code>, or a small caption builder): a caption is built for a locale that was never warmed up; a missing translation falls back to the default caption with the locale code.</li><li>Acceptance: the dialog opens with <code>en-us, de-de</code> when warm-up is skipped or fails, and every field shows the right caption.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>With two or more locales, the Add and Edit issue status dialogs open without an assertion or a console error, whether or not warm-up ran.</li><li>Every label field shows a caption in its own locale, or the fallback caption described above.</li><li>A full <code>ai test prometheus</code> run finishes with a summary, and the issue-statuses scenarios pass.</li><li>Saving labels, deriving the value, and the list behave exactly as before (aprom-3977). Lint passes.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: making <code>ai test</code> continue after a QUnit global failure (a dev-tools issue); upgrading ember-intl; aprom-4155 itself.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4166	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	c1423e736ae0-47e3-e593-83ca45da5ba0	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-27 17:58:35	aprom	0	0
e48aa3c76aef-1a22-399b-9b41346c905f	Task Board: the ezSearch Filter modal opens behind the overlay	2026-11-08 00:48:36	2026-11-08 01:21:01	0	<p>On the Task Board, clicking Filter in the compact search opens the builder modal under the dark overlay, so it can't be used. It works on the idea list. Cause: <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> renders its <code>bootstrap-modal</code> inline inside the component (<code>app/components/ez-search-compact/index.hbs</code> ~l.82-97). On the board the component sits in <code>.milestone-filters</code>, which has its own stacking level (aprom-4344, needed for the suggestion menu). The modal is trapped inside it, while Bootstrap's backdrop is added to <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> and covers it.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Render the builder modal at body level with <code>{{#in-element}}</code>, the same way <code>app/components/idea/message-screen.hbs</code> ~l.11 renders its screen modal (<code>{{#in-element this.modalRoot insertBefore=null}}</code>, with <code>modalRoot</code> resolved in the component class). The modal then works in any container, whatever its stacking.</li><li>Check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> in any async close path. Closing (Cancel, Search, Clear, Esc, backdrop click) still removes the modal and the backdrop. Focus returns to the Filter button.</li><li>Check <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code>'s own modals (save dialog pages) aren't affected. They are rendered by pages, outside the search.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An acceptance test on the Task Board: open Filter, and the modal's dialog element is the top element at its centre (<code>document.elementFromPoint</code>). Add a condition and Search: the query applies and the modal and backdrop are gone.</li><li>The same flow still works on the idea list and the Gantt.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing <code>bootstrap-modal</code> itself, the board's z-index values.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4344</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4347	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	1542abd76aef-718a-399b-124467afff6f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 01:21:01	aprom	0	0
eef04cc76ad7-d41d-2b49-e6106c38f089	Workflows: automation with users and agents as actors	2026-10-20 17:12:15	2026-11-09 14:59:22	0	<p>Part of agaia-4026 (Agents).</p><p><strong>Design (from the UI mockups, 2026-10-20):</strong> a generic workflow module, like a JIRA workflow or n8n, replacing the per-agent workflows first planned in the Agents epic.</p><ul><li><strong>Trigger</strong>: an entity event (Issue created / modified / assignee changed / status changed, Comment added, Wiki page modified, Time logged, …, any module) or a schedule.</li><li><strong>Conditions</strong>: Filter (field conditions) and Switch (one output per case).</li><li><strong>Actors</strong>: users and agents. 'Run agent' runs an agent and continues on its outcome (done, needs input, blocked, failed, limit); 'Ask a user' waits for a reply.</li><li><strong>Actions</strong>: assign, set field/status, add comment, create issue / wiki page, notify, call a tool (tool catalog), end.</li><li>Values are expressions over the event: <code>{issue.number}</code>, 'issue assignee', 'the agent's sponsor'.</li><li>A workflow has a scope (projects) and a status (Draft, Active, Disabled). Agents show the workflows that reference them.</li><li>Gaia evaluates and runs workflows; 'Run agent' steps are sent through Hermes to the machine that runs the agent (Talos), which reports the outcome back to Gaia.</li></ul><p><strong>Issues:</strong> Gaia agaia-4049 agaia-4050 agaia-4051 agaia-4052 agaia-4053 agaia-4054; Hermes ah-4055; Prometheus aprom-4056 aprom-4038 aprom-4057 aprom-4058 aprom-4059; dev-tools adt-4047.</p><p>Mockups: the screenshots attached to this issue (from the 'Agents Screens' design canvas, https://claude.ai/artifact/9WYrFcT3LacRG9QLeBSQUL, private until shared).</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4048	2026-12-18	2026-10-20	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7a626c876ad7-b7ec-4943-0da4f6053570	864a5c576ad7-b7ec-4943-13e891fa3ea1	cb9835c25acd-06d6-1141-d64018bb91b3	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	e5d798e66af1-1c21-b4fe-3f7ed97d6f93	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 14:59:22	agaia	0	0
4468b4e46afc-72fe-b62c-20b5e64f9f2f	External Request: Service sockets: accept service tokens and `service:<kind>` scoped intents	2026-11-17 16:22:28	2026-11-18 09:43:21	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Semantic Search", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Gaia's search needs Ares (a backend service) to hear a <code>search.semantic.changed</code> event for records in every project. Today sockets authenticate users through <code>user/me</code> and intents must name a project the user is a member of (D-008), so a service would have to join every project and stay under 100 intents. Gaia requests service-scoped subscriptions, mirroring user-scoped events (D-009). Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li>Handshake: a token with no user is checked with Gaia's introspection (<code>POST /api/v1/introspect</code>, D-065: <code>actorType: service</code>, <code>serviceKind</code>); user tokens work as today.</li><li>A new list of service-scoped events in <code>src/contract/names.js</code> (first: <code>search.semantic.changed</code>, added to the allowlist). Their <code>projectId</code> is <code>service:&lt;kind&gt;</code>; a socket may subscribe only when its <code>serviceKind</code> equals that kind (<code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code>). Service sockets cannot subscribe to project or user events.</li><li>Gaia publishes such events with <code>projectId: "service:ares"</code> through the existing <code>POST /publish</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/auth</code> (introspection with Hermes' own service token, cached like D-012), <code>src/contract/names.js</code>, <code>src/intents/evaluate.js</code>, a new ADR in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>, tests with the stub loader.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a service socket of kind ares subscribes to <code>service:ares</code>/<code>search.semantic.changed</code> and receives a published envelope; a user socket is rejected for it; a service socket is rejected for project events.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> other service events.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4657	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	861790376ad5-1449-a602-a25bd5e6e2b8	43a91f286afc-72fe-b62c-61807f42bdd5	\N	87076e976ad5-1449-a602-7787246bb3ff	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	3f1fc4866afc-9bce-b62c-58c2b846ae7f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 09:43:21	ah	0	0
739d7c896af3-a609-a385-9debcdc72302	Threads: the thread box has an extra shadow and border unlike other boxes	2026-11-10 14:55:47	2026-11-10 15:07:41	0	<p>The thread (discussion) box on the Threads page (aprom-4439) has a shadow and border that don't match the rest of the application's boxes.</p><ul><li>Find the custom rules added for the thread box (likely in <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code> or a new thread partial) and remove the extra shadow/border, so it looks exactly like a standard <code>box box-primary</code> (design system: no new shadows, square edges).</li><li>Don't restyle AdminLTE's <code>.box</code> globally.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the thread box matches the issue page's record box side by side in the running app. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other layout changes.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4439</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 2</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> threads-fixed.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4456	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	d9c3e5976af3-a609-a385-30585e0db6b0	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 15:07:42	aprom	0	0
8a29d4466aef-4618-07ee-a9f65b75a25a	Gantt Cal: timeline starts below the search, leaving empty space at the top	2026-11-08 01:34:02	2026-11-08 10:06:42	0	<p>Since aprom-4337 put the compact search at the top of the Gantt's task list, the whole timeline side (the Days/Weeks tabs <code>.gantt-time-scale-selector</code> and the date header <code>AppUi::GanttChart::TimelineHeader</code>) is pushed down by the search block's height. That leaves an empty band at the top right. 4337's description asked for exactly that offset to keep task rows and timeline rows aligned, and it was the wrong approach. The engineer wants the timeline to start at the top, level with the top of the filter.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In <code>components/app-ui/gantt-chart.hbs</code> and <code>app/styles/modules/gantt.scss</code>, remove the top offset 4337 added to the timeline side.</li><li>Make the chart's top one header band across both columns:<ul><li>Left: the <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> block at the top, the <code>.gantt-header</code> column row (Milestone / Start - End) at the bottom.</li><li>Right: the Days/Weeks tabs at the top, level with the top of the search; the timeline date header at the bottom, level with the left column row.</li></ul>For example, a shared header row (grid or flex with <code>align-items: stretch</code>) where each side puts its column or date header at the bottom (<code>margin-top: auto</code>).</li><li>Any extra height (the search is taller than the tabs) sits between the tabs and the date header on the right, never above the tabs. When the chips row is empty, the band is no taller than the left side needs.</li><li>Task rows and timeline rows stay aligned row for row, also while the chips row appears or disappears (applying or clearing a search), and after switching Days/Weeks.</li><li>The issue panel mode (<code>gantt-timeline-hidden</code>), scrolling (slimscroll on <code>.gantt-tasks</code>, horizontal timeline scroll) and the scale conversion overlay are unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An integration or acceptance check:<ul><li>The top of the Days/Weeks tabs equals the top of the search block (within 2px).</li><li>The bottom of the left column header row equals the bottom of the timeline date header.</li><li>The first task row and the first timeline row share the same top. This holds with no search applied and with chips showing.</li></ul></li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the search itself, the Task Board.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4337</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4348	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	ad8a81c46aef-4618-07ee-e2f81310ca6b	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 10:06:42	aprom	0	0
4d2553326afc-72fe-b62c-b2abecca069d	Search: keep semantic text current, publish `search.semantic.changed`, daily `search reindex`	2026-11-17 16:22:37	2026-11-17 16:22:37	0	<p>Ares embeds a searchable record when Gaia announces that its semantic text changed. Gaia keeps the stored canonical text and hash current in the same write as the change, from a model hook so every write path (REST, MCP, workflows, CLI) is covered, and re-publishes stale records daily because Hermes keeps no history.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Event name <code>search.semantic.changed</code> in <code>support/EventNames.php</code> (lockstep with Hermes <code>names.js</code>, service-scoped).</li><li><code>searchIndexBehavior</code>, attached automatically to every model with a <code>search</code> block that has <code>semantic</code> fields. Before create, and before update when a <code>semantic</code> field changed: set <code>searchSemanticText</code> and <code>searchSemanticHash</code> from <code>SemanticText</code> (same write, no extra query). After the save, if the hash changed: publish through <code>HermesPublisher</code> with <code>projectId: "service:ares"</code> and payload <code>{type, resource, recordId}</code>. Fail open: a Hermes failure is logged and never fails the write. Not triggered by the Ares embedding write.</li><li><code>core/tasks/SearchTask.php</code> (parses and prints; logic in <code>core/libs/search/</code>): <code>php cli.php search reindex [type]</code> pages through every non-deleted searchable record; recomputes text and hash and updates them (bound UPDATE, no audit/dateModified) where missing or different (backfills existing rows, follows rule changes); then publishes the event, paced, where <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> is null or differs from <code>searchSemanticHash</code>; prints counts.</li><li>Unit tests with a fake publisher: create sets text/hash and publishes, a semantic edit updates and publishes, a non-semantic edit does neither, an edit that leaves the text identical does not publish, publish failure does not break the save, reindex backfills and selects only stale records.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> creating an issue or editing its description stores its new text and hash and publishes one event; after <code>search reindex</code> every issue has text and hash, and events go out only for issues without an up-to-date embedding.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> scheduling the command (separate issue), the Ares consumer.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4656, ah-4657</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	4658	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	new	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	1fb236126afc-72fe-b62c-bf3c9291dd47	\N	cbb506d05acd-06d6-1141-68969b9fd562	Agent Nestor	Agent Nestor	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-17 16:22:37	agaia	0	0
55e99c616afc-72fe-b62c-1fc3d8e3e777	Ares service kind: read the stored semantic text and write embeddings only for the current hash (409 when stale)	2026-11-17 16:22:45	2026-11-17 16:22:45	0	<p>Ares computes embeddings and stores them through Gaia, signing in as a service client (D-065/D-066). Service tokens can only <code>get</code> today, writes are closed until it is decided who a service write is stamped as (D-066), and the search columns are <code>system</code> fields hidden from the API. This issue opens one narrow, explicit path. Because events can be handled out of order, an embedding is stored only if it was made from the record's current semantic text; a slow, older write must never overwrite a newer embedding.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Service kind <code>ares</code> in <code>config/serviceclients.php</code> with default scopes for the searchable modules' <code>get</code>/<code>update</code>.</li><li>Every model with a <code>search</code> block opens <code>get</code> to kind <code>ares</code> (injected from the block, same mechanism as <code>acl.service</code>). For that kind only, <code>fields=</code> may return the stored system fields <code>searchSemanticText</code>, <code>searchSemanticHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code>. Users never see them.</li><li>A filtered <code>update</code> for kind <code>ares</code> (like D-068): body <code>{searchEmbedding (768 numbers, validated), searchEmbeddingHash}</code> only; anything else is 400. In one transaction: lock the row (<code>SELECT ... FOR UPDATE</code>) and compare the sent <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code> with the stored <code>searchSemanticHash</code>; if they differ, return <strong>409</strong> and write nothing; otherwise store vector and hash and set <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> to now. Deleted or missing record: 404.</li><li>The write is a bound <code>UPDATE</code> of the search columns that skips audit, created/modified-user and dateModified behaviours, live events and the search behaviour (no loop).</li><li>Record the decisions in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code> (new D-number, referencing D-066): unstamped service write of system search columns, hash precondition with 409.</li><li>api-tester cases: ares token reads <code>searchSemanticText</code>/<code>searchSemanticHash</code>; PATCH with the current hash 200; PATCH with an old hash after a subject change 409 and the stored vector unchanged; PATCH of <code>subject</code> 400; a user cannot read or write the search fields; other service kinds 401. Unit test for the lock-and-compare path.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the cases pass; an accepted PATCH leaves the issue's audit, dateModified and modifiedUser unchanged; a stale PATCH never overwrites a newer embedding.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> issuing the Ares client credentials in deployments.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4658</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	4659	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	new	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	1fb236126afc-72fe-b62c-bf3c9291dd47	\N	cbb506d05acd-06d6-1141-68969b9fd562	Agent Nestor	Agent Nestor	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-17 16:22:46	agaia	0	0
e308eb806af0-7a5b-8669-a5d66a329f83	ezSearch: Enter no longer runs the search; Ctrl/Cmd+Enter or the Search button does	2026-11-08 10:28:51	2026-11-08 11:14:09	0	<p>Pressing Enter in ezSearch runs the search too eagerly: while typing, Enter starts a search, and on first load Enter runs a query even when the bar is empty. That is the behaviour aprom-4297 specified (Enter with the suggestion menu closed formats and runs). The engineer wants searches to run only on purpose. Change it in the shared search bar (<code>app/components/ez-search/search-bar.{js,hbs}</code>), so <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code> (both layouts) behave the same everywhere.</p><p><strong>New keyboard behaviour</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Enter</strong>:<ul><li>With the suggestion menu open: accept the highlighted suggestion (unchanged).</li><li>With the menu closed: parse and format the text into the exact query and show any error, without calling <code>@onRun</code>/<code>@onApply</code>.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Ctrl+Enter</strong> (<strong>Cmd+Enter</strong> on macOS, i.e. <code>ctrlKey || metaKey</code>): format and run, the same as clicking Search. It works with the menu open too: the typed text runs, the highlighted suggestion is not accepted.</li><li><strong>Search button</strong>: unchanged; it runs.</li><li><strong>Guard</strong> (in the shared base, <code>app/components/ez-search/base.js</code>, so the button and the shortcut both use it): don't apply when the bar is empty and no query is currently applied, or when the formatted query equals the one last applied. Clear still applies the empty query when something was applied.</li><li>Tab, Up, Down and Esc are unchanged. Blur still formats without running.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>The search bar's keydown handling and the base's apply guard, as above.</li><li>The menu's hint line (<code>components.ezSearch.searchBar.hint</code> in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>): "Enter to accept · Ctrl+Enter to search · Esc to close". The Search button's <code>title</code> mentions Ctrl+Enter.</li><li>Update the search bar's and the base's integration tests.</li><li>Update the acceptance step definitions that run a query by pressing Enter (Issue, Project, Agents, Workflows, idea list, Gantt, Task Board scenarios) to use Ctrl+Enter or the Search button. Prefer one shared step so the features don't each change.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Integration tests:<ul><li>Enter with the menu closed formats and doesn't call <code>@onApply</code>.</li><li>Enter with the menu open accepts the suggestion.</li><li>Ctrl+Enter and Cmd+Enter apply.</li><li>Ctrl+Enter or Search on an empty bar with nothing applied does nothing.</li><li>An unchanged query is not applied twice.</li><li>Clear after an applied search applies the empty query.</li></ul></li><li>An acceptance check on the Issue list: loading the page and pressing Enter in the empty bar makes no new <code>/issue</code> request.</li><li>All ezSearch acceptance suites pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the builder modal's buttons, other shortcuts.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4349	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	4c60faf06af0-8d62-8669-62d0513bcd78	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 11:14:10	aprom	0	0
3bdf94686af0-b3ed-60c0-51eb0f45ce9d	QuickList: core component (box, header, item frame, named blocks, states)	2026-11-08 11:47:07	2026-11-08 12:45:19	0	<p>Several narrow lists in Prometheus (the idea browser, the Gantt task list, notifications, latest issues) each build their own markup. This issue adds the root <code>QuickList</code> component and sets its contract. Other issues build the pagination, group heading, toolbar and selection bar separately as standalone components, and a later issue connects them to this root, so don't build those parts here. The attached screens are a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the existing components decide that.</p><ul><li>New Glimmer components in <code>app/components/quick-list/</code>: <code>QuickList</code> (root <code>box box-primary quick-list</code>), <code>QuickList::Header</code> (box title with the count: <code>64</code>, or <code>0 of 64</code> when the shown count and <code>@total</code> differ, plus <code>box-tools</code>) and <code>QuickList::Item</code> (the row frame: link via <code>@route</code>/<code>@model</code>, a 3px crimson left bar when active, light row separator).</li><li>Named blocks: <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> (header tools), <code>&lt;:search&gt;</code> (a slot for <code>&lt;EzSearchCompact&gt;</code>, which is not wrapped), <code>&lt;:item as |record|&gt;</code> rendering <code>QuickList::Item</code> with <code>&lt;:primary&gt;</code> (bold title that wraps, status label on the right) and <code>&lt;:secondary&gt;</code> (12px grey line cut off with an ellipsis, plus optional tags), and <code>&lt;:empty&gt;</code>.</li><li>Arguments: <code>@items</code>, <code>@total</code>, <code>@activeId</code>, <code>@isLoading</code>, <code>@error</code>, <code>@onRetry</code>, <code>@onClearSearch</code>, <code>@title</code>. The component never loads data; the caller owns the queries.</li><li>States: loading = three skeleton rows (reuse the existing <code>skeleton-line</code> styles / <code>AppUi::Skeleton</code>); empty = grey <code>fa-info-circle</code> text, with "Clear the search" when <code>@onClearSearch</code> is passed; error = red <code>fa-exclamation-triangle</code> text with "Try again" (<code>@onRetry</code>).</li><li>Styles in <code>app/styles/components/quick-list.scss</code> (imported in <code>app.scss</code>), all under <code>.quick-list</code>: square edges, colours from <code>variables.scss</code>, no shadows. Strings under <code>components.quickList.*</code> in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>YUIDoc on the class and every argument and block, describing the contract for future users.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests render items through the named blocks, mark the active item, and show the loading, empty (default and replaced) and error states with working actions.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: pagination, grouping, sorting, selection, and adopting the component in any page.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> quick-list-default.png, quick-list-states.png</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4350	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	acc3cc096af0-b3ed-60c0-3201b84c3ea3	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 12:45:19	aprom	0	0
2b8c1fb76ae5-a3a8-9f4e-e8327a842beb	Remove the case-duplicate docs/classes/index.html that leaves every checkout modified	2026-10-31 12:50:51	2026-10-31 13:27:24	0	<p>The repo tracks both <code>docs/classes/Index.html</code> and <code>docs/classes/index.html</code>. On Windows (case-insensitive) they are one file, so every checkout and every Talos workspace (.runs/issue-*/prometheus) shows <code>docs/classes/Index.html</code> as modified straight after checkout. Agents then leave it uncommitted or trip over it (#4224's summary: "left docs/classes/Index.html uncommitted").</p><ul><li>Find which name the doc generator writes and remove the other one from git.</li><li>Check the doc generation step (yuidoc) doesn't recreate the duplicate.</li><li>Verify a fresh clone on Windows has a clean <code>git status</code>.</li></ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4229	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	c5cdd7846ae5-92fb-c743-55eed54e7f08	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	3cece6c06ae5-a3a8-9f4e-0d5282888995	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 13:27:24	aprom	0	0
5f0890e46afc-72fe-b62c-da0b1d983c74	Run `search reindex` every 24 hours in the Gaia containers	2026-11-17 16:22:55	2026-11-17 16:22:55	0	<p>No container runs cron today (<code>docker/dev/start.sh</code> only migrates), so scheduled CLI tasks never run. Search needs <code>php cli.php search reindex</code> once a day to backfill semantic text and catch records whose event Ares missed.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Pick a scheduler that needs no new package if possible (busybox <code>crond</code> or the base image's cron) and run it in the deployed image (<code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code>, <code>start.sh</code>) and the local stack; a crontab file in the repo (UTC), output to the container log, no overlapping runs.</li><li>Ask the reviewer whether to also enable the existing <code>workflow schedule</code> (documented as cron-driven, never run).</li><li>Document the schedule in the README; a check that the crontab lines parse.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the container's crontab runs <code>search reindex</code> daily and its output appears in the container log.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a job queue system, production infrastructure outside the images.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4658</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	4660	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	new	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	1fb236126afc-72fe-b62c-bf3c9291dd47	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Agent Nestor	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-17 16:22:55	agaia	0	0
161e51b06ae0-243e-868d-cb8afd6e32c0	ai test dev-tools: sim and nestor server tests intermittently time out on their first request (5 s urlopen timeout)	2026-10-27 11:29:26	2026-10-27 11:39:37	0	<p><b>Seen while shipping adt-4147</b> (three consecutive <code>dev-tools/ai/ai test dev-tools</code> runs on the same tree): run 1 failed <code>nestor:test_refuses_what_it_should</code>, run 2 failed <code>sim:test_resources_publish_and_sse</code>, run 3 passed. Both failures are the same trace: <code>urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=5)</code> against the test's own in-process HTTP server (<code>lib.server.serve</code> on a thread) never gets a status line and times out (<code>socket.readinto</code>). Logs: <code>dev-tools/ai/state/test-dev-tools-{nestor,sim}.log</code>.</p>\n<p><b>What</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Find the cause (candidates: the request is sent before the server thread is accepting; a previous test's server/thread still holds the port or a keep-alive connection; Windows loopback + 5 s budget too tight under the full suite's load).</li>\n<li>Make the server fixtures deterministic: bind to port 0, wait until the socket accepts before the first request, close connections in <code>tearDown</code>, and give the first request a bounded retry rather than a single 5 s timeout.</li>\n<li>Until fixed, <code>ai test</code> marks these two as unexpected, which blocks <code>ai ship</code> on an unrelated flake; a re-run is the workaround.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Depends on:</b> nothing. <b>Exit:</b> 10 consecutive <code>ai test dev-tools</code> runs with no server-test timeout.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4148	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	8fe2ae046adf-8154-4904-8f5112ed5746	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	231522376ae0-c62c-da92-aa36380e20fb	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-27 11:39:38