18d639126ad3-d9f8-3034-cf09b7a97b31	Issue status form: a translated label per language and a value derived from input	2026-10-17 21:48:08	2026-11-11 12:27:33	0	<p>The Add/Edit issue status modal (Settings &gt; Issue Statuses) takes a translated label per language, and derives the status value from input. Depends on #4098 (translations loaded on boot, supported locales service).</p>\n<h3>Backend contract</h3>\n<p>Create/update Issuestatus accepts labels with the status in one request, e.g. <code>translations: {"en-us": "In Progress"}</code>. The status value can't be changed after creation.</p>\n<h3>Scope</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>One label field per supported locale (from the locales service). <code>en-us</code> is required; others are optional.</li>\n<li>Last field: the status <b>value</b>, transformed as the user types: lowercase, spaces become <code>_</code>, anything outside <code>[a-z0-9_]</code> removed, at most 30 characters. Suggest it from the <code>en-us</code> label until the user edits it.</li>\n<li>Save sends the status and its labels in one request.</li>\n<li>On edit, the value is read-only; labels and the other fields can change.</li>\n<li>After saving, the new labels show without a reload.</li>\n<li>Labels keep rendering through the <code>status-label</code> helper (<code>views.app.issue.lists.status.&lt;name&gt;</code>, falling back to the name). Check the Settings list, board lanes, issue badges, gantt task-row, widgets and conversation-item.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Tests</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Typing "In Review 2!" gives <code>in_review_2</code>; the value is capped at 30 characters.</li>\n<li>Can't save without an <code>en-us</code> label.</li>\n<li>Create sends one request with the labels; the new label appears in the list and on the board.</li>\n<li>Value is read-only on edit; changing a label updates it everywhere.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: complex</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	3977	2026-10-25	2026-10-18	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	23eaf9c46adf-9342-d519-5077383291bf	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-27 11:30:43	aprom	0	0
33e14cf86ae0-507f-ae7e-713d912b7468	Issue types: save a type and its translated labels in one request	2026-10-27 12:16:51	2026-10-27 15:02:39	0	<p><strong>What</strong><br>Issue types become a value with a translated label per language, the same way issue statuses work (#205). Today <code>issuetypes.name</code> holds display text (<code>Change Request</code>, <code>Sub Task</code>), so it can't be translated.</p>\n<p><strong>Changes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Migration</strong>: turn every type <code>name</code> into a value (lowercase, spaces become <code>_</code>, only <code>[a-z0-9_]</code> kept, at most 30 characters; e.g. <code>Change Request</code> → <code>change_request</code>, <code>Sub Task</code> → <code>sub_task</code>). Save the old name as the type's <code>en-us</code> Translation row at <code>views.app.issue.lists.type.&lt;value&gt;</code>. Clear the cached translation files. Deletes nothing and is safe to run more than once.</li>\n<li><strong>Create and update</strong> (POST/PATCH <code>issuetype</code>): accept <code>translations</code> (locale → label), saved in the same transaction as the type so a failed label write rolls the type back.\n<ul>\n<li><code>en-us</code> is required on create; locales must be supported.</li>\n<li>The value must match <code>^[a-z0-9_]+\\z</code>, at most 30 characters.</li>\n<li>The value can't change after creation (422, including collection PATCH).</li>\n<li>Labels for a value an active system type uses need <code>setting.update</code>.</li>\n<li>A PATCH whose <code>attributes.id</code> and <code>data.id</code> differ is rejected.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong>Read</strong>: every type returns <code>translations</code>; <code>projectCount</code> still works.</li>\n<li><strong>Delete</strong>: a type's labels are deleted once no other live type uses its value.</li>\n<li><strong>Shared code</strong>: generalise <code>IssueStatusRules</code>, <code>IssueStatusLabels</code> and <code>TransactionScope</code> over a label path and reuse them rather than copying.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tests</strong>: api-tester cases mirroring the issue-status ones, plus a migration test.</p>\n<p><strong>Contract impact</strong>: <code>issuetype.name</code> is now a value and <code>translations</code> is added to its attributes. Anything matching types by display name breaks (Prometheus <code>issue-planning.js</code>, gaia MCP); see the linked issues aprom-3699 and the A Dev Tool MCP issue.</p>\n<p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: cleaning up junk types (<code>Asdf</code>, <code>D</code>); they just become <code>asdf</code> and <code>d</code>.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4152	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	in_review	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	f5a84d556ae0-dee3-8e33-646533b28507	f605b4e862c6-4e44-047e-0b80b34dd385	2026-10-27 15:02:40	agaia	0	0
df26df996ae0-2b69-ae7e-75223fbba1a7	ai test gaia: run tests/tools after the harness rewrites fixtures/default.json, as CI does	2026-10-27 12:23:59	2026-10-27 14:28:36	0	<p>Gaia CI runs <code>prepare-test-db.sh</code> before PHPUnit. The harness rewrites <code>tools/api-tester/fixtures/default.json</code> from its own hardcoded list, and the graph and api-cases checks in <code>tests/tools</code> read that file. Locally, <code>ai test gaia</code> runs PHPUnit against the committed file, so a fixture value added only to the JSON passes locally and fails CI.</p>\n<p><b>Seen on gaia#217 (agaia-4027):</b> <code>agentPermissionId</code> was added to default.json but not to the harness. The full local suite passed twice. CI failed <code>GraphExportCommandTest::testCommittedRepositoryGraphIsUpToDate</code> and <code>ScaffoldResourceTest::testScaffoldingAResourceIntoACopyOfTheSourcesIsCheckGreen</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Fix:</b> in the full run, prepare the test DB first and then run <code>tests/tools</code> on the tree the harness left, or fail when the harness output differs from the committed default.json ("fixtures/default.json differs from what prepare-test-db.sh writes: add the value to the harness"). A gaia-dev check comparing the two would also let <code>ai ship</code>'s gate catch it.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4154	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	da6f95176ae0-32bb-7641-0436ea273bfc	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-27 14:28:37	adt	0	0
9e6500146af3-a609-a385-aa1b5c5dc96c	Threads: Linked issue box shows the issue status untranslated	2026-11-10 14:56:30	2026-11-10 16:49:00	0	<p>The Linked issue box in the thread info column shows the raw issue status (e.g. <code>in_progress</code>) instead of the translated label.</p><ul><li>Render it like the issue page does (<code>components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> ~l.19): <code>status-label</code> helper for the text and <code>status-style</code> + the status class for the colour.</li><li>Check the list rows and any other place the Threads code shows an issue status for the same mistake.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> integration test: a linked issue with status <code>in_progress</code> shows the translated label. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other boxes.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4458</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 2</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> threads-fixed.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4459	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	6762e0256af3-41f4-8178-29e2ab20f3d0	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 16:49:00	aprom	0	0
940b5b786af8-c4a5-09ef-bd32e69cd0e3	Document lint as part of CI/CD: commands, the strict baseline and best practices	2026-11-14 22:58:28	2026-11-14 23:10:15	0	<p>Since aprom-4558, CI runs ESLint 9 (flat config, <code>eslint-suppressions.json</code>) and ember-template-lint 7 (<code>.lint-todo</code>) before the tests. PRs keep failing on rules nobody wrote down. You asked for this on aprom-4560.</p>\n<h4>Document</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><b>What CI runs</b> (<code>lint:js</code>, <code>lint:hbs</code>) and how to run the same thing locally. Give every command in both a <b>PowerShell</b> and a <b>bash</b> form, and say where it runs (the test container, since the checkouts have no <code>node_modules</code>).</li>\n<li><b>The strict baseline:</b>\n<ul>\n<li>A violation you fix must be removed from the baseline: <code>npm run lint:js:prune</code>, or <code>npx ember-template-lint &lt;file&gt; --clean-todo</code>. Otherwise CI fails.</li>\n<li>Editing a line that has a recorded template-lint violation makes it count as new: fix it.</li>\n<li>Never add new entries to the baseline to get a PR through.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><b>Inline disables:</b> only when the rule cannot apply, scoped to the line, with a reason. Example: Ember Data's <code>init()</code> on the issue model in #790.</li>\n<li><b>Windows line endings:</b> todos hash the template source. <code>.gitattributes</code> forces LF for <code>*.hbs</code> and <code>.lint-todo</code>. A checkout created before that rule must check its templates out again. Give the command in both PowerShell and bash.</li>\n<li><b>Common rules and how to satisfy them:</b> <code>require-button-type</code>, <code>no-invalid-interactive</code>, <code>no-builtin-form-components</code>, <code>require-input-label</code>, <code>no-mut-helper</code>, <code>ember/no-classic-classes</code>, <code>ember/no-jquery</code>, <code>ember/no-get</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Where</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>The <code>prometheus/CLAUDE.md</code> (short, a link to the detail).</li>\n<li>A <code>docs/</code> page in Prometheus for people.</li>\n<li>The workspace <code>run-tests</code> skill. That lives in the Pr4M repo, so it is a separate workspace change.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Coordinate with adt (lint in <code>ai test</code>) so the documented local command matches what <code>ai test</code> runs.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4565	2026-11-22	2026-11-15	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	2c26f3a96af8-18b0-09ef-4b5ec0f6d058	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-14 23:10:15	aprom	0	0
aa71ed286af3-a609-a385-646558a7eef8	QuickList: group/sort toolbar overflows its box instead of wrapping	2026-11-10 14:56:42	2026-11-10 15:27:25	0	<p>In the Threads QuickList, when the column is narrow, the group-by/sort toolbar (<code>QuickList::Toolbar</code>, aprom-4353) overflows the box instead of wrapping. It's a component bug, so the fix belongs in QuickList and helps every user (Ideas, Roles, Threads, the component library entry).</p><ul><li>Let the toolbar's controls wrap onto a second line (flex-wrap with a gap, right-aligned) inside the QuickList box at any width; long option labels truncate with an ellipsis rather than pushing the box wider.</li><li>Styles stay in the QuickList partial, scoped under the component's class.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a narrow col-md-3 (e.g. 1280px window) the toolbar stays inside the box on Threads, Ideas and Roles; integration test or demo state in the component library entry covers a narrow width. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> new toolbar options.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4460	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	2c29ea276af3-4381-5cc4-b0af36fd2355	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 15:27:25	aprom	0	0
7110d7966afc-72fe-b62c-e0616469e02a	External Request: Sign in to Gaia as the `ares` service client and a Gaia gateway for search fields	2026-11-17 16:23:13	2026-11-17 16:23:13	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Semantic Search", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>To store embeddings through Gaia, Ares needs its own Gaia identity: a service client of kind <code>ares</code> (Gaia D-065/D-066). Gaia lets it read a searchable record's stored <code>searchSemanticText</code>, <code>searchSemanticHash</code> and <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, and PATCH <code>{searchEmbedding, searchEmbeddingHash}</code>; Gaia answers 409 when the hash no longer matches the record's current text. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>adapters/gaia_auth.py</code>: OAuth <code>client_credentials</code> with <code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code> (env only, never logged); caches the token and refreshes before expiry or on 401.</li><li><code>adapters/gaia_client.py</code> (one class owning transport): <code>get_search_state(resource, id)</code> (the three fields above) and <code>store_embedding(resource, id, embedding, text_hash)</code> (<code>PATCH /api/v1/&lt;resource&gt;/&lt;id&gt;</code>); typed results/errors for 404, <strong>409 stale</strong>, 401/403 and 5xx.</li><li>Update <code>CLAUDE.md</code> Boundaries: Ares stays stateless but now reads from and writes to Gaia as the ares service.</li><li>Tests with a mocked HTTP transport: token reuse and refresh, 404 and 409 mapped to typed results, secrets never in logs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> against local Gaia with an ares client, Ares reads an issue's semantic text and hash and stores an embedding; a stale hash comes back as the 409 result.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the event listener.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4659</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	4662	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	new	medium	1eea33316ad5-4d5d-a602-c8a9c24d9846	67ac49466afc-72fe-b62c-106fa6a45dc7	\N	1f67df496ad5-4d5d-a602-02e2ffaeea96	Agent Nestor	Agent Nestor	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-17 16:23:13	aa	0	0
7fe41eb96af3-a609-a385-9921c10c968c	Threads: remove the 'Discussion' / 'Vote' label above the thread title	2026-11-10 14:55:59	2026-11-10 15:55:43	0	<p>The thread box shows a small uppercase type label ("Discussion") above the subject. No other page in the app has such a label, so Threads shouldn't either. It came from the spec and screen of aprom-4439; ignore it in the screens attached to the other Threads issues (vote, participants, create issue, activity).</p><ul><li>Remove the label from the thread header (and its styles and translation keys if unused). The subject is the box title (<code>h3.box-title</code>), followed by "Started by ... · date".</li><li>The room type stays visible in the list row icon and the vote body.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> no type label in the thread header for discussions or votes; tests updated. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> the list rows.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4439</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> threads-fixed.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4457	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	2e6f20d06af3-9c88-4d1f-eaa93db4da94	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 15:55:44	aprom	0	0
5a9c15876af3-a609-a385-b94985887536	Threads: remove the extra page header (title + second breadcrumb) added by the list layout	2026-11-10 14:55:22	2026-11-10 15:34:28	0	<p>The project layout <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> already renders the page header for every project page: the project name linking to the project (<code>h1 &gt; small &gt; LinkTo</code>) and the one <code>&lt;BreadCrumb/&gt;</code>. The new Threads layout (aprom-4437) added a <strong>second</strong> header with a "Threads" title and its own breadcrumb, so the breadcrumb shows twice and Threads has a title row that Task Board and Gantt Cal don't have. This came from the spec and screens of aprom-4437; ignore that header in the screens attached to the other Threads issues too.</p><ul><li>Remove only the header section the Threads templates render themselves (title row + breadcrumb, in <code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code> or wherever 4437 put it). <strong>Do not touch</strong> <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code>: the project link and the single breadcrumb stay exactly as on the Task Board.</li><li>Check the breadcrumb definitions for <code>app.project.conversation</code>, <code>.index</code> and <code>.page</code> in <code>services/breadcrumb.js</code> so the one breadcrumb shows Threads (and the thread on the page route).</li><li>Keep any button that lived in the removed header working until the next issue moves it into the QuickList header.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> Threads shows the project link and exactly one breadcrumb, like the Task Board, and no extra title row (acceptance test counts the breadcrumbs on the index and a thread page). <strong>Out of scope:</strong> New thread placement (next issue).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4437</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> threads-fixed.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-