7f56cc376afc-72fe-b62c-b47413cbb90a	External Request: Listen for `search.semantic.changed` and keep record embeddings up to date	2026-11-17 16:23:27	2026-11-17 16:23:27	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Semantic Search", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Ares creates and updates embeddings when Gaia announces a change. Gaia publishes <code>search.semantic.changed</code> through Hermes to <code>projectId: "service:ares"</code> with <code>{type, resource, recordId}</code>. Ares checks the record's dirty state, embeds the canonical text Gaia stores and sends it back with the hash of that text; Gaia rejects it with 409 if the text changed meanwhile. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>python-socketio</code> (async client; approved by the engineer). <code>adapters/hermes_listener.py</code> connects to <code>HERMES_URL</code> with the ares service token (fresh token on every reconnect), sends <code>intents:set</code> for <code>service:ares</code>/<code>search.semantic.changed</code>, reconnects with backoff; started from the FastAPI lifespan.</li><li><code>services/search_index_service.py</code>: <code>get_search_state</code>; if <code>searchSemanticHash</code> equals <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, nothing to do. Otherwise embed <code>searchSemanticText</code> with the <code>document</code> task (no own text building) and <code>store_embedding</code> with <code>searchSemanticHash</code>. <strong>409: drop the result</strong> (a newer event or the daily reindex brings the current text). 404 or empty text: skip.</li><li>Events processed through a bounded async queue with limited concurrency, duplicates within a short window collapsed; other failures logged and left for Gaia's daily reindex (no retry storm).</li><li>Tests with fake listener, Gaia client and embedder: dirty record embeds and stores with the read hash, clean record does nothing, 409 is dropped without retry, missing record skipped, embedder failure stores nothing.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the local stack, editing an issue's description gives it a new embedding within seconds; two quick edits never leave the older text's embedding stored.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> chunking long records.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aa-4661, aa-4662, agaia-4658</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	4663	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	new	medium	1eea33316ad5-4d5d-a602-c8a9c24d9846	67ac49466afc-72fe-b62c-106fa6a45dc7	\N	1f66dc406ad5-4d5d-a602-31fba0bb69e8	Agent Nestor	Agent Nestor	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-17 16:23:27	aa	0	0
658e64f16af3-1b04-8178-a1c982a9f855	OAuth2 authenticator: use Object.assign instead of the deprecated assign from @ember/polyfills	2026-11-10 16:33:41	2026-11-10 16:58:03	0	<p><code>assign</code> from <code>@ember/polyfills</code> is deprecated in Ember 4 (ID <code>ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign</code>). The only use in <code>app/</code> is the OAuth2 authenticator. Removing it is part of cutting the deprecation noise in the test runs.</p><ul><li><code>app/authenticators/oauth2.js</code>: remove the <code>import { assign } from '@ember/polyfills'</code> (line 11) and replace <code>response = assign(response, { 'expires_at': expiresAt })</code> in <code>authenticate()</code> (~line 106) with <code>Object.assign</code>. The behaviour stays the same: the response object gets <code>expires_at</code>.</li><li>Extend <code>tests/unit/authenticators/oauth2-test.js</code> to check that <code>authenticate()</code> resolves with <code>expires_at</code> when the server returns <code>expires_in</code>, if that case isn't covered yet.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>grep -r "@ember/polyfills" app tests mirage</code> finds nothing; the oauth2 unit test and the sign-in acceptance feature pass; the full suite passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> deprecations raised by addons (handled in the test helper issue and the later stack upgrade); lodash <code>_.assign</code> in <code>adapters/application.js</code> (not deprecated).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 2</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4461	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	ff5a87796af3-4f70-a2c3-fb4afe24124d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 16:58:03	aprom	0	0
88d015876afc-72fe-b62c-f22b54e8116f	External Request: p4m stack: pgvector Postgres image and Ares Gaia/Hermes settings	2026-11-17 16:23:36	2026-11-17 17:41:11	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Semantic Search", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Gaia's new search stores embeddings with the Postgres <code>vector</code> extension, and Ares now signs in to Gaia as a service and listens to Hermes. The stack <code>p4m</code> generates needs both. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>installer/p4m.py</code>: Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code> for the dev DB and gaia-test containers (same major version, existing volumes stay readable).</li><li>Ares env in the generated compose: <code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>HERMES_URL</code>, <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>/<code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code> read from <code>p4m.env</code> (secrets only there); <code>p4m configure</code> asks for them; README explains creating the ares service client and the bigger Ares image (embedding model).</li><li>Unit tests for the generated compose.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after <code>p4m up</code>, <code>CREATE EXTENSION vector</code> works in dev and test databases and Ares has its Gaia/Hermes settings.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> production infrastructure.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4664	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	pending	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	8827d1386afc-72fe-b62c-6000c7191220	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Agent Odysseus	52ee06686afc-097f-af35-04338abd1efe	2f68d74162c6-8e43-a8e0-a879eaeffc5e	2026-11-17 17:41:11	adt	0	0
97e521696ad7-b7ec-4943-4d15dfdd1cb1	Agent login: OAuth2 client_credentials grant and agent credential endpoints	2026-10-20 11:37:59	2026-10-27 14:08:47	0	<p>Part of agaia-4026 (Agents).</p><ul><li>Add the bshaffer <code>client_credentials</code> grant to <code>OAuthServer</code>; access tokens stay 1 hour and resolve to the agent user, so <code>RestController::authorize()</code> and the ACL path are unchanged.</li><li>Each agent gets its own <code>oauth_clients</code> row bound to its user; client secrets are stored hashed (override the Pdo storage's plaintext check).</li><li><code>client_credentials</code> only for type=Agent users; the <code>password</code> grant is refused for agents; accountStatus still checked, so disabling an agent cuts it off within the token lifetime.</li><li>Endpoints to issue, rotate and revoke an agent's credentials (secret shown once), as their own ACL action/resource so they can be granted separately from editing an agent.</li><li>While here: bind the parameters in <code>RestController::setUser()</code> and <code>OAuthServer::addRefreshTokenGrant</code> (currently string-concatenated SQL).</li></ul><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4027</p><h4>Changes after the UI mockups (2026-10-20)</h4><ul><li>Client ID <code>agent-&lt;handle&gt;</code>. Store who created the secret, when, and when it was last used (shown on the agent page).</li><li>Rotating revokes the previous secret at once. Give secrets a recognisable prefix (e.g. <code>p4m_cs_</code>) so leaked ones can be found by scanners.</li></ul><p>Mockups: the screenshots attached to this issue (from the 'Agents Screens' design canvas, https://claude.ai/artifact/9WYrFcT3LacRG9QLeBSQUL, private until shared).</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	4028	2026-10-27	2026-10-20	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7a626c876ad7-b7ec-4943-0da4f6053570	864a5c576ad7-b7ec-4943-13e891