b008b6246af7-3fb3-e127-cb22483be444	Convert models and routes from .extend to native classes; replace {{mut}}	2026-11-14 01:04:48	2026-11-14 23:49:18	0	<p>Several files still use the classic object model:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>23 models use <code>Model.extend({})</code>.</li>\n<li>21 routes use <code>Route.extend({})</code>.</li>\n<li><code>router.js</code>, a few serializers, a transform, a helper and a util use <code>.extend</code>.</li>\n<li>7 template calls use <code>{{mut}}</code>:\n<ul>\n<li><code>application-header.hbs</code></li>\n<li><code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code></li>\n<li><code>wiki/edit.hbs</code></li>\n<li><code>user/create.hbs</code></li>\n</ul></li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Do</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Convert them to native classes, with <code>@attr</code>/<code>@belongsTo</code>/<code>@hasMany</code> decorators for models and <code>@service</code> for injections. Drop the <code>this.get</code>/<code>set</code> calls they contain.</li>\n<li>Replace each <code>(fn (mut this.x) value)</code> with an <code>@action</code> setter on the controller or component.</li>\n<li>The full suite must stay green. No behaviour change.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Depends on 4558. Do not run it at the same time as 4555: both touch controllers.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4561	2026-11-21	2026-11-14	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	3aa773816af8-c5ce-e809-c7a0db0302ed	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-14 23:49:18	aprom	0	0
918865356afc-72fe-b62c-b577c93f29cc	Embeddings service: Gaia client for the Ares /embeddings endpoint (query embedding)	2026-11-17 16:23:45	2026-11-18 16:07:25	0	<p>Semantic search embeds the user's query at search time through Ares (<code>POST /embeddings</code>, task <code>query</code>, 768 dimensions). Like <code>core/services/LLM.php</code>, the external system sits behind one class that owns configuration and transport.</p><p><strong>Contract (Ares)</strong>: request <code>{"texts": [...], "task": "document"|"query"}</code>; 200 <code>{"model", "dimensions", "embeddings": [[...]]}</code>; 422 invalid; 503 model unavailable.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/services/Embeddings.php</code>: <code>embedQuery(string $text): array</code>; Guzzle, base URL <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL</code>, short timeout from env (~3 s).</li><li>Failures throw <code>EmbeddingsUnavailableException</code> with the reason; never an empty vector. Validates shape and dimension count.</li><li>Register it in <code>ServiceFactory</code> if that is how services are resolved.</li><li>Unit tests with a mocked Guzzle handler: success, 422, 503, timeout, malformed body, wrong dimensions.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests pass without network.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> document embeddings (Ares makes those itself).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aa-4661</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4665	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	in_review	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	1fb236126afc-72fe-b62c-bf3c9291dd47	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Agent Odysseus	8f671ec76afd-ba15-8aba-a19a17f0e784	f605b4e862c6-4e44-047e-0b80b34dd385	2026-11-18 16:07:25	agaia	0	0
6dc7b3466af3-1b04-8178-ec2cc3263e4c	Tests: hide the deprecate-assign deprecation and print one count per deprecation ID at the end of the run	2026-11-10 16:33:49	2026-11-10 17:16:27	0	<p>A full Prometheus test run writes about 18.7k deprecation stack traces: Ember's debug build sends each deprecation to <code>console.warn</code> with a stack, and testem captures all of them. That bloats the run log that <code>ai test</code>, Talos and CI read, and hides real failures. Most of them come from addons, not from <code>app/</code> code (the app's only <code>assign</code> from <code>@ember/polyfills</code> is in the oauth2 authenticator, which acceptance tests skip by logging in with <code>authenticateSession</code>). Fixing the addons belongs to a later stack upgrade. This issue hides one deprecation ID in tests and reports the rest, so the remaining IDs can be handled one by one later.</p><ul><li>In <code>tests/test-helper.js</code>, register a handler with <code>registerDeprecationHandler</code> from <code>@ember/debug</code>, before <code>start()</code>. Use no new dependency (not ember-cli-deprecation-workflow).</li><li>Keep the list of hidden deprecation IDs in a small test-support module (e.g. <code>tests/helpers/deprecations.js</code>). It holds only <code>ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign</code> for now; more IDs get added later, one at a time. For a hidden ID, count it and don't call <code>next</code>, so nothing is logged.</li><li>Count every deprecation by ID, hidden or not. Other IDs still go to <code>next</code>, so they log as before.</li><li>On <code>QUnit.done</code>, print one <code>console.log</code> line per ID with its count (e.g. <code>DEPRECATIONS ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign: 18734</code>), and print nothing when there were none.</li><li>Before the change, run the full suite and record in the PR the number of deprecation lines per ID and the log size. Record them again after the change.</li><li>Unit test for the counting and hiding logic in the helper module.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the full suite passes with the same number of tests; the run log has no stack traces for <code>ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign</code>; other deprecation IDs still log as before; the end-of-run summary lists the counts per ID; the PR shows the before and after numbers.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> hiding any deprecation ID other than <code>ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign</code>; upgrading the addons that raise the deprecations; making deprecations fail tests; hiding deprecations outside tests (dev and production builds are unchanged); ember-exam / parallel test runs.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4462	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	ca8e05116af3-6d42-8333-7a6c337d55d3	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 17:16:28	aprom	0	0
162cbbe36af2-3a5f-d015-cb59eee4ad37	Threads: check the own-reply race between the comment save and the Hermes "comment created" event	2026-11-10 08:08:54	2026-11-10 17:08:56	0	<p>Raised by the design review of aprom-4439. Believed to be already solved; this issue is to confirm it, not to change behaviour unless the check fails.</p><p><strong>The case:</strong> a user posts a reply on a thread. The layout controller's <code>saveComment</code> (<code>app/controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code>) creates the comment with <code>store.createRecord</code> and saves it. Hermes sends <code>conversation.comment.created</code> for the same comment to the same browser. If the event arrives <em>before</em> the save response, the handler (<code>handleCommentCreated</code> in <code>app/controllers/app/project/conversation/page.js</code> for the open thread, and the layout controller's handler for other rooms) calls <code>peekOrPush</code> (<code>app/utils/live/collection.js</code>), which pushes a record with the server id. When the save then resolves, Ember Data assigns the same id to the record made by <code>createRecord</code>. That can assert ("id already exists") or show the reply twice.</p><p>If the save response wins, there is no problem: the loader dedups by record identity.</p><p><strong>To check:</strong></p><ul><li>Whether the event can reach the sender before the save response (Gaia publishes after commit; does Hermes exclude the sender, and does the envelope carry the actor?).</li><li>What Ember Data (the version in Prometheus) does when a pushed record and a saving new record end up with the same id.</li><li>Whether an existing guard already covers it (the composer's pending comments, <code>peekOrPush</code>, the Hermes service).</li><li>The same path on the issue page comments (<code>app/components/issue/issue-details.js</code> <code>saveComment</code> and its live handlers).</li></ul><p><strong>Outcome:</strong> a unit test that delivers the created event before the save resolves and shows one comment and no error. If it fails, a fix proposal (for example ignoring a created event from the current user while a post is pending) as a separate issue.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing the thread page or the comment components.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4449	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae8215b05acb-1902-6b9c-d7cf4132daaf	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	0e54fbc56af3-bc7c-a2c3-d24fdd027510	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 17:08:56	aprom	0	0
99f093196afc-72fe-b62c-323b5f1ee106	Search core: exact, FTS and fuzzy searchers with module ACL scope and rank fusion	2026-11-17 16:23:53	2026-11-17 16:23:53	0	<p>The domain layer for module-agnostic search, driven by the <code>search</code> metadata via <code>SearchableRegistry</code>. Every search runs all matching kinds; the caller only gives types and the query. The HTTP controller is the next issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong> in <code>core/libs/search/</code>:</p><ul><li><code>SearchRequest</code>: types, query text (trimmed, 2-200 chars), limit (default 20, max 50).</li><li><code>ExactMatcher</code>: rows whose <code>exact</code> fields equal the query (type-aware: numeric fields match only an integer query, also <code>#123</code>); pinned first.</li><li><code>FtsSearcher</code>: <code>websearch_to_tsquery</code> against the model's system <code>searchVector</code> column (same text search config), <code>ts_rank_cd</code>, snippet via <code>ts_headline</code> on the display snippet field.</li><li><code>FuzzySearcher</code>: <code>pg_trgm</code> <code>word_similarity</code> on fuzzy fields, threshold from config (default 0.3).</li><li><code>RankFusion</code>: Reciprocal Rank Fusion (k = 60) over each searcher's ranked ids, open to more searchers (semantic comes later); items carry <code>matchedBy</code> and the fused score; exact matches stay on top.</li><li><code>SearchService</code>: per type require <code>&lt;module&gt;.get</code> through <code>Acl</code> (denied type = 403, as for unauthorized query criteria, D-027); apply the module's record scope (<code>Acl::applyRecordScope</code>, <code>acl.groupKeys</code>, D-060) and <code>deleted = 0</code> inside each candidate query, before ranking and LIMIT (D-022). A searcher is skipped for a type when the user lacks read on a field it matches; denied display fields are omitted. Bound parameters only.</li><li>Tests: ranking order, exact pin, typo tolerance, a members-scope user never sees other projects' issues, field-ACL skip.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>SearchService</code> returns fused, ACL-scoped Issue results from exact, FTS and fuzzy matching.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> semantic matching, the HTTP endpoint.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4656</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	4666	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	new	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	1fb236126afc-72fe-b62c-bf3c9291dd47	\N	cbb506d05acd-06d6-1141-68969b9fd562	Agent Nestor	Agent Nestor	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-17 16:23:54	agaia	0	0
8f5c72366af0-b3ed-60c0-4f4eeb5adfb4	QuickList: assemble pagination, grouping, toolbar and selection into the root	2026-11-08 11:48:31	2026-11-08 13:45:57	0	<p>The root <code>QuickList</code> and its standalone parts (pagination, group heading + <code>group-items</code> helper, toolbar, select-all + selection bar) were built separately. This issue connects them into one component and imports their style partials. The attached screens are a guide only.</p><ul><li><code>components/quick-list/index.{hbs,js}</code>: new arguments <code>@page</code>, <code>@limit</code>, <code>@onPage</code> (renders <code>QuickList::Pagination</code> under the items, disabled while <code>@isLoading</code>); <code>@groupOptions</code> (<code>[{key, label, groupKey, groupLabel}]</code>), <code>@groupBy</code>, <code>@onGroup</code>, <code>@sortOptions</code>, <code>@sort</code>, <code>@order</code>, <code>@onSort</code> (render <code>QuickList::Toolbar</code> under the search when any options are given). When <code>@groupBy</code> is set, items are grouped with <code>groupItems</code> and rendered in <code>QuickList::Group</code>; collapsed groups are remembered per groupBy for the component's lifetime; a <code>&lt;:group as |group|&gt;</code> block passes through to the heading.</li><li>Selection: <code>@selectable</code> adds a checkbox before each <code>QuickList::Item</code> body (<code>fa-square-o</code> / crimson <code>fa-check-square</code>, checked rows <code>#f9fafc</code>; clicking it doesn't follow the row link) and <code>QuickList::SelectAll</code> in the toolbar's <code>&lt;:start&gt;</code>. While anything is selected, <code>QuickList::SelectionBar</code> replaces the toolbar with the <code>&lt;:selectionActions as |selected clear|&gt;</code> block. QuickList keeps the selected ids, reports them via <code>@onSelect(ids)</code>, and clears them when <code>@items</code> changes to another page or search.</li><li>Import the partials <code>styles/components/quick-list/_pagination.scss</code>, <code>_group.scss</code>, <code>_toolbar.scss</code>, <code>_selection.scss</code> from <code>quick-list.scss</code>. Update the YUIDoc contract.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for paging, grouped rendering with counts and collapse, group/sort callbacks, selection (rows, select-all states, bar swap, yielded actions, clearing on new items).</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: selecting across pages, shift-click ranges.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4350, aprom-4351, aprom-4352, aprom-4353, aprom-4354</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> quick-list-default.png, quick-list-selection-grouped.png, quick-list-states.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4357	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	cca805e06af0-e26d-d494-87c189cef688	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 13:45:57	aprom	0	0
8ed57f476adc-9973-8304-7fdbae5e2693	Talos: give Nestor the images referenced in idea messages	2026-10-24 07:17:34	2026-10-27 14:57:38	0	<p>Engineers will attach screenshots to idea messages (Prometheus issue of this plan). This issue waits on <strong>agaia-4106</strong> (upload download 404), which must be fixed first. Nestor only sees message bodies as text, so an image reference means nothing to it unless Talos hands over the file. Nestor can Read image files and see them.</p><ul><li><strong>Contract (shared with the Prometheus issue of this plan):</strong> an image in a message body is <code>![&lt;file name&gt;](upload:&lt;uploadId&gt;)</code>.</li><li><code>talos/lib/ideas/conversation.py</code> <code>_prompt</code> (~l.55): for the new messages and the replayed history, find <code>upload:&lt;id&gt;</code> image references. Download each with <code>client.download</code> (<code>lib/ideas/client.py</code> -&gt; <code>lib/tracker.py</code> <code>download</code>) into <code>&lt;LOCAL_DIR&gt;/talos/state/ideas/&lt;ideaId&gt;/images/&lt;uploadId&gt;.&lt;ext&gt;</code>, cached so an image is downloaded once. Build the path from <code>LOCAL_DIR</code>, not the module folder (runtime copy rule). In the prompt, replace the reference with e.g. <code>[image "&lt;name&gt;": &lt;absolute path&gt;]</code>.</li><li>A failed download doesn't fail the turn: the reference becomes <code>[image "&lt;name&gt;" could not be downloaded]</code>, and the failure is logged.</li><li><code>talos/agents/nestor/role.md</code>: one line saying that engineer messages can reference images by path and that Nestor should Read them when they matter to the plan. Check that <code>agents/nestor/agent.json</code> allows Read on that folder (its deny list only blocks <code>state/*.db</code> and <code>state/logs</code>).</li><li>Windows and Linux per <code>dev-tools/CLAUDE.md</code>: <code>pathlib</code>, binary writes, no shell.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests (no network, temp dirs) cover: a reference is downloaded once and rewritten to its path; history replay rewrites too; a failed download yields the placeholder and the turn goes on; a message without images is unchanged. A manual run shows Nestor describing a pasted screenshot.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> images in Nestor's own replies (it has nestor-screen), cleanup of old image files, the standalone Nestor UI and sim.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4106</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4115	2026-10-31	2026-10-24	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	e6b8c9706ad9-192a-43e2-651b129a8936	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	dc0f60f96ae0-f6b3-bba4-3bd37bc084f6	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-27 14:57:38	adt	0	0
dde3d1446ae0-36a5-29af-265631b3afdd	Talos: per-issue workspaces (.runs/issue-N with a git worktree), ai follows P4M_WORKSPACE	2026-10-27 16:18:37	2026-10-27 21:02:44	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. Every Talos run works in the one checkout: <code>talos/lib/runner.py</code> <code>run()</code> starts Claude with <code>cwd=WORKSPACE</code>, and <code>ai start</code> (<code>ai/lib/workflow.py</code> <code>sync_dev</code>/<code>cmd_start</code>) checks out <code>dev</code> and then <code>claude-issue-N</code> inside <code>Pr4M/&lt;repo&gt;</code>. Two runs would switch branches under each other.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Talos creates <code>&lt;workspace&gt;/.runs/issue-N/</code> with: <code>&lt;repo&gt;/</code> as a <code>git worktree</code> of the main repo on <code>claude-issue-N</code>; <code>dev-tools</code> as a junction (Windows) or symlink (Linux) to the runtime copy; <code>CLAUDE.md</code>. The workspace is sticky: it lives until the issue is finished (uncommitted work survives a needs_input pause).</li>\n<li>Claude runs with that folder as cwd (it has to be the cwd, so Read/Edit on <code>gaia/...</code> hit the worktree), so <code>dev-tools/ai/ai</code> paths, prompts and <code>allowedTools</code> don't change. <code>runner.run</code> takes a <code>cwd</code>; Talos sets <code>P4M_WORKSPACE</code> for the run.</li>\n<li><code>ai</code> (<code>ai/lib/common.py</code> <code>WORKSPACE</code>/<code>repo_dir</code>) resolves repos from <code>P4M_WORKSPACE</code> when set; per-machine files stay under <code>LOCAL_DIR</code>.</li>\n<li><code>sync_dev</code>/<code>cmd_start</code> fetch and branch from <code>origin/&lt;base&gt;</code> without checking out <code>dev</code> in a shared folder (git refuses one branch in two worktrees, a free per-issue lock).</li>\n<li>Interactive use without <code>P4M_WORKSPACE</code> behaves as today.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Done when</strong>: two issues in the same repo can be started one after the other and each keeps its own branch and uncommitted changes; works on Windows (junction) and Linux (symlink); unit tests cover workspace creation and the env override.</p>\n<p>Depends on: none</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4158	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	bcb698486ae0-36a5-29af-ebb1949fa852	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	ef08bae16ae1-5e79-b6bb-de6ed1be52ad	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-27 21:02:44	adt	0	0
b98946236af3-3341-a2c3-ef94b54cd8d1	Own comment shown twice when the Hermes "comment created" event beats the save response	2026-11-10 16:43:37	2026-11-10 17:11:31	0	<p>Found by aprom-4449. When a user posts a comment, Gaia publishes <code>conversation.comment.created</code> to Hermes inside the request (<code>LiveEventsComponent::afterCreate</code>, before the response is sent), and Hermes emits it to the whole room (<code>io.to(room)</code>), the sender's socket included. The sender's browser therefore usually gets the event <em>before</em> its own <code>comment.save()</code> resolves. The Hermes service's local-echo guard (<code>noteLocalWrite</code>/<code>isLocalEcho</code>) does not help: nothing calls <code>noteLocalWrite</code>, and the id of a new comment is not known until the save returns.</p><p><strong>What happens (Ember Data 4.1):</strong> no assertion. The live handler pushes a record with the server id (<code>peekOrPush</code> on the thread page and layout, <code>store.findRecord</code> on the issue page); when the save resolves, the <code>createRecord</code> record gets the same id. The store then holds two <code>comment</code> records for one comment:</p><ul><li>Open thread (<code>conversation/page.js</code> <code>handleCommentCreated</code> + <code>postComment</code>): the reply is shown twice (<code>ThreadComments.add</code> dedups by record identity).</li><li>Issue page (<code>issue/page.js</code> <code>applyCommentCreated</code> + <code>issue-details.js</code> <code>_createComment</code>, which uses <code>pushObject</code>): the reply is listed twice.</li><li>Other listed room (layout <code>handleCommentCreated</code> + <code>saveComment</code>): listed once (<code>pushIfMissing</code> dedups by id) but the store still has the duplicate record.</li></ul><p>Reproduced by <code>tests/unit/live/own-reply-race-test.js</code> (three <code>test.todo</code> cases, added by aprom-4449). The fix turns them into plain tests.</p><p><strong>Options:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Recommended:</strong> skip a <code>conversation.comment.created</code> whose <code>actorId</code> is the current user while this tab has a comment post pending in that room; the save result adds the comment. Keeps the store at one record. Needs a small "pending own posts" tracker (per room) shared by the three handlers, and care for the same user in another tab (no pending post there, so the event still applies).</li><li>Dedup by id where the save result is added (<code>ThreadComments.add</code>, <code>_createComment</code>): fixes the double listing but leaves two store records with one id, which later <code>peekRecord</code>/updates can hit.</li><li>After the save resolves, unload the pushed duplicate and swap it in the lists: works but fights Ember Data's identity map.</li></ol><p>Complexity: complex because the guard's shape (where the pending set lives, multi-tab behaviour) is a design choice.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4463	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	new	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	433244346af3-89a1-8333-e57c9082233a	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-10 16:43:37	aprom	0	0
066ca2b16ae0-008b-29af-7b40c7980fe1	Talos: dispatcher worker pool with concurrency caps, slot leases and shared-state locks	2026-10-27 16:19:18	2026-10-28 06:31:13	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. <code>talos/lib/dispatcher.py</code> is a serial worker per agent ("its runs share working trees and the local stack"). With per-issue workspaces (adt-4158) and test slots (adt-4159) runs can overlap.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>N worker threads per agent instead of one; the existing <code>_pending</code> set still drops duplicates of an issue. Each job leases a free test slot before it runs and releases it after (slot passed to the run's environment for <code>ai test --slot</code>).</li>\n<li><code>agent.json</code>: <code>maxParallel</code> (default 1 = today's behaviour), <code>maxParallelByRepo</code> and <code>maxParallelByModel</code> (opus 1 by default).</li>\n<li>Queue order: resumptions (<code>in_review</code>, <code>feedback</code>, <code>pending</code>) first, then issue priority, then first-in first-out.</li>\n<li>File lock (or per-issue files) for <code>ai/state/timers.json</code>; a <code>dev-stack</code> lock for browser checks against the shared dev stack (gaia-dev, Prometheus on :4200).</li>\n<li><code>talos status</code> lists every run in flight.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Done when</strong>: with <code>maxParallel: 3</code>, three assigned issues run at once, each in its own workspace and slot, and the caps are respected; unit tests cover lease/release, caps and ordering.</p>\n<p>Depends on: #4158, #4159</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4162	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	bcb698486ae0-36a5-29af-ebb1949fa852	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	2790cb126ae1-4dea-a6de-12c80e324fe9	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 06:31:14	adt	0	0
