6cb7b2b26afc-23ae-1683-a4cdd239863d	ACL: sort/groupBy and fields= expressions bypass field ACL and system-field checks	2026-11-17 16:53:00	2026-11-17 16:53:00	0	<p>Found during the review of #4653 (system fields, D-071). This gap is older than that change: it also affects field ACL (D-033/D-036).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>sort / groupBy:</b> <code>Acl::getClauseFieldReferences()</code> only reads the leading identifier of each comma-separated part.\n<ul>\n<li><code>(Model.field)</code> and <code>LENGTH(Model.field)</code> slip past the field-ACL 403 and the system-field 400.</li>\n<li><code>Clause::prepareOrderBy</code> and <code>prepareGroupBy</code> pass them on to PHQL unvalidated. That lets a client sort or group on a denied or hidden column, which works as an oracle on its values.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><b>fields= / count:</b> <code>Acl::parseSelectColumn()</code> returns null for anything other than a plain <code>Alias.field</code>, and <code>filterAuthorizedFields()</code> keeps those columns unfiltered.\n<ul>\n<li>Affected forms: <code>FUNC(Model.field) AS x</code>, <code>Model.*</code>, <code>rel.*</code> and bare names.</li>\n<li>Most are probably stripped later on output by <code>applyACLOnFields</code>. Expression aliases are not, because <code>getAliasByFields</code> splits on <code>.</code>.</li>\n</ul></li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Suggested fix:</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Allow only plain <code>[alias.]field [ASC|DESC]</code> sort/group parts, and return 400 for any other form.</li>\n<li>In <code>filterAuthorizedFields</code>, expand <code>Alias.*</code> against the metadata, minus denied and system fields.</li>\n<li>Drop or reject expression columns that reference a denied or system field.</li>\n<li>Add unit tests and api-tester cases for each form.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Design decision for the reviewer: reject expressions outright (simpler, could break clients that use them), or parse them and check every token.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4669	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	new	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-17 16:53:01	agaia	0	0
e2b041f26ae0-36a5-29af-69cdb5b54413	p4m test: test slots, each with its own test database (from a template) and slot-keyed test containers	2026-10-27 16:18:42	2026-10-27 21:24:52	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. <code>installer/testenv.py</code> already starts per-checkout test containers (<code>p4m-test-gaia-&lt;hash&gt;</code>), but they copy gaia-test's env, so every one uses <code>DB_NAME=pr4m_test</code> on the same Postgres: two gaia suites at once corrupt each other's data. adt-4143 added a <code>pr4m_test</code> lock in <code>ai test</code> that serialises them today.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>A fixed set of slots 1..N (config). Slot k owns database <code>pr4m_test_k</code>, created with <code>CREATE DATABASE … TEMPLATE</code> from a migrated and seeded template database and reset from it when leased (seconds, no re-seeding).</li>\n<li>Slot k's test containers are keyed by slot instead of by checkout path, with <code>DB_NAME</code> overridden; a checkout is synced into the slot (changed files only, as today).</li>\n<li><code>p4m test slots setup|status|reset</code>; <code>p4m test --slot k</code> (and <code>ai test --slot k</code>) runs a checkout in that slot. The <code>pr4m_test</code> lock becomes per-slot.</li>\n<li>Without <code>--slot</code> everything behaves as today; <code>p4m test clean</code> also removes slot containers.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Done when</strong>: two gaia suites run at the same time in two slots without touching each other's data; the template is rebuilt when migrations or seeds change; unit tests (fake docker, as in <code>test_testenv.py</code>) cover slot naming, DB override and reset.</p>\n<p>Depends on: none</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4159	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	bcb698486ae0-36a5-29af-ebb1949fa852	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75