c11000f36af3-8d6f-4330-0481e1967780	Threads: section.content is nested twice	2026-11-10 18:30:25	2026-11-10 18:52:30	0	<p>The project layout <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> already wraps every project page in <code>&lt;section class="content"&gt;{{outlet}}&lt;/section&gt;</code>. <code>templates/app/project/conversation.hbs</code> opens another <code>&lt;section class="content"&gt;</code> around the Threads row, so the DOM has <code>section.content &gt; section.content &gt; div.row.conversation-wrapper</code> and AdminLTE's <code>.content</code> padding applies twice. No other <code>app/project/*</code> template does this (Task Board, Gantt start directly with their content).</p><ul><li>Remove the inner <code>&lt;section class="content"&gt;</code> wrapper from <code>conversation.hbs</code>; the template starts with the <code>.row.conversation-wrapper</code> (keep any modal/in-element markup that lived inside the section).</li><li>Check <code>conversation-loading.hbs</code> and the Threads child templates (<code>conversation/index.hbs</code>, <code>conversation/page.hbs</code>) for the same wrapper; check any styles that targeted the nested section.</li><li>Leave <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the Threads page has exactly one <code>section.content</code> (acceptance test asserts the count) and the list starts at the same left/top offset as the Task Board. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> other pages.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4455</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 2</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4464	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	016ffdb66af2-3028-5ed1-e8572ffabaa7	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	43c829896af3-15a1-4330-4cec7f054cbc	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 18:52:30	aprom	0	0
296baee06af3-9aaa-2a4b-e369d970d3d9	Acceptance and unit tests for the auth flows, run against ember-simple-auth before it is replaced	2026-11-10 18:53:29	2026-11-10 19:47:31	0	<p><strong>Why:</strong> we are replacing ember-simple-auth (ESA) with a native session service (see the switch issue in milestone aga-Auth). A throwaway replacement passed the whole suite (1337 tests), which shows the suite does not exercise the real auth paths. These tests are the safety net: they must pass on ESA <em>now</em>, and unchanged after the switch.</p>\n<p><strong>Gaps today:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The sign-in feature step "User click on signin button" calls <code>authenticateSession</code> directly; no test signs in successfully through the form and <code>authenticator:oauth2</code>. Only the inactive-user scenario submits the form, and that covers a failure.</li>\n<li>Tests use ESA's in-memory store, so restoring a persisted session at boot is never run.</li>\n<li>Deep-link redirect after sign-in is only unit-tested with a stubbed router.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Add (Gherkin on Mirage where it's a user flow, unit tests otherwise):</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Successful sign-in through the form: fill email/password, submit, Mirage <code>/token</code> returns a token, user lands on <code>/app</code> and the session holds <code>access_token</code>, <code>refresh_token</code> and <code>expires_at</code>.</li>\n<li>Deep link: visiting <code>/app/project/&lt;code&gt;</code> signed out goes to <code>/signin</code>; after signing in the user lands on the deep link (regression for aprom-3362). A stored <code>/signin</code> URL is ignored and the user lands on <code>/app</code>.</li>\n<li>Signed-in user visiting <code>/signin</code> is sent to <code>/app</code>.</li>\n<li>Sign-out: session is no longer authenticated and an authenticated route redirects to <code>/signin</code> (extend the existing sign-out feature if it fits).</li>\n<li>Expired access token: the first API request triggers one refresh_token POST and is sent with the new token.</li>\n<li>401 from the API forces a refresh and the request is retried once (adapter <code>ajax</code> retry path).</li>\n<li>Refresh fails (Mirage <code>/token</code> returns 400): the session is invalidated.</li>\n<li>Unit: restoring from a persisted session (store holds <code>authenticated</code> with <code>authenticator:oauth2</code>) authenticates the session; a persisted session without <code>access_token</code> does not.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Keep existing regression tests for multi-tab refresh (aprom-4181) and cross-tab post-auth routing (aprom-3943) passing; add a case if one is missing.</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong> test through public behaviour (routes, DOM, the <code>session</code> service's public API: <code>isAuthenticated</code>, <code>data</code>, <code>authenticate</code>, <code>invalidate</code>), not ESA internals, so the same tests run unchanged after the switch. Put ESA's <code>test-support</code> imports behind one helper module (<code>tests/helpers/session.js</code>) re-exporting <code>authenticateSession</code>, <code>currentSession</code>, <code>invalidateSession</code>, so the switch changes one file. Add a Mirage <code>/token</code> handler for password and refresh_token grants if the current one doesn't cover them.</p>\n<p><strong>Done when:</strong> the new tests pass on ESA and the full suite stays green. No app code changes.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4466	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	0691c6036af3-9aaa-2a4b-eff9d4d60f47	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	ab5ae5d96af3-9aaa-2a4b-d8d08ad3b31c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 19:40:03	aprom	0	0
e7762fd96ae0-36a5-29af-a9a44ecee074	Talos: pause the queue on Claude usage/rate limits instead of failing the issue	2026-10-27 16:18:47	2026-10-28 05:23:58	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. Today a run that hits a Claude usage or rate limit ends as an error: <code>talos/lib/dispatcher.py</code> counts it as an iteration, comments "run failed" and hands the issue back as <code>pending</code>. With several runs in flight one limit would fail them all.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Recognise a usage/rate-limit result from <code>claude -p</code> (first capture a real one from <code>state/logs/</code> to learn its exact shape; keep the matcher in <code>policy.py</code>, pure and tested).</li>\n<li>On a limit: stop dispatching until the reset time in the result (or an exponential backoff when none is given); re-queue the issue without counting the iteration (<code>runs</code> unchanged, the run row records outcome <code>limited</code>); log the pause; comment on the issue once only if the pause is longer than a configurable number of hours.</li>\n<li>Optional: rolling 5-hour and 7-day spend thresholds from the <code>runs</code> table that lower concurrency as spend approaches them, and time-of-day caps in config (fuller effect once the dispatcher pool exists).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Done when</strong>: a simulated limit result leaves the issue assigned to the agent and queued, its iteration count unchanged, and dispatch resumes after the reset time; unit tests cover detection and the re-queue.</p>\n<p>Depends on: none (useful with serial runs already)</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4160	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	bcb698486ae0-36a5-29af-ebb1949fa852	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	bcc628146ae1-12f0-205e-c98cb2129c5e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 05:23:58	adt	0	0
1a29c3876ae0-008b-29af-9ea70dd23e5c	Talos: runner interface with a container backend (phase B)	2026-10-27 16:19:38	2026-10-28 07:20:05	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. After phase A, runs are isolated locally. Phase B lets the same job execute in a container, so agents can run on any Docker host that reaches Gaia, Hermes, the odysseus git remote and the Anthropic API.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Extract a <code>Runner</code> interface from <code>talos/lib/runner.py</code>: <code>LocalRunner</code> (phase A: per-issue workspace + slot) and <code>ContainerRunner</code>.</li>\n<li><code>ContainerRunner</code>: an image with the Claude CLI, node, python and the dev-tools runtime; it is given the Claude token, the agent's <code>GAIA_*</code> credentials and the Odysseus git token (never baked into the image); it clones the repo, runs tests against a configured Docker host, and returns the outcome JSON on stdout as <code>claude -p</code> does today.</li>\n<li>A per-issue volume for <code>~/.claude</code> keeps sessions resumable; without it runs use the existing cold-resume catch-up.</li>\n<li>The runner is chosen per agent in <code>agent.json</code>. Talos stays the single coordinator (Hermes listener, policy, tracker writes, <code>talos.db</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Done when</strong>: one issue runs end to end in a container on the local Docker host with the same tracker outcome and <code>runs</code> row as a local run; credentials handling is documented in the Talos README.</p>\n<p>Depends on: #4162</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4164	2026-11-03	2026-10-27	done	low	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	bcb698486ae0-36a5-29af-ebb1949fa852	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	f01f12a06ae1-cc32-dd79-c57a766bc2c4	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 07:20:05	adt	0	0
2e632a696af3-9aaa-2a4b-95393872f14f	Auth status page and persisted auth event log, reachable without signing in	2026-11-10 18:53:34	2026-11-10 19:56:56	0	<p><strong>Why:</strong> before we replace ember-simple-auth (see the switch issue in milestone aga-Auth), we need a way to see what auth is doing when signing in is broken. This lands first, on ESA, so ESA and the native session can be compared on the same page.</p>\n<p><strong>Auth event log</strong> (e.g. <code>app/utils/auth/auth-log.js</code>):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A ring buffer of the last ~100 events persisted in localStorage (own key, e.g. <code>prometheus_auth_log</code>), so it survives reloads and redirect loops. Each entry: timestamp, tab id, event name, small detail object.</li>\n<li>Events: sign-in started / succeeded / failed (error key only), session restored / restore rejected, refresh started / skipped (already fresh) / succeeded / failed (status), cross-tab lock waited / acquired, cross-tab session update received, invalidated (local or cross-tab), 401 retry in the adapter, post-auth navigation destination.</li>\n<li>Hooks go in <code>services/session.js</code>, <code>authenticators/oauth2.js</code> and <code>adapters/application.js</code> as one-line calls; the log is its own module (single responsibility), the session doesn't format or store entries.</li>\n<li><strong>Never log tokens, passwords or client secrets.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Status page:</strong> public route <code>/auth-status</code>, added to <code>ENV.publicRoutes</code> so the application route skips the auth redirect. AdminLTE box layout per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>. Shows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Session: authenticated yes/no, authenticator, access token present (redacted, e.g. last 4 chars), refresh token present, <code>expires_at</code> as a time plus "expires in", token type and scope.</li>\n<li>Last refresh result and error, last cross-tab event.</li>\n<li>The event log, newest first, with a copy-to-clipboard button for bug reports.</li>\n<li>A "Clear session and sign in again" button: removes the session storage key (<code>ember_simple_auth-session</code>) and the refresh lock key, then reloads at <code>/signin</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Reads only the <code>session</code> service's public API (<code>isAuthenticated</code>, <code>data</code>) and the log module, so it keeps working unchanged after the switch.</p>\n<p><strong>Tests:</strong> unit tests for the log (ring size, persistence, redaction); an acceptance test that <code>/auth-status</code> renders signed out and signed in, and that the clear button empties the session.</p>\n<p><strong>Done when:</strong> the page works signed out and signed in on the dev stack, and the full suite is green.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4467	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	0691c6036af3-9aaa-2a4b-eff9d4d60f47	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	bd05cd136af3-9aaa-2a4b-b146afd8785b	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 19:56:57	aprom	0	0
686234c26afc-72fe-b62c-9f5ddad9cd12	External Request: Run nomic-embed-text in-process and serve POST /embeddings	2026-11-17 16:23:04	2026-11-18 10:11:13	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Semantic Search", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Gaia is adding semantic search. Ares will compute all embeddings itself with the <code>nomic-embed-text</code> model running inside Ares (no external model server): for records (from search events, a later issue) and for search queries, which Gaia sends over HTTP. Please accept, adapt or decline the contract.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li><code>POST /embeddings</code> request <code>{"texts": ["..."], "task": "document"|"query"}</code>; 1 to 64 non-empty texts of at most 8000 characters; 422 otherwise.</li><li>200 <code>{"model": "nomic-embed-text-v1.5", "dimensions": 768, "embeddings": [[...]]}</code>, same order, L2-normalised. 503 with a clear message if the model is not loaded; never a fake vector.</li><li>Ares adds the task prefixes (<code>search_document: </code> / <code>search_query: </code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New dependency <code>fastembed</code> (ONNX Runtime, CPU, no PyTorch; approved by the engineer for this feature).</li><li><code>routers/embeddings.py</code> (Pydantic only) -&gt; <code>services/embedding_service.py</code> (reused by the search listener) -&gt; <code>adapters/base_embedding_adapter.py</code> + <code>adapters/fastembed_adapter.py</code> via the factory. Model loaded once; inference in a thread pool so async routes are not blocked.</li><li>Env <code>EMBEDDING_MODEL</code> (default <code>nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5</code>), <code>EMBEDDING_CACHE_DIR</code>, thread count. <code>Dockerfile</code> downloads the weights at build time; <code>/health</code> reports the model loaded.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter: validation, prefixes, order, 503.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the built image returns 768-dimension vectors offline; tests pass without downloading the model.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> GPU, other models, result caching.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4661	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	1eea33316ad5-4d5d-a602-c8a9c24d9846	67ac49466afc-72fe-b62c-106fa6a45dc7	\N	1f66dc406ad5-4d5d-a602-31fba0bb69e8	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	b93548116afc-6695-b4da-fa4ad55f760f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 10:11:13	aa	0	0
45cf2ac26af3-9aaa-2a4b-f2cd12fb4af8	Replace ember-simple-auth with a native session service	2026-11-10 18:53:57	2026-11-10 20:40:35	0	<p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4466 (auth flow tests) and aprom-4467 (auth status page and event log). Both must be merged first; this issue rewrites <code>services/session.js</code>, which 4467 also touches.</p>\n<p><strong>Why:</strong> ember-simple-auth (ESA) 4.x pins us to old peer dependencies and blocks the Ember upgrade (4.1 to 6.12 LTS). Our session code already owns token refresh and cross-tab locking, and reaches into ESA private internals (<code>this.get('session')</code>, <code>store.restore/persist</code>, <code>_validate</code>, <code>_absolutizeExpirationTime</code>, <code>Configuration</code>) that change between ESA majors. Owning ~400 lines removes the dependency. Use only APIs present in both Ember 4.1 and 6.12 (native classes, <code>@tracked</code>, router service, <code>fetch</code>; no Evented or mixins).</p>\n<p><strong>A throwaway proved it:</strong> the full suite (1337 tests) passed with ESA removed. The diff is attached to this issue (<code>native-auth-throwaway.diff</code>). Port it properly; don't paste it.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>app/services/session.js</code>: native <code>Service</code> with <code>@tracked isAuthenticated</code> and <code>data</code>. Owns what ESA's internal session did: <code>setup()</code> (restore, then enable handlers), <code>authenticate(name, ...args)</code>, <code>invalidate()</code>, <code>requireAuthentication</code> (keeps and later retries <code>attemptedTransition</code>), <code>prohibitAuthentication</code>, <code>handleAuthentication</code> (existing post-auth destination rules), <code>handleInvalidation</code> (reload at rootURL, skipped in tests), cross-tab session sync. Keep <code>ensureFreshToken</code>, single-flight and the cross-tab lock unchanged.</li>\n<li><code>app/authenticators/oauth2.js</code>: plain <code>EmberObject</code>; own form-encoded <code>makeRequest</code> (rejects with the response carrying <code>responseJSON</code>, as the sign-in controller expects); <code>restore</code> resolves any data with an access token (expired too); no refresh scheduling.</li>\n<li>Session stores: localStorage store with <code>storage</code>-event sync, and an in-memory store used in tests. Plain classes; split persistence from the session per SRP.</li>\n<li><code>routes/application.js</code>: <code>await this.session.setup()</code> first in <code>beforeModel</code> (ESA's deprecated initializer did this implicitly).</li>\n<li><code>tests/helpers/session.js</code> (from 4466): implement <code>authenticateSession</code>, <code>currentSession</code>, <code>invalidateSession</code> natively with a test authenticator.</li>\n<li>Remove <code>ember-simple-auth</code> from <code>package.json</code>. Replace <code>ENV['ember-simple-auth']</code> with a Prometheus config key. Keep the 4467 log hooks.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rollback compatibility (must keep):</strong> the localStorage key <code>ember_simple_auth-session</code> and the persisted shape <code>{ authenticated: { authenticator: 'authenticator:oauth2', access_token, refresh_token, expires_at, ... } }</code> stay exactly as ESA writes them. Signed-in users then stay signed in across the switch, and reverting this issue's PR restores ESA with no migration.</p>\n<p><strong>Done when:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The full suite and the 4466 tests pass unchanged (only <code>tests/helpers/session.js</code> changes).</li>\n<li>Manual check on the dev stack, using <code>/auth-status</code> to watch: sign in; reload stays signed in; already-signed-in session from before the deploy survives; second tab follows sign-in and sign-out; deep link while signed out returns there after sign-in; token near expiry refreshes once across two tabs; sign-out reloads to sign-in.</li>\n<li>No <code>ember-simple-auth</code> modules in the build.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4468	2026-11-17	2026-11-10	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	0691c6036af3-9aaa-2a4b-eff9d4d60f47	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	86f06ba76af3-be4d-e565-dfcfdaa82aee	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 20:36:27	aprom	0	0
0bc53c866ae1-affe-9a2f-90beb4dcc1d8	Talos: DependencyGate class, unreadable vs unmet dependencies, release off the Hermes thread	2026-10-28 07:28:11	2026-10-28 08:16:44	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups 1-5 from the PR comment on adt-4161 (dev-tools#43).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Extract a <code>DependencyGate</code> class from <code>talos/lib/dispatcher.py</code> that owns the held set and the comment-once memory. Move <code>parse_dependencies</code> so that <code>policy</code> doesn't need to import the tracker.</li><li>Tell an unreadable dependency (Gaia error) apart from one that isn't done. Add a status-only lookup. If the status can't be read, retry later without posting the waiting comment.</li><li><code>release_held</code> runs on the Hermes listener thread and re-reads every held issue on each status event. Re-check only the held issues that depend on the changed issue, and do it on a worker, not the listener thread.</li><li>Read the done statuses from config, defaulting to <code>done</code>/<code>closed</code>, instead of a hard-coded constant.</li><li>Log when a held issue leaves the held set because it is no longer actionable.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests cover a Gaia error (no comment), targeted release, config statuses and the log line; the existing gating tests still pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: storing the held set in <code>talos.db</code> across restarts.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4169</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4170	2026-11-04	2026-10-28	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	de9b75226ae1-e6a4-3631-f6ac3c3a2b69	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 08:16:45	adt	0	0
1694c5676af3-8c4a-22e6-d049e8219a48	Auth route guards follow-up after the native session (PR 738)	2026-11-10 20:48:22	2026-11-10 21:17:55	0	<p>Follow-up to aprom-4468 / PR 738 (review comment r4530081034). Native auth is merged and has been checked by hand: signing in and out works, and ember-simple-auth is gone from package.json, the app source and the compiled build. The tests pass (1369, 0 fail). These items were not blocking.</p>\n<h4>How the routes are guarded now (unchanged by PR 738)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><code>routes/application.js</code> <code>beforeModel</code>: <code>session.setup()</code> restores the session, <code>ENV.publicRoutes</code> are let through, and a signed-out user's URL is saved as <code>session.oldRequestedUrl</code> before redirecting to <code>signin</code>.</li>\n<li><code>routes/app.js</code>: <code>session.requireAuthentication(transition, 'signin')</code> stores <code>attemptedTransition</code>.</li>\n<li><code>routes/signin.js</code>: <code>session.prohibitAuthentication('app')</code>.</li>\n<li>After sign-in, <code>handleAuthentication()</code> retries <code>attemptedTransition</code>; failing that it goes to <code>oldRequestedUrl</code>, then to <code>routeAfterAuthentication</code>. After sign-out, <code>handleInvalidation()</code> reloads the app at <code>rootURL</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>To do</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Add acceptance tests for the auth routing:\n  <ul>\n  <li>signed out on a deep link, then sign-in, lands back on the original URL;</li>\n  <li>signed in and opening <code>/signin</code> goes to <code>app</code>;</li>\n  <li>sign-out reloads the app at <code>rootURL</code> (assert that <code>handleInvalidation</code> is called, since tests skip the reload).</li>\n  </ul>\n  Coordinate with aprom-4466 so the tests aren't duplicated.</li>\n<li>The two redirect paths overlap: <code>oldRequestedUrl</code> in the application route and <code>attemptedTransition</code> in the app route. Either document why both exist, or merge them into one.</li>\n<li>Decide whether <code>reset-password</code> should send a signed-in user to <code>app</code> (today it is let through as a public route).</li>\n<li>Remove the leftover ember-simple-auth wording from the docs:\n  <ul>\n  <li><code>docs/architecture/live-updates/architecture.md</code> (line 45) and <code>decisions.md</code> (line 40) should name the native session service;</li>\n  <li><code>docs/classes</code>, <code>docs/files</code> and <code>docs/data.json</code> are old generated YUIDoc that still show the mixins: regenerate them or drop them.</li>\n  </ul>\n  The comments in <code>services/session.js</code> and <code>session-stores/local-storage.js</code> that explain why the stored data format and localStorage key stay compatible with ember-simple-auth are intentional; keep them.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4469	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	0691c6036af3-9aaa-2a4b-eff9d4d60f47	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	008bf8916af3-b741-22e6-e8b466633bfb	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 21:17:56	aprom	0	0
1a0a3d196ae1-affe-9a2f-48981ae43fe8	p4m test slots: one template database per seed key, Slots.prepare and a separate psql gateway	2026-10-28 07:28:26	2026-10-28 08:45:23	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups from adt-4159 (dev-tools#41). There is one template database, and it is rebuilt whenever the checkout under test has a different key (schema fingerprint + seed files). Baseline reruns in a slot use a different checkout, so two branches with different seeds keep rebuilding the template in turn.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Keep a template per key (e.g. <code>pr4m_test_tpl_&lt;short key&gt;</code>), keep at most a configurable number of them (default 3), and drop the least recently used. Clone a slot from the template that matches its checkout.</li><li>Move the orchestration (slot lock, template ensure, clone, container sync) into <code>Slots.prepare(slot, src, lock)</code> in <code>installer/testslots.py</code>.</li><li>Split the psql calls into their own gateway class (single responsibility).</li><li>Keep the lock order: slot lock, then template lock.</li><li><code>p4m test slots status</code> lists the templates with their keys.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: running a branch and its baseline one after another doesn't rebuild a template the second time; unit tests (fake docker/psql, as in <code>test_testslots.py</code>) cover per-key selection, eviction and lock order.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: slots for suites other than Gaia.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4172	2026-11-04	2026-10-28	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	e53e68076ae1-41d3-5e9e-9d778f55642c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 08:45:24	adt	0	0
4a6c17346af3-b741-232a-16687fb54197	Translation tests before replacing ember-intl	2026-11-10 20:53:30	2026-11-10 22:05:57	0	<p>First of three issues to replace ember-intl with a native intl service. These tests run against the current ember-intl, so they define the behaviour the replacement must keep. Prometheus uses ember-intl only through the <code>intl</code> service and <code>{{t}}</code>. Nothing imports ember-intl directly, <code>@ember-intl/cp-validations</code> is unused, and <code>{{format-date}}</code> is our own helper.</p>\n<h4>Tests to add</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Unit tests for <code>intl.t</code>:\n  <ul>\n  <li>fallback keys via <code>default</code> (a string or an array);</li>\n  <li>escaping with <code>htmlSafe: true</code>, which returns a SafeString;</li>\n  <li>the <code>Missing translation "key" for locale "x"</code> text;</li>\n  <li>an empty string and numbers returned as-is;</li>\n  <li>plural with <code>=N</code>, <code>offset:</code> and <code>#</code>;</li>\n  <li>select;</li>\n  <li>ICU apostrophe rules (<code>''</code>, and <code>'{literal}'</code> as literal text);</li>\n  <li>HTML tags left as plain text;</li>\n  <li>an error when a placeholder value is missing.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n<li>Unit tests for the other service methods the app uses: <code>exists</code>, <code>lookup</code>, <code>translationsFor</code>, <code>addTranslations</code> (merging into a locale), <code>setLocale</code> (normalising <code>en_US</code> to <code>en-us</code>), <code>locale</code>, <code>primaryLocale</code> and <code>formatNumber</code>.</li>\n<li>An integration test showing that a rendered <code>{{t}}</code> updates after <code>setLocale</code> or <code>addTranslations</code>, and that <code>&lt;html lang&gt;</code> follows the locale.</li>\n<li>A test that formats every message in <code>translations/*.json</code> (each placeholder given a sample value), so a malformed ICU string fails CI.</li>\n<li><code>services/translations.js</code>: Gaia translations merge over the built-in ones, and a locale Gaia doesn't support falls back to the default.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Every test must pass on today's ember-intl, with no changes to app code. aprom-4469 also adds tests, so check for file overlap if both are worked at the same time.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4470	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	0691c6036af3-9aaa-2a4b-eff9d4d60f47	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	cb8dbcb96af3-1130-359d-ea388fd50889	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 22:05:57	aprom	0	0
297e84136afc-72fe-b62c-cf327ee69e8a	Migrations: Postgres extensions, vector and generated tsvector columns, GIN/trigram/HNSW indexes	2026-11-17 16:22:01	2026-11-18 11:00:43	0	<p>Search needs column and index kinds the declarative migrations cannot create today: they only know primary, unique and plain/multi-column indexes (<code>core/libs/meta/migration.php</code> ~215-271, <code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> ~242). This issue adds the generic capabilities; the search metadata that uses them comes later.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Extensions: migrate runs <code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector</code> and <code>pg_trgm</code> (declared in config, idempotent).</li><li>Field type <code>vector</code> with <code>dimensions</code> (maps to <code>vector(N)</code>) in <code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code> <code>getFieldType</code> and the Postgres dialect.</li><li>Field type <code>tsvector</code> with a <code>generated</code> definition (source field =&gt; weight A-D, text search config default <code>english</code>), migrated as <code>GENERATED ALWAYS AS (setweight(to_tsvector(config, coalesce(field,'')), 'A') || ...) STORED</code>.</li><li>Index kinds <code>gin</code> (tsvector), <code>gin_trgm</code> (<code>gin_trgm_ops</code> on a text field), <code>hnsw_cosine</code> (<code>USING hnsw (col vector_cosine_ops)</code>).</li><li>Re-running migrate is a no-op; changing a generated column's sources recreates it.</li><li><code>docker-compose.yaml</code> Postgres image <code>pgvector/pgvector:pg16</code>.</li><li>Unit tests for type mapping and generated DDL; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a fixture model with a vector field, a generated tsvector field and the three index kinds migrates as expected and re-migrates cleanly; existing models are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>search</code> metadata block, any real model.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4654	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	1fb236126afc-72fe-b62c-bf3c9291dd47	\N	cbb506d05acd-06d6-1141-68969b9fd562	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	363012e06afc-9bce-b62c-defc493542c3	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 11:00:43	agaia	0	0
5e4525436af3-b741-232a-e7bcb563f1d2	Replace ember-intl with a native intl service	2026-11-10 20:53:50	2026-11-10 22:45:59	0	<p>Depends on aprom-4470 (the tests must be merged first). Replaces ember-intl and @formatjs with a native service built on the browser's <code>Intl</code> APIs. It uses only public Ember APIs, so it works on Ember 4.1 and 6.12. A throwaway proved the approach; its diff is attached as <code>native-intl-throwaway.diff.txt</code> (based on dev <code>e0383f56</code>). Throwaway results:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>1337 tests, 0 failures, the same as the baseline;</li>\n<li>no ember-intl or formatjs code left in the build;</li>\n<li>a comparison with <code>intl-messageformat</code> 9.13 over <code>en-us.json</code> matched on 9732 of 9736 outputs. The 4 mismatches all come from the unused <code>views.app.theme</code> string, where formatjs is the one producing wrong output.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Changes</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><code>app/services/intl.js</code>: the same service name and API, so none of the roughly 2,700 <code>t</code> call sites change. It provides:\n  <ul>\n  <li><code>t</code>, <code>exists</code>, <code>lookup</code>, <code>setLocale</code>, <code>addTranslations</code>, <code>translationsFor</code>, <code>locale</code>, <code>primaryLocale</code>, <code>locales</code>, <code>formatNumber</code>, <code>formatDate</code> and <code>formatMessage</code>;</li>\n  <li>tracked state, so <code>{{t}}</code> updates on a locale switch;</li>\n  <li>the same <code>htmlSafe</code> escaping, missing-translation text and <code>default</code> fallback as ember-intl.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n<li><code>app/utils/intl/message-format.js</code>: an ICU formatter supporting <code>{arg}</code>, plural (<code>=N</code>, <code>offset:</code>, <code>#</code>), select and apostrophe quoting, built on <code>Intl.PluralRules</code> and <code>Intl.NumberFormat</code>.</li>\n<li><code>app/helpers/t.js</code>: a class helper.</li>\n<li><code>lib/bundled-translations.js</code>: a broccoli plugin that turns <code>translations/*.json</code> into the module <code>prometheus/utils/intl/bundled-translations</code>. It is merged into <code>trees.app</code> in <code>ember-cli-build.js</code>.</li>\n<li>Add <code>broccoli-plugin</code> and <code>broccoli-merge-trees</code> to devDependencies. The throwaway used ember-cli's copies of them.</li>\n<li>Remove <code>ember-intl</code>, <code>@ember-intl/cp-validations</code> and <code>config/ember-intl.js</code>. None of the build-time checks in that config are switched on, so nothing is lost.</li>\n<li>Unit tests for the formatter. Commit the comparison script (formatting every message with both our formatter and intl-messageformat) as a dev tool that can be re-run.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Verification (paste results into the PR)</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Baseline on dev before the change:\n  <ul>\n  <li>the size of a production build;</li>\n  <li>screenshots of the issue list, an issue page and sign-in, in English and in a second locale from Gaia.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n<li><code>ai test prometheus</code>: the same pass count, 0 failures, and the aprom-4470 tests unchanged.</li>\n<li>The comparison script on <code>en-us.json</code> plus every locale Gaia returns.</li>\n<li>A production build containing no <code>ember-intl/</code> or <code>@formatjs</code> modules, with the bundled-translations module present. Compare its size with step 1.</li>\n<li>In <code>prometheus-dev</code>: editing <code>translations/en-us.json</code> makes the app reload with the new text.</li>\n<li>In the browser:\n  <ul>\n  <li>switching to the second locale updates the UI without a reload;</li>\n  <li><code>&lt;html lang&gt;</code> changes;</li>\n  <li>a missing key shows <code>Missing translation "…"</code>;</li>\n  <li>the screens match the baseline screenshots.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Rollback:</strong> revert this PR. There is no stored state or data format to migrate.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4471	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	0691c6036af3-9aaa-2a4b-eff9d4d60f47	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Agent Agamemnon	099fa2276af3-2bc4-c7f8-8637fc4240db	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 22:45:59	aprom	0	0
70d1bea56af0-b3ed-60c0-bd96e15757db	QuickList: standalone select-all box and selection bar	2026-11-08 11:48:00	2026-11-08 12:28:54	0	<p>QuickList can let users select rows and run actions on them; it's optional and the idea browser won't use it. Build the select-all box and the selection bar as standalone components; a later issue connects them (and the per-row checkbox) to the root <code>QuickList</code>. The attached screen is a guide only.</p><ul><li>New <code>QuickList::SelectAll</code> (<code>app/components/quick-list/select-all.{hbs,js}</code>): square <code>btn-default btn-xs</code> showing <code>fa-square-o</code> (none), <code>fa-minus-square-o</code> (some) or <code>fa-check-square</code> (all). Arguments <code>@state</code> ('none'|'some'|'all') and <code>@onToggle</code>; it has an accessible label.</li><li>New <code>QuickList::SelectionBar</code> (<code>selection-bar.{hbs,js}</code>): a row with <code>#f9fafc</code> background: <code>SelectAll</code>, bold "N selected", the <code>&lt;:actions&gt;</code> block, and a × <code>btn-default btn-xs</code> that calls <code>@onClear</code>. Arguments <code>@count</code>, <code>@state</code>, <code>@onToggleAll</code>, <code>@onClear</code>.</li><li>Styles in a new partial <code>app/styles/components/quick-list/_selection.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.quick-list-selection</code>, not imported (the assemble issue imports it). Strings under <code>components.quickList.selection.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for the three select-all states, the count text, the yielded actions and clearing.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: keeping the selection state, row checkboxes, and connecting them to QuickList (the assemble issue).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> quick-list-selection-grouped.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4354	20