f79d64206ae1-3497-9a2f-c715aedce3ae	Talos workspaces: gaia_pack in the worktree, clear error for a checked-out branch, one base-branch table	2026-10-28 07:27:51	2026-10-28 07:44:05	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups 4, 5 and 6 from the PR comment on adt-4158 (dev-tools#40). With per-issue workspaces (<code>talos/lib/workspaces.py</code>, <code>.runs/issue-N</code>), some code still assumes the main checkout.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/runner.py</code> <code>gaia_pack</code> (~l.238) runs <code>ai context</code> with <code>cwd=WORKSPACE</code> and no <code>P4M_WORKSPACE</code>, so the Gaia pack is built from the main checkout. Build it from the issue's workspace: pass the workspace folder and <code>workspaces.env(folder)</code>. If the workspace doesn't exist yet when the pack is built, reorder the calls so it is created first.</li><li>If <code>claude-issue-N</code> is checked out in the main checkout, git refuses the worktree and the run fails with git's raw message. Detect this case before creating the worktree. Hand the issue back with a clear comment (which folder holds the branch and how to free it) instead of a generic failure, and don't count it as an iteration.</li><li><code>workspaces.py</code> has its own base-branch table next to <code>ai/lib/common.py</code> <code>base_branch</code>. Use the <code>ai</code> one only.</li><li>Move the rule that pr4m (workspace root) issues get no worktree from the dispatcher into <code>workspaces.py</code>.</li><li>When an existing <code>claude-issue-N</code> branch is reused, log whether it is behind <code>origin/&lt;base&gt;</code>. Don't rebase it.</li><li>Add a regression test that <code>ai test</code> run with <code>P4M_WORKSPACE</code> passes the worktree as <code>--src</code> (<code>ai/lib/tests.py</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: a Gaia run's pack comes from the worktree; the checked-out-branch case gives a readable hand-back; there is one base-branch source; unit test