8bed99f36afd-7db8-49c2-0f2f0d596d2c	App start: static skeleton in index.html until the application route is ready, skeleton on loading-assets	2026-11-18 10:31:39	2026-11-18 11:43:50	0	<p>On a cold load, Prometheus shows a blank page until several steps finish one after another. First the bundles load: the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> of <code>app/index.html</code> holds only the two script tags. Then <code>routes/application.js</code> <code>beforeModel</code> awaits <code>session.setup()</code>, which restores the session and may refresh the token. Then it awaits <code>translations.load()</code>. No loading template exists at the top level. After that, <code>app.loading-assets</code> shows only a hardcoded <code>&lt;h1&gt;Loading Assets...&lt;/h1&gt;</code> in the app shell while it loads the user, users, roles, projects and settings. Loading must follow the existing skeleton standard (design system section 9: <code>AppUi::Skeleton</code>), with no new loader, class or CSS.</p><ul><li><code>app/index.html</code>: inside <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>, before the scripts, add static markup marked with <code>data-boot-loader</code> that copies the app shell, with every part a skeleton (see the attached screen):<ul><li><code>wrapper</code>;</li><li><code>main-header</code>: <code>.logo</code> holding a <code>skeleton-line</code>, a <code>global-search</code> skeleton bar, and <code>navbar-custom-menu</code> &gt; <code>ul.nav.navbar-nav</code> with three <code>li &gt; a &gt; skeleton-line--xs</code> for New, notifications and user;</li><li><code>main-sidebar</code> with a <code>sidebar-menu</code> of <code>skeleton-line</code> rows;</li><li><code>content-wrapper</code> containing the markup of <code>AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader</code> (<code>page-skeleton-header</code> plus <code>components/app-ui/skeleton/page-loading-body.hbs</code>).</li></ul>Use existing <code>.skeleton-*</code>, AdminLTE and header classes only, with no inline styles, no new CSS and no text (translations aren't loaded yet). Add a comment in <code>index.html</code> and in <code>page-loading-body.hbs</code> pointing to each other, so the copies stay in sync.</li><li><code>routes/application.js</code>: remove the <code>[data-boot-loader]</code> element once <code>beforeModel</code> has finished, including when it ends in a redirect (signin, public routes) and when restore fails. It must be a no-op when the element is missing (<code>tests/index.html</code> has none).</li><li><code>app/templates/app/loading-assets.hbs</code>: replace the hardcoded heading with <code>&lt;AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader={{true}} /&gt;</code>.</li><li>Tests: a unit test that the application route removes the boot skeleton after <code>beforeModel</code> and tolerates its absence. An integration or acceptance test that loading-assets renders <code>[data-test-page-loading]</code> while its model is pending.</li><li>Compare the static skeleton with the real shell in the running app (sidebar width, header height, content offset) so the handover to the app doesn't jump.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> from the first paint of a cold load (signed in or not) until the first real screen, the page always shows a skeleton (header, sidebar and content), never a blank white page. The static skeleton is gone once the sign-in page or the app shell renders. There is no hardcoded user-facing text and no new CSS.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a skeleton state for the real <code>ApplicationHeader</code> during loading-assets, making the boot requests themselves faster (session restore, translations, loading-assets data), and the app.project route wait.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> boot-splash.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4670	2026-11-25	2026-11-18	do