23e0d9096af7-01e1-767c-a68be2a3936b	Move data loading off the legacy store request methods to store.request with builders	2026-11-14 00:02:43	2026-11-15 10:31:26	0	<h4>Why</h4><ul><li>From ember-data 5.8, <code>findRecord</code>, <code>findAll</code>, <code>query</code>, <code>queryRecord</code> and <code>save</code>/<code>destroyRecord</code> raise <code>warp-drive:deprecate-legacy-request-methods</code>. The aprom-4549 trial counted about 416,000 in one suite run.</li><li>ember-data 6 removes these methods, so this has to be done before the next major.</li></ul><h4>Start when</h4><p>"Upgrade to Ember 7.4 LTS and ember-data 5.9" is merged.</p><h4>Do</h4><ul><li><b>Design pass first:</b> how <code>store.request</code> with the JSON:API builders, or custom builders, fits Gaia's query-string API.<ul><li>Gaia's API has singular paths, <code>api/v1</code>, a <code>query</code>/<code>rels</code>/<code>limit</code>/<code>sort</code> query string, and the Bearer token with refresh through <code>services/session.js</code>.</li><li>Keep token refresh in the request path, either through a handler or the adapter. Use <code>utils/state/</code> (<code>ListLoader</code>, <code>AsyncResource</code>) as the seams.</li></ul></li><li>Propose a split by module for approval (base routes and list loader first, then module by module) before migrating.</li><li>When done, remove the deprecation-workflow silence for <code>deprecate-legacy-request-methods</code>.</li></ul><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4552	2027-01-15	2026-12-14	new	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	ecaa08696af9-1368-4631-e5f7125d9e3e	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-15 10:31:26	aprom	0	0
57b3aea56af0-b3ed-60c0-13c501627f9f	QuickList: grouping helper and group heading component	2026-11-08 11:47:35	2026-11-08 12:43:15	0	<p>QuickList lists can be grouped (by status, creator, ...). Grouping works on the page the caller loaded: Gaia's <code>group</code> parameter is a SQL GROUP BY and can't produce headed groups, so items are grouped and counted in JS. Build the helper and the heading as standalone pieces; a later issue connects them to the root <code>QuickList</code>. The attached screen is a guide only.</p><ul><li>Pure helper <code>app/utils/quick-list/group-items.js</code>: <code>groupItems(items, option)</code> with <code>option = {key, groupKey(record), groupLabel(key)}</code> -&gt; ordered groups <code>[{key, label, items, count}]</code>, keeping first-seen order (the caller sorts by the group field first so groups continue across pages). Unit tests, including empty input and null keys (one "None" group).</li><li>New <code>QuickList::Group</code> (<code>app/components/quick-list/group.{hbs,js}</code>): heading with caret (<code>fa-caret-down</code>/<code>-right</code>), label in 12px bold uppercase, Bootstrap <code>badge</code> with the count; <code>#f4f4f4</code> band with a <code>#ddd</code> bottom border. Arguments <code>@group</code>, <code>@collapsed</code>, <code>@onToggle</code>. It yields the default block for the group's items (hidden while collapsed) and a <code>&lt;:heading as |group|&gt;</code> block that replaces the label.</li><li>Styles in a new partial <code>app/styles/components/quick-list/_group.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.quick-list-group</code>, not imported (the assemble issue imports it).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests for the helper; integration tests for the heading, the count, collapsing and a replaced heading.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: totals per group across all pages; connecting it to QuickList.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> quick-list-selection-grouped.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4352	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	c804ef026af0-b3ed-60c0-53e5298c96a2	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 12:43:15	aprom	0	0
fddf90586ae1-3497-9a2f-6b6951179d19	Talos workspaces: per-issue runs share the workspace's Claude auto-memory	2026-10-28 07:27:57	2026-10-28 07:56:35	0	<p>Part of adt-4157, follow-up 3 on adt-4158. Claude Code keys its per-project data, including auto-memory (<code>~/.claude/projects/&lt;cwd-slug&gt;/memory/MEMORY.md</code>), by the working folder. Talos runs Claude in <code>&lt;workspace&gt;/.runs/issue-N</code>, so every run starts with an empty memory. Agents lose the team's memories (for example: never <code>p4m db migrate</code> from Pr4M, no permission seeds, guard async after destroy) and write new ones into folders nobody reads again.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Find out how Claude Code resolves the memory folder: a setting, an environment variable, or the slug of the cwd. Pick the least fragile way for a run in <code>.runs/issue-N</code> to read and write the workspace's memory: a setting if one exists, otherwise a junction (Windows) or symlink (Linux) from the run's slug folder to the workspace's <code>memory</code> folder, created by <code>workspaces.py</code> along with the workspace.</li><li>Writes from parallel runs go to the same folder. Document how concurrent writes to <code>MEMORY.md</code> behave, and accept the risk or guard against it.</li><li>The container runner (<code>talos/lib/container.py</code>) mounts <code>~/.claude</code>. Make sure container runs get the same memory, or document why they don't.</li><li><code>talos gc</code> removes the link together with the workspace, never the shared memory itself.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: a run in <code>.runs/issue-N</code> loads the workspace's MEMORY.md (check it in a real session); a memory saved in a run shows up in the workspace's memory folder; unit tests cover link creation and removal on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: changes to what goes into memory.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4167</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-