7e70dcd96af3-1487-2734-9c70e5b58d2f	Dependency hygiene: declare indirect dependencies, remove unused ones and old Ember globals	2026-11-10 21:32:46	2026-11-11 07:23:53	0	<p>Clean up <code>package.json</code> and leftover globals before the upgrade, so later breakage is easier to trace.</p><p><strong>Declare</strong> what the app uses but only gets through other packages:</p><ul><li><code>@ember/render-modifiers</code>: <code>did-insert</code> / <code>did-update</code> are used in 19 templates and currently come in through ember-power-select 4. The spike showed they disappear once power-select is upgraded.</li><li><code>@ember/string</code>: imported in 4 files. It's a separate package from Ember 5.</li></ul><p><strong>Remove</strong> unused packages (0 imports): <code>ember-ajax</code>, <code>ember-fetch</code>, <code>ember-lodash</code>, <code>ember-cli-accounting</code>, <code>qunit-parameterize</code>, <code>@cucumber/cucumber</code> (a runtime dependency), <code>install</code>, <code>ember-cli-release</code>.</p><p><strong>Globals</strong>:</p><ul><li>Remove <code>import Ember from 'ember'</code> and the <code>Ember.Logger</code> fallback from <code>app/initializers/setup-logger.js</code>. <code>Ember.Logger</code> was removed in 4.0.</li><li>Remove <code>App.injectTestHelpers()</code> from <code>tests/test-helper.js</code>. It belongs to the old global test helpers.</li></ul><p>Out of scope: ember-concurrency (its own issue) and anything related to ember-intl or ember-simple-auth.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4474	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	14c0c0916af3-72eb-1180-92ce40607afc	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 07:23:54	aprom	0	0
ae27ea516afd-7db8-49c2-7216ff557a5e	Project route: stop blocking nested routes on the all-issues preload	2026-11-18 10:32:14	2026-11-18 15:31:56	0	<p><code>routes/app/project.js</code> <code>afterModel</code> loads every issue of the project (<code>limit: -1</code>; fields id, subject, issueNumber, statusId, projectId) and returns that promise, so every nested route (board, issue list, issue page, ideas, conversations, ...) waits for it before its own request starts. The list only feeds the <code>issuesList</code> getter in <code>controllers/app/project.js</code> (<code>@computed('projectId', 'issues')</code>). It is read by <code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code> and <code>controllers/prometheus/projectrelated.js</code>, and from there by <code>components/message-box.js</code> and <code>components/summer-note.js</code>.</p><ul><li>Start the issues query without returning it from <code>afterModel</code>. When it resolves, set <code>issues</code> on the <code>app.project</code> controller (and the route, if still read there); report errors with <code>errorManager.handleError</code> as today. Ignore a result that arrives after the user has switched to another project.</li><li>Make sure the <code>issuesList</code> getter updates when <code>issues</code> arrives later, and that every reader handles the empty list (only the blank entry) until then without errors.</li><li>Tests: a route/acceptance test that a nested route's model request starts before the issues preload resolves, and that the list fills in once it does.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on a cold load of a project page, the nested route's request starts right after the project request, without waiting for the all-issues request. Issue pickers that use <code>issuesList</code> show the issues once loaded. Switching projects never shows another project's issues.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing the preload with server-side search in the pickers, the store.request migration (aprom-