88c946c56af3-1487-2734-afef9bf8212b	Import Mirage classes from miragejs instead of ember-cli-mirage	2026-11-10 21:32:56	2026-11-11 12:47:08	0	<p>ember-cli-mirage 3 (needed for Ember 5+) no longer re-exports Mirage's classes or exposes its internal paths. In the spike, every factory failed to load (<code>Factory</code> undefined), which blocked all acceptance tests.</p><ul><li><code>import { Factory } from 'ember-cli-mirage'</code> → <code>from 'miragejs'</code>: 48 factories, plus <code>JSONAPISerializer</code> (2) and <code>Response</code> (1).</li><li><code>import Collection from 'ember-cli-mirage/orm/collection'</code> → <code>import { Collection } from 'miragejs'</code>: 12 files (<code>mirage/helpers/paginate.js</code>, two route handlers, nine step files).</li></ul><p>Safe on the current ember-cli-mirage 2.2, which re-exports these from miragejs. Keep <code>discoverEmberDataModels</code> and <code>setupMirage</code> from ember-cli-mirage. The <code>mirage/config.js</code> default-export change belongs to the Ember 6.12 upgrade issue, because 2.2 may read a default export as the old-style routes function.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4475	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	6f4ce2426af4-8867-c218-9bdcd5d74054	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 12:47:08	aprom	0	0
7f920d446af9-1368-4631-112f03dd4381	Component composition rules, ember-test-selectors and design-reviewer checklist	2026-11-15 10:25:03	2026-11-15 11:10:21	0	<p>Write down the agreed rules for building views from components, so people and agents follow the same ones.</p>\n<h4>Rules (add to <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>, short pointer in <code>prometheus/CLAUDE.md</code>)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><b>R1 Rule of three:</b> extract a shared component only when the same markup <i>and</i> behaviour exists in 3+ places. Two copies stay copies.</li>\n<li><b>R2 Blocks before arguments:</b> optional or variable content is a named block or a yielded contextual component (like QuickList). Args are for data and simple switches; more than ~10 args triggers a design review.</li>\n<li><b>R3 Data in, events out:</b> components take records, descriptors and callbacks; they never inject a controller or load route data. Services are fine for cross-cutting concerns (intl, acl, notifications).</li>\n<li><b>R4 Change only with a benefit:</b> pages move to shared components when they are a pilot target or are being edited anyway.</li>\n<li><b>R5 Test selectors are <code>data-test-*</code> only:</b> stripped from production builds by ember-test-selectors; CSS and app JS never use them. Existing <code>data-field</code>/<code>data-btn</code>/<code>data-column</code> stay (4 stylesheets and <code>form-fields/label.js</code>, <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code>, <code>modifiers/initialize-sortable.js</code> depend on them) and are replaced only when a page is touched.</li>\n<li><b>R6</b> Every shared component ships with a ui-docs page, a contract manifest (see the manifest issue) and integration tests.</li>\n<li><b>R7</b> Generic UI lives in <code>app-ui/</code>, domain UI in <code>&lt;domain&gt;/</code>. No new top-level components.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Also</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Install <code>ember-test-selectors</code> and confirm <code>data-test-*</code> attributes are absent from a production build.</li>\n<li>Add R1–R4 to the <code>design-reviewer</code> agent's checklist (dev-tools; separate PR in dev-tools if needed).</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Acceptance</h4>\n<ul><li>Rules in the design system and CLAUDE.md; addon installed and verified stripped in production; reviewer checklist updated; lint and tests green.</li></ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4566	2026-11-22	2026-11-15	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	c20442936af9-46d1-1107-4f20781595f3	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-15 11:10:22	aprom	0	0
12d6cd376ae1-affe-9a2f-1c83cecde5ce	Talos: lease test slots only for Gaia runs, none when maxParallel is 1, validate testSlots at load	2026-10-28 07:28:18	2026-10-28 08:25:24	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups 1 and 2 from the PR comment on adt-4162 (dev-tools#44). Only Gaia suites use <code>pr4m_test</code> and slots (adt-4159), but the dispatcher leases a slot for every run, and with <code>maxParallel: 1</code> it still sets <code>P4M_TEST_SLOT=1</code> (<code>talos/lib/dispatcher.py</code> ~l.203). As a result, Prometheus, Hermes and dev-tools runs wait for a slot they never use.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Lease a slot only when the issue's repo is <code>gaia</code>. Other repos pass the caps without a slot.</li><li>With <code>maxParallel: 1</code>, lease no slot and set no <code>P4M_TEST_SLOT</code>, so <code>ai test</code> behaves as before adt-4159.</li><li>When <code>agent.json</code> is loaded (<code>talos/lib/registry.py</code>), check that <code>testSlots</code> is no larger than <code>TEST_SLOTS</code> in p4m.env (<code>installer/testslots.py</code> <code>slot_count</code>). Fail with a clear message if it is.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests show that a Prometheus run gets no slot, a Gaia run does, <code>maxParallel: 1</code> sets no slot, and a bad <code>testSlots</code> fails at load.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: changes to slot management in p4m.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4169</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4171	2026-11-04	2026-10-28	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	1ceb6e916ae1-01a9-3631-2cbc601c83d0	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 08:25:25	adt	0	0
87031ee16af0-b3ed-60c0-be62b5df9e83	Ideas: server-side paging, sort and archived filter for the idea browser query	2026-11-08 11:48:23	2026-11-08 13:06:37	0	<p>The idea browser loads every idea (<code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code> ~l.47, limit -1) and filters open/archived in the browser (<code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> <code>listedIdeas</code> ~l.300). Before it moves to QuickList with 20 ideas per page, the query has to page and sort on the server. This issue changes only the data side; the browser looks the same.</p><ul><li>Controller query params <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>order</code> next to the existing search params. The idea query sends <code>limit</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code> (default <code>Idea.dateModified</code>), <code>order</code> (default DESC) and exposes the total from the response meta as <code>totalIdeas</code>.</li><li>A <code>pageSize</code> property on the controller that defaults to <code>-1</code> (all ideas, as today), so the current list keeps working; the QuickList issue sets it to 20.</li><li>Move the open/archived split into the query: open ideas by default (<code>Idea.status : open</code> ANDed with the search); when "show archived" is on, the status condition is dropped. The footer toggle and counts keep working.</li><li>Load the creator via the hasOne rel <code>createdBy</code> only (no hasMany rels). Hermes idea events re-run the current query, not a full reload.</li><li>Mirage: make the idea handler honour <code>limit</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>sort</code>/<code>order</code> and the status condition and return the total in meta; update the existing idea browser acceptance tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: the browser looks and works as before; tests show the query sends the sort, order and status condition, and that page/sort query params reach the request.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: the QuickList UI, page size 20, grouping.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4356	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	86ee41b96af0-28c5-df3e-942a93c3b443	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 13:06:37	aprom	0	0
64c7bd706af0-b3ed-60c0-bb5e290d2655	QuickList: standalone group-by and sort toolbar	2026-11-08 11:47:48	2026-11-08 13:06:39	0	<p>QuickList lists get a toolbar row with Group by and Sort menus. Build it as a standalone component; a later issue connects it to the root <code>QuickList</code>. The attached screens are a guide only.</p><ul><li>New <code>QuickList::Toolbar</code> (<code>app/components/quick-list/toolbar.{hbs,js}</code>): a flex row with a <code>&lt;:start&gt;</code> block on the left (for the select-all box later) and, on the right, <strong>Group by ▾</strong> (<code>fa-object-group</code> + current label) and <strong>Sort ▾</strong> (<code>fa-sort-amount-desc</code>/<code>-asc</code> + current label) as square <code>btn-default btn-xs</code> dropdowns using the existing <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code>.</li><li>Arguments: <code>@groupOptions</code> (<code>[{key, label}]</code>, with "None" first), <code>@groupBy</code>, <code>@onGroup(key)</code>, <code>@sortOptions</code> (<code>[{key, label}]</code>), <code>@sort</code>, <code>@order</code>, <code>@onSort(key, order)</code>. Picking the current sort again flips the order. Each menu is hidden when it has no options. The current choice is marked in crimson with a check (group) or the order icon (sort).</li><li>Styles in a new partial <code>app/styles/components/quick-list/_toolbar.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.quick-list-toolbar</code>, not imported (the assemble issue imports it). Strings under <code>components.quickList.toolbar.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for both menus, the marked current choice, order flipping, hidden menus and the <code>&lt;:start&gt;</code> block.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: sorting more than one field; connecting it to QuickList.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> quick-list-states.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c2