9dc035a56afd-7db8-49c2-7c34260e77b6	Project route: show a skeleton while the project loads and render the outlet without the extra project query	2026-11-18 10:31:57	2026-11-18 12:18:54	0	<p>On a fresh load of any project URL (e.g. <code>/app/project/aprom/issue/4198</code>), the content area stays blank until the parent <code>app.project</code> route finishes its hooks, before the nested route's own request even starts. Ember finds no loading substate for <code>app.project</code>: <code>app/project-loading.hbs</code>, <code>app/loading.hbs</code> and <code>loading.hbs</code> don't exist. The existing <code>app/project/loading.hbs</code> and <code>*-loading.hbs</code> templates only cover child routes. They are also hidden, because <code>templates/app/project.hbs</code> renders <code>{{outlet}}</code> only inside <code>{{#if this.projectId}}</code>, and <code>setupController</code> in <code>routes/app/project.js</code> sets <code>projectId</code> in the <code>.then()</code> of a second project query, although <code>beforeModel</code> already loaded the project.</p><ul><li>Add <code>app/templates/app/project-loading.hbs</code> with <code>&lt;AppUi::Skeleton::PageLoading @showHeader={{true}} /&gt;</code>, following <code>app/templates/app/settings-loading.hbs</code> and the design system.</li><li><code>routes/app/project.js</code>: keep the project record loaded in <code>beforeModel</code> on the route. In <code>setupController</code>, set <code>model</code>, <code>projectId</code> and <code>projectName</code> from it straight away, and remove the second <code>store.query('project', { fields: 'Project.id,Project.name' ... })</code>.</li><li>When no project matches the short code, keep today's error handling (<code>errorManager</code>) and don't throw on <code>objectAt(project, 0).id</code>.</li><li>Tests: an acceptance or route test that visits a project child route with a delayed project response and asserts the project skeleton is shown. Also check that the child's loading template renders while its own model is pending.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a cold load or reload of a project page never shows an empty content area. The project skeleton shows while the project loads, then the child skeleton, then the page. Only one project request is made per project entry. The project name and breadcrumb are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the all-issues preload in <code>afterModel</code> (separate issue), the app start before the app shell.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> project-loading.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4671	2026-11-25	2026-11-18	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	8b3cce606afd-7db8-49c2-cbb96709c7c9	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	17aa57b56afd-bd48-7b61-0189a087e573	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 12:18:54	aprom	0	0
