2ece5cd86ae1-affe-9a2f-87fb0a6643ef	talos gc: move into lib with tests, run when an issue is done, remove container volumes	2026-10-28 07:28:46	2026-10-28 08:55:45	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups from adt-4163 (dev-tools#45), adt-4164 (container volumes) and adt-4158 #1 (remove the workspace on close or merge).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Move the <code>gc_workspaces</code> orchestration from <code>talos.py</code> into <code>talos/lib/workspace_gc.py</code>, so the status lookup can be unit-tested. Move <code>pr_merged</code> out of the policy module.</li><li>Add tests for <code>pr_merged</code> (fake <code>gh</code>), the Gaia status lookup (including an error, which keeps the workspace) and the hook at <code>talos run</code> start.</li><li>Also collect one workspace when Talos sees its issue become done/closed/wont_fix (reconcile or a Hermes status event), not only at startup. Never touch a run in flight.</li><li>Remove the per-issue Claude volumes and leftover containers of finished issues created by the container runner (<code>talos/lib/container.py</code>), with the same rules.</li><li>Make <code>talos run --dry-run</code> report what gc would remove instead of skipping it.</li><li>Leave the shared memory link from the auto-memory issue alone, apart from removing the link itself.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests cover status resolution, the PR lookup, the done trigger and volume removal; <code>talos gc --dry-run</code> lists workspaces and volumes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: gc on remote Docker hosts.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4168</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4174	2026-11-04	2026-10-28	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	5dd2b5186ae1-db9a-5e9e-40a10a396136	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0a