3557ed836ae1-affe-9a2f-11d6bf8da850	Talos container runner: non-root image user, opt-in docker socket, design for keys on remote hosts	2026-10-28 07:28:53	2026-10-28 10:04:37	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. Follow-ups from adt-4164 (dev-tools#47). The runner image runs as root, and the container always gets the docker socket, which gives root on the Docker host. Key files and the bind-mounted home must exist at the same path on a remote <code>dockerHost</code>.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Run the image as a non-root user, with a matching uid/gid for the bind-mounted <code>~/.claude</code> on Linux. Check that Windows Docker Desktop still works.</li><li>Mount the docker socket only when <code>agent.json</code> asks for it (e.g. <code>dockerSocket: true</code>). Without it, tests that need Docker fail with a clear message.</li><li>Key delivery to remote Docker hosts: write the options (docker secrets, env-only, a per-run volume fed by <code>docker cp</code>) and a recommendation into the Talos README. Don't build it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: a container run works end to end as non-root on the local Docker host, with and without the socket option; unit tests cover the docker arguments; the README covers the security notes and the remote-key options.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: implementing key delivery to remote hosts.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4175	2026-11-04	2026-10-28	done	low	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	dff2bef26ae1-843b-0663-37b3eb706590	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 10:04:37	adt	0	0
a264fd806af0-b3ed-60c0-3dfe2a23c6a4	Settings > Developer > UI: QuickList showcase with fixture data	2026-11-08 11:48:50	2026-11-08 14:18:31	0	<p>Fill the empty QuickList page under Settings &gt; Developer &gt; UI so developers see QuickList with every feature on, including selection, which no product list uses yet. The attached screens are a guide only.</p><ul><li>Fixture <code>app/utils/dev/quick-list-fixture.js</code>: about 45 records (title, status from the issue status classes, creator, created/updated dates, tags).</li><li><code>controllers/app/settings/ui/quick-list.js</code>: in-memory paging (20 per page), sort (updated, created, title), group (status, creator) and a title filter, all on the fixture. No Gaia calls, so no Mirage handler.</li><li><code>templates/app/settings/ui/quick-list.hbs</code>: QuickList in a <code>col-md-4</code> (the idea browser's width) with a header action, every named block (primary with status label, secondary with creator/date, tags), <code>@selectable</code>, and dummy selection actions "Archive" and "Delete" that only show a toast with the count. A small <code>btn-group</code> beside it switches the list into the loading, empty and error states.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; extend the settings acceptance test to cover paging, grouping, selection and the state switches.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: showcases of other components.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4357, aprom-4355</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> quick-list-selection-grouped.png, quick-list-states.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4358	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	51e6d0806af0-5856-9221-e46915