0babc1616af0-c789-00cd-39b16cb6cfc4	Ideas: pagination never shows; page by fetching one extra row (limit + 1) and record the decision	2026-11-08 15:02:35	2026-11-08 16:07:44	0	<p>The idea browser (aprom-4359) shows no ‹ › pagination, while Settings &gt; Developer &gt; UI does. Gaia's list response has no total (<code>meta.count</code> is the rows on this page only), so the browser falls back to counting the loaded ideas, <code>@total</code> is never above 20, and <code>QuickList::Pagination</code> hides because everything seems to fit on one page.</p><p><strong>Architecture decision (engineer, 2026-11-08):</strong> Prometheus never asks for totals or runs count queries to page. To show N rows it asks Gaia for N + 1. If N + 1 rows come back, there is a next page and only N are shown; fewer means this is the last page. One extra row costs nothing, while a count query (with joins) is wasted work.</p><ul><li>New pure helper <code>app/utils/quick-list/page-window.js</code>: <code>requestLimit(pageSize)</code> returns <code>pageSize + 1</code>, and <code>pageWindow(records, pageSize)</code> returns <code>{ items: first pageSize records, hasNext: records.length &gt; pageSize }</code>. Unit tests.</li><li><code>QuickList::Pagination</code> (<code>components/quick-list/pagination.{hbs,js}</code>) and the root <code>QuickList</code>: new <code>@hasNext</code>; <code>@total</code> becomes optional. Without a total, show the list-page style <code>1-20 / 20+</code> when there's a next page and <code>21-25 / 25</code> on the last page; enable ‹ when page &gt; 1 and › when <code>@hasNext</code>; hide only on page 1 with no next page. The header count uses the same text. With a total, behaviour is unchanged (the dev showcase keeps working).</li><li>Idea browser (<code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code>, <code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>): request <code>limit = requestLimit(20)</code>, render <code>pageWindow(...).items</code>, pass <code>@hasNext</code>; drop the total fallback that counts loaded ideas and any count queries used for paging.</li><li>Record the decision in <code>prometheus/docs/architecture/lists/decisions.md</code> (new; same format as <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md</code>): context, the limit + 1 rule, why not totals, and the helper to use.</li><li>Mirage idea handler: honour <code>limit</code> as sent (it may return limit rows of the N + 1 asked).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: with 25 ideas the browser shows <code>1-20 / 20+</code> with › enabled, then <code>21-25 / 25</code> with › disabled; the request carries <code>limit=21</code>. Unit tests for the helper, integration tests for pagination without a total, acceptance test for the browser.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: other lists (they adopt the helper when they move to QuickList).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4360	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	5d6283296af0-c789-00cd-52e84fd876b5	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 16:07:44	aprom	0	0
bf3b4bb96afc-30ee-311d-82d9b3c66cbd	Mentions: record mentions in idea descriptions and idea messages	2026-11-17 15:37:35	2026-11-18 14:13:43	0	<p>Turn on the mentions behavior (from the mention-framework issue) for ideas. Idea messages are markdown, so mentions there are markdown links to <code>/app/user/&lt;id&gt;</code>; the parser already handles them. Messages written by agents (e.g. Nestor) count too.</p><ul><li><code>app/metadata/model/Idea.php</code>: <code>mentions</code> field <code>description</code>, behavior added.</li><li><code>app/metadata/model/Ideamessage.php</code>: field <code>body</code>, behavior added after the existing ones.</li><li>api-tester cases for create and update of both.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> mentions of project members in ideas and idea messages are recorded once.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> an @-mention picker in Prometheus' idea composer (a Prometheus follow-up).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4645</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4647	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7b8e27936afc-30ee-311d-92e7628909b7	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	40d72c316afd-0da1-3ebc-3368c42b031b	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 14:13:43	agaia	0	0
78b3bce56ae3-3554-5d14-d93a3d51cfb5	ai test gaia: skip phpunit folders the checkout doesn't have (tests/services breaks the gate on dev)	2026-10-29 16:16:56	2026-10-30 22:22:40	0	<p><code>d3b3abb</code> (adt-4123) added <code>tests/services</code> to <code>PHPUNIT_FOLDERS</code> in <code>ai/lib/tests.py</code>. That folder only exists on gaia's unmerged <code>claude-issue-4117</code> branch, not on <code>origin/dev</code> (which has api, foundation, libraries, models, tools). Every Gaia full run on a branch from dev therefore fails with <code>Cannot open file "tests/services"</code>, and <code>ai ship</code> refuses to ship. This blocked agaia-4183, whose run then reverted <code>d3b3abb</code> in place inside <code>.dev-tools-runtime</code> (the guard for that is a separate issue).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>When building the phpunit suites, skip any folder in <code>PHPUNIT_FOLDERS</code> that doesn't exist in the checkout under test, and say so in the run output ("tests/services: not in this checkout, skipped"). Keep <code>tests/services</code> listed so it runs once gaia-4117 merges.</li><li>A skipped folder is neither a pass nor a failure in the summary, and it doesn't block <code>ai ship</code>.</li><li>Keep the <code>testmap.py</code> comment accurate (core/services and core/tasks are covered by tests/services when it exists).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests cover a checkout with and without <code>tests/services</code>; <code>ai test gaia</code> on a branch from current dev passes the phpunit stage; the 4123 assertion on <code>PHPUNIT_FOLDERS</code> still holds.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4191	2026-11-05	2026-10-29	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	8315f7c16ae3-dfe2-e2b6-bc822b27132e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-29 17:13:40	adt	0	0
cdc28a016ae6-3f4e-5224-297eae140aba	Gaia MCP: list an issue's attachments and fetch them (agents can't see mockups)	2026-10-31 17:43:41	2026-11-02 08:29:25	0	<p>Agents can't see the files attached to an issue. <code>gaia_get_issue</code> doesn't return them, and no tool downloads them. Talos agents therefore stop on issues whose design is in attached mockups (aprom-4044, aprom-4036). <code>Gaia.download()</code> already exists in <code>gaia-mcp/server.py</code> but no tool uses it.</p><ul><li><code>gaia_get_issue</code> also returns <code>files</code>: id, name, fileType, fileSize, dateCreated, read through the issue's <code>files</code> relation in its own query. <code>GET /upload</code> has no list action.</li><li>New tool <code>gaia_get_file(issue_number, name | upload_id)</code>. It returns an image as an MCP <code>image</code> content block, so the agent sees it directly. Any other file it saves to a local temp folder and returns the path. It refuses a file that isn't attached to that issue, and anything over 10 MB.</li><li>Unit tests in <code>gaia-mcp/tests/test_server.py</code>, and a README update.</li></ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4240	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	134fdb476ae6-2683-add7-c62777ae86b4	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-02 08:29:26	adt	0	0
e09b3a816aeb-2e52-8b27-fe45564a1ced	Workflow editor: avatars in the actor dropdown overflow the dropdown items	2026-11-04 22:42:40	2026-11-05 00:18:34	0	<p>In the workflow editor's properties panel (aprom-4057), the avatar in the Run agent step's Agent dropdown is too big: it overflows the dropdown item. The options are rendered by <code>related-fields/relate-actor</code>.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Render the avatar at the small size the user picker uses (<code>related-fields/relate-user</code>): same classes and size, avatar and name on one line, vertically centred. Reuse the existing classes. Only if none fits, add a scoped rule in the editor's module stylesheet.</li><li>Check the selected value in the closed select and the Ask a user picker, which use the same renderer.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Avatars fit inside each dropdown item and the closed select, matching the user picker's look.</li><li>No overflow at any item height.</li></ul><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4283	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	31c332686aeb-3897-5028-4ad08f945182	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-05 00:18:34	aprom	0	0
be99bdc36af3-1487-2734-819c1bfeaaec	Declare ember-concurrency and move tasks to the async-arrow syntax	2026-11-10 21:33:50	2026-11-11 16:41:13	0	<p>The app imports <code>ember-concurrency</code> in 7 files, but it isn't in <code>package.json</code>. It only comes in through ember-power-select 4, as ember-concurrency 2.3.7, which has no async-arrow transform.</p><p>ember-concurrency 5 (needed with power-select 9) removed generator tasks. In the Ember 6.12 spike they failed with <code>Using task(...) in any form other than task(async () =&gt; {}) is no longer supported</code> (about 24 failures).</p><h4>Step 1: tests first (they must pass on the current generator tasks)</h4><p>The current tests check the results of the searches and the permission save, but not how the tasks behave when they overlap. Uploads and the editor's <code>#</code> issue search have no tests at all. Add these before converting:</p><ul><li><strong>Search debounce and cancel</strong> (for example the global search in <code>application-header</code>): type twice within 500 ms and check that Mirage received exactly one search request and the results match the second query.</li><li><strong>Upload queue</strong> (<code>handleUpload</code>, <code>maxConcurrency(3).enqueue()</code>), for issue attachments in <code>issue-details</code> and wiki attachments in <code>wiki/page</code>: add 4–5 files with ember-file-upload's <code>selectFiles</code> / <code>dragAndDrop</code> test helpers. Check that no more than 3 upload requests are in flight at once, that every file finishes uploading, and that a file over the size limit is rejected.</li><li><strong>Editor <code>#</code> issue search</strong> (<code>projectrelated.js</code> <code>search</code>, passed to toast-ui as <code>@issueSearch</code>), on one screen such as issue create: type <code>#</code> plus text and check that the issue suggestions appear and the chosen one is inserted. The editor's existing mention tests only cover emoji suggestions.</li><li><strong>Role permission save</strong> (<code>updatePermission</code> → <code>updatePermissionTask</code>): add a case where one permission request fails, and check that the failure is reported.</li></ul><h4>Step 2: declare the dependency and convert the tasks</h4><ul><li>Add <code>ember-concurrency</code> to <code>package.json</code> directly, at the newest major that still supports Ember 4.1 (check its compatibility table) and has the async-arrow transform. Enable the transform if that version needs it.</li><li>Convert <code>task(function* () {…})</code> to <code>task({ …modifiers }, async () =&gt; {…})</code>, using <code>await</code> instead of <code>yield</code>, drop the <code>_self = this</code> workarounds, and pass modifiers as options (<code>.maxConcurrency(3).enqueue()</code> → <code>{ maxConcurrency: 3, enqueue: true }</code>). The 9 tasks:<ul><li><code>components/app-layouts/application-header.js</code>: <code>search</code></li><li><code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code>: <code>handleUpload</code> (enqueue, max 3) and <code>search</code>. <code>search</code> uses the bare <code>@task(function*…)</code> decorator form.</li><li><code>controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code>: <code>linkIssueSearch</code></li><li><code>controllers/app/project/issue/create.js</code>: <code>parentIssueSearch</code></li><li><code>controllers/app/project/wiki/page.js</code>: <code>handleUpload</code> (enqueue, max 3)</li><li><code>controllers/app/role/page.js</code>: <code>updatePermission</code> and <code>updatePermissionTask</code></li><li><code>controllers/prometheus/projectrelated.js</code>: <code>search</code>. It uses the classic <code>search: task(…)</code> property form in an <code>.extend()</code> class, which board, conversation, issue create and wiki create/edit inherit.</li></ul></li><li>The templates' <code>(perform …)</code> calls stay as they are.</li><li><strong>Watch out:</strong> only <code>await</code>s written directly in the task body can be cancelled. An <code>await</code> inside a helper method the task calls (e.g. <code>loadSearchData</code>) can't be. The generator version behaves the same way, so the step 1 tests should catch any difference.</li></ul><h4>Done when</h4><ul><li>The step 1 tests pass both before and after the conversion.</li><li>The full suite is green.</li><li>A search for <code>function*</code> in <code>app/</code> finds nothing.</li></ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4480	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	e454dd816af4-8f98-77af-0d745d58f664	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 16:41:13	aprom	0	0
13e5c6316af0-c789-00cd-f23e5efc26aa	Ideas: a search lists open ideas only unless "show archived" is on; server order only	2026-11-08 15:02:43	2026-11-08 16:30:59	0	<p>Today a search in the idea browser matches every status, and when search or "show archived" is on, the browser lists open ideas before archived ones within each page. With server paging, that reordering makes the rows disagree with the pages (aprom-4356/4359 notes). Engineer's decision: a search returns open ideas only unless "show archived" is on, and the order comes only from the server.</p><ul><li>In the idea query (<code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> / <code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code>): always AND <code>(Idea.status : open)</code> with the search unless show archived is on; with show archived, no status condition.</li><li>Remove the client-side open-before-archived ordering; render the page in the order Gaia returns.</li><li>Keep the "show archived" toggle visible during a search (today it's hidden then), so archived ideas can still be found.</li><li>Update the idea browser acceptance tests (search hides archived ideas; with show archived the search finds them; order follows the sort).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: as above; the request's query carries the status condition when show archived is off.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: putting show archived in the URL (separate issue).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4361	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	6bb9c9956af0-c789-00cd-6d1654a179de	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 16:30:59	aprom	0	0
1cef71d56af0-c789-00cd-09afea6c7b20	Ideas: keep "show archived" in the URL	2026-11-08 15:02:52	2026-11-08 15:19:04	0	<p>"Show archived" in the idea browser is controller state only (aprom-4356), so a reload or a shared link drops it. Engineer's decision: put it in the URL like <code>group</code>, <code>sort</code> and <code>page</code>.</p><ul><li>New query param <code>archived</code> (boolean, default false) on the idea controller, used by the footer toggle and the idea query; the route refreshes the list when it changes (page back to 1).</li><li>Links inside the idea area (<code>linkQuery</code>, the idea page links) keep it. Reset it with the other list params when leaving the idea area.</li><li>Acceptance test: turn show archived on, reload, archived ideas are still listed and the toggle shows "Hide archived".</li></ul><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4362	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	8aec46916af0-c789-00cd-fb16610093d1	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 15:19:01	aprom	0	0
