04066f646ad7-3bb5-2b49-3aa0ee427268	Workflow actor steps: Run agent (dispatched to the agent's runtime) and Ask a user	2026-10-20 17:12:36	2026-10-30 17:08:10	0	<p>Part of agaia-4048 (Workflows).</p><ul><li>'Run agent' creates a pending step (agent, prompt with expressions resolved, session new/resume, model rule, max turns) and publishes the user-scoped Hermes event <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> to the agent's user.</li><li>An endpoint where the agent's runtime, authenticated as the agent (client credentials, agaia-4028), claims the step and reports its outcome (done, needs input, blocked, failed, limit) with a comment; the engine continues along that output.</li><li>Timeouts: a step not claimed or not finished in time takes the 'failed' output.</li><li>'Ask a user': posts the question, waits for that user's reply comment or reassignment, then continues.</li></ul><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4051, ah-4055</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4052	2026-10-27	2026-10-20	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7a626c876ad7-b7ec-4943-0da4f6053570	eef04cc76ad7-d41d-2b49-e6106c38f089	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	b50f11866ae4-2bfe-db7f-d2862625e962	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 17:08:10	agaia	0	0
c47eb7986af0-9f8e-3bb7-a855f552f54c	p4m test ember: set JOBS=4 in Prometheus test containers (24 Babel worker threads hold ~4 GiB each), and a doctor check that it is in effect	2026-11-08 15:44:04	2026-11-08 16:17:37	0	<p><strong>Problem.</strong> Each warm Prometheus test container (<code>p4m-test-prometheus-*</code>) holds 4–5 GiB of private memory after building, and 5–7 GiB during a full suite. With 19.5 GiB for Docker, 3–4 of them fill it and Docker has had to be restarted (Agamemnon was paused to stop a repeat on the aga-Quick List milestone).</p>\n<p><strong>Cause (measured 2026-11-08).</strong> Almost all of it is in the single <code>ember build --watch</code> process. The main V8 heap is only 0.14 GB. <code>broccoli-babel-transpiler/lib/parallel-api.js:9</code> sizes its worker pool with <code>Number(process.env.JOBS) || os.cpus().length</code>: Docker reports 24 CPUs, so about 23 worker threads (34 threads in total), each with its own V8 heap, all kept alive by the watch build. <code>broccoli-persistent-filter</code> reads <code>JOBS</code> too. <code>--max-old-space-size</code> does not help (tested: 6.1 vs 6.8 GiB peak, 4.1 GiB idle either way).</p>\n<p><strong>Measurements</strong> (throwaway checkout of origin/dev, cold full suite, then edit + targeted test ×3, then a warm full suite):</p>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Setting</th><th>Cold build</th><th>Full suite</th><th>Peak, cold suite</th><th>Peak, warm suite</th><th>Idle after building</th></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>24–31 s</td><td>245 s</td><td>6.8 GiB</td><td>5.0 GiB</td><td>4.0–5.1 GiB</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>JOBS=4</strong></td><td>25–28 s</td><td>221 s</td><td>3.3 GiB</td><td>2.1 GiB</td><td>1.2–1.4 GiB</td></tr>\n<tr><td>JOBS=1</td><td>44 s</td><td>–</td><td>~2 GiB</td><td>–</td><td>1.7 GiB</td></tr>\n<tr><td>JOBS=2 / 8</td><td>32 s / 24 s</td><td>–</td><td>2.9 / 4.1 GiB</td><td>–</td><td>1.5 / 1.9 GiB</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>Test results are unchanged (1,116–1,117 passing). One test fails in some runs and passes in others, with or without the setting.</p>\n<p><strong>Do.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>installer/testenv.py</code> <code>PrometheusTestContainer.ensure()</code>: add <code>-e JOBS=4</code> to the <code>docker run</code>, next to <code>CI</code>/<code>TRAVIS</code>. Make it a named constant so it can be tuned.</li>\n<li>Existing containers keep their old environment. Recreate a container whose environment lacks <code>JOBS</code> (as <code>ensure</code> already does for a stopped one), so nobody has to run <code>p4m test clean</code> by hand.</li>\n<li><code>ai doctor</code>: when a warm Prometheus test container exists, warn if its <code>ember</code> process has more than about 20 threads (it has 15 with JOBS=4, 34 without). This catches a future toolchain change (for example a move to Embroider/Vite, where <code>JOBS</code> is ignored) that would silently bring the memory back.</li>\n<li>Check <code>prometheus-dev</code> (<code>ember serve</code>), which was not measured: if it has the same thread count, set <code>JOBS</code> there too.</li>\n<li>Unit tests for the run arguments and the doctor check.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Downsides.</strong> Cold-build memory still peaks at about 3.3 GiB, so several cold builds at once can still spike. The setting relies on the Broccoli <code>JOBS</code> convention (ember-cli 4.1.1, ember-cli-babel 7.26.11, broccoli-babel-transpiler 7.8.1 are pinned by the lock file), which the doctor check covers.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4369	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	651fc5416af0-c320-5488-ff4346165831	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 16:17:37	adt	0	0
3b6157c66afc-72fe-b62c-0f249642d38b	Issue: add the `search` metadata block	2026-11-17 16:22:19	2026-11-18 16:08:39	0	<p>Issue is the first searchable module. Add its <code>search</code> block to <code>app/metadata/model/Issue.php</code> so the migration adds the search columns and indexes to <code>issues</code>.</p><ul><li><code>'search' =&gt; ['type' =&gt; 'issue', 'fts' =&gt; ['subject' =&gt; 'A', 'description' =&gt; 'B'], 'fuzzy' =&gt; ['subject'], 'semantic' =&gt; ['subject', 'description'], 'exact' =&gt; ['issueNumber'], 'display' =&gt; ['title' =&gt; 'subject', 'snippet' =&gt; 'description']]</code></li><li>Run migrate locally and confirm the columns and indexes; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> and the graph.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>issues</code> has <code>searchVector</code> (filled for existing rows), <code>searchSemanticText</code>, <code>searchSemanticHash</code>, <code>searchEmbedding</code>, <code>searchEmbeddingHash</code>, <code>searchEmbeddedAt</code> and the indexes; Issue GET/PATCH payloads are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> filling the semantic columns (search behaviour and reindex), other modules.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4655</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 2</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4656	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	in_review	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	1fb236126afc-72fe-b62c-bf3c9291dd47	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Agent Odysseus	fb614f806afd-51e5-5cea-050afa8404e1	f605b4e862c6-4e44-047e-0b80b34dd385	2026-11-18 16:08:39	agaia	0	0
9fd1d5036ae2-1975-ad45-d515484870b5	Remember Me is overwritten by any later login: session expiry is stored per user, not per session	2026-10-28 15:58:23	2026-10-28 17:13:41	0	<h3>Problem</h3><p><code>TokenController::setSessionExpiration</code> writes one <code>sessionExpires</code> on the <strong>User</strong> row: +14 days with Remember Me (<code>sessionTimeoutForRememberMe</code>), +1 day without (<code>sessionTimeout</code>). <code>OAuthServer::addRefreshTokenGrant</code> refuses to refresh once <code>user.sessionExpires</code> has passed. So any later password login as the same user, without Remember Me, cuts every existing Remember Me session to 1 day. That includes another browser, a phone, or a re-login. Tools that log in as that user (a <code>GAIA_EMAIL</code> in gaia-mcp.env, api-tester profiles) do the same.</p><p>Also, Remember Me is a fixed 14-day limit from login that refreshing never extends. We need to decide whether that is intended or whether it should slide.</p><h3>Proposed direction (design decision needed)</h3><ul><li>Store the session expiry per session/refresh token, e.g. a column on <code>oauth_refresh_tokens</code> that is carried over on rotation, or a session record the refresh tokens belong to. <code>addRefreshTokenGrant</code> then checks the expiry of the token being used, not the user's.</li><li>Decide whether the expiry is fixed or sliding and document it in <code>docs/architecture/*/decisions.md</code>.</li><li>Optional: a short grace window (a few seconds) during which a just-rotated refresh token is still accepted, so a duplicate client request doesn't end the session.</li><li>Keep <code>AclLockoutGuard</code> soft-disable and session revocation (agaia-3954) working: revoking a user must still end all of their sessions.</li></ul><h3>Acceptance criteria</h3><ul><li>Test first: log in with Remember Me, then log in again without it; refreshing with the first session's token still works after 1 day and stops after 14.</li><li>A non-Remember-Me session still expires after <code>sessionTimeout</code>.</li><li>A soft-disabled user can't refresh any session.</li><li>TokenControllerTest and api-tester cases updated. The migration adds columns only.</li></ul><p>Related: aprom multi-tab refresh race (filed alongside), aprom-3942.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4182	2026-11-04	2026-10-28	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	18b878e66ae2-440d-ad45-2976c9f8f805	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 17:13:41	agaia	0	0
ea6df7856af0-9f8e-3bb7-ccf0fa323c97	p4m test ember: 4.5 GiB memory limit per Prometheus test container, and ai test reports an out-of-memory kill as such	2026-11-08 15:44:42	2026-11-08 16:28:03	0	<p><strong>Depends on adt-4369 (JOBS=4).</strong> Without it, every cold full suite goes over the limit (6.8 GiB peak), so this issue must not be merged first.</p>\n<p><strong>Problem.</strong> Test containers have no memory limit. When several build or test at once, one container can take Docker's whole 19.5 GiB VM down with it, and every run fails, not just the one that grew.</p>\n<p><strong>Sizing (measured with JOBS=4).</strong> The container total, including page cache, which the limit counts, peaked at 3.45 GiB on a cold full suite and 2.34 GiB on a warm one. Samples were 3 s apart, so short spikes may have been missed. 4.5 GiB leaves about 1 GiB of headroom. (4 GiB would leave only 0.55 GiB.)</p>\n<p><strong>Do.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>installer/testenv.py</code> <code>PrometheusTestContainer.ensure()</code>: <code>--memory 4.5g</code> as a named setting (overridable from <code>p4m.env</code>), and recreate a container whose limit differs, as for JOBS in adt-4369.</li>\n<li>Detect an out-of-memory kill and say so in the <code>ai test</code> summary, not as a test failure. The kernel kills the biggest process in the container, which may be the watch build, Chrome or <code>ember test</code>:\n<ul>\n<li><code>ember test</code> exits 137 → "killed: out of memory".</li>\n<li>Chrome killed → testem reports the browser exited or disconnected while the exit code is not 137: check the container's <code>memory.events</code> <code>oom_kill</code> count before and after the run.</li>\n<li>Watch build killed → the existing "ember build stopped" path: add the same <code>oom_kill</code> check to its message.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li>A suite stopped by OOM counts as a failed run that should be retried, never as a pass, and never as known failures.</li>\n<li>Unit tests for the run arguments and the OOM classification (exit 137; oom_kill increased with a browser error; no OOM).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Not tested yet.</strong> How each OOM case shows up in practice. Verify by running a suite in a container limited to 2 GiB before relying on the messages.</p>\n<p><strong>Downsides.</strong> A run that hits the limit fails and has to be re-run. The limit needs raising as the suite grows (the doctor or the OOM message should point at the setting).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4370	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	4052b7d66af0-621f-5488-2b0b9f1db123	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 16:28:03	adt	0	0
24b61c406af7-4c57-5be9-d904d408a68b	External Request: Docs: docassist model, adapter, Mirage and a doc-ai service	2026-11-13 14:13:56	2026-11-18 15:04:54	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>The Docs AI features (ghost text, Ask AI, AI Reviewer) all call Gaia's <code>Docassist</code> resource. This issue adds the shared data layer so each feature only builds its UI.</p><ul><li>Ember Data <code>docassist</code> model (docId, projectId, kind, instruction, status, result, inputChars, outputChars, createdUser, dateCreated, plus the request-only <code>selectionHtml</code>, <code>context</code>, <code>text</code>), adapter and serializer following the existing ones; request-only attributes are sent on create and never read back.</li><li><code>services/doc-ai.js</code>: <code>ask(doc, instruction, selectionHtml, context)</code>, <code>complete(doc, context)</code>, <code>review(doc, text)</code>. Latest request wins per kind (a newer call makes an older pending result be ignored); errors are thrown with Gaia's message, and 429 becomes a "too many requests, try again shortly" error.</li><li>Mirage: a <code>docassist</code> factory and a POST handler that returns canned results per kind (and a 429 scenario).</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the service (latest wins, error mapping, review result parsed from JSON).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the service returns parsed results from Mirage for each kind and surfaces errors.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any UI.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4537</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4539	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	deferred	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f77