b940f8d76ace-c075-2b63-f041f3d9bef2	Dashboard shows 404 for new users (invalid default widgets)	2026-10-13 15:56:41	2026-11-05 13:36:21	0	<p><strong>What happens:</strong> for any newly created user, the Dashboard link (<code>/app/</code>) renders the 404 "Oops! Page not found" page.</p>\n<p><strong>Root cause (verified):</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Gaia <code>app/api/v1/controllers/components/DashboardComponent.php</code> <code>afterCreate()</code> gives every new user a default dashboard with widgets <code>'issuesToday, weeklyMilestones'</code>.</li>\n<li>Prometheus only defines <code>recentIssues</code>, <code>activeMilestones</code>, <code>weeklyActivities</code>, <code>weeklyIssueTimelogs</code>, <code>weeklyConversations</code> (<code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>, <code>Dashboard.widgets</code>).</li>\n<li><code>app/routes/app/index.js</code> <code>model()</code> reads <code>widgetSettings[widget].model</code> for each widget, so an unknown name throws <code>TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'model')</code> in route <code>app.index</code>, which ends on the 404 page.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Older users (e.g. Hammad Hassan, Rana Nouman) have the five valid widgets, which is why the dashboard works for them. Reproduced with the new user claude-hammad@projects4.me.</p>\n<p><strong>Fix:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Prometheus: skip unknown widget names in <code>routes/app/index.js</code> (and keep the error inside the existing try/catch) so a bad setting can never break the page.</li>\n<li>Gaia (separate issue in A Gaia): change the default to valid widget names.</li>\n<li>Data: fix existing dashboards that hold <code>issuesToday, weeklyMilestones</code>.</li>\n</ul>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	4015	2026-10-20	2026-10-13	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	cc67bd526ace-6847-2b63-30230a156600	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-05 13:36:21	aprom	0	0
c1c1a5616ae4-c535-4a75-aa34b05b9f5f	Nestor: size budget per planned issue (≤10 hand-written files, 15 max with a reason), estimatedFiles in the plan block, validated by Talos	2026-10-30 18:06:57	2026-10-30 18:28:05	0	<p>Issues that touch many files take disproportionately longer for Agent Odysseus to generate: more files read into context, longer runs, more tokens, compaction, and more hallucinated or skipped areas (e.g. a PHPStan failure that went unnoticed). Review suffers too: across 98 CodeRabbit-reviewed gaia/prometheus PRs, findings per 1k changed lines fall from 9.4 (≤5 files) to 0.3 (26+ files), while Major findings per PR are highest on the largest PRs. Agent Nestor plans the issues, so the budget belongs in the plan.</p>\n<p><strong>Budget</strong> (what the agent has to write by hand):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Count every hand-written file the issue creates or changes, <strong>tests included</strong> (they cost generation tokens too).</li>\n<li>Don't count tool-generated output: <code>gaia/docs/generated/**</code>, the gaia-dev graph, <code>tools/api-tester/apis/backend.json</code>, lockfiles.</li>\n<li>Target ≤10 files. 11–15 only with a stated reason. Never more than 15: split instead.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Changes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>talos/agents/nestor/role.md</code>, "Splitting the work": the budget above and how to split along seams that still ship on their own (Gaia: framework capability → resource → behaviour/ACL cases; Prometheus: data layer/route → component → page integration). Never a half resource that leaves <code>dev</code> broken. "The plan block": the new fields.</li>\n<li>Plan block: each issue gets a required <code>estimatedFiles</code> (integer, hand-written files incl. tests) and a <code>sizeReason</code> (text), required when <code>estimatedFiles</code> &gt; 10.</li>\n<li><code>talos/lib/ideas/plan.py</code> <code>parse()</code>: reject a missing, non-integer or &lt;1 <code>estimatedFiles</code>, more than 15, or more than 10 without <code>sizeReason</code>. The errors go through the existing one-retry path (<code>FIX_PLAN</code>). Update the module docstring. Keep both fields in the normalised issue.</li>\n<li>When Talos creates the issue, add an "Estimated files: N" line (plus the reason when present) next to the "Depends on"/"Complexity" lines, so Agent Odysseus and the ship-time size check (adt-4196) can compare against it.</li>\n<li>The plan card in the Nestor UI (<code>nestor/web/app.js</code>) shows the estimate per issue if it's a one-line change; otherwise leave it out.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Unit tests in <code>talos/tests/test_ideas.py</code> for: valid estimate, missing estimate, 11–15 with and without reason, &gt;15, non-integer.</li>\n<li>Created issues carry the estimate line.</li>\n<li><code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes on Windows and Linux rules (dev-tools CLAUDE.md).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> measuring the real diff at ship time (adt-4196); changing <code>complexity</code> semantics (size is still not complexity).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4195	2026-11-06	2026-10-30	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	2e4dcfa66ae4-03ef-dd82-7c439b08959d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 18:28:05	adt	0	0
c36f1a806af9-dc19-2b19-98c763b4c050	AppUi::Tabs -- UI	2026-11-15 13:59:31	2026-11-15 22:40:51	0	<p>AppUi::Tabs (aprom-4568) renders bare <code>nav nav-tabs</code>, while the app's tabs use AdminLTE's <code>nav-tabs-custom</code> (task board milestone tabs <code>app-ui/task-board.hbs</code>, role permissions <code>role/permissions.hbs</code>, Gantt time scale). It has no consumer yet.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Render <code>nav-tabs-custom</code> markup exactly as the task board and role permissions do: same active tab marker, spacing, font and the optional count label (<code>label label-default milestone-tab-count</code>).</li>\n<li>Support tools on the right of the tab bar if the existing tabs have them; no new options otherwise.</li>\n<li>Move <code>role/permissions.hbs</code> onto it as the first consumer, with no visual change (screenshots before/after in a comment).</li>\n<li>Developer section: the demo follows the QuickList / EzSearch demo layout, with tabs with and without counts.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the control sidebar tabs (<code>nav-justified</code>) and the Gantt selector.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4582	2026-11-22	2026-11-15	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	06193c946af9-5202-2b19-0a77b09e0933	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-15 22:40:51	aprom	0	0
f134a6296af0-9f8e-3bb7-bede3b645a6b	Talos: stop a Prometheus test container 15 min after its issue's last run (not only under memory pressure after 72 h), with Agamemnon's resolve-conflict tests under the same budget	2026-11-08 15:44:49	2026-11-08 17:09:20	0	<p><strong>Problem.</strong> A Talos issue's Prometheus test container stays up from its first <code>ai test</code> until the issue is done (<code>workspace_gc</code>), through <code>awaiting_bot_review</code>, <code>in_review</code>, conflict waits and review rounds. On 2026-11-08 three of the five containers were idle at 0% CPU, holding about 8 GiB. <code>docker_free</code> (adt-4277) stops idle containers only when Docker is under memory pressure <em>and</em> the issue has been unchanged for 72 h, which doesn't cover these.</p>\n<p><strong>Measured cost of a restart.</strong> <code>ensure()</code> removes a stopped container (<code>testenv.py:432</code>), so the next <code>ai test</code> starts cold: about 40 s in isolation and 58 s median under load (first versus later targeted runs, 85 workspaces). A stopped container restarted with its files kept is ready in 31 s, only about 10 s better, so simply stopping or removing it is fine. Follow-up runs (422) have a median of 4.4 min, so the restart adds about 15–23% to them. With adt-4369 an idle container holds about 1.3 GiB instead of about 4, so this matters less after that issue lands.</p>\n<p><strong>Do.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Extend <code>talos/lib/docker_free.py</code> rather than adding a second mechanism: an idle rule that applies without memory pressure. A Talos workspace's test container whose issue has no run in flight and whose last run ended more than <code>idleTestContainerMinutes</code> ago (default 15) is stopped. Use the end of the last run (<code>talos.db</code>), not the tracker's modified time.</li>\n<li>Only containers labelled under <code>&lt;workspace&gt;/.runs</code>: never a checkout used interactively, and never a gaia slot container.</li>\n<li><strong>Agamemnon.</strong> <code>resolve-conflict</code> runs <code>ai test &lt;repo&gt; --changed</code> in the issue's workspace (<code>agamemnon/tool.py</code> <code>test_changed</code>), outside Odysseus's <code>maxParallel</code>. Once idle containers are stopped, every conflict fix starts a cold container that no budget counts. Make it take part in the same accounting as an Odysseus run. Either it counts as a run in flight in the dispatcher's gate, or it waits (<code>wait-for slot</code>) when the agent is at <code>maxParallel</code>. Decide which and record it in the README. The idle rule must also not stop a container while a <code>resolve-conflict</code> test is using it.</li>\n<li>README (Talos gc / docker_free) and unit tests: idle rule chosen or skipped (run in flight, inside the window, interactive checkout, slot container), and Agamemnon counted.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Downsides.</strong> A cold start of 40–60 s on each follow-up run after the window. A resumed issue loses its warm incremental build. Conflict fixes may wait for a free run slot, which delays merges.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4371	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	753c3a176af0-13d9-5f7c-0234d2e1cc81	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 17:09:21	adt	0	0
d03ceb906ae4-c535-4a75-cbe9dea78c17	ai ship: diff-size check against the file budget; ai rabbit digest: harvest and categorise CodeRabbit findings across agent PRs	2026-10-30 18:07:12	2026-10-30 18:28:54	0	<p>Nestor's per-issue file budget is an estimate. This issue measures the real change when it ships, so overruns are visible and the budget can be tuned. It also makes the CodeRabbit findings analysis (done by hand on 2026-10-30 across 98 PRs) repeatable, so the self-review rules stay current.</p>\n<p><strong>1. Size check in <code>ai ship</code></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Count the hand-written files in <code>files</code> (tests included). Exclude generated paths, configured in <code>ai/config.json</code>: <code>gaia/docs/generated/**</code>, the gaia-dev graph, <code>tools/api-tester/apis/backend.json</code>, lockfiles.</li>\n<li>Over 10: print a warning. Over 15: refuse unless <code>ship.json</code> has <code>sizeReason</code>, which then goes into the tracker notes and the PR's Notes section.</li>\n<li>When the issue has an "Estimated files: N" line (from the Nestor budget issue), print the estimate next to the actual count.</li>\n<li>Put the check in its own small module next to the existing cost gate (adt-4140), not inline in the ship command.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>2. <code>ai rabbit digest</code></strong> (extends <code>ai rabbit</code> from adt-4188)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>For Agent Odysseus PRs in <code>codeRabbitRepos</code> (optionally <code>--since DATE</code>, <code>--repo</code>), fetch CodeRabbit's inline comments and review bodies through the odysseus <code>gh</code>. Parse the inline findings plus the "Outside diff range" and nitpick/Trivial sections: PR, file, severity, category, title, whether it was addressed.</li>\n<li>Output a markdown report: counts by severity and category, the list of findings, and findings per PR by size bucket (files, and per 1k changed lines).</li>\n<li>Skip CodeRabbit's replies to the agent and its walkthrough/summary comments.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Unit tests: size counting with generated-path exclusion; the &gt;15 refusal and the <code>sizeReason</code> override; digest parsing on fixture bodies in both CodeRabbit formats (old <code>_⚠️ Potential issue_</code> and new <code>**Category** | **Severity**</code>, including <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code> outside-diff entries).</li>\n<li><code>ai ship --dry-run</code> shows the size line.</li>\n<li>No network in tests.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> automatically editing the rules files from the digest.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4196	2026-11-06	2026-10-30	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	7ebb39306ae4-03ef-dd82-d31778f13aea	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 18:28:54	adt	0	0
f6d382686af0-9f8e-3bb7-e1675a258e61	Talos: test slots for Prometheus runs, leased when tests start, with the baseline using the calling run's slot	2026-11-08 15:44:54	2026-11-09 12:08:26	0	<p><strong>Parked.</strong> Do this only if Docker memory is still tight after adt-4369, the memory-limit issue and the idle-container issue. After those, a Prometheus test container needs about 1.3 GiB idle and 2.1–3.3 GiB at peak, so about 5 can test at once in the 19.5 GiB VM.</p>\n<p><strong>Problem.</strong> Only Gaia runs lease a test slot (<code>SLOT_REPO = "gaia"</code> in <code>talos/lib/dispatcher.py</code>). Prometheus runs, and their test containers, are capped only by <code>maxParallel</code>, and the baseline container (<code>ai/state/baseline/prometheus</code>) is outside any cap.</p>\n<p><strong>Do.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Leasing a slot for the whole run wastes most of it. Measured on Gaia: 71% of a run's time is spent before its first test call, and work runs that end in <code>ready_to_ship</code> spend 94% of their time without one. So lease the slot when <code>ai test</code> / <code>p4m test ember</code> starts, not when Claude starts. This needs a lease that works across processes (for example lock files per slot under <code>state/</code>), because <code>ai</code> runs as a subprocess and the current <code>pool.Gate</code> exists only inside Talos.</li>\n<li>When no slot is free, <code>ai test</code> ends with a clear "no test slot" result instead of blocking inside the session. The run ends with a wait outcome, and Talos resumes it first when a slot frees.</li>\n<li><strong>Baseline: use the calling run's slot.</strong> <code>baseline.require</code> holds a machine-wide lock per repo and runs inside a run's <code>ai test</code>. If the baseline needed a slot of its own, the run holding the lock would wait for a second slot while the others wait on the lock until <code>LOCK_WAIT</code> and fail: a deadlock.</li>\n<li>Agamemnon's <code>resolve-conflict</code> tests lease a slot too, building on the accounting from the idle-container issue.</li>\n<li>README (parallel runs) and unit tests: lease at test time, no slot free, baseline using the caller's slot.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Downsides.</strong> When more Prometheus runs need tests than there are slots, they wait, which lowers throughput while the queue is busy. A session that waits for a slot for over an hour resumes with a cold prompt cache, and <code>dev</code> may have moved on, so it should sync first.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4372	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	deferred	low	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	6eb106c16af0-61d2-5f7c-da1db189353c	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-09 12:08:26	adt	0	0
15b840c86aee-ae56-c810-01b38ea03133	Nestor screens: allow a scoped <style> block for new components, and a design checklist	2026-11-06 20:31:17	2026-11-06 20:57:01	0	<p>Nestor's UI screens can only use classes that already exist in Prometheus: the screen sanitiser (<code>talos/lib/ideas/sanitize.py</code>, <code>SCREEN</code> policy) drops every <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> element and <code>style</code> attribute. A new component (for example a query builder, an autocomplete menu or AND/OR group blocks) has no existing classes, so Nestor has to fake it with boxes, tables and <code>form-control</code>, and the result looks generic next to a hand-built mockup. This issue lets a screen carry a small, tightly checked stylesheet, and gives Nestor a design checklist.</p>\n<h4>Changes</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>talos/lib/ideas/sanitize.py</code></strong>: add <code>clean_css(text)</code> and let the <code>SCREEN</code> policy keep one <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block per screen, with its content passed through <code>clean_css</code>. Rules:\n<ul>\n<li>Class selectors only: each selector in a list starts with <code>.</code> (descendant/child combinators and pseudo-classes such as <code>:hover</code> allowed; no element, id, attribute or universal selectors at the start).</li>\n<li>An allowlist of properties: layout (display, flex*, grid*, gap, align/justify*, position limited to relative/absolute, top/right/bottom/left, width/height/min-/max-, overflow, z-index), spacing (margin*, padding*), borders (border*, except <code>border-radius</code>), colours (color, background-color, border-color), type (font-size, font-weight, font-style, line-height, text-align, text-transform, letter-spacing, white-space, text-overflow), opacity, cursor, box-sizing.</li>\n<li>Colours only from the design system palette: the values in <code>prometheus/app/styles/variables.scss</code>, the fixed surfaces (<code>#fff</code>, <code>#ecf0f5</code>, <code>#f9fafc</code>, <code>#f4f4f4</code>, <code>#ddd</code>, <code>#aaa</code>, <code>#444</code>) and the issue status colours from <code>styles/issue/issue-status.scss</code>, plus <code>transparent</code>/<code>inherit</code>. Keep the list in one constant with a comment pointing at those files.</li>\n<li><code>border-radius</code> only as <code>50%</code> (design-system rule: square edges).</li>\n<li>Reject anything with <code>url(</code>, <code>@import</code>, <code>@font-face</code>, any other at-rule, <code>expression</code>, <code>behavior</code>, <code>javascript:</code>, backslash escapes or <code>&lt;/</code>.</li>\n<li>At most 8 KB of CSS after cleaning.</li>\n<li>Drop offending declarations or rules (not the whole block) and return a short reason for each.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong><code>talos/lib/ideas/screens.py</code></strong>: pull the style block out of the screen HTML, clean it, store it as <code>css</code> on the screen, and add the dropped-rule reasons to the existing <code>problems</code> list so Nestor is told.</li>\n<li><strong><code>talos/lib/ideas/page.py</code></strong>: put the cleaned CSS in a <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> after the stylesheet links, for both the app shell and <code>shell="none"</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>talos/agents/nestor/role.md</code></strong>, section "UI screens":\n<ul>\n<li>When a screen shows markup that has no existing class, add one <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block with classes scoped under the component's root class (e.g. <code>.query-builder …</code>), following the rules above. Existing classes first; never restyle existing ones.</li>\n<li>A short checklist: use the page pattern from the design system; existing classes first; show the empty, error and loading states that matter; realistic data from <code>ai kb</code>; for an interactive component show the key states as separate screens (e.g. menu open, error shown).</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong>Tests</strong> in <code>talos/tests</code> for <code>clean_css</code>, the screen parse and the page build.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Acceptance criteria</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>A screen with a style block using palette colours and class selectors renders with those styles in the PNG.</li>\n<li>Rules with an off-palette colour, <code>url()</code>, an at-rule, a non-class selector or a rounded corner are dropped and reported in <code>problems</code>; the rest of the block is kept.</li>\n<li>Screens without a style block render exactly as before.</li>\n<li>Existing talos tests pass.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Out of scope</h4>\n<ul><li>Letting Nestor preview its screen before replying (separate issue). Inline <code>style</code> attributes stay forbidden.</li></ul><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4291	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	ea9f39526ae8-fb0c-741d-cc93d6052db4	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	e5ae86866aee-ae56-c810-5a1c9ed82f6d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-06 20:57:01	adt	0	0
6ca8c7a66af3-b741-232a-0a83058b800e	Follow-up: clean-up and docs after the native intl service	2026-11-10 20:54:04	2026-11-10 23:04:28	0	<p>Depends on aprom-4471.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove the remaining ember-intl wording from docs and code comments, such as "service offered by ember-intl" in JSDoc and the architecture docs. Regenerated YUIDoc can wait for the docs clean-up in aprom-4469.</li>\n<li>Write the formatter's limits in <code>app/utils/intl/message-format.js</code> and in the translations section of the docs. Only <code>{arg}</code>, plural and select are supported; <code>number</code>, <code>date</code>, <code>time</code>, <code>selectordinal</code> and the other argument types throw "Unsupported argument type". Anyone adding them to a translation, from the app or from Gaia, must extend the formatter first.</li>\n<li>Fix or delete <code>views.app.theme</code> in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>. Nothing references it, and its <code>'&gt;</code> renders as broken link HTML under formatjs.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4472	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	0691c6036af3-9aaa-2a4b-eff9d4d60f47	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Agent Agamemnon	596023f06af3-e051-126b-2cffc369e970	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 23:04:28	aprom	0	0
490082836af0-c789-00cd-c60164cc12e4	QuickList: move selection and group-collapse state out of the root component	2026-11-08 15:03:37	2026-11-08 16:07:01	0	<p>The assemble issue (aprom-4357) left the root <code>QuickList</code> component holding the selected ids, the collapsed groups per groupBy, and the rendering, plus a group heading fallback written both in <code>index.hbs</code> and <code>group.hbs</code>. Its design review suggested splitting these.</p><ul><li>Move the selection into a small class (e.g. <code>app/utils/quick-list/selection.js</code>: tracked <code>Set</code> of ids, toggle, toggleAll(items), clear, state 'none'|'some'|'all') and the collapse state into another (<code>collapse-state.js</code>, per groupBy). The root creates and uses them; its arguments and blocks don't change.</li><li>Keep the group heading fallback in <code>QuickList::Group</code> only.</li><li>Unit tests for both classes; the existing integration tests must pass unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: no change in behaviour or public contract; the root component code shrinks to wiring and rendering.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4367	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	2a59b3986af0-4dec-01a7-016500c11e38	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 16:07:01	aprom	0	0
29b8c3c06aee-ae56-c810-4900725fb20b	Nestor: preview a screen before replying (ai screen render)	2026-11-06 20:31:37	2026-11-06 21:07:04	0	<p>Nestor writes a <code>nestor-screen</code> block and Talos renders it to a PNG only after Nestor has replied, so Nestor never sees what it designed and can't fix spacing, overflow or clipped text. This issue gives Nestor a command to render a screen during its turn, look at the PNG and correct it once before replying. It builds on adt-4291 (scoped style blocks), so the preview goes through the same cleaning as the final screen.</p>\n<h4>Changes</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>ai/lib/screen.py</code></strong> (new), registered in <strong><code>ai/ai.py</code></strong> as <code>ai screen render</code>:\n<ul>\n<li>Reads one <code>nestor-screen</code> block (the same fenced syntax Nestor puts in its reply) from stdin. Nestor can't use Write, so it pipes the block in with a heredoc.</li>\n<li>Parses and cleans it with <code>talos/lib/ideas/screens.py</code> (<code>parse</code>), renders it with Talos' <code>Renderer</code> (<code>talos/lib/ideas/render.py</code>, same stylesheet lookup as Talos: running Prometheus first, else the checkout's CSS).</li>\n<li>Writes the PNG to <code>dev-tools/talos/state/nestor/previews/&lt;key&gt;.png</code> (create the folder; overwrite on re-render) and prints the path, the stylesheet source used, and any cleaning problems.</li>\n<li>Clear, non-zero exits for: no block on stdin, invalid block, no Chromium-based browser found (reuse <code>RenderError</code>'s message).</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong><code>talos/agents/nestor/agent.json</code></strong>: add <code>Bash(dev-tools/ai/ai screen:*)</code> to <code>allowedTools</code>. Check that <code>Read</code> of the previews folder isn't covered by a <code>deniedTools</code> pattern.</li>\n<li><strong><code>talos/agents/nestor/role.md</code></strong>, section "UI screens": before replying, render each screen once with <code>ai screen render</code>, Read the PNG, fix what's wrong (overlaps, overflow, clipped text, empty areas, wrong pattern), then put the final block in the reply. One preview per screen per reply, to keep the cost down; mention in the reply anything still not right.</li>\n<li><strong><code>ai/README.md</code></strong>: document the command.</li>\n<li><strong>Tests</strong> in <code>ai/tests</code>: block parsing from stdin, output path, problem reporting, and the missing-browser error (renderer stubbed).</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Acceptance criteria</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>From the workspace root, piping a valid block into <code>dev-tools/ai/ai screen render</code> writes the PNG and prints its path.</li>\n<li>In a Nestor run, Nestor can render a screen, Read the PNG and revise the block within one turn, using only its allowed tools.</li>\n<li>Cleaning problems (including dropped CSS rules from adt-4291) are printed.</li>\n<li>The PNG matches what Talos renders for the same block afterwards.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Out of scope</h4>\n<ul><li>Interactive prototype pages (claude.ai artifacts) from Nestor; that needs a separate check of whether the Artifact tool works in Talos' headless runs.</li></ul>\n<p>Depends on adt-4291.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4292	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	ea9f39526ae8-fb0c-741d-cc93d6052db4	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	5e87f1826aee-4078-adb7-af4e96561d89	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-06 21:07:04	adt	0	0
d5c005466ae4-c535-4a75-89c9fe740d57	Pre-PR self-review from CodeRabbit history: path-scoped correctness rules, correctness-reviewer agent, ship-issue and address-review updates	2026-10-30 18:07:17	2026-10-30 18:39:56	0	<p>CodeRabbit raised about 185 findings (about 50 Major) on 98 Agent Odysseus PRs (gaia #189–234, prometheus #526–577). Almost none were about the main flow. They were about what happens when something fails, repeats, races, gets odd input or meets a user without permission. Today's pre-PR <code>design-reviewer</code> only checks layering and SOLID, is optional, and even missed the layering findings. This issue moves those lessons to the point where the code is written, and adds a required correctness pass before the PR. Changes are in the Pr4M workspace repo (<code>.claude/</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>Finding classes</strong> (≈count; example PRs)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Input edge cases (30): <code>false</code> vs null/'' (g195), trailing newline (g205), conflicting ids (g205), unknown CLI options (g206/209), arrays where objects expected (p554/555).</li>\n<li>Async races/stale state, Prometheus (24): an older response overwriting newer state (p544/545/546/553), double submit while pending (p528/561), unhandled rejections (p543/544/574), work after destroy (p563).</li>\n<li>Security/permissions (22): escalation via Permission/RestController (g216/217), SSRF-type issues (g226), XSS (p527/543), missing <code>setting.update</code> (g205), ACL scope (g230).</li>\n<li>Tests that can't fail (20): status-only assertions (g199/203), no rejection-path tests (p544/557), fixtures that hide a regression (p550/552).</li>\n<li>Partial failure/rollback (15): p553 (6 Major), a failed side write breaking the main flow (g219/226/233).</li>\n<li>Keyboard/a11y (11): modal focus, mouse-only toggles, IME Enter, unlinked labels, screen-reader state (p533/549/550/551/559/560/562).</li>\n<li>Failures reported as success, gaia-dev tooling (10): unchecked <code>file_put_contents</code>/<code>json_encode</code>/regeneration results, exit code 0 on failure (g206/211/212).</li>\n<li>Atomicity/transactions (7): g192/193/196/198/234.</li>\n<li>Layering/style placement (6): g192/217/219, p533/558/560.</li>\n<li>Existing data/backward compatibility, seeds, docs, CI (14): p526/574, g196/212, g207.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Changes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Path-scoped rules in <code>.claude/rules/</code>, same format as <code>gaia-acl.md</code>. Each rule is one line saying what to do, citing the PR it came from:\n<ul>\n<li><code>gaia-correctness.md</code> (<code>gaia/core/**</code>, <code>gaia/app/**</code>): input edges, permissions, partial failure, atomicity, existing data.</li>\n<li><code>gaia-dev-tooling.md</code> (<code>gaia/tools/gaia-dev/**</code>): check every write/encode result, non-zero exit on failure, reject unknown options.</li>\n<li><code>prometheus-async-a11y.md</code> (<code>prometheus/app/**</code>): one default pattern for "latest request wins" and "drop the second submit" (check whether ember-concurrency is a direct dependency, it's imported in 7 files), rollback on failed save, keyboard/focus rules.</li>\n<li>A test-strength line in <code>api-tester.md</code> and the Prometheus file: every new test fails if the line it covers is reverted; every failure path gets a rejection test.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li>New agent <code>.claude/agents/correctness-reviewer.md</code> (Sonnet, read-only, separate from <code>design-reviewer</code> to keep design and correctness apart). It walks the diff with the classes above: for every await, write, endpoint, input, interactive element and test, what happens on failure, repeat, race, odd input or missing permission. Same output format and finding cap as <code>design-reviewer</code>.</li>\n<li><code>.claude/skills/ship-issue/SKILL.md</code> step 2: run <code>design-reviewer</code> and <code>correctness-reviewer</code> in parallel on every code change (not only "non-trivial" ones).</li>\n<li><code>.claude/skills/address-review/SKILL.md</code>: when a valid CodeRabbit finding belongs to a class not yet in the rules, add the rule line in the same change.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> the main Pr4M checkout has uncommitted edits in <code>.claude/settings.json</code>, <code>.claude/skills/*</code> and an untracked <code>.claude/rules/</code>. Work from a fresh branch and don't overwrite or include those.</p>\n<p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> the rules files load on matching paths. Running the new agent on a past PR with known findings (e.g. prometheus #553 or gaia #205 at their first commit) reports at least half of CodeRabbit's Major findings.</p>\n<p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> running CodeRabbit's CLI locally; changes to <code>design-reviewer</code>'s checklist.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4197	2026-11-06	2026-10-30	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	032b87e86ae4-0f71-dd82-03e4bed5273c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 18:39:56	adt	0	0
71937bd66af3-1487-2734-de60aaf747c5	Use explicit this in templates (remove implicit-this fallback)	2026-11-10 21:32:33	2026-11-10 23:45:06	0	<p>Ember 6 removed the implicit <code>this</code> fallback, so <code>{{projectList}}</code> must be <code>{{this.projectList}}</code>. In the Ember 6.12 spike this was the first build error: templates fail to compile.</p><p><strong>Scope</strong>: ember-template-lint's <code>no-implicit-this</code> rule finds 283 violations in 42 of the 338 templates. Most are property lookups (<code>definition</code> alone is 153, then <code>currentUser</code>, <code>model</code>, <code>data</code>, <code>value</code>, …) and arguments in <code>form-fields/*.hbs</code> (<code>v-focus</code>, <code>focus-out</code>, …).</p><ul><li>Prefix property lookups with <code>this.</code>. Leave component invocations such as <code>{{application-controlbar}}</code> as they are.</li><li>Turn on <code>no-implicit-this</code> in the template-lint config so new violations can't come back.</li></ul><p>Works on the current Ember 4.1; no dependency changes.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4473	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	d52348e16af3-f72b-26ef-3082e40b5c4d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-10 23:45:06	aprom	0	0
