b26004f76afd-eb4a-95cd-6f7392ab2dcf	ai ship: a failing gaia-dev drift check in a run worktree doesn't say to regenerate with ai gaia-dev (agaia-4665 blocked)	2026-11-18 15:30:58	2026-11-18 15:37:15	0	<p>agaia-4665 blocked at <code>ai ship</code>: <code>docs generate --check</code> reported <code>profiles.md is stale</code>. The failure only repeats gaia-dev's own hint (<code>run tools/gaia-dev/bin/gaia-dev docs generate</code>), so the agent tried host php, found no <code>vendor/</code>, and <code>composer install</code> failed. <code>ai gaia-dev docs generate</code> already runs gaia-dev in a throwaway <code>gaia-gaia</code> container with the <code>gaia_vendor</code> volume, but nothing pointed at it.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>ai/lib/ship.py</code>: when a drift check fails, name the regenerate command (<code>dev-tools/ai/ai gaia-dev docs generate</code> / <code>graph export</code>).</li><li><code>ai/lib/gaiapack.py</code> <code>gaia_dev_command</code>: container path mounts the checkout at <code>/src</code>, the <code>gaia_vendor</code> volume read-only at <code>/src/vendor</code>, and uses <code>--entrypoint php</code>; still <code>--network none</code> and the caller's uid:gid. The host path stays when <code>vendor/autoload.php</code> exists.</li><li>Unit tests for the command and the ship hint; README note.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> from a run worktree with an empty <code>vendor/</code>, the checks run, <code>ai gaia-dev docs generate</code> writes files owned by the host user, and dev-tools tests pass.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4675	2026-11-25	2026-11-18	in_review	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	222806746afd-5c80-c5f9-c414173379ce	