e5ba51966aee-99ea-ca02-c2bd61c9a4d3	ezSearch: query tree model, operator registry, schema helpers and Gaia serializer	2026-11-06 21:38:45	2026-11-06 22:35:55	0	<p>First step of ezSearch, the native replacement for jQuery QueryBuilder. A query is one tree (groups and conditions) edited by a search bar and a visual builder. This issue adds the pure model and the serializer to Gaia's existing wire format, for example <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND (Issue.status !: done))</code>. The wire format, saved searches and the API do not change. There are no component or page changes. Leave <code>utils/query/parser.js</code>, <code>utils/query/builder.js</code> and <code>utils/metadata/querybuilder-operators.js</code> alone; they are removed in a later phase.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/query/ast.js</code>:<ul><li>Node factories <code>group(conjunction 'AND'|'OR', children)</code> and <code>condition(field, operator, value)</code>. <code>value</code> is a string, an array for IN, <code>[from, to]</code> for BETWEEN, or null for nullary operators.</li><li>Each node gets a stable <code>id</code> for UI keys.</li><li>Immutable helpers: add, replace, remove and move a node; set a conjunction; <code>isComplete(condition)</code>.</li><li><code>normalize(tree)</code> merges nested groups that have the same conjunction, unwraps one-child groups and drops empty ones. A group always has exactly one conjunction.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/utils/query/operators.js</code>: ONE registry. Each entry has:<ul><li>a key and the Gaia symbol;</li><li>the text aliases accepted when typing;</li><li>a translation key for its label;</li><li>its arity (0, 1, 2 or n);</li><li>the field types it applies to (text, number, enum, user, date).</li></ul>It covers all Gaia operators (<code>: !: &lt; &lt;: &gt; &gt;: CONTAINS !CONTAINS STARTS !STARTS ENDS !ENDS BETWEEN !BETWEEN NULL !NULL EMPTY !EMPTY</code>) plus IN and NOT IN. Text aliases: <code>= != &gt;= &lt;= ~ IN</code>, case-insensitive. Lookup helpers: by symbol, by alias, valid for a type, and the default operator for a type.</li><li><code>app/utils/query/schema.js</code>: <code>createSchema({module, fields, textField, values})</code>, where a field is <code>{id, aliases, labelKey, type, valueSource}</code>. Field resolution, case-insensitive, in this order:<ol><li>the id;</li><li>the id without its module prefix (<code>startdate</code> gives <code>Issue.startDate</code>);</li><li>an alias or the label;</li><li>a unique prefix of an alias or label.</li></ol>Otherwise a word without a module prefix defaults to <code>&lt;Module&gt;.&lt;word&gt;</code> as a text field, and an unknown <code>Module.field</code> is kept as a text field (so there is no unknown-field error). Value resolution for enum and user fields: an exact match first, then a unique prefix gives the stored value, and an ambiguous prefix returns the candidates. The module is pure: values are passed in, nothing is loaded here.</li><li><code>app/utils/query/serializer.js</code>: <code>serialize(tree)</code> returns <code>{query, errors}</code> and never throws. Rules:<ul><li>Every group and every condition is in brackets, with one conjunction per group (normalize first).</li><li>Incomplete conditions are left out, and an empty tree gives an empty string.</li><li>IN is written as <code>CONTAINS 'a','b'</code> and NOT IN as <code>!CONTAINS 'a','b'</code>; a one-value IN or NOT IN is written as <code>:</code> or <code>!:</code>.</li><li><code>BETWEEN a AND b</code>; values with spaces are quoted with <code>'</code>; single spaces between field, operator and value.</li><li>It refuses, with an error code and the node id, values that contain <code>(</code>, <code>)</code> or <code>'</code>, or uppercase <code>NULL</code> or <code>EMPTY</code>. Gaia's <code>core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php</code> can't handle these yet; the agaia requests in the same plan fix that, and this refusal is relaxed in a later phase.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/utils/query/composer.js</code>: <code>compose(baseTree, userTree)</code> returns an AND of both, normalized. Boards use it in a later phase.</li><li>Errors are <code>{code, params, nodeId?}</code> with no intl inside the utils. Add the English messages and the operator labels to <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (unit tests)</p><ul><li>ast (helpers, normalize), operators (alias and symbol lookups, types), schema (every resolution step, including the default-module rule and ambiguous prefixes), serializer (every rule, the one-value IN, the nested merge, each refusal) and composer.</li><li><code>group(AND,[priority:High, group(OR,[type:Bug,type:Story])])</code> serializes to <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND ((issuetype.name : Bug) OR (issuetype.name : Story)))</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> parsing text, real schemas, components.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4293	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	4ef163156aee-a7e9-ca02-76c25a6aa71d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-06 22:35:55	aprom	0	0
a50899676ae2-1975-ad45-79e71c25b85d	SQL injection in refresh_token grant: OAuthServer::addRefreshTokenGrant concatenates request input into findFirst	2026-10-28 15:58:29	2026-10-28 18:09:26	0	<h3>Problem</h3><p><code>core/libs/authorization/OAuthServer.php</code> <code>addRefreshTokenGrant()</code> builds its conditions by string concatenation:</p><ul><li>line 102: <code>Oauthrefreshtoken::findFirst("refresh_token = '$refreshToken'")</code>, where <code>$refreshToken</code> comes straight from the request body.</li><li>line 106: <code>User::findFirst("email = '$email'")</code>, with a value taken from the DB row.</li></ul><p><code>POST /api/v1/token</code> is unauthenticated (<code>TokenController::$authorization = false</code>), so anyone can inject into the condition. A crafted <code>refresh_token</code> such as <code>' OR '1'='1</code> could match another user's refresh token row and pass the checks in front of the grant. This breaks the Gaia rule against building SQL/PHQL by concatenation.</p><h3>Fix</h3><ul><li>Use bound parameters: <code>findFirst(['conditions' =&gt; 'refresh_token = :token:', 'bind' =&gt; ['token' =&gt; $refreshToken]])</code>, and the same for the user lookup.</li><li>Check that the bshaffer grant then still validates the token itself.</li></ul><h3>Acceptance criteria</h3><ul><li>Test first: a refresh_token grant with an injection payload returns 401 "Invalid Token" and issues no token.</li><li>A normal refresh still works. TokenControllerTest and api-tester token cases pass.</li></ul><p>Found while investigating the Remember Me multi-tab logout.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4183	2026-11-04	2026-10-28	done	critical	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	bb535f386ae2-0ec0-7254-ef209825ab1d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-