027792286ae2-5841-26f7-b1a017f64f11	Task board: wrap long words in the card subject and cut it to 3 lines	2026-10-28 18:03:46	2026-10-28 18:25:06	0	<p>On the task board, a card subject with a word longer than the card is wide (for example <code>OAuthServer::addRefreshTokenGrant</code>) runs past the right edge of the card, because <code>.issue-card-subject a</code> has no wrap rules. A subject of 10 to 15 words also makes the card very tall.</p><ul><li>In <code>app/styles/modules/board.scss</code>, under <code>.issue-card-subject a</code> (around line 281), add <code>overflow-wrap: anywhere</code> (with <code>word-break: break-word</code> as a fallback) so long tokens break inside the card. Words of normal length still wrap at spaces.</li><li>In the same rule, cut the subject to 3 lines with an ellipsis: <code>display: -webkit-box; -webkit-box-orient: vertical; -webkit-line-clamp: 3; overflow: hidden;</code>. Keep the font size and line height as they are.</li><li>In <code>app/components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code> (subject <code>LinkTo</code>, around line 62), add <code>title={{issue.subject}}</code> so the full subject shows on hover. The plain-text <code>title</code> attribute is enough; don't render the subject as HTML.</li><li>Check that clicking the subject still opens the quick view and that dragging cards still works.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A subject with a single 40+ character token stays inside the card in every lane, at the narrowest lane width.</li><li>A 15-word subject shows at most 3 lines and ends with an ellipsis. Hovering over it shows the full subject.</li><li>Short subjects look the same as before.</li><li>An integration test for the task board renders a card with a long unbroken subject, checks that the subject link has the <code>title</code> attribute, and checks that the subject does not overflow the card (<code>scrollWidth &lt;= clientWidth</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing the font size, and the subject on the quick view or the issue page.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4184	2026-11-04	2026-10-28	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	64f095546ae2-0730-ad4c-0f4f79bfce54	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 18:25:06	aprom	0	0
f082db426aee-99ea-ca02-5c9025f48d6a	ezSearch: lexer and parser for loose text and Gaia format, with round-trip tests	2026-11-06 21:38:56	2026-11-06 23:39:58	0	<p>The ezSearch bar lets people type loosely and formats the query on Enter. This issue turns text into the query tree from the query-model issue, with plain errors that carry positions. The text is either loose input or Gaia's wire format from saved searches and <code>?query=</code> URLs. Pure utils only; the old <code>app/utils/query/parser.js</code> stays untouched.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/query/lexer.js</code>: tokens with <code>start</code>/<code>end</code> and a kind (field, operator, value, quoted value, comma, and/or keyword, bracket, bare word). Quotes may be <code>'</code> or <code>"</code>, and quoted text may contain spaces and and/or. The SearchBar reuses the tokens to colour the query, so keep the kinds stable.</li><li><code>app/utils/query/parse.js</code> (a new name, because <code>parser.js</code> is the old one): <code>parse(text, schema)</code> returns <code>{tree, errors}</code>, using <code>createSchema</code> from the query-model issue. Grammar:<ul><li>Brackets nest groups, and redundant brackets are allowed.</li><li>AND/OR in any case, and AND is implied between conditions.</li><li><strong>Every group has one conjunction: mixing AND and OR in the same group without brackets is an error, never interpreted. An implied AND counts as AND.</strong></li><li>Inside a bracketed leaf the value runs to the closing bracket and is trimmed (Gaia wire format, e.g. <code>(assignedTo.name : Hammad Hassan)</code>, <code>(Issue.milestoneId : 5 )</code>). Outside brackets a value is one word unless quoted.</li><li>Comma lists after IN or CONTAINS; <code>BETWEEN a AND b</code>; NULL and EMPTY take no value.</li><li>Consecutive bare words become one <code>textField CONTAINS 'phrase'</code> condition.</li></ul></li><li>Binding through the schema:<ul><li>Fields resolve as in <code>schema.js</code>, including the default-module rule.</li><li>The operator must be valid for the field type.</li><li>Enum and user values resolve to the stored value (exact first, then a unique prefix).</li><li>Dates accept <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>, <code>MM/DD/YYYY</code> and <code>today</code>, and are output as <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Error codes with params and positions:<ul><li>missing operator ("Choose an operator after Priority") and missing value;</li><li>mixed AND/OR ("AND and OR can't be mixed in one group. Add brackets", at the second conjunction);</li><li>unknown value with the allowed choices ("'zzz' isn't a Status. Pick one of: …") and ambiguous value;</li><li>operator not valid for the type;</li><li>bad date, and BETWEEN needs two values;</li><li>unbalanced bracket.</li></ul>Add the English messages to <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.errors.*</code>.</li><li><code>tests/helpers/query-schema.js</code>: a fixture Issue schema (priority, status, type, milestone, assignee, start date, subject) with static values, reused by later issues.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (unit tests)</p><ul><li>These loose inputs serialize exactly:<ul><li><code>priority:high</code> gives <code>(Issue.priority : High)</code>.</li><li><code>prio = hi status != done</code> gives <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND (Issue.status !: done))</code>.</li><li><code>assignee in rana, hammad</code> gives <code>(assignedTo.name CONTAINS 'Rana Nouman','Hammad Hassan')</code>.</li><li><code>timezone</code> gives <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS timezone)</code>.</li><li><code>start between 05/01/2026 and 2026-08-31</code> gives <code>(Issue.startDate BETWEEN 2026-05-01 AND 2026-08-31)</code>.</li><li><code>(type:bug OR type:story) milestone:v0.1.1</code> gives <code>(((issuetype.name : Bug) OR (issuetype.name : Story)) AND (issuemilestone.name : v0.1.1))</code>.</li><li><code>description ~ crash</code> gives <code>(Issue.description CONTAINS crash)</code>.</li></ul></li><li><code>status:new or type:bug milestone:v0.1.1</code> gives the mixed error at the implied AND.</li><li>Round trip: <code>parse(serialize(parse(q)))</code> deep-equals <code>parse(q)</code>, and serializing again is stable, for:<ul><li>every query built in <code>routes/app/project/board.js</code> (l.58, 71, 77, 83, 90-97, 140, 161, 166) and <code>gantt.js</code> (l.59, 76-78);</li><li>the header search query in <code>components/app-layouts/application-header.js</code>;</li><li>the saved-search formats the jQuery builder produced (equal, not_equal and contains on strings; date comparisons and BETWEEN; nested groups).</li></ul></li><li>Each error code is tested with its position.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> suggestions, components, removing the old parser.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4293</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4294	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	7b6571e16aee-2bf2-c2c7-c4f253c17dc5	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-06 23:39:58	aprom	0	0
92bd45a46af3-1487-2734-45fa05072c1f	Declare async and inverse explicitly on all ember-data relationships	2026-11-10 21:33:06	2026-11-11 12:41:00	0	<p>ember-data 5 requires <code>async</code> and <code>inverse</code> on every <code>belongsTo</code> / <code>hasMany</code>; it throws <code>Expected options.async from @belongsTo('user', options) to be a boolean</code>. In the Ember 6.12 spike this was behind almost all 385 acceptance failures: Mirage model discovery fails, then the steps die on <code>user.update is not a function</code>.</p><p><strong>Scope</strong>: 110 declarations in 26 files under <code>app/models</code>. About 6 set <code>async</code> and about 14 set <code>inverse</code>.</p><ul><li>Set <code>async: true</code> everywhere unless a relationship is known to be synchronous. It's the current default, so behaviour stays the same.</li><li>Decide <code>inverse</code> per relationship: the matching relationship name, or <code>null</code> when there's none. This needs judgement; check each pair of models.</li><li>Add <code>polymorphic: true</code> where relationships are polymorphic.</li></ul><p>All of these options exist in ember-data 4.1, so this works today. Mirage 2.2 reads the same options, so the acceptance tests check the inverse choices.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4476	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	9a048ca96af4-e6e7-5c94-06cc8929efb2	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 12:41:00	aprom	0	0
114100546aee-a7e9-ca02-a22c1cde2f99	EzSearch::SearchBar: typed queries with suggestions, formatting and errors	2026-11-06 21:39:29	2026-11-07 01:04:15	0	<p>The text editor of ezSearch. Today the Issue list search input is readonly and only opens the jQuery panel. This component lets people type a loose query that is formatted into Gaia's exact format. It is standalone: <code>&lt;EzSearch::SearchBar @tree @schema @placeholder @onChange @onRun /&gt;</code>. The <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> container (later issue) keeps it in sync with the visual builder, and no page uses it yet.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search/search-bar.{js,hbs}</code> (Glimmer):<ul><li>Uses <code>FormFields::FieldText</code> (modifiers through <code>...attributes</code> for keydown and the caret position) and holds the draft text while editing.</li><li>On Enter (menu closed) or blur, <code>parse</code> against <code>@schema</code>. If it parses, call <code>@onChange(tree)</code> and replace the text with <code>serialize(tree)</code>, which uses exact ids such as <code>Issue.priority</code>, not labels. Enter also calls <code>@onRun()</code>.</li><li>When there are errors, show the translated message with its position under the input (<code>span.error.text-red</code>, screen <code>bar-error</code>), keep the text, and never call <code>@onChange</code> or <code>@onRun</code>.</li><li>When <code>@tree</code> changes from outside while not editing, show <code>serialize(@tree)</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Suggestion menu from <code>complete()</code> (completer issue): a Bootstrap <code>dropdown-menu</code> under the input with section headers and key hints (screen <code>toolbar-typing</code>). Up and Down move, Tab or Enter accept, Enter with the menu closed runs, Esc closes. Keep it open while typing and close it on blur.</li><li><code>app/components/ez-search/query-text.{js,hbs}</code>: shows the formatted query when the bar is not focused, with fields, operators and and/or keywords coloured from lexer tokens. Render plain text in spans, never <code>htmlSafe</code>. Clicking it focuses the input.</li><li><code>app/styles/components/ez-search-bar.scss</code>, imported in <code>app/styles/app.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.ez-search-bar</code>. Colours are <code>$secondaryColor</code> for fields, <code>$primaryColor</code> for operators and <code>$highlightColor</code> for keywords; square edges. It is a separate file so the Panel PR doesn't conflict.</li><li>Mobile (below 768px, screen <code>mobile-views</code>): the bar takes the full width, the suggestion menu spans the bar's width, and the hint line is hidden.</li><li>Strings (menu headers, hints) go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.searchBar.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests with the fixture schema)</p><ul><li>Typing <code>prio = hi status != done</code> and pressing Enter calls <code>@onChange</code> and <code>@onRun</code> and shows <code>((Issue.priority : High) AND (Issue.status !: done))</code>.</li><li>Typing <code>prio</code> opens the menu with Priority highlighted; Tab inserts it.</li><li>Arrow keys and Esc behave as described.</li><li><code>status:zzz</code> shows the unknown-value error, and <code>status:new or type:bug milestone:v1</code> shows the mixed AND/OR error; neither calls anything.</li><li>An outside <code>@tree</code> change updates the text.</li><li>Coloured tokens are rendered as text, not HTML.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the toolbar (Saved Searches, Builder, Search, Clear), page integration.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4296</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> toolbar-typing.png, bar-error.png, mobile-views.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704