afa120556af9-dc19-2b19-2f4f346844ed	AppUi::Avatar and AppUi::UserChip -- UI	2026-11-15 13:59:11	2026-11-15 14:42:49	0	<p>AppUi::Avatar (aprom-4569) invented a new avatar system (<code>.app-avatar</code> with its own 24/36/64px sizes, grey background and initials) instead of standardising the one the app already uses. It also duplicates <code>Agent::UserAvatar</code>, which already handles people and agents.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Follow the existing markup: AdminLTE <code>img-circle</code> with <code>img-sm</code> / <code>img-xs</code> (see <code>conversation-ui/comment-frame.hbs</code>, <code>issue/issue-details.hbs</code>, <code>widgets/weekly-conversations.hbs</code>, <code>app-ui/notifications/notification.hbs</code>). Sizes are the ones those classes give; no new sizes.</li>\n<li>Agents must show the agent avatar exactly as <code>Agent::UserAvatar</code> does today (<code>Agent::Avatar</code>). Build on <code>Agent::UserAvatar</code> or make it the implementation; don't keep two avatar components.</li>\n<li>Remove the initials fallback and <code>styles/modules/app-avatar.scss</code> unless something already in the app does the same; if a fallback is needed, propose it in a comment first.</li>\n<li>UserChip: the avatar plus name the way the issue list shows the assignee (<code>templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs</code> assignee column) and issue details show it; same spacing and font, linked where those link.</li>\n<li><code>project/member-avatars.hbs</code> (the one consumer) must look as it did before 4569.</li>\n<li>Developer section: the demo follows the QuickList / EzSearch demo layout, showing a person, an agent and a missing image in each existing size.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> moving the ~15 other avatar usages; they move when touched.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4578	2026-11-22	2026-11-15	done