839229216af4-a328-1af5-0c4f72c43788	External Request: Docs: Doc resource (title, body, owner, locked, tags) as standard project-scoped CRUD	2026-11-11 09:59:31	2026-11-11 12:01:09	0	<p>Projects get a Docs module where teams create, list and open documents. This adds the backing <code data-tomark-pass="">Doc</code> resource as plain REST CRUD, following the new-resource guide <code data-tomark-pass="">docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code> (exemplar gaia#193, Idea).</p>\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass=""><code data-tomark-pass="">app/metadata/model/Doc.php</code>, table <code data-tomark-pass="">doc</code>: <code data-tomark-pass="">title</code> varchar(255) required, <code data-tomark-pass="">body</code> text (nullable), <code data-tomark-pass="">projectId</code> varchar(36) required, <code data-tomark-pass="">ownerId</code> varchar(36) required, <code data-tomark-pass="">locked</code> bool default false, plus the standard <code data-tomark-pass="">id</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">dateCreated</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">dateModified</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">createdUser</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">modifiedUser</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">deleted</code>. Behaviours: <code data-tomark-pass="">createdUserBehavior</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">modifiedUserBehavior</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">dateCreatedBehavior</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">dateModifiedBehavior</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">softDeleteBehavior</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">auditBehavior</code>.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Relationships: <code data-tomark-pass="">project</code> belongsTo Project, <code data-tomark-pass="">owner</code> hasOne User (via <code data-tomark-pass="">ownerId</code>), <code data-tomark-pass="">createdBy</code>/<code data-tomark-pass="">modifiedBy</code> hasOne User, <code data-tomark-pass="">tag</code> hasManyToMany Tag via Tagged (<code data-tomark-pass="">relatedTo = 'doc'</code>), <code data-tomark-pass="">tagged</code> hasMany Tagged. Add the inverse <code data-tomark-pass="">doc</code> relationship on <code data-tomark-pass="">Tagged</code> and <code data-tomark-pass="">docs</code> on <code data-tomark-pass="">Project</code>, the same way Issue is wired.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">ACL metadata: <code data-tomark-pass="">'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via <code data-tomark-pass="">projectId</code>, so only project members with the <code data-tomark-pass="">doc.*</code> permissions can read/create/update/delete.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Empty <code data-tomark-pass="">app/models/Doc.php</code> and <code data-tomark-pass="">DocController</code> (RestController subclass), the <code data-tomark-pass="">'Doc'</code> line in <code data-tomark-pass="">core/config/models.php</code>, the <code data-tomark-pass="">doc</code> route in <code data-tomark-pass="">core/config/routes.php</code>, <code data-tomark-pass="">routes.v1.json</code>, the placeholders in <code data-tomark-pass="">generate-backend-apis.php</code> and a regenerated <code data-tomark-pass="">backend.json</code>.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">api-tester: harness table and seed rows, fixture ids, <code data-tomark-pass="">acl.json</code> cases (member with and without <code data-tomark-pass="">doc.*</code>, non-member) and <code data-tomark-pass="">client.json</code> cases (create, list by project, get with <code data-tomark-pass="">owner</code> and <code data-tomark-pass="">tag</code> rels, delete).</li><li data-tomark-pass="">New <code data-tomark-pass="">docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>, D-001: Docs is a new, independent module built from scratch and shares no code or tables with Wiki (beyond the generic Tag/Tagged tagging). Wiki is kept unchanged while Docs is built; once the Docs module is complete, the Wiki code is retired. Whether existing wiki content is migrated into Docs or dropped is decided at retirement, once the Docs body format is settled.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">No permission seed SQL (the reviewer grants <code data-tomark-pass="">doc.*</code> by hand). Regenerate the gaia-dev graph and <code data-tomark-pass="">docs/generated</code>.</li></ul>**Acceptance:** a project member with <code data-tomark-pass="">doc.create</code> can POST a doc and list it with <code data-tomark-pass="">((Doc.projectId : X))</code>; a user without <code data-tomark-pass="">doc.read</code> or outside the project gets 403/empty; tags attach through Tagged; the full test suite and CI drift checks pass.\n<p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> live events, enforcing <code data-tomark-pass="">locked</code>, owner-change rules, body format/versioning, any change to Wiki.</p>\n<p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 13 (A new resource has a fixed set of touchpoints (metadata, parent relationships, model, controller, models/routes config, api-tester catalog and acl/client cases) that must ship together, or dev is left with a resource that has no ACL cases; the decision doc is one small file.)</p>\n<p>Complexity: simple</p>\n	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4488	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	82e4bfb76af4-a328-1af5-a2e822effc3f	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	1b0f56806af4-cbb8-f1c6-017157bdbfb0	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 12:01:09	agaia	0	0
3cc7b9a16aee-a7e9-ca02-05e7f68eb615	EzSearch::Panel: visual builder with groups and conditions	2026-11-06 21:40:12	2026-11-07 01:33:55	0	<p>The visual editor of ezSearch: nested groups with an AND/OR switch, and rows of field / operator / value. It is standalone: <code>&lt;EzSearch::Panel @tree @schema @onChange /&gt;</code>. The <code>&lt;EzSearch&gt;</code> container (later issue) keeps it in sync with the search bar, opens it inline under the bar and adds Save Search. No page uses it yet.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search/panel.{js,hbs}</code>: renders the root group; an empty tree shows one empty AND group.</li><li><code>app/components/ez-search/group.{js,hbs}</code>:<ul><li>A bordered block with a crimson (<code>$primaryColor</code>) left edge for AND and a plum (<code>$highlightColor</code>) one for OR. A group has exactly one conjunction.</li><li>The header has an AND/OR <code>btn-group btn-xs</code> switch, "Condition" and "Group" buttons, and a remove button (not on the root).</li><li>Groups nest to any depth.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/components/ez-search/condition.{js,hbs}</code>:<ul><li>A row with the field (<code>FormFields::FieldRelate</code> over the schema fields by label), the operator (<code>FieldRelate</code> over the operators valid for the field type), <code>EzSearch::ValueEditor</code> and a remove <code>btn-box-tool</code>.</li><li>Changing the field resets the operator to the type's default and clears an incompatible value.</li><li>An incomplete row stays in the tree with a muted "Incomplete: left out of the query" note, and the serializer skips it.</li><li>Serializer refusals for the row (brackets, apostrophes, NULL/EMPTY) show under it.</li></ul></li><li>All changes go through the immutable helpers in <code>app/utils/query/ast.js</code> and come out as <code>@onChange(newTree)</code>; the components never mutate <code>@tree</code>.</li><li>Responsive, using the Bootstrap grid (screens <code>builder-open</code>, <code>mobile-views</code>):<ul><li>From 768px a row is field <code>col-sm-3</code>, operator <code>col-sm-2</code>, value <code>col-sm-6</code> and remove <code>col-sm-1</code>.</li><li>Below 768px the field and the remove button share the first line, and the operator and the value each take a full line.</li><li>Below 768px the group buttons are icon-only (texts <code>hidden-xs</code>) and nested groups are indented less.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/styles/components/ez-search-panel.scss</code>, imported in <code>app/styles/app.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.ez-search-panel</code>. Square edges, existing tokens only, no shadows. Strings go in <code>translations/en-us.json</code> under <code>components.ezSearch.panel.*</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>The tree from screen <code>builder-open</code> renders: an AND group with status IN, start date BETWEEN, one incomplete assignee row and a nested OR group with two type rows.</li><li>Toggling AND/OR, adding and removing conditions and groups, and changing the field each emit the expected tree.</li><li>The incomplete row is in the tree and absent from <code>serialize</code>.</li><li>A value with <code>(</code> shows the refusal.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> drag and drop of rows, the toolbar, page integration.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4298</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> builder-open.png, mobile-views.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4299	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	f1e4c6896aee-7faa-7e7e-d6c002c8918b	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 01:33:55	aprom	0	0
b48a99686af9-dc19-2b19-bc9cd41a8a44	AppUi::StatusLabel and labels/tags -- UI	2026-11-15 13:59:16	2026-11-15 15:01:11	0	<p>Labels, tags and status badges are drawn in several different ways (colour, border, font, size) across the app and the developer section. AppUi::StatusLabel (aprom-4570) should be the one way to show a status, and tags need one way too.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>StatusLabel must look exactly like the status in the issue list (<code>templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs</code>: <code>badge</code> + <code>status-style</code> + <code>status-label</code>) and the Recent Issues widget: same font size, weight, padding, colours and square edges.</li>\n<li>Check <code>conversation/linked-issue-box.hbs</code> (its one consumer) matches the issue list.</li>\n<li>Tags: list every way a tag/label is drawn today (e.g. <code>label label-default</code> in the QuickList demo, <code>issue-card-tags</code> on the task board, <code>user-skills-tags</code>, wiki tags, <code>agent-grant</code>, <code>role-record__granted</code>) and post the list with screenshots as a comment. Then add <code>AppUi::Tag</code> following the most used existing look (likely <code>label label-default</code>), unless the comment shows a better existing candidate.</li>\n<li>The developer section's demos (StatusLabel, QuickList, list page, DataTable) must show statuses and tags only through these two components, so every demo looks the same.</li>\n<li>Developer section: the StatusLabel/Tag demo follows the QuickList / EzSearch demo layout, showing every issue status.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Depends on aprom-4575 (it changes the DataTable demo).</p>\n<p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> moving every existing label in the app; pages move when touched.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4579	2026-11-22	2026-11-15	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	f28dd8a76af9-0656-6c4c-82722a1e3c3f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-15 15:01:11	aprom	0	0
5138a1586af0-c789-00cd-9fbb8e1a1a13	Ideas: move the browser's sort and group definitions into a util with unit tests	2026-11-08 15:03:45	2026-11-08 17:14:36	0	<p>The idea browser's QuickList options (sort list, group list with <code>groupKey</code>/<code>groupLabel</code> closures, creators map, <code>buildSort</code>) live in a getter in <code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> and have no unit tests (aprom-4359 notes).</p><ul><li>Move them to <code>app/utils/ideas/list-options.js</code> as pure functions taking what they need (intl, progress lookup, creator lookup); the controller only calls them.</li><li>Unit tests for the sort list, the group list (none, plan status, created by) and <code>buildSort</code> (created-by grouping puts <code>Idea.createdUser</code> first).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: no change in behaviour; new unit tests pass.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4368	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	3b34c2b96af0-b3ed-60c0-369a444a326a	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	b96e07436af0-1cbd-01a7-e0cef18f0856	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 17:14:36	aprom	0	0
509fe8e26aee-a7e9-ca02-85ed803cd96f	EzSearch: one tree for search bar and panel, toolbar and public API	2026-11-06 21:40:32	2026-11-07 02:17:51	0	<p>Ties ezSearch together: one query tree as tracked state, edited live by <code>EzSearch::SearchBar</code> and <code>EzSearch::Panel</code>, with the list toolbar around them. This is the component pages use from the next phase: <code>&lt;EzSearch @schema @query @baseQuery @savedSearches @onApply @onSave @aclContext /&gt;</code>. No page uses it in this issue.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/components/ez-search/index.{js,hbs}</code> (Glimmer):<ul><li><code>@tracked tree</code>, parsed from <code>@query</code> (the Gaia string) when it changes. If a stored query fails to parse, its errors are shown under the bar.</li><li>SearchBar and Panel both get <code>tree</code> and both update it through <code>onChange</code>, so they stay in sync live. Applying text from the bar replaces the tree, so incomplete builder rows are dropped (accepted).</li><li>Check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after every await.</li></ul></li><li>Toolbar, in the existing <code>.search</code> layout (screens <code>toolbar-typing</code>, <code>builder-open</code>):<ul><li>Saved Searches <code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> over <code>@savedSearches</code> (<code>{name, query}</code>): picking one loads its query into the tree and marks it active with <code>fa-check</code>.</li><li>Then the SearchBar.</li><li>A Builder <code>btn-default</code> (<code>fa-sliders</code>, <code>active</code> while open) that toggles the Panel inline under the bar, closed by default.</li><li>Search (<code>AppUi::Button btn-primary</code>, <code>@aclContext</code>), disabled while the bar has errors.</li><li>Clear, which empties the tree and applies.</li></ul></li><li>Mobile (below 768px, screen <code>mobile-views</code>): the toolbar wraps. The bar takes the first full-width row; the second row has Saved Searches as <code>fa-bookmark</code> plus a caret and Builder as an icon on the left, and Search and Clear on the right. Save Search is full width. Styles go in <code>app/styles/components/ez-search.scss</code>, scoped under <code>.ez-search</code>.</li><li>Applying (Search, or Enter in the bar) calls <code>@onApply(queryString)</code>. The query string is <code>serialize(compose(parse(@baseQuery), tree))</code>; <code>@baseQuery</code> is never shown in the bar or panel. Nothing is applied when serializing gives errors.</li><li>When <code>@onSave</code> is given, a Save Search <code>btn-primary</code> at the bottom right of the open panel calls <code>@onSave(serialize(tree))</code>. The page owns the save dialog.</li><li>Labels: reuse <code>global.form.search</code>, <code>global.form.clear</code>, <code>global.form.savesearch</code> and <code>views.app.issue.list.savedsearch.label</code>, and add <code>components.ezSearch.builderToggle</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> (integration tests, fixture schema)</p><ul><li>Typing in the bar updates the open panel, and editing the panel updates the bar text.</li><li><code>@query</code> in Gaia format loads into both.</li><li>Choosing a saved search loads it.</li><li>Search calls <code>@onApply</code> with the base query ANDed in.</li><li>Clear empties both editors and applies the base query only.</li><li>An invalid bar disables Search.</li><li>Builder toggles the panel; Save Search appears only with <code>@onSave</code>.</li><li>Checked in the browser at desktop width and at 390px.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> using it on the Issue list or other views, removing jQuery QueryBuilder (next phases).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4297, aprom-4299</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> toolbar-typing.png, builder-open.png, bar-error.png, mobile-views.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4300	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	2e369f496aee-7be2-e5ce-ca7fee79279d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 02:17:51	aprom	0	0
fe4718986ae6-bdab-5224-0bac9d1c9016	Assignee picker: People and Agents groups, agents shown with 'runs for <sponsor>'	2026-10-31 17:48:46	2026-11-02 09:49:57	0	<p>Part of agaia-4026 (Agents). Split out of aprom-4044.</p><ul><li>The issue assignee picker lists project members in two groups, People and Agents.</li><li>Agents show the robot avatar from aprom-4044 and, on the right, 'runs for &lt;sponsor name&gt;'.</li><li>Extend the existing relate-user field, not a new picker. Ask before adding a new generic component.</li><li>Mirage and acceptance tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4044, adt-4240</p><p>Mockup: <code>agents-in-context-and-identities.png</code> (the Assignee dropdown), attached here. Read it with <code>gaia_get_file</code>.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4241	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	f7553b636ae8-ebca-18a1-5c6cd479ad6e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-02 09:49:57	aprom	0	0
5e1942206af0-970b-16ca-9542899db6df	Developer section: route, admin nav item, component registry and Components box	2026-11-08 17:20:30	2026-11-08 17:51:12	0	<p>We are building a Component Library for developers: one page per reusable UI component with a live demo, controls, an event log and docs. It must be isolated from Settings (developer-only, and it keeps Settings light). This issue builds the section and its navigation; the entry boxes and the docs box are built in parallel issues and the entries come after.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li><strong>Routes</strong> in <code>app/router.js</code> under <code>app</code>: <code>developer</code> (path <code>/developer</code>) with <code>components</code> and <code>component</code> (<code>/components/:name</code>). <code>developer.index</code> and <code>developer.components</code> redirect to the first registered component. An unknown <code>:name</code> shows an error box with a link back to the first component, not a crash.</li><li><strong>Nav</strong>: a <code>Developer</code> item in <code>views.Navigation.adminItems</code> (<code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> ~l.173; icon <code>code</code>, route <code>app.developer</code>, anchorRoute <code>developer</code>, aclContext <code>setting.read</code>, projectRelated false). Add every new route to <code>routeMaps</code> in <code>services/acl.js</code> mapped to <code>setting.read</code>. No new Gaia permission.</li><li><strong>Registry</strong> <code>app/utils/developer/component-registry.js</code>: an ordered list of entries <code>{ name, label, group, status (stable|experimental), summary, usedIn: [{label, route}], demo (component name), doc (file name in public/ui-docs), variants (optional count/labels) }</code> plus helpers <code>find(name)</code> and <code>grouped(filter)</code>. Groups: Lists, Search, Forms, Overlays, Menus. Ship it empty of real components except a placeholder entry if needed for tests; entries are added by later issues.</li><li><strong>Layout</strong> <code>templates/app/developer.hbs</code>: content-header "Developer Component Library", <code>col-md-3</code> <code>box box-primary</code> "Components" (count badge, a search input filtering the registry by label/summary client-side, group headings, active item marked) + <code>col-md-9</code> outlet. Put the box in <code>components/developer/component-nav.{hbs,js}</code>. Below md the box stacks above the entry.</li><li><strong>Entry route</strong> <code>routes/app/developer/component.js</code> resolves the registry entry and the template renders the entry's demo component with <code>{{component}}</code>; the demo composes the entry boxes from the parallel issue itself.</li><li>Developer-facing text is English only in this section (engineer's decision: no translations for the Developer section); the nav item label still uses a translation key like the other nav items.</li><li>Styles scoped under <code>.developer</code> in <code>app/styles/modules/developer.scss</code>; design system, square edges.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: an admin sees Developer in the Admin nav; the Components box lists registry entries grouped, the search filters them, the active one is marked; deep links work; a user without <code>setting.read</code> neither sees the item nor reaches the route. Acceptance test (Gherkin) for nav, search and unknown name.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: the entry boxes, the docs box, real entries, removing Settings -&gt; UI.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> library-entry.png</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4374	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	5d51af446af0-970b-16ca-455730e26234	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Ha