beaa47376af9-dc19-2b19-2fc5e9a2bb4f	AppUi::Box -- UI	2026-11-15 13:59:26	2026-11-15 15:24:00	0	<p>AppUi::Box (aprom-4571) must render exactly like the boxes on existing pages (<code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>: gradient top bar, 18px title, square edges). Compare it with the issue list box and the project overview boxes side by side.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The header takes a title (<code>box-title</code>) the way every page writes it, plus the <code>tools</code> block for <code>btn btn-box-tool</code> buttons; check the tools sit and size like the issue list's.</li>\n<li>Support the existing box modifiers the pages use (<code>list-view</code>, <code>box-body no-padding</code>, <code>collapsed-box</code> if used) instead of new ones.</li>\n<li>Use AppUi::Box inside the new list components (DataTable / ListToolbar demos) so the developer section shows the real page box.</li>\n<li>Developer section: the demo follows the QuickList / EzSearch demo layout, showing each variant used in the app (primary, default, with tools, with footer, no-padding body).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Depends on aprom-4575 and aprom-4576.</p>\n<p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> moving existing boxes (new code only, as agreed).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4581	2026-11-22	2026-11-15	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	26e06f336af9-195e-6c4c-c60122e5cb92	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-15 15:24:00	aprom	0	0
b4f13b566ae5-f83a-391a-0b0b7895847f	Talos: orchestrator agent kind and Agent Agamemnon (feed Odysseus, restart mechanical stops)	2026-10-30 20:40:20	2026-10-30 21:35:55	0	<p>After planning, the reviewer assigns issues to Agent Odysseus one at a time, and assigns back issues that stopped for a purely mechanical reason. Agent Agamemnon takes over both jobs. It is a deterministic Talos agent of kind <code>orchestrator</code>: no LLM and no Claude runs.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> #4199, #4200</p><h4>Scope</h4><ul><li>Agamemnon works only on milestones whose name starts with <code>aga-</code> (case-insensitive), e.g. <code>aga-v1</code>, in Odysseus's projects.</li><li>It has its own Gaia user (<code>agent.agamemnon@projects4.me</code>), with credentials in <code>dev-tools/gaia-mcp/agamemnon.env</code>. It needs no git or GitHub identity.</li><li>Odysseus must list Agamemnon's user id in <code>acceptAssignmentsFrom</code>.</li></ul><h4>Triggers</h4><ul><li>Hermes <code>issue.status.changed</code> and <code>issue.assignee.changed</code> events through the existing <code>Listener</code>, debounced a few seconds before the sweep.</li><li>A sweep on every (re)connect.</li><li>A periodic sweep every <code>sweepMinutes</code> (default 5).</li></ul><h4>Sweep</h4><ol><li><strong>Capacity:</strong> free slots = <code>maxInFlight</code> (default: the worker's <code>maxParallel</code>) minus the issues assigned to Odysseus across its projects.</li><li><strong>Restarts first.</strong> A restart candidate meets all of these:<ul><li>it is in an <code>aga-</code> milestone, assigned to an owner, with status feedback or pending;</li><li>Odysseus was its last modifier, so the reviewer hasn't touched it since the handback;</li><li>its Talos <code>handoff_reason</code> is in <code>autoRetryReasons</code> (turn_budget, cost_budget, interrupted, branch_checked_out, talos_error);</li><li><code>auto_retries</code> is below <code>maxAutoRetries</code> (2).</li></ul>For branch_checked_out, wait until the branch is no longer checked out in another folder; Agamemnon never touches that checkout. Add a public <code>workspaces.branch_holder()</code> for this check.</li><li><strong>New issues:</strong> status new, unassigned or assigned to an owner, not an Epic, and every "Depends on" issue done. Order by priority, then milestone name, then issue number.</li><li><strong>Assign:</strong><ul><li>re-read and re-check the issue;</li><li>set only the assignee to Odysseus, leaving the status alone so Odysseus's own action for new, feedback or pending runs;</li><li>post a short comment saying why it was assigned. For a restart, the comment also gives the restart count and says there is nothing new from the reviewer and the work should continue where it stopped;</li><li>increment <code>auto_retries</code> on restarts.</li></ul></li></ol><h4>Safety</h4><ul><li>Circuit breaker: after <code>failStreakLimit</code> (default 3) consecutive non-restartable failed or blocked handbacks, Agamemnon pauses itself.</li><li><code>talos pause|resume agamemnon</code>.</li><li><code>--dry-run</code> only logs what it would do.</li><li><code>enabled: false</code> by default.</li></ul><h4>Code</h4><ul><li><code>registry.py</code>: kind <code>orchestrator</code> and fields milestonePrefix, worker, owners, maxInFlight, sweepMinutes, autoRetryReasons, maxAutoRetries, failStreakLimit, with validation.</li><li>New <code>lib/orchestrator/</code>:<ul><li><code>policy.py</code>: pure functions is_new_candidate, is_restart_candidate, rank, free_slots, breaker_tripped;</li><li><code>worker.py</code>: the Orchestrator class.</li></ul></li><li><code>tracker.py</code>: <code>issues_in</code>, an assignee-only <code>assign</code>, and <code>type</code> in <code>issue()</code>.</li><li><code>talos.py</code>: start the orchestrator next to the ideas branch in <code>cmd_run</code>; add pause/resume; show state in status.</li><li><code>agents/agamemnon/agent.json</code>.</li><li>A README section.</li></ul><h4>Tests</h4><p>Policy unit tests, plus worker tests with a fake tracker covering: capacity, restarts before new work, the retry cap, skipping when the reviewer modified the issue, waiting on the branch, the dependency skip, the epic skip, the non-<code>aga-</code> skip, the breaker and dry-run.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4201	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0d690f56ad7-404c-ce18-27bd5d2a1517	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	94b000b56ae5-07a8-de02-39f47a67afdf	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 21:35:55	adt	0	0
6f7591f66af0-970b-16ca-daeca3f706fb	Developer section: entry header, Controls and Event log components	2026-11-08 17:20:47	2026-11-08 17:48:26	0	<p>Every Component Library entry has the same frame: a header box, the demo, a Controls box and an Event log. This issue builds those shared pieces so each entry only writes its demo and its controls.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li><code>Developer::EntryHeader</code> (<code>components/developer/entry-header.{hbs,js}</code>): <code>box box-primary</code> with the label, a status label (stable = <code>label-success</code>, experimental = <code>label-warning</code>) in <code>box-tools</code>, the summary and "Used in" links (LinkTo per <code>usedIn</code> item). Takes a registry entry.</li><li><code>Developer::Entry</code> (<code>components/developer/entry.{hbs,js}</code>): the frame. Named blocks <code>&lt;:demo&gt;</code> (in a <code>box box-default</code> "Demo" <code>col-md-7</code>, with a Reset box-tool calling <code>@onReset</code>), <code>&lt;:controls&gt;</code> (in <code>box box-default</code> "Controls" <code>col-md-5</code>) and <code>&lt;:docs&gt;</code> (full width below). Yields an event logger to the blocks.</li><li><code>Developer::StateSwitch</code>: btn-group for forced states (<code>@states</code>, default normal/loading/empty/error; <code>@value</code>, <code>@onChange</code>).</li><li>Event log: a small class <code>utils/developer/event-log.js</code> (tracked list, newest first, capped at 50; <code>log(name, ...args)</code>, <code>wrap(name, fn)</code> returning a function that logs then calls <code>fn</code>, <code>clear()</code>) and <code>Developer::EventLog</code> (box "Event log", table time / <code>@name</code> / payload as short JSON, Clear box-tool, empty state "No events yet").</li><li>Controls inside entries use existing <code>FormFields::*</code> (checkbox, relate-simple selects) per the 