8da7b9526af9-ba4e-b3ac-cca56b2c8a9e	ai ship: bring an unshipped branch up to date with its base before refusing	2026-11-15 15:32:29	2026-11-15 15:46:09	0	<p>aprom-4580 stalled because <code>ai ship</code> stops with "origin/dev has moved past this branch" while the work is still uncommitted. <code>git merge origin/dev</code> then refuses because a file is changed both locally and on dev, and the agent tried a WIP commit under a throwaway identity, which the permission classifier rightly denied. The issue went to the owner as <code>pending</code>. Unblocking it by hand took <code>git stash push</code>, <code>git merge --ff-only origin/dev</code>, <code>git stash pop</code>.</p>\n<h4>Change</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>In <code>ai ship</code> (<code>ai/lib/</code>, the base check before committing): when the branch has no commits of its own beyond its base and the base has moved, update it itself: stash (with a named message, since worktrees share the stash list), <code>merge --ff-only</code> the base, pop.</li>\n<li>Pop clean: re-run the full test (the tree changed) before committing; report that it did so.</li>\n<li>Pop conflicts: leave the conflict in the tree (or restore the stash) and hand back with a message the Agamemnon classifier maps to <code>merge_conflict</code> (e.g. "merge conflict after updating to origin/dev: &lt;files&gt;"), so the existing triage handles it.</li>\n<li>Branches that already have commits or a pushed PR keep today's behaviour (merge dev, don't rebase).</li>\n<li>Worker instructions (Talos worker prompt / ship-issue skill): never commit under another identity; let <code>ai ship</code> update the branch.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Acceptance</h4>\n<ul><li>Unit tests with a temp repo: base moved + uncommitted changes (clean pop, conflicting pop), base moved + no changes, branch with own commits unchanged.</li><li>README / <code>ai/README.md</code> updated. Works on Windows and Linux.</li></ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d4294