abd9b6696af4-a328-1af5-a6d823755ed2	Docs: Create Doc form (app.project.doc.create) and sidebar entry	2026-11-11 10:00:11	2026-11-11 13:37:10	0	<p>Lets a project member with <code>doc.create</code> start a new doc. The body is written later in the editor, so the form asks only for title and tags.</p><ul><li><code>app/router.js</code>: add <code>this.route('create')</code> to the <code>doc</code> route. <code>services/acl.js</code> <code>routeMaps</code>: <code>app.project.doc.create</code> → <code>doc.create</code>.</li><li>Sidebar: add <code>actions.section1.create</code> "Create Doc" (route <code>app.project.doc.create</code>, <code>aclContext: 'doc.create'</code>) to the Docs item in <code>utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>; if the Docs item isn't there yet, add it (icon <code>file-text-o</code>, route <code>app.project.doc</code>, <code>aclContext: 'doc.read'</code>). If All Docs has shipped, add its "New doc" button (<code>aclContext="doc.create"</code>) to the list's box-tools.</li><li>Route/controller <code>app/project/doc/create</code> (native classes) and <code>templates/app/project/doc/create.hbs</code> on the create/edit pattern: <code>col-md-8</code> form box with <code>FormFields::FieldText</code> title (required, validation message) and <code>FormFields::FieldRelateMulti</code> for tags (existing project tags), <code>col-md-4</code> side box with owner (current user) and project; Save/Cancel below the boxes.</li><li>Save: creates the doc with <code>projectId</code> and <code>ownerId</code> = current user, then the Tagged rows (<code>relatedTo: 'doc'</code>), then transitions to <code>app.project.doc.page</code>. Ignore a second submit while saving and disable Save; on failure show the error and roll back. Cancel returns to <code>app.project.doc.index</code> (or the project dashboard if that route doesn't exist yet).</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>; acceptance <code>.feature</code> with a per-feature steps file: create with title and tags lands on the doc page; empty title shows validation; failed save shows an error; no <code>doc.create</code> → route blocked and sidebar child hidden.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> scenarios pass on Mirage; a created doc appears in All Docs; screen matches an existing create form side by side; tests and lint pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> body editing, creating new tags inline, templates, edit route.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4490</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4492	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	deferred	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	8d7fb7c86af4-a328-1af5-dd696378a14c	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	\N	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-11 13:37:10	aprom	0	0
92105ae36af9-ba4e-b3ac-92b89ddd1def	Agamemnon: triage a local test failure the diff did not cause	2026-11-15 15:32:34	2026-11-15 22:39:21	0	<p>aprom-4582 was handed back because a test outside its diff failed locally before any PR existed (a timing-dependent AppUi::Avatar test that a later merge had already removed from dev). The classifier (<code>talos/lib/agamemnon/classifier.py</code>) mapped it to <code>other</code>, which is outside the premise, so Agamemnon left it with the owner. The <code>ci_failed</code> premise already has the right idea (fails on the base too → file a Bug and hold), but it only applies to CI on an open PR.</p>\n<h4>Change</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>New incident type, e.g. <code>base_test_failed</code>: a worker handback saying the full suite fails on tests its diff does not touch. Add a classifier rule and a structured handback reason so this does not rely on free text alone.</li>\n<li>Premise (<code>agents/agamemnon/premise.json</code>): read the failing test names; bring the branch up to date with the base (same mechanism as the <code>ai ship</code> update issue) and retry once; if it still fails, run those tests on a clean checkout of the base.\n<ul><li>Fails on the base: file a Bug (or link the open one) and hold-until-done, as for <code>ci_failed</code>.</li>\n<li>Passes on the base: send the issue to Odysseus with the failing test and a log excerpt (the diff likely causes it).</li></ul></li>\n<li>Respect the existing limits (sessions per type, test slots) and keep the base check in a throwaway worktree, never the issue's workspace.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Acceptance</h4>\n<ul><li>Classifier and premise unit tests for the new type; a triage test for each outcome (passes after update, fails on base → Bug + hold, passes on base → Odysseus).</li><li>Talos README updated.</li></ul>\n<p>Depends on the <code>ai ship</code> branch-update issue (reuses its update step).</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-b