8183b7296af0-970b-16ca-ec27e763f9cc	Developer section: Documentation box loading static markdown from public/ui-docs	2026-11-08 17:21:05	2026-11-08 17:51:11	0	<p>Component docs must not grow the app bundle (engineer's decision), so they are markdown files served as static assets from <code>public/ui-docs/&lt;name&gt;.md</code> and downloaded only when an entry opens. This issue builds the box that shows them and fixes the doc format.</p><ul><li><code>Developer::Docs</code> (<code>components/developer/docs.{hbs,js}</code>): <code>box box-info</code> "Documentation" with the file path in <code>box-tools</code>. Loads <code>/ui-docs/&lt;@doc&gt;</code> with <code>fetch</code> (a static file of the app itself, not Gaia, so the store/adapter rule does not apply; say so in a code comment); add the app version as a query param for cache busting. Splits the markdown on <code>## </code> headings into Bootstrap <code>nav nav-tabs</code> (first tab active, tab state internal) and renders each section with the existing <code>render-markdown</code> modifier (toastui viewer). States: loading (<code>AppUi::Loader</code>), missing file ("No documentation yet" with the expected path), fetch error. Guard async work after destroy.</li><li>Doc format in <code>public/ui-docs/README.md</code>: sections <code>## Overview</code>, <code>## Arguments</code> (table: Argument, Type, Default, Meaning), <code>## Blocks</code>, <code>## Events</code> (callback, payload), <code>## Do and Avoid</code>. No copy-ready code snippets (engineer's decision). Link the folder from <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code> section 9.</li><li>Check that <code>broccoli-asset-rev</code> leaves <code>.md</code> files unfingerprinted and that they are in the production build output.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration test with a stubbed fetch (tabs from headings, missing file state, error state); <code>ember build</code> output contains <code>ui-docs/README.md</code>; the app bundle size does not c