d48005666af4-c968-1af5-830935133082	Project dashboard: paginate the Project Milestones box (5 per page)	2026-11-11 10:05:08	2026-11-11 11:53:35	0	<p>The Project Milestones box on the project dashboard (<code>app/templates/app/project/index.hbs</code>, <code>project-milestones-section</code>, in the col-md-4 side column) lists every milestone of the project. On projects with many milestones the box runs far down the page. Paginate it in the browser using the existing shared <code>Pagination</code> component.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>The route <code>routes/app/project/index.js</code> keeps loading all milestones (<code>limit: -1</code>, sort <code>Milestone.startDate</code> DESC). The estimated-vs-spent chart filter (<code>milestonesByDateCreatedDesc</code>) and the per-milestone issue counts need the full list. No API change.</li><li>In <code>controllers/app/project/index.js</code>, track the current milestone page and add a getter for the visible slice (page size 5, in the list's existing order). Add an <code>onPageChange({page, pageSize})</code> action that sets the page and returns <code>{ hasMore }</code>. The getter must react to the <code>milestones</code> list, so milestones added through <code>saveMilestone</code> or edited show up without a reload.</li><li>In the milestones <code>box-body</code>, wrap the <code>{{#each}}</code> of <code>Project::Milestones</code> in <code>&lt;Pagination @pageSize={{5}} @onPageChange=... @containerClass="project-milestones-pagination"&gt;</code>. Use the <code>&lt;:center&gt;</code> block to show <code>first – last / total</code> (e.g. <code>1 – 5 / 14</code>) from a translation in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Render the pager only when there are more than 5 milestones. Keep the <code>Exceptions::NothingFound</code> empty state as it is.</li><li>After adding a milestone, the total and the › button update. If the current page becomes empty (should not happen today; there is no delete), fall back to the last page.</li><li>Only add styles if needed, scoped under <code>.project-milestones-section</code> in <code>styles/modules/project.scss</code>, and follow the design system (square edges, existing colours).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>With 14 milestones the box shows the first 5, the footer reads <code>1 – 5 / 14</code>, ‹ is disabled, and › moves to <code>6 – 10 / 14</code>. The last page shows <code>11 – 14 / 14</code> with › disabled.</li><li>With 5 or fewer milestones there is no pager. With none, the existing empty state shows.</li><li>Adding a milestone through the + dialog updates the total right away. The edit pencil and the milestone links still work on every page.</li><li>The estimated-vs-spent chart filter still lists all milestones.</li><li>Tests: an integration or acceptance test (Mirage, 14 milestones) covering page 1, next, last page and no pager at ≤5. Each test fails if the slicing is reverted.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: server-side paging of milestones, a page-size selector, filtering by status, and reducing the full milestone/issue load on this route.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> milestones-paginated.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4493	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	b43cc5046ae8-20b5-32a1-13b222266c79	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	4ad985766af4-066a-1af5-12c2b132d359	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 11:53:35	aprom	0	0
218f9c086af4-a1f0-1af5-ffa38a16c7df	Retro - aga-Parallel Runtime	2026-11-11 10:10:41	2026-11-11 10:10:41	0	<p>2026-10-31 to 2026-11-30 · 1 issue (1 done, 0 carried over) · 2m logged vs no estimate</p>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>The milestone held a single Bug, #4229, which removed a case-duplicate docs/classes/index.html that left every Windows checkout and Talos workspace showing docs/classes/Index.html as modified. It was assigned, implemented, reviewed and merged on 2026-10-31, about 35 minutes after creation, with no rework. With one issue, everything below is anecdote, not pattern.</p>\n<h2>Numbers</h2>\n<table><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Planned / added</td><td>1 / 0 (no history of additions visible; the issue was created on the start date)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Delivered</td><td>1 of 1 (100%)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Estimate accuracy</td><td>not computable (estimate 0m, logged 2m)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Late</td><td>0 (PR merged 2026-10-31, milestone ends 2026-11-30)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Rework</td><td>0</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Waiting</td><td>0 issues in feedback or pending (no such comments in the thread)</td></tr></table>\n<h2>What went well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The issue description named the root cause, the file to remove and a verification step, and the change landed as a one-file, 10-line deletion — #4229</li>\n<li>The ship note recorded a decision with its reason: index.html is not added to .gitignore because it is tracked, and regenerating docs with yuidoc on Linux/macOS will recreate it, so it must not be committed — #4229</li>\n<li>Fast flow: Agamemnon assigned the issue at 12:51, the PR opened at 12:52 and merged at 13:27 UTC. CodeRabbit raised no actionable comments, and there were no human review rounds on PR 589 — #4229</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What didn't go well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Nothing was undelivered. Single case: the third acceptance bullet (verify a fresh clone on Windows has a clean git status) has no recorded result in the comments, and tests were marked "not applicable" — #4229</li>\n<li>Single case: the risk the ship note flags (yuidoc regenerating the duplicate on Linux/macOS) is left as a warning with no guard, so it could recur — #4229</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Patterns</h2>\n<p>None can be established from one issue. Estimate overrun/underrun: none measurable, as the issue had no estimate.</p>\n<h2>Surprises</h2>\n<ul><li>Single case: the issue was caused by tracked file names differing only in case (a Windows-only symptom that surfaced in every agent workspace); an earlier agent run (#4224) had hit it and reported leaving the file uncommitted, as quoted in #4229's description.</li></ul>\n<h2>Proposed actions</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Add a check, such as a CI or pre-commit step, that fails when the tracked file list contains names that differ only in case — addresses the recurrence risk in #4229 — Prometheus repo CI. Worked if the check fails on a deliberately added duplicate.</li>\n<li>Have the ship note state the result of each verification bullet in the issue, or say it was not run — addresses the unrecorded Windows clean-clone check in #4229 — /ship-issue skill.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Data gaps</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Estimate accuracy and overruns: the issue has no estimate (0m).</li>\n<li>Added or moved-out issues: no milestone history is available beyond the current issue list.</li>\n<li>Status history (bounces, waiting time): only comments are visible, not status transitions.</li>\n<li>Whether the Windows clean-clone check was done is not recorded.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Issue ledger</h2>\n<table><tr><th>#</th><th>Title</th><th>Status</th><th>Est</th><th>Actual</th><th>Review rounds</th><th>Notes</th></tr>\n<tr><td>4229</td><td>Remove the case-duplicate docs/classes/index.html that leaves every checkout modified</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>2m</td><td>0 human, 0 CodeRabbit actionable</td><td>Bug, high, complexity simple; PR 589 merged 2026-10-31; ship cost 2.6k output tokens, 10 turns, 2 sessions; no model escalation recorded</td></tr></table><p>Complexity: simple</p>	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	1	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	4494	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	new	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729		\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Hera	Hera	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-11 10:10:41	aprom	0	0
0e3984926ad7-3bb5-2b49-4de188d7eac0	Seed the 'Agent coding loop' workflow (replaces Talos' own status logic)	2026-10-20 17:12:46	2026-10-30 21:18:20	0	<p>Part of agaia-4048 (Workflows).</p><p>A seed for the workflow on the mockup: Issue assignee changed → Filter (assignee is Agent Achilles or Agent Odysseus, changed by the agent's sponsor, milestone Claude-v1 or Agents) → Switch on status (New: start, In Progress/Feedback/Pending: resume, In Review: address review) → Run agent → Switch on outcome (done: end; needs input: Feedback + assign sponsor + comment; blocked/failed/limit: Pending + assign sponsor + comment). Prompts copied from <code>dev-tools/talos/agents/odysseus/agent.json</code>.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4052</p><p>Mockups: the screenshots attached to this issue (from the 'Agents Screens' design canvas, https://claude.ai/artifact/9WYrFcT3LacRG9QLeBSQUL, private until shared).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4054	2026-10-27	2026-10-20	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7a626c876ad7-b7ec-4943-0da4f6053570	eef04cc76ad7-d41d-2b49-e6106c38f089	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	57d59f956ae5-2f9f-8ff0-b9177056f4f3	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 21:18:26	agaia	0	0
be5c77706afa-fe7f-5cb2-b8f7ad3e1def	Framework: in-process sub-request runner (one REST call dispatched with its own Request/Response, result captured, not sent)	2026-11-15 23:09:50	2026-11-16 01:02:12	0	<p>The Bulk API needs to run an ordinary REST call (method, URL with query, JSON body) inside the current PHP request. The call must go through the normal router, <code>RestController</code>, authentication and ACL, and give back its status and body without writing anything to the client. Today the code assumes one request per process: <code>public/index.php</code> calls <code>Phalcon\\Mvc\\Application::handle()</code> once, <code>RestController</code> reads <code>request-&gt;getJsonRawBody()</code> / <code>getQuery()</code> / the method from the DI <code>request</code>, and <code>authorize()</code> sets <code>$GLOBALS['currentUser']</code>.</p><ul><li>New domain-side class (e.g. <code>core/libs/http/SubRequestRunner.php</code>): <code>run(string $method, string $url, ?array $body, string $authorization): SubResult</code>. <code>SubResult</code> holds the status, the decoded body and the duration in ms.</li><li>For each call, register a fresh request object in the DI (a <code>Phalcon\\Http\\Request</code> subclass that returns the given method, URI, query parameters, raw/JSON body and Authorization header instead of reading superglobals and php://input), and a fresh <code>response</code>. Dispatch through the existing router/dispatcher (<code>core/mvc/Router.php</code>). Restore the outer request, response and <code>$GLOBALS['currentUser']</code> afterwards, also when the call throws.</li><li>Catch <code>Gaia\\Exception\\*</code> and turn it into the result with <code>toResponse()</code> (from the error-responses issue). Any other <code>Throwable</code> becomes a 500 with a generic error. Log it, and never put a stack trace in the body. One call's failure must not leak state into the next call.</li><li>Every call runs the full authentication and ACL check of the target action with the caller's token. Nothing in the runner skips or weakens authorization.</li><li>Unit tests (fake controller/route): success, 404 route, Gaia exception -&gt; its status, unexpected exception -&gt; 500, state restored between consecutive calls, query and body passed correctly. Add a short note under <code>docs/architecture/</code> (new <code>bulk/decisions.md</code>) on why sub-requests run in-process and sequentially.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two consecutive <code>run()</code> calls in one PHP process (e.g. GET /api/v1/issue?query=... and a PATCH that fails ACL) return the same status and body as the separate HTTP calls, and nothing is sent to the client.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>bulk</code> resource and its validation (next issue), parallel execution, transactions.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4585</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4586	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	6fd53d836afa-af75-0d65-c532824126b5	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 01:02:12	agaia	0	0
abda80d16af4-a1f0-1af5-3a7007c2e089	Retro - aga-Component Library	2026-11-11 10:12:59	2026-11-11 10:12:59	0	<p>2026-11-08 to 2026-12-08 (all work logged 2026-11-08 to 2026-11-09) · 9 issues (9 done, 0 carried over) · 2h23m logged vs no time estimate set (file-count estimates only)</p>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>All nine issues were delivered. The Developer section, its shared frame and docs box, five component entries and the removal of the old Settings page were built in roughly 2h23m of logged agent time. The main friction was not the code but integration: four entry PRs conflicted on the same two shared files (registry and Gherkin feature), and every PR skipped CodeRabbit because of its review limit, so all review fell to a person. Hand-written file counts ran above the estimate on 8 of 9 issues.</p>\n<h2>Numbers</h2>\n<table><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Planned / added</td><td>9 / 0 (by issue creation dates; all created 2026-11-08 17:20-17:22)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Delivered</td><td>9 of 9 (100%)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Estimate accuracy</td><td>Not computable: all issues have 0m time estimate. Files: 60 estimated vs 95 hand-written (1.6×)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Late</td><td>0 by dates seen (work finished 2026-11-09, milestone ends 2026-12-08); done dates not read per issue</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Rework</td><td>4 issues needed merge-conflict rounds after PR opened (#4377, #4378, #4380, #4381)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Waiting</td><td>Not measurable (no feedback/pending status history visible); PR open to merge-conflict flag was ~8-10 min, and #4380/#4381 sat flagged for ~1h before human replies</td></tr></table>\n<h2>What went well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Dependency ordering worked: shell (#4374), frame (#4375) and docs box (#4376) built first, then entries listed "Depends on" them and were assigned only when those were done — #4377, #4378, #4379, #4380, #4381 (assignment comments by Agamemnon).</li>\n<li>The two issues with no conflict rounds, #4375 and #4379, merged straight after one PR; #4375 and #4379 were assigned and merged by a person within about 15-55 min of opening.</li>\n<li>Design review inside the ship step improved the work before the PR: #4376 extracted a service and util and dropped a cache-busting param that would not have worked (<code>ENV.APP.version</code> undefined); every PR from #4377 on lists follow-ups explicitly for the reviewer — #4376, #4377, #4379, #4381.</li>\n<li>Issue descriptions fixed design, arguments, out-of-scope and acceptance, and no scope changes after start appear in any thread — all nine.</li>\n<li>Full suite passed on every PR (1157-1190 tests, 0 failures) — all nine.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What didn't go well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>No issue was left undelivered, so nothing to report under not delivered.</li>\n<li>Merge conflicts on shared files: #4378 needed three separate conflict rounds (5m + 1m + 5m logged), #4377, #4380 and #4381 one each. Conflicts were in <code>component-registry.js</code> and <code>component-library.feature</code> (hard-coded entry count), each fixed by merging dev and re-counting entries — #4377, #4378, #4380, #4381.</li>\n<li>CodeRabbit never reviewed: every PR comment says "32 of 25 reviews used in the last 24 hours", so review was manual only — #4374 to #4382 (all nine).</li>\n<li>Planned checks left unverified: <code>ember build</code> output and .md fingerprinting were not verified though they are acceptance criteria (#4376); no lint run and no browser check (#4375).</li>\n<li>Design-review follow-ups were deferred rather than done on several issues, so debt remains: demo pipeline into utils (#4377), per-field demo split (#4379), Dropdown callbacks and theme variables (#4381), missing Gherkin scenarios for entries (#4378, #4381).</li>\n<li>Possible cross-repo leftover: translation keys for the removed Settings UI were not found in prometheus (#4382).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Patterns</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Parallel issues editing one shared list:</strong> five entry issues all append to the registry and a feature file that asserts the count; four of five hit conflicts (#4377, #4378, #4380, #4381). #4380 removed the hard-coded count to stop recurrence; #4379 avoided it only by merging first.</li>\n<li><strong>File estimates run low:</strong> estimated vs hand-written files: #4374 10/23, #4375 10/16, #4376 6/8, #4377 6/10, #4378 5/8, #4379 5/6, #4380 4/6, #4381 4/7, #4382 10/11. The two largest overruns (#4374, #4375) include tests in the count; #4374 and #4375 gave the reason in the ship note.</li>\n<li><strong>Time is spread evenly:</strong> 9-22 min per issue; the ship step (suite, design review, PR) took as long as or longer than building on #4376, #4379, #4380, #4381. Review-round time on #4377, #4378, #4380, #4381 was 4-16 min, almost all merge-conflict handling.</li>\n<li><strong>Estimates missing:</strong> every issue has 0m time estimate, so the overrun measure cannot be used (#4374 to #4382).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Surprises</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Single case (#4378): a merge commit was made with plain <code>git commit</code> and is authored by the reviewer's account, not the shared agent identity; it was left unrewritten.</li>\n<li>Single case (#4380): <code>(component)</code> with Modal failed with a dynamic-component error, so the demo invokes <code>bootstrap-modal</code> directly; a select with <code>eq</code> in <code>selected=</code> also broke rendering.</li>\n<li>Single case (#4381): AppUi::Dropdown has no callbacks, so open/close is logged with a MutationObserver coupled to markup.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Proposed actions</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Make the registry conflict-resistant: no hard-coded counts in the feature (as in #4380), and a one-entry-per-file registry or generated index, so entry issues stop colliding — addresses "parallel issues editing one shared list" — Prometheus repo / issue template for Component Library entries. Worked if later entry PRs show no conflict rounds.</li>\n<li>When issues in one milestone touch the same file, have Agamemnon serialise them or note "touches registry" in the description — addresses the same pattern — Agamemnon / issue-creation guidance. Worked if no issue needs more than one conflict round.</li>\n<li>Set a time estimate on issues at creation so overruns can be measured — addresses "estimates missing" — Nestor/issue-creation process. Worked if the next retro can compute estimate accuracy.</li>\n<li>Calibrate file estimates to include tests (23 vs 10 on #4374) — addresses "file estimates run low" — issue-creation guidance.</li>\n<li>Record unverified acceptance items (build output, fingerprinting) as a follow-up issue proposal in the ship step — addresses "planned checks left unverified" — <code>/ship-issue</code> skill.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Reviewer to approve before any follow-up issue is created; candidate follow-ups: Dropdown callbacks and theme variables (#4381), per-field demo split (#4379), demo pipeline util (#4377), Gherkin scenarios for entries (#4378, #4381), cleaning removed Settings translation keys elsewhere (#4382), verifying <code>ember build</code> output for ui-docs (#4376).</p>\n<h2>Data gaps</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Time estimates are 0m on all issues, so estimate accuracy and overruns could not be computed.</li>\n<li>Issue status history and done dates were not available, so Late and Waiting are only approximated from comment timestamps.</li>\n<li>PR review threads were not read via gh; review rounds come from issue comments only. "Rework" is counted as merge-conflict rounds because no returns to feedback are visible.</li>\n<li>Planned/added is inferred from creation dates; milestone membership history was not visible.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Issue ledger</h2>\n<table><tr><th>#</th><th>Title</th><th>Status</th><th>Est</th><th>Actual</th><th>Review rounds</th><th>Notes</th></tr>\n<tr><td>4374</td><td>Developer section: route, nav, registry, Components box</td><td>done</td><td>none (10 files)</td><td>14m (23 files)</td><td>0</td><td>Complexity complex; PR #690</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4375</td><td>Entry header, Controls, Event log</td><td>done</td><td>none (10 files)</td><td>11m (16 files)</td><td>0</td><td>PR #689; no lint or browser check</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4376</td><td>Documentation box</td><td>done</td><td>none (6 files)</td><td>17m (8 files)</td><td>0</td><td>PR #691; build output unverified</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4377</td><td>QuickList entry</td><td>done</td><td>none (6 files)</td><td>18m (10 files)</td><td>1 (conflict)</td><td>PR #694</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4378</td><td>ezSearch entry</td><td>done</td><td>none (5 files)</td><td>22m (8 files)</td><td>3 (conflicts)</td><td>PR #692; merge commit author note</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4379</td><td>Form fields entry</td><td>done</td><td>none (5 files)</td><td>11m (6 files)</td><td>0</td><td>PR #693; follow-ups listed</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4380</td><td>Modal entry</td><td>done</td><td>none (4 files)</td><td>20m (6 files)</td><td>1 (conflict)</td><td>PR #695; removed hard-coded count</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4381</td><td>Dropdown entry</td><td>done</td><td>none (4 files)</td><td>21m (7 files)</td><td>1 (conflict)</td><td>PR #696; follow-ups listed</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4382</td><td>Remove Settings Developer UI page</td><td>done</td><td>none (10 files)</td><td>9m (11 files)</td><td>0</td><td>PR #697; translation keys not found</td></tr></table><p>Complexity: simple</p>	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	1	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	4495	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	new	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729		\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Hera	Hera	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-11 10:13:00	aprom	0	0
6a54d3346ae4-8b17-1141-45b0b741343e	Show a pending comment while it is being posted	2026-10-30 20:22:02	2026-11-11 12:27:17	0	<p>When a user posts a comment on a conversation or an issue, nothing happens until the save returns, so on a slow connection the comment looks stuck.</p><p>On Post:</p><ul><li>Clear the comment box straight away, and only that box. Today a global <code>clearContents</code> clears every open editor.</li><li>Show the comment at the end of the list right away: dimmed, with the user's avatar and name and an animated "Posting…" indicator.</li><li>Once it is saved, remove the pending item and show the real comment.</li><li>If the save fails, keep the pending item and mark it as not posted, with Retry and Discard actions, so the text is never lost.</li></ul><p>Applies to conversation comments and issue comments, which share <code>ConversationUi::MessageBox</code>.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4198	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	49902a956ae4-9faf-391a-5e9e3427c007	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 21:31:38	aprom	0	0
c6e614686afa-fe7f-5cb2-e9b9b597bbae	Bulk API: `bulk` resource (POST /api/v1/bulk) runs up to N REST calls, one result per call	2026-11-15 23:09:58	2026-11-16 01:57:13	0	<p>Screens like the Task Board and Dashboard need several Gaia calls whose shape is known in advance. Sending them one by one costs a network round trip each. This adds a CRUD resource <code>bulk</code> (POST only, never stored, like other non-persisted resources such as agentspec) that runs a batch of REST calls with the sub-request runner and returns every result. A failing call affects only its own result.</p><ul><li><strong>Request:</strong> <code>{"requests": [{"id": "lanes", "method": "GET", "url": "/api/v1/issue?query=...", "body": null}, ...]}</code>. <code>id</code> is a client string, unique within the batch. <code>method</code> is GET, POST, PATCH or DELETE. <code>body</code> is optional JSON.</li><li><strong>Response 200:</strong> <code>{"responses": [{"id": "lanes", "status": 200, "body": {...}, "durationMs": 12}, {"id": "x", "status": 403, "body": {"error": "..."}, "durationMs": 3}]}</code>, in request order.</li><li><strong>Execution:</strong> items run sequentially in the order sent, through <code>SubRequestRunner</code>, with the caller's Authorization header. There is no rollback: a successful write stays even if a later item fails. Live events and other side effects behave as for separate calls.</li><li><strong>Batch validation</strong> (400 and nothing runs if any check fails): <code>requests</code> is a non-empty array; at most <code>BULK_MAX_REQUESTS</code> items (default 25, read via <code>getenv()</code> in a <code>config/bulk.php</code>); the request body stays under a size limit (config); ids are unique; every URL is a relative <code>/api/v1/&lt;resource&gt;...</code> path that the router resolves. Refused: <code>/api/v1/bulk</code> itself (no nesting), OAuth/token, unauthenticated routes and the streaming endpoints (upload file streams, download, preview).</li><li><strong>Security:</strong> the bulk call itself needs a valid token and the <code>bulk.create</code> permission (ACL metadata, no permission seed: the reviewer grants it). Every item is then authorized on its own exactly like a direct call, so a batch can never do more than its separate calls. Log one line per batch (user, item count, statuses, total time), never bodies.</li><li>Keep the controller thin: request parsing and response shaping in <code>BulkController</code>; batch validation in its own class (e.g. <code>core/libs/http/BulkRequestValidator.php</code>); execution in a small service that loops over the runner.</li><li><strong>Tests:</strong> phpunit for the validator, plus api-tester cases. Acl: no token -&gt; 401; no bulk.create -&gt; 403. Behaviour: mixed success + 404 + 403 items each return their own status; a write followed by a failing item keeps the write; too many items / nested bulk / unknown route -&gt; 400.</li><li>Extend <code>docs/architecture/bulk/decisions.md</code> with the contract, the limits and the no-rollback decision; regenerate <code>docs/generated</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a Task Board-style batch (milestones, issues of a milestone, statuses) returns all three results in one call. One item without permission returns 403 and the others still return 200.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> all-or-nothing mode, references between items (<code>$ref</code>), parallel execution, the Prometheus client.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4586</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4587	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbb506d05acd-06d6-1141-68969b9fd562	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	deaf4cf26afa-ad44-5288-3045737dd686	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 01:57:13	agaia	0	0
f8dcbbc06af4-a1f0-82e9-fd6323afa549	Retro - aga-Identity	2026-11-11 10:14:16	2026-11-11 10:14:16	0	<p>2026-11-09 to 2026-12-09 (all work finished 2026-11-08 to 2026-11-09) · 4 issues (4 done, 0 carried over) · 59m logged vs no estimate recorded</p>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>All four issues (three Settings/Agents UI tasks and one bug) were delivered through four Prometheus PRs (#698-#701), each approved and merged by a person, with the Ember suite green on every PR. The milestone closed roughly a month before its end date. Work ran with little rework, but every PR reached the reviewer without CodeRabbit because the 24-hour review quota was exhausted, and the file-count estimates were exceeded on all three feature tasks. One bug (#4410) was a direct follow-on of the feature work in #4404.</p>\n<h2>Numbers</h2>\n<table><tbody>\n<tr><th>Measure</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Planned / added</td><td>Not determinable (see Data gaps); 4 issues in the milestone at close</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Delivered</td><td>4 of 4 (100%)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Estimate accuracy</td><td>Not computable: no time estimates on any issue (logged 59m)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Late</td><td>0 (all done 2026-11-09, end date 2026-12-09)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Rework</td><td>0 status bounces seen; 1 fix-up bug (#4410, caused by #4404)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Waiting</td><td>0 issues in feedback or pending; PR open-to-merge: #698 4h16m, #699 3h31m, #700 7m, #701 11m</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>What went well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Every issue was delivered with a passing full suite (1193 to 1202 tests, 0 failures) and merged on the first review, with no feedback cycles — #4402, #4403, #4404, #4410</li>\n<li>Issues carried explicit dependencies, scope, acceptance criteria and out-of-scope lines, and were picked up in dependency order (#4402 merged before #4403's PR was opened) — #4402, #4403, #4404</li>\n<li>The built-in design review step produced concrete fixes before shipping and logged follow-ups for the reviewer (error handling, duplicate state removed, token secret cleared on route exit) — #4402, #4403</li>\n<li>The bug was fixed in a small client-side PR (17 lines added) in 14m and merged in 11m — #4410</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What didn't go well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>All four PRs were "Not sent to CodeRabbit" because the 24-hour quota was over (29 to 32 of 25 reviews used), so review relied on a person alone — #4402, #4403, #4404, #4410</li>\n<li>#4410 (agent edit crashed with "delegationScopes ?? [] .map is not a function") appeared the day #4404 was merged: the new field assumed an array but Gaia returns another shape. Likely a contract gap between the Gaia and Prometheus issues — #4404, #4410</li>\n<li>No issue was delivered unfinished; there are no not-delivered issues.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Patterns</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Size estimates were low on all three feature tasks: files estimated vs actual 9 vs 16 (#4402), 9 vs 13 (#4403), 6 vs 9 (#4404). Reasons stated in the threads: router, ACL, breadcrumb, translations, Mirage and test wiring (#4402); Mirage and tests (#4403). Pattern across 3 of 3 feature issues.</li>\n<li>Design review follow-ups repeat: controllers doing too much, derived state computed in controllers, logic that should live in a component or model (#4403, #4404). These were left as suggestions, not done.</li>\n<li>Assumptions about the Gaia contract were made rather than verified: ACL contexts and list query (#4402), delegationScopes shape (#4410, with Achilles' note that Gaia could return a real array).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Surprises</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Single case: the bug #4410 was created 2026-11-09 10:05 and merged 10:31, after #4404 had already been merged, so a regression surfaced within hours.</li>\n<li>Single case: #4403 (13 files, +1035 lines) took 19m logged and its PR was merged 7m after opening, much faster than #4402/#4404 (3.5 to 4h), suggesting review latency depends on reviewer availability, not PR size (likely, with only four data points).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Proposed actions</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Add a cross-repo contract check to the Prometheus "External Request" issue template: state the field's JSON shape (array vs string) and verify it against a Gaia response before merging — addresses the contract-gap pattern (#4404, #4410) — issue template / Agamemnon issue-writing prompt. It worked if no follow-up bugs for a Gaia-fed field appear next milestone.</li>\n<li>Count wiring files (router, ACL, breadcrumb, translations, Mirage, test steps) when estimating "Estimated files" for new pages — addresses the file-count underestimates (#4402, #4403, #4404) — the issue-writing guidance. Worked if actual is within 1.3x of estimate.</li>\n<li>Record a time estimate on each issue, so estimate accuracy can be measured — addresses the data gap — Agamemnon/Nestor issue creation. Worked if the next retro can compute accuracy.</li>\n<li>Decide whether design-review follow-ups (components, models, clipboard service) become backlog issues or are dropped, so they are not lost — addresses repeated design follow-ups (#4403, #4404) — reviewer triage after merge.</li>\n<li>Reduce CodeRabbit quota pressure (batch or defer small-PR reviews) or treat the manual-review path as the plan — addresses all PRs unreviewed by CodeRabbit (#4402 to #4404, #4410) — ai ship configuration.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Data gaps</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>No time estimates exist on any issue (all show 0m), so estimate accuracy and overruns are not computed.</li>\n<li>Planned vs added: the history of additions or removals to the milestone was not visible; #4410 was created 2026-11-09, so it was plausibly added after the others (not confirmed).</li>\n<li>Status transition history is not visible, only comments; bounce counts rely on comments and show none.</li>\n<li>Dependencies on Gaia issues (agaia-4384, 4388, 4390) belong to another project and were not read.</li>\n<li>CodeRabbit comments were absent; the "claude" review contents on the PRs were not read in detail, only their state (COMMENTED).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Issue ledger</h2>\n<table><tbody>\n<tr><th>#</th><th>Title</th><th>Status</th><th>Est</th><th>Actual</th><th>Review rounds</th><th>Notes</th></tr>\n<tr><td>#4402</td><td>Settings > Services: list service clients and disable them</td><td>done</td><td>none (9 files)</td><td>18m</td><td>1 human approval (PR #698)</td><td>16 files, +544; PR open 4h16m</td></tr>\n<tr><td>#4403</td><td>Settings > Services: approve enrollment requests, create tokens</td><td>done</td><td>none (9 files)</td><td>19m</td><td>1 human approval (PR #700)</td><td>13 files, +1035; merged 7m after open</td></tr>\n<tr><td>#4404</td><td>Agents: Delegation scopes field</td><td>done</td><td>none (6 files)</td><td>8m</td><td>1 human approval (PR #699)</td><td>9 files, +212; PR open 3h31m; led to #4410</td></tr>\n<tr><td>#4410</td><td>Unable to edit Agent after identity updates</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>14m</td><td>1 human approval (PR #701)</td><td>Bug, 3 files, +17; merged 11m after open</td></tr>\n</tbody></table><p>Complexity: simple</p>	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	1	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	4496	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	new	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729		\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Hera	Hera	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-11 10:14:17	aprom	0	0
b61ac6a06afa-fe7f-5cb2-e34e2ff68524	Exceptions: build the error response without sending it (toResponse), handle() sends it	2026-11-15 23:09:42	2026-11-15 23:30:37	0	<p>The Bulk API (POST /api/v1/bulk, a later issue) runs several REST calls in one request. Each one's error must come back as that item's result. Today every <code>Gaia\\Exception\\*</code> class in <code>core/exceptions/</code> builds its error response in <code>handle()</code> and calls <code>send()</code> immediately, and <code>public/index.php</code> (~l.234-264) relies on that. As a result, the first failing item would end the whole batch.</p><ul><li>Give every exception class in <code>core/exceptions/</code> (Access, BadRequest, Exception, FileNotFound, InvalidGrant, MigrationDriver, Permission, ResourceLocked, ResourceNotFound, TooManyRequests, UnAuthorized) a <code>toResponse(): \\Phalcon\\Http\\Response</code>. It builds the same status, headers (e.g. Retry-After on TooManyRequests, WWW-Authenticate where set) and JSON body that <code>handle()</code> builds today, without sending anything.</li><li><code>handle()</code> becomes <code>toResponse()-&gt;send()</code>. The HTTP output of a normal request stays byte for byte the same.</li><li>Put the shared part (a new Response with status and JSON error) in one place, e.g. a protected helper on a common base or a small <code>ErrorResponse</code> builder, so the classes don't repeat it.</li><li>Unit tests: <code>toResponse()</code> returns the expected status and body for each class and sends nothing (headers not sent, no output).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> all existing api-tester and phpunit suites pass unchanged, and every Gaia exception can produce its response object without sending it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the <code>\\Phalcon\\Exception</code> branch in <code>index.php</code> (agaia-4251 covers JSON for Phalcon exceptions), and any change to error messages or status codes.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 13 (The same mechanical change has to land in all 11 exception classes at once, plus one shared helper and one test file. Splitting it would leave some exceptions still sending their response directly.)</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4585	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	f1969f646afa-5047-dae4-eeb4d375ee00	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-15 23:30:38	agaia	0	0
