c7c3adf76afc-30ee-311d-bf03b684260c	Events: publish user.mentioned when a mention is recorded	2026-11-17 15:37:43	2026-11-18 18:27:28	0	<p>Agents, workflows and the UI need to know when someone is mentioned. Mentions are now recorded as <code>Mention</code> rows (mention-framework issue) from every write path, so the event is published when a row is created, the way <code>app/models/Systemnotificationrecipient.php</code> publishes <code>notification.created</code> through <code>NotificationLiveEvents</code> after create.</p><ul><li>After a <code>Mention</code> is created, publish <code>user.mentioned</code>, scope <code>user:&lt;userId&gt;</code> (the mentioned user). Ids only: mentionId, relatedTo, relatedId, projectId, actor id.</li><li>A small publisher class next to <code>NotificationLiveEvents</code>; constant in <code>EventNames</code>; registry entry in <code>app/metadata/events.php</code> (scope user, channel hermes, consumers talos, prometheus).</li><li>Tests (published once per row, fail-open when Hermes is down) and api-tester <code>hermes.expect</code> on a comment with a mention.</li><li>Contract change: linked Hermes PR (allowlist + user scope).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a comment mentioning two members sends two events, each to that user; an edit that adds nobody sends none.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the workflow channel for mentions.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4640, agaia-4645</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4648	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7b8e27936afc-30ee-311d-92e7628909b7	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	abdb6cf56afd-85bb-2994-d0a4c83236b9	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-18 18:27:28	agaia	0	0
a783ab446af4-6d0e-82e9-1d26c0ae38d8	Retro - aga-threads	2026-11-11 10:17:11	2026-11-11 10:17:11	0	<p>2026-11-10 to 2026-12-10 (all work logged on 2026-11-09/10) · 21 issues (21 done, 0 carried over) · 5h15m logged (315 min) vs no time estimate recorded</p>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>The milestone moved the Threads page to the QuickList list + detail layout, added the thread page, vote body, Participants, Activity and Create-issue-from-thread, and removed the old feed. All 21 issues are done and every one has a merged PR or a clear closure. Eight issues (#4454-#4460, #4464) were bug fix-ups for layout and styling mistakes that came from the specs and screens of #4437 and #4439, and #4465 wrote the design-system rules to prevent a repeat. The costliest issue was #4439 (56 min, 5 sessions, an escalation and a failed run). Time estimates were never recorded, so time accuracy can't be judged.</p>\n<h2>Numbers</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Planned / added</td><td>21 by the end; the issue dates are all 2026-11-10, so planned vs added can't be separated (see Data gaps)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Delivered</td><td>21 of 21 (100%); #4450 was closed without work here (handled in A Dev Tools)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Estimate accuracy</td><td>not computable: estimated time is 0m on every issue; 315 min logged</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Estimated files vs actual files</td><td>feature and task issues exceeded their file estimate by more than 1.5x in 8 of 8 cases (see Patterns)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Late</td><td>0 (all work done by 2026-11-10, milestone end 2026-12-10)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Rework</td><td>8 fix-up Bug issues (#4454-#4460, #4464) plus 3 human review rounds (#4457, #4458, #4464)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Waiting</td><td>#4464 held by Agamemnon for ~4 min; #4439 waited on a human decision from 00:54 to 10:41 (~10h); status history in feedback/pending is not visible</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>What went well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The dependency chain worked. Each issue carried "Depends on" and Agamemnon assigned the next ready one. It also held #4464 back because #4465 touched the same files and avoided a merge conflict. #4454 to #4460 were assigned within minutes of each other and all passed their tests — #4454, #4455, #4464</li>\n<li>Small fixes were cheap: seven bug issues took 6-11 min each — #4455, #4456, #4459, #4460, #4458, #4464, #4465.</li>\n<li>Design review found real structural problems before the PR and they were fixed in the same issue (components calling the store, state held in two places, util with side effects) — #4439, #4442, #4440</li>\n<li>Agent notes recorded decisions, rejected options and follow-ups consistently, which made this retro possible — #4442, #4454, #4456</li>\n<li>A known issue was turned into a rule: #4465 added the shell/QuickList/status-label rules to the design system.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What didn't go well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix-up wave: eight bugs were raised after #4437/#4439 for a duplicate page header, button placement, extra shadow, redundant label, duplicated linked-issue line, untranslated status, nested <code>section.content</code> and toolbar overflow. The descriptions of #4454 and #4457 say they came from the spec and screens of #4437 and #4439 — #4454, #4455, #4456, #4457, #4458, #4459, #4460, #4464</li>\n<li>#4439 was the single largest cost: 56 min, 25 files, 128k output tokens, 5 sessions. The first run escalated from Sonnet after a design-review blocker, then "failed" because it reported ready_to_ship where that isn't usable, and was left with the owner. The reviewer attributed the earlier failure to the container being killed for memory, and it shipped on a later attempt — #4439</li>\n<li>Three PRs needed a human review round, and in all three the change was to remove a test the agent had added (a section-count scenario, a negative linked-issue assertion, a no-label assertion). The comments themselves ("Update required") don't say why, so the reason is an inference — #4464, #4458, #4457</li>\n<li>#4450 (full test suite OOM-killed about every second run, 4 of 7 runs) was filed in this milestone, but was handled in A Dev Tools and has no work or time here — #4450. It is the reason #4439 stalled per the reviewer.</li>\n<li>Some acceptance checks were not performed: visual comparison with Task Board and "threads-fixed.png" were not verified; lint couldn't run locally (no node_modules) — #4464, #4459, #4456, #4448, #4437</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Patterns</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Spec/screen errors propagate:</strong> the layout, label and duplicated-info mistakes in #4437/#4439 were built as specified and fixed afterwards as eight issues. Of the eight, #4454 and #4457 say so directly; the rest depend on those two. Evidence: #4454-#4460, #4464, #4465.</li>\n<li><strong>File estimates were low for features, accurate for bugs:</strong> actual vs estimated files: #4437 29 vs 11, #4439 25 vs 10, #4440 15 vs 8, #4442 11 vs 6, #4444 11 vs 5, #4447 11 vs 6, #4441 9 vs 5, #4436 10 vs 5. Bugs were within one file of the estimate (#4454 3 vs 4, #4460 2 vs 3). The big ones carried notes that the tests and splits were not separable (#4437, #4439). Likely cause: updated Gherkin steps and Mirage handlers aren't counted.</li>\n<li><strong>Ship step dominates tiny changes:</strong> the code change was 2 min, while "full suite and shipping" took 4-26 min — #4456 (3 / 5), #4455 (2 / 5), #4459 (2 / 4), #4460 (2 / 9), #4458 (2 / 8), #4457 (2 / 17), #4454 (2 / 26). #4454's 26 min included a step-dictionary fix that made two scenarios report Undefined Step, so not all of it is suite time. Cause of the longer ones can't be separated from OOM retries (#4450) with the data.</li>\n<li><strong>Design-review follow-ups are left open:</strong> #4437, #4438, #4440, #4441, #4444, #4447 each list unaddressed review suggestions as follow-ups in the PR notes. No issue exists for them in this milestone (only #4439 created #4449).</li>\n<li><strong>Biggest time overruns relative to scope:</strong> #4439 (56 min, escalation and re-ship), #4444 (32 min, 67 turns, 11 files), #4454 (28 min, test-step conflict). Fastest relative to scope: #4437 (24 min for 29 files, merged by Agamemnon without a human round).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Surprises</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Single case: #4439's failed run was a handoff outcome mismatch ("ready_to_ship where it can't be used"), not a code problem; the work was complete and the suite had passed.</li>\n<li>Single case: #4447 needed a Gaia permission (<code>conversationroomcount.get</code>) that isn't seeded, so rows show no counts until it is granted by hand — #4447.</li>\n<li>Single case: #4450 was closed with 0 time because the fix went to a different project — #4450.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Proposed actions</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>When a list/detail or page-shell issue is specced, check it against <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code> (now updated by #4465) and strip decorative elements from attached mockups before the build; the issue template should say which parts of a screen are "guide only". Addresses spec/screen errors. Lives in the Nestor/planning prompt and the issue template. We'll know it worked if the next UI milestone has no fix-up Bug issues about duplicate headers, labels or info.</li>\n<li>Count test, Gherkin step and Mirage files in "Estimated files" for feature issues, or state them separately. Addresses file estimates. Lives in the planning skill. It works if actual/estimated files stays under 1.5x.</li>\n<li>Make the planning step record a time estimate on each issue (all 21 had 0m). Addresses the estimate gap. Lives in Nestor/Agamemnon issue creation. It works if the next retro can compute estimate accuracy.</li>\n<li>Add a rule to the start-issue/ship skill: do not add absence/negative assertions unless the issue asks for them. Addresses the three removed tests. Lives in <code>/start-issue</code> and the test conventions. It works if no human round in the next milestone is only about removing a test. (Reason is inferred; the reviewer to confirm.)</li>\n<li>Create follow-up issues for the design-review suggestions left open in the PR notes (#4437, #4438, #4440, #4441, #4444, #4447) and for the unseeded <code>conversationroomcount.get</code> permission (#4447), for the reviewer to approve. Lives in the backlog. It works if the list is closed or explicitly dropped.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Data gaps</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Time estimates: all issues show 0m estimated, so estimate accuracy, overruns (1.5x) and the time-based Late measure aren't computed; "Estimated files" is used instead, and it is an estimate by the planner, not a measurement.</li>\n<li>Planned vs added: every issue has start date 2026-11-10 and the milestone started 2026-11-10, and no history of issues moved in or out is available, so Planned/Added and the delivery rate beyond 21/21 are not split.</li>\n<li>Status history: bounces between in_review, feedback and in_progress are not shown by the tools. Review rounds are taken from comments and PR data only; the "Waiting" figure for #4439 is from comment timestamps.</li>\n<li>CodeRabbit: the ship notes say PRs weren't sent to it (40 of 25 reviews used), so there are no CodeRabbit round counts. <code>gh</code> shows 2 reviews and 1 comment on most PRs, 3-5 reviews on #714, #727, #729 and #735; the content of the reviews was not read.</li>\n<li>Cost and size come from the agent's ship notes where present; #4450 and #4465 have no size or cost, and #4450 has no work.</li>\n<li>Wall-clock time per issue (creation to done) was not computed; the time logs are the agent's active time only.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Issue ledger</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Title</th><th>Status</th><th>Est</th><th>Actual</th><th>Review rounds</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>4436</td><td>ezSearch metadata incl. Liked by</td><td>done</td><td>none (5 files)</td><td>11m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>10 files; design review no blockers</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4437</td><td>QuickList list + detail layout</td><td>done</td><td>none (11 files)</td><td>24m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>29 files; merged by Agamemnon; spawned #4454-#4458 fix-ups</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4438</td><td>Row counts and vote tallies (separate calls)</td><td>done</td><td>none (6 files)</td><td>13m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>8 files; merged by Agamemnon</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4439</td><td>Thread page for discussions</td><td>done</td><td>none (10 files)</td><td>56m</td><td>failed run, escalation, retry</td><td>25 files, 5 sessions, 128k output tokens; follow-up #4449 created</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4440</td><td>Vote body and Result box</td><td>done</td><td>none (8 files)</td><td>21m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>15 files; follow-ups listed</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4441</td><td>Participants box</td><td>done</td><td>none (5 files)</td><td>8m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>9 files</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4442</td><td>Create issue from thread</td><td>done</td><td>none (6 files)</td><td>20m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>11 files; navigation chosen over modal; dev-tools proposal made</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4444</td><td>Activity box</td><td>done</td><td>none (5 files)</td><td>32m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>11 files, 67 turns</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4445</td><td>Create modal FormFields</td><td>done</td><td>none (5 files)</td><td>6m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>3 files; merged by Agamemnon</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4447</td><td>Counts with one Gaia call</td><td>done</td><td>none (6 files)</td><td>8m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>11 files; permission not seeded</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4448</td><td>Remove old feed and code</td><td>done</td><td>none (10 files)</td><td>9m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>7 files; lint not run locally</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4450</td><td>Test suite OOM kills</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>0m</td><td>n/a</td><td>handled in A Dev Tools; 4 of 7 runs killed on 2026-11-10</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4454</td><td>Remove extra page header</td><td>done</td><td>none (4 files)</td><td>28m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>fix-up; step dictionary fix</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4455</td><td>New thread button into QuickList header</td><td>done</td><td>none (3 files)</td><td>7m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>fix-up</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4456</td><td>Extra shadow and border</td><td>done</td><td>none (2 files)</td><td>8m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>fix-up; not checked visually</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4457</td><td>Remove Discussion/Vote label</td><td>done</td><td>none (3 files)</td><td>24m</td><td>1 human</td><td>fix-up; test assertion removed</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4458</td><td>Remove linked issue line from header</td><td>done</td><td>none (3 files)</td><td>11m</td><td>1 human</td><td>fix-up; negative assertion removed</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4459</td><td>Untranslated issue status</td><td>done</td><td>none (2 files)</td><td>6m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>fix-up; screen not produced</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4460</td><td>QuickList toolbar overflow</td><td>done</td><td>none (3 files)</td><td>11m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>component fix; visual check left as follow-up</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4464</td><td>section.content nested twice</td><td>done</td><td>none (2 files)</td><td>10m</td><td>1 human</td><td>fix-up; added test removed</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4465</td><td>Design system doc rules</td><td>done</td><td>none (2 files)</td><td>2m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>docs only; Roles/Threads templates not re-verified</td></tr>\n</tbody></table><p>Complexity: simple</p>	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	1	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	4497	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	new	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729		\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Hera	Hera	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-11 10:17:11	aprom	0	0
c60e0e666af0-970b-16ca-94852a2f9964	Settings: remove the Developer -> UI page (moved to the Developer section)	2026-11-08 17:22:14	2026-11-08 18:50:14	0	<p>The QuickList demo now lives in the Developer section's Component Library, which is kept apart from Settings on purpose. Remove the old Settings page.</p><ul><li>Remove the <code>developer</code> group from <code>views.Navigation.settingsItems</code> in <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> (~l.280).</li><li>Remove the <code>ui</code> routes from <code>app/router.js</code> (~l.74), <code>routes/app/settings/ui/index.js</code>, <code>controllers/app/settings/ui/quick-list.js</code>, <code>templates/app/settings/ui.hbs</code>, <code>templates/app/settings/ui/quick-list.hbs</code>, their <code>services/acl.js</code> routeMaps entries (~l.91-93), their translation keys (<code>views.app.settings.ui.*</code>, <code>views.nav.menu.settings.ui</code>, <code>views.nav.menu.settings.group.developer</code>) and their tests. Keep <code>utils/dev/quick-list-fixture.js</code> if the new entry uses it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: Settings shows Access, Projects and System only; <code>/app/settings/ui</code> no longer exists; the Developer -&gt; Components -&gt; QuickList entry still works; tests pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: anything else in Settings.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4377</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4382	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	5d51af446af0-970b-16ca-455730e26234	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	497bae016af0-9907-a42e-8c51788fb3e3	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 18:50:14	aprom	0	0
3f8b82706afa-4169-5cb2-10ddc3f78b33	AppUi::Avatar: standard sizes xs/s/m/l, default image, person vs agent	2026-11-15 23:16:15	2026-11-15 23:39:25	0	<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library (Developer -&gt; Components). <code>AppUi::Avatar</code> needs standard sizes, a default image and a clear person vs agent look. Scope is the component, its demo and its docs only: do not change pages that use it (if a page then looks different, that is accepted).</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><p>Today: <code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code> renders <code>Agent::UserAvatar</code> (<code>components/agent/user-avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, uses the <code>agentDirectory</code> service) with AdminLTE <code>img-circle</code> + <code>img-sm</code>/<code>img-xs</code>; with no size the image shows at its file size; a missing image is broken; for an agent it renders <code>Agent::Avatar</code> without <code>@user</code> (so an agent's own picture never shows) and without the size.</p><ul><li><code>@size</code>: <code>xs</code> 20px, <code>s</code> 30px, <code>m</code> 40px (default), <code>l</code> 96px; <code>sm</code> stays an alias of <code>s</code>. Unknown values fall back to m.</li><li>Person: the user image (<code>/userimage/get/&lt;id&gt;</code>); when there is no id or the image fails to load (<code>error</code> event), show <code>/img/default.png</code> at the same size (see <code>isDefaultProfilePicture</code> in <code>models/user.js</code>). Never a broken image.</li><li>Agent: pass the user to <code>Agent::Avatar</code> so its picture shows; with a picture add a small round robot marker (<code>fa-android</code>, plum <code>$highlightColor</code>, white 1px ring) at the bottom right from size s up; without a picture the robot icon on plum, sized to the avatar. Title/alt says the name and that it is an agent.</li><li>Styles in a new <code>app/styles/components/app-ui-avatar.scss</code>, imported in <code>app/styles/app.scss</code> on the line right after <code>@import "modules/agent.scss";</code>. Round (50%) is the only allowed radius. Do not edit <code>modules/agent.scss</code> page rules.</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>: rows person / person without image / agent with picture / agent without picture, columns xs-l; controls for size and "image fails". Do not edit <code>styles/components/developer-entry.scss</code> (another issue changes it).</li><li>Docs: <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-avatar.md</code> and the manifest <code>app-ui-avatar.json</code> (sizes, aliases, agent behaviour).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for each size, the alias, the image error fallback, agent with and without picture. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing pages or <code>Agent::Avatar</code> users elsewhere, initials avatars.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> avatar-tag-standards.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4588	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	c8a5e4056afa-4169-5cb2-b20d13172825	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-15 23:39:25	aprom	0	0
b953ccc56af4-5dd8-82e9-a6fdb696952b	Retro - aga-Quick List	2026-11-11 10:21:45	2026-11-11 10:21:45	0	<p>Work 2026-11-08 to 2026-11-10 (milestone window 2026-11-08 to 2026-12-08) · 31 issues (31 done, 0 carried over) · 8h39m logged (519 min) vs no time estimate recorded. Every issue has an estimate of 0m; only an "Estimated files" count exists.</p>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>All 31 issues were delivered, each through its own PR (31 PRs, all merged), well inside the milestone window. The milestone built the QuickList component family (#4350-#4358, #4367), moved the idea browser onto it (#4359, #4356, #4360-#4366, #4368, #4428), added a page-state toolkit (#4425-#4427) and moved the Roles page onto QuickList (#4429-#4435). Small, tightly specified issues went through quickly. The main friction was parallel work colliding on shared files (<code>translations/en-us.json</code>), specs that contradicted what Gaia or an earlier issue had actually shipped, and a nine-issue fix-up batch after the first idea-browser build. A known failing test sat in about 13 PR test runs before #4373 fixed it.</p>\n<h2>Numbers</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Planned / added</td><td>Only creation dates are visible: 20 issues created on the start date (2026-11-08), 11 created on 2026-11-09 (#4425-#4435). No milestone history, so "added" is approximate.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Delivered</td><td>31 of 31 (100%)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Estimate accuracy</td><td>Not computable: no time estimates recorded (519 min logged)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Late</td><td>0 (all done before 2026-12-08; last PR activity 2026-11-10)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Rework</td><td>10 fix-up issues named in the thread of an earlier issue: #4360-#4368 (from #4353, #4356, #4357, #4359) and #4435 (from #4432). Plus #4428, which re-did the idea browser's loading on the new state toolkit.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Merge conflicts</td><td>4 issues: #4350, #4352, #4353, #4366</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Waiting</td><td>3 issues held by the dispatcher for a file overlap: #4361 (about 64 min), #4368 (about 86 min), #4355 (about 3 min; #4360 about 6 min). #4360 also waited about 17 min for a reviewer decision. No feedback/pending status history available.</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>What went well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>100% delivery, nothing carried over, all 31 PRs merged — #4350-#4435.</li>\n<li>Tightly specified issues (named files, arguments, acceptance, out of scope) shipped with a single PR and no review round, e.g. the QuickList parts and the Roles polish tasks — #4351, #4354, #4358, #4362, #4364, #4365, #4427, #4429, #4431, #4434, #4435.</li>\n<li>An agent stopped before building when the spec contradicted Gaia's real paging (limit + 1 would skip rows), investigated how existing lists page, and the reviewer approved a revised plan. That avoided a silent data-hiding bug and produced a recorded decision (D-001) — #4360.</li>\n<li>Later issues followed the recorded decision over the stale issue text and said so in the PR note — #4425, #4430.</li>\n<li>Splitting QuickList into five standalone parts plus one assemble issue with explicit "Depends on" lines worked: the assemble and showcase issues shipped in 19 and 12 min — #4350-#4354, #4357, #4358.</li>\n<li>Ship notes record size, cost, design-review findings and what was not verified, which made follow-ups easy to turn into issues (the #4360-#4368 batch was created from such notes) — #4356, #4359, #4357.</li>\n<li>The dispatcher held issues that touch the same files as an in-flight one, avoiding more conflicts — #4355, #4360, #4361, #4368.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What didn't go well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Parallel standalone parts all added keys to <code>translations/en-us.json</code> (and the style imports), so three PRs conflicted on merge; #4350's merge also broke three integration tests after the textual merge. Logged conflict-resolution time: #4350 15 min, #4353 6 min, #4366 5 min (+ a 16 min review round on #4353 that included the merge) — #4350, #4352, #4353, #4366.</li>\n<li>The first idea-browser build left a large backlog of follow-ups found in design review (archived/search semantics, URL state, hover colour, raw id for creator, reset of sort/order, Mirage two-field sort, controller too large): nine fix-up issues created the same day — #4356, #4359, #4360-#4368.</li>\n<li>Specs contradicted reality twice: "limit + 1" conflicted with Gaia's offset (#4360), and #4425 referenced a <code>requestLimit</code> helper that #4360 never shipped. #4430 repeated "limit + 1" wording as well.</li>\n<li>The Taskboard EzSearchCompact failure was reported as "known" in about 13 PR test runs (#4350, #4351, #4353-#4357, #4359-#4361, #4363, #4367, #4368) until #4373 fixed it. The first fix attempt broke two other tests and was narrowed — #4373.</li>\n<li>Reviewer feedback after the PR was a missed translation for a label (#4352) and a design-system violation in existing code found by the reviewer (#4433, raw <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>). Both are things the issue text or checklist could carry.</li>\n<li>#4435 (Role box wastes space) followed #4432 within the same day; #4432 had kept the form-field inline edit that #4435 replaced with <code>AppUi::InlineEditable</code>. Both were not verified in a browser — #4432, #4435.</li>\n<li>#4368 ended with an agent asking whether review comments existed (none found), then the issue is done — a single case, cause unclear — #4368.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Patterns</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Shared-file collisions (4 issues):</b> three components built in parallel touched <code>translations/en-us.json</code> and the SCSS imports; one test file in #4366. Merge-conflict handling by the dispatcher resolved one (#4352) and handed back one with notes (#4350). Evidence: #4350, #4352, #4353, #4366; dispatcher holds on #4355, #4360, #4361, #4368.</li>\n<li><b>Ship phase is most of the logged time for small issues:</b> build 2-4 min versus 8-12 min for the full suite, design review and PR on #4351 (3/7), #4354 (2/8), #4363 (2/12), #4364 (2/4), #4365 (2/8), #4366 (3/8), #4368 (2/8), #4429 (3/4), #4434 (2/5). #4367 logged 4 min of build and 35 min of review fixes and the test run. Two or more issues, so a pattern; the logs do not split test-run wait from review time.</li>\n<li><b>Size beyond the "Estimated files" figure:</b> #4430 35 vs 11, #4360 18 vs 9, #4359 14 vs 6, #4355 12 vs 9, #4432 11 vs 7, #4428 11 vs 7, #4356 9 vs 6. Each ship note gave a reason (tests, Mirage handlers, shared components), and in #4430 and #4360 the issue text itself warned that splitting would leave the suite broken. Under-runs: #4357 (6 vs 8), #4426 (2 vs 3). Largest cost: #4430 (72.8k output tokens, 89 turns, peak context 190.7k), #4428 (56.4k), #4356 (46.3k).</li>\n<li><b>Open design decisions discovered after the build:</b> search and archived semantics (#4356 → #4361, #4362), grouping with paging (#4359 → #4365, #4366, #4368), pagination model (#4360). The engineer's decisions were written into later issues, which then shipped without friction.</li>\n<li><b>CodeRabbit capacity:</b> 29 ship notes say the PR was not sent to CodeRabbit (reviews used 25 or more of 25 in 24 hours), so review was by hand (only the first two QuickList PRs had a CodeRabbit round: #4352 got one later, #4353 hit the limit on re-review). Evidence: #4350-#4435 ship notes.</li>\n<li><b>Verification gaps reported at ship:</b> ESLint not run (no node_modules in the run checkout) in #4350, #4428, #4425, #4430, #4366; no browser check in #4358, #4359, #4432, #4434, #4435; new test not seen failing first in #4363, #4428.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Surprises</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Single case: #4355 escalated to Opus with nothing committed after a test-order failure (<code>Settings | Developer UI</code> passed filtered, failed in the full run), then shipped 6 min later; the cause was the quick-list route overriding <code>setupController</code> (<code>detectTimezoneChange</code> only exists on the App controller).</li>\n<li>Single case: #4427 (architecture docs for the state toolkit) logged 2 min and its ship note says no page uses the toolkit yet, so the example was illustrative. #4428 adopted it a few hours later and the note about route seeding is worth checking against it.</li>\n<li>Single case: #4352 had a conflict resolved by the dispatcher (new head 077965b) while the assignee ran a review round with "no open threads", so the same conflict got two actors in 6 minutes (#4352).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Proposed actions</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>When splitting a feature into parallel components, give each a different translation sub-file or namespace, or serialise the issues that edit <code>translations/en-us.json</code> and <code>app.scss</code> — addresses shared-file collisions — dispatcher (Agamemnon) overlap rule and the issue-splitting guidance. Works if no parallel-built issue in the next milestone has a translations conflict.</li>\n<li>Add an "assumptions check" line to <code>/start-issue</code> and issue-writing: before building, verify every helper, endpoint and server behaviour the issue names exists in dev or Gaia (limit + 1, <code>requestLimit</code>) — addresses spec versus reality — <code>/start-issue</code> skill and Nestor issue template. Works if ship notes stop listing "deviation from the issue text".</li>\n<li>Fix known-failing tests as an issue as soon as the first PR reports it, before the next dispatch — addresses the Taskboard failure in 13 runs — dispatcher triage and Hera/Nestor intake. Works if "known failure" is absent from ship notes after a week.</li>\n<li>Add a pre-ship checklist to <code>/ship-issue</code>: translated strings, FormFields components, design-system rules, browser check for UI-only issues — addresses reviewer-found rule misses (#4352, #4433) and the "not verified in a browser" notes — <code>/ship-issue</code> skill. Works if reviewer feedback on these items stops.</li>\n<li>Record a time estimate on every issue (Nestor/Agamemnon set it at creation) — addresses missing estimate data — issue creation tooling. Works if the next retro can compute estimate accuracy.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Data gaps</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Estimate accuracy and overruns: every issue has 0m estimated time, so only "Estimated files" versus hand-written files could be compared.</li>\n<li>Status bounces and time in feedback or pending: no status history is exposed, so only comments were used. The "waiting" figures come from the dispatcher's hold and assign comments (timestamps).</li>\n<li>Planned versus added: no milestone history; only issue creation dates.</li>\n<li>Human review rounds on GitHub: review counts were read for all 31 PRs (mostly 2 reviews each; #4352's PR 7 and #4353's PR 5), but the bot and human split and comment contents were not read, so "review rounds" in the ledger come from Gaia threads.</li>\n<li>Time logs mix PKT and server timestamps, and tests runs are not split from review time, so the ship-phase pattern is indicative only.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Issue ledger</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Title</th><th>Status</th><th>Est</th><th>Actual</th><th>Review rounds</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>4350</td><td>QuickList core component</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>30m</td><td>1 (conflict, 3 failing tests after merge)</td><td>PR 671; est. files 10, actual 10</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4351</td><td>QuickList pagination</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>10m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 670</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4352</td><td>Grouping helper and heading</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>13m</td><td>2 (translations feedback, conflict)</td><td>PR 669</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4353</td><td>Group-by and sort toolbar</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>41m</td><td>2 (review round, translations conflict)</td><td>PR 672; CodeRabbit limit reached</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4354</td><td>Select-all and selection bar</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>10m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 673</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4355</td><td>Settings Developer UI group</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>19m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 676; one Opus escalation; held 3 min by overlap; est. files 9, actual 12</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4356</td><td>Idea browser server paging/sort</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>36m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 674; est. 6 vs 9; two open decisions led to #4361/#4362</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4357</td><td>Assemble QuickList root</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>19m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 675; follow-ups became #4367</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4358</td><td>QuickList showcase</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>12m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 677; no browser check</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4359</td><td>Idea browser uses QuickList</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>14m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 678; est. 6 vs 14; follow-ups became #4360-#4368</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4360</td><td>Idea paging never shows</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>30m</td><td>2 decision rounds before build</td><td>PR 685; spec deviation (no limit + 1); est. 9 vs 18; waited about 17 min, then held about 6 min</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4361</td><td>Search lists open ideas only</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>14m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 686; held about 64 min for #4360</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4362</td><td>Show archived in URL</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>7m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 679</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4363</td><td>Selected option invisible on hover</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>14m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 681; fix not seen failing first</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4364</td><td>Created-by shows raw id</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>6m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 680</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4365</td><td>Leaving the page resets group only</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>10m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 682</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4366</td><td>Mirage two-field sort</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>16m</td><td>1 (conflict)</td><td>PR 683</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4367</td><td>Move selection/collapse state out of root</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>39m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 684; 35 min in review fixes and test run</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4368</td><td>Sort/group util with unit tests</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>10m</td><td>0 (agent asked about missing review comments)</td><td>PR 688; held about 86 min for #4365</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4373</td><td>EzSearch board test failing</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>22m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 687; first fix broke two tests; test-only change</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4425</td><td>AsyncResource and ListLoader</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>12m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 702; spec referenced a helper that did not exist</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4426</td><td>UrlState</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>23m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 703; est. files 3, actual 2</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4427</td><td>Docs: page state architecture</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>2m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 704; examples unchecked against an adopter</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4428</td><td>Ideas: list-only reload</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>27m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 705; est. 7 vs 11; no fail-first check; open design-review findings</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4429</td><td>QuickList leading block</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>7m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 706</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4430</td><td>Roles list + detail with QuickList</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>22m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 707; est. 11 vs 35; 72.8k output tokens</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4431</td><td>Remove Role::Card, rewrite doc</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>10m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 708</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4432</td><td>Role detail as three boxes</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>13m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 709; est. 7 vs 11; needs visual check</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4433</td><td>Role permissions raw select</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>18m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 710</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4434</td><td>Delete role into Role box header</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>7m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 711</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4435</td><td>Role box InlineEditable</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>6m</td><td>0</td><td>PR 712; no browser check</td></tr>\n</tbody></table><p>Complexity: simple</p>	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-