752474976ae1-c1d3-53f6-4bd85719d3e1	Dashboard route tolerates unknown or missing widgets	2026-10-28 12:49:57	2026-11-11 12:27:22	0	<p>The <code>/app</code> route (<code>app/routes/app/index.js</code>) splits <code>currentUser.user.dashboard.widgets</code> and reads <code>widgetSettings[widget].model</code> for each name. A widget name that isn't in the <code>Dashboard</code> widgets view metadata (<code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code>) makes this throw, and so does a dashboard that is missing or has an empty widget list. The dashboard then fails to load.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Trim the widget names and drop empty ones and any name that has no entry in the widget settings, before querying.</li>\n<li>If the user has no dashboard, or no valid widgets are left, fall back to the default widget list: <code>recentIssues, activeMilestones, weeklyActivities, weeklyIssueTimelogs, weeklyConversations</code>.</li>\n<li>Log a dropped widget name at debug level. Show no error to the user.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Tests</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Acceptance tests (Mirage) where <code>/app</code> renders for these users:\n<ul>\n<li>a user whose dashboard lists an unknown widget;</li>\n<li>a user whose dashboard has an empty widget list;</li>\n<li>a user with no dashboard.</li>\n</ul></li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4178	2026-11-04	2026-10-28	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	a5644c666ae1-661c-b56e-4a11d83447f9	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-29 10:05:40	aprom	0	0
500171c56afa-4169-5cb2-1b996a90644b	AppUi::Tag: standard tag look (Task Board style), palette colours from text, removable	2026-11-15 23:16:32	2026-11-16 00:38:01	0	<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library. <code>AppUi::Tag</code> (<code>components/app-ui/tag.hbs</code>) is a bare <code>label label-&lt;variant&gt;</code> with no styles or manifest. Standardize it on the Task Board tag look. Scope is the component, its demo and docs only: do not change pages that use it, and do not change the board.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><p>Reference markup to copy the look from: <code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code> ~l.102-110 (<code>.badge.issue-type-tag</code>, <code>.info-tag</code>) with styles in <code>styles/modules/board.scss</code> ~l.432-446 and the colour in <code>milestones.js</code> <code>getIssueTypeTagStyle</code> ~l.509 (border + text in the colour, 16% tint behind).</p><ul><li>Look: 1px border and text in the variant colour, a 16% tint of it as background (<code>rgba()</code> of the variable in SCSS), 11px semibold, padding 2px 7px, square edges, 4px gap between tags, wraps in a row. Variants <code>default</code> (#ddd border, #444 text, #f9fafc), <code>primary</code>, <code>info</code>, <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>danger</code> from <code>app/styles/variables.scss</code> only.</li><li><code>@colorKey</code>: when set (and no <code>@variant</code>), pick the variant deterministically from the key (simple string hash over the five coloured variants), so the same text always gets the same palette colour. No ColorHash free colours.</li><li><code>@onRemove</code>: shows a small <code>fa-times</code> button inside the tag (grey, darker on hover, aria-label) that calls it.</li><li>Long text: max width with ellipsis and the full text in <code>title</code>.</li><li>Add <code>components/app-ui/tag.js</code> for the logic; styles in new <code>app/styles/components/app-ui-tag.scss</code>, imported in <code>app/styles/app.scss</code> on the line right after <code>@import 'components/dropdown.scss';</code>.</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/tag.{hbs,js}</code>: variants, colour from text, removable (logs <code>@onRemove</code>), a wrapping row with a long tag. Do not edit <code>developer-entry.scss</code>.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-tag.md</code> and a new manifest <code>app-ui-tag.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests for variants, colorKey stability, onRemove, truncation title. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing the Task Board or other pages; status labels (<code>AppUi::StatusLabel</code>).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4588</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> avatar-tag-standards.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4589	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	ed6d4d306afa-5733-216d-b63d4f093838	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 00:38:01	aprom	0	0
d05e69006afc-30ee-311d-49260b39354a	Notifications: notify a user when they are mentioned	2026-11-17 15:37:52	2026-11-18 18:58:25	0	<p>A mentioned user should get a notification. Mentions are recorded as <code>Mention</code> rows from every write path; create the notification when a row is created, next to the <code>user.mentioned</code> publish.</p><ul><li>A notification builder (e.g. <code>components/notifications/modules/MentionNotification.php</code> or a service beside it): <code>CreateModel::execute('systemnotification', ...)</code> + <code>RecipientService::notifyUsers($notification, [$userId])</code>, which already publishes <code>notification.created</code>. Description per relatedTo, following the existing templates: <code>{{User@actor}} mentioned you in {{Issue@id}}</code>; for a comment, the issue (or thread) it is on; for an idea or idea message, the idea. <code>relatedTo</code>/<code>relatedId</code> and <code>context</code> (projectShortcode, issueNumber or ideaId, commentId, userId, userName) as in <code>CommentNotification</code>. Set the Mention's <code>notified</code> to true.</li><li>No double notification: <code>CommentNotification::onCreate</code> and <code>IssueNotification::onCreate</code> exclude users mentioned in that same record (Mention rows exist by then, the behavior runs at model save) via the <code>excludeIds</code> of <code>notifyIssueRecipients</code>.</li><li>Tests for each relatedTo and for the exclusion.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a mentioned member gets one mention notification and no second "commented" one; others are notified as before; a failure doesn't fail the save.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> emails; Prometheus rendering of idea/thread notification links (Prometheus follow-up).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4648</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708