b18772376ad7-b7ec-4943-dddcccbf4386	Tool catalog: tool_servers, tools, agent_tools and refresh from MCP tools/list	2026-10-20 11:38:25	2026-10-29 10:06:30	0	<p>Part of agaia-4026 (Agents).</p><ul><li><code>tool_servers</code>: name, <code>kind</code> (mcp | openapi | builtin), <code>location</code> (runtime | ares | external), transport, endpoint/command, spec (OpenAPI JSON).</li><li><code>tools</code>: toolServerId (null for runtime built-ins such as Read/Edit/Bash), name, description, inputSchema (JSON Schema).</li><li><code>agent_tools</code>: agentId, toolServerId or toolId (a server-only row grants the whole server, e.g. <code>mcp__gaia</code>), <code>permissionRule</code> (e.g. <code>Bash(dev-tools/odysseus/odysseus:*)</code>).</li><li>A refresh action fetches a server's tools and schemas with MCP <code>tools/list</code>: the implementation owns the schema; Gaia owns the catalog entry, rules and grants.</li></ul><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4027</p><h4>Changes after the UI mockups (2026-10-20)</h4><ul><li>Servers list with 'Runs in' (Runtime, Ares, External), tool count, agent count, schema refresh time and a Refresh button.</li><li>Per server: its tools with description, inputs and who has them.</li><li>Per grant on a runtime tool: permission rules (e.g. <code>Bash(git status:*)</code>).</li><li>The workflow action 'Call a tool' uses this catalog (agaia-4051).</li></ul><p>Mockups: the screenshots attached to this issue (from the 'Agents Screens' design canvas, https://claude.ai/artifact/9WYrFcT3LacRG9QLeBSQUL, private until shared).</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	1	4031	2026-10-27	2026-10-20	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7a626c876ad7-b7ec-4943-0da4f6053570	864a5c576ad7-b7ec-4943-13e891fa3ea1	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Hammad Hassan	2d5a0ba56ae2-ca37-925f-18a5267fdd5b	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-29 10:06:30	agaia	0	0
33c06c406ae3-2d66-a456-4cc1068cd631	Test slot templates take their schema from the checkout, not from the shared pr4m database	2026-10-29 10:21:39	2026-10-29 17:35:54	0	<p>Part of adt-4157. The gaia harness (<code>tools/api-tester/harness/prepare-test-db.sh</code>) builds the test database from the schema of <code>SOURCE_DB</code>, default <code>pr4m</code>, the engineer's dev database. The slot templates (<code>installer/testslots.py</code>, adt-4159/adt-4172) key on <code>pr4m</code>'s schema fingerprint. A branch's new models only reach its tests after someone migrates <code>pr4m</code> from that branch.</p>\n<p>With parallel runs this breaks. On 2026-10-29, 4030 (<code>Useridentity</code>), 4031 (<code>Tool</code>, <code>Toolserver</code>, <code>Agenttool</code>, <code>Agent</code> columns) and 4032 (<code>Skill</code>, <code>Agentskill</code>, <code>Agent</code>) all changed Gaia models at once. <code>pr4m</code> had been migrated from the 4031 branch, so 4030's suite failed with <code>relation "user_identities" does not exist</code>. The migrate is declarative and drops columns that aren't in the migrating checkout's metadata, so migrating <code>pr4m</code> from one branch undoes another's schema and changes the engineer's dev database.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>When building a template: dump <code>pr4m</code> into a scratch database <code>pr4m_src_&lt;key&gt;</code>, migrate it with the checkout's code in that checkout's test container (<code>php cli.php migration migrate</code>, <code>DB_NAME=pr4m_src_&lt;key&gt;</code>), then run the harness with <code>SOURCE_DB=pr4m_src_&lt;key&gt;</code> (the script already reads it). Drop the scratch database afterwards.</li>\n<li>The template key hashes the checkout's model metadata (<code>app/metadata</code>) and seed sources, not <code>pr4m</code>'s live schema.</li>\n<li>Agent runs never migrate <code>pr4m</code>: say so in the Odysseus role prompt and the run-tests skill, and make <code>ai</code> refuse <code>p4m db migrate</code> inside a run workspace (<code>P4M_WORKSPACE</code> set).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Done when</strong>: two branches that add different models test in parallel slots without touching <code>pr4m</code>; unit tests (fake psql and docker) cover the scratch-database build, the new key and the refusal.</p>\n<p>Depends on: none</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4186	2026-11-05	2026-10-29	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	bcb698486ae0-36a5-29af-ebb1949fa852	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	d5bf5cf96ae3-8c4a-8b3e-a0859c105dd1	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-29 17:35:55	adt	0	0
44abd2766ae3-8697-28f8-41bd6c3108d7	ai ship / address-review: keep the issue in progress with the agent until CodeRabbit is settled	2026-10-29 14:25:08	2026-10-29 15:17:57	0	<p>Depends on adt-4188 (<code>ai rabbit</code>).</p><p>Today <code>ai ship</code> and the <code>/address-review</code> skill finish by setting the issue to <code>in_review</code> and assigning it to the reviewer, so the reviewer is handed a PR CodeRabbit hasn't finished with. The automated review should be invisible to the reviewer: the issue stays <code>in_progress</code> and assigned to the agent until the CodeRabbit loop is done, just like the agent's own design review before the PR.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>ai ship --defer-handoff</code>: commit, push, open the PR and post the usual "PR opened" tracker notes, but leave the issue <code>in_progress</code> and assigned to the agent. Record the pending handoff (repo, PR, issue) in <code>ai/state</code> so the step after it can finish it.</li><li><code>ai handoff &lt;issue&gt;</code>: does the deferred part (status <code>in_review</code>, assign the reviewer) and clears the record. <code>ai ship</code> without the flag keeps working as now, by calling the same code.</li><li><code>/address-review</code> gets a "bot round" mode: work only CodeRabbit's open threads (from <code>ai rabbit</code>), fix or decline each with evidence in a reply, push, and <em>don't</em> hand off or post a review-round comment to the tracker. Rounds started by the reviewer keep today's behaviour.</li><li>Manual sessions (no Talos): <code>/ship-issue</code> runs <code>ai rabbit --wait</code> after the PR, runs bot rounds while it reports <code>findings</code> (at most 3), then <code>ai handoff</code>. Any state other than <code>clean</code> or <code>findings</code> (<code>paused</code>, <code>absent</code>, round cap reached) hands off as normal.</li><li>Time for bot rounds is logged with <code>ai time</code> as usual.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests for <code>--defer-handoff</code> and <code>ai handoff</code> (no status or assignee change until handoff; handoff is idempotent); skills updated; README updated.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: Talos driving the loop (separate issue).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4189	2026-11-05	2026-10-29	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	caa020816ae3-b6e7-b574-69807b4c2ac1	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-29 15:17:57	adt	0	0
163787346af4-e076-82e9-5f4dc4aefd1a	Retro - aga-Auth	2026-11-11 10:23:18	2026-11-11 10:23:18	0	<p>2026-11-10 to 2026-12-10 (milestone dates; all issue activity falls on 2026-11-10/11) · 7 issues (7 done, 0 carried over) · 2.1h logged (128m) vs no estimate recorded</p>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>All seven issues were delivered and merged within a day of work, well before the milestone end date. The auth safety-net tests (#4466) and status page (#4467) landed first, so the ember-simple-auth replacement (#4468) went through with no review comments and a green suite. The milestone also carried a second, unrelated stream (replacing ember-intl: #4470, #4471, #4472) that follows the same "tests first, then replace, then clean up" shape. The main friction was environmental: CI resolved a different ember-intl version than the local container (#4470), and review feedback arrived as short comments (#4466, #4467).</p>\n<h2>Numbers</h2>\n<table><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Planned / added</td><td>7 / 0 known (issues created 2026-11-10 18:53-20:54; start dates 11-10 for 4466-4468, 11-11 for 4469-4472; the history does not show which were in the milestone on its start date)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Delivered</td><td>7 of 7 (100%)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Estimate accuracy</td><td>Not computable: no issue has an estimate (all 0m)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Late</td><td>0 (all done by 2026-11-10 23:04 per comments; milestone ends 2026-12-10)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Rework</td><td>3 issues had a post-PR fix round: #4466, #4467, #4470. #4469 logged 13m fixing a unit-test regression before shipping.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Waiting</td><td>Not computable: status history is not readable. #4470 had a handback failure, retried within about 1 minute.</td></tr></table>\n<h2>What went well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Safety net first, then the risky switch: #4466 and #4467 merged before #4468, which rewrote the session service (20 files) and merged with the suite green (1366, 0 fail) and no review comments. Dependencies were declared in the issue text and Agamemnon only assigned ready issues. — #4466, #4467, #4468</li>\n<li>Rollback was designed in: #4468 kept the localStorage key and persisted shape so reverting needs no migration; the description made this a "must keep". — #4468</li>\n<li>Same pattern reused for ember-intl (tests, replace, follow-up docs). #4471 (12 files) and #4472 merged with no review comments. — #4470, #4471, #4472</li>\n<li>Issue descriptions that fix design and contract (with throwaway diffs attached) kept the larger issues small in time: #4468 and #4471 took 16m and 22m logged. — #4468, #4471</li>\n<li>Hand-off notes recorded decisions, deviations and follow-ups (e.g. the one test file changed outside the stated scope in #4468). — #4468, #4467</li>\n<li>Characterisation tests surfaced a real defect: #4466 found the deep link lost after sign-in (marked KNOWN GAP); #4469's time log mentions the deep link fix. — #4466, #4469</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What didn't go well</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>All seven issues are done, so nothing was not delivered.</li>\n<li>Test quality feedback after the PR: "You are not using Mirage properly" required a review round to move seeding into the feature file. — #4466 (single case)</li>\n<li>CI failed on #4470 after the local suite passed: local container had ember-intl 6.0.0 while CI resolved 6.5.x (no lockfile); <code>setLocale('en_US')</code> threw. Took about 10m across two entries to fix. — #4470</li>\n<li>#4470 finished but was not handed back (status stayed in_progress); Agamemnon retried once. — #4470 (single case)</li>\n<li>#4467's six CodeRabbit threads were fixed in a round (6m), after design review had already run. — #4467</li>\n<li>Design-review findings were deferred as follow-ups with no tracker issue visible in the milestone: SRP split of the intl service, RangeError fallback and plugin error handling (#4471); auth-log injectable service, redaction regex, formatting out of controller (#4467). — #4467, #4471</li>\n<li>Manual verification not done in #4467 ("manual check signed out/signed in" listed as not done).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Patterns</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scope and naming:</strong> milestone "aga-Auth" describes auth replacement, but 3 of 7 issues are about ember-intl (#4470, #4471, #4472). Reports by milestone mix two goals. Evidence: milestone description vs those issues.</li>\n<li><strong>Environment drift between local and CI:</strong> #4470 (ember-intl 6.0.0 vs 6.5.x, no lockfile) and #4471 (broccoli deps pinned to what was in node_modules because ^4.x failed the dependency checker; <code>ai call</code> fails in .runs workspaces). Two issues point to tooling/dependency friction.</li>\n<li><strong>Cross-issue test overlap:</strong> #4469 and #4470 both flagged overlap risk with each other and with #4466; #4469 was told to coordinate with #4466 and re-covered deep-link and sign-in redirect scenarios. Handled by comments, no conflicts recorded.</li>\n<li><strong>Size vs time:</strong> longest logged was #4466 (26m) and #4470 and #4471 (22m each); smallest #4472 (7m). The largest PRs by file count (#4468 at 20 files, #4467/#4471 at 12) were not the longest. Task complexity did not track time here, though with no estimates this cannot be tested.</li>\n<li><strong>Review feedback:</strong> 3 of 7 had human or bot feedback after the PR (#4466, #4467, #4470); all 3 were fixed in one round. CodeRabbit was not used on any initial PR ("0 of 25 reviews used", small PRs go to a human) except #4467.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Surprises</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A throwaway proved the whole suite (1337 tests) passed with ESA removed, showing the old suite did not cover the real auth paths; this motivated #4466. — #4466, #4468</li>\n<li>The unused <code>views.app.theme</code> string was the only formatter mismatch and was deleted. — #4472 (single case)</li>\n<li>A failed review-round tracker comment (bad /tmp path) was noted in #4470 (single case).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Proposed actions</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Commit a lockfile or pin dependency versions in Prometheus so local, agent containers and CI resolve the same versions; success: no CI-only failures from version drift in the next milestone — addresses environment drift (#4470, #4471) — prometheus repo.</li>\n<li>Add a "design-review follow-ups" step to /ship-issue that lists deferred findings in the hand-off so the reviewer can approve them as issues; success: every deferred finding in a PR note maps to a proposed issue — addresses deferred findings (#4467, #4471) — dev-tools ai skills.</li>\n<li>Add Mirage conventions (seed in feature/Given steps, handlers over inline stubs) to the test-writing guidance in /start-issue or the run-tests skill; success: no Mirage-use review comment on the next test-only issue — addresses test quality (#4466) — workspace skill run-tests.</li>\n<li>Record an estimate on each issue when created (Agamemnon or the issue template) so estimate accuracy can be measured; success: next retro can compute accuracy — addresses missing data (#4466-#4472) — Gaia issue creation / Agamemnon.</li>\n<li>Fix <code>ai call</code> to fall back to the main workspace gaia in .runs workspaces (reported in #4471) — addresses tooling friction — dev-tools issue (to be created on approval).</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Data gaps</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Estimates: none recorded, so estimate accuracy and overruns are not computed.</li>\n<li>Status history and time in feedback/pending: not readable via the tools, so Waiting is not computed.</li>\n<li>Planned vs added: milestone membership history not visible.</li>\n<li>PR review history was not read with <code>gh</code>; review rounds come from issue comments only. #4468, #4469, #4471 and #4472 show no human comment in the thread, but PR comments may exist. #4469 and #4470 show no "merged by a person" comment from Agamemnon, although status is done.</li>\n<li>Time logs are agent time only; human review time is not logged.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Issue ledger</h2>\n<table><tr><th>#</th><th>Title</th><th>Status</th><th>Est</th><th>Actual</th><th>Review rounds</th><th>Notes</th></tr>\n<tr><td>4466</td><td>Auth flow tests on ESA</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>26m</td><td>1 human</td><td>PR 737; Mirage feedback; deep-link app bug found</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4467</td><td>Auth status page and event log</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>19m</td><td>1 (CodeRabbit, 6 threads)</td><td>PR 736; manual check not done</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4468</td><td>Native session service</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>16m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>PR 738; 20 files; one test file changed outside scope</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4469</td><td>Auth route guards follow-up</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>16m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>PR 739; 13m on a unit-test regression</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4470</td><td>Translation tests before ember-intl</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>22m</td><td>CI failure fix</td><td>PR 740; handback failure and retry; version drift</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4471</td><td>Native intl service</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>22m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>PR 741; 12 files; deferred design findings</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4472</td><td>Clean-up and docs after intl</td><td>done</td><td>none</td><td>7m</td><td>0 seen</td><td>PR 742</td></tr></table><p>Complexity: simple</p>	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	1	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b	4499	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	new	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729		\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Hera	Hera	\N	bf3f206262c6-8e43-047e-2160cab7abb6	2026-11-11 10:23:18	aprom	0	0
d4a911126af4-b02b-fdcc-456d7e799da3	gaiapack.gaia_dev uses host php without vendor/, so ai ship's gaia-dev drift checks fail on Linux Talos worktrees	2026-11-11 11:47:32	2026-11-11 11:49:37	0	<p><code>gaia_dev()</code> in <code>ai/lib/gaiapack.py</code> runs <code>php tools/gaia-dev/bin/gaia-dev</code> on the host whenever <code>php</code> is on PATH, and only falls back to <code>docker run ... gaia-gaia</code> with the <code>gaia_vendor</code> volume when php is missing. On Linux hosts php exists, but the gaia checkout/worktree has no <code>vendor/</code> (it lives only in the <code>gaia_vendor</code> volume), so every call fails with "gaia-dev needs nikic/php-parser" and <code>ai ship</code> refuses to ship (seen on Gaia #4488 and earlier).</p><h4>Fix</h4><ul><li>Use host php only when <code>&lt;root&gt;/vendor/autoload.php</code> exists; otherwise use the docker-run branch; keep <code>(None, reason)</code> when neither works.</li><li>Unit tests in <code>ai/tests/test_gaiapack.py</code> covering each branch (mocked <code>shutil.which</code>, no real docker).</li></ul><p>Takes effect after merge plus <code>p4m runtime update</code> and a <code>talos run</code> restart.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4500	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	wont_fix	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	4b213c226af4-51ea-fdcc-94e5f1829a27	57f2151162c6-8e43-a8e0-a01f2b171f5b	2026-11-11 11:49:37	adt	0	0
369ae9826ae3-8697-28f8-3c372c1405f7	ai rabbit: report CodeRabbit's review state for a PR's head commit	2026-10-29 14:24:54	2026-10-29 15:06:33	0	<p>First step towards letting the coding agent and CodeRabbit settle a PR before the reviewer sees it. Today someone has to open GitHub to see whether CodeRabbit has finished and whether it found anything. This issue adds a read-only command that answers that question; it changes no handoff behaviour.</p>\n<p><strong>Signals</strong> (all on GitHub; CodeRabbit's own API is Enterprise-only):</p>\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">Commit status context <code data-tomark-pass="">CodeRabbit</code> on the head SHA: <code data-tomark-pass="">pending</code> "Review in progress", then <code data-tomark-pass="">success</code> "Review completed" (one per pushed head).</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Findings: a <code data-tomark-pass="">coderabbitai[bot]</code> review whose body starts <code data-tomark-pass="">**Actionable comments posted: N**</code>, plus N inline comments.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">No findings: no bot review; the walkthrough issue comment (contains <code data-tomark-pass="">summarize by coderabbit.ai</code>) says "No actionable comments were generated in the recent review".</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Auto review pauses after 5 reviewed commits; the plan allows about 10 reviews an hour.</li></ul>**Changes**\n<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass="">New <code data-tomark-pass="">ai/lib/coderabbit.py</code> and an <code data-tomark-pass="">ai rabbit <repo data-tomark-pass=""> <pr data-tomark-pass=""></pr></repo></code> command. It prints and returns (exit code and <code data-tomark-pass="">--json</code>) one of:<ul data-tomark-pass=""><li data-tomark-pass=""><code data-tomark-pass="">pending</code>: no status yet, or status pending on the head SHA;</li><li data-tomark-pass=""><code data-tomark-pass="">clean</code>: review completed on the head SHA and no open bot threads;</li><li data-tomark-pass=""><code data-tomark-pass="">findings</code>: completed, with open bot threads (count and comment ids). A thread is open by the same rule <code data-tomark-pass="">ai review --open</code> uses: not resolved, and not answered by the agent unless the bot followed up;</li><li data-tomark-pass=""><code data-tomark-pass="">paused</code>: CodeRabbit says auto review is paused, or rate-limited;</li><li data-tomark-pass=""><code data-tomark-pass="">absent</code>: no CodeRabbit status appeared within the timeout (CodeRabbit not enabled on the repo, or it never ran).</li></ul></li><li data-tomark-pass=""><code data-tomark-pass="">--wait [--timeout MIN]</code> polls (about every 30 s) until the state is not <code data-tomark-pass="">pending</code>.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">Reuse the thread logic in <code data-tomark-pass="">ai/lib/review.py</code> (<code data-tomark-pass="">resolved_threads</code>, the answered rule) rather than copying it.</li><li data-tomark-pass="">README entry under the <code data-tomark-pass="">ai</code> commands.</li></ul>**Acceptance**: unit tests cover each state using recorded GitHub API responses (pending, clean, findings, declined thread counted as answered, paused, absent); running it against a real gaia PR gives the right state.\n<p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing ship, address-review or Talos (separate issues).</p>\n<p>Complexity: simple</p>\n	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	1	1	4188	2026-11-30	2026-10-29	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	32d95d366ae3-963c-8e82-a97a7d67258c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-29 15:06:33	adt	0	0
a7dac2986af0-970b-16ca-8f38ee56553c	Component Library: Form fields entry (FormFields::*)	2026-11-08 17:21:43	2026-11-08 18:13:50	0	<p>The house rules require <code>FormFields::*</code> for every form, so developers and agents need to see them and their options in one place. Add a Form fields entry to the Component Library.</p><ul><li><code>components/developer/demos/form-fields.{hbs,js}</code>: a field picker in Controls switching between FieldText, FieldTextArea, FieldRelate (<code>@relateType="relate-simple"</code>), FieldRelateMulti, FieldMultiSelect, FieldDate, FieldCheckbox, FieldSwitch, FieldUpload, FieldSearch, with fixture options (users with avatars for relate).</li><li>Common controls: disabled/read-only, a validation error (<code>@validate</code> + <code>@message</code>, <code>FormFields::ValidationMessages</code>), placeholder, <code>@searchEnabled</code> where supported. Show the current value under the demo. Value changes go to the event log. FieldUpload must not upload: log the file instead.</li><li>Registry entry (group Forms, stable, variants = the field count) and <code>public/ui-docs/form-fields.md</code>: per field its arguments, <code>@data-field</code> and <code>@aclContext</code> (field-level ACL), and Do and Avoid (never a bare <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;PowerSelect&gt;</code>, no helper text under fields: info-icon tooltips, labels come from translations in product screens).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: every listed field renders and reports its value; validation state shown; docs tabs render; integration test of the demo.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: the legacy root-level field components (<code>components/field-*.js</code>), changes to the fields.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4374, aprom-4375, aprom-4376</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9f