540379986ae3-8697-28f8-c359d55723d5	Talos: run the CodeRabbit loop after a PR and hand the issue to the reviewer only when it settles	2026-10-29 14:25:24	2026-10-29 16:10:47	0	<p>Depends on adt-4188 (<code>ai rabbit</code>) and adt-4189 (<code>--defer-handoff</code>, <code>ai handoff</code>, bot-round mode).</p><p>When an agent's ship session opens a PR, Talos should let the agent and CodeRabbit finish their back-and-forth and only then assign the issue to the reviewer, so the reviewer gets a PR with no outstanding bot findings. The issue stays <code>in_progress</code> and assigned to the agent the whole time, and nothing about the loop is posted to the tracker.</p><p><strong>Flow</strong></p><pre>PR pushed -&gt; wait for the CodeRabbit status on the head SHA\n  clean                          -&gt; ai handoff (in_review, reviewer)\n  findings                       -&gt; bot round (/address-review, bot threads only) -&gt; push -&gt; wait again\n  paused / absent / cap reached  -&gt; ai handoff</pre><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>The ship session runs <code>ai ship --defer-handoff</code>. A new outcome (e.g. <code>awaiting_bot_review</code>, with repo and PR) tells Talos to wait instead of checking the issue left the agent.</li><li>A waiting issue doesn't hold the agent's run slot: Talos polls <code>ai rabbit</code> for it in the background (it keeps a record in its state db so a restart picks it up, the same way missed assignments are reconciled).</li><li><code>findings</code>: queue a bot-round run for the issue (resumes the session while the cache is warm, like other actions). It counts towards <code>maxIterations</code>.</li><li><strong>Round cap</strong>: a new agent setting <code>botReviewRounds</code>, default 3. When it's reached, Talos hands off as normal; open bot threads are left on the PR for the reviewer.</li><li>The wait has a timeout (setting, e.g. 20 min per round). <code>absent</code> or <code>paused</code> hands off straight away.</li><li>If the reviewer or someone else reassigns the issue while it's waiting, Talos drops the wait.</li><li>README: the flow, the setting, and the fact that the reviewer only receives the issue after the loop.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests with a faked <code>ai rabbit</code> cover clean on the first pass, findings then clean, cap reached, timeout, absent, a restart while waiting, and a reassignment while waiting; one real end-to-end run on a dev-tools or gaia PR where CodeRabbit leaves findings ends with the issue assigned to the reviewer in <code>in_review</code>.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4190	2026-11-05	2026-10-29	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	88eb0ba56ae3-b001-010a-ec6ed12af9b9	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-29 16:10:47	adt	0	0
7c8cf0e06ae3-3554-5d14-9752e788a146	Talos: stop agents from editing or checking out branches in .dev-tools-runtime	2026-10-29 16:17:00	2026-10-30 22:23:02	0	<p>The runtime copy (<code>.dev-tools-runtime</code>, adt-4084) must only change through <code>p4m runtime update</code>. On 2026-10-28 it was changed twice by agents:</p><ul><li>21:40–21:44: branch <code>claude-issue-4123</code> was checked out, rebased and committed (<code>d3b3abb</code>) inside the runtime worktree instead of the dev-tools checkout.</li><li>22:48: the agaia-4183 run (log <code>odysseus-4183-20261028-224737</code>) edited <code>ai/lib/tests.py</code>, <code>ai/lib/testmap.py</code> and <code>ai/tests/test_lib.py</code> through the run workspace's <code>dev-tools</code> junction, which points at the runtime copy. The edit was never committed, and the next runtime check failed with "the runtime copy has local changes".</li></ul><p>A read-only junction isn't enough on its own: runs legitimately write <code>ai/state</code> (ship-*.json, kb.db) inside the runtime copy.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Prevent</strong>: in the agents' settings, deny Edit/Write/NotebookEdit under the workspace's <code>dev-tools/</code> link and under <code>.dev-tools-runtime</code>, except <code>ai/state/</code>. Deny Bash git commands that change the runtime worktree's HEAD or index (checkout, switch, rebase, reset, commit, stash) when run in it.</li><li><strong>Detect</strong>: after every run, Talos checks <code>git status</code> and HEAD of the runtime copy against what it was before the run. On a change: save the diff to the run log, restore the copy (checkout files, back to the recorded HEAD), comment on the issue that tooling must not be edited in place, and hand the issue to <code>handoffTo</code> as blocked.</li><li><strong>Instruct</strong>: the role prompt says a fault in dev-tools becomes a proposed dev-tools issue (described in the handoff), never an edit to the tooling the run uses. This holds even when the reviewer says "fix it in dev-tools"; for that, the agent asks for a dev-tools issue.</li><li>Find out why the 4123 session worked in the runtime worktree (wrong workspace path, or <code>dev-tools</code> resolving to the runtime copy) and fix that path so dev-tools issues always get their own worktree.</li><li>README: the rule and the post-run check.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests for the post-run check (no change; file edit; HEAD moved; only ai/state changed, which is allowed); a run that tries to edit a file under <code>dev-tools/ai/lib</code> is denied; a dev-tools issue run works in its own worktree and leaves the runtime copy clean.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4192	2026-11-05	2026-10-29	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	a095bbe06ae3-916e-e2b6-4e4474cd4eed	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-29 17:01:23	adt	0	0
bb8f8d876af0-970b-16ca-8ff71d19cc40	Component Library: Dropdown entry (AppUi::Dropdown)	2026-11-08 17:22:03	2026-11-08 19:32:18	0	<p><code>AppUi::Dropdown</code> (<code>components/app-ui/dropdown.{hbs,js}</code>, styles <code>styles/components/dropdown.scss</code>) is used for Saved Searches menus and board filters; alignment (<code>right: 0</code> by default) and hover/selected colours caused several bugs (aprom-4309, 4346). Document it in the Component Library.</p><ul><li><code>components/developer/demos/dropdown.{hbs,js}</code>: a trigger with fixture items (plain, with icons, a selected item, a divider, a long label). Controls: placement near the left edge / right edge of the demo box, scoped left alignment as used by ezSearch, many items (scroll).</li><li>Event log: open, close, item chosen.</li><li>Registry entry (group Menus, stable, used in: ezSearch saved searches, Task Board) and <code>public/ui-docs/dropdown.md</code>: arguments and blocks, and Do and Avoid (scope alignment overrides under the user's root class, never restyle globally; hover/selected colours).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: all variants demonstrable; events logged; docs tabs render; integration test of the demo.</p><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing the dropdown.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4374, aprom-4375, aprom-4376</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4381	2026-11-15	2026-11-08	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	5d51af446af0-970b-16ca-455730e26234	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	2d75e2156af0-f6b3-5263-0aa87432ba29	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 19:32:18	aprom	0	0
96723b096afc-30ee-311d-c5c2264450f7	External Request: CI: check the event allowlist against Gaia's event registry export	2026-11-17 15:36:54	2026-11-18 19:36:15	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Event Registry", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Gaia now has a file-based event registry and exports it as <code>docs/generated/events.json</code> in the gaia repo. Hermes keeps its own allowlist (<code>src/contract/names.js</code>) by design; CI should fail when the two drift (the local copy seems to miss <code>user.access.changed</code>, which Gaia publishes).</p><ul><li>A small Node script (e.g. <code>scripts/check-event-registry.js</code>) reads Gaia's <code>events.json</code> (path or URL argument) and compares: the names that are enabled and on the <code>hermes</code> channel must equal <code>EVENT_ALLOWLIST</code>; those with scope <code>user</code> must equal <code>USER_SCOPED_EVENTS</code>. It prints the differences and exits non-zero.</li><li><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code>: a step that fetches <code>events.json</code> from gaia's <code>dev</code> branch and runs the script. If the gaia repository isn't publicly readable, use a read-only token secret and say so in the PR.</li><li>Fix the allowlist if it really misses <code>user.access.changed</code> (and its user scope).</li><li>Unit test the comparison; mention the check where the docs describe the allowlist rule.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> CI passes on dev; tests show a missing and an extra name both fail.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> generating names.js from Gaia.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4641</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4643	2026-11-24	2026-11-17	done	medium	861790376ad5-1449-a602