b3ab8dd96afd-d3df-b689-4e90f97b4233	Events registry: multiple scopes (runtimes, service:<kind>) and planned entries; list doc.* and search.semantic.changed	2026-11-18 18:55:47	2026-11-18 19:26:06	0	<p>Hermes' drift check (ah-4643) compares <code>hermes/src/contract/names.js</code> with Gaia's registry export <code>docs/generated/events.json</code> (agaia-4640, agaia-4641). The registry can't describe what Hermes already has: it knows only scope <code>project</code> or <code>user</code>, one per event, and only events Gaia raises today. Hermes also allows <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code>, <code>doc.deleted</code> (Gaia publishing: agaia-4531, pending) and <code>search.semantic.changed</code> on the service scope <code>service:ares</code> (Gaia publishing: agaia-4658), and routes <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> to both <code>user:&lt;id&gt;</code> and the <code>runtimes</code> scope (<code>AgentRunLiveEvents</code> already publishes to both).</p><ul><li><code>app/metadata/events.php</code>: replace <code>scope</code> with <code>scopes</code>, a list of <code>project</code>, <code>user</code>, <code>runtimes</code>, <code>service</code>; an entry with <code>service</code> also has <code>serviceKind</code> (e.g. <code>ares</code>). Update every entry; <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> gets <code>user</code> + <code>runtimes</code>. Update the header comment.</li><li>New optional flag <code>planned: true</code>: Hermes may already allow the event, but Gaia doesn't raise it yet. A planned entry is not in <code>EventNames::ALL</code> and <code>HermesPublisher</code> treats it as not allowed.</li><li>Add planned entries: <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code>, <code>doc.deleted</code> (scopes project, channel hermes, consumers prometheus, collab) and <code>search.semantic.changed</code> (scopes service, serviceKind ares, channel hermes, consumers ares).</li><li><code>core/libs/events/EventRegistry.php</code>: <code>scopes(name)</code>, <code>serviceKind(name)</code>, <code>planned(name)</code>; <code>names(channel)</code> excludes planned and disabled entries. Validate on load: known scopes only, <code>serviceKind</code> required with <code>service</code> and only then.</li><li><code>tools/gaia-dev/src/Check/LiveEventsCheck.php</code>: a planned entry must have no <code>EventNames</code> constant emitted by code; when code emits it, fail with "remove planned from &lt;name&gt; in app/metadata/events.php". Planned entries need no test case.</li><li><code>tools/gaia-dev/src/Docs/EventsExport.php</code>: each item becomes <code>{name, scopes, serviceKind?, channels, enabled, planned, description}</code>; regenerate <code>docs/generated/events.json</code>.</li><li>ADR update in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/decisions.md</code> (the registry decision): scopes list, planned entries, and the drift rule Hermes applies: Gaia's enabled, non-planned hermes names must be in the allowlist; every allowlisted name must be in the registry on the hermes channel (planned included); user/runtimes/service scope sets must match.</li><li>Tests: registry (scopes, serviceKind validation, planned excluded from names), check (planned and emitted fails), export shape.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> events published today are unchanged; <code>events.json</code> lists doc.* and search.semantic.changed as planned with their scopes and <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> with user + runtimes; gaia-dev check passes on dev.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> publishing doc.* (agaia-4531) or search.semantic.changed (agaia-4658), which must each drop <code>planned</code> when they publish; the Hermes script (ah-4643).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4676	2026-11-25	2026-11-18	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7b8e27936afc-30ee-311d-92e76