7c0e25e36afa-4169-5cb2-62f1a6a4eeb9	EzSearch: icon-only Saved Searches, Builder, Search and Clear when its own box is narrow	2026-11-15 23:17:16	2026-11-15 23:54:54	0	<p>EzSearch (<code>components/ez-search/index.{hbs,js}</code>) only drops its button labels at the xs viewport (<code>hidden-xs</code>). Inside a narrow box (a list in a side column, ListToolbar with actions) the buttons eat the space and the input gets squeezed. The input must take priority. Scope: the component, its demo and docs.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li>New modifier <code>app/modifiers/observe-width.js</code> (ResizeObserver on the element, calls back with the width; cleans up on destroy; no-op where ResizeObserver is missing; the only current ResizeObserver use is <code>app-ui/gantt-chart.js</code> ~l.1034-1084 for reference). Reusable by ListToolbar later.</li><li>EzSearch measures its own root: below a threshold (start at 560px, constant in the component) it adds <code>ez-search--narrow</code>: Saved Searches shows <code>fa-bookmark</code> only (saved name in the title), Builder <code>fa-sliders</code> only, Search <code>fa-search</code> only, Clear <code>fa-times</code> only; every icon button keeps its title and aria-label. The input flexes and keeps a min width (about 160px). The existing xs behaviour stays.</li><li><code>@narrow</code> (true/false) forces the mode; when not given it is automatic.</li><li>Styles in <code>app/styles/components/ez-search.scss</code> (scoped under <code>.ez-search--narrow</code>).</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/ez-search.{hbs,js}</code>: a width control (full / 50% / 320px) to show the switch. Docs <code>public/ui-docs/ez-search.md</code> (+ manifest if present).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests: forced narrow shows icon-only buttons with titles; automatic switch with a stubbed width; modifier unit test. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: EzSearchCompact, ListToolbar, page changes.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> list-toolbar-table.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4593	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	0f9c42986afa-ed55-dae4-70d9a9fe0ec4	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-15 23:54:54	aprom	0	0
df201b196ae5-0313-c311-a5391ed1c8b5	Issue statuses: label text colour is always dark or light (default light)	2026-10-31 00:14:23	2026-11-11 12:26:51	0	<p>The label text colour of an issue status is always <code>dark</code> or <code>light</code>. The automatic option (<code>null</code>) is removed. New and existing statuses default to <code>light</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Changes</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>app/metadata/model/Issuestatus.php</code>: <code>textColor</code> gets <code>'default' =&gt; 'light'</code>, so a database that adds the column fills existing rows with <code>light</code>.</li>\n<li>Model:\n<ul>\n<li><code>isValidTextColor()</code> accepts only <code>dark</code> or <code>light</code>, in any case, stored lowercase;</li>\n<li><code>beforeValidation()</code> sets <code>light</code> when no text colour was given (a create without <code>textColor</code>).</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li>Controller: an explicit <code>"textColor": null</code> is rejected with 422 on POST, PATCH and the collection PATCH, along with any value other than dark or light.</li>\n<li><code>db/seeds/issue_statuses.sql</code>: an idempotent backfill, <code>UPDATE issue_statuses SET "textColor" = 'light' WHERE "textColor" IS NULL</code>, for databases where the column already exists.</li>\n<li>The message becomes "Text colour must be dark or light."</li>\n<li>Regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> (graph and docs).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Tests</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>PHPUnit:\n<ul>\n<li><code>null</code> is no longer a valid text colour;</li>\n<li>a status saved without a text colour gets <code>light</code>.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li>api-tester client cases:\n<ul>\n<li>creating without <code>textColor</code> returns <code>light</code>;</li>\n<li>PATCH with <code>null</code> returns 422;</li>\n<li>the clear-to-null case is replaced.</li>\n</ul></li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4216	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	377d68b06ae5-ae73-c875-706564943ab0	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-02 13:23:16	agaia	0	0
c6bdb3776ae3-b6e2-0c1c-a2a05cf87bae	ai rabbit: read CodeRabbit's check run (it no longer posts a commit status), so the loop sees gaia reviews	2026-10-29 16:39:34	2026-10-29 17:17:37	0	<p>Follow-up to adt-4188/4190. <code>ai rabbit</code> reads only the legacy commit status with context <code>CodeRabbit</code>. CodeRabbit now reports as a <strong>check run</strong> named <code>CodeRabbit</code> from the app <code>coderabbitai</code> (seen on gaia #228 and #229; ares #3 on 2026-10-19 still had the old status). So on gaia every PR reads as <code>pending</code>:</p><pre>ai rabbit gaia 229 -&gt; pending   (CodeRabbit completed, with findings)\nai rabbit gaia 228 -&gt; pending   (CodeRabbit completed, "No actionable comments")</pre><p>Talos then never runs a bot round on gaia; each PR waits <code>botReviewWaitMinutes</code> (20) and is handed to the reviewer with CodeRabbit's findings still open.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In <code>ai/lib/coderabbit.py</code>, read the head commit's check runs (<code>repos/{repo}/commits/{sha}/check-runs</code>) and use the one from app slug <code>coderabbitai</code>: <code>queued</code>/<code>in_progress</code> = pending; <code>completed</code> + <code>success</code> = review done (then the open bot threads decide clean or findings); other conclusions = absent with the conclusion as detail.</li><li>Fall back to the legacy commit status when there is no check run, so both forms work.</li><li>Keep the paused/rate-limit detection from the bot comments.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests with recorded check-run responses (in progress, completed with findings, completed clean, failure) and with the legacy status; <code>ai rabbit gaia 229</code> reports <code>findings</code> (or <code>clean</code> if its threads are all answered) and <code>ai rabbit gaia 228</code> reports <code>clean</code>; the CodeRabbit section of the ai and Talos READMEs names the check run.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4193	2026-11-05	2026-10-29	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	b1a296116ae0-36a5-29af-371308f931b7	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	032cc6e06ae3-decc-e2b6-e7bdc43acf4a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-29 17:17:37	adt	0	1
64baf8256ae5-7d7f-843d-ada0f9a51156	Issue list view: match the list-control buttons to the project list view	2026-10-30 21:43:00	2026-10-30 22:03:35	0	<p>The list-control buttons on the issue list view (<code>app.project.issue.index</code>, <code>app/templates/app/project/issue/index.hbs</code>) should match the project list view (<code>app/templates/app/projects/index.hbs</code>). Both the top and bottom bars should show exactly: Select all, Delete, Mass update, Export, the selected count, and Prev/Next page.</p>\n<h4>Remove from the bottom bar</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Share</strong> (<code>fa-share-alt</code>). It has no action.</li>\n<li><strong>Discuss</strong> (<code>fa-comments-o</code>). It has no action.</li>\n<li><strong>Refresh</strong> (<code>fa-refresh</code>, <code>reloadPage</code>). The project list has no Refresh button.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Align</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Hook up the Delete button on both bars to <code>@onClick={{this.deleteSelected}}</code>, which is inherited from <code>PrometheusListController</code>. It has no action today.</li>\n<li>Add <code>data-btn="delete-issues"</code> and <code>data-btn="mass-update-issues"</code> to both bars, matching the project list's <code>delete-projects</code>/<code>mass-update-projects</code>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>global.list.selectedCount</code> for the selected count, as the project list does.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Out of scope</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>The search bar, the column sort buttons and the per-row actions stay unchanged.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Acceptance</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Both bars of the issue list show the same buttons as the project list, with no Share, Discuss or Refresh.</li>\n<li>Selecting issues and clicking Delete deletes them.</li>\n<li>Acceptance tests that cover the issue list still pass, and the tests are updated if they reference the removed buttons.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4203	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Odysseus	Rana Nouman	5763c7436ae5-b7f5-613b-74b7070780c3	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 22:03:33	aprom	0	0
88c571756afa-4169-5cb2-9550be46c612	AppUi::ListToolbar: selection bar tied to the list's selection, space-conscious search	2026-11-15 23:17:28	2026-11-16 00:34:42	0	<p>We are finalizing the core components of the Component Library. <code>AppUi::ListToolbar</code> (<code>components/app-ui/list-toolbar.hbs</code>, styles <code>styles/components/app-ui-list-toolbar.scss</code>) leaves selection to the page (the demo <code>components/developer/demos/list-page.{hbs,js}</code> hand-rolls select-all, bulk buttons and "(Selected : N)" unrelated to the table) and gives the search no priority in small spaces. Fix the component, the list-page demo and the docs; do not change pages that use it.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li><code>@selection</code> (the <code>Selection</code> from <code>utils/state/selection.js</code>, the same instance passed to <code>AppUi::DataTable</code>) + <code>@rows</code> (current page rows): when <code>count &gt; 0</code> the toolbar shows a selection bar like <code>QuickList::SelectionBar</code> (<code>components/quick-list/selection-bar.hbs</code>; reuse its markup/classes or the component): tri-state select-all for the page, "N selected" + "X on this page, Y on other pages", <code>&lt;:bulkActions as |ids clear|&gt;</code>, a clear button. With nothing selected: the page select-all icon and a muted hint. The pager stays on the right. The old <code>&lt;:selection&gt;</code> block keeps working when <code>@selection</code> is not given.</li><li>Narrow mode: measure the toolbar with <code>modifiers/observe-width.js</code>; below the threshold pass <code>@narrow={{true}}</code> to the search (document that EzSearch goes in the search block) and yield <code>narrow</code> to <code>&lt;:actions as |narrow|&gt;</code> so callers can show icon-only buttons. The search block flexes first (min width), actions never push it below that; if still too narrow, actions wrap under it.</li><li>Demo <code>list-page</code>: one Selection shared by ListToolbar and DataTable across fixture pages, bulk actions log the ids, EzSearch in the search block with the saved-search wiring, a width control (full / col-md-4) to show narrow mode.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/list-toolbar.md</code> + <code>list-toolbar.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: integration tests: bar appears with the right counts across pages, bulk block gets ids, clear empties the selection, narrow passes @narrow and yields it to actions. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: changing Agents/Workflows list pages, select all matching.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4591, aprom-4593</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> list-toolbar-table.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4594	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	54e7a9156afa-2dd7-0d65-33e557c8fd3d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 00:34:42	aprom	0	0
e880c5456af0-cd0b-cccd-1e2d7f5f8441	ACL: tokens with scopes are held to them on top of the actor's ACL	2026-11-08 20:39:04	2026-11-08 21:47:52	0	<p>Delegated agent tokens (later issue) must never do more than their scopes allow, even when the agent's roles would. Today scopes on tokens are ignored. Effective access becomes: the actor's ACL AND the token's scopes. Scopes only narrow; tokens without scopes (people, agents' own credentials) are unchanged.</p><ul><li>Scope vocabulary = existing permission names (<code>issue.get</code>, <code>comment.create</code>) with <code>*</code> wildcards (<code>issue.*</code>, <code>*.get</code>).</li><li>In <code>RestController::authorize()</code> (after <code>verifyResourceRequest</code>), when the access token has a scope, the requested <code>controller.action</code> must match one; related and included resources (RBAC D-020) are checked the same way and omitted when not covered (D-021).</li><li>Hard exclusions for scoped tokens regardless of scope: agentcredential.*, serviceclient.*, enrollment resources, role.*, userrole.*, permission.*, agent create/update/delete.</li><li>Keep the check in one class under <code>core/libs/security</code> (not inline in the controller); decision entry in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for matching, wildcards, related reads and exclusions; api-tester cases with a scoped token. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> issuing scoped tokens.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4385	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	dee441406af0-cd0b-cccd-253efc87745a	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	56b105b36af0-7d1c-cccd-e7b71cdbe784	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 21:47:52	agaia	0	0
113e4a7668ed-a704-fb30-8b37208078d9	Issue types: translated labels in Settings and everywhere types are shown	2025-10-14 06:09:21	2026-11-11 12:27:43	0	<p>For now we are using issue types directly inside the template, whereas we have to render these as translated.</p>\n<p><strong>What</strong><br>Settings &gt; Issue Types works like Settings &gt; Issue Statuses (aprom-3977): a label per language and a value derived from what's typed. The translated label is shown everywhere a type appears.</p>\n<p><strong>Changes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Model and serializer</strong>: convert <code>issuetype</code> to a native class, add <code>@attr() translations</code>, send <code>translations</code> only when they changed.</li>\n<li><strong>Shared utils</strong>: generalise <code>utils/issue-status/{label,value,form}.js</code> over a label path and use them for both statuses and types. Statuses behave exactly as before.</li>\n<li><strong>Settings &gt; Issue Types</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Modal: a <code>FormFields::FieldText</code> label per supported locale (<code>en-us</code> required); a value field suggested from the <code>en-us</code> label until the user types in it, read-only when editing; a description field.</li>\n<li>List: Label, Value, Description and Projects using columns. Label = the one saved in Gaia, then the translated name, then the value.</li>\n<li>New labels are added to intl right away so they show without a reload.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong>Display</strong>: translated type label in the issue list, issue details, board, milestones, gantt panel, issue create select and project create select. List sort stays on the value.</li>\n<li><strong><code>issue-planning.js</code></strong>: find the sub-task type by value <code>sub_task</code> instead of <code>'Sub Task'</code>.</li>\n<li>All strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tests</strong>: update <code>issue-types.feature</code> and steps (add, edit, read-only value, labels per locale); unit tests for the generalised utils; a scenario for the translated label in the issue list and details; Mirage fixtures switched to values plus <code>translations</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Depends on</strong>: agaia-4152 (Gaia API and migration). Related: adt-4153 (gaia MCP).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	3699	2025-10-17	2025-10-14	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Agent Odysseus	e83a28176ae1-affe-9a2f-34db2be3f844	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-28 10:33:24	aprom	0	0
66bdada56afa-4169-5cb2-83b730f9d591	List selection model shared by DataTable and ListToolbar, kept across pages	2026-11-15 23:16:54	2026-11-15 23:37:15	0	<p>DataTable selection only knows the current page (<code>@selectedIds</code>/<code>@onSelect</code>/<code>@onSelectAll</code> in <code>components/app-ui/data-table.{hbs,js}</code>), and ListToolbar has no link to it. We need multi-page selection that the table and the toolbar share. This issue adds the model and DataTable support; the look and the toolbar are separate issues.</p><ul><li>New <code>app/utils/state/selection.js</code> class <code>Selection</code> (next to <code>AsyncResource</code>/<code>ListLoader</code>/<code>UrlState</code>): tracked set of ids (strings); <code>has(id)</code>, <code>toggle(id)</code>, <code>set(ids, on)</code>, <code>clear()</code>, <code>count</code>, <code>ids</code>, <code>stateFor(rows)</code> returning none|some|all for the given page rows, <code>countIn(rows)</code>. Kept across page changes; no totals (lists use limit+1 paging, see <code>docs/architecture/lists/decisions.md</code>), so no "select all matching".</li><li><code>AppUi::DataTable</code> takes <code>@selection</code> (a Selection): row toggles and the header select-all (current page) use it; <code>@onSelectionChange</code> fires with the ids. The existing <code>@selectedIds</code>/<code>@onSelect</code>/<code>@onSelectAll</code> keep working when <code>@selection</code> is not given.</li><li>Document it in <code>docs/architecture/state/</code> (one section) and in <code>public/ui-docs/data-table.md</code> + <code>data-table.json</code> (new args/events).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests for Selection; integration test: select on page 1, change rows (page 2), select, go back: page 1 rows still selected, count = both. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: checkbox look, toolbar selection bar, QuickList adopting it, select all matching.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4591	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	dde7cfa16afa-4169-5cb2-ff6754c99cb0	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-15 23:37:15	aprom	0	0
cad1b3a96afa-23c6-fe2e-8cf3fbe9a0e3	Data layer: bulk query service that batches store queries into one POST /api/v1/bulk	2026-11-16 02:09:14	2026-11-16 02:41:03	0	<p>Gaia now has a <code>bulk</code> resource (agaia-4587) that runs several REST calls in one request. Screens that make many independent queries (Task Board first, later Dashboard and Gantt) pay one network round trip per query today. This adds a reusable client so routes can batch their queries and still get ordinary Ember Data records.</p><p><strong>Gaia contract</strong> (see <code>gaia/docs/architecture/bulk/decisions.md</code>): <code>POST /api/v1/bulk</code> with <code>{"requests": [{"id": "lane-1", "method": "GET", "url": "/api/v1/issue?query=...&amp;rels=...&amp;limit=-1", "body": null}]}</code> returns 200 <code>{"responses": [{"id", "status", "body", "durationMs"}]}</code> in request order. There can be at most 25 items (BULK_MAX_REQUESTS). The call needs the <code>bulk.create</code> permission, and each item is authorized like a direct call.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>New service <code>app/services/bulk.js</code> with <code>query(items)</code>, where each item is <code>{id, modelName, query}</code> and <code>query</code> is the same options object passed to <code>store.query</code> (<code>query</code>, <code>rels</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>order</code>, <code>limit</code>). It returns a map id → <code>{records}</code> or <code>{error}</code>.</li><li>Build each item's URL with the model's adapter (<code>buildURL</code>/<code>urlForQuery</code>, serialized query params), so it matches what <code>store.query</code> sends, made relative as <code>/api/v1/...</code>.</li><li>Send the batch through the application adapter's <code>ajax</code> (<code>app/adapters/application.js</code> ~l.256) so token refresh, the 401 retry and the test waiter apply. No raw <code>fetch</code>.</li><li>For each 2xx item, normalize the body with <code>store.serializerFor(modelName).normalizeResponse(store, modelClass, body, null, 'query')</code> and <code>store.push</code> it. Non-2xx items become an <code>error</code> for that id only.</li><li>Split batches above the limit into several bulk calls (limit in <code>config/environment.js</code> <code>ENV.APP.bulkMaxRequests</code>, default 25) and merge the results.</li><li>Fallback: when the bulk call itself fails (403 because the role lacks <code>bulk.create</code>, network error, non-200), run the items as separate <code>store.query</code> calls in parallel and return the same shape. Log one warning.</li><li>Mirage: a <code>/bulk</code> POST handler that answers each GET item with the same data the existing Mirage handlers return for that resource (at least <code>issue</code>, <code>milestone</code>, <code>issuestatus</code>).</li><li>A short doc section in <code>docs/architecture/</code> (a new <code>bulk/</code> folder) on when to use the service and the fallback.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests: URL building matches <code>store.query</code>, results land in the store, one failing item doesn't affect the others, more than 25 items are split, and a failed or 403 bulk call falls back to separate queries.</li><li>Lint and the full test suite pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> writes (POST/PATCH/DELETE items), using it on any screen (separate issues), milestone overviews.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4595	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	3957ee086afa-1752-9ce6-d9c74d024b9a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 02:38:45	aprom	0	0
