079482d96af0-7d1c-cccd-e006ecd49135	Service enrollment: single-use enrollment tokens for unattended deploys	2026-11-08 20:39:35	2026-11-08 23:56:47	0	<p>Deployed services (Hermes, later Ares) can't wait for someone to approve a code. A deploy pipeline gets a single-use enrollment token and passes it to the container; the service enrolls with it and is approved automatically.</p><ul><li>Resource <code>Serviceenrollmenttoken</code>: kind, name, expiresAt (15 minutes), usedAt, createdUser. Admin POST returns the token once (stored hashed); list and DELETE (revoke).</li><li>An enrollment request (<code>Serviceenrollment</code> POST) carrying a valid, unused, unexpired token of the same kind is approved at once; the token is marked used. Invalid tokens are refused without saying why.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for single use, expiry, kind mismatch, revoke; api-tester acl cases. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> UI.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4387</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4388	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	dee441406af0-cd0b-cccd-253efc87745a	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	a7ebb1c66af0-b0f8-e90a-b617baf1dcc3	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 23:56:47	agaia	0	0
