eba6b1d96afe-167c-9848-5b36024e0353	Mentions: replace the legacy notified column with a boolean isNotified so mentions can be saved on Postgres	2026-11-18 20:39:07	2026-11-18 21:16:35	0	<p><strong>Problem</strong></p><p>Mentions are never recorded on Postgres, so nobody gets the "mentioned you" notification. Seen on ah-4652: three comments with a valid <code>&lt;a href="/app/user/1"&gt;</code> mention created no Mention row on devapi.</p><ul><li><code>mentions.notified</code> is still <code>smallint</code> from the MySQL port (<code>tinyint(1)</code>). The metadata declares it <code>bool</code>, and the Postgres migration deliberately leaves bool/smallint differences alone (<code>core/mvc/db/migration/Postgres.php</code> <code>isVarcharLengthChange</code>).</li><li>Gaia binds bool fields as <code>PDO::PARAM_BOOL</code> (<code>core/libs/meta/manager.php</code>). Postgres rejects that for a smallint column: <code>invalid input syntax for type smallint: "f"</code>. Checked with PDO in gaia-dev; binding <code>0</code> as an int works.</li><li><code>MentionRecorder::save()</code> sets <code>notified = false</code>, the insert fails, and <code>mentionsBehavior</code> only logs it (fail-open), so the comment saves but no mention is recorded. <code>MentionNotification</code> would fail the same way on <code>notified = true</code>.</li><li>Tests missed it: the recorder and notification tests override the save, and <code>pr4m_test</code> has the same legacy column.</li><li>The name <code>notified</code> also trips the Phalcon PHQL parser bug (agaia-4678), so <code>GET /api/v1/mention</code> fails with <code>column Mention.ified does not exist</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Change</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/metadata/model/Mention.php</code>: replace <code>notified</code> with <code>isNotified</code> (type <code>bool</code>, <code>'null' =&gt; false</code>, <code>'default' =&gt; false</code>). The default matters: columns added to an existing table start out nullable, and devapi has a 2016 seed row. The migration then adds a real <code>boolean</code> column and drops <code>notified</code> (CASCADE).</li><li>Update <code>core/libs/mentions/MentionRecorder.php</code> (line ~192), <code>MentionNotification.php</code> (line ~101), <code>MentionNotificationTest</code>, and the label (<code>LBL_MENTIONS_NOTIFIED</code>) if it is renamed.</li><li>Add a test that saves a real Mention row to the test database (no stubbed save), so a type mismatch fails the suite.</li><li>Check the row that references <code>Mention.notified</code> in the committed dumps (e.g. <code>db/Dump20260710.sql</code> line ~48479; looks like a field ACL or permission entry). Report it so the reviewer can clean it up by hand; no seed SQL.</li></ul><p><strong>Why the house rule's three-step rename is skipped:</strong> the column has never held real data (the only row is the 2016 seed, value 0) and no code reads it yet. Say this in the PR.</p><p><strong>Rejected names:</strong> nothing starting with "not" (e.g. <code>notifiedAt</code> parses as <code>ifiedAt</code>). <code>isNotified</code> parses correctly.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after <code>p4m db migrate</code>, <code>mentions.isNotified</code> is <code>boolean</code> and <code>notified</code> is gone. Mentioning a project member in a comment creates a Mention row and a "mentioned you" notification. <code>GET /api/v1/mention</code> returns rows including <code>isNotified</code>. The full suite passes.</p><p><strong>Deploy note:</strong> each environment (devapi/OVH included) needs <code>p4m db migrate</code>, run by someone with access. Then take the new dump (agaia-4679).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4677	2026-11-26	2026-11-19	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7b8e27936afc-30ee-311d-92e7628909b7	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6