a00637f16ae5-f83a-391a-d6fd2d30b638	Talos: record a reason code with every handback	2026-10-30 20:40:00	2026-10-30 21:09:02	0	<p>Today the reason Talos hands an issue back exists only as comment text, so nothing can tell a mechanical stop from a real question for the reviewer. Agent Agamemnon will restart mechanical stops automatically, so Talos needs to store the reason as a code.</p><h4>Store</h4><ul><li><code>talos/lib/db.py</code>: add columns <code>handoff_reason</code>, <code>handoff_detail</code> (JSON), <code>handoff_at</code> and <code>auto_retries</code> (INTEGER DEFAULT 0) to <code>issues</code>. Migrate idempotently in <code>connect()</code>: run <code>ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN</code> when <code>PRAGMA table_info</code> doesn't list the column.</li><li><code>sessions.update</code> and <code>sessions.get</code> carry the new fields. <code>talos reset &lt;agent&gt; &lt;issue&gt;</code> also clears <code>auto_retries</code>.</li></ul><h4>Codes, set by <code>Dispatcher._hand_off(..., reason, detail=None)</code></h4><ul><li><code>turn_budget</code> / <code>cost_budget</code>: <code>read_outcome</code> budget stop (subtype <code>error_max_turns</code> / <code>error_max_budget_usd</code>)</li><li><code>interrupted</code>: <code>recover_interrupted</code></li><li><code>branch_checked_out</code>: <code>_branch_checked_out</code>, with detail {branch, folder, repo}</li><li><code>talos_error</code>: the <code>"talos error"</code> subtype (exception around runner.execute), or a WorkspaceError that failed the run</li><li><code>agent_needs_input</code> / <code>agent_blocked</code>: Claude's own outcomes, including escalation at the top model</li><li><code>run_error</code>: Claude error result, or no valid outcome</li><li><code>iteration_limit</code>: <code>_iteration_limit</code></li><li><code>not_handed_back</code>: <code>_check_handed_back</code></li></ul><p><code>policy.read_outcome</code> returns the reason code alongside the outcome, and its callers are updated to match. Comments and statuses stay as they are.</p><h4>Tests</h4><p>The db migration runs on an old schema and a second time. Each handback site records its code. <code>reset</code> clears <code>auto_retries</code>.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4200	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	30c8c4d46ae5-1185-de02-ab975db62d2e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 21:09:02	adt	0	0
9de606356af3-1487-2734-6aba546d585b	Replace the {{action}} helper and modifier with {{on}} and {{fn}}	2026-11-10 21:33:17	2026-11-11 13:49:42	0	<p>Ember 6.0 removed the <code>{{action}}</code> helper and modifier. In the spike they caused about 105 test failures (<code>Attempted to resolve `action`, which was expected to be a helper</code>).</p><p><strong>Scope</strong>: 278 uses in 66 templates.</p><ul><li><code>&lt;button {{action "save"}}&gt;</code> → <code>&lt;button {{on "click" this.save}}&gt;</code>; <code>(action "foo" x)</code> → <code>(fn this.foo x)</code>; <code>(action "foo")</code> passed as an argument → <code>this.foo</code>.</li><li>Handlers must be bound: use <code>@action</code> in native classes, or <code>foo: action(function () {…})</code> in classic <code>.extend()</code> components, instead of the <code>actions: {}</code> hash.</li><li><strong>Watch out:</strong> <code>{{action}}</code> on an element calls <code>preventDefault()</code> by default and <code>{{on}}</code> doesn't. Forms and <code>&lt;a href&gt;</code> handlers must call <code>event.preventDefault()</code> themselves.</li><li><code>value="target.value"</code> needs a small handler that reads <code>event.target.value</code>.</li></ul><p><code>{{on}}</code> and <code>{{fn}}</code> have existed since Ember 3.11, so this works on 4.1. It touches many templates, so check file overlap before running it in parallel with other issues.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4477	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	237405846af4-3bdf-7fa2-354b443dcae7	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 13:49:42	aprom	0	0
d3e966706afa-23c6-fe2e-1439607c2414	Task Board: load milestones, backlog, statuses and milestone lanes in two bulk requests	2026-11-16 02:09:23	2026-11-16 03:04:09	0	<p>The Task Board route makes 3 + N requests: active milestones, backlog issues and issue statuses one after another, then one issue query per milestone. With many active milestones this adds visible latency. Switch it to the <code>bulk</code> service (the bulk-client issue) so the board loads in two requests.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong> in <code>app/routes/app/project/board.js</code> <code>model</code> (~l.61-131):</p><ul><li>Round 1, one <code>bulk.query</code>: the milestones query (l.67-72), the backlog issues query (l.80-88, including the ezSearch <code>searchQuery</code> AND) and the project's issue statuses (l.92-95). Same query strings, rels, sort and limits as today.</li><li>Round 2, one <code>bulk.query</code> with one item per returned milestone (the per-milestone query of l.99-112, with <code>searchQuery</code>), then <code>replaceRecords(milestone.issues, records)</code> as today.</li><li>Keep today's error handling: a failed item goes through <code>errorManager.handleError</code> (with <code>moduleName: 'milestone'</code> for the milestones item), and a failed lane shows as empty instead of breaking the board. Backlog milestone creation (<code>getBacklogMilestone</code>), <code>afterModel</code> (system statuses fallback, sort) and <code>loadSearchData</code> stay unchanged.</li><li>Extend the board's acceptance coverage (e.g. <code>tests/acceptance/taskboard/render-milestone.feature</code>) so it runs through the Mirage <code>/bulk</code> handler and checks that lanes and backlog render as before, including with an ezSearch query applied.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Opening the board makes two <code>POST /bulk</code> requests and no per-milestone <code>GET /issue</code> (verify in the running app's network tab).</li><li>Lanes, backlog, status columns, filtering and live updates behave as before.</li><li>If the user's role lacks <code>bulk.create</code>, the board still loads (service fallback).</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the controller's own reloads (<code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> ~l.1119), Hermes-driven refreshes, Dashboard and Gantt.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4595</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4596	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	f0d8c4046afa-5d2e-1a87-b51e7be3911e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 03:04:09	aprom	0	0
f36ee3d46afe-167c-9848-b8524ae1d5a5	After the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon upgrade: check whether PHQL still strips "not" from column names; if so, add a metadata gate and an ADR	2026-11-18 20:39:15	2026-11-18 21:01:56	0	<p><strong>Background</strong></p><p>Phalcon 4.1.2's PHQL parser strips a leading <code>not</code> from an unbracketed column name after a dot. Checked with <code>Phalcon\\Mvc\\Model\\Query\\Lang::parsePHQL</code> in gaia-dev:</p><ul><li><code>SELECT Mention.notified</code> parses as column <code>ified</code> (the alias too). On devapi, <code>GET /api/v1/mention</code> failed with <code>column Mention.ified does not exist</code>.</li><li><code>Mention.nothing</code> becomes <code>hing</code>; <code>Mention.notes</code> becomes <code>es</code>; <code>Mention.notifiedAt</code> becomes <code>ifiedAt</code>.</li><li><code>[Mention].[notified]</code> parses correctly.</li><li>Other prefixes tested are fine: <code>isNotified</code>, <code>inboxed</code>, <code>ordered</code>, <code>asked</code>, <code>byUser</code>, <code>andy</code>.</li></ul><p>After agaia-4677 renames <code>Mention.notified</code> to <code>isNotified</code>, no field, relationship or model name in <code>app/metadata</code> starts with "not". Nothing triggers the bug today.</p><p><strong>Decision (2026-11-19):</strong> don't rewrite the query layer to bracket identifiers. Wait for the planned PHP 8.5 + latest Phalcon upgrade and re-test there first.</p><p><strong>Work, after the upgrade lands</strong></p><ol><li>Re-run the parser check on the new Phalcon: <code>Lang::parsePHQL("SELECT Mention.notified FROM Mention")</code> and the other cases above. Record the result on this issue.</li><li><strong>If fixed:</strong> close this issue with the evidence.</li><li><strong>If still broken:</strong><ul><li>Add a gate test that reads all model metadata and fails when <code>parsePHQL</code> returns a different name than the one written, for any field (<code>Model.field</code>), relationship (<code>rel.field</code>) or model name. Compare parsed against written names, not a hard-coded "not" rule, so the test keeps passing if a later Phalcon fixes it.</li><li>Add an ADR to <code>docs/architecture/*/decisions.md</code>: field, relationship and model names must survive the PHQL parser unchanged (no "not" prefix), enforced by the gate. Record why the query layer is not bracketing identifiers.</li></ul></li></ol><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the parser behaviour on the upgraded stack is recorded. Either this issue is closed as fixed upstream, or the gate test and ADR are merged and the full suite passes.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> the PHP 8.5 / Phalcon upgrade milestone; agaia-4677</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 2</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	4678	2026-11-26	2026-11-19	deferred	low	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	7b8e27936afc-30ee-311d-92e7628909b7	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Achilles	Agent Achilles	478d03436afe-8d72-9848-5dfea7f483f0	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-18 21:01:57	agaia	0	0
