437203156ae5-f5b6-1173-6029d6d02c43	Ideas list: show each idea's progress from the status of its latest plan	2026-10-30 22:08:03	2026-10-31 07:40:13	0	<p>The ideas browser (<code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>, ~l.21) labels every idea with <code>Idea.status</code>, which is only <code>open</code> or <code>archived</code>, so every listed idea reads "Open". The engineer wants the list to show where each idea is: the status of its latest plan.</p><ul><li><strong>Status shown:</strong> <code>archived</code> idea: "Archived" (<code>deferred</code> label, as today). Open idea with no plan: "Brainstorming" (<code>new</code> label). Otherwise the status of the idea's plan with the highest <code>version</code>: proposed "Plan proposed", approved "Approved", creating "Creating issues", created "Issues created", failed "Failed". Add these under a new key such as <code>views.app.idea.progress.*</code> in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>. An unknown status falls back to <code>views.app.idea.plan.status.*</code>.</li><li><strong>Label colours:</strong> move <code>STATUS_LABELS</code> (plan status to label class) out of <code>components/idea/plan-box.js</code> into a shared util (e.g. <code>app/utils/idea/plan-status.js</code>), used by the plan box and the list, so both always use the same colours. The plan box keeps behaving as now.</li><li><strong>Data:</strong> in <code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code>, after <code>loadIdeas</code>, load the plans of the listed ideas in one <code>store.query('ideaplan', …)</code> (Ideaplan has <code>ideaId</code>, no <code>projectId</code>: filter by the loaded idea ids, or through the <code>idea</code> rel's projectId if Gaia's query supports it). No hasMany rels. The layout controller (<code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>) holds the latest plan status per idea id and gives the template the status and class per row. Keep the logic out of the template.</li><li><strong>Tests:</strong> the Mirage <code>ideaplan</code> handler supports the query. Acceptance cases in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-browser.feature</code>: idea without plan = Brainstorming; latest version wins (v1 created, v2 proposed = Plan proposed); archived idea = Archived. Unit test for the util.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> each idea in the browser shows Brainstorming, its latest plan's status or Archived, coloured like the plan box's status label, after loading or reloading the page.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> live updates on plan events (separate issue), the Open/Archived label in the conversation box header, any Gaia change, filtering or sorting by status.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4207	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	0f8f45126ae5-8a27-d0d9-9e60d0bedcbc	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 07:40:14	aprom	0	0
ae05dda26af7-ea0a-5be9-f679a8c1585e	Docs: require doc.update for Doc/Doccontent writes and reject writes on locked docs	2026-11-13 14:11:58	2026-11-16 09:52:43	0	<p>The collab server and the UI rely on Gaia to refuse writes a user isn't allowed to make. The review of agaia-4488 (gaia#264) found that a project member with only <code>doc.get</code>/<code>doc.create</code> got 200 on <code>PATCH /api/v1/doc/{id}</code>, and that <code>Doc.locked</code> is stored but not enforced.</p><ul><li>Find why update was authorized without <code>doc.update</code> (check how RestController/ACL authorizes PATCH for project-group resources, and whether other resources are affected) and fix it at the root. If the cause is in shared ACL code, fix it there and add denial cases for one other resource too.</li><li>Enforce <code>locked</code>: while a doc is locked, updates to its <code>Doccontent</code> are rejected (403 or a validation error, following the layering in the Design section). Only the doc's owner (<code>ownerId</code>) or a user with the project admin role may change <code>locked</code>, like the wiki lock today.</li><li>api-tester acl.json cases: Doc update and delete denied without doc.update/doc.delete; Doccontent update denied without doccontent.update; Doccontent update rejected on a locked doc; lock/unlock by the owner allowed, by another editor denied.</li><li>Record the lock rule as a decision in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the new denial cases pass and the existing Doc cases still pass.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-doc sharing roles, ownerId validation against project members.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4526</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4527	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	a489fe216af7-ea0a-5be9-d65370042b0c	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	9e53c3716af7-5b5b-7458-f19218ee5431	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 09:52:43	agaia	0	0
582a58746af0-7d1c-cccd-c738d0454d18	External Request: Socket auth through Gaia introspection, disconnect at token expiry	2026-11-08 20:40:56	2026-11-09 01:10:26	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Inter application Communication", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Replace the per-socket <code>/user/me</code> + membership lookup with the user's token (<code>src/auth/gaia-session.js</code>) by one Gaia introspection call made with Hermes' service token. Contract with the A Gaia introspection issue.</p><ul><li>Session = <code>sub</code>, <code>actorType</code>, <code>projectIds</code>, <code>exp</code> from introspection; cache as today (<code>session-cache.js</code>), never past <code>exp</code>.</li><li>Accept user and agent tokens (delegated included); refuse service tokens on normal intents (the runtimes room comes later).</li><li>Disconnect a socket when its token's <code>exp</code> passes (Prometheus already reconnects with the refreshed token, <code>services/hermes.js</code>).</li><li>ADR update for D-002, D-011, D-012.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests with a stub introspection: active, inactive, service token refused, expiry disconnect, cache bounded by exp. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> live revocation.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> ah-4395, agaia-4392</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4396	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	861790376ad5-1449-a602-a25bd5e6e2b8	d59707896af0-cd0b-cccd-6c0c771196c7	\N	87099ee46ad5-1449-a602-5f7a1f6605b7	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	087b2cd86af1-97fb-a09f-1ea234038472	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 01:10:26	ah	0	0
1743b9586afa-79f5-7528-cde93d86ad50	Dashboard: widgets register their first load through metadata and load in one bulk request	2026-11-16 09:55:35	2026-11-16 11:25:50	0	<p>The dashboard route loads the issue statuses and then each widget's first query one at a time (<code>app/routes/app/index.js</code> ~l.61-83, a <code>for … await</code> loop), so load time grows with every widget. Dashboards will soon be customizable and have more widgets, so the set of calls has to follow the widgets the user actually shows. Use the bulk service (aprom-4595) and make each widget's metadata entry its registration for the first load.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Registration contract: a widget registers its first load by declaring <code>model</code> + <code>options</code> in <code>views.Dashboard.widgets.&lt;name&gt;</code> (<code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> ~l.592; already the format, keep it). A widget without a declaration loads itself. Write this contract into a short doc under <code>docs/architecture/</code> (the bulk doc from aprom-4595).</li><li><code>routes/app/index.js</code>: after <code>_getValidWidgets</code> (the user's list, <code>currentUser.user.dashboard.widgets</code>), build one <code>bulk.query</code> with the system issue statuses item plus one item per visible widget that declares a load (options as prepared by <code>_getWidgetSettings</code>). Map results back to <code>widgetResults[widget]</code>.</li><li>A failed item gives that widget an empty result and goes through <code>errorManager.handleError</code>. The other widgets render. The service splits batches over the limit.</li><li>Widgets keep fetching directly after the first load (paging, week switching, refresh in <code>components/widgets/*.js</code>). Don't change them.</li><li>Acceptance: extend a dashboard feature (e.g. <code>tests/acceptance/dashboard/active-milestones/check-list-of-milestones.feature</code> or <code>tolerate-invalid-widgets.feature</code>) to cover the bulk path, including one widget whose item fails.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> opening the dashboard makes one <code>POST /bulk</code> for the statuses and all widget first loads, and no per-widget GET. A user with a different widget list gets a batch with only their widgets. Unknown widgets are still dropped as today.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the customizable dashboard itself, the milestone overviews (separate issue), runtime (same-tick) batching.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4595</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4598	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	0b92eaa36afa-8715-b3ee-794f1c04268c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 11:25:50	aprom	0	0
b425a5406af3-1487-2734-e66dce78e323	Remove Array prototype extension usage and disable EXTEND_PROTOTYPES.Array	2026-11-10 21:33:40	2026-11-11 15:05:21	0	<p>Ember 6.0 removed the Array prototype extensions. Plain arrays no longer have <code>pushObject</code>, <code>removeObject</code>, <code>addObject</code>, <code>filterBy</code>, <code>findBy</code>, <code>mapBy</code>, <code>sortBy</code>, <code>uniqBy</code>, <code>objectAt</code>, <code>firstObject</code>, <code>lastObject</code>, etc.</p><p><strong>Scope</strong>: about 280 call sites in roughly 90 app files, plus 73 in 31 test files.</p><ul><li>Set <code>EmberENV.EXTEND_PROTOTYPES: { Array: false }</code> in <code>config/environment.js</code>. The suite will then expose every remaining call on 4.1.</li><li>Replace them with native methods (<code>push</code>, <code>filter(x =&gt; x.prop === v)</code>, <code>find</code>, <code>map</code>, <code>[0]</code>, <code>at(-1)</code>). Where a template must react to the change, use a reassignment or <code>tracked-built-ins</code>.</li><li><strong>Caveat:</strong> ember-data 4.1 record arrays and has-many arrays still rely on their own <code>toArray</code>, <code>objectAt</code> and <code>filterBy</code>. Leave those for the ember-data upgrade; only plain arrays are in scope.</li></ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4479	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	58a057176af4-2978-7a99-55c8558ee835	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 15:05:22	aprom	0	0
4c76e3446ae5-f5b6-1173-29673d378d4b	Ideas list: update the plan status live on plan events	2026-10-30 22:08:12	2026-10-31 11:23:29	0	<p>After the ideas list shows each idea's latest plan status, it must stay current while Nestor proposes a plan or Talos creates the issues, without a page reload.</p><ul><li><code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> <code>registerHermesIntents</code> handles only <code>idea.created</code> and <code>idea.updated</code>. Also handle <code>idea.plan.created</code> and <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code> (already in the Hermes contract; the idea page controller uses them) by reloading the plans the list uses (the plan loader added by the list status issue, passed in by <code>routes/app/project/idea.js</code> like <code>loadIdeas</code>).</li><li>Keep the <code>reloadSequence</code> guard so a slower, earlier reload can't overwrite a newer one, and nothing runs after the route is left.</li><li>Tests: acceptance or integration case where a pushed <code>idea.plan.status.changed</code> (created) changes the row's label from Plan proposed to Issues created.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with the ideas page open, a new plan version or a plan status change updates that idea's label within the usual live-update delay.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> Gaia or Hermes changes (none needed).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4207</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4208	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	766dd6616ae5-c57f-5798-56ca4b4a2eae	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 11:23:30	aprom	0	0
1690fc416ae5-6104-d0d9-756be09743d1	Settings → Issue Statuses: replace colour swatches with a colour picker	2026-10-30 22:28:38	2026-11-11 12:27:12	0	<p>In the add/edit dialog of Settings → Issue Statuses, users pick a colour from 5 fixed swatches (<code>STATUS_COLORS</code> in <code>app/controllers/app/settings/issue-statuses.js</code>). Replace them with a colour picker so users can choose any colour for a status.</p>\n<p><b>Depends on</b> agaia #4209 (Gaia accepts any <code>#rrggbb</code> colour, returned lowercase). Until that is merged, Gaia answers 422 for a non-palette colour.</p>\n<h4>Changes</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Replace the swatch radio buttons in the dialog (<code>app/templates/app/settings/issue-statuses.hbs</code>, <code>data-field="issuestatus.color"</code>) with:\n<ul>\n<li>a native <code>&lt;input type="color"&gt;</code>;</li>\n<li>a hex text field (<code>#rrggbb</code>) kept in step with the picker;</li>\n<li>a live preview of the status label in the chosen colour.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li>Validate the hex field in the form (<code>#rrggbb</code> only), with a translated message. Remove <code>STATUS_COLORS</code> and its colour-name translations.</li>\n<li>Opening an existing status shows its saved colour. A new status starts with a default colour, e.g. <code>#80b5d3</code>.</li>\n<li>Status list table: paint each row's label with any valid hex colour. Today only palette colours get a style (the <code>STATUS_COLORS.find(...)</code> in the controller's rows).</li>\n<li>Readable labels: status labels use white text, which is unreadable on light colours. Choose black or white text from the background colour's brightness. Apply this wherever a status colour is painted: the settings table, issue labels (<code>status-style</code> helper) and task board columns.</li>\n<li>Follow <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code> (AdminLTE box, square edges).</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Tests</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Gherkin acceptance tests on Mirage:\n<ul>\n<li>add a status with a custom colour;</li>\n<li>edit a status to a new colour;</li>\n<li>an invalid hex shows the validation message and is not saved;</li>\n<li>a light colour renders dark label text.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li>Feature-only steps go in a per-feature steps file.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4210	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	6ba71de26ace-1e5c-2b63-25d38169aba6	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Odysseus	Agent Odysseus	b2460f116ae5-00a8-4220-41557033724e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-03 11:24:06	aprom	0	0
202681c36afa-79f5-7528-d1a744a515a4	Bulk service: plain JSON GET items; Active Milestones loads its overviews in one bulk request	2026-11-16 09:55:44	2026-11-16 10:31:08	0	<p>The Active Milestones widget loads one milestone overview per milestone with raw <code>fetch</code> and a hand-passed token (<code>app/utils/milestone-overview-api.js</code> <code>fetchMilestoneOverview</code>/<code>fetchMilestoneOverviewsBulk</code>, called from <code>components/widgets/active-milestones.js</code> ~l.72-110). That is N requests and it bypasses the adapter's token refresh (house rule: no raw fetch). Overviews are not Ember Data records, so the bulk service (aprom-4595) needs plain JSON items.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>services/bulk.js</code>: also accept <code>{id, url}</code> items (a relative <code>/api/v1/...</code> GET). They return <code>{status, body}</code> with the parsed JSON instead of records and are never pushed to the store. The fallback for a failed bulk call runs them through the adapter's <code>ajax</code>.</li><li><code>milestone-overview-api.js</code>: replace the raw fetches with one <code>bulk.query</code> of overview items (same URL as <code>buildMilestoneOverviewUrl</code>). Keep the return shape <code>[{id, overview}]</code> with <code>null</code> for failures. Drop the token argument.</li><li><code>active-milestones.js</code>: call it without the token, for both the first load and "load more" (<code>merge: true</code>).</li><li>Unit tests for the plain JSON items and the util. Mirage: the <code>/bulk</code> handler answers overview GETs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> the widget shows the same overviews with one <code>POST /bulk</code> per load or load more, and no <code>GET /milestoneoverview</code> calls. A failed overview shows as today (null).</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> non-GET plain items.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4595</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simpl