0121d4d06ae5-b903-1173-3f6137cc76f0	Issue statuses: accept any hex colour, not only the fixed palette	2026-10-30 22:11:13	2026-10-30 22:42:18	0	<p>Users should be able to give an issue status any colour they choose. Today <code>IssuestatusController::rejectInvalidAttributes()</code> returns 422 unless <code>color</code> is one of the 5 values in <code>IssuestatusController::COLORS</code>.</p>\n<h4>Changes</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Accept any valid 6-digit hex colour <code>#rrggbb</code> (case-insensitive) for <code>color</code> on create and update, stored lowercase. <code>null</code> stays allowed.</li>\n<li>Reject anything else with 422 and a clear message, e.g. <code>red</code>, <code>#fff</code>, <code>#12345g</code>, <code>url(...)</code>, values longer than 7 characters.</li>\n<li>The <code>color</code> column is already <code>varchar(7)</code>, so no migration is needed. Keep the existing palette values only where they are still used as defaults or seeds; remove <code>COLORS</code> if nothing else needs it.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Tests</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>PHPUnit and api-tester cases: a custom hex (e.g. <code>#1A2B3C</code>) saves and is returned as <code>#1a2b3c</code>; the invalid values above return 422; <code>null</code> is still accepted.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4209	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	92ae09c66ace-1e5c-2b63-d1da9630092c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Odysseus	Rana Nouman	e9aa3fb56ae5-8a27-d0d9-dd661cef6b10	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 22:42:15	agaia	0	0
c8c77f626af3-1487-2734-afd448ec857b	Replace ember-export-application-global and the Prometheus.__container__ lookups with getOwner	2026-11-10 21:34:00	2026-11-11 17:05:38	0	<p><code>ember-export-application-global</code> calls <code>Ember.String.classify</code>, which no longer exists on Ember 5+. In the spike it threw <code>Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'classify')</code> during startup, so every test failed.</p><p>The app relies on the global it creates:</p><ul><li><code>app/components/field-view.js:37</code>: <code>Prometheus.__container__.lookup('template:…')</code></li><li><code>app/components/form-fields.js:223-228</code>: <code>Prometheus.__container__</code> / <code>Prometheus._applicationInstances</code></li></ul><p>Replace these with <code>getOwner(this).lookup(…)</code> from <code>@ember/owner</code> (<code>@ember/application</code> on 4.1), then remove the add-on. Check that no Mirage or test code reads <code>window.Prometheus</code>.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4481	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	248b5a046af4-c475-725c-539156d65053	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 17:05:38	aprom	0	0
d354e1346af3-1487-2734-a23045595d6e	Move the Prometheus images to Node 22	2026-11-10 21:34:11	2026-11-11 19:30:52	0	<p>The Prometheus dev and test containers run Node 16.13 on Debian buster. ember-cli 6.x needs Node 20+; the spike used Node 22 with Chromium on bookworm.</p><ul><li>Update the base image (<code>docker/dev</code>, <code>docker/qa</code>, the root <code>Dockerfile</code> / the <code>rananoman/prometheus</code> base) to Node 22 on bookworm, with headless Chrome or Chromium for testem.</li><li>Update <code>engines</code> in <code>package.json</code>.</li><li>Check that the current Ember 4.1 / ember-cli 4.1 build and the full suite still pass on Node 22 (unverified), and that <code>p4m test ember</code> and <code>ai test prometheus</code> still work.</li></ul><p>Doing this before the Ember upgrade separates runtime breakage from framework breakage.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4482	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	07043ec96af4-42bf-35cc-10d75656939b	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 19:30:52	aprom	0	0
203eca776ae5-0b6a-881c-ec25914ea33d	Agamemnon keeps agent PRs mergeable: update behind branches, Odysseus resolves conflicts	2026-10-30 22:54:24	2026-10-30 23:59:12	0	<p>Several issues can change the same files. Once one PR merges, another open agent PR can fall behind <code>dev</code> or conflict with it. Agamemnon detects this, and Odysseus resolves it, so the pipeline keeps moving.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> #4211, #4212</p><h4>Detect</h4><p>When an issue in the worker's projects becomes <code>done</code>, which covers merges by the reviewer too, and on every sweep, Agamemnon reads GitHub's mergeable state for the other open agent PRs (<code>claude-issue-N</code>) in that repo.</p><h4>Behind, no conflict</h4><p>Update the branch through GitHub as Agamemnon. This merges dev into the branch, in line with the team's rule against rebasing. The new head commit then goes through CI and CodeRabbit again; if the issue is waiting in the CodeRabbit loop, it waits again.</p><h4>Real conflict (dirty)</h4><ul><li>Hand the issue to Odysseus with a new reason code, <code>merge_conflict</code>, plus a comment naming the PR or issue merged into dev that caused it.</li><li>A new Odysseus action and prompt for this:<ol><li>check out <code>claude-issue-N</code> and merge <code>origin/dev</code>;</li><li>resolve the conflicts so both changes survive, reading the other issue and PR;</li><li>run the full suite and push;</li><li>end with <code>awaiting_bot_review</code>, so the PR goes through CodeRabbit again.</li></ol></li><li>One attempt per issue (<code>maxConflictAttempts</code>, default 1). After that, or if the tests fail, the issue goes to the reviewer with the reason.</li><li>The run counts toward <code>maxIterations</code>.</li></ul><h4>Rules</h4><ul><li>Never update or touch a branch a human is working on, i.e. one checked out outside the Talos <code>.runs</code> folders.</li><li>Never merge a conflict resolution until CodeRabbit and CI pass again on the new commit.</li></ul><h4>Tests</h4><p>Classifying the mergeable states, the update-branch call, the handoff with reason, the attempt limit, and skipping branches held by a human.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4214	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	fb9764e06ae5-9703-881c-050eefa94e43	\N	a0d690f56ad7-404c-ce18-27bd5d2a1517	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	3994f2796ae5-10a5-de15-47caf5ff13f2	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 23:59:13	adt	0	0
4ce4d4906af4-5ff4-ad59-10f8e1ebd67e	Replace the small helper addons, ember-moment and ember-lodash with app code	2026-11-11 19:47:24	2026-11-11 21:08:46	0	<p>Part of reducing addons before the Ember upgrade. Nothing in JavaScript imports these addons (apart from <code>helpers/moment-format.js</code>). Helpers with the same names in <code>app/helpers/</code> take over automatically, so <strong>no template changes</strong>. Usage counts are from dev <code>c19e054d</code>.</p>\n<h4>Add app helpers (each with unit tests)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>ember-math-helpers:</strong> <code>add</code> ×25, <code>sub</code> ×24, <code>mult</code> ×24. Each takes any number of arguments, like the addon.</li>\n<li><strong>ember-composable-helpers:</strong> <code>find-by</code> ×39, <code>call</code> ×23, <code>includes</code> ×6, <code>join</code> ×4, <code>inc</code> ×3, <code>slice</code>, <code>queue</code>, <code>optional</code>, <code>keys</code> (×2 each) and <code>noop</code> ×1. Keep the addon's argument order and behaviour. <code>find-by</code> and <code>includes</code> must work on Ember Data record arrays and proxies as well as plain arrays, so test both. <code>(array)</code> is built into Ember and is not part of this.</li>\n<li><strong>ember-cli-string-helpers:</strong> <code>lowercase</code> ×9, <code>dasherize</code> ×2 (use <code>@ember/string</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>ember-moment:</strong>\n  <ul>\n  <li>rewrite <code>helpers/moment-format.js</code> on <code>moment</code> directly (it currently extends ember-moment's class), keeping <code>'-'</code> for empty values;</li>\n  <li>add <code>moment-from-now</code>, used once in <code>templates/app/agent/tools.hbs</code>;</li>\n  <li>moment and moment-timezone stay for now.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Use <code>helper()</code> from <code>@ember/component/helper</code> (or a class Helper) so they work on Ember 4.1 and 6.x. Plain functions as helpers need Ember 4.5 or later.</p>\n<h4>Remove</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><code>ember-math-helpers</code>, <code>ember-composable-helpers</code>, <code>ember-cli-string-helpers</code>, <code>ember-moment</code>.</li>\n<li><code>ember-lodash</code>, which is unused: all 20 files use <code>import _ from 'lodash'</code>, and <code>lodash</code> is already a direct dependency (resolved by ember-auto-import).</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Check</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Full <code>ai test prometheus</code> passes.</li>\n<li>The build contains no modules from the removed addons.</li>\n<li>In the browser: a list or board using <code>find-by</code>/<code>call</code>, a date shown with <code>moment-format</code>, and the agent tools page.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Goes first: aprom-4505 and aprom-4507 build on the rewritten <code>moment-format</code>. Series: 4504 → 4505 and 4506 (in parallel) → 4507.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4504	2026-11-19	2026-11-12	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	47204d066af4-9b63-d758-88d8a4078ae0	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 21:08:46	aprom	0	0
fcc441086ae5-9703-881c-40173eed6014	Agent Agamemnon GitHub identity: agamemnon wrapper for gh	2026-10-30 22:53:48	2026-10-30 23:07:20	0	<p>Agent Agamemnon will approve and merge agent PRs. It needs its own GitHub identity, so the agent that writes the code (Odysseus) is never the one that accepts it. <code>dev</code> requires an approving review, and GitHub doesn't let a PR's author approve their own PR.</p><ul><li>GitHub account <code>agent-agamemnon</code>, a maintainer on the repos. It uses a fine-grained token in <code>dev-tools/agamemnon/agamemnon.env</code> (<code>GH_TOKEN=…</code>), which is git-ignored.</li><li><code>dev-tools/agamemnon/agamemnon</code> and <code>agamemnon.cmd</code>: run <code>gh</code> with that token, mirroring <code>odysseus/odysseus</code>, including the hand-over to the runtime copy. There is no git subcommand: Agamemnon never commits.</li><li>An <code>agamemnon.env.example</code> file, a README, and a <code>.gitignore</code> entry.</li><li><code>talos check</code> confirms the token works and has write access to the repos the worker uses.</li><li>Not part of <code>p4m configure</code>: the token file is placed by hand.</li></ul><p>Works on Windows and Linux.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4211	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	fb9764e06ae5-9703-881c-050eefa94e43	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	8945b9456ae5-91af-5d2e-1f131a5e6481	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 23:07:20	adt	0	0
5fa94a606af4-5ff4-ad59-a4862a63cfbc	Date utility module (still on moment) and move all moment calls onto it	2026-11-11 19:47:43	2026-11-11 22:28:36	0	<p>Depends on aprom-4504. Step 1 of replacing moment. All date handling moves behind one module, with tests that pin today's behaviour. Afterwards moment is used in exactly one file, so aprom issue 4 can swap the implementation without touching callers.</p>\n<h4>The module</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><code>app/utils/date.js</code>, a small, named API covering what the app uses. Today that is 98 moment calls in 33 files:\n  <ul>\n  <li>parse, with Gaia timestamps <code>YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss</code> treated as UTC, and date-only <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code> as a local calendar date;</li>\n  <li>format, supporting the tokens in use (<code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>, <code>YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss</code>, <code>YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss.0</code>, <code>MMM DD, YYYY</code>, <code>MMM DD</code>, <code>DD MMMM YYYY</code>, <code>DD MMM</code>, <code>DD-MM</code>, <code>ddd</code>, <code>MMM</code>, <code>YYYY</code>, <code>DD</code>, <code>HH:mm</code>, <code>Z</code>);</li>\n  <li>add and subtract;</li>\n  <li><code>startOf</code> and <code>endOf</code> (day, week, isoWeek, month, year);</li>\n  <li>isBefore, isAfter, isSame and diff;</li>\n  <li>isValid and toISOString;</li>\n  <li>relative time ("from now") and duration humanize;</li>\n  <li>timezones: <code>toUserTimezone(date, zone)</code>, <code>guessTimezone()</code>, and <code>timezoneList()</code> with offset and abbreviation, as used by <code>user/create/timezones.js</code>.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n<li>Implement it on moment and moment-timezone for now.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Tests (the contract for the native version)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Unit tests for every function. Cover:\n  <ul>\n  <li>UTC timestamps from Gaia shown in a user timezone ahead of UTC and one behind it;</li>\n  <li>date-only values not shifting a day;</li>\n  <li>month-end arithmetic (Jan 31 + 1 month);</li>\n  <li>DST boundaries;</li>\n  <li>week start;</li>\n  <li>invalid input.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n<li>The tests must not depend on the machine's timezone: pass the zone explicitly.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Move callers</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Every <code>moment(</code>, <code>moment.utc</code> and <code>moment.tz</code> call in <code>app/</code> uses <code>utils/date</code>. That includes <code>helpers/moment-format.js</code>, <code>helpers/format-date-time.js</code>, <code>format-date.js</code>, <code>get-humanized-date.js</code>, the activity blocks, <code>controllers/app.js</code>, <code>controllers/app/user/page.js</code>, <code>models/user.js</code> and <code>user/create/timezones.js</code>.</li>\n<li>Do not touch the date picker (<code>modifiers/date-picker.js</code>, the <code>field-date</code> components). aprom issue 3 replaces them in parallel.</li>\n<li>Done when moment is used only in <code>utils/date.js</code> and the date-picker files (grep it).</li>\n<li>Full test run passes. The 10 test files that use moment may keep it for building fixtures, or move to <code>utils/date</code>.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4505	2026-11-19	2026-11-12	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	c9ad20156af4-e8ff-cdb9-845e217af184	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 22:28:37	aprom	0	0
