734dce066af4-5ff4-ad59-f588dfad21c1	Replace bootstrap-daterangepicker with the native date input	2026-11-11 19:48:03	2026-11-11 23:00:59	0	<p>Independent of aprom-4505, and can run alongside it. Step 2 of replacing moment: <code>bootstrap-daterangepicker</code> needs both moment and jQuery, so it must go first. Decision: use the browser's built-in date input to reduce dependencies. Keep the current field box styling where possible. A native calendar pop-up that looks different from today's is accepted.</p>\n<h4>Current use</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>21 <code>FormFields::FieldDate</code> call sites, all single dates (<code>@singleDatePicker={{true}}</code>), none using ranges or <code>timePicker</code>. They go through <code>modifiers/date-picker.js</code> in <code>components/form-fields/field-date.hbs</code>.</li>\n<li>19 call sites use <code>@format="YYYY-MM-DD"</code> (or <code>this.dateFormat</code> in <code>ez-search/value-editor.hbs</code>; check its values).</li>\n<li>2 call sites use <code>@format="DD-MM"</code>: the birthday fields in <code>templates/app/user/create.hbs</code> and <code>templates/app/user/page.hbs</code>.</li>\n<li>Old users of <code>daterangepicker</code>: <code>components/field-date.js</code>, <code>field-view.js</code>, <code>form-fields.js</code>. Check whether they are still used; delete them if dead.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Change</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><code>FieldDate</code> renders <code>&lt;input type="date"&gt;</code> and keeps its arguments, so call sites don't change:\n  <ul>\n  <li><code>@value</code>, <code>@update</code> (still called with a <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code> string);</li>\n  <li><code>@minDate</code>/<code>@maxDate</code>, mapped to <code>min</code>/<code>max</code>;</li>\n  <li><code>@placeholder</code>, <code>@disabled</code>, the label, validation and the <code>data-field</code> attributes.</li>\n  </ul>\n  Ignore picker-only arguments (<code>@showDropdowns</code>, <code>@positionX/Y</code>, <code>@autoApply</code>, <code>@parentEl</code>, <code>@timePicker*</code>, <code>@maxSpan</code>, <code>@minYear/@maxYear</code>), and list them in the PR.</li>\n<li><strong>DD-MM (a birthday with no year):</strong> two native <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> elements (day 1–31, month names from the intl service), styled like the other fields. <code>@update</code> is still called with <code>DD-MM</code>. Invalid combinations such as 31-02 are not allowed.</li>\n<li><strong>Styling:</strong> the input keeps the current box (border, height, padding, floating label, square edges, per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>). Style the calendar icon where the browser allows (<code>::-webkit-calendar-picker-indicator</code>). The pop-up itself is the browser's.</li>\n<li>Remove:\n  <ul>\n  <li><code>modifiers/date-picker.js</code>;</li>\n  <li>the <code>app.import</code> of <code>bootstrap-daterangepicker</code> in <code>ember-cli-build.js</code>;</li>\n  <li>the <code>bootstrap-daterangepicker</code> package;</li>\n  <li>its styles in <code>styles/app.scss</code> and <code>styles/modules/user.scss</code>.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n<li>Update the acceptance steps and tests that drive the old picker so they use <code>fillIn</code> on the input.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Check</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Full test run passes.</li>\n<li>In the browser, with screenshots before and after in the PR:\n  <ul>\n  <li>issue create (start/end dates), the issue details inline dates, project create, the milestone dates on the task board, the ez-search date filter, and the user birthday;</li>\n  <li>keyboard entry, clearing a value, and min/max enforcement.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Don't touch <code>utils/date.js</code> or the moment callers (aprom-4505).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4506	2026-11-19	2026-11-12	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	dc6c9bc16af4-7f78-21d6-8c2253c7c9c5	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 23:00:59	aprom	0	0
0206e1a46ae5-0b6a-881c-cc6a254236e7	ai mergecheck / ai merge: deterministic merge gate for agent PRs	2026-10-30 22:53:54	2026-10-30 23:07:21	0	<p>A fixed merge check, run on a PR's current head commit, for Agent Agamemnon's automatic merges. It uses no LLM.</p><h4><code>ai mergecheck &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt; [--json]</code></h4><p>Pass or fail, with a reason for each check:</p><ul><li>CodeRabbit: <code>ai rabbit</code> classifies the head commit as <code>clean</code>, with no open CodeRabbit threads;</li><li>CI: every check run and commit status on the head commit has succeeded, and none is still pending;</li><li>tests: the PR body has the passing result that <code>ai ship</code> recorded;</li><li>mergeable: GitHub's mergeable state is clean (not dirty or behind);</li><li>no human review asking for changes, and no human comments left unanswered since the latest commit;</li><li>no <code>do-not-merge</code> label.</li></ul><h4><code>ai merge &lt;repo&gt; &lt;pr&gt;</code></h4><p>Runs the check again, then as Agent Agamemnon (through the <code>agamemnon</code> wrapper):</p><ol><li>approves the PR;</li><li>merges it the same way the reviewer does (a merge commit);</li><li>prints the merge commit.</li></ol><p>If any check fails, it refuses with a non-zero exit code.</p><p>Tests use fake GitHub API responses.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> none</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4212	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	fb9764e06ae5-9703-881c-050eefa94e43	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	a1b39a806ae5-22ef-5d2e-99876f252830	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 23:07:21	adt	0	0
849bb9996af4-5ff4-ad59-56af554cb5ba	Switch the date module to native Intl and remove moment and moment-timezone	2026-11-11 19:48:20	2026-11-11 23:48:02	0	<p>Depends on aprom-4505 (the date module and its tests) and aprom-4506 (the date picker no longer needs moment). This is the final step of replacing moment.</p>\n<h4>Change</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Re-implement <code>app/utils/date.js</code> with no libraries:\n  <ul>\n  <li><code>Date</code>, <code>Intl.DateTimeFormat</code> (with <code>timeZone</code> and <code>formatToParts</code>), <code>Intl.RelativeTimeFormat</code> and <code>Intl.NumberFormat</code>;</li>\n  <li>a strict parser for Gaia's <code>YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss</code> (UTC) and for date-only <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>. Never rely on <code>new Date(string)</code>: date-only strings are read as UTC and shift a day in timezones behind UTC;</li>\n  <li>timezone conversion through <code>formatToParts</code>;</li>\n  <li><code>guessTimezone()</code> from <code>Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone</code>;</li>\n  <li>offsets and abbreviations through <code>timeZoneName: 'shortOffset'</code> / <code>'short'</code>;</li>\n  <li>month and day names from <code>Intl</code> in the user's locale.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n<li>All aprom-4505 tests must pass unchanged. Add tests only for behaviour that moment didn't define.</li>\n<li><strong>Timezone list:</strong> <code>Intl.supportedValuesOf('timeZone')</code> needs Chrome 99, but the test runner is Chrome 97. Either upgrade Chrome in the Prometheus test image (preferred, and the image is shared with CI), or bundle a static IANA zone list as a fallback. Record the choice in the PR. Existing saved user timezones must still match the list.</li>\n<li>Remove <code>moment</code> and <code>moment-timezone</code>: the packages, and their <code>app.import</code> lines in <code>ember-cli-build.js</code>. Also remove <code>fullcalendar</code> and <code>fullcalendar-scheduler</code>, which are unused (only a commented-out import remains) and depend on moment. Rename <code>helpers/moment-format.js</code> to something library-neutral, keeping an alias only if that is needed to avoid touching its 19 call sites.</li>\n<li>Test files that used moment for fixtures switch to <code>utils/date</code> or plain strings.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Verification (results in the PR)</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Full test run passes.</li>\n<li>A production build with no moment or moment-timezone code. Compare the bundle size with dev from before the change; the full timezone data should be the bulk of the saving.</li>\n<li>In the browser, with the user timezone set to one ahead of UTC (e.g. Asia/Karachi) and one behind it (e.g. America/New_York):\n  <ul>\n  <li>activity times and the "time ago" text;</li>\n  <li>issue start/end dates (no shift of a day);</li>\n  <li>the task board and milestone dates;</li>\n  <li>the timezone picker list on the user page;</li>\n  <li>the birthday field.</li>\n  </ul></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Rollback:</strong> revert this PR; <code>utils/date.js</code> goes back to running on moment and callers are unaffected.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4507	2026-11-19	2026-11-12	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	361209516af4-cabf-ef36-e61b05d44469	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-11 23:48:02	aprom	0	0
1ae631246ae5-0b6a-881c-9c0c68eeb157	Agamemnon auto-merges CodeRabbit-clean PRs in autoMergeMilestones (aga-v1)	2026-10-30 22:54:18	2026-10-30 23:22:46	0	<p>An experiment: when CodeRabbit is satisfied with an agent PR, Agamemnon merges it instead of the reviewer. This only applies to issues in milestones listed in Agamemnon's <code>autoMergeMilestones</code> (<code>["aga-v1"]</code>). Every other issue still goes to the reviewer.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> #4211, #4212</p><h4>Flow</h4><ul><li><strong>Routing:</strong> when the Talos CodeRabbit loop (<code>lib/bot_review.py</code>) reaches <code>clean</code> on an issue in <code>autoMergeMilestones</code>, it hands the issue to Agamemnon's Gaia user (in_review) instead of the reviewer. <code>paused</code>, <code>absent</code>, a timeout or the round limit still go to the reviewer.</li><li><strong>Merge:</strong> Agamemnon (<code>lib/orchestrator</code>) sweeps in_review issues assigned to itself, finds the PR from the issue or the bot-review record, and runs <code>ai merge</code>. On success it:<ul><li>sets the issue to <code>done</code>;</li><li>comments that it merged automatically after CodeRabbit was clean, with the round count and a link to the merge commit;</li><li>logs the time. Setting <code>done</code> frees the issues that depend on it.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Gate fails:</strong> hand the issue to the reviewer (in_review) with a comment listing the checks that failed. CI or CodeRabbit still pending means waiting until the next sweep, up to a deadline.</li><li><strong>Limits:</strong><ul><li>the existing limits still apply (<code>botReviewRounds</code>, <code>maxIterations</code>);</li><li>a new <code>maxAutoMergesPerDay</code> (default 5); once it is reached, the issue goes to the reviewer;</li><li>pause and the circuit breaker stop merging as well.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Audit:</strong> <code>talos status</code> lists today's automatic merges, and they are recorded in talos.db.</li></ul><h4>Tests</h4><p>Routing (in scope or not; clean versus the other verdicts), gate pass and fail, the daily limit, pause, and a dry run.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4213	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	fb9764e06ae5-9703-881c-050eefa94e43	\N	a0d690f56ad7-404c-ce18-27bd5d2a1517	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	4c6022286ae5-d515-4220-8226db5fbc84	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-30 23:22:46	adt	0	0
d661c0356af0-cd0b-cccd-57975d86bff9	External Request: Ingest: timing-safe secret check and no default secret outside local dev	2026-11-08 20:38:46	2026-11-08 20:45:25	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Inter application Communication", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Gaia publishes to <code>POST /publish</code> with a shared secret (<code>X-Hermes-Secret</code>). The check in <code>src/http/middleware/require-secret.js</code> uses <code>!==</code> (not timing-safe), and <code>src/config.js</code> falls back to <code>hermes-dev-secret</code> in every non-production environment. This hardens the secret until Hermes gets a service identity (later issues in this milestone).</p><ul><li>Compare the secret with <code>crypto.timingSafeEqual</code> on equal-length buffers (different lengths = reject without leaking timing).</li><li><code>config.js</code>: use the dev default only when <code>NODE_ENV</code> is <code>development</code> or <code>test</code>; any other value without <code>HERMES_SECRET</code> fails at startup with a clear message. Also refuse to start with <code>HERMES_SECRET=hermes-dev-secret</code> outside development/test.</li><li>Never log the secret; ADR entry in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests for wrong, missing, different-length and correct secrets; startup tests for each NODE_ENV case. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing the shared secret.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4383	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	high	861790376ad5-1449-a602-a25bd5e6e2b8	d59707896af0-cd0b-cccd-6c0c771196c7	\N	87099ee46ad5-1449-a602-5f7a1f6605b7	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	f70813296af0-cd0b-cccd-3d135293c269	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 20:45:25	ah	0	0
e9d802696af3-1487-2734-e8cddc52676c	Upgrade the remaining add-ons as far as Ember 4.x allows	2026-11-10 21:34:33	2026-11-12 07:59:48	0	<p>Reduce the jump at upgrade time by moving add-ons to the newest majors that still support Ember 4.1. Ember 6.12 targets from the spike:</p><ul><li>ember-power-select 4.1 / ember-basic-dropdown 3.1 → 9. v9 removed <code>&lt;PowerSelectMultiple&gt;</code> (7 files); see whether an intermediate major already offers the replacement.</li><li>ember-file-upload 6 → 10. v10 moved <code>UploadFile</code>, <code>FileSource</code> and the Mirage <code>upload</code> handler (now <code>uploadHandler</code>) to the package root; affects <code>services/image-upload.js</code> and <code>mirage/route-handlers/upload.js</code>. It needs <code>tracked-built-ins</code> as a peer dependency.</li><li>ember-modifier 3 → 4, ember-truth-helpers 3 → 5, ember-composable-helpers 4 → 5, ember-math-helpers 2 → 5, ember-cli-string-helpers 6 → 8, ember-page-title 7 → 9, ember-resolver 8 → 13, ember-load-initializers 2 → 3, ember-cli-app-version 5 → 7, ember-cli-htmlbars 6 → 7, ember-cli-babel 7 → 8.</li><li>ember-moment 10 → 11. Relative-date text changes ("N days ago") broke 8 assertions in the spike; review it or replace the helpers.</li></ul><p>Out of scope: ember-simple-auth and ember-intl, which are being removed separately.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4484	2026-11-18	2026-11-11	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	1f17d2b76af5-e408-db66-65bc82aa0a0b	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-12 07:59:48	aprom	0	0
291c5db76afa-79f5-7528-70768a21d82e	Gantt: load all milestone lanes in one bulk request	2026-11-16 09:55:53	2026-11-16 10:28:35	0	<p>The Gantt route loads the active milestones and then one issue query per milestone (<code>app/routes/app/project/gantt.js</code> ~l.90-124), the same pattern the Task Board had (aprom-4596). Use the bulk service (aprom-4595) for the per-milestone queries.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Keep the milestones query (it decides the lanes). Then send one <code>bulk.query</code> with one item per milestone: the same query string (including the ezSearch <code>searchQuery</code> AND), rels and limit as today. Then <code>replaceRecords(milestone.issues, records)</code>.</li><li>A failed lane goes through <code>errorManager.handleError</code> and stays empty. Timeline bounds and <code>loadSearchData</code> (~l.152) stay unchanged.</li><li>Extend <code>tests/acceptance/gantt/gantt-search.feature</code> (or a Gantt render feature) to run through the Mirage <code>/bulk</code> handler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> opening the Gantt chart makes one milestones GET and one <code>POST /bulk</code>, and no per-milestone <code>GET /issue</code>. Lanes, search and the timeline behave as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the controller's reloads and Hermes refreshes.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4595</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4600	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	288725f16afa-8715-b3ee-7096f921e57d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 10:28:35	aprom	0	0
1b9ff1156af5-4088-65e3-311e27a141ac	Project dashboard: page the Project Milestones box from the server (ListLoader + QuickList pagination footer)	2026-11-12 09:25:47	2026-11-16 09:28:56	0	<p>aprom-4493 paginated the Project Milestones box on the project dashboard in the browser only: the route still loads every milestone (<code>limit: -1</code>) and the controller slices the list. Make it real lazy loading: each page is its own request of 5 milestones. Use the ideas browser pattern (<code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code> with <code>utils/state/list-loader.js</code>, footer pager <code>QuickList::Pagination</code>).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Box data</strong>: in <code>controllers/app/project/index.js</code>, add a <code>ListLoader</code> for <code>milestone</code> (page size 5). Its request is <code>(Milestone.projectId : &lt;id&gt;)</code>, sort <code>Milestone.startDate</code> DESC, <code>page</code>. Keep the page in a tracked controller property, not a query param, and reset it to 1 in the route's <code>setupController</code>. <code>hasNext</code>, the loading flag and the error come from the loader. A page that fails to load shows the error with a retry, as the QuickList does.</li><li><strong>Issue counts per row</strong>: after each page loads, attach to its milestones the matching issues from the issues the route already loads (<code>issuetime</code>, filter by <code>milestoneId</code>), as <code>loadMilestones</code> in <code>routes/app/project/index.js</code> does today. Keep the <code>willTransition</code> unload working.</li><li><strong>Footer</strong>: in <code>templates/app/project/index.hbs</code> (~368), render the current page's <code>Project::Milestones</code> rows in the <code>box-body</code>. Put <code>&lt;QuickList::Pagination @page @limit @hasNext @count @disabled={{isLoading}} @onPage&gt;</code> in a <code>box-footer</code> of the box, unchanged, so it reads <code>1-5 / 5+</code> while there is a next page and <code>6-9 / 9</code> on the last. It hides itself when there is only one page. Keep the <code>Exceptions::NothingFound</code> empty state.</li><li><strong>Remove the aprom-4493 client paging</strong>: <code>milestonesPageSize</code>, <code>milestonesPage</code>, <code>visibleMilestones</code>, the range getters, the previous/next actions (~244-372), the inline pager markup and its <code>pageRange</code> translation if nothing else uses it.</li><li><strong>Chart filter</strong>: the estimated-vs-spent milestone dropdown still lists all milestones. The route's all-milestones query becomes a light one (<code>fields: 'Milestone.id,Milestone.name,Milestone.dateCreated'</code>, <code>limit: -1</code>, as in <code>utils/state/thread-votes.js</code>) used only for <code>estimatedSpentMilestoneOptions</code> and the default selection. <code>estimatedSpentChartIssues</code> filters <code>issuetime</code> by <code>milestoneId</code> instead of reading <code>milestone.issues</code>.</li><li><strong>Adding a milestone</strong> (<code>saveMilestone</code>): reload page 1 of the box instead of <code>pushObject</code> into the full list, and add it to the chart options. Editing keeps the current page.</li><li>Mirage: make the milestone handler page with <code>meta.links.next</code> like the idea handler (<code>mirage/helpers/paginate.js</code>), if it doesn't already.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>With 9 milestones, opening the dashboard requests only 5 for the box (<code>limit: 5</code>). The footer shows <code>1-5 / 5+</code>, ‹ is disabled, and › requests page 2 and shows <code>6-9 / 9</code> with › disabled.</li><li>With 5 or fewer milestones there is no pager. With none, the empty state shows.</li><li>Each row's issue count and progress match today's values. The edit pencil and the milestone links work on every page.</li><li>The estimated-vs-spent dropdown still lists every milestone, and the chart shows the selected milestone's issues.</li><li>Adding a milestone shows page 1 again with the new milestone counted. A failed page load shows the error and retry, and the arrows are disabled while a page loads.</li><li>Tests: acceptance or integration tests on Mirage covering the first page request, next and last page, no pager at ≤5, the chart dropdown with more than 5 milestones, and a failed page load. Each test fails if its line is reverted.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: no longer loading every issue on the dashboard (totals, charts and counts still use it), server-side issue counts per milestone, and a page-size selector.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> milestones-paginated.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4508	2026-11-19	2026-11-12	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	b43cc5046ae8-20b5-32a1-13b222266c79	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	d0c5db516af5-e4dd-65e3-bd732d0f2fca	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 09:28:56	aprom	0	0
1996d0a56af5-e861-033c-de7201e7272a	Prometheus test containers: own image and node_modules per checkout, keyed on Dockerfile and package.json	2026-11-12 13:37:29	2026-11-12 14:07:50	0	<p><b>Problem.</b> <code>p4m test ember</code> and <code>ai test prometheus</code> run in containers (<code>installer/testenv.py</code>, <code>PrometheusTestContainer.ensure</code>) that borrow the dev stack's image (<code>prometheus-dev</code>'s or <code>prometheus:latest</code>) and its shared <code>prometheus_prometheus_node_modules</code> volume. Both come from the <code>Pr4M/prometheus</code> checkout, not from the checkout under test:</p><ul><li><code>p4m.ensure_prometheus_deps</code> reinstalls the volume only when <code>Pr4M/prometheus/package.json</code> changes. If that checkout is behind <code>dev</code> (repo sync skips it when it has uncommitted changes), every run gets old packages.</li><li>The image is built from that same checkout. Locally it is Node 16 / npm 8.1.2, while <code>dev</code>'s Dockerfile and CI are on Node 22. npm 8.1 ignores the <code>overrides</code> block in <code>package.json</code>, so <code>@ember/test-waiters</code> resolved to 3.x, <code>ember-file-upload</code> failed to load, and every page with an upload field failed ("Attempted to load a helper, but there wasn't a helper manager").</li><li>Every dependency change blocks agent runs. aprom-4483 shipped with <code>--no-tests</code>, and aprom-4505 was blocked until the volume was reinstalled by hand with npm 9.</li></ul><p><b>Scope</b></p><ul><li><b>Image:</b> the test container uses an image built from the checkout's own <code>Dockerfile</code>, tagged by its hash (e.g. <code>p4m-test-prometheus:&lt;dockerfile-hash&gt;</code>). It is built when missing and reused otherwise.</li><li><b>Dependencies:</b> one <code>node_modules</code> volume per <code>package.json</code> (+ lockfile, if any) hash, e.g. <code>p4m-test-prometheus-nm-&lt;hash&gt;</code>. It is installed once with that image's npm (<code>npm install --no-audit --no-fund</code>) and shared by checkouts with the same hash. Hold a lock during install so parallel runs on the same hash don't install at the same time.</li><li>Test runs never write to the dev stack's <code>prometheus_prometheus_node_modules</code> volume.</li><li><code>talos gc</code> / <code>p4m</code> remove test images and volumes that no checkout or container uses any more.</li><li>Document the manual workaround's retirement: no more <code>npx npm@9 install</code> in the shared volume.</li></ul><p><b>Done when:</b></p><ul><li>a branch that changes <code>package.json</code> or the <code>Dockerfile</code> passes <code>ai test prometheus</code> with no manual step;</li><li>two parallel runs with different <code>package.json</code> don't affect each other or the dev stack;</li><li>unit tests cover the hash keys, reuse, rebuild-on-change and the lock.</li></ul><p><b>Related (out of scope, worth a separate issue):</b></p><ul><li>Talos <code>workspaces.remove()</code> can delete another run's git worktree entry when names are reused (aprom-4505 lost <code>prometheus14</code> when the #4483 workspace was collected).</li><li><code>ensure()</code> only checks that <code>.git</code> exists, not that the worktree works.</li></ul><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4509	2026-11-19	2026-11-12	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	7b96fd466af5-85c1-a035-6a4f61e98c0a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-12 14:07:50	adt	0	0
1d9a62b46af5-f84a-d19d-5c84b758bc40	External Request: Uploads: return fileThumbnail as a data URI on upload reads, not the raw 0/1 flag	2026-11-12 14:45:49	2026-11-12 15:24:09	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Prometheus (idea "Thumbnail of image broke", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p><strong>Request from A Prometheus.</strong> On the issue detail page, clicking an attachment opens the preview modal (<code>Issue::FilePreview</code>). The modal fetches a one-time token with <code>GET /api/v1/upload/:id?download=true</code>. Ember Data merges that response into the same <code>upload</code> record the attachment list uses. The response has <code>fileThumbnail: "1"</code> (the raw DB flag), not the base64 data URI the issue read returned. So after the modal closes, the thumbnail renders as <code>&lt;img src="1"&gt;</code> and shows as a broken image. Prometheus needs <code>fileThumbnail</code> to mean the same thing on every read.</p><p><strong>Cause:</strong> <code>FilethumbComponent::afterRead</code> (<code>app/api/v1/controllers/components/FilethumbComponent.php</code>) only converts upload entries in <code>finalData['included']</code>. <code>IssueController</code> and <code>WikiController</code> use it, but <code>UploadController</code> (<code>$uses = ['Fileattachment']</code>, custom <code>getAction</code>/<code>listAction</code>) does not. Its reads return the smallint flag.</p><p><strong>Proposed change</strong> (please accept, adapt or decline):</p><ul><li>Extend <code>FilethumbComponent::afterRead</code> so it also converts <code>type == 'upload'</code> entries in <code>finalData['data']</code>, handling both a list and a single resource. Move the conversion into one private method shared by <code>data</code> and <code>included</code>.</li><li>Add <code>'Filethumb'</code> to <code>UploadController::$uses</code>. Check that <code>getAction</code> and <code>listAction</code> fire <code>rest:afterRead</code> after <code>finalData</code> is built (<code>getAction</code> does; verify <code>listAction</code>). The <code>downloadLink</code> attribute must still be returned.</li><li>If the thumbnail file under <code>filesystem/uploads/thumbnail/thumb_&lt;id&gt;.jpg</code> is missing or unreadable, return <code>"0"</code> (the value the UI already reads as "no thumbnail") instead of a data URI of an empty string. Apply the same rule to issue and wiki reads.</li><li>Keep the <code>"0"</code>/null behaviour for uploads without a thumbnail.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li><code>GET /upload/:id</code> and <code>GET /upload/:id?download=true</code> for an image with a thumbnail return <code>fileThumbnail</code> starting with <code>data:</code>, identical to the value in the issue read's <code>included</code>.</li><li><code>GET /upload</code> (list) does the same for every upload with a thumbnail.</li><li>Uploads without a thumbnail, or whose thumbnail file is missing, return <code>"0"</code>.</li><li>Issue and wiki reads are unchanged except for the missing-file case.</li><li>A test (api-tester case and/or unit test) fails before the fix and passes after. gaia-dev graph and generated docs are refreshed (the <code>uses</code> list of <code>upload</code> changes).</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> replacing the flag/data-URI field with a thumbnail URL endpoint, and any Prometheus changes.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4510	2026-11-19	2026-11-12	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	5f5bbdf46aec-f3eb-ed75-4f1de682f8f8	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	c43083506af5-f84a-d19d-ae7f6f563693	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-12 15:24:09	agaia	0	0
30e9f7366afa-5450-9afe-ee132e7883f4	AppUi::Avatar: initials on a stable per-user generated background when there is no image	2026-11-16 10:17:20	2026-11-16 10:57:23	0	<p>Change request on <code>AppUi::Avatar</code> (built in aprom-4588: sizes xs/s/m/l, agent look). When a person has no image or the image fails to load, show the user's initials instead of <code>/img/default.png</code>. A shared grey placeholder makes users hard to tell apart, and a background that changes between views is confusing, so the background is generated at run time from the user and is always the same for that user. Scope: the component, its demo and docs; do not change pages that use it.</p><p>The attached screen is a guide for layout and content, not the final look: the design system and the real components win.</p><ul><li>New pure util <code>app/utils/ui/avatar-identity.js</code>: <code>initials(name, size)</code> (first letter of the first and last word, uppercase, Unicode-safe; one word = one letter; xs always one letter; empty name = null) and <code>identity(key)</code> returning <code>{ base, accent, pattern }</code> from a stable string hash (e.g. FNV-1a) of the key. Base colour from the dark palette colours that keep white text readable (<code>$primaryColor</code>, <code>$highlightColor</code>, <code>$secondaryColor</code>, <code>$dangerColor</code>, <code>$warningColor</code>, <code>$darkColor</code>, mirrored as constants with a comment pointing to <code>app/styles/variables.scss</code>), accent = a different colour from the same list, pattern from a fixed list (half-bottom, half-left, corner circle top-right, corner circle bottom-left, ring). Document that the order of these lists must never change (reordering changes every user's avatar).</li><li>Key = the user id; fall back to the name when there is no id. Nothing is stored.</li><li><code>AppUi::Avatar</code>: for a person, render the initials avatar when there is no id or the image <code>error</code> event fires (replaces 4588's default.png fallback); round (50%), the avatar size, base colour background, the pattern as an absolutely positioned shape in the accent colour at 50% opacity, white semibold initials scaled to the size; no name = <code>fa-user</code> icon on the same background. <code>title</code>/<code>alt</code> = the name. Colours via classes (e.g. <code>app-ui-avatar--c3</code>, <code>app-ui-avatar--p2</code>) defined in <code>app/styles/components/app-ui-avatar.scss</code>, not inline styles. Agents keep the robot look from 4588 (no initials).</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>: a row of sample people without images in every size, and an "image fails" control showing the switch. Docs <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-avatar.md</code> + <code>app-ui-avatar.json</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance</strong>: unit tests for initials (one/two words, extra spaces, non-Latin, xs) and identity (same key = same result, different keys spread over colours/patterns, accent never equals base); integration tests: no id, image error, name missing, agent unaffected. <strong>Out of scope</strong>: users whose stored picture is the default placeholder (they still load an image; handled separately if approved), uploading pictures, page changes.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4588</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> avatar-initials.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4604	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae6454575acb-1902-6b9c-f2ffa11a2697	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	9e865a376afa-3830-9afe-27257da9ad83	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 10:57:23	aprom	0	0
