85c19f616ae5-ae73-c875-146832767652	Talos: a failed handback leaves the issue with the agent; done issues count as in flight	2026-10-31 00:21:25	2026-10-31 00:43:36	0	<p>Two ways an issue can hold one of Agamemnon's slots for the worker forever:</p><ul><li><strong>A failed handback.</strong> When <code>Dispatcher._hand_off</code> fails (a Gaia error, for example the gaia-mcp memory error), it only logs <code>hand-off failed</code>. The issue stays in_progress and assigned to the agent. Reconcile then skips it ("last changed by a user who can't hand this agent work"), so nobody works it. This happened to #4207.</li><li><strong>Finished issues counted as in flight.</strong> Agamemnon counts every issue assigned to the worker, including done ones. #4191, #4192 and #4194 held all 3 slots.</li></ul><h4>Change</h4><ul><li>Record a failed handback in talos.db with reason <code>handoff_failed</code> and the intended status and assignee. Retry it on the next status change, reconnect, or every few minutes until it succeeds, and log each attempt.</li><li><code>talos status</code> lists handbacks still pending.</li><li>Agamemnon's in-flight count leaves out issues in finished statuses (the worker's <code>dependencyDoneStatuses</code> plus wont_fix), and issues waiting only on a pending handback.</li></ul><h4>Tests</h4><p>A failed handback is recorded and retried until it succeeds; done or wont_fix issues don't count as in flight.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4218	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	fb9764e06ae5-9703-881c-050eefa94e43	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	68d216f66ae5-3cc5-7b19-d2e21cfb0d57	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 00:43:36	adt	0	0
f3cd5c206af0-cd0b-cccd-99ddec09fd1b	ACL: deny-by-default access path for service tokens	2026-11-08 20:39:15	2026-11-08 22:31:54	0	<p>A service token has no user, so <code>RestController::setUser()</code> rejects it today. Runtimes must read a few things as themselves (delegable agents, specs, grants). This adds a separate, deny-by-default path that never touches RBAC roles or the resolution mode.</p><ul><li>Resources opt in to service access in their model ACL metadata (which actions, which service kinds). A service token is allowed only when the resource opted in AND <code>controller.action</code> is in the service client's scopes; everything else 401.</li><li>Optional per-resource record filter for service tokens (metadata hook), so a resource can limit rows (e.g. only delegable agents).</li><li>No current user for service requests: behaviours and components that need one must not run or must handle it (list them in the PR).</li><li>Requests by a disabled client fail; <code>lastUsedAt</code> updated.</li><li>Decision entry in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit with a test resource opted in and one not; api-tester acl cases with a service token. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> opting real resources in (later issues).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4384</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4386	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	dee441406af0-cd0b-cccd-253efc87745a	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	174057f66af0-cd3e-4f0e-d33e05ce06d4	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 22:31:54	agaia	0	0
324678f26afa-79f5-7528-eb287a9193f9	Agent page: load the agent's related data in one bulk request	2026-11-16 09:56:02	2026-11-16 10:25:05	0	<p>The agent page route loads the agent and then 9 queries in parallel (<code>app/routes/app/agent/page.js</code> ~l.30-54: userroles, memberships, identities, tool grants, skill grants, tools, tool servers, skills, activities). That is more than the browser runs at once over HTTP/1.1, so some of them wait. Use the bulk service (aprom-4595).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Keep the agent query. Replace the <code>Promise.all</code> of 9 queries with one <code>bulk.query</code> using the same options, mapping results to the same variables.</li><li>Keep today's error behaviour for the page (a failing item is handled like the failing query today).</li><li>Make the agent page acceptance test go through the Mirage <code>/bulk</code> handler.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong> the agent page makes one agent GET and one <code>POST /bulk</code>, and every box shows the same data as before.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the agent create, edit, tools and skills routes.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4595</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4601	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	365a60866afa-8715-b3ee-3c19fd4d0ee8	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 10:25:05	aprom	0	0
80cee8976ae5-ae73-c875-abe684165678	gaia-mcp: fetch project relations separately and only when needed; treat a Gaia error page as an error	2026-10-31 00:21:20	2026-10-31 00:32:35	0	<p>Before <code>update_issue</code> and <code>create_issue</code> resolve their fields, <code>project_options</code> reads the project with <code>rels=members,milestones,issuetypes,issuestatuses</code> in one request. On the server that request sometimes runs Gaia out of memory: about 1 in 8 to 2 in 5 attempts against A Prometheus, which has 6 members, 64 milestones and 7 types. Gaia then returns a PHP fatal-error page (<code>Allowed memory size of 134217728 bytes exhausted … RestController.php</code>).</p><p>gaia-mcp turns that page into <code>{"raw": …}</code>, <code>flatten</code> gives no rows, and <code>project()</code> silently falls back to the project record without relations. Every assignee lookup then fails with <code>'1' is not a member of A Prometheus</code>. This broke Talos's handback of #4207 and left the issue stuck with the agent.</p><p>Measured on the server, 8 times each: all four relations together failed 1 in 8 and took 3.1 s on average. Each relation alone failed 0 in 8 and took 0.6 to 1.7 s.</p><h4>Change</h4><ul><li><code>project_options</code> reads each relation in its own request, and only the ones the call needs:<ul><li>members for an assignee;</li><li>milestones for a milestone;</li><li>issue types for a type;</li><li>statuses for a status.</li></ul>Creating an issue still needs the defaults.</li><li><code>Gaia.request</code>: a reply that isn't JSON (PHP fatal error, HTML) raises a GaiaError with the first part of the body, instead of returning <code>{"raw": …}</code>. Reads (GET) are retried once.</li><li><code>project()</code>: no silent fallback to the record without relations when the query with relations returns nothing; that raises.</li><li><code>project_options</code>'s other callers (<code>gaia_project_options</code>, Talos tracker milestones and issues_in) keep working.</li></ul><h4>Tests</h4><p>Which relations are requested for each combination of arguments; an error page raises with its message; a GET is retried once; <code>project()</code> no longer falls back.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4217	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	fb9764e06ae5-9703-881c-050eefa94e43	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	ee487e396ae5-4e86-c875-9f230954d26e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 00:32:35	adt	0	0
64d69f826af6-f90a-2196-04b9603d869f	Clean up after the Ember 6.12 upgrade and clear the Ember 7 deprecations	2026-11-13 00:18:44	2026-11-13 13:12:01	0	<p>Start this after aprom-4486 (Ember 6.12) is merged. A trial upgrade on <code>dev</code> @ 9c68b5fe got the full suite green (1461 pass), but left the items below. None of them fail a test today; the deprecations become errors in Ember 7.</p><h4>1. Leftover classic component templates</h4><ul><li>Ember 6 no longer resolves component templates from <code>app/templates/components/</code>; aprom-4486 moves the ones that have a component class next to that class. About 30 templates remain there that nothing invokes by name: <code>application-wrapper</code>, <code>application-header</code>, <code>application-sidebar</code>, <code>application-footer</code>, <code>nav-bar</code>, <code>time-line</code>, <code>form-fields/*</code> (text, relate, checkbox, textarea, image, radio, upload, relatemulti), <code>activity-blocks/{closed,created,updated}</code>, plus the old copies of <code>activity-blocks/*</code> and <code>milestone-blocks/*</code> that also exist next to their components. Confirm each is unused, then delete it.</li><li>The <code>field/*/create|list|detail</code> templates are looked up by name (<code>getOwner(this).lookup('template:' + …)</code>) in <code>components/field-view.js</code>, <code>components/form-fields.js</code>, <code>components/milestone-block.js</code> and <code>components/activity-block.js</code>. Check whether these classic components (and <code>field-relatemulti.js</code> and similar) are still rendered anywhere. Delete them if they're dead; if they're live, replace the lookups with imported components, the way aprom-4486 does for <code>app-ui/milestone-block</code>. No test covers this today, so check the screens by hand if they're live.</li><li>Remove the unused <code>getOwner</code> import left in <code>components/app-ui/milestone-block.js</code>.</li></ul><h4>2. Ember 7 deprecations</h4><ul><li><code>importing-inject-from-ember-service</code>: replace <code>import { inject as service } from '@ember/service'</code> with <code>import { service } from '@ember/service'</code> (about 124 files; mechanical).</li><li><code>using-amd-bundles</code>: turn on the <code>use-ember-modules</code> optional feature. Check that the vendor scripts loaded with <code>app.import</code> in <code>ember-cli-build.js</code> (jQuery UI, Bootstrap, slimscroll, at.js, summernote, AdminLTE…) still work, since they rely on the global jQuery.</li><li>ember-data: the Store class extends <code>EmberObject</code> (deprecated). Follow the deprecation's guide to mark the app's store as not needing it, and fix any <code>EmberObject</code> APIs used on the store (<code>get</code>/<code>set</code>, etc.).</li><li>Run the suite with deprecations reported (<code>tests/helpers/deprecations</code>) and fix or record any other deprecation that ends in 7.0.</li></ul><h4>Done when</h4><ul><li><code>app/templates/components/</code> holds no component templates.</li><li>The test run reports no deprecations that end in 7.0.</li><li>The full suite is green, and the app runs locally (dropdowns, modals, milestone and activity blocks checked in the browser).</li></ul><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4512	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	5acddff36af7-8fc1-68cb-0a83d9b5e0ad	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-13 13:12:02	aprom	0	0
