8a129df86ae5-ae73-c875-0e2963ecda18	ai test prometheus: isolate parallel runs from different checkouts	2026-10-31 00:21:30	2026-10-31 00:51:34	0	<p>Talos runs several issues in parallel, each in its own <code>.runs/issue-N</code> checkout. For the Prometheus suite, <code>ai test prometheus</code> writes the ember test log and summary to a shared place, so runs from other checkouts overwrite each other. #4207 was blocked because the agent couldn't get a trustworthy full-suite result after 4 runs, and <code>ai ship</code> requires one.</p><p>Gaia already has test slots (<code>P4M_TEST_SLOT</code>); Prometheus has nothing equivalent.</p><h4>Change</h4><ul><li>Give each checkout, or each Talos test slot, its own test log, summary and results under <code>ai/state</code>, keyed by the checkout or slot.</li><li>Check whether the ember test server port or the Chrome profile also collide, and separate those too.</li><li><code>ai ship</code>'s test gate reads the result for its own checkout.</li><li>Until this is fixed, the workaround is <code>maxParallelByRepo: {"prometheus": 1}</code> in the worker's agent.local.json.</li></ul><h4>Tests</h4><p>Two runs with different checkouts or slots write separate results, and the ship gate reads its own.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4219	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	fb9764e06ae5-9703-881c-050eefa94e43	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	3c822d176ae5-4529-7b19-0f72697969b1	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 00:51:34	adt	0	0
a963b8636af6-72ab-189d-7abfade95b3c	Issues breaking due to HTTPS	2026-11-12 18:42:49	2026-11-13 12:51:48	0	<p><span class="colour" style="color:rgb(191, 191, 191)" data-tomark-pass="">Ember Data 4.1 used its own UUID generator built on&nbsp;</span><code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">crypto.getRandomValues</code><span class="colour" style="color:rgb(191, 191, 191)" data-tomark-pass="">, which works on plain HTTP. 4.12 switched the default to&nbsp;</span><code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">crypto.randomUUID()</code><span class="colour" style="color:rgb(191, 191, 191)" data-tomark-pass="">, which browsers only provide on HTTPS or&nbsp;</span><code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">localhost</code><span class="colour" style="color:rgb(191, 191, 191)" data-tomark-pass="">. prom.projects4.me is HTTP-only, so every&nbsp;</span><code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">createRecord</code><span class="colour" style="color:rgb(191, 191, 191)" data-tomark-pass="">&nbsp;now throws there. Local dev and the Mirage tests run on&nbsp;</span><code data-backticks="1" data-tomark-pass="">localhost</code><span class="colour" style="color:rgb(191, 191, 191)" data-tomark-pass="">, which is why the upgrade's tests didn't catch it.</span></p>\n	1	1	1	1	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4511	2026-11-30	2026-11-12	deferred	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	f37335d16af3-1487-2734-ddb12b85d11c	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Hammad Hassan	Rana Nouman	d79e6e096af7-2a8a-7359-302aa81f2773	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-13 12:51:49	aprom	0	0
658b4b536ae5-3a9e-bbf4-2d129d5e00ef	Idea page: plan review mode with the plan in the wide column	2026-10-31 09:48:21	2026-10-31 11:22:36	0	<p>The idea page (<code>templates/app/project/idea/page.hbs</code>) puts the conversation in <code>col-md-8</code> and the Plan, Created Issues and Summary boxes in <code>col-md-4</code>. The page itself sits in the <code>col-md-9</code> beside the ideas browser. That suits chatting, but reviewing a plan with several issues in about a quarter of the screen is hard. Engineers need to switch to a layout that favours the plan.</p><ul><li>Add a box-tool button to the Plan box header (<code>components/idea/plan-box.hbs</code>, <code>btn btn-box-tool</code>, <code>fa-expand</code> / <code>fa-compress</code>, title from <code>translations/en-us.json</code>) that toggles review mode through an action passed from the page.</li><li>Review mode: the side column (Plan, Created Issues, Summary) becomes <code>col-md-8</code> and the conversation <code>col-md-4</code>, with the plan column first, so the plan is on the left. The composer stays usable. Normal mode is today's layout.</li><li>State: query param <code>view=plan</code> on the page route (<code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>), so the mode survives reload and can be linked. Opening another idea keeps the mode. Leaving the ideas route resets it.</li><li>The plan's screen row and issue rows use the extra width (screens larger than in the side column). No new colours or components: reuse the plan box markup and classes in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code>.</li><li>Tests: acceptance cases in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-plan.feature</code>: the button switches the columns, a reload with <code>?view=plan</code> opens in review mode, toggling back restores the layout.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> from any idea with a plan, one click gives the plan the wide column and the conversation the narrow one. Another click goes back. Approve and version tabs work in both modes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> collapsing the ideas browser (separate issue), resizable columns.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4223	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	826b8f226ae5-0477-bbf4-18eed22a1099	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 11:22:36	aprom	0	0
694b71406af7-29da-7359-e38158be353c	Task board: show issue count on each milestone tab	2026-11-13 12:58:17	2026-11-13 19:25:46	0	<p>The task board's milestone tabs show only the type and name, so users must open each tab to see how much work it holds. Add the issue count to every tab, backlog included.</p><ul><li>In <code>app/components/app-ui/task-board.hbs</code> (the <code>ul.milestone-tabs</code> loop), render <code>milestone.issues.length</code> after the milestone name as an AdminLTE <code>label</code> (per <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>), with a <code>data-milestone-issue-count</code> attribute and a translated title/tooltip such as "12 issues" (new key in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>).</li><li>Use the same <code>milestone.issues</code> array as the milestone header's "x/y issues" (<code>components/app-ui/task-board/milestones.hbs</code>). <code>controllers/app/project/board.js</code> already keeps it in sync on create, move between milestones (including drop on a tab via <code>modifiers/initialize-sortable.js</code>) and delete, so the count must update without a reload.</li><li>If a style is needed (spacing next to the name, contrast on the active tab), add it under <code>.milestone-tabs</code> in <code>app/styles/modules/board.scss</code>. Use palette colours only and keep square edges. The label must not break the tab drop zones (<code>.drop-zone-area</code>).</li><li>When a board filter is active, the count reflects the issues loaded on the board, consistent with the lane counts.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Every milestone tab, including the backlog, shows its issue count. A milestone with no issues shows 0.</li><li>Creating an issue in a milestone, dragging an issue onto another milestone's tab or between milestones, and deleting an issue update the affected tab counts right away.</li><li>Integration test in <code>tests/integration/components/app-ui/task-board/layout-test.js</code> covering the counts, including 0 and a count change after an issue moves.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-status or open/closed counts on the tab, and server-side totals that ignore the active filter.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4515	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	b43cc5046ae8-20b5-32a1-13b222266c79	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	592e72846af7-73da-e54f-044c1d4fb232	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-13 19:25:47	aprom	0	0
963fd2666afa-5122-b3db-1f35bf604a24	Test env: run a fake-ares container and point the Gaia test containers at it	2026-11-16 11:10:14	2026-11-17 07:30:00	0	<p>Gaia's api tests for the docs AI calls (agaia #4537) need a fake Ares. Gaia ships one at <code>tools/api-tester/fake-ares/router.php</code>, served with <code>php -S 0.0.0.0:8000</code>. Gaia's own compose has a <code>fake-ares</code> service, and the test containers get <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL=http://fake-ares:8000</code>.</p>\n<p>The shared test containers that dev-tools creates (gaia-test, gaia-test-hermes-down and the <code>p4m-test-gaia-slotN</code> containers that <code>ai test gaia</code> uses) don't have it yet. Gaia therefore calls the unreachable <code>ares:8000</code>, and the docassist success cases answer 502.</p>\n<h4>Change</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><code>dev-tools/installer/testenv.py</code> and the p4m compose override: start a <code>fake-ares</code> container on the test network.\n<ul>\n<li>Use image <code>rananoman/gaia:env-dev</code>, entrypoint <code>php -S 0.0.0.0:8000 /fake-ares/router.php</code>, with the checkout's <code>tools/api-tester/fake-ares</code> mounted read-only at <code>/fake-ares</code>.</li>\n<li>Slots run other checkouts, so either mount each slot's checkout or share one container. The fake server has no state, so one shared container is fine.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><code>GaiaTestContainer.env()</code>: set <code>LLM_SERVICE_URL=http://fake-ares:8000</code> for gaia-test, gaia-test-hermes-down and the slot containers. Make sure they can resolve <code>fake-ares</code>.</li>\n<li>When the checkout has no <code>tools/api-tester/fake-ares</code> (branches before agaia #4537), skip the container. Setting the URL anyway is harmless.</li>\n<li><code>dev-tools/ai/lib/tests.py</code>: <code>PHPUNIT_FOLDERS</code> is a fixed list, so <code>tests/libraries/docs</code>, <code>conversations</code>, <code>workflows</code> and <code>query</code> never run in <code>ai test gaia</code>. Run <code>tests/libraries</code> as a whole instead.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Acceptance</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>With agaia #4537's branch checked out, <code>ai test gaia</code> passes <code>acl-members-docassist-ask-allowed</code>, <code>client-docassist-ask-returns-html</code>, <code>client-docassist-complete-returns-completion</code> and <code>client-docassist-review-returns-findings</code>.</li>\n<li><code>client-docassist-ares-failure-returns-502</code> still answers 502, because the fake server fails on <code>STUB_FAIL</code>.</li>\n<li><code>ai test gaia</code> runs <code>tests/libraries/docs</code>.</li>\n</ul><p>Complexity: simple</p>	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4605	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	deferred	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Odysseus	Rana Nouman	dd27bd696afa-1926-b3db-9245d788bb86	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-17 07:30:00	adt	0	0
8578e8916af7-7919-f6fb-b7b6a3befc5f	Component Library: AppUi::Modal on the native dialog element	2026-11-13 13:32:53	2026-11-13 14:19:37	0	<p>Add <code>AppUi::Modal</code>, a Glimmer component on the native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> (<code>showModal()</code>), to replace <code>BootstrapModal</code> (Bootstrap 3 jQuery plugin). This issue only adds the component; screens move in the following migration issues, so both components live side by side until the cleanup issue.</p>\n<h4>API: same as BootstrapModal</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><code>@title</code>, <code>@closeLabel</code>, <code>@confirmLabel</code>, <code>@leftLabel</code>/<code>@leftAction</code>, <code>@containerClass</code>, <code>@removeConfirmBtn</code>, <code>@disableSaveBtn</code>, <code>@dataSaveBtn</code>, <code>@onClose</code> (was <code>close</code>).</li>\n<li><code>@confirm</code>: returning <code>true</code> closes; returning a Promise makes the modal busy (buttons disabled, spinner on Confirm, Esc and backdrop ignored) until it settles; closes on truthy, stays open on falsy/reject.</li>\n<li>Opens when rendered, so callers keep <code>{{#if this.showX}}</code>. Removing it from the page closes it. No caller may reach into the DOM to close it.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Markup and styling</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Keep the inner markup: <code>.modal-dialog &gt; .modal-content.box.box-primary &gt; .modal-header/.modal-body/.modal-footer</code>, the <code>data-btn</code> hooks and the header close icon, so existing <code>containerClass</code> rules (<code>.idea-screen-modal</code>, <code>.issue-plan-modal</code>, …) and test selectors keep working.</li>\n<li>Do not put Bootstrap's <code>.modal</code> class on the dialog (Bootstrap 3 hides it). Styles in <code>app/styles/components/modal.scss</code>: transparent full-viewport dialog that scrolls, Bootstrap-like fade/slide via <code>@starting-style</code>, <code>::backdrop</code> at 50% black with the 0.5rem blur from <code>document.scss</code>, scroll lock with <code>body:has(dialog[open])</code>, <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>.</li>\n<li>Esc goes through the <code>cancel</code> event (preventDefault while busy); backdrop click is a click whose target is the dialog itself. Nested modals stack natively.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Things that render into body</h4>\n<p><code>showModal()</code> makes everything outside the dialog inert and draws it under the top layer.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Messenger</strong> (39 call sites, used for errors when a confirm fails and the modal stays open) must show above an open dialog and be clickable, e.g. its container as a <code>popover="manual"</code> re-shown after a dialog opens. Decide and document the approach.</li>\n<li><strong>PowerSelect / ember-basic-dropdown</strong> content renders in the body wormhole; inside a modal it must render in place (or into a destination inside the dialog). Decide the approach and document it on the Component Library entry, so the migrations apply it.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Tests</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Integration tests for the component (open, confirm true/Promise/falsy/reject, busy blocks Esc and backdrop, left action, close callback, nested).</li>\n<li>Update the shared acceptance steps (<code>tests/acceptance/steps/common-steps/modal-steps.js</code>, <code>list-steps.js</code>) so they work with both components; the migration issues should not need to touch them.</li>\n<li>Component Library entry next to the existing Modal entry, including the overflow/transform box case (no <code>in-element</code> needed).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Reference: throwaway demo comparing both against the real app CSS showed identical rendering (2026-11-13).</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4516	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	d0d108486af7-8395-cc28-680200392574	402f