6e7313c06ae5-3a9e-bbf4-c235c818907b	Ideas: collapse the ideas browser so the idea page uses the full width	2026-10-31 09:48:30	2026-10-31 10:28:40	0	<p>The ideas browser takes <code>col-md-3</code> of the ideas layout (<code>templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code>), so an open idea (conversation and plan) only gets <code>col-md-9</code>. Engineers working in one idea want the full width for the conversation and the plan.</p><ul><li>Add a collapse button to the browser box header (<code>box-tools</code>, <code>btn btn-box-tool</code>, <code>fa-angle-double-left</code>, title in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>) next to the "New" button.</li><li>Collapsed: the browser column is hidden and the outlet column becomes <code>col-md-12</code>. A small box-tool button (<code>fa-angle-double-right</code>) at the left of the outlet expands it again.</li><li>State: a tracked flag on <code>controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>, kept in <code>localStorage</code> so the choice survives reloads. Default expanded.</li><li>The New Idea page (create route) and the idea page both follow the flag.</li><li>Styles, if any, scoped under <code>.idea-wrapper</code> in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code>. Square edges, existing colours.</li><li>Tests: acceptance cases in <code>tests/acceptance/ideas/idea-browser.feature</code>: collapse hides the list and widens the content, expand restores it, the state survives a reload.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> one click hides the ideas list and the idea page spans the content area. One click brings it back. The choice is remembered.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> plan review mode (separate issue), mobile layout changes.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4224	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-3