fc870bc36af0-cd0b-cccd-a089a1c91cd1	Service enrollment: request, admin approval with a code, secret delivered to the service	2026-11-08 20:39:24	2026-11-08 22:57:51	0	<p>No secret may be copied by hand. A service enrolls itself: it asks Gaia, shows a short code, an admin approves the matching request, and the service receives its secret straight from Gaia (device-authorization style, RFC 8628).</p><ul><li>Resource <code>Serviceenrollment</code>: name, kind, status (pending | approved | denied | expired | delivered), userCode (e.g. <code>KQ7-3MX</code>), expiresAt (15 minutes), approvedBy, serviceclientId.</li><li>Anonymous POST creates a pending request and returns id, userCode, expiresAt and a pollToken (shown once, stored hashed). Rate limited per IP.</li><li>Anonymous GET by id with the pollToken: returns status; once approved, returns clientId and clientSecret <strong>once</strong> (status delivered), creating the Serviceclient with its kind's default scopes.</li><li>Admin list + PATCH status approved/denied (ACL like other admin resources). Expired requests can't be approved.</li><li>Only these two actions are anonymous: decide how (controller <code>$authorization</code> is controller-wide today) and record it in the decisions doc. Standard CRUD only, no custom routes.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit for the state machine (expiry, double delivery, wrong pollToken, deny); api-tester cases for anonymous and admin paths. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> enrollment tokens, UI.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4384</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4387	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	dee441406af0-cd0b-cccd-253efc87745a	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	255f2b556af0-cd3e-4f0e-24537bf2e754	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 22:57:52	agaia	0	0
36bc7c996ae8-8cc9-eb41-fac9838fc22e	External Request: Talos: allow only one `talos run` per workspace (single-instance lock)	2026-11-02 12:38:14	2026-11-02 13:02:13	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Prometheus (idea "Got multiple answers based on single prompt", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Nothing stops a second <code>talos run</code> from starting while one is already running. On 2026-11-02 two instances ran side by side from 15:39 (talos.log has a <code>[talos] starting</code> with no <code>stopped</code> before it). Every agent then worked each event twice: Nestor posted two answers to one idea message, and both instances ran Agamemnon and the Hermes listeners. Each instance only removes duplicates from its own in-memory queue (<code>lib/ideas/worker.py</code> <code>IdeaWorker._pending</code>), so the guard has to cover the whole process.</p><ul><li>In <code>talos/talos.py</code> <code>cmd_run</code>, take an exclusive lock before any other work (before <code>db.import_legacy()</code> and the workspace gc) and hold it until the command returns. Use <code>installer/filelock.py</code> <code>held(path, wait_seconds=0)</code>, the lock every dev tool already uses (msvcrt on Windows, fcntl elsewhere; the OS drops it when the holder dies; it writes the holder's PID).</li><li>Lock file: <code>STATE_DIR / "talos-run.lock"</code> (from <code>lib/config.py</code>). <code>STATE_DIR</code> comes from <code>LOCAL_DIR</code>, so the runtime copy (<code>.dev-tools-runtime</code>) and the <code>dev-tools/</code> checkout share it.</li><li>If the lock is held, catch <code>filelock.LockTimeout</code> and fail with a <code>TalosError</code> such as <code>Talos is already running (pid N (command line)); stop it first</code>, using <code>filelock.describe_holder</code>. Exit non-zero and don't write a <code>[talos] starting</code> line.</li><li><code>--dry-run</code> takes the lock as well: its dispatchers and listeners still react to events.</li><li>Other subcommands (<code>runs</code>, <code>pause</code>, status, etc.) don't take the lock.</li><li>README: one line in the run section saying only one <code>talos run</code> per workspace is allowed and what the error means.</li><li>Tests (OS-independent, temp dir with STATE_DIR patched): a second <code>cmd_run</code> while the lock is held raises <code>TalosError</code> naming the holder's PID; after the holder releases the lock, <code>cmd_run</code> takes it again. Stub out agent loading and the sleep loop so the test doesn't start listeners.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with <code>talos run</code> running, a second <code>talos run</code> (from either the runtime copy or the checkout) exits at once with the running instance's PID and command line; after the first is stopped or killed, <code>talos run</code> starts normally; this works on Linux and Windows; <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> an atomic Nestor turn claim (claiming <code>answered_upto</code> before a turn) and locks for other long-running tools.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4246	2026-11-09	2026-11-02	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	0c6f2e576ae8-4d7a-2c72-6fab7a1cfa99	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-02 13:02:11	adt	0	0
d4c043406ae5-92fb-c743-5f5e769d571e	Agamemnon: route clean re-reviews to it, hold over-limit merges, re-run a failed CI job once	2026-10-31 12:49:24	2026-10-31 13:25:09	0	<p>Deterministic fixes (no AI) for three cases that sent aga-v1 issues to the owner on 2026-10-31.</p><ul><li><b>Clean re-review:</b> when Odysseus's in_review action (address-review) finds nothing to change on an issue in an auto-merge milestone, route it through the CodeRabbit loop / MergeRoute to Agamemnon instead of handing it straight to the reviewer. Seen on #4208 and #4223 at 16:07.</li><li><b>Daily limit:</b> when the daily auto-merge limit is reached, keep the issue with Agamemnon and merge it on the next day's allowance instead of handing it back. Seen on #4223 (PR 587).</li><li><b>Failed CI:</b> when the merge gate fails only on CI, re-run the failed job(s) once (as Agamemnon) and wait; on a second failure send the issue to Odysseus with the failing job and log link. Seen on #4208 (PR 585), flaky Build-and-Test.</li></ul><p>Record each step in auto_merges and comment it on the issue.</p><p>Code: talos/lib/orchestrator/merging.py, policy.py, bot_review.py, ai/lib/mergegate.py.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4225	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	c36638756ae5-92fb-c743-0dd51d887bec	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	151c35e16ae5-a3a8-9f4e-b09a17a3baa5	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 13:25:09	adt	0	0
1753c8606af0-7d1c-cccd-03d471d00bd9	Service clients rotate their own secret	2026-11-08 20:39:51	2026-11-08 23:16:03	0	<p>No service secret should live forever and nobody should handle rotation. A service replaces its own secret with its current service token.</p><ul><li>Opt <code>Serviceclient</code> PATCH in to service access (the service access path in this milestone) for the client's own record only, field <code>rotateSecret: true</code>; the response carries the new secret once. The old secret stays valid for 10 minutes so a crash mid-rotation doesn't lock the service out.</li><li>Scope <code>serviceclient.rotate</code> in every kind's defaults.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> phpunit (own record only, grace period, old secret refused after it); api-tester case. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> rotation schedule (each service decides).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4386</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4389	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	dee441406af0-cd0b-cccd-253efc87745a	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	7d3d1be76af0-4df0-9303-2e45fbe0ed8e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-08 23:16:04	agaia	0	0
