ffb172f86ae5-c662-9f4e-3763b2b37dc0	Talos gc: remove a finished issue's p4m test containers (they fill Docker's memory and crash it)	2026-10-31 12:58:39	2026-10-31 13:25:37	0	<p>Docker has crashed or OOM-killed test runs repeatedly since Agamemnon started feeding Prometheus issues in parallel (#4207 03:35 and 05:18, ~13:50, #4222 16:44; Docker logged an OOM kill at 16:47).</p><p><b>Cause:</b> <code>ai test prometheus</code> from a Talos workspace starts a throwaway <code>p4m-test-prometheus-&lt;hash&gt;</code> container for that checkout and keeps an <code>ember build --watch</code> running in it (about 3 GB each). Nothing removes it: Talos's workspace gc only removes the container-runner leftovers, never the <code>p4m.test</code> containers. On 2026-10-31 four of them held ~12 GB of the 15.3 GB Docker VM, for issues already merged or done (4208, 4221, 4223, 4224).</p><p>Also, gc keeps every finished Prometheus workspace as "uncommitted changes" because of the case-duplicate docs file (aprom-4229), so even the workspace removal never happens.</p><p><b>Fix:</b></p><ul><li>When gc finds an issue finished (done, closed, wont fix, or PR merged) and no run in flight, remove the <code>p4m test</code> containers labelled with the issue's worktree paths (through <code>p4m test clean --src</code>), whether or not the workspace itself is kept.</li><li>Report them like the other leftovers (<code>talos gc --dry-run</code> lists them).</li><li>Docker unreachable: nothing removed, the gc carries on.</li></ul><p>Out of scope: stopping the warm build after each run, and a cap on concurrent Prometheus test containers (follow-ups if still needed).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4234	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	blocker	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	fb9764e06ae5-9703-881c-050eefa94e43	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	17af72036ae5-0e19-123