f49beae56ae5-92fb-c743-8bda49cafd2e	Agamemnon: hold an issue whose predicted files overlap an issue in flight	2026-10-31 12:49:56	2026-10-31 13:46:04	0	<p>Deterministic check (no AI) before Agamemnon assigns an issue to Odysseus: predict the files the issue will touch and, when they overlap the files of an issue already in flight in the same repo, hold it until that one is done or its PR merged. Parallel issues editing the same files caused most of the merge conflicts in aga-v1 (#4207, #4221).</p><ul><li>Prediction: files and classes named by <code>ai context</code> for the issue, plus Nestor's plan files when present. For in-flight issues use the branch's real diff against base once it exists.</li><li>Ignore generated files (e.g. docs/) and files on a configurable allowlist of additive registries if they prove noisy.</li><li>Comment once on the held issue naming the overlapping issue and files; release it on the next sweep after the blocker clears.</li><li>Unknown prediction (no files found) does not hold the issue.</li><li><code>talos status</code> shows held issues and why.</li></ul><p>Depends on: adt-4225</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4226	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	c36638756ae5-92fb-c743-0dd51d887bec	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	b4e2dc626ae5-3157-5f17-1d20b7a0f060	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 13:46:04	adt	0	0
a8441df26ae5-0199-8e20-7c656f3f4c37	gaia-mcp: a failed create_issue leaves a new milestone behind; deleted relation rows are treated as live	2026-10-31 13:56:56	2026-10-31 14:05:04	0	<p>On 2026-10-31 two failed <code>gaia_create_issue</code> calls in A Prometheus each created a duplicate "aga-Parallel Runtime" milestone (12:49:28 and 12:49:51 UTC) next to the one created explicitly at 12:49:09. The duplicates were soft-deleted by hand.</p><p><b>1. Milestone created before the issue is validated.</b> <code>Tools.create_issue</code> calls <code>_ensure_milestone</code> before <code>_resolve_fields</code>, so a call that then fails (here: "Unknown type") still creates the milestone. Fix: resolve and validate every field first, create a missing milestone only right before posting the issue. If the issue POST fails after a milestone was just created, say so in the error (with its id) instead of leaving it silently.</p><p><b>2. Soft-deleted rows read as live.</b> Gaia's <code>project?rels=milestones</code> returns soft-deleted milestones (<code>deleted: 1</code>), so <code>_ensure_milestone</code>, <code>project_options</code> and Talos's milestone reads can match a deleted one. Filter <code>deleted</code> rows out of every project relation gaia-mcp reads (milestones, members, types, statuses).</p><p>(Trigger: the session's MCP process predated adt-4217, so the project read came back without milestones and types; that part is already fixed.)</p><p>Tests: a bad type creates no milestone; a POST failure after a new milestone names it; deleted relation rows are ignored by name lookup.</p><p>Out of scope: Gaia returning soft-deleted rows in relations (Gaia side; raise separately if wanted).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4235	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	c36638756ae5-92fb-c743-0dd51d887bec	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	A