9cc48ab16af1-31f2-1bb8-4aeac19d2824	ai test / ai ship: refuse to run from a .runs/issue-N folder when P4M_WORKSPACE is not set	2026-11-09 00:02:36	2026-11-09 00:13:14	0	<p><b>Problem:</b> <code>ai test</code> and <code>ai ship</code> pick the checkout from <code>P4M_WORKSPACE</code>, not from the current directory. Run from <code>Pr4M/.runs/issue-N/&lt;repo&gt;</code> with the variable unset, they silently target <code>Pr4M/&lt;repo&gt;</code>, which may be on a different branch. On agaia-4388 the full suite reported PASS for Pr4M/gaia (branch claude-issue-4028) instead of the run checkout, and the recorded result would have gated the ship of the wrong tree.</p><p><b>Change:</b></p><ul><li>When the cwd is inside a <code>.runs/issue-N</code> folder and <code>P4M_WORKSPACE</code> is unset, or points to a different workspace, <code>ai test</code> and <code>ai ship</code> stop with a clear error naming the expected <code>P4M_WORKSPACE</code> value.</li><li>Print the resolved checkout path and branch at the start of <code>ai test</code> and <code>ai ship</code>.</li></ul><p><b>Acceptance:</b></p><ul><li>Unit tests cover: cwd in .runs with the variable unset (refused), with a matching value (runs), with a mismatching value (refused), and cwd in Pr4M (runs as today).</li></ul><p>Found while unblocking agaia-4388 (PR projects4me/gaia#257).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4405	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	712014526af0-7d1c-cccd-ee6dc2488b11	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Agent Agamemnon	f7e604246af1-31f2-1bb8-d77a4098ed3c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 00:13:14	adt	0	0
b51252426ae8-20b5-32a1-46086816d465	Issue detail: live status, assignee and comments with Messenger toasts	2026-11-02 13:44:21	2026-11-11 10:38:18	0	<p>While a user has an issue's detail page open, status, assignee and comment changes made by other users (or agents) only appear after a reload. Gaia and Hermes already publish everything needed, so only the issue page needs to subscribe. Follow the existing screen pattern (<code>docs/architecture/live-updates/</code>). The closest example is <code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>, which only handles events for the open idea.</p><p><strong>Events (no contract change):</strong></p><ul><li><code>issue.status.changed</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the issue id. <code>changes</code> may carry <code>status</code>, <code>statusId</code> or both. Changes made through the gaia MCP client send only <code>statusId</code>.</li><li><code>issue.assignee.changed</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the issue id. <code>changes</code> carries the new assignee id (check <code>IssueLiveEventsComponent</code> for the field name).</li><li><code>conversation.comment.created</code> / <code>updated</code> / <code>deleted</code>: <code>resource.id</code> is the comment id. <code>meta.conversationId</code> (also <code>changes.relatedId</code>) is the room id. Issue comments are posted to the issue's room (<code>issue-details.js</code> <code>_createComment</code>, relatedId <code>issue.conversationRoomId</code>).</li></ul><p><strong>Changes:</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/controllers/app/project/issue/page.js</code>: inject <code>hermes</code> and <code>currentUser</code>. Add <code>registerHermesIntents(projectId)</code> / <code>unregisterHermesIntents()</code> with a disposer, as in <code>idea/page.js</code>. Event names are literals at the register site (D-005).</li><li>Status handler: apply only when <code>resource.id</code> is the open issue. Set <code>statusId</code> and <code>status</code>. When only <code>statusId</code> is sent, take the name from <code>issueStatuses</code>. Don't save the record.</li><li>Assignee handler: same issue check. Set <code>assignedTo</code> from the store, using <code>findRecord('user', id)</code> when the user isn't loaded. A null id clears the assignee.</li><li>Comment handlers: apply only when the room id equals <code>issue.conversationRoomId</code>.<ul><li>Created: <code>store.findRecord('comment', id)</code>, then add it to <code>issue.comments</code> once (guard by id).</li><li>Updated: reload that comment if it is listed.</li><li>Deleted: remove it from the list and unload it.</li></ul>Use the handlers in <code>controllers/app/project/conversation.js</code> (~line 1139) as reference.</li><li>Toasts: when <code>envelope.actorId</code> is set and is not the current user, post <code>new Messenger().post({message, type: 'info', showCloseButton: true})</code>, the pattern already used in <code>components/issue/issue-details.js</code>:<ul><li>"&lt;user&gt; changed the status to &lt;status&gt;"</li><li>"&lt;user&gt; assigned this issue to &lt;user&gt;"</li><li>"&lt;user&gt; commented" / "&lt;user&gt; edited a comment"</li></ul>No toast for deletes. Take the actor's name from the store (or <code>createdUserName</code> on comments). Put every string in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>After every <code>await</code> in a handler, check that the controller isn't destroyed and that the same issue is still open. Catch failures: log them, leave the page unchanged, and show no toast.</li><li><code>app/routes/app/project/issue/page.js</code>: register in <code>setupController</code> with the tracked project id. Unregister on exit (<code>resetController</code>) and when moving to another issue.</li><li>Docs: in <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/architecture.md</code>, add the issue page row to the "Which screens register which events" table and remove issue detail from the "not live" line. In <code>decisions.md</code>, change D-011 so the issue page is no longer silent (its activity list stays silent), and add a decision: the issue page shows a Messenger toast for changes made by other actors, never for its own.</li></ul><p><strong>Tests</strong> (Mirage + Fake Hermes, D-012):</p><ul><li>QUnit tests for the controller handlers:<ul><li>status and assignee are applied for the open issue and ignored for another issue;</li><li>a <code>statusId</code>-only change resolves the name;</li><li>a comment is added once and ignored for another room; update and delete are applied;</li><li>a toast appears only when the actor is someone else;</li><li>a failed <code>findRecord</code> leaves the page unchanged.</li></ul></li><li>One Yadda acceptance scenario: open an issue, inject status, assignee and comment envelopes from another user, and see the changes and the toasts. Steps used only by this feature go in a per-feature steps file, not in <code>steps.js</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong></p><ul><li>With an issue open, a status (including a <code>statusId</code>-only change), assignee or comment change made elsewhere shows without a reload, with no duplicates.</li><li>Changes by another user show a Messenger toast; the user's own changes don't.</li><li>Events for other issues or rooms change nothing. Leaving the page removes its intents.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the live activity list, dates and other issue fields, the issue list page, and any change to Gaia or Hermes.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4248	2026-11-09	2026-11-02	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	b43cc5046ae8-20b5-32a1-13b222266c79	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	73e28df76ae8-e7b9-2948-97962512868d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-03 11:11:16	aprom	