a14a97a56af1-31f2-1bb8-2dda562b4cae	ai test gaia: run tests/libraries/authorization and tests/models in the full suite	2026-11-09 00:02:41	2026-11-09 00:12:25	0	<p><b>Problem:</b> <code>ai test gaia</code> runs the security, utils and tools PHPUnit groups but not <code>tests/libraries/authorization</code> or <code>tests/models</code>. On agaia-4388, <code>ServiceEnrollmentTokensTest</code> had 3 ArgumentCountErrors that the full suite never showed, and <code>ai ship</code> accepted the PASS. They were only caught by running <code>p4m test phpunit</code> on those folders by hand.</p><p><b>Change:</b></p><ul><li>Add <code>tests/libraries/authorization</code> and <code>tests/models</code> (including <code>tests/models/behaviors</code>) to the phpunit groups of <code>ai test gaia</code>, skipping a folder the checkout doesn't have, as is already done for other folders (adt-4191).</li><li>Check that CI runs the same folders. If CI is missing them too, add them there so the local suite and CI stay the same.</li><li>Map changes under <code>core/libs/authorization</code> and <code>core/mvc/models</code> to these groups wherever changed files are mapped to tests.</li><li>Check the base commit for failures that already exist in these folders and record them as known.</li></ul><p><b>Acceptance:</b> the full-suite summary lists the two new groups with their counts. A failing test in either one fails the run and blocks <code>ai ship</code>.</p><p>Found while unblocking agaia-4388 (PR projects4me/gaia#257).</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4406	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	712014526af0-7d1c-cccd-ee6dc2488b11	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	06c72f316af1-f548-1bb8-9414034e431e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 00:12:25	adt	0	0
52b483c16ae5-a3a8-9f4e-d8d19a30a33d	Agamemnon: AI triage session for incidents within its premise	2026-10-31 12:51:30	2026-10-31 14:55:47	0	<p>Where the deterministic orchestrator would hand an issue to the owner, and the classifier puts it in an incident type from the premise, Agamemnon runs a headless Claude Code session instead (the way Nestor runs) with the incident packet as input and only <code>aga</code> available.</p><ul><li>Role prompt (talos/agents/agamemnon/role.md): act only within the premise; prefer the least visible reversible action; explain the reasoning in each action; escalate when unsure.</li><li>Model: Sonnet by default, Opus for merge_conflict.</li><li>Limits: turns and cost per incident, a daily cost cap, at most N actions per incident; the same incident on the same issue a second time goes to the owner. All configurable in agent.json.</li><li>Incidents outside the premise, or a session that ends without resolving, go to the owner as today, with a comment.</li><li>Live from the start (no shadow mode): review is through the issue comments and <code>talos agamemnon log</code>.</li><li><code>talos status</code> shows open incidents and today's cost.</li></ul><p>Depends on: adt-4228, adt-4230, adt-4231</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4232	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	c36638756ae5-92fb-c743-0dd51d887bec	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	34b47b306ae5-4d5d-ae8f-0bd346360f84	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 14:55:47	adt	0	0
500076f76af0-7d1c-cccd-7b7e631e768d	External Request: Hermes enrolls with Gaia and keeps a service token	2026-11-08 20:40:48	2026-11-09 00:53:11	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Inter application Communication", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Hermes gets its own identity from Gaia (service client of kind <code>hermes</code>) so it can call Gaia as itself. No secret is copied by hand.</p><ul><li>One gateway module in <code>src/auth/</code>: on start, if no stored credential, enroll with <code>GAIA_ENROLLMENT_TOKEN</code> (auto-approved) or, without one, create a request and log its user code for an admin to approve, then poll until delivered.</li><li>Store the client id and secret in a file at a configured path (mounted volume, mode 600), so unattended restarts need no new enrollment token. ADR in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>: credential file is not domain storage (Hermes stays a relay).</li><li>Get a new client_credentials token at every start and refresh it before expiry; rotate its secret weekly via Gaia's rotation.</li><li>Never log the secret, token or user code beyond the one log line for approval.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> in-process tests with a stub Gaia (D-015) for both enrollment paths, restart with stored credential, token refresh and rotation. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> using the token (next issue).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4388, agaia-4389</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4395	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	861790376ad5-1449-a602-a25bd5e6e2b8	d59707896af0-cd0b-cccd-6c0c771196c7	\N	87099ee46ad5-1449-a602-5f7a1f6605b7	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	90a899496af1-64a9-1bb8-4d112b28d5c2	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 00:53:11	ah	0	0
dc14cc106afa-b805-5654-9428c669248e	Project::MemberAvatars: pass a size to AppUi::Avatar instead of resizing it with CSS	2026-11-16 11:28:28	2026-11-16 16:22:28	0	<p><code>components/project/member-avatars.hbs</code> already renders <code>AppUi::Avatar</code>, but its size is forced by CSS on the wrapper: <code>.member-avatars .member-avatar</code> 4rem (<code>styles/modules/project.scss:318</code>) and 2.4rem in role rows (<code>styles/modules/role.scss:70</code>). Use the component's sizes instead.</p><ul><li>Add <code>@size</code> to MemberAvatars (default m), passed to each <code>AppUi::Avatar</code>; the overflow badge (<code>.member-avatars-overflow</code>) takes the same diameter.</li><li>Callers: projects list (<code>templates/app/projects/index.hbs:111</code>, 40px) -&gt; m; role rows (<code>templates/app/role.hbs:79</code>, 24px) -&gt; s; thread participants (<code>components/conversation/participants-box.hbs:7</code>) -&gt; m.</li><li>Remove the width/height overrides from project.scss and role.scss; keep the overlap margin and hover.</li><li>YUIDoc for <code>@size</code>; integration test per size.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the stacks render at 40px (projects, participants) and 30px (role rows) through <code>@size</code>, with no CSS size override left.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4612</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4613	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	4bd0afa46afb-708f-7e86-d2b33dc9a3f7	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 16:22:29	aprom	0	0
8f727a026ae5-ae73-c875-1fa4fcd2b95f	GET project with several hasMany rels runs out of memory in RestController::prepareData	2026-10-31 00:21:35	2026-11-09 16:52:35	0	<p>On the server (128M memory_limit), <code>GET /project?query=(Project.id : …)&amp;rels=members,milestones,issuetypes,issuestatuses</code> sometimes dies:</p><p><code>Allowed memory size of 134217728 bytes exhausted (tried to allocate 24576 bytes) in core/mvc/controllers/RestController.php on line 1194</code></p><p>This is in <code>prepareData</code>, while it iterates the hydrated result set.</p><p>For A Prometheus (6 members, 64 milestones, 7 issue types) the combined request failed 1 in 8 and took 3.1 s on average. Each relation requested alone never failed and took 0.6 to 1.7 s. That suggests the hasMany relations are joined in one query and multiplied (6 × 64 × 7 ≈ 2,700 rows) before being grouped again. The failures will get more frequent as milestones and issues grow.</p><h4>Investigate and fix</h4><ul><li>Confirm how several hasMany rels are loaded: one joined query (a cross product), or one query per relation.</li><li>Load each hasMany relation in its own query, or otherwise avoid the cross product, so memory grows with the sum of the related rows, not their product.</li><li>A PHP fatal error should not return an HTML page with HTTP 200.</li></ul><p>Clients already avoid the combined request (gaia-mcp fetches relations separately), but Prometheus or any other client asking for several hasMany rels can hit it.</p><h4>Tests</h4><p>A project with many milestones, members and types, read with all four rels, uses bounded memory (or a check on the query count). The api-tester case for project with rels still passes.</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4220	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	in_review	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	\N	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	21e100346ae6-73fb-a51a-ef7d1249e787	f605b4e862c6-4e44-047e-0b80b34dd385	2026-11-07 07:31:01	agaia	0	0
5debc5e86ae5-a3a8-9f4e-22fa6059f1fb	Agamemnon: resolve merge conflicts itself, within guards	2026-10-31 12:51:41	2026-10-31 15:38:57	0	<p>Agamemnon resolves a PR's merge conflict itself before sending it to Odysseus.</p><ul><li>Always merge origin/&lt;base&gt; into the branch; never rebase.</li><li>Back up the branch first (<code>aga backup</code>).</li><li>Work in the issue's own workspace, never one with a run in progress.</li><li><b>Guard:</b> every conflicting hunk must be additive on both sides (e.g. both added scenarios, steps, routes, registry entries); the resolved file must contain every line both sides added, and nothing else changed. A tool checks this, not the model.</li><li>Then the tests for the changed files (<code>ai test &lt;repo&gt; --changed</code>) must pass before the push.</li><li>Push the merge commit to the PR's branch the way Odysseus's runs do (Odysseus identity, <code>odysseus</code> remote); the journal and the issue comment record that Agamemnon made it.</li><li>Otherwise (non-additive hunk, failing tests): abort, restore, send to Odysseus for one attempt with notes, then the owner.</li><li>The PR goes back through the CodeRabbit loop after the push.</li></ul><p>Example: #4221 (PR 588), idea-plan.feature and idea-plan-steps.js, both sides added scenarios and steps.</p><p>Depends on: adt-4232</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4233	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	c36638756ae5-92fb-c743-0dd51d887bec	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	a12d96536ae6-73fb-a51a-a9a969b53977	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 15:38:57	adt	0	0
11a5f5d96ae5-9c1a-ae8f-156027ef2e31	Idea screens: open the full-size screen in a modal instead of a new tab	2026-10-31 14:24:17	2026-10-31 16:11:22	0	<p>Clicking a screen on the idea page (thread and plan box, both <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code> in <code>components/idea/message-screen.{hbs,js}</code>) opens <code>/preview/get/&lt;token&gt;</code> in a new tab. The engineer wants the preview in a modal on the same page.</p><ul><li>Replace the <code>open</code> action's <code>window.open</code> with a tracked <code>previewOpen</code>. Render the existing <code>bootstrap-modal</code> only while it is set, with the <code>close</code> callback clearing it (pattern: <code>components/idea/conversation-box.hbs</code> ~l.48). Use <code>@removeConfirmBtn={{true}}</code> so only Close shows.</li><li>The modal title is a new translation (e.g. <code>views.app.idea.screen.preview</code>), because <code>bootstrap-modal</code> passes its title through <code>t</code>. The body shows the screen title and version (<code>views.app.idea.conversation.screenVersion</code>), then the image at full width.</li><li>Get a fresh address with <code>uploadPreview.previewUrl(uploadId)</code> each time the modal opens (tokens are single-use, and the inline image already used its own). Show a spinner while it loads, and the <code>fa-picture-o</code> placeholder plus a translated message if it fails. Check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after the await.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/idea.scss</code>, scoped by a <code>@containerClass</code> (e.g. <code>idea-screen-modal</code>): a wide dialog (about 90% of the viewport), the image <code>max-width: 100%</code>, the body scrolls for tall screens. Square edges, design-system colours only.</li><li>Tests: an integration test for <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code> with Mirage: a click opens the modal with the image at the preview address, no new tab opens, Close removes the modal, and a failed token shows the placeholder.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> on the idea page, clicking any screen in a message or in the plan box shows it full size in a modal over the page. Closing it returns to the same place.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> images pasted into messages (<code>modifiers/render-markdown.js</code>, still a new tab), zoom/next/previous, and smaller images for the plan box.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4237	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae459c625acb-1902-6b9c-4dab4f2a0678	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	bc3fc0706ae5-9c1a-ae8f-68afe1bb3208	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 16:11:22	aprom	0	0
d2aa04946af1-f548-1bb8-4659e1749d0a	Service enrollment: the poll that delivers the secret also returns serviceClientId, so a service can rotate its own secret	2026-11-09 00:07:46	2026-11-09 00:24:18	0	<p><b>Problem.</b> A service rotates its secret with <code>PATCH /api/v1/serviceclient/{id}</code> and <code>{id, rotateSecret: true}</code> (D-068). Here <code>{id}</code> is the <b>Serviceclient record id</b>, not the OAuth <code>clientId</code>: see <code>ServiceclientController::assertIdMatches</code> and <code>ServiceClientSecrets::rotateServiceClient($serviceClientId)</code>. No service can currently learn that id:</p><ul><li>The delivering poll (<code>ServiceenrollmentController::getAction</code>) adds only <code>clientId</code> and <code>clientSecret</code> to <code>document()</code>. <code>ServiceEnrollments::poll</code> already saves <code>$enrollment-&gt;serviceclientId</code>, but the response leaves it out.</li><li>Serviceclient's <code>acl.service</code> opens only <code>update</code> (filter <code>Serviceclient.clientId = :serviceClientId:</code>), so a service token cannot read its own record.</li><li><code>TokenIntrospection</code> returns <code>clientId</code>, not the record id.</li></ul><p>Hermes (ah-4395) blocks on this, and the runtime (adt-4399) needs the same.</p><p><b>Change:</b></p><ul><li>When a poll delivers the secret, its attributes also include <code>serviceClientId</code>: the delivered Serviceclient's record id, taken from <code>$issued['serviceclient']-&gt;id</code> via <code>ServiceEnrollments::poll</code>'s result. As with <code>clientId</code>, it is returned only on that delivering poll. Polls that are pending, delivered or expired don't change.</li><li>Amend the enrollment decision, <b>"D-066 — Services enroll themselves…"</b> in <code>docs/architecture/rbac/decisions.md</code>. The delivering poll returns <code>clientId</code>, <code>clientSecret</code> and <code>serviceClientId</code>, and the service keeps the id to rotate (D-068). Add a change-log row.</li><li>api-tester (client.json):<ul><li>extend <code>serviceenrollment-poll-delivers-secret</code> to assert <code>serviceClientId</code>;</li><li>make <code>serviceenrollment-poll-delivers-only-once</code> assert it is absent on the second poll;</li><li>optionally, add a case where the enrolled client rotates its own secret with that id and its service token.</li></ul></li><li>Unit test in <code>tests/libraries/authorization</code> (ServiceEnrollments poll), if <code>poll()</code>'s return value changes.</li><li>Regenerate <code>docs/generated</code> if the gaia-dev checks require it.</li></ul><p><b>Contract:</b> one new attribute on a response that already carries the secret. No new endpoint, ACL or access surface (option 1 on ah-4395, chosen by Hammad). Callers that ignore unknown attributes are unaffected.</p><p><b>Out of scope:</b></p><ul><li>Letting a service read its own Serviceclient record (option 2, rejected).</li><li>Exposing the id from introspection.</li><li>Two decisions are numbered D-066 on dev: "Service tokens reach only resources that opt in" and "Services enroll themselves". Renumbering them is a separate cleanup; don't do it here.</li></ul><p><b>Linked PR:</b> Hermes ah-4395 is built against this field now (its stub Gaia returns it). The two PRs merge together.</p><p><b>Estimated files:</b> 3–5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4408	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	high	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	dee441406af0-cd0b-cccd-253efc87745a	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Achilles	Agent Agamemnon	4c88ef486af1-5e79-e3a5-da9825eed0de	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 00:24:15	agaia	0	0
4f6e1f526ae6-76ba-935c-39f13b91b9f8	Idea thread: the screen preview modal shows a 30px image because it renders inside the comment	2026-10-31 16:58:55	2026-10-31 17:16:04	0	<p>Since aprom-4237, clicking a screen opens <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code>'s preview modal. From the plan box it shows the full-size screen. From the conversation thread (Brainstorm) it shows a tiny image. The cause is confirmed in the browser: in the thread the modal is rendered inside the message's <code>.box-comment</code> (<code>ConversationUi::CommentFrame</code> via <code>components/idea/message-item.hbs</code>). AdminLTE's rule <code>.box-comments .box-comment img, .img-sm, .user-block.user-block-sm img</code> (30px, <code>!important</code>) then applies to the modal image. Prometheus' <code>styles/modules/conversation.scss</code> (~l.180, ~l.232) adds more <code>!important</code> image rules for comments.</p><ul><li>Start with an integration test that fails today: <code>Idea::MessageScreen</code> rendered inside a <code>.box-comments .box-comment</code> opens a modal whose image is not a descendant of the comment.</li><li>Render the preview modal outside the thread, e.g. <code>{{#in-element}}</code> to a target outside the conversation box (Bootstrap modals usually sit at the end of <code>body</code>). Don't fight the AdminLTE rule with more <code>!important</code> overrides, and don't change <code>conversation.scss</code>: issue comments rely on it.</li><li>Give the modal image its own class (not <code>idea-message-screen-image</code>), so the inline screen sizes don't apply.</li><li>Keep the aprom-4237 behaviour: a fresh <code>uploadPreview.previewUrl</code> per opening, spinner, placeholder on failure, Close only, the isDestroying/isDestroyed guards. The plan box (normal and wide) opens the same way.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> clicking a screen in a Nestor message in the thread opens the modal with the full-size screen, as from the plan box. Closing it leaves the thread where it was. The ember suite passes.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> images pasted into messages (<code>render-markdown.js</code>), the inline thumbnail sizes, and the ideas page layout.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4238	2026-11-07	2026-10-31	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	165d13e86ae6-57e5-e410-6551dd1a6456	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-10-31 17:16:04	aprom	0	0
fbf232c86ae8-8685-9cef-964e4cec12a7	ai: comment "@coderabbitai full review" on every new agent PR in CodeRabbit repos	2026-11-02 08:34:04	2026-11-07 11:02:41	0	<p>CodeRabbit doesn't review agent PRs on its own; it needs a <code>@coderabbitai full review</code> comment on the PR. Without that comment the bot-review loop (<code>ai/lib/coderabbit.py</code>, <code>talos/lib/bot_review.py</code>) waits for a review that never starts. Agents should post the comment themselves every time they open a PR.</p><ul><li>Add <code>"codeRabbitTrigger": "@coderabbitai full review"</code> to <code>dev-tools/ai/config.json</code>. An empty value or a missing key turns the trigger off.</li><li>In <code>dev-tools/ai/lib/workflow.py</code> <code>open_pr</code>: after <code>gh pr create</code> succeeds, if <code>coderabbit.enabled(repo)</code> and the trigger is set, post the trigger as a PR comment as Agent Odysseus (<code>ody(repo, "gh", "pr", "comment", url, "--repo", REPOS[repo], "--body", trigger)</code>). Print <code>say("CodeRabbit: requested full review")</code>. Watch for an import cycle (<code>coderabbit</code> imports <code>review</code>); import it inside the function if needed.</li><li>If the comment fails, print a warning and keep going. The PR is already open, so the handoff must still finish.</li><li>Both <code>ai pr</code> (<code>cmd_pr</code>) and <code>ai ship</code> (<code>ship.py</code> <code>cmd_ship</code>) go through <code>open_pr</code>, so both get the comment. When <code>ai ship</code> resumes and finds a PR it opened earlier (<code>existing_pr</code>), it doesn't post the comment again.</li><li>Unit tests in <code>dev-tools/ai/tests/</code> with <code>ody</code> mocked: the comment is posted for an enabled repo; it isn't posted for a disabled repo (e.g. ares) or when the trigger is empty; a failed comment still returns the PR URL.</li><li>Document the behaviour and the <code>codeRabbitTrigger</code> key in <code>dev-tools/ai/README.md</code>, where CodeRabbit is described.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a PR opened with <code>ai ship</code> or <code>ai pr</code> in gaia, prometheus or hermes has exactly one <code>@coderabbitai full review</code> comment from Agent Odysseus, and CodeRabbit starts a review. A PR in ares has no comment. <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> posting the trigger again after later pushes (CodeRabbit's incremental reviews handle those); changes to the bot-review polling.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4245	2026-11-09	2026-11-02	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	bfd094216ae8-2182-9cef-a06a6f9a90b4	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 11:02:41	adt	0	0
2dae71606ae8-879a-51f2-c99dba52fafb	Agent create: page stays on the form after a successful save, with no message	2026-11-02 16:19:57	2026-11-02 19:07:29	0	<p>Saving a new agent stores it in Gaia, but the page stays on the create form: no success message and no move to the agent page. The agent pages are from aprom-4044.</p><p><strong>What the code shows</strong></p><ul><li>The base <code>controllers/prometheus/create.js</code> <code>_save</code> (~l.222) calls <code>afterSave(data).then(...)</code> without returning it and without a <code>catch</code>. When <code>afterSave</code> rejects, <code>navigateToSuccess</code> and <code>showSuccess</code> never run, the error is swallowed, and the save promise never settles.</li><li>The agent's <code>afterSave</code> (<code>controllers/app/agent/create.js</code> ~l.232) saves the agent user's <code>accountStatus</code>, then creates and deletes <code>userrole</code> and <code>membership</code> records. Any one of these failing leaves the page stuck.</li><li>Likely culprit: <code>syncMembers</code> creates memberships with <code>deleted: '0'</code>, but Gaia's Membership has no <code>deleted</code> field (no soft delete, see <code>gaia/docs/generated/models/Membership.md</code>). Also check whether <code>agent.user</code> and <code>agent.userId</code> are set on the POST response.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Reproduce it in the running app and in a failing test first. Find the call that fails and fix it.</li><li>In <code>_save</code>, return the <code>afterSave</code> chain and handle its failure: show the error through <code>errorManager</code> and settle the promise. The record is already saved, so still go to the success route and tell the user which follow-up step failed. Check the other create controllers that override <code>afterSave</code> still behave.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Creating an agent with roles, projects and Active set shows the success message and opens the agent page with them saved.</li><li>If a follow-up save fails, the user sees an error and the page doesn't hang.</li><li>Tests cover both cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> moving the role, project and status sync into a service (a design-review follow-up from aprom-4044).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4249	2026-11-09	2026-11-02	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	7d2977b86ae8-73b7-51f2-bb09f6d9625a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-02 19:07:30	aprom	0	0
71c1f7d76af0-7d1c-cccd-d7758159f72c	External Request: Talos: enroll as a runtime service client and keep a service token	2026-11-08 20:41:21	2026-11-09 00:32:56	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Inter application Communication", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Talos becomes a registered runtime in Gaia with no hand-copied secret, the first step towards running Gaia-declared agents (and later running inside Ares).</p><ul><li>Through gaia-mcp (the only tracker client): enrollment (create request, poll, receive secret once), service client_credentials token, token refresh, self-rotation of the secret (weekly).</li><li><code>talos enroll</code> (and on <code>talos run</code> when no credential): uses <code>TALOS_ENROLLMENT_TOKEN</code> if set, otherwise prints the user code for an admin to approve in Prometheus and waits.</li><li>Credential stored under <code>LOCAL_DIR</code> state (git-ignored, owner-only permissions on both platforms); never logged.</li><li>README for Talos and gaia-mcp; stdlib only.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests with a fake Gaia for both enrollment paths, restart with a stored credential, refresh and rotation. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> agent discovery.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4388, agaia-4389</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4399	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	712014526af0-7d1c-cccd-ee6dc2488b11	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	9ee45c966af1-64a9-1bb8-539f949f076a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 00:32:56	adt	0	0
f56af6936af7-7919-f6fb-533b37c03e67	PowerSelect: own select test helpers instead of importing ember-power-select's	2026-11-13 13:34:45	2026-11-13 20:09:38	0	<p>24 test files import ember-power-select / ember-basic-dropdown test helpers (<code>selectChoose</code>, <code>selectSearch</code>, <code>removeMultipleOption</code>, <code>clearSelected</code>, …) directly, so any change to the select ripples through them.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add <code>tests/helpers/select.js</code> with our own helpers (choose, search, remove option, clear, open, read selected/options), targeting the <code>AppUi::Select</code> <code>data-test-*</code> hooks from #4523. They may wrap the power-select helpers internally.</li>\n<li>Move every acceptance step file and integration test to them (agents, global search, sidebar project, conversation, issue create/assignee, profile, project members, roles, settings email/issue-statuses, workflows, <code>application-header-test.js</code>, <code>language-test.js</code>, <code>field-delegation-scopes-test.js</code>). Review <code>tests/test-helper.js</code> and <code>tests/helpers/test-helpers-legacy-paths.js</code>.</li>\n<li>Done when only <code>tests/helpers/select.js</code> (and <code>test-helper.js</code> if setup needs it) references <code>ember-power-select</code>/<code>ember-basic-dropdown</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Order: after #4523 and after the modal migrations #4517–#4521, which edit some of the same step files.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4524	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	e5115ea36af7-581a-5a96-373635bd4e9c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-13 20:09:39	aprom	0	0
35ba4dc16ae8-879a-51f2-b43f89a4fa28	Agent detail page fails with 404 and a non-JSON 'PhalconException' response	2026-11-02 16:20:05	2026-11-02 19:16:43	0	<p>Opening an agent's detail page (<code>app.agent.page</code>) fails. The console shows <code>Error while processing route: app.agent.page Unexpected token 'P', "PhalconExc"... is not valid JSON</code> and a 404. Gaia's <code>public/index.php</code> (~l.233) catches <code>\\Phalcon\\Exception</code> and prints <code>PhalconException: &lt;message&gt;</code> as plain text, so one of the page's requests hits a Phalcon error. The JSON error fix in Gaia is a separate request issue.</p><p><strong>What the page loads</strong> (<code>routes/app/agent/page.js</code>)</p><ul><li><code>agent</code> with <code>query (Agent.id : id)</code> and <code>rels user,sponsor</code>, then <code>userrole</code> (rels role), <code>membership</code> (rels project) and <code>useridentity</code> by <code>userId</code>.</li><li>The page's boxes load their own data too: Credentials (aprom-4045), Tools and Skills (4036), Workflows (4059), Activities (4242) and Identities (4037).</li><li>When a query fails, the route's <code>catch</code> calls <code>errorManager.handleError</code> and returns <code>undefined</code>, and <code>setupController</code> then destructures it.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Find the failing request: run each one against the local Gaia and read the Phalcon message. Fix the Prometheus request: the query, rels or field names it uses.</li><li>If the cause is in Gaia, not in the request, stop and report the failing request and its Phalcon message in a comment, so a Gaia issue can be filed.</li><li>Make the route handle a failed load cleanly: an error message or the not-found page, never a crash in <code>setupController</code>.</li><li>Check the edit route (<code>routes/app/agent/edit.js</code>), which uses the same agent query.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>The detail page opens for an agent with and without a sponsor, roles, projects and identities.</li><li>A failed load shows an error instead of a broken page.</li><li>An acceptance test covers opening the page.</li></ul><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4250	2026-11-09	2026-11-02	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	895b6f946ae8-73b7-1ab1-f72f74fcc27d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-02 19:16:42	aprom	0	0
f60d9da46afa-b805-5654-1bb57ca08641	Use AppUi::Avatar in the user and actor relate fields	2026-11-16 11:28:54	2026-11-17 10:09:09	0	<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px; image with an initials fallback, agent look built in). The relate renderers show people as a 25px raw image and agents through <code>Agent::Avatar</code>; <code>relate-user</code> passes no user, so an agent's picture never shows.</p><ul><li><code>components/related-fields/relate-user.hbs</code>: one <code>AppUi::Avatar @size="xs"</code> for people and agents, with <code>(hash id=@data.value name=@data.label)</code> (add <code>type</code> when <code>@data.isAgent</code>); keep the sponsor text.</li><li><code>components/related-fields/relate-actor.hbs</code>: same for <code>kind</code> user and agent (<code>@data.user</code> for agents); the expression icon stays.</li><li>Remove <code>.user-relate-icon</code> (<code>styles/modules/form-fields.scss:226</code>) if unused afterwards, and the <code>.relate-user.relate-agent .agent-avatar</code> size rule (<code>styles/modules/agent.scss:97</code>), which would override the avatar size; keep the sponsor line-height aligned.</li><li>Check select rows in issue create (assignee), the workflow properties panel (actor) and agent sponsor pickers: same row height, no overflow (aprom-4283).</li><li>Update tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> people and agents show 20px AppUi avatars in these selects (agents with their picture when they have one); rows don't grow.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4616	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da787