a53b73256af7-ea0a-5be9-d6ed7313a5d1	Docs: Doccontent resource (Yjs state, HTML and plain text) and drop Doc.body	2026-11-13 14:11:49	2026-11-13 20:17:40	0	<p>Docs become real-time co-edited documents. A doc's content is a Yjs CRDT state kept live by a collab server and saved to Gaia. The content gets its own resource so that the frequent autosaves don't rewrite the doc metadata, aren't copied into the audit log (<code>auditBehavior</code> stores old and new values of every changed field) and never travel with list queries.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Doccontent</code> (table <code>doccontent</code>), following <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code> (exemplar gaia#264, the Doc resource): <code>docId</code> varchar(36) required, <code>projectId</code> varchar(36) required (the doc's project, for the ACL group), <code>state</code> text nullable (base64-encoded Yjs update), <code>html</code> text nullable, <code>plainText</code> text nullable, <code>byteSize</code> int, plus the standard id, dates, createdUser, modifiedUser and deleted fields. Behaviours: createdUser, modifiedUser, dateCreated, dateModified, softDelete. <strong>No auditBehavior.</strong></li><li>Relationships: <code>doc</code> hasOne Doc (docId); inverse <code>content</code> hasOne Doccontent on <code>Doc</code>.</li><li>Validation: one Doccontent per doc (a second create for the same <code>docId</code> fails validation); <code>docId</code> must be a doc in the same <code>projectId</code>.</li><li>Remove the <code>body</code> field from <code>Doc</code> metadata and its api-tester cases. Existing doc rows are test data only, so their body is dropped.</li><li>ACL metadata <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via projectId, permissions <code>doccontent.get/create/update/delete</code>. No permission seed SQL.</li><li>Model, empty controller, <code>core/config/models.php</code>, <code>core/config/routes.php</code>, <code>routes.v1.json</code>, backend api placeholders and regenerated outputs as in B.md. api-tester harness/seed rows plus acl.json (member with and without doccontent.*, non-member) and client.json cases (create, get by docId, update, duplicate docId rejected).</li><li><code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>: D-002 (the Yjs state in Doccontent is the master copy; <code>html</code> and <code>plainText</code> are derived copies for export, search and AI, written by the collab server and never edited directly; base64 in text because the REST API is JSON), D-003 (content is written with the connected user's own token, so Gaia ACL and modifiedUser stay authoritative; no service account), D-004 (one merged snapshot row per doc, no update log).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a project member with doccontent.* can create, read and update one content row per doc; non-members are denied; Doc has no body field; the regenerated docs and graph have no drift.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> version history, lock enforcement (separate issue), sharing, full-text search.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 13 (A standard new-resource bundle per B.md (metadata, model, controller, config, routes, api-tester cases) plus removing Doc.body and the decisions doc; splitting it would leave a half resource that breaks dev.)</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4526	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	a489fe216af7-ea0a-5be9-d65370042b0c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	e063bb946af7-f535-42e6-db50d640d785	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-13 20:17:40	agaia	0	0
febbd5f56afa-b805-5654-c25e4c594d14	Use AppUi::Avatar on the agent list and agent page	2026-11-16 11:29:02	2026-11-16 13:55:21	0	<p>We are adopting the Component Library: every user picture uses <code>&lt;AppUi::Avatar @user={{...}} @size=... /&gt;</code> (<code>components/app-ui/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>, sizes xs 20, s 30, m 40, l 96px). It renders <code>Agent::Avatar</code> for agents itself, plus the robot marker when the agent has a picture.</p><ul><li><code>templates/app/agent/index.hbs:49</code> <code>Agent::Avatar @user=agent.user</code> (36px) -&gt; <code>AppUi::Avatar @user=agent.user @size="m"</code>; keep the 10px gap to the name (<code>.agents-list .agent-cell</code> in agent.scss, move it to the wrapper).</li><li><code>templates/app/agent/page.hbs:54</code> and <code>:58</code> <code>Agent::Avatar @large</code> (96px), inside <code>User::Edit::ProfilePicture</code> and its fallback -&gt; <code>@size="l"</code>; the upload click and crop flow keep working.</li><li>Remove agent.scss page rules that only sized these avatars, if unused afterwards. Keep <code>Agent::Avatar</code> itself (AppUi::Avatar uses it).</li><li>Update the agent list and page tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the agent list shows 40px and the agent page 96px avatars with the agent look; uploading a picture still works and shows it.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4616</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4617	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	5cad96756afa-a6df-0e26-2d2ff706492e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 13:55:21	aprom	0	0
45c4bbc96ae8-879a-51f2-2bd786ebfdb8	Agents: upload a profile picture, and show it instead of the robot avatar	2026-11-02 16:20:21	2026-11-02 17:01:37	0	<p>An agent is a user (users.type = Agent), so it has the user's <code>profilePicture</code>, but the agent pages give no way to set it. <code>Agent::Avatar</code> takes no user and always draws the robot, so a picture wouldn't show either.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>On the agent detail page header (<code>templates/app/agent/page.hbs</code> ~l.40), reuse <code>User::Edit::ProfilePicture</code> (<code>components/user/edit/profile-picture.hbs</code>) and <code>User::ProfilePictureCropper</code> with the user page's flow: <code>controllers/app/user/page.js</code> <code>uploadImage</code> (~l.307, type and size checks from <code>ENV.app.upload.profilePicture</code>) and <code>applyCrop</code> (~l.349: set the cropped base64 on <code>profilePicture</code>, save the user, roll back on error). Apply it to the agent's user (<code>agent.user</code>). Don't copy the code: move the shared part into a helper or service if both controllers need it.</li><li>Gate the edit control on <code>user.update</code>.</li><li><code>Agent::Avatar</code>: take the user and show its picture when there is one, the robot otherwise. Keep the AGENT badge next to it. Update the callers that have a user at hand: agent list rows, the detail header, and the aprom-4244 badge places.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>On an agent's page, a user with <code>user.update</code> can upload and crop a picture, and it shows after a reload.</li><li>Agents without a picture still show the robot.</li><li>Integration tests cover both avatar cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a picture field on the create form.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4252	2026-11-09	2026-11-02	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	9585b9d36ae8-73b7-1ab1-20327212acac	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-02 17:01:38	aprom	0	0
b72a6d626af7-ea0a-5be9-45074d115d3a	External Request: Docs collab server: self-contained collab/ package (Hocuspocus) with Gaia auth and Doccontent persistence	2026-11-13 14:12:07	2026-11-16 07:45:55	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Projects4Me Docs need Google-Docs-style co-editing. Each doc is a Yjs CRDT document that must be held in memory, synced between browsers and saved to Gaia. The relay can't do this (D-001 locked stateless relay, D-002 browsers never publish), so a collab server is added to this repo as a <strong>self-contained package in <code>collab/</code></strong>: its own process, port and container, sharing no code or dependencies with the relay, so it can later move to its own repo by moving the folder.</p><ul><li><strong>Isolation:</strong> its own <code>collab/package.json</code> (dependencies <code>@hocuspocus/server</code>, <code>yjs</code>, <code>@tiptap/html</code> and the Tiptap extensions below, approved for this module; pick versions that run on Node 18, Hermes' runtime), its own entrypoint <code>collab/server.js</code>, its own Dockerfile and docker-compose service. No imports from the relay's <code>src/</code> and no changes to relay code: its own small Gaia client module, modelled on <code>src/auth/gaia-session.js</code>.</li><li><strong>ADR D-016</strong> in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code>: the collab server lives in <code>collab/</code> as a separate process; it holds Yjs documents and awareness in memory only and persists only through Gaia; the relay rules D-001 to D-015 are unchanged. It moves to its own repo when it takes on agents or export, or when its releases start to clash with the relay's.</li><li><code>CLAUDE.md</code>: scope the rule "Hermes stays a locked relay: no domain logic, no storage" to the relay (<code>src/</code>), and add a short <code>collab/</code> section (what it may do, its own package.json, no imports across the two).</li><li>Root test script also runs <code>collab/</code> tests, so the existing hermes test command covers both.</li><li>Document name contract: <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>. The client sends the user's Gaia OAuth access token as the Hocuspocus token. Never log tokens or document content.</li><li>onAuthenticate: call Gaia <code>GET /api/v1/user/me</code> with the token. Reject without <code>doc.get</code> in <code>aclPermissions</code>, then <code>GET /api/v1/doc/&lt;id&gt;</code> with the same token (reject on 403/404). The connection is read-only when the user lacks <code>doc.update</code> or the doc is <code>locked</code>; updates from read-only connections are dropped by the server.</li><li>onLoadDocument: load the Doccontent for the doc (<code>GET /api/v1/doccontent</code> filtered by docId) and apply the base64 <code>state</code>; start empty if there is none. Unload a doc from memory after it has been saved and nobody is connected.</li><li>onStoreDocument (debounce about 2 s, max 10 s): encode the state and create or PATCH the Doccontent <code>state</code> and <code>byteSize</code>. After about 30 s without changes and on the last disconnect, also write <code>html</code> and <code>plainText</code>, generated from the editor fragment only (other shared types in the Y.Doc, such as the review <code>notes</code> map, are saved with the state but not rendered). Use the token of a connected user who has write access; on 401, try another connected writer.</li><li><strong>Schema</strong> in <code>collab/schema.js</code>, matching the Prometheus editor: StarterKit, Underline, Link, Table/TableRow/TableHeader/TableCell, TaskList/TaskItem, and two marks <code>suggestionInsert</code> / <code>suggestionDelete</code> (attrs <code>id</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>authorId</code>, <code>actedFor</code>, <code>requestId</code>, <code>reason</code>, <code>createdAt</code>; rendered as <code>&lt;ins data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;del data-suggestion-id&gt;</code>). Document it in <code>collab/README.md</code> with the env config (<code>GAIA_URL</code>, <code>COLLAB_PORT</code>) and how to run it.</li><li>Unit tests with a stubbed Gaia: rejected token, missing doc.get, read-only for no doc.update and for locked, load applies stored state, store creates then updates the content, html/plainText written on idle and on last disconnect.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two clients editing <code>doc:&lt;id&gt;</code> converge; after a restart the content reloads from Gaia; unauthorized users can't connect; read-only users can't change the document; the relay's tests and image are unchanged apart from the test script.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> access changes while connected (separate issue), agents as server-side peers, version snapshots, comments, scaling beyond one instance.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4526</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 13 (A new self-contained service package: entrypoint, auth, Gaia client/persistence and schema modules, its package.json, Dockerfile and compose service, README, ADR, CLAUDE.md, root test script and two test files. Auth and persistence can&#x27;t ship apart, because the server is unusable without both.)</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4528	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	done	medium	861790376ad5-1449-a602-a25bd5e6e2b8	b66d76d16af7-ea0a-5be9-ee5080a2cdac	\N	87099ee46ad5-1449-a602-5f7a1f6605b7	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	ad93b4626af7-5b5b-7458-5ea290d7a1b7	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 07:45:55	ah	0	0
bfc117f46af7-ea0a-5be9-7c2f44d86647	External Request: Docs collab server: internal access-change endpoint, client messages and write limits	2026-11-13 14:12:15	2026-11-16 10:46:56	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>When a doc is locked or deleted, people who already have it open must switch to read-only or be closed at once. Otherwise their edits keep spreading to others in memory while Gaia refuses to save them. Gaia tells the collab server (<code>collab/</code>) through a server-to-server call; the collab server re-checks each connection with Gaia and informs the clients.</p><ul><li><code>POST /internal/docs/:docId/access</code> on the collab server's HTTP port, authenticated with a shared secret (<code>COLLAB_SECRET</code> env, header <code>X-Collab-Secret</code>, compared in constant time). Body <code>{reason: locked|unlocked|deleted|access}</code>. Returns 202. Rejects without the secret.</li><li>On a call: for every connection to <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>, re-check with Gaia using that connection's token (same checks as onAuthenticate). Switch it to read-only or back to editable, or close it when the doc is gone or access was lost.</li><li>Stateless messages to clients (JSON, documented in <code>collab/README.md</code> as the contract with Prometheus): <code>{type: 'access', readOnly: bool, reason}</code>, <code>{type: 'deleted'}</code>, <code>{type: 'unsaved', since: ISO date}</code> when saving to Gaia has failed for over 2 minutes (and <code>{type: 'saved'}</code> once it recovers). Retry failed saves with back-off.</li><li>Limits: maximum size per incoming Yjs update (env, default 512 KB) and a per-connection update rate limit; offending connections are closed with a reason. Check the WebSocket <code>Origin</code> against an allowed list from env.</li><li>Add an ADR entry next to D-016 for the internal endpoint and its secret.</li><li>Unit tests with a stubbed Gaia: missing or wrong secret rejected, lock switches connections to read-only and sends the message, unlock restores editing, delete closes connections, unsaved message after the save-failure threshold, oversized update rejected.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> after the endpoint is called for a locked doc, open editors stop being able to change it within a second and are told why.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-doc sharing changes (later), multi-instance coordination.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> ah-4528</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4529	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	done	medium	861790376ad5-1449-a602-a25bd5e6e2b8	b66d76d16af7-ea0a-5be9-ee5080a2cdac	\N	87099ee46ad5-1449-a602-5f7a1f6605b7	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	0f4a00216afa-fd60-81fa-05d11e4b7c18	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 10:46:56	ah	0	0
5cb110f46af1-a2e3-a09f-64ac861b2282	Service identity: prove the relay keeps working while Gaia enrollment fails, and document the deploy settings	2026-11-09 00:52:44	2026-11-09 01:01:24	0	<p>A follow-up to ah-4395 (PR projects4me/hermes#7) from reviewing that PR. The identity is off unless <code>HERMES_CREDENTIAL_FILE</code> is set and can't crash the relay. Two things are missing.</p><p><b>1. A test that the relay doesn't depend on the identity.</b> The ah-4395 tests run <code>ServiceIdentity</code> on its own, and <code>tests/app.test.js</code> is unchanged. Add in-process tests that start Hermes the way <code>server.js</code> does: app plus identity, with a credential file configured, against <code>tests/support/stub-gaia.js</code>. Then check that while Gaia enrollment fails:</p><ul><li>a socket client connects and authenticates (stub <code>/api/v1/user/me</code> answers);</li><li><code>POST /publish</code> with <code>HERMES_SECRET</code> delivers to the room;</li><li><code>/health</code> answers 200.</li></ul><p>Cover each way enrollment can fail:</p><ul><li>Gaia unreachable (connection refused);</li><li>404 on <code>/api/v1/serviceenrollment</code> (endpoint not deployed);</li><li>500 on the enrollment request;</li><li>an unreadable or broken credential file.</li></ul><p>Each case should be logged and retried, with no unhandled rejection. To make this testable, move the start-up wiring in <code>server.js</code> into a small function, for example <code>startHermes(config, deps)</code>, that the tests call. <code>server.js</code> then just calls it. Don't change the identity's behaviour.</p><p>This matters before ah-4396, where socket auth starts using the service token and the identity is no longer optional.</p><p><b>2. Deploy documentation.</b> Add a "Service identity" deploy section to <code>README.md</code> or <code>docs/architecture/architecture.md</code>. The helm chart (<code>values-dev.yaml</code>) lives on the OVH server, not in this repo, so this issue only documents what it needs:</p><ul><li><code>HERMES_CREDENTIAL_FILE</code> must be on a persistent volume the container user can write to. Without one, every pod restart loses the credential, and Hermes logs a new user code that an admin must approve.</li><li><code>GAIA_ENROLLMENT_TOKEN</code> is single-use and expires 15 minutes after it is issued (Gaia D-070). Issue it just before the first deploy that sets <code>HERMES_CREDENTIAL_FILE</code>. Leaving it in the values afterwards has no effect.</li><li>Run one replica per credential file; two pods sharing a file would each enroll and rotate.</li><li>The steps to turn it on: issue the token in Projects4Me, set both env vars and the volume, deploy, check the log for "Hermes enrolled with Gaia", then remove the token from the values.</li><li>To turn it off, unset <code>HERMES_CREDENTIAL_FILE</code>.</li></ul><p><b>Acceptance:</b> the new tests pass with the full suite, and the deploy section covers the points above.</p><p><b>Out of scope:</b> changing the helm chart on the server, exponential backoff, and changes to the identity's behaviour.</p><p><b>Depends on:</b> ah-4395</p><p><b>Estimated files:</b> 3–4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4409	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	861790376ad5-1449-a602-a25bd5e6e2b8	d59707896af0-cd0b-cccd-6c0c771196c7	\N	87099ee46ad5-1449-a602-5f7a1f6605b7	Agent Achilles	Agent Agamemnon	b19f6d296af1-a2e3-a09f-7e132f44daa3	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 01:01:24	ah	0	0
3d9f68636ae8-879a-51f2-7f0d9851df90	External Request: Return Phalcon exceptions as JSON:API errors instead of plain text	2026-11-02 16:20:13	2026-11-02 18:55:49	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Prometheus (idea "Agents In Prometheus", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>A Prometheus needs every Gaia error to come back as JSON. Today a <code>\\Phalcon\\Exception</code> that reaches <code>public/index.php</code> (~l.233) is printed as plain text, <code>PhalconException: &lt;message&gt;</code>, keeping whatever status was set. Ember Data can't parse that, so the user sees <code>Unexpected token 'P'... is not valid JSON</code> instead of the real error. This hid the cause of the agent detail page 404 in Prometheus.</p><p><strong>Proposed change</strong> (please accept, adapt or decline)</p><ul><li>Handle <code>\\Phalcon\\Exception</code> like the <code>\\Gaia\\Exception\\*</code> classes: a JSON:API <code>errors</code> document with the Content-Type the other errors use.</li><li>Status: 404 for dispatcher not-found errors, 500 for the rest.</li><li>Keep the raw Phalcon message (it can name tables, columns or PHQL) out of the response unless debug is on. Log it on the server.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A request that raises a Phalcon exception gets a JSON:API error body with a 404 or 500 status.</li><li>A test covers both statuses.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> fixing the exceptions themselves.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4251	2026-11-09	2026-11-02	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	77c73c366ae8-73b7-51f2-b6608da2587e	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	0df1c3736ae8-ddce-02b1-bff1d1c95a56	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-02 18:55:49	agaia	0	0
a58b7df76af1-31f2-1bb8-e1725a3c604a	ai gaia-dev: run gaia-dev generators and checks against the current checkout, so headless Talos runs can regenerate graph.json and docs/generated	2026-11-09 00:02:45	2026-11-09 00:54:28	0	<p><b>Problem:</b> Headless Talos runs have no PHP runner. When a Gaia change needs <code>docs/generated</code> or <code>graph.json</code> regenerated, the agent blocks: agaia-4388 (Agent Achilles) blocked for this reason. The shared gaia-dev container mounts the Projects4Me checkout, not the run's worktree. The manual workaround was a throwaway <code>gaia-gaia-test</code> container that mounts the run checkout plus the <code>gaia_vendor</code> volume.</p><p><b>Change:</b> add <code>ai gaia-dev &lt;args…&gt;</code>, which:</p><ul><li>resolves the checkout the same way <code>ai test</code> does (<code>P4M_WORKSPACE</code>);</li><li>runs gaia-dev in a throwaway container with that checkout mounted, so it writes to the worktree and never to the shared container or Projects4Me;</li><li>handles the <code>dev-tools</code> → <code>.dev-tools-runtime</code> symlink in .runs worktrees;</li><li>allows at least <code>graph export</code>, <code>docs generate</code>, their <code>--check</code> forms, <code>check api-cases</code> and <code>check resource &lt;Name&gt;</code>;</li><li>does not allow anything that touches the database, such as <code>migration migrate</code>. See the adt-4150 incident and the rule to never run <code>p4m db migrate</code> from Pr4M.</li></ul><p>Allow <code>ai gaia-dev</code> for Talos agents and mention it in the run-tests / ship-issue guidance, so agents regenerate files instead of blocking.</p><p><b>Acceptance:</b></p><ul><li>From a <code>.runs/issue-N</code> worktree, <code>ai gaia-dev docs generate</code> updates that worktree's <code>docs/generated</code> and leaves Pr4M/gaia unchanged.</li><li>Unit tests cover the argument allowlist and the mount path.</li></ul><p>Found while unblocking agaia-4388 (PR projects4me/gaia#257).</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4407	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	712014526af0-7d1c-cccd-ee6dc2488b11	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	5745f6276af1-601c-e3a5-1cc89515a0ad	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 00:54:29	adt	0	0
d11085946af7-ea0a-5be9-1a38ed146e5a	Docs: publish doc.created/updated/deleted live events and notify the collab server on lock and delete	2026-11-13 14:12:33	2026-11-17 07:37:28	0	<p>Docs lists and open doc pages must update live when a doc is created, renamed, locked or deleted, and open editors must turn read-only as soon as a doc is locked. Gaia publishes doc events through Hermes and calls the collab server's internal access endpoint.</p><ul><li><code>DocLiveEventsComponent</code> in <code>app/api/v1/controllers/components/events/</code>, following <code>docs/generated/bundles/E.md</code> (precedent <code>UserAccessLiveEventsComponent</code>, <code>IdeaLiveEventsComponent</code>): publish <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code> (with the changed field names: title, locked, ownerId, parent and status as they exist) and <code>doc.deleted</code>, scoped to the doc's project. Add the names to <code>support/EventNames.php</code>; they must match <code>hermes/src/contract/names.js</code>, so this ships together with the Hermes allowlist change.</li><li>New <code>CollabNotifier</code> class (one class owns the collab server's URL, secret and transport, like <code>HermesPublisher</code>): <code>POST {COLLAB_URL}/internal/docs/{docId}/access</code> with header <code>X-Collab-Secret</code> and body <code>{reason: locked|unlocked|deleted}</code>. Called after a doc's <code>locked</code> changes and after a doc is deleted. Config via <code>getenv()</code> in <code>config/*.php</code>; never logged.</li><li>Side effects fail open: Hermes or the collab server being down must not fail the user's write; log the failure.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the component (right event and payload per change, no event for unchanged saves) and the notifier (sends on lock, unlock and delete; failures don't throw), with the transports stubbed.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> renaming, locking or deleting a doc publishes the matching event; locking or deleting calls the collab server; both failing leaves the write successful.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> events for Doccontent saves, sharing events.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4527, ah-4530, ah-4529</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4531	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	pending	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	a489fe216af7-ea0a-5be9-d65370042b0c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	8800ea226afa-7438-35fc-243ff17d4660	2f68d74162c6-8e43-a8e0-a879eaeffc5e	2026-11-17 07:37:28	agaia	0	0
eb5b73a16ae8-fb0c-741d-8526e1b3528e	External Request: Talos ideas: post the working notice with message kind 'working'	2026-11-02 19:13:47	2026-11-06 20:58:21	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Prometheus (idea "Add animation on ideas", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>When Talos starts a turn on a Gaia idea it posts "&lt;Agent&gt; is working on it." as an idea message of kind <code>system</code>. Other real notices also use <code>system</code> (e.g. from <code>lib/ideas/approval.py</code>), so the UI can't tell this temporary status apart from them. The idea page needs a dedicated kind to show it as an animated indicator and hide it once the reply arrives.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/ideas/client.py</code> <code>set_state</code>: post the notice with role/kind <code>working</code> instead of <code>system</code> (the body stays "&lt;display name&gt; is working on it."). Update the module docstring that describes the kinds.</li><li>Check that nothing in <code>lib/ideas/</code> (<code>policy.py</code>, <code>conversation.py</code>) treats the new kind as a user or agent message: turns start only on <code>kind: message</code>, and history replays only the <code>user</code>/<code>agent</code> roles.</li><li><code>talos/tests/test_gaia_ideas.py</code>: update the expectations that assert <code>("system", "Agent Nestor is working on it.")</code> and add a test that a <code>working</code> message neither starts a turn nor shows up in the replayed history.</li><li><code>talos/README.md</code> (Idea client section): say that the turn starts with a <code>kind: working</code> notice.</li></ul><p><strong>Contract:</strong> idea messages gain the kind <code>working</code>, which the Prometheus idea page renders as a transient indicator. Gaia needs no change (<code>Ideamessage.kind</code> is free text).</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a new turn on a Gaia idea posts one message with kind <code>working</code>; replies, errors and approval notices keep their current kinds; <code>ai test dev-tools</code> passes on Windows and Linux.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the sim client, live progress events.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4254	2026-11-10	2026-11-03	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	ea9f39526ae8-fb0c-741d-cc93d6052db4	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	1ab869a96ae8-863a-741d-452ab16a733f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-06 20:58:22	adt	0	0
daeb29c46af7-ea0a-5be9-1b5ae837a862	External Request: Docs: Tiptap editor component with toolbar, tables, checklists, outline and suggestion marks	2026-11-13 14:12:42	2026-11-18 15:00:53	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>The Docs module needs a structured rich-text editor that can co-edit through Yjs. Toast UI can't, so Docs uses Tiptap (open-source packages only). This issue builds the editor as a standalone component. Real-time wiring and suggestion behaviour come in later issues.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>@tiptap/core</code>, <code>@tiptap/starter-kit</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-underline</code>, <code>-link</code>, <code>-table</code>, <code>-table-row</code>, <code>-table-header</code>, <code>-table-cell</code>, <code>-task-list</code>, <code>-task-item</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>utils/docs/schema.js</code>: the single list of extensions, plus two marks <code>suggestionInsert</code> and <code>suggestionDelete</code> (attrs <code>id</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>authorId</code>, <code>actedFor</code>, <code>requestId</code>, <code>reason</code>, <code>createdAt</code>; rendered as <code>&lt;ins data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;del data-suggestion-id&gt;</code> with a <code>doc-suggestion</code> class). The collab server builds the stored HTML from the same list (<code>hermes/collab/schema.js</code>), so a change here needs the same change there.</li><li><code>Docs::Editor</code> (<code>components/docs/editor.{js,hbs}</code>): mounts Tiptap on an element. Args <code>@content</code> (initial HTML), <code>@editable</code>, <code>@extensions</code> (extra extensions added to the schema list), <code>@onReady(editor)</code>. Destroys the editor on teardown. No persistence.</li><li><code>Docs::Toolbar</code>: bold, italic, underline, strike, H1 to H3, bullet and ordered list, checklist, blockquote, code block, link, insert table and add/remove rows and columns. Buttons are <code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code> with Font Awesome 4 icons, <code>aria-pressed</code> for active marks, and the toolbar is hidden when not editable. It yields a slot for extra button groups.</li><li><code>Docs::Outline</code>: a <code>col-md-4</code> side box listing the document's headings; clicking or pressing Enter scrolls to the heading.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code> (square edges, colours from <code>variables.scss</code> only), including the suggestion marks (inserted text underlined, deleted text struck through, in existing colours). Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Integration tests: renders the content, a toolbar action applies a mark, read-only hides the toolbar and blocks typing, the outline lists headings and scrolls, suggestion marks render with their attributes.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the component renders and edits formatted content, tables and checklists, renders suggestion marks, and follows <code>docs/ui/design-system.md</code>.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> saving, real-time collaboration, accepting/rejecting suggestions, images and attachments, comments.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 11 (Editor, toolbar and outline components (js+hbs each), the schema module, styles, translations and tests. The toolbar and outline are small and only make sense with the editor they drive.)</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4532	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	deferred	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	da3e78706af7-ea0a-5be9-52b16668b269	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	bce8a1046af7-baa9-a180-1e0da063f9a1	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-18 15:26:20	aprom	0	0
154bf5326ae8-863a-741d-d1d6690edd77	Issue detail: editing an estimate doesn't work (description handler wired without fn)	2026-11-02 19:14:29	2026-11-03 10:16:58	0	<p>On the issue detail page, editing an existing estimate (pencil icon in the Estimates box) doesn't work. Editing a time log works.</p><p><strong>Cause</strong>: in <code>app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> the edit-estimate modal (~401-433) passes <code>@onContentChange={{@selectStatic this.editingLog 'description'}}</code> to <code>AppUi::ToastUi</code>, without <code>fn</code>. So <code>selectStatic</code> runs once during render instead of being passed as the change handler. The edit-timelog modal (~549) correctly uses <code>{{fn @selectStatic this.editingLog 'description'}}</code>. The ToastUi there also has a stray <code>@label</code> argument that the time log one doesn't have.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Wire the edit-estimate description with <code>fn</code>, matching the edit-timelog modal.</li><li>In <code>editLog</code> (<code>issue-details.js</code> ~655): when validation fails, keep the modal open with the error instead of closing it. Add a catch on <code>log.save()</code> that shows the error and calls <code>rollbackAttributes()</code>. When the modal is closed without saving, roll back the unsaved changes so the list doesn't show values that were never saved. Ignore a second Save while one is pending.</li><li>Check the estimate save end to end against Gaia (PATCH of the timelog with <code>context: est</code>) and fix anything else that stops it from saving.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Start with an acceptance test (Mirage) that edits an estimate's time and description and asserts the saved values and the 'Time estimated has been updated' message. It fails before the fix.</li><li>Editing an estimate's days/hours/minutes and description saves and shows the new values.</li><li>Cancelling the edit leaves the estimate unchanged; a failed 