ea54a5066af7-ea0a-5be9-e42b1cb24d0f	External Request: Docs: real-time co-editing on the doc page with autosave status and offline recovery	2026-11-13 14:12:58	2026-11-18 15:05:08	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Connects the Docs editor to the collab server (<code>hermes/collab</code>), so several people edit one doc live and changes save themselves with no Save button.</p><ul><li>New dependencies: <code>yjs</code>, <code>@hocuspocus/provider</code>, <code>y-indexeddb</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration</code> (approved for this module).</li><li><code>config/environment.js</code>: <code>ENV.docs.collabUrl</code> (no secrets).</li><li><code>services/doc-collab.js</code>: <code>open(docId)</code> creates a Y.Doc, an <code>IndexeddbPersistence</code> for offline recovery and a <code>HocuspocusProvider</code> (name <code>doc:&lt;docId&gt;</code>, token = the session's current access token; refresh it through <code>services/session.js</code> and reconnect before it expires). Exposes the Y.Doc, the provider's awareness, tracked <code>status</code> (connecting, saving, saved, offline) and <code>readOnly</code> (from the server). <code>close()</code> destroys both. One responsibility: the connection; no UI.</li><li>Doc page from aprom-4490 (<code>app.project.doc.page</code>): renders <code>Docs::Editor</code> with the Collaboration extension bound to the Y.Doc. Editable only when <code>acl</code> allows doc.update, the doc isn't locked and the server didn't mark the connection read-only. Opens on route enter and closes on exit. A new doc starts empty.</li><li><code>Docs::SaveStatus</code> in the record box header: "Saving…", "All changes saved", "Offline – changes are kept on this device".</li><li>Tests: the service with a stubbed provider (status transitions, readOnly, close on exit) and an acceptance test of the page in read-only and editable modes with the service stubbed (Mirage has no websocket).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> two browsers on the same doc see each other's edits live; reloading keeps the content; edits made offline sync after reconnecting; a locked doc, or a user without doc.update, gets a read-only editor.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> presence and cursors, live metadata and server messages (separate issues), version history.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4532, ah-4528, aprom-4489, aprom-4490</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4533	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	deferred	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	da3e78706af7-ea0a-5be9-52b16668b269	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	\N	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-18 15:05:08	aprom	0	0
4dc896e76ae8-879a-51f2-1d33a8cc7cf6	Agent create/edit: projects multi-select doesn't select, search or sort	2026-11-02 16:20:29	2026-11-02 19:36:58	0	<p>In the agent form's Access box (<code>templates/app/agent/create.hbs</code> ~l.173, shared by create and edit), the Projects list opens, but clicking a project doesn't select it, you can't search it, and the list isn't sorted. It stays a multi-select.</p><p><strong>What the code shows</strong></p><ul><li><code>FormFields::FieldRelateMulti</code> (<code>components/form-fields/field-relate-multi.hbs</code>) passes <code>@searchEnabled</code> on to <code>PowerSelectMultiple</code>, but the agent form doesn't set it. <code>@searchField="label"</code> is set.</li><li>The options come unsorted from <code>routes/app/agent/create.js</code> <code>loadOptions</code> (<code>store.query('project', {limit: -1})</code>, mapped to <code>{label, value}</code>).</li><li>Why a click doesn't select is unknown: <code>selectProjects</code> sets the tracked <code>selectedProjects</code>. Check the <code>AccessControl</code> wrapper (<code>@aclContext="membership.create"</code>), the <code>related-fields/relate-simple</code> option template, and whether the options array is rebuilt on each render. The Roles select next to it uses the same setup: check it too.</li></ul><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Fix the selection.</li><li>Turn on search for Projects and Roles.</li><li>Sort both lists by name: in the query if Gaia's sort fits, else when mapping.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Several projects and roles can be picked and removed.</li><li>Typing filters the list, and options are in alphabetical order.</li><li>The picks are saved and shown again on edit.</li><li>An integration or acceptance test covers picking and searching.</li></ul><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e