7d4196e96af0-7d1c-cccd-381dfa375260	External Request: Talos: discover Gaia agents and run them on delegated tokens	2026-11-08 20:41:33	2026-11-09 01:17:21	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Inter application Communication", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Talos stops naming Gaia agents locally (<code>gaiaAgent</code> in agent.json, <code>talos/lib/registry.py</code> ~l.131-165) and asks Gaia which agents it may run, with its runtime service token.</p><ul><li>Periodically list delegable agents and load each spec (reuse <code>talos/lib/agent_spec.py</code> <code>settings_from</code>), tool grants and skills.</li><li>Per agent, get a delegated token (Gaia delegation grant) and cache it; renew about 5 minutes before expiry; every Gaia call and the Hermes connection made for that agent's runs use it.</li><li>Gaia-declared agents take work from Gaia workflow run requests only (adt-4047 path); agent.json stays for Talos' own agents (Odysseus, Nestor, Agamemnon) with their own credentials. Remove <code>gaiaAgent</code> support and its README section (Hera moves to a workflow on the milestone-completed trigger, agaia-4271).</li><li>Agent disabled or delegation emptied in Gaia: stop starting new runs for it.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests: discovery adds and removes agents, token cache renewal, refusal handling. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> runtimes room (next issue).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4399, agaia-4391</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4400	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	712014526af0-7d1c-cccd-ee6dc2488b11	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	13d60ca86af1-efa6-2dd5-4a0f631f3588	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026