f378faa66af7-ea0a-5be9-e9d62f8e7b14	External Request: Docs: live doc metadata on list and page, and collab server messages (locked, deleted, not saved)	2026-11-13 14:13:07	2026-11-18 15:05:05	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Everything about a doc should update live: a rename or lock shows at once in the All Docs list and on the open page, a deleted doc closes, and editors learn immediately when they can no longer edit or when their changes aren't reaching the server.</p><ul><li>Register for Hermes <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code> and <code>doc.deleted</code> with <code>hermes.register(owner, projectId, handlers)</code> from the controllers of the All Docs list (aprom-4491) and the doc page (aprom-4490), following <code>docs/architecture/live-updates/</code>; filter on the doc id on the page (precedent <code>controllers/app/project/idea/page.js</code>). The list reloads or updates the affected row; the page reloads the doc record (title, lock). Add the registrations to the live-updates registration table.</li><li>Handle the collab server's stateless messages in <code>services/doc-collab.js</code> (contract in <code>hermes/collab/README.md</code>): <code>access</code> switches the editor to read-only or back and shows a Messenger notice with the reason ("This doc was locked"); <code>deleted</code> closes the connection and goes to the All Docs list with a notice; <code>unsaved</code>/<code>saved</code> drive a "Not saved to server yet" state in <code>Docs::SaveStatus</code>.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: handlers update the list and page (Hermes stubbed), each message type changes the editor state and notice as expected.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with two browsers, renaming or locking in one updates the other's list and page without reload; locking turns the other's open editor read-only with a notice; deleting closes it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> live updates for sharing (later).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4533, agaia-4531, aprom-4491</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4534	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	deferred	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	da3e78706af7-ea0a-5be9-52b16668b269	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	\N	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-18 15:05:05	aprom	0	0
880334646ae8-0360-4071-8e4396717745	gaia-mcp: look up agents and their spec	2026-11-02 21:03:04	2026-11-02 21:35:22	0	<p>Talos is starting to run agents defined in Gaia (Agent module, agaia-4027) instead of in local <code>agent.json</code> files. It needs to find an agent and read its spec. Gaia serves the spec as the read-only resource <code>GET /api/v1/agentspec/{agentId}</code> (agaia-4043; needs <code>agentspec.get</code>). The spec holds the role prompt, model config, limits, permission mode, tool grants and skills.</p><ul><li><code>gaia_list_agents</code>: the agents visible to the caller (id, name, email, purpose, account status).</li><li><code>gaia_get_agent_spec</code> (agent name, email or id): resolves the agent, then returns the agentspec document as is.</li><li>A plain method on the Gaia client (e.g. <code>Gaia.agent_spec(name_or_id)</code>) that both the tool and Talos (which imports gaia-mcp in-process, see <code>talos/lib/tracker.py</code>) can call.</li><li>Clear errors: unknown agent, several matches, or 403 when the caller lacks <code>agentspec.get</code> (say which permission is missing).</li><li>Code: <code>gaia-mcp/server.py</code>, README, unit tests with a stubbed Gaia.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> both tools listed and tested; the spec of an agent can be fetched by name.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> workflow and skill lookup tools; editing agents.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4260	2026-11-10	2026-11-03	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	e7acc8b06ae8-998a-64ae-1e1139f03fa8	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-02 21:35:23	adt	0	0
98a645316ae8-0360-4071-9ffa81d768f3	Talos: new agent kind 'events' that runs an agent once per Hermes event	2026-11-02 21:03:20	2026-11-02 21:25:20	0	<p>Talos agents run today on assigned issues (kind <code>issues</code>), ideas (<code>ideas</code>) or as an orchestrator. A retrospective agent must instead run when something happens in Gaia, starting with <code>milestone.completed</code>. Gaia already publishes that event via <code>MilestoneLiveEventsComponent</code>, project-scoped, and Hermes already allows it.</p><ul><li><code>registry.py</code>: add <code>events</code> to <code>KINDS</code>. Such an agent needs <code>name</code>, <code>gaiaEnv</code>, <code>projects</code> and <code>triggers</code>, a map of event name to <code>{prompt}</code>. It needs no <code>actions</code>, <code>acceptAssignmentsFrom</code> or <code>handoffTo</code>.</li><li>Subscribe to the trigger events in the agent's projects through the existing Hermes listener (<code>lib/hermes.py</code> <code>intents(project_ids, events)</code>), as the agent's own Gaia user.</li><li>On an event: render the trigger prompt with the event's fields (<code>{{projectName}}</code>, <code>{{projectShortcode}}</code>, <code>{{resourceId}}</code> and the event's changes, e.g. <code>{{name}}</code>) and run Claude once with the agent's role prompt and limits, using the runner, workspace and usage-pause machinery the other kinds use. No issue is claimed.</li><li>Run each (agent, event name, resource id) at most once: record it in the Talos db, so a re-sent or duplicate event (several projects, reconnects) doesn't run twice. Failures are logged and kept for <code>talos status</code>; there is no hand-off target.</li><li>README section; unit tests for loading, prompt rendering and dedupe (no Hermes or Claude needed).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> an events agent with a <code>milestone.completed</code> trigger runs once when a milestone in one of its projects is marked completed, and not again for the same milestone.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> replaying events missed while Talos was down; events other than those named in triggers; workflow-dispatched runs (adt-4047).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 9</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4262	2026-11-10	2026-11-03	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	fe12b5136ae8-0360-4071-734876991ed5	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-02 21:25:20	adt	0	0
903a6eb76ae8-0360-4071-7cfeca206c33	Talos: take an agent's role prompt, model and limits from its Gaia agentspec	2026-11-02 21:03:12	2026-11-03 05:40:51	0	<p>Agents are now defined in Gaia (Agent + agentspec, agaia-4027/4043), but Talos still reads every agent's role prompt, model and limits from <code>talos/agents/&lt;name&gt;/agent.json</code>. This issue lets an agent.json point at a Gaia agent and take those settings from its spec, so the definition lives in Gaia and is edited there.</p><ul><li>agent.json gains optional <code>gaiaAgent</code> (agent name or id). When set, <code>rolePrompt</code> and <code>model</code> are no longer required in <code>registry.py</code> <code>load_agent</code> (~l.130).</li><li>New module (e.g. <code>talos/lib/agent_spec.py</code>, single responsibility: spec to Talos settings) that maps the spec onto the <code>Agent</code> dataclass: role prompt, model (from modelConfig), maxTurns, permission mode. Validate the permission mode against Claude Code's modes and refuse unknown values instead of passing them through.</li><li>The spec is fetched with the agent's own credentials (its <code>gaiaEnv</code>) via gaia-mcp's <code>Gaia.agent_spec</code>. It is fetched when Talos starts and again before each run, so edits in Gaia take effect without a restart. If Gaia is unreachable, the run uses the last good spec and logs it; with no spec at all the agent is not started, with a clear error.</li><li>Machine-local settings stay in agent.json: gaiaEnv, projects, allowedTools/deniedTools, runner, parallelism. The spec's tool grants and skills are ignored for now (logged once).</li><li>README section; unit tests for the mapping, the fallback and the loader with and without <code>gaiaAgent</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> an agent with <code>gaiaAgent</code> runs with the role prompt and model set in Gaia; changing the role prompt in Gaia changes the next run; existing agents (Odysseus, Nestor, Agamemnon) load unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> skills, mapping tool grants to Claude Code tools, moving existing agents to Gaia.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4260, adt-4041</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4261	2026-11-10	2026-11-03	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	373445066ae9-0e2a-9418-5130e2459e78	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-03 05:40:51	adt	0	0
fce463086af7-ea0a-5be9-48774cc5f027	External Request: Docs: who's in the doc, live cursors and selections, 'is typing' and 'asking AI'	2026-11-13 14:13:16	2026-11-18 15:05:00	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Collaborators should see who else is in a doc, where they are working and when someone is waiting on AI, like Google Docs. This uses the collab server's awareness channel from <code>services/doc-collab.js</code>; nothing is stored.</p><ul><li>Dependency: <code>@tiptap/extension-collaboration-cursor</code> (approved for this module).</li><li>Awareness state: <code>{ user: { id, name, color }, typing: boolean, ai: null | 'ask' | 'review' }</code>. Pick the colour deterministically from the user id out of a fixed palette of existing <code>variables.scss</code> colours; no new colours. Expose a small setter on the service so other features can set <code>ai</code>.</li><li>Live cursors and selections in the editor, each with a name label in the user's colour (styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>).</li><li>A "who's in the doc" avatar stack in the record box header, reusing the existing avatar markup (<code>components/project/member-avatars.hbs</code> pattern, <code>userimage/get</code>). One entry per user even with several tabs, with a tooltip of the name.</li><li>Status line under the avatars: "<em>Name</em> is typing…" (set <code>typing</code> on local input, clear it after about 2 s), "<em>Name</em> is asking AI…" and "<em>Name</em> is running the AI Reviewer…" from <code>ai</code>.</li><li>Tests: the avatar stack de-duplicates users and hides the current user; the typing flag clears after the timeout; the ai flag shows the right text; the colour is stable for an id.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> with two users in a doc each sees the other's avatar, cursor, selection, typing and AI status, and these disap