9fcc69186ae9-639d-5b13-1e0076514a8b	Ideas: show the New idea button disabled while the Start an idea form is open	2026-11-03 07:43:27	2026-11-03 07:43:53	0	<p>The <strong>New idea</strong> button in the idea browser stays an active blue button while the user is already on the <em>Start an idea</em> form, so it looks as if it does something. While the form is open, it should look disabled and not be clickable.</p><ul><li><code>app/controllers/app/project/idea.js</code>: inject the <code>router</code> service and add an <code>isCreating</code> getter (YUIDoc) that is true when <code>router.currentRouteName === 'app.project.idea.create'</code>.</li><li><code>app/templates/app/project/idea.hbs</code> (box-tools, inside the existing <code>AccessControl @aclContext="idea.create"</code>): when <code>isCreating</code> is true, render <code>&lt;span class="btn btn-default btn-sm disabled" aria-disabled="true" data-new-idea&gt;</code> with the same icon and label instead of the <code>LinkTo</code>. Otherwise keep the current <code>LinkTo</code> with <code>btn btn-primary btn-sm</code>. Use only Bootstrap classes and add no new styles.</li><li>Acceptance test (Gherkin, ember-cli-yadda on Mirage): on the create page the <code>[data-new-idea]</code> button has the <code>disabled</code> class and is not a link. After you open an existing idea or cancel the form, it is the blue link again. Put any feature-only steps in a per-feature steps file, not <code>steps.js</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>On <code>app.project.idea.create</code>, the New idea button is grey (<code>btn-default disabled</code>), cannot be clicked or reached with Tab, and has <code>aria-disabled="true"</code>.</li><li>On the ideas index and on an idea page, the button looks and works as it does today.</li><li>The button still shows only for users with the <code>idea.create</code> permission.</li><li>Tests and lint pass.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any other chan