ge to the idea browser or the create form.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> create-open.png, idea-open.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4266	2026-11-10	2026-11-03	done	low	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	b43cc5046ae8-20b5-32a1-13b222266c79	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	1e250f536ae9-dc19-2c6d-eeec423a0bdf	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-03 10:47:19	aprom	0	0
064d4a386af7-4c57-5be9-6d94176239de	External Request: Docs AI endpoints: /docs/ask, /docs/complete and /docs/review	2026-11-13 14:13:26	2026-11-16 10:03:05	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Projects4Me Docs get AI help: answer a writer's request about selected text, complete the sentence being written, and review a whole document. Gaia (<code>core/services/LLM.php</code>) stays the only caller; it sends the text and returns the result to the editor.</p><ul><li>New router <code>routers/docs.py</code> (prefix <code>/docs</code>) with Pydantic request/response models, one service per use case in <code>services/</code>, prompts kept out of the router. Register it in <code>main.py</code>.</li><li><code>POST /docs/ask</code>: request <code>{instruction: str (required, max 1000), selectionHtml: str (max 8000), context: {title, headingPath: [str], before: str (max 2000), after: str (max 500)}}</code>. Response <code>{html: str}</code>: the replacement for the selection, using only the tags p, h1-h3, ul, ol, li, strong, em, u, s, a, blockquote, code, pre.</li><li><code>POST /docs/complete</code>: request <code>{title, headingPath, before (max 2000), after (max 500)}</code>. Response <code>{text: str}</code>: plain text continuing the sentence, at most about 200 characters, possibly empty. Uses a fast model from env (<code>ARES_DOCS_COMPLETE_MODEL</code>, default <code>claude-haiku-4-5-20251001</code>) with a low max-token limit, since it is called often.</li><li><code>POST /docs/review</code>: request <code>{title, text (max 60000, plain text with headings on their own lines)}</code>. Response <code>{findings: [{quote: str, category: unclear|open_question|inconsistency|missing|wording, message: str, replacement?: str}]}</code>, at most 20. <code>replacement</code> is the corrected text for <code>quote</code> when there is a concrete fix; without it the finding is a note. Every <code>quote</code> must be an exact substring of <code>text</code>: the service drops findings whose quote isn't found.</li><li>Model names and token limits come from env; extend the adapter so a service can pick its model.</li><li>Document text and the writer's instruction are untrusted input: prompts treat the document as content, never as instructions.</li><li>Errors: invalid input gives 422; a provider failure gives a clear error status and message, never empty or fake output.</li><li>Tests with a fake adapter (no live calls): each endpoint's request validation and response shape, review drops non-matching quotes, complete truncates long output.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the three endpoints return the documented shapes with the fake adapter; no prompt or provider logic in the router.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming, agent loops, storing anything.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 11 (Three endpoints that share one router, one set of request/response models and one adapter change; each service and its test is small.)</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4536	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	done	medium	1eea33316ad5-4d5d-a602-c8a9c24d9846	058ab9e76af7-4c57-5be9-d0fb6cb50fb9	\N	1f67df496ad5-4d5d-a602-02e2ffaeea96	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	c5d6df586af7-baa9-a180-93d2c219b47c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 10:03:05	aa	0	0
0f32a4976af7-4c57-5be9-7e094448e3a3	Docs: Docassist resource for AI help (ask, complete, review) via Ares	2026-11-13 14:13:35	2026-11-18 14:53:46	0	<p>The Docs editor asks for AI help: a writer's request about selected text, sentence completion while writing, and a document review. Gaia owns access and must record who asked, so each request is a <code>Docassist</code> record created through standard CRUD. The create calls Ares and returns the result in the response.</p><ul><li>New resource <code>Docassist</code> (table <code>docassist</code>) per <code>docs/generated/bundles/B.md</code>: <code>docId</code>, <code>projectId</code> (varchar(36), required), <code>kind</code> (ask|complete|review), <code>instruction</code> varchar(1000) nullable (required for ask), <code>status</code> (done|failed), <code>result</code> text nullable (ask: HTML; review: JSON findings; complete: not stored), <code>inputChars</code> and <code>outputChars</code> int, standard fields and behaviours (no audit). The person who asked is <code>createdUser</code> (the <code>actedFor</code> of the resulting suggestions).</li><li>Request-only inputs, never stored: <code>selectionHtml</code>, <code>context</code> {title, headingPath, before, after}, <code>text</code> (review). Decide how the framework accepts non-persisted create inputs (e.g. a component on create) and record it in <code>docs/architecture/docs/decisions.md</code>.</li><li>On create: check the doc exists in <code>projectId</code> and the caller has <code>doc.update</code> on it; enforce input limits (instruction 1000, selection 8000, before 2000, after 500, text 60000 chars); rate-limit per user (complete 40/min, ask and review 10/min, counted from the user's recent Docassist rows) with 429; call Ares through <code>core/services/LLM.php</code> (new methods for <code>/docs/ask</code>, <code>/docs/complete</code>, <code>/docs/review</code>, with timeouts of about 5 s, 30 s and 60 s); save the row with <code>status</code> and return the result in the response (<code>result</code> for ask and review; a transient <code>completion</code> field for complete).</li><li>A failed or timed-out Ares call saves <code>status = failed</code> and returns an error status with a message, never an empty success.</li><li>ACL metadata <code>'groups' =&gt; ['Project']</code> via projectId; permissions <code>docassist.create/get</code>. No permission seed SQL.</li><li>api-tester with a stubbed LLM service in the test environment (no live Ares): acl cases (member with and without docassist.create, without doc.update, non-member) and client cases (each kind returns its shape, ask without instruction is rejected, input over the limit is rejected, rate limit returns 429, Ares failure gives an error and a failed row, completion text is not stored).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the three kinds work end to end with the stub; only users who can edit the doc can ask; every request leaves a row with who, when, kind and status.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> streaming, cost accounting in money, agents.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aa-4536, agaia-4526</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 14 (A new-resource bundle per B.md plus the LLM service methods, the request-only input handling, the rate limit and a test stub for the LLM service; the AI call and the resource that carries it can&#x27;t ship apart.)</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4537	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	deferred	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	a489fe216af7-ea0a-5be9-d65370042b0c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	447a14b76afa-8715-b3ee-74f36b3c3804	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-18 14:53:46	agaia	0	0
1837e4056af7-4c57-5be9-c4ebd05d285f	External Request: Docs: apply, accept and reject suggestions with a Suggestions box	2026-11-13 14:13:44	2026-11-18 15:04:58	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Changes made by AI in a doc never land directly: they arrive as suggestions that people accept or reject, each showing who it was made for and, when given, why. The editor schema already has the <code>suggestionInsert</code>/<code>suggestionDelete</code> marks; this issue adds the behaviour and the Suggestions box, the single place where suggestions are reviewed. Because suggestions are marks in the shared Y.Doc, they and their accept/reject are live for everyone. Suggesting mode for people's own typing is not part of this issue.</p><ul><li><code>utils/docs/suggestions.js</code>: <code>proposeReplacement(editor, from, to, html, attrs)</code> marks the old range with <code>suggestionDelete</code> and inserts the new content with <code>suggestionInsert</code>, both with the same <code>id</code>; <code>proposeInsertion</code>; <code>accept(id)</code> (removes inserted marks, deletes text marked deleted); <code>reject(id)</code> (deletes inserted text, removes deleted marks); <code>acceptAll</code>/<code>rejectAll(requestId)</code>; <code>list(editor)</code> groups pending suggestions by <code>requestId</code>. All as single editor transactions, so they sync and undo like normal edits.</li><li><code>Docs::SuggestionsBox</code>: a <code>box-info</code> side box on the doc page (see the ai-reviewer screen) listing pending suggestions grouped by request, with Accept/Reject per suggestion and Accept all/Reject all per group. The group header shows the source name ("Ask AI" or "AI Reviewer", from <code>source</code>) with <code>Agent::Badge</code> and the "for {name}" sponsor text (as <code>components/agent/user-tag.hbs</code> does) and the time. Each entry shows its <code>reason</code> when present. It yields a slot per group for extra entries (used for reviewer notes) and re-renders when the document changes. Empty state: "No suggestions in this doc".</li><li>Clicking an entry scrolls to and selects the suggestion; clicking a suggestion in the text shows a small Accept/Reject popover (keyboard reachable).</li><li>Buttons only for users who can edit; others see the suggestions read-only.</li><li>Styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>, strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the helpers (replacement then accept and reject give the expected document; acceptAll per request) and an integration test of the box (grouping, reason, sponsor text, read-only hides buttons, empty state).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a suggestion added through the helper shows inline and in the box; accept and reject change the document as expected for everyone in the doc.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> Suggesting mode for people's typing, comments on suggestions, notifications.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4533</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> ai-reviewer.png</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4538	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	deferred	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	da3e78706af7-ea0a-5be9-52b16668b269	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	\N	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-18 15:04:58	aprom	0	0
689072e06af0-7d1c-cccd-d95cc8924287	External Request: Runtimes room: runtime service tokens receive workflow.agent.run.requested	2026-11-08 20:41:12	2026-11-09 02:17:38	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Inter application Communication", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Talos runtimes take run requests on one socket. Gaia also publishes <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> with the scope <code>runtimes</code>. Contract change: merges together with the matching A Gaia issue.</p><ul><li>Accept that scope on <code>/publish</code> for this event only.</li><li>Only sockets whose introspection says <code>actorType: service</code> and <code>serviceKind: runtime</code> may set an intent for it; everyone else is refused it; runtime tokens may set no other intent.</li><li>ADR entry (alongside D-009 and D-017).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests: runtime token receives the event, user and agent tokens refused, runtime token refused on project intents. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-runtime routing.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> ah-4396</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4398	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	861790376ad5-1449-a602-a25bd5e6e2b8	d59707896af0-cd0b-cccd-6c0c771196c7	\N	87099ee46ad5-1449-a602-5f7a1f6605b7	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	dbdc30f76af1-7dda-8962-696b7e5c171d	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 02:17:39	ah	0	0
9c3d03046afa-b805-5654-1b5da02bcfe4	AppUi::Avatar: add size ml (64px) for member grids	2026-11-16 11:27:24	2026-11-16 11:54:08	0	<p>We are moving every user picture in the app to <code>AppUi::Avatar</code>. The member grids (project overview Members, issue Members box, role page Members) render avatars at about 70-80px today, between m (40px) and l (96px), so the scale needs one more size.</p><ul><li><code>components/app-ui/avatar.js</code>: add <code>ml</code> to <code>SIZES</code> (order xs, s, m, ml, l). Unknown values still fall back to m.</li><li><code>styles/components/app-ui-avatar.scss</code>: <code>.app-ui-avatar-ml</code> 64px x 64px; agent icon font size and initials text scaled between m and l; the robot marker shows (as from s up).</li><li>Update the header comment of the scss and the component YUIDoc.</li><li>Demo <code>components/developer/demos/avatar.{hbs,js}</code>: add the ml column and size option.</li><li>Docs <code>public/ui-docs/app-ui-avatar.md</code> and its manifest json: list ml 64px and when to use it (stacked member grids with the name below).</li><li>Integration test: ml renders 64px, with initials and with the agent marker.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>@size="ml"</code> renders a 64px avatar for a person, a person without an image and an agent; the existing sizes are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing any page that uses the avatar.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4606	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	69b873786af9-1368-4631-55b621317e73	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	3d524b986afa-b4ca-5654-6975458c8937	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 11:54:08	aprom	0	0
2da292786af7-4c57-5be9-a13a8c2c5d33	External Request: Docs: Ask AI floating menu on selected text, result inserted as a suggestion	2026-11-13 14:14:05	2026-11-18 15:04:42	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>When a writer selects text, a small floating menu appears with an <strong>Ask AI</strong> option. They type what they want ("make this clearer", "turn into a checklist") and the answer replaces the selection as a suggestion that needs approval. There is no separate AI panel and no preview step.</p><ul><li>Dependency: <code>@tiptap/extension-bubble-menu</code> (open source, approved for this module).</li><li><code>Docs::SelectionMenu</code>: a bubble menu shown for a non-empty text selection, only to users who can edit. It holds bold, italic, link and an <strong>Ask AI</strong> button (<code>fa-magic</code>). Ask AI turns the menu into a request field (<code>FormFields::FieldText</code> with label "Ask AI" and help text "The answer is added as a suggestion. Enter to send, Esc to close."). Enter sends (ignored during IME composition), Esc closes and returns focus to the editor.</li><li>On send: set the awareness <code>ai</code> flag to <code>ask</code> (so others see "<em>Name</em> is asking AI…") and clear it when done; call <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>ask()</code> with the instruction, the selection as HTML and context (doc title, heading path, up to 2000 characters before and 500 after). Show <code>AppUi::Loader</code> in the menu and disable the field while waiting.</li><li>On success: replace the original range with <code>proposeReplacement</code> from <code>utils/docs/suggestions.js</code> (<code>source: ask</code>, <code>actedFor</code> = current user, <code>requestId</code> = the Docassist id), close the menu and highlight the new group in the Suggestions box. Track the selection with Yjs relative positions while waiting; if the selected text changed, don't insert and show "The text changed, try again" in the menu.</li><li>Errors (including 429) show in the menu with a retry; one request at a time.</li><li>Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>, styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>.</li><li>Integration test with Mirage: select text, menu shows Ask AI, send a request, a suggestion with the right attrs appears, the ai flag is set and cleared; error path; read-only users get no Ask AI.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> matches the ask-ai screen; nothing becomes final until someone accepts the suggestion.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> preset actions, streaming, Ask AI without a selection.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4539, aprom-4538, aprom-4535</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> ask-ai.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4540	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	deferred	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	da3e78706af7-ea0a-5be9-52b16668b269	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	\N	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-18 15:04:42	aprom	0	0
ef2657e66aeb-ef61-c1c6-decea6fbd5ca	External Request: Talos: run 'Run agent' workflow steps that aren't about an issue (no repo workspace)	2026-11-04 20:13:35	2026-11-04 20:38:21	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Prometheus (idea "Agents In Prometheus", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>A workflow can now ask an agent to work on a record that isn't an issue: first case, a Retrospective agent started by 'Milestone completed', which reads the milestone and creates an issue. Gaia's Run agent step works with any record (<code>entityType</code>/<code>entityId</code> on the actor step), but Talos refuses it: <code>talos/lib/workflow_steps.py</code> <code>_subject</code> (~l.197) says 'Talos runs agents on issues only'. <code>dispatcher.run_step</code> (~l.274) and <code>_start</code> assume an issue and its repo: workspace, branch, Gaia pack, ship flow and CodeRabbit loop.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In <code>workflow_steps.py</code>, issue steps run exactly as today. Any other <code>entityType</code> becomes a record run.</li><li>A record run: Claude with the step's prompt, the agent's spec (role prompt, model, tool grants, permission mode, turn cap) and a short context block (record type, id and project; for a milestone, its name and dates through gaia-mcp <code>get_milestone</code>).</li><li>Its cwd is a scratch folder under the per-machine state (from <code>LOCAL_DIR</code>), not a repo checkout. No branch, no commit, no PR, no ship session, no CodeRabbit loop, no test slot.</li><li>Sessions are keyed by record (type + id), so <code>session: resume</code> works per record.</li><li>Report the outcome with the existing five (done, needs_input, blocked, failed, limit), and handle usage limits as issue steps do.</li><li>Keep the step logic in <code>lib/</code> functions that can be unit tested. Update the Talos README.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A Run agent step on a milestone is claimed, runs in a scratch folder without touching any repo, and reports done or a hand-off.</li><li>Issue steps behave exactly as before.</li><li>Unit tests cover the issue/record split, the record context and the outcome reporting.</li><li>Works on Windows and Linux.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> record runs that change code.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 7</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4272	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	\N	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	\N	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	812eafb76aeb-e1dc-c1c6-3e9926ef7442	\N	2026-11-04 20:38:21	adt	0	1
1e1ad3b46ae8-863a-741d-a7687782cf02	Issue detail: wrap long estimate and time log descriptions and scroll inside a capped height	2026-11-02 19:14:38	2026-11-11 10:38:16	0	<p>In the Estimates and Time logs boxes on the issue detail page, a description is cut to one line with an ellipsis. Anything longer can't be read.</p><p><strong>Today</strong>: <code>app/styles/modules/issue.scss</code> (~130) styles <code>.time-log .log-description</code> with <code>white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis</code>. The markup is in <code>app/components/issue/issue-details.hbs</code> (<code>span.log-description</code> in both boxes, rendering the HTML description).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Let the description wrap (including long words and URLs) and cap its height (about 150px) with <code>overflow-y: auto</code>, so a long description scrolls inside its row. Short descriptions look as they do today, without an empty scroll area.</li><li>Keep the rich-text content (lists, code, images) within the row width.</li><li>Same rule for Estimates and Time logs. Style in <code>issue.scss</code> only, colours from <code>variables.scss</code>, no inline styles.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A multi-paragraph description is fully readable by scrolling inside its row; the box layout doesn't break.</li><li>A one-line description shows as before.</li><li>Checked in the running app next to the current issue page.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope</strong>: an expand/collapse toggle, and changes to the description editor.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 2</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4258	2026-11-10	2026-11-03	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	b43cc5046ae8-20b5-32a1-13b222266c79	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	c831eb966ae8-6485-4143-9bf6d6b96406	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-03 11:57:27	aprom	0	0
be4473366aeb-4599-8fd2-f5cb804a11cd	Talos: read Docker's state (daemon, memory, containers) with an ok/pressured/down verdict	2026-11-04 21:21:02	2026-11-04 21:31:19	0	<p>Agamemnon and the dispatcher know nothing about Docker today: the triage packet's <code>docker</code> field is always <code>None</code> (<code>talos/lib/agamemnon/triage.py</code> <code>run</code>), and the only probe is <code>installer/p4m.py</code> <code>docker_running</code>. Runs keep dying because Docker is down or out of memory (see adt-4234), and nothing notices. This issue adds the reader and the verdict everything else builds on.</p><ul><li>New module <code>talos/lib/docker_state.py</code>. The <code>docker</code> calls sit behind small functions (stdin given, no shell) so the logic is unit tested without Docker.</li><li><code>read()</code> returns a dict: <code>cli</code> (found or not), <code>daemon</code> (reachable or not, plus the error text), <code>serverVersion</code>, <code>memTotal</code> (from <code>docker info</code>), <code>memUsed</code> and per-container usage (name, memory, CPU; <code>docker stats --no-stream</code> in JSON format), and <code>p4mTestContainers</code> (the count of those labelled by p4m test).</li><li><code>verdict(state, high, low, was)</code> returns <code>down</code> (CLI missing or daemon unreachable), <code>pressured</code> (used/total at or above <code>high</code>, or still above <code>low</code> when the previous verdict was pressured: hysteresis), otherwise <code>ok</code>.</li><li>Config in the agent's agent.json: <code>docker: {"memoryHighPercent": 85, "memoryOkPercent": 70}</code>, read in <code>talos/lib/registry.py</code> with these defaults.</li><li><code>talos status</code> prints one Docker line: the verdict, used/total memory and the number of test containers.</li><li>README: a Docker state section.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests cover parsing <code>docker info</code>/<code>stats</code> output, a missing CLI, an unreachable daemon, and the verdict thresholds including hysteresis. Windows and Linux both work.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> starting Docker, holding dispatch, freeing memory, aga commands (later issues).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4274	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	33d807056aeb-7205-8fd2-1688da96e2ec	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-04 21:31:19	adt	0	0
e749e2696aeb-4599-8fd2-2f867bafc34d	aga: docker, start-docker, restart-docker, stop-stale-containers and hold-until-docker verbs	2026-11-04 21:21:43	2026-11-04 22:59:31	0	<p>Agamemnon's triage sessions can't read Docker or act on it: the premise grants <code>docker_down</code> a <code>pause</code> tier that no verb uses. This issue adds the commands. Their use is granted per incident type in the follow-up issue.</p><ul><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/verbs.py</code>: <code>docker</code> (tier read, level READ: <code>docker_state.read()</code> plus its verdict); <code>start-docker</code> and <code>restart-docker</code> (new tier <code>engine</code>, level PRIVATE, added to the tier list in <code>talos/agents/agamemnon/premise.json</code>); <code>stop-stale-containers</code> (new tier <code>free</code>, level PRIVATE, uses <code>docker_free</code>, same rule: no run in flight, and deferred, won't fix or unchanged for more than 72h); <code>hold-until-docker</code> (tier wait, level PRIVATE).</li><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/tool.py</code>: <code>start-docker</code> is refused when the daemon is already up. <code>restart-docker</code> is refused while another issue has a run in flight, unless the verdict is <code>down</code> (those runs are already failing). Both use <code>docker_engine</code>, wait until ready and report the stack containers that are missing.</li><li><code>hold-until-docker</code> works like <code>_hold_until_tomorrow</code> (refused with a run in flight, in in_review or already held; assigns the issue to Agamemnon), but the journal hold has a condition <code>docker</code> instead of a time.</li><li><code>talos/lib/agamemnon/holds.py</code> <code>release_due</code> and <code>journal</code>: a Docker hold is due when the verdict is <code>ok</code>. Give back at most one Docker-held issue per sweep, oldest first, so they don't all start at once. A hold ends without giving the issue back when the issue was moved to deferred or won't fix, and goes to the owner with a comment after <code>docker.holdMaxHours</code> (default 72). Undo releases the hold, as for time holds.</li><li>Talos README (The <code>aga</code> tool): the new verbs.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for each verb's refusals, the one-per-sweep release, the deferred/won't-fix release, the 72h handover and undo. These paths are in <code>agamemnonProtected</code>, so the merge gate's self check fails by design and the PR needs a manual merge.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> the classifier, premise grants and role text (next issue).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4275, adt-4277</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 10</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4278	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	6e2c4cc56aeb-2e52-8b27-a7633f20f4e9	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-04 22:59:31	adt	0	0
602fc7e06af0-7d1c-cccd-9fcbeabb2e7a	External Request: Allowlist user.access.changed and re-check that user's sockets	2026-11-08 20:41:04	2026-11-09 02:23:44	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Inter application Communication", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Gaia publishes <code>user.access.changed</code> (user-scoped) when a user is disabled, sessions are revoked or memberships change. Contract change: merges together with the matching A Gaia issue.</p><ul><li>Add the name to <code>src/contract/names.js</code> (must match Gaia <code>EventNames.php</code>); ADR entry.</li><li>On it: evict the user's cached sessions, re-introspect each of the user's sockets; disconnect if inactive, otherwise re-apply intents so rooms of projects no longer in <code>projectIds</code> are left.</li><li>Not forwarded to clients.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests for membership removal (room left), disable (disconnect), unchanged access (no effect). <strong>Out of scope:</strong> role changes.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> ah-4396</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4397	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	861790376ad5-1449-a602-a25bd5e6e2b8	d59707896af0-cd0b-cccd-6c0c771196c7	\N	87099ee46ad5-1449-a602-5f7a1f6605b7	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	cc9ed3256af1-7dda-8962-c0dd7b37f5f5	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 02:23:44	ah	0	0
d00f26886aeb-4599-8fd2-281e021cb250	Talos dispatcher: hold dispatch while Docker is down or at 85% memory, start a stopped engine	2026-11-04 21:21:20	2026-11-04 22:15:02	0	<p>Starting runs while Docker is full only produces more OOM-killed runs and handbacks to the owner. When Talos runs on a server, it may also start before Docker is ready at boot. The dispatcher should wait for Docker the same way it waits out a Claude usage limit.</p><ul><li>New class <code>DockerPause</code> in its own module, modelled on <code>talos/lib/usage_pause.py</code> <code>UsagePause</code> (one lock, interruptible wait, <code>stop()</code>). It holds the last verdict from <code>docker_state</code> and re-reads it at most every <code>docker.checkSeconds</code> (default 30).</li><li><code>talos/lib/dispatcher.py</code>: before a job is taken (next to the usage-limit wait ~l.193), wait while the verdict is <code>down</code> or <code>pressured</code> (85% high, 70% ok, from agent.json). Log once when the hold starts and once when it ends. No issue comments, since no issue is affected yet.</li><li>When the verdict is <code>down</code> and <code>docker.autoStart</code> is true (default true), call <code>docker_engine.start()</code> once per hold, after a short grace period so a Docker that is still booting isn't started twice. If it fails, log it and keep waiting. Never restart from here.</li><li>A run already in flight is not touched.</li><li><code>talos status</code> shows a Docker hold and since when; README updated.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests show the dispatcher waits while down or pressured, resumes when ok (with hysteresis), tries one start per hold after the grace period, and that <code>stop()</code> releases waiters.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> freeing memory (next issue), holding single issues (aga issue).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4274, adt-4275</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4276	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	a5bdf8306aeb-877c-b1c2-67265a3c35f6	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-04 22:15:02	adt	0	0
dbc424b36aeb-4599-8fd2-0843aedd16df	Talos: free Docker memory by stopping test containers of stale, deferred or won't-fix issues	2026-11-04 21:21:31	2026-11-04 22:39:47	0	<p>A warm Prometheus test container holds about 3 GB. Talos gc (adt-4234) removes them only for done, closed or won't fix issues, or merged PRs, so containers of issues that are parked or deferred keep filling Docker. When Docker is short of memory, Talos should stop the containers nobody is using, and only those.</p><ul><li>New module <code>talos/lib/docker_free.py</code>: <code>stoppable(containers, issues, running, now)</code> (pure) chooses the issues whose p4m test containers may be stopped. An issue qualifies when it has no run in flight <strong>and</strong> either its status is deferred or won't fix, or it has not changed (Gaia modified time) for more than <code>docker.staleHours</code> (default 72). Status names are normalised like <code>workspace_gc._norm</code>.</li><li><code>stop(names)</code> runs <code>docker stop</code> (not remove: the workspace and the next <code>ai test</code> still work). Containers come from <code>workspace_gc.test_containers</code> ({issue: names}).</li><li>The dispatch hold (<code>DockerPause</code>) calls it once when a <code>pressured</code> hold starts, then re-checks the verdict. Each stopped container is logged with its issue and reason; the issue gets no comment.</li><li><code>talos gc --dry-run</code> or <code>talos status</code> lists which containers would be stopped; README updated.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for <code>stoppable</code> (in-flight issue never chosen; deferred, won't fix and stale over 72h chosen; 71h not chosen; unreadable issue not chosen) and the hold calling it once per pressured hold. Docker unreachable: nothing stopped, the hold carries on.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> stopping the warm ember build inside a container that is otherwise in use, removing containers (gc's job).</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4276</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4277	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	98a23a966aeb-cbb2-6ab7-37d480dc980e	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-04 22:39:47	adt	0	0
f5d664d66aeb-833c-a4f5-22402fa6159a	Hand-off: send design-reviewed dev-tools issues to Agamemnon to merge, through the existing merge route	2026-11-04 21:34:45	2026-11-04 22:39:48	0	<p>After adt-4280, a dev-tools PR can pass the merge check, but no dev-tools issue ever reaches Agamemnon. For a repo not in <code>codeRabbitRepos</code>, <code>ai ship</code> hands the issue straight to the reviewer (<code>ai/lib/ship.py</code> ~l.197: <code>defer = args.defer_handoff and coderabbit.enabled(repo)</code>). The hand-off to Agamemnon only happens in Talos' CodeRabbit loop (<code>talos/lib/bot_review.py</code> <code>Watcher.check_one</code>, using <code>MergeRoute</code> in <code>talos/lib/orchestrator/setup.py</code>).</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><strong><code>ai ship</code>:</strong> with <code>--defer-handoff</code>, also defer for repos in <code>mergeReviewers</code>, using the shared lookup from adt-4280. The issue ends <code>awaiting_bot_review</code> as for CodeRabbit repos. Other repos still hand off straight away.</li><li><strong>Talos watcher:</strong> for a <code>mergeReviewers</code> repo there is no CodeRabbit to wait for and no bot rounds. On the first check:<ul><li>if the PR body has the design-review line, treat it as clean and route it through <code>self.route(issue)</code>. Agamemnon gets it when the milestone is in <code>autoMergeMilestones</code> and Agamemnon isn't paused; otherwise it goes to the reviewer, as now.</li><li>without the line, hand the issue to the reviewer, with the reason in the log and in an issue comment.</li></ul>Keep the CodeRabbit path unchanged.</li><li>Update the Talos README's CodeRabbit-loop section.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>A dev-tools issue in an auto-merge milestone, shipped with a recorded clean design review, is handed to Agent Agamemnon. Agamemnon merges it when <code>ai mergecheck</code> is ok.</li><li>The same issue goes to the reviewer when the milestone isn't an auto-merge one, when Agamemnon is paused, or when the design-review line is missing.</li><li>Gaia, Prometheus and Hermes issues follow the CodeRabbit loop exactly as before.</li><li>Unit tests for the ship defer decision and the watcher's new branch.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> adding a dev-tools milestone to <code>autoMergeMilestones</code>. That is a config change for the owner.</p><p>Depends on: #4280</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4281	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	7edc8c366ae8-0360-4071-f0d5103ebc86	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	c409b9456aeb-5e4d-6ab7-100f53c34459	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-04 22:39:48	adt	0	0
3a7f70c76af7-4c57-5be9-d1d39b9e8668	External Request: Docs: always-on ghost-text AI completion while writing (Tab to accept)	2026-11-13 14:14:18	2026-11-18 15:04:38	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>While writing, AI suggests how the sentence continues, shown right away as grey text after the cursor. It is always on for people who can edit. Accepting it is the writer's own choice, so accepted text is a normal edit, not a suggestion.</p><ul><li>A Tiptap extension <code>utils/docs/ghost-text.js</code>, added to the doc page editor for users who can edit: after about 500 ms without typing, with the cursor at the end of a non-empty text block and no selection, ask <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>complete()</code> with the title, heading path, up to 2000 characters before and 500 after. Show the result as a widget decoration (local only, not synced, not saved).</li><li>Tab inserts the text at the cursor; Esc, any typing, moving the cursor or losing focus dismisses it. A newer request makes older responses be ignored, and a pending request is dropped when the writer types again. Ignore while composing (IME), in read-only mode and while the Ask AI menu is open.</li><li>On 429 or errors, show nothing and back off for 30 s; no toasts.</li><li>Ghost text style in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code> (muted colour from <code>variables.scss</code>); a short hint "Tab to accept" comes from <code>translations/en-us.json</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the extension (debounce, shown only at block end, Tab inserts, typing dismisses, stale response ignored, back-off after an error) and a page test that read-only users get no ghost text.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> pausing at the end of a paragraph shows a completion that Tab inserts; typing dismisses it; read-only users never trigger requests.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> multi-paragraph completions, completions in the middle of text, a per-user on/off setting.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4539, aprom-4533</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> ask-ai.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4541	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	deferred	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	da3e78706af7-ea0a-5be9-52b16668b269	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	\N	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-18 15:04:39	aprom	0	0
857d65406af0-7d1c-cccd-75649a54a3c8	External Request: Talos: take workflow run requests from the Hermes runtimes room	2026-11-08 20:41:41	2026-11-09 02:55:44	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Inter application Communication", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>One socket per runtime instead of one per agent: Talos listens to <code>workflow.agent.run.requested</code> in the runtimes room with its service token and hands each request to the discovered agent it names.</p><ul><li>Listener in <code>talos/lib/hermes.py</code> with the service token (fresh on every reconnect, as today).</li><li>Requests for agents this runtime doesn't run are ignored; the step claim decides between runtimes.</li><li>Drop the per-agent run-request subscription for Gaia agents.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> unit tests for routing, unknown agent and reconnect. <strong>Out of scope:</strong> per-runtime routing.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4400, ah-4398, agaia-4394</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 5</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4401	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	712014526af0-7d1c-cccd-ee6dc2488b11	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	68ba37706af1-d30f-f56f-f04a684d88e7	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 02:55:44	adt	0	0
d74af4a16aeb-2e52-8b27-6b262041160f	Workflow editor: Run agent's agent dropdown shows the robot instead of the agent's picture	2026-11-04 22:42:31	2026-11-05 00:19:19	0	<p>In the workflow editor's properties panel (aprom-4057), the Run agent step's Agent dropdown always draws the default robot, even for agents with a profile picture. aprom-4252 made <code>Agent::Avatar</code> take the agent's user and show <code>profilePicture</code> when there is one. The panel's option renderer, <code>related-fields/relate-actor</code> (added by aprom-4057 for user pictures, agent avatars and expressions), still renders it without the user.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>Pass the agent's user to <code>Agent::Avatar</code> in <code>relate-actor</code>, for the options and for the selected value.</li><li>Make sure the agent options are loaded with their user (<code>rels: 'user'</code> on the agent query of the editor's catalog data, loaded by the route or service, not the component) so <code>profilePicture</code> is there.</li><li>Check the other actor pickers that use <code>relate-actor</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Agents with a picture show it in the dropdown and in the selected value. Agents without one show the robot.</li><li>An integration test covers both cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4282	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	f59d90b96aeb-2e52-8b27-7005c5ae8b72	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-05 00:19:09	aprom	0	0
473753296af7-4c57-5be9-d0569c65dd64	External Request: Docs: AI Reviewer toolbar button with fixes as suggestions and shared review notes	2026-11-13 14:14:31	2026-11-18 15:04:35	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>An <strong>AI Reviewer</strong> button in the editor toolbar reviews the whole document: unclear wording, open questions, inconsistencies and missing parts. Concrete fixes arrive as suggestions with their reason; findings without a fix become notes. Fixes and notes live in the shared Y.Doc, so everyone in the doc sees them appear and get resolved live. Everything is reviewed in the Suggestions box; there is no separate AI panel.</p><ul><li>Toolbar button (<code>btn btn-default btn-sm</code>, <code>fa-magic</code>, "AI Reviewer") in the toolbar's extra slot, for users who can edit. While running it shows "Reviewing…" with <code>aria-busy</code>, is disabled, and sets the awareness <code>ai</code> flag to <code>review</code> (cleared when done). Afterwards it shows the number of open findings as a <code>label</code>.</li><li>On click: send the doc's plain text (headings on their own lines) through <code>services/doc-ai.js</code> <code>review()</code>.</li><li>For each finding with a <code>replacement</code>: find its <code>quote</code> in the current document. If it occurs exactly once and doesn't overlap another fix, apply <code>proposeReplacement</code> with <code>source: review</code>, <code>actedFor</code> = current user, <code>requestId</code> = the Docassist id and <code>reason</code> = the category and message. Otherwise treat it as a note, so a fix never lands in the wrong place.</li><li><strong>Notes</strong> are stored in a shared <code>Y.Map</code> named <code>notes</code> in the doc's Y.Doc (saved with the doc state by the collab server, not rendered into the HTML): <code>{id, requestId, category, message, quote, anchorFrom, anchorTo (encoded Yjs relative positions), actedFor, createdAt, resolved, resolvedBy}</code>. Anchors follow the text as people edit.</li><li>The Suggestions box shows the open notes of each review group through its group slot: category <code>label</code>, message and a Resolve button (resolving is shared and live). Clicking a note selects its anchored text, or shows "Text changed since the review" if that text was deleted.</li><li>Errors (including 429) show next to the button with a retry. Strings in <code>translations/en-us.json</code>, styles in <code>styles/modules/doc.scss</code>.</li><li>Tests: unit tests of the notes map helpers (add, anchor, resolve) and integration tests with Mirage: fixes become suggestions with reasons, an ambiguous quote becomes a note, notes render and select their text, resolving hides the note, read-only users get no button.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> matches the ai-reviewer screen; fixes need approval in the Suggestions box and are attributed to the person who ran the review; another person in the doc sees the fixes and notes appear and get resolved without reloading.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> turning notes into comments, scheduled or automatic reviews.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4539, aprom-4538, aprom-4535</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 8</p><p><strong>Screens:</strong> ai-reviewer.png</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	4542	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	deferred	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	da3e78706af7-ea0a-5be9-52b16668b269	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Rana Nouman	\N	d293f53862c6-8e43-047e-1fffdc448fcf	2026-11-18 15:04:35	aprom	0	0
