fa5ca1d76afa-3684-5afc-8eb85abfebf5	ai test prometheus: give lint fixes as test-container commands, never a host npx	2026-11-16 12:28:42	2026-11-16 12:50:24	0	<p><strong>What happened (aprom-4609):</strong> Achilles's <code>ai test prometheus</code> failed lint on <code>notification.hbs</code> (<code>no-duplicate-attributes</code> + <code>invalid-todo-violation-rule</code>). It followed the printed hint <code>npx ember-template-lint &lt;file&gt; --clean-todo</code> and ran ember-template-lint on the host. Neither <code>.runs/issue-N/prometheus</code> nor <code>Pr4M/prometheus</code> has a <code>node_modules</code>, so <code>npx</code> ran an unrelated build (it reports version 0.0.0). That build gave different results (a <code>no-curly-component-invocation</code> error the real 7.9.4 doesn't report). Achilles then concluded the <code>.lint-todo</code> entries had "expired" (they don't: the 13-digit field is the creation date and <code>daysToDecay</code> is empty) and blocked the issue.</p><p><strong>Real cause:</strong> a recorded todo's hash covers the violating element's source. Editing inside the <code>&lt;li&gt;</code> made the todo stale, so the old violation counted as new. The fix was to remove the duplicate attribute and clean the todo inside the test container (PR prometheus#832).</p><ul><li><code>ai/lib/tests.py</code> <code>lint()</code>: replace the <code>npx ember-template-lint {f} --clean-todo</code> and <code>npm run lint:js:prune</code> hints with commands that run in the run's test container. For example, add <code>p4m test lint --src &lt;checkout&gt; --clean-todo &lt;file&gt;</code> / <code>--prune</code>. It runs in <code>PrometheusTestContainer</code> after <code>sync()</code> and copies <code>.lint-todo</code> / <code>eslint-suppressions.json</code> back to the checkout.</li><li>When a file has both a violation and an <code>invalid-todo-violation-rule</code> for the same rule, say so in the summary: "your edit made the recorded todo for &lt;rule&gt; stale: fix the violation (preferred), then clean the todo". Don't suggest re-adding a todo.</li><li>Worker guidance (Talos worker role prompt and the <code>run-tests</code> skill): never run npm/npx lint or tests on the host checkout; it has no <code>node_modules</code>. Use <code>ai test</code> / <code>p4m test lint</code>. Note that <code>.lint-todo</code> entries don't expire.</li><li>Tests for the new <code>p4m test lint</code> options and the summary text.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a stale-todo lint failure prints a container command that fixes it, and running that command changes only <code>.lint-todo</code> in the checkout; no hint or doc tells a worker to run npx on the host.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4619	2026-11-23	2026-11-16	done	medium	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	84aeed166ad8-5eae-b551-f3f3cea8503c	\N	a13debc86ad7-404c-ce18-75327b747d1b	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	6c1a22d46afa-8ccb-5afc-bbf4c5c14f38	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 12:50:24	adt	0	0
fe98fc756aeb-2e52-8b27-9847e6086d1f	Workflow editor: zoom only on Ctrl/⌘ + scroll; plain scroll scrolls the page	2026-11-04 22:43:10	2026-11-05 00:11:51	0	<p>The workflow canvas (aprom-4038, own SVG layer) zooms on every mouse-wheel turn. The canvas is large, so the pointer is usually over it, and scrolling down to the step settings zooms instead. The common convention (Figma, Miro, n8n) is to zoom on Ctrl+scroll (⌘+scroll on macOS). Trackpad pinch arrives as a wheel event with <code>ctrlKey</code>, so pinch keeps zooming.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>In the canvas's wheel handler, zoom only when <code>ctrlKey</code> or <code>metaKey</code> is held: call <code>preventDefault</code> then, and zoom around the pointer as today.</li><li>Without a modifier, don't handle the event or prevent its default, so the page scrolls.</li><li>Panning by dragging the background and the zoom and fit buttons stay as they are.</li><li>Tooltip on the zoom controls: 'Ctrl + scroll to zoom'.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Plain scroll over the canvas scrolls the page.</li><li>Ctrl/⌘ + scroll and trackpad pinch zoom.</li><li>A test covers both wheel cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4286	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	facb90b66aeb-3404-8b27-781c0f77007f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-05 00:11:52	aprom	0	0
5a8b16796af1-35f0-87ea-4a00d5a28adf	p4m configure: back up every credential and config file before rewriting it	2026-11-09 11:45:30	2026-11-09 12:15:37	0	<p>On 2026-11-09 a <code>p4m configure</code> run rewrote <code>dev-tools/gaia-mcp/gaia-mcp.env</code> and dropped <code>GAIA_PASSWORD</code>. The file is git-ignored and configure keeps no copy, so the password was lost and Odysseus/Achilles and Agamemnon could not sign in.</p><p><strong>Change:</strong> before <code>write_private</code>/<code>write_json</code> replace an existing file in <code>installer/configure.py</code>, copy it to <code>&lt;file&gt;.&lt;YYYYmmdd-HHMMSS&gt;.bak</code> next to it, owner-only (same <code>restrict</code> as the original), and print where the copies went. Skip the copy when the content would not change. Keep the last 5 copies per file. <code>.bak</code> files stay git-ignored.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests: rewriting an existing env file leaves a byte-identical owner-only .bak; unchanged content makes no .bak; pruning keeps 5.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> none</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4412	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	712014526af0-7d1c-cccd-ee6dc2488b11	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Agent Agamemnon	a0a406706af1-35f0-87ea-56b0ef66712f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 12:15:37	adt	0	0
6b9ff9956af1-35f0-87ea-f291852432db	p4m configure: never drop existing credentials; support password users and Gaia Agent records	2026-11-09 11:45:47	2026-11-09 13:27:12	0	<p>Since b129862 configure writes <code>gaia-mcp.env</code> with only <code>GAIA_CLIENT_ID</code>/<code>GAIA_CLIENT_SECRET</code>. The local agents (Achilles/Odysseus, Agamemnon, Nestor) are Gaia <strong>users</strong> that sign in with a password, not Agent records. Without <code>GAIA_PASSWORD</code> gaia-mcp falls back to client_credentials and Gaia refuses: <code>Client credentials are only for active agents</code>.</p><p><strong>Change</strong> (<code>installer/configure.py</code>):</p><ul><li>When rewriting an env file, keep every existing key configure does not set itself (merge, never replace), including <code>GAIA_PASSWORD</code>.</li><li>Per agent, ask how it signs in: <em>password</em> (user) or <em>client credentials</em> (Gaia Agent record). Default to what the existing file has. Write the keys for that mode and never remove the other mode's keys.</li><li>Verify the sign-in before writing; on failure keep the old file untouched and say why.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> tests: re-running configure on an env with <code>GAIA_PASSWORD</code> keeps it; unknown keys survive; a failed sign-in leaves the file unchanged.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> adt-4412</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4413	2026-11-16	2026-11-09	done	high	9f00a9366ad7-404c-ce18-9081c0a9fec6	712014526af0-7d1c-cccd-ee6dc2488b11	\N	a0df54476ad7-404c-ce18-8b3ef9fc16e9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	a30999316af1-538f-6ff5-11b4d1a2794c	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-09 13:27:12	adt	0	0
c84238c56af7-ea0a-5be9-e7768e3ec46f	External Request: Relay: allow doc.created, doc.updated and doc.deleted events	2026-11-13 14:12:24	2026-11-16 07:45:48	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Gaia (idea "Docs", raised by Rana Nouman). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p>Docs lists and open doc pages update live when a doc is created, renamed, locked or deleted. Gaia publishes these as domain events; the relay only needs to accept the names (D-003 allowlist).</p><ul><li>Add <code>doc.created</code>, <code>doc.updated</code> and <code>doc.deleted</code> to <code>src/contract/names.js</code>, matching Gaia's <code>EventNames.php</code>. Payloads follow the existing closed envelope (project-scoped, ids plus changed field names for <code>doc.updated</code>).</li><li>ADR entry in <code>docs/architecture/decisions.md</code> for the new names, as the contract rules require.</li><li>Tests: the names are accepted by <code>/publish</code> and delivered to sockets with a matching intent; unknown <code>doc.*</code> names are still rejected.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a published <code>doc.updated</code> reaches a project member's socket registered for it.</p><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> any doc content traffic (that goes through the collab server).</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4530	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	done	medium	861790376ad5-1449-a602-a25bd5e6e2b8	b66d76d16af7-ea0a-5be9-ee5080a2cdac	\N	87099ee46ad5-1449-a602-5f7a1f6605b7	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	e8bc6f086af7-f535-42e6-59d929b76670	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-16 07:45:48	ah	0	0
f60c3b846aeb-2e52-8b27-b9ff2aee7a1f	Workflow editor: fill a Run agent step's settings from the agent when one is picked	2026-11-04 22:43:02	2026-11-05 01:35:52	0	<p>When an agent is picked in a Run agent step (properties panel, aprom-4057), every other setting stays blank. The user should start from the agent's defaults and be able to edit them.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li>On picking an agent, fill the empty settings in the draft:<ul><li><code>maxTurns</code>: the agent's <code>maxTurns</code>.</li><li><code>session</code>: <code>new</code>.</li><li><code>claimTimeout</code>: <code>15</code> and <code>timeout</code>: <code>240</code> (Gaia's defaults in <code>RunAgentActor::CLAIM_MINUTES</code> / <code>FINISH_MINUTES</code>).</li></ul>All values are strings (Gaia types every Run agent setting as a string).</li><li>Model: leave it empty and show the agent's choice as the empty option, e.g. 'Agent's default (simple: sonnet, complex: opus)' from the agent's <code>modelConfig</code>. An empty model lets the runtime pick by the issue's complexity, and a filled one would switch that off.</li><li>Never overwrite a value the user typed. When the agent changes, only refill the settings that still hold the previous agent's defaults.</li><li>Field help as info-icon tooltips (what each default comes from).</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Picking an agent fills the settings above.</li><li>They can be edited and are saved as edited.</li><li>Switching agents keeps the user's edits.</li><li>An integration test covers fill, edit and switch.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> a default prompt.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4284</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 4</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4285	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	medium	add12ff55ac