094a70976ad3-4a62-f0f7-f2925ca8edcb	Task board doesn't live-update when another user changes an issue's status or assignee	2026-10-17 22:13:29	2026-11-05 13:36:17	0	<p><strong>What happens:</strong> with the task board open, issue changes made by another user don't show up until the page is reloaded. Seen 2026-10-15 to 10-18 while Agent Odysseus (through Talos) moved issues <code>new</code> → <code>in_progress</code> → <code>in_review</code> and reassigned them to Hammad. The board kept the old lane and assignee.</p>\n<p><strong>Expected:</strong> the issue moves lane and shows the new assignee live, the same as for changes made in the same browser.</p>\n<p><strong>What is known:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Gaia publishes <code>issue.status.changed</code> and <code>issue.assignee.changed</code> on every issue PATCH (<code>IssueLiveEventsComponent</code>). Hermes delivers them: Talos receives the same <code>issue.assignee.changed</code> events.</li>\n<li>The board registers handlers for both (<code>app/controllers/app/project/board.js</code>, <code>registerHermesIntents</code>, <code>handleIssueStatusChanged</code>, <code>handleIssueAssigneeChanged</code>), so the gap is somewhere between the socket and the lane rendering.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>To check:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Whether the board's socket is connected and its intents are accepted (the Hermes <code>/health</code> counters, browser devtools).</li>\n<li>Whether <code>changes.status</code> / <code>statusId</code> from the envelope match what the lanes group by (name vs id), and whether <code>applyRemoteIssueLaneMove</code> moves the card.</li>\n<li>Whether <code>findIssueAcrossMilestones</code> finds issues from the milestone being shown.</li>\n<li>Whether the board was open during the expired local certificate on 2026-10-17, which would have broken the socket. Reproduce on a fresh page load first.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Reproduce: open the A Gaia board, then change an issue's status and assignee from a second use