b8aadc826aec-7eb6-459b-3ae76c314cfc	Header quick create: show module icons before the entry names	2026-11-05 16:11:36	2026-11-05 16:26:57	0	<p>The "New" quick-create dropdown in the header lists only module names. To match the navigation menu, each entry should show its module icon before the name. The attached screen <code>quick-create-icons</code> shows the result. Keep the dropdown's current look; only the icons are new.</p><ul><li><strong>Template</strong> <code>app/components/app-layouts/application-header.hbs</code> (~l.30-39): in each <code>LinkTo</code> inside <code>div.create-module-dropdown-content</code>, add a Font Awesome 4 icon before the label: <code>&lt;i class="fa fa-fw fa-tasks"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;</code> for Issue, <code>fa-comments</code> for Conversation, <code>fa-briefcase</code> for Project. These are the icons the nav menu uses in <code>app/utils/metadata/metadata.js</code> (<code>views.Navigation.items</code>). <code>fa-fw</code> keeps the labels lined up. Leave the disabled (<code>pointer-none</code>) state without a project as it is; the icon follows the link's muted colour.</li><li><strong>Styles</strong> <code>app/styles/modules/header.scss</code>: the dropdown sits inside <code>button.create-module-btn</code>, so the rule <code>.create-module-btn i</code> (margin-left 0.5rem, font-size 1.2rem) would also hit the new icons. Scope it to the caret (e.g. <code>&gt; i.fa-caret-down</code>). If needed, add a small right margin for the icons inside <code>.create-module-dropdown-content a</code>. No new colours, shadows or border-radius (design-system.md).</li><li><strong>Test</strong> <code>tests/integration/components/app-layouts/application-header-test.js</code>: when the dropdown is open, each entry renders its icon (<code>fa-tasks</code>, <code>fa-comments</code>, <code>fa-briefcase</code>) before the translated label.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Opening "New" shows Issue, Conversation and Project, each with its n