6bd18a306aee-a7e9-ca02-35851eb7a0d7	External Request: Query: recognise NULL and EMPTY by the operator, not by text anywhere in the leaf	2026-11-06 21:40:59	2026-11-07 06:50:38	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Prometheus (idea "Query Builder", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p><strong>Request from A Prometheus (ezSearch).</strong> Prometheus is replacing jQuery QueryBuilder with ezSearch, a search bar plus a visual builder that produce Gaia's existing query format. Gaia misparses any leaf that contains the uppercase words NULL or EMPTY, even inside a value. For example, <code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS NULL pointer)</code> is treated as a nullary operator and fails. Until this is fixed, ezSearch refuses such values. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Where</strong></p><ul><li><code>core/mvc/models/query/Clause.php</code> <code>prepareWhere</code> ~l.159: <code>preg_match('@NULL|EMPTY@', $substatement)</code> decides the value offset from the whole leaf text.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed change</strong></p><ul><li>Split the leaf into field and operator first, and treat it as nullary only when the operator token itself is <code>NULL</code>, <code>!NULL</code>, <code>EMPTY</code> or <code>!EMPTY</code>.</li><li>Every other operator keeps its value, even when the value contains those words.</li><li>The wire format does not change.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Tests (api-tester cases on <code>GET /issue?query=</code>, see the run-tests skill):<ul><li><code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS NULL pointer)</code> and <code>(Issue.subject : EMPTY box)</code> filter by those strings.</li><li><code>(Issue.milestoneId NULL)</code>, <code>(Issue.milestoneId !NULL)</code>, <code>(Issue.milestoneId EMPTY)</code> and <code>(Issue.milestoneId !EMPTY)</code> behave as today.</li><li><code>: null</code> still means IS NULL (<code>isNullSentinelValue</code>).</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> binding values (separate request), quoted values with brackets.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 3</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4301	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	77c73c366ae8-73b7-51f2-b6608da2587e	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	f010d4196aee-a7e9-ca02-ec0d92d2abd6	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 06:50:38	agaia	0	0
672039386aec-f3eb-ed75-e9d63c0de9c8	Docker: copy custom.ini (memory_limit 512M) into the Gaia images	2026-11-05 07:29:43	2026-11-11 12:26:37	0	<p><code>docker/php/conf.d/custom.ini</code> sets <code>memory_limit = 512M</code>, but only the bind mounts in <code>docker-compose.yaml</code> apply it. Neither Dockerfile copies it, so the deployed image built from <code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code> runs with the base image's default memory limit.</p><ul><li><code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code>: add <code>COPY ./docker/php/conf.d/custom.ini /usr/local/etc/php/conf.d/zz-custom.ini</code> next to the existing <code>zz-opcache.ini</code> copy.</li><li><code>Dockerfile</code> (local build): add the same <code>COPY</code> so the image is correct without compose too. The existing compose mounts stay as they are.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>An image built from <code>docker/dev/Dockerfile</code> reports <code>memory_limit =&gt; 512M</code> from <code>docker run --rm &lt;image&gt; php -i | grep memory_limit</code>, with no volumes mounted.</li><li>The same holds for an image built from <code>Dockerfile</code>.</li><li>The local compose stack still starts and reports 512M.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> changing the base image in <code>docker-images/gaia</code>, other ini settings and the compose mounts.</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 2</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	8a024ab56ad5-2c2e-412a-dd21fa8ef390	4289	2026-11-12	2026-11-05	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	5f5bbdf46aec-f3eb-ed75-4f1de682f8f8	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Agent Odysseus	8ec31dc66aec-f3eb-ed75-4f121f0433e8	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-05 09:16:49	agaia	0	0
c53a43286af7-7919-f6fb-018e1f3c954d	Modal migration: roles, settings, agents and profile to AppUi::Modal	2026-11-13 13:33:57	2026-11-13 15:33:34	0	<p>Depends on #4516. Move these screens from <code>BootstrapModal</code> to <code>AppUi::Modal</code> and remove their <code>$('.modal').modal('hide')</code> calls: close by returning <code>true</code>/a Promise from <code>@confirm</code>, or by flipping the <code>{{#if}}</code> that renders the modal.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>app/templates/app/role.hbs</code> (2) and <code>app/controllers/app/role.js</code></li>\n<li><code>app/templates/app/role/page.hbs</code> (2) and <code>app/controllers/app/role/page.js</code> (2 jQuery hide calls)</li>\n<li><code>app/templates/app/settings/issue-statuses.hbs</code>, <code>issue-types.hbs</code> and their controllers (2 jQuery hide calls each)</li>\n<li><code>app/templates/app/settings/services.hbs</code> (3)</li>\n<li><code>app/components/agent/credentials.hbs</code> (2)</li>\n<li>Two hand-built modals that use Bootstrap modal markup without <code>BootstrapModal</code>: <code>app/templates/app/settings/email.hbs</code> (test-settings modal) and <code>app/components/user/profile-picture-cropper.hbs</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Update the integration and acceptance tests of these screens only (role, settings, agent and profile steps). Do not edit the shared <code>modal-steps.js</code>/<code>list-steps.js</code>. Apply the PowerSelect-in-modal and Messenger approach documented in #4516. Runs in parallel with the other migration issues: they share no files.</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	549d42946ad7-581a-8cbb-bbef380694da	1	4521	2026-11-20	2026-11-13	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	70a8ecd06af3-1487-2734-22a7ca0b5d62	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Achilles	Hammad Hassan	de472e046af7-8e6b-a180-e59f1f8e7c9f	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-13 15:33:34	aprom	0	0
fb5f83236aee-99ea-ca02-67e54fceedc7	ezSearch: Issue and Project schemas and the query-schema service	2026-11-06 21:39:07	2026-11-06 23:11:55	0	<p>ezSearch needs to know, per module, which fields can be queried, their types and their values. Today that lives in each controller's <code>metadata.filters</code> in the jQuery plugin's format (<code>controllers/app/project/issue/index.js:35-144</code>, <code>controllers/app/projects/index.js:30</code>). This issue moves it into schemas built with <code>createSchema</code> (query-model issue) and a service that loads the values. No page uses it yet, and the controllers stay as they are.</p><p><strong>Changes</strong></p><ul><li><code>app/utils/query/schemas/issue.js</code>, module <code>Issue</code>, with the same field ids as today's Issue filters:<ul><li><code>Issue.issueNumber</code> and <code>parentissue.issueNumber</code> are number fields.</li><li><code>Issue.subject</code> is the text field.</li><li><code>Issue.status</code>, <code>issuemilestone.name</code>, <code>issuetype.name</code> and <code>Issue.priority</code> are enum fields.</li><li><code>Issue.startDate</code> and <code>Issue.endDate</code> are dates.</li><li><code>assignedTo.name</code>, <code>ownedBy.name</code> and <code>reportedBy.name</code> are user fields.</li><li>Aliases: number/#, subject, status, milestone, type, priority/prio, start, end, parent, assignee, owner, reporter.</li><li>Labels use the existing <code>views.app.issue.fields.*</code> keys.</li></ul></li><li><code>app/utils/query/schemas/project.js</code>, module <code>Project</code>: <code>Project.name</code> (the text field), <code>Project.shortCode</code>, <code>Project.status</code> and <code>manager.name</code>, matching today's projects filters.</li><li><code>app/services/query-schema.js</code>: <code>load(module, {projectId})</code> returns a Promise of a schema with its values loaded in parallel through the store, using the same stored values as today:<ul><li>status by name (as <code>statusOptionsByName</code>, issue statuses of the project);</li><li>milestone names of the project;</li><li>issue type names;</li><li>priority from <code>views.app.issue.lists.priority</code>;</li><li>member names, carrying each user's id and profile picture for avatars.</li></ul>Values are cached per module and project; callers check <code>isDestroying</code>/<code>isDestroyed</code> after awaiting.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li>Unit tests: each schema resolves its aliases and labels, and the service returns the loaded values from Mirage (add handlers only where missing) and caches per project.</li><li>The parser's loose examples also pass against the real Issue schema with Mirage data.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> schemas for other modules, changing the controllers.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> aprom-4293</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: simple</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	51754f446ae4-9faf-391a-2704d46e39cb	4295	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Agent Nestor	Agent Agamemnon	921b78626aee-2bf2-c2c7-a8bbd55033fd	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-06 23:11:55	aprom	0	0
812984526aee-a7e9-ca02-bc54a4506bcc	External Request: Query: quote-aware leaf parsing so values may contain brackets and apostrophes	2026-11-06 21:41:21	2026-11-07 12:28:26	0	<p><strong>External Request</strong> from A Prometheus (idea "Query Builder", raised by Hammad Hassan). Evaluate it before implementing it: accept, adapt or decline it on this issue.</p><p><strong>Request from A Prometheus (ezSearch).</strong> ezSearch writes values with spaces in single quotes and would like to allow any text in a value. Gaia's leaf extraction is a regex (<code>@\\([^(]*[^)]\\)@</code> in <code>Clause.php</code> ~l.152, another one in <code>query/Meta.php</code> <code>extractWhereSubstatements</code> ~l.223 and in <code>Clause::extractWhereSubstatements</code> ~l.360). So a value containing <code>(</code> or <code>)</code>, even when quoted, splits the leaf, and an apostrophe can't be written at all. ezSearch refuses these characters until this is fixed. Please accept, adapt or decline.</p><p><strong>Proposed contract</strong></p><ul><li>A value may be wrapped in single quotes, and inside quotes <code>(</code>, <code>)</code>, <code>,</code> and the words AND, OR, NULL and EMPTY are plain text.</li><li>An apostrophe inside a quoted value is written as two apostrophes (<code>'O''Brien'</code>).</li><li>IN lists stay <code>CONTAINS 'a','b'</code>, now split on commas outside quotes.</li><li>Unquoted values keep today's behaviour, so existing saved searches and URLs keep working.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed change</strong></p><ul><li>One small quote-aware tokenizer for the where string (e.g. <code>core/mvc/models/query/WhereTokenizer.php</code>) that yields the leaves with their positions, used by <code>Clause::prepareWhere</code>, <code>Clause::extractWhereSubstatements</code> and <code>Meta</code> in place of the regexes.</li><li>It works on top of the bound values from the bind-values request.</li></ul><p><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong></p><ul><li><code>(Issue.subject CONTAINS 'fix (urgent)')</code>, <code>(Issue.subject : 'O''Brien')</code> and <code>(assignedTo.name CONTAINS 'Rana Nouman','Hammad Hassan')</code> filter correctly.</li><li>All existing query cases pass unchanged.</li><li>Tests added per the run-tests skill.</li></ul><p><strong>Out of scope:</strong> double-quoted values, changes to the operators. Prometheus relaxes its refusals in a later phase, once this is merged.</p><p><strong>Depends on:</strong> agaia-4302</p><p><strong>Estimated files:</strong> 6</p><p>Complexity: complex</p>	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	b7844c206ad7-8b87-6fc0-22987a8fb708	1	4303	2026-11-14	2026-11-07	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	77c73c366ae8-73b7-51f2-b6608da2587e	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Agent Nestor	Hammad Hassan	572396636aee-7d6c-248d-6527ef890f4a	402f48b562c6-8e43-a8e0-0abdb1b2f5be	2026-11-07 12:28:26	agaia	0	0
