2b77eab6690c-69f4-a91c-3a952b4b6fea	A Spacer	2025-11-06 10:40:43	2026-09-15 08:17:40	2025-11-06	2025-12-31	as	Kanban	1	1	<h2>Project Vision Document: Spacer</h2>\n<h3>1. Project Overview and Name</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Project Name:</strong> Spacer</li>\n<li><strong>Company:</strong> Rolustech</li>\n<li><strong>Vision Statement:</strong> To empower every Rolustech employee with a unified, intuitive platform for <strong>automated collaboration and communication</strong>, seamlessly bridging physical meeting rooms and persistent digital discussions through Google Spaces, while ensuring centralized administrative control.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. Goals and Problem Statement</h3>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<h4>Key Problem Solved</h4>\n<p>Currently, organizing collaboration is fragmented and overly dependent on a few administrators. This includes manual, email-based management of <strong>physical meeting room bookings</strong> and limited access to <strong>Google Space creation</strong>. This bottleneck slows down team coordination and limits reactive discussion startup.<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<h4>Core Goals</h4>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Automate Resource Management:</strong> Provide a clear, real-time view of physical meeting room availability and enable easy, conflict-free booking for all employees.</li>\n<li><strong>Decentralize Digital Collaboration:</strong> Empower authorized Managers and select Admins to instantly create and manage Google Spaces, shifting space creation from a single-point bottleneck to a dynamic, role-based function.</li>\n<li><strong>Unify Scheduling:</strong> Offer a dedicated in-app calendar view that aggregates and visualizes both physical room bookings (via Google Calendar sync) and scheduled virtual meetings.</li>\n<li><strong>Maintain Control:</strong> Ensure that while user access is expanded, overall administrative oversight (e.g., room configuration, manager permissions, and the single-proxy Google account) remains centralized.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<h4>Definition of Success</h4>\n<p>The project will be considered a success when we achieve a measurable <strong>increase in the number of authorized users</strong> (Managers and expanded Admin group) who are empowered to perform essential functions, specifically:<br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Effective <strong>role-based creation and management of Google Spaces</strong>.</li>\n<li>Successful, <strong>conflict-free booking of physical meeting rooms</strong> by the general employee population.</li>\n<li>The system facilitates a more <strong>efficient and decentralized organizational workflow</strong> for meetings and follow-up discussions.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. Scope and Key Features</h3>\n<p>| <strong>Area</strong> | <strong>Feature/Functionality</strong> | <strong>User Role</strong> | <strong>Details</strong> |<br>\n|<br>\n| <strong>Physical Room Management</strong> | <strong>Room Booking</strong> | All Employees | Users can book available physical meeting rooms without conflict. |<br>\n|  | <strong>Availability Calendar</strong> | All Employees | Dedicated in-app calendar showing real-time booked slots for all rooms. |<br>\n|  | <strong>Room Configuration</strong> | Admins Only | Control over adding, modifying, or removing physical meeting rooms. |<br>\n| <strong>Digital Space Management</strong> | <strong>Space Creation</strong> | Managers &amp; Admins | Ability to instantly create new Google Spaces for team discussions. |<br>\n|  | <strong>Space Management</strong> | Managers &amp; Admins | Tools to view and manage Spaces they have created. |<br>\n| <strong>Core Platform</strong> | <strong>Google Calendar Sync</strong> | All Users | Synchronization with Google Calendar to determine room availability. |<br>\n|  | <strong>Authentication</strong> | All Employees | Mandatory Single Sign-On (SSO) using Rolustech's $\\text{rolustech.com}$ and $\\text{rolustech.net}$ domains. |</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Future enhancements, such as attending Google Meets and taking in-app notes, are explicitly out of the scope for the Minimum Viable Product (MVP).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>4. Technical Requirements &amp; Integrations</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Authentication:</strong> Google SSO ($\\text{rolustech.com}$ and $\\text{rolustech.net}$).</li>\n<li><strong>Physical Room Integration:</strong> Requires synchronization/linking with existing Google Calendar resources (meeting room emails) to verify availability.</li>\n<li><strong>Google Spaces Integration:</strong> A <strong>single, proxy Google account</strong> will be utilized at the backend to facilitate the creation and initial management of Google Spaces on behalf of the authorized Managers/Admins, abstracting the complexity from the end-user.</li>\n<li><strong>Calendar:</strong> Must support a dedicated application-side calendar view.</li>\n</ul>\n	in_progress		\N	1	\N	\N	Hammad Hassan	Hammad Hassan	0	1
