COPY public.skills (id, name, description, content, version, "createdUser", "createdUserName", "modifiedUser", "modifiedUserName", "dateCreated", "dateModified", deleted) FROM stdin;
3cf32f346ae8-21c5-cab4-5ab0d9b98253	Milestone Retrospective	The skill to generate retrospective reports	# Milestone retrospective\n\nYou review one completed milestone and write its retrospective. This skill is the method: what to gather,\nwhat to measure and what the report must contain. Your role prompt decides where the report goes: the one\n`Retro - <milestone name>` issue, created or updated as it describes. That issue is your only write. Never\nchange, comment on, assign or log time on any other issue, and do not create wiki pages.\n\n## 1. Gather the facts\n\nFor the milestone you were given (project + milestone name and id):\n- The milestone: name, start and end dates, status, description.\n- Every issue in it: number, subject, type, status, priority, assignee, start and end dates, estimate,\n  time logged, parent, and when it was moved to done.\n- Issues that were in the milestone and were moved out, or added after its start, when the history shows it.\n- The threads of issues that went to feedback, pending or were reopened: read why.\n\nIf you cannot read the milestone or its issues, stop and finish with outcome `blocked`, saying exactly\nwhat you could not read and what you did gather. Do not create a half-finished retro issue. Never\nestimate or invent a number you could not read.\n\n## 2. Work out the numbers\n\n| Measure | How |\n|---|---|\n| Planned | issues in the milestone at its start date |\n| Added | issues added after the start date |\n| Delivered | issues with status done |\n| Not delivered | everything else, by status |\n| Delivery rate | delivered ÷ (planned + added) |\n| Estimate accuracy | total time logged ÷ total estimate, over issues with both |\n| Overruns | issues whose time logged is more than 1.5 × their estimate |\n| Late | done after the milestone end date, or not done |\n| Rework | issues that went back from in_review/done, or had a fix-up issue |\n| Waiting | issues that spent time in feedback or pending, and how long |\n\nLeave a measure out, and say so under Data gaps, when the data for it is missing.\n\n## 3. Write the report into the retro issue\n\nThe retro issue's description follows the shape in your role prompt (header line, Summary, What went\nwell, What didn't go well, Patterns, Surprises, Proposed actions, Data gaps, Issue ledger). Fill it from\nthis skill as follows:\n\n- **Header line:** dates, issue counts and logged vs estimated hours from the numbers above.\n- **Numbers:** add this table directly after Summary, with the measures you could compute:\n\n      ## Numbers\n      | Measure | Value |\n      |---|---|\n      | Planned / added | 12 / 3 |\n      | Delivered | 13 of 15 (87%) |\n      | Estimate accuracy | 1.3× (logged 52h against 40h estimated) |\n      | Late | 2 |\n      | Rework | 1 |\n      | Waiting | 2 issues, 3d in feedback |\n\n- **What didn't go well:** include the not-delivered issues, each with its status and why (from the thread).\n- **Patterns:** include the biggest estimate overruns and underruns, with a one-line reason each and any\n  pattern by type, repo or size.\n- **Proposed actions:** at most five, most valuable first. Each says what to change, which process or tool\n  owns it (never a person), and how we'll know it worked, and traces to a point above.\n- **Data gaps:** every measure you left out and why.\n\nKeep the prose to about 800 words; the tables carry the detail.\n\n## Rules\n- Blameless: talk about work, process and tools, never about a person's or agent's performance.\n- Every claim points to its evidence: an issue number (`#1234`), a date or a number from the tables.\n- Report what the data shows; label opinions as such ("likely", "suggests").\n- Use the tracker's names exactly (status, issue type, milestone).\n- Finish with outcome `done`, giving the retro issue's number and the three most important findings.	1	1	Hammad Hassan	1	Hammad Hassan	2026-11-02 20:27:41	2026-11-09 12:17:41	f
\.
