22bb1b486af1-a449-3228-2561d11276b2	22ae5ae16af1-a449-3228-0ebe34227084	2	d883f1756aeb-924f-f101-622ecbc66dce	actor	run_agent	completed	blocked	{"agentId":"73094b556ae8-11b0-bd37-4da81643c41f","prompt":"Project ID: add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729 \\nMilestone ID: 9cacd6286ae5-b7f5-613b-853cf931f5e8 Milestone Name: aga-v1"}	{"agentId":"73094b556ae8-11b0-bd37-4da81643c41f","actorUserId":"72e3d4a86ae8-11b0-bd37-a3bd55a4171b","claimBy":"2026-11-09 12:20:54","finishBy":"2026-11-09 16:05:54","outcome":"blocked","comment":"<p><strong>Blocked: cannot create the retro issue.<\\/strong><\\/p><p>Every <code>gaia_create_issue<\\/code> call in A Prometheus fails with <em>Gaia GET issuestatus returned 403: Access Denied<\\/em>. This happened with an explicit status and type, and again with only the required fields. <code>gaia_project_options<\\/code> fails with the same 403, and <code>gaia_whoami<\\/code> could not read Hera's memberships (also 403). So Hera's Gaia account seems to lack read access to issuestatus (and membership) in A Prometheus. No search found an existing \\"Retro - aga-v1\\" issue, and nothing was written to the tracker.<\\/p><p><strong>What would unblock it:<\\/strong> grant agent.hera read access to issuestatus (and membership) in A Prometheus, or create an empty \\"Retro - aga-v1\\" issue assigned to Hammad Hassan with no milestone, and I will fill it in. Then re-dispatch Hera.<\\/p><p><strong>Gathered (all 79 issues read):<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Delivered 78 of 79 (99%); #4341 is wont_fix because #4339 had already fixed the overlap.<\\/li><li>1,527 min (25h 27m) logged, all agent active minutes. No issue has a time estimate (0m everywhere), so estimate accuracy and overruns cannot be computed.<\\/li><li>Nothing was late: every issue was done before 2026-11-30.<\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong>Three most important findings:<\\/strong><\\/p><ol><li>Test infrastructure caused the most lost cycles: Docker down (#4207, #4208, #4222, #4242, #4244, #4287, #4340, #4343), flaky tests (edit project: #4205-#4208; file-preview: #4273, #4282, #4283, #4287), and a shared test log giving contradictory results (#4207).<\\/li><li>Missing \\"Depends on\\" links on the first batch (#4036, #4045, #4056, #4057, #4058, #4059) meant each was assigned, blocked and reset before shipping on 2026-11-02. The ezSearch chain, by contrast, was serialised cleanly by file-overlap holds.<\\/li><li>From #4323 on, PRs were not sent to CodeRabbit (credit used up), and browser checks on 21 UI issues plus many design-review follow-ups were left to the human reviewer. #4338's Task Board search design also led to five follow-up issues (#4339, #4340, #4341, #4344, #4347).<\\/li><\\/ol><p>The full retro text (summary, numbers, went well and didn't, patterns, surprises, five proposed actions, data gaps and the 79-row ledger) is drafted. I did not create a partial issue.<\\/p>"}	\N	2026-11-09 12:05:54	2026-11-09 12:32:04	1570000	2026-11-09 12:05:54	2026-11-09 12:32:04	f
